{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "HYFR (Hell Ya Fucking Right)", "line": "She say she hate that she love me and she wish I was average", "vault_lines": ["And I say hell yeah, hell yeah, hell yeah", "I was aggressive and she was sober", "She say she hate that she love me and she wish I was average"], "meaning": "Pertaining to how in love this woman is of Drake, possibly a fan of his, he shares with everybody how much she wishes he wasn’t famous…. assuming she doesn’t hold the same status as he.\n“she wish I was average”\n“i flew jet, she flew commercial”\nthere is an obvious difference in their money and societal status…", "annotation_id": "25999967", "url": "https://genius.com/25999967", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "HYFR (Hell Ya Fucking Right)", "line": "Uh, so much for being optimistic", "vault_lines": ["Uh, so much for being optimistic"], "meaning": "we want to reiterate how annoyed Drake is of this woman. “Uh So much for being optimistic” he thought she was gone, but in the coming lyrics we see she’s back and he can’t do anything about it.\n🍵", "annotation_id": "25999950", "url": "https://genius.com/25999950", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "HYFR (Hell Ya Fucking Right)", "line": "And I say hell yeah, hell yeah, hell yeah Fuckin’ right, fuckin’ right, alright And we say hell yeah, hell yeah, hell yeah Fuckin’ right, fuckin’ right, alright", "vault_lines": ["And I say hell yeah, hell yeah, hell yeah", "Fuckin' right, fuckin' right, alright", "And we say hell yeah, hell yeah, hell yeah", "Fuckin' right, damn right, alright", "And we say hell yeah, yeah, yeah, hell yeah", "Fuckin' right, damn right, alright, aw, yeah"], "meaning": "His answers show irrelevance, carelessness, and a “i give no fuck” attitude. Drake is so tired of these women…..\n\nbasically he’s answering her with a “blah, blah, blah”\nlisten…. “fuck right, fucking right alright” “hell yeah”, that he doesn’t care", "annotation_id": "25999935", "url": "https://genius.com/25999935", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "HYFR (Hell Ya Fucking Right)", "line": "There’s women to call, there’s albums to drop, there’s liquor involved There’s stories to tell, we been through it all, damn Interviews are like confessions Get the fuck up out my dressing room, confusing me with questions like", "vault_lines": ["There's women to call, there's albums to drop, there's liquor involved", "There's stories to tell, we been through it all, damn", "Interviews are like confessions", "Get the fuck up out my dressing room, confusing me with questions like", "But interviews are like confessions", "Get the fuck up out my bedroom, confusing me with questions like"], "meaning": "Drake blows up here. He mentions a list of more important things he has to do – “albums to drop” “women to call”.\n\nhe ultimately is over this girl when he says “get the fuck up out of my dressing room”\n\n👀", "annotation_id": "25999908", "url": "https://genius.com/25999908", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "HYFR (Hell Ya Fucking Right)", "line": "Even though it’s fucked up, girl, I’m still fuckin’ with ya, damn", "vault_lines": ["Even though it's fucked up, girl, I'm still fuckin' with ya, damn"], "meaning": "He never liked her, but he still cares. An image of how we date now-a-days.", "annotation_id": "25999898", "url": "https://genius.com/25999898", "state": "pending", "votes": -2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "HYFR (Hell Ya Fucking Right)", "line": "I learned workin’ with the negatives could make for better pictures", "vault_lines": ["I learned workin' with the negatives could make for better pictures"], "meaning": "When developing film photographs, you begin with the “negatives”, named as such because the colours or light/dark areas are inverted. The negatives are then developed and turned into pictures with the true colours or light/dark areas restored. These are called “positives”\n\n\n\nThus the line becomes “…workin' with the negatives could make for better positives”. Confronting the darkness in himself and his life, Drake has found light (a more positive outlook).\n\nMore pessimistically, Drake could be lamenting that focusing on negativity and pain in his music/in interviews makes for better publicity. The “pictures” here are those taken by the paparazzi.", "annotation_id": "25176907", "url": "https://genius.com/25176907", "state": "pending", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "HYFR (Hell Ya Fucking Right)", "line": "But we still met later that night After my session, she came over I was aggressive and she was sober", "vault_lines": ["But we still met later that night", "After my session, she came over", "I was aggressive and she was sober"], "meaning": "Even though they got there in different ways, they arrived at the same destination.\n\nThe session Wayne’s referring to is a recording session. After he finished recording music in the studio she came over (probably to his house).", "annotation_id": "13296067", "url": "https://genius.com/13296067", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "HYFR (Hell Ya Fucking Right)", "line": "I learned Hennessy and enemies is one hell of a mixture", "vault_lines": ["I learned Hennessy and enemies is one hell of a mixture", "And I say hell yeah, hell yeah, hell yeah"], "meaning": "Drake plays off of mixtures of different types of alcohol and/or drugs being dangerous and potentially deadly; he compares it to drinking while beefing with someone. This might mean Drake’s acted irrationally around his enemies in the past because he was drunk. It could also mean physically fighting his enemies was more dangerous when he was intoxicated, and it led to more extreme results (injuries, damaged property etc) in the past.\n\nHennessy is a brand of cognac owned by Moët Hennessy and headquartered in Cognac, France.", "annotation_id": "13296007", "url": "https://genius.com/13296007", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "HYFR (Hell Ya Fucking Right)", "line": "Met a female dragon, had a fire conversation", "vault_lines": ["Met a female dragon, had a fire conversation"], "meaning": "Dragons are mythical creatures that breathe fire. Fire is slang for something incredible or amazing. Wayne and this girl hit it off emotionally; they connected when they met by having a great conversation​.", "annotation_id": "13295782", "url": "https://genius.com/13295782", "state": "accepted", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "HYFR (Hell Ya Fucking Right)", "line": "My nuts hang like ain’t no curfew", "vault_lines": ["My nuts hang like ain't no curfew"], "meaning": "A curfew is a regulation requiring people (usually teens) to remain indoors between specified hours, typically at night. If curfews didn’t exist people would hang out outside until morning.\n\nLil Wayne’s nuts are hanging during sexual intercourse; when a guy inserts his penis into his partner the only thing visible is his balls hanging. His balls hanging like there’s no curfew probably means him and this girl are going at it all night.", "annotation_id": "13295727", "url": "https://genius.com/13295727", "state": "accepted", "votes": 37, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "HYFR (Hell Ya Fucking Right)", "line": "Promises, I hope I never break ’em", "vault_lines": ["Promises, I hope I never break 'em"], "meaning": "Being in the industry ain’t easy and he gets really busy with his schedule, so he hopes in doesn’t make promises and gets them broken by tight schedules.\n\nThis could also be a reference to the previous line; Wayne has been with a married woman for the past month now, and as a result, she is breaking the promise of marriage. Though Wayne probably isn’t hoping he breaks such a promise (seeing as how it’s been a while since his marriage ended and Toya left), he still has those around him he wouldn’t want to hurt in such a way.", "annotation_id": "765475", "url": "https://genius.com/765475", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "HYFR (Hell Ya Fucking Right)", "line": "I took her for sushi, she wanted to fuck So we took it to go, told ’em don’t even plate it", "vault_lines": ["I took her for sushi, she wanted to fuck", "So we took it to go, told 'em don't even plate it"], "meaning": "To “plate” a dish, is to arrange the food in an appetizing way that is both visually appealing and encourages the diner to consume the dinner in a certain manner/order. Drake is telling the chef (more likely the waiter) not to bother with “plating” the dish, because they are leaving.", "annotation_id": "765456", "url": "https://genius.com/765456", "state": "accepted", "votes": 56, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "HYFR (Hell Ya Fucking Right)", "line": "[Intro: Drake] Gotta do what I gotta do Yeah Uh", "vault_lines": ["Gotta do what I gotta do"], "meaning": "“Gotta do what I gotta do” is a lyric from the song which the instrumental is taken. Swangin' and Bangin' by ESG is often regarded as a Screw-ston Anthem, as it embodies the Houston, TX lifestyle. The instrumental heard on this song is a sample of DJ Screw’s chopped and screwed mix of the song. The original instrumental can be heard on E.S.G.’s album Ocean’s of Funk, whereas another version of the song (released in ‘95: different beat) became more popular. Drake isn’t exactly swangin’ (changing lanes/switching his style up) with this track but he is certainly bangin' with this screwed up beat, which is absolutely a tip of the hat to some Houston old heads. Shortly after this song’s release on Take Care, E.S.G. recorded a freestyle over the throwback instrumental.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CAayy3659W8\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=s9LF1qBvCQs\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SpZfry8FFrM", "annotation_id": "549568", "url": "https://genius.com/549568", "state": "accepted", "votes": 36, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "HYFR (Hell Ya Fucking Right)", "line": "Do you love this shit? Are you high right now? Do you ever get nervous? Are you single? I heard you fuck your girl, is it true? You gettin’ money? You think them niggas you with is with you?", "vault_lines": ["Do you love this shit?", "Are you high right now?", "Do you ever get nervous?", "I heard you fuck your girl, is it true?", "You think them niggas you with is with you?"], "meaning": "Here Wayne imitates the sometimes ridiculous questions rappers get asked that have nothing to do about their music, life or really anything important at all. Just dumb, nosey and irrelevant questions kind of like this Wiz interview:\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=f4hmzE5lzS4", "annotation_id": "496185", "url": "https://genius.com/496185", "state": "accepted", "votes": 206, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "HYFR (Hell Ya Fucking Right)", "line": "And I think I text her and told her I made it And that’s when she text me and told me she prayed it And that’s when I text her and told her I love her Then right after, texted and told her I’m faded She asked what have I learned since getting richer?", "vault_lines": ["And I think I text her and told her I made it", "And that's when she text me and told me she prayed it", "And that's when I text her and told her I love her", "Then right after, texted and told her I'm faded", "She asked what have I learned since getting richer?"], "meaning": "Drake texts his ex right around the time of his success and to let her know he’s finally become a star. Instead of bitterness she expresses how she always wanted him to make it and Drizzy slips up and confesses he still has feelings for her (then blames it on being intoxicated).\n\nDrake borrowed the idea of rapping an awkward phone conversation from one of his favorite Wayne verses on Mario’s “Crying Out For Me.”", "annotation_id": "476877", "url": "https://genius.com/476877", "state": "accepted", "votes": 87, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "HYFR (Hell Ya Fucking Right)", "line": "We eat each other whenever we at the dinner table", "vault_lines": ["We eat each other whenever we at the dinner table"], "meaning": "The primary meaning of this line is to highlight the tension in the relationship between the protagonist (Weezy) and his girl. To “eat [at] each other” in this context means to fight viciously. Even when sitting down for a nice dinner, they can’t help but argue and attack each other.\n\nBut it’s also a double entendre––\"eat each other\" as engaging in oral sex. This particular meal is a favorite of Weezy’s.", "annotation_id": "441094", "url": "https://genius.com/441094", "state": "accepted", "votes": 51, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "HYFR (Hell Ya Fucking Right)", "line": "Or they go to Georgia State where Tuition is handled by some random nigga that live in Atlanta That she only see when she feels obligated", "vault_lines": ["Or they go to Georgia State where", "Tuition is handled by some random nigga that live in Atlanta", "That she only see when she feels obligated"], "meaning": "Drake is referring to a “sugar daddy”, a man who gives a girl money and other things in return for sex. He’s paying her tuition, and the only reason she even stays in contact with him is because she feels she has to so that he will keep giving her money.\n\nGeorgia State University is a college located in downtown Atlanta, Georgia. The school actually landed on Huffington Post’s list of Top 20 Sugar Baby Colleges.", "annotation_id": "441058", "url": "https://genius.com/441058", "state": "accepted", "votes": 74, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "HYFR (Hell Ya Fucking Right)", "line": "Is it the fall? Time for me to revisit the past", "vault_lines": ["Is it the fall? Time for me to revisit the past"], "meaning": "Drake’s birthday is October 24th, and his attachment to that month has led him to becoming a part of October’s Very Own.\n\nDuring the fall season, clocks are turned back one hour in some places, almost as if to “revisit the past” in a sense since the time had already passed.\n\nTake Care dropped November 15th, 2011, and on many tracks including this one Drake revisits past experiences.", "annotation_id": "436268", "url": "https://genius.com/436268", "state": "accepted", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "HYFR (Hell Ya Fucking Right)", "line": "All my exes live in Texas like I’m George Strait", "vault_lines": ["All my exes live in Texas like I'm George Strait"], "meaning": "Referencing legendary country music artist “King George” Strait and his 1987 single “All My Ex’s Live in Texas”.\n\nStrait has sold more than 68.5 million albums in the United States and his certifications from the RIAA include 13 multi-platinum, 33 platinum, and 38 gold albums.\n\n\n\nAccording to the RIAA, George Strait is the 12th best-selling album artist in the U.S.; Drake clearly aspires to have such stats, can you blame him? Drizzy raps about the Strait again, referencing the King of Country’s “Here For A Good Time” on Big Sean’s 2015 track “Blessings.”\n\nWhile making a reference to George Strait’s classic hit, Drake could also be speaking of all his ex’s that he’s accumulated in his days hanging out in Houston; alternatively, Drizzy might be using a little homophone wordplay (“Texas” and “texts,” of course)\n\nOf course Drake is always mentioning the great state of Texas, with songs like 9AM in Dallas and HoustonlantaVegas, the artist is no stranger to the area.", "annotation_id": "435609", "url": "https://genius.com/435609", "state": "accepted", "votes": 118, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "HYFR (Hell Ya Fucking Right)", "line": "She say this shit gon’ catch up to me, I keep tissue paper", "vault_lines": ["She say this shit gon' catch up to me, I keep tissue paper"], "meaning": "She told Wayne that ‘what goes around, comes around’. But he thinks he got it covered, he’s prepared.\n\nShe thinks that shit—as in bad karma—is going to catch up to Wayne, so he is prepared to wipe it up with toilet paper—something you’d use for wiping shit or feces.", "annotation_id": "434850", "url": "https://genius.com/434850", "state": "accepted", "votes": 83, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "HYFR (Hell Ya Fucking Right)", "line": "Bitch, if you wave, then I will surf you", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, if you wave, then I will surf you"], "meaning": "All you have to do is make the first move. And he’ll be on that, no problem!\n\n\n\n“On a wave” or “wavey” also refers to being fucked up (drunk or on pills). This could also mean that if the girl is intoxicated, Weezy will let her ride, and then he’ll drive her crazy. This foreshadows the line that comes later in the verse, “I gave her pills… she… started undressing…”\n\nCould also be heard as “if you wave then I will serve you”, as in waving to a waiter to get their attention.", "annotation_id": "434839", "url": "https://genius.com/434839", "state": "accepted", "votes": 51, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "HYFR (Hell Ya Fucking Right)", "line": "They say love is in the air, so I Hold my breath ’til my face turn purple", "vault_lines": ["They say love is in the air, so I", "Hold my breath 'til my face turn purple"], "meaning": "Apparently, Weezy doesn’t want to get married or have a titled relationship. Shocking.\n\nWayne has historically been very clear on this point and has used a line similar to this one.\n\nWayne is poking fun of the old adage that says “love is in the air.”  He wants no part of it, so he holds his breath and his face turns blue from the lack of oxygen (also known as cyanosis).", "annotation_id": "434498", "url": "https://genius.com/434498", "state": "accepted", "votes": 102, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "HYFR (Hell Ya Fucking Right)", "status": "done", "targets": 23, "clicked": 23, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-hyfr-hell-ya-fucking-right-lyrics", "genius_title": "HYFR (Hell Ya Fucking Right)"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Riddance (Aristo Diss)", "line": "Yes I took an L on my own and they didn’t damage me", "vault_lines": ["Yes I took an L on my own and they didn't damage me"], "meaning": "In the track “Good Morning (Drake Diss)”, Aristo brought up an incident where Drake was jumped at a function. Drake admitted that hands were put on him over a female, but brushed it off as if nothing happened. Drake briefly explained the situation when he called into Crack House Radio, after Aristo dropped the diss track.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ghy6YCEV-j0", "annotation_id": "8985990", "url": "https://genius.com/8985990", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Riddance (Aristo Diss)", "line": "Good riddance Aristo I just retired you!", "vault_lines": ["Good riddance Aristo I just retired you!"], "meaning": "After this track, Drake went on to become highly successful – creating multiple platinum albums, countless hit singles, and selling out arenas worldwide.\n\nAs for Aristo… he seems to have vanished. Looks like Drake really did end his career.", "annotation_id": "4361825", "url": "https://genius.com/4361825", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Riddance (Aristo Diss)", "line": "And Breana, I don’t mean to alarm ya", "vault_lines": ["And Breana, I don't mean to alarm ya"], "meaning": "Drake is making fun of Aristo’s birth name, Breana. (Just remember what they say about glass houses, Aubrey)", "annotation_id": "3897101", "url": "https://genius.com/3897101", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Riddance (Aristo Diss)", "line": "Some of them believe you got money you little liar you", "vault_lines": ["Some of them believe you got money you little liar you"], "meaning": "Aristo was lying about how much money he had and people believed it. Drake is also, again making fun of Aristo’s height by calling him “little”.", "annotation_id": "3002166", "url": "https://genius.com/3002166", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Riddance (Aristo Diss)", "line": "You can call me the Grinch, cause y’all are nothing but Who’s", "vault_lines": ["You can call me the Grinch, cause y'all are nothing but Who's"], "meaning": "Brigante compares him to the Grinch, one of the most famous Dr. Seuss characters. In How the Grinch Stole Christmas!, the Grinch was a cruel, grouchy creature who ended up stealing presents, ornaments, and everything else Christmas related, from families in Whoville.\n\n\n\nAristo must be a Who, since that’s what anybody says when his name is mentioned.\n\nRandom person: Have you heard of Aristo?\nBrigante: Who?", "annotation_id": "2641204", "url": "https://genius.com/2641204", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Riddance (Aristo Diss)", "line": "But you need to get outside the car to shoot this video in Parma (Tony!)", "vault_lines": ["But you need to get outside the car to shoot this video in Parma (Tony!)"], "meaning": "Parma Court is one of the hardest parts in toronto. Aristo shot part of the video for “100 Strong Arm” in Parma with Young Tony, but was too scared to get out of the car when filming.", "annotation_id": "1525260", "url": "https://genius.com/1525260", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Riddance (Aristo Diss)", "line": "You try to cover up your lies like a canopy", "vault_lines": ["You try to cover up your lies like a canopy"], "meaning": "A canopy can be either a roof-like structure or the uppermost layer of trees in a forest. Either way, canopies cover whatever is below them, similar to how Aristo tries to cover up his fake image by trying to act real.", "annotation_id": "571180", "url": "https://genius.com/571180", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Riddance (Aristo Diss)", "line": "They say Drake killed it like young girls at a private school", "vault_lines": ["They say Drake killed it like young girls at a private school"], "meaning": "In this line, Drake uses “killed” as a homonym for “kilt.”\n\n\n\nKilts are a garment with immense Scottish history, and although they’re wore by men in Scotland, their counterpart, the skirt, is a main staple in any female private school uniform.", "annotation_id": "338534", "url": "https://genius.com/338534", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
