{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Dash", "line": "(Freebandz)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Future founded his record label Freebandz in December of 2012. His signed artists are collectively known as Freeband Gang.\n\n\n\nFreebandz logo", "annotation_id": "29587826", "url": "https://genius.com/29587826", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Dash", "line": "(Wizard)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "In a 2019 interview with Genius, Future explained the origin of his alias “THE WIZRD” and the meaning behind his 2019 project that would be named after it:\n\nMy uncle used to always call me “THE WIZRD,” rest in peace. But, that was his thing—he called me “THE WIZRD.” And it was just showing love to him. Also, it was just like dedicating this album to him. And the name that he respected and I feel like I’ve worked for and I’ve worked to become. Everything like he seen before it even happened.\n\nFuture has used the moniker throughout his music, for example:\n\nHe uses it multiple times on 2014’s Monster, such as on “Hardly”:\n\nThis that Super Future, Fire Marshall Future, Future Hendrix\nYou know, THE WIZRD, you understand me?\n\nOn Beast Mode tracks like “Forever Eva”:\n\nFuture Hendrix forever\nTHE WIZRD\n\nThroughout his July, 2015 LP DS2 on tracks such as “Rotation”:\n\nTHE WIZRD, top shotta", "annotation_id": "29577340", "url": "https://genius.com/29577340", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Dash", "line": "(Metro Boomin want some more, nigga)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The sample from “Some More” by Young Thug has become a very common production tag for Metro Boomin. This line is sung by Young Thug.", "annotation_id": "11914021", "url": "https://genius.com/11914021", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Dash", "line": "I just took me a trip out to Africa (Africa) See how we came from the mud and the bottom, we did it (Bottom, we did it, we did it, woo) I see how they counted us out, bet they never gon’ do it again", "vault_lines": ["I know how to cook it (Cook it)", "I just took me a trip out to Africa (Africa)", "See how we came from the mud and the bottom, we did it (Bottom, we did it, we did it, woo)", "I see how they counted us out, bet they never gon' do it again", "Super just showed out again", "And we just keep servin' and servin' again and again and again and again", "I did the digital dash (I did it)", "And I got the, I got the, I got the, I got the, I"], "meaning": "Future grew up in Kirkwood, Atlanta. The neighbourhood makes up part of the police Zone 6, infamous for it’s drug and gang related activity. The majority of the people who grew up there will never see the outside of Atlanta, let alone Africa.\n\n\n\nFuture’s not the only rapper to have visited Africa recently. Kendrick Lamar’s album, To Pimp A Butterfly was heavily influenced by his experience on the continent.", "annotation_id": "7844499", "url": "https://genius.com/7844499", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Dash", "line": "Super just showed out again And we just keep servin’ and servin’ again and again and again and again", "vault_lines": ["Super just showed out again", "And we just keep servin' and servin' again and again and again and again"], "meaning": "Drake and Future (Super Future) have dropped seven tapes combined in the last year, including: Monster, Honest, Beast Mode, 56 Nights, DS2, If You’re Reading This It’s Too Late, and What a Time to Be Alive. They just keep serving the populous with back to back hits.", "annotation_id": "7841469", "url": "https://genius.com/7841469", "state": "accepted", "votes": 55, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Dash", "line": "Scooter in here with the zombies Gucci get out, it’s a problem", "vault_lines": ["Scooter in here with the zombies", "Gucci get out, it's a problem"], "meaning": "Young Scooter (and the Black Migo Gang) is down with Future and FreeBandz, as well as Gucci Mane, the locked up ATL trap music pioneer.\n\nGucci has been locked up since September 13, 2013 for possession of a firearm as a convicted felon. Despite this, he continues to release new music. Gucci Mane was released from jail May 26, 2016. Upon release, Gucci released 3 new tracks, including the Drake assisted “Back on The Road.”", "annotation_id": "7839743", "url": "https://genius.com/7839743", "state": "accepted", "votes": 63, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Dash", "line": "You see why these niggas be hatin’, ignorin’, I’m goin’ right in (Yeah) I was born to get this money in this life of sin (Life of sin) I poured up before they got my dawg on murder again (Murder) See the fire come out the ass on the Lamborghini (Skrrt)", "vault_lines": ["Rollin' in the coupe, yeah", "They get on my motherfuckin' nerves (My motherfuckin' nerves)", "I pull up right now, I'm parallel (Skrrt)", "You see why these niggas be hatin', ignorin', I'm goin' right in (Yeah)", "I was born to get this money in this life of sin (Life of sin)", "I poured up before they got my dawg on murder again (Murder)", "See the fire come out the ass on the Lamborghini (Skrrt)", "I got the digital dash", "I got my foot on they neck and my foot on the gas", "And I got the, I got the, I got the, I got the, I"], "meaning": "Future was born to be a hustler in the harshest of environments.  He’s seen it all, including murder.\n\nThis isn’t the first time Future has shown his affection for money. On “Future Back” he raps,\n\nBut you good cause I love money, February", "annotation_id": "7838445", "url": "https://genius.com/7838445", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Dash", "line": "Had a stick on me, that’s a first (Yeah) Got your bitch on me gettin’ murked (Let’s get it) I post up and that’s confident (That’s confident) I boast up in a drop six (Drop six) Had a Ghost Royce and I pop shit (Pop shit) I’m a dope boy with that car trip (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Get it, get it, hey", "Come back on your bitch in a six-trey (Woo)", "Had a stick on me, that's a first (Yeah)", "Got your bitch on me gettin' murked (Let's get it)", "I post up and that's confident (That's confident)", "I boast up in a drop six (Drop six)", "Had a Ghost Royce and I pop shit (Pop shit)", "I'm a dope boy with that car trip (Yeah)", "And I got the, I got the, I got the, I got the, I"], "meaning": "Future’s got quite the car collection. After mentioning a 7 Series BMW earlier in this verse, he goes onto name drop the BMW 6 Series and a Rolls Royce Ghost. The 6 series comes comes in convertible (droptop) and manual (stick).\n\n\n\n“Stick” is slang for a gun and is popular in Southern America. It’s called a “stick” because of the length of the magazine clip.\n\nIn contrast to what he says, this isn’t the first time Future has had a stick on him.", "annotation_id": "7836770", "url": "https://genius.com/7836770", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Dash", "line": "I got my foot on they neck and my foot on the gas", "vault_lines": ["I got the digital dash", "I got my foot on they neck and my foot on the gas", "And I got the, I got the, I got the, I got the, I"], "meaning": "Drake’s not slowing up, and neither is his work ethic. He’ll step on anyone who gets in the way (i.e Meek Mill) if he needs to. “Foot on the gas” means he’s going extra hard in the studio.\n\nThis line is reminiscent of Kendrick Lamar’s on his 2013 BET Cypher verse,\n\nI got my thumb on Hip Hop, and my foot in the back of your ass", "annotation_id": "7835888", "url": "https://genius.com/7835888", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Dash", "line": "That’s when you know it’s a body Zone 6, they know it’s a body Kirkwood, they know it’s a body Lil Mexico know it’s a body", "vault_lines": ["That's when you know it's a body", "Zone 6, they know it's a body", "Kirkwood, they know it's a body", "Lil Mexico know it's a body"], "meaning": "Lil Mexico is a nickname for Kirkwood, a hood in East Atlanta, known for drugs and gang violence. Zone 6 is the police zone. This is also where Future, Gucci Mane, and funnily enough, Quentin Miller grew up.\n\nIs Drake trolling us? It’s not uncommon for an MC has been tripped up by a “ghostwriter” referring people/places the performing MC would not be familiar with.", "annotation_id": "7835595", "url": "https://genius.com/7835595", "state": "accepted", "votes": 63, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Dash", "line": "I move the game up, I’m reckless I’m Harlem shaking through the pressure I might put Diddy on my next shit I might could fit you in on Wednesday I’m not here for no pretend shit", "vault_lines": ["I move the game up, I'm reckless", "I'm Harlem shaking through the pressure", "I might put Diddy on my next shit", "I might could fit you in on Wednesday", "I'm not here for no pretend shit"], "meaning": "A direct reference to the original Harlem Shake, made popular by Diddy and G. Dep in the “2001 (Let’s Get It)” video.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=az7pn5zfUsU\n\nThis is the first time Drake has mentioned Diddy since the pair allegedly beefed over the “0 to 100” beat, which led to Diddy punching Drake in the face. Diddy has since denied this.\n\nDrake feels reckless making so much music and pushing hip-hop to new heights. So scheduling you in next Wednesday might be an issue…Drizzy only made $39.5 million dollars in 2014.", "annotation_id": "7835540", "url": "https://genius.com/7835540", "state": "accepted", "votes": 82, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Dash", "line": "I’m single and shit, now she latch on me (I’m single) I told ’em I’m back, I’m a bachelor (I’m back) I get focused on millions and everything (Focused)", "vault_lines": ["I'm single and shit, now she latch on me (I'm single)", "I told 'em I'm back, I'm a bachelor (I'm back)", "I get focused on millions and everything (Focused)"], "meaning": "Future was engaged to singer Ciara before she broke up with him in August 2014. She ended the engagement after claims he cheated on her with his stylist. The pair have a son together, Future Zahir Wilburn.\n\n\n\nNow Future’s an eligible bachelor, any girl he pays attention to wants to latch on to his celebrity.", "annotation_id": "7835523", "url": "https://genius.com/7835523", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Dash", "line": "Hit her sideways when I banged her (I fucked) In the driveway on a Perc’ (A Perc’) I was sideways on a Perc’ (Pour up)", "vault_lines": ["Hit her sideways when I banged her (I fucked)", "In the driveway on a Perc' (A Perc')", "I was sideways on a Perc' (Pour up)"], "meaning": "Future enjoys highs of Percocet. The drug is commonly known as “percs” which treats severe pain and can create clumsiness. This explains why Future is “sideways,” but this time he’s inside a car, rather than a strip club.", "annotation_id": "7835491", "url": "https://genius.com/7835491", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Dash", "line": "These bitches be naggin’ the kid (Fuck ’em) They get on my motherfuckin’ nerves (My motherfuckin’ nerves) I showed up with racks and they love me (They love me) I’m smokin’ that pack and on muddy (That gushy) Taliban on these hoes (Hoes) Give a Xan’ to these hoes (These hoes) Got ’em playing with they nose (Yeah) I sleep on a beach off the avenue (The avenue)", "vault_lines": ["These bitches be naggin' the kid (Fuck 'em)", "They get on my motherfuckin' nerves (My motherfuckin' nerves)", "I showed up with racks and they love me (They love me)", "I'm smokin' that pack and on muddy (That gushy)", "Taliban on these hoes (Hoes)", "Give a Xan' to these hoes (These hoes)", "Got 'em playing with they nose (Yeah)", "I sleep on a beach off the avenue (The avenue)", "These bitches be nagging the kid", "I got the digital dash", "I got my foot on they neck and my foot on the gas", "And I got the, I got the, I got the, I got the, I"], "meaning": "With so many girls chasing him, Future sounds like he’s regretting becoming successful. He smokes the “taliban” strain of weed and sips lean while his playmates pop Xanax and snort amphetamines. Even though Xanax is commonly used to treat anxiety and panic disorders, it’s often used recreationally to help people relax.", "annotation_id": "7835461", "url": "https://genius.com/7835461", "state": "accepted", "votes": 52, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Dash", "line": "My niggas ain’t nothin’ but some bangers (Throw up) I sit in the trap with the gangsters These niggas can’t come around here ’cause it’s dangerous", "vault_lines": ["My niggas ain't nothin' but some bangers (Throw up)", "I sit in the trap with the gangsters", "These niggas can't come around here 'cause it's dangerous", "Scooter in here with the zombies"], "meaning": "Future is from Kirkwood, Atlanta. The neighbourhood is also known as Lil Mexico due to high levels of drug and gang violence. This is where Future’s “hood fame” status came from.\n\nHe’s one of two people listed on Kirkwood’s Wikipedia page under “notable people.” The other is rapper Young Scooter.", "annotation_id": "7835458", "url": "https://genius.com/7835458", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Dash", "line": "You remind me of a quarterback, your shit is all in the past", "vault_lines": ["You remind me of a quarterback, your shit is all in the past"], "meaning": "A quarterback’s main (sometimes only) job is to pass the ball. Drake plays off of this to hint that his washed up competition is living in the past (“passed”) and needs to move on with their life.\n\n\n\nSince QB Russell Wilson is dating Future’s ex Ciara – a part of his past – it’s not out of the question that this line could be aimed towards him.", "annotation_id": "7835456", "url": "https://genius.com/7835456", "state": "accepted", "votes": 76, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Dash", "line": "I came to your city with revenue (Miami) I put in work, it was evident (It was) I slide on your ass in a seven-deuce (I slide on ’em) Come back on your bitch in a six-trey (Woo) Chevy, Mercedes, I keep ‘em comin’ (Keep ’em comin’) Fuck all these bitches, I keep ‘em comin’ (Foreign) I pull up right now, I’m parallel (Skrrt) I hit your block with them swangers (I hit ’em)", "vault_lines": ["I came to your city with revenue (Miami)", "I put in work, it was evident (It was)", "I slide on your ass in a seven-deuce (I slide on 'em)", "Come back on your bitch in a six-trey (Woo)", "Chevy, Mercedes, I keep 'em comin' (Keep 'em comin')", "Fuck all these bitches, I keep 'em comin' (Foreign)", "I pull up right now, I'm parallel (Skrrt)", "I hit your block with them swangers (I hit 'em)", "I was sideways on a Perc' (Pour up)", "I boast up in a drop six (Drop six)", "I told 'em I'm back, I'm a bachelor (I'm back)"], "meaning": "Future talks cars and girls interchangeably. He name drops a 1972 Chevy Impala, and an AMG 6.3L Mercedes. In this instance, “coming” alludes to his girls climax.\n\n\n\n“Swangers” are rims that poke out about 6-8 inches.", "annotation_id": "7835375", "url": "https://genius.com/7835375", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Dash", "line": "I did the digital dash (I did it) I fucked that bitch on the passenger (One hundred) I gave that junky a blast (One hundred) I sell that dope to your mama, though (Your mama) Hot on the street like thermometers (Thermometers) You rats’ll never be honorable (Fuck ’em) They know I’ma keep that my word (Yeah) I hustle the first to the first (Future)", "vault_lines": ["I gave that junky a blast (One hundred)", "I sell that dope to your mama, though (Your mama)", "Hot on the street like thermometers (Thermometers)", "You rats'll never be honorable (Fuck 'em)", "They know I'ma keep that my word (Yeah)", "I hustle the first to the first (Future)", "I know how to cook it (Cook it)", "My dope in the bushes, I know how to cook it", "I did the digital dash (I did it)", "I got the digital dash", "I fucked that bitch on the passenger (One hundred)", "I fucked that bitch in the passenger"], "meaning": "A “digital dashboard” is the instrument cluster found in luxury vehicles. Future can afford such an expensive car because he works from the first day of each month to the first day of the next month. Avoiding “rats” (snitches) helps his work ethic and gets his bread up.\n\n\n\nFuture has released five solo projects over the last year, including: Monster, Honest, Beast Mode, 56 Nights, and DS2. Add on smash hits such as “Fuck Up Some Commas,” and it ain’t hard to tell that he’s the one heating things up in the streets.", "annotation_id": "7835232", "url": "https://genius.com/7835232", "state": "accepted", "votes": 118, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Dash", "line": "I might take Quentin to Follies You hate your life, just be honest", "vault_lines": ["I might take Quentin to Follies", "You hate your life, just be honest"], "meaning": "“Quentin” being Quentin Miller, Drake’s personal writer and the man behind the infamous Drake-Meek Mill beef. Following their exchange of diss tracks, Drake had become the undisputed most-talked about rapper in the game. Since he has a lot to thank Quentin for, it’s no wonder he would take him to Follies, the most popular strip club in Atlanta.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/wordonrd/status/634511301105057792\n\nPost-beef, there’s only one person who Drizzy thinks should hate his life: Meek Mill.", "annotation_id": "7835123", "url": "https://genius.com/7835123", "state": "accepted", "votes": 96, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Dash", "line": "These bitches be nagging the kid Fuck it, it is what it is If you get hit, you get hit I don’t forget or forgive Told myself never again I don’t let nobody in", "vault_lines": ["These bitches be naggin' the kid (Fuck 'em)", "Get it, get it, hey", "These bitches be nagging the kid", "Fuck it, it is what it is", "If you get hit, you get hit", "I don't forget or forgive", "Told myself never again", "I don't let nobody in"], "meaning": "This reiterates Drake’s “No New Friends” mantra. Whether he’s commenting on his feud with Meek Mill, or referring to girls he’s sleeping with, the message is clear: Drake’s a one time offer.", "annotation_id": "7835023", "url": "https://genius.com/7835023", "state": "accepted", "votes": 91, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Dash", "line": "When you say you love a nigga, do you really mean it? (No) When I was sleepin’ on the floor, you should see how they treated me (Hah) I pour the Actavis, pop pills so I can fight the demons (Oh)", "vault_lines": ["I was sideways on a Perc' (Pour up)", "When you say you love a nigga, do you really mean it? (No)", "When I was sleepin' on the floor, you should see how they treated me (Hah)", "I pour the Actavis, pop pills so I can fight the demons (Oh)"], "meaning": "Future pours himself lean (Activis is cough syrup consisting of codeine and promethazine) and pops pills (presumably Xanax, as previously mentioned) to forget his worries.\n\nThis isn’t the first time Future has admitted to using drugs to “fight the demons.” He’s rapped about taking Xanax on songs like “Hardly” and spoken candidly about using drugs to get over his ex-fiancée, Ciara, on songs like “Just Like Bruddas,”\n\nOff 2 milligrams, I forgot about my ex-ho", "annotation_id": "7835002", "url": "https://genius.com/7835002", "state": "accepted", "votes": 45, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Dash", "line": "I got the digital dash She want a picture with all of my niggas to just make the visual last But she too embarrassed to ask", "vault_lines": ["I did the digital dash (I did it)", "I got the digital dash", "She want a picture with all of my niggas to just make the visual last", "But she too embarrassed to ask", "And I got the, I got the, I got the, I got the, I"], "meaning": "People are envious of Drake since he became so rich and famous. As mentioned in the hook, a “digital dash” refers to an expensive car.\n\nYou know you’ve made it when fans are too afraid to ask for your picture. This was depicted in the “Energy” video.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/7LnBvuzjpr4?t=77", "annotation_id": "7834945", "url": "https://genius.com/7834945", "state": "accepted", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Dash", "line": "Just walked in with a girl that’s making triple what I’m making, what an entrance", "vault_lines": ["Just walked in with a girl that's making triple what I'm making, what an entrance"], "meaning": "Seeing that Drake had a net worth of 75 million dollars, it must be hard to find someone at his level. As of September 2015, rumours swirled that Drake was seeing Serena Williams, whose net worth is 130 million.\n\nThis has been on Drake’s to-do list since the beginning of his career—mature women with more than him were the first to tempt him.", "annotation_id": "7834898", "url": "https://genius.com/7834898", "state": "accepted", "votes": 79, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Dash", "line": "Rollin’ in the coupe, yeah Yeah Get it Get it, get it, hey", "vault_lines": ["Rollin' in the coupe, yeah", "Get it, get it, hey"], "meaning": "Future keeps his drugs in the bushes so the feds don’t find anything when they come knocking. After all, he’s no stranger to moving dope.\n\nJay Rock rapped similar lyrics on Kendrick Lamar’s “Money Trees”,\n\nDrop that work up in the bushes\nHope them boys don’t see my stash\nIf they do, tell the truth\nThis the last time you might see my ass", "annotation_id": "7834889", "url": "https://genius.com/7834889", "state": "accepted", "votes": 90, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Dash", "line": "Esco and Boomin, they got it on smash And I got the, I got the, I got the, I got the, I", "vault_lines": ["I got the digital dash", "I got my foot on they neck and my foot on the gas", "Esco and Boomin, they got it on smash", "And I got the, I got the, I got the, I got the, I"], "meaning": "Dj Esco is Future’s tour DJ, while Metro Boomin is a producer that Future has frequently collaborated with. Both are credited on What A Time To Be Alive.\n\nMetro Boomin produced almost all of Future’s Dirty Sprite 2. He’s also produced hits like “Tuesday.”\n\nEarlier this year, DJ Esco got thrown in a Dubai prison, inspiring Future’s mixtape 56 Nights.\n\nMore recently, under the name “Esco Boomin,” both made a set on OVO Sound Radio Episode 3.", "annotation_id": "7834861", "url": "https://genius.com/7834861", "state": "accepted", "votes": 88, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
