{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Overdose", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-overdose-lyrics", "genius_title": "Overdose"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Shoe Fits", "line": "Meanwhile, that nigga out in my city fuckin’ on bitches If they even mention me and showin’ me love, then it’s finished", "vault_lines": ["Meanwhile, that nigga out in my city fuckin' on bitches", "If they even mention me and showin' me love, then it's finished"], "meaning": "We now see why this girl’s man is so worried about her cheating–it’s because he’s a huge cheater himself, and he’s projecting. When he’s home, he’s slapping her just for knowing some other guy, but when he’s in Toronto, he’s cheating on her with countless women. However, this man is so pathetically insecure that he refuses to cheat with women if they mention anything about Drake.", "annotation_id": "38064746", "url": "https://genius.com/38064746", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Shoe Fits", "line": "Maybe you could stop gettin’ involved in some shit when you not involved", "vault_lines": ["Maybe you could stop gettin' involved in some shit when you not involved"], "meaning": "Drake has made it a point to address fans particularly female ones under The Shade Room‘s celebrity gossip posts. In typical fashion, he’s responding to comments suggesting fans are prying too much into his personal life or other celebrities  affairs, emphasizing that certain matters are not anyone else’s business.", "annotation_id": "33651600", "url": "https://genius.com/33651600", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Shoe Fits", "line": "She settled for an NBA star that’s through playin’", "vault_lines": ["She settled for an NBA star that's through playin'"], "meaning": "Based on earlier lyrics in the song\n\n“For all the n*ggas who act twelve\nThe fake gangsters with a MAC-12”\n\nIt can be concluded that Drake is referring to Memphis Grizzlies NBA star, Ja Morant. The words “through playin’” tell us that the woman being referred to, settled for Ja Morant, with the idea that he was ready to commit to a relationship and done “playing” games with others emotions. However, we can tell by the lyrics in the following line, that was not the case and Ja Morant continued to play games which started to cause separation between him and the woman.", "annotation_id": "31527763", "url": "https://genius.com/31527763", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Shoe Fits", "line": "More weeks of recovery clinics, front like you love every minute", "vault_lines": ["More weeks of recovery clinics, front like you love every minute"], "meaning": "Drake highlights the dark side of females getting work done on their body to fit the current social norms that social media makes the mass general (in this case women) feel like they have to look like in order to be perceived a certain type of way.\n\nIn the second line Drake takes a stab at women who pretend to love the process and buying into the lifestyle even though what comes with it usually is worse then expected.", "annotation_id": "30607338", "url": "https://genius.com/30607338", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Shoe Fits", "line": "But he wants you covering it up, so your dresses is loose", "vault_lines": ["But he wants you covering it up, so your dresses is loose"], "meaning": "Drake is alluding to the same unknown woman’s boyfriend that he got her a BBL but now her boyfriend is making her cover it up by wearing loose clothing (dress)", "annotation_id": "30116052", "url": "https://genius.com/30116052", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Shoe Fits", "line": "Act like you somebody daughter", "vault_lines": ["Relax, drink some water, act like you somebody daughter"], "meaning": "A common put-down of young women online (namely TikTok and Instagram) is to accuse them of “fatherless behavior”. Its a popular term amongst  traditional or red-pilled men who disapprove of women not adhering to the traditional feminine values expected of them.\n\nIn this thinly veiled reference and the following bars, Drake shoots off some lazy stereotypes about young women. That they are spending too much time on their phones when they should be looking after their children.\n\nThe verse is in keeping with a major theme of All the Dogs: Drake’s frustration that young women aren’t what he wants them to be", "annotation_id": "30115323", "url": "https://genius.com/30115323", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Shoe Fits", "line": "Can’t get a tan from your phone light", "vault_lines": ["Can't get a tan from your phone light"], "meaning": "He jokes that girls spend so much time on their phones nowadays that they’re spending less time outside in the sun — less time exposed to UV where they could get a tan.\n\nInstead, these girls think that the exposure to the blue light from their phones can help them to look like instagram models.\n\nBasically, he’s telling them hoes to touch some grass.", "annotation_id": "30111508", "url": "https://genius.com/30111508", "state": "pending", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Shoe Fits", "line": "That nigga on the field before the game, he just practicin’ throwing", "vault_lines": ["That nigga on the field before the game, he just practicin' throwing"], "meaning": "Referencing the previous line, Drake’s ex has found herself with a backup quarterback who only sees the field pregame when “warming up” for an unlikely appearance in the game.\n\nThis is a slight to her ability to replace him with someone of the same stature, as he is one of the music industry’s biggest heavyweights", "annotation_id": "30110331", "url": "https://genius.com/30110331", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Shoe Fits", "line": "Leave for a month to Colombia and now everything bigger", "vault_lines": ["Leave for a month to Colombia and now everything bigger"], "meaning": "Here, Drake refers to the fact that it has become popular for women to go to South America, especially Colombia, for plastic surgeries such as Brazilian Butt Lifts (BBL), hence “everything bigger”. Drake also shouts out Brazilian Butt Lifts on “BBL Love – Interlude” on his 2023 album ‘For All The Dogs’.", "annotation_id": "30109025", "url": "https://genius.com/30109025", "state": "pending", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Shoe Fits", "line": "You know you can’t control a Gemini, that’s facts", "vault_lines": ["You know you can't control a Gemini, that's facts"], "meaning": "Gemini is an astrological sign (also known as a “zodiac sign”), which serves as a follow-up to Taurus.\n\nGeminis are often considered “playful” and “intellectually curious” according to a 2023 Aliza Kelly article.", "annotation_id": "30108719", "url": "https://genius.com/30108719", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Shoe Fits", "line": "To all the ladies wonderin’ why Drake can’t rap like that same old guy It’s ’cause I don’t know how anymore I don’t know how, yeah", "vault_lines": ["But I just don't know how anymore, love", "To all the ladies wonderin' why", "Drake can't rap like that same old guy", "I just don't know how, yeah", "It's 'cause I don't know how anymore", "I don't know how, yeah", "So, to all the ladies wonderin' why", "I don't know how"], "meaning": "As of this song’s release, Drake is 37 years old and speaks on the ongoing drama within his community on how he “fell off” after community-proclaimed albums: 2016’s Views, 2017’s More Life, and  2018’s Scorpion.\n\nTo “fall off” is to rapidly decline from a once popular status, or not perform as well as before.\n\nFollowing the release of his highly-anticipated 2023 album, For All The Dogs, despite the album debuting and peaking at #1 on the Billboard 200, the album gained Business Insider’s title of “the worst Drake album ever”—fueling this ongoing community drama.\n\nInterestingly enough, Drake somewhat predicted this future outcome in his 2016 track “4PM in Calabasas”:\n\nI got a lot to lose ‘cause in every situation I’m the bigger artist\nAlways gotta play it smarter\nY'all shook up, I’m here on the cookup\nCameras pointing every time I look up", "annotation_id": "30107943", "url": "https://genius.com/30107943", "state": "accepted", "votes": 72, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Shoe Fits", "line": "You boys becomin’ detectives, but ain’t in no trench coats", "vault_lines": ["You boys becomin' detectives, but ain't in no trench coats"], "meaning": "The stereotypical detective from a police force usually wears a trench coat to obscure their identity from the public while on a investigation for a case, or for weather purposes as well.\n\nDrake is simply implying that people are becoming more concerned in trying to dig up evidence, drama, or dirt against him. Much like a detective would, except they’re not wearing trench coats.", "annotation_id": "30105030", "url": "https://genius.com/30105030", "state": "pending", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Shoe Fits", "line": "For all the niggas who act twelve The fake gangsters with a MAC-12", "vault_lines": ["For all the niggas who act twelve", "The fake gangsters with a MAC-12"], "meaning": "Drake calls out people for posing with and publicly carrying hand guns when they are not gang-affiliated. Moreover, there is no official gun called MAC-12 (However there are both MAC-10’s and MAC-11’s). This could mean that the “fake gangsters” either have no gun knowledge or that they are possessing fake guns.\n\nActing “twelve” serves three different meanings:\n\n  \nDrake calling out NBA player Ja Morant (Who wears number 12) after he was suspended for flashing a gun on live. Knowing that Ja’s not a gangster but a wannabe (fake gangster).\n\nActing like the federal police, being armed in public. The cops being labeled \"12\" originates from the police radio code “10-12”.\n\nActing immature and childish as if you were only 12 years old.  \n\n\n\n\n\nPictured:  Cobray MAC-11/9, a variant of the MAC-11", "annotation_id": "30104132", "url": "https://genius.com/30104132", "state": "pending", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Shoe Fits", "line": "Baddies not the only ones worried ‘bout strikin’ a pose You orderin’ one bottle to split between five of the bros All your boos think it’s Halloween and they went ghost", "vault_lines": ["Baddies not the only ones worried 'bout strikin' a pose", "You orderin' one bottle to split between five of the bros", "All your boos think it's Halloween and they went ghost"], "meaning": "Drake uses a triple entendre with the word “Boos” tying everything together. Meaning:\n\n\n“Boos” = Baddies\n“Boos” Referring to the bottle of alcohol (Booze)\nTheme of Halloween.", "annotation_id": "30103861", "url": "https://genius.com/30103861", "state": "pending", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Shoe Fits", "line": "And now they thinkin’ you sweet with the bread like French toast", "vault_lines": ["And now they thinkin' you sweet with the bread like French toast"], "meaning": "French toast, bread fried with eggs, is usually eaten with maple syrup, among other things.\n\nDrake is saying the person he’s referencing makes his “boos” think he has money, or “bread” when he really doesn’t.", "annotation_id": "30103110", "url": "https://genius.com/30103110", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Shoe Fits", "line": "What’s your baby’s shoe size? Could tell by the laces, they tight Or are you only focused on the steps that I’m taking in life?", "vault_lines": ["What's your baby's shoe size? Could tell by the laces, they tight", "Or are you only focused on the steps that I'm taking in life?"], "meaning": "Here, Drake pretends like he primarily cares for the child of the woman he’s addressing.\nNoticing the baby has tight shoes on and asks what size shoes he requires, playfully letting her know he could purchase some for her child.\n\nBut really, off that observation he states that she’s too busy being focused on the steps he’s taking rather than her being worried or as cautious with her child’s comfortability", "annotation_id": "30103100", "url": "https://genius.com/30103100", "state": "pending", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Shoe Fits", "line": "Baby, it’s late June, open the blinds, get out The Shade Room", "vault_lines": ["Baby, it's late June, open the blinds, get out The Shade Room"], "meaning": "Drake tells the women talking down on him to go outside and touch some grass.\n\nHe’s letting them know that no matter how long they stay on their phone the light from their phone screens won’t get their skins tanned.\n\nHe then goes on to say ‘open the blinds, get out the shade room’, which is a play on words with the popular Instagram page handle, ‘The Shade Room’.\n\nThe Shade Room (TSR) is a media company, founded by Angelica Nwandu in March 2014. Instagram-based, The Shade Room offers celebrity and trending news on an hourly basis, predominantly within the African American community; The New York Times called it the “TMZ of Instagram”.", "annotation_id": "30103061", "url": "https://genius.com/30103061", "state": "pending", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Shoe Fits", "line": "He said if I ain’t watching, then that nigga ain’t startin’” She point to the guy that she talkin’ ’bout and it’s James Harden", "vault_lines": ["He said if I ain't watching, then that nigga ain't startin'\"", "She point to the guy that she talkin' 'bout and it's James Harden"], "meaning": "James Harden is an NBA basketball player, and considered one of the best point guards of his time.\n\n\n\nJames Harden.\n\nWhile Drake praises Harden’s historic scoring ability by invoking his nickname “The Sniper,” he may also be poking fun at Harden’s infamous reputation for prioritizing strip clubs and nightlife over basketball.", "annotation_id": "30101901", "url": "https://genius.com/30101901", "state": "accepted", "votes": 98, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Shoe Fits", "line": "To all the ladies on my case with a look on they face Allow me to put these bums right back in they place", "vault_lines": ["To all the ladies wonderin' why", "To all the ladies on my case with a look on they face", "Allow me to put these bums right back in they place"], "meaning": "This is a reference to Notorious B.I.G.’s Big Poppa.\n\n“To all the ladies in the place with style and grace\nAllow me to lace these lyrical douches in your bushes (uh)”", "annotation_id": "30101575", "url": "https://genius.com/30101575", "state": "pending", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Shoe Fits", "line": "She took dick in Ibiza, you turn into Dick Tracy", "vault_lines": ["She took dick in Ibiza, you turn into Dick Tracy"], "meaning": "Dick Tracy is an American comic character created by Chester Gould. This character is a tough and intelligent police detective. Here Drake makes a wordplay between this character’s name and a woman that is very sexually active. Possibly, Drake might also be suggesting that the woman’s boyfriend is “dick tracing” (trying to find out if she cheated and with whom).", "annotation_id": "30101405", "url": "https://genius.com/30101405", "state": "pending", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Shoe Fits", "line": "Now you on a flight to Bogotá just to get it reduced", "vault_lines": ["Now you on a flight to Bogotá just to get it reduced"], "meaning": "Medical tourism is a growing trend among those who seek to receive cosmetic medical procedures, such as Brazilian Butt Lifts (BBLs), outside of their home country. Patients are often motivated by more affordable prices and shorter wait times.\n\nColombia, and its capital Bogota, is a frequent destination for medical tourism. In this case, the girl and her man are embarrassed by the results of their BBL but can’t afford a surgery in their home country, and have to resort to a cheaper alternative.\n\nIt should be noted that medical tourism is associated with potentially life threatening outcomes. Surgeries can be complicated by infection, disfiguring results, and even use of lower quality implants that are more prone to rupture in order to cut costs for the procedure. It is generally advised against going on medical tourism trips, as outcomes are often not what patients expect and there is often a lack of valid or trustworthy licensure to perform these surgeries and procedures as well.", "annotation_id": "30101387", "url": "https://genius.com/30101387", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Shoe Fits", "line": "Actin’ Hulk tough, but you only turn green because your necklace is gold-plated", "vault_lines": ["Actin' Hulk tough, but you only turn green because your necklace is gold-plated"], "meaning": "If your jewelry is gold plated instead of being made of actual gold, the plating will wear down and expose the cheaper metal underneath. Also the skin will react to the cheaper metal, most likely copper, and leave a green stain. Furthermore, the Marvel superhero Bruce Banner aka “Hulk” famously turns green and buff when angry – similarly, people with fake jewelry might get angry when called out for their materialistic lies.\n\n\n\nMoreover, turning green is also associated with jealousy and a person with fake gold, e.g. brass, might be jealous of people with the real deal.", "annotation_id": "30101350", "url": "https://genius.com/30101350", "state": "pending", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Shoe Fits", "line": "I’ve had my beliefs tested, my faith broken in half I try to joke and I laugh But I just don’t know how anymore, love I don’t know how, yeah", "vault_lines": ["But I just don't know how anymore, love", "I just don't know how, yeah", "It's 'cause I don't know how anymore", "I don't know how, yeah", "I've had my beliefs tested, my faith broken in half", "I try to joke and I laugh", "I don't know how"], "meaning": "Drake directly addresses critics who seem to tarnish his name. Drake addresses people claiming he cannot rap like his “old self” referring to his older projects from 2009-2013 and other fan-favorites that gave Drake fame, with the release of “For All The Dogs”, Drake claimed “the Old Drake” would be present. Many didn’t feel “the Old Drake” and instead felt a lazier effortless version of Drake they disliked.", "annotation_id": "30101270", "url": "https://genius.com/30101270", "state": "pending", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Shoe Fits", "line": "Then you got the ones that travel ’cross the globe Everything is paid, they don’t need a man Don’t listen to Drake, never been a fan You got a million hoes, yeah, I understand I’m never fuckin’ you, so take that out your plans I’m good on all you niggas ’til a ring is on my hand Then I search your name, find you on the ’Gram Click the Linktree and see you suckin’ dick on cam, what the fuck?", "vault_lines": ["Then you got the ones that travel 'cross the globe", "Everything is paid, they don't need a man", "Don't listen to Drake, never been a fan", "You got a million hoes, yeah, I understand", "I'm never fuckin' you, so take that out your plans", "I'm good on all you niggas 'til a ring is on my hand", "Then I search your name, find you on the 'Gram", "Click the Linktree and see you suckin' dick on cam, what the fuck?", "I would never guess that you niggas is this crazy", "You niggas so jaded", "I don't know how, yeah", "You niggas is out of line"], "meaning": "Linktree is a popular social media service that allows users to host all their important links on one page. Most users put a link to it in their social media bios:\n\nhttps://blog.hubspot.com/hs-fs/hubfs/instagram%20linktree%20example%20tiktok.webp?width=500&height=501&name=instagram%20linktree%20example%20tiktok.webp  The Linktree page for social media app TikTok.\n\nDrake implies that this wealthy, pompous, and financially independent woman is a pornstar, as the Linktree on her Instagram profile led him to a video of her performing oral sex. It fits, as some of the most successful in the industry can earn up to millions by the end of their career.\n\nDrake points out what he feels is an irony in this independent woman who prides herself on not needing a man having a career that, in many ways, caters to men.", "annotation_id": "30101238", "url": "https://genius.com/30101238", "state": "accepted", "votes": 113, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Shoe Fits", "status": "done", "targets": 24, "clicked": 24, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-the-shoe-fits-lyrics", "genius_title": "The Shoe Fits"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Kick, Push (Remix)", "line": "[Hook: Lupe Fiasco] And so they kick, push, kick, push Kick, push, kick, push; coast And away they rolled Just rebels without a cause with no place to go And so they kick, push, kick, push Kick, push, kick, push; coast So come roll with me Just a rebel looking for a place to be So let’s kick, uh, uh And push, yeah, yeah And coast Ah ha, Swanky", "vault_lines": ["And so he kick, push, kick, push", "Kick, push, kick, push; coast", "And away he rolled", "Just a rebel to the world with no place to go", "So come and skate with me", "Just a rebel looking for a place to be", "Kick and a snare", "So I kick, push Kick, push", "So I kick, push", "Kick, push Kick, push", "Just a rebel, lookin' for a place to go", "So I kick Then push", "And so they kick, push, kick, push", "And away they rolled", "Just rebels without a cause with no place to go", "So come roll with me", "So let's kick, uh, uh"], "meaning": "The chorus, which repeats throughout the song, emphasizes the skateboarders' actions of “kick, push, coast”, which represents their movements on the board.", "annotation_id": "28023154", "url": "https://genius.com/28023154", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Kick, Push (Remix)", "line": "[Hook: Drake] So I kick, push Kick, push Kick, push Kick, push Coast Fast as the wheels replaced I gotta find another hobby just to fill the space So I kick, push Kick, push Kick, push Kick, push Coast Peep the way I roll Just a rebel, lookin’ for a place to go So I kick Then push And coast", "vault_lines": ["And so he kick, push, kick, push", "Kick, push, kick, push; coast", "Just a rebel to the world with no place to go", "Just a rebel looking for a place to be", "Kick and a snare", "So I kick, push Kick, push", "Fast as the wheels replaced", "I gotta find another hobby just to fill the space", "So I kick, push", "Kick, push Kick, push", "Peep the way I roll", "Just a rebel, lookin' for a place to go", "So I kick Then push", "And so they kick, push, kick, push"], "meaning": "The chorus, which repeats throughout the song, emphasizes the skateboarders' actions of “kick, push, coast”, which represents their movements on the board.", "annotation_id": "28023153", "url": "https://genius.com/28023153", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Kick, Push (Remix)", "line": "[Verse 3: Lupe Fiasco] Yeah, yeah Before he knew, he had a crew that wasn’t no punk In they Spitfire shirts and SB dunks They would push ’til they couldn’t skate no more Office building lobbies wasn’t safe no more And it wasn’t like they wasn’t getting chased no more Just the freedom was better than breathing, they said An escape route they used to escape out When things got crazy, they needed to break out They’d head to any place with stairs Any good grinds, the world was theirs And their four wheels would take them there Until the cops came and said “There’s no skating here”", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, he said it was something so appealing", "He knew he couldn't doubt it, couldn't understand it", "And so he kick, push, kick, push", "Just a rebel to the world with no place to go", ", a kickflip in the air", "Before he knew, he had a crew that wasn't no punk", "In they Spitfire shirts and SB dunks", "They would push 'til they couldn't skate no more", "Office building lobbies wasn't safe no more", "And it wasn't like they wasn't getting chased no more", "Just the freedom was better than breathing, they said", "An escape route they used to escape out", "When things got crazy, they needed to break out", "They'd head to any place with stairs", "Any good grinds, the world was theirs", "And their four wheels would take them there", "Until the cops came and said \"There's no skating here\"", "And so they kick, push, kick, push", "Just rebels without a cause with no place to go"], "meaning": "In the third verse, Lupe Fiasco describes how the boy from the first verse found a community of skateboarders who shared his love for the sport. They would skate together and explore the world around them, but were constantly chased away by authorities who banned skating in certain areas.", "annotation_id": "28023151", "url": "https://genius.com/28023151", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Kick, Push (Remix)", "line": "[Hook: Lupe Fiasco] And so he kick, push, kick, push Kick, push, kick, push; coast And away he rolled Just a rebel to the world with no place to go And so he kick, push, kick, push Kick, push, kick, push; coast So come and skate with me Just a rebel looking for a place to be So let’s kick And push And coast Uh, uh, uh", "vault_lines": ["And so he kick, push, kick, push", "Kick, push, kick, push; coast", "And away he rolled", "Just a rebel to the world with no place to go", "So come and skate with me", "Just a rebel looking for a place to be", "Kick and a snare", "So I kick, push Kick, push", "So I kick, push", "Kick, push Kick, push", "Just a rebel, lookin' for a place to go", "So I kick Then push", "And so they kick, push, kick, push", "And away they rolled", "Just rebels without a cause with no place to go", "So come roll with me", "So let's kick, uh, uh"], "meaning": "The chorus, which repeats throughout the song, emphasizes the skateboarders' actions of “kick, push, coast”, which represents their movements on the board.", "annotation_id": "28023135", "url": "https://genius.com/28023135", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Kick, Push (Remix)", "line": "[Verse 2: Drake]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "In the second verse, Drake shares his own experiences of growing up and skateboarding in Memphis, where he faced obstacles such as financial difficulties and disapproval from his family. He eventually found refuge in his uncle’s basement, where he could skateboard and pursue his passion.", "annotation_id": "28023133", "url": "https://genius.com/28023133", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Kick, Push (Remix)", "line": "[Verse 1: Lupe Fiasco] First got it when he was six, didn’t know any tricks Matter of fact, first time he got on it, he slipped Landed on his hip and busted his lip For a week, he had to talk with a lisp, like thisss Now we can end the story right here But shorty didn’t quit, it was something in the air Yeah, he said it was something so appealing He couldn’t fight the feeling, something about it He knew he couldn’t doubt it, couldn’t understand it Branded, since the first kickflip he landed, uh Labeled a misfit, a bandit Ka-kunk, ka-kunk, ka-kunk; his neighbors couldn’t stand it So, he was banished to the park Started in the morning, wouldn’t stop ’til after dark", "vault_lines": ["So, check it out, uh", "First got it when he was six, didn't know any tricks", "Matter of fact, first time he got on it, he slipped", "Landed on his hip and busted his lip", "For a week, he had to talk with a lisp, like thisss", "Now we can end the story right here", "But shorty didn't quit, it was something in the air", "Yeah, he said it was something so appealing", "He couldn't fight the feeling, something about it", "He knew he couldn't doubt it, couldn't understand it", "Branded, since the first kickflip he landed, uh", "Labeled a misfit, a bandit", "Ka-kunk, ka-kunk, ka-kunk; his neighbors couldn't stand it", "So, he was banished to the park", "Started in the morning, wouldn't stop 'til after dark", "And so he kick, push, kick, push", ", a kickflip in the air"], "meaning": "In the first verse, Lupe Fiasco tells the story of a boy who started skateboarding at a young age, despite getting injured and facing criticism from his neighbors. He became hooked on the feeling of skating and continued to pursue it passionately.", "annotation_id": "28023130", "url": "https://genius.com/28023130", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Kick, Push (Remix)", "line": "Yes, I’m literally Larnell Lewis with a Kick and a snare", "vault_lines": ["Yes, I'm literally Larnell Lewis with a", "Kick and a snare"], "meaning": "Larnell Lewis is a well known and very talented drummer who is from Toronto, where Drake is from. Being around the same age and in the Toronto music scene at the same time they probably knew each other at some point.\n\nDrake compares his skills on the mic/skateboard to Lewis' drumming skills.", "annotation_id": "20437957", "url": "https://genius.com/20437957", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Kick, Push (Remix)", "line": "My cousin’s after Doe, like re-mi-fa-so", "vault_lines": ["My cousin's after Doe, like re-mi-fa-so"], "meaning": "Solfege, a method to teach pitch, uses seven syllables:\nDo, Re, Mi, Fa, So, La, and Ti\n\n\n\nIn the context of this line Drake’s cousin is chasing the money, or “doe”.", "annotation_id": "2809864", "url": "https://genius.com/2809864", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Kick, Push (Remix)", "line": "It gets boring growing up in Memphis Tryna become a pro, but keep showing up apprentice", "vault_lines": ["It gets boring growing up in Memphis", "Tryna become a pro, but keep showing up apprentice"], "meaning": "Drake spent his summers in Memphis, Tennessee with his aunt and uncle. The second line could be referring to his skateboarding skills (explains why he broke a few boards), or his rhyming skills. He knew he had “room for improvement” in both areas.", "annotation_id": "515080", "url": "https://genius.com/515080", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Kick, Push (Remix)", "line": "My style is very Tennessee mixed with some Terry Kennedy", "vault_lines": ["My style is very Tennessee mixed with some Terry Kennedy"], "meaning": "Although Drake is originally from Toronto, he spent his summer vacations at his aunt and uncle’s house in Memphis, Tennessee, where he spent his days skateboarding.\n\nTerry Kennedy is a skateboarder from Compton, also known to occasionally kick some raps.", "annotation_id": "504163", "url": "https://genius.com/504163", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
