{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Calling For You", "line": "Ah, he lied to me Yo, he lied to me Like I didn’t even give a fuck that we sat in economy I gave a fuck ’cause he said the economy was full It was not full He said, “Economy was—” He said, “There was no first class, so we’re sitting in economy” I get up on that plane I see so many seats in first class Twelve, like, twelve, fourteen seats Right I sat in the back of the plane Fucking crazy And then, I go on that wack-ass vacation The chef is feeding us the same meal every day like I was, like, in jail still or something I’m like, “Why are we eating jerk chicken and oxtail every single day, can we switch it up?” No, the oxtail was fire though, but can we switch it up? I can’t eat that shit every day, what? And then you proceed to go through my phone You wanted to cry You were lookin’ for something That’s on you, it’s on you Sorry for your loss", "vault_lines": ["I was in the club 'fore she even had it", "You fucked on a nigga I see as my son, so what?", "Yeah, I was in the club, but I was in the cut", "Callin', callin' for you", "Callin' for you, callin' for you", "Need you to guide my eyes, feel it on me", "Needin' you to hold me", "It was on my mind, felt it on me", "Ah, he lied to me", "Yo, he lied to me", "Like I didn't even give a fuck that we sat in economy", "I gave a fuck 'cause he said the economy was full", "It was not full", "He said, \"Economy was—\"", "He said, \"There was no first class, so we're sitting in economy\"", "I get up on that plane", "I see so many seats in first class", "Twelve, like, twelve, fourteen seats", "I sat in the back of the plane", "And then, I go on that wack-ass vacation", "The chef is feeding us the same meal every day like I was, like, in jail still or something", "I'm like, \"Why are we eating jerk chicken and oxtail every single day, can we switch it up?\"", "No, the oxtail was fire though, but can we switch it up?", "I can't eat that shit every day, what?", "And then you proceed to go through my phone", "You wanted to cry", "You were lookin' for something", "That's on you, it's on you", "Sorry for your loss"], "meaning": "This interlude is voiced over by Mirna Mahrous Habib, otherwise known as @babymirnz.\n\nDillon Brooks and Drake have had a feud. Habib was an escort having sexual relations with Brooks, and further on, Brooks would be humiliated by Drake and Habib for Brooks' careless spending, and developing an emotional connection for Habib. This is also inferred from track 21 of For All The Dogs, “Another Late Night”, where Drake would name drop:\n\nShawty rinsin' Dillon Brooks, can’t believe this nigga talkin', damn\n\nAdditionally, Drake raps earlier on “Calling For You”, likely supporting the account:\n\nYou fucked on a nigga I see as my son, so what?\n\nOn October 31, 2022, Habib was sentenced to four months in prison for aggravated identity theft, and charged with $683,243.23 to compensate the victims. Afterward, Brooks bought Habib’s trip mentioned throughout this spoken word.", "annotation_id": "29744874", "url": "https://genius.com/29744874", "state": "accepted", "votes": 57, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Calling For You", "line": "Keep a .19 like I’m Mac Dre", "vault_lines": ["Keep a .19 like I'm Mac Dre (21)"], "meaning": ".19 as in a GLOCK 19\n\n21 may be refrencing the Mac Dre lyrics in get loud\n\n“I think she on puss' too, maybe not\nBaby cot, nineteen, with her own spot\nA day wit' Dre, I’ll have her on robot”\nhttps://genius.com/Mac-dre-get-loud-lyrics", "annotation_id": "29730651", "url": "https://genius.com/29730651", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Calling For You", "line": "She suck on my neck like she Dracula (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["She suck on my neck like she Dracula (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Count Dracula is the title character of Bram Stoker’s 1897 gothic horror novel Dracula. He is a vampire which is known by turning people into vampires by sucking their neck.", "annotation_id": "29728825", "url": "https://genius.com/29728825", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Calling For You", "line": "21 gang 4L, these niggas gon’ tell", "vault_lines": ["21 gang 4L, these niggas gon' tell"], "meaning": "“4L” is 21 Savage and Young Nudy’s shared gang. 21 references it a lot and even has a track named “4L”.", "annotation_id": "29728627", "url": "https://genius.com/29728627", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Calling For You", "line": "I see he be on his dork shit (21) Nah, I ain’t judgin’, but they in the nosebleeds You know I be on my court shit (Facts)", "vault_lines": ["I see he be on his dork shit (21)", "Nah, I ain't judgin', but they in the nosebleeds", "You know I be on my court shit (Facts)"], "meaning": "The nosebleed section are the seats of a public area, usually an athletic stadium or gymnasium, that are highest and, usually, farthest from the desired activity.\n\n\n\n21 Savage brags about how, unlike his opps, he’s always on the court side. The court side encompasses the area immediately bordering the official court of play and tickets for these seats can be ridiculously expensive.\n\n\n\nIn addition, the second realization of this thought is a nosebleed – as a consequence of cocaine use, Savage does not do this dork shit.", "annotation_id": "29725500", "url": "https://genius.com/29725500", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Calling For You", "line": "Fuck nigga wanna get fired on (21) Starch a nigga up, put the iron on him (21)", "vault_lines": ["Fuck nigga wanna get fired on (21)", "Starch a nigga up, put the iron on him (21)"], "meaning": "The term “iron” in slang refers to a firearm. Thus, 21 Savage is alluding to shoot somebody i.e. “put the iron on him.”\nAdditionally, the mention of starch refers to spray starch, which is a traditional aid for ironing natural fabrics like cotton, linen, bamboo, and rayon. It helps the iron glide smoothly over the fabric and adds body or crispness to shirt collars and pleats.", "annotation_id": "29725304", "url": "https://genius.com/29725304", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Calling For You", "line": "And Addy in my system, see a opp, I’ma hit ’em up", "vault_lines": ["And Addy in my system, see a opp, I'ma hit 'em up"], "meaning": "Adderall is a brand name for an ADHD-treating drug that has a combination of amphetamine and dextroamphetamine.\n\nDrake employs wordplay here alluding to him having one of his opposition’s “addy”—slang for “Address”—resulting in him firing at his enemies.", "annotation_id": "29724852", "url": "https://genius.com/29724852", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
