{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Lord Knows", "line": "Still allergic to broke, prescription straight to the paper", "vault_lines": ["Still allergic to broke, prescription straight to the paper"], "meaning": "He put molly on the pen’s cup it ain’t even know\nHe took it and started fcking the ink it ain’t even know", "annotation_id": "32343837", "url": "https://genius.com/32343837", "state": "pending", "votes": -4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Lord Knows", "line": "I’m really killin’ shit, fuck all the jiggy rappin", "vault_lines": ["I'm really killin' shit, fuck all the jiggy rappin"], "meaning": "‘F*ck all the jiggy rapping’ is Drake’s response to those who claim he’s a pop artist. In this particular bar he’s referencing Pop Rap Smash hit ‘Gettin’ Jiggy Wit It’ by Will Smith. Drake doesn’t want to be seen in the same light as someone like Will who’s not known explicitly as a rapper but rather a Pop Rapper who only makes music for the charts and doesn’t actually compete lyrically with other rappers.\n\n‘Lord Knows’, as a whole, is a track about Drake proving himself in the game as one of the best, and this line is a testament to that.", "annotation_id": "30074719", "url": "https://genius.com/30074719", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Lord Knows", "line": "Never the flow, though, they know I run that", "vault_lines": ["Never the flow, though, they know I run that"], "meaning": "Drake could be referring to several things here :\n\n\nHe runs the flow of the mainstream. Due to his insane popularity in the mainstream and the way he changed rap by fusion it with RnB, Drake knows he runs the ‘flow’ of the mainstream.\nDrake could be referring to the flows in his verses. At this time in his career Drake was much more lyrical and his music had an increased emphasis on lyrics and flows, and Drake considered himself a ‘competitive rapper’ in many interviews – for this reason he defends his ability to flow well on his songs. In this case he could be claiming he has the best flow in the game.", "annotation_id": "29941706", "url": "https://genius.com/29941706", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Lord Knows", "line": "But that’s just the result of me paying attention To all these women that think like men with the same intentions", "vault_lines": ["But that's just the result of me paying attention", "To all these women that think like men with the same intentions"], "meaning": "Here Drake mentions his bad habit of paying attention to women who ‘think like men’, which alludes to the fact that the women he talks to are overtly sexual, a comparison which he makes to testosterone filled men who are normally he ones who ‘think’ that way.\n\nDue to the fact that the women he talks to are overtly sexual in this manner, he cannot trust any of them because they’ll hook up with anybody due to their nature.", "annotation_id": "29941663", "url": "https://genius.com/29941663", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Lord Knows", "line": "And these niggas talkin’ like hoes, they mad they not in my shoes", "vault_lines": ["And these niggas talkin' like hoes, they mad they not in my shoes"], "meaning": "When he’s talkin bout shoe’s in this case he means financially, (his POV) and perhaps literally (a great double entendre).", "annotation_id": "29149278", "url": "https://genius.com/29149278", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
