{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fancy", "line": "If it sounds like you, then let me hear you repeat it", "vault_lines": ["If it sounds like you, then let me hear you repeat it"], "meaning": "Drake is saying if you are one of these girls with diplomas, homes, money, and good looking then sing along to the song.", "annotation_id": "33937153", "url": "https://genius.com/33937153", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fancy", "line": "Yeah, but shout out to the homeowners The girls that got diplomas and enough money to loan us A little something extra, should we ever need it", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, but shout out to the homeowners", "The girls that got diplomas and enough money to loan us", "A little something extra, should we ever need it"], "meaning": "Drake is paying respect to hardworking women who have degrees, and have earned enough money to buy a house, and could also lend some more money to their partners, as opposed to being dependent on a man’s money", "annotation_id": "31672879", "url": "https://genius.com/31672879", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fancy", "line": "I’m down for whatever, you just lead the way We go to dinner, you don’t even look at me to pay", "vault_lines": ["I'm down for whatever, you just lead the way", "We go to dinner, you don't even look at me to pay"], "meaning": "Drake references being involved with females who are on par with or above his wealth level. Signalling a level of growth on the part of Drake who feels as this is a breakthrough in the world of his love-life, while previously he may have been involved with woman who he spent money on just to gain an physical feeling, he feels that these new woman allow him to connect on a emotional level as well.", "annotation_id": "31354792", "url": "https://genius.com/31354792", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fancy", "line": "They get a baller, figure they ain’t got to pick a career Guess they plan on suckin’ dicks until some millions appear Like “Voilà!” You do it right, he just might buy you a car", "vault_lines": ["They get a baller, figure they ain't got to pick a career", "Guess they plan on suckin' dicks until some millions appear", "Like \"Voilà!\" You do it right, he just might buy you a car"], "meaning": "This is one of many examples where Drake talks about women only wanting to get around him for money lacking genuine connection. For example on Search & Rescue where Drakes says “I need someone to be patient with me\nSomeone to get money with, not take it from me”.", "annotation_id": "30657728", "url": "https://genius.com/30657728", "state": "pending", "votes": -10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fancy", "line": "I just knew that she was fine like a ticket on the dash", "vault_lines": ["I just knew that she was fine like a ticket on the dash"], "meaning": "shes sexy as fuck", "annotation_id": "30363618", "url": "https://genius.com/30363618", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fancy", "line": "Time heals all and heels hurt to walk in", "vault_lines": ["Time heals all and heels hurt to walk in"], "meaning": "“Time heals all” is a popular phrase that means every problem you have will fix itself given time.\nThe negative effects of wearing heels are well documented, but people still wear them for fashion purpouses.\n\n\n\nFurthermore, Drake also uses a figure of speech called antithesis, juxtaposing the words heal and hurt.\n\nTime heals all and heels hurt to walk in", "annotation_id": "14990893", "url": "https://genius.com/14990893", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fancy", "line": "Champagne Range, triple-white Jag", "vault_lines": ["Champagne Range, triple-white Jag"], "meaning": "T.I. is just adding to the expensive and extravagant lifestyle with foreign cars. In this case, he is talking about a champagne colored Range Rover and a white-on-white Jaguar (white paint with white interior).", "annotation_id": "13494171", "url": "https://genius.com/13494171", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fancy", "line": "Said, “Go Cinderella, go Cinderella” Orgasm blush, lipstick and concealer", "vault_lines": ["Said, \"Go Cinderella, go Cinderella\"", "Orgasm blush, lipstick and concealer"], "meaning": "Cinderella is the archetype of what a girl can become if dressed up appropriately. She managed to attract a prince at a ball despite just hours earlier being in rags. It took the fairy godmother to turn her from a peasant to a princess. Drake is suggesting if a girl dresses up right she can become a princess, regardless of her origin. This could also be Drake referring to himself as a prince, implying that you have to make a big effort to please him.\n\n\n\n“Orgasm blush” is referencing the most popular shade of Nars blush, Orgasm. It’s a pink-ish orange tone that’s also very expensive, following the kind of brands mentioned in the previous verse.", "annotation_id": "8545010", "url": "https://genius.com/8545010", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fancy", "line": "[Produced by Swizz Beatz & Noah “40” Shebib]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The background for this beat consists of a sped up sample of Ace Spectrum’s “I Don’t Want to Play Around.”\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TJTovmN3YY4#t=20", "annotation_id": "3272651", "url": "https://genius.com/3272651", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fancy", "line": "And when I find it is when I find you And we can do the things we never got the time to", "vault_lines": ["And you don't do it for the men, men never notice", "And when I find it is when I find you", "And we can do the things we never got the time to"], "meaning": "Like the Prince that found Cinderella’s glass slipper, he searched all over the town with the small evidence and found his Princess.\n\nWhen Drake finds what is real or finds one of his past lovers that has always been down for him before fame, he will have found his soulmate.", "annotation_id": "1802520", "url": "https://genius.com/1802520", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fancy", "line": "Well, aren’t you a breath of fresh air? From all these superficial gold diggin’ bitches in here", "vault_lines": ["Well, aren't you a breath of fresh air?", "From all these superficial gold diggin' bitches in here"], "meaning": "T.I has finally encountered a woman who isn’t just seeking his fortune. That’s why he describes her as “a breath of fresh air”.\n\nhttp://imgur.com/t5cyCyS\n\nA “gold digging bitch” as T.I so eloquently says, is a woman who is simply after your money and is pretending to like you to gain access.\n\nKanye West wrote an entire song dedicated to these money hungry ladies where he says:\n\nWe all went to dine and then I had to pay\nIf you fucking with this girl then you better be paid", "annotation_id": "1775513", "url": "https://genius.com/1775513", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fancy", "line": "And my NY girls (Woo), let me see your hands", "vault_lines": ["Atlanta girls (Woo), let me see your hands (Yeah)", "And my NY girls (Woo), let me see your hands", "And my LA girls (Oh), let me see your hands (Bounce)", "(Come on) And my TO girls (Right), let me see your hands"], "meaning": "Drake has said in an interview that there are “a lot of good women in New York”, and that he suspects his ideal woman probably lives there.", "annotation_id": "619345", "url": "https://genius.com/619345", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fancy", "line": "[Chorus: Swizz Beatz, Swizz Beatz & Mary J. Blige, Mary J. Blige]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The final hook contains Mary J. Blige vocals. The song originally was supposed to be on her album, Stronger With Each Tear, with Swizz Beatz. Swizz later revealed that he gave the record to Drake after Drizzy asked for it.", "annotation_id": "231954", "url": "https://genius.com/231954", "state": "accepted", "votes": 36, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fancy", "line": "Closet full of brand new clothes and handbags Alexander McQueen, Prada, Gucci, Chanel D&G, BCBG, Versace, Louis and Bebe", "vault_lines": ["Closet full of brand new clothes and handbags", "Alexander McQueen, Prada, Gucci, Chanel"], "meaning": "Mentioning all the expensive, high-end brands that modern society worships, T.I. emphasizes how our culture is very superficial. To be fashionable, one must spend ridiculous amounts of money, all for the purpose of fitting in or conforming to what society thinks is “stylish”.", "annotation_id": "190915", "url": "https://genius.com/190915", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fancy", "line": "Now here you are with your girls havin’ drinks at the bar I say I’m buyin’, you decline, that is kinda bizarre", "vault_lines": ["Now here you are with your girls havin' drinks at the bar", "I say I'm buyin', you decline, that is kinda bizarre"], "meaning": "Buying girls a drink at the bar in attempts to pick them up is the oldest trick in the book. And more times than not the girl will accept the drink to be polite, even if she’s not interested. So the fact that this girl says no means that she is sending a message – she is an independent woman and can afford her own drinks.", "annotation_id": "190910", "url": "https://genius.com/190910", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fancy", "line": "They tell me time is money, well, we’ll spend it together", "vault_lines": ["They tell me time is money, well, we'll spend it together"], "meaning": "If time is money,then you have to spend money. If you wanna spend money,then you need time. Drake’s basically saying that the girl he is talking about is worth his time, and he wants to spend it with her. He may also mean that he wants to spend money on her, and buy her clothes and what not.\n\n\n\nThis girl is not a gold-digger; she is genuine and likes Drake for who he is, not for his success. That’s why he’s so eager to spend time with him.", "annotation_id": "31269", "url": "https://genius.com/31269", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fancy", "line": "And the confidence to overlook my past ways", "vault_lines": ["And the confidence to overlook my past ways"], "meaning": "Drake needs his girl to be confident enough in herself to believe that despite his past exploits with women, he really does think that this girl is special. If she’s insecure and is constantly worrying he’s going to leave her for someone “better”, the relationship is never going to work out.", "annotation_id": "25747", "url": "https://genius.com/25747", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fancy", "line": "Mature women with more than me were the first to tempt me And Jason had this girl Tammy with a purple Bentley How she got it, I ain’t never get to ask", "vault_lines": ["Mature women with more than me were the first to tempt me", "And Jason had this girl Tammy with a purple Bentley", "How she got it, I ain't never get to ask"], "meaning": "As a young man, Drake longed for a Cougar to educate him in the sexual arts. Older women have their own money, which is nice too..\n\nHis friend Jason whet his appetite by dating a cougar (Tammy) with a ‘fancy’ car:\n\n\n\nDrake could possibly be referencing the same Tammy that once dated Lil Wayne.", "annotation_id": "24601", "url": "https://genius.com/24601", "state": "accepted", "votes": 45, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fancy", "line": "Or in the mall steady rackin’ up the air miles", "vault_lines": ["Or in the mall steady rackin' up the air miles"], "meaning": "This is a play on the meaning of “fly”; this girl is so fly (pretty / well-dressed) that she could rack up frequent flier miles (called “Air Miles” in Drake’s homeland).", "annotation_id": "22442", "url": "https://genius.com/22442", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fancy", "line": "Devil in a tight dress, girl you a killer And ain’t nobody realer, and ain’t nobody realer, go Go, go, go, go, go, go, go (Showtime) Go, go, go, go, go (As we proceed)", "vault_lines": ["A-go, go, go 'head (Go, go, go)", "A-go, go, go, go, go, go 'head", "A-go, go, go, go, go, a-go 'head", "Devil in a tight dress, girl you a killer", "And ain't nobody realer, and ain't nobody realer, go", "Go, go, go, go, go, go, go (Showtime)", "Go, go, go, go, go (As we proceed)"], "meaning": "This is a play on the title of the movie Devil In A Blue Dress.", "annotation_id": "19857", "url": "https://genius.com/19857", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fancy", "line": "Cinderella ’bout to lose the glass off her foot", "vault_lines": ["Cinderella 'bout to lose the glass off her foot"], "meaning": "Cinderella loses the glass shoe off of her foot as she’s fleeing the ball because her whip is about to change back to big ass pumpkin.\n\n\n\nThe prince (Drake in this case) uses that glass shoe (not flexible) to find Cinderella because it doesn’t fit just any old ho. When the glass shoe (slipper) finally fits Cinderella, a poor girl, the prince takes her away and they leave freakily ever after.", "annotation_id": "19817", "url": "https://genius.com/19817", "state": "accepted", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fancy", "line": "Uh, five and a half in boys, ass is off the hook", "vault_lines": ["Uh, five and a half in boys, ass is off the hook"], "meaning": "This girl wears boys' shoes (size 5 ½) which is 7 ½ in women’s.\n\n\n\nThis couplet is borrowed from Ghostface Killah’s “Strawberry,” originally released in 2001. Cam'ron also references this line in “Soap Opera,” except his girl’s feet are smaller.", "annotation_id": "19816", "url": "https://genius.com/19816", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fancy", "line": "You ain’t needy, greedy or easy as these other breezy’s Who fuck for bottles of Riesling and bowls of baked ziti", "vault_lines": ["You ain't needy, greedy or easy as these other breezy's", "Who fuck for bottles of Riesling and bowls of baked ziti"], "meaning": "TI’s girls in this song DO NOT require anything to be bought for them. A few bars earlier she declines TI buying her a drink.\n\nBaked Ziti and Riesling are just examples of how cheap hoes can get. Baked Ziti (approx $15 entree) and Riesling (approx $6/glass) don’t cost too much, however, there are still some girls willing to trick themselves out for them.", "annotation_id": "19814", "url": "https://genius.com/19814", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fancy", "line": "Man, she play these suckers just like B.o.B play the guitar", "vault_lines": ["Man, she play these suckers just like B.o.B play the guitar"], "meaning": "Getting “played” means to get tricked out of your money. This girl plays dudes like T.I.’s labelmate and fellow ATL rapper B.o.B. plays the guitar.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jUmfhYsA5r0\n\nThis line would later be sampled in B.o.B’s 2011 song “Play the Guitar.”", "annotation_id": "19809", "url": "https://genius.com/19809", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fancy", "line": "Intelligent too, ooh, you my sweetheart I’ve always liked my women book and street smart Long as they got a lil’ class like half days", "vault_lines": ["Intelligent too, ooh, you my sweetheart", "I've always liked my women book and street smart", "Long as they got a lil' class like half days"], "meaning": "Half days are school days that get out at around noon, so you only have to attend a little bit of class. Similarly, all Drake requires from his girls are a little bit of class, beauty, and intelligence if they want to stick with him.\n\n\n\nA little class is also a play on words, as classes are shortened during high school “half days”, when students are let out early.", "annotation_id": "19806", "url": "https://genius.com/19806?", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fancy", "line": "Hit the gym, step on the scale, stare at the number You say you droppin’ ten pounds preparin’ for summer And you don’t do it for the men, men never notice You just do it for yourself, you the fuckin’ coldest", "vault_lines": ["Hit the gym, step on the scale, stare at the number", "You say you droppin' ten pounds preparin' for summer", "And you don't do it for the men, men never notice", "You just do it for yourself, you the fuckin' coldest"], "meaning": "She’s dropping 10 pounds for the summer for her own personal reasons. “Coldest” means she’s determined and kinda bad-ass about it.\n\nDrake points out that men stereotypically have a tendency to not notice subtle changes to a women appearance. Therefore the women in the song gets dressed up for her self. This is a “cool” trait.", "annotation_id": "19805", "url": "https://genius.com/19805", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fancy", "status": "done", "targets": 31, "clicked": 31, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-fancy-lyrics", "genius_title": "Fancy"}
