{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Ride", "line": "And you got a drop, but you ride around with the top up", "vault_lines": ["And you got a drop, but you ride around with the top up"], "meaning": "Referencing a convertible/ drop-top car, however serves also as a double entendre about how ‘you’ have the potential, but lack the confidence and ability to be the best you can be. This follows the motif of the whole song where Drake is saying he is better than everyone.", "annotation_id": "38735294", "url": "https://genius.com/38735294", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Ride", "line": "Season switching over I come through them bitches, still scorchin’ as if I didn’t notice", "vault_lines": ["I come through them bitches, still scorchin' as if I didn't notice"], "meaning": "Drake uses the seasons in his music quite often- this also alludes to the overall stage he set in the opening about it being “after summer’s rolled on”. In this case he’s still heated up from summer so to speak", "annotation_id": "36966652", "url": "https://genius.com/36966652", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
