{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Give Ya", "line": "Canadian visitor, lady exhibitor", "vault_lines": ["Canadian visitor, lady exhibitor"], "meaning": "Although the featured artist is Trey, the Canadian visitor that he is talking about is none other than Drizzy him self, being born in Toronto, Ontario, Canada. There was not many rappers from Canada, so it’s kind of a big deal that Drake is Canadian. Drake would go on to put the whole country of Canada on the map in the rap game.\n\nTrey is either saying that he himself takes his women out to be shown off, or that Drake does.", "annotation_id": "15710823", "url": "https://genius.com/15710823", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Give Ya", "line": "Back again return of the mack again", "vault_lines": ["Back again return of the mack again"], "meaning": "Reference to the song “return of the mack” by Mark Morrison.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uB1D9wWxd2w\n\nDon’t edit: working on this right now.", "annotation_id": "9101646", "url": "https://genius.com/9101646", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Give Ya", "line": "Drake take Patrón to the face ’til he wasted", "vault_lines": ["Drake take Patrón to the face 'til he wasted"], "meaning": "Seems like they switched favorite drinks because on the video of “HYFR” Trey can be seen taking a straight shot of Patron from the bottle!!\n\n\n\nhttps://twitter.com/TreySongz/status/242298029196054528", "annotation_id": "3933513", "url": "https://genius.com/3933513", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Give Ya", "line": "I gave up a lot to make a progress I give it to you, and you take it the best", "vault_lines": ["I gave up a lot to make a progress", "I give it to you, and you take it the best"], "meaning": "Drake gave up a lot of things to get into music and try and give everyone the best music ever, he discussed them in his future songs just as “Look What You’ve Done.”", "annotation_id": "1882056", "url": "https://genius.com/1882056", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Give Ya", "line": "I’m sonnin’ them all I live in the shade", "vault_lines": ["I'm sonnin' them all I live in the shade"], "meaning": "It’s a play on words, Drake is ruling over all these dudes, it’s like they’re sons to him. This plays off the homophone with ‘sun,’ considering sunlight is the opposite of shade. His living in the shade equates to him being relaxed and chill – giving no effort.", "annotation_id": "1882054", "url": "https://genius.com/1882054", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Give Ya", "line": "Most valuable player baby listen it’s game time We could take a couple shots break down ya d’s", "vault_lines": ["Most valuable player baby listen it's game time", "We could take a couple shots break down ya d's"], "meaning": "The start of basketball imagery in the next few lines, Trey’s playing the role of the MVP when it comes to bitches. They could take shots of liquor and break down a possible wall she might have, which is a double entendre because taking shots in a basketball game could help break down the defense.", "annotation_id": "529091", "url": "https://genius.com/529091", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Give Ya", "line": "I’m blowin ‘til I’m gon’ outta space in the Matrix Call me Mr. Anderson huh", "vault_lines": ["I'm blowin 'til I'm gon' outta space in the Matrix", "Call me Mr. Anderson huh"], "meaning": "Mr. Anderson is what Agent Smith, the main villain, calls Neo throughout the Matrix movie series. Thomas Anderson being Neo’s real name.", "annotation_id": "318309", "url": "https://genius.com/318309", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
