{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "HEATED", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-heated-drake-reference-lyrics", "genius_title": "HEATED (Drake Reference)"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "New Bestie", "line": "Yeah, real bad breeder, street sweeper", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, real bad breeder, street sweeper"], "meaning": "“Bad breeder” (from Jamaican patois “bad breed”) refers to someone who is wild, reckless, and known for violent or unpredictable behaviour.\n\n“Street sweeper” refers to someone with a feared reputation who can “clean up” or control situations on the streets, either through force or influence.\n\nPut together, Drake is describing someone in his circle as a wild, feared individual who can handle confrontation and clears the way when they show up.", "annotation_id": "40278051", "url": "https://genius.com/40278051", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "New Bestie", "line": "You can’t beat dem tings through a speaker", "vault_lines": ["You can't beat dem tings through a speaker"], "meaning": "Drake is referencing his firearms with a play on the word “beat.” In Jamaican patois, a slang term widely used in Toronto and the UK, “beat” can mean to let off shots or fire a gun. Drake taps into that street slang here, giving the line a tougher edge while playing on the word’s more common meaning.", "annotation_id": "40205912", "url": "https://genius.com/40205912", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "New Bestie", "line": "Fever, you lookin’ hot inna di FaceTime", "vault_lines": ["Fever, you lookin' hot inna di FaceTime"], "meaning": "This bar plays on the word “fever.” On one level, a fever is a symptom that causes a hot body temperature. On another, being hot describes someone looking especially attractive or desirable.\n\nGiven the lines that follow—where Drake references Vybz Kartel through nicknames like “Addi,” “Di Teacher,” and “Gaza Grim Reaper”—the lyric also appears to be a nod to Kartel’s hit song Fever.", "annotation_id": "40205859", "url": "https://genius.com/40205859", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "New Bestie", "line": "Libra, now you think we the same side", "vault_lines": ["Libra, now you think we the same side"], "meaning": "This girl may be a fellow October baby. However she is a Libra and Drake is a Scorpio.", "annotation_id": "40078787", "url": "https://genius.com/40078787", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "New Bestie", "line": "And a killion tings pon waist like diva", "vault_lines": ["And a killion tings pon waist like diva"], "meaning": "The correct lyrics are:\n\nAnd the killy have tings pon waist like beeper.”\n\nDrake’s shooters have guns similar to how people used to wear beepers… Around their waists.", "annotation_id": "39992990", "url": "https://genius.com/39992990", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "New Bestie", "line": "You like man that the killy have beef with", "vault_lines": ["You like man that the killy have beef with"], "meaning": "Should be “You like man that Kylian beef with”. Noting this woman messes with athletes and star soccer players throughout Europe.", "annotation_id": "39868727", "url": "https://genius.com/39868727", "state": "pending", "votes": -4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "New Bestie", "line": "Gaza grim reaper", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "It is a nickname rather than a formal geographical location, popularized in the mid-2000s by dancehall superstar Vybz Kartel. “Gaza” in Jamaica refers to the Waterford community in Portmore. Kartel, who is from the area, coined the term to reflect the harsh living conditions and struggle for survival, drawing a thematic comparison to the conflict in the Middle Eastern Gaza Strip.\n\nUnlikely it is a reference to Gaza Slim, whose real name is Vanessa Saddler (often going by the stage name Vanessa Bling), is a Jamaican dancehall and reggae singer. She rose to fame in the early 2010s as a prominent member of Vybz Kartel’s “Gaza” music empire, collaborating on hit tracks like “One Man,” “Anything a Anything,” and “Clarks.”", "annotation_id": "39803995", "url": "https://genius.com/39803995", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "New Bestie", "line": "Yeah, Addi, yah mi daddy, yah di teacher Yeah, big up the teacher Make Kartel get one line for the teacher", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, Addi, yah mi daddy, yah di teacher", "Yeah, big up the teacher", "Make Kartel get one line for the teacher"], "meaning": "“Addi” is a common reference to Vybz Kartel (born Adidja Azim Palmer), the legendary Jamaican dancehall artist whose stage name has spawned various “Addi” variations and monikers (often spelled Addi, Addy) used by his family and fans. His son is also known as Likkle Addi.\n\nHe’s also commonly referred to as the teacher as a sign of respect.\n\nAddi yah mi daddy\n\nis a common saying effectively calling Vybz his father, not in literal sense but as a show of respect.", "annotation_id": "39803971", "url": "https://genius.com/39803971", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "New Bestie", "line": "Pamela, you’re too unruly and bad, yuh kna", "vault_lines": ["Pamela, you're too unruly and bad, yuh kna"], "meaning": "Popcaan, a dancehall artist that has several collaborations with Drake, including on MAID OF HONOUR, was formerly signed to OVO. Drake pays homage to him, as Drake is rapping in Patois.\n\n“Unruly Bad” is a massive dancehall track by Jamaican artist Popcaan, released on the Henging Tree Riddim. The hook reads\n\nYou nuh bad like Unruly\n\nPopcaan says “unruly” so frequently, often multiple times in a single song and across his social media that it serves as his signature catchphrase, record label name (Unruly Entertainment), and lifestyle brand (Unrulystate).", "annotation_id": "39803703", "url": "https://genius.com/39803703", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "New Bestie", "line": "Mi waan flood out the chain like Katrina", "vault_lines": ["Mi waan flood out the chain like Katrina"], "meaning": "When a chain is completely covered in diamonds or other precious stones, it is flooded or iced-out.\n\nDrake compares a chain he wants to cover in diamonds to Hurricane Katrina, which hit Louisiana and other surrounding U.S. states in August 2005 and left around 80% of New Orleans flooded in water.", "annotation_id": "39800850", "url": "https://genius.com/39800850", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "New Bestie", "line": "Yeah, ayo, Noel tek out the bass line", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, ayo, Noel tek out the bass line"], "meaning": "Drake’s longtime OVO sound engineer, Noel Cadastre (OVO Noel).\n\nNoel is a core OVO member from Toronto, heavily involved in mixing/mastering on albums like Scorpion, More Life, and the recent 2026 projects (Iceman, Maid of Honour, Habtiti).", "annotation_id": "39798113", "url": "https://genius.com/39798113", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "New Bestie", "line": "Yeah, I want a Latina, I want a Latina I want a G like Karolina", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I want a Latina, I want a Latina", "I want a G like Karolina"], "meaning": "Drake name-drops Karol G (“Karolina”) as his ideal Latina — her real name is Carolina Giraldo Navarro.\n\n @karolg is a Colombian reggaeton superstar known for megahits like “Bichota” and “Provenza”.\n\nThe timing of this lyric is fitting: Karol G made history at Coachella 2026 as the first Latina artist to ever headline the festival, further cementing her status as one of the biggest names in music.\n\n\n\nAlthough Charlamagne tha God fueled massive hype on The Breakfast Club by claiming she would feature on ICEMAN, she was ultimately left off the official tracklist.", "annotation_id": "39779064", "url": "https://genius.com/39779064", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
