{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Must Hate Money", "line": "I’ve got it made thats what I’m talking about Going down to the fashion store and get myself fitted out Going down to the dealers buy myself a brand new car So me and my lady can ride", "vault_lines": ["I've got it made thats what I'm talking about", "Going down to the fashion store and get myself fitted out", "Going down to the dealers buy myself a brand new car", "So me and my lady can ride"], "meaning": "A sample from the Willie Hutch song “Aint That Mellow”.", "annotation_id": "698988", "url": "https://genius.com/698988", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Must Hate Money", "line": "If bein’ fly against the law bitch call the police", "vault_lines": ["If bein' fly against the law bitch call the police"], "meaning": "Similar to the Kurt Cobain quote, “If it’s illegal to rock and roll then throw my ass in jail”", "annotation_id": "444950", "url": "https://genius.com/444950", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Must Hate Money", "line": "But you can’t call me Champagne Charlie", "vault_lines": ["But you can't call me Champagne Charlie"], "meaning": "This is a continuation on the Hugh Grant metaphor. Hugh Grant was in a French-Canadian drama television series called Champagne Charlie, the show being named after a (slightly derogatory) term for those living the jet-set lifestyle which Drake wasn’t a part of at the time (although he almost certainly is now).\n\nHe probably wouldn’t appreciate being called a Champagne Charlie these days, although he has no qualms about being called Champagne Papi (his Instagram and his production name).", "annotation_id": "353941", "url": "https://genius.com/353941", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Must Hate Money", "line": "Haters wanna see me dead like John Tucker", "vault_lines": ["Haters wanna see me dead like John Tucker"], "meaning": "He is reffering to the name of the movie “John Tucker Must Die”. People want Rich Boy to die because they envy the success and fame he has in the rap game.", "annotation_id": "353938", "url": "https://genius.com/353938", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Must Hate Money", "line": "’Cause when I’m in the spot it’s popping like Christopher’s single", "vault_lines": ["'Cause when I'm in the spot it's popping like Christopher's single"], "meaning": "Christopher is Chris Brown, who had a single called “Poppin'”. Looking back, this line is pretty funny because at the time it was just a throwaway pop culture reference. Drake and Chris have since developed a pretty complicated and tumultuous relationship (mostly centered around Rihanna), but at the time he was really just talking about the single “Poppin'”.", "annotation_id": "219684", "url": "https://genius.com/219684", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Must Hate Money", "line": "That prometh with that sprite and jolly rancher so flamingo", "vault_lines": ["That prometh with that sprite and jolly rancher so flamingo"], "meaning": "Prometh refers to Promethazine Codeine cough syrup, the main ingredient in sizzurp (or “Lean”), a drink that mixes the codeine syrup with a carbonated beverage (in this case, Sprite).\n\nCodeine cough syrup appears purple, but when mixed with Sprite, it turns pink, thus, giving the appearance of a flamingo colored drink.", "annotation_id": "219676", "url": "https://genius.com/219676", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Must Hate Money", "line": "It started out about a boy like Hugh Grant", "vault_lines": ["It started out about a boy like Hugh Grant"], "meaning": "Hugh Grant played a role in a movie called “About a Boy”, which he mentored a kid who was bullied in school.  Drake might be refering to himself as a boy but he turned himself into the man he is today.", "annotation_id": "219659", "url": "https://genius.com/219659", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Must Hate Money", "line": "Back when “fuck bitches, get money” was the new chant", "vault_lines": ["Back when \"fuck bitches, get money\" was the new chant"], "meaning": "This is probably a biggie reference, “Fuck Bitches, Get Money” was a popular chant that biggie started during his rapping career.", "annotation_id": "219657", "url": "https://genius.com/219657", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Must Hate Money", "line": "My true religion is money, check out the pant seams", "vault_lines": ["My true religion is money, check out the pant seams"], "meaning": "Drake is using a double entendre mixed with a pun to convey that the only thing he follows is his money, and his pant seams are proof because the brand name is “True Religion” (an expensive clothing brand)\n\n\n\nSaying “my True Relgion is money” is also Drake’s way of showing his approval of the brand.  Saying something is “money” is east coast slang for good or high quality.", "annotation_id": "219609", "url": "https://genius.com/219609", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
