{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Resistance", "line": "Carry the weight for my city like a cargo ship", "vault_lines": ["Carry the weight for my city like a cargo ship"], "meaning": "Aubrey states how he feels as though he has to do all the heavy lifting in terms of carrying his city, Toronto, into the spotlight.\n\n\n\nIn recent years, alongside fellow Canadian superstars such as The Weeknd and Tory Lanez, Drizzy has thrust Toronto’s rap scene onto the world stage as one of the most important musical cities on Earth.", "annotation_id": "19556801", "url": "https://genius.com/19556801", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Resistance", "line": "It’s like I’m high right now, the guy right now", "vault_lines": ["It's like I'm high right now, the guy right now"], "meaning": "Drake,“The Boy”,  has evolved from what he used to be, just a boy on the come up that everyone had acknowledged but not taken the most serious. This feeling of finally being recognized for the artist Drizzy truly is, leaves him feeling a high, maybe one that can not compare to any drug.", "annotation_id": "16505601", "url": "https://genius.com/16505601", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Resistance", "line": "I said that we could kiss the past goodbye But you weren’t excited", "vault_lines": ["I said that we could kiss the past goodbye", "But you weren't excited"], "meaning": "While the 6 god wants to move past old mistakes and leave them in the past, the girl he tells this too has no hope or expectations in forgetting the wrongs he or perhaps they have both made.", "annotation_id": "16505577", "url": "https://genius.com/16505577", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Resistance", "line": "Yeah, I just need some closure Ain’t no turnin’ back for me, I’m in it ’til it’s over", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I just need some closure", "Ain't no turnin' back for me, I'm in it 'til it's over"], "meaning": "Alludes to the next song on the album “Over” where he explains he’s going to be in this rap game for a long time until it as aforementioned over", "annotation_id": "15134587", "url": "https://genius.com/15134587", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Resistance", "line": "I know, but same time I’m quick to forget", "vault_lines": ["I know, but same time I'm quick to forget"], "meaning": "Drake’s girlfriend at the time “set him up” and helped some guys rob Drake. The “two guns” suggest that it was two guys or maybe one.\n\nDrake knows very well who did this against him and who wants to hurt him in general. However, he doesn’t have time to dedicate his thought and “energy” to these things. He’s too busy dropping music and making money.", "annotation_id": "8299506", "url": "https://genius.com/8299506", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Resistance", "line": "But in fact, I haven’t seen them since they locked Big Rich up", "vault_lines": ["But in fact, I haven't seen them since they locked Big Rich up"], "meaning": "Big Rich is a Bay Area rapper, who got locked up in prison.", "annotation_id": "6610067", "url": "https://genius.com/6610067", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Resistance", "line": "Yesterday, when we were getting high You were invited, you woulda liked it", "vault_lines": ["Yesterday, when we were getting high", "You were invited, you woulda liked it"], "meaning": "In “Karaoke”, Drake revealed there were troublesome times between him and his girl. He would often invite her to come hang out, but she’d turn him down.", "annotation_id": "1656940", "url": "https://genius.com/1656940", "state": "accepted", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Resistance", "line": "Uh, I live by some advice this girl Lissa told me The other day Lissa told me that she miss the old me", "vault_lines": ["Uh, I live by some advice this girl Lissa told me", "The other day Lissa told me that she miss the old me"], "meaning": "DJ Lissa Monet, a DJ from Toronto told Drake that she misses the old him. In the next verse, he reminisces, trying to find out when he changed towards his friends.", "annotation_id": "1193187", "url": "https://genius.com/1193187", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Resistance", "line": "But hit “re-dial,” you’ll see that I just called Some chick I met at the mall that I barely know at all and Plus, this woman that I messed wit’ unprotected Texted sayin’ she wished she woulda kept it The one that I’m layin’ next to just looked over and read it", "vault_lines": ["But hit \"re-dial,\" you'll see that I just called", "Some chick I met at the mall that I barely know at all and", "Plus, this woman that I messed wit' unprotected", "Texted sayin' she wished she woulda kept it", "The one that I'm layin' next to just looked over and read it"], "meaning": "Not only does Drake reveal to us that he has stopped talking to his grandmother, but he also has been ignoring her to hook up with random girls he won’t even talk to the next day. He even goes so far as to reveal that he got one of the girls pregnant and forced her to get an abortion.\n\nWhile a frequent knock against Drake is that he’s too emotional/girly, this provides a level of insight into the life of a rapper that is just about unparalleled in hip-hop. Complain all you like, but most would agree this is a refreshing change of pace to a genre where most artists attempt to portray themselves as superhuman.", "annotation_id": "67351", "url": "https://genius.com/67351", "state": "accepted", "votes": 123, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Resistance", "line": "Did I just trade free time for camera time?", "vault_lines": ["Did I just trade free time for camera time?"], "meaning": "What Drake didn’t realize about fame is that it isn’t like you get to pick and choose when you’re a celebrity; the cameras are going to be following you 24/7 and this can have some negative effects on your personal life.", "annotation_id": "25755", "url": "https://genius.com/25755", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Resistance", "line": "I’m tryna do better than good enough", "vault_lines": ["I'm tryna do better than good enough"], "meaning": "In a sentiment that everyone can relate to (regardless of profession), Drake wants to be the best in his chosen field. He also “did” a documentary about his album release entitled Better Than Good Enough.", "annotation_id": "20476", "url": "https://genius.com/20476", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Resistance", "line": "What am I afraid of? This is s’posed to be what dreams are made of But people I don’t have the time to hang wit’ Always look at me and say the same shit They say, “You promised me you would never change up” Uh-uh, uh, uh-uh, uh “You promised me you would never change up”", "vault_lines": ["What am I afraid of?", "This is s'posed to be what dreams are made of", "But people I don't have the time to hang wit'", "Always look at me and say the same shit", "They say, \"You promised me you would never change up\"", "\"You promised me you would never change up\""], "meaning": "A popular theme in rap: money changes the rapper’s personality in spite of his best efforts to avoid it.\n\nIn most of Drake’s raps (commonly when he is the only one rapping), how people perceive him in his famous position is his topic of choice. His old friends think the money and fame has changed him.", "annotation_id": "20474", "url": "https://genius.com/20474", "state": "accepted", "votes": 69, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Resistance", "line": "It’s ironic, ’cause my mother was a florist And that’s how she met my pops And now my garden is enormous", "vault_lines": ["It's ironic, 'cause my mother was a florist", "And that's how she met my pops", "And now my garden is enormous"], "meaning": "Drake understands irony as well as fellow Canadian ironist Alanis Morissette (not well). While it is coincidence that his mother was a florist and that he also plants seeds (albeit metaphorical seeds in his case), it is certainly not ironic", "annotation_id": "19888", "url": "https://genius.com/19888", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Resistance", "line": "“It’s happening, Penny Lane, just like you said”", "vault_lines": ["\"It's happening, Penny Lane, just like you said\""], "meaning": "This is taken from the movie Almost Famous, where love interest Penny Lane predicted the main character would get famous. So throughout the movie, he keeps repeating this quote to her as he gets closer to fame.\n\n\n\n“Penny Lane” could also be a reference to his former Degrassi co-star Stacey Farber, as Farber looks like the actress who plays Penny – Drake even put up an Instagram of he and Farber together, with a caption that read “Stacey Farber/Ellie Nash/Penny Lane”. So it’s possible that Farber is like his version of Penny Lane, someone that has believed he was going to make it big ever since the beginning.", "annotation_id": "19231", "url": "https://genius.com/19231", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Resistance", "line": "Uh, I’m 23 wit’ a money tree Growing more too, I just planted a hunnid seeds", "vault_lines": ["Uh, I'm 23 wit' a money tree", "Growing more too, I just planted a hunnid seeds"], "meaning": "A play on the old adage “money doesn’t grow on trees”. Drake is saying that he’s so rich that he pretty much does own a money tree, and he plans on planting more seeds so he can keep growing it.", "annotation_id": "19230", "url": "https://genius.com/19230", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Resistance", "line": "I heard they just moved my grandmother to a nursin’ home And I be actin’ like I don’t know how to work a phone", "vault_lines": ["I heard they just moved my grandmother to a nursin' home", "And I be actin' like I don't know how to work a phone"], "meaning": "Drake used to be close with his grandmother, but now he’s famous and he hasn’t been calling her even though she’s lonely in the nursing home. Another example of how fame can change your life and personality no matter how hard you try not to let it.", "annotation_id": "18695", "url": "https://genius.com/18695", "state": "accepted", "votes": 55, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Resistance", "line": "Maybe it was the fast-paced switch up Or the two guns in my face durin’ the stick up Maybe ’cause a girl I thought I trusted Was who set the whole shit up", "vault_lines": ["Maybe it was the fast-paced switch up", "Or the two guns in my face durin' the stick up", "Maybe 'cause a girl I thought I trusted", "Was who set the whole shit up"], "meaning": "Drake begins to contemplate what has caused him to begin to act differently. His best guesses are either his sudden rise to fame before he could adjust himself to the new lifestyle, or the time he was robbed at gunpoint in 2009. Drake has revealed that he believes the robbery was set-up by a girl he was dating, so this would certainly explain his trust issues when it comes to women.", "annotation_id": "18187", "url": "https://genius.com/18187", "state": "accepted", "votes": 55, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Resistance", "line": "Will I blow all of this money, baby, hammer time?", "vault_lines": ["Will I blow all of this money, baby, hammer time?"], "meaning": "Rapper MC Hammer notoriously blew through a fortune until he was broke.\n\n“Stop: (spending your money wildly) Hammer Time!”", "annotation_id": "17945", "url": "https://genius.com/17945", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Resistance", "line": "I don’t really wanna worry ‘bout gettin’ back on I’m just tryin’ to stay on, get my fuckin’ buffet on", "vault_lines": ["I don't really wanna worry 'bout gettin' back on", "I'm just tryin' to stay on, get my fuckin' buffet on"], "meaning": "Now that Drake is finally successful, he wants to make sure he stays “eating” – he doesn’t want to “pull an Eminem” and have to re-emerge after spending time away from the limelight.", "annotation_id": "17940", "url": "https://genius.com/17940", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Resistance", "line": "When 40 got some shit for me to snap on Now that I’m on", "vault_lines": ["When 40 got some shit for me to snap on", "Now that I'm on"], "meaning": "“Snapping” on a track means to really go in over an instrumental. Drake’s longtime producer Noah “40” Shebib is close friends with Drizzy and has produced many of his best-known songs where he tends to snap – such as this one.", "annotation_id": "17939", "url": "https://genius.com/17939", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Resistance", "line": "Uh (Oh), am I wrong for makin’ light of my situation? Clap on", "vault_lines": ["What am I afraid of?", "Uh (Oh), am I wrong for makin' light of my situation? Clap on"], "meaning": "Drake tries to “make light” of his somewhat serious problems so that he doesn’t come off as overly whiny, but sometimes he wonders if this is the best way to deal with his problems. This is also a pun on The Clapper™, since owners of The Clapper™ can literally “make light” by clapping their hands and turning the lights on.", "annotation_id": "17938", "url": "https://genius.com/17938", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Resistance", "line": "I avoided the coke game and went with Sprite instead Uh-uh, that’s word to the millions that they putting up", "vault_lines": ["I avoided the coke game and went with Sprite instead", "Uh-uh, that's word to the millions that they putting up"], "meaning": "Drake avoided drug dealing and chose to make his millions legally through endorsements with companies like Sprite. Additionally, Drake drug of choice is not cocaine but rather codeine, and his preferred drink to mix it with is not Coke but rather Sprite.", "annotation_id": "17935", "url": "https://genius.com/17935", "state": "accepted", "votes": 94, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Resistance", "line": "I blew myself up, I’m on some martyr shit", "vault_lines": ["I blew myself up, I'm on some martyr shit"], "meaning": "Martyrs are people that die for their religious beliefs – a suicide bomber, for example. While Drake didn’t blow himself up literally, he takes a great deal of credit in making himself as popular as he is now.", "annotation_id": "17930", "url": "https://genius.com/17930", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Resistance", "line": "Uh, should I spend the weekend in Vegas? I’m living inside a moment, not taking pictures to save it I mean, how could I forget? My memory’s never faded", "vault_lines": ["I'm living inside a moment, not taking pictures to save it", "I mean, how could I forget? My memory's never faded", "Uh, should I spend the weekend in Vegas?"], "meaning": "Drake lives in the moment – while most people would make sure to take pictures of memorable vacations like a Vegas trip, Drake doesn’t have to because his vacations are unforgettable. Additionally, he enjoys living in the moment more than reflecting on the past, so pictures don’t mean much to him.\n\nProbably also a commentary on the fact that, even in 2010 when this album came out, most people were more concerned with showing their experiences on Twitstagram rather than living in their moments. Also, “my memory’s never faded” is a play on the fact that HE often is, though his memory isn’t.", "annotation_id": "17927", "url": "https://genius.com/17927", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Resistance", "status": "done", "targets": 33, "clicked": 33, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-the-resistance-lyrics", "genius_title": "The Resistance"}
