{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "That’s why I’m movin’ all elusive These boys on they last resort and it’s givin’ us all inclusive", "vault_lines": ["That's why I'm movin' all elusive", "These boys on they last resort and it's givin' us all inclusive"], "meaning": "Drake here drops a double entendre. The other guys competing with Drake are now on their last legs after all their other attempts have failed. But when he says all inclusive, he also shows the gap between him and his competition financially as an all-inclusive resort is much cheaper than the non-inclusive resorts Drake stays at.", "annotation_id": "37868394", "url": "https://genius.com/37868394", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "Yayo so clean, I told ’em call it, “Ajax”", "vault_lines": ["Yayo so clean, I told 'em call it, \"Ajax\""], "meaning": "“Yayo” is slang for cocaine, and Ajax is a brand of household cleaner. When cocaine is considered “clean,” it’s in its purest form—meaning it isn’t cut with any other substances like baking soda or talcum powder to save costs. Essentially, Ross only sells high quality product.", "annotation_id": "37256829", "url": "https://genius.com/37256829", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "Damn, how can I forgive like this? I gotta dead a lot of shit just to live like this I had to fuck a lot of girls to get a kid like this I had to get a lot of cribs to get a crib like this", "vault_lines": ["Damn, how can I forgive like this?", "I gotta dead a lot of shit just to live like this", "I had to fuck a lot of girls to get a kid like this", "I had to get a lot of cribs to get a crib like this"], "meaning": "Drake is using the word “crib” as a double entendre. Initially, it refers to houses or luxury homes, suggesting that he had to work hard, invest, and buy multiple properties to be able to afford his current lifestyle. Metaphorically, it reflects the idea that achieving a high level of success requires gaining experience, and putting in effort and resources over time.\n\nDrake currently owns a $100-million mansion called The Embassy in his hometown of Toronto, which is the “crib” he is likely referring to in this line.", "annotation_id": "34114548", "url": "https://genius.com/34114548", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "All my chains look like snakes, that’s some real diamondbacks", "vault_lines": ["All my chains look like snakes, that's some real diamondbacks"], "meaning": "Weezy F shows off his vintage wordplay here, comparing his collection of snake chains to that of a Diamondback Rattlesnake. More people are bitten by the Western Diamondback each year than any other snake in the USA.", "annotation_id": "26461719", "url": "https://genius.com/26461719", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "Brrrt, may I speak to pussy niggas? I just call it like I see it, I ain’t even lookin’, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Brrrt, may I speak to pussy niggas?", "I just call it like I see it, I ain't even lookin', nigga", "I just walk it like I speak and I ain't speakin' to them niggas"], "meaning": "This could be a callback to a lyric on Wayne’s December 2010 hit, “6 Foot 7 Foot,” where he raps:\n\nAnd I call it like I see it, and my glasses on", "annotation_id": "25145559", "url": "https://genius.com/25145559", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "I got sentenced, took some time and it was easier than simple", "vault_lines": ["I got sentenced, took some time and it was easier than simple"], "meaning": "In March 2010 Wayne got sentenced to 1 year in prison at Rikers Island for a weapons charge from a July 2007 incident. While Wayne was away there was a big ‘Free Weezy’ movement in the hip-hop world, and he was released in November after serving 8 months, going right back to running the rap game.\n\nWhile in jail, Wayne was mostly held in protective custody away from other prisoners, and his album I Am Not a Human Being became the first album since 2Pac’s 1995 album Me Against The World to reach the top position on the Billboard 200 while its artist was in prison. Safe to say his jail time was fairly easy.", "annotation_id": "24032128", "url": "https://genius.com/24032128", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "Yeah, they plottin’ on me but they gotta do somethin’ Told my dawg two-somethin’ just to shoot somethin’ (M-M—) Left them niggas stretched out on the train tracks Rather you than me, here come that payback Got ‘em lookin’ for that paper that they can’t tax", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, they plottin' on me but they gotta do somethin'", "Told my dawg two-somethin' just to shoot somethin' (M-M—)", "Left them niggas stretched out on the train tracks", "Rather you than me, here come that payback", "Got 'em lookin' for that paper that they can't tax"], "meaning": "Ross likely makes a nod here back to his ninth studio album, Rather You Than Me which was released in March 2017.", "annotation_id": "23987829", "url": "https://genius.com/23987829", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "Whip that big body Maybach like it’s a little Pontiac", "vault_lines": ["Whip that big body Maybach like it's a little Pontiac"], "meaning": "In his video for “Laugh Now Cry Later,” Drake displays concept cars.\nhttps://twitter.com/WordOnRd/status/1294162910932078592?s=20", "annotation_id": "23879902", "url": "https://genius.com/23879902", "state": "pending", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "Hialeah celebrated when Fidel died", "vault_lines": ["Hialeah celebrated when Fidel died"], "meaning": "Hialeah, the sixth largest city in Florida, has the highest percentage of Cuban and Cuban American residents of any city in the United States, at 73.37% of the population, making them a typical and prominent feature of the city’s culture.\n\nWhen Cuban dictator Fidel Castro died, the city erupted into a huge street party.", "annotation_id": "23878911", "url": "https://genius.com/23878911", "state": "pending", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "Yeah, two-point-two for the Rafael Nadal", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, two-point-two for the Rafael Nadal"], "meaning": "This is likely a reference to the limited edition RM 27-04 watch made by Swiss watch company Richard Mille in partnership with Spanish Tennis player Rafael Nadal. In July 2021, Drake is known to have purchased one of these watches, of which only 50 were made available to the public. The watch was made to celebrate the 10 year anniversary of Richard Mille’s sponsorship of Nadal, who himself is known to wear some incredibly expensive sports watches during his Tennis matches.\n\n‘Two point two’ is most likely referring to a price of $2.2 million that Drake paid for the watch. The word ‘point’ could also be referring to a point in a game of Tennis.\n\n\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/CQ-ZPPJjmPj/?utm_source=ig_embed\n\nDrake wearing the watch\n\n\n\nRafael Nadal wearing the watch", "annotation_id": "23876337", "url": "https://genius.com/23876337", "state": "accepted", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "Unthinkable when I think of the way these niggas been actin’ Yeah, I never did you nothin’ and you play like we family, huh? Next thing, you wanna shoot me down, it can’t be love Not sure where you was tryna send it, it can’t be up That day you sounded like a bitch, you fancy, huh?", "vault_lines": ["Unthinkable when I think of the way these niggas been actin'", "Yeah, I never did you nothin' and you play like we family, huh?", "Next thing, you wanna shoot me down, it can't be love", "Not sure where you was tryna send it, it can't be up", "That day you sounded like a bitch, you fancy, huh?"], "meaning": "Drake is sending shots at Swizz Beatz, who reportedly did an Instagram Live with Busta Rhymes back in June 2020 while being intoxicated and seemingly called Drake a “pussy” over a possible record leaking and threatened to “shooting down” Drizzy’s newly acquired private jet. Even though Swizz did apologize the next day while saying “it’s all love”, Drizzy still remember the disrespect.\n\nSo here, Drake strung together “Unthinkable”, the title of a song he wrote with Alicia Keys, who is Swizz’s wife and interpolated ”Fancy”, a song from his own album Thank Me Later that he featured Swizz Beatz on the chorus.", "annotation_id": "23876246", "url": "https://genius.com/23876246", "state": "accepted", "votes": 72, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "Her ears popped, she lick my lollipop and my teardrops, Tunechi", "vault_lines": ["Her ears popped, she lick my lollipop and my teardrops, Tunechi"], "meaning": "Here Lil Wayne is suggesting she was so into his music, she “licked” him down below and on the face.\n\nLil Wayne has tear drop tattoos on his face. They’re controversial because a teardrop on the face can represent someone you’ve killed – Wayne has avoided this fact. https://www.stotkertattoo.com/tips/why-does-lil-wayne-have-a-teardrop-tattoo.html\n\nHe also released “Lollipop” on “Tha Carter III” in 2008:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2IH8tNQAzSs", "annotation_id": "23875398", "url": "https://genius.com/23875398", "state": "pending", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "I got bitches doin’ lines, I’m Adidas to ’em, nigga", "vault_lines": ["I got bitches doin' lines, I'm Adidas to 'em, nigga"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is suggesting he has girls “doin' lines” which could be a reference to cocaine. He is comparing himself to adidas as they are iconic for everyone wearing their 3 lines. Also they release successful lines of clothing.", "annotation_id": "23875379", "url": "https://genius.com/23875379", "state": "pending", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "Been spazzin’ since CB was chunkin’ up the deuces, nigga Your shit was boo-boo, excuses, excuses, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Been spazzin' since CB was chunkin' up the deuces, nigga", "Your shit was boo-boo, excuses, excuses, nigga"], "meaning": "Chris Brown dropped the popular track “Deuces” in 2011 which Drake also featured on the remix. Drake is implying he has been doing his thing for over ten years now.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=11aMClGbrKE", "annotation_id": "23875368", "url": "https://genius.com/23875368", "state": "accepted", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "M-M—, M-M—", "vault_lines": ["Back to the real niggas glowin' in the dark (M-M—)", "Real niggas deserve to live twice (M-M—)", "Told my dawg two-somethin' just to shoot somethin' (M-M—)"], "meaning": "This is the famous adlib for Maybach Music Group – voiced by Jessica Gomes.", "annotation_id": "23875355", "url": "https://genius.com/23875355", "state": "accepted", "votes": 59, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "Catalog is immaculate Still runnin’ the game, don’t ask me about the practice", "vault_lines": ["Still runnin' the game, don't ask me about the practice"], "meaning": "Describing his dominance over the rap industry, Drake references NBA Hall of Famer Allen Iverson’s infamous “practice” press conference from 2002. When a reporter asked Iverson about missing one practice, he expressed his displeasure at the question, responding with the following:\n\nWe’re talking about practice. Not a game! Not a game! Not a game! We’re talking about practice. Not a game; not the game that I go out there and die for and play every game like it’s my last, not the game, we’re talking about practice, man. I mean, how silly is that? We’re talking about practice.\n\nAs a basketball icon and NBA MVP, Iverson was upset that his premier status and willingness to practice were called into question. The lengthy nature of Iverson’s response also may have been triggered by the murder of his best friend, Rahsaan Langeford, seven months prior to the press conference. Like AI, Drake finds that his position or “run” atop the rap game will only continue and that “running” in practice is not of other’s concern.", "annotation_id": "23875131", "url": "https://genius.com/23875131", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "Patti LaBelle, who knew that we would sell pies?", "vault_lines": ["Patti LaBelle, who knew that we would sell pies?"], "meaning": "Patti LaBelle is an American R&B and Soul artist known for  songs such as “If Only You Knew” and “On My Own.” In 2015, she began selling sweet potato pies at Walmart stores throughout the United States. Following a viral review from social media personality James Wright, the pies quickly sold out. In the years following the video, the pies continue to be a commercial success, with more than 36,000 sold each day.\n\nRoss uses pies as a double entendre to reference Patti LaBelle’s sweet potato dessert and drug trafficking. A pie is a slang term for a kilogram of cocaine, an amount which he expresses disbelief in his ability to sell. Ross himself drew his rap name from drug kingpin “Freeway” Ricky Ross, who established an extensive distribution network throughout Los Angeles in the 1980s and ‘90s.", "annotation_id": "23874932", "url": "https://genius.com/23874932", "state": "accepted", "votes": 45, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "line": "Ho, you go on vacation, don’t ask me about relaxin’ Not sure if you know but I’m actually Michael Jackson The man I see in the mirror is actually goin’ platinum", "vault_lines": ["Ho, you go on vacation, don't ask me about relaxin'", "Not sure if you know but I'm actually Michael Jackson", "The man I see in the mirror is actually goin' platinum"], "meaning": "Drake compares his success in the music industry to legendary pop icon Michael Jackson. Jackson is remembered today for his live performances, his memorable record releases and the consistency of his music after departing from the The Jackson 5 group to start a solo career. After the King of Pop’s untimely death in 2009, his legacy was succeeded by his posthumous music, including his appearance on Drake’s 2018 album Scorpion, on the track “Don’t Matter to Me.” The song samples a once unreleased Jackson track and highlighted the similarity of both singers' careers. In 2016, Drake broke MJ’s record for most American Music Award nominations, establishing both as significant figures at the top of their respective genres.\n\nInterestingly enough, Drake boasts an appearance on the 2016 2 Chainz track “Big Amount,” rapping:\n\nMichael Jackson talkin' to me in my dreams\nAnd he say, “You bad and you know it”\nBetter shamone with my check then\nI’m a J. Prince investment\n\nIn those lines, Drake mentions the hit 1987 single “Bad,” similar to how he slyly mentions Jackson’s “Man in the Mirror” from 1988 on this track. Here, Drake uses the track’s title to boast his countless platinum certifications and is crowned as the top certified singles artist of the RIAA.", "annotation_id": "23874414", "url": "https://genius.com/23874414", "state": "accepted", "votes": 61, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "You Only Live Twice", "status": "done", "targets": 18, "clicked": 18, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-you-only-live-twice-lyrics", "genius_title": "You Only Live Twice"}
