{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Congratulations", "line": "I’m next to blow, pause", "vault_lines": ["I'm next to blow, pause"], "meaning": "“Blow” usually means giving oral sex to someone, a man hopefully. Drake says he is the next to blow, which people would probably think he’s next to suck dick.\nBy blow he means blow up", "annotation_id": "23258308", "url": "https://genius.com/23258308", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Congratulations", "line": "Uh, black hearts on my cardigan", "vault_lines": ["Uh, black hearts on my cardigan"], "meaning": "Refers to the heart logo of the Comme des Garcons label CDG PLAY, which Drake liked to wear at the time.", "annotation_id": "22617571", "url": "https://genius.com/22617571", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Congratulations", "line": "My deal like Weezy first week, one point somethin’", "vault_lines": ["My deal like Weezy first week, one point somethin'"], "meaning": "Drake was signed to Young Money and Cash Money Records in 2009, with So Far Gone being his first release on the label(s). When an artist is signed to a record label, they receive a sum of money, usually somewhere between $500,000 and $2 million, and in return make music for the company to sell. On this line, Drake brags that the money he received from getting signed was over a million dollars.\n\nThis is also a reference to the first-week sales of fellow rapper and labelmate Lil Wayne’s 2008 album Tha Carter III, which sold over a million copies in its first seven days of release. The album would also go on to become the highest-selling LP of the year. In other words, Lil Wayne’s album sold over a million and Drake received over a million.", "annotation_id": "17772381", "url": "https://genius.com/17772381", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Congratulations", "line": "Yeah, I tried to tell ’em, Future let ’em know Send the haters all my love, X and O", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I tried to tell 'em, Future let 'em know", "Send the haters all my love, X and O"], "meaning": "By “Future”, Drake is referring to his long-time friend and collaborator DJ Future The Prince, and “X and O” is a way of writing “hugs and kisses”. This song appeared on Drake’s third mixtape So Far Gone, released in 2009. At this point, neither Future nor The Weeknd had launched their careers, but Drake predicts the future (no pun intended) and inadvertently shouts out two of his frequent future collaborators in consecutive lines.\n\nMuch like Drake’s OVO, The Weeknd’s label is called XO.\n\n\n\n#FBGOVOXO", "annotation_id": "11793790", "url": "https://genius.com/11793790", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Congratulations", "line": "If he don’t fuck with y’all, then don’t bother him", "vault_lines": ["If he don't fuck with y'all, then don't bother him"], "meaning": "Seems like he wasn’t into making new friends since the beginning of his career.\n\nHe would also later rap on his “All Me” verse:\n\nY'all don’t fuck with us, then we don’t fuck with y'all; it’s no different over on this side.", "annotation_id": "3891164", "url": "https://genius.com/3891164", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Congratulations", "line": "Like I said we pull your card and find out you’re a Hallmark", "vault_lines": ["Like I said we pull your card and find out you're a Hallmark"], "meaning": "To pull someone’s card means to take them out, maybe kill the person.\n\nHallmark is the largest manufacturer of greeting cards in the United States. They won’t have to kill you since you’re as sweet as this Justin Bieber Hallmark Card.", "annotation_id": "3891129", "url": "https://genius.com/3891129", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Congratulations", "line": "Just know I’m breakin’ world records, no false start", "vault_lines": ["Just know I'm breakin' world records, no false start"], "meaning": "#Drake’s breaking records\n\nMost number ones ever, how long did it really take me?\n\nDrake is holding the record for the most nr. #1 songs on the Billboard R&B/Hip-Hop charts and also Drake is the current record holder for most #1s on Billboard’s Rap charts.", "annotation_id": "3454425", "url": "https://genius.com/3454425", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Congratulations", "line": "I just spent it all once, ’bout to get rich twice", "vault_lines": ["I just spent it all once, 'bout to get rich twice"], "meaning": "Drake got rich off of starring in “Degrassi” but his role ended and the money was blown. Drake was stressed out while making So Far Gone because he was out of money. After this tape, he blew up and got rich again.", "annotation_id": "189179", "url": "https://genius.com/189179", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Congratulations", "line": "Damn! I’m so Catriona smarter than", "vault_lines": ["Damn! I'm so Catriona smarter than"], "meaning": "Referring to his good friend and Toronto native Catriona Smart who is co-owner of Coco & Lowe. .", "annotation_id": "85058", "url": "https://genius.com/85058", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Congratulations", "line": "Dad named me Drake, Footz named me Drizzy", "vault_lines": ["Dad named me Drake, Footz named me Drizzy"], "meaning": "Dad chose Drake for his middle name (his full name is Aubrey Drake Graham).\n\nOriginal ATF member Footz gave Drake the nickname Drizzy.", "annotation_id": "45741", "url": "https://genius.com/45741", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Congratulations", "line": "I got a monopoly, catch me on my boardwalk", "vault_lines": ["I got a monopoly, catch me on my boardwalk"], "meaning": "In economic terms, a monopoly is characterized by a specific person that has a lack of competition for the goods or service they provide. This is a clever metaphor from Drake, saying he doesn’t have any competition among other rappers. In monopoly, the boardwalk spot on the board is equivalent to having property in Times Square.\n\n\n\nHe also throws in a reference to the popular game “Monopoly” which is played on a game board.", "annotation_id": "26758", "url": "https://genius.com/26758", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Congratulations", "line": "And my verses gettin’ stupider Wayne if you’re on Mars, can you pick me up from Jupiter?", "vault_lines": ["And my verses gettin' stupider", "Wayne if you're on Mars, can you pick me up from Jupiter?"], "meaning": "Weezy often refers to himself as a martian and in many songs makes references to being on Mars, such as in “I Feel Like Dying”. Drake’s verses are great (“stupid”), hence him being in space also. .\n\nAlso a play on words in reference to the childhood nursery rhyme “boys are from Jupiter to get more stupider.”", "annotation_id": "26722", "url": "https://genius.com/26722", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Congratulations", "line": "I will break a leg, break an arm and a fibula", "vault_lines": ["I will break a leg, break an arm and a fibula"], "meaning": "“Break a leg” is an expression said to actors, meaning good luck, before they go on stage. Drake goes as far as saying, not only will he break a leg, he will also break an arm and a fibula because he is just that good. Seeing as the fibula is a bone in the leg, he essentially says he’ll break a leg twice. .\n\nIronically, Drake tore a ligament in his knee while performing onstage around the time this song was recorded. .", "annotation_id": "26703", "url": "https://genius.com/26703", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
