{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Presentation", "line": "The city is mine, I control this, you know this ’Cause you are nothing like it and I’m so this, the coldest", "vault_lines": ["The city is mine, I control this, you know this", "'Cause you are nothing like it and I'm so this, the coldest"], "meaning": "A reference to the song “City is Mine”, which appears in his first mixtape “Room For Improvement” and also in this one, Comeback Season", "annotation_id": "22497485", "url": "https://genius.com/22497485", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Presentation", "line": "And like a nigga turned Blood, I came out the blue", "vault_lines": ["And like a nigga turned Blood, I came out the blue"], "meaning": "He is talking about when a member of the Crips gang (represented by the color blue) switches sides and becomes a Blood gang member (represented by the color red). the Crip and Blood gangs have one of the biggest gang rivalries in the United States.\n\nAlso, out of the blue is an expression that means that something appeared or happened unexpectedly. Thus, Drake is saying that he came into the rap game out of the blue like he switched from the Crip to the Blood gang", "annotation_id": "22497402", "url": "https://genius.com/22497402", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Presentation", "line": "You a Gucci groupie, my nigga, and I’m a prodigy", "vault_lines": ["You a Gucci groupie, my nigga, and I'm a prodigy"], "meaning": "Wordplay with the clothing label Prada (prodigy) and Gucci Mane, who takes the first half of his rap name from the clothing label.", "annotation_id": "19108777", "url": "https://genius.com/19108777", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Presentation", "line": "That you are les like NextSelection", "vault_lines": ["That you are les like NextSelection"], "meaning": "A play on Ryan Leslie’s name (R-Les) and the name of his record label, NextSelection Lifestyle Group.", "annotation_id": "18629910", "url": "https://genius.com/18629910", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Presentation", "line": "Get it? Kraft, single, cheese, process Sit back and admire the talent that I possess", "vault_lines": ["Get it? Kraft, single, cheese, process", "Sit back and admire the talent that I possess"], "meaning": "Drake felt that his subliminal bar would pass the audience, so he takes the time to bring it together.\n\nKraft is cheese company, mostly known for their packs of single sliced cheese.", "annotation_id": "12511205", "url": "https://genius.com/12511205", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Presentation", "line": "I’m keepin’ it cleaner than Little X direction", "vault_lines": ["I'm keepin' it cleaner than Little X direction"], "meaning": "Little X, more commonly known as Director X, is well-known for putting together music videos for rappers such as Jay-Z, Nicki Minaj, and Mr. West.\n\nX, also a Toronto native, directed the video for Drake’s “Started From The Bottom.”\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RubBzkZzpUA", "annotation_id": "1575015", "url": "https://genius.com/1575015", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Presentation", "line": "You was playin’ Uno, I was doing you know Whatever us rappers do to develop a new flow, I promise", "vault_lines": ["You was playin' Uno, I was doing you know", "Whatever us rappers do to develop a new flow, I promise"], "meaning": "Drakes says that these other rappers were playing games while he was working hard to become a better rapper. He says “whatever us rapper do” implying  that they aren’t real rappers and wouldn’t know what he’s doing.\n\n\n\nTo be honest, UNO sounds like more fun.", "annotation_id": "560375", "url": "https://genius.com/560375", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Presentation", "line": "I’m sure it can be resolved, I’m just hopin that they make up", "vault_lines": ["I'm sure it can be resolved, I'm just hopin that they make up"], "meaning": "He wishes Jay Z and Damon Dash well wishes on the rekindling of their relationship, hoping that it will benefit him with a deal.\n\nUpdate\n\nJay-Z and Damon Dash solved their issues in 2013.", "annotation_id": "424785", "url": "https://genius.com/424785", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Presentation", "line": "On my Chris Brown shit, I’m still here, gimme that", "vault_lines": ["On my Chris Brown shit, I'm still here, gimme that"], "meaning": "A reference to Chris Brown’s 2006 hit song Gimme That", "annotation_id": "402644", "url": "https://genius.com/402644", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Presentation", "line": "And homie, you ain’t even on my altitude", "vault_lines": ["And homie, you ain't even on my altitude"], "meaning": "Altitude – the height of an object or point in relation to sea level or ground level.\n\nDrake is telling his counterparts that they are not at the same level as him in the rap-game.\nThis line could also imply that Drake is high on weed which wouldn’t be surprising since he has mentioned smoking in numerous songs, such as “U With Me?”:\n\nAnd my house is the definition\nOf alcohol and weed addiction", "annotation_id": "402641", "url": "https://genius.com/402641", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Presentation", "line": "I’m tellin’ you, I got enough clout for two", "vault_lines": ["I'm tellin' you, I got enough clout for two"], "meaning": "There are three possible explanations here:\n\n\nHe’s on such a high level that he’s hanging in the clouds\nHe’s high, and the “clouds” he’s talking about are smoke clouds from the weed\nHere, “cloud” also sounds like “clout,” which is slang for respect and influence; Drake has respect in his city and among his group", "annotation_id": "401572", "url": "https://genius.com/401572", "state": "accepted", "votes": -2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Presentation", "line": "Shout out to 40-40 Yeah, my right hand!", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, my right hand!"], "meaning": "This is Noah “40” Shebib, and he is a canadian producer who makes most of Drake’s beats.", "annotation_id": "220700", "url": "https://genius.com/220700", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Presentation", "line": "Bar Mitzvah kid,", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Yes, Drake is Jewish. For those who don’t know, a Bar Mitzvah is when a 13 year old Jewish boy first reads from the Torah and becomes a man.", "annotation_id": "220694", "url": "https://genius.com/220694", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Presentation", "line": "Me and Rich united like van Nistelrooy", "vault_lines": ["Me and Rich united like van Nistelrooy"], "meaning": "Ruud van Nistelrooy is a soccer player who played for Manchester United at the time this was recorded. Drake describes his relation with the producer with a pun.", "annotation_id": "192629", "url": "https://genius.com/192629", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Presentation", "line": "I’m in Jamaica, docked at the bay, what up Otis?", "vault_lines": ["I'm in Jamaica, docked at the bay, what up Otis?"], "meaning": "Here, he is referring to Otis Redding’s song, “(Sittin' On) The Dock of the Bay”.", "annotation_id": "113456", "url": "https://genius.com/113456", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Presentation", "line": "They like “Damn who’s Drake, where’s wheelchair Jimmy at?”", "vault_lines": ["They like \"Damn who's Drake, where's wheelchair Jimmy at?\""], "meaning": "Before rapping, Drake was as an actor playing the handicapped Jimmy Brooks on Degrassi. With the release of Room for Improvement, his opponents are startled at his sudden entrance into the rap game.", "annotation_id": "95779", "url": "https://genius.com/95779", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
