{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Amen", "line": "Prayin’ that there’s not no other girl I’m prayin’ that these girls’ll never know", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake contrasts the woman’s prayers with his own. While she hopes that Drake is being loyal and monogamous to her, he acknowledges that there are in fact other women in his life, and he is attempting to ensure they all don’t find out about each other.", "annotation_id": "37526051", "url": "https://genius.com/37526051", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Amen", "line": "I just went and paid her car note", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "A “car note” is the monthly payment on a car loan. Drake flexes that he paid off the woman’s car loan for her.", "annotation_id": "37526046", "url": "https://genius.com/37526046", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Amen", "line": "And you my baby, so I gotta put you in the crib", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Continuing the theme of financial success and providing for a woman, with a playful wordplay on the words “baby” (which is also a common nickname for a sexual partner) and “crib” (which is also a slang for a residence).", "annotation_id": "29813547", "url": "https://genius.com/29813547", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Amen", "line": "Church like a priest, Turks for the week", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake references going to church, indicating a sense of spirituality juxtaposed with a trip to Turks and Caicos, a luxurious vacation spot.\n\nDrake references Turks and Caicos a lot throughout his career:\n\n\nSend ‘em to Lagos or Turks and Caicos\nBarbados, Trinidad and Tobago\n- Omertà\n\nI see you back in Turks\nRemember who took you there first and don’t you forget it\n- Desires (feat. Future)\n\nI just got a mansion out in Turks and it’s a beachfront (Okay)\nIf she’s bringin' four friends, I know I’ll hit at least one (Okay, slatt, slatt, slatt, slatt)\n- Pain 1993 (feat. Playboi Carti)\n\nNaw, naw, piece of cake, naw, naw, Turks and Caic', yeah, yeah\nGo and get your friends, we can sneak away, yeah, yeah\n- Popstar (by DJ Khaled)\n\nVoodoo curse, it got him while I flew to Turks\nKnow the dogs had to hit them where we knew it hurts\n- Knife Talk (feat. 21 Savage & Project Pat)\n\nWe ain’t even out in Turks, she finna take sand\nRidin' ‘round with F&N, we like to hold hands\n- Jumbotron Shit Poppin", "annotation_id": "29813534", "url": "https://genius.com/29813534", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Amen", "line": "Turn to your neighbor Say “Neighbor”", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "While Teezo Touchdown is inviting listeners to join him on his spiritual journey towards Christ and thankfulness, he is also referencing his song, Neighborhood, on his debut studio album, “How Do You Sleep At Night?”. This line also speaks to a common expression heard at African-American churches on Sunday morning where the Pastor will ask church goers to turn to their neighbors, often to repeat a significant line from the sermon.", "annotation_id": "29806901", "url": "https://genius.com/29806901", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Amen", "line": "Thank you for calling Mercedes Benz in Beaumont If you know your party’s extension, you may dial it at any time, or dial “9” for company directory For sales, please press “1”", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Beaumont is where Teezo & the voice (his hairstylist, Monique Avant), are from. In this sample, a sample is heard of a call to Mercedes-Benz Beaumont Customer Service on (855) 910-9885. The caller presses 1 on the keypad for the sales division.", "annotation_id": "29731219", "url": "https://genius.com/29731219", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Amen", "line": "Father God I come to You to say thank You That’s all, I don’t wanna ask for anything, I just wanna say thank You, Lord Thank You", "vault_lines": ["I just wanna thank God"], "meaning": "Prayers include three parts: 1) praise, 2) pardon and 3) petition. In the intro, Teezo is expressing praise by simply saying, “Thank you.” This prayer is rather short as he has no pardons nor any petitions to God. Teezo has a lot to be grateful for after his appearances on Tyler, The Creator’s 2021 album, CALL ME IF YOU GET LOST, and Travis Scott’s UTOPIA. He also just dropped his debut album, How Do You Sleep At Night?", "annotation_id": "29730661", "url": "https://genius.com/29730661", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Amen", "line": "Prayin’ ’til you find a man That’s gon’ treat you That’s gon’ treat you like I can (Amen, amen) That’s gon’ please you That’s gon’ please you like I can", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Amen, which is also the track’s title, is a word of Biblical Hebrew origin and it is used in Jewish, Christian, and Muslim practices as a concluding word, or as a response to a prayer.\nTeezo uses the similiarity between “a man” and “Amen” (and even pronounces the “a man” in a way that sounds like “Amen) in order to both emphasising his prayer and praying for her to find someone that will treat and please her the way Teezo did.", "annotation_id": "29730389", "url": "https://genius.com/29730389", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Amen", "line": "Same neighborhood where Ashton Kutcher live I’m just doin’ what that punk should have did (Thank You, Lord)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Both Drake and Ashton Kutcher, which is an American actor and producer, lives in Beverly Hills, a city / neighborhood in Los Angeles, California.\n\nDrake uses the fact that his neighbor (Kutcher) co-created, produced, and hosted the pranks show “Punk’d” (he even pranked Drake on the show), to form a wordplay that implies he treats girls good and respectfully, just like their exes should have treated them.\nKutcher and Drake on “Punk’d”\n\nDrake could also be taking a jab at Kutcher’s recent behavior. In 2023, Kutcher released a public apology and resigned as chair of the board of Thorn, an anti-human trafficking organization that targets child sex abuse, because the public learned he submitted a character letter on behalf of Danny Masterson in his rape trial.\n\nThough there is nothing to suggest any animosity between Drake and Kutcher, you can’t put it beneath Drake to add a secondary layer to his pop cultural references.", "annotation_id": "29727866", "url": "https://genius.com/29727866", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Amen", "line": "Know you don’t do Percs, baby, but (Take your time) That’s the perks of datin’ me Red Merces with the red seats Buy red wig, part the Red Sea", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake uses homophones to allude to the drug Percocet—which is the brand name for a painkiller that combines oxycodone with acetaminophen—and the financial benefits (perks) that comes with being his partner, resulting to luxury cars, specifically Mercedes.\n\nPlaying with the track’s biblical nature, Drake also references the crossing of the Red Sea depicted in Exodus 14: 19–31, which features one of Judaism’s and Christianity’s most influential prophets, Moses, parting the sea—allowing his people to pass through safely without interference.\n\nDrake uses this to reference his partner entering from a poor lifestyle to a lavish one.\n\n\n\n Pictured: A depiction of Moses parting the Red Sea", "annotation_id": "29724649", "url": "https://genius.com/29724649", "state": "accepted", "votes": 37, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
