{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "Suitcase, I been livin’ out a suitcase", "vault_lines": ["Suitcase, I been livin' out a suitcase"], "meaning": "Could it also be “Living out of a suitcase” in terms of money from a deal he still hasnt gotten done spending yet?", "annotation_id": "4999687", "url": "https://genius.com/4999687", "state": "verified", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "Yeah, she invite me to the telly, keep the blade with me When I go to check a bitch, ain’t no tellin’", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, no tellin', ain't no tellin'", "Hopin' for a check again, ain't no tellin'", "Yeah, she invite me to the telly, keep the blade with me", "When I go to check a bitch, ain't no tellin'", "Yeah, no tellin', man ain't no tellin'", "Ain't no tellin', yeah", "Take time, ain't no tellin'", "Oh my, ain't no tellin'", "Ain't no tellin', yeah, ain't no tellin'"], "meaning": "In pimp culture a blade is where hoes pick up clients. To check a bitch is for a pimp to collect his money from his hoes.", "annotation_id": "4998611", "url": "https://genius.com/4998611", "state": "verified", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "There’s no code of ethics out here Anyone will take shots at you, yeah", "vault_lines": ["There's no code of ethics out here", "Anyone will take shots at you, yeah"], "meaning": "This also might be a nod to Kendrick who mentioned him in the Control verse. Drake & Kendrick were friends, Drake took Kendrick with him during the Club Paradise tour, and also delivered a verse for Kendrick’s GKMC, yet Kendrick ignored any ethics and still mentioned him despite how much Drake helped his career.", "annotation_id": "4995379", "url": "https://genius.com/4995379", "state": "verified", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "Thinkin’ they lions and tigers and bears I go huntin’, put heads on my fireplace, oh my", "vault_lines": ["Thinkin' they lions and tigers and bears", "I go huntin', put heads on my fireplace, oh my"], "meaning": "shortly before drake released this album meek mill put up a picture of a lion on instagram describing his mood after getting with nicki minaj, maybe this is a shot at meek mill cause drake was supposed to be first in line? lol", "annotation_id": "4993614", "url": "https://genius.com/4993614", "state": "verified", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "V-Live, I order that Alfredo pasta Then eat in the kitchen like I’m in the mafia Houston, they get me though", "vault_lines": ["V-Live, I order that Alfredo pasta", "Then eat in the kitchen like I'm in the mafia", "Houston, they get me though"], "meaning": "Yo Drizzy, if you need an Italian cook shoot me a PM, Alfredo pasta is lowkey garbage", "annotation_id": "4983762", "url": "https://genius.com/4983762", "state": "verified", "votes": 36, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "True say, I been goin’ hard, but then again They think I’m soft, think I’m innocent", "vault_lines": ["True say, I been goin' hard, but then again", "They think I'm soft, think I'm innocent"], "meaning": "True Say is also Toronto/Jamaican urban vernacular as an affirmation to let the listener know the speaker means what they said similar to the phrase “Word is Born” used by various New York rappers. In “Deadly Combination (Remix)”, Big L says:\n\nBitches be warned – word is born, you’ll get torn", "annotation_id": "4971370", "url": "https://genius.com/4971370", "state": "verified", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "True say, I been goin’ hard, but then again They think I’m soft, think I’m innocent", "vault_lines": ["True say, I been goin' hard, but then again", "They think I'm soft, think I'm innocent"], "meaning": "By personifying the word TRUE he could be talking about “Two Chains” and people do think he’s soft there’s about a million memes about this if you haven’t seen them then your not on Twitter", "annotation_id": "4962870", "url": "https://genius.com/4962870", "state": "verified", "votes": -3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "Yeah, I stay up late at night, thinkin’ ’bout my life Want a lot, will I get it all? Ain’t no tellin’ Ain’t no tellin’, yeah, ain’t no tellin’ Yeah, no tellin’, ain’t no tellin’", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, no tellin', ain't no tellin'", "Yeah, no tellin', man ain't no tellin'", "Ain't no tellin', yeah", "Take time, ain't no tellin'", "Oh my, ain't no tellin'", "Yeah, I stay up late at night, thinkin' 'bout my life", "Want a lot, will I get it all? Ain't no tellin'", "Ain't no tellin', yeah, ain't no tellin'"], "meaning": "It sounds to me like he says “will I get it all in? No tellin.”", "annotation_id": "4958468", "url": "https://genius.com/4958468", "state": "verified", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "Thinkin’ they lions and tigers and bears I go huntin’, put heads on my fireplace, oh my", "vault_lines": ["Thinkin' they lions and tigers and bears", "I go huntin', put heads on my fireplace, oh my"], "meaning": "A reference to Tyga, and could also be a reference to Puffy/diddy. Puff often posts pics of lions on his instagram. After Drake and Diddy’s alleged altercation outside of a club back in December 2014, Diddy posted a picture of a black panther and wrote “#Fact.”", "annotation_id": "4957803", "url": "https://genius.com/4957803", "state": "verified", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "I took the summer off to get it right Yeah, I gave these boys a shot and they fuckin’ failed Niggas like, “You took the summer off? We couldn’t tell”", "vault_lines": ["I took the summer off to get it right", "Yeah, I gave these boys a shot and they fuckin' failed", "Niggas like, \"You took the summer off? We couldn't tell\""], "meaning": "“Gave those boys a shot” has dual meanings of giving someone a chance and shooting them down. They missed their chance, alternately were felled by Drakes deadly flow.", "annotation_id": "4952035", "url": "https://genius.com/4952035", "state": "verified", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "OVO, Unruly One shot to make it in a life From the Six to the fucking 8-7-6", "vault_lines": ["One shot to make it in a life", "From the Six to the fucking 8-7-6"], "meaning": "This recording can also be heard on an OVO produced video called “6 in the 876”, where Drake’s crew go to Jamaica to get back to their heritage. You can hear the excerpt at 12:51\n\n\n\n\n 6 IN THE 876 from OVONiko on Vimeo.", "annotation_id": "4951720", "url": "https://genius.com/4951720", "state": "verified", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "Okay, I had to switch the flow up on you niggas The shit was gettin’ too predictable, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Okay, I had to switch the flow up on you niggas", "The shit was gettin' too predictable, yeah"], "meaning": "Drizzy’s flow is so dope that it isn’t cutting it anymore. He’s constantly changing up his sound to transcend rap.", "annotation_id": "4951711", "url": "https://genius.com/4951711", "state": "verified", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "Thinkin’ they lions and tigers and bears I go huntin’, put heads on my fireplace, oh my", "vault_lines": ["Thinkin' they lions and tigers and bears", "I go huntin', put heads on my fireplace, oh my"], "meaning": "What a coincidence, ain’t no tellin…", "annotation_id": "4941130", "url": "https://genius.com/4941130", "state": "verified", "votes": 116, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "Yeah, she invite me to the telly, keep the blade with me When I go to check a bitch, ain’t no tellin’", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, no tellin', ain't no tellin'", "Hopin' for a check again, ain't no tellin'", "Yeah, she invite me to the telly, keep the blade with me", "When I go to check a bitch, ain't no tellin'", "Yeah, no tellin', man ain't no tellin'", "Ain't no tellin', yeah", "Take time, ain't no tellin'", "Oh my, ain't no tellin'", "Ain't no tellin', yeah, ain't no tellin'"], "meaning": "Telly = Hotel. Common slang used in Toronto.", "annotation_id": "4937664", "url": "https://genius.com/4937664", "state": "verified", "votes": 81, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "I gotta keep watchin’ for oppers ’Cause anything’s possible, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I gotta keep watchin' for oppers", "'Cause anything's possible, yeah"], "meaning": "I believe this to be about the infamous U.K. sniper, AWP. Those who use this bolt-action rifle are known as AWPers. Hence, the next sentence in which he raps “anyone will take shots at you”.", "annotation_id": "4937334", "url": "https://genius.com/4937334", "state": "verified", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "True say, I been goin’ hard, but then again They think I’m soft, think I’m innocent", "vault_lines": ["True say, I been goin' hard, but then again", "They think I'm soft, think I'm innocent"], "meaning": "People always have something negative to say about Drake. This mainly has to do with the fact that hes ‘lightskined\" and came from a “rich” class and a nice neighborhood.[which he didnt exactly, both his mom and him lived in a middle class home and sometimes they had struggles with money.] They think hes had it all, but in all reality, he started out from the very bottom just like every other amazing rapper. He may not have grown up on the streets, but he had many close friends there.", "annotation_id": "4937318", "url": "https://genius.com/4937318", "state": "verified", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "Niggas think they can come take what I got Let’s be logical, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Niggas think they can come take what I got", "Let's be logical, yeah"], "meaning": "Drake might be referring to Logic here, as Logic’s “I’m Gone” on Under Pressure sounds like Drake’s 2nd half of “Furthest Thing” on NWTS. Logic used to go by Psychological. Also you could compare “Buried alive” on Under Pressure (Drake also has a song called Buried Alive) to “The Motion”.", "annotation_id": "4932894", "url": "https://genius.com/4932894", "state": "verified", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "I gotta keep watchin’ for oppers ’Cause anything’s possible, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I gotta keep watchin' for oppers", "'Cause anything's possible, yeah"], "meaning": "“Ops” is also slang for the police. He’s gotta stay on the lookout because even money can’t get you out of certain trouble. The next line also alludes to recent police involved shootings/deaths (such as Michael Brown), saying anyone, even the police, can take shots at you.", "annotation_id": "4932705", "url": "https://genius.com/4932705", "state": "verified", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "Thinkin’ they lions and tigers and bears I go huntin’, put heads on my fireplace, oh my", "vault_lines": ["Thinkin' they lions and tigers and bears", "I go huntin', put heads on my fireplace, oh my"], "meaning": "There’s also this scene from Wolf Of Wall Street https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EBSRcy8b_Bk", "annotation_id": "4931385", "url": "https://genius.com/4931385", "state": "verified", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "I gotta keep watchin’ for oppers ’Cause anything’s possible, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I gotta keep watchin' for oppers", "'Cause anything's possible, yeah"], "meaning": "Sounds like Abos, not oppos/oppers. Abo means father in Somali (East African language). In the streets, the term used for older men i.e. old heads, OGs, etc.\n\nBut here he clearly means these older men dont operate on code or ethics anymore—‘anyone can take shots at you’.\n\nPlus he fucks with somalis enough to use the term properly.", "annotation_id": "4930702", "url": "https://genius.com/4930702", "state": "verified", "votes": -8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "What’s the word these days? Bunch of niggas chasing after all these women they don’t even know (Wooo!) Buncha’ out of season women fuckin’ off-season niggas To get last season wardrobe (Woo!)", "vault_lines": ["What's the word these days?", "Bunch of niggas chasing after all these women they don't even know (Wooo!)", "Buncha' out of season women fuckin' off-season niggas", "To get last season wardrobe (Woo!)"], "meaning": "Buncha' out of season woman\nFuckin' off-season niggas to get the last SZN wardrobe (WOOO)", "annotation_id": "4927234", "url": "https://genius.com/4927234", "state": "verified", "votes": 13, "second_sense": false, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "I gotta keep watchin’ for oppers ’Cause anything’s possible, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I gotta keep watchin' for oppers", "'Cause anything's possible, yeah"], "meaning": "Drake always has to remain on the lookout for new opportunities (oppers) because since his come up, he knows that anything is possible. “Trynna turn MMs to BBs in this bitch”", "annotation_id": "4926733", "url": "https://genius.com/4926733", "state": "verified", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "[Interlude: Popcaan]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Interlude taken from the short movie “Jungle” released a few days prior to If Your Reading This It’s Too Late.", "annotation_id": "4926230", "url": "https://genius.com/4926230", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "Suitcase, I been livin’ out a suitcase", "vault_lines": ["Suitcase, I been livin' out a suitcase"], "meaning": "This line could be a reference to the song “Suit Case” by Rome Fortune and OG Maco.  That song’s hook is this exact line word for word.", "annotation_id": "4923463", "url": "https://genius.com/4923463", "state": "verified", "votes": -5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "Got the club goin’ up on a Tuesday", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Another theory:\n\n“If it’s done I’ll take the D'usse / Oops, aye, fuck it all you niggas two-faced”\n\nLil Wayne dropped a track called D'usse last year in anticipation of CV. Drake could be suggesting he’s siding with Lil Wayne against Cash Money and Birdman (“all you niggas two-faced”)", "annotation_id": "4916067", "url": "https://genius.com/4916067", "state": "verified", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "Niggas think they can come take what I got Let’s be logical, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Niggas think they can come take what I got", "Let's be logical, yeah"], "meaning": "Drake is in street mode (uses “chiraq” term “oppers” a few lines ago) and could also be speaking in a literal sense,you’ll know your chances of jacking Drake are slim to none when your being logical.", "annotation_id": "4915972", "url": "https://genius.com/4915972", "state": "verified", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "Yeah, I stay up late at night, thinkin’ ’bout my life Want a lot, will I get it all? Ain’t no tellin’ Ain’t no tellin’, yeah, ain’t no tellin’ Yeah, no tellin’, ain’t no tellin’", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, no tellin', ain't no tellin'", "Yeah, no tellin', man ain't no tellin'", "Ain't no tellin', yeah", "Take time, ain't no tellin'", "Oh my, ain't no tellin'", "Yeah, I stay up late at night, thinkin' 'bout my life", "Want a lot, will I get it all? Ain't no tellin'", "Ain't no tellin', yeah, ain't no tellin'"], "meaning": "Drake has come a far way as arguably the best artist of his era, however he still has not accomplished all he has set out to do. According to the theories of Abraham Maslow, this is normal: as Drake reaches self-actualization, performing historic art, he will still always be wanting more. To the extent where he still finds his insomnia getting the best of him as he thinks about what is to come, and humbly accepting he is yet to be satisfied.", "annotation_id": "4914996", "url": "https://genius.com/4914996", "state": "verified", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "I gotta keep watchin’ for oppers ’Cause anything’s possible, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I gotta keep watchin' for oppers", "'Cause anything's possible, yeah"], "meaning": "Drake has to remain on the outlook for enemies/ opposition (oppas) because he acknowledges that anything is possible.", "annotation_id": "4914900", "url": "https://genius.com/4914900", "state": "verified", "votes": 73, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "Thinkin’ they lions and tigers and bears I go huntin’, put heads on my fireplace, oh my", "vault_lines": ["Thinkin' they lions and tigers and bears", "I go huntin', put heads on my fireplace, oh my"], "meaning": "Lions and Tygas and bears, this is vocalising Drakes beef with label mate / ex label mate tyga.", "annotation_id": "4912030", "url": "https://genius.com/4912030", "state": "verified", "votes": 66, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "Niggas think they can come take what I got Let’s be logical, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Niggas think they can come take what I got", "Let's be logical, yeah"], "meaning": "Drake is by far the best rapper in the game right now and these other rappers think they can take the throne from him let’s be honest who is better then drizzy right now? I mean kills everything he’s on.", "annotation_id": "4909363", "url": "https://genius.com/4909363", "state": "verified", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "There’s no code of ethics out here Anyone will take shots at you, yeah", "vault_lines": ["There's no code of ethics out here", "Anyone will take shots at you, yeah"], "meaning": "This is possibly a line referring to his on going beef his with Young Money member Tyga. Drake is talking about how even the people on the same label as you will diss you. There’s no more loyalty in the rap game.", "annotation_id": "4909261", "url": "https://genius.com/4909261", "state": "verified", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "Yeah, she invite me to the telly, keep the blade with me When I go to check a bitch, ain’t no tellin’", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, no tellin', ain't no tellin'", "Hopin' for a check again, ain't no tellin'", "Yeah, she invite me to the telly, keep the blade with me", "When I go to check a bitch, ain't no tellin'", "Yeah, no tellin', man ain't no tellin'", "Ain't no tellin', yeah", "Take time, ain't no tellin'", "Oh my, ain't no tellin'", "Ain't no tellin', yeah, ain't no tellin'"], "meaning": "In “The Resistance,” Drake tells a story of how he was robbed at gunpoint,  a robbery set up by the girl he was dating. Wanting to prevent that from happening again, Drake keeps a knife on him at all times for protection.", "annotation_id": "4899650", "url": "https://genius.com/4899650", "state": "accepted", "votes": 100, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "Okay, I had to switch the flow up on you niggas The shit was gettin’ too predictable, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Okay, I had to switch the flow up on you niggas", "The shit was gettin' too predictable, yeah"], "meaning": "Drake wants to be the one changing the sound rather than to change with the sound. He doesn’t limit himself to only one style because then the listener would know what to expect; Drizzy is always a step ahead.", "annotation_id": "4898387", "url": "https://genius.com/4898387", "state": "accepted", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "Dawg, just bought a island, gotta sail to it", "vault_lines": ["Dawg, just bought a island, gotta sail to it"], "meaning": "Quite the boast, but Drake didn’t really buy an island. He’s being playful because he could buy one if he wanted to. Whenever he chooses to take the summer off he’d just chill at his very own island.\n\nDrake has spent time on the Muskoka Lakes, located North of Toronto. Many wealthy Canadians have purchased Islands in that region and Drake must have considered buying one of his own\n\nDrake’s Island is also the name of an island located in Plymouth Sound, a stretch of water nearby England. The island doesn’t belong to Aubrey, but he often brings it up as if it does when flirting with the ladies.", "annotation_id": "4897881", "url": "https://genius.com/4897881", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "Yeah, I stay up late at night, thinkin’ ’bout my life Want a lot, will I get it all? Ain’t no tellin’ Ain’t no tellin’, yeah, ain’t no tellin’ Yeah, no tellin’, ain’t no tellin’", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, no tellin', ain't no tellin'", "Yeah, no tellin', man ain't no tellin'", "Ain't no tellin', yeah", "Take time, ain't no tellin'", "Oh my, ain't no tellin'", "Yeah, I stay up late at night, thinkin' 'bout my life", "Want a lot, will I get it all? Ain't no tellin'", "Ain't no tellin', yeah, ain't no tellin'"], "meaning": "When Drake philosophizes during night he doesn’t ponder on life’s great mysteries, instead he wonders how much he’ll accomplish. The road ahead is uncertain, but one thing he knows is that he’ll give it his all.", "annotation_id": "4893869", "url": "https://genius.com/4893869", "state": "accepted", "votes": 64, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "I’m just lookin’ in the mirror like I’m really him Man, I’m really him, you just fillin’ in", "vault_lines": ["I'm just lookin' in the mirror like I'm really him", "Man, I'm really him, you just fillin' in"], "meaning": "Drake’s success is so great it’s hard for him to believe it so he gotta look in the mirror to remind himself of who he is. While Drake is here to stay, everyone else are only here temporarily.", "annotation_id": "4893740", "url": "https://genius.com/4893740", "state": "accepted", "votes": 45, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "OVO, Unruly One shot to make it in a life From the Six to the fucking 8-7-6", "vault_lines": ["One shot to make it in a life", "From the Six to the fucking 8-7-6"], "meaning": "The Jamaican voice you hear in the background is Popcaan, an artist that represents Unruly Gang. OVO is Drake’s squad. 416 & 647 are Toronto’s area codes, and 876 is Jamaica’s.", "annotation_id": "4893724", "url": "https://genius.com/4893724", "state": "accepted", "votes": 86, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "V-Live, I order that Alfredo pasta Then eat in the kitchen like I’m in the mafia Houston, they get me though", "vault_lines": ["V-Live, I order that Alfredo pasta", "Then eat in the kitchen like I'm in the mafia", "Houston, they get me though"], "meaning": "V-Live is a famous strip club/restaurant in Houston that Drake has referenced before. Mobsters often use restaurants as their front for their criminal activities. Much like the mafia, Drake can eat in the kitchen of the club where no other regular person would be allowed access.\n\nAlso, J. Prince, the CEO of Houston-based Rap-a-Lot Records, threatened Diddy’s family because of his altercation with Drake. Houston got love for Drizzy.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZCv1T3C6JHc", "annotation_id": "4889542", "url": "https://genius.com/4889542", "state": "accepted", "votes": 50, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "Thinkin’ they lions and tigers and bears I go huntin’, put heads on my fireplace, oh my", "vault_lines": ["Thinkin' they lions and tigers and bears", "I go huntin', put heads on my fireplace, oh my"], "meaning": "“Lions and tigers and bears, oh my!” is a quote by Dorothy from The Wizard of Oz.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NecK4MwOfeI\n\nOther rappers view themselves as forces to be reckoned with, but they are no match to Drake. He’ll hunt them down and hang their heads above his mantle as trophies.\n\n\n\nAlso could be a shot at another Young Money rapper, Tyga.", "annotation_id": "4888860", "url": "https://genius.com/4888860", "state": "accepted", "votes": 128, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "What’s the word these days? Bunch of niggas chasing after all these women they don’t even know (Wooo!) Buncha’ out of season women fuckin’ off-season niggas To get last season wardrobe (Woo!)", "vault_lines": ["What's the word these days?", "Bunch of niggas chasing after all these women they don't even know (Wooo!)", "Buncha' out of season women fuckin' off-season niggas", "To get last season wardrobe (Woo!)"], "meaning": "Using different plays on types of “seasons,” Drizzy calls out unattractive women fucking no names for last year’s clothes.", "annotation_id": "4888656", "url": "https://genius.com/4888656", "state": "accepted", "votes": 58, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "All the rappers that you vouch for Need to get out of the house more, they washed up And even if the team was religious with it I can’t really see another squad tryna’ cross us, nah (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["All the rappers that you vouch for", "Need to get out of the house more, they washed up", "And even if the team was religious with it", "I can't really see another squad tryna' cross us, nah (Woo)"], "meaning": "Drake makes a religious reference to explain how no other crew can go up against the OVO posse; Jesus was infamously nailed to the holy Cross.\n\n\n\nThis line could be a subliminal diss to Ab-soul on TDE who’s album is Ab-soul crucified on the cross. Additionally, this builds off of an interview that Ab-soul did with Montreality speaking about Drake.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/cv-XArspMmA?t=281", "annotation_id": "4888440", "url": "https://genius.com/4888440", "state": "accepted", "votes": 59, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "Yeah, police comin’ ‘round lookin’ for some help On a case they gotta solve, we never help ’em", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, police comin' 'round lookin' for some help", "On a case they gotta solve, we never help 'em"], "meaning": "When 12 rolls around asking questions about Drake’s current crime-solving odyssey, Drizzy and the OVO crew keep quiet because snitches get stitches. This goes along with the theme of the track; there ain’t no tellin'!\n\nBut your shit is like the police askin' us questions nigga, we don’t know shit", "annotation_id": "4888430", "url": "https://genius.com/4888430", "state": "accepted", "votes": 45, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "True say, I been goin’ hard, but then again They think I’m soft, think I’m innocent", "vault_lines": ["True say, I been goin' hard, but then again", "They think I'm soft, think I'm innocent"], "meaning": "Drake has taken a more hard-hitting approach to his music, but people can’t seem to shake off the R&B association. They must not pay much attention.", "annotation_id": "4888234", "url": "https://genius.com/4888234", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "Suitcase, I been livin’ out a suitcase", "vault_lines": ["Suitcase, I been livin' out a suitcase"], "meaning": "To “live out of a suitcase” means you are constantly traveling and never settling in one place. Drake is at a point in his life where’s he’s always on the road.", "annotation_id": "4888181", "url": "https://genius.com/4888181", "state": "accepted", "votes": 36, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "Envelopes comin’ in the mail, let her open ’em Hopin’ for a check again, ain’t no tellin’", "vault_lines": ["Envelopes comin' in the mail, let her open 'em", "Yeah, no tellin', ain't no tellin'", "Hopin' for a check again, ain't no tellin'", "Yeah, no tellin', man ain't no tellin'", "Ain't no tellin', yeah", "Take time, ain't no tellin'", "Oh my, ain't no tellin'", "Ain't no tellin', yeah, ain't no tellin'"], "meaning": "Drake has million dollar checks coming to his 10 million dollar house every week. He lets his girl open the envelope hoping there’s more cash. Now that’s a good life.\n\n\n\nDrake uses “let her open ‘em” as a homophone for “letter opener” – a small knife for opening mail (and possibly the blade being referred to in the next line).\n\nThese lines are also likely a shot at the Cash Money controversy, as Birdman is notorious for not paying those on his label, so there “ain’t no tellin'” if a check will come in the mail for Drake.", "annotation_id": "4888126", "url": "https://genius.com/4888126", "state": "accepted", "votes": 104, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "You pick the casket, I’ll put the nail through it I ain’t gotta do it, but fuck it, somebody gotta do it Hate if someone else did it, fuck, I may as well do it, damn!", "vault_lines": ["You pick the casket, I'll put the nail through it", "I ain't gotta do it, but fuck it, somebody gotta do it", "Hate if someone else did it, fuck, I may as well do it, damn!"], "meaning": "Killing other rappers is inevitable, but being the nice guy that he is, Drake is at least offering you options.", "annotation_id": "4888012", "url": "https://genius.com/4888012", "state": "pending", "votes": 64, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "It’s our year (Aww, yeah) Aww, yeah I mean, besides Ricky Ross, Aubrey the biggest boss here (Huh)", "vault_lines": ["It's our year (Aww, yeah)", "I mean, besides Ricky Ross, Aubrey the biggest boss here (Huh)"], "meaning": "Rick Ross, a close friend of Drake’s, is often referred to by his nickname, The Boss. Drake claims to be the second biggest boss, behind Rozay.\n\nThis line is followed by Ross' signature grunt. Later in the verse, you can also hear Ricky’s “woo!” adlib.\n\nhttps://genius.com/2876786/Rick-ross-sanctified/Ross-grunt", "annotation_id": "4887911", "url": "https://genius.com/4887911", "state": "accepted", "votes": 143, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "Still drinkin’ Henny, if it’s done, I’ll take the D’USSÉ Oops, ayy, fuck it, all you niggas two-faced", "vault_lines": ["Still drinkin' Henny, if it's done, I'll take the D’USSÉ", "Oops, ayy, fuck it, all you niggas two-faced"], "meaning": "Nights fulla Hennessey\nWhen Hov around we switch up to that D'usse\n\nBoth Hennessy and D'usse have developed a strong relevancy in hip hop culture through many name-drops from various rappers.\n\n\n\nDespite Jay’s fatherly words to Drake on “Light Up”, the two went on to have a minor beef.", "annotation_id": "4887851", "url": "https://genius.com/4887851", "state": "accepted", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "Got the club goin’ up on a Tuesday", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drizzy helped ILoveMakonnen tremendously when he hopped on the remix for “Tuesday.”", "annotation_id": "4887822", "url": "https://genius.com/4887822", "state": "accepted", "votes": 89, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Tellin’", "line": "I took the summer off to get it right Yeah, I gave these boys a shot and they fuckin’ failed Niggas like, “You took the summer off? We couldn’t tell”", "vault_lines": ["I took the summer off to get it right", "Yeah, I gave these boys a shot and they fuckin' failed", "Niggas like, \"You took the summer off? We couldn't tell\""], "meaning": "During the Summer of 2014, Drizzy hardly released any music, save for a few features. By keeping quiet, Drake gave other artists a chance to steal the spotlight. Despite the 6 God’s absence, his name was still buzzing. No one could tell he was off his grind til he pointed it out on this track!", "annotation_id": "4887798", "url": "https://genius.com/4887798", "state": "accepted", "votes": 85, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
