{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "40K a night to sleep at the Mark", "vault_lines": ["40K a night to sleep at the Mark"], "meaning": "The Mark Hotel is a high end hotel located in Manhattan, NYC. Supposedly Drake  stayed there for his Apollo Theater show in back in January 2023. It happened to be that he stayed at the $75,000-a-night penthouse there (reportedly the largest and most expensive hotel room in North America.)\n\nDrake happens to be a recurring guest there, he would notably stay at the hotel again in July 2023 where he was seen exiting the establishment wearing a dog mask, to promote the release of his much anticipated album at the time, For All My Dogs.\n\nhttps://filepicker-images.genius.com/b1e282eafe187b4c204a4357f0197f31dfa9eec879af36767ee840783410661b%2Fnna9slugvg", "annotation_id": "37622058", "url": "https://genius.com/37622058", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "We comin’ to tear the what off? Roof They raise your tax, we raise the roof", "vault_lines": ["We comin' to tear the what off? Roof", "They raise your tax, we raise the roof"], "meaning": "Interestingly, another BARK Radio segment also appears at the end of the song “7969 Santa” by Snoop Dogg which precedes the album’s other single, “Slime you out\" by Drake and SZA\n\nThis radio is also referring to the album title “For All The Dogs”", "annotation_id": "34801544", "url": "https://genius.com/34801544", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "Ayy, Sosa, baby", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The lyric “Ayy, Sosa, baby” is a reference to Chief Keef himself, whose real name is Keith Cozart, with “Sosa” being his nickname. In his music, “Sosa” is often used as a term of self-identification and a symbol of his persona in the rap industry.", "annotation_id": "32346181", "url": "https://genius.com/32346181", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "What’s on top of the house? Roof What’s in the top of your mouth? Roof", "vault_lines": ["What's on top of the house? Roof", "What's in the top of your mouth? Roof"], "meaning": "In the first line, “What’s on top of the house? Roof,” it straightforwardly refers to the architectural feature that covers a building. The second line, “What’s in the top of your mouth? Roof,” takes a playful twist by comparing the pronunciation of “roof” to the part of your mouth that’s often referred to as the roof (the hard palate). This creates a pun where “roof” has a dual meaning depending on context.", "annotation_id": "32346111", "url": "https://genius.com/32346111", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "This is the starchild, a.k.a. DJ Pooper Scooper", "vault_lines": ["This is the starchild, a.k.a. DJ Pooper Scooper"], "meaning": "Reference to Lift Yourself by Kanye?", "annotation_id": "31313668", "url": "https://genius.com/31313668", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "Me, my evil twin, we one in the same", "vault_lines": ["Me, my evil twin, we one in the same"], "meaning": "Drake is referring to himself and “Baby M” Mirna Mahrous Habib as evil twins, two of a kind, cut from the same cloth. Something that he has even posted on his IG story.", "annotation_id": "30942882", "url": "https://genius.com/30942882", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "Shout to lil’ Izzy, she work as a stewardess", "vault_lines": ["Shout to lil' Izzy, she work as a stewardess"], "meaning": "lil Izzy is likely referring to air line stewardess Isabel Bonacci. @isabelbonacci on ig.\n\nBonacci has recently been posting herself backstage and in the soundbooth at numerous shows on Drake’s recent “Its all a blur tour.”\n\nIt is not confirmed whether or not Bonacci is a personal stewardess on Air Drake or not, but it can safely be assumed that she is the lil'Izzy that Drake is referring to here.\n\nHer display name on IG is Izzy and her caption is “Probably on a plane” (referring to her job as a stewardess)\n\nDrake even recently posted a picture on his IG story of Bonaccis mother in a T-shirt that she wore to the Toronto it’s all a blur show.", "annotation_id": "30942678", "url": "https://genius.com/30942678", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "In this 6ix side town, a dead end world", "vault_lines": ["In this 6ix side town, a dead end world"], "meaning": "Drake refers to his hometown of Toronto, Canada, which has been awarded the moniker “6,” which represents Toronto’s six boroughs: East York, Etobicoke, North York, Scarborough, Toronto, and York whilst also representing Toronto’s area codes “416” and “647.”", "annotation_id": "29937340", "url": "https://genius.com/29937340", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "What do a dog say? Roof", "vault_lines": ["What do a dog say? Roof"], "meaning": "A dogs “roof” is a sound representation of the sound it makes when it barks. A dog barks for many reasons, including warning, communicating, or showing emotion to others. The repetition of the word “roof” in this outro pays homage to earlier projects by George Clinton, who worked with Snoop Dogg.", "annotation_id": "29881185", "url": "https://genius.com/29881185", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "Shout to lil’ A1 from Foxwell and Jane", "vault_lines": ["Shout to lil' A1 from Foxwell and Jane"], "meaning": "A1 is a Toronto based vintage streetwear company. Drake is believed to have grown up somewhere in the vicinity of Foxwell Street and Jane Street in Toronto.", "annotation_id": "29880421", "url": "https://genius.com/29880421", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "Three Baby M out the shackle and chain", "vault_lines": ["Three Baby M out the shackle and chain"], "meaning": "This is referring to IG model Baby M or known as Mirna Mahrous Habib who faced charges and served four months in jail. Allegedly, Drake payed all her lawyers fees, what he is referring to here.\nShe is mentioned quite a bit throughout FATD and previous Drake songs.\n\nhttps://www.justice.gov/usao-wdok/pr/four-defendants-sentenced-conspiracy-fraudulently-acquire-personal-protective-equipment", "annotation_id": "29806175", "url": "https://genius.com/29806175", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "Them shorties don’t listen to Weeknd", "vault_lines": ["Them shorties don't listen to Weeknd"], "meaning": "Might be a shot at The Weeknd. They’ve both had beef over woman but they’ve postet party pictures of themselves in 2022 on Instagram so it might be a reach.", "annotation_id": "29757170", "url": "https://genius.com/29757170", "state": "pending", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "And they live in a crib with a cheap rent, yeah", "vault_lines": ["And they live in a crib with a cheap rent, yeah"], "meaning": "Because these girls are focused on the party lifestyles and not their career they are forced to live in houses that are inexpensive due to their low income.", "annotation_id": "29748733", "url": "https://genius.com/29748733", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "Used to be a smarty Used to wanna study, now I drop the addy", "vault_lines": ["Used to be a smarty", "Used to wanna study, now she poppin' Addies", "Used to wanna study, now I drop the addy", "Used to wanna study, now I send the addy"], "meaning": "Unlike Sosa’s meaning on the previous chorus, Drake is referring here to dropping the addy in the context of dropping the address for either of a party, which only selected people can get in, or his place, in order to have sex.\nDrakes tells that the girl gave up on her diligence and her education in order to either live a luxury lifestyle and going into his exclusive parties or being with Drake.", "annotation_id": "29748707", "url": "https://genius.com/29748707", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "Shout to Lil’ Palestine, she with the gang", "vault_lines": ["Shout to Lil’ Palestine, she with the gang"], "meaning": "The line refers to fashion model Bella Hadid, who herself is a Palestinian and is an avid advocate for the freedom of the Citizens that are often oppressed by the Israeli government due to historical tensions over territory. The bar is also a subtle diss to Canadian Singer The Weeknd, who has dated Hadid in the past. The line “she with the gang” is a reference to Hadid’s 21st birthday party in 2017 that Drake threw at the Socialista lounge in New York City.", "annotation_id": "29738470", "url": "https://genius.com/29738470", "state": "pending", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "We heavy guys like obese men", "vault_lines": ["We heavy guys like obese men"], "meaning": "Heavy is a word used to describe someone that is dangerous.\n\nDrake is saying that him and his friends are dangerous.\n\n“Obese” is another word for extremely fat or overweight. Obese men which are heavy due to their weight.", "annotation_id": "29738375", "url": "https://genius.com/29738375", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "And they ain’t graduate but they geekin’", "vault_lines": ["And they ain't graduate but they geekin'"], "meaning": "“Geek” is another word for nerd, other words for being someone who is usually knowledgeable of a specific topic but the word is misused, used instead for thinking someone being smart.\n\nGeeking is something you usually say about someone who overly excited, or someone who is using drugs and is tweaking.\n\nDrake is saying that they haven’t gratuated but they are instead using drugs and tweaking out of their mind.", "annotation_id": "29738202", "url": "https://genius.com/29738202", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "Girl, you such a thottie", "vault_lines": ["Girl, you such a thottie", "Girl, you such a thottie, ayy", "Girl, you need a hobby"], "meaning": "Sosa refers to this woman as a “thottie”, well-known slang term that was essentially coined by Chief Keef himself. Effectively working as a synonym for a promiscuous woman.\n\nHe even has a song titled, “Love No Thotties”.", "annotation_id": "29733558", "url": "https://genius.com/29733558", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "Used to be a smarty Used to wanna study, now she poppin’ Addies", "vault_lines": ["Used to be a smarty", "Used to wanna study, now she poppin' Addies"], "meaning": "Chief Keef recognizes the differences in this woman’s past compared to her current situation. Stating that she has swapped out studying/wanting to be smart for partying and taking drugs like Adderall, also referred to as “addies”.", "annotation_id": "29733554", "url": "https://genius.com/29733554", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "Walk-in closet, got more Chrome in than Stark", "vault_lines": ["Walk-in closet, got more Chrome in than Stark"], "meaning": "Drake alludes to renowned fictional character based off of Marvel’s Iron Man and Avengers franchises, Tony Stark, who was a multi-billionaire, founder of the Avengers, however most notably, the CEO of Stark Industries.\n\nIn one of the scenes featured in Iron Man 3, Tony can be literally seen walking into a closet filled with Iron Man suits, most notably being Iron Man Mark II:\n\n\n\n Pictured: Tony Stark walking into an Iron Man-filled wardrobe, with Iron Man Mark II being featured on the left \n\n\nThese lyrics can also be seen as a double entendre, referring to Richard Stark, who’s an American fashion designer and co-founder of American luxury fashion brand Chrome Hearts—a brand Drake has showed his admiration for throughout his rap lyrics and previously collaborated with to design a custom “Chrome Hearts Cullinan.”", "annotation_id": "29731358", "url": "https://genius.com/29731358", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "[Outro: George Clinton]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The Outro is performed by legendary funk artist George Clinton. He infuses more dog-themed radio-style commentary, as does Snoop Dogg and Sade elsewhere on the album.\n\nClinton’s cameo follows a similar style to his appearance on the “G-Funk Intro”, from Snoop’s 1993 debut album, “Doggystyle”.", "annotation_id": "29730890", "url": "https://genius.com/29730890", "state": "pending", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "We coppin’ cars like policemen", "vault_lines": ["We coppin' cars like policemen"], "meaning": "Police are also called cops.\nCoppin' is slang for buying something", "annotation_id": "29730505", "url": "https://genius.com/29730505", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "Girl, you need a hobby", "vault_lines": ["Girl, you such a thottie", "Girl, you such a thottie, ayy", "Girl, you need a hobby"], "meaning": "This woman is losing herself and Drake is using “hobby” as a metaphor for finding her passions and what she really wants to do in life. The line can also be interpreted as a double entendre as it can be heard as “girl you need a hubby”, meaning she needs a husband instead of loving Sosa.", "annotation_id": "29727655", "url": "https://genius.com/29727655", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "And I wish I could dead all the beefin’ And I wish I could dead all the dissin’ deceased friends I wish we could be friends Probably sound like I’m preachin’ The city might sleep in some peace then But it’s not realistic", "vault_lines": ["And I wish I could dead all the beefin'", "And I wish I could dead all the dissin' deceased friends", "I wish we could be friends", "Probably sound like I'm preachin'", "The city might sleep in some peace then", "But it's not realistic"], "meaning": "Drake has faced criticism for not openly supporting local artists in Toronto, but his hesitance can be understood given the complex and historical context.\n\nHe witnessed a deadly gang conflict erupt among close personal friends like Pressa and Smoke Dawg, leading to a spike in Toronto’s homicide rate in 2018 and 2019, surpassing that of New York City. This ongoing conflict has likely claimed the lives of many in his circle.\n\n\n\nDrake expresses a desire to unite the city and end the senseless violence, but he acknowledges the limitations of his influence in controlling all contributing factors. Since his 2017 tour with Smoke Dawg and Pressa, which indirectly played a role in this situation, Drake has rarely publicly endorsed or associated himself with Toronto artists. Nevertheless, he patiently awaits the day the city will be at peace again.", "annotation_id": "29727039", "url": "https://genius.com/29727039", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "I love all y’all niggas the same, I wish this was back in the day, for real", "vault_lines": ["I love all y'all niggas the same, I wish this was back in the day, for real"], "meaning": "Drake makes it clear that despite all these artists beefing he loved them all the same.\n\nDrake reminisces back to a time before all the problems and deaths between the artists, most-likely referring to back in 2017 when he brought both Pressa and Smoke Dawg out to perform on his ‘Boy Meets World Tour.’\n\n\nEven-though Pressa and Smoke Dawg had problems with each-other due to their gang affiliation they seemed to hit it off  while on tour even collaborating on music that will never see an official release.", "annotation_id": "29726833", "url": "https://genius.com/29726833", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "Money on my mind, I’m rackin’ my brain", "vault_lines": ["Money on my mind, I’m rackin' my brain"], "meaning": "To rack means to cause extreme pain, anguish, or distress to. Drake is alluding to how his obsession with making money causes him harm.\nAdditionally, rack is a slang term for money.", "annotation_id": "29726127", "url": "https://genius.com/29726127", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "Doctor’s office was the last time that you niggas even had your name on a chart", "vault_lines": ["Doctor's office was the last time that you niggas even had your name on a chart"], "meaning": "Being a stable presence on the music charts, Drake dismisses his adversaries' relevance in the industry. The line jokingly hints that the only chart his competitors can claim to have their names on is a medical chart, not a music chart where artists measure commercial success. A medical chart is a form containing personal info like a patient’s name.", "annotation_id": "29726086", "url": "https://genius.com/29726086", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "Shout to Machine from the Wood, free 17 from the Jane R.I.P. Smoke, it’s a shame, I’m bumpin’ ’em all in the Range", "vault_lines": ["Shout to Machine from the Wood, free 17 from the Jane", "R.I.P. Smoke, it's a shame, I’m bumpin' 'em all in the Range"], "meaning": "Pressa aka Press Machine is from the Driftwood neighbourhood of Toronto.\n\nDuvy aka 17, is from the south side Jane & Finch neighborhood known as Connections in Toronto. Duvy was arrested for the October 6, 2022 murder of Osman Bangura aka CYB Bangs.\n\nSmoke Dawg is from the Regent Park neighbourhood of Toronto. He was shot and killed on June 30, 2018 by members of the Driftwood Crips while celebrating the Canada Day long weekend at a club in Toronto.\n\n\n\nPressa (left) & Drake (right)\n\n\n\n\nDrake (left) & Smoke Dawg (right)", "annotation_id": "29726057", "url": "https://genius.com/29726057", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "She at all the parties, T’d up with 3Hunna", "vault_lines": ["She at all the partiеs, T'd up with 3Hunna", "And she at all the parties, T'd up with 3Hunna"], "meaning": "A set in the South Side of Englewood, Chicago\n\nChief Keef often refer to it in his songs (and even got a song with the same name – “3hunna”), as it is where he is from and it is the gang he claim and set.", "annotation_id": "29725802", "url": "https://genius.com/29725802", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "Guess it’s time for me to cover the shark", "vault_lines": ["Guess it’s time for me to cover the shark"], "meaning": "Drake is referencing the matching shark tattoo that he and his former love interest Rihanna got in 2016. In 2021, people noticed that Rihanna had her shark covered up.\n\n\n\nDrake considers doing the same as she’s moved on, having had two children with her partner of approximately six years (when this track dropped,) rapper A$AP Rocky.\n\nDrake references Rihanna and Rocky numerous times on this album, including on “Virginia Beach,” “Fear of Heights,” and “Another Late Night.”", "annotation_id": "29725717", "url": "https://genius.com/29725717", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "She just did her body, she in love with Sosa", "vault_lines": ["She just did her body, she in lovе with Sosa", "Showin’ off her body, she in love with Sosa"], "meaning": "Reference to Chief Keef’s song – “Love Sosa”:\n\nThese bitches love Sosa", "annotation_id": "29725153", "url": "https://genius.com/29725153", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "I bought the Rolls just to take it apart", "vault_lines": ["I bought the Rolls just to take it apart"], "meaning": "Rolls is a short term for the luxury car manufacturer Rolls-Royce. Drake commissioned Chrome Hearts to customize a one-of-a-kind Rolls-Royce Cullinan SUV that exudes Gothic style.", "annotation_id": "29725132", "url": "https://genius.com/29725132", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "What’s Babe name? Roof", "vault_lines": ["What's Babe name? Roof"], "meaning": "Reference to the American former-professional baseball player, Babe Ruth.", "annotation_id": "29725109", "url": "https://genius.com/29725109", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "My bitches playin’ PND and them", "vault_lines": ["My bitches playin' PND and them"], "meaning": "PND is another name for fellow Canadian singer, songwriter, and record producer PARTYNEXTDOOR.\n\nPARTYNEXTDOOR is signed with Drake’s ‘OVO Sound’ record label, and has released seven projects so far under the label. Him and Drake have collabed on multiple hit records like ‘Come and See Me’, ‘Recognize’ and ‘With You’. He is also featured on Drake’s 8th studio album ‘For All The Dogs’ on the track ‘Members Only’.", "annotation_id": "29725075", "url": "https://genius.com/29725075", "state": "pending", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "I bought the house just to knock that shit down", "vault_lines": ["I bought the house just to knock that shit down"], "meaning": "Here he is making reference to his Toronto mansion (also known as “The Embassy”), which he built form zero.\nIn 2015, he purchased the two-acre property for $6.7 million and hired Canadian home designer and builder Ferris Rafauli to make his custom home.", "annotation_id": "29725035", "url": "https://genius.com/29725035", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "East End boys and West End girls, yeah East End boys and West End girls, ayy", "vault_lines": ["East End boys and West End girls, yeah", "East End boys and West End girls, ayy"], "meaning": "Interpolates English synth-pop duo Pet Shop Boys' ‘80s hit “West End Girls”.\n\nLondon in the ‘80s was divided (and still is) into the wealthy West End and the more down-at-heel, East End.\n\nThe major entertainment centre of London is based around the West End and boys used to hang around there in the hopes of landing a West End girl in an effort to climb the social ladder.\n\nThrough an Instagram post, the duo has immediately pointed out the fact that Drake did not request permission to sing this nor did he give credit.", "annotation_id": "29724976", "url": "https://genius.com/29724976", "state": "accepted", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "line": "Me and KD ’bout to turn up the art", "vault_lines": ["Me and KD 'bout to turn up the art"], "meaning": "Here Drake is making a reference to Phoenix Suns' forward, Kevin Durant (KD), being listed in the A&R credits of the album For All The Dogs (The art).", "annotation_id": "29724974", "url": "https://genius.com/29724974", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "All The Parties", "status": "done", "targets": 37, "clicked": 37, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-all-the-parties-lyrics", "genius_title": "All The Parties"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "You cannot find no one better than this Tryna do right by you, but we can’t mix, I try", "vault_lines": ["You cannot find no one better than this", "Tryna do right by you, but we can't mix, I try", "'Cause you cannot find no one better than this"], "meaning": "Drake explores the friction between his self-perceived value and his functional inability to maintain a relationship. this is a self-referential callback to his Take Care era themes of romantic incompatibility\n\nThe first line showcases Drake’s trademark braggadocio. By claiming, “You cannot find no one better than this,” he positions himself as the ultimate partner. This high-value ego is a staple of his persona, echoing the “overdosed on confidence” sentiment he famously established on Headlines. However, he immediately pivots to a moment of vulnerability. The phrase “tryna do right by you” serves as a thematic callback to Doing It Wrong, where he laments the difficulty of acting with good intentions when a relationship is failing.\n\nThe admission that they “can’t mix” acts as a metaphor for chemical incompatibility, like oil and water. This is a direct parallel to his later work, specifically Polar Opposites, where he explores how two people can be attracted to each other yet remain fundamentally mismatched. The final, trailing “I try” functions as a defensive plea, shifting the blame from a lack of effort to an inevitable tragedy of circumstance, a recurring trope in his more melancholic tracks like Trust Issues", "annotation_id": "39699898", "url": "https://genius.com/39699898", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "You in the city, you laid up with him While I’m on the road with no one to see", "vault_lines": ["You in the city, you laid up with him", "While I'm on the road with no one to see"], "meaning": "Drake says something similar in “You Broke My Heart”, a track in the Scary Hours edition of the album, when he says “Four months' not a long time but you f*cked somebody you just couldn’t wait.” Both of these lines capture the disloyalty that Drake thinks hometown women show to him while he’s on tour.", "annotation_id": "37830061", "url": "https://genius.com/37830061", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "Since you know I got a soft spot for you, this has turned into a civil war", "vault_lines": ["Since you know I got a soft spot for you, this has turned into a civil war"], "meaning": "A civil war is a war between two groups within the same country. While Drake wants to fight, or go to “war” with this woman (likely baby M), he has a strong fondness for her (a soft spot) and is finding it difficult to fight her. Instead, due to his hesitancy he is at war with himself over deciding what to do, a “civil war” because he is fighting himself.\nAlternatively, he could mean that due to his strong affection for her, any war between them is a civil war, because fighting with her is like fighting against a part of himself.", "annotation_id": "36388389", "url": "https://genius.com/36388389", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "That tale wasn’t much of a fairy Christmas, it wasn’t that merry", "vault_lines": ["That tale wasn't much of a fairy", "Christmas, it wasn't that merry"], "meaning": "Drake contrasts their current toxic love affair detailed in the previous lines with a “fairytale”, a story often with a happy ending or positive message.\n\nAs a result of their on again off again relationship, the Christmas holiday wasn’t happy and joyful as it should be, providing a second contrast to having a “merry” Christmas.", "annotation_id": "36388355", "url": "https://genius.com/36388355", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "And when you layin’ on your stomach, only time I ever wanna get my lick back", "vault_lines": ["And when you layin' on your stomach, only time I ever wanna get my lick back"], "meaning": "Aubrey’s “lick back” line is a clever double entendre. Figuratively, it’s about getting revenge, but literally, it plays on “licking back,” evoking a sense of sexual intimacy, since he talks about Baby M lying on her stomach. The phrase blends the idea of payback with a sensual moment, showing Drakes clever wordplay and zestiness.", "annotation_id": "34163991", "url": "https://genius.com/34163991", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "Ayy, I’m the one that you was wishin’ for when you was married", "vault_lines": ["Ayy, I'm the one that you was wishin' for when you was married", "Ayy, I'm the one that you was wishin' for"], "meaning": "Regardless of being supposedly in a “content” marriage, the girl was still thinking about Drake.\n\nThis may be a reference to his to his iconic 2018 hit Emotionless from his Scorpion album, where he raps\n\nI know a girl happily married ‘til she puts down her phone", "annotation_id": "31623733", "url": "https://genius.com/31623733", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "Takin’ three months off, then fuckin’ again After you said we not fuckin’ again", "vault_lines": ["Takin' three months off, then fuckin' again", "After you said we not fuckin' again"], "meaning": "Drake is referencing his on and off relationship with “Baby M” also known as Mirna Habib.", "annotation_id": "30028734", "url": "https://genius.com/30028734", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "Man enough to not put it in a song For the world to sing along", "vault_lines": ["Man enough to not put it in a song", "For the world to sing along", "Man enough to admit that"], "meaning": "Drake has written several songs in dedication and in reference to”Baby M,” and believes he could’ve addressed directly instead of speaking about it through his music.", "annotation_id": "30028708", "url": "https://genius.com/30028708", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "I can’t picture you with him", "vault_lines": ["I can't picture you with him"], "meaning": "This lyric references Dillon Brooks, who Drake takes several jabs at throughout the album.\n\nDillon Brooks dated “Baby M,” and Drake cannot believe that someone “like” Dillon Brooks is comparable to him. He can’t believe she’d even consider him in comparison to himself, and believes it’s embarrassing.\n\nHe also references this a little in “Hours in Silence” when he says: “Got you ridin’ round with n-ggas that are nothing like me. “", "annotation_id": "30028699", "url": "https://genius.com/30028699", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "Way I’m feelin’ on this album, really took it easy on you, coulda written more", "vault_lines": ["Way I'm feelin' on this album, really took it easy on you, coulda written more"], "meaning": "As you can tell already from the song and many of the other tracks on the album, Drake has a lot to say about this woman.\nHowever, he’s actually saying he’s taking it easy on her because he didn’t write as much as he should have!", "annotation_id": "29891430", "url": "https://genius.com/29891430", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "Steez sayin’ that you miss me and I won’t say it to you, but I miss you more", "vault_lines": ["Steez sayin' that you miss me and I won't say it to you, but I miss you more"], "meaning": "Steez is the nickname of Simon Gebrelul, who is a close friend of drake and a manager for plenty of drake’s friends.\nThe girl keeps checking up on Drake thorugh Steez probably referring to the fact that Drake blocked / ghosted her due to the fact she backstabbed him.", "annotation_id": "29855024", "url": "https://genius.com/29855024", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "Said we got each other back and then you put the knife in it like the kitchen drawer", "vault_lines": ["Said we got each other back and then you put the knife in it like the kitchen drawer"], "meaning": "Nice little double entendre, when one is usually done using utensils, it’s cleaned and put back into the drawer. Clever word play. He’s claiming that despite their previous claims about having each other’s back, she’s still doing him wrong by putting the knife in (in his back/backstabber) it.", "annotation_id": "29825086", "url": "https://genius.com/29825086", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "Don’t make me bring out them racks again Your two best friends are some savages", "vault_lines": ["Don't make me bring out them racks again", "Your two best friends are some savages"], "meaning": "Drake tries to tempt her to not let him throw out racks at her two best friends who work at the Strip Club.\n\nProbably referring to The Strip Club Booby Trap, as he says at the end of the song.", "annotation_id": "29764197", "url": "https://genius.com/29764197", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "Why you act like just ’cause I go to the strip club, girl, that I don’t love you? You still listenin’ to R Kelly in the whip, baby girl, and I don’t judge you", "vault_lines": ["Why you act like just 'cause I go to the strip club, girl, that I don't love you?", "You still listenin' to R Kelly in the whip, baby girl, and I don't judge you"], "meaning": "Drake’s lifestyle of being on tour often includes late nights of clubbing and going to the strip clubs. Just because Drake is with strippers he still has love for his girl, as he’s able to separate lust from true love; just like how his girl is able to separate the art from the artist. She still bumps R. Kelly in the whip even though he has been sentenced to 30 years in prison for child sex crimes. If he doesn’t judge her then he feels as if his love shouldn’t be judged or questioned either.", "annotation_id": "29757055", "url": "https://genius.com/29757055", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "That’s just so embarrassin’ I want to die, to die", "vault_lines": ["That's just so embarrassin'", "I want to diе, to die", "And that's just so embarrassin'", "I want to die, to die"], "meaning": "Drake states on Calling For You, “You fucked on a n*gga I see as my son, so what?” But clearly has conflicting feelings here as he cannot believe this girl he adores is with someone who he views as way inferior. Drake doesn’t care if a smash piece gets with someone below him, which is evident in Calling For You, but we realize here that it hits closer to home when its someone he has love for.", "annotation_id": "29757045", "url": "https://genius.com/29757045", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "In Booby Trap, throwin’ more bills than your baby daddy trap", "vault_lines": ["In Booby Trap, throwin' more bills than your baby daddy trap"], "meaning": "Drake shouts out popular strip-club in Miami, Florida, Booby Trap.\n\n\n\nHe boasts about the amount of money he is throwing in the club, saying that the number surpasses that of this woman’s “baby daddy’s trap”. A slang term essentially pointing towards the total amount of money her baby daddy receives from his hustle.\n\nIt isn’t the first time that Drake mentions Booby Trap strip club in a song, since he mentioned it on his track from his and 21 Savage’s album, “Her Loss” – “Major Distribution”:\n\n Booby Trap, we need a business office\nMagic City need a business office\nTwenty-nine, I keep a business office", "annotation_id": "29735290", "url": "https://genius.com/29735290", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "Act like you need some insurance on it We didn’t get here on accident", "vault_lines": ["Act like you need some insurance on it", "We didn't get here on accident"], "meaning": "Drake is expanding on the process mentioned in the previous line of he and this woman going back and forth repeatedly by likening her tendency to continue to have sex with him over time, to having insurance on their sex life.\n\nHe makes a play on the word accident, as well, clarifying that they are not in their current situation by accident while simultaneously relating it to accident insurance. As she would not want to actually lose Drake.\n\nInsurance – an arrangement providing protection against a possible loss", "annotation_id": "29735142", "url": "https://genius.com/29735142", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "If the shoe was on the other foot and it was me, it woulda been guerilla war", "vault_lines": ["If the shoe was on the other foot and it was me, it woulda been guerilla war"], "meaning": "Guerrilla warfare is a form of unconventional warfare in which small groups of irregular military, such as rebels, partisans, paramilitary personnel or armed civilians including recruited children, use ambushes, sabotage, terrorism, raids, petty warfare or hit-and-run tactics in a rebellion, in a violent conflict, in a war or in a civil war to fight against regular military, police or rival insurgent forces.\n\nDrake mentioned in the beginning of this verse that the women he’s referring to was married, and he’s saying that if the shoe was on the other foot and he was her husband, it would have been a war over her.", "annotation_id": "29734892", "url": "https://genius.com/29734892", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "Mouth dry over twenty that I never bother gettin’ no prescription for", "vault_lines": ["Mouth dry over twenty that I never bother gettin' no prescription for"], "meaning": "Drake referencing his use of stimulant medications for ADHD (Adderal, Vyvanse, Ritalin, etc.), in this case which he does not obtain legally through a prescription. These type of amphetmines are often administered in a 20mg capsule and also known to make one’s mouth dry.", "annotation_id": "29732895", "url": "https://genius.com/29732895", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "Somethin’ is different, not genuine", "vault_lines": ["Somethin' is different, not genuine"], "meaning": "Drake could be referencing Ginuwine’s 2001 R&B track, Differences.", "annotation_id": "29729341", "url": "https://genius.com/29729341", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "I’ma end this shit and let the 40 beat play before I snap", "vault_lines": ["I'ma end this shit and let the 40 beat play before I snap"], "meaning": "Noah “40” Shebib is a known OVO producer, and helped define Drake’s sound with his slow, ambient beats such as this one and jungle", "annotation_id": "29728724", "url": "https://genius.com/29728724", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "It’s fucked up that we was goin’ once and now you’re goin’ twice like a biddin’ war", "vault_lines": ["It's fucked up that we was goin' once and now you're goin' twice like a biddin' war"], "meaning": "In an auction, participants bid money to win the auction item/event. The auctioneer rattles off prices while participants bid until someone bids too much for the other people to compete with. The auctioneer then goes: “going once… going twice… sold.” Hence where the girl Drake sings about “going twice” ties together.", "annotation_id": "29727968", "url": "https://genius.com/29727968", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "How the outsiders know the inside? They was never supposed to get that, nah", "vault_lines": ["How the outsiders know the inside? They was never supposed to get that, nah"], "meaning": "Drake is questioning his girl on how and why the people outside of their relationship got to know the inside of their relationship. The outsiders could potentially be other men getting to know the inside of his girl, the real her, and the details of her and Drake’s relationship.\nDrake is also wondering how his girl could cheat on him, letting other men be inside of his girl’s vagina.\nThis line reminds us of Miguel’s 2012 release “Pussy is Mine”.", "annotation_id": "29726855", "url": "https://genius.com/29726855", "state": "pending", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "In Miami and the owls with me like they just put my ass in Gryffindor", "vault_lines": ["In Miami and the owls with me like they just put my ass in Gryffindor"], "meaning": "“Don’t count your owls before they are delivered.”\n– Albus Dumbledore\n\nDrake is in Miami with his “owls”, i.e. his friends and people on his side. According to ovosound.com some of these people could be PND, dvsn, Majid Jordan, Roy Woods, POPCAAN, BAKA NOT NICE, and Smiley.\nDrake uses “Gryffindor”, from J.K. Rowling’s Harry Potter series, as a simile to describe the feeling of having all his friends around him since there are so many owls. Gryffindor is one of the four Houses of Hogwarts School of Witchcraft and Wizardry.\nStudents who live in Gryffindor are known for “their nerve, chivalry, daring, courage, bravery and determination” (https://pottermore.fandom.com/wiki/Gryffindor#:~:text=Gryffindor%20is%20one%20of%20the,%2C%20courage%2C%20bravery%20and%20determination.). Which can also describe artists signed with OVO Sound label.\n\nIn Rowling’s Harry Potter series owls have many meanings and symbols. Found in “The Harry Potter Lexicon” [o]wls in the wizarding world are regarded both as pets and as the primary method of communication. They are of course used to deliver letters and packages as part of owl post service, but to wizards they mean more than just that. On many occasions Harry thinks of Hedwig as a friend, especially when the two of them are locked into number four, Privet Drive together (OP3). Owning an owl is also something of a status symbol and owls reflect their owners’ wealth; the Weasleys’ owl, Errol, is old and frequently collapses at the ends of journeys (PA1) while the Malfoys have an enormous, handsome eagle owl (PS8) that not even the post office is mentioned as having (PA14). An owl carving is the one hint of the wizarding community on the outside of the Woolworth Building (Pm) (https://www.hp-lexicon.org/creature/birds/owl/).\n\nPROPOSED SUGGESTION: textfull okayable", "annotation_id": "29726297", "url": "https://genius.com/29726297", "state": "pending", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "Movin’ like Snoopy and Charlie Brown Feel like you tryna dog the kid", "vault_lines": ["Movin' like Snoopy and Charlie Brown", "Feel like you tryna dog the kid"], "meaning": "Snoopy is a comic-strip character with a spotted white beagle. As the pet dog of the hapless Peanuts character Charlie Brown, Snoopy became one of the most iconic and beloved characters in the history of comics.", "annotation_id": "29725942", "url": "https://genius.com/29725942", "state": "pending", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "The athlete that you rollin’ with, I saw his game last night, he didn’t score", "vault_lines": ["The athlete that you rollin' with, I saw his game last night, he didn't score"], "meaning": "Multiple digs in this line; Drake claims he watched a sports game the previous night and his girl is now dating one of the players on the team. Too bad for her because the man is a trash player and has no game/ skills. He didn’t even score a point.\n\nOn the other hand, Drake could have seen the athlete and his girl out in public together and she never ended up going home with him/ he didn’t score her number due to his lack of romantic abilities like flirting, making jokes, etc.", "annotation_id": "29725687", "url": "https://genius.com/29725687", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "Artists hittin’ on you, broke as fuck, I swear them niggas probably live in Singapore", "vault_lines": ["Artists hittin' on you, broke as fuck, I swear them niggas probably live in Singapore"], "meaning": "Broke artists do not blow up because they are not good at their job. Drake makes a pun by saying broke artists live in Singapore (sing-a-poor).", "annotation_id": "29725600", "url": "https://genius.com/29725600", "state": "accepted", "votes": 55, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "Waitin’ on you like a backend", "vault_lines": ["Waitin' on you like a backend"], "meaning": "In software development, a backend is the part of the system that delivers content upon request from a frontend (e.g. a web application). The frontend waits for the backend to respond with the content before displaying it.\n\nDrake is waiting for the girl the same way an app waits for a backend.\n\nPROPOSED SUGGESTION: He’s waiting on the girl like a back-end music deal, where royalties are earned based on sales", "annotation_id": "29725260", "url": "https://genius.com/29725260", "state": "pending", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Drew A Picasso", "line": "You a trophy to me like the Larry", "vault_lines": ["You a trophy to me like the Larry"], "meaning": "The Larry O'Brien Trophy is awarded to the winner of the NBA finals", "annotation_id": "29724879", "url": "https://genius.com/29724879", "state": "accepted", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
