{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Thrill Is Gone", "line": "With", "vault_lines": ["Trying to excel with the brake on", "I'll have you stuck in the same spot with the tires burnin'", "And I'm a liar turnin' 19, jaded with no faith", "Some dudes they turn purple with hurt faces, circling workplaces", "When some of the best kicked it with Drake in fact", "I bet that they knew it cause in my mind I play through it with", "Like a mansion with the projects behind it", "I tend to freak with this", "And come up with tin foil", "And you picture that she just slept with me for nothing"], "meaning": "Whole line is missing after this line. Should be:\n\nI bet that they knew it cause in my mind I play through it with\nWith Yoshi Lee and A Lewis a couple things that they true in\nAnd in the end I listen but I don’t see me as they do", "annotation_id": "25557449", "url": "https://genius.com/25557449", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Thrill Is Gone", "line": "That’s why I envy Omar Because so far I’m nowhere close to Malik and Deja And that’s some higher learning", "vault_lines": ["Because so far I'm nowhere close to Malik and Deja", "And that's some higher learning", "That's why I envy Omar"], "meaning": "He is talking about Omar Epps and Tyra Banks. Those two were a couple in the movie called Higher Learning", "annotation_id": "23685839", "url": "https://genius.com/23685839", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Thrill Is Gone", "line": "I met this recent lady She knew a piece of Sadie by Spinners", "vault_lines": ["I met this recent lady", "She knew a piece of Sadie by Spinners"], "meaning": "Drake is noting that they connected based on familiarity with the same music. “Sadie” is a 1974 song by the Atlantic Records group The Spinners.\n\nSpending time with his father in the south, Drake would have heard this song on the radio or on records. Knowing her familiarity with the song, he calls this “recent lady” decent because he assumes she was likely brought up with the same values that he was.", "annotation_id": "11538272", "url": "https://genius.com/11538272", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Thrill Is Gone", "line": "It’s like I’m using some bread to sop up some decent gravy Now I’m out of both and I’ve been thinkin’ of Alisha lately", "vault_lines": ["It's like I'm using some bread to sop up some decent gravy", "Now I'm out of both and I've been thinkin' of Alisha lately"], "meaning": "When it comes to this line drake is referring to the woman he met and the feelings he had for her. Some people use bread to soak up gravy or soup when ever they are about to run out. So in Drake situation he was using the female (bread) to soak up the rest of his feelings (the gravy). Since he ran out of the feelings he had for the female, she left. Since he didn’t have her anymore he drifted back into his feelings for his ex-girlfriend Alisha Phillips.", "annotation_id": "7637511", "url": "https://genius.com/7637511", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Thrill Is Gone", "line": "I guess in my southern eyes that she decent maybe", "vault_lines": ["I guess in my southern eyes that she decent maybe"], "meaning": "He should have been more Southern\n\nConsensual sex isn’t much of a thing in Canada apparently. In actuality, this is a reference to the concept of Southern Hospitality. The “smoothness” of southern people create a sense that a visitor is more welcome in their home.", "annotation_id": "953335", "url": "https://genius.com/953335", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Thrill Is Gone", "line": "They get to first bases Then they get to retreating cause if she cheatin’ He wanna know what the first trace is", "vault_lines": ["They get to first bases", "Then they get to retreating cause if she cheatin'", "He wanna know what the first trace is"], "meaning": "Men get comfortable with women and even start on the sexual baseball game, until they find out about the cheating and start tracing back to see what the first clue of deceit was.", "annotation_id": "220643", "url": "https://genius.com/220643", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
