{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Demons", "line": "Sponsor (Sponsor), I take a Perc, now I’m turned to a monster (Turned to a monster)", "vault_lines": ["Sponsor (Sponsor), I take a Perc, now I'm turned to a monster (Turned to a monster)"], "meaning": "A  perc is short for percocet; Backstory: Percocet is the brand name for a combination of Oxycodone and acetaminophen. Cultural connotations: Percocet has become a favorite reference in Hip-Hop culture, in part because its reputation as a painkiller evokes a DGAF attitude: Pop a Perc, drink some alcohol, get happy, black out.\n\nFivio Foreign is known for doing all kinds of stuff (drug abuse) and claims that he turns into a ‘monster’. Meaning he turns very agressive or in a very ubnormal kind of behavior like at a party or just some standard kind of moment like chilling in his home or even with his fellow associates with the “Woos” or “Big 092MLBOA”.", "annotation_id": "23515549", "url": "https://genius.com/23515549", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Demons", "line": "Mike Amiri, best believe they fitted", "vault_lines": ["Mike Amiri, best believe they fitted"], "meaning": "Mike Amiri is a fashion designer known for his work crafting stage pieces. He has most notably worked with rockers Axl Rose, the lead vocalist for Guns N' Roses, and Steven Tyler, the frontman for Aerosmith.\n\nHe gained prominence in hip hop after creating his own brand in 2014, which has since attracted a celebrity following.\n\n\n\nMike Amiri in his own brand", "annotation_id": "19730191", "url": "https://genius.com/19730191", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Demons", "line": "Like what? (Who made this?) Yeah, yeah (JB made this, hahahaha)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "JB Made It is a UK drill producer based in London. He’s a member of Finesse Foreva, a collection of London based producers that specialize in the UK Drill sound.\n\nUK drill production is commonly used by Brooklyn drill artists, including Fivio Foreign’s June 2019 breakout hit “Big Drip” while Drake has experimented with the UK drill sound on several occasions, one being December 2019’s “War.”", "annotation_id": "19717662", "url": "https://genius.com/19717662", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Demons", "line": "I’m in this bitch with the Wooski", "vault_lines": ["I'm in this bitch with the Wooski"], "meaning": "Wooo (We On Our Own), from Brownsville, and Woo (We One Order) are two affiliated collectives of gang sets from Brooklyn, New York. Though made famous beyond NY by drill artist Pop Smoke, there are many rappers within the Brooklyn drill scene that are associated with the Woo, such as Fivio Foreign, or Wooo, such as Sosa Geek, hence the shoutout provided here.", "annotation_id": "19717632", "url": "https://genius.com/19717632", "state": "accepted", "votes": 70, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Demons", "line": "Skrrt ’round there in your ends, whole southside on ten", "vault_lines": ["Skrrt 'round there in your ends, whole southside on ten"], "meaning": "“Ends'” is a London slang term for a neighborhood. Drake first used the term on his February 2015 song “Used To” when he quoted lyrics from UK artist Skepta’s June 2014 song “That’s Not Me”:\n\nShout out to the G’s from the ends\nWe don’t love no girls from the ends\n\n“Ten”—short for “Ten Toes”—is a London slang term for being on foot and “Southside” refers to the southside of Galloway, an area in Scarborough, Toronto.", "annotation_id": "19717510", "url": "https://genius.com/19717510", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Demons", "line": "If they Woo walk, I probably taught ’em (I did)", "vault_lines": ["If they Woo walk, I probably taught 'em (I did)"], "meaning": "The “wooo walk” is a dance popularized by New York Drill rappers like Pop Smoke, Fetty Luchiano and Sosa Geek. Its name derives from the local “Wooo” gang.\n\nThe dance consists of three moves: sideways heel kicking, alternating steps from toe to heel, followed by an ‘in and out’ singing motion of the legs.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=A1Y0Yi_sOyQ&has_verified=1", "annotation_id": "19717187", "url": "https://genius.com/19717187", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Demons", "line": "That’s how a man get blem, you and your friends", "vault_lines": ["That's how a man get blem, you and your friends"], "meaning": "“Blem” is slang for being high. While it is used in Toronto, it has Jamaican origins. Jamaican communities have adopted slightly different meanings for the word, as it originally meant the blending of marijuana and grabba, a tobacco leaf.\n\nDrake has used on the term on his March 2017 track, “Blem”:\n\nI’m blem for real, I might just say how I feel", "annotation_id": "19717006", "url": "https://genius.com/19717006", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Demons", "line": "Six, six, six, six, six, six", "vault_lines": ["Six, six, six, six, six, six"], "meaning": "Drake uses the number six to refer to his hometown of Toronto, as it refers to the 416 and 647 area codes in the city. For instance, in “0 to 100 / The Catch Up” he raps:\n\nYeah, the 6 ain’t friendly but that’s where I lay up", "annotation_id": "19716948", "url": "https://genius.com/19716948", "state": "pending", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Demons", "line": "Talkin’ Henny, it better be Privilège, ayy Baow, what? It better be Privilège", "vault_lines": ["Talkin' Henny, it better be Privilège, ayy", "It better be Privilège"], "meaning": "Hennesy V.S.O.P (Very Special Old Pale) Privilège is one of Hennessy’s more expensive cognacs, costing around $80/L. As opposed to cheaper blends, Privilège is aged at least four years.", "annotation_id": "19714706", "url": "https://genius.com/19714706", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Demons", "line": "My TD Bank is on what? (What?) My TD Bank is on Kylie (Ayy, ayy)", "vault_lines": ["My TD Bank is on what? (What?)", "My TD Bank is on Kylie (Ayy, ayy)"], "meaning": "The Toronto-Dominion Bank (TD Bank) is a Canadian multinational bank spanning into the United States of America.\n\nDrake compares his bank account to be as opulent as Kylie Jenner, socialite and businesswoman. In 2019, Forbes named Jenner as the youngest billionaire in history at 21 years old. Drake and Jenner have previously been rumored to be romantically linked. While they have been spotted partying together, nothing has come out of the relationship.\n\n\n\nDrake has shouted out his hometown bank before, on Lil Wayne’s 2018 track “Family Feud”:\n\nAyy, tell me if TD Bank is approvin' loans\nI’m thinkin' of payin' Wayne what Universal owes\n\nKylie and her sister Kendall Jenner were also referenced in an unreleased Drake collaboration with Future, titled “20 Hoez”:\n\nReal shit, Kylie Jenner, that’s a side piece\nYeah, I got 20 mothafuckin' Kylies\nNigga, I got 20 damn Kylies\nYeah, I got 20 damn Kendalls (20, ayy)", "annotation_id": "19714590", "url": "https://genius.com/19714590", "state": "accepted", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Demons", "line": "Ball in the summer like Drew League", "vault_lines": ["Ball in the summer like Drew League"], "meaning": "The Drew League is an annual basketball league located in Los Angeles, California that takes place in the summer months of the calendar year. Many NBA players have played and continue to play at The Drew League- some of the players can be seen here.\n\nDrake is ballin' or stunting at a high level off the court like the players at The Drew League are ballin' on the court.", "annotation_id": "19600985", "url": "https://genius.com/19600985", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Demons", "line": "Sosa (Sosa), Fivi (Fivi), lookin’ like KD and Kyrie (I am)", "vault_lines": ["Sosa (Sosa), Fivi (Fivi), lookin' like KD and Kyrie (I am)"], "meaning": "Drake likens Brooklyn’s Sosa Geek and Fivio Foreign to the Brooklyn Nets Kevin Durant and Kyrie Irving. The Nets signed Durant and Irving to four-year contracts in July 2019.", "annotation_id": "19600959", "url": "https://genius.com/19600959", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
