{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I Guess It’s Fuck Me", "line": "And the six upside down, it’s a nine You already know the vibe", "vault_lines": ["And the six upside down, it's a nine", "You already know the vibe"], "meaning": "Reference to Track 2 off Drake’s 2016 album Views, 9, where he raps:\n\nAnd I turn the six upside down, it’s a nine now", "annotation_id": "27073859", "url": "https://genius.com/27073859", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I Guess It’s Fuck Me", "line": "Like that nigga not nice, I don’t know polite", "vault_lines": ["Like that nigga not nicе, I don't know polite"], "meaning": "Drake is making a reference to his fellow Toronto rapper and OVO Sound signee Baka Not Nice.", "annotation_id": "27057849", "url": "https://genius.com/27057849", "state": "pending", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I Guess It’s Fuck Me", "line": "Couldn’t even land in the Hamptons, they didn’t have the stairs for the shit I fly Swear it’s like a metaphor, I can’t even get down from the shit I climb", "vault_lines": ["Couldn't even land in the Hamptons, they didn't have the stairs for the shit I fly", "Swear it's like a metaphor, I can't even get down from the shit I climb", "Can't even get down from the shit I climb"], "meaning": "Drake is talking about the fact that he could not land his Boeing 767 in the East Hampton Airport, as the airport did not have airstairs high enough for his plane, meaning he could not get off the plane.\n\nThis is a metaphor for Drake having progressed too far in life, as he now has a plane so big that he cannot get off it, representing the fact that he cannot fall off from the highs he has reached as an artist.\n\n\n\nDrake has to land his plane in the West Hampton Beach airport whereas most smaller aircraft land in the East Hampton airport", "annotation_id": "27054477", "url": "https://genius.com/27054477", "state": "pending", "votes": 59, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I Guess It’s Fuck Me", "line": "Don’t go hiding again Tired of asking where you been You left so abruptly I guess it’s fuck me Tell me, what did I do wrong? Tell me, what did I do wrong? Tell me, what did I do wrong? Tell me, what did I do wrong? Before it’s over I need you to come over once again And before you give me closure Need you to come a little bit closer", "vault_lines": ["And before you give me closure", "Need you to come a little bit closer", "Don't go hiding again", "Tired of asking where you been", "You left so abruptly", "I guess it's fuck me", "Tell me, what did I do wrong?", "I need you to come over once again"], "meaning": "While this relationship appears to be crumbling, Drake’s tone shows he seeks closure and forgiveness while admitting guilt. This lyric may be reminiscent to some of his songs, such as his 2013 song “Hold on, we’re going home,” in which Drake opens up about missing a specific someone.\n\nI got my eyes on you\nYou’re everything that I see\nI want your hot love and emotion endlessly\nI can’t get over you\nYou left your mark on me\nI want your hot love and emotion endlessly\n\nHe also appears to be ruminating on a failed romance, which could be similar to his 2021 song “Fucking Fans,” which depicts Drake deep in his emotions while acknowledging he’s at fault:\n\nI’m still working on me\nAnd I’m coming back better for you (I’m comin' back, oh-ooh)\nMost times it was my selfishness and\nYour helplessness that I took advantage of\nYou sit in the house and I be out\nAnd I know why you’re worried, uh", "annotation_id": "27053033", "url": "https://genius.com/27053033", "state": "accepted", "votes": 80, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I Guess It’s Fuck Me", "line": "The pain that I seen in my mother’s eyes in 2009", "vault_lines": ["The pain that I seen in my mother's eyes in 2009"], "meaning": "Drake expresses his mother’s worry as he became a conflict of interest as he rose to stardom. He reflects upon trauma such as being robbed at gunpoint in his hometown of Toronto on May 31, 2009. Drake also referenced this incident in his song From Florida With Love off of his fifth mixtape Dark Lane Demo Tapes.", "annotation_id": "27052576", "url": "https://genius.com/27052576", "state": "accepted", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
