{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Star67", "line": "Goddamn, we ain’t even gotta scam", "vault_lines": ["Goddamn, we ain't even gotta scam"], "meaning": "Drake asserts him and his crew can make money and gain success through music instead of resorting to crime like scamming.", "annotation_id": "31651280", "url": "https://genius.com/31651280", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Star67", "line": "Four, five chains, man, the gold gettin’ tangled My nigga Biz said, “The first mill’ gon’ change you” Change for the better, hit it, then dead her That’s my vendetta, keep this shit together, yeah (Bomba rassclaat)", "vault_lines": ["Four, five chains, man, the gold gettin' tangled", "My nigga Biz said, \"The first mill' gon' change you\"", "Change for the better, hit it, then dead her", "That's my vendetta, keep this shit together, yeah (Bomba rassclaat)"], "meaning": "Drakes life is changing for the better, his gold chains are adding up so much they are getting tangled. A “problem” only associated with rich/successful people.\n\n“Biz” possibly Biz Markie advised Drake that the first million you make will change your life. Drake reiterates this and that he’s going to keep going by “hit it” then move on for a prolonged period of time – “vandetta”.", "annotation_id": "26663881", "url": "https://genius.com/26663881", "state": "pending", "votes": -6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
