{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Lucky Lefty", "line": "Ladies, it’s June, July, where all the Cancers is? Show me your hands and shit Even if you ain’t a Cancer, throw up your hands to this ’Cause most of y’all cancerous", "vault_lines": ["Ladies, it's June, July, where all the Cancers is?", "Show me your hands and shit", "Even if you ain't a Cancer, throw up your hands to this", "'Cause most of y'all cancerous"], "meaning": "Cancer is a Zodiac Sign for people born June 21 – July 22 as seen in the picture below.", "annotation_id": "23260435", "url": "https://genius.com/23260435", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Lucky Lefty", "line": "Michael B. Jordan call you right now, you answerin’", "vault_lines": ["Michael B. Jordan call you right now, you answerin'"], "meaning": "Michael B. Jordan is an American actor known to be one of the sexiest celebrities. In 2020, he was named PEOPLE’s Sexiest Man Alive. The lines highlight how many women who claim to be loyal to their partners would drop them if given the chance to date an attractive celebrity, especially one they are a fan of.\n\n\n\nThe lines seem to be a jab at Lori Harvey who is the stepdaughter of well-known comedian Steve Harvey. In January 2021, Harvey and Jordan confirmed they were dating.\n\nThe American model has previously dated artists in the hip-hop industry, including Future and Sean “Diddy” Combs. Drake has previously been featured on a song with Meek Mill, who was  roasted online after the couple became official. In the 2018 “Going Bad” Meek Mill expressions his feeling about the model:\n\nI got Lori Harvey on my wish list\n\nIt makes sense why Drake would make a jab at the new couple, seeing as he is know to be friends with fellow rapper Future and has featured Diddy on a track in this album.", "annotation_id": "21955356", "url": "https://genius.com/21955356", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Lucky Lefty", "line": "They don’t wanna talk mansions, mine look like a campus", "vault_lines": ["They don't wanna talk mansions, mine look like a campus"], "meaning": "This is a reference to his Toronto mansion, dubbed “The Embassy,” which is projected to be worth over 100 million dollars. The house measures around 50,000 square feet with a 3,200 square feet master bedroom, a two story closet, and amenities such as an outside pool and an NBA regular sized indoor court called “The Sanctuary”.", "annotation_id": "21785418", "url": "https://genius.com/21785418", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Lucky Lefty", "line": "This shout goes out to Hov ’cause it’s him and then me For real", "vault_lines": ["This shout goes out to Hov 'cause it's him and then me"], "meaning": "Lucky Lefty used to be Jay Z’s (Hov) nickname. Drake is saying that Jay is the greatest of all time but he’s right behind him.\n\nEven though on Gyalchester he previously said “I know I said top five, but I’m top two, and I’m not two” here he seems to be claiming that second spot.", "annotation_id": "21783556", "url": "https://genius.com/21783556", "state": "pending", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Lucky Lefty", "line": "“Oh, you fancy, huh?”", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Interpolates one of Drake’s first big songs from 2010, “Fancy”.", "annotation_id": "21783513", "url": "https://genius.com/21783513", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Lucky Lefty", "line": "I’ll leave you red-shirted like the twins from Kansas", "vault_lines": ["I'll leave you red-shirted like the twins from Kansas"], "meaning": "“The twins from Kansas” is a reference to former Kansas University women’s basketball team, Dylan and Dakota Gonzalez, also known as the Gonzalez twins.\n\nA “Red-shirt” freshman is college student-athlete who sits out of gameplay during their freshman year to cheat the four year period rule of participation in college athletics. Drake is being figurative here, saying he’ll keep you from being in the game. He may also be implying that he’d shoot his enemies, leaving them with blood-stained shirts hence “red-shirted.”\n\nDrake had previously attended a women’s college basketball game between Pepperdine and University of Nevada, Las Vegas to support the Gonzalez twins, who played for UNLV at the time.\n\n\n\n  Dylan and Dakota Gonzalez", "annotation_id": "21783497", "url": "https://genius.com/21783497", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Lucky Lefty", "line": "Now I gotta tell you how lucky I am", "vault_lines": ["Now I gotta tell you how lucky I am"], "meaning": "Drake says this as the sample begins in reference to the title / content of the song being sampled, The Isley Brothers‘ “How Lucky I Am.”", "annotation_id": "21783463", "url": "https://genius.com/21783463", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
