{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Company", "line": "Bitch so bad could’ve thought I owed her somethin’ by the way I broke her off (Broke her off)", "vault_lines": ["Bitch so bad could've thought I owed her somethin' by the way I broke her off (Broke her off)"], "meaning": "Travis is playing on the two meanings of “broke her off.”\nFinancially, it means giving someone a cut or share of money, so “owed her somethin’” makes it sound like Travis was paying off a debt.\nSexually, “broke her off” means satisfying her sexually. Travis deliberately connects the two meanings: the way he “broke her off” was so generous you’d think he literally owed her.", "annotation_id": "41429628", "url": "https://genius.com/41429628", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Company", "line": "And lately we’ve been fightin’ on some “Why you love the strippers?” shit", "vault_lines": ["And lately we've been fightin' on some \"Why you love the strippers?\" shit"], "meaning": "This lyric goes both ways, as many couples argue over both stripping and watching stripping. If taken as “Stripping,” rather than “strippers,” Drake could be suggesting hes upset that his girlfriend or side chic is genuinely in love with stripping, as it could be seen as a red flag. On the other hand, Drakes girl/side chic could be mad that Drake is in love with watching strippers, and making his girl feel insignificant.", "annotation_id": "31066677", "url": "https://genius.com/31066677", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Company", "line": "It’s kinda lit right now that you’re here right now", "vault_lines": ["It's kinda lit right now that you're here right now"], "meaning": "Travis is excited that this girl is with him in the club\n“Lit” is when something is popping or exciting", "annotation_id": "28453703", "url": "https://genius.com/28453703", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Company", "line": "So let’s go find a place that we can sip right now", "vault_lines": ["So let's go find a place that we can sip right now"], "meaning": "Following off his previous line of “it’s a couple faces in here that a nigga piped down” Travis wants to find a secluded place to “sip” with this girl. They may be sipping lean or in taking alcohol. Needless to say Travis wants intimate time with this girl rather than be around former sexual partners of his", "annotation_id": "28453687", "url": "https://genius.com/28453687", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Company", "line": "Oh, me, I don’t deserve it (At least you fuckin’ know it) She’s just a little too perfect, she’s just a little too worth it I don’t deserve her at all, no, not at all I only text her, man, I never call I’m still a canine at heart, I’m a dog", "vault_lines": ["Oh, me, I don't deserve it (At least you fuckin' know it)", "She's just a little too perfect, she's just a little too worth it", "I don't deserve her at all, no, not at all", "I only text her, man, I never call", "I'm still a canine at heart, I'm a dog"], "meaning": "She knows she’s too good for him and hearing her voice likely hurts him or brings pain of some kind.", "annotation_id": "28339941", "url": "https://genius.com/28339941", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Company", "line": "I know a girl I should propose to, but we just on some different shit She on some up at 9 A.M. already cookin’ in the kitchen shit", "vault_lines": ["I know a girl I should propose to, but we just on some different shit", "She on some up at 9 A.M. already cookin' in the kitchen shit"], "meaning": "This is a classic right person, wrong time. Drake knows this girl is a true keeper, and he knows that he should lock her down, but he can’t. He’s too deep into the lifestyle that he’s been living the past 7-8 years. He’s still making appearances at clubs and performing at shows but this girl seems to have a very stable life always waking up at 9AM and cooking breakfast. Their lifestyles are simply too different for it to work.", "annotation_id": "28316513", "url": "https://genius.com/28316513", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Company", "line": "I need you to take my mind off being in my prime, some company", "vault_lines": ["I need some company, I need some company", "I need you to take my mind off being in my prime, some company"], "meaning": "Drake is trying to tell everybody that having fame can be depressing, and exhausting.\n\nDrake has been in his prime since 2009, since he dropped his 3rd mixtape “So Far Gone”", "annotation_id": "24978428", "url": "https://genius.com/24978428", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Company", "line": "It’s a couple faces in here that a nigga piped down", "vault_lines": ["It's a couple faces in here that a nigga piped down"], "meaning": "to “pipe” or “piping” refers to the act of a male having sexual intercourse with a female. Travis refers to there being a few females in the venue/club that he recognizes because he has had sexual intercourse with them in the past.", "annotation_id": "24670833", "url": "https://genius.com/24670833", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Company", "line": "Yeah, she workin’ with the spatula, I know she love flippin’ shit, oh", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, she workin' with the spatula, I know she love flippin' shit, oh"], "meaning": "Spatula is a broad, flat, flexible blade used to mix, spread and lift material including foods, drugs, plaster and paints. In a previous line, Drake mentions that the female is up at 9AM cooking in the kitchen, likely making breakfast. Many breakfast foods such as eggs or pancakes require the use of a spatula when preparing, therefore it’s likely that she is using a spatula for whatever she is cooking.", "annotation_id": "24670743", "url": "https://genius.com/24670743", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Company", "line": "I’m posted at the Derek up on Westheimer, hit me when you’re done your shift, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I'm at the St. Regis up on Briar Oaks, hit me when you done your shift", "I'm posted at the Derek up on Westheimer, hit me when you're done your shift, yeah"], "meaning": "This is a famous hotel in Houston, TX. This is drakes second reference to a hotel in the city, in this song", "annotation_id": "21100795", "url": "https://genius.com/21100795", "state": "pending", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Company", "line": "Drank so long, for a year I didn’t cough (Cough)", "vault_lines": ["Drank so long, for a year I didn't cough (Cough)"], "meaning": "“[Purple] drank”, also known as lean, is a recreational mixture of codeine-based cough syrup and soda, typically Sprite. It’s used for its sedative and euphoric effects, but is also highly addictive and dangerous. Trav humorously states that he hasn’t coughed in a year due to the amount of cough syrup he’s consumed via lean, playing on the idea that the cough-suppressing properties of the syrup have prevented him from coughing for an extended period.", "annotation_id": "21030520", "url": "https://genius.com/21030520", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Company", "line": "I’m at the St. Regis up on Briar Oaks, hit me when you done your shift", "vault_lines": ["I'm at the St. Regis up on Briar Oaks, hit me when you done your shift", "I'm posted at the Derek up on Westheimer, hit me when you're done your shift, yeah"], "meaning": "The St. Regis Houston is a luxury 5-star hotel on Briar Oaks Ln, found in a wealthy area of Uptown Houston.\n\nDrake is telling the woman in question to pay him a visit at this location after she has finished working her shift.", "annotation_id": "20390107", "url": "https://genius.com/20390107", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Company", "line": "Is you single or what? I need a girl from the country", "vault_lines": ["Is you single or what? I need a girl from the country", "I need a girl from Kentucky, I need a shawty from Houston"], "meaning": "Drake doesn’t want to waste time and money on a girl who’s already cuffed; he uses this line to give the girl the opportunity to quickly put her man in the past and leave with him.\n\nDrake, although not as potent with women who have dated other rappers as Lil Wayne is, has had his fair share of women with baggage, most famously being linked to Rihanna, which caused a few issues with Chris Brown.", "annotation_id": "4891896", "url": "https://genius.com/4891896", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Company", "line": "Saturday nights, off in my bed right now Call up your girl to put them heels on It’s gettin’ rowdy, rowdy right now (Yeah) I’m on a Mo City trip, I’m a dog (Ooh)", "vault_lines": ["I'm a dog, I'm in heat, baby, heat, baby", "I'm a dog, I'm in heat, baby", "I'm a dog, I'm a dog, I'm in heat, baby", "Mo City trip, Mo City trip right now", "Yeah, I'm on a Mo City trip, I'm on a Mo City trip right now", "Ayy, ayy, a Mo City trip right now", "Mo City trip, I'm on a Mo City right now", "Saturday nights, off in my bed right now", "Call up your girl to put them heels on", "It's gettin' rowdy, rowdy right now (Yeah)", "I'm on a Mo City trip, I'm a dog (Ooh)", "Mo City trip right now, Mo City trip right now", "Mo City trip right now"], "meaning": "Travi$ brags how when he’s bored on a typical Saturday he can just hit up your girl for a booty call. Heels and all son! Mo city’s a reference to Missouri city in Texas, where Travi$ is from.\n\nHe references the previous line to explain that he and the girl he has chosen for the night are on drugs, hence their trip, as well as them cruising around his home town.", "annotation_id": "4891579", "url": "https://genius.com/4891579", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Company", "line": "Pop a couple Percs, let’s get it in right now", "vault_lines": ["Pop a couple Percs, let's get it in right now"], "meaning": "Percocet is a popular prescription pill containing Oxycodone/Acetaminophen. Popping a couple of these along with lean will definitely get you faded.", "annotation_id": "4889938", "url": "https://genius.com/4889938", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Company", "line": "Gotta come through quick, quick Oh, you at the club cashin’ out with Eric, damn, hit me when you done your shift", "vault_lines": ["Gotta come through quick, quick", "Oh, you at the club cashin' out with Eric, damn, hit me when you done your shift", "Yeah, that's why you gotta come through quick, quick"], "meaning": "The ‘Eric’ Drizzy is referring to is DJ Eric, a popular DJ in Houston who also spins for H-Town legend Z-Ro. DJ Eric is also the main DJ at V-Live. An infamous Houston strip club that Drake has referenced before in songs such as Lil Wayne’s “Believe Me”. “Cashin out with Eric” means this female stripper is paying the DJ his tip out so she can get off work & come to the hotel where Drake’s at.", "annotation_id": "4889786", "url": "https://genius.com/4889786", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Company", "line": "I’m a dog (Woo), I go ham, I’m a hog (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["I'm a dog (Woo), I go ham, I'm a hog (Woo)"], "meaning": "Note the palindrome: “Go ham, I’m a hog” spelled backwards is “Go ham, I’m a hog.” Clever wordplay.", "annotation_id": "4889084", "url": "https://genius.com/4889084", "state": "accepted", "votes": 96, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Company", "line": "Do you mind if we just menage just a little? Yeah (La Flame, woo)", "vault_lines": ["Do you mind if we just menage just a little? Yeah (La Flame, woo)"], "meaning": "“Menage” or “ménage à trois” is french for a “household of three” in which all members participate in a love/sexual relationship. Doing it “just a little” could imply a threesome.", "annotation_id": "4888809", "url": "https://genius.com/4888809", "state": "accepted", "votes": 71, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Company", "line": "I need a girl from Kentucky, I need a shawty from Houston", "vault_lines": ["Is you single or what? I need a girl from the country", "I need a girl from Kentucky, I need a shawty from Houston"], "meaning": "Drake is a big fan of Kentucky – both the basketball team and the girls. Unfortunately, the Wildcats issued a cease and desist letter to prevent him from interacting with potential recruits.\n\nHouston isn’t necessarily the “country,” but it’s one of Aubrey’s favorite Southern cities. One of Drake’s original hits, “Houstatlantavegas” shouts out Houston as a spot for nightlife and beautiful women. Houston is also the hometown of Travis Scott.", "annotation_id": "4888565", "url": "https://genius.com/4888565", "state": "accepted", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Company", "line": "Someone that’s so proud to be with me She walk right up to her ex, look him dead in the face And say, ”You ain’t got the juice like that (Woo) You ain’t got the juice like that” That’s cold, ice cold, girl, you ain’t have to do him like that (Like that) Why you had to do him like that? (Like that)", "vault_lines": ["Someone that's so proud to be with me", "She walk right up to her ex, look him dead in the face", "And say, \"You ain't got the juice like that (Woo)", "You ain't got the juice like that\"", "That's cold, ice cold, girl, you ain't have to do him like that (Like that)", "Why you had to do him like that? (Like that)"], "meaning": "Every guy wants a woman who’s not ashamed to be with him and has no qualms about defending him to her ex. In Drake’s case, his new girl didn’t hesitate to inform her old flame about his inadequate juice – whether that’s his sex drive or ejaculate, we’ll never know.\n\nIn the movie Juice featuring Tupac Shakur, a character says “You got no juice.” The juice represented respect and authority, something this girl’s ex no longer has.", "annotation_id": "4888518", "url": "https://genius.com/4888518", "state": "accepted", "votes": 158, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Company", "line": "Mo City trip, Mo City trip right now Yeah, I’m on a Mo City trip, I’m on a Mo City trip right now Ayy, ayy, a Mo City trip right now Mo City trip, I’m on a Mo City right now", "vault_lines": ["Mo City trip, Mo City trip right now", "Yeah, I'm on a Mo City trip, I'm on a Mo City trip right now", "Ayy, ayy, a Mo City trip right now", "Mo City trip, I'm on a Mo City right now", "I'm on a Mo City trip, I'm a dog (Ooh)", "Mo City trip right now, Mo City trip right now", "Mo City trip right now"], "meaning": "As we learned in Z-Ro’s “Mo City Don Freestyle,” “Mo City” is Missouri City – a city just southwest of Houston.\n\nTravi$ is a native of Mo City.", "annotation_id": "4887930", "url": "https://genius.com/4887930", "state": "accepted", "votes": 228, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
