{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Make Me Proud", "line": "Can’t you tell by how they looking at you everywhere you go?", "vault_lines": ["Can't you tell by how they looking at you everywhere you go?"], "meaning": "Yeah", "annotation_id": "40303467", "url": "https://genius.com/40303467", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": false, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Make Me Proud", "line": "And I love it when your hair still wet ’cause you just took a shower", "vault_lines": ["And I love it when your hair still wet 'cause you just took a shower"], "meaning": "Drake loves when a girl lays on his bed with her wet ass hair and ruins his pillow. Not sure why he loves this, I can’t fucking stand it but to each their own.", "annotation_id": "29315568", "url": "https://genius.com/29315568", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Make Me Proud", "line": "And my shit’s so wet, you gotta paddle in", "vault_lines": ["And my shit's so wet, you gotta paddle in"], "meaning": "Double Entendre\n\n1.) The obvious meaning\n\n2.) ‘Shit’s so’ sounds like Shih-Tzu (a dog). Dogs are known to be natural swimmers", "annotation_id": "29008268", "url": "https://genius.com/29008268", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Make Me Proud", "line": "Done did the pop tour, I’m the realest still", "vault_lines": ["Done did the pop tour, I'm the realest still"], "meaning": "Nicki talks about how she is still the realest in the rap game, despite doing a full pop tour.\n\nAdditionally, ‘still’ is a homophone for ‘steel’, so she is essentially saying that she still goes as hard as steel.", "annotation_id": "29008251", "url": "https://genius.com/29008251", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Make Me Proud", "line": "I wonder why the moon looks nice, girl Maybe it’s just right for the night You said niggas coming on too strong, girl They want you in they life as a wife That’s why you wanna have no sex, why you wanna protest Why you wanna fight for your right ’Cause you don’t love them boys Pussy run everything, fuck that noise", "vault_lines": ["I wonder why the moon looks nice, girl", "Maybe it's just right for the night", "You said niggas coming on too strong, girl", "They want you in they life as a wife", "That's why you wanna have no sex, why you wanna protest", "Why you wanna fight for your right", "'Cause you don't love them boys", "Pussy run everything, fuck that noise", "That's why you're bad as fuck and you—"], "meaning": "We can tell this woman is a feminist. Drake uses words like “protest”, “no sex” “fight for your right”, just a few words we hear in the feminist movement today. Throughout the song he’s praising her…. and defending her against the other men who want her too. she’s valuable to Drake and she knows her worth…\n\n“cause you don’t love them boys”\n“they want you in they life as a wife”\n“you said niggas coming on too strong, girl”", "annotation_id": "26006551", "url": "https://genius.com/26006551", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Make Me Proud", "line": "Might’ve been a time where I loved her too But you take that away and you’ve always been the one, one", "vault_lines": ["Might've been a time where I loved her too", "But you take that away and you've always been the one, one"], "meaning": "Though Drake may have had serious feelings for another woman before meeting the woman he is currently involved with, she makes it seem as though they were always destined to be together.\n\nDrake plays on the homophones too and two to make a mathematical play on words:\n\nMight’ve been a time when I loved her too\nBut you take that away and you’ve always been the one\n\n2 – 1 = 1", "annotation_id": "15574831", "url": "https://genius.com/15574831", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Make Me Proud", "line": "I like a woman with a future and a past A little attitude problem all good, it’ll make the shit last", "vault_lines": ["I like a woman with a future and a past", "A little attitude problem all good, it'll make the shit last"], "meaning": "Drake’s ideal woman has lived a life and has a lot of living left to do. The reference to her “past” is likely an innuendo implying sexual experience, which is explored in more detail on “Practice” later in the album.\n\nOne’s past is symbolically associated with being behind them, while the future is associated with being ahead. Therefore, “a woman with a future and a past” is also a double entendre about a woman with a notable bust and behind.", "annotation_id": "15574806", "url": "https://genius.com/15574806", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Make Me Proud", "line": "The best legal team, so the deals is ill It’s MAC, OPI, and a fragrance too Apparel, I’m dominatin’ every avenue", "vault_lines": ["The best legal team, so the deals is ill", "It's MAC, OPI, and a fragrance too", "Apparel, I'm dominatin' every avenue", "I'm so, I'm so, I'm so, I'm so—"], "meaning": "Nicki’s taking over every business venture she can. She has a deal with MAC Cosmetics. She has her own nail polishes, and is working on a fragrance and clothing line. She’s dominating every avenue, especially 5th Avenue, New York’s fashion district.\n\nNicki was “dominating every avenue” as she was the most popular Halloween costume that year.\n\n\n\nHer lipstick!", "annotation_id": "402693", "url": "https://genius.com/402693", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Make Me Proud", "line": "‘Cause I’m fl-fl-fly, I’m flyin’ high", "vault_lines": ["'Cause I'm fl-fl-fly, I'm flyin' high"], "meaning": "There is a reference to flying, or being fly, in almost every verse she does.\n\nA reference to her song “Fly” from Pink Friday.", "annotation_id": "398181", "url": "https://genius.com/398181", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Make Me Proud", "line": "He asked my sign, I said a Sag’", "vault_lines": ["He asked my sign, I said a Sag'"], "meaning": "Nicki was born on December 8, making her a Sagittarius. Jay also says he’s a Sag in Already Home.", "annotation_id": "397213", "url": "https://genius.com/397213", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Make Me Proud", "line": "Sound so smart like you graduated college Like you went to Yale, but you probably went to Howard, knowing you", "vault_lines": ["Sound so smart like you graduated college", "Like you went to Yale, but you probably went to Howard, knowing you"], "meaning": "Yale is an Ivy League school and Howard is a very prestigious HBCU (historically black college or university). So she is both intelligent and a proud black woman.\n\nDrake has shown love for educated girls before:\n\nAll my exes live in Texas like I’m George Strait\nOr they go to Georgia State…\"", "annotation_id": "397207", "url": "https://genius.com/397207", "state": "accepted", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Make Me Proud", "line": "Double-D up, hoes, Dolly Parton", "vault_lines": ["Double-D up, hoes, Dolly Parton"], "meaning": "In basketball, “D up” means to put heavy defensive pressure on the team with the ball.\n\nThe country singer Dolly Parton also has “double-Ds” (size 40DD to be specific).", "annotation_id": "397178", "url": "https://genius.com/397178", "state": "accepted", "votes": 65, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Make Me Proud", "line": "I’m a star, sheriff badge", "vault_lines": ["I'm a star, sheriff badge"], "meaning": "Nicki is a six-point star (better than a regular, five-point star). Meaning she’s a mega-celebrity.\n\nEither that or she’s Jewish (like Drake)\n\n\n\nAlso catch the connection to the previous line – Sagittarius as well as the other Zodiac signs are also called star signs and are based on constellations.\n\nNote Nicki’s un-ironic use of the Supa Dupa flow, something that Drake avoids on this record with one pointed exception\n\nAnd if you’re all into the idea that this song is about Nicki, look here, where Drake also talks about bringing girls home to Mom:\n\nThe most intense thing I’ve ever done was bring a girl to Passover dinner. [My mom] just wants me to be happy, but I’m sure she’d love it if I married a Jewish girl.\"\n\nVery possibly one of the worst lines of all time.", "annotation_id": "397176", "url": "https://genius.com/397176", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Make Me Proud", "status": "done", "targets": 13, "clicked": 13, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-make-me-proud-lyrics", "genius_title": "Make Me Proud"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Spin Bout U", "line": "Smoke a nigga top for you, baby girl", "vault_lines": ["Smoke a nigga top for you, baby girl"], "meaning": "he’d kill for her and or kill anybody for her and do anything of the above.\n\n‘smoke’ is a term used for violence and or murdering someone, example:\n\n“i’ll smoke you out!”\nor just like his other song with SZA, “Slime You Out,”\n\nto ‘slime out’ someone, it’s the same as violence and killing someone, or as a threat.", "annotation_id": "40542848", "url": "https://genius.com/40542848", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
