{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Astalavista (2025)", "line": "I might start posting all of my publishing checks just like Russ", "vault_lines": ["I might start posting all of my publishing checks just like Russ"], "meaning": "Independent rapper Russ frequently shares his massive six-figure TuneCore distribution and publishing payouts—often totaling around $100,000+ per week—to prove that artists can achieve massive financial success and retain 100% of their rights without signing away percentages to major labels.", "annotation_id": "40792673", "url": "https://genius.com/40792673", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Astalavista (2025)", "line": "They called it a L, but it’s looking like a whole lot of M’s And they know my body, like it makes no sense to size up", "vault_lines": ["They called it a L, but it’s looking like a whole lot of M’s", "And they know my body, like it makes no sense to size up"], "meaning": "Double entendre:\n\n\nThey called his fued with Kendrick an L, but despite that he’s still enormously paid, and people still know not to pick a fight, or “size up” with him\nThe size Large (L) is the ‘size up’ from Medium (M) on clothing.", "annotation_id": "40792644", "url": "https://genius.com/40792644", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Astalavista (2025)", "line": "When they said they bought out the charts, they meant this shit, huh", "vault_lines": ["When they said they bought out the charts, they meant this shit, huh"], "meaning": "Slight reach, but could be a diss towards how multiple artists in recent times have been accused of using bots to boost their streams, effectively “buying the charts.” He makes many references to that as well in ICEMAN", "annotation_id": "40792623", "url": "https://genius.com/40792623", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Astalavista (2025)", "line": "I gotta choose my vice like election night, huh", "vault_lines": ["I gotta choose my vice like election night, huh"], "meaning": "It’s a homophone, with “vice” sounding identical to “vice” in Vice President.\n\nOn election night, Americans are choosing who will become the Vice President alongside the President. At the same time, Drake is using the more common meaning of vice—a personal weakness, temptation, or indulgence (such as women, alcohol, gambling, etc.).\n\nIn other words, he’s saying he has to decide which temptation he’s going to give in to, while cleverly comparing that decision to voters choosing a Vice President on election night.", "annotation_id": "40446583", "url": "https://genius.com/40446583", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Astalavista (2025)", "line": "Hoes thirsty for me, like electrolytes", "vault_lines": ["Hoes thirsty for me, like electrolytes"], "meaning": "The first bar is a straightforward simile. Drake says women are “thirsty” for him. He compares that to electrolytes, which your body craves when you’re dehydrated or thirsty, making the comparison fit literally and figuratively.", "annotation_id": "40446579", "url": "https://genius.com/40446579", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Astalavista (2025)", "line": "Last year showed me what rejection’s like, huh Saw Meek’s face in the reflection It flashed in the mirror for a quick second Guess I know what his stress was like, huh", "vault_lines": ["Last year showed me what rejection's like, huh", "Saw Meek’s face in the reflection", "It flashed in the mirror for a quick second", "Guess I know what his stress was like, huh"], "meaning": "Drake is once again referring to the feud between himself and Kendrick Lamar and comparing it, in a sense, to when Drake battled Meek Mill.\n\nBack in 2015, Meek Mill had accused Drake of having ghostwriters and the feud developed from there. It wasn’t much for a discussion as everyone thought Drake was the clear winner.\n\nSo when people started to believe that Kendrick was winning, Drake could relate for a split second to the feeling Meek once had in 2015", "annotation_id": "40446472", "url": "https://genius.com/40446472", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Astalavista (2025)", "line": "It’s usually on them So I feel like for once, they was hype to have me jammed up", "vault_lines": ["It’s usually on them", "So I feel like for once, they was hype to have me jammed up"], "meaning": "In the past and other instances, Drake is usually on the “winning” side of his battles. There was a lot of discussion over the Drake/Kendrick feud with many feeling like Kendrick was getting the upper hand. Drake is saying that people must have been pretty excited to see him get in a tough predicament.", "annotation_id": "40446415", "url": "https://genius.com/40446415", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Astalavista (2025)", "line": "Fuck taking y’all advice, suggestion times up", "vault_lines": ["Fuck taking y’all advice, suggestion times up"], "meaning": "J Hova diss", "annotation_id": "40360266", "url": "https://genius.com/40360266", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Astalavista (2025)", "line": "They say Drake’s name, so press can line up And pretend that they care about anything other than what y’all gotta say about the best of all time", "vault_lines": ["They say Drake’s name, so press can line up"], "meaning": "Aimed at Drake’s ex-friends such as Rick Ross, who in interviews are asked a lot of questions about Drake, which they happily answer as they know it will get them views.", "annotation_id": "40360249", "url": "https://genius.com/40360249", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Astalavista (2025)", "line": "Ain’t had no good rest in nine months, who’s next to rise up?", "vault_lines": ["Who’s next to hype up? Who’s next to pipe up?", "Ain’t had no good rest in nine months, who’s next to rise up?"], "meaning": "Pregnancy lasts 9 months, so if Drake has been out of the picture for this long, he expects someone else to take his spot.\n\nHe’s asking if the rap beef has birthed a new G.O.A.T.", "annotation_id": "40360219", "url": "https://genius.com/40360219", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Astalavista (2025)", "line": "I’m set to pass Mike, like my dog wanna rhyme and bless the mic up", "vault_lines": ["I’m set to pass Mike, like my dog wanna rhyme and bless the mic up"], "meaning": "Drake officially surpassed Michael Jackson to become the solo male artist with the most number-one hits on the ⁠Billboard Hot 100. Drake secured his 14th career No. 1 hit when his track “Janice STFU” debuted at the top of the chart.\n\nThis song was likely recorded prior to the release of “ICEMAN”.\n\nDrake made headlines by purchasing one of Michael Jackson’s legendary Swarovski-crystal stage gloves at auction for an estimated $123,000. He prominently featured the glove in his ICEMAN era rollout, wearing it on the album cover and in promotional imagery.", "annotation_id": "40360164", "url": "https://genius.com/40360164", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Astalavista (2025)", "line": "Like two-three on the bulls, your chest is mic’d up", "vault_lines": ["Like two-three on the bulls, your chest is mic'd up"], "meaning": "Michael Jordan played for the Chicago Bulls, and wore the number “23” on his jersey. To be be mic’d up means that they are federal informants, which could be a diss to Rick Ross, who was previously a correctional officer.", "annotation_id": "40360153", "url": "https://genius.com/40360153", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Astalavista (2025)", "line": "You niggas drinks is clean, the rest is spiked up You scaring the hoes trying to be extra nice, huh Statements where you boys confess get typed up", "vault_lines": ["You niggas drinks is clean, the rest is spiked up", "You scaring the hoes trying to be extra nice, huh", "Statements where you boys confess get typed up"], "meaning": "Diss to Pusha T and JAY-Z, who were mentioned in the Epstein Files.", "annotation_id": "40360144", "url": "https://genius.com/40360144", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Astalavista (2025)", "line": "Since our crib got ‘For Sale’ signs up", "vault_lines": ["Since our crib got 'For Sale' signs up"], "meaning": "Drake has referenced this on “OMW”, which is said to be a Kanye diss, however it is likely aimed at Kendrick, as Drake has dissed him for leaving his hood and moving to LA.\nOn “Family Matters”\n\nDon’t even go back to your hood and plant no money trees\n\nOn “OMW”\n\nYou got that big ol' crib now and the sign says “Sold”\n\nOn “Janice STFU”\n\nHandin' out turkeys on camera inside of your hood, then you go back to the hills", "annotation_id": "40360078", "url": "https://genius.com/40360078", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Astalavista (2025)", "line": "Who’s next, can you please stand up Who’s next, can you please stand up All you niggas been shady as fuck But will the real Shady please stand up?", "vault_lines": ["Who’s next, can you please stand up", "All you niggas been shady as fuck", "But will the real Shady please stand up?"], "meaning": "He interpolates Eminem’s “The Real Slim Shady”.\n\nMay I have your attention, please?\nMay I have your attention, please?\nWill the real Slim Shady please stand up?\nI repeat\nWill the real Slim Shady please stand up?\n\nDrake has interpolated Eminem before on the track\n“Chicago Freestyle”.\n\nEminem is often regarded as one of the greatest rappers of all time. He feels that if all of these rappers want to dethrone him as the next great, they have to choose the new G.O.A.T. He speaks about this on “Make Them Pay”.\n\nAnd now they got a new GOAT and we gotta test the position", "annotation_id": "40360038", "url": "https://genius.com/40360038", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
