{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Best I Ever Had", "line": "See, this the type of joint you gotta dedicate to somebody Just make sure they that special somebody Young Money, yeah, yeah You know who you are I got you", "vault_lines": ["I say, you the fuckin'", "See, this the type of joint you gotta dedicate to somebody", "Just make sure they that special somebody", "You know who you are"], "meaning": "Drake confirmed that\nthe girl who inspired this record is his former Canadian flame Nebby whom he has mentioned in songs such as “Look What You’ve Done” and “Hotline Bling” .\n\nDrake confirms it in this interview posted on Soundcloud at the 0:29 mark:\nhttps://soundcloud.com/ovobeanomo/drake-says-bieh-is-about-nebby", "annotation_id": "32647463", "url": "https://genius.com/32647463", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Best I Ever Had", "line": "All up in your slot ’til a nigga hit the jackpot, I’m saying", "vault_lines": ["All up in your slot 'til a nigga hit the jackpot, I'm saying"], "meaning": "A slot machine is a gambling machine operated by inserting coins into a slot, and then pulling a handle that activates a set of symbols. A jackpot is achieved when all symbols are the same.\n\nDrake plays on the analogy of a slot machine, likening the women’s vagina to the slot and his penis as the coins entering the slot, saying he will continue to enter until she orgasms, which is an analogy for the jackpot.", "annotation_id": "30192502", "url": "https://genius.com/30192502", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Best I Ever Had", "line": "Every single show, she out there reppin’ like a mascot", "vault_lines": ["Every single show, she out there reppin' like a mascot"], "meaning": "A mascot is a person or animal, traditionally adopted by a sports team, as a symbolic figure that intends to bring good luck. Drake is saying his girl is at every show of his representing him, just how a mascot for a sports team would be at every game supporting the team.\n\n  The Toronto Raptors Mascot", "annotation_id": "30192449", "url": "https://genius.com/30192449", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Best I Ever Had", "line": "She call me the referee ’cause I be so official My shirt ain’t got no stripes, but I can make your pussy whistle", "vault_lines": ["She call me the referee 'cause I be so official", "My shirt ain't got no stripes, but I can make your pussy whistle"], "meaning": "Drizzy firstly plays on the homonym official, which can mean to have authority and be certified, but is also another word for a referee. Drake’s saying she calls him a referee because he of the authority he holds in the rap game, just like a referee (or official) holds when referring.\n\nDrake continues the referee puns by stating his shirt doesn’t have stripes, like a referee’s traditionally does, but he can still make her vagina whistle, meaning to make noises from orgasm, like the sound a referee makes when he blows a whistle when calling a foul.", "annotation_id": "27453760", "url": "https://genius.com/27453760", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Best I Ever Had", "line": "Yup", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "That’s Trey Songz (Which he makes an appearance in the video)", "annotation_id": "18393654", "url": "https://genius.com/18393654", "state": "pending", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Best I Ever Had", "line": "You know, a lot of girls be Thinkin’ my songs are about them This is not to get confused This one’s for you", "vault_lines": ["You know, a lot of girls be", "Thinkin' my songs are about them", "This is not to get confused", "This one's for you", "You know who you are"], "meaning": "Drake knows a lot of girls and he’s been romantically involved with quite a few, so naturally a handful of them would be under the impression that they are the subject matter of his songs. But in reality, Drake’s songs are actually about one special girl.\n\nThis intro is especially clever because it could be referring to any of the girls who think Drake’s songs are about them, and the special girl remains unknown.", "annotation_id": "17270088", "url": "https://genius.com/17270088", "state": "accepted", "votes": 52, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Best I Ever Had", "line": "Sweatpants, hair tied, chillin’ with no make-up on That’s when you’re the prettiest I hope that you don’t take it wrong", "vault_lines": ["I say, you the fuckin'", "Sweatpants, hair tied, chillin' with no make-up on", "That's when you're the prettiest", "I hope that you don't take it wrong"], "meaning": "At the time Drake was writing this, he was dating model and actress Teyana Taylor.\n\n\n\nShortly after, he dated model Cat Washington after she appeared in his “Best I Ever Had”  video.\n\nAs models, both these ladies probably wear makeup frequently. Drizzy prefers them au naturale.\n\n\n\nFrequent Drake collaborator Lil Wayne feels the same way. In “Love Me,” he raps:\n\nWith no makeup she a ten\n\nThe song also features Drake.", "annotation_id": "10226047", "url": "https://genius.com/10226047", "state": "accepted", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Best I Ever Had", "line": "I be hittin’ all the spots that you ain’t even know was there", "vault_lines": ["I say, you the fuckin'", "I be over there, shawty, I be over there", "I be hittin' all the spots that you ain't even know was there"], "meaning": "When reached, the G-spot triggers powerful orgasms for women. It’s very elusive—finding it is seen as a measure of sexual success. Its existence has yet to be proven, but many report that it does indeed exist.", "annotation_id": "10226022", "url": "https://genius.com/10226022", "state": "accepted", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Best I Ever Had", "line": "Know you got a roommate, call me when there’s no one there Put the key under the mat and you know I be over there", "vault_lines": ["I say, you the fuckin'", "Know you got a roommate, call me when there's no one there", "Put the key under the mat and you know I be over there", "I be over there, shawty, I be over there"], "meaning": "Placing a spare key under the doormat is common practice for people who want to let someone in when they’re out, or when they’re already in bed.\n\n\n\nDrake uses this double entendre as a metaphor for the girl to let him into his life, and have an easy way of entering her place late night.", "annotation_id": "8608752", "url": "https://genius.com/8608752", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Best I Ever Had", "line": "Baby, you my everything, you all I ever wanted We could do it real big, bigger than you ever done it You be up on everything, other hoes ain’t never on it I want this forever, I swear I can spend whatever on it", "vault_lines": ["Baby, you my everything, you all I ever wanted", "We could do it real big, bigger than you ever done it", "You be up on everything, other hoes ain't never on it", "I want this forever, I swear I can spend whatever on it"], "meaning": "Drake nods to fellow Young Money artist Lil Wayne, who used similar lyrics on his unreleased track “That’s My Nigga”:\n\nWe can do it real big\nBigger than you’ve ever done it\nEverything you ever wanted\nI can spend whatever on it", "annotation_id": "2056382", "url": "https://genius.com/2056382", "state": "accepted", "votes": 54, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Best I Ever Had", "line": "And she a patient in my waiting room Never pay attention to the rumors and what they assume And until them girls prove it I’m the one that never get confused with, ’cause", "vault_lines": ["And she a patient in my waiting room", "Never pay attention to the rumors and what they assume", "And until them girls prove it", "I'm the one that never get confused with, 'cause"], "meaning": "She’s patient because she is waiting, but she is also like a patient waiting for the doctor to see them.\n\nAs noted in this video, the metaphor itself undermines Drake’s message that his girl’s the only one. If there are patients in the waiting room, that usually means the doctor is dealing with another patient—that would suggest Drake is with someone else before seeing to her. We know from the hook that’s indeed the case.", "annotation_id": "39570", "url": "https://genius.com/39570", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Best I Ever Had", "line": "Like the Andy Griffith theme song", "vault_lines": ["Like the Andy Griffith theme song"], "meaning": "The theme song to The Andy Griffith Show called “The Fishing Hole” features a whistling tune.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TvSXdO7SDCE", "annotation_id": "22670", "url": "https://genius.com/22670", "state": "accepted", "votes": 45, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Best I Ever Had", "line": "Sex, Love, Pain, baby, I be on that Tank shit", "vault_lines": ["Sex, Love, Pain, baby, I be on that Tank shit"], "meaning": "Sex, Love, & Pain is an album by R&B artist Tank.\n\nTank actually gave his thoughts about the first time he he heard the song and this particular line on Vlad TV… which eventually led to their collaborative track, “Celebration”.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/0H7tV3Ovr6k?t=189", "annotation_id": "22588", "url": "https://genius.com/22588", "state": "accepted", "votes": 48, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Best I Ever Had", "line": "Double cup love, you the one I lean on", "vault_lines": ["I say, you the fuckin'", "Double cup love, you the one I lean on"], "meaning": "Drake could like leaning on her breasts.\nHe could be getting high to her – drinking codeine syrup (“lean”), which is often drunk in double-cupped styrofoam.\nHe could also be dependent on her for emotional support.", "annotation_id": "22498", "url": "https://genius.com/22498", "state": "accepted", "votes": 66, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Best I Ever Had", "line": "Buzz so big I could probably sell a blank disc", "vault_lines": ["Buzz so big I could probably sell a blank disc"], "meaning": "Shout out to Danger Mouse!\n\nThough Drake hadn’t yet dropped an album, people were buzzing after his 2006 mixtape Room for Improvement and 2007’s Comeback Season.  He knew people were amped for So Far Gone.\n\nWhat he is really saying here is that everyone is so hyped for his releases that he could sell a “blank disc” (an album with no songs on it) and it would sell very well, because, relating to the next line, people would buy it solely because Drake made it.", "annotation_id": "22495", "url": "https://genius.com/22495", "state": "accepted", "votes": 50, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
