{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Do What You Do", "line": "You hatin’ my song but your wife wanna burn it So now you at the store for some blank CDs", "vault_lines": ["You hatin' my song but your wife wanna burn it", "So now you at the store for some blank CDs"], "meaning": "Drake is saying that his verses are so hot that he could steal your girl. The wife is going to make CDs with Drake’s songs and the husband is going to wish Aubrey Graham never dropped any music.", "annotation_id": "20215067", "url": "https://genius.com/20215067", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Do What You Do", "line": "A lot of dudes in my city, they ain’t saying nothin’", "vault_lines": ["A lot of dudes in my city, they ain't saying nothin'"], "meaning": "Here, Drake maybe recycling a Biggie lyric from “B.I.G. Interlude” hey says..\n\n“other emcees, man they ain’t saying nothing”\n\nWhen he uses this he’s saying these others rappers aren’t making any real moves in the rap game, or that their lyrics aren’t meaningful and lack content", "annotation_id": "13134615", "url": "https://genius.com/13134615", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Do What You Do", "line": "For features, y’all better get me while it’s cheaper than dinner", "vault_lines": ["For features, y'all better get me while it's cheaper than dinner"], "meaning": "At the time of this song’s release, Drake was a very little known artist in the game. With the way he has charted recently , it’s hard to imagine how much someone might have to pay for a guest verse.\n\nBack in 2014, MTV found that a Kendrick Lamar verse would cost about $250,000 so Drizzy must be soaking in the cash on his features.", "annotation_id": "12508537", "url": "https://genius.com/12508537", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Do What You Do", "line": "’Bout to ink with a major like sheets through a printer", "vault_lines": ["'Bout to ink with a major like sheets through a printer"], "meaning": "Drake is on the verge of signing with a major label, and this could be in reference to being approached to sign by Rock-A-Fella twice by 2008.", "annotation_id": "3002169", "url": "https://genius.com/3002169", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Do What You Do", "line": "‘Whats he worth?’ Fans keep trying to guess it", "vault_lines": ["'Whats he worth?' Fans keep trying to guess it"], "meaning": "This is the situation Drake lived in that period. He was young and unknown, So people was wondering about his skills, He was under microscope as he worked on the mixtape with DJ Smallz.", "annotation_id": "2744320", "url": "https://genius.com/2744320", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Do What You Do", "line": "[Bridge] Two years ago, a friend of mine Asked me to kick some new school lines And so I sent him a rhyme, it was fresh to death Now not signing me is somethin’ that the rest regret Then I, hopped inside the Cadillac The chauffeur drove off and we never came back", "vault_lines": ["Two years ago, a friend of mine", "Asked me to kick some new school lines", "And so I sent him a rhyme, it was fresh to death", "Now not signing me is somethin' that the rest regret", "Then I, hopped inside the Cadillac", "The chauffeur drove off and we never came back"], "meaning": "This entire bridge is a homage to Run-D.M.C.’s famous song, “Sucker M.C.’s.” In the very first verse to this song, Run says:\n\nTwo years ago, a friend of mine\nAsked me to say some MC rhymes\nSo I said this rhyme I’m about to say\nThe rhyme was Def a-then it went this way\nTook a test to become an MC\nAnd Orange Krush became amazed at me\nSo Larry put me inside, his Cad-illac\nThe chauffeur drove off and we never came back", "annotation_id": "2639100", "url": "https://genius.com/2639100", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Do What You Do", "status": "done", "targets": 7, "clicked": 7, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-do-what-you-do-lyrics", "genius_title": "Do What You Do"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Don’t You Have a Man", "line": "And I’m in her body like ‘Gray’s Anatomy’", "vault_lines": ["Next minute, it's all good, and I'm in her body like 'Gray's Anatomy'"], "meaning": "This not a reference to the ABC drama “Grey’s Anatomy” but it’s namesake, a book “Gray’s Anatomy”.\n\nA book published in the 1850s which gives it’s readers a detailed look into the human body and how it works. Despite it’s publishing date it’s still considered to be a very relevant book today and is still being used by med school students.\n\nLet’s face it, Phonte has some of the best punchlines in the game!", "annotation_id": "217112", "url": "https://genius.com/217112", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Don’t You Have a Man", "line": "Look – we had a lil’ thing, a wintertime fling You some getback for your man mistreating", "vault_lines": ["Look – we had a lil' thing, a wintertime fling", "You some getback for your man mistreating"], "meaning": "Pooh is talking to a woman that he previous had a fling with. Her man had just cheated on her so she wanted some getback (revenge) so she hooked up with Pooh who was likely just horny.\n\n\n\nGetback is the title of Little Brother’s third album which they were working on around the time Drake’s Comeback Season was released. More than likely this song was recorded for Getback, but for one reason or another ended up on Drake’s mixtape.", "annotation_id": "217089", "url": "https://genius.com/217089", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Don’t You Have a Man", "line": "And still, she want this chap’s stick like Napoleon Dynamite", "vault_lines": ["And still, she want this chap's stick like Napoleon Dynamite"], "meaning": "In a double entendre, Drake uses the British term chap to link into this exchange from the film Napoleon Dynamite:\n\nNapoleon Dynamite: Well, will you do me a favor then? Can you bring me my chapstick?\nKip: No, Napoleon.\nNapoleon Dynamite: But my lips hurt real bad!\nKip: Just borrow some from the school nurse. I know she has like five sticks in her drawer.\nNapoleon Dynamite: I’m not gonna use hers, you sicko!", "annotation_id": "217085", "url": "https://genius.com/217085", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Don’t You Have a Man", "line": "Tryna save you like a goalie in line-of-sight", "vault_lines": ["Tryna save you like a goalie in line-of-sight"], "meaning": "Leave to a Canadian rapper to create a hockey reference not dealing with ice.\n\nDrake’s trying to save this girl like a goalie trying to make a save for his team by blocking the other team’s offense.", "annotation_id": "217083", "url": "https://genius.com/217083", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Don’t You Have a Man", "line": "Why you over there looking at me While your man standing right beside ya?", "vault_lines": ["Why you over there looking at me", "While your man standing right beside ya?"], "meaning": "Good question. She’s going to blow both their covers and create unnecessary drama\nParaphrased from Mase’s “Lookin' At Me” which was also used in in Jay-Z’s “2 Many Hoes”.", "annotation_id": "217081", "url": "https://genius.com/217081", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Don’t You Have a Man", "line": "Don’t you have a man? (Don’t you got a man?) Why are you trying to be my girl? (Yeah) I can’t believe it (I know you got a man) Don’t you have a man? (Don’t you got a man?) It’s all right with me, my girl We can do anything (Kick it to you like this)", "vault_lines": ["Don't you have a man? (Don't you got a man?)", "Why are you trying to be my girl? (Yeah)", "I can't believe it (I know you got a man)", "It's all right with me, my girl", "I don't understand why God sent me to you", "We can do anything, baby", "We can do anything (Kick it to you like this)"], "meaning": "The hook is sung from the perspective of a man engaged in affair with a woman. That woman already has a boyfriend but is putting pressure on him to get more serious. While the narrator isn’t exactly ready to get serious he’s enjoying the sex that comes with the fling.", "annotation_id": "217079", "url": "https://genius.com/217079", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
