{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Night and Good Luck", "line": "I never bust a gun, I’m Mister C-T-V At least, I’m not Mister Dick Riding C-T-E", "vault_lines": ["I never bust a gun, I'm Mister C-T-V", "At least, I'm not Mister Dick Riding C-T-E"], "meaning": "He is saying whilst he is not gun toting thug (because he is on Canadian Television… Maybe even Degrassi) At least he is not trying to copy Young Jezzy and Jeezy’s CTE (Corporate Thuggin Entertainment). Aristo, the person that this song is attacking, copies Young Jeezy.", "annotation_id": "21719329", "url": "https://genius.com/21719329", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Night and Good Luck", "line": "You get flow and you done fo’", "vault_lines": ["You get flow and you done fo'"], "meaning": "I think the line is actually “You get one flow and you do fo'” Which is to say either the ones dissing him only get one song to do so; or you put out one song and people start to take shots.", "annotation_id": "956378", "url": "https://genius.com/956378", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Night and Good Luck", "line": "But you making out all these dumb tracks, ya LL sixteens Cause I listen to them and I don’t call it a comeback It’s more like a shame or disgrace", "vault_lines": ["But you making out all these dumb tracks, ya LL sixteens", "Cause I listen to them and I don't call it come BACK", "It's more like a shame or disgrace"], "meaning": "Drake references LL Cool J’s 16\" record “Mama Said Knock You Out”, which starts off with the famous line “don’t call it a comeback”.\n\nIn LL’s case, he didn’t want his record to be called a comeback because he felt like he had never fallen off. But Drake is saying that Aristo can’t call his diss track a comeback because it did nothing to help his already unremarkable career.", "annotation_id": "218678", "url": "https://genius.com/218678", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Night and Good Luck", "status": "done", "targets": 3, "clicked": 3, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-good-night-and-good-luck-lyrics", "genius_title": "Good Night and Good Luck"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Still Fly (Freestyle)", "line": "Lebanon Dons in this bitch.", "vault_lines": ["You know what it is man, Lebanon Dons in this bitch."], "meaning": "Oliver & 40 are both Lebanese Canadian\n\nNoah Shebib, better known as “40”, is Drake’s producer and co-founder of OVO (alongside Drake and Oliver El-Khatib). He was born in Canada but is of Lebanese descent\n\nOliver El-Khatib, on the other hand, is Drake’s co-manager and co-founder of OVO (alongside Drake and 40) Oliver was also born in Canada but is of Lebanese descent. El-Khatib is credited to be the genius behind Drake’s global branding existence.", "annotation_id": "34340082", "url": "https://genius.com/34340082", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Still Fly (Freestyle)", "line": "Paige, I hope you don’t mind, I hope you don’t mind me, uhm havin’ a little fun you know?", "vault_lines": ["Paige, I hope you don't mind, I hope you don't mind me, uhm havin' a little fun you know?"], "meaning": "He minded.", "annotation_id": "30506854", "url": "https://genius.com/30506854", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": false, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
