{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Still Fly (Freestyle)", "line": "Took over my city and I never asked permission to;", "vault_lines": ["Took over my city and I never asked permission to;"], "meaning": "Since the start of his career, Drake has always paid respect to his hometown of Toronto, aka the 6, and is credited for bringing international fame to the city. He did this through interviews and songs like “The City is Mine”.\n\nDrake continues to emphasise that he has control over Toronto, implying that he was the only notable rapper who came from the 6 and so did not have to compete with others to become the “6 God”.", "annotation_id": "10194040", "url": "https://genius.com/10194040", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Still Fly (Freestyle)", "line": "We got, we got the real life entourage", "vault_lines": [", we got, we got the real life entourage"], "meaning": "Reference to the famous HBO TV Series “Entourage”. A recurring theme in Entourage is the strength of male camaraderie and its importance over work, and that’s one of the reasons the show was so well received. It also featured guest appearances by a lot of rappers. Drake compares these guys to his own Crew since they’re also all very good friends from the same city, and judging by what we’ve seen through the years he might just be right..\nDrake of course would be the “Vincent Chase” to the OVO Crew.", "annotation_id": "3886757", "url": "https://genius.com/3886757", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Still Fly (Freestyle)", "line": "That’s where you find all the exclusives at", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Since the beginning of Drake’s jump to stardom all of his songs and his breakthrough mixtape So Far Gone were released on their blog, and until this day his exclusive songs and also releases from OVO affiliated artists such as P Reign, Jimmy Johnson are posted on the website.", "annotation_id": "3886751", "url": "https://genius.com/3886751", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Still Fly (Freestyle)", "line": "[Outro]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Here Drake shouts out almost of his OVO Crew, who at the time were just a bunch of unknown names (this song was released in 2009) but now has become more than just his mostly Toronto-based crew. It’s a brand, it’s a movement, and its grown immensely since it started. In 2012, Drake, Noah “40” Shebib and Oliver El-Khatib founded “OVOSound”, a record label currently distributed by Warner Bros. Records.", "annotation_id": "3886732", "url": "https://genius.com/3886732", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Still Fly (Freestyle)", "line": "John B.", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Jonny Roxx, Drake’s personal trainer. Pictured below with Johnny Manziel, who is also an OVO affiliate, and Drake.", "annotation_id": "3886718", "url": "https://genius.com/3886718", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Still Fly (Freestyle)", "line": "And man, my DJ shoulda won that Nelissa and Wristpect, Man the city owe us one back", "vault_lines": ["And man, my DJ shoulda won that", "Nelissa and Wristpect, Man the city owe us one back"], "meaning": "This line refers to his Dj at the time Dj Wristpect losing at the Toronto Stylus Awards when he was deserving of winning that year.", "annotation_id": "191823", "url": "https://genius.com/191823", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Still Fly (Freestyle)", "line": "October’s Very Own", "vault_lines": ["You know October's Very Own"], "meaning": "http://octobersveryown.blogspot.ie/ (aka OVO) is a record label founded by Drake, his producer 40 and Oliver El-Khatib.\n\nMembers of the record label include PARTYNEXTDOOR, Roy Woods, Majid Jordan and dvsn. Furthermore, OVO has in-house producers such as 40, Nineteen85 and Boi-1da.\n\nHere is more info on the entire crew.", "annotation_id": "85855", "url": "https://genius.com/85855", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Still Fly (Freestyle)", "line": "Niko just came and scooped me from the airport", "vault_lines": ["Drizzy's home baby. Niko just came and scooped me from the airport"], "meaning": "Niko, Drake’s good friend (producer) picked him up from the Toronto airport.\n\nNiko is one of Drake’s oldest and closest friends from Toronto, Niko introduced the rapper to his own barber when the former “Degrassi” star needed a fresh look. He’s now responsible for OVO’s Merchandising.", "annotation_id": "84649", "url": "https://genius.com/84649", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Still Fly (Freestyle)", "line": "Freeko Suave, Oliver, the Parisian Gangster", "vault_lines": [", it's like me, Freeko Suave, Oliver, the Parisian Gangster"], "meaning": "Oliver El-Khatib is one of OVO Sound' founders alongside Drake and 40, and is also Drake’s Manager, producer (he’s credited in The Resistance and creative Director.", "annotation_id": "49350", "url": "https://genius.com/49350", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Still Fly (Freestyle)", "line": "Responsible for everything you listen to", "vault_lines": ["Responsible for everything you listen to"], "meaning": "Drake had three hit singles the year that this freestyle was released (“Forever”, “Best I Ever Had”, and “Successful”)\n\nIt’s all the radio would play! Drake Drake Drake!", "annotation_id": "49346", "url": "https://genius.com/49346", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
