{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Members Only", "line": "Are you slappin’ them or slappin’ us?", "vault_lines": ["Are you jackin' them or jackin' us?", "Are you slappin' them or slappin' us?"], "meaning": "In some regional slang, particularly in Toronto, the word “slap” is used to refer to engaging in sexual activity with someone.\n\nParty asks the girl if she’s having sex with them or the other side.\nSee Drake’s “Slap The City”", "annotation_id": "30003378", "url": "https://genius.com/30003378", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
