{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Members Only", "line": "You used to jack the other side, but that shit doesn’t faze me", "vault_lines": ["You used to jack the other side, but that shit doesn't faze me"], "meaning": "PND previously questions this girls loyalty as to which side she riding for during his verse, “Are you jackin’ them, or jackin' us?”\nDrake confirms this girl used to ride for his opps, but his feelings have grown so strong for her that he’s willing to overlook her past alliances.", "annotation_id": "29789885", "url": "https://genius.com/29789885", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Members Only", "line": "Going deeper inside, my feelings can’t subside These walls are so thin, you gon’ wake up the whole eastside, girl", "vault_lines": ["Going deeper inside, my feelings can't subside", "These walls are so thin, you gon' wake up the whole eastside, girl", "All jokes aside, you gon' wake up the whole eastside", "Wake up the whole eastside"], "meaning": "As Drake begins to engage in sexual activities with her his feelings couldn’t possibly become any less intense for her. As he goes deeper, his girl gets louder and since the walls are thin he’s saying that the whole city gonna hear his girl scream.", "annotation_id": "29789857", "url": "https://genius.com/29789857", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Members Only", "line": "Red flag, blue flag, green flag, and a white flag to surrender (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Red flag, blue flag, green flag, and a white flag to surrender (Yeah)"], "meaning": "In gang culture most gangs represent themselves by wearing paisley printed bandanas in various colors. Red, blue, and green being very popular flags to represent gangs, while the last flag represents a metaphor. In times of battle or combat a way to submit without continuing would be to wave a white flag or towel to symbolize acceptance of the loss.", "annotation_id": "29742529", "url": "https://genius.com/29742529", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Members Only", "line": "I know, I know I could have us both Both comin’ at the same time like, “Jinx,” I’m talkin’ dirty", "vault_lines": ["I know the answer", "I know, I know I could have us both", "Both comin' at the same time like, \"Jinx,\" I'm talkin' dirty"], "meaning": "Drake recognizes that he is capable of making this woman and himself come at the same time, as in reaching an orgasm. He relates this to the term, “jinx”, a term that is said when two people inadvertently say the same thing at the same time.", "annotation_id": "29741859", "url": "https://genius.com/29741859", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Members Only", "line": "I live like forty minutes from you, that sex drive is crazy", "vault_lines": ["I live like forty minutes from you, that sex drive is crazy"], "meaning": "Drake acknowledges the lenghty duration of his literal driving route to this woman’s place. He relates this to the sex drive of either himself or his woman. Confirming that their interest in having sex together is equally as crazy.", "annotation_id": "29741809", "url": "https://genius.com/29741809", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Members Only", "line": "You know the airport is callin’ our name You know the Clearport is callin’ our name", "vault_lines": ["You know the airport is callin' our name", "You know the Clearport is callin' our name"], "meaning": "A clearport is a term used to describe  an airport utilized by private aviation charter companies for private flights.\nParty references the airport in purpose of convincing this woman that he and she are destined to take a trip together.", "annotation_id": "29741753", "url": "https://genius.com/29741753", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Members Only", "line": "All your friends keep judgin’ us, it’s like you’re my attorney", "vault_lines": ["All your friends keep judgin' us, it's like you're my attorney"], "meaning": "Drake makes a play on the word “judging,” as in forming conclusions or opinions, but also relating it to an actual judge, a public official authorized to hear and decide cases in a court of law. Therefore, also relating his relationship with this woman to that of an attorney and client because of the constant judging she and Drake continue to receive from her friends.\n\nAttorney – a person appointed to act for another in business or legal matters", "annotation_id": "29733451", "url": "https://genius.com/29733451", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Members Only", "line": "Say you started datin’ girls now, say it to me with a straight face", "vault_lines": ["Say you started datin' girls now, say it to me with a straight face"], "meaning": "Here, Drake plays on the homonym “straight.” On the one hand, “straight face” means to display a serious facial expression, generally accompanied with a serious statement, meaning Drake is telling his girl to be honest if she’s actually started dating girls.\n\nOn the other hand, “straight” means to be heterosexual, which is wordplay playing on the fact Drizzy’s girl is claiming to be lesbian or bisexual as she is now dating girls.", "annotation_id": "29730541", "url": "https://genius.com/29730541", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Members Only", "line": "You standin’ tall like the star-spangled", "vault_lines": ["You standin' tall like the star-spangled"], "meaning": "“The Star Spangled Banner” is the national anthem to the United States of America.\nPeople are instructed to stand with their hands over their heart or salute to the American flag whenever the anthem is played.", "annotation_id": "29729053", "url": "https://genius.com/29729053", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Members Only", "line": "I can’t wait for September ‘Cause that means that next month, it’s goin’ down like timber", "vault_lines": ["I can't wait for September", "'Cause that means that next month, it's goin' down like timber"], "meaning": "After September comes October. Drake’s affection for the month of October is well known, with it not only being his birth month, but also the name of his label/brand – “October’s Very Own”.\n\nThe second line is a reference to Pitbull’s song (featuring Kesha) – “Timber”:\n\nIt’s goin’ down, I’m yellin’ timber", "annotation_id": "29728038", "url": "https://genius.com/29728038", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Members Only", "line": "N-Y-see me later when I’m right there like New Jersey", "vault_lines": ["N-Y-see me later when I'm right there like New Jersey"], "meaning": "Drake uses the similarity of pronunciation of “And why see” and “NYC” for a clever wordplay.\nNYC borders New Jersey, which makes Drake wonder why does she have to see him later instead of right now since the fact that New York City is right next to New Jersey.", "annotation_id": "29728035", "url": "https://genius.com/29728035", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Members Only", "line": "Comin’ from Jahron B side", "vault_lines": ["Comin' from Jahron B side"], "meaning": "Drake refers to PARTYNEXTDOOR’s government name, “Jahron Anthony Braithwaite”, as Jahron B. He is saying this woman comes from where PND comes from – Mississauga, west of Toronto, in contrast to the fact that she wakes up the whole eastside.", "annotation_id": "29726623", "url": "https://genius.com/29726623", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Members Only", "line": "I’ll take you farther than Biscayne, my girl", "vault_lines": ["I'll take you farther than Mexico (Yeah, yeah)", "I'll take you farther than Biscayne, my girl"], "meaning": "PARTYNEXTDOOR is from Ontario, Canada. Biscayne is a southern region of Florida. This is a reference to a previous bar in this song. This could also be a reference to the Bahama islands, which are very close to Biscayne, but farther south. As the lyric says, he’ll take her farther than Biscayne, which from the starting location of Ontario, would be the Bahamas.", "annotation_id": "29726454", "url": "https://genius.com/29726454", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Members Only", "line": "When you ride around the 6ix, girl", "vault_lines": ["When you ride around the 6ix, girl"], "meaning": "The 6 is a moniker for Toronto, Drake’s hometown. Drake has made plenty references to the number in his music (and as a hand gesture).\n\n\nThe reason Toronto is called “The 6” / “6” / “6ix” is because of the six municipalities making up Metro Toronto before they were all joined in 1998. Furthermore, the name is also derived from the main area code in Toronto, 416.", "annotation_id": "29726013", "url": "https://genius.com/29726013", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Members Only", "line": "You’re too down with the members You’re too down for the O, girl, fuck November, December", "vault_lines": ["You're too down with the", "You're too down with the gangy, with the gangy", "You're too down with the members", "You're too down for the O, girl, fuck November, December", "You're too down for the O, girl, the O, girl", "You're too down with the gangy, you're one of my members"], "meaning": "Drake is acknowledging this girls willingness to be involved with his members, referring to them as “the O”, as in October’s Very Own. He takes a shot at the following months, November and December, for the purpose of showing the importance of the O.", "annotation_id": "29725665", "url": "https://genius.com/29725665", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Members Only", "line": "Time to arch that back and put both hands down like 6:30", "vault_lines": ["Time to arch that back and put both hands down like 6:30"], "meaning": "This is a reference to the doggy-style position, which includes an arched back and all fours.\n\nDrake describes the girl to have her hands down like 6:30. The hands of an analog clock points downwards at this time.\n\nAlso Drake says “Time to” alluding time on a clock.", "annotation_id": "29725661", "url": "https://genius.com/29725661", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Members Only", "line": "Hop off the block if you’re Jenny for me (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Hop off the block if you're Jenny for me (Yeah)"], "meaning": "PARTY both plays on the word ‘genuine’ and references Jennifer Lopez‘ September 2002 hit single, “Jenny from the Block,” as he previously did on his cut “Rendezvous,” from his June 2017 EP, Colours 2, in which he interpolated J. Lo’s classic on the pre-chorus:\n\nI’m not fooled by the money that you got (Got)\nYou’re still Jenny from the motherfuckin' block (Block)", "annotation_id": "29725279", "url": "https://genius.com/29725279", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
