{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Language", "line": "Come get your girl She been here for three days and she way too attached to me", "vault_lines": ["Come get your girl", "She been here for three days and she way too attached to me", "Hate when they get too attached to me"], "meaning": "In light of recent beef events and the nature of this specific song, Drake might be alluding to sleeping with the long-time girlfriend of Kendrick Lamar, Whitney Alford.", "annotation_id": "36611629", "url": "https://genius.com/36611629", "state": "pending", "votes": -6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Language", "line": "Someone just talking that bullshit Man, someone just gave you the run-around", "vault_lines": ["Someone just talking that bullshit", "Man, someone just gave you the run-around"], "meaning": "Whoever is hyping up or bigging up these other rappers in the game and making them feel like the top MC’s right now must be bullshitting them… well at least that’s how Drake sees it.\n\nThis line may be directed at Kendrick considering he is one of the hottest MC’s out right now, however Drake doesn’t see it because Drake believes he’s the only one that is putting out the hottest records and definitely putting the numbers on the board.\n\nDrake was even one of the few that helped promote Kendrick Lamar’s stardom by having him as a guest feature on his album and not to mention that one of the most popular Kendrick Lamar singles featured Drake himself.", "annotation_id": "2308722", "url": "https://genius.com/2308722", "state": "accepted", "votes": 36, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Language", "line": "Big Tyme ”Sunshine”,", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Stunnaman dropping some more references – firstly to his past duo with Mannie Fresh Big Tymers, and secondly to a track entitled “Sunshine” off the Rich Gang album (a collaborative effort between the Young Money and Cash Money record labels).\n\n\n\nAs the blimp says, get your shine on.", "annotation_id": "2233756", "url": "https://genius.com/2233756", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Language", "line": "It could all be so simple", "vault_lines": ["It could all be so simple"], "meaning": "In an album full of subtle Wu-Tang Clan references, it’s not outside the realm of possibility that this could be alluding to “Can It Be All So Simple”, a nostalgia track off 36 Chambers", "annotation_id": "2215138", "url": "https://genius.com/2215138", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Language", "line": "Get what I can out the country And then I just get on the jet and go back to the cold", "vault_lines": ["I got to get on the bus and get back on the road", "Get what I can out the country", "And then I just get on the jet and go back to the cold"], "meaning": "Drake tours all over the USA, collecting profits and then returns to Toronto–where a lot of people don’t realize how cold it gets during the winter. Drake makes touring sound like an obligation here, in the same way he did on Over My Dead Body:\n\nJust performed at a Bar Mitzvah over in the States\nUsed half of the money to beat my brother’s case\n\n\n\nThat’s word to Toronto", "annotation_id": "2213861", "url": "https://genius.com/2213861", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Language", "line": "This has been years in the makin’ It’s all for the city, they know I come right every summer", "vault_lines": ["This has been years in the makin'", "It's all for the city, they know I come right every summer"], "meaning": "“This has been years in the making” is most likely referring to how long it took to put together Nothing Was The Same. His previous album Take Care was released in 2011 – hence NWTS has literally been 2 years in the making.\n\nA second interpretation is that Drake is talking about his success as an artist being years in the making. Since releasing his first mixtape Room For Improvement back in 2006, he has won a Grammy and now has the most number one singles on 2 Billboard charts.\n\nEither way, Drizzy says this is all for Toronto – his hometown. Starting in 2010, Drake hosts the annual OVO Fest in Toronto over the Canadian Civic Holiday long weekend. It headlines a large number of quality artists – even Yeezus himself made a surprise appearance this year. As accurately stated in this article:\n\nAnyone who accuses Drake of not caring about Toronto has never been to OVO Fest.", "annotation_id": "2213663", "url": "https://genius.com/2213663", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Language", "line": "I don’t know why they been lyin’, but your shit is not that inspirin’", "vault_lines": ["I don't know why they been lyin', but your shit is not that inspirin'"], "meaning": "Drake doesn’t find your art inspiring, and people are just lying/caught up in the hype. This could be a response to Kendrick Lamar on his “Control” verse, where he called out Drake along with many other rappers, saying:\n\nI got love for you all but I’m tryna murder you niggas\n\nWhile Kendrick’s verse was seen positively by some for encouraging others to step up their game, Drake doesnt seem to agree with those statements.\n\nAlthough, this could just be a “one-size-fits-all” shot.", "annotation_id": "2213416", "url": "https://genius.com/2213416", "state": "accepted", "votes": 111, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Language", "line": "Fuck going platinum, I look at my wrist and it’s already platinum", "vault_lines": ["Fuck going platinum, I look at my wrist and it's already platinum"], "meaning": "Drake is metaphorically comparing his platinum Rolex timepiece to the state of his record (despite the fact Take Care and So Far Gone hit platinum)\n\nIn an interview with Jet magazine he says\n\nI bought a platinum Rolex, which is something I’ve always wanted. Everybody raps about Rolex — it’s such a fixture in hip-hop music. But only a certain amount of people can get the platinum one… The gold one is a staple, and I had that when I first started; I just always said to myself, ‘Yo I wanna be able to get that platinum one and not have to worry about the price.’ I finally was able to get it this year.\n\n\n\nThis could be interpreted as another Kendrick shot. The attention Kendrick got from his “Control” verse helped him finally achieve platinum for good kid, m.A.A.d city in Aug. 2013 – about 10 months after it was released. Drake, on the other hand, is downplaying the significance of achieving platinum by saying that in the time it takes to look at his watch, it – NWTS – will have already gone platinum.", "annotation_id": "2213304", "url": "https://genius.com/2213304", "state": "accepted", "votes": 74, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Language", "line": "Cash Money Records forever, I’m always big timin’", "vault_lines": ["Cash Money Records forever, I'm always big timin'"], "meaning": "The Big Tymers was a music duo formed in the late 90s consisting of Birdman and producer Mannie Fresh.\n\nRecently, Lil Wayne announced that another Big Tymers album is coming soon featuring himself, Birdman, and Drizzy. Mannie, who’s notably not involved in the reincarnation of his old group, isn’t a huge fan of this idea…\n\nHopefully the album art will at least remain consistent.", "annotation_id": "2213237", "url": "https://genius.com/2213237", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
