{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "TSU", "line": "Baby blue, but you are not a baby", "vault_lines": ["Baby blue, but you are not a baby"], "meaning": "Safe to assume that Drake is referring to Tiffany & Co, which is a fancy jewelry company known for their baby blue packaging.\n\n\n\nHe has rapped before about Tiffany’s sway on his song REDEMPTION in his 4th studio album VIEWS (2016)\n\nhttps://genius.com/Drake-redemption-lyrics#note-9072695", "annotation_id": "24068331", "url": "https://genius.com/24068331", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "TSU", "line": "Baby blue, but you are not a baby,", "vault_lines": ["Baby blue, but you are not a baby"], "meaning": "Safe to assume he’s referring to Tiffany & Co, which is a fine jewelry company known for their baby blue packaging.\n\n\n\n Drake has rapped about Tiffany before on ‘Redemption’ “Tiffany on you, you know you poppin'”.", "annotation_id": "24050997", "url": "https://genius.com/24050997", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "TSU", "line": "Swishahouse, baby", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Swishahouse is a Houston-based independent record label that was co-founded by OG Ron C in 1997. The label came about alongside the rise of Houston’s famous chopped and screwed music, a style that has lasted decades and remains highly influential. It has been used directly by artists like Drake and Travis Scott, while others have instituted it through full project recreations, including artists like 21 Savage and Brent Faiyaz to Houston’s own Megan Thee Stallion and Don Toliver. Even Ron C’s vocals on this intro are edited in the style.", "annotation_id": "23879783", "url": "https://genius.com/23879783", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "TSU", "line": "What’s up to all the ladies on the north side, south side, east side, west side? What’s up in Bay City? What’s up to all the ladies in Louisiana? What’s up to all the ladies in Dallas, Austin, San Antonio?", "vault_lines": ["What's up to all the ladies on the north side, south side, east side, west side?", "What's up in Bay City?", "What's up to all the ladies in Louisiana?", "What's up to all the ladies in Dallas, Austin, San Antonio?"], "meaning": "In this intro, OG Ron C shouts out various parts of the state of Texas, including Bay City, Dallas, Austin, San Antonio, Marshall, Wharton County, Texas City, and Houston. He also briefly mentions the state of Louisiana.\n\nAmongst these shoutouts, OG Ron C shouts out two of the Houston area’s historically black universities (HBCUs): Prairie View A&M University, which is located in Prairie View, TX (northwest of Houston), and Texas Southern University, which is in the heart of Houston and the song’s namesake.\n\nTSU acknowledged the shoutout in a tweet on the day of the album’s release.\nhttps://twitter.com/texassouthern/status/1433825834855501824?s=21\n\nWhile fans speculated that Ron C and Drake could be talking about other universities in the state of Texas, those other universities, such as Texas State University, go by different acronyms (TxST), while Texas Southern uses either TSU or TxSU.\n\nDrake has a deep-rooted connection to the city of Houston, and he has shown his love and admiration for it throughout his career. This is evident with songs like his early 2009 track, “Houstatlantavegas,” collaborations with several Houston artists, and his recurring Houston Appreciation Weekend.", "annotation_id": "23874088", "url": "https://genius.com/23874088", "state": "accepted", "votes": 63, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "TSU", "line": "Little side hustle with the Fashion Nova", "vault_lines": ["Little side hustle with the Fashion Nova"], "meaning": "Fashion Nova is an online fast fashion retailer which increasingly uses artists, influencers and models as social media ambassadors to do paid endorsements in advertisement campaigns.\n\n\n\nDrake rocking a Fashion Nova fit", "annotation_id": "23877783", "url": "https://genius.com/23877783", "state": "pending", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "TSU", "line": "I give you this bread, you run me some head And then you go glow up a bit", "vault_lines": ["I give you this bread, you run me some head", "And then you go glow up a bit"], "meaning": "“Head” is slang for oral sex. Drake noted on Nicki Minaj’s December 2014 song “Only” that he likes girls who are able to perform such actions exceptionally well:\n\nYeah, that’s right, I like my girls BBW\nYeah, type that wanna suck you dry and then eat some lunch with you", "annotation_id": "22265285", "url": "https://genius.com/22265285", "state": "accepted", "votes": 56, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "TSU", "line": "She moved out of state and shit done went left, she’s seekin’ forgiveness She used to dance, but she want a loan to start up a business Her daddy is not around, her mama is not around I watch her climb to the top of the pole and then get to slidin’ down I make it rain in this bitch, I make it snow in this bitch She tryna get out of the mix, shawty is goin’ legit Shawty is goin’ legit, me, I’m supportin’ this shit This is a story, it came from my life and I’m just recordin’ this shit", "vault_lines": ["She moved out of state and shit done went left, she's seekin' forgiveness", "She used to dance, but she want a loan to start up a business", "Her daddy is not around, her mama is not around", "I watch her climb to the top of the pole and then get to slidin' down", "I make it rain in this bitch, I make it snow in this bitch", "She tryna get out of the mix, shawty is goin' legit", "Shawty is goin' legit, me, I'm supportin' this shit", "This is a story, it came from my life and I'm just recordin' this shit", "You know I'm supportin' this shit", "I got a Drac' in the studio, and I don't just mean that I'm in this bitch", "Please make the most of this shit", "I watch her climb to the top of the pole and then get to s—", "Her daddy is not around, mama is definitely not around", "I watch her climb to the top of the pole and then get to slidin', slidin'", "This is a story, it came from my life and I'm just rec— ayy"], "meaning": "The chorus and the song’s theme draws similarities to Drake’s November 2011 song, “The Real Her.” On the Take Care slow cut, Drake praises a female stripper for being independent and able to take care of herself. Additionally, Drake even mentions the idea of “saving” her, which means to date and financially support a licentious woman:\n\nThey keep telling me don’t save you\n\nDrake keeps the same idea here. Since this girl’s parents have cut her out of their lives due to her stripping, he’s willing to support her and help her move on with her life.", "annotation_id": "22263761", "url": "https://genius.com/22263761", "state": "accepted", "votes": 140, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "TSU", "line": "I got like four on the wrist and an adorable kid", "vault_lines": ["I got like four on the wrist and an adorable kid"], "meaning": "Drake’s child is Adonis Graham, who was born on October 11, 2017. His birth was kept under wraps from much of the public until May 2018 when Pusha T released his diss track, “The Story of Adidon.” On the track, Push claimed Drake was hiding Adonis from the world and made references to his mother, Sophie Brussaux, who is a former French pornstar:\n\nAdonis is your son\nAnd he deserves more than an Adidas press run; that’s real\nLove that baby, respect that girl\nForget she’s a pornstar, let her be your world, yuugh!\n\nOn June 2018’s “Emotionless,” Drake responded to the lines and said he was hiding the world from Adonis, due to his high-profile lifestyle:\n\nI wasn’t hidin' my kid from the world\nI was hidin' the world from my kid\n\n\n\nThe “four” in the line “four on the wrist” likely refers to $400,000, meaning Drake paid $400,000 for a luxurious watch.", "annotation_id": "22263525", "url": "https://genius.com/22263525", "state": "accepted", "votes": 52, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "TSU", "line": "I got a Drac’ in the studio, and I don’t just mean that I’m in this bitch", "vault_lines": ["I got a Drac' in the studio, and I don't just mean that I'm in this bitch"], "meaning": "A “Draco,” or more specifically a Romanian Draco AK-47 Pistol, is a type of AK-47 assault rifle with a shortened back.\n\nDrake plays on “Draco,” as the first syllable in the word matches the first syllable of his own name.\n\nNotably, Lil Durk used a similar line on Drake’s August 2020 hit “Laugh Now Cry Later,” rapping:\n\nBring Drake to the hood, surround Drake around Dracs", "annotation_id": "20163731", "url": "https://genius.com/20163731", "state": "accepted", "votes": 63, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "TSU", "line": "You popped a 325, you feelin’ too good to worry tonight", "vault_lines": ["You popped a 325, you feelin' too good to worry tonight"], "meaning": "Drake is referencing Percocet® 5/325, a combination of oxycodone (5 mg) with acetaminophen (325 mg), an opioid analgesic used to treat moderate to severe short-term pain.", "annotation_id": "19795907", "url": "https://genius.com/19795907", "state": "accepted", "votes": 57, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
