{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wants and Needs", "line": "She came for me twice, I didn’t even nut for her once, you know I’m a pleaser", "vault_lines": ["She came for me twice, I didn't even nut for her once, you know I'm a pleaser"], "meaning": "While engaging in sexual intercourse with this woman she climaxed twice while Drake didn’t at all because he knows how to outlast a woman in order to pleasure her. This might also be a reference to his mentor Lil Wayne’s song “Dick Pleaser” which is about women pleasuring Lil Wayne instead of him doing it for them.", "annotation_id": "33771413", "url": "https://genius.com/33771413", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wants and Needs", "line": "We walk around with them bands in our britches", "vault_lines": ["We walk around with them bands in our britches"], "meaning": "The line could also be ‘We walk around with them Bens in our britches’ instead of “bands”.\n\nBens would refer to 100 US dollar bills which have Benjamin Franklin’s face on them.\n\nBritches are a type of pants that only go down to the knees that people used to wear in Benjamin Franklin’s time.\n\nThe Benjamin Franklin statue in this image is wearing britches.", "annotation_id": "27078196", "url": "https://genius.com/27078196", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wants and Needs", "line": "Haven’t fallen off yet, yee", "vault_lines": ["Haven't fallen off yet, yee"], "meaning": "Drake raps the first 16 bars with a syncopated flow that almost sounds offbeat about halfway through to the end—so much so that it almost sounds like a polyrhythm:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=U4fECon4qxk\n\nStill, right as he finishes the intro he brags that he’s still on top of the industry and hasn’t “fallen off yet\"—and coincidentally, he also hasn’t fallen off the beat of the song yet either.\n\nAs a side note, Drake’s flow here feels like a perfected version of the syncopation he used towards the end of his verse on “Only You” feat. Headie One, which also stretched the rhythm to the point that it felt off-beat:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=znQriFAMBRs&t=1m45s", "annotation_id": "25569465", "url": "https://genius.com/25569465", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wants and Needs", "line": "I gave her four Birkins at once for a starter (Skrrt)", "vault_lines": ["I gave her four Birkins at once for a starter (Skrrt)"], "meaning": "The Birkin bag (or simply, Birkin) is a line of tote bags by the French luxury goods maker Hermès. Birkin bags are handmade from leather and are named after the English actress and singer Jane Birkin. Baby here is suggesting that he has enough money to be able to buy this girl four Birkin bags, with one being for the girl’s daughter. A lot of money spent here. In 2020, prices started at US$11,000 for regular leather and have reached up to US$380,000.", "annotation_id": "23398110", "url": "https://genius.com/23398110", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wants and Needs", "line": "Deposit the money to Brenda, LaTisha, or Linda, Felicia", "vault_lines": ["Deposit the money to Brenda, LaTisha, or Linda, Felicia"], "meaning": "Drake makes a slick nod to DMX’s second verse from his June 2000 hit, “What These Bitches Want,” where he names a list of different women:\n\nThere was Brenda, LaTisha, Linda, Felicia\n\nDrake previously sampled the song on April 2016’s “U With Me?,” a cut from his fourth studio album, Views.", "annotation_id": "22366083", "url": "https://genius.com/22366083", "state": "accepted", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wants and Needs", "line": "The earrings are real, the petty is real, might charge my ex for a feature", "vault_lines": ["The earrings are real, the petty is real, might charge my ex for a feature"], "meaning": "In December 2020, Drake got his ears pierced with diamonds which, according to TMZ, cost around $70,000.\n\n\n\n There are several women in the music industry that Drake could be referring to for a feature, notably SZA, Rihanna, Jorja Smith, and even Jennifer Lopez.", "annotation_id": "22363168", "url": "https://genius.com/22363168", "state": "accepted", "votes": 97, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wants and Needs", "line": "I’m not a GOAT, but I fit the description", "vault_lines": ["I'm not a GOAT, but I fit the description"], "meaning": "Lil Baby uses wordplay to acknowledge his status as a self-proclaimed “GOAT”—an acronym for “Greatest Of All Time”—whilst obviously making it clear that he is not an actual “goat.” From winning “Best New Artist” at the 2019 BET Awards, to his sophomore studio album My Turn being the first album of the year to be certified double platinum by the RIAA in September 2020, Baby has proved countless times that he is a unique artist who pushes himself and strives to be the best.\n\nThis is not the first time he has described himself to fit the title either; in May 2020, he was featured on the song “3 Headed Goat,” with fellow rappers Lil Durk and Polo G.", "annotation_id": "22362607", "url": "https://genius.com/22362607", "state": "accepted", "votes": 130, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wants and Needs", "line": "Whippin’ Benz concept", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake references the Mercedes-Maybach 6 Cabriolet concept car, which can be seen in the music video for his 2020 single “Laugh Now Cry Later”.", "annotation_id": "22362210", "url": "https://genius.com/22362210", "state": "accepted", "votes": 92, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wants and Needs", "line": "Come with a classic, they come around years later and say it’s a sleeper", "vault_lines": ["Come with a classic, they come around years later and say it's a sleeper"], "meaning": "This line is specifically referencing Drake’s album Views. Initially when the album dropped, it received underwhelming reviews, but a couple of years later some fans consider it to be an underrated album.\n\n\n\nDrake also predicts that his upcoming album Certified Lover Boy is going to receive similar reviews to Views at first, but eventually listeners are going to love it.", "annotation_id": "22361998", "url": "https://genius.com/22361998", "state": "accepted", "votes": 116, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wants and Needs", "line": "Yeah, I probably should go link with Yeezy, I need me some Jesus But soon as I started confessin’ my sins, he wouldn’t believe us", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I probably should go link with Yeezy, I need me some Jesus", "But soon as I started confessin' my sins, he wouldn't believe us", "Should repent, I need me some Jesus in my life"], "meaning": "“Yeezy” is Kanye West, who Drake has had years of issues with dating back to 2010. Some of their drama include the infamous fallacious rumors that Drake slept with Ye’s wife at the time, Kim Kardashian after he seemingly rapped about going to Ye’s house on Travis Scott’s August 2018 hit, “SICKO MODE.” A popular Twitter thread, later made by fans, somewhat supported this theory.\n\nIn 2019, Kanye reformed his image to be more religious, becoming a “born-again Christian” as he described himself in interviews. Along that year came Ye’s ninth studio album, JESUS IS KING, which was his first gospel record.\n\nDrake pokes fun about confessing his sins to Kanye due to his Christian faith, similar to how one would confess their sins to a priest in a church.", "annotation_id": "22361690", "url": "https://genius.com/22361690", "state": "accepted", "votes": 296, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wants and Needs", "line": "(6ix)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "“The 6” is a nickname for Toronto, which comes from the 416 and 647 area codes in the city. Also, at one point, Toronto was broken up into six areas, Old Toronto, Scarborough, East York, North York, Etobicoke, and York, giving the nickname more significance.\n\nThe “six” here is sampled from Chuck D’s intro on The Notorious B.I.G.’s March 1997 classic, “Ten Crack Commandments.”", "annotation_id": "22361622", "url": "https://genius.com/22361622", "state": "accepted", "votes": 111, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wants and Needs", "line": "I lost a Ferrari, Las Vegas, Nevada", "vault_lines": ["I lost a Ferrari, Las Vegas, Nevada"], "meaning": "Since Lil Baby mentions Las Vegas, he’s likely talking about gambling money the value of a Ferrari in a casino, and losing it. The most affordable Ferrari on the market, the 488 GTB, has a starting price of $252,000.\n\nBaby previously name-dropped the car brand on his May 2018 Drake collaboration, “Yes Indeed,” in reference to the new $7 million LaFerrari Drake bought at the time:\n\nCartier glasses, I won’t even peek at you\nYellow Ferrari like Pikachu", "annotation_id": "22361222", "url": "https://genius.com/22361222", "state": "accepted", "votes": 120, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wants and Needs", "line": "I’m from the four, but I love me a threesome", "vault_lines": ["I'm from the four, but I love me a threesome"], "meaning": "Lil Baby is from Oakland City, a neighborhood within patrol Zone 4 of the Atlanta Police Department.    4 Pockets Full or 4PF is also the name of his brand and label imprint.\n\nHere, Baby plays on the number three and four to describe his love for group intimacy. He could also be implying an affection for the Zone 3 patrol area, the original home of his mentor Young Thug. Thug has supported Baby since he began rapping and even paid him to leave Zone 4 to focus on music.", "annotation_id": "22361035", "url": "https://genius.com/22361035", "state": "accepted", "votes": 179, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wants and Needs", "line": "Forty-two millimeter, was made in Geneva", "vault_lines": ["Forty-two millimeter, was made in Geneva"], "meaning": "Some luxury watch companies have headquarters in Geneva, Switzerland, for example Patek Philippe and Rolex.\n\nIn this line, he also may be referencing his 42mm Patek Philippe Nautilus customized by Virgil Abloh.", "annotation_id": "22360920", "url": "https://genius.com/22360920", "state": "accepted", "votes": 63, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wants and Needs", "line": "Heaven-sent, God-sent Least that’s what my mom says", "vault_lines": ["Least that's what my mom says"], "meaning": "Throughout his verse, Drake humorously addresses his controversial relationship with his faith: in fact,  he was raised Jewish through the family of his mother, and then attended a Jewish day school in his youth. Like the typical Jewish boy, he had a bar mitzvah at the age of 13, and even celebrated his 31st birthday in 2017 by throwing himself a “Re-Bar Mitzvah” party.\n\nDrake takes his point further by mentioning the Yeshiva (ישיבה), a Hebrew term that indicates a special type of school, dedicated to Talmudic and biblical studying and usually attended by scholars who want to train to become a rabbi and/or gain a broader understanding of religious texts.\n\nDrake is saying that he should probably be acting conservatively and fulfilling his religious obligations, rather than traveling to Ibiza, Spain, one of the world’s most notorious party destinations.", "annotation_id": "22360531", "url": "https://genius.com/22360531", "state": "accepted", "votes": 98, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wants and Needs", "line": "I’m screamin’ out “YOLO,” yeah, that’s still the motto", "vault_lines": ["I'm screamin' out \"YOLO,\" yeah, that's still the motto"], "meaning": "The term “YOLO” stands for “you only live once.” This is a shoutout to Drake as he popularized the term when he used it on his November 2011 Take Care bonus track, “The Motto”:\n\nYou only live once: that’s the motto, nigga, YOLO", "annotation_id": "22360474", "url": "https://genius.com/22360474", "state": "accepted", "votes": 163, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wants and Needs", "status": "done", "targets": 16, "clicked": 16, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-wants-and-needs-lyrics", "genius_title": "Wants and Needs"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "We Made It Freestyle", "line": "Nigga we made it, ayy We made it Nigga we made it, ayy Damn, we made it Nigga we made it, ayy We made it, ayy Nigga we made it, ayy We made it", "vault_lines": ["Now I walk into the buildin' and go off like \"Nigga we made it!\" (Go off)", "It needed a moment of silence, nigga we made it!", "Oh, we made it", "I'ma just hand her a business card and say \"Nigga we made it!\"", "Then I send a message to both of they asses like \"Nigga we made it!\"", "Ayy, we made it", "When Baka came home for the holidays, I was like \"Nigga we made it!\"", "I would just look at you dead in yo' face and say \"Nigga we made it!\"", "And my resolution for New Years is nigga we made it!", "Then I pick up my brush and I sign at the bottom like \"Nigga we made it!\"", "Nigga we made it! Damn, I'm up in Las Vegas", "Every night, fuckin' a bad bitch, nigga we made it!", "Ha, nigga we made it!", "Nigga we made it, ayy", "I look a nigga in his face and say \"Nigga we made it!\"", "Nigga we made it!", "Brrt brrt, nigga we made it", "Damn, we made it", "We made it, ayy"], "meaning": "Soulja Boy has “made it” (his single “Crank That” reached number one on the US Billboard Hot 100) and reiterates it throughout the chorus.\n\nDrake has also made it and expresses his accomplishments on songs like “Started From The Bottom,” this song is an emphasis on Drizzy’s achievements.", "annotation_id": "2606371", "url": "https://genius.com/2606371", "state": "accepted", "votes": 55, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "We Made It Freestyle", "line": "Kinda makes me wonder why the hell so many people are tryna tell me to slow down. Seems like motherfuckers should be shuttin’ the hell up and enjoyin’ the show", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This could allude to the fact that Drake had been on top of his game in 2013. With an album, tour, singles and features, it’s hard to believe that many people still want Drake to slow his momentum  and not be successful.\n\nDrake feels like these people should relax and watch what he does next because he wasn’t always at the top, remember?", "annotation_id": "2606089", "url": "https://genius.com/2606089", "state": "accepted", "votes": 52, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "We Made It Freestyle", "line": "OVO, Reps Up, and P. Reign is next up, watch Gway go crazy", "vault_lines": ["OVO, Reps Up, and P. Reign is next up, watch Gway go crazy"], "meaning": "Drake is saying P. Reign is next up on the OVO/Reps Up agenda and his hood in Toronto called Galloway will be going crazy.\n\nSimilar to an ill-fated prediction Kanye West made about Really Doe in “Diamonds from Sierra Leone”.\n\nIn “0-100/The Catch Up”, Drizzy drops a similar bar that specifically says that these forces will kick off in 2015.", "annotation_id": "2606027", "url": "https://genius.com/2606027", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "We Made It Freestyle", "line": "I swear that we made it, selloff that ting, I’m the king in Jamaica", "vault_lines": ["Oh, we made it", "Ayy, we made it", "I swear that we made it, selloff that ting, I'm the king in Jamaica", "Ha, nigga we made it!", "Nigga we made it, ayy", "Nigga we made it!", "Brrt brrt, nigga we made it", "Damn, we made it", "We made it, ayy"], "meaning": "Many Jamaicans say “ting” rather than “thing” as their accents are strong. Although he is not from Jamaica, Drizzy loves performing in Jamaica, has recorded songs there, and is very well liked. His pronunciation just reinforces his claim to the king of Jamaica.\n\n\n\nTing is also a popular grapefruit drink in Jamaica. He’s so big in Jamaica, his dominance is comparable to Ting.", "annotation_id": "2605919", "url": "https://genius.com/2605919", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "We Made It Freestyle", "line": "You don’t know how long I waited, I coulda been waitin’ on tables, my karma’s amazin’", "vault_lines": ["You don't know how long I waited, I coulda been waitin' on tables, my karma's amazin'"], "meaning": "His first mixtape came out in 2006 (Room For Improvement) but Drake didn’t blow up worldwide until 2009 when his So Far Gone mixtape was released and changed the game.\n\nHe’s saying he waited a long time to get here and if he wasn’t so lucky he could still be waiting for a break, whilst literally being a waiter in his spare time\n\n\n\nI guess he really did Start From The Bottom", "annotation_id": "2605900", "url": "https://genius.com/2605900", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "We Made It Freestyle", "line": "Then I send a message to both of they asses like “Nigga we made it!”", "vault_lines": ["It needed a moment of silence, nigga we made it!", "Oh, we made it", "Then I send a message to both of they asses like \"Nigga we made it!\"", "Ayy, we made it", "Ha, nigga we made it!", "Nigga we made it, ayy", "Nigga we made it!", "Brrt brrt, nigga we made it", "Damn, we made it", "We made it, ayy"], "meaning": "I sent ya girl a message, said I’ll see ya when I can\nShe sent me one back, but I ain’t never read it\nCause pussy’s only pussy and I get it when I need it\n\nThe girls are talking about how good the sex was with Drake but he’s more focused on his career and his accomplishments, no love for these bitches, he said this year is all business. It’s not even the first time that he’s done it:\n\nThat’s when I text her and told her I made it.", "annotation_id": "2605782", "url": "https://genius.com/2605782", "state": "accepted", "votes": 37, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "We Made It Freestyle", "line": "[Intro 1: Eastbound & Down (Kenny Powers)] The only thing I’m seein’ I’d like to put an amend on, perhaps a little more room here for the fixins, you know what I’m talkin’ about? Oh, we gon’ have a lot of fixins. We gonna have so many fuckin’ fixins up in this motherfucker, this shit gon’ go through the roof. Got damn I’m shittin’ gold these days", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XG97kfnaFOA", "annotation_id": "2605742", "url": "https://genius.com/2605742", "state": "accepted", "votes": 93, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "We Made It Freestyle", "line": "Now turn this shit down while I issue my statement It needed a moment of silence, nigga we made it!", "vault_lines": ["Now turn this shit down while I issue my statement", "It needed a moment of silence, nigga we made it!", "Oh, we made it", "Ayy, we made it", "Ha, nigga we made it!", "Nigga we made it, ayy", "Nigga we made it!", "Brrt brrt, nigga we made it", "Damn, we made it", "We made it, ayy"], "meaning": "Drake recollects his thoughts from Nothing Was The Same:\n\nI can’t even listen, you wilding\nI’d much rather sit here in silence\n\n­\n\nBench players talkin' like starters, I hate it\nStarted from the bottom, now we here, nigga, we made it\n\nDrake is the best in the game and he knows it, so when he jumps on a track other rappers should just be quiet and listen to what he has to say.\n\nNotice the beat fades away for a few seconds during this line.", "annotation_id": "2605739", "url": "https://genius.com/2605739", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "We Made It Freestyle", "line": "My family get all of my loyalty, all of my patience (Go off)", "vault_lines": ["My family get all of my loyalty, all of my patience (Go off)"], "meaning": "Fuck a fake friend, where yo real friends at\n\nDrake is loyal to the OVO family and his actual family. He is often saying that nobody else counts in his life, and even if due to his career choices he had to stay away from them, he always tries his best to spend time with them.\n\nI’ll compromise if I have to, I gotta stay with the family\n\nIn a lot of his tracks you can find reference to his mom, his uncle and his dad.", "annotation_id": "2605729", "url": "https://genius.com/2605729", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "We Made It Freestyle", "line": "Yeah, she said she workin’ for Walgreens but not in the store, at the head office The head was so good it makes sense why you work at the head office", "vault_lines": ["The head was so good it makes sense why you work at the head office", "Yeah, she said she workin' for Walgreens but not in the store, at the head office"], "meaning": "The Walgreen Company is one of the largest drug retailing chains in the United States.\n\n\n\nBy telling Drake that she works in the main corporate office as opposed to a lowly cashier at one of the pharmacies, she probably wants to make sure that she looks smarter than what Drizzy thinks.\n\nDrake connects with the previous line using a wordplay; in this case “head” means oral sex, she’s good at it so Drizzy isn’t surprised by the fact that she’s got an above-average role at Walgreens.", "annotation_id": "2605703", "url": "https://genius.com/2605703", "state": "accepted", "votes": 62, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "We Made It Freestyle", "line": "In 2007, I sat in the lobby of Motown and waited", "vault_lines": ["In 2007, I sat in the lobby of Motown and waited"], "meaning": "Before linking up with mentor and Young Money label head Lil Wayne, Drake had taken a trip to Motown’s New York headquarters to audition for Sylvia Rhone in hopes of getting signed, but Rhone opted to pass on him at the time.\n\nDrake mentioned also Sylvia in “Say What’s Real:”\n\nI’ve always been something that these labels can’t buy\nEspecially if they tryin' to take a piece of my soul\nAnd Sylvia be tellin' Tez, “Damn, Drake fly”\nAnd he just be like, “Silly motherfucker, I know\nThat was your bad, how could you pass up on ‘em?", "annotation_id": "2605690", "url": "https://genius.com/2605690", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "We Made It Freestyle", "line": "Now I walk into the buildin’ and go off like “Nigga we made it!” (Go off) When I walk through these halls, man this beat should be playin’ (Go off) I just came to make sure you not missin’ no payments", "vault_lines": ["Now I walk into the buildin' and go off like \"Nigga we made it!\" (Go off)", "When I walk through these halls, man this beat should be playin' (Go off)", "I just came to make sure you not missin' no payments", "Oh, we made it", "Ayy, we made it", "When Baka came home for the holidays, I was like \"Nigga we made it!\"", "Ha, nigga we made it!", "Nigga we made it, ayy", "Nigga we made it!", "Brrt brrt, nigga we made it", "Damn, we made it", "We made it, ayy"], "meaning": "5.5 million records later!\n\nYMCMB are notorious for not willingly paying their artists, this may be what Drake is referring to – as you might remember, Tyga recently said that he only got paid from them once.", "annotation_id": "2605676", "url": "https://genius.com/2605676", "state": "accepted", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "We Made It Freestyle", "line": "When Baka came home for the holidays, I was like “Nigga we made it!” And all of those lawyer fees, nigga I paid it (Go off)", "vault_lines": ["Now I walk into the buildin' and go off like \"Nigga we made it!\" (Go off)", "Oh, we made it", "Ayy, we made it", "When Baka came home for the holidays, I was like \"Nigga we made it!\"", "And all of those lawyer fees, nigga I paid it (Go off)", "Ha, nigga we made it!", "Nigga we made it, ayy", "Nigga we made it!", "Brrt brrt, nigga we made it", "Damn, we made it", "We made it, ayy"], "meaning": "Referring to his friend, Baka, from the outro on “From Time.” As he’s making over $20 million yearly at the moment, Drake got his brothers covered when it comes to lawyer fees.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/Drake/status/386797539971698688\n\nhttp://instagram.com/p/iXoMfzjQDg/", "annotation_id": "2605642", "url": "https://genius.com/2605642", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "We Made It Freestyle", "line": "That’s ignorant, ain’t it? Sometimes I question myself when I think ’bout the pictures I painted Then I pick up my brush and I sign at the bottom like “Nigga we made it!”", "vault_lines": ["Oh, we made it", "Ayy, we made it", "Then I pick up my brush and I sign at the bottom like \"Nigga we made it!\"", "Ha, nigga we made it!", "Nigga we made it, ayy", "Nigga we made it!", "Brrt brrt, nigga we made it", "Damn, we made it", "We made it, ayy"], "meaning": "Even though Drizzy is a Grammy award winning artist, sometimes he questions the decisions that he’s made to get where he currently is.\n\nNote, Drake is a fan of paintings, as you can tell from the cover art on his album, Take Care.\n\n\n\nRegardless of these decisions he has made, Drake knows that he’s in a good place now, so he isn’t afraid to continue to metaphorically paint more pictures. He uses this metaphor to relate to signing a deal, only with a paintbrush instead of a pen.", "annotation_id": "2605630", "url": "https://genius.com/2605630", "state": "accepted", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
