{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "That’s Just How I Feel", "line": "I used to put chains on all of the necks of my broskis, my OG’s", "vault_lines": ["I used to put chains on all of the necks of my broskis, my OG's"], "meaning": "This is a reference to A$AP Rocky and other members of the public Rap civil\n\nIn a 2026 interview with DJ akemics, he explained how Drake gave him a Yams chain to celebrate and pay respects to former A$AP member A$AP Yams who passed away", "annotation_id": "38858401", "url": "https://genius.com/38858401", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "That’s Just How I Feel", "line": "MRI machine scanning my knee Like, how long you been runnin’ the streets? For real, yeah", "vault_lines": ["MRI machine scanning my knee"], "meaning": "Drake has had multiple knee injuries, most recently in 2020 when he had surgery to repair a torn meniscus, which delayed his Certified Lover Boy project’s release until 2021. He connects this with a reoccurring theme in the song, that he has been on top of the rap game for several years now with no competition (running the game). Someone who physically runs the streets, like how he “runs” the rap game may also suffer a knee injury.", "annotation_id": "36946896", "url": "https://genius.com/36946896", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "That’s Just How I Feel", "line": "And you old niggas think you can touch me?", "vault_lines": ["And you old niggas think you can touch me?"], "meaning": "Drake is likely talking about Pusha T, Kanye West, Pharrell Williams, and Rick Ross, as they have all recently had problems with drake.\n\nIn the song, “What Would Pluto Do?” Drake says something similar to this.\n\nYou know I’m beefin' with much older guys (Much older guys)\n\nDrake is saying that these rappers cannot touch him on the charts, and also shows that their beef continues.", "annotation_id": "36862159", "url": "https://genius.com/36862159", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "That’s Just How I Feel", "line": "Big steppin’ in whatever country", "vault_lines": ["Big steppin' in whatever country"], "meaning": "This line is another subtle jab at Kendrick, referencing his 2022 studio album Mr. Morale & The Big Steppers.\n\nIt also ties back to their ongoing feud specifically Drake’s diss track “Push Ups,” where he dissed Kendrick with the bar:\n\n“How the fuck you big steppin’ with a size 7 mens on?”", "annotation_id": "36861749", "url": "https://genius.com/36861749", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "That’s Just How I Feel", "line": "Not the same way y’all fucked up last summer", "vault_lines": ["Not the same way y’all fucked up last summer"], "meaning": "Drake is referring to the 2024 Rap Civil War and how he fucked up on trusting too many people.", "annotation_id": "36824253", "url": "https://genius.com/36824253", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "That’s Just How I Feel", "line": "Eighteen years and we haven’t been rusty", "vault_lines": ["Eighteen years and we haven't been rusty"], "meaning": "Drake’s first mixtapes dropped in 2006 and 2007 with “Room for Improvement” and “Comeback Season”. Since then and for the last 18 years, Drake has relentlessly recorded and released albums, gone on world tours, and stayed on top of the rap game with no extended period of time off. Because Drake has been running the game for so long with no breaks, he has not become out of practice (rusty).", "annotation_id": "36828894", "url": "https://genius.com/36828894", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "That’s Just How I Feel", "line": "When I come back from tour this fall Will you really had saved it for me?", "vault_lines": ["When I come back from tour this fall", "Will you really had saved it for me?"], "meaning": "Drake is currently on a UK/EU tour that ends on September 23, in Hamburg, Germany. Drake is asking the woman if she is saving herself/her body all for him, and waiting for him to return from his tour. Her reply comes in the next line in the affirmative when she texts ‘oui oui oui’ (yes yes yes in french)", "annotation_id": "36827485", "url": "https://genius.com/36827485", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "That’s Just How I Feel", "line": "And my broski just re-did his hairline, now, he out here fuckin’ the same hoes as me, for real, yeah", "vault_lines": ["And my broski just re-did his hairline, now, he out here fuckin' the same hoes as me, for real, yeah"], "meaning": "This line likely refers to either Future the Prince or 40, as both have had hair transplants and both are close Drake associates. Since his improved appearance due to the procedure, Drake’s broski is having sex with the same women Drake does.\n\nAlternatively, this could be an insincere use of “broski” and instead be yet another jab at LeBron James. It is widely presumed that LeBron received a hair transplant to “redo” his hairline.\n\nLeBron has been married to his wife Savannah since 2013. However, in a January 2025 livestream, DJ Akademiks made several claims including that Drake helped facilitate encounters between LeBron and several women while he was in Toronto, and engaged in “two-man” encounters with LeBron and the same women, which could explain the second part of this line as the two “fucking the same hoes”.\n\nRecently, Drake has repeatedly dissed LeBron including most recently in the song “What did I miss” from ICEMAN episode 1.", "annotation_id": "36824410", "url": "https://genius.com/36824410", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "That’s Just How I Feel", "line": "I wonder how long I’ll be at the top if they don’t kill me", "vault_lines": ["I wonder how long I'll be at the top if they don't kill me"], "meaning": "Reigning at the top of the music industry for over a decade, Drake implies that he is confident that he will be able to maintain this status for many years to come and that the only way for someone to dethrone him is through extreme measures such as killing him.", "annotation_id": "36823915", "url": "https://genius.com/36823915", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "That’s Just How I Feel", "line": "I wonder how long it’ll take ’em to count out two thousand million (Aha! Like that?)", "vault_lines": ["I wonder how long it'll take 'em to count out two thousand million (Aha!"], "meaning": "Drake’s net worth has long been a subject of speculation. As of 2025, most sources generally estimate it to be around $250 to $300 million. However, the numbers don’t seem to quite add up. Around 2021, Drake signed a massive deal with Universal Music Group (UMG) reportedly worth about $400 million, which alone suggests his accumulated wealth is substantially higher. Additionally, Drake owns an extraordinarily luxurious mansion in Toronto known as “The Embassy,” valued at around $100 million.\n\nDespite these figures, Drake does not publicly flaunt billionaire status, even though speculation exists that he may have already crossed or is close to crossing the billionaire threshold. This could be a subtle confirmation that he actually did it, possibly even multiplied by two.\n\nOn another note, this figure could be what Drake is looking to make out of his case against UMG in damages, or even the amount he is seeking if he were to extend his contract with the label.", "annotation_id": "36823813", "url": "https://genius.com/36823813", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "That’s Just How I Feel", "line": "Shout out to Kiki, she love me", "vault_lines": ["Shout out to Kiki, she love me"], "meaning": "A nod to Drake’s 2018 hit “In My Feelings”, where he famously asked “Kiki, do you love me?” widely believed to reference singer Keshia Chanté, a known past flame. In this line, Drake flips the question into a confident statement, suggesting the love is mutual now, or at least remembered fondly.", "annotation_id": "36821667", "url": "https://genius.com/36821667", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "That’s Just How I Feel", "line": "[Part I]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake’s license plate “355554 VA” works like a cryptic flex in plain sight. “VA” can reference both Virginia (Pusha T’s home state) and Virginia Williams (Pusha’s wife). The numbers aren’t random either—35 + 55 + 54 = 143, a numeric shorthand for “I love you” (1 = I, 4 = Love, 3 = You). Put together, the plate reads as “I love you, Virginia,” a layered subliminal aimed right at Pusha.", "annotation_id": "36820535", "url": "https://genius.com/36820535", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "That’s Just How I Feel", "line": "Probably would slow me down if I carry my trophies", "vault_lines": ["Probably would slow me down if I carry my trophies"], "meaning": "Drake has accumulated countless awards throughout his illustrious career, including 5 grammy awards and a record 41 billboard music awards. If he was to carry around these awards with him, they’d slow him down because they would be cumbersome.", "annotation_id": "36818488", "url": "https://genius.com/36818488", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
