{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "What Would Pluto Do", "line": "Last time I saw you, you was talkin’ about reduction Lookin’ at you now, I see you ain’t get rid of Lookin’ at you now, I see you ain’t get rid of nothin’", "vault_lines": ["Last time I saw you, you was talkin' about reduction", "Lookin' at you now, I see you ain't get rid of", "Lookin' at you now, I see you ain't get rid of nothin'"], "meaning": "The last time he saw this girl she talked to him about breast reduction surgery. However, now that he has seen her again more recently he notices she did not follow through with the surgery.", "annotation_id": "29733506", "url": "https://genius.com/29733506", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "What Would Pluto Do", "line": "Wigglin’ back into my old ways", "vault_lines": ["Wigglin' back into my old ways"], "meaning": "Drake is referring to his past gig with the Wiggles in this bar. He wore the red shirt I think.", "annotation_id": "29732121", "url": "https://genius.com/29732121", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "What Would Pluto Do", "line": "New Rolls, bought it for the thrill Too lazy to even change out the wheel", "vault_lines": ["New Rolls, bought it for the thrill", "Too lazy to even change out the wheel"], "meaning": "In this lyric, Drake is referring to how he was “too lazy” to take up Rolls-Royce on their offer to upgrade the steering wheel on its flagship car, the Phantom—of which Drake owns a custom version—to a thicker form, for which they provide a price on request.\n\nThe thicker steering wheel option at 4mm thicker than the standard steering wheel gives an increased feeling of grip and a more dynamic feel.\n\nSource: Rolls-Royce", "annotation_id": "29731295", "url": "https://genius.com/29731295", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "What Would Pluto Do", "line": "Get inside and bend a dick just like the pope (Mm)", "vault_lines": ["Get inside and bend a dick just like the pope (Mm)"], "meaning": "Drake cleverly plays on the homophone sound of «bend a dick» and «Benedict», which was the name given to the former Pope of the Catholic Church and Bishop of Rome between 2005-2013, Pope Benedict XVI.\n\n\n\nPictured: Pope Benedict XVI", "annotation_id": "29728228", "url": "https://genius.com/29728228", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "What Would Pluto Do", "line": "Lost my Sprite deal ‘cause Wayne kept pourin’ fives", "vault_lines": ["Lost my Sprite deal 'cause Wayne kept pourin' fives"], "meaning": "Drake has partnered with soft drink brand, Sprite, back in 2010 and more recently in 2023, Sprite sponsored Drake’s “It’s All A Blur” Tour.\n\nPourin fives means to pour 5oz of promethazine in a drink to make lean (usually the drink is a 20oz sprite).\n\nDrake is saying that Lil Wayne making Dirty Sprite caused him to lose his Sprite deal.", "annotation_id": "29727748", "url": "https://genius.com/29727748", "state": "accepted", "votes": 67, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "What Would Pluto Do", "line": "You know I’m beefin’ with much older guys (Much older guys) ’Fore I catch up with them, then probably Ayy, what, R.I.P. them fuck niggas (Damn, what) What, really hate a rap nigga Let’s not even talk about them fuck niggas, fuck them", "vault_lines": ["You know I'm beefin' with much older guys (Much older guys)", "'Fore I catch up with them, then probably", "Ayy, what, R.I.P. them fuck niggas (Damn, what)", "What, really hate a rap nigga", "Let's not even talk about them fuck niggas, fuck them"], "meaning": "Drake references his beef with Pusha T, Pharrell Williams and potentially Kanye West – all being over 45. Drake claims he doesn’t care if they live or die after how much his hatred has developed.", "annotation_id": "29726742", "url": "https://genius.com/29726742", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "What Would Pluto Do", "line": "So the question is, the question is (Yeah) What would Pluto do? He’d fuck the ho, so I did it (Yeah, yeah) What would Pluto do? He’d fuck the ho, so I did it (Yeah, yeah) What would Pluto do? He definitely fuckin’ on this ho, ayy", "vault_lines": ["So the question is, the question is (Yeah)", "What would Pluto do? He definitely fuckin' on this ho", "What would Pluto do? He'd fuck the ho, so I did it (Yeah, yeah)", "What would Pluto do? He definitely fuckin' on this ho, ayy"], "meaning": "The phrase “What would Jesus do?” is common among adherents of Christianity, who uses it as a reminder of their belief in a moral imperative to act in a manner demonstrating the love of Jesus through their actions.\nDrake asks himself what would Pluto do instead, referring to one of rapper Future’s many aliases. He answers the question himself, as he knows Future would go through with it and have sex with this woman.\nThere’s plenty of reasons to believe that would be Future’s course of action:\n\nCruelest thing to do is to be cool with a nigga and fuckin' on his bitch\nI know niggas’d do it to me so I’m always gon' send that hit\n- Future – Rockstar Chainz\n\n\n\nIt’s worth mentioning that this might be a shot at Drake’s rival, Pusha T, who made a similar title song called “What Would Meek Do”, refering to the rapper Meek Mill.", "annotation_id": "29725698", "url": "https://genius.com/29725698", "state": "accepted", "votes": 72, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "What Would Pluto Do", "line": "Think I’m ’Luminati ’cause I’m rich, well, okay", "vault_lines": ["Think I'm 'Luminati 'cause I'm rich, well, okay"], "meaning": "The Illuminati is a conspiracy theory about a secret society that conspire to rule the world behind the scenes. Many people believe those who are heavily rich are apart of the Illuminati and that is the reason they have continued success and wealth. Many who believe in this conspiracy theory will mention Drake as a member due to his high amount of wealth.\n\nAs Drake is one of the biggest rappers in the world, it is no doubt that he has a high amount of wealth. In 2022, he reportedly made $500 million off one record deal alone and he seemingly confirmed this record deal in his song “Major Distribution” stating:\n\nFive-hundred million, just for Aubrey", "annotation_id": "29725373", "url": "https://genius.com/29725373", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "What Would Pluto Do", "line": "Baby girl, Adonis need a sister, okay And my baby mama out the picture, okay", "vault_lines": ["Baby girl, Adonis need a sister, okay", "And my baby mama out the picture, okay"], "meaning": "Adonis Graham is Drake’s son. Adonis also created the cover to For All The Dogs and even gives vocals on two tracks of the album – “Daylight” and “First Person Shooter”. Drake suggests that he wouldn’t mind raising another child, predominantly a sister, alongside Adonis but would not go back to Adonis' mother for a sibling. Adonis' mother is Sophie Brussaux and use to be a former porn star before becoming a painter. Drake has stated in the past that he feels ashamed having a child with a porn star as he barely knew Sophie, only meeting her twice before Adonis' birth. Drake suggests that he would rather have Adonis' sister to be birthed by a different woman who Drake has a stronger connection and bond with rather than going back to Sophie.", "annotation_id": "29725370", "url": "https://genius.com/29725370", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "What Would Pluto Do", "line": "Droppin’ two Cialis in a liquid, okay", "vault_lines": ["Droppin' two Cialis in a liquid, okay"], "meaning": "Cialis, scientifically knows as Tadalafil, is a medication used for people with sexual dysfunction. After taking it, people’s libido and sexual drive increases significantly. It belongs to the same class of medication as the famous Viagra.\n\nNormally taken as one, Drake mentions the use of two Cialis to boost up his sexual drive. He later implies that this drive and his recklessness might result in having a baby, possibly a sister for Adonis.", "annotation_id": "29724982", "url": "https://genius.com/29724982", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "What Would Pluto Do", "line": "Diamonds in the sky", "vault_lines": ["Diamonds in the sky"], "meaning": "This line is suggesting for Drake’s friends or girlfriends to put their jewellery in the sky to show it off, as Drake is often known for the deluxe and expensive jewellery he gets for women and his friends.\nWhile the lyrics are open for interpretation, this line could also be considered a reference to Kanye West’s “Diamond’s from Sierra Leone” in which he raps: ‘throw your diamonds in the sky if you feel the vibe.’\nThis suggestion could be unlikely, however, given their possibly ongoing rap feud. Although they supposedly quashed their feud at their “Free Larry Hoover” benefit concert in which they performed together, Drake has nonetheless made a number of potential sneak disses to Kanye in some songs released since the concert.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=92FCRmggNqQ\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VENMfOLxkZw", "annotation_id": "29724862", "url": "https://genius.com/29724862", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
