{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Comeback Season", "line": "[Produced by Nottz]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The sample in this song comes from Idris Muhammad’s “Could Heaven Ever Be Like This?”\n\nAt the very beginning of Drake’s song, you can hear the introduction to this track. This same portion also serves as a breakdown used throughout the beat.\n\nhttp://youtu.be/a96OgR6hjDY", "annotation_id": "3386936", "url": "https://genius.com/3386936", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Comeback Season", "line": "I’m clearin’ the air, I’m a humidifier", "vault_lines": ["I'm clearin' the air, I'm a humidifier"], "meaning": "Contrary to this excellent multi-syllabic punchline’s intended meaning, humidifiers don’t actually “clear the air.” They just increase humidity to help out with nasal congestion and dry skin and lips…( maybe Gucci Mane should have his own personal humidifier with him at all times?). Perhaps he meant to say “exhaust fan,” but he grossly misspelled it while typing on his Blackberry", "annotation_id": "48057", "url": "https://genius.com/48057", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Comeback Season", "line": "Can’t help it, I been brainwashed to kill ’em all", "vault_lines": ["Can't help it, I been brainwashed to kill 'em all"], "meaning": "This song, and titular mixtape, “Comeback Season” was released in 2008. Drake references Gyllenhaal’s performance in Donnie Darko from 2001, whereby a troubled teenager (Jake) is plagued by visions of a large bunny rabbit that manipulates him to commit a series of crimes, after narrowly escaping a bizarre accident.  Drake often uses movie plots as punchlines years after the movie was popular, as can be found in “Right Above It” and “9AM in Dallas”", "annotation_id": "39986", "url": "https://genius.com/39986", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Comeback Season", "line": "I got ice all over my windshield", "vault_lines": ["I got ice all over my windshield"], "meaning": "This line, and the next three lines, are references to one of his earliest songs “Come Winter” off Room for Improvement.  This ice on his windshield and the cold winter are metaphors for how much life changes, according to Drake, in Toronto during the winter, as mentioned in “Come Winter”.  However, Drake’s saying that he’s going to keep bringing that heat (metaphorically)", "annotation_id": "39860", "url": "https://genius.com/39860", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Comeback Season", "line": "We go by the name of A-T-F", "vault_lines": ["We go by the name of A-T-F"], "meaning": "ATF (All Things Fresh) is Drake’s official Fansite created by close friends and affiliates", "annotation_id": "37557", "url": "https://genius.com/37557", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
