{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "7969 Santa", "line": "You know he comin’ to the H-Town to tear the roof off that motherfucker", "vault_lines": ["You know he comin' to the H-Town to tear the roof off that motherfucker"], "meaning": "H-Town is a nickname for the city of Houston, Texas.", "annotation_id": "30267400", "url": "https://genius.com/30267400", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "7969 Santa", "line": "That’s that new Teezo Touchdown, “Stray”", "vault_lines": ["That's that new Teezo Touchdown, \"Stray\""], "meaning": "Snoop Dogg acts as a radio DJ premiering the outro as a new song by Teezo Touchdown called “Stray”.", "annotation_id": "30085007", "url": "https://genius.com/30085007", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "7969 Santa", "line": "Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, damn Damn, that’s how you’re dealin’ with me, damn Damn, that’s how you’re, that’s how you’re Ayy, look, look", "vault_lines": ["Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, damn", "Damn, that's how you're dealin' with me, damn", "Damn, that's how you'rе dealin' with me, damn", "Damn, that's how you're, that's how you're"], "meaning": "During the downfall of a relationship, most girls have their own way of coping. In this song, Drake makes it known that the girl he used to  mess with is lowering her standards and doing things she wouldn’t normally do. All in spite to get back at him.\n\n“Damn, that’s how you dealing with me? Damn”\n\nYou can hear the disappointment in his voice in this, alluring to the fact that he was not expecting the girl he once loved to go out of her way to get back at him, or to give herself self gratification by devoting her attention to other men & activities. In the song he explains what she has done to give him such deep disappointment.", "annotation_id": "29981482", "url": "https://genius.com/29981482", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "7969 Santa", "line": "Because you really think you out here movin’ stealth", "vault_lines": ["Because you really think you out here movin' stealth"], "meaning": "Drake is implying that the girl he’s messing with thinks she’s getting away with the stuff she’s doing behind his back, but at the end of the day he knows exactly what she’s up to. Hence the next bar.", "annotation_id": "29981470", "url": "https://genius.com/29981470", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "7969 Santa", "line": "(Baby) Dogs will be dogs (You know I’m in the streets) Though we may roam (But I promise) Leave the door open Tonight, I’m comin’ home (I’m comin’ home) Dogs will be dogs (I know you feel me, baby) No leash in sight Leave the door open I’m comin’ home tonight (I mean the dogs) Ah-ooh, ah-woo Ah-ooh, ah-woo (I mean the dogs) Ah-ooh (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["(Baby) Dogs will be dogs", "(You know I'm in the streets) Though we may roam", "(But I promise) Leave the door open", "Tonight, I'm comin' home (I'm comin' home)", "No leash in sight", "I'm comin' home tonight (I mean the dogs)"], "meaning": "Teezo uses the metaphor of “dogs” whilst paraphrasing the famous saying “Boys will be boys”, meaning that you can expect from boys a behavior peculiar to boys.\n\nIn the song’s context, Teezo alludes to staying out late at Delilah—the nightclub located at 7969 Santa Monica Blvd, West Hollywood, which Drake raps about throughout the track—and potentially hooking up with women other than his significant other.\n\nTeezo asks his partner to metaphorically, and quite literally, “leave the door open” as if he were a dog so that he can return to her, as despite his urges to partake in fornication and other late-night activities with Drake and his crew, or “dogs,” he will forever belong to her.\n\n“A dog always find his way back home and it’s so true”", "annotation_id": "29968503", "url": "https://genius.com/29968503", "state": "pending", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "7969 Santa", "line": "Who the fuck is that? It’s a disguise", "vault_lines": ["Who the fuck is that? It's a disguise"], "meaning": "Drake looks disappointed with Lilahpi after he publicly wished her a happy birthday and realized that she wasn’t who he thought she was", "annotation_id": "29845932", "url": "https://genius.com/29845932", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
