{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "7969 Santa", "line": "BARK Radio, live from Chapel Hill", "vault_lines": ["And you're listenin' to BARK Radio, live from Chapel Hill"], "meaning": "Chappel Hill is a small Texas city in-between Houston and Austin known for its beautiful bluebonnets, Texas’s state flower.\n\nhttps://visitbrenhamtexas.com/beyond-brenham/chappell-hill/#:~:text=Home%20of%20the%20Official%20Bluebonnet%20Festival%20of%20Texas!&text=Today%2C%20this%20quaint%20historic%20town,Festival%20and%20Fall%20Scarecrow%20Festival.", "annotation_id": "29812033", "url": "https://genius.com/29812033", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "7969 Santa", "line": "Beaumont", "vault_lines": ["For all the dogs that's drivin' around in Beaumont"], "meaning": "Teezo Touchdown (Aaron [Ay-ren] LaShane Thomas) was born on Halloween of 1992 in Beaumont, Texas. Area code 409 (see 5 O’Clock), Beaumont is a small town near Louisiana, & prior to his becoming famous, his dad predicted he would put it “on the map.”  📍", "annotation_id": "29805735", "url": "https://genius.com/29805735", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "7969 Santa", "line": "I don’t like what you did to your lips", "vault_lines": ["I don't like what you did to your lips", "I don't like what you did on them trips"], "meaning": "On theme with the rest of this album calling out his famous exes, it’s hard to not read this as a shot at Kylie Jenner who is famous (among other things) for her cosmetic surgery especially to her lips.\n\nIn a more generic way its hard not see this as calling out some IG thot for sucking some rich dick to have a vacation. Which is aligned with the previous line about said vacation.", "annotation_id": "29801508", "url": "https://genius.com/29801508", "state": "pending", "votes": -4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "7969 Santa", "line": "I don’t like what you did to your lips", "vault_lines": ["I don't like what you did to your lips", "I don't like what you did on them trips"], "meaning": "Lilah pi got bad lip fillers and Drake didn’t like it\n\n\n\nher before & after. The Boy is right\n\n\n\nOn theme with the rest of this album calling out his famous exes, it’s hard to not read this as a shot at Kylie Jenner who is famous (among other things) for her cosmetic surgery especially to her lips.\n\nIn a more generic way its hard not see this as calling out some IG thot for sucking some rich dick to have a vacation. Which is aligned with the previous line about said vacation.", "annotation_id": "29801507", "url": "https://genius.com/29801507", "state": "pending", "votes": -5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "7969 Santa", "line": "Blame this shit on bein’ twenty-five", "vault_lines": ["Blame this shit on bein' twenty-five", "Blame that shit on bein' twenty-five"], "meaning": "The girl Drake talks about is probably Lilah Pi, who dated Drake. Meeting at Delilah going to have her on his mind because of the similarity between the names Delilah and Lilah.\nLilah is 25 years old, so the line “Blame this shit on bein' twenty-five” might be another hint.\n\nDrake mentioned Lilah previously on J Hus‘ track “Who Told You” and on a track from his own album, Honestly, Nevermind, “Flight’s Booked”:\n\n\nI find love and it slowly dies\nSo Lilah Pi, don’t make my eye cry\n- Who Told You\n\nLilah\nI know it’s getting late\nAnd I’m struggling to let go\n- Flight’s Booked", "annotation_id": "29790831", "url": "https://genius.com/29790831", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "7969 Santa", "line": "I don’t like what you did on them trips", "vault_lines": ["I don't like what you did to your lips", "I don't like what you did on them trips"], "meaning": "This line might be a foreshadowing for the track “Bahamas Promises” later on the album, on which Drake laments that an ex of his ruined a Bahamas trip.\n\n\nYou fucked up our Bahamas trip― Drake – Bahamas Promises", "annotation_id": "29765927", "url": "https://genius.com/29765927", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "7969 Santa", "line": "We got some new Drake and SZA comin’ up", "vault_lines": ["We got some new Drake and SZA comin' up"], "meaning": "The track after this, “Slime You Out” is a Drake and SZA collaboration and is the album’s lead single.\n\nInterestingly, another BARK Radio segment also appears at the end “All The Parties” which precedes the album’s other single, “8am in Charlotte.”", "annotation_id": "29732057", "url": "https://genius.com/29732057", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "7969 Santa", "line": "Zack keep sayin’, “Meet at seven-nine”", "vault_lines": ["Zack keep sayin', \"Meet at seven-nine\""], "meaning": "Zack Bia, Drake’s friend, is a promoter in Los Angeles and works for “H.Wood Group”, which also owns “Delilah”, a nightclub in West Hollywood which addressed at 7969 Santa Monica Blvd.\n\n\n\nZack is telling Drake to meet at Delilah, so they can drink and forget about these women who are giving Drake problems and causing distress.", "annotation_id": "29729588", "url": "https://genius.com/29729588", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "7969 Santa", "line": "All you pitbulls should know by now that hundreds in a roll look like tuna in a bowl to ’em", "vault_lines": ["All you pitbulls should know by now that hundreds in a roll look like tuna in a bowl to 'em"], "meaning": "Long Beach, California and Vienna, Austria connect!\n\nSnoop compares the image of a stack of United States one-hundred-dollar bills to finely-cut tuna in a bowl.\n\nI’m not so sure.\n\nA similar and perhaps more accurate comparison was made by the Austrian rapper Yung Hurn on his 2018 song “Lachs Anthem,” where he raps:\n\nIn der Hand ein Lachs\n\nTranslating from German, this roughly means, “Got a salmon in my hand,” and is a reference to the orange hue of 10 euro notes, which resemble a filleted salmon when many are stacked.", "annotation_id": "29726954", "url": "https://genius.com/29726954", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "7969 Santa", "line": "[Outro: Snoop Dogg]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Full circle moment for Snoop Dogg. Despite the namesake, he had a mock radio deejay for his earlier albums like Doggystyle (1993). Instead of BARK Radio, the radio station from Snoop’s albums was W-Ballz. Skits from those albums segue into an upcoming song from the album. The deejay, and his alter ego DJ EZ-Dick was performed by the late Ricky Harris.", "annotation_id": "29725962", "url": "https://genius.com/29725962", "state": "pending", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "7969 Santa", "line": "Got you out here movin’ waist like a belt", "vault_lines": ["Got you out here movin' waste like a belt"], "meaning": "“Waste” has been used as a homonym for waist to refer to the “belt.”", "annotation_id": "29725844", "url": "https://genius.com/29725844", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "7969 Santa", "line": "(Shit I don’t like)", "vault_lines": ["I don't like what you did to your lips", "I don't like the tone of your replies (Shit I don't like)", "I don't like the look that's in your eyes (Shit I don't like)", "I don't like you tellin' just one side (Shit I don't like)", "I don't like the fact you never cry (Shit I don't like)", "I don't like what you did on them trips"], "meaning": "This samples from Chief Keef’s March 2012 hit “I Don’t Like”, featuring Lil Reese:\n\nA fuck nigga, that’s that shit I don’t like (Bang-bang)\nA snitch nigga, that’s that shit I don’t like (Bang-bang)\nA bitch nigga, that’s that shit I don’t like (Bang-bang)\nSneak dissers, that’s that shit I don’t like (Bang-bang)\n\nhttps://youtu.be/2WcRXJ4piHg\n\nKeef also appears on the 16th track of this album, “All the Parties”.", "annotation_id": "29724691", "url": "https://genius.com/29724691", "state": "accepted", "votes": 55, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "7969 Santa", "status": "done", "targets": 20, "clicked": 20, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-7969-santa-lyrics", "genius_title": "7969 Santa"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "[Verse 1: Drake]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This first verse has the same lyrics as the song before it National Treasures. It serves as a transition between the two songs", "annotation_id": "40501613", "url": "https://genius.com/40501613", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "I know I just gotta adapt, ayy", "vault_lines": ["I know I just gotta adapt, ayy"], "meaning": "This line captures the core theme of ICEMAN: survival through strategic evolution. Following intense rap feuds and corporate battles, Drake realizes he can no longer be vulnerable. To protect himself, he must harden his exterior, numb himself to the noise, and adapt to a colder reality.", "annotation_id": "40003224", "url": "https://genius.com/40003224", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "I’m talkin’ spicy, hot, sizzlin’", "vault_lines": ["I'm talkin' spicy, hot, sizzlin'"], "meaning": "The subliminal continues. “Spicy, hot, sizzlin’” plays on “flaming” (slang for flamboyantly gay).\n\n“Don’t stick around if you visitin’” warns the girl or the listener to avoid the implied “freak off” or physical risks tied to the earlier fissure reference. This is classic IYKYK wordplay. The four lines work together as one layered diss.", "annotation_id": "39938558", "url": "https://genius.com/39938558", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "Your boyfriend a fisherman, that’s just the word in the industry Don’t mean to be in y’all business", "vault_lines": ["Your boyfriend a fisherman, that's just the word in the industry", "Don't mean to be in y'all business"], "meaning": "Drake uses “fisherman” as a pun on “fissureman.” This is an industry slang rumor implying the boyfriend is secretly gay or on the down low.\nIt references an anal fissure (a tear in the anal lining often associated with receptive anal sex).\n\n“Don’t mean to be in y’all business” serves as a tongue in cheek disclaimer while he spreads the gossip anyway.", "annotation_id": "39938536", "url": "https://genius.com/39938536", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "Bank tellers better stay clocked in Bank tellers better", "vault_lines": ["Bank tellers better stay clocked in"], "meaning": "He is putting a contrast of how long it takes to count the Billions of dollars funds if he was to cash out.\n\nBank tellers would need to keep clocking, reporting for work to continue counting the cash, even if it means switching shifts.\n\nThis continues the line of “Bank withdrawal need a Duffle Bag”\n\nHe is over the counter withdrawing Billions of Dollars and bank tellers just counting and counting and counting to make the withdrawal.", "annotation_id": "39919272", "url": "https://genius.com/39919272", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "You pussies could never get back with the gang", "vault_lines": ["You pussies could never get back with the gang"], "meaning": "Straight dig at people who he considered friends but faltered on him in 2024 when he had a scuffle with Kendrick Lamar.\n\nHe is letting them know off the bat that no amends will ever be made, they chose a side. J.Cole is part of this group as Drake has also added along the album, even has a song named Burning Bridges.\n\nHe does not want people he thought he could never question his friendship with him try to reconcile after the 2024 feud he had with Kendrick Lamar.", "annotation_id": "39919114", "url": "https://genius.com/39919114", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "It’s B’s on the table, B’s on the table B’s on the table, B’s on the table", "vault_lines": ["There's B's on the table, B's on the table (Yeah)", "B's on thе table (Okay then), B's on the tablе", "What did they put on the table?", "(B's on the table, B's on the table) Yeah, what?", "What? B's on the table", "It's B's on the table, B's on the table", "B's on the table, B's on the table"], "meaning": "Drake’s current UMG deal — reportedly worth $400 million and signed in 2022 — covers recordings, publishing, merchandise, and visual media. The triple album drop is widely read as the move to fulfill those remaining obligations and walk.\n\n“B’s” means billions which is reportedly the amount awaiting on the other side of that exit. Reports emerged within days of ICEMAN dropping that Drake had been in advanced talks to negotiate a $2 billion private-equity deal set to take effect once his UMG contract concludes.\n\nEverything Drake did between the beef and ICEMAN — the 100 gigabytes of archival content released through his burner account, the self-funded rollout, the CN Tower projection, the four livestreamed episodes, the simultaneous triple drop — reads as a deliberate audition that he can move units and execute at the highest level without the machine behind him.", "annotation_id": "39906803", "url": "https://genius.com/39906803", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "Don’t stick around if you visitin’", "vault_lines": ["Don't stick around if you visitin'"], "meaning": "No love being shown by Drizzy in Toronto to anyone including rappers, actors, entertainers and all others who chose a side. Handle your business and leave on your plane, train or automobile", "annotation_id": "39869443", "url": "https://genius.com/39869443", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "Kevin Hart liquor, he shook, I’ma put you in sticky predicaments", "vault_lines": ["Kevin Hart liquor, he shook, I'ma put you in sticky predicaments"], "meaning": "Kevin Hart launched his own tequila brand Gran Coramino but the liquor reference is really just the setup for a subliminal at JAY-Z.\n\n\n\nAt the 2013 NBA All-Star Weekend in Houston, Kevin Hart accidentally spilled an entire pitcher of juice all over both Jay and Beyoncé.. Shocked, Jay replied, “Are you kidding me, Kev?”\n\nHart’s famous sticky predicament involved spilling all over the man Drake has been targeting throughout ICEMAN.", "annotation_id": "39857835", "url": "https://genius.com/39857835", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "I’m used to this, I’m numb to that", "vault_lines": ["I'm used to this, I'm numb to that"], "meaning": "Inference to drake’s song with future called « Used to this »\n\nAlso, that song has a line « thought they had my back against the wall", "annotation_id": "39854850", "url": "https://genius.com/39854850", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "There’s no need to check where the temperature is You know what it is if you double back", "vault_lines": ["There's no need to check where the temperature is", "You know what it is if you double back"], "meaning": "VERY clever wordplay here tying into the previous bar that mentions the 16th—the freezing temperature for water is 32°F, so by doubling back the previously mentioned number (aka multiplying it by 2), you get the temperature needed for ice(man) to exist: 16 x 2 = 32\n\nThe double entendre here is that if you double back (aka return to) the previous bar, you’d see there’s no need to check Drake’s temperature (aka demeanor), he’s cold (aka distant).", "annotation_id": "39851746", "url": "https://genius.com/39851746", "state": "pending", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "Go to the hotel right after your game Or come to your show and get back on the plane", "vault_lines": ["Go to the hotel right after your game", "Or come to your show and get back on the plane"], "meaning": "This recycles his lyrics from “National Treasures,” where he fires at DeMar DeRozan and Kendrick Lamar:\n\nGo to the hotel right after your game\nCome do your show and get back on the plane\nBut don’t stick around in the 6ix\nDon’t stick around in the 6ix", "annotation_id": "39845007", "url": "https://genius.com/39845007", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "Bank withdrawal, need a duffle bag What is the offer they said? What did they put on the table? What does that say on that paper? Fuck that, they gotta double that, triple that", "vault_lines": ["Bank withdrawal, need a duffle bag", "What is the offer they said?", "What did they put on the table?", "What does that say on that paper?", "Fuck that, they gotta double that, triple that", "(B's on the table, B's on the table) Yeah, what?", "What? B's on the table", "It's B's on the table, B's on the table", "B's on the table, B's on the table"], "meaning": "Drake flexes the enormous amount of money and leverage he has in the music industry, making it clear that standard offers are no longer enough for someone at his level. The imagery of needing a duffle bag emphasizes how excessive the cash and deal sizes have become.\n\nThe back and forth about offers and paperwork sounds like label executives or business partners presenting contracts, but Drake dismisses them almost instantly, implying that his value is far beyond what’s currently being proposed. The tone comes across as confident, demanding, and fully aware of the power he holds in negotiations.", "annotation_id": "39839598", "url": "https://genius.com/39839598", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "This contract talk is fryin’ my brain The numbers they talkin’ are actually insane", "vault_lines": ["This contract talk is fryin' my brain", "The numbers they talkin' are actually insane"], "meaning": "Drake sounds mentally exhausted by all the behind the scenes business talks and contract negotiations happening around him. Even though the money is huge, the constant discussions and pressure seem to be taking a toll on him.\n\nThe “insane” numbers also tie into the title “B’s on the Table,” which could be Drake hinting that the offers being discussed are in the billions. It reinforces the idea that his value in the industry has reached a level where the business side of his career is almost unreal.", "annotation_id": "39839553", "url": "https://genius.com/39839553", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "Can’t even talk to my dogs, can’t even talk to my bitch Sometimes, I sit in the parking garage and I talk to my watch or I talk to my whip", "vault_lines": ["Can't even talk to my dogs, can't even talk to my bitch", "Sometimes, I sit in the parking garage and I talk to my watch or I talk to my whip"], "meaning": "Drake is at a point where his closest friends can’t help him express his inner thoughts and feelings so instead he talks to his prized possessions to make up for people not understanding him.", "annotation_id": "39837821", "url": "https://genius.com/39837821", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "Better treat me like Shayne Coplan", "vault_lines": ["Better treat me like Shayne Coplan"], "meaning": "Shayne Coplan is the CEO of Polymarket, an online platform where people bet on the outcomes of real-world events—like elections, sports results, crypto prices, or even geopolitical events.", "annotation_id": "39832472", "url": "https://genius.com/39832472", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "Just trust me, I know there’s—", "vault_lines": ["Just trust me, I know there's—"], "meaning": "This line is also said by Drake. Needs to be italicized", "annotation_id": "39829677", "url": "https://genius.com/39829677", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "I’ve been on my just in case shit I got a whole lot of names and dates and pictures of faces Saved for whenever the right time and place is", "vault_lines": ["I've been on my just in case shit", "I got a whole lot of names and dates and pictures of faces", "Saved for whenever the right time and place is"], "meaning": "This could be Drake  saying he is keeping “receipts” or screenshots of what others have said. This is “just in case” they say anything that is different from what they may have said to or about Drake earlier, therefore he is keeping these names, dates and pictures of faces to hold these individuals accountable for what they said in the case where they say something different or switch up. These 3 lines could be interpreted as Drake staying alert.", "annotation_id": "39821689", "url": "https://genius.com/39821689", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "Should’ve stood over and double-tapped", "vault_lines": ["Should've stood over and double-tapped"], "meaning": "Refers to a widespread duty in the streets where someone is stood over and shoots to ‘confirm’ killing and finish the job.\nThis tends to happen mainly during important or personal killings.\n\nDrake is saying no rappers took advantage of when Drake was feeling low, Kendrick, allegedly having more diss tracks locked and loaded for Drake, but didn’t end up releasing them after the dust settled. This is a prime example of how Rapper’s missed their opportunity\n\n\n\nDouble tapping on social media generally refers to liking a post, in the form of a red heart. This is more of a stretch but could mean\nDrake is also saying, you should’ve checked his heart, his pulse, before concluding he was dead.", "annotation_id": "39806514", "url": "https://genius.com/39806514", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "I don’t wanna talk ’bout M’s, I don’t wanna talk ’bout friends I don’t wanna talk about how this shit started, man, I wanna talk about how this shit ends", "vault_lines": ["I don't wanna talk 'bout M's, I don't wanna talk 'bout friends", "I don't wanna talk about how this shit started, man, I wanna talk about how this shit ends"], "meaning": "This is a refusal-to-recap narrative line—he’s explicitly rejecting discussion of past details and focusing on outcomes.\n\n“I don’t wanna talk ‘bout M’s, I don’t wanna talk 'bout friends”\n“M’s” = millions (money) or possibly coded references to deals/success metrics\n“friends” = alliances, relationships, loyalty circles\n\nMeaning:\n\nhe is not interested in money talk or personal ties right now\n\nThis removes both financial flexing and social context from the conversation.\n\n“I don’t wanna talk about how this shit started”\n\nThis dismisses origin stories:\n\nbeef history\npast events\nwho did what first\n\nIt signals:\n\nthe beginning is irrelevant at this point\n\n“man, I wanna talk about how this shit ends”\n\nThis is the pivot.\n\nMeaning:\n\nfocus is on resolution, consequences, and final outcome—not narrative buildup\n\nIt carries a sharper undertone:\n\nimplies escalation is already assumed\nshifts from explanation → conclusion\nsuggests confidence or inevitability about how things will finish", "annotation_id": "39796764", "url": "https://genius.com/39796764", "state": "pending", "votes": -3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "Should’ve put another blade in my back", "vault_lines": ["Should've put another blade in my back"], "meaning": "Many former friends and associates deserted and betrayed Drake during the rap beef and ensuing fall out, “stabbing him in the back.” Drake says they should have finished him off while they had the chance, and stabbed him in the back again. Instead they did not, and he survived.", "annotation_id": "39793948", "url": "https://genius.com/39793948", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "Spent months in the corner, just me and my back", "vault_lines": ["Spent months in the corner, just me and my back"], "meaning": "To be “backed into a corner” means someone is forced into a difficult, restrictive, or unpleasant situation with limited options left and is essentially trapped. Drake reflects on the time since the rap beef, with former friends and associates deserting him and many in the industry writing him off and predicting the end of the reign.", "annotation_id": "39793918", "url": "https://genius.com/39793918", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "Yeah, the chef two Michelin", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, the chef two Michelin"], "meaning": "The Michelin Guide is a prestigious restaurant rating system originally created by the French tire company Michelin in 1900. Restaurants are awarded one, two, or three stars, with three being the highest; reserved for cuisine worth traveling specifically to experience.\n\nEarning a Michelin star is widely regarded as one of the most coveted and rewarding recognitions in the culinary world.\n\nDrake is talking about, presumably, a personal chef, whose earned a Michelin star. Drake has that same level of culinary excellence cooking for him and him only. He doesn’t go to Michelin starred restaurants; the chef comes to him.", "annotation_id": "39779805", "url": "https://genius.com/39779805", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "The messages you ’bout to send on the sixteenth Please don’t hit send on none of that", "vault_lines": ["The messages you 'bout to send on the sixteenth", "Please don't hit send on none of that"], "meaning": "Drake’s album trio (MAID OF HONOR, HABIBTI and ICEMAN) all dropped simultaneously at 12am EST on Friday, May 15, 2026. The people who weren’t there for the hard times will be flooding his phone on the 16th – the next day once the numbers settle in and the perception is shaped– not out of genuine love, but to use the moment as a foot in the door back into his circle.\n\nThe line also works as a double entendre. Drake could also be addressing rappers he references throughout the project. In rap, a “16” commonly refers to a 16-bar verse, so “the messages\" can be interpreted as diss tracks or lyrical retaliations aimed at him.", "annotation_id": "39779787", "url": "https://genius.com/39779787", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "I’m fightin’ the man, not suin’ the rapper, you boys is not listenin’, ah", "vault_lines": ["I'm fightin' the man, not suin' the rapper, you boys is not listenin', ah"], "meaning": "Drake is clarifying here that his lawsuit is against the label and the music establishment as a whole, NOT specifically Kendrick Lamar, despite what online gossip blogs and even mainstream media others have reported as fact.", "annotation_id": "39779400", "url": "https://genius.com/39779400", "state": "pending", "votes": 57, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "Come to the 6ix and we dippin’ you boys like a christenin’", "vault_lines": ["Come to the 6ix and we dippin' you boys like a christenin'"], "meaning": "The 6ix is a common nickname of Drake’s hometown, Toronto, Ontario.\n\nA Christening is a Christian religious ceremony in which a person or baby is baptized. Baptism is the Christian rite involving the dipping of an individual in holy water to signify spiritual cleansing and admission into the Christian church.\n\nDipping is slang for stabbing someone, which is used typically in multicultural London, England and Toronto.", "annotation_id": "39777893", "url": "https://genius.com/39777893", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "Killy might come take a stick off a pussy like they was transitionin’", "vault_lines": ["Killy might come take a stick off a pussy like they was transitionin'"], "meaning": "Gender affirming surgery, (or bottom surgery) involves the reconstruction of male genitalia into its female counterparts. Drake crudely plays on this, with the word “stick” referring to both a gun and a penis. The line refers to Toronto rapper KILLY, and that he might take a gun (stick) off a person who is viewed as a “pussy”.", "annotation_id": "39776694", "url": "https://genius.com/39776694", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "Let’s wait on your Spotify Wrapped", "vault_lines": ["Let's wait on your Spotify Wrapped"], "meaning": "Drake was commonly found on users of Spotify’s end of year review “Wrapped”. Many people online mentioned how they didn’t think they listened to a lot of Drake but were surprised to see him on the list.\n\nThis is Drake saying that, even if they don’t realize it, he’s always in everyone’s rotation.", "annotation_id": "39776284", "url": "https://genius.com/39776284", "state": "accepted", "votes": 87, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "line": "Yeah, none of you pussies is actin’ the same Mind on my money, I’m rackin’ my brain", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, none of you pussies is actin' the same", "Mind on my money, I'm rackin' my brain"], "meaning": "Drake interpolates these lyrics from “National Treasures”:\n\nMy mind on the money, I’m rackin' my brain\nAnd none of you pussies is actin' the same\n\nHe also used a similar lyric from his 2023 song “All the parties”:\n\nMoney on my mind, I’m rackin' my brain\n\nDrake is focused on the accumulation and preservation of his wealth (mind on my money), but says the same cannot be said for his competitors.\n\n“Racking my brain” means someone is trying hard to remember something or solve a problem, here, the accumulation of money.\n\nFinally, Drake links these two common sayings with a double entendre. A “rack” is slang for a large amount of money, typically $1,000 that is racked or banded together, and is a term often used in rap music to exhibit wealth.", "annotation_id": "39775341", "url": "https://genius.com/39775341", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "B’s On The Table", "status": "done", "targets": 29, "clicked": 29, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-and-21-savage-bs-on-the-table-lyrics", "genius_title": "B’s On The Table"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "City Is Mine", "line": "Connections", "vault_lines": ["Up North I got me a couple of troubles, couple connections"], "meaning": "This could be referring to JayDees Connections, a former clothing store on Eglinton Ave in West York, Toronto that Drake used to work at whenever Jason let him.", "annotation_id": "22072764", "url": "https://genius.com/22072764", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "City Is Mine", "line": "I’m just a writer flamin’ pages of a notebook, my Rachel McAdams get at ’em when I ignite her (Haha!)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This line is a nod to Rachel McAdams, an actress who starred in the 2004 romance, The Notebook.", "annotation_id": "21810940", "url": "https://genius.com/21810940", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "City Is Mine", "line": "I don’t own no ice, I just got clean rap", "vault_lines": ["I don't own no ice, I just got clean rap"], "meaning": "In the early stage of his career, Drake didn’t feel the need to show off any wealth. But all of those priorities have seemingly changed with lines like:\n\nI wear every single chain, even when I’m in the house", "annotation_id": "12508578", "url": "https://genius.com/12508578", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "City Is Mine", "line": "Memphis is the reason that my rhymin’ and my speech slow", "vault_lines": ["I got the diamonds in my teeth flow, Memphis is the reason that my rhymin' and my speech slow"], "meaning": "Drake undoubtedly reps his home of Toronto, but has deep Memphis roots via his father, Dennis Graham. After a divorce, Dennis moved back to Memphis where Drake would visit him in the summers while growing up. Dennis credits his own musical background in Memphis as a major contributor to his son’s success.\n\nDrake alludes to his heritage by embracing Memphis rap culture, which has often lauded the perception-slowing sizzurp.", "annotation_id": "131892", "url": "https://genius.com/131892", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "City Is Mine", "line": "And me and Nickel F. go together like burgers and diners, yes", "vault_lines": ["And me and Nickel F. go together like burgers and diners, yes"], "meaning": "Drake is referring to Nickelus F, a rapper and contemporary R&B writer who has been known to collaborate with Drake", "annotation_id": "109467", "url": "https://genius.com/109467", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "City Is Mine", "line": "Break it down like you working for your tuition at Howard Momma", "vault_lines": ["Break it down like you working for your tuition at Howard"], "meaning": "Howard University is a historically black college based in Washington, D.C. The school is famous in hip-hop culture because it’s Sean “P. Diddy” Combs' alma mater.", "annotation_id": "109463", "url": "https://genius.com/109463", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "City Is Mine", "line": "With trays in both hands, place an order, I can cater, uh", "vault_lines": ["With trays in both hands, place an order, I can cater, uh"], "meaning": "Drake is adept at waiting tables so his flow can accommodate large orders\n\nAn alternate, more gangsta meaning could be that “treys” refer to .357 magnum revolvers. Drake’s warning you that your hating will lead to him bringing out the guns and going all Tough Tony on you\n\n“Don’t mess around and make me catch a body like that”", "annotation_id": "109462", "url": "https://genius.com/109462", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "City Is Mine", "line": "This the record that my backpack underground fans get to skippin’", "vault_lines": ["This the record that my backpack underground fans get to skippin'"], "meaning": "“Backpackers” or “hipsters” refuse to listen to this song because it’s too hype and not personal enough, when ironically it still manages to be be somewhat personal with plenty of nice lines\n\nThis is a song that should have been more popular than replacement girl, but the hipsters would have hated it then for being too “mainstream”", "annotation_id": "109132", "url": "https://genius.com/109132", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "City Is Mine", "status": "done", "targets": 8, "clicked": 8, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-city-is-mine-lyrics", "genius_title": "City Is Mine"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Daylight", "line": "Shot him in daylight Shot him in daylight Shot him in daylight (Shot him, he shot him,", "vault_lines": ["He shot him in... (Damn)", "Shot him in daylight", "(Shot him, he shot him,", "what? Shot him, what?)"], "meaning": "Drake diss XXXTentacion also referring to moonlight by xxx", "annotation_id": "38366345", "url": "https://genius.com/38366345", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Daylight", "line": "My doggy got booked for actin’ like Book", "vault_lines": ["My doggy got booked for actin' like Book"], "meaning": "Word play on shooting. Devin Booker is a shooting guard in basketball aka a “shooter.” Drakes dog is a hitter aka a “shooter.” Also word play with booked as in given a sentence by a judge or getting jailed by the cops and Booker.\n\nAdditionally, at the time of this song’s release, Devin Booker plays for the Phoenix Suns. This could potentially be a reference to the song saying he “shot him in daylight.”, as the Sun being out produces daylight.", "annotation_id": "29729529", "url": "https://genius.com/29729529", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Daylight", "line": "Don’t talk to my man like that", "vault_lines": ["Don't talk to my man like that", "My, my, my, my man"], "meaning": "Adonis is warning those who go against him to not mess with him or his friends. Although he is being raised in a 100 million dollar mega-mansion.", "annotation_id": "35140857", "url": "https://genius.com/35140857", "state": "pending", "votes": -11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Daylight", "line": "(808 Mafia)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This is the producer tag for 808 Mafia, an American producer collective. The group is led by Southside, with other founding members including TM88 and Lex Luger. They are known for creating the modern-day sound of trap music, with the use of heavy 808 drums.\n\nThe tag is voiced by Southside’s children, which was revealed by him in a August 2023 interview.", "annotation_id": "30068059", "url": "https://genius.com/30068059", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Daylight", "line": "Like what’s on your wrist, we clockin’ niggas", "vault_lines": ["Like what's in your shoe, we sockin' niggas", "Like what's on your wrist, we clockin' niggas"], "meaning": "In this line, Drake is referring to 2 things:\n1. The watch on his wrist which in a sense is a clock\n2. To clock someone means to hit someone, especially on the head or face", "annotation_id": "30068040", "url": "https://genius.com/30068040", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Daylight", "line": "Like, “Anyone home?,” we knockin’ niggas", "vault_lines": ["Like, \"Anyone home?,\" we knockin' niggas"], "meaning": "This is a double entendre. When you say “Anyone home?” you may be knocking on someone’s door. But Drake is also knocking his opps out cold. Hard", "annotation_id": "29846277", "url": "https://genius.com/29846277", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Daylight", "line": "We clumsy as fuck, we droppin’ niggas", "vault_lines": ["We clumsy as fuck, we droppin' niggas"], "meaning": "Drake uses clever wordplay phrasing how he’s clumsy, equaling in dropping stuff from his hands, but actually means an alternative form of ”dropping” someone, meaning to kill them.", "annotation_id": "29750660", "url": "https://genius.com/29750660", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Daylight", "line": "Like what’s in your shoe, we sockin’ niggas", "vault_lines": ["Like what's in your shoe, we sockin' niggas", "Like what's on your wrist, we clockin' niggas"], "meaning": "This is a clever play on words by drake. Most of the time, when people where shoes, they wear socks under the shoe, meaning that they have socks in their shoes. Socking can also be slang for hitting someone with a closed fist, meaning that drake most likely punched a homie.", "annotation_id": "29748529", "url": "https://genius.com/29748529", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Daylight", "line": "Capo the type to show up to the wake", "vault_lines": ["Capo the type to show up to the wake"], "meaning": "“Capo” refers to a made member of the Italian mafia. If a Capo shows up to the wake it is likely one of his crew members has been the result of a killing.", "annotation_id": "29732951", "url": "https://genius.com/29732951", "state": "pending", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Daylight", "line": "I will always, watchin’ for you", "vault_lines": ["I will always, watchin' for you"], "meaning": "Adonis is on opp-patrol. Always keeping an eye out for the crew.", "annotation_id": "29730713", "url": "https://genius.com/29730713", "state": "pending", "votes": 252, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Daylight", "line": "She said she was vegan, she eatin’ a goat", "vault_lines": ["She said she was vegan, she eatin' a goat"], "meaning": "Here Drake plays with the meaning of goat in rap and the double entendre of the word “eating” as a sexual act.\n\nVegans don’t eat meat and Drake is a Goat.", "annotation_id": "29729504", "url": "https://genius.com/29729504", "state": "pending", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Daylight", "line": "Free all the dogs and fuck all the witnesses They sittin’ down, we standin’ on bidiness Ayy, standin’ on bidiness Standin’ on bidiness Standin’ on bidiness", "vault_lines": ["Ayy, standin' on bidiness", "Free all the dogs and fuck all the witnesses", "They sittin' down, we standin' on bidiness"], "meaning": "It’s common for people to feel negative emotions toward someone who serves as a witness in a criminal case against people they love.\n\nDrake could potentially be making a reference to the currently incarcerated Young Thug who’s currently on trial facing a RICO indictment after being arrested in May 2022.\n\nIn Thug’s trial, twenty-eight people were arrested, facing a fifty-six-count RICO indictment charge filed by the state of Georgia. However, at the time of the song’s release (Oct. 2023), there were only seven remaining defendants including Thugger as the rest have turned witness for the state or have accepted plea deals to receive less jail time.\n\nIt’s worth noting that Young Thug’s June 2023 third studio album—released while incarcerated—is titled BUSINESS IS BUSINESS. The title is a supposed reference to Gunna—Thug’s signee, and co-defendant—as he has been labelled a “snitch” after taking a plea in December 2022. On BUSINESS IS BUSINESS, Drake appeared on two tracks, the intro, “Parade on Cleveland,” and the ninth track, “Oh You Went.”\n\n“Standing on business” means taking care of your responsibilities, practicing what you preach, or showing that you mean what you say/you can back up your claims. Drake is saying that he and his friends don’t just make claims, but they back them up as well.", "annotation_id": "29728854", "url": "https://genius.com/29728854", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Daylight", "line": "My doggy got booked for actin’ like Book", "vault_lines": ["My doggy got booked for actin' like Book"], "meaning": "He refers to Devin Booker and he goes by a lot of names (DB, DBook and Book) and he’s a good shooter. Devin Booker also plays for the Pheonix Suns. On the jersey is a Sun. Daylight is caused by the sun shining. This is a double entendre, for when Devin Booker shoots while wearing the Phoenix Suns jersey. “Shot him in Daylight”.", "annotation_id": "29725860", "url": "https://genius.com/29725860", "state": "pending", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Daylight", "line": "She went to Jung and she bought a body", "vault_lines": ["She went to Jung and she bought a body"], "meaning": "Dr. Calvin Jung is a Cosmetic Surgeon and owner of Premier Surgical Arts  located in Houston, TX.", "annotation_id": "29725521", "url": "https://genius.com/29725521", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Daylight", "line": "I wasn’t there when they caught the body TPS think that I bought the body Internet swear that I bought the body Take more than that to go pop somebody Them niggas talk about everybody So lowkey I’m happy they got somebody, nigga, what?", "vault_lines": ["I wasn't there when they caught the body", "TPS think that I bought the body", "Internet swear that I bought the body", "Take more than that to go pop somebody", "Them niggas talk about everybody", "So lowkey I'm happy they got somebody, nigga, what?"], "meaning": "Drake addresses the rumors surrounding his involvement in XXXTENTACION’s murder, going as far to reveal he was probed by TPS (Toronto Police Services) for his involvement.\n\nHe concludes by proclaiming his innocence and states he is content with the case being solved as it allows him to distance himself from the situation.", "annotation_id": "29725431", "url": "https://genius.com/29725431", "state": "accepted", "votes": 114, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Daylight", "line": "Treat all my exes like Jehovah’s Witnesses", "vault_lines": ["Treat all my exes like Jehovah's Witnesses"], "meaning": "Drake treats all of his ex-partners as if they are Jehovah’s Witnesses, who are known for their practice of shunning/excommunicating former members. In other words, he ignores or avoids them and does not engage in any communication or contact with them. This could be interpreted as a way for Drake to move on from his past relationships and focus on his present and future endeavors. It also suggests that he does not want to be bothered by his exes, similar to how people often avoid or ignore Jehovah’s Witnesses when they come knocking on their doors.", "annotation_id": "29725406", "url": "https://genius.com/29725406", "state": "pending", "votes": 48, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Daylight", "line": "Like combo number one, we whoppin’ niggas, nigga, what?", "vault_lines": ["Like combo number one, we whoppin' niggas, nigga, what?"], "meaning": "Whopper is a meal at Burger King. Drake whoops people. There is also a double entendre on combo, because combo number 1 at Burger King is the Whopper, and Drake is talking about performing a fighting combo on people.", "annotation_id": "29725179", "url": "https://genius.com/29725179", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Daylight", "line": "[Outro: Adonis]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Adonis Graham is Drake’s first child who has been heavily involved with the rollout of this album.\n\nAdonis is credited for creating the cover art of For All The Dogs and has been featured in the “8am in Charlotte” music video describing the creation of the cover art.\n\nThis is Adonis' first musical appearance of his career.", "annotation_id": "29725166", "url": "https://genius.com/29725166", "state": "accepted", "votes": 194, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Daylight", "line": "Like Lenny Kravitz show, we rockin’ niggas", "vault_lines": ["Like Lenny Kravitz show, we rockin' niggas"], "meaning": "Lenny Kravitz releases music considered to be reggae and rock. There is a double entendre on “rockin'” as it also means that Drake is knocking out people.", "annotation_id": "29725137", "url": "https://genius.com/29725137", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Daylight", "line": "Like tennis indoors, we squashin’ niggas", "vault_lines": ["Like tennis indoors, we squashin' niggas"], "meaning": "Squash is a racket-and-ball sport played by two or four players in a four-walled court with a small, hollow, rubber ball. In a game, the players alternate in striking the ball with their rackets onto the playable surfaces of the four walls of the court. The objective of the game is to hit the ball in such a way that the opponent is not able to play a valid return.\nSquash is normally regarded as indoor tennis.", "annotation_id": "29724864", "url": "https://genius.com/29724864", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Daylight", "line": "You’re all a bunch of fucking assholes You know why? You don’t have the guts to be what you wanna be You need people like me You need people like me so you can point your fucking fingers And say that’s the bad guy", "vault_lines": ["You're all a bunch of fucking assholes", "Don't know what I took", "You don't have the guts to be what you wanna be", "You need people like me", "You need people like me so you can point your fucking fingers", "And say that's the bad guy"], "meaning": "The legendary line from the 1983 movie Scarface.\n\nIt’s the voice of the lead character Tony Montana, played by Al Pacino.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/Yky4QtRX_DI?si=zrz7Ywhowcrc9MQl&t=87", "annotation_id": "29724828", "url": "https://genius.com/29724828", "state": "accepted", "votes": 66, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Daylight", "status": "done", "targets": 21, "clicked": 21, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-daylight-lyrics", "genius_title": "Daylight"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Desires", "line": "I’m in that 8 and that 1 and that 2, this a different Ferrari, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I'm in that 8 and that 1 and that 2, this a different Ferrari, yeah"], "meaning": "This is a nod to the Ferrari 812, although there are two versions—the Superfast and its convertible version, the GTS. The 812 Superfast, which made its debut at the 2017 Geneva Motor Show, carries a base MSRP of $335,275 and has a top speed of 211 mph—making it the fastest and most powerful of all Ferrari models.\n\nThe 812 GTS, on the other hand, features the same performance as the Superfast. The only difference is a slightly adjusted design, weight, price, and the inclusion of a V12 engine—the first convertible model offered by Ferrari in 50 years that has one.\n\n\n\nThe 812 GTS", "annotation_id": "19727139", "url": "https://genius.com/19727139", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Desires", "line": "I should’ve put you somewhere where no one could find you Mansion out in the sticks with nothin’ around you Katy, Texas, Dallas, Texas, you know, a different environment (Ayy)", "vault_lines": ["I should've put you somewhere where no one could find you", "Mansion out in the sticks with nothin' around you", "Katy, Texas, Dallas, Texas, you know, a different environment (Ayy)"], "meaning": "The phrase “out in the sticks” is used to describe a location out in the middle of nowhere, typically in the country or on the outskirts of a city.\n\nThe city of Katy, Texas is located directly west of the city of Houston and considered a part of the Greater Houston metropolis. In the 1960s, local land developers began to develop neighborhoods and suburban communities throughout Katy, due to the overgrowing population in Houston. Today, communities in Katy, south of I-10, are predominantly upper-middle class, in which mansions and golf courses are not uncommon. The I-10 corridor, a major highway that runs through the city of Houston, passes through Katy, which makes it convenient for residents to access Houston’s Downtown district.\n\n\n\nDrake appears to believe Katy would have been a better location for his girl to live, since it’s further away from the trouble, temptations, or influences that seem to exist for his girl in Houston. Drake even goes as far as to consider the city of Dallas, the third most populated city in the state of Texas, and four hours away of Houston, as another possible home for his girl. Since Dallas has several areas of luxurious housing as well, it could be a comfortable place for his girl to live, and more importantly, away from Houston, as far as the rapper is concerned.\n\n\n\nDowntown Dallas", "annotation_id": "19719777", "url": "https://genius.com/19719777", "state": "accepted", "votes": 58, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Desires", "line": "And you just wanna hear some chune, some music I think, you know, you found the right spot", "vault_lines": ["And you just wanna hear some chune, some music", "I think, you know, you found the right spot"], "meaning": "“Chune” is the Jamaican Patois pronunciation of the word “tune,” which is used to refer to a song. Drake used the term on his March 2017 song, “Free Smoke”:\n\nAnd more chune for your headtop\nSo watch how you speak on my name, you know?", "annotation_id": "19717853", "url": "https://genius.com/19717853", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Desires", "line": "I’m outside in an AMG Right outside, TT", "vault_lines": ["I'm outside in an AMG"], "meaning": "In this audio recording, Drake is singing the lyrics to “Time Flies,” which is the next song on the mixtape, so this creates a seamless segue.", "annotation_id": "19717188", "url": "https://genius.com/19717188", "state": "accepted", "votes": 53, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Desires", "line": "I was too good to you, should’ve stayed solid", "vault_lines": ["I was too good to you, should've stayed solid"], "meaning": "Drake feels as if he’s been taken for granted by this girl. On his April 2016 song “Too Good,” he sang about the same thing:\n\nI’m too good to you\nI’m way too good to you\nYou take my love for granted\nI just don’t understand it", "annotation_id": "18984324", "url": "https://genius.com/18984324", "state": "accepted", "votes": 57, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Desires", "line": "Ayy Self-control has never been your thing Don’t think it’ll help if there’s a ring with a rock in it", "vault_lines": ["Self-control has never been your thing", "Don't think it'll help if there's a ring with a rock in it"], "meaning": "Drake doesn’t think marrying this girl will solve their relationship problems. On the other hand, he has expressed interest in marriage—a source close to Drake told Hollywood Life in 2017 Drake’s marriage plans once he finds the right girl:\n\nDrake does want to settle down and have kids one day, and he’s confident that the right woman will come along at the right time. Until then, Drake’s not forcing anything, and he’s making the most of the lifestyle that comes along with being Drake.", "annotation_id": "18984273", "url": "https://genius.com/18984273", "state": "accepted", "votes": 51, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Desires", "line": "You had me down on my knees every day, had to talk with Messiah", "vault_lines": ["You had me down on my knees every day, had to talk with Messiah"], "meaning": "In the Bible, Messiah was the name prophesied in the Old Testament to describe the coming King to redeem the people of Israel, Jesus Christ. For example, John 4:25 reads:\n\nThe woman saith unto him, I know that Messias cometh, which is called Christ: when he is come, he will tell us all things.\n\nOn his 2012 song “Future Back,” Future also talked about praying to the Messiah:\n\nI pray to Messiah, told him, “I want it all\nPut me in the game, or I crawl behind the wall”", "annotation_id": "18984167", "url": "https://genius.com/18984167", "state": "accepted", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Desires", "line": "D. Hill (D. Hill)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This is D. Hill’s producer tag. It first made an appearance on Yung Mal’s January 2018 song, “GodZilla.”\n\nThis is his second collaboration with Drake and Future following “Life Is Good”—released three weeks prior to this song.", "annotation_id": "18983517", "url": "https://genius.com/18983517", "state": "accepted", "votes": 52, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Desires", "line": "How the fuck you keep so many secrets?", "vault_lines": ["How the fuck you keep so many secrets?", "How the fuck you've seen so many beaches?"], "meaning": "Drake is not a fan of his significant other keeping secrets from him as he noted on his June 2010 song, “Karaoke”:\n\nI tried to keep us together, you were busy keeping secrets\nSecrets you were telling everybody but me", "annotation_id": "18983475", "url": "https://genius.com/18983475", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Desires", "line": "Got you a whip, but then you got back on your shit I had to tell Eric go get it", "vault_lines": ["Got you a whip, but then you got back on your shit", "I had to tell Eric go get it"], "meaning": "Drake may be talking about DJ Eric, a radio and strip club DJ from Houston. Drake and Eric are friends—for instance, in October 2017, Drake called in his radio show on his birthday and in July 2017, Drake posted a picture of Eric on his Instagram account.\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/BW3210iDuLO/?utm_source=ig_embed", "annotation_id": "18955600", "url": "https://genius.com/18955600", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Desires", "line": "How the fuck you’ve seen so many beaches? Tickets to them places don’t come cheap, and I see you back in Turks Remember who took you there first and don’t you forget it", "vault_lines": ["How the fuck you keep so many secrets?", "How the fuck you've seen so many beaches?", "Tickets to them places don't come cheap, and", "I see you back in Turks", "Remember who took you there first and don't you forget it"], "meaning": "The Turks and Caicos Islands is an archipelago of 40 islands, located in the Atlantic Ocean. They are known for their beautiful beaches. In May 2019, Drake took a vacation there.\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/BxijXjMFoec/?utm_source=ig_web_copy_link\n\nThe implication in these lines is that this girl has been cheating on Drake with men that have bought stuff for her, including a ticket to the Turks.", "annotation_id": "18955569", "url": "https://genius.com/18955569", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Desires", "line": "How you goin’ vegan, but still beefin’ with me again?", "vault_lines": ["How you goin' vegan, but still beefin' with me again?"], "meaning": "“Beef” is used in two ways here as it’s meat from a cow and it means to have a problem with someone.\n\nA “vegan” is somebody who does not eat or use animal products like meat, eggs, or dairy. Drake uses the word “vegan” in a literal sense and “beef” in its slang sense to make a play on words, asking this girl how she can claim to be “vegan” if she’s contradicting that claim by “beefing” with him.", "annotation_id": "18954899", "url": "https://genius.com/18954899", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Desires", "line": "Where I’m from, they serve the soda clean (Clean, clean) You come from a city where there’s lean with the rocks in it", "vault_lines": ["Where I'm from, they serve the soda clean (Clean, clean)", "You come from a city where there's lean with the rocks in it"], "meaning": "“Lean” is a mixture of promethazine codeine and soda. It originated in Houston in the 1960s when blues musicians would mix Robitussin with alcohol. It’s usually served with ice, which is also referred to as “rocks.”\n\nThis may also be a nod to the Atlanta rap group Dem Franchize Boyz January 2006 hit, “Lean Wit It, Rock Wit It.” Therefore, the girl Drake’s addressing could be from Atlanta or Houston.", "annotation_id": "18954046", "url": "https://genius.com/18954046", "state": "accepted", "votes": 52, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
