{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "More M’s", "line": "Takin’ less L’s, makin’ more M’s", "vault_lines": ["Takin' less L's, makin' more M's"], "meaning": "L stands for Loses and M stand for Millions/Money", "annotation_id": "35010091", "url": "https://genius.com/35010091", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "More M’s", "line": "Way that I ran shit, you’d think I was Iranian", "vault_lines": ["Way that I ran shit, you'd think I was Iranian"], "meaning": "In this line, Drake is boasting about his control and leadership in the music scene.\nThe second part of the line is a wordplay, connecting the word “ran” with “Iranian.” It might be a metaphorical comparison, likening Drake’s way of running things to something associated with Iran. Given that Iran has a rich history and cultural significance, this could be an attempt to evoke a sense of exoticism, strength, or other qualities that Drake wants to associate with his leadership in the music industry.", "annotation_id": "29360175", "url": "https://genius.com/29360175", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "More M’s", "line": "(Metro) Metro in this bitch goin’ brazy", "vault_lines": ["Metro in this bitch goin' brazy"], "meaning": "Reference to the producer of this track, Metro Boomin. 21 first introduced this tag line for Metro on song “No Opp Left Behind” off their collaboration album SAVAGE MODE II:\n\nMetro in this bitch goin brazy", "annotation_id": "27475949", "url": "https://genius.com/27475949", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "More M’s", "line": "Walk around like Prince ’cause I got a lot of lady friends", "vault_lines": ["Walk around like Prince 'cause I got a lot of lady friends"], "meaning": "Prince Rogers Nelson was one of the most popular and influential artists ever. Prince was famous for wearing high heels & eyeliner, but having the most beautiful women of all time around him. From Vanity, to Apollonia, Kim Basinger, Carmen Electra, Misty Copeland, Madonna, Sheila E. and many more.", "annotation_id": "27169314", "url": "https://genius.com/27169314", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "More M’s", "line": "Might’ve fucked a rapper, girl, but you ain’t fucked Drake yet Yeah", "vault_lines": ["Might've fucked a rapper, girl, but you ain't fucked Drake yet"], "meaning": "Drake playfully mocks women with an inflated sense of worth because they have slept with rappers, inferring that he chooses to entangle with a higher-calibre of women.\n\nThis is also a reference to a line from Lizzo’s August 2021 song “Rumors” featuring Cardi B:\n\nNo, I ain’t fuck Drake yet (Ha)", "annotation_id": "27078327", "url": "https://genius.com/27078327", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "More M’s", "line": "Baptize a nigga, send him home in a blanket", "vault_lines": ["Baptize a nigga, send him home in a blanket"], "meaning": "A baptism is a Christian act of washing away sins, but refers to killing someone, usually in a bloody fashion, as a baptism with blood, rather than water.\n\nSending one in a blanket is likely a reference to the biblical story of Moses, who was sent in a basket under a blanket in a river to save his life..\nThis obviously also references a [body bag.](https://images.genius.com/10b8df9e8aabb5f2a43b91d57f0687b4.1000x1000x1.jpg.", "annotation_id": "27072148", "url": "https://genius.com/27072148", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "More M’s", "line": "Niggas ain’t got love for the boy, so they fake it Crack a couple jokes to some bitches on some snake shit But if I send a verse to they ass, then they’ll take it", "vault_lines": ["Niggas ain't got love for the boy, so they fake it", "Crack a couple jokes to some bitches on some snake shit", "But if I send a verse to they ass, then they'll take it", "Take it to the paint, take it to the rim"], "meaning": "Drake says that a lot of the love he gets from other rappers is fake, his proof being that when they’re around women, they’ll make jokes at his expense. The punchline is that, despite all that snake behavior, said rappers will still gladly accept a verse from Drake.", "annotation_id": "27067649", "url": "https://genius.com/27067649", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "More M’s", "line": "What happened to that nigga claiming OVO? We traded him", "vault_lines": ["What happened to that nigga claiming OVO? We traded him"], "meaning": "DJ Charlie B Was recently kicked out of OVO for supposedly sleeping with chubbz’s baby mom", "annotation_id": "27065404", "url": "https://genius.com/27065404", "state": "pending", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "More M’s", "line": "Dissin’ on his album and it flopped, he deserved it", "vault_lines": ["Dissin' on his album and it flopped, he deserved it"], "meaning": "Drake subliminally addresses an adversary whose album had a less-than-stellar commercial performance.\n\nNotably, Drizzy’s long-term rival Pusha T dropped fourth studio album, It’s Almost Dry in April 2022, earning 55,000 album-equivalent units in its first week, debuting at number one on the US Billboard 200 chart.\n\nHowever, as Pusha refrained from dissing Drake on the project, this is more likely a diss towards The Game. The Game’s tenth studio album, DRILLMATIC – Heart vs. Mind, was released in August 2022 and contains references to many artists. Notably, he disses Drizzy’s “Forever” collaborator Eminem on the track “The Black Slim Shady.” The album peaked at number 12 on the US Billboard 200.\n\nIn July 2022, The Game stirred up controversy whilst promoting his then-forthcoming album. He commented on Drake, insinuating that he took shots at Kendrick Lamar on the pair’s 2015 track “100.”", "annotation_id": "27061350", "url": "https://genius.com/27061350", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "More M’s", "line": "Put her Skims on, now she actin’ like she Kim", "vault_lines": ["Put her Skims on, now she actin' like she Kim"], "meaning": "21 refers to Skims, an American shapewear and clothing brand co-founded by Kim Kardashian, Emma Grede, and Jens Grede.\n\nKardashian is often noted as a “influencer” and “fashion icon.” Thus, 21’s girl gains a similar level of confidence by wearing articles of Skims clothing.\n\nNotably, Kardashian credited her former husband, Drake’s collaborator Ye, as being her “Ghost Creative Director” and for creating the company’s logo.\n\n\n\nFollowing the album’s release, Kardashian used this lyric as an Instagram caption.", "annotation_id": "27061102", "url": "https://genius.com/27061102", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "More M’s", "line": "Got so many hits, it wouldn’t be fair to do no verses", "vault_lines": ["Got so many hits, it wouldn't be fair to do no verses"], "meaning": "Verzuz, when said sounds like “versus”, is referring to a live stream series created by Timbaland and Swizz Beatz where two artists or groups compete in a battle style comparison of their respective discographies, featuring two rounds and up to ten songs per round. Verzuz was created & popularized during the initial lockdown in the CoVid-19 Pandemic.\n\nDrake explains in this line that it wouldn’t be fair for him to compete with any artist in a Verzuz, because he has too many hits and would easily win.", "annotation_id": "27059277", "url": "https://genius.com/27059277", "state": "pending", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "More M’s", "line": "Skatin’ through this album like a Montreal Canadien", "vault_lines": ["Skatin' through this album like a Montreal Canadien"], "meaning": "The Montreal Canadiens are a professional ice hockey team hailing in the National Hockey League. Over the course of their rich history, the Habs have won 24 stanley cups, making them the most successful franchise in the sport.\n\nDrake plays with the image of skating—as a Canadien would—to demonstrate his ease on the beats selected on HER LOSS. He paints himself as a hockey player skillfully gliding over the competition with his smooth, yet efficient, flow.\n\nBeing from Canada, Drake has been immersed in hockey culture, notably taking a picture with Carey Price, Montreal’s legendary goaltender, at the NHL’s 2012 All-Star game where he performed in front of the fans:\n\n\n\nPictured: Carey Price (left) posing with Drake (right) at the NHL’s 2012 All-Star game\n\nDrake notably received some negative feedback for promoting his hometown’s most prominent rival on such a big platform. In 2021, the Toronto Maple Leafs and the Canadiens faced off against one another in the first round of the playoffs. The Leafs initially took a 3-1 series lead but couldn’t clinch the series following a breathtaking comeback from the Habs, further igniting the rivalry.\n\nThis is not the first time Drake mentioned Québec—the French-speaking province of Canada—in 2022. In “Sticky”, he writes:\n\nAyy, two sprinters to Quebec\nChérie, où est mon bec?", "annotation_id": "27058824", "url": "https://genius.com/27058824", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "More M’s", "line": "Wells Fargo where I’m banking, nigga Heard your album sales tankin’, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Wells Fargo where I'm banking, nigga", "Heard your album sales tankin', nigga"], "meaning": "Wells Fargo Bank is the fourth largest bank and one of the oldest financial institutions in the United States. 21 Savage boasts of his financial success, juxtaposed with the struggles some artists are facing. Interestingly, this is not the first time that 21 references the bank—on his July 2017 song “Dead People,” he raps:\n\nWalked out of Wells Fargo and ran to Chase\nHopped out a Bentley truck and jumped inside the Wraith\nYoung Savage, I was trappin' on the back street", "annotation_id": "27055097", "url": "https://genius.com/27055097", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "More M’s", "line": "Thought I was a popstar, I’m Slaughter Gang, I baited ’em", "vault_lines": ["Thought I was a popstar, I'm Slaughter Gang, I baited 'em"], "meaning": "Drake references his July 2020 song with DJ Khaled, “POPSTAR.” Drake references the change in style, flow, and personality he has on this album with 21, adopting a more aggressive sound as opposed to his previous songs.", "annotation_id": "27053063", "url": "https://genius.com/27053063", "state": "accepted", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
