{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Goin In", "line": "Money flowin’ like a slit wrist, no bandage", "vault_lines": ["Money flowin' like a slit wrist, no bandage"], "meaning": "If your wrist is slit without a bandage, your blood would flow insanely fast. Drake compares the fast blood flow to his income. Saying that his money comes in with speeds similar to those a slit wrists.", "annotation_id": "16364844", "url": "https://genius.com/16364844", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Goin In", "line": "[Verse 2: Drake]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake’s co-writer for this verse was most likely Nickelus F.\nHe made it clear in a Complex interview that this is the only verse on the album he wrote a verse for.", "annotation_id": "7433969", "url": "https://genius.com/7433969", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Goin In", "line": "Bad to the gristle, hat to the rizzle", "vault_lines": ["Bad to the gristle, hat to the rizzle"], "meaning": "“Bad to the bristle” is Australian Bayou slang equivalent to saying “Bad to the bone”\n\nWeezy wears his hat with the brim tilted to the right (“rizzle” when put into Snoop Dogg’s -izzle dialect) because of his close affiliation to the Bloods, who wear their hats tilted to the right as gang identification", "annotation_id": "17824", "url": "https://genius.com/17824", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Goin In", "line": "Chicks get hammered, big-dicked bandit", "vault_lines": ["Chicks get hammered, big-dicked bandit"], "meaning": "Drake treats having sex with women like a robbery; he leaves just as fast as he got in\n\n“Big dick bandit” is a standard nickname in hip-hop; Drake probably bit it from MJG or The Seventh Floor Crew (specifically, current NFL linebacker Tavares Gooden)", "annotation_id": "15457", "url": "https://genius.com/15457", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Goin In", "line": "Cover me, I’m goin’ in, and buckin’ when the hook drop", "vault_lines": ["I'm goin' in, I'm goin' in", "Bitch I'm goin' in, I'm goin' in", "Cover me, I'm goin' in, and buckin' when the hook drop"], "meaning": "A play on “hook shots” above:\n\n\nDrake will “buck” (slang for “go crazy”, i.e. “buck wild”) when the hook “drops” (goes in the basket\nDrake will “buck” (slang for “shoot”) when the hook (i.e., the chorus of the song) starts playing", "annotation_id": "10020", "url": "https://genius.com/10020", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Goin In", "line": "The feds tryin’ to clip us, but we ain’t even trippin’", "vault_lines": ["The feds tryin' to clip us, but we ain't even trippin'"], "meaning": "To “trip” is to worry; Lil Wayne doesn’t worry about the federal agents on his tail trying to “clip” him, which means to get arrested.\n\nIn pro football the penalty “clipping” is the act of tripping, which brings up an interesting double meaning.", "annotation_id": "8944", "url": "https://genius.com/8944", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Goin In", "line": "No need for a room, yeah you know I’m fuckin’ in it", "vault_lines": ["I'm goin' in, I'm goin' in", "No need for a room, yeah you know I'm fuckin' in it"], "meaning": "A reference to the song “Love In This Club” by Usher, which Jeezy was featured on.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cB5e0zHRzHc", "annotation_id": "8864", "url": "https://genius.com/8864", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Goin In", "line": "She actin’ like she not, but she know she fuckin’ wit it", "vault_lines": ["She actin' like she not, but she know she fuckin' wit it"], "meaning": "Nobody wants to admit that they’re getting the better end of the bargain in hooking up: you’d like to think you’re hot enough that you’re doing your partner a favor.  Jeezy’s girl acts like she’s not winning in the exchange, but he believes he’s the more valuable person in their interaction because he’s famous", "annotation_id": "5308", "url": "https://genius.com/5308", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Goin In", "line": "Cost a few hundred bands and I’m motherfuckin’ in it", "vault_lines": ["I'm goin' in, I'm goin' in", "Cost a few hundred bands and I'm motherfuckin' in it"], "meaning": "His car costs a few hundred bands (stacks of money rubber-banded together).  While there’s no standardized amount to which “a band” refers, in the context of a rap brag it’s probably at least $1,000.  So he’s probably talking about a Lamborghini or a Maybach or some other very expensive car", "annotation_id": "5302", "url": "https://genius.com/5302", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Goin In", "line": "Me and Wayne lean like Kareem doin’ hook shots", "vault_lines": ["Me and Wayne lean like Kareem doin' hook shots"], "meaning": "“Leaning” is a euphemism for drinking Purple Drank, the notorious cough syrup concoction of the southern crunk movement, known for causing hallucinations and general battiness\n\nBasketball legend Kareem Abdul-Jabbar leaned toward the basket while pulling his patented sky hook", "annotation_id": "5298", "url": "https://genius.com/5298", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Goin In", "line": "And I don’t sit still, I keep it moving like a drive-by", "vault_lines": ["And I don't sit still, I keep it moving like a drive-by"], "meaning": "In a drive-by shooting, a car drives by and people shoot at their targets on the street.  Stopping isn’t exactly an option: the point is to avoid getting shot back at.  Drake’s always innovating or trying to make music: he’s not content to rest on his laurels", "annotation_id": "5295", "url": "https://genius.com/5295", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Goin In", "line": "Blowin’ purple clouds, nigga I’m so sky high", "vault_lines": ["Blowin' purple clouds, nigga I'm so sky high"], "meaning": "Purple weed, which Drake is smoking, is one of the most potent strands of marijuana", "annotation_id": "5291", "url": "https://genius.com/5291", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Goin In", "line": "Never see me out ’cause I live in my workplace", "vault_lines": ["Never see me out 'cause I live in my workplace"], "meaning": "“Now, you too can have an exciting career from home with Google! Simply order the Google Work From Home Kit, only pay the $2.95 for shipping. (The shipping cost allows Google to screen for serious people)”\n\nActually, Drake is bragging about how hard he works and/or being able to afford having a music studio in his house", "annotation_id": "5286", "url": "https://genius.com/5286", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Goin In", "line": "Making hoes wobble like a bridge in a earthquake", "vault_lines": ["Making hoes wobble like a bridge in a earthquake"], "meaning": "Girls' knees shake from excitement when they see sexy man Drake\n\n\n\nAlso, ‘wobble’ often refers to oral sex (as in Lil' Wayne’s Steady Mobbin).\n\nAnother reading could suggest Drake intends to fuck the girls so hard they won’t walk straight afterwards, and therefore ‘wobble’, or making their asses “wobble” as in shake a lot", "annotation_id": "5285", "url": "https://genius.com/5285", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Goin In", "line": "Let her suck my pistol", "vault_lines": ["Bitch named Crystal, let her suck my pistol"], "meaning": "This is not the first time Lil Wayne has referred to his dick as a pistol; in one particularly subtle sexual metaphor on Get Em, Wayne says “One pistol two clips, I aim at lips” to refer to his dick, his balls, and the girl’s vaginal lips, respectively", "annotation_id": "5281", "url": "https://genius.com/5281", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Goin In", "line": "Stomping on this beat like a motherfucking Sigma", "vault_lines": ["Stomping on this beat like a motherfucking Sigma"], "meaning": "“Stompin' like a Sigma” refers to the signature dance of the predominantly African-American fraternity, Phi Beta Sigma, which is known for its aggressive choreography\n\nThis form of dance is technically called “stepping,” but stomping is a more forceful (and accurate) apellation", "annotation_id": "5277", "url": "https://genius.com/5277", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
