{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Ready For You", "line": "[Interlude: Nneka]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This entire interlude was sampled from this song by Nneka\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=player_detailpage&v=-lulJdMKaZw#t=32s", "annotation_id": "53451", "url": "https://genius.com/53451", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m Ready For You", "status": "done", "targets": 3, "clicked": 3, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-im-ready-for-you-lyrics", "genius_title": "I’m Ready For You"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "line": "I count all these racks that I have on me now, I’ma have you like, “Woah”", "vault_lines": ["I count all these racks that I have on me now, I'ma have you like, \"Woah\""], "meaning": "Future wears his wealth. Whether he is draped in designer clothing or weighed down by flooded chains, there’s a bank account worth of cash hanging off his body.\n\n\n\nAccording to Celebrity Net Wealth, Future is worth 30 million dollars. Since a “rack” is worth 1,000, that’s 30,000 racks Future has to count.", "annotation_id": "7850205", "url": "https://genius.com/7850205", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "line": "Way too much codeine and Adderall We just count up paper racks, woah", "vault_lines": ["Way too much codeine and Adderall", "We just count up paper racks, woah"], "meaning": "Codeine is a depressant, whilst Adderall is a stimulant. Combining the two is called “Speedballing,” and results in a specific high.\n\nSuch is Future’s dependence on these drugs, he requires an abnormal amount of codeine to feel “normal” in order to function. To balance, and to actually be able to move around and rap, he pops Adderall to provide energy.\n\nHe actually does seem to care. As he recently said on The Breakfast Club, “{It’s} too much. I need to stop. Now. For my sons that’s listening, I’m about to stop.”", "annotation_id": "7850113", "url": "https://genius.com/7850113", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "line": "Dopeman, dopeman, dopeman, dopeman, dopeman, dopeman Money on the counter, choppers on the floor", "vault_lines": ["Dopeman, dopeman, dopeman, dopeman, dopeman, dopeman", "Money on the counter, choppers on the floor"], "meaning": "Equating his drug dealing skills with that of Michael Jordan’s sporting ability could be fraught with danger, but time and time again Future has claimed to be an expert trapper. His current drug intake would suggest he’s getting very high off his own supply, and the imagery of guns laying about and money everywhere doesn’t feel romantic at all; it feels like hard-boiled ghetto life.", "annotation_id": "7850062", "url": "https://genius.com/7850062", "state": "accepted", "votes": 36, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "line": "A bunch of girls goin’ wild when your chain flooded And I had ’em like wow, cup dirty", "vault_lines": ["A bunch of girls goin' wild when your chain flooded", "And I had 'em like wow, cup dirty"], "meaning": "Liquid is never far from Future’s mind, or body. And picking up girls at a strip club isn’t easy, even when you are the plug. Flooding a chain is even harder. It might be easy to flood a big faced Rolex, but a chain is more difficult.\n\nAnything can be done for the right price though…\n\n\n\nA cup full of dirty sprite and a chain iced out with diamonds is a surefire way to impress the opposite sex.", "annotation_id": "7850041", "url": "https://genius.com/7850041", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "line": "Way too many questions, you must think I trust ya You searchin’ for answers, I do not know nothing, woo", "vault_lines": ["Way too many questions, you must think I trust ya", "You searchin' for answers, I do not know nothing, woo"], "meaning": "After Drake’s famous line on “Back To Back”:\n\nYou gon' make me buy bottles for Charlamagne\nYou gon' make me go out of my fuckin' way\n\nHe continues the reference (and confirms the sneak Meek diss) by alluding to the hashtag #IDontKnoNothing, popularized by Charlemagne collaborator Wax.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/waxkyng/status/644365428601585664\n\nHe “doesn’t know nothing,” which means he knows something. A dig at the wealth of double negatives in rap music. This concept has been reiterated by Drake on several occasions, such as the outro of his song “Used To” and his verse on “HYFR.”", "annotation_id": "7843045", "url": "https://genius.com/7843045", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "line": "Tell her, “Stay the night, valet your car, come fuck me now”", "vault_lines": ["Tell her, \"Stay the night, valet your car, come fuck me now\""], "meaning": "An incredibly considerate gesture. Drake has the girl’s car parked for her so she doesn’t have to worry about parking. Parking is evidently at a premium, despite his huge acreage. The driveway is most likely packed with cars due to Drake’s exuberant loins.", "annotation_id": "7841304", "url": "https://genius.com/7841304", "state": "accepted", "votes": 51, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "line": "If Young Metro don’t trust you, I’m gon’ shoot you Yeah, ah, yeah Halloween Taliban, Taliban I’m gon’ shoot you (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I'm gon' shoot you (Yeah)"], "meaning": "“If Young Metro don’t trust you” is a sample taken from Uncle Murda’s song “Right Now.” On the chorus of “Right Now,” Future drops this line. Here, it is used as Metro Boomin’s production tag, similar to DJ Mustard’s “Mustard on the beat, ho!”\n\nHalloween is in October, thus, referring to October’s Very Own, as seen on “I’m the Plug.”\n\nTaliban represents the trap music movement.  The name was popularized in hip-hop by The Diplomats back in 2003, but Metro Boomin revitalized it after reminding his Twitter followers of a lyric from “Rubber Band Man” by T.I.:\n\nhttps://twitter.com/metroboomin/status/192823085345415168\n\n“Freeband Taliban” is a song by Future and Stuey Rock and Metro sometimes uses “Taliban” as a hashtag in his tweets.\n\nNotably, the reference to the Taliban was removed from the censored version of the song and was also omitted from Apple Music’s ad featuring Taylor Swift.", "annotation_id": "7841166", "url": "https://genius.com/7841166", "state": "accepted", "votes": 335, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "line": "Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman, them boys up to somethin’ They just spent like two or three weeks out the country Them boys up to somethin’, they just not just bluffin’", "vault_lines": ["Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman, them boys up to somethin', woo", "Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman", "Them boys just not bluffin', them boys just not bluffin'", "Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman, them boys up to somethin'", "They just spent like two or three weeks out the country", "Them boys up to somethin', they just not just bluffin'"], "meaning": "Air Jordan’s logo is the Jumpman, and its namesake, Michael Jordan, wore #23 during his NBA career. When Drake posted a picture of himself with Future on Instagram, speculation about a collaboration between the two artists began.\n\n\n\n“Up to something,” coupled with leaving the country, implies some kind of illegal activity. In the What A Time to Be Alive vlog, Drake and Future’s crews are in Atlanta. Since Drake’s Canadian, it’s likely he really did spend a few weeks in the United States to record the project. The felony? Dropping this tape on the rap game unannounced.", "annotation_id": "7840626", "url": "https://genius.com/7840626", "state": "accepted", "votes": 290, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "line": "I know I’ma get my bitch back, woah", "vault_lines": ["I know I'ma get my bitch back, woah"], "meaning": "Future’s relationship with Ciara ended in 2014. The breakup has turned messy with aggressive exchanges between him and her new boyfriend, Russell Wilson.\n\nFuture has stated that he didn’t actually break up with her, he just called off their wedding.\n\nThe celebrity denied that he broke up with the “I Bet” singer, instead saying that he just called off the wedding after some disagreements on the direction of the actual wedding planning.", "annotation_id": "7836616", "url": "https://genius.com/7836616", "state": "accepted", "votes": 68, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "line": "She was tryna join the team, I told her wait Chicken wings and fries, we don’t go on dates", "vault_lines": ["She was tryna join the team, I told her wait", "Chicken wings and fries, we don't go on dates"], "meaning": "Drake’s treatment of the lower classes is picked up by Future, who plays with the basketball theme of the track, and vetoes this girl’s attempt to join his entourage. Don’t forget Future has incredibly high standards. If you’re lacking, you won’t be put on rotation.", "annotation_id": "7836406", "url": "https://genius.com/7836406", "state": "accepted", "votes": 74, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "line": "Bentley Spurs and Phantom, Jordan fadeaway", "vault_lines": ["Bentley Spurs and Phantom, Jordan fadeaway"], "meaning": "Future’s Bentley Flying Spur has the same colorway as the San Antonio Spurs: black, white, and silver.\n\n\n\nHe also owns a Rolls Royce Phantom, so you can never catch up to him like defenders couldn’t stop Michael Jordan’s fadeaway jumpshot.", "annotation_id": "7836304", "url": "https://genius.com/7836304", "state": "accepted", "votes": 68, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "line": "I see ’em tweakin’, they know something’s comin’, woo", "vault_lines": ["I see 'em tweakin', they know something's comin', woo"], "meaning": "Like drug addicts, Drake’s fans can’t wait for their next full length album dosage. Whilst no concrete release date has been set for his huge project, Views From The 6, Drake continues to drop hints that it is on it’s way.", "annotation_id": "7835597", "url": "https://genius.com/7835597", "state": "accepted", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "line": "Jumpman, Jumpman, live on TNT, I’m flexin’, woo", "vault_lines": ["Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman", "Jumpman, Jumpman, live on TNT, I'm flexin', woo"], "meaning": "NBA games air on TNT. Drake is regularly seen courtside during games. Flexing with his lint roller…\n\n\n\nIn 2013, Drake was named the ambassador for his hometown team, the Toronto Raptors.", "annotation_id": "7835544", "url": "https://genius.com/7835544", "state": "accepted", "votes": 50, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "line": "Chanel N°9, Chanel N°5, well, you got ’em both", "vault_lines": ["Chanel N°9, Chanel N°5, well, you got 'em both"], "meaning": "Chanel N°9 and Chanel N°5 are luxury perfumes by French designer Coco Chanel.\n\n\n\nChanel N°5 is still produced today and is considered a standard in luxury perfume. Chanel N°9 has not been produced since the early 1900s and is very rare, sightings are even rarer.\n\nAdditionally, “Chanel No. 9” is also an expensive combination of high-quality cocaine, pure ecstasy, and Special K that produces waves of euphoria lasting for hours.", "annotation_id": "7835516", "url": "https://genius.com/7835516", "state": "accepted", "votes": 61, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "line": "Jump when I say jump, girl, can you take direction? Woo", "vault_lines": ["Jump when I say jump, girl, can you take direction? Woo"], "meaning": "This line plays on the expression, “When I say ‘Jump!’, you say ‘How high?’” It is typically used to convey a sense of dominance.\n\nDrake is either a mentor, or a dominant lover in this situation. He echoed the same sentiment on “Preach”,\n\nI’ve got to do some reflecting\nI’ve got to find me one out here that is good at taking direction\n\nA much calmer mindset focused on cultivating a relationship rather than cultivating a dominant sexual situation.", "annotation_id": "7835371", "url": "https://genius.com/7835371", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "line": "Yeah, Jumpman, Jumpman, I don’t need no introduction Jumpman, Jumpman, Metro Boomin on production, wow", "vault_lines": ["Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman", "Yeah, Jumpman, Jumpman, I don't need no introduction", "Jumpman, Jumpman, Metro Boomin on production, wow"], "meaning": "At this point, Drake is as recognizable in hip hop as Michael Jordan is in sport. Both are titans of pop culture. Both have such distinctive characteristics (Drake’s voice, the Air Jordan symbol) that introductions are not necessary.\n\nMetro Boomin, however, is not quite at that level, although he has been a central player in the formation of the ATL Trap sound. He is credited as the executive producer on What A Time to Be Alive, as he produced or co-produced 7 of the 11 tracks on the project, including this one. Drake also shouted young Metro out on “Scholarships.”", "annotation_id": "7835343", "url": "https://genius.com/7835343", "state": "accepted", "votes": 117, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "line": "Trappin’ is a hobby, that’s the way for me Money comin’ fast, we never gettin’ sleep I, I just had to buy another safe", "vault_lines": ["Trappin' is a hobby, that's the way for me", "Money comin' fast, we never gettin' sleep", "I, I just had to buy another safe"], "meaning": "Future’s relationship with dealing is storied and extensive, and it is a persona he is unwilling to part with.  He’s earned enough money to leave the trap life alone, but it’s a hobby and a passion for him, so he keeps his hand in the game.\n\nIf Future has the means to drop $60k on a Monday at a strip club, he no longer requires his trap house income.", "annotation_id": "7835271", "url": "https://genius.com/7835271", "state": "accepted", "votes": 36, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "line": "Chi-Town, Chi-Town, Michael Jordan just had text me, woo", "vault_lines": ["Chi-Town, Chi-Town, Michael Jordan just had text me, woo"], "meaning": "Jordan is a confirmed Drake fan, with their sneaker collaboration dating back to 2013. The OVO Jordan 10’s are set for a re-release after their April debut, and Drake joins some distinguished alumni in the “I’ve got Jordan on the text” school.\n\nOf course Drake’s love of basketball has led some corners to claim he is the perfect basketball wife.", "annotation_id": "7835236", "url": "https://genius.com/7835236", "state": "accepted", "votes": 213, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "line": "Uh, uh, uh, I think I need some Robitussin", "vault_lines": ["Uh, uh, uh, I think I need some Robitussin"], "meaning": "Robitussin is a brand of cough syrup that can be used to make an alternative version of syrup (lean), with DXM, but though this is a odd reference by Drake to stay with the rhyme scheme, there is a Robitussin Syrup with Codeine in it:\n ROBITUSSIN AC guaifenesin/codeine.\n\nRobitussin rhymes wonderfully with “up to something”, but with the wealth of Actavis references on the record, and given its discontinuation and the fact it is difficult to obtain legally, Drake is stepping clean around those he can’t trust.\n\nIt’s also a reference to Jordan’s famous “Flu Game” during the 1997 NBA Finals. Just before Game 5, Jordan was barely able to sit up due to severe food poisoning. He managed to complete the game and dominate it for the Bulls, completing one of the most iconic games of basketball of all time.\n\n\n\nDrake also fake coughs three times to start this line, implying that he isn’t sick enough to warrant taking Robitussin, but that he still wants to take Robitussin to feel the effects of the high.", "annotation_id": "7835186", "url": "https://genius.com/7835186", "state": "accepted", "votes": 144, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "line": "Jumpman, Jumpman, they gave me my own collection, woo", "vault_lines": ["Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman, Jumpman", "Jumpman, Jumpman, they gave me my own collection, woo"], "meaning": "Although Jordan Brand usually only collaborates with athletes, they’ve repeatedly collaborated with Drake. His Jordan collection includes OVO-themed colorways of classic models: the 8, 10, and the 12.", "annotation_id": "7835163", "url": "https://genius.com/7835163", "state": "accepted", "votes": 36, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "line": "Nobu, Nobu, Nobu, Nobu, Nobu, Nobu I just throwed a private dinner in LA", "vault_lines": ["Nobu, Nobu, Nobu, Nobu, Nobu, Nobu", "I just throwed a private dinner in LA"], "meaning": "Nobu is worldwide chain of high quality Japanese restaurants, with this particular reference to the West Hollywood location, designed by world renowned architect David Rockwell. Renting one of the dining rooms out for a private dinner is a sure sign of wealth. Their website doesn’t list a price. If you have to ask…\n\n\n\nAdditionally, Nobu sounds like “no boo”, and could be considered a continuation of the previous line, suggesting Future doesn’t like to take women on dates.\n\nNobu gets a solid following with the hip-hop crowd. Drake referenced it on “Who Do You Love”:\n\nAnd man shout my nigga Game he just rolled through / Eatin' crab out in Malibu at Nobu", "annotation_id": "7835104", "url": "https://genius.com/7835104", "state": "accepted", "votes": 74, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "line": "I just found my tempo like I’m DJ Mustard, woo", "vault_lines": ["I just copped that tempo, DJ Mustard, woo", "I just found my tempo like I'm DJ Mustard, woo"], "meaning": "Producer DJ Mustard has made countless hits off his Bay Area sound. His songs typically reside around the 95 BPM range. He’s also hit on a sound that is incredibly popular and stuck with it, unflinchingly.\n\nAs it turns out, DJ Mustard’s favorite rapper is Drake.", "annotation_id": "7835089", "url": "https://genius.com/7835089", "state": "accepted", "votes": 181, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "line": "You don’t have to call, I hit my dance like Usher, woo", "vault_lines": ["You don't have to call, I hit my dance like Usher, woo"], "meaning": "An allusion to Usher’s popular song, “U Don’t Have to Call.” Usher’s known for being an exceptional dancer, so it makes sense for Drake to emulate him, as Drake famously attempted at OVO Fest 2014.\n\n\n\nIncidentally, a version of “U Don’t Have to Call” made its way on to Erykah Badu’s stellar 2016 release “U Cain’t Use My Phone,” a concept-mixtape of telephonic songs, which may have taken as its jumping off point Drake’s other massive hit of the year, “Hotline Bling.”", "annotation_id": "7835060", "url": "https://genius.com/7835060", "state": "accepted", "votes": 88, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "line": "Mutombo with the bitches, you keep gettin’ rejected, woo", "vault_lines": ["Mutombo with the bitches, you keep gettin' rejected, woo"], "meaning": "Former NBA center Dikembe Mutombo is widely regarded as one of the best shot-blockers of all time. He was well-known for his “finger-wag” gesture after blocking a shot. The ladies “reject” Drake’s competition much like Dikembe denied shots on the court.\n\n\n\nRumor has it, Dikembe once entered a Georgetown club and said “WHO WANTS TO SEX MUTOMBO?” We can imagine Drake getting away with something similar.", "annotation_id": "7835056", "url": "https://genius.com/7835056", "state": "accepted", "votes": 130, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "line": "Hundred cousins out in Memphis, they so country, wow", "vault_lines": ["Hundred cousins out in Memphis, they so country, wow"], "meaning": "Drake has deep ties with Memphis, his father’s hometown and a regular haunt of his during childhood.\n\nI miss Memphis, Tennessee, my cousins, my dad\nThe simplistic beauty that all of them Southerners have.", "annotation_id": "7835039", "url": "https://genius.com/7835039", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "line": "Lobster and Celine for all my babies that I miss Chicken fingers, french fries for them hoes that wanna diss", "vault_lines": ["Lobster and Celine for all my babies that I miss", "Chicken fingers, french fries for them hoes that wanna diss"], "meaning": "Drake is no stranger to lacing women with expensive items. Céline is a high end French fashion label, and Drizzy has been known to indulge in the odd lobster and steak. On the flip side, women below the Drake stratosphere are treated to fast food.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/Whataburger/status/627129622086352897\n\nWomen that seek to diss Drake turn their twitter fingers in to chicken fingers, made even more potent by Meek Mill’s conspicuous absence.", "annotation_id": "7835029", "url": "https://genius.com/7835029", "state": "accepted", "votes": 96, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "line": "Heard they came through Magic City on a Monday Heard they had the club wild, it was star-studded", "vault_lines": ["Heard they came through Magic City on a Monday", "Heard they had the club wild, it was star-studded"], "meaning": "“Magic City” is the name of a famous Atlanta strip club, known for being the place where:\n\nFortunes rain from the rafters, where women with impossible bodies call the shots, and where a DJ who spins your track can make you a star.\n\nIt’s an exclusive strip club for rappers and producers to meet, listen to live music on stage, and get crazy intoxicated. DJ Esoco’s set is on a Monday night, so it’s likely Drake and Future stopped by while recording the mixtape.\n\n\n\nFuture is a frequent visitor to this spot, and in fact jumpstarted his career by getting publicity from playing his music at the club:\n\nConsider the rapper Future. Not five years ago, Future was virtually unknown. He used to hang out at Magic City every week, back near the DJ booth. Esco started playing Future’s music. Esco started playing his music a lot. Eventually Future started to dominate Magic City. And when he started dominating Magic City, suddenly he was played on the radio; suddenly he signed a major record deal. Suddenly, Future became a guy who gets engaged to Ciara and takes her to sit in the front row at Milan Fashion Week.", "annotation_id": "7835027", "url": "https://genius.com/7835027", "state": "accepted", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "line": "I hit that Ginóbili with my left hand up like woo", "vault_lines": ["I hit that Ginóbili with my left hand up like woo"], "meaning": "Drake shouts out fellow Toronto rapper Mo-G’s song “Still,” which has its own dance. Drake mimics the dance in his “Energy” video.\n\nSan Antonio Spurs shooting guard Manu Ginobili shoots left-handed, so that hand will always be raised on his followthrough. Drake actually shoots right-handed, but we get the feeling he won’t be hitting threes anytime soon.", "annotation_id": "7834934", "url": "https://genius.com/7834934", "state": "accepted", "votes": 156, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumpman", "status": "done", "targets": 28, "clicked": 28, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-and-future-jumpman-lyrics", "genius_title": "Jumpman"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Little Bit", "line": "And I will never ever be the first, to say it", "vault_lines": ["And I will never ever be the first, to say it"], "meaning": "Drake says he never ever will be the first one to reveal his love for a girl, if she wants to be in a relationship with him she has to tell him she loves him, not the other way around.", "annotation_id": "38374820", "url": "https://genius.com/38374820", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Little Bit", "line": "You could teach me many things I’m just scared to learn a lesson", "vault_lines": ["You could teach me many things", "I'm just scared to learn a lesson"], "meaning": "He sees genuine growth and connection with her, but fears it’ll fall apart and leave him hurt, calling it a “lesson.” He’s scared of opening up only to regret it.", "annotation_id": "37885503", "url": "https://genius.com/37885503", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Little Bit", "line": "Hands down, I’m too proud for love But with eyes shut, it’s you I’m thinkin’ of", "vault_lines": ["Hands down, I'm too proud for love", "But with eyes shut, it's you I'm thinkin' of"], "meaning": "“hands down i’m too proud for love but whit eyes shut, it’s you i’m thinking of”\n\nLykke Li is saying that she’s unwilling for a relationship but thinks of her ‘lover’ but don’t want to be whit them because SHE’S TOO PROUD FOR LOVE.", "annotation_id": "36085011", "url": "https://genius.com/36085011", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Little Bit", "line": "A little bit, a little bit A little bit in love with you I guess that I’m a little bit, a little bit A little bit in love with you", "vault_lines": ["A little bit in love with you", "I guess that I'm a little bit, a little bit", "I love you, love you, a little bit", "I think I'm a little bit, little bit", "Little bit in love with me", "A little bit in love with you, oh", "A little bit, a little bit"], "meaning": "Drake calls it “a little bit” in love as a way to protect himself, and make the confession feel safer. He downplays his love to see how she reacts. If she pulls back, he can say it wasn’t serious. If she leans in, he can reveal more. He’s clearly falling deeper than he wants to admit, but he downplays it to avoid looking vulnerable or getting hurt.\n\nDrake recently did a skit, before his release of $ome $exy $ongs 4U with PartyNextDoor, highlighting how men from Toronto find anyway to confess their love for a girl without explicitly saying, “I love you.” Here, Drake understates his love by saying “A little bit.”", "annotation_id": "35371382", "url": "https://genius.com/35371382", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Little Bit", "line": "And basically, to see a change in me I’d be losing, so I just ignore you, yeah", "vault_lines": ["And basically, to see a change in me", "I'd be losing, so I just ignore you, yeah"], "meaning": "Drake means if he changes for this girl, he would be losing himself because he’s sure he’s gonna get played. But he still loves her and doesn’t wanna hurt her so he ignores her otherwise he’d end up saying something stupid.", "annotation_id": "31891347", "url": "https://genius.com/31891347", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
