{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jaded", "line": "And like guns with the ink in, you’re gettin’ under my skin", "vault_lines": ["And like guns with the ink in, you're gettin' under my skin"], "meaning": "“Guns with the ink” are tattoo guns, and to “get under skin” means to be irritating. The ink in tattoo guns also literally gets under the skin.\n\nOn a side note, Drake got a tattoo of an 11, representing Jorja Smith’s birthday of June 11, but now dedicates that same 11 tattoo to his son, Adonis, as he states on the final track, “March 14”:\n\nI got this 11 tatted for somebody, now it’s yours", "annotation_id": "15027145", "url": "https://genius.com/15027145", "state": "accepted", "votes": 48, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jaded", "line": "Lowdown, dirty, shameful, crazy", "vault_lines": ["Lowdown, dirty, shameful, crazy"], "meaning": "A Low Down Dirty Shame is a 1994 action comedy film, written, directed and starring Keenen Ivory Wayans and featuring Jada Pinkett Smith. In the film, Detective Shame (Wayans) develops feelings for a much younger Peaches (Pinkett Smith), who was 16 when they first met. When Peaches is 22, going on 23, Shame decides to work with her and the two become romantically involved.", "annotation_id": "15003315", "url": "https://genius.com/15003315", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jaded", "line": "Dragged me like two hours to your family’s house, for what?", "vault_lines": ["Dragged me like two hours to your family's house, for what?"], "meaning": "Drake booked multiple shows in London at 02 Arena in 2017, and Jorja Smith lives in London. Around the same time, he was spotted shopping with her in Walsall, West Midlands, where she’s from and where her parents still reside.  London to Walsall is about a two hour drive.", "annotation_id": "14989176", "url": "https://genius.com/14989176", "state": "accepted", "votes": 64, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jaded", "line": "Already got what you needed, I guess", "vault_lines": ["Already got what you needed, I guess", "Already gave you what you needed, I guess (Ooh yeah)"], "meaning": "Drake collaborated with Jorja Smith on two tracks—“Jorja Interlude” and “Get It Together,” from his 2017 playlist, More Life. He even let Jorja make guest appearances at his concerts in England. Drake could be alluding to their relationship and her moving on from him after gaining some exposure.", "annotation_id": "14904137", "url": "https://genius.com/14904137", "state": "accepted", "votes": 68, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jaded", "line": "We coulda waited, I wasn’t rushin’, difference in ages You’re old enough, but you’re still a baby", "vault_lines": ["We coulda waited, I wasn't rushin', difference in ages", "You're old enough, but you're still a baby"], "meaning": "In early 2017, Drake was 30 and Jorja was 19 when rumors surfaced that they were dating. In most of the world, 18 is considered “old enough” or the legal adult age.", "annotation_id": "14902774", "url": "https://genius.com/14902774", "state": "accepted", "votes": 118, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jaded", "line": "I need to know how the new nigga you got does the same thing I do for a living, but is way less wavy", "vault_lines": ["I need to know how the new nigga you got does the same thing", "I do for a living, but is way less wavy"], "meaning": "In a 2018 Billboard interview, Jorja revealed that she was dating Joel Compass, a singer from London:\n\nA lot of people are like, ‘Maybe you shouldn’t have a boyfriend at this [crucial] time,’” she says, “but I’m like, ‘I think I’m good. I’m writing good songs.’\"", "annotation_id": "14902385", "url": "https://genius.com/14902385", "state": "accepted", "votes": 56, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jaded", "line": "You played me, you played me, you played me", "vault_lines": ["You wanna hit me up when you make it", "You wanna get with me, stop", "You played me, you played me, you played me"], "meaning": "“Playing” people means to lead them on and give them a false impression. In this case, Drake could be expressing his thoughts towards Jorja Smith. He may feel that she used him to advance her music career.\n\nThis line is similar to a line from his 2015\n collab track, “Diamonds Dancing”:\n\nDoing me dirty, you doing me dirty", "annotation_id": "14877474", "url": "https://genius.com/14877474", "state": "accepted", "votes": 61, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jaded", "line": "Pretty little young thing (Young thing)", "vault_lines": ["Pretty little young thing (Young thing)"], "meaning": "“Pretty little Young Thing” is possibly a callback to Michael Jackson’s 1982 track “PYT.” Jackson also makes a posthumous appearance on the Scorpion track, “Don’t Matter to Me.”\n\nJorja Smith was only 19 years old at the time she allegedly started dating Drake.", "annotation_id": "14876871", "url": "https://genius.com/14876871", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
