{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Neatly", "line": "Slave to the cat, I prove it, God gave me six lives too", "vault_lines": ["Slave to the cat, I prove it, God gave me six lives too"], "meaning": "Drake says “prove it” in a way that mimics a cat’s purr.\nHe also says he also has 6 lives too, like a cat. Whilst cats have 9 lives, Drake only has 6, because 6 upside down is a 9 (no pun intended). Also, I’m sure everyone knows already but “the 6” is Drake’s hometown, Toronto.", "annotation_id": "36702289", "url": "https://genius.com/36702289", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Neatly", "line": "Your ex, your ex, well, he move like six times two He a whole fuckin’ 12 ass nigga", "vault_lines": ["Your ex, your ex, well, he move like six times two", "He a whole fuckin' 12 ass nigga"], "meaning": "Drake uses math equations, which after multiplying, equates to the product of “12,” which is a colloquialism for the police—originating from police radio code 10-12 (a code used to notify officers of a presence in a specific location) and the 1968 police crime drama television series Adam-12.\n\nDrake has also had his fair share of past controversial experiences with the law, as he was previously detained by Swedish law enforcement in July 2022 for resisting arrest—with a letter being sent to him shortly after the incident:", "annotation_id": "29894619", "url": "https://genius.com/29894619", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Neatly", "line": "I’ma have to move neatly for you", "vault_lines": ["I'ma have to move neatly for you"], "meaning": "“Neatly” is common Toronto slang that, unsurprisingly, has more or less the same definition as the word itself.\n\nIt is often used as a hyperbolic expression in a variety of contexts:\n\nWe fucked that guy up, he got dealt with neatly.", "annotation_id": "28992718", "url": "https://genius.com/28992718", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Neatly", "line": "The HK bussin’ like an AK for real", "vault_lines": ["The HK bussin' like an AK for real"], "meaning": "An older version of Neatly used to include the lyric “That thing stay bussin' like an AK for real” , in the newest version posted on OVO Sound Radio Season 3 Episode 15 Drake says “The H.K. bussin'” H.K. Referring to Heckler & Koch, a german gun manufacture famous for making guns such as the G36C, and MP5… He’s stating that this H.K. gun he is reffering to is shooting similar to a AK47, AK47’s being very mainstream and robust, while H.K. guns tend to be more of a niche high quality tactical weapons.", "annotation_id": "24730193", "url": "https://genius.com/24730193", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Neatly", "line": "The HK bussin’ like an AK for real", "vault_lines": ["The HK bussin' like an AK for real"], "meaning": "An older version of Neatly used to include the lyric “That thing stay bussin' like an AK for real” , in the newest version posted on OVO Sound Radio Season 3 Episode 15 Drake says “The H.K. bussin'” H.K. Referring to Heckler & Koch, a german gun manufacture famous for making guns such as the G36C, and MP5… He’s stating that this H.K. gun he is reffering to is shooting similar to a AK47, AK47’s being very mainstream and robust, while H.K. guns tend to be more of a niche high quality tactical weapons.", "annotation_id": "24730173", "url": "https://genius.com/24730173", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
