{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "OVO Sound Radio Episode 53 Tracklist", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-ovo-sound-radio-episode-53-tracklist-lyrics", "genius_title": "OVO Sound Radio Episode 53 Tracklist"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Up All Night", "line": "I’m busy gettin’ rich, I don’t want trouble I made enough for two niggas, boy: stunt double", "vault_lines": ["I'm busy gettin' rich, I don't want trouble", "I made enough for two niggas, boy: stunt double"], "meaning": "On the surface, Drake is bragging about how much money he’s making and how hard he’s able to stunt. The word “stunt” works as a double entendre: in modern slang, it means showing off wealth, jewelry, cars, or status, while its original meaning refers to performing a daring or impressive feat. .\n\nThere’s also a deeper rap reference here. The line can be read as a nod to Wayne and Birdman’s classic song Stuntin' Like My Daddy. By invoking that phrase, Drake pays homage to the two Cash Money figures who helped launch his career. At the same time, he’s implying that he earns enough money to keep both Wayne and Birdman’s pockets full, suggesting that he has no issue with his deal because everyone involved is eating.", "annotation_id": "40113761", "url": "https://genius.com/40113761", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Up All Night", "line": "Fixate", "vault_lines": ["I got that kinda—wait, wait—fixate"], "meaning": "Fixate / Fix 8\n\nNicki’s play on words here is fire—she’s dropping a double entendre. The way she flows at the start of the verse is clever, instead of ending her line exactly at the 8-count, she cuts it off just before. The song’s structure is based on an 8-count (a standard in music theory, where a bar is divided into eight beats).\n\nWhen she says, “Wait, wait—Fix 8,” she’s signaling the shift. She locks in the new line right on the new 8-count, not a moment too soon or too late. It’s a precise move that shows off her control over the beat.\n-Phetolo Kepadisa", "annotation_id": "32688362", "url": "https://genius.com/32688362", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Up All Night", "line": "Plus the game is in my pocket, nigga, this is what I does, ahh", "vault_lines": ["Plus the game is in my pocket, nigga, this is what I does, ahh"], "meaning": "Continuing the jeans analogy, Drake is saying that he’s got the rap game completely under control. He’s says he’s BEEN doing this and he thinks he’s doing pretty damn good.", "annotation_id": "31756042", "url": "https://genius.com/31756042", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Up All Night", "line": "I got money in these jeans, so they fit me kinda snug", "vault_lines": ["I got money in these jeans, so they fit me kinda snug"], "meaning": "Drake is saying he carries so much money on him that it is making it uncomfortable for him to wear his jeans because the cash is stretching them out.", "annotation_id": "31756034", "url": "https://genius.com/31756034", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Up All Night", "line": "M6 in front of M2", "vault_lines": ["M6 in front of M2"], "meaning": "Nicki has a manual transmission BMW M6 parked in front of M2, a night club that was presumably popping off in Chelsea at the time of the song’s release but has since permanently closed.", "annotation_id": "29945868", "url": "https://genius.com/29945868", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Up All Night", "line": "Cap on, brim bent, Denzel, every time", "vault_lines": ["Cap on, brim bent, Denzel, every time"], "meaning": "Drake refers to Denzel Washington always being seen in a baseball cap.  The brim on his baseball caps are always bent.", "annotation_id": "28441744", "url": "https://genius.com/28441744", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Up All Night", "line": "Niggas with no money act like money isn’t everything", "vault_lines": ["Niggas with no money act like money isn't everything"], "meaning": "People who are broke will act like money isn’t a big deal, but they are only saying it as an excuse for being broke and if they had money, then they wouldn’t be saying that.", "annotation_id": "28441720", "url": "https://genius.com/28441720", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
