{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Up All Night", "line": "Man, for Pete’s sake, scratch that—sweepstakes", "vault_lines": ["Man, for Pete's sake, scratch that—sweepstakes"], "meaning": "For Pete’s sake is an idiom that means to express frustration or annoyance.\n\nTo scratch that means to disregard what you were previously going to do.\n\nScratch-off tickets are made with the intention of making the games as fun as possible for players, which includes offering an easy user experience that conceals the results until the final scratch.", "annotation_id": "26863142", "url": "https://genius.com/26863142", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Up All Night", "line": "On a diet, but I’m doin’ donuts in a 6-speed", "vault_lines": ["On a diet, but I'm doin' donuts in a 6-speed"], "meaning": "Nicki says she is on a diet but she is doing donuts, which is the confectionary treat, hence relating to the diet part .\n\nDoing donuts is also spinning a car around in circular motion which is popular among rap culture, so she is implying that she is doing this committing this act in a 6 speed which  typically means a manual transmission that has six gears  Nicki would later reference this in Trey Songz ’s ‘Bottoms Up’ track.\n\n\n\n‘'I rep Young Money ,you know Slim , Baby\nAnd we be doin donuts while we waving the 380’'", "annotation_id": "26113454", "url": "https://genius.com/26113454", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
