{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Up All Night", "line": "That was just a keepsake, bought the president The Louis presidential briefcase, never been a cheapskate", "vault_lines": ["That was just a keepsake, bought the president", "The Louis presidential briefcase, never been a cheapskate"], "meaning": "-‘'A cheapskate’‘ is someone who tries to avoid paying a fair share of costs or expenses.\nBut Nicki is saying for the reminder that she bought the president a louis vuitton presidential briefcase.", "annotation_id": "25254598", "url": "https://genius.com/25254598", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Up All Night", "line": "I’m a bad bitch, I ain’t never been a mixed breed", "vault_lines": ["I'm a bad bitch, I ain't never been a mixed breed"], "meaning": "‘'A mongrel, mutt or mixed-breed dog’‘ dogs considerd lower in bloodline linege than pure bred dogs. So when she calls herself a ’‘bad bitch’‘ ( Bad bitch is a female dog) she saying she’s pure bad bitch, no other ’‘mixes\"involved.", "annotation_id": "25254436", "url": "https://genius.com/25254436", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Up All Night", "line": "Man I love my team, I would die for them niggas, aww", "vault_lines": ["Aww, man I love my team", "Man I love my team, I would die for them niggas, aww"], "meaning": "He is most likely referring to his OVO Crew. The most notable members of his OVO Crew, some of which are his day-one friends, include Noah “40” Shebib, Oliver North, Ryan, OB, Niko, Chubbs, Boi-1da, and Future the Prince.", "annotation_id": "24751175", "url": "https://genius.com/24751175", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Up All Night", "line": "I mean, we can’t even rock them shoes If it don’t got a comma on the price tag, you know? I mean, I mean but then again Who, who looks at the price tag, you know?", "vault_lines": ["I mean, we can't even rock them shoes", "If it don't got a comma on the price tag, you know?", "I mean, I mean but then again", "Who, who looks at the price tag, you know?"], "meaning": "Nicki Minaj & Drake are two of raps biggest names. Seeding from Lil Wayne’s cosign, to literal signing and raising up in their early careers, the artists have reached undeniable recognition and renown as potentially the biggest male and female MCs of all time, especially as well as a duo.\n\nNicki Minaj boasts a net worth of $80M, Drake checks in at $180M. It only makes sense why the two artists would filter their shopping to items in the thousand and up price class. Shopping in this manner solidifies the status check of competitive artists as such. The New York native female artist then disregards the previous statement to signify that her financial status is so high she doesn’t have a care for the price on the tag. She knows she can afford it because of her level as one of the biggest and richest female rappers of all time.", "annotation_id": "24751155", "url": "https://genius.com/24751155", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Up All Night", "line": "Which bitch you know made a million off a mixtape?", "vault_lines": ["Which bitch you know made a million off a mixtape?"], "meaning": "Nicki flaunts the success of her third mixtape, Beam Me Up Scotty (2009), released a year earlier to critical and commercial acclaim. The song “I Get Crazy” charted in the top 40 on the U.S. Billboard Hot Rap Songs and Hot R&B/Hip-Hop Songs charts. According to MTV News, the Beam Me Up Scotty mixtape and her appearance on Lil Wayne’s “Come Up” DVD are the projects that helped cement Nicki’s fan base.", "annotation_id": "20383246", "url": "https://genius.com/20383246", "state": "pending", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Up All Night", "line": "[Verse 2: Nicki Minaj]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "In November 2016, Billboard claimed Minaj out-rapped Drake with this verse, elaborating:\n\nLike most of Drake’s verses, his two sets on ‘Up All Night’ are passable, but Nicki’s personality and ambidextrous flow is what shines here. She turns the awkward pause and stutter into a work of art, never losing the beat like a stumbling practitioner of drunken boxing: wobbly but untouchable. Again, the male rapper on the track sets the style and tone, then Nicki picks it up and does it better than he does.", "annotation_id": "19711765", "url": "https://genius.com/19711765", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Up All Night", "line": "And pop bottles with my team, Young Money ’til the death of me", "vault_lines": ["And pop bottles with my team, Young Money 'til the death of me"], "meaning": "To “pop bottles” means to celebrate. Nicki and Drizzy are successful members of the label Young Money, founded by Lil Wayne and Birdman, and have a lot to celebrate for their achievements.\n\nBirdman and Wayne also released the song “Pop Bottles” in 2007:\n\nStart with straight shots and then pop bottles (yeah)\nFlirt with the hood rats then pop models (uh-huh)", "annotation_id": "19674726", "url": "https://genius.com/19674726", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Up All Night", "line": "We got the Hawks, I ain’t talkin’ about the Peach State", "vault_lines": ["We got the Hawks, I ain't talkin' about the Peach State"], "meaning": "The “Peach State” is a nickname for the US state of Georgia, and is known to house several spots teams referencing birds in their title, including the Atlanta Hawks and the Atlanta Falcons. However, Nicki claims she isn’t talking about them, and instead uses the word “hawk” to refer to the act of selling goods and hustling, and Hawks has been also used as slang for guns.", "annotation_id": "18873781", "url": "https://genius.com/18873781", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Up All Night", "line": "Man I love my team, I would die for them niggas, aww", "vault_lines": ["Aww, man I love my team", "Man I love my team, I would die for them niggas, aww"], "meaning": "He is most likely referring to his OVO Crew. The most notable members of his OVO Crew, some of which are his day-one friends, include Noah “40” Shebib, Oliver North, Ryan, OB, Niko, Chubbs, Boi-1da, and Future the Prince.", "annotation_id": "14355852", "url": "https://genius.com/14355852", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Up All Night", "line": "Fame is like a drug that I’ve taken too much of But I never ever trip, just peace, happiness and love", "vault_lines": ["Fame is like a drug that I've taken too much of", "But I never ever trip, just peace, happiness and love"], "meaning": "Drake utilizes some smooth double entendre here regarding the homonym “trip”:\n\n\nHe isn’t letting fame get to him and he’s not about to fall off.\nHe elaborates on the “Fame is like a drug” phrase by alluding to the effects of psychedelic drugs (such as LSD or magic mushrooms). Drizzy keeps the metaphor going with “peace, happiness and love”—a common core value set of hippies (who are known to ingest entheogens).\n\n\n\nDrake is letting the listener know that, despite rising to the highest ranks, it hasn’t changed him.", "annotation_id": "13868715", "url": "https://genius.com/13868715", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Up All Night", "line": "(Ha ha ha ha ha)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "An interpolation of Biggie’s laugh in “What’s Beef?\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=94bNyh6BBB0#t=27", "annotation_id": "3231474", "url": "https://genius.com/3231474", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Up All Night", "line": "Drizzy say get her, I’ma get her", "vault_lines": ["Drizzy say get her, I'ma get her"], "meaning": "Either a nod to Nicki’s beef with Lil Kim or instructions to go get a girl like she did for Usher on “Little Freak”.\n\nThis is also a show of homage from Nicki to Remy Ma, who used a similar line to start her first verse on her 2005 record “Whuteva”.", "annotation_id": "17969", "url": "https://genius.com/17969", "state": "accepted", "votes": 37, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Up All Night", "status": "done", "targets": 24, "clicked": 24, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-up-all-night-lyrics", "genius_title": "Up All Night"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wu-Tang Forever", "line": "[Produced by Noah “40” Shebib]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The sample for this track is Loss Config by Zodiac:\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kV4rm1LOaGI", "annotation_id": "2682529", "url": "https://genius.com/2682529", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wu-Tang Forever", "line": "Open cases on me for a half a million each", "vault_lines": ["Open cases on me for a half a million each"], "meaning": "Drake’s court cases are numerous, people love to sue him. Drizzy may have his legal fiascoes, but the cases of drinks he’s been opening are just as pricey…", "annotation_id": "2201205", "url": "https://genius.com/2201205", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wu-Tang Forever", "line": "People like Mazin who was a best friend to me Start to become a distant memory Things change in that life, and this life started lacking synergy And fuckin’ with me mentally, I think it’s meant to be", "vault_lines": ["People like Mazin who was a best friend to me", "Start to become a distant memory", "Things change in that life, and this life started lacking synergy", "And fuckin' with me mentally, I think it's meant to be"], "meaning": "Mazin Elsadig was an actor on Degrassi and once close friends with Drake, as well as a collaborator. But now, he’s just a part of Drake’s past. No new friends, but sometimes you’re too busy for old ones.\n\n\n\nWith regards to “that life and this life started lackin' synergy,” his music career started to interfere with his acting career, but that was probably for the best .\n\nIn an interview with Ryan Seacrest, Drake acknowledged this line and clearly stated that Mazin is still his best friend. The line is just meant to indicate that most of his friends from the acting world aren’t as close to him as Mazin is.", "annotation_id": "2201167", "url": "https://genius.com/2201167", "state": "accepted", "votes": 122, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wu-Tang Forever", "line": "Then I hit you with the 9 a.m. in Dallas Who you like, baby, who you like?", "vault_lines": ["I could fuck you so good, then I hit you with the 9 a.m. in Dallas", "Who you like, baby, who you like?"], "meaning": "Drake wants to have sex with this girl and reference his song “9am in Dallas” at the same damn time!\n\nWho you like, tell me who it is\nI'mma make sure that that woman is the next one on my list\n\n\n\nDrake extends the “rap game” metaphor here as well, asking her (the rap game) which Drake does she like the most? “9AM in Dallas” Drake or “Shot For Me” Drake?", "annotation_id": "2201159", "url": "https://genius.com/2201159", "state": "accepted", "votes": 68, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wu-Tang Forever", "line": "I just gave the city life, it ain’t about who did it first It’s ’bout who did it right, niggas looking like “Preach”", "vault_lines": ["I just gave the city life, it ain't about who did it first", "It's 'bout who did it right, niggas looking like \"Preach\""], "meaning": "Drizzy is more concerned about who’s doing it best than who did it first. He was the one to make Toronto matter in rap and he’s setting records. Notable predecessors on the Torontonian hip hop scene include Kardinal Offishall, K-os, and K'naan (none of whom have achieved the fame Drake has)\n\nThis could also be applicable in terms of a relationship; being a girl’s last is better than being her first.\n\nSometimes when you’re spittin the truth it be like:", "annotation_id": "2201145", "url": "https://genius.com/2201145", "state": "accepted", "votes": 74, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wu-Tang Forever", "line": "Yeah, paranoid, always rolling with my mothafuckin’ boys But you gotta understand when it’s yours They don’t really leave your ass with a mothafuckin’ choice, man", "vault_lines": ["It's yours, it's yours, it's yours, it's yours", "Yeah, paranoid, always rolling with my mothafuckin' boys", "But you gotta understand when it's yours", "They don't really leave your ass with a mothafuckin' choice, man"], "meaning": "Drake rolls deep….\n\n\n\nIn his videos, at home, in the club, Drake has his OVO crew. Oh the price of fame, always having to hang out with your friends…\n\n“Trust issues” are a reoccurring theme in Drake’s music. In the previous line he talks about how he lost a good friend, and now he’s paranoid and doesn’t know if all of his friends are legit.\n\nUltimately, he still has a lot of boys that have his back.\n\nSeeing as how Drake is paying homage to vintage hip-hop on this track, it’s possible that these lines could be a reference to the classic Geto Boys song, “Mind Playing Tricks On Me.” Willie D spits a similar line in his verse.\n\nI take my boys everywhere I go because I’m paranoid", "annotation_id": "2201129", "url": "https://genius.com/2201129", "state": "accepted", "votes": 67, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wu-Tang Forever", "line": "And nowadays when I ask about who got it They say it’s yours, nobody else’s Yeah, this shit belong to nobody It’s yours, nobody else’s Yeah, this shit belong to nobody It’s yours, it’s yours, it’s yours, it’s yours That’s for sure, that’s for sure (Yeah) It’s yours, it’s yours, it’s yours, it’s yours That’s for sure, that’s for sure", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, this shit belong to nobody and that", "And nowadays when I ask about who got it", "They say it's yours, nobody else's", "It's yours, it's yours, it's yours, it's yours", "That's for sure, that's for sure (Yeah)", "Baby, it's yours, nobody else's", "Yeah, this shit belong to nobody", "It's yours, nobody else's"], "meaning": "Drake is coming through on his Wu-Tang, because he borrows “it’s yours” from Wu’s ‘97 triumphant hit “It’s Yourz” (which was originally sampled from “It’s Yours” by T La Rock & Jazzy Jay)\n\nWu’s track was more of a motivational call to action, whereas Drizzy is claiming the game and whatever this girl’s got to give.", "annotation_id": "2201124", "url": "https://genius.com/2201124", "state": "accepted", "votes": 124, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wu-Tang Forever", "line": "Machine gun raps for all my niggas in the back Stadium packed, just glad to see the city on the map", "vault_lines": ["(Machine gun rap for all my niggas in the back) Uh", "(Machine gun rap for all my niggas in the back) I", "Machine gun raps for all my niggas in the back", "Stadium packed, just glad to see the city on the map"], "meaning": "Paying homage to Raekwon who started Wu’s “It'z Yourz” with these exact bars.\n\nDrizzy added the note about his city to emphasize how he put Toronto on the map. He’s pleased to see that where he comes from matters in the game.", "annotation_id": "2201107", "url": "https://genius.com/2201107", "state": "accepted", "votes": 79, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wu-Tang Forever", "status": "done", "targets": 8, "clicked": 8, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-wu-tang-forever-lyrics", "genius_title": "Wu-Tang Forever"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "About the Game", "line": "Nowadays I peak they interests Especially when life’s bringing them pain and lately they been stressed", "vault_lines": ["Nowadays I peak they interests", "Especially when life's bringing them pain and lately they been stressed"], "meaning": "Drake has gained appeal in the rap game for his “singsongy” delivery and songs that describe the sad feelings that he was experiencing. He even gained the nickname “Heartbreak Drake” due to his mixtape of the same name. His relatable and depressed themes have made people enjoy listening to his music and has resulted in widespread fame.", "annotation_id": "13911572", "url": "https://genius.com/13911572", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "About the Game", "line": "To land in the top ten slip in the top five Same thing in the top four trust I’m hot boy Maybe even the top three Trey you got me?", "vault_lines": ["To land in the top ten slip in the top five", "Same thing in the top four trust I'm hot boy", "Maybe even the top three Trey you got me?"], "meaning": "Even from the start, Drake had plans of slowly rising in the rap game until he made it to top three status (and beyond). After reaching studio and commercial success, he finally accomplished his goal and continued to rise. On “Grammies”, Drake said:\n\nTop five, no debatin'\nTop five, top five, top five\n\nSince then, on his track “Gyalchester”, Drake proved that he had already achieved top 5 potential and was actually number one when he rapped:\n\nI know I said top five, but I’m top two\nAnd I’m not two and I got one\nThought you had one, but it’s not one, nigga, nah", "annotation_id": "13911529", "url": "https://genius.com/13911529", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "About the Game", "line": "But it’s all eyes on me like I’m copying some vows for the bar", "vault_lines": ["But it's all eyes on me like I'm copying some vows for the bar"], "meaning": "At the time of this track’s release in 2007, Drake was only just starting to gain popularity and traction in his career. Drake didn’t reach the Billboard Top 10 until 2009—with “Best I Ever Had”—and didn’t get his first #1 hit until 2010, with a song he was only featured on—Rihanna’s “What’s My Name.”\n\nThe word “eye” is homophonous with the subject “I.” The same goes for their plurals: “eyes” and “I’s”.\n\nAt most weddings, each partner is expected to recite a Declaration of Consent. This involves an officiant asking each partner if they will abide to a certain vow. Each partner responds with either “I do,” or “I will.” The traditional Declaration of Consent has from 3 to 6 “I will\"s and \"I do\"s, and can even be greater than that depending on the version of the Declaration.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kRIbYZS36sE", "annotation_id": "13911499", "url": "https://genius.com/13911499", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "About the Game", "line": "By nineteen I might seem destined for millions", "vault_lines": ["By nineteen I might seem destined for millions"], "meaning": "When Room For Improvement was released (2006) Drake was 19, and it already seemed like he was going to be a huge star.\n\nBy the time Drake turned 25 he already had 25 mill, and now, his net worth is 30 million, so Drake was definitely destined for millions.", "annotation_id": "2679805", "url": "https://genius.com/2679805", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "About the Game", "line": "See broke niggas is the problem and us is the scape goat", "vault_lines": ["See broke niggas is the problem and us is the scape goat"], "meaning": "The problem with capitalism is that there will always be the rich, and always be the poor. It’s the rich people’s fault that the poor people are struggling.\n\nDrake could also be commenting on society’s perception of black people, where the poorer ones are likely to be problematic and so they are quick to heap blame on the more successful artists living a lavish lifestyle.", "annotation_id": "2073552", "url": "https://genius.com/2073552", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "About the Game", "status": "done", "targets": 5, "clicked": 5, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-about-the-game-lyrics", "genius_title": "About the Game"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CRYING IN CHANEL", "line": "Like my love language ain’t felt, damn", "vault_lines": ["Like my love language ain't felt, damn"], "meaning": "Gift-giving is one of the “five love languages.” This song is about Drake attempting to express his emotions by gift-giving.", "annotation_id": "38083721", "url": "https://genius.com/38083721", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CRYING IN CHANEL", "line": "You know I love you, girl, but it’s goin’ one way It’s goin’ in one ear and out the other way", "vault_lines": ["You know I love you, girl, but it's goin' one way", "It's goin' in one ear and out the other way"], "meaning": "Drake does not feel like his expression of love is being reciprocated by this woman, despite the amount of money he is willing to spend on her. This is because he cannot buy her love.", "annotation_id": "38083703", "url": "https://genius.com/38083703", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CRYING IN CHANEL", "line": "’Cause that price on your love", "vault_lines": ["Put that price on your love", "'Cause that price on your love"], "meaning": "“Is there a price on your love?”\n\nDrake is struggling to comprehend that he cannot buy this woman’s love.", "annotation_id": "38083699", "url": "https://genius.com/38083699", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CRYING IN CHANEL", "line": "Showtime", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This “showtime” soundbite is also used on the track “Celibacy.”", "annotation_id": "38083681", "url": "https://genius.com/38083681", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CRYING IN CHANEL", "line": "And it’s drivin’ me crazy", "vault_lines": ["And it's drivin' me crazy"], "meaning": "Drake is struggling with the fact that this woman is holding sentimental attachment to gifts she received in a previous relationship.\n\nDrake interprets these gifts as more than material attachment.", "annotation_id": "38083605", "url": "https://genius.com/38083605", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CRYING IN CHANEL", "line": "Five hundred bands, you better be mine", "vault_lines": ["Hundred bands, you're mine", "Five hundred bands, you better be mine"], "meaning": "Even Drake has a limit, albeit not monetary. He goes on naming dollar amounts, starting at 10 bands ($10,000) and ends up stopping at 500 bands (half a million).\nThis suggests that while he arguably could spend a lot more than that, his limit stems not from a lack of money but rather from a lack of willingness to pour endless money into a woman when he’s clearly still assessing whether she’s “his”.", "annotation_id": "37285054", "url": "https://genius.com/37285054", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CRYING IN CHANEL", "line": "That you just can’t part ways with", "vault_lines": ["that you just can't part ways with", "You just can't part ways with it", "Sentimental gifts that you just can't part ways with"], "meaning": "Drake employs some situational irony in this bar, naming gifts with a lot of monetary value, and claiming she only has sentimental “value” for them, suggesting that she either does not care for their monetary worth (unlikely) or that she uses sentiment as an excuse to hide the fact that she values the gifts beyond the fact that they were gifted by past lovers.", "annotation_id": "37285044", "url": "https://genius.com/37285044", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CRYING IN CHANEL", "line": "Put you on a jet ’cause I miss you and I love you And I wanna see my baby", "vault_lines": ["Put you on a jet 'cause I miss you and I love you", "And I wanna see my baby"], "meaning": "Drake pays for a plane ticket for the woman to come visit him because he loves and misses her dearly. Several other Drake songs contain similar themes of being away from someone and/or paying for women’s travel, including Flight’s Booked from Honestly Nevermind.", "annotation_id": "36986343", "url": "https://genius.com/36986343", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CRYING IN CHANEL", "line": "Carti’ bracelets", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Cartier is a luxury French jewelery maker. Their bracelets are highly desirable, often costing several thousand dollars each.\n\n\n\nDrake has a history with Cartier jewelry, including in September 2023, when he gifted Sexyy Red an iced-out Cartier watch after they met at his “It’s All a Blur” tour.", "annotation_id": "36977476", "url": "https://genius.com/36977476", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CRYING IN CHANEL", "line": "Cuban links", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Cuban links are chains made of expensive gold, and are typically thick, high-quality, and often diamond-encrusted.", "annotation_id": "36977459", "url": "https://genius.com/36977459", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CRYING IN CHANEL", "line": "Bustdown watches", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "A “bust down watch” is a luxury timepiece that has been modified with diamonds or other precious gemstones, which are drilled and set into the watch’s dial and bracelet. A bustdown is a customization process, and can be applied to any of the luxury watch brands such as Rolex,  Audemars Piguet, or Patek Philippe.", "annotation_id": "36977434", "url": "https://genius.com/36977434", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CRYING IN CHANEL", "line": "She say things I do for her, I did for someone else I’m just tryna help, make me feel bad about myself", "vault_lines": ["She say things I do for her, I did for someone else", "I'm just tryna help, make me feel bad about myself"], "meaning": "The girl knows Drake has bought Chanel for other women before.", "annotation_id": "36860374", "url": "https://genius.com/36860374", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CRYING IN CHANEL", "line": "Shawty right here cryin’ in the middle of Chanel Are those tears of joy from your eyes? I can’t tell", "vault_lines": ["Shawty right here cryin' in the middle of Chanel", "Are those tears of joy from your eyes? I can't tell"], "meaning": "Drake is confused—he brought this girl to the Chanel store to buy her nice pieces and she is crying. She is carrying baggage from past relationships and it is coming out in the Chanel store in front of Drake.", "annotation_id": "36860359", "url": "https://genius.com/36860359", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CRYING IN CHANEL", "line": "Whoever set the stone, baby, that ain’t gon’ cut it", "vault_lines": ["Whoever set the stone, baby, that ain't gon' cut it"], "meaning": "The stone setting technique on the woman’s current jewelry is not up to the standard of the jewelry Drake typically buys.", "annotation_id": "36860349", "url": "https://genius.com/36860349", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CRYING IN CHANEL", "line": "I’ll buy somethin’ better for you, fuck it Point somethin’ out, I’ll get it for you, fuck it", "vault_lines": ["I'll buy somethin' better for you, fuck it", "Point somethin' out, I'll get it for you, fuck it"], "meaning": "Drake is saying he can afford better jewelry than her previous exes.", "annotation_id": "36860341", "url": "https://genius.com/36860341", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CRYING IN CHANEL", "line": "Say you went through too much for it You had to fake fall in love for it", "vault_lines": ["Say you went through too much for it", "You had to fake fall in lovе for it"], "meaning": "The girl had to endure a toxic relationship to get the jewelry that her ex boyfriend bought her. She likely considered leaving the relationship, but the jewelry acted as a bandaid on an otherwise broken relationship.", "annotation_id": "36860317", "url": "https://genius.com/36860317", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CRYING IN CHANEL", "line": "Even if I replace it You just can’t part ways with it", "vault_lines": ["that you just can't part ways with", "Even if I replace it", "You just can't part ways with it", "Sentimental gifts that you just can't part ways with", "(I just wanna ride with you), I just wanna ride", "I just wanna ride with you"], "meaning": "Drake is saying he can rebuy, and even buy better versions, of the jewelry that her previous bought her. But, she still treasures a small part of that previous relationship, so she is having trouble letting go of the pieces.", "annotation_id": "36860306", "url": "https://genius.com/36860306", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CRYING IN CHANEL", "line": "I could tell you love your prized possessions, what’s your favorite?", "vault_lines": ["I could tell you love your prized possessions, what's your favorite?"], "meaning": "The “prized possessions” here are gifts (particularly jewelry) that a previous man bought this woman. Drake is quasi mockingly asking her which is her favorite of these gifts.", "annotation_id": "36860288", "url": "https://genius.com/36860288", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CRYING IN CHANEL", "line": "When I met you, you was in the club servin’ bottles Workin’ for Mickey", "vault_lines": ["When I met you, you was in the club servin' bottles"], "meaning": "Manish Mickey Oberoi is a Toronto-based entrepreneur and brand strategist known for his work in event production, marketing, and brand activations. He began his career organizing social and music events and has since expanded to collaborating with A-list celebrities, Fortune 500 companies, and globally recognized brands.\nDrake is talking about meeting this young lady working at a club or event hosted by Mickey.", "annotation_id": "35278846", "url": "https://genius.com/35278846", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CRYING IN CHANEL", "line": "All you got to show for that is sentimental gifts", "vault_lines": ["All you got to show for that is sentimental gifts"], "meaning": "Drake speaks of the gifts his girl has been gifted by previous partners. He would like her to get rid of these gifts to facilitate a fresh start. However, she is emotionally attached to the presents and does not want to throw them away, likely due to their nostalgic and sentimental value.", "annotation_id": "35028825", "url": "https://genius.com/35028825", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CRYING IN CHANEL", "line": "Van Cleef necklace", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Van Cleef is a high-end jewelry brand particularly known for its shamrock motives. Especially the bracelets and necklaces with the shamrock pieces have become popular.", "annotation_id": "35028782", "url": "https://genius.com/35028782", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CRYING IN CHANEL", "line": "Had to tell you to gwan easy", "vault_lines": ["Had to tell you to gwan easy"], "meaning": "“Gwan Easy” is Toronto slang for telling someone to “take it easy” or “calm down”. The term originates from Jamaican language, as Toronto is home to a large Jamaican population.", "annotation_id": "34570182", "url": "https://genius.com/34570182", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CRYING IN CHANEL", "line": "I’ll trick-trick on you like I’m Detroit thuggin’", "vault_lines": ["I'll trick-trick on you like I'm Detroit thuggin'"], "meaning": "Christian Anthony Mathis (aka Trick-Trick), is a rapper and gangster from Detroit.\n\nA trick is also a term for somebody who spends a lot of money on women.\n\nThis might also be a subtle diss to Rick Ross, as in 2014, Trick Trick’s mob reportedly blocked Rick Ross' Detroit concert from happening.", "annotation_id": "34566555", "url": "https://genius.com/34566555", "state": "pending", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CRYING IN CHANEL", "line": "(Can I trust you?)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake samples the tag of Metro Boomin. Specifically this particular tag is from the April 2024 track featuring A$AP Rocky, “Show of Hands”. The track is one from Future and Metro’s April 2024 album WE STILL DON’T TRUST YOU.\n\nThe track was seen as another shot at Drake from the duo and from Rocky, who has a long-standing feud with the Toronto native.", "annotation_id": "34560632", "url": "https://genius.com/34560632", "state": "accepted", "votes": 67, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CRYING IN CHANEL", "status": "done", "targets": 24, "clicked": 24, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-crying-in-chanel-lyrics", "genius_title": "CRYING IN CHANEL"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Do It All", "line": "N.Y. forever, nigga, Diddy", "vault_lines": ["N.Y. forever, nigga, Diddy"], "meaning": "It’s possible this was a reference track meant for Diddy. Drake collaborated with Combs around this time frame on his Dirty Money album and it was also rumored that his song 0-100 was originally a demo for Diddy.\n\nWhen the later track was never given to Diddy, it was rumored to have started the two’s ongoing beef with eachother that extended to 2015’s 4PM in Calabasas.", "annotation_id": "35750830", "url": "https://genius.com/35750830", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Do It All", "line": "You can’t have my heart, the doctor told me I’d be dead without it", "vault_lines": ["You can’t have my heart, the doctor told me I’d be dead without it"], "meaning": "you heart pumps blood to everything in your body so you’re dead if someone else has it, scientifically speaking", "annotation_id": "30937649", "url": "https://genius.com/30937649", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
