{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Girls Love Beyoncé", "line": "’Cause those other men are practice", "vault_lines": ["'Cause those other men are practice"], "meaning": "Drake references his 2011 song Practice from Take Care.", "annotation_id": "37095986", "url": "https://genius.com/37095986", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Girls Love Beyoncé", "line": "Say my name, say my name", "vault_lines": ["Say my name, say my name", "Let me make you say my name"], "meaning": "Drizzy is looking for reassurance from this woman. He wants her to announce that he is the only one that’s on her mind; in private and in public.\n\nThis is the self-conscious side of Drake that we see on lamenting tracks such as “Brand New” and “Marvin’s Room.”", "annotation_id": "2103160", "url": "https://genius.com/2103160", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Girls Love Beyoncé", "line": "I need someone I leave through the front door with", "vault_lines": ["I need someone I leave through the front door with"], "meaning": "This line is followed by “‘Cause we don’t wanna hide no more” because he wants to have a relationship that he can make public. He wants to walk right out the front door of a restaurant or a store where paparazzi will be waiting and taking photos rather than using the back door so no one will see them.\n\nHe wants them to be a real couple no hiding. Or / And he need someone to be with him not just be there at certain times he need them all the time and someone who really cares about a relationship", "annotation_id": "1738287", "url": "https://genius.com/1738287", "state": "pending", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Girls Love Beyoncé", "line": "No, I’m not alone", "vault_lines": ["No, I'm not alone"], "meaning": "He’s really saying that he’s not the only one experiencing this kind of feeling. How does he “have her” when he’s talking about trying to find “her?”\n\nPlaying into the next line, “ Even though nothing was the same” could also be Drake answering a girlfriend’s/lover’s question about cheating (“Are you alone right now? Who are you with?”); Drake answers honestly (“I’m not alone” = I’m with a girl), but “nothing was the same” means that sex with the other girl wasn’t as good or meaningful as sex with his lover / steady girl. He’s being honest and self-loathing.", "annotation_id": "1685185", "url": "https://genius.com/1685185", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Girls Love Beyoncé", "line": "[Chorus: James Fauntleroy, James Fauntleroy & Drake]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "You might recognize Fauntleroy from the intro to “Clique”, or Frank Ocean’s cover of his song “Fertilizer”.\n\nFauntleroy is a former member of The Underdogs production team, a member of The Y’s production group (along with Justin Timberlake) and a collaborator of the Cocaine 80s collective (with No I.D. and Common – under this group he has made two mixtapes and is gathering underground hype with songs such as “Nameless”). He is signed to Jay-Z’s Roc Nation.", "annotation_id": "1681754", "url": "https://genius.com/1681754", "state": "accepted", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Girls Love Beyoncé", "line": "But if you’re alone, then", "vault_lines": ["But if you're alone, then"], "meaning": "Regardless of how many people she is seeing, Drake will be there for her if she is alone.\n\nDrake references the famous Destiny’s Child song “Say My Name”, a song about cheating (Drake previously used similar wording on Rihanna’s “What’s My Name?”). He is telling his girl that if  no other dudes are around, she can prove it by saying his name straight up (and not talk in code). This serves to segue into the cover chorus by James Fauntleroy.", "annotation_id": "1681237", "url": "https://genius.com/1681237", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Girls Love Beyoncé", "line": "You try to act like it’s just me, but I am not alone", "vault_lines": ["You try to act like it's just me, but I am not alone"], "meaning": "She acts like he’s the only one she’s seeing, but he knows he’s not the only one. Drake often calls out girls for this type of behavior, in songs like “Poetic Justice”.\n\nDrake knows he’s not the only one that has admirers calling his phone, and the girls act like it only happens to him. The “but I am not alone” is also somewhat ironic, because he is ‘not alone’ in the sense that he is not the only one, but in reality he actually is alone.", "annotation_id": "1681218", "url": "https://genius.com/1681218", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Girls Love Beyoncé", "line": "I’m just trying to find a reason not to go out every evening", "vault_lines": ["I'm just trying to find a reason not to go out every evening"], "meaning": "When you go out and party every single night, it starts to get old. One motivation behind going out every evening is to get in touch with women, mostly on a superficial level, to distract himself from the loneliness and the desire for a deep relationship with someone he loves. So he wants to find a girl that fulfills this desire, and therefore gives him a reason not to go out every evening seeking an emotional connection.", "annotation_id": "1681161", "url": "https://genius.com/1681161", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Girls Love Beyoncé", "line": "And this ain’t no time for actin’ And this ain’t no time for games And this ain’t no time for uncertainty", "vault_lines": ["And this ain't no time for actin'", "And this ain't no time for games", "And this ain't no time for uncertainty", "And this ain't no time for locking your phone and not coming home"], "meaning": "At this point in his life he doesn’t have time to deal with petty bullshit. This circles back to the first two lines claiming that all girls are the same, which is why he is distant towards all of them\n\nThis isn’t the time in his life for girls to make mistakes, mess around, and be uncertain about things. He needs girls who can commit and be serious.\n\nAlso referring to the first two lines; he’s telling the woman not to act or play games because she should know by now he is “the one” and her other relationships were just “practice.”", "annotation_id": "1681084", "url": "https://genius.com/1681084", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Girls Love Beyoncé", "line": "Now forget how it felt when this shit move slow", "vault_lines": ["Now forget how it felt when this shit move slow"], "meaning": "He’s forgotten what it’s like to not be famous and live a normal lifestyle. Earlier in his career when he was an underground artist he had time, to work slowly on projects and building hype. Now, in 2013, the demand for him and his music is overwhelming and he feels like he has to rush projects out to keep the public happy.\n\nIn “Free Spirit”, Drake raps:\n\nThese days keep going by too fast, so give me anything to make shit go slow", "annotation_id": "1681077", "url": "https://genius.com/1681077", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Girls Love Beyoncé", "line": "I come through in whips that make a young boy take the long way home", "vault_lines": ["I come through in whips that make a young boy take the long way home"], "meaning": "Two possible meanings:\n\n\nHis cars are so nice that guys with basic cars go out of their way to avoid driving alongside Drake and being humiliated.\nHe drives the kind of car that would make a guy take the long way home so he can spend more time driving the car", "annotation_id": "1681062", "url": "https://genius.com/1681062", "state": "accepted", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Girls Love Beyoncé", "line": "Even though nothing was the same", "vault_lines": ["Even though nothing was the same"], "meaning": "He’s probably letting the girl he’s conversing with know that no relationship that he’s had with other girls has been quite the same since their relationship, which must’ve been GREAT.\n\nAlso a reference to his 3rd album Nothing Was The Same", "annotation_id": "1681052", "url": "https://genius.com/1681052", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Girls Love Beyoncé", "line": "All my young boys ’round me saying, “Get money and fuck these hoes” Where we learn these values? I do not know what to tell you", "vault_lines": ["All my young boys 'round me saying, \"Get money and fuck these hoes\"", "Where we learn these values? I do not know what to tell you"], "meaning": "Many of the men who Drake hangs out with, not to mention thousands around the globe, have a mentality to essentially, “fuck bitches, get money.” Many women see this lifestyle and mind state to be vulgar and unappealing.\n\nDrake wants to stress to his girl that he is not like this and is somewhat ashamed of the aforementioned mentality that his former self and his peers share.", "annotation_id": "1681038", "url": "https://genius.com/1681038", "state": "accepted", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Girls Love Beyoncé", "line": "I’ve been avoiding commitment That’s why I’m in this position", "vault_lines": ["This is why I've been saying", "I've been avoiding commitment", "That's why I'm in this position"], "meaning": "Here he admits that he his partially at fault for being in the situation he’s in. If he wasn’t always so distant in his past relationships he wouldn’t be stuck alone now. This could also be a play on the word “position” because he’s avoiding commitment by always just having sex in different “positions.”\n\nAs we know from other tracks, Drake is a  romantic guy. But because of the limelight he’s forced to avoid long-term relationships. And he already knows too well the good ones go if you wait too long.\n\nIt’s hard to commit because your scared to fail at something you want so bad.", "annotation_id": "1681036", "url": "https://genius.com/1681036", "state": "accepted", "votes": 37, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Girls Love Beyoncé", "line": "’Cause we don’t wanna hide no more Plus you’re not shy no more Neither of us wanna play the side no more", "vault_lines": ["'Cause we don't wanna hide no more", "Plus you're not shy no more", "Neither of us wanna play the side no more"], "meaning": "He doesn’t want to have to sneak around and keep his relationship hidden from everyone. Because “she” isn’t shy anymore, he can finally bring “her” out into the public light.\n\nHe also says that neither of them would like to be the side chick/dude/affair of the other person and that would be more of an incentive for them to finally go public with their relationship.\n\nThese lines probably recall the girl that he talked about on both Karaoke and in his feature verse on The Zone; not only is she getting used to the fame and the spotlight, but she’s liking it too and she doesn’t want to stay on the sideline anymore.", "annotation_id": "1681033", "url": "https://genius.com/1681033", "state": "pending", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Girls Love Beyoncé", "line": "These days it’s hard to meet women Feel like my love life is finished", "vault_lines": ["These days it's hard to meet women", "Feel like my love life is finished"], "meaning": "Fame can make it harder it is to meet someone genuine and start something special. All of his recently failed relationships have him feeling hopeless about the situation, similar to his verse in “Unthinkable (Remix)”. At this stage in the game it’s tough for Drake to find a woman who wants something real.\n\nAlso, note how he talks about ‘women’, whereas in the previous lines he’s been talking about ‘girls’. Drake has expressed his desire for a real woman before.", "annotation_id": "1681026", "url": "https://genius.com/1681026", "state": "accepted", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Girls Love Beyoncé", "line": "No new friends, no, no, no", "vault_lines": ["No new friends, no, no, no"], "meaning": "“No new friends” has become Drake’s catchphrase of late.\n\nAlthough Drake says “no no no” in the song “No New Friends,” the line could also be a reference to the Destiny’s Child Song, “No No No”, as the hook of this song is a cover of another Beyoncé…er…Destiny’s Child song.", "annotation_id": "1681023", "url": "https://genius.com/1681023", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Girls Love Beyoncé", "line": "This is not four years ago Time escapes me", "vault_lines": ["This is not four years ago"], "meaning": "Four years ago his career was just beginning, and nowhere near what it is now in 2013. After the success of his So Far Gone mixtape and subsequent albums catapulted him to stardom, he has risen through the ranks to become one of the hottest rappers in the game.\n\nFour years ago he may have wanted to settle down with a woman, but their timelines didn’t align so he was rejected and got hurt. Since then he’s been in and out of various relationships, including stints with Nebby, Jade, and Rihanna. He is seemingly struggling to find someone to settle down with long-term.", "annotation_id": "1681018", "url": "https://genius.com/1681018", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Girls Love Beyoncé", "line": "Look, I know girls love Beyoncé", "vault_lines": ["Look, I know girls love Beyoncé"], "meaning": "Ask any girl her opinion on Bey –  it’ll be positive! This is largely because Beyoncé’s tunes are frequently narratives spoken by and directed towards women\n\nAs a result, Beyoncé is widely considered to be the strongest female role model in popular American music. Drake is commenting on his perception that some girls take the “Beyoncé thing” too far, becoming cold-hearted players like the men they were leveling the playing field with.", "annotation_id": "1681010", "url": "https://genius.com/1681010", "state": "accepted", "votes": 84, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Girls Love Beyoncé", "line": "And this ain’t no time for locking your phone and not coming home And startin’ some shit when I’m in the zone", "vault_lines": ["And this ain't no time for actin'", "And this ain't no time for games", "And this ain't no time for uncertainty", "And this ain't no time for locking your phone and not coming home", "And startin' some shit when I'm in the zone", "No, I'm not alone"], "meaning": "He doesn’t have time to deal with his girl locking her phone (either shutting her phone off and not answering him, or activating the lock function so Drake can’t see her texts/call history), not coming back home at the end of the night, and starting altercations when he’s “in the zone” (leaning, smoking, writing, recording).\n\nThe line can be taken in the same context as a Wale line from his song “Contemplate”", "annotation_id": "1681005", "url": "https://genius.com/1681005", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Girls Love Beyoncé", "line": "Say my name, say my name When no one is around you Say, “Baby, I love you” If you ain’t running games Say my name, say my name You actin’ kinda shady, baby Why the sudden change? Say my name Say my name Say my name Say my name, say my name If no one is around you", "vault_lines": ["Say my name, say my name", "When no one is around you", "Say, \"Baby, I love you\"", "If you ain't running games", "You actin' kinda shady, baby", "Why the sudden change?", "If no one is around you"], "meaning": "James covers the hook from classic Destiny’s Child song “Say My Name”. Drake has been known to cover this track in several live performances.\n\nInterestingly enough, although probably not related, Common used this sample on his “Stay Schemin' Remix” diss directed at Drake.\n\n\n\nThe original chorus reflects the tale of a woman who has a boyfriend, she suspects him cheating on her because he won’t call her name and they barely engage in conversation. However, Drake and James put a spin on it, so that it tells the story of a guy who suspects his girlfriend cheating on him because she won’t call his name and talk to him. Also may be an ironic callback to his hit with Rihanna, “What’s My Name.”", "annotation_id": "1680999", "url": "https://genius.com/1680999", "state": "accepted", "votes": 81, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Girls Love Beyoncé", "status": "done", "targets": 21, "clicked": 21, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-girls-love-beyonce-lyrics", "genius_title": "Girls Love Beyoncé"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Hate Sleeping Alone", "line": "Cause if I wasn’t who I am, she would’ve been movin’ in by now", "vault_lines": ["'Cause if I wasn't who I am, she would've been movin' in by now"], "meaning": "Drake acknowledges that his commitment issues keeps them from forming something real, as he avoids an emotional connection, he’d rather keep it physical with her", "annotation_id": "31990725", "url": "https://genius.com/31990725", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Hate Sleeping Alone", "line": "And", "vault_lines": ["And by the time I end up stoppin'", "And she gives me all her trust and I'm abusin' it right now", "So I'ma call somebody up and see if they'd be down", "So she's here and we're both so gone", "Full name and birthday, I book a flight and you come to me", "And when you're fuckin' someone else", "And hangs up, yeah, how dare you tell me it's tougher for you?", "I was in love two years ago and gave the baggage to my ex"], "meaning": "After their interaction on the call and the girl having expressed how she feels its tougher for her as he has someone else … Drake justifies how tough it is for him and how the other woman is just a means of him not feeling lonely and isn’t better than her .", "annotation_id": "28962401", "url": "https://genius.com/28962401", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Hate Sleeping Alone", "line": "Half the time, we don’t end up fucking, I don’t ask her for nothing You leave me in the morning, I don’t see her for months But I just hate sleepin’ alone, I hate sleepin’ alone", "vault_lines": ["And by the time I end up stoppin'", "Fuck me like you hate me", "'Cause I hate sleepin' alone, I hate sleepin' alone", "Half the time, we don't end up fucking, I don't ask her for nothing", "You leave me in the morning, I don't see her for months", "But I just hate sleepin' alone, I hate sleepin' alone"], "meaning": "Drake enforces the fact that he isn’t really interested in the woman that he calls by saying he barely has sex with her, and barely sees her at all. This shows that Drake called her just to have some company until the morning.", "annotation_id": "609766", "url": "https://genius.com/609766", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Hate Sleeping Alone", "line": "Fuck me like you hate me", "vault_lines": ["She says, \"Kiss me like you miss me", "Fuck me like you hate me", "Just fuck her like she ain't me\""], "meaning": "In contrast to the first half of the line in which this girl claims she wants to be kissed with the tender embrace only someone who hasn’t seen her can give, she tells Drake to also give her extremely rough sex. She likes hate fucking (or makeup sex, it’s the best).", "annotation_id": "587606", "url": "https://genius.com/587606", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Hate Sleeping Alone", "line": "Damn, those words are scary Those words are scary, Virgin Mary I just tell her to spare me", "vault_lines": ["Damn, those words are scary", "Those words are scary, Virgin Mary", "I just tell her to spare me"], "meaning": "Drake doesn’t want to make a commitment to this girl.\n\nShe looked pure and innocent, Drake didn’t expect those words to come out of her mouth. Her personality changed after they had sex and hes asking her to “spare him” the fight.", "annotation_id": "447732", "url": "https://genius.com/447732", "state": "accepted", "votes": 37, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Hate Sleeping Alone", "line": "You just told me I ain’t shit, I guess I’m provin’ it right now, oh", "vault_lines": ["You just told me I ain't shit, I guess I'm provin' it right now, oh", "You just said I never learn, I guess I'm proving it right now, oh"], "meaning": "Drake admits it – she’s right, he is a shitty guy. But it’s because he has so much going on his life with the recording, the touring, the media appearances. It’s Hard Out Here for a Pimp", "annotation_id": "444598", "url": "https://genius.com/444598", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Hate Sleeping Alone", "line": "So she’s here and we’re both so gone", "vault_lines": ["So she's here and we're both so gone", "She's here, we're so gone"], "meaning": "“Gone” is slang for being messed up on Drake’s favorite recreational drug, the codeiene/promethezine/soda mixture known as purple drank", "annotation_id": "444326", "url": "https://genius.com/444326", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Hate Sleeping Alone", "status": "done", "targets": 7, "clicked": 7, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-hate-sleeping-alone-lyrics", "genius_title": "Hate Sleeping Alone"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Hot 97 Freestyle", "line": "I belong to the youngest Grammy nominated crew", "vault_lines": ["I belong to the youngest Grammy nominated crew"], "meaning": "When Drake dropped that line in his iconic 2009 Hot 97 Freestyle—the one where he famously read the bars off his BlackBerry—he was flexing the elite status of Young Money Entertainment as the new powerhouse in hip-hop. By calling them the “youngest Grammy nominated crew,” he was bragging that he, Nicki Minaj, and Lil Wayne were hitting the industry’s highest milestones while they were still the new kids on the block, essentially skipping the “waiting your turn” phase that most rappers had to endure. It was a statement of pure confidence meant to show that his squad wasn’t just a group of rookies, but a commercially dominant force that the Recording Academy was already forced to respect. The line cemented the idea that the Young Money era had officially begun, though in the years since, it’s become a bit of a meme among fans who track the “Grammy count” between Drake and his rivals.", "annotation_id": "38577156", "url": "https://genius.com/38577156", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Hot 97 Freestyle", "line": "I’m in the Aston doin’ doughnuts", "vault_lines": ["I’m in the Aston doin' doughnuts"], "meaning": "An Aston Martin is an expensive-ass luxury sports car; doing donuts in one would be considered the definition of wasting money\n\n\n\nThis isn’t the only time Drake has referenced Aston Martins", "annotation_id": "47226", "url": "https://genius.com/47226", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
