{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pipe Down", "line": "You’re the reason we’ll be going separate ways You’re the reason we cannot communicate It’s not the things you say, it’s what you don’t say I’m not in your way, you’re in your own way", "vault_lines": ["You're the reason we'll be going separate ways", "You're the reason we cannot communicate", "It's not the things you say, it's what you don't say", "I'm not in your way, you're in your own way"], "meaning": "Drake comes to a switching point where he starts pinpointing the reasons the relationship happened to go wrong and why it’ll never workout because of how the girl is her biggest enemy.", "annotation_id": "30563470", "url": "https://genius.com/30563470", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pipe Down", "line": "You know I love you more than all them niggas put together", "vault_lines": ["You know I love you more than all them niggas put together"], "meaning": "Drakes love for his partner is more than any of the other dudes on the outside put together but even with that being said the girl is blind to it and doesn’t acknowledge the amount of love being showed to her.", "annotation_id": "30563452", "url": "https://genius.com/30563452", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pipe Down", "line": "If it was ride or die then you should’ve been dead right now", "vault_lines": ["If it was ride or die then you should've been dead right now"], "meaning": "To “ride or die” for someone is a way of expressing your extreme loyalty to them, sticking with them through ups and downs.\n\nDrake uses the slang term’s word choice literally, questioning how she is still alive after claiming her loyalty and then leaving afterwards.", "annotation_id": "27118283", "url": "https://genius.com/27118283", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pipe Down", "line": "The world is yours, but the city’s mine", "vault_lines": ["The world is yours, but the city's mine"], "meaning": "This could simultaneously be a reference to the famous sentence from the 1983 movie Scarface as well as the songs from Jay-Z (City Is Mine) and Nas (The World Is Yours). Jay-Z and Nas are known for their beef and Drake might therefore be implying that his complications with this girl are comparable to rap beef.\nDrake could also be mentioning his song ‘City Is Mine’ from his second project, Comeback Season.\n\n\n\nPROPOSED SUGGESTION: Drake is implying the woman in question can live anywhere else in the world just not his city. She has probably moved out of town to get away from him and he is fine with that.\n\nPROPOSED SUGGESTION: the world is yours ties with the previous line of a literary tattooed passport.", "annotation_id": "24053762", "url": "https://genius.com/24053762", "state": "pending", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pipe Down", "line": "Angel eyes, but you’ve been giving me hell all night", "vault_lines": ["Angel eyes, but you've been giving me hell all night"], "meaning": "In 2001 Jennifer Lopez, one of Drake’s notable past flings, starred in a movie titled Angel Eyes. This line also contrasts his significant other as describing her as having “angel eyes” but instead she is “giving him hell all night”. This is a callback to the biblical concepts of the angels and the existence of hell.", "annotation_id": "23902989", "url": "https://genius.com/23902989", "state": "accepted", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pipe Down", "line": "And when you see Chanel, I wish that’s how you saw me", "vault_lines": ["And when you see Chanel, I wish that's how you saw me", "That shit you tell Chanel, I wish that's how you called me"], "meaning": "It was reported that Drake gave out Chanel handbags to the women who attended his birthday party in 2018.\n\nDrake was giving out Chanel bags at his birthday party. pic.twitter.com/hrKKOytMXP\n— Drizzy Source (@DrizzySource), October 24, 2018", "annotation_id": "23875507", "url": "https://genius.com/23875507", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pipe Down", "line": "I was on your ass like back pockets", "vault_lines": ["I was on your ass like back pockets"], "meaning": "To be on someones ass is to pressure them to do something.\n\n‘On your ass’ could also mean he was chasing her as this was when he first saw. This obviously implies that Drake was very attracted to this female.", "annotation_id": "23875125", "url": "https://genius.com/23875125", "state": "accepted", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pipe Down", "line": "I tatted your passport up Now it’s lookin’ like a arm sleeve Just know that was all me", "vault_lines": ["I tatted your passport up", "Now it's lookin' like a arm sleeve", "Just know that was all me"], "meaning": "When traveling abroad, airports will stamp a passport on both the arrival and departure of the visitor. The stamp can contain information on the type of travel, the allotted time for the visitor, and the date of the stamp itself.\n\n\n\nAn example of a stamped passport.\n\nDrake compares the stamping of the passport to an arm sleeve, either a collection of small tattoos or one large tattoo that covers the arm in full.", "annotation_id": "23875106", "url": "https://genius.com/23875106", "state": "accepted", "votes": 55, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pipe Down", "line": "(I’m working on dying)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The tag of popular producer group Working on Dying. The group-member that produced this song is FaxOnly.\nIt’s not the first time that the group’s producer tag is on a Drake’s track, since Oogie Mane, one of the group members, produced Drake’s 2018 single, “I’m Upset”.", "annotation_id": "23874009", "url": "https://genius.com/23874009", "state": "accepted", "votes": 88, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pipe Down", "line": "(She belongs to the streets)", "vault_lines": ["Said you belong to the streets but the streets belong to me", "It's like home to me (She belongs to the streets)"], "meaning": "A sample from a video of the rapper Future.\n“She belongs to the streets” is a phrase to say a girl is a hoe. If a girl belongs to the streets she isn’t just sleeping with one man she is with “the streets”.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NvhKepTnZ-M", "annotation_id": "23873998", "url": "https://genius.com/23873998", "state": "accepted", "votes": 149, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pipe Down", "status": "done", "targets": 10, "clicked": 10, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-pipe-down-lyrics", "genius_title": "Pipe Down"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Replacement Girl", "line": "Since Jay and Kellz ain’t doin’ they thing no more, guess me and the boy Songz the replacement", "vault_lines": ["Since Jay and Kellz ain't doin' they thing no more, guess me and the boy Songz the replacement"], "meaning": "Drake references rapper JAY-Z and singer R. Kelly. Both artists are known for their collaborations, specifically their two collab albums: 2002’s The Best of Both Worlds and 2004’s Unfinished Business.\n\nDrake is saying that he and Trey Songz, the feature on the song can take their spot.", "annotation_id": "38184616", "url": "https://genius.com/38184616", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Replacement Girl", "line": "I was birthed up top but was raised at the bottom of the map", "vault_lines": ["Let me show you what it is, I was birthed up top but was raised at the bottom of the map"], "meaning": "Drake was born in Canada but he spent a lot of summer with his father down in Memphis, Tennessee.\n\nWhich is where he learned a lot about music being that his father and uncle were musicians.", "annotation_id": "110766", "url": "https://genius.com/110766", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
