{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cameras", "line": "Before I’m on the next ting, YMCMB, ah", "vault_lines": ["Before I'm on the next ting, YMCMB, ah"], "meaning": "YMCMB stands for Young Money Cash Money Billionaires, the rap collective that launched Drake into hip-hop royalty. Drake’s basically shouting them out before moving onto “the next ting\", showing love to the team while also flexing how fast his life moves now.", "annotation_id": "39954797", "url": "https://genius.com/39954797", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cameras", "line": "Baby, she look like a star, but only on camera Only on camera, only on camera It look like we in love, but only on camera Only on camera, only on camera", "vault_lines": ["Baby, she look like a star, but only on camera", "Only on camera, only on camera", "It look like we in love, but only on camera", "It might look like I care, but only on camera"], "meaning": "Him and his girl act differently on camera (most likely as a perfect couple) compared to real life.", "annotation_id": "34670886", "url": "https://genius.com/34670886", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cameras", "line": "Callin’ on, callin’ on you No, no, no I been callin’ on, callin’ on you", "vault_lines": ["Callin' on, callin' on you", "I been callin' on, callin' on you", "You keep me callin' on you (You keep me callin' on you)"], "meaning": "This is sampled from intro of single Callin on You by Jon B.", "annotation_id": "33518880", "url": "https://genius.com/33518880", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cameras", "line": "Bunch of Underground Kingz,", "vault_lines": ["Bunch of Underground Kingz,"], "meaning": "This is a reference to Port Arthur, Texas hip-hop duo UGK (which stands for Underground Kingz). Drake has been vocal about his admiration for the group in the past, and even has a song called “Under Ground Kings” on this very same album. Drake collaborated with Bun B, one half of UGK, on his 2009 song “Uptown.” Pimp C had already died from a combination of overconsumption of lean and sleep apnea (rest in peace) when “Uptown” was released, so unfortunately Drake never got to collaborate with the full group.\n\n\n\nDrake and Bun B circa 2009.", "annotation_id": "17479295", "url": "https://genius.com/17479295", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cameras", "line": "[Produced by Noah “40” Shebib]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This track samples a sped up portion of Jon B’s “Calling on You”\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kb6mZ9LJVZU", "annotation_id": "3385438", "url": "https://genius.com/3385438", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cameras", "line": "Ah, call on you Just mail me my ring back Oh, I wanna call on you, baby Can’t keep that shit Oh, I wanna call on you, baby She said I could call on you, baby (Hahaha) Ayy La, da, da, da, da, la, da, da, da, da, baby", "vault_lines": ["Callin' on, callin' on you", "I been callin' on, callin' on you", "You keep me callin' on you (You keep me callin' on you)", "Ah, call on you", "Just mail me my ring back", "Oh, I wanna call on you, baby", "Can't keep that shit", "She said I could call on you, baby (Hahaha)", "La, da, da, da, da, la, da, da, da, da, baby"], "meaning": "Drake obviously proposed to one of his past loves but either she wasn’t feeling it or Drake called it off.\n\n\n\nDrake reemphasizes this same frustration in the second line of Good Ones Go (Interlude) (the next song).", "annotation_id": "1945681", "url": "https://genius.com/1945681", "state": "accepted", "votes": 50, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cameras", "line": "Don’t listen to the lies, I swear they all lies", "vault_lines": ["Don't listen to the lies, I swear they all lies"], "meaning": "Clearly every allegation with Drake being with a woman is a lie. He clearly has it out for whoever his ex is, and the prime driving force behind the ‘'Take Care’‘ mellow approach . He’s telling her that its only for the cameras, behind the scenes he’s still the Drake she knows", "annotation_id": "1632414", "url": "https://genius.com/1632414", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cameras", "line": "How you mean? How you mean? What you know about the team?", "vault_lines": ["How you mean? How you mean? What you know about the team?", "How you mean? How you mean?"], "meaning": "First he’s been asking how do you NOT know about us? and now he’s asking do you really know us? you only know what the media  puts out there.\n\n“How you mean, how you mean” is an allusion to the song How You Mean by London rapper Sneakbo whom Drake has shouted out on Twitter and stated his admiration for in interviews.", "annotation_id": "937902", "url": "https://genius.com/937902", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cameras", "line": "You know, I could be your knight in shining Armor All tires", "vault_lines": ["You know, I could be your knight in shining Armor All tires"], "meaning": "In the medieval days knights had the most  chivalry and were the most noble men around.\n\n\n\n“Armor All” is a brand of tire shiner used on cars. the line is a juxtaposition of modern day chivalry. Instead of a knight in shinning armor ridding a horse Drake picks up his women with his freshly Amor All-buffed stead of choice. Most likely this:", "annotation_id": "761495", "url": "https://genius.com/761495", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cameras", "line": "How you mean? How you mean? Thought you knew about the team, ayy, yeah That’s why I asked you, how you mean? How you mean? Thought you knew about the team, ayy, yeah, heh, uh", "vault_lines": ["Thought you knew about the team, ayy, yeah", "That's why I asked you, how you mean? How you mean?", "Thought you knew about the team, ayy, yeah, heh, uh", "How you mean? How you mean? What you know about the team?", "Thought you knew about the team, ayy, yeah, heh", "Thought you knew about the team, ayy", "That's why I asked you", "How you mean? How you mean?"], "meaning": "“How you mean” is a term originating in the West Indies, popular in most places with a sizable diaspora ie. Canada, London etc. etc.\n\nIt means, “what do you mean”?\n\nDrake got inspiration from UK MC Sneakbo for this line (see 3:45).\n\nWhat do you mean what do I mean?\n— Drizzy (@Drake) June 30, 2013", "annotation_id": "441767", "url": "https://genius.com/441767", "state": "accepted", "votes": 77, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cameras", "line": "You know, I could be your knight in shining Armor All tires", "vault_lines": ["You know, I could be your knight in shining Armor All tires"], "meaning": "A pun here, as Drake conflates the idea of a knight in shining armor, a “person, usually a man, who comes to the aid of another, usually a woman, in a gallant and courteous manner,” and his own propensity for fancy cars, usually shining courtesy of Armor All sprays and wipes.", "annotation_id": "440908", "url": "https://genius.com/440908", "state": "accepted", "votes": 51, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cameras", "line": "Ooh, finally got you right here (Said I finally got my baby) Tonight, I’ll ease your mind (Tonight, I’ll ease your mind) That’s why I’m callin’ on you (Why I’m callin’ on you) And, ooh, oh Soft, you’re love’s desire (Soft, you’re love’s desire) It’s hard to stay away (Stay away) You keep me callin’ on you (You keep me callin’ on you)", "vault_lines": ["Callin' on, callin' on you", "Ooh, finally got you right here (Said I finally got my baby)", "Tonight, I'll ease your mind (Tonight, I'll ease your mind)", "That's why I'm callin' on you (Why I'm callin' on you)", "Soft, you're love's desire (Soft, you're love's desire)", "It's hard to stay away (Stay away)", "I been callin' on, callin' on you", "You keep me callin' on you (You keep me callin' on you)", "Oh, I wanna call on you, baby", "That's why I asked you"], "meaning": "Sample from Jon B’s “Calling On You”.  Noah “40” Shebib, Drake’s producer and right-hand man, explained Drizzy’s use of 90’s r&b in a recent GQ interview:\n\nGQ: What were some of the records you listened to and shared together?\n\n I could go on forever, you know? I had a very distinct taste for R&B music, growing up listening to it my entire life and I love producing it first and foremost. It was everything from SWV and Jon B to Silk and Playa and any you could possibly think of. Even Tank, that intro off Sex, Love, and Pain, that kind of slow R&B vibe that lasts, somehow a line came out of “Best I Ever Had.” We’re always surrounding ourselves with music like that. Even on Take Care you’ll see a lot of ‘90s R&B samples, you know? A lot of different artists from the R&B world of the '90s—we’re trying to keep that prominent, like the last album with the Aaliyah stuff. I’ve been an Aaliyah fan since I was a kid—me and my sister—so that stuff comes up as well. That Timbaland/Ginuwine era, too", "annotation_id": "439279", "url": "https://genius.com/439279", "state": "accepted", "votes": 82, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cameras", "line": "Girl, they love me like I’m Prince, like the new king with the crown", "vault_lines": ["Girl, they love me like I'm Prince, like the new king with the crown"], "meaning": "Saying that he is the new Prince, while also comparing himself to an actual prince\n\n\n\nAnd you know in Purple Rain, Prince’s character was referred to as “the kid.”\n\nAlso building off the medival reference from the previous line “knight in shining armor”", "annotation_id": "437517", "url": "https://genius.com/437517", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cameras", "line": "Word on road is the clique about to blow", "vault_lines": ["Word on road is the clique about to blow"], "meaning": "Drake most likely talking about the two-man crew, OVOXO. The group consists of Drake (October’s Very Own) and The Weeknd (XO), and how they are quickly on the rise (especially The Weeknd, he’s popular among white teenage girls these days!)\n\n\n\nHe’s also name-dropping Word On Road, his official fan website. Plus, the word “clique” sounds like “click”, the onomatopoeic word usually used to describe camera shutters taking a picture.\n\nTo make this all work, he slightly alters the famous idiom “word on the street” saying instead “word on road”.", "annotation_id": "434351", "url": "https://genius.com/434351", "state": "accepted", "votes": 89, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cameras", "status": "done", "targets": 14, "clicked": 14, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-cameras-lyrics", "genius_title": "Cameras"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "[Verse 2]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "“If it’s up to me”\n\nThis is a direct message to Kendrick Lamar referencing his 2024 single featuring SZA ‘Luther’", "annotation_id": "41251491", "url": "https://genius.com/41251491", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "I don’t know nothin’ ’bout you on them tracks", "vault_lines": ["I don't know nothin' 'bout you on them tracks, let's go", "I don't remember nothin' 'bout them raps", "I don't know nothin' 'bout you on them tracks"], "meaning": "He is claiming that his opponent’s rap songs (“tracks”) left zero lasting impression on him. Paired with “I don’t remember one word in your raps,” he’s saying their discography is completely forgettable and unmemorable.", "annotation_id": "40837019", "url": "https://genius.com/40837019", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "Got a real big heart, I’m a fucked-up guy, though", "vault_lines": ["Got a real big heart, I'm a fucked-up guy, though"], "meaning": "I love Drake but this line is corny asl", "annotation_id": "40533318", "url": "https://genius.com/40533318", "state": "pending", "votes": -4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "I am, I am, I am", "vault_lines": ["I am, I am, I am", "I am not better or wiser, Future the Prince is my trusted advisor"], "meaning": "He’s referencing Joel Osteen’s book, “The Power of I Am.”\n\nHe’s trolling Kendrick because in the song Euphoria, Kendrick states:\n“Am I battlin' ghost or AI?\nNigga feelin' like Joel Osteen (or Joel Hale Osteen)\nFunny, he was in a film called \"AI”\nAnd my sixth sense tellin' me to off him\"\n\nSome people think this was a mistake because Joel Osteen wasn’t in A.I (or in Sixth Sense). Haley Joel Osment was and their names are similar.\n\nSome people think it was on purpose, most people ignore it.\n\nMaybe Drake is trolling Kendrick in a personal/direct way or trying to remind listeners of Kendricks “mistake” by adding in this simple easter egg.", "annotation_id": "40389632", "url": "https://genius.com/40389632", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "New Year’s Eve, police escort ’cause I can’t miss the fireworks", "vault_lines": ["New Year's Eve, police escort 'cause I can't miss the fireworks"], "meaning": "One of the many references on Iceman to Drake’s early catalog. On the opening track to Thank Me Later titled “Fireworks” Drake rapped:\n\n“I’ve missed them before but won’t miss them again”\n\nHere Drake revisits the idea with new perspective. Due to the success he’s been able achieve he no longer has to worry about missing the fireworks. Now he gets police escorts to important events and can bypass the traffic.\n\nAlso worth noting that at the end of the fourth episode of the Iceman livestreams, where the album was initially released, there was a lengthy firework display.", "annotation_id": "40242834", "url": "https://genius.com/40242834", "state": "pending", "votes": -2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "I am, I am, I am", "vault_lines": ["I am, I am, I am", "I am not better or wiser, Future the Prince is my trusted advisor"], "meaning": "He’s referencing Joel Osteen’s book, “The Power of I Am.”\n\nHe’s trolling Kendrick because in the song Euphoria, Kendrick states:\n“Am I battlin' ghost or AI?\nN***a feelin' like Joel Osteen (or Joel Hale Osteen)\nFunny, he was in a film called \"AI”\nAnd my sixth sense tellin' me to off him\"\n\nSome people think this was a mistake because Joel Osteen wasn’t in A.I (or in Sixth Sense). Haley Joel Osment was and their names are similar.\n\nSome people think it was on purpose, most people ignore it.\n\nMaybe Drake is trolling Kendrick in a personal/direct way or trying to remind listeners of Kendricks “mistake” by adding in this simple easter egg.", "annotation_id": "40123196", "url": "https://genius.com/40123196", "state": "pending", "votes": -5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "If it’s up to me, then you all on a list, man, everyone signed up If it’s up to me, it’s already made, I ain’t makin’ my mind up", "vault_lines": ["If it's up to me, I get everyone hit, I get everyone lined up", "If it's up to me, I been clockin' you pussy, man, everyone time's up", "If it's up to me, if it's up to me, ayy", "If it's up to me, then you all on a list, man, everyone signed up", "If it's up to me, it's already made, I ain't makin' my mind up"], "meaning": "This bar seemingly confirms the legitimacy of Drake’s rumored “opp list” that circulated online in late 2024. The list was notably discussed by 50 Cent during an interview on Big Boy TV and included a wide range of names, from fellow rappers and media personalities to streamers and YouTubers. Drake’s reference suggests there may have been some truth behind the viral list after all.", "annotation_id": "40102241", "url": "https://genius.com/40102241", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "You know I love you so much", "vault_lines": ["You know I love you so much"], "meaning": "He loves the girls so much 🤯", "annotation_id": "40064696", "url": "https://genius.com/40064696", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "And make sure you’re good ’til the next time we meet up But now I gotta send it up", "vault_lines": ["And make sure you're good 'til the next time we meet up", "But now I gotta send it up"], "meaning": "Drake is talking directly to the fans by explaining his time away from music as if he’s a partner explaining his absence to a lover.\n\nHe references his February 2025 collab album with PARTYNEXTDOOR, $$$4U, as the project he left to keep the fans fed whilst he handles some things.\n\nHe explains the decision behind dropping the collab project during a time when everyone was anticipating the ICEMAN project he had been teasing since summer 2024.\n\nBut now I gotta send it up\n\nDrake closes off this melodic explanation through a shift in energy. He’s saying that whatever he had to handle is sorted now and he’s ready to turn up. The apologetic tone he was using ends here. He’s no longer explaining himself, he’s settling the scores from here onwards.", "annotation_id": "40059589", "url": "https://genius.com/40059589", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "Let’s go", "vault_lines": ["I don't know nothin' 'bout you on them tracks, let's go", "I don't remember nothin' bein' facts, let's go"], "meaning": "in the music video for “Dust”, Drake’s son Adonis sings along to this line and it is a sweet moment", "annotation_id": "39865491", "url": "https://genius.com/39865491", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "The boy’s about to break some news", "vault_lines": ["The boy's about to break some news"], "meaning": "“The boy” is a nickname for Drake and he’s implying that he’s about to reveal something new", "annotation_id": "39848924", "url": "https://genius.com/39848924", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "If it’s up to me, I get everyone hit, I get everyone lined up If it’s up to me, I been clockin’ you pussy, man, everyone time’s up", "vault_lines": ["If it's up to me, I get everyone hit, I get everyone lined up", "If it's up to me, I been clockin' you pussy, man, everyone time's up", "If it's up to me, if it's up to me, ayy"], "meaning": "In the previous lyric Drake submits that he’s not acting on his own accord and advice. Referring to Future The Prince as his “trusted advisor”. This should be a sigh of relief for his opposition. As he reveals here that if he was acting on his own accord, without a wise advisor like Future, he’d have had his opposition “hit” by now.\n\nHe states he’s been “clocking” them, which could mean he’s been paying attention to their motives and intentions. May have been be derived from the slang “clocking tea” which means to “to recognize, acknowledge, or call out the truth in a situation, especially when it comes to gossip, drama, or something someone is trying to hide”.\n\nWhatever they are up to, their “time” would have been “up” by now if it was up to him.", "annotation_id": "39836660", "url": "https://genius.com/39836660", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "If it’s up to me, if it’s up to me, ayy", "vault_lines": ["If it's up to me, I get everyone hit, I get everyone lined up", "If it's up to me, I been clockin' you pussy, man, everyone time's up", "If it's up to me, if it's up to me, ayy", "If it's up to me, then you all on a list, man, everyone signed up", "If it's up to me, it's already made, I ain't makin' my mind up"], "meaning": "Drake paying homage to the greatest underground album ever “Up 2 Më”", "annotation_id": "39827032", "url": "https://genius.com/39827032", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "All the numbers are final, no t-shirts, no vinyl Y’all ’bout to make me richie like Lionel, for real And that’s the truth", "vault_lines": ["All the numbers are final, no t-shirts, no vinyl", "Y'all 'bout to make me richie like Lionel, for real", "And that's the truth"], "meaning": "A well known industry trick for inflating chart numbers is bundling album units with merchandise, as in buying a t-shirt or a vinyl comes packaged with an album download, which artificially boosts the sales count. Drake is distancing himself from these gimmicks. Several artists have been criticized for relying heavily on merch bundles to hit number one, so Drake is implying his chart performance stands on its own without those crutches.\n\nRichie is Lionel Richie’s surname, but it’s also a play on the word “rich” dressed up within his name. Lionel Richie is one of the best-selling music artists in history (somewhere north of 100 million records sold worldwide.)\n\n\n\nDrake isn’t just talking to his fans, he’s also addressing everyone streaming the album out of spite or obsession with the beef. They all will still count the same on the dashboard.", "annotation_id": "39809082", "url": "https://genius.com/39809082", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "They was like, ”Go blow the dust off your plaques Go blow the dust off your plaques” What was the year that they say you had slaps? ‘Cause I don’t remember it goin’ like that I don’t remember one word in your raps", "vault_lines": ["They was like, \"Go blow the dust off your plaquеs", "Go blow the dust off your plaques\"", "What was the year that they say you had slaps?", "'Cause I don't remember it goin' like that", "I don't remember one word in your raps", "Go blow the dust off your plaques, what?"], "meaning": "Drake is going straight at Kendrick’s commercial record. Kendrick does have a lot of certifications, but they’ve been sitting long enough to collect dust, a shot at his infamous release gaps and hiatuses. Five years between DAMN. and Mr. Morale, another two before GNX. For someone crowned the GOAT, the catalog gets quiet for long stretches.\n\nAs the “hitmaker,” Drake attacks Kendrick’s relevance as in how many of Kendrick’s songs does the average person actually know word for word? Some have long argued that his catalog is overrated; this claim became especially big in the discussion around whether he has enough hits to justify headlining the biggest pop‑culture stage on the planet, the Super Bowl.", "annotation_id": "39797989", "url": "https://genius.com/39797989", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "Those ain’t my haters, those are my secret admirers", "vault_lines": ["Those ain't my haters, those are my secret admirers"], "meaning": "Drake said in 2017 on (More Life) Do Not Disturb, “I am a reflection of all of your insecurities. Behind closed doors, a lot of 6 God worshiping”\n\nOver the years, it’s become almost a “trend” to hate on Drake for clicks and views even though he has remained the most streamed rapper of all time. The “so-called”\nDrake haters are actually secret admirers. Because behind closed doors, he’s their favorite artist.\n\nThis becomes obvious year after year when the “Drake Haters” post their Spotify Wrapped stats and Drake is always the most streamed artist. Drake officially finished 2025 as Spotify’s most-streamed rap artist for the 11th consecutive year, racking up over 18.4 billion streams on the platform.\n\nDrake also stated in 2011 on (Take Care) Over My Dead Body, “And I be hearin' the shit you say through the grapevine. But jealousy is just love and hate at the same time”", "annotation_id": "39795556", "url": "https://genius.com/39795556", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "A BTC crypto big-timer", "vault_lines": ["A BTC crypto big-timer"], "meaning": "Drake has publicly shown signs that he owns or at least heavily uses Bitcoin, though the exact amount he holds is unknown.\n\nSome examples:\n\n\nHe has placed large sports bets in Bitcoin through  Stake.com and has won and lost millions worth of BTC publicly.\nIn 2022, he showed off a diamond-covered Ledger hardware wallet on Instagram, which is commonly used to store cryptocurrency like Bitcoin.\nHe reposted Michael Saylor discussing Bitcoin to his 146+ million Instagram followers in 2024.\nDrake has also invested in crypto-related companies like  MoonPay.", "annotation_id": "39793241", "url": "https://genius.com/39793241", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "I don’t remember nothin’ bein’ facts, let’s go", "vault_lines": ["I don't know nothin' 'bout you on them tracks, let's go", "I don't remember nothin' bein' facts, let's go"], "meaning": "Drake is doubling down on what he laid out on “THE HEART PART 6” (his direct response to Kendrick’s diss campaign,) where he pushed back on every major allegation thrown at him, calling the whole thing fiction designed to destroy his reputation:\n\nYou know, but\nJust let me know when we’re gettin' to the facts\nEverything in my shit is facts (Prove it)\nI’m waitin' on you to return the favor, like", "annotation_id": "39786299", "url": "https://genius.com/39786299", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "Girls from Atlanta call me Santa", "vault_lines": ["Girls from Atlanta call me Santa"], "meaning": "Drake buys gifts for women so they call him Santa (Claus), who is a legendary figure who, according to Western folklore, brings gifts to children on Christmas Eve.", "annotation_id": "39785887", "url": "https://genius.com/39785887", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "If it wasn’t for me reachin’ my hand, you never’d climbed up", "vault_lines": ["If it wasn't for me reachin' my hand, you never'd climbed up"], "meaning": "He’s talking about how he supported Kendrick early in his career — bringing him on tour, shouting him out, doing songs together, putting more people onto him. So “reaching my hand” means Drake helping him up, and “climbed up” means Kendrick becoming a huge artist.", "annotation_id": "39783478", "url": "https://genius.com/39783478", "state": "pending", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "I’m a corporate-America hit survivor", "vault_lines": ["I'm a corporate-America hit survivor"], "meaning": "By “corporate-America hit survivor” he could be talking about how music executives and major labels like UMG conspired against him and planned a “hit” on his career, particularly during the 2024 rap feud, in an effort to weaken his position and gain leverage in negotiating his next deal.\n\n“Hit” also could refer to his successful songs, saying that he has survived making massive hits for over a decade, and is still relevant.", "annotation_id": "39778775", "url": "https://genius.com/39778775", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "I heard your brother got flipped, did it sloppy, so that wasn’t our work", "vault_lines": ["I heard your brother got flipped, did it sloppy, so that wasn't our work"], "meaning": "“Flipped” means killed or attacked. Drake is distancing his crew from a recent hit, insulting the ones who actually did it by calling the job “sloppy”.\n\n“Flipped” could also mean snitched on, as in “flipped on,” hinting that someone close to his opps folded under pressure and started talking, then insults how “sloppy” his opps handle their business.", "annotation_id": "39778731", "url": "https://genius.com/39778731", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "Sixteen hours ahead in Melbourne, I don’t even know what’s goin’ on back home, straight", "vault_lines": ["Sixteen hours ahead in Melbourne, I don't even know what's goin' on back home, straight"], "meaning": "Melbourne is the capital city of the Australian state of Victoria. Drake performed four shows there at the Rod Laver Arena in February 2025, as part of the Anita Max Win Tour.\n\nMelbourne uses the Australian Eastern Time Zone and Toronto uses the Eastern Time Zone, making Toronto 16 hours behind Melbourne, but only when daylight saving time ends in Toronto.", "annotation_id": "39778618", "url": "https://genius.com/39778618", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "I just gotta handle somethin’ bigger than us", "vault_lines": ["I just gotta handle somethin' bigger than us"], "meaning": "Drake seems to be referring to the reasoning behind why he ended up cancelling his final shows on the ‘Anita Max Win Tour’ which included; his third Brisbane show, fourth Sydney show, and two Auckland shows. The reasoning behind this cancellation is a reason that carries more weight than  being able to complete the final shows of the tour.", "annotation_id": "39778425", "url": "https://genius.com/39778425", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "An FTX penthouse high-riser, yeah Samuel Bankman, free all my guys up, yeah", "vault_lines": ["An FTX penthouse high-riser, yeah", "Samuel Bankman, free all my guys up, yeah"], "meaning": "Samuel Bankman-Fried is a convicted crypto scammer who owned the bankrupt FTX exchange.\n\nHe was sentenced to 25 years in prison for wire fraud in 2023 after stealing approximately $4 billion in cryptocurrency from his customers.", "annotation_id": "39778300", "url": "https://genius.com/39778300", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "I am not better or wiser, Future the Prince is my trusted advisor", "vault_lines": ["I am, I am, I am", "I am not better or wiser, Future the Prince is my trusted advisor"], "meaning": "Drake continues with his commonly used financial bars.\n\n“Future the Prince” is a Canadian DJ and one of Drake’s day-one friends. This is not the first time Drake has shouted him out on a track. He has previously done so on tracks like “6PM In New York”:\n\nI’m managed by my friends that I grew up with\nI’d rather give that 15 percent to people I fuck with\nIf me and Future hadn’t made it with this rappin'\n\n\n\nAlso on “Nonstop”:\n\nFuture took the business and ran it for me\n\nAnd finally on “Champagne Poetry”:\n\nhttps://genius.com/23900093\n\nDrake is ultimately expressing how much trust he has in Future.", "annotation_id": "39776281", "url": "https://genius.com/39776281", "state": "pending", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "I’m with the mob at Graycliff, twenty cigars and they fuckin’ my eyes up", "vault_lines": ["I'm with the mob at Graycliff, twenty cigars and they fuckin' my eyes up"], "meaning": "Graycliff Hotel is a luxury spot in the Bahamas known for hosting celebrities, housing one of the world’s largest private wine cellars (175,000+ bottles), and particularly for its in-house cigar company.\n\n“The mob” refers to Drake’s close group of friends in his inner circle.\n\nSmoking twenty cigars without irritation exaggerates toughness and comfort in excess.", "annotation_id": "39776246", "url": "https://genius.com/39776246", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "I’m in a sold-out show with your girl on a riser", "vault_lines": ["I'm in a sold-out show with your girl on a riser"], "meaning": "A ‘riser’ is a raised platform at concerts or clubs, usually for VIP guests or dancers.\n\nThis could be a diss towards Ye fka Kanye West, from the time his ex-wife, Kim Kardashian, pulled up to Drake’s 2023 concert. Kim could be heard reciting her sample from Drake’s Search & Rescue\" where she said:\n\nI didn’t come this far just to come this far, and not be happy\n\nPotentially also a reference to the viral clip/meme of Andy Byron – the former CEO of Astronomer, caught on the Jumbotron with another woman at a Coldplay concert.", "annotation_id": "39776233", "url": "https://genius.com/39776233", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dust", "line": "Girls from Australia, what can I tell ya?", "vault_lines": ["Girls from Australia, what can I tell ya?"], "meaning": "Drake once again references the Anita Max Win Tour, where he visited four Australian cities: Perth, Melbourne, Sydney and Brisbane, in February 2025.\n\nAdditionally, Drake hosted a private, phone-free karaoke show in Maison Batard’s Le Club on Bourke Street, Melbourne. The event was said to have featured 25 Miss Universe contestants.", "annotation_id": "39775991", "url": "https://genius.com/39775991", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
