{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Forgot I Was Famous", "line": "Brought her to the crib, she walked through front door on some, “Holy shit”", "vault_lines": ["Brought her to the crib, she walked through front door on some, “Holy shit\""], "meaning": "Referring to his mansion in Canada, which he reportedly spent a whopping 100 million for.", "annotation_id": "28535918", "url": "https://genius.com/28535918", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Forgot I Was Famous", "line": "Talkin’ ’bout, ”They took my bitch”, you know that ain’t my only bitch", "vault_lines": ["You, my darling, you", "Talkin' 'bout, \"They took my bitch\", you know that ain't my only bitch"], "meaning": "Drake has been known to have had many partners throughout his career. He even went as far as having a necklace made with 42 diamond engagement rings, 1 for each girl he’s contemplated proposing to throughout his life.\n\nhttps://www.tmz.com/2022/12/13/drake-previous-engagements-chain-42-diamonds-propose/", "annotation_id": "28359319", "url": "https://genius.com/28359319", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Forgot I Was Famous", "line": "Don’t ask for no feature, only rappin’ on my homies’ shit", "vault_lines": ["Don't ask for no feature, only rappin' on my homies' shit"], "meaning": "Drake won’t do a feature just for anyone that has the money to pay for it. He will only do features for people in the industry that he’s friends with.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z1B7iYsyWKE", "annotation_id": "28359292", "url": "https://genius.com/28359292", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Forgot I Was Famous", "line": "Uzi good, he don’t need shit", "vault_lines": ["Me? I'm good, I don't need shit", "Uzi good, he don't need shit"], "meaning": "Drake is saying that Lil Uzi is fine and doesn’t need any help. This song was made before Lil Uzi announced they would go by they/them pronouns so during the time, Uzi was going by he/him pronouns.\n\nhttps://pitchfork.com/news/lil-uzi-vert-pronouns-are-they-them/", "annotation_id": "28359279", "url": "https://genius.com/28359279", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Forgot I Was Famous", "line": "Marni raincoat, yeah, just in case it start rainin’ (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Marni raincoat, yeah, just in case it start rainin' (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Marni is an Italian luxury fashion brand founded in 1994 by Consuelo Castiglioni in Milan, Italy. Uzi is referencing how he’ll be “dripped” out in his raincoat. Uzi has been seen wearing Marni on occasions.\n\n\n\nUzi wore a Marni colorful hat and matching scarf during his Rolling Loud New York performance in 2022.", "annotation_id": "28341782", "url": "https://genius.com/28341782", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Forgot I Was Famous", "line": "If we on a island then you know it’s not no Coney shit No, it’s not no Staten shit, I ain’t on no phony shit", "vault_lines": ["If we on a island then you know it's not no Coney shit", "No, it's not no Staten shit, I ain't on no phony shit"], "meaning": "Drake raps about several different areas in New York City calling them phony or fake. He also has gotten frustrated with rumors of his relationship with Ice Spice, a female rapper from New York. He recently slammed rumors of AI generated songs featuring him and Ice Spice.\n\n\n\nIt’s worth mentioning that in 2020, he visited Barbados, an island country in Caribbean – home to Rihanna. Rihanna and Drake have a lot of history dating back to 2009. During the 2016 MTV VMAs, he states – “She’s someone I’ve been in love with since I was 22 years old”.\nhttps://people.com/tv/mtv-vmas-2016-drake-opens-up-about-relationship-with-rihanna/\n\nHe could be comparing the authenticities of the two relationships here followed by some self assurance.", "annotation_id": "28310430", "url": "https://genius.com/28310430", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Forgot I Was Famous", "line": "Turn us into legends in the streets, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Turn us into legends in the streets, yeah"], "meaning": "Reference to Legend – Drake from 2018 where he talks about dying a legend. Here he’s mentioning it with reference to how he and his friends want to be remembered. It also tees up the death rumor line.", "annotation_id": "28310370", "url": "https://genius.com/28310370", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Forgot I Was Famous", "line": "Let my brothers come up off my name and they don’t owe me shit I can’t let you come up off my name till I’m at the gates, pearly", "vault_lines": ["You, my darling, you", "Me? I'm good, I don't need shit", "Let my brothers come up off my name and they don't owe me shit", "I can't let you come up off my name till I'm at the gates, pearly"], "meaning": "Pearly gates is an informal name to the gateway to Heaven. Following the other references in the song around the theme of death, Drake is stating that he will allow his brothers and homies to come up off his name but not anything or anyone else unless he’s passed away to Heaven.", "annotation_id": "28309113", "url": "https://genius.com/28309113", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Forgot I Was Famous", "line": "Now I’m in my bag to say the least They was tryna label me deceased Someone gotta show me the receipts, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Now I'm in my bag to say the least", "They was tryna label me deceased", "Someone gotta show me the receipts, yeah"], "meaning": "A false claim circulated roughly around December 2015 on social media, to which Drake passed away in a fatal car crash with most people misled by this rumor. Social media trolls began spreading the word using the hashtag “#RIPDrake” and to their success – it pathed its way through into well-known websites such as BuzzFeed.\n\nThe deception started when people commented on Drake’s July 2015 track “Hotline Bling,” to which they pointed out his “death” and gained widespread attention. News outlets became suspicious of the claim and eventually erased the information.", "annotation_id": "28247382", "url": "https://genius.com/28247382", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Forgot I Was Famous", "line": "Came back Richie, Hermès", "vault_lines": ["Came back Richie, Hermès"], "meaning": "Richie, a nickname for the Swiss luxurious watch company, Richard Mille, founded in 2001 by Dominique Guenat and Richard Mille, based in Les Breuleux, Switzerland. The brand specialises in very high-priced clockwork watches which have been criticised by some as “ridiculous” and “unnecessarily extravagant.”\n\nHermès, is a French luxury design house established in 1837. It specializes in leather goods, lifestyle accessories, home furnishings, perfumery, jewelry, watches and ready-to-wear. Its logo, since the 1950s, is of a Duke carriage with horse.", "annotation_id": "28246905", "url": "https://genius.com/28246905", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Forgot I Was Famous", "line": "I put my diamonds in my Spirit of Ecstasy, yeah (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I put my diamonds in my Spirit—, nah, nah, I got it (Yeah, yeah)", "I put my diamonds in my Spirit of Ecstasy, yeah (Yeah)"], "meaning": "The Spirit of Ecstasy is the bonnet ornament sculpture on Rolls-Royce cars. It is in the form of a woman leaning forwards with her arms outstretched behind and above her. Billowing cloth runs from her arms to her back, resembling wings.", "annotation_id": "28246883", "url": "https://genius.com/28246883", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Forgot I Was Famous", "line": "Fake woke, niggas fake deep You ain’t know fame before me Gave yo’ ass a lil’ sneak peek, yeah Now you gotta take a back seat", "vault_lines": ["Fake woke, niggas fake deep", "You ain't know fame before me", "Gave yo' ass a lil' sneak peek, yeah", "Now you gotta take a back seat"], "meaning": "Kendrick Lamar diss.\n\nDrake claims Kendrick’s rise to fame was on his own shoulders due to Drake giving Kenny a verse on Take Care (Buried Alive Interlude) in 2011.\n\nDrake also tells Kendrick he has to take the “back seat” as in step down and give Drake the crown in the rap game.\n\n“Back seat” likely referring to Kendrick’s hit song Backseat Freestyle.", "annotation_id": "28234461", "url": "https://genius.com/28234461", "state": "pending", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Forgot I Was Famous", "line": "Cut that top off the Cullinan, now that shit brainless (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Cut that top off the Cullinan, now that shit brainless (Yeah)"], "meaning": "The Rolls-Royce Cullinan is a 4-wheel Luxury SUV. Lil Uzi Vert owns a customized, roofless Rolls-Royce Cullinan named the “Cullinan Vert Edition”.\n\nhttps://x.com/Shtreetwear/status/1742233149453553961?s=20", "annotation_id": "28227762", "url": "https://genius.com/28227762", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Forgot I Was Famous", "line": "Ten K, I borrowed it from Skete", "vault_lines": ["Ten K, I borrowed it from Skete"], "meaning": "Could be another shot at Kanye by mentioning “Skete”, the nickname given to Pete Davidson during the time he dated Kim Kardashian or I misheard and he said something else.", "annotation_id": "28227433", "url": "https://genius.com/28227433", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Forgot I Was Famous", "line": "24-karat Wagyu, your boy’s got the shine off the beef, yeah", "vault_lines": ["24-karat Wagyu, your boy's got the shine off the beef, yeah"], "meaning": "Wagyu is a beef cattle breed from Japan. It is one of the most expensive and luxurious meats in the world due to its unique texture and marbling.\n\nLuxury restaurants including celebrity chef Nusret Gokce’s steakhouse also serve this beef wrapped in a tasteless 24-karat gold foil, costing a significant premium over the regular steak.", "annotation_id": "24753293", "url": "https://genius.com/24753293", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Forgot I Was Famous", "status": "done", "targets": 19, "clicked": 19, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-forgot-i-was-famous-lyrics", "genius_title": "Forgot I Was Famous"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Glow", "line": "‘Member doin’ shows, ain’t nobody show up Pour your heart out, ain’t nobody show love", "vault_lines": ["'Member doin' shows, ain't nobody show up", "Pour your heart out, ain't nobody show love"], "meaning": "Kanye recalls his early days in the music industry, where he would perform at shows with barely any people at them. He would put his heart and soul into his music, yet nobody turned up to his concerts.", "annotation_id": "34657311", "url": "https://genius.com/34657311", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Glow", "line": "They gon’ bang this here all summerti-i-ime", "vault_lines": ["They gon' bang this here all summerti-i-ime"], "meaning": "Somehow Kanye believed people would be listening to this God awful song all summer long – they in fact did not.", "annotation_id": "34657296", "url": "https://genius.com/34657296", "state": "pending", "votes": -8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Glow", "line": "‘Cause I be drivin’ ’round this bih with no sunroof", "vault_lines": ["'Cause I be drivin' 'round this bih with no sunroof"], "meaning": "Kanye drives a car that doesn’t have a roof, pretty self explanatory ig", "annotation_id": "34657291", "url": "https://genius.com/34657291", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Glow", "line": "Yeah, yeah Turn me way up, my voice is really low Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, okay", "vault_lines": ["Turn me way up, my voice is really low"], "meaning": "Kanye’s no stranger to having his volume raised on record, as he had done so on 2011’s “Gotta Have It”:\n\nTurn my headphones up, louder, uh-huh, uh-huh\n\nAs well as on the 2015 demo “When I See It”:\n\nLet me get more volume\nNah, nah\nLouder than my voice", "annotation_id": "20848517", "url": "https://genius.com/20848517", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Glow", "line": "We about to get the whole nine The whole nine, we just landed on a gold mine", "vault_lines": ["We about to get the whole nine", "The whole nine, we just landed on a gold mine"], "meaning": "Here the ‘whole nine’ refers to the phrase ‘the whole nine yards’, meaning ‘all of it/everything’. So Kanye is saying he is going to achieve everything, from riches from the proverbial ‘gold mine’ he has found, to other things such as fame and influence.\n\nThis could also be a reference to Drake’s own song “9”. That particular track is about Drake’s influence over his hometown of Toronto, so Kanye could be saying that his influence is going to felt everywhere.", "annotation_id": "11737169", "url": "https://genius.com/11737169", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Glow", "line": "I just take the dreams I’ve been sold And sell ’em for more, you already know", "vault_lines": ["I just take the dreams I've been sold", "And sell 'em for more, you already know"], "meaning": "Here Drake is saying that he is influenced by artists from before, reworked their styles and then sold his own music based off of those influences.\n\nFor instance, Drake took the music of artists like Jay-Z and Kanye and created his own style, and now he is influencing a whole new generation of artists from all over the world.\n\nAlso, a common dream that is sold through rap music is one that relates to having a lot of money and riches, as well as fame. Drake includes these themes a lot in his music therefore he is passing on those dreams to others through his own tracks.", "annotation_id": "11737149", "url": "https://genius.com/11737149", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Glow", "line": "We so certified, we so certifi-i-ied", "vault_lines": ["We so certified, we so certifi-i-ied"], "meaning": "Certified means that something is officially approved and revered, especially in the rap game. Certified also has connotations of ‘going platinum’ or being ‘certified platinum’ in the music industry, something Kanye has done time and time again.", "annotation_id": "11737130", "url": "https://genius.com/11737130", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Glow", "line": "Time to shake the dice, time to change the li-i-ight", "vault_lines": ["Time to shake the dice, time to change the li-i-ight"], "meaning": "When someone is about to roll the dice, they often shake the dice in their hand before casting them out onto the table.\n\n\n\nKanye is saying that he is going to roll the dice in an attempt to change his future, because winning big in gambling is something that can grant someone a massive fortune.\n\nIt could also refer tie into his decision to leave Jay-Z’s music-streaming platform Tidal.", "annotation_id": "11737113", "url": "https://genius.com/11737113", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Glow", "line": "They used to laugh when my whip was on the tow truck ‘Til me and bein’ broke finally broke up", "vault_lines": ["They used to laugh when my whip was on the tow truck", "'Til me and bein' broke finally broke up"], "meaning": "This is a reference to Kanye’s car crash on October 23, 2002. In the crash, he fractured his jaw and had to have it wired shut.\n\nDespite this, he recorded the song “Through The Wire” for his debut studio album “The College Dropout.”\n\nThe album was critically acclaimed and began his journey to fame and fortune.", "annotation_id": "11617904", "url": "https://genius.com/11617904", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Glow", "line": "Man, the glow got me feelin’ like I’m gunproof", "vault_lines": ["Man, the glow got me feelin' like I'm gunproof"], "meaning": "When Kanye’s on his game aka “glow’d up,” he feels invincible. This may be a reference to the glow that was shown at the end of The Last Dragon when Bruce Leroy caught a bullet with his teeth, essentially making him “gunproof.”", "annotation_id": "11582735", "url": "https://genius.com/11582735", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Glow", "line": "Hope I deal with karma ’fore my son do", "vault_lines": ["Hope I deal with karma 'fore my son do"], "meaning": "This idea originates from Bible verse Exodus 20:5:\n\nYou shall not bow down to them or worship them; for I, the Lord your God, am a jealous God, punishing the children for the sin of the parents to the third and fourth generation of those who hate me.\n\nAfter all the controversies Kanye’s been involved with, he’d rather he deal with the bad karma that’s going to come back around, rather than his son.\n\nJay Z expressed a similar idea on Kanye collaboration “New Day” from Watch the Throne, and before that on Kingdom Come’s “Beach Chair.”", "annotation_id": "11557044", "url": "https://genius.com/11557044", "state": "pending", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Glow", "line": "Tryin’ to avoid more confrontation I just gotta try harder", "vault_lines": ["Tryin' to avoid more confrontation", "I just gotta try harder"], "meaning": "Drake famously got caught up in beef with Meek Mill in 2015 this led to the release of Drake’s diss track “Back to Back.”\n\nDrake is now stating that he wishes to avoid more confrontation, this may be perceived as him no longer being involved in diss tracks and trying to avoid social media beef.\n\nDespite saying this on a song with Kanye West, Drake couldn’t avoid beef with Kanye himself. Kanye called Drake out in a rant in November 2016 during his Pablo tour. Drake talked about Ye’s rant during an interview with DJ Semtex. Drake also seemingly made fun of Kanye’s rant in a comment on DJ Khaled’s Instagram.", "annotation_id": "11532846", "url": "https://genius.com/11532846", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Glow", "line": "[Outro: Earth, Wind & Fire] Through devotion Blessed are the children We love y’all too! We believe if there’s anything y’all, you wanna do in life You need devotion Can I hear right on? Through devotion Blessed are the children We live for it Clap your hands this evening Come on, y’all I said it’s alright Clap your hands this evening Come on, y’all", "vault_lines": ["Blessed are the children", "We love y'all too!", "We believe if there's anything y'all, you wanna do in life", "Can I hear right on?", "We live for it", "Clap your hands this evening", "I said it's alright"], "meaning": "This sample is from a live version of “Devotion” by Earth, Wind and Fire.\n\nThe sample echoes the idea of the artists reaching new heights and “glowing” up.  The EWF song says if the children stay devoted, presumably to their religious teachings, they will be rewarded and live prosperous lives.\n\nIn Drake, Kanye and any aspiring rappers case, by staying devoted to their craft and working hard at it, they will find success.", "annotation_id": "11532540", "url": "https://genius.com/11532540", "state": "accepted", "votes": 153, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Glow", "line": "No more 9 to 5, autopilot dri-i-ive", "vault_lines": ["No more 9 to 5, autopilot dri-i-ive"], "meaning": "Autopilot is the name of a feature on the luxury electric car brand Tesla. The feature allows for limited autonomous driving. Kanye doesn’t need a 9 to 5 job when his musical career (with notoriously irregular hours) has made him so rich he has cars that can drive themselves.\n\nIt’s worth noting that Kanye and the founder of Tesla, Elon Musk, have a very close relationship. Elon profiled ‘Ye for Time’s Top 100 Most Influential People, and Kanye has claimed that he regularly discusses “the futch” with Musk and that he told President Obama that he should “sit with Elon Musk”.", "annotation_id": "11532287", "url": "https://genius.com/11532287", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Glow", "line": "Your boy all glowed up", "vault_lines": ["Your boy all glowed up"], "meaning": "Kanye’s already completed his full transformation, from a kid from Chicago who couldn’t even afford clothes on layaway to his position today as one of the most influential figures in music, fashion, and culture as a whole.", "annotation_id": "11532104", "url": "https://genius.com/11532104", "state": "accepted", "votes": 50, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Glow", "line": "We the new Abu Dhabi, this is our time", "vault_lines": ["We the new Abu Dhabi, this is our time"], "meaning": "In August 2016, when the billboard, pictured below, appeared in Los Angeles, many fans speculated on a joint album between Drake and Kanye. The logos of Kanye West’s GOOD Music record label and Drake’s OVO Sound record label appeared together at the bottom of the sign.\n\nAbu Dhabi is the capital of the United Arab Emirates.\n\nWhen Drake and Kanye say “We the new Abu Dhabi,” they are talking about how Abu Dhabi started from nothing and had a “glo up”. Calabasas is the city that they reside in and is inspiration on what their collaborative was supposed to be.", "annotation_id": "11532046", "url": "https://genius.com/11532046", "state": "accepted", "votes": 85, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Glow", "line": "We go suit and tie, we gon’ touch the sky-y-y", "vault_lines": ["We go suit and tie, we gon' touch the sky-y-y"], "meaning": "“Touch the Sky” is a song Kanye wrote highlighting his story from rags to riches. He references these songs to present a stark contrast between his current situation and his fast-food employee days in the previous line.", "annotation_id": "11531935", "url": "https://genius.com/11531935", "state": "accepted", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Glow", "line": "Watch out for me, I’m bound to glow You better watch out for me, I’m bound to glow", "vault_lines": ["Watch out for me, I'm bound to glow", "(Watch out) Watch out", "You better watch out for me, I'm bound to glow", "Watch out for me, I'm about to glow"], "meaning": "Glow is short for “glo' up” which signifies an incredible transformation of not only a person’s appearance, but of their whole character.\n\nFrom their (relatively) humble beginnings, Kanye and Drake have clearly glo’d up into influential figures in the world of music, fashion and culture.\n\nIt should be noted that throughout the chorus, Drake sings Watch out for me, I’m about to glow. However, Kanye uses bound to, which is probably a reference to his Yeezus joint, “Bound 2.”", "annotation_id": "11531866", "url": "https://genius.com/11531866", "state": "accepted", "votes": 138, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Glow", "line": "Used to work the fries, now we supersi-i-ize", "vault_lines": ["Used to work the fries, now we supersi-i-ize"], "meaning": "Although Kanye has never stated that he worked in a restaurant, he has revealed that he used to work in ‘Customer Services’ for the clothing brand, GAP.\n\nKanye also mentioned fries in his poem “The McDonald’s Man” that he wrote for Frank Ocean’s first magazine, Boys Don’t Cry. In the poem, Kanye admitted to thinking that french fries are truly evil. McDonald’s eventually responded to Kanye with this tweet.\n\nYe’s fixation on fries dates back to his 2005 track “Gold Digger,\" when he made a similar comparison between his success and climbing the ladder of the fast food work force:\n\nHe got that ambition baby look at his eyes\nThis week he mopping floors, next week it’s the fries", "annotation_id": "11531547", "url": "https://genius.com/11531547", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Glow", "line": "I started out way down low Started from the bottom, now we here now", "vault_lines": ["I started out way down low", "Started from the bottom, now we here now"], "meaning": "This is an interpolation of Drake’s 2013 hit single “Started From the Bottom” from his album Nothing Was the Same.\n\n\n\nLike Drake, Kanye West says he worked hard his way from being unknown to now being one of the greatest hip-hop artists of all time.", "annotation_id": "11531097", "url": "https://genius.com/11531097", "state": "accepted", "votes": 66, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Glow", "status": "done", "targets": 20, "clicked": 20, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-glow-lyrics", "genius_title": "Glow"}
