{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jungle", "line": "She said, “You’re my everything” “I love you through everything” I done did everything to her She forgave me for everything This a “forever” thing", "vault_lines": ["She said, \"You're my everything\"", "\"I love you through everything\"", "I done did everything to her", "She forgave me for everything", "This a \"forever\" thing", "This shit is everything to me"], "meaning": "What I comprehend from this is, this girl starts off by saying “your my everything\n , you know you’ve done shit to me but regardless I love you through everything, drake himself says I done did everything to her! But she forgave him….. why do you ask yourself? Because this is a “forever” thing, this is not no 1 month relationship I kissed you we held hands a couple dates NAH. This is like a I farted around you. I held you through the toughest times. Your biggest burdens you told me about them. Type of forever thing. Love like this is rare really a “forever\" typa love", "annotation_id": "35300425", "url": "https://genius.com/35300425", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jungle", "line": "Our relationship changed that, or it never existed", "vault_lines": ["Our relationship changed that, or it never existed"], "meaning": "They are no longer as close as they used to be, connecting like they used too. Drake has to wonder if it was ever a real relationship or just felt like one.", "annotation_id": "22955699", "url": "https://genius.com/22955699", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jungle", "line": "Hate that I treat it like it’s a “whatever” thing", "vault_lines": ["Hate that I treat it like it's a \"whatever\" thing"], "meaning": "This other person isn’t taking this relationship seriously and this makes Drake mad, simply because Drake is taking the relationship more seriously", "annotation_id": "20399298", "url": "https://genius.com/20399298", "state": "pending", "votes": -50, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jungle", "line": "Feel like we one and the same", "vault_lines": ["Feel like we one and the same"], "meaning": "Drake and this other person seem to have the interest and seem to get along with each other", "annotation_id": "20399293", "url": "https://genius.com/20399293", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jungle", "line": "Listen, you can hear them callin’ my name I’m all over the place, I can’t sit in one place I’m not ashamed at all Still findin’ myself, let alone a soulmate, I’m just sayin’", "vault_lines": ["Still findin' myself, let alone a soulmate, I'm just sayin'", "I'm just like a baby, droolin' over you", "You still down? You still down? You still down?", "Listen, you can hear them callin' my name", "I'm all over the place, I can't sit in one place", "I'm not ashamed at all"], "meaning": "“Still findin' myself, let alone a soulmate, I’m just sayin'”–\n\nAlso, some individuals will focus first on FULLY finding themselves and knowing who they truly are completely before actually feeling ready to accept, find or even entertain the thought of, in some cases, a partner/soulmate.\n\n\n\n“I’m just sayin'” can even be interpreted as a protagonist stating to the recipient of the message that he’s just taking some “me” time in order to better himself for the best of the relationship at hand. Therefore, “I’m just sayin'” could be a polite way of interrupting/nipping in the bud/clarifying/diminishing/disputing any negative thoughts that the recipient of his message may be thinking or feeling, as well as hopefully buying more time and conveying the absolute importance of PATIENCE. :)", "annotation_id": "8077003", "url": "https://genius.com/8077003", "state": "verified", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jungle", "line": "Yeah, these days, these new girls, they got me nervous They go to school and do bottle service They can’t decide, they keep switchin’ majors Being indecisive makes me anxious", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, these days, these new girls, they got me nervous", "They go to school and do bottle service", "They can't decide, they keep switchin' majors", "Being indecisive makes me anxious"], "meaning": "Drake is getting older, believe it or not. It’s getting harder for him to relate to college girls, especially those that can’t decide on a major. Think about it. Drake is 28. College girls are stereotypically between 17-22. That’s an average difference of 8 & a half years. And it’s showing. You can’t deny that when a verse starts with, “These days…” it has an “Ahh, I remember the golden days…” ring to it. Another point of relevance, Drake says he’s “anxious” and “nervous”, emotions commonly associated with older people. The young are wild, free, and indecisive because they still have time, but maybe time is becoming the one luxury Drake cannot afford.\n\nAlso, “being indecisive makes me anxious” could be a double entendre wherein Drake is also referring to himself being indecisive, not just “these new girls”.", "annotation_id": "6721047", "url": "https://genius.com/6721047", "state": "verified", "votes": 51, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jungle", "line": "Listen, you can hear them callin’ my name I’m all over the place, I can’t sit in one place I’m not ashamed at all Still findin’ myself, let alone a soulmate, I’m just sayin’", "vault_lines": ["Still findin' myself, let alone a soulmate, I'm just sayin'", "I'm just like a baby, droolin' over you", "You still down? You still down? You still down?", "Listen, you can hear them callin' my name", "I'm all over the place, I can't sit in one place", "I'm not ashamed at all"], "meaning": "1 interpretation – seems he is torn with his fame and his relationship.\n\n-‘the things i cant change’ -his fame, his celebrity, his status – make her love him but..\nthe fame leads to difficulties because:\n- ‘calling my name’ – fans\n- ‘im all over the place, i cant sit in one place’ – touring the country\n\n2nd interpretation -\nThe lines could also be describing his difficulties committing due to other women, ‘calling my name’ and his feelings are ‘all over the place, i cant sit in one place’\n‘im not ashamed at all’\n\nthis would fit with the next line where he explicitly states he is not interested in settling down,\n‘still finding myself let alone a soul mate’", "annotation_id": "5380974", "url": "https://genius.com/5380974", "state": "verified", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jungle", "line": "Listen, you can hear them callin’ my name I’m all over the place, I can’t sit in one place I’m not ashamed at all Still findin’ myself, let alone a soulmate, I’m just sayin’", "vault_lines": ["Still findin' myself, let alone a soulmate, I'm just sayin'", "I'm just like a baby, droolin' over you", "You still down? You still down? You still down?", "Listen, you can hear them callin' my name", "I'm all over the place, I can't sit in one place", "I'm not ashamed at all"], "meaning": "Drake knows that his fame has reached everyone and that everyone talks about him, so he tells that one lady that he’s all over the place.", "annotation_id": "4973166", "url": "https://genius.com/4973166", "state": "verified", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jungle", "line": "Yeah, these days, these new girls, they got me nervous They go to school and do bottle service They can’t decide, they keep switchin’ majors Being indecisive makes me anxious", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, these days, these new girls, they got me nervous", "They go to school and do bottle service", "They can't decide, they keep switchin' majors", "Being indecisive makes me anxious"], "meaning": "Many young women are just going to school with no purpose or vision other than the degree itself. They are caught up in the party scene and their lack of focus makes him nervous as he has alot at stake and he simply can’t afford to let them fuck that shit up.", "annotation_id": "4949126", "url": "https://genius.com/4949126", "state": "verified", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jungle", "line": "Whenever they say somethin’ ’bout us, you listen But fuck what they talkin’ about on your timeline That’s cuttin’ all into my time with you Fuck what they talkin’ about on your timeline That’s cuttin’ all into my time with you My time with you, my", "vault_lines": ["Whenever they say somethin' 'bout us, you listen", "But fuck what they talkin' about on your timeline", "That's cuttin' all into my time with you", "Fuck what they talkin' about on your timeline", "My time with you, my"], "meaning": "“Fuck what they talking' about on your timeline\nThat’s cutting all into my time with you”\n- Drake is with a girl, and she is constantly checking her phone. He’s saying ‘stop checking Facebook’– they’re finally together, and Drizzy wants all her attention.", "annotation_id": "4906519", "url": "https://genius.com/4906519", "state": "verified", "votes": 140, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jungle", "line": "Whenever they say somethin’ ’bout us, you listen But fuck what they talkin’ about on your timeline That’s cuttin’ all into my time with you Fuck what they talkin’ about on your timeline That’s cuttin’ all into my time with you My time with you, my", "vault_lines": ["Whenever they say somethin' 'bout us, you listen", "But fuck what they talkin' about on your timeline", "That's cuttin' all into my time with you", "Fuck what they talkin' about on your timeline", "My time with you, my"], "meaning": "Drake is frustrated that the girl pays attention to all the gossip and rumors surrounding their relationship. He urges her to ignore social media and focus instead on their precious time together.", "annotation_id": "4888941", "url": "https://genius.com/4888941", "state": "accepted", "votes": 148, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jungle", "line": "(Put a bib on me) (Put a bib on me) Rock me real slowly Put a bib on me I’m just like a baby, droolin’ over you The things you do", "vault_lines": ["Rock me real slowly", "Put a bib on me", "I'm just like a baby, droolin' over you", "The things you do"], "meaning": "The hook is sampled from Gabriel Garzón Montano’s “6 8.”\n\nhttps://soundcloud.com/gabriel-garzonmontano/a\n\n“I’m honored that he was moved to make a tune over mine,” Garzón-Montano said. “I respect his incredible work ethic. His time feel is ridiculous. And, of course, I love his songs about winning. Motivational music!”\n\nGabriel Garzon Montano’s lyrics suggest a feeling of dependence on his significant other, comparing his need to that of a baby for its mother.", "annotation_id": "4888543", "url": "https://genius.com/4888543", "state": "accepted", "votes": 506, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jungle", "line": "Call your number and it’s out of service Who can I call for your information? What am I supposed to do after we done everything that we done? Who is your replacement?", "vault_lines": ["I done did everything to her", "Call your number and it's out of service", "Who can I call for your information?", "What am I supposed to do after we done everything that we done?", "Who is your replacement?"], "meaning": "The girl in question has changed her number—He’s at a loss.\n\nDrake will be lost without this girl, but is hesitant to find a replacement because they’ve been through a lot together.\n\nDrake also implies earlier in the song that their relationship is covert, perhaps suggesting that he can’t call this girl’s friends to ask about her without exposing their relationship to the world.", "annotation_id": "4888431", "url": "https://genius.com/4888431", "state": "accepted", "votes": 125, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jungle", "line": "Yeah, these days, these new girls, they got me nervous They go to school and do bottle service They can’t decide, they keep switchin’ majors Being indecisive makes me anxious", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, these days, these new girls, they got me nervous", "They go to school and do bottle service", "They can't decide, they keep switchin' majors", "Being indecisive makes me anxious"], "meaning": "The new women surrounding Drake make him uncomfortable. Their life, divided between studying and partying, makes him suspicious of their character. Their propensity to switch majors at school makes him wonder if they are frivolous and shallow.\n\nDrake’s time is also divided between his serious pursuits and hedonism, between passionate love affairs and casual flings, so the anxiety surrounding the “new girls” indecision might just be a reflection of his own divided self.", "annotation_id": "4888270", "url": "https://genius.com/4888270", "state": "accepted", "votes": 162, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jungle", "line": "Listen, you can hear them callin’ my name I’m all over the place, I can’t sit in one place I’m not ashamed at all Still findin’ myself, let alone a soulmate, I’m just sayin’", "vault_lines": ["Still findin' myself, let alone a soulmate, I'm just sayin'", "I'm just like a baby, droolin' over you", "You still down? You still down? You still down?", "Listen, you can hear them callin' my name", "I'm all over the place, I can't sit in one place", "I'm not ashamed at all"], "meaning": "Drake invokes the sound of fans chanting his name to express his celebrity.\n\nHe enjoys the touring life, but he knows it would be hard in a relationship. He is proud of his fame, but has not yet matured to the point where he could settle down with one woman.", "annotation_id": "4888254", "url": "https://genius.com/4888254", "state": "accepted", "votes": 141, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jungle", "line": "Trust me, girl, this shit is everything to me She from the jungle She from the jungle I take somebody else’s car, drive there undercover This shit is everything to me This shit is everything", "vault_lines": ["She forgave me for everything", "Trust me, girl, this shit is everything to me", "She from the jungle", "I take somebody else's car, drive there undercover", "This shit is everything to me", "This shit is everything"], "meaning": "“The jungle” is a slang name for Lawrence Heights, a neighborhood in Toronto known for its recurrent gang violence.\n\n\n\nHe doesn’t want to attract too much attention when visiting her so he has no other option but to drive a car that’s not recognizable. She is worth the trouble.", "annotation_id": "4887967", "url": "https://genius.com/4887967", "state": "accepted", "votes": 151, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jungle", "line": "These days I’m lettin’ God handle all things above me", "vault_lines": ["These days I'm lettin' God handle all things above me"], "meaning": "Drake’s lyric loosely resembles the famous Serenity Prayer:\n\nGod, grant me the serenity to accept the things I cannot change,\nThe courage to change the things I can,\nAnd the wisdom to know the difference.\n\nOften torn between humility and arrogance, here Drake is resigned to whatever God has planned for him.\n\nHe acknowledges that things beyond his control are why he’s loved. One could reasonably ask what is beyond Drake’s control: Is it his fortune and fame or is it his inner self?", "annotation_id": "4887960", "url": "https://genius.com/4887960", "state": "accepted", "votes": 211, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jungle", "line": "Don’t know where we stand I used to hit you ’bout everything, oh Are we still good? Are we still good? Are we still good? Are we still good? If I need to talk, are you around? Are you down for the cause? Are you down? Are you down? Are you down? Are you down for the cause? Are you down? Are you down? Are you down? Are you down for the cause? You still down? You still down? You still down?", "vault_lines": ["\"I love you through everything\"", "Don't know where we stand", "I used to hit you 'bout everything, oh", "Are we still good? Are we still good?", "If I need to talk, are you around?", "Are you down for the cause?", "Are you down? Are you down? Are you down?", "You still down? You still down? You still down?"], "meaning": "Drake’s no longer sure where his relationship stands, he is falling out of touch with the girl and wonders aloud whether she’s still emotionally available and supportive.\n\nThe beginning of Big Sean’s second verse of “Blessings,” which features Drake and Kanye West, also explores whether someone’s still down.", "annotation_id": "4887942", "url": "https://genius.com/4887942", "state": "accepted", "votes": 277, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jungle", "status": "done", "targets": 18, "clicked": 18, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-jungle-lyrics", "genius_title": "Jungle"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Love All", "line": "When I could destroy you, that takes some fuckin’ discipline", "vault_lines": ["When I could destroy you, that takes some fuckin' discipline"], "meaning": "Self explanatory. It takes discipline/strength to not crash out on folks that did you wrong", "annotation_id": "40615673", "url": "https://genius.com/40615673", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Love All", "line": "I could send a team to come drill you I got a billion or two and I know where the fuck you live", "vault_lines": ["I could send a team to come drill you", "I got a billion or two and I know where the fuck you live"], "meaning": "Implying he’d send a hit to someone’s house, beings though he know where they live, and have the money to do it. ALLEGEDLY", "annotation_id": "40615661", "url": "https://genius.com/40615661", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Love All", "line": "This ain’t the same Shawn that you knew once", "vault_lines": ["This ain't the same Shawn that you knew once"], "meaning": "saying that it’s not the JAY-Z (Shawn Carter) that people once knew, he has changed and he’s not the same. He’s above the rest.", "annotation_id": "39410463", "url": "https://genius.com/39410463", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Love All", "line": "Best thing I can do is not build with you", "vault_lines": ["Best thing I can do is not build with you"], "meaning": "Jay-Z has referenced DeHaven multiple times in his music, including in the song “No Hook,” where he raps, “So fuck DeHaven for caving, that’s why we don’t speak // Made men ain’t supposed to make statements”. Jay-Z cut ties with DeHaven back in the 1990s, which ultimately meant that he did not bring him along on his rise to the top.", "annotation_id": "33384960", "url": "https://genius.com/33384960", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Love All", "line": "Niggas wanted to kill me and y’all still with ’em Nigga, y’all chill with ’em, and y’all wonder why we not friends?", "vault_lines": ["Niggas wanted to kill me and y'all still with 'em", "Nigga, y'all chill with 'em, and y'all wonder why we not friends?", "Niggas wanted to kill me and y'all want me to be friendly"], "meaning": "Choke No Joke has discussed how this was directed at DeHaven Irby, a former friend and associate of Jay-Z.\n\nDeHaven has also admitted that this was directed at him.\n\nChoke No Joke mentioned that Jay-Z was shot at during a bad drug deal. He described an incident where tensions escalated due to a drug transaction that went wrong, leading to Jay-Z being targeted. Choke noted that this situation was part of the larger fallout between Jay-Z and DeHaven\n\nDeHaven Irby is a former associate of Jay-Z, known for his close friendship with the rapper during their youth in Brooklyn’s Marcy Projects. He has been vocal about their complicated relationship and has shared insights into Jay-Z’s early life and career.\n\n\n\nChoke No Joke, whose real name is Arthur Alston, is a filmmaker and hip-hop journalist recognized for his documentaries and commentary on hip-hop culture. He gained prominence for his work on projects like “The Hip-Hop Nucleus” and has been involved in discussions about Jay-Z and his relationships within the music industry.", "annotation_id": "33384820", "url": "https://genius.com/33384820", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Love All", "line": "Can’t burn a bridge just to light my way", "vault_lines": ["Can't burn a bridge just to light my way"], "meaning": "Clever double entendre here:\n\n\n“Burning a bridge” pretty much means to cut someone out of your life. However, Drake feels like he can’t simply cut someone off in order to “light [his] way” towards success\nQuite literally setting a bridge on fire would produce a great deal of light", "annotation_id": "28649454", "url": "https://genius.com/28649454", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Love All", "line": "Long way down from the heights I’m chasin’", "vault_lines": ["Long way down from the heights I'm chasin'"], "meaning": "Here, Drake is comparing the altitude of a plane in the air, to the greatness of the achievements he is chasing. This might refer to him trying to get into heaven, or that he is reaching for things which are ‘out of this world’, due to a plane’s trajectory coming quite close to the earth when comparing it to the earth’s layers and space.", "annotation_id": "27136629", "url": "https://genius.com/27136629", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Love All", "line": "I don’t shine shoes, uh, this ain’t what you want, no", "vault_lines": ["I don't shine shoes, uh, this ain't what you want, no"], "meaning": "Jay-Z continues its mafia reference citing a scene from Goodfellas", "annotation_id": "26866377", "url": "https://genius.com/26866377", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Love All", "line": "Grab the top spot like “pardon my reach” Woke up one day and it was all on me If it comes down, it’s gon’ fall on me", "vault_lines": ["Grab the top spot like \"pardon my reach\"", "Woke up one day and it was all on me", "If it comes down, it's gon' fall on me"], "meaning": "Drake is arguably one of the biggest names in the entertainment industry and has ruled the charts almost unmatched for the past decade. Drake has the most entries on the Hot 100 chart ever, with 237 total, including 9 number one hits.\n\nDue to being at the top, Drake faces internal and external pressures to constantly one-up himself. Drake references the pressures and fear of falling from the “top” in Money In The Grave:\n\nI was on top when that shit meant a lot\nStill on top like I’m scared of the drop", "annotation_id": "24253065", "url": "https://genius.com/24253065", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Love All", "line": "Never had a lot, this is all I need", "vault_lines": ["Never had a lot, this is all I need"], "meaning": "While born into mediocrity, Drake had dreams of something bigger since a child. This is shown in his childhood acting roles, but resonates more through his music career given his vast success.\n\nDrake discussed his aspirations early in his career. Notably, he shared a similar sentiment on the 2009 track “Successful,\" rapping:\n\nJust enough to solve your problems, too much’ll kill ya\n\nIt appears Drake is finally reaching a level where he can say he’s attained all that he has desired.", "annotation_id": "23956101", "url": "https://genius.com/23956101", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Love All", "line": "Niggas wanted to kill me and y’all want me to be friendly Niggas want sympathy after they wanted to end me", "vault_lines": ["Niggas wanted to kill me and y'all still with 'em", "Niggas wanted to kill me and y'all want me to be friendly", "Niggas want sympathy after they wanted to end me"], "meaning": "On instagram, Dehaven confirms that the lyrics are about him and admits that Jay-Z “almost lost his life” behind a falling out between the two.", "annotation_id": "23895131", "url": "https://genius.com/23895131", "state": "pending", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Love All", "line": "People never care ’til it’s R.I.P.", "vault_lines": ["People never care 'til it's R.I.P."], "meaning": "Drake places attention on a common problem within the Hip Hop industry, being the toxic culture of listeners to multiply after the death of an artist. Some have attributed this to supporting past artists becoming ‘trendy’.\nAn example of this, outlined by a ‘Variety’ article [link at bottom], saw a 500% increase in streams after the late rapper Juice WRLD passed away [pictured below]\n\n\n\nTo be clear, Drake isn’t suggesting that these late artists aren’t worthy of this level of success but is merely asking the Hip Hop and Rap community to recognize talent for what it is and appreciate artists before they pass.\n\nVariety Article:\nhttps://variety.com/2019/music/news/juice-wrld-streams-nearly-500-percent-death-1203432379/,", "annotation_id": "23884815", "url": "https://genius.com/23884815", "state": "pending", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Love All", "line": "All that back and forth on the internet Nigga, we don’t tennis that, y’all gotta do something, yeah", "vault_lines": ["All that back and forth on the internet", "Nigga, we don't tennis that, y'all gotta do something, yeah"], "meaning": "Hov mentions the sport tennis as the ball goes' back and forth' during games between two players. He also uses creative wordplay: ‘do something’ sounds like ‘deucemthing’ mentioning the tennis term ‘deuce’. A term to describe a 40-40 between two players in a set. This is a possible reference to Drake’s producer 40.", "annotation_id": "23875656", "url": "https://genius.com/23875656", "state": "pending", "votes": 53, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Love All", "line": "Lotta ‘42 on the flights I’m takin’", "vault_lines": ["Lotta '42 on the flights I'm takin'"], "meaning": "“‘42” is shorthand for the classic Don Julio 1942 Tequila, which he takes with him on his private flights.\n\nDon Julio 1942 Tequila is handcrafted in tribute to the year that Don Julio González began his tequila-making journey.", "annotation_id": "23874716", "url": "https://genius.com/23874716", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Love All", "line": "You know the price of everything but the value of nothing", "vault_lines": ["You know the price of everything but the value of nothing"], "meaning": "First performed in 1892, ‘Lady Windermere’s Fan, A Play About a Good Woman’ was a four-act comedy written by Oscar Wilde.  From it came the famously known “definition of a cynic”, as shown below in it’s entirety:\n\nCecil Graham: What is a cynic?\nLord Darlington: A man who knows the price of everything, and the value of nothing.", "annotation_id": "23874190", "url": "https://genius.com/23874190", "state": "accepted", "votes": 126, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Love All", "line": "Niggas turned they back on me for no good reason", "vault_lines": ["Niggas turned they back on me for no good reason"], "meaning": "When Drake started in the industry, he had a lot of respect for Kanye West, he never tried to hide this, in many interviews, he showed his respect to Kanye West.\n\nDrake in an interview during May 2009:\n\nBefore I met him, I had the utmost respect for Kanye West. I’d even go as far as to say he’s the most influential person as far as a musician that I’d ever had in my life.\n\nBut everyone has it limits, in Scorpion, his five times platinum album, Drake had this verse in “Emotionless“\n\nI can’t even capture the feeling I had at first\nMeetin' all my heroes like seein' how magic works\nThe people I look up to are goin' from bad to worse\nTheir actions out of character even when they rehearse\n\nIn case you somehow missed it, Drake and Kanye West feud is 12-year-long.\nThis originally started in 2009, from being removed in “All of the Lights“ for no reason given at 2011, to Drake doing subliminal shoots during the time, like taking the throne.\n\nIn 2016 things seemed way better between both, Drake and Kanye: there were a lot of rumours that they were planning on working on a joint album.\n\n\n\nIn the end, this didn’t end up happening. For some reason Kanye removed Drake from “Wolves”. and Drake decided to remove “The Throne” (Kanye West and Jay-Z) from “Pop Style” at “Views” album release.\n\nIt was in 2018 when the beef between both suddenly reignited, on “Duppy Freestyle” Drake responded to the ghostwritter claims by saying he was actually a ghostwritter for Kanye West, a week after, Drake was officially confirmed as a co-writer of Kanye West’s “Yikes”..\n\nAccording to some rumors, Kanye West was reportedly featured on Drake’s “Nice For What”, the same day Pusha T released the infamous “The Story of Adidon” in which he revealed Drake had a secret son, this caused a lot of controversy because later on, Drake stated it was Kanye West who leaked this information to Pusha T, however this just a rumor and Kanye West stated the following:\n\n“I’m ‘Ye. I got major things to do other than be telling him some information about Drake”.\n\nIn August 29th, 2021, Kanye West finally released his most anticipated album, ”Donda”, that includes a lot of shoots aimed at Drake, for example, in ”Pure Souls”.:\n\nMan, I swear these boys keep playin’ / We gon’ have to square up then / We gon’ have to send it up then.\n\nKanye West also leaked Drake’s address momentarily on Instagram for some reason.\n\nDrake eventually responded on Instagram:\n\nhttps://twitter.com/Akademiks/status/1429788645578379273?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1429788645578379273%7Ctwgr%5E%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nme.com%2Fnews%2Fmusic%2Fkanye-west-momentarily-leaked-drakes-home-address-on-instagram-3027185", "annotation_id": "23874041", "url": "https://genius.com/23874041", "state": "accepted", "votes": 59, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Love All", "line": "Previously on Ready To Die", "vault_lines": ["Previously on Ready To Die"], "meaning": "This is a direct sample of the intro track, “Life After Death Intro,” to late legendary rapper The Notorious B.I.G.’s sophomore album, Life After Death.", "annotation_id": "20180345", "url": "https://genius.com/20180345", "state": "accepted", "votes": 148, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
