{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Race My Mind", "line": "Picture me rollin’ through downtown in a A4", "vault_lines": ["Picture me rollin' through downtown in a A4"], "meaning": "This is a reference to Tupac’s ‘Picture Me Rollin’ off of his 1996 classic album ‘All Eyez On Me’.\n\nPicture me rollin' in my 500 Benz\n\nIn Tupac’s song he is referring to a Mercedes R129 500SL.\n\n\n\nDrake, on the other hand, is referring to an Audi A4.", "annotation_id": "40150401", "url": "https://genius.com/40150401", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Race My Mind", "line": "Know who you be around, I know that they teaming up", "vault_lines": ["Know who you be around, I know that they teaming up"], "meaning": "This could be a reference to XO, as Drake and The Weeknd were beefing at this point.  The “teaming up” suggests Drake may have been anticipating some of the events of 2024.\n\nAfter this the two artists made up and were cool for some time, but Drake and PND alluded to girl drama happening between OVO and XO on their songs “Members Only” in 2023 and “Lasers” in 2025.", "annotation_id": "35305481", "url": "https://genius.com/35305481", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Race My Mind", "line": "Them niggas just can’t understand it (Yeah, yeah, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Them niggas just can't understand it (Yeah, yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "This sample is from the Notorious B.I.G song Hope You Niggas Sleep, released in 1999 on his born again album. The song also has writing credits to Lil Wayne and Birdman.", "annotation_id": "32145018", "url": "https://genius.com/32145018", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Race My Mind", "line": "(I hope you niggas sleep)", "vault_lines": ["Then you fell fast asleep (I hope you niggas sleep)"], "meaning": "The sample comes from Notorious B.I.G. song “Hope You Niggas Sleep.”\n\nhttps://youtu.be/053L-q4iqLg?t=85", "annotation_id": "32145006", "url": "https://genius.com/32145006", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Race My Mind", "line": "All to be with niggas who just startin’ to move bossy Maybe I just handled you too softly Them boys got no Kelis in they blood", "vault_lines": ["All to be with niggas who just startin' to move bossy", "Maybe I just handled you too softly", "Them boys got no Kelis in they blood"], "meaning": "Drake refers to singer Kelis who has a song called “Bossy”\n\nhttps://youtu.be/dyWUNctImOk?si=t23gE13EdHui2r7G", "annotation_id": "29740483", "url": "https://genius.com/29740483", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Race My Mind", "line": "Cause I remember last time you wouldn’t make love to me", "vault_lines": ["'Cause I remember last time you wouldn't make love to me"], "meaning": "Another play on Rick James’s “Give it to me baby”.\n\nHis woman has been out frolicking to and fro, and when she comes home she’s assuredly too ashamed of her nightly behavior to be intimate with her partner.", "annotation_id": "23881112", "url": "https://genius.com/23881112", "state": "pending", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Race My Mind", "line": "How I’m supposed to wife it? You not Ayesha enough", "vault_lines": ["How I'm supposed to wife it? You not Ayesha enough"], "meaning": "Drake holds his love interest to a high standard by namedropping Canadian-American actress, television personality, and author Ayesha Curry, who married NBA superstar Stephen Curry in 2011. The couple has three children together and the Curry family was even featured on the cover of Parents Magazine in April 2016.\n\n\n\nDrake surprised Ayesha Curry at her book signing event in Toronto", "annotation_id": "23875479", "url": "https://genius.com/23875479", "state": "accepted", "votes": 91, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Race My Mind", "line": "Picture my signature on a pair of some J 4s", "vault_lines": ["Picture my signature on a pair of some J 4s"], "meaning": "Drake could be also alluding to his 2019 Nike Air Jordan 4 sneakers, Raptors/Drake OVO, which feature Drizzy’s signature on the tongue label.\n\n\n\nDrake chatting with the Raptors head coach Nick Nurse in his signature sneakers in 2019\n\nIn September 2020, a pair of Drake’s unreleased and scrapped Nike Air Jordan 4 prototype/sample was sold at Sotheby’s for $32,760. Drizzy had already shared the sneakers in a September 2017 Instagram post and teased:\n\nDefine Rare…Air Jordan Retro 4 ‘Multi-Color’ 👌🏽", "annotation_id": "23874993", "url": "https://genius.com/23874993", "state": "accepted", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Race My Mind", "line": "Could already tell that you’re comin’ home intoxicated", "vault_lines": ["Since you're comin' home intoxicated, oh", "Could already tell that you're comin' home intoxicated"], "meaning": "This line as well as many others throughout the song interpolate Rick James' “Give It To Me”\n\nWhen I came home last night\nYou wouldn’t make love to me\nYou went fast asleep\nYou wouldn’t even talk to me\nYou say I’m so crazy\nComing home intoxicated", "annotation_id": "20650193", "url": "https://genius.com/20650193", "state": "pending", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
