{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Another Late Night", "line": "We up in the Turks with twenty bitches, just me and my team (Us)", "vault_lines": ["We up in the Turks with twenty bitches, just me and my team (Us)"], "meaning": "Turks and Caico is an island in the British and French Territories, as it is owned in technicality by Great Britain and is a very popular vacation destination in rap lyrics (Rapper NAV has a song called Turks as he raps about the island).", "annotation_id": "29738161", "url": "https://genius.com/29738161", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Another Late Night", "line": "I’ll support the opps before I support sippin’ green (’Kay)", "vault_lines": ["I'll support the opps before I support sippin' green ('Kay)"], "meaning": "Lil Yachty is known for his lyrics, song names and substance abuse with Lean, a drink that mixes Soda with promethazine codeine syrup.\n\nThe green syrup, known by its' medical name Phenergan is a greenish-yellow colored cough syrup with a strawberry banana-ish taste, mostly used upon children’s illness.\nAnd has been used in rap lyrics, such as…\n\n“Mixing Codeine up with the Phenergan, she got thick but she wanna be thin again” ~ Central Cee, Sprinter\n\n“If I sip it, boy, it’s red or purple, I don’t drink Yoda.” ~ BabyTron,  Awful Lotta Yeah", "annotation_id": "29738112", "url": "https://genius.com/29738112", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Another Late Night", "line": "It’s Lil Boat, I’m practically now from the 6ix (Pssh, pssh)", "vault_lines": ["It's Lil Boat, I'm practically now from the 6ix (Pssh, pssh)"], "meaning": "One of Yachty’s nicknames is Lil Boat, and as a result of his close friendship to Drake in the past few years, and presumably traveling to Toronto, also known as the 6ix, to spend time with Drake, Yachty has close ties to the city.", "annotation_id": "29733283", "url": "https://genius.com/29733283", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Another Late Night", "line": "This lil’ Drizzy reppin’ ’Crete, ayy", "vault_lines": ["This lil' Drizzy reppin' 'Crete, ayy"], "meaning": "“Crete” is short for Concrete Boys, which is Lil Yachty’s collective.\n\nConcrete Boys is based on the idea of being more “solid” (i.e., loyal) to each other than concrete.\n\nYachty released an ode to Concrete Boys, aptly titled “Concrete Boys”, in 2020.\n\nIn 2023, Drake was seen sporting a Concrete Boys chain, which was gifted to him by Yachty.", "annotation_id": "29733254", "url": "https://genius.com/29733254", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Another Late Night", "line": "I let her go, she fine as hell but baby wasn’t stylish (Yeah) She had big tits like Billie Eilish but she couldn’t sing (Drip)", "vault_lines": ["I let her go, she fine as hell but baby wasn't stylish (Yeah)", "She had big tits like Billie Eilish but she couldn't sing (Drip)"], "meaning": "Yachty describes some qualities about a woman, many of them superficial, before making a misogynistic comparison to pop musician Billie Eilish.\n\nBillie gained public attention musically when she dropped “Ocean Eyes” at 13 years old in 2015, and she became increasingly sexualized and objectified as time passed. She explained her trademark style of bagging clothes for a 2017 Calvin Klein campaign, stating:\n\n I never want the world to know everything about me. I mean, that’s why I wear baggy clothes. Nobody can have an opinion because they haven’t seen what’s underneath, you know? Nobody can be like, ‘She’s slim-thick,’ ‘She’s not slim-thick,’ ‘She’s got a flat ass,’ ‘She’s got a fat ass.’ No one can say any of that because they don’t know.\n\nDespite her best efforts, she couldn’t curb social media and society’s ingrained sexism and misogyny and was sexualized and objectified regularly as a minor and beyond. For context, Reddit routinely had to delete communities dedicated to objectifying her when she was a minor. As of this song’s release, there are more communities and community members for sexualizing her than following her as a person.\n\n\n\nIn March 2020, having recently turned 18, Billie decided to engage in the conversation about her body by premiering the intentionally provocative visuals for her then-unreleased spoken word interlude, “NOT MY RESPONSIBILITY,” during her Where Do We Go? Tour live shows.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZlvfYmfefSI\n\nWith all this context, Yachty’s bar appeared problematic on arrival by directly perpetuating sexism and misogyny with his sexualization and objectification of Billie, who has specifically flagged these things as issues. However, during a November 2023 Variety interview, Billie revealed her personal development, having found a new level of self-acceptance. She disclosed that she no longer felt as insecure as she previously had and actually liked the lyric:\n\nI think it’s fun! I’m flattered! Yachty is my friend. Drake is my friend. It’s a joke. I do have big tits. I love it.", "annotation_id": "29732314", "url": "https://genius.com/29732314", "state": "accepted", "votes": 58, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Another Late Night", "line": "She a pretty little liar like she Shay, but that’s bae", "vault_lines": ["She a pretty little liar like she Shay, but that's bae"], "meaning": "Pretty Little Liar like she Shay, but that’s Bae\n\nShay Mitchell is on Pretty Little Liars and is a Sauga baddie ahlieee", "annotation_id": "29728577", "url": "https://genius.com/29728577", "state": "pending", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Another Late Night", "line": "Boost a white bitch up and now she think she really poppin’", "vault_lines": ["Boost a white bitch up and now she think she really poppin'"], "meaning": "This line could be reffering to Yachty and Drake doing interviews with Bobbi Althoff, considering after their interviews her follower count was boosted exponentially.", "annotation_id": "29728077", "url": "https://genius.com/29728077", "state": "pending", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Another Late Night", "line": "Fuck my bitch new body, sadly, I got demoitis", "vault_lines": ["Fuck my bitch new body, sadly, I got demoitis"], "meaning": "“Demoitis is the feeling that the best version is the one you are used to.”\n\nThe line also references Kanye West’s famous unreleased demo “New Body.”", "annotation_id": "29725617", "url": "https://genius.com/29725617", "state": "pending", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Another Late Night", "line": "Shawty rinsin’ Dillon Brooks, can’t believe this nigga talkin’, damn", "vault_lines": ["Shawty rinsin' Dillon Brooks, can't believe this nigga talkin', damn"], "meaning": "Dillon Brooks is a Canadian professional basketball player for the Houston Rockets as of the song’s release. As a defensive specialist, he was named for the NBA All-Defensive Second Team at the end of the 2022-2023 NBA season and the Best Defensive Player in the FIBA World Cup in 2023. He is known for his toughness and trash-talking on the court. However, Drizzy’s diss could be motivated by an August 2023 interview where Team Canada was asked to choose their favorite Canadian between Ryan Reynolds and Drake: everyone but Brooks chose Drake.", "annotation_id": "29725267", "url": "https://genius.com/29725267", "state": "accepted", "votes": 59, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Another Late Night", "line": "My doggy Luxxy ignorant, he from the bricks", "vault_lines": ["My doggy Luxxy ignorant, he from the bricks"], "meaning": "In this line Yachty refers to his long time friend Luxxy, (pronounced lucky) or @dontkallmeluxxy on Instagram.\n\nYachty also referenced Luxxy on his recent single, The Seceret Recipe, where he said:\n\nMy doggy Luxxy on the edge, holdin’ on by a thread, just like a kite\n\nSimilarly to his line in his previous single, Yachty restates that Luxxy is an ignorant man from a dangerous background", "annotation_id": "29725006", "url": "https://genius.com/29725006", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Another Late Night", "line": "My bank account is magnolia, Milly rockin’, ayy", "vault_lines": ["My bank account is magnolia, Milly rockin', ayy"], "meaning": "Reference to the most popular track by rapper Playboi Carti, hit of 2017 — «Magnolia»\n\nIn New York I Milly Rock (Rock)", "annotation_id": "29724965", "url": "https://genius.com/29724965", "state": "accepted", "votes": 72, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Another Late Night", "line": "Weirdos in my comments talkin’ ’bout some Millie Bobby, look Bring them jokes up to the gang, we get to really flockin’ Or send a finger to your mama in some FedEx boxes Open up that shit, it’s jaw droppin’, really shockin’, ayy", "vault_lines": ["Or send a finger to your mama in some FedEx boxes", "Open up that shit, it's jaw droppin', really shockin', ayy", "Weirdos in my comments talkin' 'bout some Millie Bobby, look", "Bring them jokes up to the gang, we get to really flockin'"], "meaning": "Drake references English actress and model Millie Bobby Brown, who shot into superstardom portraying Eleven in Netflix’s supernatural drama, Stranger Things.\n\nIn 2018, Millie shared that Drake was a big endorser of her work, and they keep in good contact, even getting advice about boys. This stemmed into an online talking point about grooming and bred memes as the internet generally found it weird and predatory that Drake, 31, would communicate as familiarly as he was with Millie, 14.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/lYZPKh74Li8\n\nThis is the first time Drake has mentioned this, and he dictates that he and his friends will get violent if the topic is brought up, further backing up how absurd he thinks this is. He also alludes to Mafia-threatening techniques in which they would often send decapitated body parts of their enemies, such as hands and heads, to the doorstep of their loved ones in a delivery box. Drake threatening to “send a finger” is purposeful, as most of these comments are typed and posted online.", "annotation_id": "29724647", "url": "https://genius.com/29724647", "state": "accepted", "votes": 61, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Another Late Night", "line": "I ain’t pretty flacko, bitch, this shit get really rocky, ayy, what? Damn, what?", "vault_lines": ["I ain't pretty flacko, bitch, this shit get really rocky, ayy, what? Damn, what?"], "meaning": "Drake mentions rapper A$AP Rocky using his nickname “flacko” and making a word play with his rap name. Rumours have been made over the years that Drake and A$AP Rocky have beef with each other, mainly being accelerated after A$AP Rocky got into a relationship with Rihanna which led to him having two kids with her.\n\nRihanna and Drake had an on and off relationship since 2009 which seemingly lasted until 2018 when Rihanna said:\n\n[Me and Drake] don’t have a friendship now, but we’re not enemies either. It is what it is", "annotation_id": "29498134", "url": "https://genius.com/29498134", "state": "accepted", "votes": 66, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Another Late Night", "status": "done", "targets": 26, "clicked": 26, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-another-late-night-lyrics", "genius_title": "Another Late Night"}
