{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Major Distribution", "line": "Same place you singin’, bitch, you shoppin’", "vault_lines": ["Same place you singin', bitch, you shoppin'"], "meaning": "This line is “Same place you send your bitches shoppin”,  he’s referring to Hot Topic the clothing store which he mentioned in the previous line.", "annotation_id": "29749711", "url": "https://genius.com/29749711", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Major Distribution", "line": "Booby Trap, we need a business office", "vault_lines": ["Booby Trap, we need a business office", "Magic City need a business office"], "meaning": "Booby Trap On The River is the number one strip club located in Miami, FL that is open 24/7. Drake has been there so many times that he is suggesting that they need an office in the establishment.\n\nHe recently held his album release party for “Her Loss” there along with 21 Savage, Kodak Black, G-Herbo and others. During that event he also gave away $10,000 to fans and 6 Chanel bags to a few selected dancers. Previously, he also rented out The Trap several nights for his “Honestly Nevermind” album party too.\n\n\n\nHe’s also shot multiple videos in Booby Trap including “Sticky” & “Rich Flex”.", "annotation_id": "27490437", "url": "https://genius.com/27490437", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Major Distribution", "line": "I ain’t tryna wrestle like The Rock, fuck the trish, I’d rather sip the wock", "vault_lines": ["I ain't tryna wrestle like The Rock, fuck the trish, I'd rather sip the wock"], "meaning": "Dwayne “The Rock” Johnson and Trish Stratus are faomus former wrestlers for the WWE. During their wrestling career, Johnson tried hitting on Trish, saved her from an attempted sexual assault, fought alongside her, and kissed her.\n\n\n\nTris Pharma (usually called Tris) and Wockhardt (usually called Wock) are two pharmaceutical companies and producers of cough syrup containing promethazine and codeine.\n\nCough Syrup is used combined with a soft drink to create the popular drug Lean.\n\n21 Savage is using the similarity between the words Trish and Tris and says that he prefers Wock over Tris.\n\n\n\n\n\nIt is also possible that 21 shouts out to co-writer and co-vocalist of this song, Lil Yachty, and its song – “Poland”:\n\nI took the Wock' to Poland\nI took the Wock' to Poland\nI took the Wock' to Poland", "annotation_id": "27152457", "url": "https://genius.com/27152457", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Major Distribution", "line": "Magic City need a business office Twenty-nine, I keep a business office", "vault_lines": ["Magic City need a business office", "Twenty-nine, I keep a business office"], "meaning": "Magic City is a well-known exclusive strip club in Atlanta. It’s a place for rappers and producers to meet, listen to live music on stage, and get crazy intoxicated.\nIt was previously referenced in the first song of the album, Rich Flex (it was mentioned by 21 Savage), and in other Drake songs, such as Jumpman (it was mentioned by Future) and 10 Bands.\n\n\nI’m a savage (21)\nSmack her booty in Magic (21, 21)\nI’ll slap a pussy nigga with a ratchet (Pussy)\n(From “Rich Flex”)\n\nHeard they came through Magic City on a Monday\nHeard they had the club wild, it was star-studded\n(From “Jumpman”)\n\nTake a flick, I look like Meechy, look like Bleu DaVinci\nI treat V Live like it’s 07 in Magic City\n(From “10 Bands”)\n\n\nDrake claims that as such a big platform for artists and such a successful strip club, Magic City should have a business office.\n\nIt is also possible that Drake loves Magic City strip club so much he needs space to work within the establishment, so he doesn’t have to be away from most of his muses as he works on new material.\n\nThere are two options for the “Twenty-nine” reference:\nThe first and the more likely is a refernce to Area 29, a well-known strip club in Houston, Texas. Drake spent 1 million dollars in the club in a single night.\nWith this reference-option selected, Drake’s message is that he needs / keeps some business offices at three well-known strip clubs (Booby Trap on the River, Magic City, 29 Area) in 3 different cities (Miami, Atlanta, Houston).\n\nThe second and the less likely is a refernce to Ward 29, a section in Toronto, Canada. As a child, Drake grew up on Weston Road in Toronto before moving to Forest Hill a few years later. Both locations are located within Ward 29. It was referred on another Drake song – Fair Trade\n\nI’m outside, twenty-nine, G5, seaside\nI’ve been losin' friends and findin' peace\nBut honestly that sounds like a fair trade to me\n(From “Fair Trade”)", "annotation_id": "27088953", "url": "https://genius.com/27088953", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Major Distribution", "line": "Know you’re tired, we just did dinner for three hours Lyin’ to me all night", "vault_lines": ["Lyin' to me all night", "Know you're tired, we just did dinner for three hours"], "meaning": "these 2 lines tie into the following 3 lines which i cannot annotate … but he’s saying that he was out to dinner with a chick who kept lying to him & he keeps Benz in buisness by buying women something cheap in Drake terms (references 100,000 Benz) to simply keep her out of his life\n\nalso ties into the recent leak where he spent 300,000 in a night on a model recently", "annotation_id": "27083648", "url": "https://genius.com/27083648", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Major Distribution", "line": "Cuban girl, her family grind coffee Text me on the signal, don’t call me", "vault_lines": ["Cuban girl, her family grind coffee", "Text me on the signal, don't call me"], "meaning": "Although commonly referred to the network connection that cell phones use to communicate, Drake may be alluding towards utilizing the instant messaging service, Signal– an end-to-end encrypted application where users can send messages, photos and files that are deleted after a set amount of time.\n\n\n\nDrake clearly does not want any of his private relations arising in the public – taking extra precautions with the platform he utilizes to converse with women.", "annotation_id": "27080810", "url": "https://genius.com/27080810", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Major Distribution", "line": "I’m in love with Houston", "vault_lines": ["I'm in love with Houston, Dallas, Austin"], "meaning": "Drizzy has a passionate love affair with Houston, stemming from when he met his mentor Lil Wayne for the first time there on November 18th 2008, which would jump start his career, as he went on to record the majority of his breakout mixtape So Far Gone in Houston. Drake even has a song called “Houstatlantavegas” off So Far Gone to honour H-Town, and has continued to pay homage to the city throughout his career.", "annotation_id": "27069686", "url": "https://genius.com/27069686", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Major Distribution", "line": "Bad Bunny numbers, it’s a robbery Five-hundred million, just for Aubrey", "vault_lines": ["Bad Bunny numbers, it's a robbery", "Five-hundred million, just for Aubrey"], "meaning": "Drake and Bad Bunny collaborated on the track “MÍA” off the latter’s debut album “X 100PRE”\n\nHere he gives him praise, referencing him as one of the best. A praise that is adequate for an artist that has had consistent sold out world tours, is a staple at Billboard charts, and is one of the current top 5 artists world wide with most streams in all services.\n\nIn July, 2022 Drake congratulated him on breaking his own all-time record for biggest streaming year for any artist in Spotify history with over 10.3 billion streams.\n\nMy guy is moving different.\n\nhttps://s.yimg.com/ny/api/res/1.2/z2DllLzzJ6nlZxrJMolHsw--/YXBwaWQ9aGlnaGxhbmRlcjt3PTY0MDtoPTExNzA-/https://media.zenfs.com/en/complex584/797b9843f0e976d4be7c423432b444d8\n\nIn Drink Champ’s controversial interview with Kanye West, he was asked about who his main competition was currently. Although Drake was mentioned, he implored the hosts to guess deeper.\n\n\n[If] you’re going to put an album out, you have to go after the No. 1 artist.\n\nBad Bunny, that’s who’s on our wall. That’s who’s on our wall when we make music. We’re loading up concert footage.\n\n\nEarlier this year, Drake signed a deal with Universal Music Group for $500 Million", "annotation_id": "27059640", "url": "https://genius.com/27059640", "state": "accepted", "votes": 66, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Major Distribution", "line": "Wiggin’ niggas like I played at Kansas", "vault_lines": ["Shoot his feet, got him doin' dances, wiggin' niggas like I played at Kansas"], "meaning": "Refers to Warriors' player Andrew Wiggins, who played college basketball at the University of Kansas", "annotation_id": "27057695", "url": "https://genius.com/27057695", "state": "pending", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Major Distribution", "line": "Paid a hundred, ran up somethin’ light Simple price to keep ’em out my life", "vault_lines": ["Paid a hundred, ran up somethin' light", "Simple price to keep 'em out my life"], "meaning": "Here Drake is saying that a hundred dollars is a cheap price to get rid of someone. He could probably be referring to this scene from the 1993 movie A Bronx Tale.\n\nPROPOSED SUGGESTION: Considering Drake is a multimillionaire, he probably did not mean $100 in the literal sense; More likely $100,000 if anything.", "annotation_id": "27056454", "url": "https://genius.com/27056454", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Major Distribution", "line": "4L shit, know we steppin’, y’all should get to funeral preparin’", "vault_lines": ["4L shit, know we steppin', y'all should get to funeral preparin'"], "meaning": "4L stands for “for life” and means that you’re true to your word. 21 Savage has mentioned it in several songs and has a song titled by the same acronym, “4L.\"", "annotation_id": "27055808", "url": "https://genius.com/27055808", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Major Distribution", "line": "SF90, this is not McLaren, make an IG model run my errands", "vault_lines": ["SF90, this is not McLaren, make an IG model run my errands"], "meaning": "The SF90 Stradale is a supercar made by Ferrari, the luxury sports car manufacturer many deem to be the best. 21 plays this in contrast to McLaren, who also makes supercars, but is known to sometimes have quality control issues like uneven panel gaps, with 21 suggesting his superior status as a rapper driving a Ferrari and not an “inferior” McLaren.", "annotation_id": "27053369", "url": "https://genius.com/27053369", "state": "pending", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Major Distribution", "line": "Fuckin’ on an opp nigga bitch, say she miss the golds in my teeth", "vault_lines": ["Fuckin' on an opp nigga bitch, say she miss the golds in my teeth"], "meaning": "21 used to have gold teeth, now he wearing veneer 75,000$ worth more than gold teeth.\n\nThis implied that girl is dumb to know the real price of something or probably because that girl never yet see the real luxury of someone because 21’s opp is broke nigga.", "annotation_id": "27053368", "url": "https://genius.com/27053368", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Major Distribution", "line": "Buyin’ BM’s Benzes out of spite", "vault_lines": ["Buyin' BM's Benzes out of spite"], "meaning": "One of Drake’s most exclusive Mercedes is the 20 foot V12 Maybach Pullman. It has 6 seats and a full partition to separate the driver and rear passengers.\n\nLess than 500 made.\n\nClick on the twitter thread below for more info! https://twitter.com/ifiwasperfect/status/1108181938400047105?s=20&t=h9U1jbPY3x19o0khN7QgTQ", "annotation_id": "27053348", "url": "https://genius.com/27053348", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Major Distribution", "line": "Hmm, hmm, in this mansion, I’m Macaulay Culkin", "vault_lines": ["Hmm, hmm, in this mansion, I'm Macaulay Culkin"], "meaning": "Macaulay Culkin is the actor who plays Richie Rich in a 1994 film of the same name. The film follows the life of “the world’s richest boy,” whom Drake can certainly relate to being one of the richest rappers of all time.\n\n\n\nDrake could also be referring to Home Alone, a 1990 classic Christmas film where Culkin plays Kevin McCallister.\n\n\n\nDrake would be implying that his reportedly 50,000 square foot mansion is so big that it emphasizes how small he is within it; he feels like a child who is, pun intended, home alone.", "annotation_id": "27052485", "url": "https://genius.com/27052485", "state": "accepted", "votes": 66, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Major Distribution", "line": "Major distribution, labels callin’, Harry Styles numbers, it’s a robbery My niggas go in-Zayn to catch a body, we was face to face, you could’ve shot me", "vault_lines": ["Hmm, hmm, major distribution, labels call me", "Bad Bunny numbers, it's a robbery", "Major distribution, labels callin', Harry Styles numbers, it's a robbery", "My niggas go in-Zayn to catch a body, we was face to face, you could've shot me"], "meaning": "21 compares his success to fellow Brit singer-songwriter Harry Styles. Styles is immensely successful commercially: his May 2017’s self-titled solo debut, his December 2019’s Fine Line, and May 2022’s Harry’s House all debuted at number one on the Billboard 200 chart and broke numerous records.\n\nIn keeping with the One Direction references, 21 plays on “insane” (“in-Zayn”) to describe his zealous shooters. Zayn Malik, known mononymously as ZAYN, is Styles' former bandmate and fellow musician. “INZAYN” is the name of Malik’s official website and the handle of his verified update account.\n\nhttps://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AMLnZu_jO9zq9cBfAVFVXSaOXIt0r5g4FvkDL6piS10r4A=s900-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj\nThe logo of ZAYN’s official update account.", "annotation_id": "27052481", "url": "https://genius.com/27052481", "state": "accepted", "votes": 121, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Major Distribution", "line": "Paid in full, I’m Mekhi Phif’", "vault_lines": ["Paid in full, I'm Mekhi Phif'"], "meaning": "Drake references 2002 crime drama film Paid in Full starring Mekhi Phifer.\n\n\n\nDrake, being worth $250 million, certainly is “paid in full” in the literal sense.", "annotation_id": "27052434", "url": "https://genius.com/27052434", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Major Distribution", "line": "He gon’ miss and we gon’ spin his parents, stayed in Houston long as Steve Francis", "vault_lines": ["He gon' miss and we gon' spin his parents, stayed in Houston long as Steve Francis"], "meaning": "Steve Francis is a former professional basketball player who played six seasons for the Houston Rockets in the NBA. During his time in Houston, he was in the All-Star games three times between 2002 and 2004, and also won Rookie of the Year in 2000.", "annotation_id": "27052101", "url": "https://genius.com/27052101", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
