{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Make Things Right", "line": "Couple of beavers", "vault_lines": ["And see I take a couple of breathers", "Go ahead, I couldn't give two damns like a couple of beavers"], "meaning": "There, Drake seems to make a reference to the fact that he’s from Canada by using the word beaver. That animal is emblematic of the country.", "annotation_id": "25244614", "url": "https://genius.com/25244614", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Make Things Right", "line": "To my dudes at the bar with a freak and Steady lightin’ cigars at the parties they sneak in And look forward to being a star on the weekend Ya’ll part of the speech ’cause", "vault_lines": ["To my dudes at the bar with a freak and", "Steady lightin' cigars at the parties they sneak in", "And look forward to being a star on the weekend", "Ya'll part of the speech 'cause"], "meaning": "Drake talks to the boys at the end of his chorus ‘'Ya’ll part of the speech’‘ because he feels that they are part of this dynamic who traps woman that he describes earlier in the chorus", "annotation_id": "25244606", "url": "https://genius.com/25244606", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
