{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "OVO Sound Radio Episode 56 Tracklist", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-ovo-sound-radio-episode-56-tracklist-lyrics", "genius_title": "OVO Sound Radio Episode 56 Tracklist"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Preach", "line": "I gotta do some reflecting I gotta find me one out here that’s good at taking direction I am convinced that my calls are being recorded So hit my assistant to get me the message And make the connection like, “Brrp!” I’m on that wave tonight, I hope you not the crazy type, yeah I’m in your state tonight, I might just break the bank tonight, yeah", "vault_lines": ["I gotta do some reflecting", "I gotta find me one out here that's good at taking direction", "I am convinced that my calls are being recorded", "So hit my assistant to get me the message", "And make the connection like, \"Brrp!\"", "I'm on that wave tonight, I hope you not the crazy type, yeah", "I'm in your state tonight, I might just break the bank tonight, yeah", "I want you, I'm on you"], "meaning": "This part is about Drake reflecting on what he wants in a relationship while also being cautious about who he trusts. When he says, “I gotta do some reflecting,” he means he needs to think about his choices and relationships, and “I gotta find me one out here that’s good at taking direction” suggests he wants a woman who understands him and is willing to follow his lead. “I am convinced that my calls are being recorded” shows his suspicion that his private conversations may not be secure, so instead of communicating directly, he tells people to contact his assistant to pass along messages and make the connection for him. The “Brrp!” sounds like a phone or communication sound, emphasizing that indirect communication. “I’m on that wave tonight” means he’s feeling himself, enjoying the moment, and caught up in the nightlife or party atmosphere, while “I hope you not the crazy type” shows that he wants the woman to be fun but not bring unnecessary drama. Finally, “I’m in your state tonight, I might just break the bank tonight” means he’s visiting her area and is prepared to spend a lot of money while he’s there, emphasizing his wealth and willingness to go all out for the night.", "annotation_id": "41554749", "url": "https://genius.com/41554749", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Preach", "line": "I get her hot like wasabi She think it’s wavy and gnarly I think I’ma pop one for you Drink one for you", "vault_lines": ["I get her hot like wasabi", "She think it's wavy and gnarly", "I think I'ma pop one for you", "Drink one for you"], "meaning": "This part is using playful comparisons and slang to describe attraction and the vibe between him and the woman. “I get her hot like wasabi” compares the effect he has on her to the strong, spicy heat of wasabi, meaning he gets her excited or attracted to him. “She think it’s wavy and gnarly” means she thinks what he’s doing and the overall vibe are cool, impressive, and exciting. When he says, “I think I’ma pop one for you, drink one for you,” he’s talking about celebrating or having a drink in her honor, showing that he’s enjoying the moment and associating it with her.", "annotation_id": "41554730", "url": "https://genius.com/41554730", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Preach", "line": "Don’t have to guess how I know Oh, it’s a secret? Trust me, I’ll keep it You old niggas boring as bones She put the PARTY tape on You know what’s going on, you know what’s going on", "vault_lines": ["Don't have to guess how I know", "Oh, it's a secret? Trust me, I'll keep it", "You old niggas boring as bones", "She put the PARTY tape on", "You know what's going on, you know what's going on", "I want you, I'm on you"], "meaning": "This section is about confidence, intuition, and two people understanding each other without having to say everything directly. When he says, “Don’t have to guess how I know,” he’s saying he already understands what’s happening and doesn’t need anyone to confirm it. “Oh, it’s a secret? Trust me, I’ll keep it” suggests that someone has told him something private, and he’s reassuring them that he won’t reveal it. “You old niggas boring as bones” is him dismissing older men as boring compared with the younger energy he brings. Then, “She put the PARTY tape on” refers to PARTYNEXTDOOR’s music being played, which creates a particular intimate or seductive atmosphere. When he repeats, “You know what’s going on,” he’s suggesting that both of them understand the meaning behind the situation without needing to explain it out loud.", "annotation_id": "41554726", "url": "https://genius.com/41554726", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Preach", "line": "Young nigga preach Preach, preach, preach, preach, preach, preach Young nigga preach Preach, preach, preach, preach, preach, preach", "vault_lines": ["Preach, preach, preach, preach, preach, preach", "Preach, preach, preach, preach"], "meaning": "“Preach” here is being used in the conversational sense of “tell it like it is” or “I agree with what you’re saying.”", "annotation_id": "41554707", "url": "https://genius.com/41554707", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Preach", "line": "I need a drink and some tequila with you You know what I’m tryna do", "vault_lines": ["I gotta do some reflecting", "I want you, I'm on you", "I need a drink and some tequila with you", "You know what I'm tryna do"], "meaning": "PARTY is honest with the girl, telling her that he just wants to take her home athe end of the night, reinforcing and acting on his words from the previous line. He may possibly want her drunk because she may be more freaky that way.", "annotation_id": "7770308", "url": "https://genius.com/7770308", "state": "verified", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Preach", "line": "You know Jay Wray Got girls here, going way, way, way, way, way, way—", "vault_lines": ["You know what's going on, you know what's going on", "you know Jay Wray", "Got girls here, going way, way, way, way, way, way—"], "meaning": "Continuing with the Jamaican accent, Jay Wray & Nephew Overproof White Rum is a very Strong Rum (63% alc/vol) which is consumed by many Jamaicans and is the White Rum of Choice in Jamaica. It is very potent and gets the girls going crazy!!", "annotation_id": "5037492", "url": "https://genius.com/5037492", "state": "verified", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Preach", "line": "Hey, let’s pop the E off at Liv I’ve got some time here to blow I’ve got the money to blow I’ve got the money and blow", "vault_lines": ["I've got the money to blow", "I've got the money and blow", "Hey, let's pop the E off at Liv", "I've got some time here to blow"], "meaning": "I think the last line is “I’ve got the money to blow, I’ve got the money in blow”, emphasizing he’s got equivalent money in cocaine to pay for the whole trip.", "annotation_id": "5017991", "url": "https://genius.com/5017991", "state": "verified", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
