{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Preach", "line": "You know Jay Wray Got girls here, going way, way, way, way, way, way—", "vault_lines": ["You know what's going on, you know what's going on", "you know Jay Wray", "Got girls here, going way, way, way, way, way, way—"], "meaning": "Preach (Jay Wray) is a member of PND’s crew “OMO.” Jay can get the girls to do anything, indicated by the repetition of “way” – there’s no limit.\n\n\n\nIt’s also a brand of Jamaican Rum.", "annotation_id": "4891696", "url": "https://genius.com/4891696", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Preach", "line": "Doing is one thing; doing it right is a whole different story", "vault_lines": ["Doing is one thing; doing it right is a whole different story"], "meaning": "It’s almost as if Drake set up this line with lines from “Wu Tang Forever.” The lines play with the same idea, and also includes “preach,” the title of this song.\n\nI just gave the city life, it ain’t about who did it first. It’s ‘bout who did it right, niggas looking like “Preach.”", "annotation_id": "4889753", "url": "https://genius.com/4889753", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Preach", "line": "Niggas is all in they feelings these days, all in they feelings these days", "vault_lines": ["Niggas is all in they feelings these days, all in they feelings these days"], "meaning": "Too many litte boys all emotional about the simple things in life.\n\nHere Drake is using the same flow and words as in “Own It”:\n\nNiggas talk more than bitches these days (Just let that shit sink in). Niggas talk more than bitches these days", "annotation_id": "4889280", "url": "https://genius.com/4889280", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Preach", "line": "PND ain’t with the ray-tay,", "vault_lines": ["PND ain't with the ray-tay,"], "meaning": "“Ray tay tay” is Jamaican slang for “gossip”.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/Drake/status/565282564571938816", "annotation_id": "4889185", "url": "https://genius.com/4889185", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Preach", "line": "She keep it wet like tsunami She think she sunk the Titanic", "vault_lines": ["She keep it wet like tsunami", "She think she sunk the Titanic"], "meaning": "PARTY has been spending a lot of time with Oakland-native R&B singer Kehlani. Kehlani’s nickname, which is both her name on Instagram and Twitter, is “Lani Tsunami,” so these lines seem to be a shout out to her. They’ve been featured on each other’s social media, and it’s rumored that the two are dating. PARTY brags about how wet he can get her, to the extent where her saturation level would make her believe she’d caused the Titanic to sink.\n\n\n\nhttps://twitter.com/kehlanimusic/status/566102143644348416", "annotation_id": "4888835", "url": "https://genius.com/4888835", "state": "accepted", "votes": 50, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Preach", "line": "Hey, let’s pop the E off at Liv I’ve got some time here to blow I’ve got the money to blow I’ve got the money and blow", "vault_lines": ["I've got the money to blow", "I've got the money and blow", "Hey, let's pop the E off at Liv", "I've got some time here to blow"], "meaning": "“E” is slang for ecstasy, a popular club drug that PARTY wanna pop in the exclusive Miami based nightclub, LIV. Drake also referenced the nightclub in “305 to My City.”\n\nA play on words – he has time and money to spend (“to blow”), and cocaine (“blow”).", "annotation_id": "4888547", "url": "https://genius.com/4888547", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Preach", "line": "Still in Miami, most of these girls are too messy", "vault_lines": ["Still in Miami, most of these girls are too messy"], "meaning": "Drake may be from Toronto, but he isn’t a stranger out in Miami. He is possibly tired of all the Miami girls because he has slept with too many of them.\n\nMiami is also home to Cash Money Records and Drake’s favorite strip club, King of Diamonds!", "annotation_id": "4888519", "url": "https://genius.com/4888519", "state": "accepted", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Preach", "line": "But hearing a scripture with that many 6's, you should be afraid", "vault_lines": ["But hearing a scripture with that many 6's, you should be afraid", "Boy, you should know that"], "meaning": "If Drake spits a verse on “Preach”, then his album, If You’re Reading This It’s Too Late, must be a scripture.\n\nThroughout the tape, he refers to the 6 (Toronto) many times – so many, in fact, that it’s reminiscent of the notorious number of the beast, 666. If a scripture was filled with this many hints at evil lurking, you would definitely have reason to be afraid.", "annotation_id": "4888371", "url": "https://genius.com/4888371", "state": "accepted", "votes": 139, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Preach", "line": "I’m in Miami, I need to call up Miss Cassidy", "vault_lines": ["I'm in Miami, I need to call up Miss Cassidy"], "meaning": "PARTY stays in Miami often so whenever he lands he has to call a bad ting which is Cassidy Jordan.", "annotation_id": "4888264", "url": "https://genius.com/4888264", "state": "accepted", "votes": 61, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Preach", "line": "My name is PARTY, not “Participation” Sorry for the miscommunication", "vault_lines": ["My name is PARTY, not \"Participation\"", "Sorry for the miscommunication"], "meaning": "PND is here to have fun, not to participate in a possible relationship. He apologizes for the confusion in case any women were lead to believe otherwise.", "annotation_id": "4888028", "url": "https://genius.com/4888028", "state": "accepted", "votes": 65, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Preach", "line": "Sauga-city trip, the payday Glo’d up off a Gateway, man, you can’t afford me", "vault_lines": ["Sauga-city trip, the payday", "Glo'd up off a Gateway, man, you can't afford me"], "meaning": "Sauga City, better known as Mississauga, is a suburb West of Toronto, and is the home and birthplace of PND. They’ll take a trip there once they get paid.\n\nWhen travelling Drake is most likely using his private jet, and sometimes he must do so during night. Therefore glow lights are needed to navigate the plane after he leaves the gate way. Considering his high-end transportation, low time promoters can’t afford to book him for shows.\n\nhttp://tinypic.com/r/s5k7sw/8", "annotation_id": "4887987", "url": "https://genius.com/4887987", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
