{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "9", "line": "I got it right now so I’m everybody’s friend", "vault_lines": ["I got it right now so I'm everybody's friend"], "meaning": "Drake saying “I got it right now” is him alluding to his current fame, success, and wealth within this stage of his life. He follows this up by stating he is now “everybody’s friend” not literally but figuratively. He’s saying that because he is now rich and famous it seems to him that everyone seems supportive and is suddenly a friend of his. However, this support is fake and opportunistic because they only care about him because he’s now successful. Meaning that people are only ever there for you when you’re doing great in life, and only acknowledge what you offer rather than who you are.", "annotation_id": "39791344", "url": "https://genius.com/39791344", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "9", "line": "Tried to kill me but they still want the views Tried to kill me but they still want the views", "vault_lines": ["Tried to kill me but they still want the views", "Tried to kill me but I am very much alive on the six side"], "meaning": "Isn’t this what Rihanna is saying in the unreleased track connecting this with the annotation of the outro?", "annotation_id": "39350176", "url": "https://genius.com/39350176", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
