{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Can’t Take a Joke", "line": "And I’m kitted to the toes If I touch studio then we got one", "vault_lines": ["and I'm kitted to the toes", "If I touch studio then we got one"], "meaning": "In this lyric, Drake is implying either, that he’s ready for a confrontation with his “opps” or ready to drop bars in the studio. The term “kitted” could be a reference to its usage in sports, particularly soccer, where being “kitted out” means to be in the team uniform ready for the game. However, he may also be referencing the term’s military roots, suggesting he’s fully equipped for battle.\n\nThe second part of the bar highlights Drake’s impressive track record of making hit songs. The claim that he makes a hit every time he’s in the studio is somewhat exaggerated but, carries weight. Drake has consistently topped the Billboard charts and earned numerous spots on the Hot 100, cementing his position in the music industry.", "annotation_id": "33257606", "url": "https://genius.com/33257606", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Can’t Take a Joke", "line": "And I’m kitted to the toes If I touch studio then we got one", "vault_lines": ["and I'm kitted to the toes", "If I touch studio then we got one"], "meaning": "In this lyric, Drake is implying either, that he’s ready for a confrontation with his “opps” or ready to drop bars in the studio. The term “kitted” could be a reference to its usage in sports, particularly soccer, where being “kitted out” means to be in the team uniform ready for the game. However, he may also be referencing the term’s military roots, suggesting he’s fully equipped for battle.\n\nThe second part of the bar highlights Drake’s impressive track record of making hit songs. The claim that he makes a hit every time he’s in the studio is somewhat exaggerated but, carries weight. Drake has consistently topped the Billboard charts and earned numerous spots on the Hot 100, cementing his position in the music industry.", "annotation_id": "33257521", "url": "https://genius.com/33257521", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Can’t Take a Joke", "line": "Niggas think they run the town ’Til we run ’em out of town And they gotta relocate Gotta dip from where they stay Everything will be okay", "vault_lines": ["Niggas think they run the town", "'Til we run 'em out of town", "And they gotta relocate", "Gotta dip from where they stay", "Everything will be okay"], "meaning": "With Drakes status and authority in the game, it shouldn’t be a surprise of his mob tie’s capabilities that are most definitely swept under the rug.", "annotation_id": "30899029", "url": "https://genius.com/30899029", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Can’t Take a Joke", "line": "My comment section killin’ me", "vault_lines": ["My comment section killin' me"], "meaning": "This year, Drake has limited accessibility to the comment section on his Instagram. Only those that he follows on Instagram can comment on his posts. In this line, Drake is stating that the hateful comments that some fans were posting before were getting to him.", "annotation_id": "15685886", "url": "https://genius.com/15685886", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Can’t Take a Joke", "line": "I be tryna laugh with the bros ’bout the opps that we know But they can’t take a joke, ’cause it’s not one", "vault_lines": ["I be tryna laugh with the bros 'bout the opps that we know", "But they can't take a joke, 'cause it's not one", "I be tryna laugh with the bros but they can't take a joke", "Then I know they know the deal"], "meaning": "While Drake has overshadowed most of his enemies in terms of both popularity and net worth, his enemies are no slouches themselves. Meek Mill, for example, has broken the Billboard Top 10 with every studio album he’s released. Pusha T is the president of GOOD Music and has a shoe deal with Adidas. Both Drake and his enemies have achieved a level of success unattainable by his closest friends, and because of this, Drake is the only one laughing when he belittles the accomplishments of rivals when he is among friends.", "annotation_id": "14959351", "url": "https://genius.com/14959351", "state": "accepted", "votes": 50, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Can’t Take a Joke", "line": "Skid around ends with the bros", "vault_lines": ["Skid around ends with the bros"], "meaning": "Drake is driving around ends with friends; “ends” either being Jamaican patois for a place at which people are congregating, or the two opposing ends of Toronto, the East End and the West End. Regardless of the specifics, he uses the term to describe being somewhere that he can be seen in public.", "annotation_id": "14959275", "url": "https://genius.com/14959275", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Can’t Take a Joke", "line": "We just right there up the road You could hit it with a stone", "vault_lines": ["We just right there up the road", "You could hit it with a stone"], "meaning": "Drake’s mansion is just 500 feet from West Long Valley Road, a road that begins at the gated entrance of Hidden Hills.", "annotation_id": "14959220", "url": "https://genius.com/14959220", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Can’t Take a Joke", "line": "Give me somethin’ I can feel If they come to Hidden Hills Then I know they know the deal", "vault_lines": ["UberX to Hidden Hills", "Give me somethin' I can feel", "If they come to Hidden Hills", "Then I know they know the deal"], "meaning": "“Something He Can Feel” is a song originally written by Curtis Mayfield for the 1976 film Sparkle that reached #28 on the Billboard Hot 100 after being re-recorded by Aretha Franklin for the film’s soundtrack.\n\nThe song was famously covered by En Vogue for their 1992 album, Funky Divas. While the group paid homage to the original film in the music video, the visuals removed all ambiguity, making clear that the “something he can feel” is sex.", "annotation_id": "14959081", "url": "https://genius.com/14959081", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Can’t Take a Joke", "line": "And I gotta own the things I rap about just for my pride You know when it comes to pride, I can’t put that shit aside", "vault_lines": ["And I gotta own the things I rap about just for my pride", "You know when it comes to pride, I can't put that shit aside"], "meaning": "Drake claims that he has to own the material goods that he boasts about in order to feel pride—on 2014’s “Days In The East,” he also mentions his pride:\n\nGot too much pride for my own good right now\n\nThese lyrics might also be a slight reference to a line in Pusha T’s diss track aimed at Drake, “The Story of Adidon,” where he pledged to focus on Drake’s pride:\n\nDrug dealin' aside, ghostwritin' aside\nLet’s have a heart-to-heart about your pride", "annotation_id": "14887136", "url": "https://genius.com/14887136", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Can’t Take a Joke", "line": "They be throwin’ in the towel I do yellowtail at TAO", "vault_lines": ["They be throwin' in the towel", "I do yellowtail at TAO"], "meaning": "This could be a reference to how the Drake and Pusha T beef died down after Kanye West tweeted how he isn’t about beef –\n\nhttps://twitter.com/kanyewest/status/1002784133888688128\n\nWhen Drake’s haters have given up (“thrown in the towel”), he is celebrating his success by eating the yellowtail fish sashimi on offer at TAO Los Angeles.", "annotation_id": "14882838", "url": "https://genius.com/14882838", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Can’t Take a Joke", "line": "I grew up with the Reps Up boys, we crashin’ it and splashin’ in And when I say they crashin’ it, I do not mean a accident", "vault_lines": ["I grew up with the Reps Up boys, we crashin' it and splashin' in", "And when I say they crashin' it, I do not mean a accident"], "meaning": "Reps Up Entertainment is a Canadian record label that many of Drake’s close friends are associated with. Members include Fif, Preme, OB Obrien, Boi-1da, Chubbs, Niko and more.\n\n“Crashing” and “splashing” are slang terms in the UK meaning “shooting” and “stabbing”.", "annotation_id": "14881605", "url": "https://genius.com/14881605", "state": "accepted", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Can’t Take a Joke", "line": "Ayo, blast that shit, Maxx", "vault_lines": ["Ayo, blast that shit, Maxx", "Blast that shit back if you blastin'"], "meaning": "This is the producer tag for ModMaxx, an up-and-coming producer who describes himself as an “OVO Pro Snowboarder turned Producer.”\n\nThis is his first collaboration with Drake, but he has previously worked on Roy Woods' “Snow White,” and with the artists DRIPXXXX and Tripsixxx.", "annotation_id": "14877376", "url": "https://genius.com/14877376", "state": "accepted", "votes": 78, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Can’t Take a Joke", "line": "UberX to Hidden Hills", "vault_lines": ["UberX to Hidden Hills", "If they come to Hidden Hills"], "meaning": "Uber offers a variety of car services to fit different needs. Drake recommends UberX, the cheapest and most popular of Uber’s private car services.\n\nHidden Hills is a city and gated community in Los Angeles County that borders Calabasas. The average cost of a home in Hidden Hills is $3,233,600, but Drake’s mansion cost him $7.7 million dollars.", "annotation_id": "14876837", "url": "https://genius.com/14876837", "state": "accepted", "votes": 59, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Can’t Take a Joke", "status": "done", "targets": 13, "clicked": 13, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-cant-take-a-joke-lyrics", "genius_title": "Can’t Take a Joke"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Come Thru", "line": "You should call into work if that ain’t too much to ask I could pour you up a drink and we can burn some’", "vault_lines": ["You should call into work if that ain't too much to ask", "I could pour you up a drink and we can burn some'", "I always pour you up a drink and let you burn somethin'"], "meaning": "Here Drizzy asks her to put work aside so they can relax together with a drink and smoke, returning to the comfortable intimacy they once shared back in the good old days, capturing the whole theme of the song.", "annotation_id": "40986524", "url": "https://genius.com/40986524", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Come Thru", "line": "We ain’t spoke in so long, prolly put me in the past I can still get you wet, and I can still make you laugh", "vault_lines": ["We ain't spoke in so long, prolly put me in the past", "I can still get you wet, and I can still make you laugh"], "meaning": "He knows she may have moved on, but he clearly believes their old chemistry and intimacy are still there.", "annotation_id": "40986515", "url": "https://genius.com/40986515", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Come Thru", "line": "Watch me, goin’ out of the way, when I shoulda went home Only time of the day I get to spend on my own I was trippin’ off how I used to sleep at ya crib Should drive by right where you live and pick you up on the way", "vault_lines": ["And nothin' was the same", "Watch me, goin' out of the way, when I shoulda went home", "Only time of the day I get to spend on my own", "I was trippin' off how I used to sleep at ya crib", "Should drive by right where you live and pick you up on the way"], "meaning": "Drake takes a detour instead of going home, using his rare alone time to think about the girl and their past and even confidently considering picking her up from her place.", "annotation_id": "40986484", "url": "https://genius.com/40986484", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Come Thru", "line": "Last album had it boomin’ somethin’ vicious, ya know?", "vault_lines": ["Last album had it boomin' somethin' vicious, ya know?"], "meaning": "Take Care was “booming”", "annotation_id": "40675296", "url": "https://genius.com/40675296", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Come Thru", "line": "Come through, come through, come through, come through Girl you know we got thangs to do Girl you know we got thangs to do So get your ass in that car and come through Know ya got that thang that I like Know ya, know ya got that thang that I like Come through, come through, come through Girl you know we got thangs to do Girl you know we got thangs to do So get your ass in that car and come through", "vault_lines": ["Come through, come through, come through, come through", "Girl you know we got thangs to do", "So get your ass in that car and come through", "Know ya got that thang that I like", "Know ya, know ya got that thang that I like", "Come through, come through, come through", "Girl, ya know ya got that, know ya got that thing that I like"], "meaning": "Drake is a big fan of Aaliyah. This chorus could be interpreted as a response to Aaliyah’s single “Come Over” (which is also sampled in “Fuckin' Problems”) in which she repeats:\n\nCan I come over? (can I)\nCome over? (stop by)\nCome over? (to see you)\nCome over? (tonight?)\n\nDrake replies, telling Shorty to “come thru!”", "annotation_id": "2220353", "url": "https://genius.com/2220353", "state": "accepted", "votes": 109, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Come Thru", "line": "Girl, ya know ya got that, know ya got that thing that I like Girl, you got that thing for real", "vault_lines": ["Know ya got that thang that I like", "Know ya, know ya got that thang that I like", "Girl, ya know ya got that, know ya got that thing that I like", "Girl, you got that thing for real"], "meaning": "Drake is referring to the butt cheeks by referencing the noila clap – the sound and process itself of slapping together ones ass cheeks to make a clapping sound.", "annotation_id": "2216908", "url": "https://genius.com/2216908", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Come Thru", "line": "Someone put a order in for a chicken (For a chicken) Told my girl to order in, I need the kitchen (Need the kitchen) Yeah, they know I got the hookup, they just wait on me to cook up Baby, I heat up the stove, you do the dishes, ya know?", "vault_lines": ["Girl you know we got thangs to do", "Someone put a order in for a chicken (For a chicken)", "Told my girl to order in, I need the kitchen (Need the kitchen)", "Yeah, they know I got the hookup, they just wait on me to cook up", "Baby, I heat up the stove, you do the dishes, ya know?", "And ya know I need ya back in my life", "Girl, ya know ya got that, know ya got that thing that I like"], "meaning": "The kitchen he is referring to is the studio. The chicken refers to a verse, as when someone calls and wants him to drop a verse for their song. The hook up references how all rappers know when Drake gets on a track, it will heat up.\n\nAlso, chicken is slang for a kilo of cocaine. Drizzy is setting us up for a crack / music metaphor.", "annotation_id": "2215400", "url": "https://genius.com/2215400", "state": "accepted", "votes": 64, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Come Thru", "line": "Who you been crying to? Who you been flying to? Whose bed are you sleeping in? Someone’s been hiding you Where have you been?", "vault_lines": ["Who you been crying to? Who you been flying to?", "Whose bed are you sleeping in? Someone's been hiding you", "Where have you been?"], "meaning": "The Marvin’s Room references continue.\n\nDrake wonders as to who his old flame has been seeing and associating herself with. Who’s she waking up and flying to? He knows that she’s found someone as someone’s been hiding her.\n\nHomie couldn’t have said it any better:\n\nI’m just sayin', you could do better.\n\n\n\nAlso refers to Rihanna’s Where Have You Been?", "annotation_id": "2215290", "url": "https://genius.com/2215290", "state": "accepted", "votes": 57, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Come Thru", "line": "We had the type of nights where mornin’ comes too soon And nothin’ was the same", "vault_lines": ["We had the type of nights where mornin' comes too soon", "And nothin' was the same"], "meaning": "Drake references a similar line Janet Jackson says on her “Morning (Intro)” from the 1993 studio album Janet. With this being Drizzy Drake, “morning comes too soon” probably refers to a relationship with a girl, but in the form of a one night stand (catch the sexual innuendo?). Drake wants something more than that, but he can’t act on it before the sun rises and it’s too late. After they have sex, “nothing was the same” with their previous relationship.\n\nDrizzy also makes a sly reference to his own album name, this being the 14th track on it.", "annotation_id": "2214954", "url": "https://genius.com/2214954", "state": "accepted", "votes": 58, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Come Thru", "line": "Yeah, last night I brought DOA to the studio", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, last night I brought DOA to the studio"], "meaning": "Drake is referring to the  Diamond Of Atlanta gentleman’s club. Why go to the strip club when you can bring the strip club to you!\n\n\n\nIf you go to their website, you will hear Drake’s “All Me” playing.", "annotation_id": "2214445", "url": "https://genius.com/2214445", "state": "accepted", "votes": 69, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Come Thru", "line": "Rap game, crack game, ain’t that different, ya know?", "vault_lines": ["Rap game, crack game, ain't that different, ya know?"], "meaning": "Whether it’s music or drugs the product feeds the streets. It comes from a grind, it’s dangerous, and sold to the masses for massive profits. Both can also have negative consequences due to decaying relationships. This line continues the wordplay with a kitchen setting in the previous lines.\n\n\n\nNas expresses a similar idea in “Represent”\n\nSomehow the rap game reminds me of the crack game\n\nAnd that song was again sampled in Jay Z’s joint Rap Game Crack Game.", "annotation_id": "2213339", "url": "https://genius.com/2213339", "state": "accepted", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Come Thru", "status": "done", "targets": 11, "clicked": 11, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-come-thru-lyrics", "genius_title": "Come Thru"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Easy to Please", "line": "Cliqua", "vault_lines": ["I need my moms, my pa, a bottle of cliqua"], "meaning": "Clicquot, as in Veuve Clicquot Chapagne", "annotation_id": "41377532", "url": "https://genius.com/41377532", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Easy to Please", "line": "But the Cottonelle two-ply in your neighbor’s house, I’m on some other shit", "vault_lines": ["But the Cottonelle two-ply in your neighbor's house, I'm on some other shit"], "meaning": "Cottonelle is a toilet paper brand, which is used primarily to remove excess feces and is therefore “on shit.”\n\nDrake rapped a similar line to this on his 2013 single “All Me”:\n\nLook, just understand that I’m on a roll like Cottonelle\nI was made for all of this shit", "annotation_id": "12353704", "url": "https://genius.com/12353704", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Easy to Please", "line": "The whole ATF you know who we are", "vault_lines": ["The whole ATF you know who we are"], "meaning": "ATF stands for “All Things Fresh.” It symbolized the crew that consisted of Drake, Boi-1da, Noah “40” Shebib, Niko, Oliver El-Khatib, Karla, Hush, Jas Prince, T-RexXx, Chubbs, CJ, P Reign, Courtne and more. Over time, ATF became OVO, an acronym for “October’s Very Own,” which Drake branded many of his endeavors around, including his label imprint OVO Sound.", "annotation_id": "9101417", "url": "https://genius.com/9101417", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Easy to Please", "status": "done", "targets": 3, "clicked": 3, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-easy-to-please-lyrics", "genius_title": "Easy to Please"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Get Along Better", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-get-along-better-lyrics", "genius_title": "Get Along Better"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "How Bout Now", "line": "Always felt like my vision been bigger than the bigger picture", "vault_lines": ["Always felt like my vision been bigger than the bigger picture"], "meaning": "Drake realizes that his vision is so large that most people won’t comprehend it. Their vision of what it means to make it is a fraction of his.", "annotation_id": "41369163", "url": "https://genius.com/41369163", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "How Bout Now", "line": "[Chorus] Yeah, you ain’t really fuck with me way back then But how ’bout now? (Now) ’Cause I’m up right now (I’m up right now) And you stuck right now (Stuck right now) Oh, you thought you had it all figured out back then But how ’bout now? (Now) ’Cause I’m up right now (I’m up right now) And you stuck right now, yeah (Stuck right now) You thought the little effort that you put in was enough, girl How ’bout now? Yeah Girl, how ’bout now, how ’bout now, girl? What about now, girl, how ’bout now?", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, you ain't really fuck with me way back then", "But how 'bout now? (Now)", "'Cause I'm up right now (I'm up right now)", "And you stuck right now (Stuck right now)", "Oh, you thought you had it all figured out back then", "And you stuck right now, yeah (Stuck right now)", "You thought the little effort that you put in was enough, girl", "How 'bout now? Yeah", "Girl, how 'bout now, how 'bout now, girl?", "What about now, girl, how 'bout now?", "Girl, how 'bout now? (Now)"], "meaning": "Echoing the sentiments of Drake’s 2013 hit single, Started from the Bottom, Drake here details a conversation between him and a girl, perhaps an ex-girlfriend.\n\nWhile some people didn’t believe in him back when he was still broke and wasn’t famous or ‘'didn’t fuck with’‘ him, he’s now a mega-star, with number 1 hit and multi-platinum albums as well as millions of dollars to boast.\n\nHe then repeats the question. “How ‘bout now’‘, to really ask those who back stabbed him, how they feel now.", "annotation_id": "35824498", "url": "https://genius.com/35824498", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "How Bout Now", "line": "Crazy how you gotta wait until it’s dark out to see who really with you", "vault_lines": ["Crazy how you gotta wait until it's dark out to see who really with you"], "meaning": "Drake believes that he can only know who his real friends are during hard times. He touched on this before on February 2013’s, “Started From The Bottom”:\n\nNo new niggas, nigga, we don’t feel that\nFuck a fake friend, where your real friends at?", "annotation_id": "4211210", "url": "https://genius.com/4211210", "state": "accepted", "votes": 115, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "How Bout Now", "line": "Them car rides made me feel like I was losin’ it Yeah, made me feel I ain’t have it like that Or I was average like that", "vault_lines": ["Them car rides made me feel like I was losin' it", "Yeah, made me feel I ain't have it like that", "Or I was average like that"], "meaning": "Drake shared a similar sentiment on his November 2011 track, “Under Ground Kings”:\n\nWith fame on my mind, my girl on my nerves\nI was pushing myself to get something that I deserve\nThat was back in the days, Acura days", "annotation_id": "4211150", "url": "https://genius.com/4211150", "state": "accepted", "votes": 53, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "How Bout Now", "line": "I had no money left from actin’, I was focused on the music", "vault_lines": ["I had no money left from actin', I was focused on the music"], "meaning": "Before Drake was a superstar, he played Jimmy Brooks from 2001 to 2009 in the Canadian teen-drama series, Degrassi: The Next Generation.\n\n\n\nDrake spit a similar bar on his November 2011 track, “Look What You’ve Done”:\n\nTold you I think I’m done acting, I’m more in touch with the music", "annotation_id": "4211043", "url": "https://genius.com/4211043", "state": "accepted", "votes": 75, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "How Bout Now", "line": "I used to always try and burn you CDs of my new shit You be like “who’s this?” I be like “me, girl” You be like “oh, word, true shit?” Then ask if we could listen to Ludacris", "vault_lines": ["My heart belongs to you...", "I used to always try and burn you CDs of my new shit", "You be like \"who's this?\" I be like \"me, girl\"", "You be like \"oh, word, true shit?\"", "Then ask if we could listen to Ludacris"], "meaning": "This could be a shot at Kandice Henry, Drake’s ex-girlfriend who was rumored to have dated Ludacris before Drizzy. Luda confirmed this in a 2015 Breakfast Club interview.\n\nhttp://instagram.com/p/pupjNPDQFa/\n\nDrake and Luda had a short-lived beef in 2011, when Drake called him out in an interview, which led to Luda releasing a diss track. An August 2013 Complex article suggests that Drake may have dismissed it with a line from November 2011’s “Over My Dead Body”.\n\nDrake ended his beef with Ludacris at the 2017 Billboard Music Awards.\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/BUYFe0OloEl/embed/", "annotation_id": "4211029", "url": "https://genius.com/4211029", "state": "accepted", "votes": 72, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "How Bout Now", "line": "My heart belongs to you...", "vault_lines": ["My heart belongs to you...", "I used to always try and burn you CDs of my new shit"], "meaning": "Here, Boi-1da samples Jodeci’s December 1993 smash hit, “My Heart Belongs To U.”\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Qh5h2hYMjbo\n\nDrake is a big fan of Jodeci. He even titled his June 2013 track, “Jodeci Freestyle” in their honor.", "annotation_id": "4211021", "url": "https://genius.com/4211021", "state": "accepted", "votes": 125, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "How Bout Now", "line": "That’s the shit I’m talking ‘bout though, like you changed up, you don’t even fuckin’ link nobody no more, you just dash me away like a cyattie. Yo, you cheesed me dog", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake used a voicemail from a woman before on his June 2011 song, “Marvin’s Room,” except this time Drake has ghosted the woman.\n\nThe woman uses a mix of Jamaican patois and Toronto slang. “Link” means to contact or get in touch with someone, “dash away” means to not care or respond, “cyattie” means a “rachet” female and “cheesed me” means to make someone mad.", "annotation_id": "4210920", "url": "https://genius.com/4210920", "state": "accepted", "votes": 352, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "How Bout Now", "line": "I bought your dad a bunch of shit for Christmas He ain’t even say thank you", "vault_lines": ["I bought your dad a bunch of shit for Christmas", "He ain't even say thank you"], "meaning": "Drake’s mother is Jewish, and Drake has fully embraced his Jewish heritage, as made evident in the April 2012 music video for “HYFR,” where he was “re-bar mitzvah’d as a re-commitment to the Jewish religion.”\n\n\n\nDrake going out of his way to buy his girl’s father a present for Christmas, a holiday he doesn’t even celebrate, and go to church, shows how much he cares.", "annotation_id": "4210892", "url": "https://genius.com/4210892", "state": "accepted", "votes": 101, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
