{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Real Bad Karma", "line": "Condo in Miami, sold that shit to Chalmers", "vault_lines": ["Condo in Miami, sold that shit to Chalmers"], "meaning": "Mario Chalmers is a professional basketball player that played in the NBA for ten seasons, winning multiple championships with the Miami Heat.\n\nDrake owned a condo on Biscayne National Park in Miami, but sold the real estate to Chalmers in 2012. Chalmers ended up selling the home to another owner in February of 2018.\n\nDrake has rapped about the condo before, as seen on his 2011 track “The Motto”:\n\nWrist bling, got a condo up in Biscayne\n\nIt was also the setting for the music video for DJ Khaled’s track “I’m On One,” which Drake was featured on.", "annotation_id": "18365279", "url": "https://genius.com/18365279", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Real Bad Karma", "line": "Hot boy, I feel like Dwayne Michael Carter", "vault_lines": ["Hot boy, I feel like Dwayne Michael Carter"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne, born Dwayne Michael Carter Jr., is a famous rapper from Hollygrove, New Orleans, who started his career as a member of the hip hop group Hot Boys.\n\nWhile Tiller and Wayne have yet to collaborate, the two have an interesting history. Tiller likened himself to the rap legend on his October 2015 track, “Ten Nine Fourteen”:\n\nUh, I feel like Weezy F Baby sometimes man\nCarter 3 Wayne, Carter 4 Wayne\nCarter 5, man where that shit at?\nYessir\n\nDuring his famous mixtape run in the 2010’s Wayne also freestyled over two famous Tilller tracks: November 2015’s “I’m Nice” used Tiller’s “Don’t” beat and January 2018’s “Light Years” used Tiller’s “Set It Off” beat.", "annotation_id": "18361784", "url": "https://genius.com/18361784", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Real Bad Karma", "status": "done", "targets": 2, "clicked": 2, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-real-bad-karma-lyrics", "genius_title": "Real Bad Karma"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Shot for Me", "line": "And the voice in your speaker right now, that’s me", "vault_lines": ["And the voice in your speaker right now, that's me", "And the voice in your ear, that's me"], "meaning": "the line implies that he’s gotten so big that his ex is now just a listener hearing his music instead of being part of his life like how she once was. it shows his success and how his voice is all over the world now. like “that song on the radio? that’s me mf”", "annotation_id": "39254376", "url": "https://genius.com/39254376", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Shot for Me", "line": "Okay, look, I’m honest, girl, I can’t lie, I miss you", "vault_lines": ["Okay, look, I'm honest, girl, I can't lie, I miss you"], "meaning": "t", "annotation_id": "32824138", "url": "https://genius.com/32824138", "state": "pending", "votes": -19, "second_sense": false, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Shot for Me", "line": "I can see it in your eyes, you’re angry Regret got shit on what you’re feelin’ now Mad ’cause he ain’t like me Oh, you mad ’cause nobody ever did it like me", "vault_lines": ["I can see it in your eyes, you're angry", "Regret got shit on what you're feelin' now", "Mad 'cause he ain't like me", "Oh, you mad 'cause nobody ever did it like me"], "meaning": "In these lyrics, Drake seems to be addressing someone who appears upset or angry. He suggests that the person’s current feelings surpass any regret they might have had before. Drake implies that the individual might be upset because the person they’re involved with isn’t like him and that they’re frustrated because nobody else has been able to match his actions or character. Essentially, he’s highlighting a sense of uniqueness or superiority in his own actions or personality compared to someone else in the individual’s life.", "annotation_id": "30339624", "url": "https://genius.com/30339624", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Shot for Me", "line": "This is one I know you hated when you heard it", "vault_lines": ["This is one I know you hated when you heard it"], "meaning": "Drake is acknowledging that he is aware that his ex-partner won’t like this song he wrote about her.", "annotation_id": "30034950", "url": "https://genius.com/30034950", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Shot for Me", "line": "And it’s worse because you know that I deserve it", "vault_lines": ["And it's worse because you know that I deserve it"], "meaning": "This line adds a layer of self-awareness, as Drake implies that the negative reaction his ex will have to this song is justified because he recognizes that he deserves the criticism or disapproval for whatever he expressed in the song. It reflects an understanding of the potential impact of his words on the person he’s addressing.", "annotation_id": "30034941", "url": "https://genius.com/30034941", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Shot for Me", "line": "Prayin’ for your happiness, hope that you recover, uh", "vault_lines": ["Prayin' for your happiness, hope that you recover, uh"], "meaning": "Drake expresses empathy and conveys a genuine desire for his ex’s well-being and recovery, hoping that they find happiness again.", "annotation_id": "30034904", "url": "https://genius.com/30034904", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Shot for Me", "line": "She says, ”I know you changed I never see you ‘cause you’re always busy doin’ things” I really wish she had a different way of viewin’ things", "vault_lines": ["She says, \"I know you changed", "I never see you 'cause you're always busy doin' things\"", "I really wish she had a different way of viewin' things"], "meaning": "Drake is expressing the challenges of balancing his music career with personal relationships. He acknowledges that his ex who saw his busy schedule as a lack of care or attention assumed that he changed, likely due to his increasingly demanding schedule.\n\nDrake wishes that his ex would understand and appreciate the dedication and hard work that go into his music career.", "annotation_id": "30034812", "url": "https://genius.com/30034812", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Shot for Me", "line": "And you’re wasted with your latest Yeah, I’m the reason why you always gettin’ faded", "vault_lines": ["And you're wasted with your latest", "Yeah, I'm the reason why you always gettin' faded"], "meaning": "Drake believes he is the cause of his ex’s current state of being “wasted” or constantly getting intoxicated. The word “faded” is often used to describe being under the influence of drugs or alcohol. The lyrics imply that the Drake’s influence or actions may have contributed his past lover’s choices and behavior, leading to a pattern of getting intoxicated.", "annotation_id": "30034761", "url": "https://genius.com/30034761", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Shot for Me", "line": "The way you walk, that’s me The way you talk, that’s me The way you got your hair up, did you forget that’s me?", "vault_lines": ["The way you walk, that's me", "The way you talk, that's me", "The way you got your hair up, did you forget that's me?"], "meaning": "Drake believes he played a significant role in influencing his ex’s mannerisms and style. He’s claiming credit for the way she walks, talks and even styles her hair, implying that these aspects of her identity were shaped or influenced by their past relationship.", "annotation_id": "30034753", "url": "https://genius.com/30034753", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Shot for Me", "line": "And the voice in your ear, that’s me", "vault_lines": ["And the voice in your speaker right now, that's me", "And the voice in your ear, that's me"], "meaning": "He’s making this song for all of his Ex’s. This line is almost like breaking the fourth wall but for music. He is directly speaking to his failed relationships who are listening to his music letting them know that its his voice in their speakers and that he made it big time and that they messed up by letting him go.", "annotation_id": "28316597", "url": "https://genius.com/28316597", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
