{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Shot for Me", "line": "I think the city that we’re from just kinda ruined things It’s such a small place, not much to do but talk and listen The men are jealous and the women all in competition", "vault_lines": ["I think the city that we're from just kinda ruined things", "It's such a small place, not much to do but talk and listen", "The men are jealous and the women all in competition"], "meaning": "Drake is saying that despite it being a metropolitan city, Toronto is ultimately a “small town” and gossip gets around quickly.", "annotation_id": "24416502", "url": "https://genius.com/24416502", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Shot for Me", "line": "Take a shot for me (Oh-oh-oh-oh, oh-oh-oh-oh) Take a shot for me (Oh-oh-oh-oh, oh-oh-oh-oh) Take a shot for me (Oh-oh, oh-oh, oh-oh, oh-oh, oh-oh, oh-oh) A shot for me (Oh-oh, oh-oh, oh-oh, oh-oh, oh-oh, oh-oh) A shot for me", "vault_lines": ["Take a shot for me (Oh-oh-oh-oh, oh-oh-oh-oh)", "A shot for me (Oh-oh, oh-oh, oh-oh, oh-oh, oh-oh, oh-oh)"], "meaning": "People usually tend to try and drink themselves out of their problems and depression. Through this hook, Drake is jokingly telling his ex to take a shot in memory of him and the love that could have been.\n\n\n\nThis hook plays on another meaning behind a different meaning to “taking a shot” for somebody. Taking a bullet for somebody, risking your own life, is a very selfless, reckless form of displaying immense love toward a partner.", "annotation_id": "590862", "url": "https://genius.com/590862", "state": "accepted", "votes": 196, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Shot for Me", "line": "You and the music were the only things that I’d commit to I never cheated, for the record, back when I was with you But you believed in everything but me, girl, I don’t get you", "vault_lines": ["You and the music were the only things that I'd commit to", "I never cheated, for the record, back when I was with you", "But you believed in everything but me, girl, I don't get you"], "meaning": "These lines are most likely in response to an interview in which one of his exes that he mentioned before, Catya.\n\n“I was in love.  He was in love. I’m talkin’ family dinners, we in Whole Foods pushing the cart around, it was a regular relationship.  But he started getting a little bit too loose.  He pops up in tabloids…with Malia.  Trips to Jamaica that I wasn’t invited to and never heard about.  I’m from South Philly you know we don’t go for that.  That was my DUDE, not somebody I was just kickin’ it with.” ~ Catya Washington\n\nShe basically said that Drake cheated on her with Maliah Michel which was one of the reasons that lead to their breakup and Drake is most likely clearing the air.", "annotation_id": "439062", "url": "https://genius.com/439062", "state": "pending", "votes": 114, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Shot for Me", "line": "May your neighbors respect you Trouble neglect you Angels protect you And Heaven accept you", "vault_lines": ["May your neighbors respect you", "And Heaven accept you"], "meaning": "This is an old Irish toast, to tie in to the “take a shot” theme of the tune.\n\nIt’s also a very similar lyric to Terry Callier’s song Turn You To Love where we hear him sing:\n\nMay trouble neglect you, and sunlight reflect you, may heaven protect you and turn you to love", "annotation_id": "436517", "url": "https://genius.com/436517", "state": "accepted", "votes": 233, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Shot for Me", "line": "Alisha, Catya, I know that you gon’ hear this", "vault_lines": ["Alisha, Catya, I know that you gon' hear this"], "meaning": "Alisha is Drake’s ex, mentioned in “Successful”, who he tried to marry.\n\n\n\nCatya Washington (a.k.a. Ms. Cat) is also Drake’s ex. She was featured in the “Best I Ever Had” video and was a cast member of the reality show Bad Girls Club.", "annotation_id": "434983", "url": "https://genius.com/434983", "state": "accepted", "votes": 142, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
