{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Crew Love", "line": "There’s a room full of niggas What you following me for?", "vault_lines": ["What you bothering me for?", "There's a room full of niggas", "What you following me for?"], "meaning": "The Weeknd is talking to this girl about there being more other men in the room for her to go after but she goes after him.", "annotation_id": "28662642", "url": "https://genius.com/28662642", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Crew Love", "line": "Yeah Smokin’ weed under star projectors", "vault_lines": ["Smokin' weed under star projectors"], "meaning": "“Star projectors” likely refers to the Starlight Headliner feature on certain Rolls-Royce models. Drake is a fan of the British car manufacturer, having bought a custom Rolls Bushukan for $700,000.", "annotation_id": "19336664", "url": "https://genius.com/19336664", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Crew Love", "line": "There’s times where I might blow like 50K on a vacation For all my soldiers, just to see the looks on all they faces All it took was patience", "vault_lines": ["There's times where I might do it just to do it like it's nothing", "There's times where I might blow like 50K on a vacation", "For all my soldiers, just to see the looks on all they faces", "All it took was patience"], "meaning": "Drake is very generous with his money and is never hesitant to buy things for himself and his posse. His enjoyment comes from seeing the people he cares about happy, and he won’t\n\nLil Wayne has mentioned Drake’s generosity before, including on the outro of the track, “Sick”, where he said:\n\nCraziest shit Drake ever bought me as a gift was um probably some, some jewelry or something like Drake buy real extravagant gifts like so, I don’t, you know, forgive me for saying I don’t remember but it’s like the gift be so extravagant meaning like I probably use it every day so when you use something everyday you totally forget who got that shit for you,I ’m sorry you just do. and so he get you those type of gifts when I say extravagant I mean like uh the house I probably live in was probably bought by Drake you know what I mean shit like that.", "annotation_id": "15422132", "url": "https://genius.com/15422132", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Crew Love", "line": "I guess we’ll never know where Harvard gets us But seein’ my family have it all Took the place of that desire for diplomas on the wall", "vault_lines": ["I guess we'll never know where Harvard gets us", "But seein' my family have it all", "Took the place of that desire for diplomas on the wall", "All it took was patience"], "meaning": "Drake dropped out of high school after receiving a starring role at the TV show Degrassi.\n\nThe average Harvard graduate receives a respectable $140,000 annual salary. Although Drake never had the chance to go to one of the best colleges in the US, he has no reason to be regretful. In 2012 alone, he earned over $42,000,000 from his Club Paradise Tour, far exceeding the amount the average Harvard graduate would receive.\n\nDespite this, he does care about his “diplomas on the wall” to a certain extent. In 2012, Drake boasted on Twitter about finally passing high school, nearly 10 years after he dropped out.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/Drake/status/258731694687920130", "annotation_id": "13082075", "url": "https://genius.com/13082075", "state": "accepted", "votes": 56, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Crew Love", "line": "That OVO and that XO is everything you believe in, I know", "vault_lines": ["That OVO and that XO is everything you believe in, I know"], "meaning": "OVO, an abbreviation for October’s Very Own, is the name of Drake’s label, while XO is the name of The Weeknd’s crew and label, registered under Republic Records.\n\n\n\nThe Weeknd later tweeted that his fans should believe in XO just like they would a religion, echoing Drake’s line:\n\nhttps://twitter.com/theweeknd/status/215962242817064960?lang=en\n\nKendrick Lamar also brought up the combination of the crews on Drake’s “Buried Alive (Interlude)”:\n\nSo blame it on Mr. OVOXO\"", "annotation_id": "12209517", "url": "https://genius.com/12209517", "state": "accepted", "votes": 65, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Crew Love", "line": "Twenty, keep the bar rollin’ Fake IDs in the trash, we goin’ Straight to the top, rooftop glows With a handful of girls and they all so foreign", "vault_lines": ["Twenty, keep the bar rollin'", "Fake IDs in the trash, we goin'", "Straight to the top, rooftop glows", "With a handful of girls and they all so foreign"], "meaning": "Abel paints a picture of what it’s like being a 20 year old crooner on the come up in Toronto.\n\n“We going straight to the top” isn’t just referencing the fact that he went from being homeless to having access to rooftop parties, but also that he’s on his way to the top of the game.", "annotation_id": "12209449", "url": "https://genius.com/12209449", "state": "accepted", "votes": 61, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Crew Love", "line": "It’s ’cause we blowing like a C4 Got my whole crew blowin’ like a C4", "vault_lines": ["It's 'cause we blowing like a C4", "Got my whole crew blowin' like a C4", "'Cause we blowin' like a C4"], "meaning": "Blowing up is a term meaning a substantial, sudden burst in popularity, usually the result of an unprecedented contribution to the music industry. The Weeknd’s music is unlike any other, and he, Drake, and the rest of OVOXO are blowing up as a result.\n\nBut, judging from Abel’s other music, and the opening line of this song, he could very well be using “blow” to refer to cocaine.\n\nC4 is a type of plastic explosive.", "annotation_id": "689806", "url": "https://genius.com/689806", "state": "accepted", "votes": 89, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Crew Love", "line": "[Verse 1: The Weeknd]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This song was originally created as The Weeknd’s, but after Drake heard it, he asked if he could rap on it and throw it on Take Care.\n\nThe original cut that The Weeknd released in early 2013 can be found here.", "annotation_id": "549644", "url": "https://genius.com/549644", "state": "accepted", "votes": 98, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Crew Love", "line": "Take your nose off my keyboard What you bothering me for?", "vault_lines": ["Take your nose off my keyboard", "What you bothering me for?", "What you following me for?"], "meaning": "There are a few different meanings this could have:\n\nAs much as Abel loves drugs, he still finds it annoying when the ladies are doing lines off his piano.\n\nAlso a play on words as pianos have “white keys”.\n\n\n\nAlso, he finds it annoying when groupies follow him around or peer over his shoulder possibly when he’s texting or on the phone.", "annotation_id": "549643", "url": "https://genius.com/549643", "state": "accepted", "votes": 158, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Crew Love", "line": "The realest niggas say, “Your lyrics do shit for me”", "vault_lines": ["The realest niggas say, \"Your lyrics do shit for me\""], "meaning": "His lyrics have touched some of the people he considers “the realest niggas”.\n\nDrake received some criticism for his lyrics initially, as they lacked any real substance niggas in the hood and in the streets could relate to (i.e., no drug dealing escapades, gang bangin', and/or braggin' bout how much money he got), so while Drake stuck to his style and got ridiculed for his street credibility, he eventually received acclaim for “his story.”", "annotation_id": "478949", "url": "https://genius.com/478949", "state": "accepted", "votes": 48, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Crew Love", "line": "This ain’t no fuckin’ sing-along So, girl, what you singin’ for?", "vault_lines": ["What you bothering me for?", "What you following me for?", "This ain't no fuckin' sing-along", "So, girl, what you singin' for?"], "meaning": "He’s referring to girls singing around him thinking they will get their big break if he hears their voice. Hence the “because we’re blowing like a C4.” The girls are trying to ride them – no pun intended – to the top..\n\nThis might be about the Mod Club show that ended up a live release. Over all the songs, you just hear girls singing and telling him they love him. He’s saying that it’s a concert, not some chance to profess your love and get your voice on the live recording. Just listen to The Weeknd Live @ Mod Club.", "annotation_id": "439347", "url": "https://genius.com/439347", "state": "accepted", "votes": 109, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Crew Love", "line": "Light-skinned chick, first flight from Poland A whole lotta friends, first flight from Poland A whole lotta cash comin’ straight from Poland", "vault_lines": ["Light-skinned chick, first flight from Poland", "A whole lotta friends, first flight from Poland", "A whole lotta cash comin' straight from Poland"], "meaning": "They like the Polish girls fresh off the boat, ‘cuz Polish girls like to party!\n\n\n\nForeign girls are not familiar with The Weeknd’s lifestyle (getting high etc.) He talks about it in “Thursday” many times. Toronto, The Weeknd’s hometown, is home to a large Polish diaspora. He’s probably had a lot of experience running into Polish girls at clubs.\n\nAlso, he is speaking of an off-shore bank account in the line “A whole lot of cash coming straight from Poland” implying that he’s involved in moving drugs.", "annotation_id": "436025", "url": "https://genius.com/436025", "state": "accepted", "votes": 155, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Crew Love", "line": "Brain so poisoned, rainbows flowin’", "vault_lines": ["Brain so poisoned, rainbows flowin'"], "meaning": "What they’re drinking is “poisoned” with the codiene, promethazine, and soda mixture known as purple drank, and the drink poisons their minds, as all alcohol does–rainbows are flowing because the drink may be making them hallucinate.\n\n\n\nRainbows flowing may allude to the colorful nature of Canadian money; popular phrases up north include “catch those rainbows”, “all I see is the rainbow”, or “working for that rainbow flow”.", "annotation_id": "435123", "url": "https://genius.com/435123", "state": "accepted", "votes": 54, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Crew Love", "line": "I told my story and made history", "vault_lines": ["I told my story and made history"], "meaning": "Drake started telling his life story, then became a world-famous rapper selling out arenas. That, in turn, made ‘history’, because he’s such a huge performer and ‘his story’ because he changed the lives (stories) of his crew members as well.  This line is, as we pointed out, the first real groaner of the record.\n\n\n\nDrake’s experiences are the basis of imitation by other rappers, i.e., he made it cool to be vulnerable/introspective.\n\nAlso,  Drake is referring to the “realest nigga” in the previous line saying that Drake’s own story was so relatable to the “realest niggas” story that it also made it “HIS-STORY.”\n\nUsed in the same way that Michael Jackson did for his album, HIStory. His story as in Drake’s story, and history as stuff for the record books.", "annotation_id": "435053", "url": "https://genius.com/435053", "state": "accepted", "votes": 104, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
