{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "High Fives", "line": "Two, let your pussy talk, I’ma do the ad-libs", "vault_lines": ["Two, let your pussy talk, I'ma do the ad-libs"], "meaning": "WHAT could possibly be the adlibs for the talk of a pussy????", "annotation_id": "40300467", "url": "https://genius.com/40300467", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "High Fives", "line": "Oumy say I’m up and I could never take a loss", "vault_lines": ["Oumy say I'm up and I could never take a loss"], "meaning": "The correct word is “ummi” (أمي), the Arabic word for “mother,” not “oumy.” This is the second time Drake uses Arabic on the track, the first being “mashallah.”\n\nDrake has referenced his mother throughout his career, even sampling her voice on several songs. Here, he’s saying that regardless of how people viewed the beef, his mother would never see him as having lost. In her eyes, he’s still a winner, and she’s sure to remind him of that.", "annotation_id": "40205796", "url": "https://genius.com/40205796", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "High Fives", "line": "I said, “I’m so loved and I’m so hated, so conflicted, I’m so jaded”", "vault_lines": ["I said, I'm so loved and I'm so hated, so conflicted, I'm so jadеd", "I said, \"I'm so loved and I'm so hated, so conflicted, I'm so jaded\""], "meaning": "Possible nod to Drake’s 2018 song ‘Jaded’ on scorpion, which presents a similar theme to this line.", "annotation_id": "40122762", "url": "https://genius.com/40122762", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "High Fives", "line": "High tide, make it flow for me, girl, there’s no sense in rushing", "vault_lines": ["High tide, make it flow for me, girl, there's no sense in rushing"], "meaning": "High Tide is a brand of Cannabis.  When he has smoked he’s chill and there is no need to rush into things because time is moving slowly.", "annotation_id": "40003400", "url": "https://genius.com/40003400", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "High Fives", "line": "What a ripper for the gang", "vault_lines": ["What a ripper for the gang"], "meaning": "Pretty sure it’s “what a ripper for the gang\". Slang used by hockey players or Canadiens a lot.", "annotation_id": "39969432", "url": "https://genius.com/39969432", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "High Fives", "line": "High fives from the bros for me ’cause I fucked her for nothing", "vault_lines": ["High fives from the bros for me 'cause I fucked her for nothing"], "meaning": "Drake is pointing out that his friends are congratulating him because, unlike his usual relationships where money, gifts, or luxury are involved, this time he slept with a woman without spending anything on her. The line plays into the idea of status and validation among his circle, where getting someone “for free” is seen as an accomplishment.", "annotation_id": "39969138", "url": "https://genius.com/39969138", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "High Fives", "line": "Come back to the crib, first night, baby, nobody’s judging", "vault_lines": ["Come back to the crib, first night, baby, nobody's judging"], "meaning": "Facts", "annotation_id": "39930882", "url": "https://genius.com/39930882", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": false, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "High Fives", "line": "If I ask her nice, she’ll put my Genny in her croc’ Double-S so bad, she look like Jenny from the Block", "vault_lines": ["If I ask her nice, she'll put my Genny in her croc'", "Double-S so bad, she look like Jenny from the Block", "If I ask tonight, she'll put my Jenny in her croc'"], "meaning": "In this verse, Drake compares “Double-S” to Jennifer Lopez, referencing her 2002 hit Jenny from the Block.\n\nBeyond the obvious aesthetic compliment, the slash hides a detail: Drake had a brief but highly rumored relationship with J.Lo between late 2016 and early 2017. Lopez herself later jokingly dissed him during a performance in Las Vegas in 2019, calling it just “a passing fling.”", "annotation_id": "39907141", "url": "https://genius.com/39907141", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "High Fives", "line": "Down on her knees, tryna reason with me Gotta bless her with something", "vault_lines": ["Down on her knees, tryna reason with me", "Gotta bless her with something"], "meaning": "Down on knees implying oral but also a play on praying on one’s knees. Down on knees in prayer = blessing. Down on knees performing sexual acts = blessing from male genitalia.", "annotation_id": "39869256", "url": "https://genius.com/39869256", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
