{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "RAINING IN HOUSTON", "line": "Hookah", "vault_lines": ["All these tables, booths, you want hookah"], "meaning": "Hookah or Shisha is an Indian instrument used to smoke tobacco by passing air heated by charcoal over flavorful, moist tobacco, causing it to produce smoke. The smoke then travels down a stem into a water-filled vase, where it is cooled and filtered before being inhaled by the user through a mouthpiece.", "annotation_id": "36945456", "url": "https://genius.com/36945456", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "RAINING IN HOUSTON", "line": "The hate from this year alone is confusing, my love I can’t see things getting much smoother, my love", "vault_lines": ["The hate from this year alone is confusing, my love", "I can't see things getting much smoother, my love"], "meaning": "Drake mentions that he’s been confused by the extra hate he’s received in the last year, likely due to his public feud with Kendrick Lamar.\n\nMany of Drake’s closest friends & artists he’s worked with turned their back against Drake. He might be confused because allegations of being a pedophile in Kendrick Lamar’s, “Not Like Us” diss track, have not been proved.\n\nDrake mentions the hate he’s received and friends he’s lost in his single, “No Face,” where he says:\n\nI’m just so happy that n-s who envied\nand held that shit in got to finally show it", "annotation_id": "35371357", "url": "https://genius.com/35371357", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "RAINING IN HOUSTON", "line": "Gassing you up, these American guys Are something different, they just talk looser than us You say I talk proper, it suits me, my love", "vault_lines": ["Gassing you up, these American guys", "Are something different, they just talk looser than us", "You say I talk proper, it suits me, my love", "I know you always say it's just music, my love"], "meaning": "Drake separates himself from “american guys”, proud of his canadian heritage. He says that the Americans “talk looser”, and that he talks proper.\n\nHe’s proud of the fact that he gives off a more polished persona than his american counterparts, and has progressed (since his feud with Kendrick Lamar) to blankly acknowledging the fact that he isn’t American.\n\n‘looser’ and ‘loser’ are homonyms, and this, paired with the talk about Americans talking loose might be taken as a subtle jab at Kendrick, but don’t take my word for that.", "annotation_id": "35315792", "url": "https://genius.com/35315792", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "RAINING IN HOUSTON", "line": "Textin’ me, “Don’t bother comin’ home,” as if the crib ain’t mine", "vault_lines": ["Textin' me, \"Don't bother comin' home,\" as if the crib ain't mine"], "meaning": "Drake is very wealthy and thus does not have to share a home with his woman, preferring to have her live at his crib. When she texts him “don’t bother coming home”, he finds it funny as the house is his, giving her no right to tell him not to come", "annotation_id": "35315716", "url": "https://genius.com/35315716", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "RAINING IN HOUSTON", "line": "All this time you’ve been around me You don’t spend a penny ’round me Friends are extra friendly ’round me", "vault_lines": ["All this time you've been around me", "You don't spend a penny 'round me", "Friends are extra friendly 'round me"], "meaning": "Drake doesn’t want to keep arguing with this girl, here he reminds her that she is the girl on the inside, he always makes sure she has what she needs and then some. Even her “friends” want to be in her position.", "annotation_id": "35292076", "url": "https://genius.com/35292076", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "RAINING IN HOUSTON", "line": "You got friends too, no one told you stay inside, go live your life Your life", "vault_lines": ["You got friends too, no one told you stay inside, go live your life"], "meaning": "Drake is letting this girl know that he has never stopped her from going out with her own friends and doing her own thing, yet she is trying to put restraints on his movements with his friends.", "annotation_id": "35292044", "url": "https://genius.com/35292044", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "RAINING IN HOUSTON", "line": "Blicky on us these days, it’s a glue stick, my love", "vault_lines": ["Blicky on us these days, it's a glue stick, my love"], "meaning": "“Blicky” is slang for a gun, usually a handgun. It’s often used in rap to sound tough or street-smart. Here, Drake is saying he always carry a gun and he compares it to a glue stick, meaning it’s always stuck to him.\nAnother slang term for a gun is a “stick” making this a very witty double entendre suggesting that the ‘stick’ is glued to him.", "annotation_id": "35224436", "url": "https://genius.com/35224436", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "RAINING IN HOUSTON", "line": "Pineapple juice in your cup", "vault_lines": ["Corner booth and pineapple juice in your cup"], "meaning": "Pineapple juice is often consumed in order to make sure that certain things that come out of you taste good.", "annotation_id": "35212316", "url": "https://genius.com/35212316", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "RAINING IN HOUSTON", "line": "I’m pulling strings, shit could get acoustic", "vault_lines": ["I'm pulling strings, shit could get acoustic"], "meaning": "A simple yet very effective double entendre, Drake is saying that he has the power to “pull strings” and get things to go how he wants, but also saying that he is pulling on the strings of an acoustic guitar.", "annotation_id": "35212310", "url": "https://genius.com/35212310", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "RAINING IN HOUSTON", "line": "Hop on 85, drive right past A&M (Past A&M) It’s rainin’ in Houston, we’re not arguing again", "vault_lines": ["Hop on 85, drive right past A&M (Past A&M)", "It's rainin' in Houston, we're not arguing again", "Ayy, hop on 85, right past A&M", "Hop on 85, right past A&M", "It's rainin' in Houston, my love"], "meaning": "Drake owns a home and ranch that used to be called The Inn at Dos Brisas. It’s about 85 miles outside Houston. The road right outside his house, County Road 85 (marked with an “A” in the photo), leads you onto the main route back to Houston. This route passes by Prairie View A&M, the “A&M” he mentions in this line.", "annotation_id": "34651906", "url": "https://genius.com/34651906", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "RAINING IN HOUSTON", "line": "Blue bubbles are blowing up my line", "vault_lines": ["Blue bubbles are blowing up my line"], "meaning": "Drake is implying that his girl is double and triple texting his cellular line via iMessage after a series of missed calls.", "annotation_id": "34578849", "url": "https://genius.com/34578849", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "RAINING IN HOUSTON", "line": "Maya Angelou off seven shots of ‘42, your words are cuttin’ deep, your words are hittin’ different", "vault_lines": ["Maya Angelou off seven shots of '42, your words are cuttin' deep, your words are hittin' different"], "meaning": "Here, Drake compares the harsh words of his lover with the hard-hitting and thought-provoking words of the famous author, poet, and civil rights activist, Maya Angelou.\n\nThe “hittin' different” line is a play on words with “shots of 42.” Instead of just a reference to the Don Julio 1942 tequila, it can also be taken as a nod to the Hall of Fame baseball player, Jackie Robinson, who famously wore the number 42.", "annotation_id": "34578129", "url": "https://genius.com/34578129", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "RAINING IN HOUSTON", "line": "If you got love, H-Town, put your deuces up, put your H’s up one time to my brother, DJ Screw", "vault_lines": ["If you got love, H-Town, put your deuces up, put your H's up one time to my brother, DJ Screw", "Put your H's up now"], "meaning": "Drake pays homage to “DJ Screw” a Houston DJ, known for his “Chopped and Screwed” style of music\n\nScrew unfortunately passed away in November of 2000.\n\n‘Deuces’ consist of holding the index and pinky finger out which resemble the letter ‘H’ for “H-Town”", "annotation_id": "34571807", "url": "https://genius.com/34571807", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "RAINING IN HOUSTON", "status": "done", "targets": 14, "clicked": 14, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-raining-in-houston-lyrics", "genius_title": "RAINING IN HOUSTON"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Road Trips", "line": "Somewhere out in Georgia, beyond the trapping phone", "vault_lines": ["Somewhere out in Georgia, beyond the trapping phone"], "meaning": "A trapping phone is a cheap, prepaid cell phone used strictly for illegal activities, mostly drug dealing.\n\nIt is used to keep criminal business completely separate from a person’s real identity, making it easier to throw away if law enforcement starts tracking it.\n\nIt represents the constant paranoia and hustle of dealing drugs.", "annotation_id": "40082130", "url": "https://genius.com/40082130", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
