{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Road Trips", "line": "Outside all year", "vault_lines": ["Outside all year with my ass in the air, okay"], "meaning": "Also could be interpreted as “Aubz said ‘aw yeah’…” and “I’ll sit all year…” with Aubz being Drake (Aubrey Graham).", "annotation_id": "39957896", "url": "https://genius.com/39957896", "state": "pending", "votes": -6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Road Trips", "line": "When you’re next to me, it’s ecstasy, let’s roll", "vault_lines": ["When you're nеxt to me, it's ecstasy, let's roll", "When you're next to me, it's ecstasy, let's roll"], "meaning": "Throughout the album, Drake has a recurring theme of drug use.\n\nThe best example of this is the songs ‘Outside Tweaking’ and ‘Stuck’.\n\nBoth of these tracks reflect on relationships and how they can become intertwined with drug use.\n\nThis could all play hand in hand with this being the more ‘club music’ album of the three released.", "annotation_id": "39939954", "url": "https://genius.com/39939954", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Road Trips", "line": "I’m supposed to be the one whose heart is made of ice", "vault_lines": ["I'm supposed to be the one whose heart is made of ice"], "meaning": "Drake is THE ICEMAN\nhe reference’s in all 3 of his May 15th albums (Habibti, Iceman, MOH)\n\nHe is saying he is supposed to be emotionally cold (feeling numbness) towards women, shutting down his feelings to prevent himself from getting hurt emotionally.", "annotation_id": "39821765", "url": "https://genius.com/39821765", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Road Trips", "line": "Maybe if we take out an M, then probably", "vault_lines": ["Maybe if we take out an M, then probably"], "meaning": "Taking out the M and rereading the line changes from “she’s a homebody” –> “she’s a hoe-body”\n\ntaking out a million dollars from the bank could change her lifestyle", "annotation_id": "39778691", "url": "https://genius.com/39778691", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Road Trips", "line": "When you’re next to me, it’s ecstasy, let’s roll", "vault_lines": ["When you're nеxt to me, it's ecstasy, let's roll", "When you're next to me, it's ecstasy, let's roll"], "meaning": "This is a reference to the 1977 song “It’s Ecstasy When You Lay Down Next to Me”\n\n\n\n by Barry White.", "annotation_id": "39794126", "url": "https://genius.com/39794126", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Road Trips", "line": "Why do I say sorry with my thumb on the safe?", "vault_lines": ["Why do I say sorry with my thumb on the safe?"], "meaning": "A toxic apology; thumb on the safe as in he’s pointing at her at gunpoint with his thumb on the safety.\n\n\n\nAlso could mean safe, as in a literal money safe. He’s apologizing while his thumb is on a safe dial, ready to “buy” her forgiveness.", "annotation_id": "39789920", "url": "https://genius.com/39789920", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Road Trips", "line": "Lately, your pupils are dilated Eyes red and it’s not from crying, baby", "vault_lines": ["Lately, your pupils are dilated", "Eyes red and it's not from crying, baby"], "meaning": "Dilated pupils point to psychedelic/stimulant drugs like MDMA or cocaine, while bloodshot eyes imply the use of weed or exhaustion.", "annotation_id": "39789876", "url": "https://genius.com/39789876", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Road Trips", "line": "Planes, fame, and currency exchanges", "vault_lines": ["Place fame in currency exchanges"], "meaning": "Drake is looking at reputation like a foreign currency; something volatile that you need to cash out or convert before it loses value.\n\nHe has a cynical tone here, saying that when you treat your name like a commodity, you’re constantly checking the market to see what you’re worth.", "annotation_id": "39789843", "url": "https://genius.com/39789843", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Road Trips", "line": "[Intro: E.S.G.] My boys in Houston, Texas, swanging and banging And what about down in Dallas? Swanging and banging I can’t forget San Antone, swanging and banging Yeah, we got it going on, swanging and banging And all the players in Atlanta", "vault_lines": ["My boys in Houston, Texas, swanging and banging", "And what about down in Dallas? Swanging and banging", "I can't forget San Antone, swanging and banging", "Yeah, we got it going on, swanging and banging", "And all the players in Atlanta"], "meaning": "This is an Sample from a song called Swanging and Banging made by E.S.G in 1995. This song was also sampled in Drake’s 2011 hit HYFR", "annotation_id": "39782736", "url": "https://genius.com/39782736", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Road Trips", "line": "I didn’t say that you’re the most selfish girl alive I just said that you better hope that she doesn’t die", "vault_lines": ["I didn't say that you're the most selfish girl alive", "I just said that you better hope that she doesn't die"], "meaning": "This is a Senator John Kennedy bar (who is notoriously one of the funniest American politicians out of Louisiana.)\n\nHe once said, “I’m not saying you’re the dumbest person in the world, but you better hope the dumbest person in the world doesn’t die.” 😂\n\nhttps://youtube.com/shorts/BnO_E6slPHY?si=LZ8FKeQsrbF0qh5v", "annotation_id": "39782669", "url": "https://genius.com/39782669", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Road Trips", "line": "Do you really wanna spend my money? (Hell yeah) Do you wanna take it off of me? (Hell yeah) Am I outside with the engine running? (Hell yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Do you really wanna spend my money? (Hell yeah)", "Do you wanna take it off of me? (Hell yeah)", "Am I outside with the engine running? (Hell yeah)"], "meaning": "These lines possibly interpolate Jagged Edge on “Where the Party At”:\n\nDo the Eastside run this motha for ya? (Hell yeah!)\nDo my Southside run this motha for ya? (Hell yeah!)", "annotation_id": "39778680", "url": "https://genius.com/39778680", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Road Trips", "line": "Destiny is calling and telling you to go Woah, woah, woah", "vault_lines": ["Dеstiny is telling you to go", "Destiny is telling you to go", "Destiny is calling and telling you to go"], "meaning": "Taking in the context of the rest of the verse, the usage of the word Destiny can be interpreted in two ways:\n1. Destiny in abstract, to mean fate telling you to go\n2. The name of a stripper\nDrake has been known to name-drop strippers before, and has done so on songs from the 2025 album $ome $exy $ongs 4 U.", "annotation_id": "39776845", "url": "https://genius.com/39776845", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
