{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "OVO Sound Radio Episode 59 Tracklist", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-ovo-sound-radio-episode-59-tracklist-lyrics", "genius_title": "OVO Sound Radio Episode 59 Tracklist"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Polar Opposites", "line": "Tweakin’ on vacation with me You set limitations with me Why do I get treated different?", "vault_lines": ["Tweakin' on vacation with me", "You set limitations with me", "Why do I get treated different?"], "meaning": "These lines are basically about feeling like someone is holding back from you even though you’re close to them.\n\n“Tweakin’” here can mean acting strangely, overthinking, being anxious, or behaving emotionally. He’s saying this person is acting a certain way even when they’re supposed to be relaxing and enjoying time together.\n\nDrake then says: “You set limitations with me” He feels like this person has boundaries or restrictions specifically with him. Maybe they won’t fully open up, commit, or do certain things with him.\n\nThis is the emotional core. Drake is extremely famous and a lot comes with that. Likely bringing everything he does to the public eye. He wants to be treated like anyone else, which leads him to the line: “Why do I get treated different?”\n\nThere’s a sense of confusion, hurt, and insecurity underneath it. He’s not necessarily angry—he’s questioning why the relationship feels different from what he expected.", "annotation_id": "41357100", "url": "https://genius.com/41357100", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Polar Opposites", "line": "If I mentioned the pride before the fall ’Cause I wanna risk it all for you", "vault_lines": ["If I mentioned the pride before the fall", "'Cause I wanna risk it all for you"], "meaning": "Yebba is playing on the proverb “pride comes before the fall.” She’s acknowledging that showing too much confidence or ego could lead to getting hurt, but she’s still willing to take that risk.\n\nIn this line, she’s saying that even if loving or trusting this person could be her downfall, the feelings are strong enough that she’s ready to risk everything for them.", "annotation_id": "38007565", "url": "https://genius.com/38007565", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Polar Opposites", "line": "I don’t get hurt much, but I’m not invincible", "vault_lines": ["I don't know, I don't know", "I don't get hurt much, but I'm not invincible"], "meaning": "I don’t get hurt much, but I’m not invincible", "annotation_id": "37612568", "url": "https://genius.com/37612568", "state": "pending", "votes": -4, "second_sense": false, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Polar Opposites", "line": "I adore I adore you Baby, I adore you", "vault_lines": ["Baby, I adore you"], "meaning": "This closing line is a moment of emotional vulnerability and unfiltered affection. After a song filled with confusion, miscommunication, and emotional tension, Drake ends with a simple but powerful declaration he still loves deeply. by using Yebba’s ethereal tone", "annotation_id": "36121923", "url": "https://genius.com/36121923", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Polar Opposites", "line": "You should let your sister be the voice of reason", "vault_lines": ["You should let your sister be the voice of reason"], "meaning": "“Your sister” would be the girl’s other personality since the girl Drake’s addressing is bipolar.\n\nHer other personality should be “the voice of reason” implies that she’s currently acting irrationally", "annotation_id": "32439459", "url": "https://genius.com/32439459", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Polar Opposites", "line": "You know and I know things that she didn’t know", "vault_lines": ["I don't know, I don't know", "You know and I know things that she didn't know"], "meaning": "This is likely a continued reference to\nMarjana Mariana (@marjana.mariana). Drake and Marjana used to follow each other on Instagram for some time.\n\nThese lines are likely a reference to Jorja Smith. Marjana and Jorja Smith were friends at one point, certainly around the time More Life came out. Drake and Jorja’s falling out was the subject of several songs off Scorpion. Conspicuously, Jorja and Marjana no longer follow each other on Instagram either. Perhaps Drake had something to do with that.", "annotation_id": "30222907", "url": "https://genius.com/30222907", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Polar Opposites", "line": "No, no, you remind me of someone I think you know", "vault_lines": ["I don't know, I don't know", "No, no, you remind me of someone I think you know"], "meaning": "I think he is referring to Rihanna\nMariana rhymes with Rihanna", "annotation_id": "30214549", "url": "https://genius.com/30214549", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Polar Opposites", "line": "Either it’s your text that I’m misreading Or it’s just your actions are misleading", "vault_lines": ["Either it's your text that I'm misreading", "Or it's just your actions are misleading"], "meaning": "Expressing feelings over text can go wrong because of tone, misunderstanding and taking things out of context which could lead to the confusion of why a person can come off as acting different in person, they can say things over the phone but never hold up to it in person.", "annotation_id": "30039990", "url": "https://genius.com/30039990", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Polar Opposites", "line": "Oh, I read your last text, you’re gettin’ bold", "vault_lines": ["Oh, I read your last text, you're gettin' bold"], "meaning": "A double entendre with the two meanings of the word “bold” as in brave/confident or “bold” as in text editing", "annotation_id": "29907927", "url": "https://genius.com/29907927", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Polar Opposites", "line": "What they say ’bout the writings on the wall?", "vault_lines": ["What they say 'bout the writings on the wall?"], "meaning": "I love the use of this idiom by Yebba.\n\nIf you say that the writing is on the wall, you mean that there are clear signs that a situation is going to become very difficult or unpleasant.\n\nThis is Yebba, acknowledging that she is taking the risk and ignoring ‘the writing on the wall’.\n\nIt’s the perfect outro for this track", "annotation_id": "29843078", "url": "https://genius.com/29843078", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Polar Opposites", "line": "Plenty other ways to get over people You ain’t had to step on me to gain freedom", "vault_lines": ["Plenty other ways to get over people", "You ain't had to step on me to gain freedom"], "meaning": "When healing from a past relationship there are endless amounts of coping skills available to help you move on.\n\nSo this is eluding to the fact that his ex went about the breakup in an unhealthy way and at his expense. When she could’ve found peace by using a healthier coping mechanism – but instead intentionally brought him down to selfishly allow herself to detach emotionally.", "annotation_id": "29784930", "url": "https://genius.com/29784930", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Polar Opposites", "line": "I bet a full moon is gonna show", "vault_lines": [", I bet a full moon is gonna show"], "meaning": "A full moon showing is a metaphor for someone having their ass out. As the sun sets and the moon rises, Drake knows him and this girl will likely have sex tonight. However, he wants to know what makes her heart full, not just what turns her on- as he suggests in the following lines.", "annotation_id": "29771241", "url": "https://genius.com/29771241", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Polar Opposites", "line": "I don’t know how you run the bases with me Then say nothing sacred with me", "vault_lines": ["I don't know, I don't know", "You set limitations with me", "I don't know how you run the bases with me", "Then say nothing sacred with me"], "meaning": "Running the bases is a metaphor for different acts of foreplay. Typically getting to 1st base with a girl means kissing, 2nd is more physical touch, while 3rd may be more sexual such as oral sex. Rounding all the bases means, you guessed it- going all the way. Drake is confused and upset by the fact that him and this girl he admires engage in sexual activities but she doesn’t express true feelings for him when they are not engaged in these activities. It seems as if this girl is in it for the lust, while Drake wants to explore a deeper connection.", "annotation_id": "29771178", "url": "https://genius.com/29771178", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Polar Opposites", "line": "Wondering what rocks your boat What keeps your heavy heart afloat", "vault_lines": ["Tellin' me what rocks your boat, what keeps your heavy heart afloat", "Wondering what rocks your boat", "What keeps your heavy heart afloat"], "meaning": "“to rock the boat” is a metaphor for making someone upset.\n\nHe takes the metaphor even further by singing “your heavy heart afloat”, because boats do float.", "annotation_id": "29759889", "url": "https://genius.com/29759889", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Polar Opposites", "line": "Mariana, you broke my faith", "vault_lines": ["Mariana, you broke my faith"], "meaning": "This song could possibly be referring to instagram model/fashion designer marjana.mariana, as this past year drake followed her and vice versa but as of recent there is no drake, she still seems cool with his artist Naomi Sharon though.\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/marjana.mariana/?hl=en", "annotation_id": "29749250", "url": "https://genius.com/29749250", "state": "pending", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Polar Opposites", "line": "[Outro]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "A sample of Yebba’s single “Waterfall (I Adore You)”.\n\nOn October 8, 2023, Drake posted on his Instagram story:\n\n@yebbasmith drop the full song from end of Polar Opposites this is not a request it’s a demand 🔓", "annotation_id": "29743431", "url": "https://genius.com/29743431", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Polar Opposites", "line": "Sun is setting on the Atlantic", "vault_lines": ["Sun is setting on the Atlantic"], "meaning": "Typically, the Atlantic Ocean is to the east of North America. The sun, however, rises in the east and sets in the west. Therefore, this line is a subtle way of saying that Drake is vacationing somewhere abroad, perhaps on a boat as he alludes to later in the song.", "annotation_id": "29737054", "url": "https://genius.com/29737054", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Polar Opposites", "line": "Now you’re both leaving", "vault_lines": ["Wе just broke the ice, and now you'rе both leaving"], "meaning": "her two sides/personalities", "annotation_id": "29735452", "url": "https://genius.com/29735452", "state": "pending", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Polar Opposites", "line": "Don’t know how they do things in Pristina I just know the tension is increasing", "vault_lines": ["I don't know, I don't know", "Don't know how they do things in Pristina", "I just know the tension is increasing"], "meaning": "Drake’s reffering to the ongoing North Kosovo crisis, since Pristina is the capital and the largest city in Kosovo.\nDay after the Albanian Independence Day, Drake released a music video for the song, where he and his game-playing friends don matching red jackets, all with the national and ethnic symbol of Albania, the eagle, displayed on their backs.\n\nFor the relation between Albania and Kosovo, see more.", "annotation_id": "29730372", "url": "https://genius.com/29730372", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Polar Opposites", "line": "[Chorus] Bipolar baby, seems like it just went undiagnosed Blocked me on everything, that’s so immature, so unprovoked, I Don’t even know why", "vault_lines": ["I don't know, I don't know", "Bipolar baby, seems like it just went undiagnosed", "Blocked me on everything, that's so immature, so unprovoked, I", "Don't even know why"], "meaning": "The woman in question is sending mixed signals, happy with him one minute, and miserable the next. When she’s unhappy, she blocks him on social media and goes ‘no contact’ without explaining why. Similar to the highs and lows people with Bipolar Disorder exhibit.", "annotation_id": "29728583", "url": "https://genius.com/29728583", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Polar Opposites", "line": "Bidin’ my time with you, then things got political", "vault_lines": ["Bidin' my time with you, then things got political"], "meaning": "A reference to Joe Biden, a member of the Democratic Party. He is involved with politics as he was elected as the 46th President of the USA, he was one of Delawares senators from 1973 to 2009, and he was the Vice President in both terms to Barrack Obama.\n\nHe is also biding his time, literal meaning. He’s waiting it out with her", "annotation_id": "29725742", "url": "https://genius.com/29725742", "state": "pending", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Polar Opposites", "line": "You tried to grease me, but we’re not in Mykonos", "vault_lines": ["You tried to grease me, but we're not in Mykonos"], "meaning": "Drake plays on the “grease/greece” homophone. Mykonos is an island popularly known for its summer party atmosphere, which is located in Greece.\n\nGrease is popular Toronto slang for having sex with someone.\n\nDrake stating that she tried to grease him means that she made an advance to him but the second part of this line insinuates that he turned her down.", "annotation_id": "29725259", "url": "https://genius.com/29725259", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Polar Opposites", "status": "done", "targets": 22, "clicked": 22, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-polar-opposites-lyrics", "genius_title": "Polar Opposites"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SMALL TOWN FAME", "line": "Lost a lot of brothers to this dog-ass game What am I supposed to do with all that pain", "vault_lines": ["Lost a lot of brothers to this dog-ass game", "What am I supposed to do with all that pain"], "meaning": "Drake’s reflecting on how fame and the rap industry have cost him real friendships.\n\nPeople like Future, LeBron James, and others he used to be close with may have drifted because of success, and trust issues.\n\nThe dog-ass game = the toxic nature of the industry. It’s not just about making hits, it’s about surviving emotionally.\n\nDrake and Future:\n\nThey’ve had ups and downs for years, but things got shaky when Drake didn’t include Future on For All The Dogs, and rumors started flying that their relationship was cold again.\n\nTheir relationship went cold again after Future appeared on Metro Boomin’s We Don’t Trust You—the same album where Kendrick Lamar dissed Drake.\n\n\n\nDrake and Lebron James:\n\nIn 2025, Drake unfollowed LeBron and changed lyrics that used to praise him on “Nonstop” while performing in Australia. That happened because of:\n\n\nLeBron James Vibing to Not Like Us : A TikTok video from approximately nine months ago shows LeBron enjoying a live performance of Not Like Us.”\nLeBron Rapping “Not Like Us” Lyrics: A YouTube video titled “LeBron rapping Kendrick Lamar’s ‘Not Like Us’ bar for bar” was published around the same time, suggesting his familiarity with the song.  ￼\n\n\n\n\n\nhttps://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcQ0Z-CbBNpIlYhlSK_Frw7KOdJao4wziTx2SbK-Z6-8x2JjhrkYvuDnEfge&s=10\n\nSources: https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/799138-drake-future-beef-explained?\n\nhttps://nypost.com/2025/02/05/sports/drakes-lyric-change-fuels-lebron-james-feud-speculation", "annotation_id": "35070566", "url": "https://genius.com/35070566", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SMALL TOWN FAME", "line": "You know what, man, we’re all in this Now, whether we’re all in this together Or you’re all in it for yourself The fact of the matter is that we’re in it", "vault_lines": ["You know what, man, we're all in this", "Now, whether we're all in this together", "Or you're all in it for yourself", "The fact of the matter is that we're in it"], "meaning": "Drake samples a TikTok made by Hassan Phills, who first went viral in 2021 and has since amassed over 114k followers on the platform. The sample was used unbeknownst to the comedian, who discovered the outro when the song was released.\n\nAfter the release of the song, Hassan expressed his thoughts on getting on the outro:\n\nIronically, there’s a video I’ve put on TikTok before that is now in a song, you know, for somebody very special, actually…\n\nDrake has shown support for the comedian before, making an appearance at his December 27, 2024, show at Comedy Bar Danforth.\n\nDrake and Hassan backstage", "annotation_id": "34565244", "url": "https://genius.com/34565244", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SMALL TOWN FAME", "line": "Exfoliate that nigga that you with, he a scrub", "vault_lines": ["Exfoliate that nigga that you with, he a scrub"], "meaning": "Exfoliating scrubs remove dead skin\n\nA scrub is a type of a guy that pretends to be more than he is popularized by the song by TLC, No Scrubs\n\nA scrub is a guy who thinks he’s fine\n\nExfoliate one is to remove them from their life therefore Drake plays on the words scrub as in the activity to clean the face and to remove the particular guy out of their life", "annotation_id": "34563576", "url": "https://genius.com/34563576", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SMALL TOWN FAME", "line": "Puttin’ Charli up her nose, X on her tongue She been geekin’ hard, she done had a Brat summer", "vault_lines": ["Puttin' Charli up her nose, X on her tongue", "She been geekin' hard, she done had a Brat summer"], "meaning": "Drake mentions Charli xcx, the English singer coming off of her 2024 Grammy winning record BRAT. “Brat summer” is a trend that derived from the album, referring to accepting your imperfections while embracing the chaos.\n\nDrake uses Charli’s name as a metaphor for cocaine, as the singer frequently references the drug on her tracks. “ X on her tongue” is likely referring to extacy pills, although it may also be alluding to making out with an ex-lover.", "annotation_id": "34561226", "url": "https://genius.com/34561226", "state": "accepted", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SMALL TOWN FAME", "line": "Poppin’ out in Saginaw, poppin’ out in Salt Lake Poppin’ out in Arizona Bitch, I feel like Tate McRae", "vault_lines": ["Poppin' out in Saginaw, poppin' out in Salt Lake", "Poppin' out in Arizona", "Bitch, I feel like Tate McRae"], "meaning": "Tate McRae is a singer, songwriter, and dancer from Calgary, Canada.\n\nIn 2024, before “SMALL TOWN FAME” was released, McRae had been touring across the United States and other countries on her THINK LATER World Tour, following the release of her hit song “greedy,” which became her breakthrough hit in September 2023. She had also just announced her fifth concert tour—her first arena tour, the Miss Possessive Tour. Which began only four months after the THINK LATER World Tour and would once again travel across the United States. Drake appears to reference her global success as an artist through her demanding touring schedule.\n\nIt could be that these lyrics Drake is also referencing Tate’s song “feel like shit” where she sings about being unable to get over her first heartbreak. This may connect to the earlier lyrics in “SMALL TOWN FAME,” suggesting a similar theme of emotional detachment and unresolved relationship issues:\n\nLeavin' out the club with no hoes, it’s a dub\nYou somewhere on house arrest pretending you in love\n\nMcRae commented on the mention in an interview with GQ UK:\n\nWhat was it—Thursday [last week]? I just got a text from my friends being like, ‘Oh my God, listen to 1:23 on this song.’ It was funny. I’ve never heard my name in a song before, [and] I’ve never met Drake. You also get a little nervous listening to it, like, ‘Oh my God, why am I being mentioned?’ But it was cool. I’m a fan of him.", "annotation_id": "34561195", "url": "https://genius.com/34561195", "state": "accepted", "votes": 52, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SMALL TOWN FAME", "status": "done", "targets": 5, "clicked": 5, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-small-town-fame-lyrics", "genius_title": "SMALL TOWN FAME"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Talk To Me", "line": "Fifteen brothers, no friends when I pull up, for peace of mind", "vault_lines": ["Fifteen brothers, no friends when I pull up, for peace of mind"], "meaning": "Drake only has his closest people, or otherwise his “Brothers” at the hangout spot. This clears his mind as these are the day 1s he can trust, not like his “friends” who can backstab him.", "annotation_id": "32500859", "url": "https://genius.com/32500859", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Talk To Me", "line": "We might slide on a nigga inside this club, girl, close your eyes", "vault_lines": ["We might slide on a nigga inside this club, girl, close your eyes"], "meaning": "Drake implies that girls have this “certified lover boy” image. He is having the girl close her eyes so she doesn’t see what happens, which would ruin his image.", "annotation_id": "32500853", "url": "https://genius.com/32500853", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Talk To Me", "line": "Got the audacity to talk to me crazy, you buggin’", "vault_lines": ["Got the audacity to talk to me crazy, you buggin'"], "meaning": "He’s saying how dare you have the nerve to talk to me crazy when you didn’t even hold me down or talk to me when I was locked up and really going thru it. Like you weren’t around then so chill out because I know what you about.", "annotation_id": "22542684", "url": "https://genius.com/22542684", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Talk To Me", "line": "Fifteen brothers, no friends when I pull up, for peace of mind", "vault_lines": ["Fifteen brothers, no friends when I pull up, for peace of mind"], "meaning": "When he pulls up to the hangout or the club it’s all his bros not some randoms, which gives him some peace of mind and comfort. Knowing he’s with people he really trusts and are down for him", "annotation_id": "22542676", "url": "https://genius.com/22542676", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Talk To Me", "line": "650S, bitch, I feel like Lil Boosie", "vault_lines": ["650S, bitch, I feel like Lil Boosie"], "meaning": "The McLaren 650S is a British sports car designed and manufactured by British automobile manufacturer McLaren Automotive.\n\n\n\nHe can also be referencing his 2020 track “Lil Boosie” on his mixtape We Know The Truth.", "annotation_id": "22297715", "url": "https://genius.com/22297715", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Talk To Me", "line": "Ayy, baby, was your name on any JPays?", "vault_lines": ["Ayy, baby, was your name on any JPays?"], "meaning": "JPay is a private company connected with county, state, and federal correctional facilities in the US. It allows people to send money, eMessages, live videos, and possibly an mp3 player to an Incarcerated Inmate.", "annotation_id": "22162865", "url": "https://genius.com/22162865", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
