{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Treacherous Twins", "line": "When you tell me life is good, I want better for you (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["You tell me you want somethin', I would tell you, \"Same, same\"", "Would you die for me?", "When you tell me life is good, I want better for you (Yeah)"], "meaning": "A possible reference to the 2020 hit song by Future Life is Good featuring Drake.\n\n\n\nIt is well known that the two rappers have been close friends since the early 2010s and have collaborated on many projects since including a collaborative mixtape What a Time To Be Alive which debuted at number one on the US Billboard 200 in 2015.", "annotation_id": "27529144", "url": "https://genius.com/27529144", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Treacherous Twins", "line": "And I know the city that we from not a safe place", "vault_lines": ["And I know thе city that we from not a safe place"], "meaning": "Drake famously hails from Toronto, Canada, and grew up on Weston Road, a predominantly working class area with a relatively high crime rate. Weston has earnt itself the title of “Toronto’s Murder Capital”, hence why Drake is calling his city “not a safe place”.\n\nDrake described life growing up on Weston Road in an interview with Complex:\n\nHere’s the thing, I grew up on Weston Road. That’s near the west end of the city. It’s not the nicest area in the world. I grew up there. […] My mother was very sick. We were very poor, like broke. The only money I had coming in was off of Canadian TV, which isn’t that much money when you break it down.\n\n Weston Road (pictured)", "annotation_id": "27475802", "url": "https://genius.com/27475802", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Treacherous Twins", "line": "You my treacherous lil’ twin, and you know that we locked in", "vault_lines": ["You my treacherous lil' twin, and you know that we locked in", "You my twin, you my treacherous lil' twin"], "meaning": "Drake is loyal to his day ones and only his day ones which he often calls his Kin or Family.\n\nSimilar to what he described in CLBs No Friends in the Industry ‘My brothers been my, brothers, man You niggas ain’t no kin to me’", "annotation_id": "27239165", "url": "https://genius.com/27239165", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Treacherous Twins", "line": "Life is good", "vault_lines": ["When you tell me life is good, I want better for you (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Drake was featured on the 2020 diamond single Life is Good by Future. This could be reference to the hit song.", "annotation_id": "27129717", "url": "https://genius.com/27129717", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Treacherous Twins", "line": "Always kept me umbrellaed up when the rain came", "vault_lines": ["Always kept me umbrellaed up when the rain came"], "meaning": "This is a reference to Rihanna’s hit song “Umbrella”.\n\n“Now that it’s raining more than ever\nKnow that we’ll still have each other\nYou can stand under my umbrella”.\n\nDrake’s treacherous twin has always protected him and held him down (umbrellaed him) when times got tough (when the rain came).", "annotation_id": "27092471", "url": "https://genius.com/27092471", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
