{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Treacherous Twins", "line": "In the bed, she get wicked, with her parents she be wholesome (Woah)", "vault_lines": ["In the bed, she get wicked, with her parents she be wholesome (Woah)"], "meaning": "The first part is describing how she is Wicked in bed also known as being Naughty/Evil and then he used another word with the letter “W” with Wholesome talking about her actions and behavior with her parents.", "annotation_id": "27062971", "url": "https://genius.com/27062971", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Treacherous Twins", "line": "You my twin You my twin, you my treacherous lil’ twin You my twin, you my treacherous lil’ twin You my twin, you my treacherous lil’ twin", "vault_lines": ["You my treacherous lil' twin, and you know that we locked in", "You my twin, you my treacherous lil' twin"], "meaning": "“Twin” is often a term to refer to a close companion, however, “treacherous” means guilty of betrayal hence the heavy contrast between the two words presents a toxic friendship.", "annotation_id": "27055182", "url": "https://genius.com/27055182", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Treacherous Twins", "line": "I wanna tell you how I feel when I’m loaded", "vault_lines": ["I wanna tell you how I feel when I'm loaded (Oh)"], "meaning": "Drake could mean that his cock is loaded with cum, and it’s ready to shoot out, like a gun.", "annotation_id": "27054962", "url": "https://genius.com/27054962", "state": "pending", "votes": -40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Treacherous Twins", "line": "I would lay somethin’ down for you I would clear a whole town for you Spray the whole hundred round for you Twistin’ all my fingers for my dawg", "vault_lines": ["Twistin' up my fingers for my twin", "Would you die for me?", "I would lay somethin' down for you", "I would clear a whole town for you", "Spray the whole hundred round for you", "Twistin' all my fingers for my dawg"], "meaning": "Drake is stating that he is willing to kill for his lover.", "annotation_id": "27054328", "url": "https://genius.com/27054328", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Treacherous Twins", "line": "Five hundred million out the face, feel like K.K.", "vault_lines": ["Five hundrеd million out the face, feel like K.K."], "meaning": "Drake was rumored (and seemingly confirmed by multiple sources) that he signed a record deal with Universal Music Group or UMG, estimated worth at $500 million, which explains the reference ‘out the face’ which he expected out of nowhere.\n\nThe chairman of UMG, Sir Lucian Grainge has confirmed on Variety that ‘Drake has entered into an expansive, multi-faceted deal with the company’. The total sum was not mentioned but an insider has described the arrangement of the deal as “Lebron-sized.”\n\n\n\nDrake has also hinted & rapped about his record deal with UMG in “Major Distribution” whilst praising the Puerto Rican artist, Bad Bunny.\n\nBad Bunny numbers, it’s a robbery\nFive-hundred million, just for Aubrey\n\n\n\nHe could also be referencing to the businesswoman and media personality, Kim Kardashian who has a whopping net worth of $1.2 billion.", "annotation_id": "27053331", "url": "https://genius.com/27053331", "state": "pending", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Treacherous Twins", "line": "Would you die for me? Would you go at niggas necks like a tie for me? Do the time for a crime you didn’t do for me? Or do a crime at a time when it was loose for me?", "vault_lines": ["Would you die for me?", "Would you go at niggas necks like a tie for me?", "Do the time for a crime you didn't do for me?", "Or do a crime at a time when it was loose for me?"], "meaning": "21 is asking if you are his Ride or Die. This is the strongest friendship bond in existence, and when you are Ride or Die for someone, you’ll go at someone’s neck, do time, or commit a crime for you.", "annotation_id": "27053088", "url": "https://genius.com/27053088", "state": "pending", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Treacherous Twins", "line": "I don’t show ID at clubs, ’cause they know that I’m 21 (Woah, 21)", "vault_lines": ["I don't show ID at clubs, 'cause they know that I'm 21 (Woah, 21)"], "meaning": "Here, 21 Savage, uses a double entendre to reaffirm his high-profile state while also wrapping into part of his stage name, “21.”\n\nAn ID is an identification card which is used all over the U.S. to determine one’s age, address, and sex. Here, 21 notes that he doesn’t need to show his ID at a club because he is over the age of 21 — the national drinking age in the US.\n\nHowever, 21 also mentions how “they know that [he’s] 21,” indicating that regardless of his age, he will be let inside the club nonetheless due to his high level of fame. Furthermore, this lyric could also refer to 21’s primary genre, trap which — alongside house music — is predominantly played in clubs.", "annotation_id": "27052303", "url": "https://genius.com/27052303", "state": "accepted", "votes": 152, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Treacherous Twins", "status": "done", "targets": 16, "clicked": 16, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-and-21-savage-treacherous-twins-lyrics", "genius_title": "Treacherous Twins"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Asthma Team", "line": "And it’s cool if you spill suttin it’s only carpet That’s why I get my interior colour only dark shit", "vault_lines": ["And it's cool if you spill suttin it's only carpet", "That's why I get my interior colour only dark shit"], "meaning": "Explanation:\n\nThe lyric is about deflecting guilt or pressure before it lands.\n\n“It’s cool if you spill suttin, it’s only carpet” — the speaker is telling someone not to stress about making a mistake, specifically spilling something. “Suttin” is UK slang for “something.” The carpet is treated as worthless, disposable, not precious. That lowers the stakes of the accident.\n\n“That’s why I get my interior colour only dark shit” — the punchline. He deliberately chooses dark-colored car interiors because stains won’t show. It’s not that he’s careless with his possessions; it’s that he’s already engineered the environment so that mistakes won’t matter visually. The stain disappears into the black.\n\nThe deeper read: this is a metaphor for staying clean while operating in dirty situations. He keeps things dark so nothing can visibly mark him. It’s a flex about control, preparation, and moving through chaos without looking affected. The rhyme structure also supports it — “carpet” / “dark shit” is a half-rhyme with UK street delivery, and the internal flow mimics a casual shrug while still being intentional.", "annotation_id": "41411987", "url": "https://genius.com/41411987", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Asthma Team", "line": "My necklace suffer from depression it’s forever blue", "vault_lines": ["My necklace suffer from depression it's forever blue"], "meaning": "Blue is used to describe sadness. Drake’s chain is blue so he personifies it and describes it as suffering from depression.", "annotation_id": "35840496", "url": "https://genius.com/35840496", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Asthma Team", "line": "But once you slept with one dime man, you slept with them all, uhh", "vault_lines": ["But once you slept with one dime man, you slept with them all, uhh"], "meaning": "All of these women are the same to Drake. Good looks, no personality!", "annotation_id": "35840491", "url": "https://genius.com/35840491", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Asthma Team", "line": "I should leave Earth, nothing left to do here", "vault_lines": ["I should leave Earth, nothing left to do here"], "meaning": "In this line Drake can be using a play on words by saying I should leave (leaves – leaf) earth nothing left to do (dew) here. Dew is known to fall upon leaves so Drake is stating that he should leave earth as in to make it more green by putting leaves. Also green is mostly to referred to as money in hip hop which we can see earlier he says “the inside of my wallet is pasture green”.", "annotation_id": "22123753", "url": "https://genius.com/22123753", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Asthma Team", "line": "I parallel the Flying +Spur+ +Tony park+ it", "vault_lines": ["I parallel the Flying +Spur+ +Tony park+ it"], "meaning": "Drake parallel parks his Bentley Flying Spur.  Tony Parker is the point guard for the San Antonio Spurs.", "annotation_id": "90395", "url": "https://genius.com/90395", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Asthma Team", "line": "I run my bill up making executives calls", "vault_lines": ["I run my bill up making executives calls"], "meaning": "Making long distance calls to foreign countries such as the US, Europe and paying high rates or using certain VOIP services which would have been expensive in the year 2007 before more competitors entered the market.\n\nFirst known reference to exorbitant phone bills being in Biggie Smalls' Juicy: “Phone bill about two g’s flat/no need to worry, my accountant handles that”\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_JZom_gVfuw", "annotation_id": "82976", "url": "https://genius.com/82976", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Asthma Team", "line": "Everyday is Christmas and e’ry night is New Year’s", "vault_lines": ["Everyday is Christmas and e'ry night is New Year's"], "meaning": "Drake has a partyful lifestyle. Usually there are huge parties on Chrstmas and New Years. Unforgettable shit happens. And its supposed to be tha biggest party of the year. Well this is Drake’s life.\n\n\n\nHe also took this phrase from famous soul artist Sade’s (one of Drakes influences) 1985 song “The Sweetest Taboo”", "annotation_id": "82648", "url": "https://genius.com/82648", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Asthma Team", "line": "The inside of my wallet is pasture/ past your green", "vault_lines": ["The inside of my wallet is pasture/ past your green"], "meaning": "Very clever use of homophonic phrasing with \"pasture\" and \"past your\" green. Regardless of which of those two ideas comes to mind, it means that he’s got money and it’s probably more than what you have. This could be exaggerated braggadocio because if we fast forward to 2011, he admits that he wasn’t as rich as used to claim", "annotation_id": "82575", "url": "https://genius.com/82575", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Asthma Team", "line": "See me in the CL 6 with Haffa B", "vault_lines": ["See me in the CL 6 with Haffa B"], "meaning": "Haffa B also means half-a-B, or a 3, so you’ll see him in a Mercedes CL 63 AMG since he’s so rich.\n\nHaffa is a person from Scarborough involved with Drake. Drake also mentions him in  “Lord knows”", "annotation_id": "82566", "url": "https://genius.com/82566", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
