{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Search & Rescue", "line": "I gave you the world, but there’s other planets too, where", "vault_lines": ["I gave you the world, but there's other planets too, where"], "meaning": "he is basically saying he’ll give u anything but also is anything happens in their relationship he is protected", "annotation_id": "36851315", "url": "https://genius.com/36851315", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Search & Rescue", "line": "BNYX", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "BNYX (Pronounced Benny X), is a producer from Philadelphia who is most well known for producing for Yeat, but has collaborated with many artists such as Lil Uzi Vert, Travis Scott, Zack Fox, Zeeloperz and many more.", "annotation_id": "29542332", "url": "https://genius.com/29542332", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Search & Rescue", "line": "Not a opposition side Put you in a— I won’t put you in a fucked-up position, I", "vault_lines": ["I wanna be consistent, not a opposition side", "Put you in a—", "I won't put you in a fucked-up position, I"], "meaning": "The lyrics are “Out of all positions I put you in, I won’t put you in that fucked up position.”\n\nDrake is saying he’s put this girl in a lot of positions (sex positions). But no matter how many positions he puts her in, he’ll never put her in the fucked up position of leaving her and “going missing.” He wants to be consistent and doesn’t want this to just be another fling.", "annotation_id": "28246549", "url": "https://genius.com/28246549", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Search & Rescue", "line": "All I know is hit the mall and see what damage I could do", "vault_lines": ["All I know is hit the mall and see what damage I could do"], "meaning": "This line is about Drake’s tendency to purchase luxury items for his acquaintances, often described by him on other lyrics as well, like on his 2022 hit, Hours in Silence :\n\nI gotta stop goin' Lenci', Rollie, first week", "annotation_id": "28240649", "url": "https://genius.com/28240649", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Search & Rescue", "line": "SADPONY", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "SADPONY’s producer tag is voiced by Vancouver-born vocalist-rapper, Tommy Genesis. She’s most known for her eponymous September 2017 single, “Tommy.”", "annotation_id": "28225981", "url": "https://genius.com/28225981", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Search & Rescue", "line": "Come and rescue me, woah Take me out the club, what? Take me out the trap, what?", "vault_lines": ["Take me out the club, what? Take me out the trap, what?", "Come and rescue mе", "Take me out the club, take me out the trap", "Come and rescue me", "Come and rescue me, woah"], "meaning": "Infamous for being a playboy, Drake has reportedly been in numerous on-and-off relationships with a multitude of women. His struggles to maintain stable relationships are often reflected in his music, most notably on “Marvin’s Room.”\n\nDrake seeks “rescue” in his personal life; he desires a stable relationship. The terms “off the market” and “off from the map” mean that a person is no longer available romantically—often implying that they are in a relationship. “It’s a wrap” is an idiom that means something has concluded—in this case, his search for love. Drake is implying that he wishes to find a lifelong partner.", "annotation_id": "28218665", "url": "https://genius.com/28218665", "state": "accepted", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Search & Rescue", "line": "(Okay)", "vault_lines": ["Tell me what to do (Okay)", "Okay, now we talkin', yeah, okay, now we talkin', yeah", "Okay, now we talkin', yeah"], "meaning": "Further sampling Kim Kardashian, some fans speculate Drake may be reigniting beef with Ye, adding insult to injury after their very public breakup.\n\nThis would not be the first time Drizzy has left fans contemplating a diss towards his industry peer. In 2018 many perceived his lines on Sicko Mode as having ostensibly similar intentions. Multiple other tracks such as 7am on Bridle Path, and Circo Loco have also raised similar controversy.", "annotation_id": "28216977", "url": "https://genius.com/28216977", "state": "pending", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Search & Rescue", "line": "I need someone to be patient with me Someone to get money with, not take it from me, look They don’t even need to be as famous as me I don’t think I’ll meet ’em at the places I be", "vault_lines": ["I need someone to be patient with me", "Someone to get money with, not take it from me, look", "They don't even need to be as famous as me", "I don't think I'll meet 'em at the places I be"], "meaning": "Drake previously held an aversion to handouts on the Views track, “9”:\n\nAll these handouts, man, it’s getting outta hand\nI'ma start telling niggas “Get it how you can”\nI got it right now so I’m everybody’s friend\nIf I ever lose I bet we never speak again", "annotation_id": "28215707", "url": "https://genius.com/28215707", "state": "accepted", "votes": 71, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Search & Rescue", "line": "Don’t know how to express my love That’s why I American Expre-e-e-e-e-ess my love for you I need you, yeah, I really do, tell me what to do", "vault_lines": ["I don't really know how to confess my love", "Don't know how to express my love", "That's why I American Expre-e-e-e-e-ess my love for you", "I need you, yeah, I really do, tell me what to do", "Tell me what to do (Okay)"], "meaning": "Drake isn’t one-hundred percent when it comes to projecting love as he can often be awkward. He opts to splurge on his girl using his American Express card. It’s more than likely he uses a black credit card, which is an exclusive credit card that is solely reserved for the ultrawealthy and has no spending limits.\n\nStrangely, Drake contradicts this sentiment throughout “Search & Rescue”’s chorus:\n\nI need someone to be patient with me\nSomeone to get money with, not take it from me, look\n\nDrake previously alluded to American Express credit cards on 2019’s “Omertà”:\n\nI don’t carry cash ‘cause the money is digital\nIt’s the American Expresser, the debt collector", "annotation_id": "28197744", "url": "https://genius.com/28197744", "state": "accepted", "votes": 63, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Search & Rescue", "line": "Don’t hit me up and “WYD” me, baby, nah Send a boy a P-I-C or “See me, baby,” damn", "vault_lines": ["Don't hit me up and \"WYD\" me, baby, nah", "Send a boy a P-I-C or \"See me, baby,\" damn"], "meaning": "The abbreviation “WYD” means “What [are] you doing?” implying Drake’s low interest in sticking to a non-sexual conversation. Given the sexual tension between the two, he asks the woman to send him a nude photo or have intercourse.\n\nPromiscuous topics have been commonplace in Drake’s lyrics. In DJ Khaled’s June 2016 track “For Free,” featuring Drake, he boasts:\n\nYou know this dick ain’t free\nI got girls that I shoulda made pay for it\nGot girls that I shoulda made wait for it\nI got girls that’ll cancel a flight back home\nStay another day for it", "annotation_id": "28194354", "url": "https://genius.com/28194354", "state": "accepted", "votes": 54, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Search & Rescue", "line": "I didn’t come this far, just to come this far and not be happy Okay, that’s fair Remember that You didn’t come this far, just to come this far Yep, I saw it on the internet, hehehe", "vault_lines": ["I didn't come this far, just to come this far and not be happy", "You didn't come this far, just to come this far", "Yep, I saw it on the internet, hehehe"], "meaning": "This brief audio is taken from Keeping Up with the Kardashians. The scene contains Kim Kardashian talking with her mom, Kris Jenner, about her bitter November 2022 divorce with Kanye West.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/DMF53Rrs3ug?t=19\n\nDrake appears to be teasing Kanye West, who married Kim Kardashian between May 2014 – March 2022 after the pair had a divorce. Drake and Kanye were known for their conflict, which began early 2010, when Drake’s sample verse was removed from the final version of Kanye’s November 2010 track “All of the Lights.”\n\nFollowing onward to 2011, Drake threw shots at JAY-Z’s and Kanye’s collaborative August 2011 album, Watch the Throne on DJ Khaled’s May 2011 single, “I’m On One”:\n\nI’m just feeling like the throne is for the taking—\nWatch me take it\n\nHowever, Drake’s dad, Dennis Graham, made a notable appearance on TMZ’s Instagram post, defending his son and asserted that there’s no feud between the two stars:\n\nDrake is not trolling anyone, it’s just a song. Why try and create a Kanye and Drake beef again???????????????🤦🏽‍♂️🤦🏽‍♂️🤦🏽‍♂️🤦🏽‍♂️🤦🏽‍♂️🤦🏽‍♂️🤦🏽‍♂️🤦🏽‍♂️🤦🏽‍♂️🤦🏽‍♂️🤦🏽‍♂️🤦🏽‍♂️", "annotation_id": "28172391", "url": "https://genius.com/28172391", "state": "accepted", "votes": 97, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Search & Rescue", "line": "(I-I-I)", "vault_lines": ["I need someone to be patient with me", "I didn't come this far, just to come this far and not be happy", "Yep, I saw it on the internet, hehehe", "I don't really know how to confess my love", "Really seem like God wanna test my love for you (I-I-I)", "That's why I American Expre-e-e-e-e-ess my love for you", "I need you, yeah, I really do, tell me what to do", "All I know is hit the mall and see what damage I could do", "I gave you the world, but there's other planets too, where", "Send a boy a P-I-C or \"See me, baby,\" damn", "When we talk, you gotta listen, I don't wanna go missin'", "I wanna be consistent, not a opposition side", "I won't put you in a fucked-up position, I", "I don't think I'll meet 'em at the places I be", "But deep down I think about you all day, mami", "I know I'm a pitbull, but dale, mami", "I just wanna take you on a holiday, mami"], "meaning": "This is a snippet of Working on Dying’s collective tag. Producer BNYX® signed to the label in 2021.\n\nThe full tag can be heard on Drake’s first collaboration with the collective, May 2018’s Oogie Mane-produced “I’m Upset.”", "annotation_id": "28130705", "url": "https://genius.com/28130705", "state": "accepted", "votes": 57, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Search & Rescue", "line": "I know I’m a pitbull, but dale, mami", "vault_lines": ["I know I'm a pitbull, but dale, mami"], "meaning": "The Spanish word, “dale,” has multiple meanings. It can be roughly translated to “come on.”\n\nThe term was popularized in pop culture by Pitbull, who says it throughout his discography. It’s also the name of his ninth studio album. Over a decade before this song’s release, Drake mentioned Pitbull and his music style during a 2012 interview with NME:\n\nFor me, the David Guetta stuff just doesn’t work, I don’t really wanna go there. There’s other artists, that’s their sound. They feel in order to thrive internationally that they gotta do straightforward, four on the floor, David Guetta, Pitbull music. For me, I’d rather go to somebody like Jamie xx and tell him, ‘Look, I really wanna turn the club upside down, but I wanna do it with integrity, with soul.’\n\nDrake asks the woman to give him a chance, thereby “rescuing” him, in spite of Drake associating with contentious people. Pit bulls have a controversial reputation as they are often perceived as “vicious” due to their usage throughout dogfighting. However, in the right circumstances, pit bulls make great family pets.\n\nThree days prior to releasing “Search & Rescue,” Drake posted a photo of Pitbull with the caption “Dale Mami…” on his Instagram story. Drake also shared another photo of Pitbull on his Instagram story following the song’s release.", "annotation_id": "28123410", "url": "https://genius.com/28123410", "state": "accepted", "votes": 75, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Search & Rescue", "status": "done", "targets": 13, "clicked": 13, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-search-and-rescue-lyrics", "genius_title": "Search & Rescue"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Still Fly", "line": "Lebanon Dons in this bitch.", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Oliver & 40 are both Lebanese Canadian\n\nNoah Shebib, better known as “40”, is Drake’s producer and co-founder of OVO (alongside Drake and Oliver El-Khatib). He was born in Canada but is of Lebanese descent\n\nOliver El-Khatib, on the other hand, is Drake’s co-manager and co-founder of OVO (alongside Drake and 40) Oliver was also born in Canada but is of Lebanese descent. El-Khatib is credited to be the genius behind Drake’s global branding existence.", "annotation_id": "34340082", "url": "https://genius.com/34340082", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Still Fly", "line": "Paige, I hope you don’t mind, I hope you don’t mind me, uhm havin’ a little fun you know?", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "He minded.", "annotation_id": "30506854", "url": "https://genius.com/30506854", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": false, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
