{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Try Harder", "line": "Sometimes I feel like Lohan and Hilary Duff are the only ones with enough To feel what I’m about to say in this song", "vault_lines": ["Sometimes I feel like Lohan and Hilary Duff are the only ones with enough", "To feel what I'm about to say in this song"], "meaning": "Much like Lindsay Lohan and Hilary Duff, Drake was a teen star. Lohan starred in Disney movies like The Parent Trap and Duff starred in the Disney series Lizzie McGuire, meanwhile Drake starred in Degrassi—which may be he feels they’ll relate to this song as he vents his frustrations.", "annotation_id": "344387", "url": "https://genius.com/344387", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Try Harder", "status": "done", "targets": 1, "clicked": 1, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-try-harder-lyrics", "genius_title": "Try Harder"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "10 Bands", "line": "Yeah, shout goes out to Nike, checks all over me I need a FuelBand just to see how long the run has been", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, shout goes out to Nike, checks all over me", "I need a FuelBand just to see how long the run has been"], "meaning": "“How long the run has been” also refers to the length of time that a product is on store shelves for, since this period of time is called a “run” or a “product run” in the biz. Drake has had several collaborations with Nike in the past so…\nA) Drake could also be joking that he doesn’t even know how long his own Nike merchandise has been out for; it just makes money and he’s successful getting his cut from it all. Point proven in the line, “How much I make off deal, how the fuck should I know?”\nB) Drake is joking and using a double entendre that he’s going to use the ever-efficient Fuelband to see how long his products have been out in the market, as well as how long he’s been hustling in the rap game. Again, it’s a vibe of “I’ve been going so long, so successfully, I’m not even sure how long!”\nTo cool to care.\nSneaker collaboration example: http://pitchfork.com/news/53225-drake-announces-partnership-with-michael-jordans-nike-brand-for-ovo-sneakers-shares-pics/", "annotation_id": "7941918", "url": "https://genius.com/7941918", "state": "verified", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "10 Bands", "line": "I been in the crib with the phones off I been at the house takin’ no calls I done hit the stride, got my shit goin’ In the 6, cookin’ with the wrist motion", "vault_lines": ["I been in the crib with the phones off", "I been at the house takin' no calls", "I done hit the stride, got my shit goin'", "In the 6, cookin' with the wrist motion", "In the 6, cookin' with the wri-wri-wri-wri"], "meaning": "The “cooking with the wrist motion” also refers to the celebratory dance that is popular with the Toronto Blue Jays, which is lovingly referred to as “Stir It Up”.\n\nFor the Blue Jay’s first post-season game in 22 years, Ikea even brought “#stiritup” spoons to give away to fans. They were all confiscated when people tried to bring them into the stadium: http://www.citynews.ca/2015/10/08/trending-need-a-spoon-to-stir-it-up-for-the-jays/", "annotation_id": "7941892", "url": "https://genius.com/7941892", "state": "verified", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "10 Bands", "line": "[Chorus] Ten bands, fifty bands, hunnid bands Fuck it, man, let’s just not even discuss it, man OMG, niggas sleep, I ain’t trippin’, I’ma let ’em sleep I ain’t trippin’, let ’em rest in peace", "vault_lines": ["Ten bands, fifty bands, hunnid bands", "Fuck it, man, let's just not even discuss it, man", "OMG, niggas sleep, I ain't trippin', I'ma let 'em sleep", "I ain't trippin', let 'em rest in peace"], "meaning": "This song is about Drake’s Nike endorsements. He’s talking about getting boxes and boxes of Nike Fuel Bands in the mail in the hook and is a little embarrassed about it (“Fuck it man, let’s just not even discuss it man.”", "annotation_id": "6271642", "url": "https://genius.com/6271642", "state": "verified", "votes": 48, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "10 Bands", "line": "6 God, put both hands together, that’s amazin’ grace 6 God, selfish with the love, I need all the praise (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["6 God, put both hands together, that's amazin' grace", "6 God, selfish with the love, I need all the praise (Woo)"], "meaning": "https://genius.com/4887636/Drake-10-bands/10-bands-50-bands-100-bands-fuck-it-man-lets-just-not-even-discuss-it-man-omg-niggas-sleep-i-aint-trippin-imma-let-em-sleep-i-aint-trippin-let-em-rest-in-peace", "annotation_id": "5107867", "url": "https://genius.com/5107867", "state": "verified", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "10 Bands", "line": "Soda dirty like Diana never clean", "vault_lines": ["Soda dirty like Diana never clean"], "meaning": "He never drinks only Soda it’s mixed with Codeine. Drake used it as an Entedre referencing Michael Jackson “Dirty Diana” song", "annotation_id": "4934109", "url": "https://genius.com/4934109", "state": "verified", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "10 Bands", "line": "All my watches always timeless, you can keep the diamonds Treatin’ Diamonds of Atlanta like it’s King of Diamonds", "vault_lines": ["All my watches always timeless, you can keep the diamonds", "Treatin' Diamonds of Atlanta like it's King of Diamonds"], "meaning": "Just a thought. But, could he also be poking at Jay Z.\n\nOff WTT, Hov has a similar line about his watch being too filled with diamonds that that can’t keep time. Where Drizzy is saying he is beyond and above material items. He can continue living in this world without distraction.", "annotation_id": "4913192", "url": "https://genius.com/4913192", "state": "verified", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "10 Bands", "line": "I treat V Live like it’s 07 in Magic City", "vault_lines": ["I treat V Live like it's 07 in Magic City"], "meaning": "V Live is a steakhouse in Houston where you can get a meal, a haircut, and a beautiful view. Magic City is a strip club in Atlanta. Drake changes the spot, but continues his spending habits.", "annotation_id": "4888844", "url": "https://genius.com/4888844", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "10 Bands", "line": "Take a flick, I look like Meechy, look like Bleu DaVinci", "vault_lines": ["Take a flick, I look like Meechy, look like Bleu DaVinci"], "meaning": "Big Meech is the leader of the Black Mafia Family, a drug trafficking organization based in Detroit. They also had a large hub in Atlanta.\n\nIn 2000 the organization started the hip-hop record label BMF Entertainment as a way to legitimize their business. Bleu DaVinci was the only artist signed to the label.", "annotation_id": "4888772", "url": "https://genius.com/4888772", "state": "accepted", "votes": 44, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "10 Bands", "line": "6 God, put both hands together, that’s amazin’ grace 6 God, selfish with the love, I need all the praise (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["6 God, put both hands together, that's amazin' grace", "6 God, selfish with the love, I need all the praise (Woo)"], "meaning": "Drake refers to himself as the “6 God,” where the “6” represents Toronto. Just like people pray to God, Drizzy has people putting their hands together as if they were saying grace.\n\nThe cover art for “6 God” (left) and IYRTITL (right) also show a pair of hands pressed together as if praying (one theory is that the cover art was inspired by a 1508 painting by Albrecht Dürer).", "annotation_id": "4888683", "url": "https://genius.com/4888683", "state": "accepted", "votes": 58, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "10 Bands", "line": "This that OVO, that SZN, this that new Toronto", "vault_lines": ["This that OVO, that SZN, this that new Toronto"], "meaning": "TopSZN, pronounced “Top Season”, is a movement that celebrates victory.  Since Drake blew up he has put OVO, his record label, and Toronto, his city, on the map.", "annotation_id": "4888665", "url": "https://genius.com/4888665", "state": "accepted", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "10 Bands", "line": "I been in the crib with the phones off I been at the house takin’ no calls I done hit the stride, got my shit goin’ In the 6, cookin’ with the wrist motion", "vault_lines": ["I been in the crib with the phones off", "I been at the house takin' no calls", "I done hit the stride, got my shit goin'", "In the 6, cookin' with the wrist motion", "In the 6, cookin' with the wri-wri-wri-wri"], "meaning": "His always booming Instagram and proclivity for appearances at Toronto Raptor games might say differently, but Drake is staying by his lonely and instead focuses on himself and what he needs to do to keep up his unmatched success.\n\nThe “wrist motion” refers to Father’s cooking dance popularized through his song, “Look At Wrist.” Drake also shouted it out on his Instagram.", "annotation_id": "4888293", "url": "https://genius.com/4888293", "state": "accepted", "votes": 72, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "10 Bands", "line": "Soda dirty like Diana never clean", "vault_lines": ["Soda dirty like Diana never clean"], "meaning": "Drake alludes to Michael Jackson’s 1988 single “Dirty Diana” from his album Bad. Drake’s soda is as “dirty” as Diana – it’s mixed with codeine to make lean. Drake has been known to drink lean often.", "annotation_id": "4888145", "url": "https://genius.com/4888145", "state": "accepted", "votes": 50, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "10 Bands", "line": "I was payin’ mama’s rent when I was turnin’ seventeen", "vault_lines": ["I was payin' mama's rent when I was turnin' seventeen"], "meaning": "Drake’s parents separated when he was five, leaving his mother as the sole breadwinner. Drake changed that when he became an actor on the TV series Degrassi, at the age of 15. Only after 2 years on the show, he could provide for his mom.", "annotation_id": "4887980", "url": "https://genius.com/4887980", "state": "accepted", "votes": 48, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "10 Bands", "line": "Yeah, shout goes out to Nike, checks all over me I need a FuelBand just to see how long the run has been", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, shout goes out to Nike, checks all over me", "I need a FuelBand just to see how long the run has been"], "meaning": "Drake wears a lot of Nike apparel, a brand represented by a check mark, so he literally means Nike “checks” all over him. The company produces a device called a FuelBand that tracks your activities (including running) – Drake needs one to see how long he’s been killin' it in the game.\n\nHowever, Nike signed a sponsorship deal with Drake, so their cheques are all over him as well.", "annotation_id": "4887918", "url": "https://genius.com/4887918", "state": "accepted", "votes": 104, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "10 Bands", "line": "All my watches always timeless, you can keep the diamonds Treatin’ Diamonds of Atlanta like it’s King of Diamonds", "vault_lines": ["All my watches always timeless, you can keep the diamonds", "Treatin' Diamonds of Atlanta like it's King of Diamonds"], "meaning": "Drake loves the Atlanta scene, and has mentioned the King of Diamonds (the Miami strip club) previously in “Miss Me:”\n\nCall the King of Diamonds and tell Chyna it’d be worth the flight\n\nHowever a new club, Diamonds of Atlanta replaced the  King of Diamonds – Drizzy’s habits haven’t changed.", "annotation_id": "4887850", "url": "https://genius.com/4887850", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "10 Bands", "line": "My ex asked me, “Where you movin’?” I said, ”On to better things”, yeah", "vault_lines": ["My ex asked me, \"Where you movin'?\" I said, \"On to better things\", yeah"], "meaning": "Drake must get this a lot, as his exes include Kiesha Chante, a friend from childhood, Jade Lee whom Drake raps about in “Karaoke” & “Look What You’ve Done,” and Zineb Samir whom he wrote “Best I Ever Had” for. The full list of his exes is extensive and can be viewed here.", "annotation_id": "4887725", "url": "https://genius.com/4887725", "state": "accepted", "votes": 122, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "10 Bands", "line": "I get boxes of free Jordan like I play for North Carolina How much I make off the deal, how the fuck should I know?", "vault_lines": ["I get boxes of free Jordan like I play for North Carolina", "How much I make off the deal, how the fuck should I know?"], "meaning": "NBA legend Michael Jordan played collegiately at the University of North Carolina. UNC’s basketball team now plays in Jordan’s iconic shoes.\n\n\n\nDrake really does get free Nikes – Jordans at least. He signed to Team Jordan and has already linked up with them to make several exclusive shoes. To brag about how much he makes off this Jordan deal he sarcastically says that he doesn’t know to make it seem like it is not a big deal for him.", "annotation_id": "4887719", "url": "https://genius.com/4887719", "state": "accepted", "votes": 55, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "10 Bands", "line": "I can tell ya how it happened I can tell ya ’bout them safe house nights out in Calabasas", "vault_lines": ["I can tell ya how it happened", "I can tell ya 'bout them safe house nights out in Calabasas"], "meaning": "As Drake mentioned on “2 On/Thotful,” he owns a safe house in Calabasas, California which he uses to escape from the realms of the media. You can expect him to have many stories from the times he has spent there.", "annotation_id": "4887705", "url": "https://genius.com/4887705", "state": "accepted", "votes": 79, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "10 Bands", "line": "Man, I told my city I’d be gone ’til November then November came Then I came, right back on my worst behav’", "vault_lines": ["Man, I told my city I'd be gone 'til November then November came", "Then I came, right back on my worst behav'"], "meaning": "Drake references both Wyclef Jean’s “Gone Til November” and his own song “Worst Behavior” from Nothing Was The Same. He always talk about being gone from Toronto for long spurts of time, but he remembers to come back and stunt for his city.\n\nWayne dropped a similar line on Drake’s “Miss Me” (though while Drake was presumably away on tour, Weezy was in prison):\n\nDamn, I’ll be gone ‘til November\nBut fuck it I ain’t trippin’, I know Drizzy gonna kill ‘em", "annotation_id": "4887683", "url": "https://genius.com/4887683", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "10 Bands", "line": "[Chorus] Ten bands, fifty bands, hunnid bands Fuck it, man, let’s just not even discuss it, man OMG, niggas sleep, I ain’t trippin’, I’ma let ’em sleep I ain’t trippin’, let ’em rest in peace", "vault_lines": ["Ten bands, fifty bands, hunnid bands", "Fuck it, man, let's just not even discuss it, man", "OMG, niggas sleep, I ain't trippin', I'ma let 'em sleep", "I ain't trippin', let 'em rest in peace"], "meaning": "Similar to Jay-Z, Drake has seen an exponential rise in his wealth. He’s gone from earning $10,000 to $50,000 to $100,000 for features and shows, and has too much money to talk about.\n\nHe could also be alluding to the amount of cash he spends in strip clubs, as J. Cole said on “Cole Summer”:\n\nThrowing thousands in the strip club with Drizzy\nDifference is I’m throwing four, he’s throwing fifty", "annotation_id": "4887636", "url": "https://genius.com/4887636", "state": "accepted", "votes": 182, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
