{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cheetah Print", "status": "done", "targets": 7, "clicked": 7, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-and-sexyy-red-cheetah-print-lyrics", "genius_title": "Cheetah Print"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fire & Desire", "line": "You just like my sidekick, I just wanna ride, fulfill all your desires Keep you in the front, never in the back and never on the side, uh (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["You just like my sidekick, I just wanna ride, fulfill all your desires", "Keep you in the front, never in the back and never on the side, uh", "I give you my voice", "I give you my fortune"], "meaning": "It’s not certain that Drake’s talking about Nicki here, but he did use similar terms of affection to refer to her on his 2009 song “Miss Me.” In the song, Drake rapped:\n\nI love Nicki Minaj, I told her I’d admit it\nI hope one day we get married just to say we fucking did it\nAnd girl I’m fucking serious, I’m with it if you with it\n\nIt seems like Drake still stands by his word. But Nicki’s a “boss ass bitch,” so she might not appreciate being considered his “sidekick.” He assures her that she will never be his “side” chick, though.", "annotation_id": "9078643", "url": "https://genius.com/9078643", "state": "accepted", "votes": 62, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fire & Desire", "line": "They throwin’ dirt on my old name Only gets worse when you know things", "vault_lines": ["Only gets worse when you know things", "They throwin' dirt on my old name"], "meaning": "Drake is rumoured to have been in relationships with the likes of Rihanna, Nebby, and Serena Williams. We can assume they know some personal things about him.\n\nIn songs like “Redemption,”  we’ve seen Drake struggle to maintain a relationship because his lovers find the skeletons in his closet.", "annotation_id": "9072875", "url": "https://genius.com/9072875", "state": "accepted", "votes": 119, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fire & Desire", "line": "Dedicate, I dedicate the world Yeah, oh I dedicate, I dedicate I give you my fortune I dedicate, I dedicate I dedicate, I dedicate I dedicate, I dedicate I dedicate, dedicate, dedicate I dedicate to you I dedicate, I dedicate I dedicate, I dedicate, oh yeah I dedicate, I dedicate to you", "vault_lines": ["Dedicate, I dedicate the world", "I give you my voice", "I give you my fortune", "I dedicate, dedicate, dedicate", "I dedicate to you", "I dedicate, I dedicate, oh yeah", "I dedicate, I dedicate to you"], "meaning": "The intro and outro of “Fire & Desire” is sampled from Brandy’s “I Dedicate (Part I),” the fifth track on the R&B singer’s 1994 self-titled debut album.\n\n“I Dedicate” is broken up into three parts on the album. On “I Dedicate (Part I)”, Brandy asks Jeff “Fuzzy” Young, a member of the R&B group Somethin' for the People, if she can give a quick shout out to the people who inspired her to sing. This list includes singers Whitney Houston, Stevie Wonder, and Aretha Franklin.\n\nWhile Brandy dedicated her song to people who influenced her singing career, Drake takes a more personal approach and dedicates the song to a special woman whom he has previously been involved with.", "annotation_id": "9072136", "url": "https://genius.com/9072136", "state": "accepted", "votes": 150, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fire & Desire", "line": "You never believe me Told you I got Zs for these other girls sleepin’ on ’em Girl, I’m sleepy Sometimes I’m so indecisive", "vault_lines": ["You never believe me", "Told you I got Zs for these other girls sleepin' on 'em", "Sometimes I'm so indecisive"], "meaning": "Drake doesn’t have “eyes” for the girls who don’t pay him any mind—he has “Zzz\"s for them. He’s not concerned about their whereabouts, but the woman he’s trying to win back over isn’t totally convinced.\n\n\n\nFighting for this woman’s love isn’t as easy as Drake thought it would be. Their inability to make a clear decision about their relationship makes Drake want to reach for a pillow and hit the lights. It’s worth it, but it’s exhausting.\n\nInterestingly enough, he once mentioned his feelings towards indecisiveness in a different manner on “Jungle”:\n\nThese days these new girls, they got me nervous\nThey go to school and do bottle service\nThey can’t decide, they keep switching majors\nBeing indecisive makes me anxious", "annotation_id": "9072038", "url": "https://genius.com/9072038", "state": "accepted", "votes": 98, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fire & Desire", "line": "You a real ass woman and I like it I don’t wanna fight it", "vault_lines": ["But you get real on a pill and I like it", "You a real ass woman and I like it", "I don't wanna fight it", "You a real ass woman and I like it, yeah", "But you a real ass woman and I like it"], "meaning": "Drake’s been vocal about his admiration for goal-oriented, ambitious ladies.\n\n\nI’ve always liked my women book and street smart — “Fancy”\n\nSound so smart like you graduated college, like you went to Yale but you probably went to Howard — “Make Me Proud”\n\nRemember when you had to take the bar exam, I drove in the snow for you — “How About Now”\n\n\nWhen she thrives, he thrives. They both feed off of each other’s positive energy. Drake’s fond of women with genuine souls… and possibly genuine bodies.", "annotation_id": "9071904", "url": "https://genius.com/9071904", "state": "accepted", "votes": 141, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fire & Desire", "line": "Look, you know I’m a rider, nothin’ left to hide Your other nigga tired Talk about you like you never leave his side But I don’t really buy it", "vault_lines": ["I don't wanna fight it", "Look, you know I'm a rider, nothin' left to hide", "Your other nigga tired", "Talk about you like you never leave his side", "But I don't really buy it", "But you a real ass woman and I like it", "I dedicate to you", "I dedicate, I dedicate to you"], "meaning": "This lyric may be directed at Nicki Minaj. In his Views interview with Zane Lowe, Drake said they don’t talk anymore, and while he didn’t comment as to why, it’s obvious the situation is a result of Drake’s beef with Nicki’s boyfriend, Meek Mill.\n\n“Rider” sounds like “writer\"—Meek accused Drake of not writing his own raps. This is also a play on \"right” and “left,” since Drizzy has “nothing left to hide.”", "annotation_id": "9071764", "url": "https://genius.com/9071764", "state": "accepted", "votes": 51, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fire & Desire", "line": "You don’t see the perks of this whole thing But you get real on a pill and I like it", "vault_lines": ["You don't see the perks of this whole thing", "But you get real on a pill and I like it", "You a real ass woman and I like it", "I don't wanna fight it", "But I don't really buy it", "You a real ass woman and I like it, yeah", "But you a real ass woman and I like it"], "meaning": "This is a play on words, “perks” sounds like “percs” which is short for percocets. Percocets give you a warm and fuzzy feeling similar to alcohol.\n\n\n\nWhile this girl  doesn’t like the situation she’s in, Drake likes it when she real and takes drugs.", "annotation_id": "9070928", "url": "https://genius.com/9070928", "state": "accepted", "votes": 86, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fire & Desire", "status": "done", "targets": 7, "clicked": 7, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-fire-and-desire-lyrics", "genius_title": "Fire & Desire"}
