{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Smile", "line": "I understand that you Afro I’m tryna get to your centric", "vault_lines": ["I understand that you Afro I'm tryna get to your centric"], "meaning": "A play on words. Drake basicially broke down Afrocentric.\n\nAfrocentric involves the African-American culture", "annotation_id": "24056642", "url": "https://genius.com/24056642", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Smile", "line": "That’s why I got a bottle of Champagne and then I sent it Over where you sitting, noticed, pretend you didn’t Along with the bottle was a note attached Here’s some tickets to my show you should go to that", "vault_lines": ["That's why I got a bottle of Champagne and then I sent it", "Over where you sitting, noticed, pretend you didn't", "Along with the bottle was a note attached", "Here's some tickets to my show you should go to that", "I should feel it everywhere"], "meaning": "The girl received a bottle of Champagne with an invitation to ChampagnePapi’s show. Drake seems reluctant to approach her and hopes this romantic gesture will demonstrate his thoughtfulness, talent and wealth.", "annotation_id": "5004825", "url": "https://genius.com/5004825", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Smile", "line": "She had a rapper break her heart, had to open her So she don’t even mess with rap, only spoken word Well, I’m a poet so you know it’s get her to going down", "vault_lines": ["It's for you, it's for you, it's for you, for you", "She had a rapper break her heart, had to open her", "So she don't even mess with rap, only spoken word", "Well, I'm a poet so you know it's get her to going down"], "meaning": "Drake doesn’t come across as the stereotypical “player” type like most rappers. He brings the art of rap back to rhythm and poetry which sets himself apart from the type of guy who broke her heart in the past. Drake’s eloquence will gain him entry into the girl’s heart and pants.\n\nThat sound like poetic justice, poetic justice", "annotation_id": "5004720", "url": "https://genius.com/5004720", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Smile", "line": "Ladies up north represent representing Ladies down south represent representing When the mic is in my hand I’m never hesitant My favorite jam back in the day was Eric B For President, it’s evident", "vault_lines": ["It's for you, it's for you, it's for you, for you", "Ladies up north represent representing", "Ladies down south represent representing", "When the mic is in my hand I'm never hesitant", "My favorite jam back in the day was Eric B For President, it's evident"], "meaning": "Drake flips the opening lines from A Tribe Called Quest’s “Steve Biko”, making it clear that he reps everywhere.\n\nLinden Boulevard represent, represent\nTribe Called Quest represent, represent\nWhen the mic is in my hand, I’m never hesitant\nMy favorite jam back in the day was Eric B for President\n\nEric B & Rakim’s “Eric B Is President” came out in 1986, the same year that Drake was born. The chances of Drizzy having heard it back in the day are slim. Still, it’s a nice shout out – to Tribe and Eric B & Rakim.\n\nSide Note: In an interview with Vanessa Jasey, Eric B named Drake as one of his favorite artists. The love goes both ways.", "annotation_id": "2641736", "url": "https://genius.com/2641736", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
