{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Teach U a Lesson (Freestyle)", "line": "I’ll wipe ya ass down like Boosie baby", "vault_lines": ["When you are wet and covered in sweat, I'll wipe ya ass down like Boosie baby"], "meaning": "“Wipe Me Down (Remix)” was a popular rap song by Lil Boosie.", "annotation_id": "279005", "url": "https://genius.com/279005", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Teach U a Lesson (Freestyle)", "status": "done", "targets": 1, "clicked": 1, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-teach-u-a-lesson-freestyle-lyrics", "genius_title": "Teach U a Lesson (Freestyle)"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Last Hope", "line": "Jealousy is something I haven’t felt in years There’s nobody around for me to be jealous of", "vault_lines": ["Jealousy is something I haven't felt in years", "There's nobody around for me to be jealous of"], "meaning": "This is Drake stripping jealousy down to basically nothing—not because he’s “above it,” but because there’s no one in his immediate world that even triggers comparison. It’s less about confidence and more about isolation disguised as clarity.\n\nIn the context of Drake early mixtape era work like The Comeback Season, this fits his pattern of positioning himself outside the usual competition structure of rap. He’s not really engaging with rivals here—he’s implying they’re not even present in his lane yet.\n\nSo the bar reads more like emotional geography than flexing: jealousy disappears because the environment doesn’t offer anything to measure against, not because he’s transcended it.", "annotation_id": "39646109", "url": "https://genius.com/39646109", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Last Hope", "line": "I bet you do a show in my city and no one cheers Even if you make the music that ladies and fellas love", "vault_lines": ["I bet you do a show in my city and no one cheers", "Even if you make the music that ladies and fellas love"], "meaning": "1: He’s kinda provoking his hometown for the cold atmosphere at the live concerts.\n\n2: He’s daring you to do a show with such a good vibe like he did. People there are so accustomed to him, aka he’s the best one at home, that when other’s come they won’t even stand a chance against him.", "annotation_id": "70493", "url": "https://genius.com/70493", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
