{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "6 Man", "line": "Yeah, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, work the night shift"], "meaning": "When Drake does say in his songs “Yeah” usually is because is going to bring you in a mental journey, like how he did in this song", "annotation_id": "32818160", "url": "https://genius.com/32818160", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "6 Man", "line": "I’m here to fuck with niggas’ souls, my heart is cold It’s prolly ’cause I’m from the snow, with all my WOEs", "vault_lines": ["I'm here to fuck with niggas' souls, my heart is cold", "It's prolly 'cause I'm from the snow, with all my WOEs"], "meaning": "Drake is “fuckin with niggas souls” through his music. Music is a tool that controls people’s motives, wether consciously or unconsciously. And Drake’s motives in his music are generally materialistic and promiscuous- all pertaining to the ego. Ego robs one of spirit/soul. Drake’s music is so powerful because of how many avid listeners he has. And “from the Snow” means he’s from Canada, where it’s generally snowy. Also, With all his woes (his friends in the 6).", "annotation_id": "4958734", "url": "https://genius.com/4958734", "state": "verified", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "6 Man", "line": "I’m here to fuck with niggas’ souls, my heart is cold It’s prolly ’cause I’m from the snow, with all my WOEs", "vault_lines": ["I'm here to fuck with niggas' souls, my heart is cold", "It's prolly 'cause I'm from the snow, with all my WOEs"], "meaning": "WOEs stands for Working on Excellence. This is the name of the group of friends Drake hangs out with in the “The Six”. Think about it, im with my WOEs, basically everyone this kid surrounds himself is working towards excellence.", "annotation_id": "4946133", "url": "https://genius.com/4946133", "state": "verified", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "6 Man", "line": "(Lou)", "vault_lines": ["Boomin out in South Gwinnett like Lou Will'", "6 Man like Lou Will'", "Two girls and they get along like I'm— (Lou)", "Like I'm Lou Will', I just got the new deal"], "meaning": "Fun Fact: The “Louuuu” chant originated in Vancouver, BC, Canada when NHL goalie Roberto Luongo was apart of the Vancouver Canucks. After big saves in games, fans would chant “Louuuu” exactly like the chant Lou Williams receives after knocking down shots.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kZK5Cj5M3Dk", "annotation_id": "4929141", "url": "https://genius.com/4929141", "state": "verified", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "6 Man", "line": "No ho shit, no fuckin’ ho shit, save that for your shit I don’t need no-fuckin’-body, I run my own shit I told you, thought I told you, you didn’t listen", "vault_lines": ["No ho shit, no fuckin' ho shit, save that for your shit", "I don't need no-fuckin'-body, I run my own shit", "I told you, thought I told you, you didn't listen"], "meaning": "Jay Z refers to himself as “hov” and this line is making a reference to declining Jay Z’s offers.", "annotation_id": "4925740", "url": "https://genius.com/4925740", "state": "verified", "votes": -7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "6 Man", "line": "I’m on it, I’m like MacGyver, I’m Michael Myers I kill careers and cut the lights off, this shit is frightenin’ I knew it would end up like this, I’m fuckin’ psychic", "vault_lines": ["I'm on it, I'm like MacGyver, I'm Michael Myers", "I kill careers and cut the lights off, this shit is frightenin'", "I knew it would end up like this, I'm fuckin' psychic"], "meaning": "“Michael Myers” could also be a reference to legendary actor Mike Myers who’s from Toronto", "annotation_id": "4922950", "url": "https://genius.com/4922950", "state": "verified", "votes": -25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "6 Man", "line": "(Lou)", "vault_lines": ["Boomin out in South Gwinnett like Lou Will'", "6 Man like Lou Will'", "Two girls and they get along like I'm— (Lou)", "Like I'm Lou Will', I just got the new deal"], "meaning": "When Lou Williams shoots a three pointer for the Toronto Raptors, the fans chant “Louuu” in the same tone Drake uses here.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GoprAeCWQS8", "annotation_id": "4904934", "url": "https://genius.com/4904934", "state": "accepted", "votes": 48, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "6 Man", "line": "You know the truth, let’s not pretend, I’m not your friend Not your guy, I’m not your buddy, show no love’", "vault_lines": ["You know the truth, let's not pretend, I'm not your friend", "Not your guy, I'm not your buddy, show no love'"], "meaning": "For a man with a relatively short career, and for someone who is known as somewhat of a sensitive soul, he certainly has a long list of beefs. Drake doesn’t make new friends.\n\nThe use of “friend…guy…buddy” is a South Park reference – in that show the terms are frequently used by Canadian characters\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zuQK6t2Esng", "annotation_id": "4888742", "url": "https://genius.com/4888742", "state": "accepted", "votes": 63, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "6 Man", "line": "I know they wanna see me go, I’m on a roll I mean, I’m back on this again, I’m here again", "vault_lines": ["I know they wanna see me go, I'm on a roll", "I mean, I'm back on this again, I'm here again", "Man, I'm back on this again, I'm here again"], "meaning": "Drake is certainly on a roll. Billboard named him amongst their 40 under 40 power players in the game. Every time he drops a single, or even a feature, the internet latches on to it and plays it ad-nauseum. He is one of the most sought after features in the industry, with various outlets reporting he could make anywhere between $60,000 and $200,000 for a feature or a hook.", "annotation_id": "4888734", "url": "https://genius.com/4888734", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "6 Man", "line": "No ho shit, no fuckin’ ho shit, save that for your shit I don’t need no-fuckin’-body, I run my own shit I told you, thought I told you, you didn’t listen", "vault_lines": ["No ho shit, no fuckin' ho shit, save that for your shit", "I don't need no-fuckin'-body, I run my own shit", "I told you, thought I told you, you didn't listen"], "meaning": "This brings us back to lines from Jay Z’s “Anything”:\n\nDon’t follow no n—, that’s ho shit man\nStand on your own two, do your shit man\n\nDrake creates his own path and doesn’t need anyone’s assistance to make it. He has been predicting his success since his very first mixtape.", "annotation_id": "4888720", "url": "https://genius.com/4888720", "state": "accepted", "votes": 37, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "6 Man", "line": "I’m here to fuck with niggas’ souls, my heart is cold It’s prolly ’cause I’m from the snow, with all my WOEs", "vault_lines": ["I'm here to fuck with niggas' souls, my heart is cold", "It's prolly 'cause I'm from the snow, with all my WOEs"], "meaning": "The reason Drake likes to be on top is to mess with all those below him. There’s no wonder he’s cold-hearted when he’s from Toronto, a very chilly place. “Woes” refers to his group of friends.", "annotation_id": "4888391", "url": "https://genius.com/4888391", "state": "pending", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "6 Man", "line": "Man, I’m back on this again, I’m here again I didn’t do this fuckin’ tape for CNN I am not tryna win awards, that shit looked forced, it’s nothin’ like this", "vault_lines": ["I mean, I'm back on this again, I'm here again", "Man, I'm back on this again, I'm here again", "I didn't do this fuckin' tape for CNN", "I am not tryna win awards, that shit looked forced, it's nothin' like this"], "meaning": "He explored this sentiment extensively on “Trophies”.\n\nDrake isn’t here to put on a show and would rather appeal to his fans than “The Academy”. His goal isn’t to win awards, but is simply to produce good music. Ironically, he does have 36 awards to his name.\n\nIt is also a possible subliminal at Pusha T. In May 2014, CNN aired a piece called “Brother’s Keeper” which documented the rise of Clipse and the eventual decision by No Malice to move away from coke rap.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vK8e9F4ZzEI", "annotation_id": "4888212", "url": "https://genius.com/4888212", "state": "accepted", "votes": 44, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "6 Man", "line": "Young, but I’m makin’ millions to work the night shift", "vault_lines": ["Young, but I'm makin' millions to work the night shift", "Yeah, work the night shift", "Work, work the night shift"], "meaning": "Drake could be out partying, but he’d rather spend his nights working on his music. He may have picked up his work ethic from Lil Wayne, someone whose insatiable appetite for rap music is legendary in the industry.", "annotation_id": "4888191", "url": "https://genius.com/4888191", "state": "accepted", "votes": 111, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "6 Man", "line": "I’m on it, I’m like MacGyver, I’m Michael Myers I kill careers and cut the lights off, this shit is frightenin’ I knew it would end up like this, I’m fuckin’ psychic", "vault_lines": ["I'm on it, I'm like MacGyver, I'm Michael Myers", "I kill careers and cut the lights off, this shit is frightenin'", "I knew it would end up like this, I'm fuckin' psychic"], "meaning": "MacGyver is a secret agent known for his scientific resourcefulness. He could get out of any complex situation with the help of everyday objects. Michael Myers is the main antagonist in the Halloween film series. He’s an evil serial killer who murders innocent teenagers.\n\nCombine the resourcefulness of MacGyver and the evil nature of Michael Myers, and you get Drake. He “kills” other artists' careers by being so successful. To “cut the lights off” is a common trope used in the slasher horror film genre, and also refers to the flashing lights associated with the celebrity world. Drake will cut off your source of stardom, and you’ll be lost in the dark.", "annotation_id": "4888186", "url": "https://genius.com/4888186", "state": "accepted", "votes": 60, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "6 Man", "line": "[Outro] If you were worried about where I’ve been or who I saw or What club I went to with the homies Baby, don’t worry, you know that you got me I’ve never worried about where I’m at or who I saw or What club I go to with the homies Baby, don’t worry, I know that they got me (6ix)", "vault_lines": ["If you were worried about where", "I've been or who I saw or", "What club I went to with the homies", "Baby, don't worry, you know that you got me", "I've never worried about where", "I'm at or who I saw or", "What club I go to with the homies", "Baby, don't worry, I know that they got me (6ix)"], "meaning": "This is an interpolation of The Roots' “You Got Me.” The song features Erykah Badu, whom Drake is no stranger to.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MJCHeEQV454", "annotation_id": "4888081", "url": "https://genius.com/4888081", "state": "accepted", "votes": 141, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "6 Man", "line": "And I might go DeMarcus Cousins out in public", "vault_lines": ["And I might go DeMarcus Cousins out in public"], "meaning": "DeMarcus Cousins is an elite center who plays for the Sacramento Kings. His nickname is “Boogie,” so perhaps Drake will go out and “get down” at the club.\n\nCousins is also known to have a short fuse. He notoriously pulled his teammate, Isaiah Thomas, away from shaking hands with Chris Paul after the Clippers defeated the Kings. Drake refuses to shake hands with “the other team.”", "annotation_id": "4888054", "url": "https://genius.com/4888054", "state": "accepted", "votes": 105, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "6 Man", "line": "I am in the Matrix, and I just took the blue pill", "vault_lines": ["I am in the Matrix, and I just took the blue pill"], "meaning": "In The Matrix, Neo is given the choice between two pills:\n\nThis is your last chance. After this there is no turning back. You take the blue pill: the story ends, you wake up in your bed and believe whatever you want to believe. You take the red pill: you stay in Wonderland and I show you how deep the rabbit hole goes.\n\nSeems like Drizzy would rather wake up in bed with 2 girls like Lou Will.\n\nLife is pretty good in Drake’s reality right now, so he has no real reason to opt out, and is fine continuing to take the blue pill.", "annotation_id": "4887966", "url": "https://genius.com/4887966", "state": "accepted", "votes": 101, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "6 Man", "line": "Boomin out in South Gwinnett like Lou Will’ 6 Man like Lou Will’ Two girls and they get along like I’m— (Lou) Like I’m Lou Will’, I just got the new deal", "vault_lines": ["Boomin out in South Gwinnett like Lou Will'", "6 Man like Lou Will'", "Two girls and they get along like I'm— (Lou)", "Like I'm Lou Will', I just got the new deal"], "meaning": "“Boomin” refers to Atlanta producer Metro Boomin, who frequently creates music in South Gwinnett’s Tree Sound Studios. A few months after this song was released, Boomin, Drake and Future rented the studio for 6 days to create their collaborative project, What A Time To Be Alive.\n\nLouis Williams, a combo guard from South Gwinnett HS in Snellville, Georgia, was the 6th man for the Toronto Raptors—a team Drake has not only referenced before, but works for as an executive. Williams won the 2014-15 NBA Sixth Man of the Year award 2 months after this song was released.\n\nAside from basketball, Williams is reportedly doing his best Young Thug impersonation and is in a relationship with two women at the same time.\n\nAlthough the two have many similarities, Drake is a different type of 6 man—he runs Toronto, commonly referred to as The 6.\n\nThe 6 ain’t friendly but it’s where I lay up", "annotation_id": "4887862", "url": "https://genius.com/4887862", "state": "accepted", "votes": 224, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "6 Man", "line": "Fieri, I’m in the kitchen, I’m a magician", "vault_lines": ["Fieri, I'm in the kitchen, I'm a magician"], "meaning": "Drake is cooking up hits like celebrity chef Guy Fieri crafts meals in the kitchen. This isn’t the first time Drake has compared himself to a chef:\n\nBeen cookin' with the sauce, chef, curry with the pot, boy\n\nBack in Dec. 2012, Guy actually gave Drizzy a cooking lesson while in Toronto filming for his TV show Diners, Drive-Ins and Dives.\n\nhttp://instagram.com/p/Sv2cLlRZdD/", "annotation_id": "4887852", "url": "https://genius.com/4887852", "state": "accepted", "votes": 66, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
