{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Blue Tint", "line": "Some niggas bitter with life and they hate me They wanna put knife in my ribs, woah", "vault_lines": ["Some niggas bitter with life and they hate me", "They wanna put knife in my ribs, woah"], "meaning": "Drake suggests that jealousy and resentment can make people want to harm or betray him.", "annotation_id": "40874877", "url": "https://genius.com/40874877", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Blue Tint", "line": "President doin’ us in", "vault_lines": ["President doin' us in"], "meaning": "Drake is expressing his displeasure with the then current President of the United States, Donald Trump.\n\nDrake is no stranger to showing disapproval for the Trump administration,  going so far as to call him a “fucking idiot” live in concert", "annotation_id": "28501349", "url": "https://genius.com/28501349", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Blue Tint", "line": "And I could put that on the twins, woah", "vault_lines": ["And I could put that on the twins, woah"], "meaning": "Drake could be referring to Swedish Twins Elizabeth and Victoria Lejonhjärta. They have worked with the Rapper numerous times such as appearing in album art for Drake’s 2016 album Views and Appearing in two of his videos for the song “Nice for What” and the short film Please Forgive Me.\n\n\n\nDrake has even gone as far as to get a tattoo dedicated to them.", "annotation_id": "15386758", "url": "https://genius.com/15386758", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Blue Tint", "line": "She finish at 6 but then say she got court in the morning to fight for her kid I told her I’d pray for the kid", "vault_lines": ["She finish at 6 but then say she got court in the morning to fight for her kid", "I told her I'd pray for the kid"], "meaning": "Drake is saying that he will pray for his girl’s custody battle with her baby’s father. However, he makes it a point that he would “pray” for the kid instead of “pay” for the kid since he believes that he is guaranteed the court will grant him custody.\n\nThis may relate to Drake’s own struggles since Pusha T supposedly exposed him on his diss track, “The Story of Adidon” for not claiming his child that he had with a pornstar. He would then reveal the reasons why he “hid” his child on “Emotionless”:\n\nI wasn’t hidin' my kid from the world\nI was hidin' the world from my kid", "annotation_id": "14900047", "url": "https://genius.com/14900047", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Blue Tint", "line": "I had her on ice but then I watched the ice get thin Now, does she sink or swim?", "vault_lines": ["I watched the ice get so thin", "Now, does she sink or does she swim, now?", "I had her on ice but then", "I watched the ice get thin", "Now, does she sink or swim?"], "meaning": "Being on “thin ice” means a situation is close to the breaking point and any mistake could lead to collapse. “Ice” in this scenario could also be synonymous with the appearance of diamonds: the girl only used Drake for his fame and wealth.\n\nThese lines could be a possible reference to his track from More Life: “Ice Melts”, which is also produced by Supah Mario.\n\nDrake is saying the relationship is “sink or swim” at this point—so it’s 50/50 if it will work out.", "annotation_id": "14881746", "url": "https://genius.com/14881746", "state": "accepted", "votes": 73, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Blue Tint", "line": "Mario", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This is the producer tag of Supah Mario, who has worked with Drake previously on “Ice Melts” from More Life.", "annotation_id": "14878692", "url": "https://genius.com/14878692", "state": "accepted", "votes": 63, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Blue Tint", "line": "My window got blue in the tint (Skrrt)", "vault_lines": ["My window got blue in the tint (Skrrt)"], "meaning": "Drake is no stranger to Mercedes-Benz vehicles, most which feature a blue-ish tint on the windows and windshield that can be seen from certain angles.\n\nIn 2017, Drake purchased a Mercedes SLR McLaren, which may be the car he’s referring to, as it seems to have a certain tint in the photo below.\n\n\n\nOn his “30 for 30 Freestyle”, Drake also mentions buying a Mercedes Maybach Pullman:\n\nI just got me the Mercedes Pullman\nYou niggas never heard of it, you gotta hit up Google\n\nDrake is also rumored to have put down a $250k deposit on the Mercedes Maybach Vision.", "annotation_id": "14878070", "url": "https://genius.com/14878070", "state": "accepted", "votes": 36, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Blue Tint", "line": "Top of the charts, back in they hearts Nigga, he strikes again, woah", "vault_lines": ["Nigga, he strikes again, woah", "Top of the charts, back in they hearts"], "meaning": "Drake is referring to his recent success atop the Billboard Hot 100 in which both “God’s Plan” and “Nice for What” landed at #1. The former was able to stay atop the Billboard Hot 100 for 11 straight weeks before being knocked out by the latter, which then remained at #1 for 7 non-consecutive weeks. With those two mega hits, Drake became the first artist in the U.S. to replace a No. 1 debut with another No. 1 debut, which is likely what he is referring to by the phrase “strikes again.”\n\nBefore those two songs, Drake was in the back of many people’s minds, as his 2017 releases were limited to just a single, “Signs”, and a March “playlist”, More Life. With a couple high profile releases, Drake returned to the hearts of many fans, both casual and die hard.", "annotation_id": "14876989", "url": "https://genius.com/14876989", "state": "accepted", "votes": 51, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Blue Tint", "line": "(Blue faces)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "“Blue faces” are a reference to the new $100 dollar bills, which features a blue stripe down the middle. This stripe serves as security, and ensures the bill isn’t a fake.\n\n\n\nFuture & Drake keep a blue theme with both their money and their blue tinted diamonds. The latter has been known to be very expensive, as select blue diamonds have been priced at $250 million. The color is known as a sign of authenticity on both, and blue diamonds are a sign of wealth and luxury, while blue dollars boast abundance of money. In short, these two are flexing their superior income with their bills and jewelry.", "annotation_id": "14876835", "url": "https://genius.com/14876835", "state": "accepted", "votes": 86, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Blue Tint", "line": "Way this shit set up I live like Ronaldo But I never been in Madrid, woah", "vault_lines": ["Way this shit set up I live like Ronaldo", "But I never been in Madrid, woah"], "meaning": "Cristiano Ronaldo is a football player who, at the release of this song, played for the Spanish club Real Madrid, a team based in the capital of Spain.\n\nIn addition, Ronaldo is widely considered as one of the best football players of this generation, and is also in the debate for all-time best players. Similarly, Drake compares his position in the rap game to Ronaldo’s own legacy.\n\n\n\nDrake furthers this connection by using a little football terminology. Ronaldo plays the forward position, which means the midfielders assist (“set up”) the goals for him.\n\nLiving like the player could also allude to the amount of money they make, with Drake at an estimated $100 million net worth and Ronaldo at around $400 million. With all the money these two have amassed, they are obviously living comfortably.", "annotation_id": "14876321", "url": "https://genius.com/14876321", "state": "accepted", "votes": 167, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Blue Tint", "line": "What a time this is (Woah) To be alive for this shit (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["What a time this is (Woah)", "To be alive for this shit (Yeah)"], "meaning": "This line is a reference to the 2015 collaborative project between Drake and Future, titled What A Time to Be Alive. The commercial mixtape went on to become certified platinum by selling over 1,000,000 copies. Drake and Future have been working together since 2011, when they combined for Future’s hit “Tony Montana”, so it’s fitting for Drizzy to recognize their musical history together.", "annotation_id": "14876239", "url": "https://genius.com/14876239", "state": "accepted", "votes": 93, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
