{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Chicago", "line": "Too early, maybe later you can show me things", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "In this line he is guessing that he went to fast, and asked the girl too early and she has not have forgotten her previous relationship. He is saying maybe if he was more patient he could have a chance with here.", "annotation_id": "33873013", "url": "https://genius.com/33873013", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Chicago", "line": "Elevator up to the room", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This lyric is a genius storytelling line from Drake. As he states that he elevators up to his destination room. This links back to Drake’s history of bragging about staying in fancy hotels. With the history of Drake bragging about these hotels in mind we can deduce that Drake is within one of said Hotels and Drake is a man of wealth and fanciness so he does not take the stairs like a peasant. He takes the elevator instead. It’s a lot more fancy. And why an elevator specifically?\nBecause they take you up and down building floors. Hence why he said Elevator up to the room because that’s what elevators are for.", "annotation_id": "33071242", "url": "https://genius.com/33071242", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Chicago", "line": "Ayy, truck to the plane to the truck Truck to the hotel lobby Me, I go through underground garages", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Here Drake states the following:\n“Ayy, truck to the plane to the truck\nTruck to the hotel lobby\nMe, I go through underground garages”\n\nThis lyric is actually genius because here Drake says he goes from truck to plane then back to truck This could be a genius doubleentendre. His first line might signify that Drake travels with trucks because he’s that amazing to plane because he can fly people out and he himself out to places far away then travel by truck again. His second line says that he goes to hotels in his truck. Drake has infamousely bragged about Hotels in plenty of songs before such as in Trophies so it means he goes to grand hotels with a grand entrance too. He also goes through underground garages as he is quite the silly sneaky goose. Drake does that because he moves around in silence without anyone knowing when he’ll strike. Drake says that he can be sneaky and he can strike with a flash of glamour and the second meaning is that Drake probably really likes Trucks. Because that’s what’s unique about Drake. Other rappers pull up in Benzes, Mercedes, Lambos and Drake pulls up with a fucking truck to accommodate this massive penis energy. And I agree. Trucks are fucking awesome. Thanks for shouting out Trucks Drake :D", "annotation_id": "33071191", "url": "https://genius.com/33071191", "state": "pending", "votes": -8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Chicago", "line": "She said, “Babe, I think there was a typo” Nah, girl, I got it, that’s light though I could show you bigger things than that", "vault_lines": ["She go everywhere that I go"], "meaning": "Here  Drake basically says that the girl he was with couldn’t pay for the bill but Drake can because he’s rich. Typical Drake stuff. However because of more recent events the second part might have actually been a double entendre. The first meaning is Drake’s wealth as in Big Whips, Big Cribs etc. And the second is his big you know what. To quote Family Matters “There’s only Big D and there’s Video Proof”. So it seems like Drake was referring to 2 types of big things he could show to this girl.", "annotation_id": "32870071", "url": "https://genius.com/32870071", "state": "pending", "votes": -3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Chicago", "line": "Lot of people tryna take us viral I’m just tryin’ to have a nice night though", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "People are always trying to peep who the next relationship a celebrity has, and many try to get the picture to make it go viral, showing the world who they’re with now.", "annotation_id": "24869215", "url": "https://genius.com/24869215", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Chicago", "line": "Hit another one, it goes green Must’ve changed phones on the team ’Member when you let me in between That was 2017", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake uses an iPhone, any message sent from iPhone to a non-apple device will show up as green, instead of the iPhone to iPhone blue. If it was blue, now its green, this person probably either switched numbers or upgraded phones, thus ‘changed phone on the team’.\n\n\n\nSimultaneously, Drake could be referencing his 2017 song “Free Smoke,” where he said:\n\nI drunk text J-Lo\nOld number, so it bounce back", "annotation_id": "19392926", "url": "https://genius.com/19392926", "state": "accepted", "votes": 98, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Chicago", "line": "Shower up and then we hit the club", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "In his 2011 Complex cover story, Drake told the interviewer that he would have liked to do the interview at his apartment but he was getting installed the most luxurious addition to his bathroom: “an experience shower”.\n\nIt’s a shower that’s lit by all LED lights. It has 10 jets, an overhead, and it sprays out lavender or whatever scents you want. It’s something I’ve always wanted.\n\nHis Toronto mansion, designed by Ferris Rafauli, has a huge tub with a skylight above, along with two rooftop terrace areas with an outdoor hot tub that offers guests to soak their feet in.\n\n\n\nDrake's 4,000 lbs marble bathtub (est. worth around $30,000-$50,000).", "annotation_id": "19190766", "url": "https://genius.com/19190766", "state": "accepted", "votes": 53, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Chicago", "line": "All good, Chubbs will look around Find one that seem my type That my dawg and he know what I like He done found me plenty in my life", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake is referring to his close friend and head of security Nessel Beezer, who mainly goes by the alias “Chubbs” or “OVO Chubbs”.\n\nIn these few lines, Drake explains how Chubbs has been able to come across plenty of women that Drake finds attractive.", "annotation_id": "19185287", "url": "https://genius.com/19185287", "state": "accepted", "votes": 98, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Chicago", "line": "Problem is, I meet a girl tonight Then I go and treat her too nice Galleria credit card swipes I don’t even know if she a wife", "vault_lines": ["She go everywhere that I go"], "meaning": "Galleria is an upscale mall in Houston, TX, a city where Drake frequently raps about and visits.\n\nDrake is saying he is too nice to women who may just be using him for his fame and wealth. Hence why they are using his credit card at malls to shop even though he doesn’t know if they could ever be his wife or if they’re a wife to someone else.", "annotation_id": "19179974", "url": "https://genius.com/19179974", "state": "accepted", "votes": 90, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Chicago", "line": "Pistol on J for survival Lot of people gunnin’ for the title", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "In these lines, Drake first states and refers to his person security carrying a gun for his protection.\n\nIn the next line, he uses the previous to execute his punchline about other rappers who are out overtake him in the music industry. There are many people who are out to get Drake knocked off his perch at the top of the music industry, and potentially also want him dead. We know that Drake his people who want him dead from the line in his song “Mob Ties” from his 2018 Scorpion Album:\n\nThey want me gone but dont know why\n\nAlso from his lyrics in “I’m Upset”. a single from the album Scorpion, where Drake, in different parts of the song raps these lyrics:\n\nFifty thousand on my head, its disrespect\nHunnid thousand on my head, its disrespect and also\nHalf a million on my head I can accept", "annotation_id": "19176406", "url": "https://genius.com/19176406", "state": "accepted", "votes": 57, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Chicago", "line": "AMEX had a limit in the past I had plenty women in the past I done plenty sinnin’ in the past You don’t need to know, but you can ask", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Reminiscing about previous times, Drake reflects on changes in affection and financial circumstances. Addressing his current love interest, he highlights plenty of former relationships despite spending limits on his AMEX or American Express credit card.\n\nFor most consumers, credit card companies impose limits on the amount that one can spend each month. As a product of his established wealth, Drake has since moved on to the infamous American Express Centurion “black card,” an invitation-only charge card with no spending limits.\n\nMoving to the present, Drake finds perspective in examining past financial challenges but does not seek to detail misdeeds from lost love.", "annotation_id": "19176146", "url": "https://genius.com/19176146", "state": "accepted", "votes": 81, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Chicago", "line": "But I do know one thing though Women, they come they go Saturday through Sunday, Monday Monday through Sunday, yo Maybe I’ll love you one day Maybe we’ll someday grow ’Til then, I’ll sit my drunk ass on that runway On this one way", "vault_lines": ["She go everywhere that I go", "They go everywhere that I go"], "meaning": "Drake pays tribute to Eminem by interpolating his May 2002 song “Superman” but with slightly changed lyrics:\n\nBut I do know one thing though\nBitches, they come, they go\nSaturday through Sunday, Monday\nMonday through Sunday, yo\nMaybe I’ll love you one day\nMaybe we’ll someday grow\n‘Til then just sit your drunk ass on that fuckin’ runway, ho\n\nIn Eminem’s song, he takes a very aggressive tone. “Superman” was written in the wake of Eminem’s divorce and his falling out with Mariah Carey, with whom he allegedly had a brief relationship. In the chorus, Eminem is speaking to his admirer, who is likely Mariah, and he reminds the woman that she is dispensable. If she acts out, there are plenty of women in line that are ready to take her place.\n\nIn contrast, Drake’s interpretation of the lyrics is melancholic. He has grown tired of quick relationships and is looking for something more serious, but his current lifestyle makes that impossible. In Drake’s version, the “runway” is an airport runway, where he has boarded a one-way flight to his next show.", "annotation_id": "19173768", "url": "https://genius.com/19173768", "state": "accepted", "votes": 586, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Chicago", "line": "Two-thirty, baby, won’t you meet me by The Bean?", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "In accordance with the track’s title, Giveon drops multiple iconic characteristics of the track’s titular city.\n\nFirstly, Cloud Gate, known by its popular name “The Chicago Bean,” is a public art sculpture designed by Indian-British sculptor Anish Kapoor that was first unveiled in 2004 in Millennium Park, Chicago. The sculpture has become an iconic piece of Chicago and is one of the most popular tourist locations in the city.\n\n\n\nSecondly, Chicago’s nickname is “The Windy City.” While this nickname is usually attributed to Chicago’s freezing cold temperatures due to the winds coming from Lake Michigan, the name is thought to have been  actually derived in the 1800s with politicians in the city blowing “hot air,” which is a saying for spewing lots of words without any actual substance.", "annotation_id": "19173734", "url": "https://genius.com/19173734", "state": "accepted", "votes": 239, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Chicago", "status": "done", "targets": 16, "clicked": 16, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-and-giveon-chicago-freestyle-lyrics", "genius_title": "Chicago Freestyle"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gen 5", "line": "Cause you do not come home with no blackened eye", "vault_lines": ["'Cause you do not come home with no blackened eye"], "meaning": "she doesn’t come home with a bruise on her eye\n\nthats right", "annotation_id": "39780544", "url": "https://genius.com/39780544", "state": "pending", "votes": -8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gen 5", "line": "And you know I call you my baby girl No wonder that you been feeling pacified, yeah", "vault_lines": ["And you know I call you my baby girl", "No wonder that you been feeling pacified, yeah"], "meaning": "Drake is so popular and famous that his girl feels like she is put in a very passive position in their relationship.\n\nThe play on words here is with “baby” and “pacificy” as pacifier is given to babies so they can suck on it and calm down/stop crying.", "annotation_id": "39851893", "url": "https://genius.com/39851893", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gen 5", "line": "Yeah, how many nights can we get dressed up? Back and forth over some Italian wine", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, how many nights can we get dressed up?", "Back and forth over some Italian wine"], "meaning": "Drake points out him and his group of people have been going out (more likely partying) for too many nights in a row and seemingly doesn’t want it to go on any longer by questioning.", "annotation_id": "39800546", "url": "https://genius.com/39800546", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gen 5", "line": "Take that arrow and shoot it right through my heart", "vault_lines": ["Take that arrow and shoot it right through my heart"], "meaning": "Cupid/Amor, the Roman God of love and affection and Son of Mars and Venus is portrayed in Ancient Mythology with a bow and arrow having the power to make those fall in love whom he strikes an arrow in the heart.\n\n\n\nCupid depicted in Raphael’s Triumph of Galatea (1512)", "annotation_id": "39792339", "url": "https://genius.com/39792339", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gen 5", "line": "Swear my daddy got me a Christmas gift It’s a Gen5 and that bitch is modified", "vault_lines": ["Swear my daddy got me a Christmas gift", "It's a Gen5 and that bitch is modified"], "meaning": "A “Gen5,” refers to a fifth generation Glock handgun. They come in either the 17 or the 19 models, both available in Gen5. The 17 is full size, the 19 is compact enough to carry daily. Glock released the fifth generation in 2017 with a cleaner trigger, flared mag well for faster reloads, ambidextrous slide stop, and a Marksman barrel that increases accuracy over the previous gens.\n\nModified means it’s been taken past factory spec. Extended clip, lightweight trigger, or even the popular federally illegal “switch,” attachment.", "annotation_id": "39780501", "url": "https://genius.com/39780501", "state": "pending", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gen 5", "status": "done", "targets": 5, "clicked": 5, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-gen-5-lyrics", "genius_title": "Gen 5"}
