{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Madonna", "line": "You could be big as Madonna Just get in the car and then let’s touch the road Don’t make other plans", "vault_lines": ["You could be big as Madonna", "Just get in the car and then let's touch the road", "Don't make other plans"], "meaning": "This song is about ex girlfriend, Canadian singer Keshia Chante. He references this line in their song “Fallen” released in 2009.", "annotation_id": "8362847", "url": "https://genius.com/8362847", "state": "verified", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Madonna", "line": "[Produced by Noah “40” Shebib]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This song (and “Legend”) sample Ginuwine’s “So Anxious”, which can be heard towards the end of the track around 2:20. The specific lines sampled are:\n\n[Soon as your shift] is over\nAnd I’ll be waiting, ‘cause I can’t sleep for reminiscing\n\nAgain, it is echoing Drake’s plea for his girl to submit.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DHpUtOcwhyU", "annotation_id": "7643774", "url": "https://genius.com/7643774", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Madonna", "line": "Say you get up early, you work for the man Well, he’ll understand Pull up, I’m pullin’ up on you in ten Already on ten", "vault_lines": ["Say you get up early, you work for the man", "Pull up, I'm pullin' up on you in ten"], "meaning": "He’s ON-10, and should be arriving within 10mins", "annotation_id": "6578115", "url": "https://genius.com/6578115", "state": "verified", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Madonna", "line": "Got to remind me again where you stay Even though I think I know the way But, you know, just in case I miss the road Pulling up on you in ten just be ready to go", "vault_lines": ["Pull up, I'm pullin' up on you in ten", "Got to remind me again where you stay", "Even though I think I know the way", "But, you know, just in case I miss the road", "Pulling up on you in ten just be ready to go"], "meaning": "Pulling up on you on ten just be ready to go", "annotation_id": "5031157", "url": "https://genius.com/5031157", "state": "verified", "votes": 7, "second_sense": false, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Madonna", "line": "Got to remind me again where you stay Even though I think I know the way But, you know, just in case I miss the road Pulling up on you in ten just be ready to go", "vault_lines": ["Pull up, I'm pullin' up on you in ten", "Got to remind me again where you stay", "Even though I think I know the way", "But, you know, just in case I miss the road", "Pulling up on you in ten just be ready to go"], "meaning": "Got to remind me again where you stay\nEven though I think I know the way but just in case I miss the road\nPulling up on you just be ready to go", "annotation_id": "5015879", "url": "https://genius.com/5015879", "state": "verified", "votes": -4, "second_sense": false, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Madonna", "line": "Got to remind me again where you stay Even though I think I know the way But, you know, just in case I miss the road Pulling up on you in ten just be ready to go", "vault_lines": ["Pull up, I'm pullin' up on you in ten", "Got to remind me again where you stay", "Even though I think I know the way", "But, you know, just in case I miss the road", "Pulling up on you in ten just be ready to go"], "meaning": "He’s about to pick up the girl for their evening together, and it’s been so long since he’s see her he needs a little GPS boost to get to the spot. The move is not to linger in the area or make unnecessary stops, but to pull up and dip.", "annotation_id": "5014833", "url": "https://genius.com/5014833", "state": "verified", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Madonna", "line": "Wrote it in code then wrote it in stone So they’ll never know But I might tell you one day you never know", "vault_lines": ["Wrote it in code then wrote it in stone", "So they'll never know", "But I might tell you one day you never know"], "meaning": "https://twitter.com/Drake/status/563995236188581888\n\nDrake is telling this girl that he and the OVO crew tend to write things in code first, cryptically hinting at things such as new releases prior to their arrival:\n\nhttps://twitter.com/Drake/status/562294227569082370\n\nWhile many will never decode many of the tweets, he suggests that he may tell her the true meaning behind his veiled ways", "annotation_id": "5014226", "url": "https://genius.com/5014226", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Madonna", "line": "[Verse 2]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Missing from the original February digital version, this unreleased verse first showed up on OG Ron’s chopped & screwed mix of the song in early March and was later included on the physical “collector’s edition” version of If You’re Reading This, It’s Too Late, which hit shelves on April 21.", "annotation_id": "5014195", "url": "https://genius.com/5014195", "state": "accepted", "votes": 45, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Madonna", "line": "Say you get up early, you work for the man Well, he’ll understand Pull up, I’m pullin’ up on you in ten Already on ten", "vault_lines": ["Say you get up early, you work for the man", "Pull up, I'm pullin' up on you in ten"], "meaning": "When Drake says that he’s “on ten” in this context, he means he’s at his peak level of excitement for what could potentially happen with this girl. On a scale of one to ten, she literally has him on “ten”", "annotation_id": "5006336", "url": "https://genius.com/5006336", "state": "verified", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Madonna", "line": "Say you get up early, you work for the man Well, he’ll understand Pull up, I’m pullin’ up on you in ten Already on ten", "vault_lines": ["Say you get up early, you work for the man", "Pull up, I'm pullin' up on you in ten"], "meaning": "Going off of what Coolwhip49 said, Drake referring to being “on 10” more likely refers to him driving on I-10, which goes straight through Houston.", "annotation_id": "4945756", "url": "https://genius.com/4945756", "state": "verified", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Madonna", "line": "Say you get up early, you work for the man Well, he’ll understand Pull up, I’m pullin’ up on you in ten Already on ten", "vault_lines": ["Say you get up early, you work for the man", "Pull up, I'm pullin' up on you in ten"], "meaning": "When Drake says he’s “on ten” it’s a reference to the highway “10” in Ontario, the proper abbreviation is “ON-10 for Ontario – 10” in a way it’s word play.\nHe’s physically driving and he’s on ON-10 and he will see her in 10 minutes.", "annotation_id": "4921509", "url": "https://genius.com/4921509", "state": "verified", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Madonna", "line": "What if I pick you up from your house? We should get out, we haven’t talked in a while We should roll to see where it goes", "vault_lines": ["We should get out, we haven't talked in a while", "We should roll to see where it goes", "Or what you should wear", "What if I pick you up from your house?"], "meaning": "“Roll” refers to rolling a joint, which Drake occasionally does. It also refers to rolling, in form of driving.", "annotation_id": "4919917", "url": "https://genius.com/4919917", "state": "verified", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Madonna", "line": "Say you get up early, you work for the man Well, he’ll understand Pull up, I’m pullin’ up on you in ten Already on ten", "vault_lines": ["Say you get up early, you work for the man", "Pull up, I'm pullin' up on you in ten"], "meaning": "Another persepctive for “Already on ten” — He’s saying that the woman, who could be as big as Madonna, is already at a level of 10 (assuming a scale of 1-10) on whatever ambiguous variable(s) Drake is referring to.  So if she is already on 10 from the jump, imagine how big she can become in the future (as big as Madonna, of course).", "annotation_id": "4916751", "url": "https://genius.com/4916751", "state": "verified", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Madonna", "line": "Say you get up early, you work for the man Well, he’ll understand Pull up, I’m pullin’ up on you in ten Already on ten", "vault_lines": ["Say you get up early, you work for the man", "Pull up, I'm pullin' up on you in ten"], "meaning": "This suggests that the lady in question isn’t in the same industry as Drake. “The Man” refers to authorities in position of power and is sometimes used in a negative connotation. She’s likely employed in a dull 9-5 day job, working for a boring boss who probably doesn’t even have a Genius account, but Drake pleads that he’ll understand her wanting to come on the road with him.\n\nYou should call into work if that ain’t too much to ask\n“Come Thru”\n\n“Already on ten” indicates that he’s on tenth avenue. It could also mean he’s already ready to go sexually.", "annotation_id": "4894342", "url": "https://genius.com/4894342", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Madonna", "line": "[Chorus] Breathe through, ride through Damn, girl, oh man, I don’t know Pilled up, filled up Damn, girl, I’ll be gettin’ back to you for sure (Man, man) Laced up, dripped up, sauced up Damn, girl, I wanna ride with you Waved up, goin’ up, glowin’ up, growin’ up Had to get it poppin’ with you", "vault_lines": ["Breathe through, ride through", "Damn, girl, oh man, I don't know", "Pilled up, filled up", "Damn, girl, I'll be gettin' back to you for sure (Man, man)", "Laced up, dripped up, sauced up", "Damn, girl, I wanna ride with you", "Waved up, goin' up, glowin' up, growin' up", "Had to get it poppin' with you"], "meaning": "Houston slang made popular by H-town’s very own, Bun B to describe a clean whip. Drake has a dope whip and he wants to ride with her.", "annotation_id": "4889381", "url": "https://genius.com/4889381", "state": "accepted", "votes": 127, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Madonna", "line": "What if I pick you up from your house? We should get out, we haven’t talked in a while We should roll to see where it goes", "vault_lines": ["We should get out, we haven't talked in a while", "We should roll to see where it goes", "Or what you should wear", "What if I pick you up from your house?"], "meaning": "Drake wants to pick up an old flame and just chill with her like old times. It’s been some time since they’ve last spoken and he wants to see where this time will go. “Roll” also refers to smoking.\n\nDrake and Madonna even had Instagram exchanges where Drake stated the first two lines of this verse.", "annotation_id": "4888584", "url": "https://genius.com/4888584", "state": "pending", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Madonna", "line": "You could be big as Madonna Just get in the car and then let’s touch the road Don’t make other plans", "vault_lines": ["You could be big as Madonna", "Just get in the car and then let's touch the road", "Don't make other plans"], "meaning": "Is he talking about Madonna’s looks? Her $500 million net-worth? Her legacy? Either way, everything about the Queen of Pop is big. Not only is she popular, but she is arguably one of the most influential artists of all time. This is pretty high praise for the girl.\n\nDrake is also referencing lines from “Get In The Car” by Francis & The Lights:\n\nSo get in the car\nYou could be bigger than Madonna\nGet in the car\nC'mon you know you wanna\n\nFrancis also co-wrote and produced Karaoke, from Drake’s debut album.", "annotation_id": "4888326", "url": "https://genius.com/4888326", "state": "accepted", "votes": 76, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
