{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "OVO Sound Radio Episode 46 Tracklist", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-ovo-sound-radio-episode-46-tracklist-lyrics", "genius_title": "OVO Sound Radio Episode 46 Tracklist"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Right Hand", "line": "You got a lot on your plate That’s why you’re always working out Taking pictures of yourself You don’t see anybody else", "vault_lines": ["You got a lot on your plate", "That's why you're always working out", "Taking pictures of yourself", "You don't see anybody else"], "meaning": "The pressure to attain money and fame is weighing heavy on this girl’s chest as she’s constantly hitting the gym, stepping on the scales and staring at the number in hopes to perfect her body. Her success depends on her ability to attract attention, whether she’s dancing on a pole or modelling on Instagram.\n\n“Hotline Bling” was released alongside this track and parallels many of these themes. Drake comments on how this girl is wearing less and going out more and how her success has allowed her to travel the world. This track may even prequel “Hotline Bling,” as Drake here seems certain of this girl’s exclusivity, but questions it in the latter track.", "annotation_id": "7976584", "url": "https://genius.com/7976584", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Right Hand", "line": "I just fell back with it And now your past is behind you like the car with the strap in it Thank God that’s finished", "vault_lines": ["You and all your girlfriends", "I just fell back with it", "And now your past is behind you like the car with the strap in it", "Thank God that's finished"], "meaning": "While the man she trusted had to do a lot for her attention, Drizzy gets it regardless.\n\nHe managed to bring this girl out of a rough situation. “Strap” refers to a gun. She would have driven around with a pistol in the car – alluding to a past of crime and insecurity.", "annotation_id": "7807455", "url": "https://genius.com/7807455", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Right Hand", "line": "You and all your girlfriends The ones you never bring around me ’Cause you don’t trust me like your last man Did he open doors for ya? Buy the things you can’t afford for ya? ’Cause he must have did a lot for ya", "vault_lines": ["You and all your girlfriends", "The ones you never bring around me", "'Cause you don't trust me like your last man", "Did he open doors for ya?", "Buy the things you can't afford for ya?", "'Cause he must have did a lot for ya"], "meaning": "Drake doesn’t understand why this girl won’t trust him – he treats her like a gentleman and buys her everything she wants. In Drake’s mind, he’s leagues ahead of her old flame. That’s easy to say when you’re worth millions.\n\nAs for her friends, that’s understandable, considering Drizzy’s reputation.", "annotation_id": "7483323", "url": "https://genius.com/7483323", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Right Hand", "line": "But I swear you gotta chill You wanna grip a Benz wheel And I know you can’t wait You dream big and sleep late", "vault_lines": ["You dream big and sleep late", "But I swear you gotta chill", "You wanna grip a Benz wheel", "And I know you can't wait"], "meaning": "This girl has lofty goals. Drake likes girls who aspire to do better. On his song “Can I” with Beyoncé, he rapped:\n\n‘Fore I turn the lights out, tell me who the fuck you want to be\n\nA “Benz” refers to a Mercedes-Benz, the hallmark of a lavish lifestyle. While she wants to go 0-100, Drake just wants her to relax and enjoy life for a minute.", "annotation_id": "7446749", "url": "https://genius.com/7446749", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Right Hand", "line": "’Cause now it’s back to business Any more Henny and you’re past the limit You told me ’bout the picture, now you have to send it I would never put you on blast when I get it", "vault_lines": ["'Cause now it's back to business", "Any more Henny and you're past the limit", "You told me 'bout the picture, now you have to send it", "I would never put you on blast when I get it"], "meaning": "This girl cannot control herself once she has too much to drink. Hennessy is a popular brand of cognac.\n\nDrake tries to earn her trust by letting her know that even if she sends him a nude photo, he would not expose her. As he rapped on “Marvins Room,”\n\nI think I’m addicted to naked pictures\n\n\n\nThe way he says it is a nod to the “Back to Back” track—which had not yet dropped as of this song’s release date.", "annotation_id": "7446207", "url": "https://genius.com/7446207", "state": "accepted", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Right Hand", "line": "You my right hand, you my go to Told me everything about you, that’s a bold move I know that you’re out here And there’s things you gotta go through Just know that these streets just don’t love you like I do Yeah, and they never will", "vault_lines": ["You my right hand, you my go to", "And you're like, \"Oh well\"", "But you my right hand, you my go to", "Told me everything about you, that's a bold move", "I know you want to go to Maui", "I know that you're out here", "And they never will", "And there's things you gotta go through", "Just know that these streets just don't love you like I do", "Yeah, and they never will", "And I know you can't wait"], "meaning": "Drake’s talking about a girl he trusts. This is new territory for him, considering he has a song called “Trust Issues” and often raps about his lack of trust in women. While he understands this girl needs space, it pains him to sit on the sidelines and see her get hurt.\n\n\n\nThe final lyric is interpolated from Tanya Stephen’s chorus on “These Streets.” Stephens is a Jamaican reggae artist. This comes as no surprise – Drake has been borrowing from the Caribbean for a minute.", "annotation_id": "7446042", "url": "https://genius.com/7446042", "state": "accepted", "votes": 118, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Right Hand", "line": "Okay, I know you want the Audi I know you want to go to Maui", "vault_lines": ["Okay, I know you want the Audi", "I know you want to go to Maui"], "meaning": "Drake begins the second verse in a similar vein to the first – by name dropping an expensive car.\n\nThis girl wants finer things in life like expensive cars and vacations in exotic places. The cost of a high-end Audi could start at over $100,000, whilst Maui is an island of Hawaii, a vacation hotspot for celebrities.", "annotation_id": "7445978", "url": "https://genius.com/7445978", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Right Hand", "line": "And you’re like, “Oh well” You’re like, “Fuck it, oh well” My past behind me like a ponytail", "vault_lines": ["And you're like, \"Oh well\"", "You're like, \"Fuck it, oh well\"", "My past behind me like a ponytail"], "meaning": "Drake switches to the girl’s perspective to end his verse. This girl keeps her past behind her the same way a ponytail sits on the back of the head.\n\nAs hinted on in the hook, these lyrics reiterate this girl’s involvement in the “street” lifestyle – was she a stripper in a past life? Drizzy’s habit of “saving the stripper” dates back to his mixtape days, most notably the track “Houstatlantavegas.” Drake details his experience with an ambitious stripper he felt a connection to. He did the same on “The Real Her”:\n\nHouston girls, love the way it goes down\nAtlanta girls, love the way it goes down\nVegas girls, love the way it goes down", "annotation_id": "7445943", "url": "https://genius.com/7445943", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Right Hand", "status": "done", "targets": 8, "clicked": 8, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-right-hand-lyrics", "genius_title": "Right Hand"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Swagger Like Us", "line": "Thrillin bars you think I’m writing with John Ghrisam", "vault_lines": ["Thrillin bars you think I'm writing with John Ghrisam"], "meaning": "John Ghrisam wrote the book called “The Firm” which is a “Legal Thriller” type of Genre. It sold over 7 million copies. And is a “Best Seller” book.\n\nDrake is saying his lyrics are thrilling and is comparing his bars (writing skills) to those of John Ghrisam", "annotation_id": "24021206", "url": "https://genius.com/24021206", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Swagger Like Us", "line": "I need Rose, nevermind the pricing", "vault_lines": ["I need Rose, nevermind the pricing"], "meaning": "I need Rosé nevermind the pricé", "annotation_id": "20299110", "url": "https://genius.com/20299110", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": false, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Swagger Like Us", "line": "And Ms. Rhone sorry you ain’t notice my potential", "vault_lines": ["And Ms. Rhone sorry you ain't notice my potential"], "meaning": "Sylvia Rhone is the former president of Universal Motown Record who wouldn’t sign Drake back in his earlier days. Ironically, when he finally was signed it was to Universal Motown.", "annotation_id": "605488", "url": "https://genius.com/605488", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Swagger Like Us", "line": "Check the soundscan and you can see that I’m the last hope", "vault_lines": ["Check the soundscan and you can see that I'm the last hope"], "meaning": "He states that by checking the top rap and hip-hop albums out there lately, you can’t see anything on his level.\n“The Last Hope” is the name of a song he recorded for his album Comeback Season, featuring Kardinal Offishall and Andreena, and you can check it via Soundscan.", "annotation_id": "272316", "url": "https://genius.com/272316", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Swagger Like Us", "status": "done", "targets": 4, "clicked": 4, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-swagger-like-us-lyrics", "genius_title": "Swagger Like Us"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Tried Our Best", "line": "Treat you right Treat you right", "vault_lines": ["Treated you, treat you right", "That's why you always wanna play, right?"], "meaning": "In an outro from the chorus in reference to the former statement “treat you like princess” of ‘peak’, no longer will Drake treat his future partner above himself as one would to a princess. He dismisses his people pleasing nature to treat his significant other as an equal counterpart. Do Right And kill everything 4L", "annotation_id": "30337541", "url": "https://genius.com/30337541", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Tried Our Best", "line": "Treat you like Treated you like You’re one of mine Treated you Treated you Treated you, treated you Treated you, treated you Treated you, treated you Treated you, treat you right Treat you right", "vault_lines": ["You're one of mine", "Treated you, treated you", "Treated you, treat you right"], "meaning": "“Treat you like” were the 3 words initiation the beginning of side B of drake’s scorpion album, with the song ‘peak’. Similarly (&interestingly), this line was used in the middle of “for all the dogs” with a different, more upbeat approach.\nBoth songs shared thoughtful & intricate production with premeditated and almost expertly formulated execution.\n\nDrake then proceeds to correct himself restating “treated” as this was a past relationship being reflected on. He also seems to reflect on himself having grown from where he was 5 years ago and obtaining closure (or attempting to) with himself. He cements this reflection process in the scary hours addition where he states “I’ve had my belief tested my faith broken in half I just don’t know how anymore, I just don’t know how”. RIP to dude he used to be…again", "annotation_id": "30337349", "url": "https://genius.com/30337349", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Tried Our Best", "line": "I swear that there’s a list of places that I been with you, I wanna go without you Just so I can know what it’s like to be there without havin’ to argue Swear I didn’t have the discipline to leave your ass at home, you make it hard to This life’ll take a lot of listenin’ to one another, shouldn’t have involved you I know not to lie, oh Leave you at home if I wanna have a good night Leave you at home if I wanna have a good time", "vault_lines": ["I swear that there's a list of places that I been with you, I wanna go without you", "Just so I can know what it's like to be there without havin' to argue", "Swear I didn't have the discipline to leave your ass at home, you make it hard to", "This life'll take a lot of listenin' to one another, shouldn't have involved you", "I know not to lie, oh", "Leave you at home if I wanna have a good night", "Leave you at home if I wanna have a good time"], "meaning": "Drake’s significant other is getting on his nerves throughout this first verse, as he constantly mentions that he would likely enjoy himself more when going out if he were to just simply leave his partner at home.\n\nThe mentioning of his partners starting arguments at restaurants or events is nothing new to Drake’s music:\n\nWhy you gotta fight with me at Cheesecake?\nYou know I love to go there\n“Child’s Play”", "annotation_id": "29791750", "url": "https://genius.com/29791750", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Tried Our Best", "line": "I gotta start us up a support group with a membership", "vault_lines": ["I gotta start us up a support group with a membership"], "meaning": "Following up on the previous line, where Drake says the guys that had to deal with this partner, himself included, were left with nothing to show about how strenuous it was.\n\nIn this line, Drake suggests starting up a support group for himself and her previous exes where they can bond over common ground like in other support groups.", "annotation_id": "29765691", "url": "https://genius.com/29765691", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Tried Our Best", "line": "Champagne, Eggs Benedict Zoom call with her therapist", "vault_lines": ["Zoom call with her therapist"], "meaning": "Eggs Benedict is a breakfast or brunch dish, often served with mimosas—a mix of champagne and chilled orange juice. Drake is evoking a woman with a lavish lifestyle, spending her morning at an upscale restaurant, or indulging in room service, before Zoom calling her therapist. Nevertheless, he desires to cater to her needs.\n\nIn previous work, Drake has shown an affinity for women who some may perceive as “high maintenance.” The 2016 song “Faithful” opens in conversation with Amber Rose:\n\nYou expensive, you know that?\nI’m high maintenance a little bit but not in a—\nNot in a negative way.\nI just like extremely expensive things.", "annotation_id": "29757586", "url": "https://genius.com/29757586", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Tried Our Best", "line": "Oh, oh Oh, oh Oh, oh Oh, oh Oh, oh Oh", "vault_lines": ["I know not to lie, oh"], "meaning": "Sample: Topaz Jones, ‘Black Tame’\nVocals at the end of both songs", "annotation_id": "29741139", "url": "https://genius.com/29741139", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Tried Our Best", "line": "There’s no ribbon given to anyone that you dealt with No badge of honor, no ceremony or benefits", "vault_lines": ["There's no ribbon given to anyone that you dealt with", "No badge of honor, no ceremony or benefits"], "meaning": "Friendship/relationships usually require acts of love: acts of gratitude, acts of service, loyalty, etc.\n\nDrake implies this romantic partner is selfish, as they have given their relationships nothing. She never awarded her friends/partners with such love.", "annotation_id": "29740465", "url": "https://genius.com/29740465", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Tried Our Best", "line": "Leave you at home, blue bubbles blowin’ my line, hard times", "vault_lines": ["Leave you at home, bluе bubbles blowin' my line, hard times"], "meaning": "‘Blue bubbles’ refer to the text messages on iPhones. When texting on an iPhone, the text bubbles show up as blue, while other softwares, such as Android, use green text bubbles.\n\n\n\nDrake is saying that he leaves his girl at home to clear his mind, but even then, his girl still bothers him.", "annotation_id": "29736701", "url": "https://genius.com/29736701", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Tried Our Best", "line": "Your girl’s in the bathroom laying down white lines like some premises", "vault_lines": ["Your girl's in the bathroom laying down white lines like some premises"], "meaning": "Drake compares imagery of a woman doing lines of cocaine in a bathroom to the police securing a crime scene premises. Although it is rarely practiced in real life, a white chalk outline is often portrayed in various forms of media to illustrate a murder scene and to avoid showing a victim’s dead body. Drake wittingly remarks how the friend of the woman he is interested in is laying down white lines of cocaine like a detective would draw white lines of chalk to mimic a person’s corpse.\n\nHowever, this line has a second interpretation, as “some premises” is being used as a homophone for “supremacist.” This twist to the bar again plays off of the rapper’s usage of the word “white,” as a white supremacist is a person who believes the white race is superior to all other racial groups.", "annotation_id": "29732207", "url": "https://genius.com/29732207", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Tried Our Best", "line": "I’ll cater to you, girl, but late night, you a terrorist", "vault_lines": ["I'll cater to you, girl, but late night, you a terrorist"], "meaning": "Drake uses a wordplay based on the similarity between the pronunciation of “I’ll cater” and “Al Qaeda”, an Islamist terrorist multinational organization.\nDrake says that he’ll take care of her even though she made a serious mess late night.", "annotation_id": "29732145", "url": "https://genius.com/29732145", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Tried Our Best", "line": "Fishing for some answers in that ocean with a fucking great white", "vault_lines": ["Fishing for some answers in that ocean with a fucking great white"], "meaning": "To fish for something means to ask for or try to get something in an indirect way. However, the fact that Drake talks about the great white shark at the end of the bar makes this a double entendre, referring to literal fishing as well.", "annotation_id": "29729421", "url": "https://genius.com/29729421", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Tried Our Best", "line": "The girl that the boy cherishes workin’ late night at the Pyramid, and it ain’t right", "vault_lines": ["The girl that the boy cherishes workin' late night at the Pyramid, and it ain't right"], "meaning": "The man is infatuated with a woman working at the “Pyramid,” a gentleman’s club. He has developed a genuine affection for her, but her interest in him is only entertainment, for her own monetary gain.\n\nDrake may be referencing the song “Pyramids” by Frank Ocean; the line resembles the song’s prominent chorus. Ocean appears on the opening track of For All The Dogs, titled “Virginia Beach,” and Drake has referenced Ocean’s luxury brand, Homer, in previous releases.\n\nCandidates for the club in question include The Pyramid, a nightclub in the East Village of Manhattan in New York City, and The Luxor, a giant pyramid structure situated along the Las Vegas Strip in Paradise, Nevada.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe Luxor Hotel & Casino in Paradise, Nevada.", "annotation_id": "29729177", "url": "https://genius.com/29729177", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Tried Our Best", "line": "Wockhardt and Sierra Mist", "vault_lines": ["Wockhardt and Sierra Mist"], "meaning": "Wockhardt is a global pharmaceutical company that produces cough syrup, containing promethazine and codeine,  which are key ingredients to create lean. Sierra Mist is a discontinued lemon-lime soft drink, introduced by Pepsi in 1999. However, in early 2023, Pepsi reverted the brand name to Starry.\n\nDespite referencing lean, which is an illicit beverage mixed with Wockhardt and Sprite, Drake opts to use Sierra Mist.", "annotation_id": "29726114", "url": "https://genius.com/29726114", "state": "accepted", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Tried Our Best", "line": "We in the club with your gay friends Always put you on a straight flight", "vault_lines": ["We in the club with your gay friends", "Always put you on a straight flight"], "meaning": "“Gay friends” and “straight flight” have been used to create a wordplay.", "annotation_id": "29725918", "url": "https://genius.com/29725918", "state": "pending", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Tried Our Best", "line": "I swear to God, you think I’m Shakespeare That’s why you always wanna play, right?", "vault_lines": ["I swear to God, you think I'm Shakespeare", "That's why you always wanna play, right?"], "meaning": "Drake likens himself to English playwright and poet William Shakespeare with a masterful play on words. Comparing Shakespeare’s playwriting to his woman wanting to play with him, as in acting out of character.\n\nAlso doubling down on the connection between the playwright and his own current situation, when asking “that’s why you always wanna play, right?”", "annotation_id": "29725602", "url": "https://genius.com/29725602", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Tried Our Best", "line": "You YSL like buy me some I’m YSL like a snake bite", "vault_lines": ["You YSL like buy me some", "I'm YSL like a snake bite"], "meaning": "Drake states that this woman is the type to ask him to buy her products from high-fashion designer Yves-Saint Laurent, while Drake himself is more interested in a different YSL: Young Stoner Life Records, a record label founded by Young Thug, who’s well-known to liken himself to a snake and use the reptile in various music videos and artwork.", "annotation_id": "29725483", "url": "https://genius.com/29725483", "state": "accepted", "votes": 52, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Tried Our Best", "line": "Message read like a brake light Words sharp like a steak knife", "vault_lines": ["Message read like a brake light", "Words sharp like a steak knife"], "meaning": "Drake delivers a smooth play on words, comparing the red brake lights of a car to a read text message to/from his woman.\n\nHe then compares the content or “words” of this message as sharp, likening it to the sharpness of a steak knife. For context, this is Drake’s interpretation of the common metaphor, [Their] word’s cut deeper than a knife, meaning to say something hurtful to one another.", "annotation_id": "29725425", "url": "https://genius.com/29725425", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
