{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "WNBA", "line": "Trips keep gettin’ longer and longer and longer And the trips keep gettin’ longer and longer and longer (Longer and longer)", "vault_lines": ["Somebody's birthday and the trips keep gettin' longer", "And the trips keep gettin' longer and longer and longer", "Made those plans today and the trips keep gettin' longer, longer", "Feels so far away, the trips keep gettin'", "Longer and longer and longer", "And the trips keep gettin' longer", "Trips keep gettin' longer and longer and longer"], "meaning": "Drake and his lover are growing distant emotionally and also in an sense of communication as the outro contrasts the intro starting with his lover being responsive and\n\none call away\n\nas the song progresses her responses/visits are taking longer potentially referencing ghosting culture.", "annotation_id": "39838588", "url": "https://genius.com/39838588", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "WNBA", "line": "We got so much motion, I’m takin’ shit for motion sickness", "vault_lines": ["We got so much motion, I'm takin' shit for motion sickness"], "meaning": "We got so much motion\n\nSexual motion referenced here between Drake and his lover.\n\nI’m takin' shit for motion sickness\n\nMotion sickness is where a person sees movement differently to what they hear,providing mixed signals.\nDrake uses this line cleverly to show mixed signals between a sexual relationship vs a romantic relationship with his partner.\n\nThis is strengthened within the next line", "annotation_id": "39837505", "url": "https://genius.com/39837505", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
