{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Falling Back", "line": "Time isn’t healing, wait Time is revealing, wait", "vault_lines": ["Nothing is healing, wait", "Time is just killing, wait", "Time isn't healing, wait", "Time is revealing, wait"], "meaning": "“Time heals everything” is a common phrase used around the world to convey that the best way to get over something, is through time. However, in these lines Drake exclaims that time is not healing, and is instead revealing the despair and brokenness of this relationship, more-so than  healing.", "annotation_id": "28354091", "url": "https://genius.com/28354091", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Falling Back", "line": "How do you say to my face, ”Time heals”? Then go and leave me again, unreal", "vault_lines": ["How do you say to my face, \"Time heals\"?", "Then go and leave me again, unreal", "How can you say? Wait"], "meaning": "This is classic advice after a breakup- but Drake implies that his ex is using it to pretend she cares while leaving him.", "annotation_id": "27554927", "url": "https://genius.com/27554927", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
