{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "From Florida With Love", "line": "Went and got a chain for me, I had to give it up (Yeah) Niggas had they pistols loaded pointed at my truck, ayy And you know that lesson stuck (Right) From that day I never touched the road without a (Plugg) Ayy, from that day I never saw the point in talkin’ tough (Nah) Hasn’t happened since, I guess you niggas know what’s up (Yup)", "vault_lines": ["From that day I never touched the road without a (Plugg)", "Ayy, from that day I never saw the point in talkin' tough (Nah)", "Hasn't happened since, I guess you niggas know what's up (Yup)", "YMB the gang and you know them niggas…", "Damn, and you know that lesson stuck (Right)", "Bottles in the club, ayy, know I love to touch (Ayy)", "Went and got a chain for me, I had to give it up (Yeah)", "Niggas had they pistols loaded pointed at my truck, ayy", "And you know that lesson stuck (Right)"], "meaning": "In May 2009, Drake was robbed at gunpoint after he left a restaurant with a date. The robbers, who approached Drizzy’s SUV, demanded $2,000 in cash, an Audemars Piguet watch, and a diamond chain Lil Wayne had gifted him. Drake later opened up about the incident in his 2010 GQ cover story, saying he was set-up:\n\nI knew it was a set-up because I had on a sweater and a jacket … but when they banged on the car window with a gun and opened the door, the first thing he said was, ‘Yo, run that chain.’ They didn’t rob her, and her purse was sitting right there. So I was like, ‘OK, yup — you set the whole thing up.’", "annotation_id": "19726966", "url": "https://genius.com/19726966", "state": "accepted", "votes": 94, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "From Florida With Love", "line": "YMB the gang and they down to stain anything, mhm Yeah, that’s right YMB the gang and they down to stain anything, mhm Yeah, that’s right YMB the gang and you know them niggas…", "vault_lines": ["YMB the gang and they down to stain anything, mhm", "YMB the gang and you know them niggas…"], "meaning": "YMB or Young Money Billionaires is Lil Wayne’s record label, that was once under Cash Money Millionaires, with artists such as Nicki Minaj and previously Drake.\n\nAlthough Drake is no longer under Young Money, he is still loyal to Wayne and Minaj, who all have each others' backs. For example, when Nicki and Remy Ma were beefing, Drake and Lil Wayne appeared on Nicki’s March 2017 diss track against Remy, “No Frauds,” in support of Nicki.\n\n\n\nIt’s worth noting that on the demo version of the song, Drake mentions FBG—which stands for Freeband Gang—instead of YMB in support of his close friends Casino and Future, as FBG is their crew and record label.", "annotation_id": "19718034", "url": "https://genius.com/19718034", "state": "accepted", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "From Florida With Love", "line": "Booted up, turned up, piped up (Plugg) I’m back, baby, where the love? (Where the love at?) I’m back, baby, where the love? (Where the love at?) I’m back, baby, where the love? Booted up, turned up, piped up (Plugg) I’m back, baby, where the love? (Where the love at?) I’m back, baby, where the love? (Where the love at?) I’m back, baby, where the love? (Ayy)", "vault_lines": ["Fuck that, I'm back, baby, where the love? (Love)", "Booted up, turned up, piped up (Plugg)", "I'm back, baby, where the love? (Where the love at?)"], "meaning": "“Booted up,” “turned up” and “piped up” are all terms used to describe someone intoxicated, whether by drugs or alcohol.  On Gucci Mane’s December 2016 song “Both,” Drake talked about drinking and smoking, indicating these are frequent activities for him:\n\nI don’t usually do this unless I’m drunk or I’m high\nBut I’m both right now, got me talking about my life", "annotation_id": "19717973", "url": "https://genius.com/19717973", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "From Florida With Love", "line": "When I linked with Mexiko, I knew I found a plug (Dro)", "vault_lines": ["When I linked with Mexiko, I knew I found a plug (Dro)"], "meaning": "This is a shoutout to the song’s producer MexikoDro. He’s a prominent Atlanta producer who’s known for his frequent production for fellow Altlanta native, Playboi Carti. A “plug” is someone who supplies drugs. However, Drake’s not talking about drugs, he’s talking about beats.\n\nAlso, MexikoDro is a member of the record producer group called BeatPluggz who pionereed the plug genre of trap instrumentals. The genre’s sound is earmarked with the production tag “Plugg” at the beginning and throughout the songs.", "annotation_id": "19717398", "url": "https://genius.com/19717398", "state": "accepted", "votes": 57, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "From Florida With Love", "line": "Weezy played that shit for me and Kobe on the bus", "vault_lines": ["Weezy played that shit for me and Kobe on the bus"], "meaning": "In a December 2019 interview with Rap Radar, Drake reminisced on meeting Lakers legend Kobe Bryant in 2008 on Lil Wayne’s  tour bus after he flew Drake out to Houston, Texas to open for him on his Tha Carter III tour. Kobe, at the time, was picking up an iPod with Wayne’s then-new album, Tha Carter III:\n\nI flew to Houston and you know, I went on the bus and Wayne was getting the biggest tattoo bleeding out with like black ink, I was like, I was just like ‘Oh this is crazy’ and then I remember just sitting there and like I’m looking up and like Kobe Bryant walks on the bus, you know, to get his like Carter III iPod because he wanted to get the album early.\n\nAdditionally, Lil Wayne’s March 2008 hit “Lollipop”—which Drake made a reference to above—is featured on the album.\n\nKobe Bryant died on January 26, 2020, in a helicopter crash. Drake paid tribute to Bryant by hanging his numbers 8 and 24 in his home gym and also had his jerseys in the background at the beginning of his “Toosie Slide” music video.", "annotation_id": "19717091", "url": "https://genius.com/19717091", "state": "accepted", "votes": 81, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "From Florida With Love", "line": "Rest in peace to Static, yellin’ “Shawty want a thug,” ayy Bottles in the club, ayy, know I love to touch (Ayy)", "vault_lines": ["Bottles in the club, ayy, know she wanna fuck (Ayy)", "Rest in peace to Static, yellin' \"Shawty want a thug,\" ayy", "Bottles in the club, ayy, know I love to touch (Ayy)"], "meaning": "Static Major is a rapper who passed away on February 25, 2008, due to an alleged hospital mistake.\n\nDrake pays homage to one of Static’s widely known lyrics, which were taken from his chorus on Lil Wayne’s March 2008 hit, “Lollipop”:\n\nShawty want a thug\nBottles in the club\n\nInterestingly, Static Major made a posthumous guest appearance on Drake’s June 2018 track “After Dark” from his fifth studio album, Scorpion.", "annotation_id": "19532836", "url": "https://genius.com/19532836", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
