{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "BackOutsideBoyz", "line": "Fuckin’ rap niggas’ hoes, I’m on the street, this shit sweet (Hey)", "vault_lines": ["Fuckin' rap niggas’ hoes, I’m on the street, this shit sweet (Hey)"], "meaning": "Drake has an infamous reputation for doing exactly this. During the 2024 beef, sources such as Akademiks have cited that this may have been a large contributing factor to the pile up of rappers dropping disses on Drake: takin they hoes. He even did it to his mentor, Lil Wayne, while he was imprisoned on Rikers Island.", "annotation_id": "38961771", "url": "https://genius.com/38961771", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "BackOutsideBoyz", "line": "Tropicana, that shit there the juice, yeah (Juice)", "vault_lines": ["Tropicana, that shit there the juice, yeah (Juice)"], "meaning": "Tropicana is a popular brand that Drake shouts out, known for its orange juice.\n\nhttps://images.heb.com/is/image/HEBGrocery/000145085", "annotation_id": "27131955", "url": "https://genius.com/27131955", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "BackOutsideBoyz", "line": "Tried to bring the drama to me, he ain’t know how we cha-cha slide (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Tried to bring the drama to me, he ain’t know how we cha-cha slide (Yeah)"], "meaning": "This is widely perceived as a reference to Virginia artist DRAM.\n\nIn 2015, DRAM called out Drake for copying elements of his single “Cha Cha” on Drake’s single “Hotline Bling.”\n\nOn the day of Her Loss‘ release, DRAM addressed the line, revealing that there was an altercation between the two artists approximately five years ago in which DRAM was assaulted by Drake’s bodyguards.", "annotation_id": "27072271", "url": "https://genius.com/27072271", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "BackOutsideBoyz", "line": "I spent days in the East tryna figure if I’m geeked (’Kay)", "vault_lines": ["I spent days in the East tryna figure if I'm geeked ('Kay)"], "meaning": "Drake references the time he spent on Toronto’s Eastside, which he has previously mentioned multiple times throughout his career on tracks such as “The Motion” and “Days In The East.”", "annotation_id": "27069898", "url": "https://genius.com/27069898", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "BackOutsideBoyz", "line": "Breakin’ a Brink’s truck, my right wrist Van Cleef (Cleef)", "vault_lines": ["Breakin' a Brink's truck, my right wrist Van Cleef (Cleef)"], "meaning": "Drake plays on the term “break the bank,” meaning to spend a vast sum of money on an expensive purchase. He substitutes this for a Brink’s truck, an armoured car used to transport large sums of money to and from banks.\n\n\n\nVan Cleef & Arpels is a luxury French company, known for its high-class jewelry and watches. He states that he has a Van Cleef item on his wrist, most likely one of their bracelets.\n\n\nPictured: Drake wearing Van Cleef jewelry in 2021 (via Instagram).", "annotation_id": "27061979", "url": "https://genius.com/27061979", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "BackOutsideBoyz", "line": "Wagon when she walk", "vault_lines": ["Wagon when she walk"], "meaning": "‘Wagon’ is an internet slang for a woman with big rounded shape ass.", "annotation_id": "27054114", "url": "https://genius.com/27054114", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "BackOutsideBoyz", "line": "Couple million on my cars, I went Tyson, I’m too nice (Hey, hey)", "vault_lines": ["Couple million on my cars, I went Tyson, I'm too nice (Hey, hey)"], "meaning": "Mike Tyson earned a fortune during his time as a professional boxer, allowing him to live a lavish lifestyle which included luxury cars. Over the course of his boxing career, Tyson would gift himself cars after a win, including brands like Bentley, Cadillac, and Rolls Royce. Unfortunately, Tyson filed for bankruptcy in 2003, leading to most of his cars being sold off at auction.\n\n\n\nMuch like Tyson, Drake enjoys the finer things in life, having purchased several high-end vehicles throughout his career. As of 2022, his collection is estimated at a whopping $8.8 million USD.", "annotation_id": "27053634", "url": "https://genius.com/27053634", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "BackOutsideBoyz", "line": "I don’t know nothin’ ’bout no crime or no news I’m an owl, but I’ll never tell you who (Who)", "vault_lines": ["I don't know nothin' 'bout no crime or no news", "I'm an owl, but I'll never tell you who (Who)"], "meaning": "Drake’s signature animal is an owl, which is prominently featured on Drake’s OVO brand. Owls commonly make hoo or hooting sounds and Drake compares this to the word “who”. Drake is saying that he won’t tell who because he’s loyal and doesn’t snitch.\n\nAlso, it is estimated that owl’s night vision is anywhere from 35-100 times better than ours. He’s also saying he sees a lot of things.", "annotation_id": "27053444", "url": "https://genius.com/27053444", "state": "pending", "votes": 57, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "BackOutsideBoyz", "line": "Tweakin’, the 6 God is comin’ back (Brr)", "vault_lines": ["Tweakin', the 6 God is comin' back (Brr)"], "meaning": "“6 God” is a nickname that Drake adopted after becoming the biggest artist out of Toronto, Canada, also known as “The 6ix” or “The 6”. He also has a song named “6 God” that is featured on his fourth mixtape, If You’re Reading This It’s Too Late.\n\nOn the aforementioned If You’re Reading This It’s Too Late, Drake adopts a more aggressive rapping style as opposed to the R&B influence that he implements on many songs. Thus, he denotes a return to this rapping style, marking Her Loss and “BackOutsideBoyz” as a return to form.", "annotation_id": "27053051", "url": "https://genius.com/27053051", "state": "accepted", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "BackOutsideBoyz", "line": "I’m the president, some Secret Service shit, we down to dump (Brrt) Yeah, who the president? I never voted once, ayy, yeah If I did, I would vote Teanna Trump, ayy, yeah (Hm, go)", "vault_lines": ["I'm the president, some Secret Service shit, we down to dump (Brrt)", "Yeah, who the president? I never voted once, ayy, yeah", "If I did, I would vote Teanna Trump, ayy, yeah (Hm, go)"], "meaning": "The Secret Service are a federal government department in the US which have the sole goal to protect the president from any danger.\n\nHere, Drake uses the president as a metaphor to paraphrase his superiority over the music industry, being placed as the #1 most streamed artist of 2022.\n\nSince Drake is a Canadian native, he states that he doesn’t know who the current US president is and states that he has never voted, however, notes that if he did he would vote for Teanna Trump, an adult film star. Drake uses Teanna’s last name, “Trump,” to make a reference to the infamous 45th president of the United States, Donald Trump who was impeached twice and is known as one of the worst presidents in history — possibly relating to Drake’s unseriousness regarding him “voting for” Teanna Trump.\n\n\n\nPictured: Teanna Trump at the AVN Awards red carpet", "annotation_id": "27052792", "url": "https://genius.com/27052792", "state": "accepted", "votes": 69, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "BackOutsideBoyz", "line": "She a ten tryna rap, it’s good on mute, yeah (It’s good on mute, shh)", "vault_lines": ["She a ten tryna rap, it's good on mute, yeah (It's good on mute, shh)"], "meaning": "While it is not confirmed who this refers to, this was originally heavily rumored to be referring to Ice Spice, especially after she took to Twitter to respond to the lyric:\n\nhttps://twitter.com/icespicee_/status/1588611960970809344\n\nIce Spice has since debunked the rumor in an Ebro in the Morning interview, stating that she had spoken to Drake about the line:\n\nHe didn’t [take a shot at me]. We spoke about it. He said that was not about me.", "annotation_id": "27052650", "url": "https://genius.com/27052650", "state": "accepted", "votes": 156, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
