{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cheerios", "line": "I be talkin’ to the D.A. like that nigga dumb, what? You be talkin’ to the D.A. like, “Yeah, he the one,”", "vault_lines": ["I be talkin' to the D.A. like that nigga dumb, what?", "You be talkin' to the D.A. like, \"Yeah, he the one,\""], "meaning": "The District Attorney (D.A.) is the chief prosecutor in many jurisdictions, whose office brings criminal charges to Court on behalf of the State. Drake is suggesting that while he talks to the D.A. like the D.A. himself is dumb–perhaps for the D.A. questioning whether Drake and his cohort are guilty of criminal charges–others snitch to the D.A., like pointing a perpetrator out of a line-up.\n\nEarlier in the track, Drake suggests he is skeptical of the criminal nature of the circumstances under which Young Thug and Gunna are incarcerated.", "annotation_id": "39443811", "url": "https://genius.com/39443811", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cheerios", "line": "You know Gucci let it blam, then he pass it to his man", "vault_lines": ["You know Gucci let it blam, then he pass it to his man"], "meaning": "Shoutout to TV Gucci – Drake’s long time friend. Drake has mentioned TV Gucci on his tracks before;\n\nNo Long Talk\n\nDon’t need Gucci on my back, TVGucci got my back", "annotation_id": "36987587", "url": "https://genius.com/36987587", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cheerios", "line": "And then they takin’ clothes off and bleachin’ that material I’m gone", "vault_lines": ["And then they takin' clothes off and bleachin' that material"], "meaning": "Drake continues to describe the cover-up after a shooting. Once the gun is dumped, the shooters get rid of the clothes they wore and bleach them to destroy evidence like gunpowder, DNA, bloodstains, etc. “I’m gone” signals that the job’s done and they’ve disappeared before the cops can connect it to them.", "annotation_id": "36828182", "url": "https://genius.com/36828182", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
