{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cheerios", "line": "I should probably be in there with Thug and ‘em or be in there with Gunn’ and ’em", "vault_lines": ["I should probably be in there with Thug and 'еm or be in there with Gunn' and 'em"], "meaning": "Reference to the infamous YSL trial of the last two years.", "annotation_id": "35840711", "url": "https://genius.com/35840711", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cheerios", "line": "They be wishin’ death on me like 50 Cent", "vault_lines": ["Ayy, they be wishin' death on me like 50 Cent"], "meaning": "Reference to Many Men by 50 Cent\n\n“Many men wish death upon me''\n\nDrake believes many rappers want to see his downfall. But like 50 after he was shot 9 times, he’s still breathing!\n\nThis track was recorded before the beef with Kendrick Lamar in 2024 but perhaps Drake knew about the conflict that was to come or he was just on that f everybody energy like he’s been on for his whole career. Either way, these lyrics have aged like fine wine since the beef.", "annotation_id": "35840707", "url": "https://genius.com/35840707", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cheerios", "line": "Winnin’ not enough for me, I like to be petty ’bout it", "vault_lines": ["Winnin' not enough for me, I like to be petty 'bout it"], "meaning": "Drake is well known for bragging over his success on his records. There are countless songs where Drake bragged over his success. Some notable mentions are “Trophies” and “Push Ups” consecutively\n\n\nHad hit records on my demo\n\n I can never be nobody number one fan, your first number one I had to put it in your hand\n\n\nAnother notable mention is Drake’s rapping of “Back To Back” and “Charged Up” (both disses towards Meek Mill) after winning the beef against him back in 2015.", "annotation_id": "35177829", "url": "https://genius.com/35177829", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cheerios", "line": "Drop a number one and when it’s done I just forget about it", "vault_lines": ["Drop a number one and when it's done I just forget about it"], "meaning": "Drake makes a brag over how easy it is for him to get #1 records. Drake has 13 records that have gone #1 on billboard.", "annotation_id": "35177801", "url": "https://genius.com/35177801", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cheerios", "line": "Scratched off the serial, we call that shit a Cheerio", "vault_lines": ["Scratched off the serial, we call that shit a Cheerio"], "meaning": "Refers to scratching off the serial number of the gun that Drake alludes to, but “serial” and “cereal” are homonyms – Drake cleverly employs a double entendre with his reference to Cheerio, a proper brand of cereal", "annotation_id": "35155921", "url": "https://genius.com/35155921", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cheerios", "line": "You almost 50, but you’re rappin’ like you’re 21", "vault_lines": ["You almost 50, but you're rappin' like you're 21"], "meaning": "Could be about Kanye, given the time frame this was reportedly recorded (2023) and Kanye being 45/46 at the time. If the beef with Rick Ross ages back to 2023, this could also be about him.", "annotation_id": "35129081", "url": "https://genius.com/35129081", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cheerios", "line": "J Skull", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Reference to Drakes close friend Jordan:", "annotation_id": "35123257", "url": "https://genius.com/35123257", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cheerios", "line": "How the fuck did the 6ix let in 21?", "vault_lines": ["How the fuck did the 6ix let in 21?"], "meaning": "Given this recording was made in 2022, it is supposed that 21 Savage was still dealing with VISA issues related to his case back in 2019.\n\nIt was reported in October 2023, around the time For All the Dogs was released, that his paperwork was legitimized and he was an official US citizen. Therefore, this line could be pertaining to 21 Savage’s limited ability to travel for work during this period.\n\nhttps://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/21-savage-lawful-resident-us-immigration-1234848657/", "annotation_id": "35116705", "url": "https://genius.com/35116705", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cheerios", "line": "(Tay Keith, fuck these niggas up)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "It’s Tay Keith producer tag.\nTay Keith, is an American record producer.\nHe is best known for co-producing Travis Scott’s 2018 single “Sicko Mode”.", "annotation_id": "35116107", "url": "https://genius.com/35116107", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cheerios", "line": "(Tay Keith, fuck these niggas up)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "It’s Tay Keith producer tag.\nTay Keith, is an American record producer.\nHe is best known for co-producing Travis Scott’s 2018 single “Sicko Mode”.", "annotation_id": "35116103", "url": "https://genius.com/35116103", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cheerios", "line": "Many Men, many, many, many men", "vault_lines": ["Many Men, many, many, many men"], "meaning": "Drake is referring to the song, Many Men (Wish Death) by 50 Cent.\n\nMany Men (Wish Death is one of the standout tracks from 50 Cent’s debut studio album Get Rich or Die Tryin’. The song reflects on 50 Cent’s real-life experience of getting shot 9 times in 2000. It’s a raw, emotional track about survival, betrayal, and revenge.\n\n• Widely regarded as one of 50 Cent’s most iconic songs.\n• Became a cultural reference point for resilience and street authenticity.\n• Has been sampled or referenced by artists like Pop Smoke and 21 Savage.\n\nSince Drake is referring to 21 Savage a lot in this song and the fact that 21 Savage has rapped over a sampled (Many Men) beat. This might be an appreciation to 21 Savage by Drake because 21 Savage has been on Drake’s side the whole beef Drake had with Kendrick Lamar.\n\n(21 Savage’s song that sampled Many Men is named, Many Men produced by Metro Boomin.)", "annotation_id": "35114996", "url": "https://genius.com/35114996", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cheerios", "status": "done", "targets": 16, "clicked": 16, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-cheerios-lyrics", "genius_title": "Cheerios"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Final Fantasy", "line": "You got options, but I been chosen", "vault_lines": ["You got options, but I been chosen"], "meaning": "Drake knows he isn’t the only one this girl is talking to or fucking with but he knows she chose him to be her main dude or the one she spends most of her time with. Also possibly a reference to PARTYNEXTDOOR’s 2014 song ‘'Options’'\n\n‘'You know you got options, bae\nYeah, you got options, bae\nKnow you got options, bae’'", "annotation_id": "37991171", "url": "https://genius.com/37991171", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Final Fantasy", "line": "Arch back, heart attack, cardiac", "vault_lines": ["Arch back, heart attack, cardiac"], "meaning": "Drake compares the poses used during sexual intercourse to that of someone having a heart attack. He is also interpolating a line from Young Money’s “Ms. Parker” track where Lil Wayne uses the same rhyme scheme when he raps:\n\nShe attacks my heart, heart attack\nCardiac\nCarter that nigga that she throwin it at and I caught dat", "annotation_id": "14894612", "url": "https://genius.com/14894612", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Final Fantasy", "line": "I always get your ass over here somehow", "vault_lines": ["I always get your ass over here somehow"], "meaning": "“Get over here!” is a move performed by the character Scorpion in the popular video game series Mortal Kombat. Scorpion also happens to be the title of the album this song appears on.\n\n\n\nThe track is also titled Final Fantasy, keeping with the video game references, given the eponymous franchise.", "annotation_id": "14886587", "url": "https://genius.com/14886587", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Final Fantasy", "line": "I like best when you’re fresh faced and no foundation", "vault_lines": ["I like best when you're fresh faced and no foundation"], "meaning": "Drake is telling his love interest that she doesn’t need make-up to look pretty for him, although Drake has mentioned this before. This line most notably draws parallels to the line in Drake’s song “Best I Ever Had”:\n\nSweatpants, hair tied, chillin' with no make-up on\nThat’s when you’re the prettiest\nI hope that you don’t take it wrong", "annotation_id": "14879833", "url": "https://genius.com/14879833", "state": "accepted", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Final Fantasy", "line": "You know, I need you to be open like Kai’s kitchen", "vault_lines": ["You know, I need you to be open like Kai's kitchen"], "meaning": "Drake is referring to Fring’s in Toronto, a restaurant that was owned by his friends, Kai and Levi Bent-Lee, that has now been closed down. He’s mentioned “Kai’s kitchen” previously on “Summer Sixteen”:\n\nMinus twenty we in Pitfield\nThat Kai’s kitchen in a Canada Goose", "annotation_id": "14876733", "url": "https://genius.com/14876733", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Final Fantasy", "line": "Did somebody… Who’d they say that baby look like? Drake!", "vault_lines": ["Who'd they say that baby look like?"], "meaning": "This is sampled from an episode of Maury, a tabloid talk show hosted by Maury Povich that’s most popular for its paternity tests. During the episode, the opposing side said the baby looked like Drake because the suspected father was dark-skinned and the baby was light-skinned.\n\n\n\nThis could also tie into rumors of Drake having a baby with French pornstar Sophie Brussaux; he is, of course, confirming these rumors with the release of Scorpion.", "annotation_id": "14876701", "url": "https://genius.com/14876701", "state": "accepted", "votes": 104, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Final Fantasy", "line": "I need it nasty like, like Evil Angel, like Vivid You know, nasty like how they give it", "vault_lines": ["I need it nasty like, like Evil Angel, like Vivid", "You know, nasty like how they give it"], "meaning": "Evil Angel and Vivid are production companies that are parts of the Adult Film Industry. Drake references needing it “nasty” similar to the porn made, as Evil Angel specializes in hardcore imagery, and Vivid pushes celebrity tapes.", "annotation_id": "14876583", "url": "https://genius.com/14876583", "state": "accepted", "votes": 82, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Final Fantasy", "line": "Slashin’ like Guns N’ Roses", "vault_lines": ["Slashin' like Guns N' Roses"], "meaning": "Slash is the lead guitarist for rock band Guns N’ Roses.\n\nDrake uses “slash” as a synonym for “fuck.” This can be seen in his clean performance at the 2017 Billboard Awards of “Gyalchester.”\n\nHe has previously used the term “slash” in 2017 song “Blem,” saying:\n\nI wanna know, how come we can never slash and stay friends?", "annotation_id": "14876477", "url": "https://genius.com/14876477", "state": "accepted", "votes": 58, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Final Fantasy", "line": "Ayy, freaky like the red leather Michael Zombie revival, this ain’t like you", "vault_lines": ["Ayy, freaky like the red leather Michael", "Zombie revival, this ain't like you"], "meaning": "Drake is referencing Michael Jackson and his famous outfit in the music video for his song “Thriller.” In the music video, Jackson is dressed in a red leather jacket and is attacked by zombies only to return as a dancing zombie. This strange horror look in the video became iconic for the late pop singer and was even adopted by Drake himself in a Halloween episode of Degrassi.\n\n\n\nDrake made a similar allusion to Michael Jackson’s ‘Thriller’ outfit in his 2010 single “Over”:\n\nAbout to go thriller, Mike Jackson on these niggas\nAll I need’s a fucking red jacket with some zippers\n\nAdditionally, Drake “resurrects” (samples) Michael himself two tracks prior on “Don’t Matter to Me.”", "annotation_id": "14876238", "url": "https://genius.com/14876238", "state": "accepted", "votes": 50, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Final Fantasy", "status": "done", "targets": 9, "clicked": 9, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-final-fantasy-lyrics", "genius_title": "Final Fantasy"}
