{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Overdrive", "line": "My heart is racing I cannot slow down and it’s bothering me How forward of me would it be to tell you to forward to me You should be right here anyways Your energy’s calling for me", "vault_lines": ["My heart is racing", "I cannot slow down and it's bothеring me", "How forward of me would it be to tell you to forward to me", "You should be right here anyways", "Your energy's calling for me", "Me and you, jealousy", "My heart is in overdrive"], "meaning": "In Toronto, “fawad” means to come or go somewhere, used parcitularly when inviting someone to join you. The term is derived from Jamaican Creole as a respelling of the English word “forward”.\n\nHere, Drake plays on the double meaning of “forward” and “fawad,” questioning how bold or blunt it would be to ask her to come over. As with any risky text, even the thought of sending the message has his heart racing.", "annotation_id": "36486093", "url": "https://genius.com/36486093", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
