{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "By the way, I’m Jewish", "vault_lines": ["By the way, I'm Jewish"], "meaning": "Drake references his Jewish heritage through his mother, Sandi Graham. Raised Jewish in Toronto, he attended a Jewish day school and had a bar mitzvah. The casual “by the way” presents his identity as an offhand reminder, weaving his background into the verse’s braggadocious tone.", "annotation_id": "41527059", "url": "https://genius.com/41527059", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Swagga Like Us", "line": "Thrilling bars, you’d think I’m writin’ with John Grisham pen", "vault_lines": ["Thrilling bars, you'd think I'm writin' with John Grisham pen"], "meaning": "John Grisham is an American author and politician, mostly known for his legal thrillers such as 1989’s A Time to Kill and 1991’s The Firm.", "annotation_id": "17357654", "url": "https://genius.com/17357654", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
