{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Don’t Worry", "line": "Poppin’ out on Chubbs side, it’s gonna be a party (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Poppin' out on Chubbs side, it's gonna be a party (Yеah)"], "meaning": "Capo “Chubbs“ is one of Drake‘s close friends, referenced in multiple of his songs.", "annotation_id": "39790776", "url": "https://genius.com/39790776", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Don’t Worry", "line": "I don’t know what’s up with me lately, lately", "vault_lines": ["I don't know, you tell me", "Girl, you know what's up with me, I pull up in a heartbeat (Ayy)", "I don't know what's up with me lately, lately"], "meaning": "In the previous line, Drake mentions a Persian girl. Here, the pronunciation of “lately” sounds closer to “Layli” or “Leili,” the Persian form of Layla from the classic romance story Layla and Majnun, potentially creating subtle wordplay between the two lines.", "annotation_id": "39786703", "url": "https://genius.com/39786703", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Don’t Worry", "line": "She wanna go next door, she wanna meet PARTY (Ayy, yeah) She said she was Persian and started speakin’ Farsi (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["She wanna go next door, she wanna meet PARTY (Ayy, yeah)", "She said she was Persian and started speakin' Farsi (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Drake is referencing his friend and OVO Sound artist PARTYNEXTDOOR, the first artist signed to the label in 2013. The pair have collaborated on over 30 songs together, later releasing the joint album $ome $exy $ongs 4 U in February 2025.\n\nThe following line continues the song’s upscale Toronto nightlife atmosphere. Drake mentions a Persian girl speaking Farsi, the primary language spoken in Iran, which also reflects Toronto’s large Iranian diaspora community, sometimes nicknamed “Tehranto.”\n\nThe reference also loosely connects to PARTYNEXTDOOR’s 2014 song “Persian Rugs”, another OVO-era track referencing Persian imagery and aesthetics. Drake has previously mentioned the Persian/Iranian identity on “More M’s”.", "annotation_id": "39778682", "url": "https://genius.com/39778682", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Don’t Worry", "line": "Ref1, he so drunk, he just played Nicki then some Cardi, I’m sorry", "vault_lines": ["Ref1, he so drunk, he just played Nicki then some Cardi, I'm sorry"], "meaning": "Nicki Minaj and Cardi B have had a long standing feud since 2017.\n\nIn 2018, Cardi B and Nicki Minaj got into a physical altercation at a New York Fashion Week party, after Nicki supposedly liked a comment mocking Cardi B’s parental skills.\n\nThe beef later reignited after Cardi B dropped her album Am I the Drama? in September 2025. The two artists bashed eachother’s personal lives on X (Twitter).", "annotation_id": "39778545", "url": "https://genius.com/39778545", "state": "pending", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Don’t Worry", "line": "Candy-pink paint job, she pull up like a Barbie (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Candy-pink paint job, she pull up like a Barbie (Yеah)"], "meaning": "Nicki Minaj uses the nickname “Barbie”. She also recorded a song for the “Barbie” movie, in which the main character drives a car with a candy paint paint job.", "annotation_id": "39776608", "url": "https://genius.com/39776608", "state": "pending", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
