{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Privileged Rappers", "line": "Woah, she love me so much, it seem like she biased", "vault_lines": ["Woah, she love me so much, it seem like she biased"], "meaning": "A girl who always takes drakes side being seemingly biased OR it could be a play on words of “by us” describing a fan that loves him so much that the way she talks is as if  she’s right next to him and not somewhere else entirely.\n21 eludes to this later in the song stating “we go to war with whoever ain’t never been biased” which “by us” in that context almost fits perfectly.\n\n21 goes even deeper  into this later in the song saying  “catch him outside of the studio, make him repeat what he said”  which could be eluding to him hearing something someone said that was not meant disrespectfully but with 21 constantly thinking 2 or 3 different ways to describe 1 thing , he hears something that he wanted to make sure wasn’t said with disrespect, which is subsequently what 21 would have been hinting at if he said “catchin my side of the studio” since he in that context thought he heard from somebody else, “his side” of the studio which is full of double meanings and euphemism’s.\nCatchin my side of the studio …and\nCatch him out side of the studio …are virtually indistinguishable.", "annotation_id": "37916532", "url": "https://genius.com/37916532", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Privileged Rappers", "line": "Too much respect, I used to hand out CDs before they would buy it", "vault_lines": ["Too much respect, I used to hand out CDs before they would buy it"], "meaning": "Back in his Degrassi days when he wanted to get his music career going, Drake would approach DJs and other individuals to play and push his music.", "annotation_id": "36860503", "url": "https://genius.com/36860503", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Privileged Rappers", "line": "Too much respect, all of my shawty BDs, they know not to try it", "vault_lines": ["Too much respect, all of my shawty BDs, they know not to try it"], "meaning": "Double entendre:\n\n1.) Drizzy claims to have ties to the american street gang Black Disciples (BD’s) so his opps dare not to confront him\n\n2.) All of Drakes side chicks have BD‘s (Baby daddies) who dare not to confront him about his sexual relationship with their girlfriends", "annotation_id": "29166826", "url": "https://genius.com/29166826", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
