{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Privileged Rappers", "line": "The diamonds, they hit like a rainbow, that’s ’cause the necklace a Frank (Purr)", "vault_lines": ["The diamonds, they hit like a rainbow, that's 'cause the necklace a Frank (Purr)"], "meaning": "In early 2022, Drake was seen wearing an iced-out necklace made by Frank Ocean’s Homer jewelry brand, and even sang about it on his track “Sticky” from his album “Honestly, Nevermind”:\n\nHomer hanging on my neck\nThe bracelet matches the set\n\nIn this bar, Drake says the necklace is so shiny, the sparkle or refractions look like rainbows.\n\n\n\nThis is likely a play on Frank Ocean openly identifying as a bisexual man. The LGBTQ+ community has used the rainbow flag as a symbol of pride and solidarity for decades.", "annotation_id": "27062550", "url": "https://genius.com/27062550", "state": "accepted", "votes": 84, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Privileged Rappers", "line": "Yeah, let’s have sex in the bank, tell ’em to open the safe", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, let's have sex in the bank, tеll 'em to open the safе", "Yeah, let's have sex in The Nines (Let's do it)", "Yeah, yeah, let's have sex in the car (On God)", "Let's have sex in the bank, tell 'em to open the safe"], "meaning": "“teller to open the safe” refers to going to a bank and telling a bank employee to open the safe. It also can be heard as “tell her” instead of “teller”. In this sense, Drake is having sex and wants her to open her “safe”", "annotation_id": "27060268", "url": "https://genius.com/27060268", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Privileged Rappers", "line": "I hate a privileged rapper who don’t even know what it take", "vault_lines": ["I hate a privileged rapper who don't even know what it take"], "meaning": "Drake has no sympathy—and a good dose of animus—for musicians who haven’t put in the work given that he really started from the bottom.  Drake revealed on his Instagram story on October 18, 2022, that he was paid $100 (£89) to open for Ice Cube in August 2006 at the now-defunct Kool Haus venue in Toronto. Reflecting on what was his first concert, Drake shared the IG post from The Flyer Vault on his stories with the words “this is for anybody getting 100 a show right now,“ further encouraging artists to “keep going.”", "annotation_id": "27060088", "url": "https://genius.com/27060088", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Privileged Rappers", "line": "Yeah, let’s have sex in The Nines (Let’s do it)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, let's have sex in the bank, tеll 'em to open the safе", "Yeah, let's have sex in The Nines (Let's do it)", "Yeah, yeah, let's have sex in the car (On God)"], "meaning": "The Nines Hotel: Luxury Hotel In Downtown Portland", "annotation_id": "27057363", "url": "https://genius.com/27057363", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Privileged Rappers", "line": "Send me my whole fee, I don’t do backends and fronts (21)", "vault_lines": ["Send me my whole fee, I don't do backends and fronts (21)"], "meaning": "21 wants you to send his entire payment before he sends his verse to you instead of getting a fraction of his fee before and after the completion of his verse.", "annotation_id": "27055298", "url": "https://genius.com/27055298", "state": "pending", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
