{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Elevate", "line": "This a life bid we can never separate", "vault_lines": ["This a life bid we can never separate"], "meaning": "Bid is slang for a sentence. In this case it a life sentence we cannot separate.", "annotation_id": "25159928", "url": "https://genius.com/25159928", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Elevate", "line": "When I was pumpin’ gas on road trips to go from Cincinnati on to Dayton", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Dayton Ohio and Cincinnati Ohio lye on the same interstate going north to south (I-75).  I-75 is the predominant route to take from Toronto to Memphis. having spent many of his summers in Memphis with his father, Drake recollects on two cities he often used as waypoints in his childhood (young adult) road trips.", "annotation_id": "22722057", "url": "https://genius.com/22722057", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Elevate", "line": "When I was with Ms. Creighton, that lady hates me", "vault_lines": ["When I was with Ms. Creighton, that lady hates me"], "meaning": "Ms. Creighton was Drake’s 4th grade teacher", "annotation_id": "19628860", "url": "https://genius.com/19628860", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Elevate", "line": "Ayy, elevate, elevate Only obligation is to tell it straight So much on my plate I gotta delegate", "vault_lines": ["Only obligation is to tell it straight", "So much on my plate I gotta delegate"], "meaning": "When Drake refers to how much is “on his plate”, he’s probably referring to how much hot water he’s been recently.\n\nMost importantly, Pusha T recently got into beef with Drake, which involved suggesting that Drake had a baby with a porn star, and showing a real image of him wearing Blackface.\n\nSecond, earlier this year Drake’s alleged ghostwriter threatened to expose him.\n\nDrake is “telling it straight” by, among other things, explaining why the blackface picture was taken. He said on Instagram:\n\nI know everyone is enjoying the circus but I want to clarify this image in question,“ Drake began in his Instagram note. \"This picture is from 2007, a time in my life where I was an actor and I was working on a project that was about young black actors struggling to get roles, being stereotyped and type cast. The photos represented how African Americans were once wrongfully portrayed in entertainment.", "annotation_id": "14992619", "url": "https://genius.com/14992619", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Elevate", "line": "Georgie got me up a hunnid thousand for the weekend", "vault_lines": ["Georgie got me up a hunnid thousand for the weekend"], "meaning": "“Georgie” is a nickname Drake has given to George D. Bousis as revealed by DJ Franzen. He is the founder and CEO of the company, Raise and was also a part of the 2015 Forbes “30 Under 30” list.", "annotation_id": "14927249", "url": "https://genius.com/14927249", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Elevate", "line": "I’m in bed awake, thinkin’ how’d I make All this happen for myself and my family All this happen for myself and my family There’s no way that this is real, man, it can’t be", "vault_lines": ["I'm in bed awake, thinkin' how'd I make", "All this happen for myself and my family", "There's no way that this is real, man, it can't be"], "meaning": "Drake is plagued with thoughts, both good and bad, that give him chronic insomnia, or consistent inability to sleep. He seems to be so overcome with thoughts, that he hates sleeping alone. Here, the surrealness of his massive career and accomplishments cause him to toss and turn. This is reminiscent of restlessness described on his 2015 track, “6 PM in New York”:\n\nLast night I went to sleep wanting more\nTried to decide what direction I should go towards", "annotation_id": "14906276", "url": "https://genius.com/14906276", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Elevate", "line": "Franny got the Aria setup like it’s a Freaknik", "vault_lines": ["Franny got the Aria setup like it's a Freaknik"], "meaning": "Drake shouts out DJ Franzen (Franny for short), who continues to be one of the most influential hip-hop figures in the Las Vegas nightclub scene. In addition to planning private birthday parties for the rapper over the years, Franny also assisted in recording Drake’s “The Motto,” as Drake referenced on the 2011 track:\n\nMe, Franny, and Mally Mall at the crib-o\n\nDrake last performed at the Aria Resort & Casino’s Jewel Nightclub in Vegas shortly after he released his album Views in 2016.\n\nWith Franny involved, Drake compares the excitement of a nightclub like the Aria to Freaknik, an annual spring break celebration in Atlanta, Georgia in the 1980s and 90s primarily attended by students from historically black colleges and universities.", "annotation_id": "14893226", "url": "https://genius.com/14893226", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Elevate", "line": "I see the future when I get wavy (Wavy God)", "vault_lines": ["I see the future when I get wavy (Wavy God)"], "meaning": "Rapper Max B is often credited with popularising the term “Wavy” which, according to his use, meant something like “cool” or “influential” and has since come to be used as shorthand for a “movement.” Max B has also often referred to himself as the ‘Wave God’ in the past, releasing the Wave Gods mixtape with close associate French Montana – who also ad libs the line.\n\nIncidentally, in 2016 there was some controversy when Kanye West changed the name of his then-upcoming album, before settling on The Life of Pablo, from SWISH to WAVES. Some like Wiz Khalifa and Chase N Cashe accused Kanye of “taking the wave” from Max B. However Kanye  received Max B’s blessing via the help of French Montana; which perhaps explains Drake’s choice to include him here when making reference to the Wave.\n\nThat Drake would reference Max B is appropriate, as Max B is also often credited with helping to popularise the singing/rapping combination that Drake has arguably mastered.\n\nAs rapper Roc Marciano said in an interview with Complex:\n\nIn my opinion, [Max] was the street version of what Drake is—the fans can have Drake, but the streets have Max\n\nDrake perhaps saw the future riding Max B’s wave.", "annotation_id": "14885245", "url": "https://genius.com/14885245", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Elevate", "line": "Baka passed a drug test, we gotta celebrate", "vault_lines": ["Baka passed a drug test, we gotta celebrate"], "meaning": "Drake references his longtime friend and former bodyguard, Baka Not Nice. In June of 2017, Drake praised Baka at a club in New York City and signed him to his label, OVO, on the spot.\n\nBefore this, Baka served time in prison for assaulting a 22-year-old Toronto woman and other firearms charges. Just as he celebrated Baka’s release from prison on Instagram, Drake also wants to praise Baka for passing a drug test most likely connected to these past charges.", "annotation_id": "14883390", "url": "https://genius.com/14883390", "state": "accepted", "votes": 55, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Elevate", "line": "Vegas like Marineland, that big whale treatment", "vault_lines": ["Vegas like Marineland, that big whale treatment"], "meaning": "In gambling terminology, a “whale” is a player who gambles massive amounts of money. Casinos profit immensely from whales, so they will commonly offer free amenities, including free rooms, meals, shows, etc., all to entice whales to come gamble at their establishments.\n\nDrake is saying that due to his fame and celebrity, he gets the “big whale treatment” in Vegas as if he was going to Marineland (a controversial water amusement park in Niagara Falls, Canada, which does indeed keep orca and beluga whales).\n\n\n\nOrca whales performing at Marineland", "annotation_id": "14882654", "url": "https://genius.com/14882654", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Elevate", "line": "Slowly, my mouth is goin’ off, I don’t know patience I got a chance then my niggas got it too like it’s contagious", "vault_lines": ["Slowly, my mouth is goin' off, I don't know patience", "I got a chance then my niggas got it too like it's contagious"], "meaning": "Drake feels he was blessed with the opportunity to realize his dreams, and he took it.\n\nNow that he is a top-notch rapper, he also spends a lot of time in promoting new artists, even though he doesn’t get much credit for it. Drake is giving back to the community what was also given to him a decade ago.", "annotation_id": "14879536", "url": "https://genius.com/14879536", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Elevate", "line": "But I couldn’t picture bein’ Champagne (Haan) when I would buy that shit and save it for the right occasion", "vault_lines": ["But I couldn't picture bein' Champagne (Haan) when I would buy that shit and save it for the right occasion", "I couldn't picture changes", "I couldn't gauge it"], "meaning": "Drake’s Instagram handle is @ChampagnePapi. Before becoming the successful rapper that he is today, he could not imagine himself in this position. Champagne is expensive and most people save it for special occasions, but now he set Champagne as his standard because he can afford the lifestyle.", "annotation_id": "14879467", "url": "https://genius.com/14879467", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Elevate", "line": "If you need me, you can call me, I stay busy makin’ money You know what is on my mind, all I think about is hunnids I stay busy (Bzz) workin’ on me I stay busy with my business, homie", "vault_lines": ["I stay busy (Bzz) workin' on me", "I stay busy with my business, homie", "If you need me, you can call me, I stay busy makin' money", "You know what is on my mind, all I think about is hunnids"], "meaning": "Drake has dropped Views, More Life and Scorpion in the last 3 years. So we can say that he’s been pretty busy in the studio.\n\nHowever, he has also invested in several different companies. In 2016, he launched his first Bourbon Whiskey called Virginia Black, and, in the previous year, had invested money in a new tech start-up, Omni. He also recently signed a new deal with Apple Music.\n\nThere is also a clever wordplay here. “Hunnids” might be heard as “honey”, which is why in the following line he uses the onomatopea “bzz”. Drake is a busy bee!", "annotation_id": "14879403", "url": "https://genius.com/14879403", "state": "accepted", "votes": 52, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Elevate", "line": "I already hit her when you left her lonely She is not the type that likes to take things slowly", "vault_lines": ["I already hit her when you left her lonely", "She is not the type that likes to take things slowly"], "meaning": "He might be addressing his relationship with The Weeknd and Bella Hadid. Rumors suggest that Drake hooked up with Bella Hadid after she had broken up with The Weeknd. But you can read more about it here.\n\nDrake already said in the past that patience is not his best quality, especially when it comes to women.\n\nLord forgive me, I can’t take things slowly", "annotation_id": "14879365", "url": "https://genius.com/14879365", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Elevate", "line": "I wanna thank God for workin’ way harder than Satan He’s playin’ favourites, it feels amazin’ (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I wanna thank God for workin' way harder than Satan", "He's playin' favourites, it feels amazin' (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Drake continues to attribute his incredible success to God, in many ways feeling singled-out with support as underscored on his 2018 song, “God’s Plan”:\n\nGod’s plan, God’s plan\nI can’t do this on my own, ayy, no, ayy\nSomeone watchin' this shit close, yep, close\n\nPossibly influenced by his Jewish upbringing, Drake highlights God’s overpowering intervention against the trappings of Satan.\n\nDrake has previously referenced this struggle against the Devil on his 2016 collaboration with 21 Savage, “Sneakin”:\n\nThis is all God’s doin', man, you can’t plan it\nBut if the devil’s in the details, then I’m Satanic", "annotation_id": "14876949", "url": "https://genius.com/14876949", "state": "accepted", "votes": 90, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Elevate", "status": "done", "targets": 15, "clicked": 15, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-elevate-lyrics", "genius_title": "Elevate"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Growing Up", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-growing-up-lyrics", "genius_title": "Growing Up"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jorja Interlude", "line": "Flippin’ the script like a read-through", "vault_lines": ["Flippin' the script like a read-through"], "meaning": "“Flipping the script” is a figure of speech that means to subvert expectations and do something unexpected or revolutionary. Drake credits his success to his ability to flip the script.\n\nThe double entendre here is that “read-throughs” are readings of the script for produced media done by the cast (TV, Cinema, etc.), which Drake has undoubtedly participated in(owing to his performance on Degrassi). One physically flips a printed script while reading.", "annotation_id": "37329438", "url": "https://genius.com/37329438", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jorja Interlude", "line": "Worried ‘bout takin’ my lane They ain’t even got on the road", "vault_lines": ["Worried 'bout takin' my lane", "They ain't even got on the road"], "meaning": "“Taking somebody’s lane” means surpassing them. This is a double entendre, because it refers to driving and to being more successful than Drake.\nIn the second line Drizzy tells the competition they haven’t even started yet, they cannot be on his level.\nThis could be referring to Tory Lanez, with whom Drake has beefed before.", "annotation_id": "11756967", "url": "https://genius.com/11756967", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jorja Interlude", "line": "Told me I’m lookin’ exhausted You hit it right on the nose", "vault_lines": ["Told me I'm lookin' exhausted", "You hit it right on the nose"], "meaning": "It’s no stretch of the imagination that Drake’s tired. In 2016, he embarked on his Summer Sixteen Tour (the highest-grossing hip-hop tour of all time), which lasted from July to September. Immediately after it ended, he went on his The Boy Meets World Tour to support his album Views and promote More Life.", "annotation_id": "11542376", "url": "https://genius.com/11542376", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jorja Interlude", "line": "[Outro: Drake] And more chune for your headtop So watch how you speak on my name, you know?", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The outro is sampled from Drake’s acceptance speech after winning the “Favorite Artist Award” at the 2016 American Music Awards show.\n\nDrake states in Jamaican Patois that he has more tunes (chune) coming for your head (headtop) and warns people to show him respect.\n\nThis statement was said as a promotion for the then upcoming More Life playlist.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/AMAs/status/800532136876871680\n\nDuring the last refrain and outro of this song, Drake samples the harmonica, which is played by Stevie Wonder, from the outro of his song “Doing It Wrong” off his sophomore album Take Care", "annotation_id": "11541451", "url": "https://genius.com/11541451", "state": "accepted", "votes": 78, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jorja Interlude", "line": "You out here tellin’ everybody everything You niggas move like the one-two, yeah", "vault_lines": ["You out here tellin' everybody everything", "You niggas move like the one-two, yeah"], "meaning": "“12,” or 1-2 as Drake uses it, is a slang term for the police that derives from the 1960s and 1970s TV show Adam-12. Revealing operative information is a big part of undercover law enforcement work. Police officers are required to testify in cases when they have pertinent intel, and undercover detectives infiltrate gangs to glean information about them.\n\nDrake may be addressing Remy Ma’s claims that Meek Mill told her about all the intimate details of his relationship with Nicki Minaj. Drake previously called out Meek on Nicki’s diss track “No Frauds”:\n\nWhy do niggas that are not involved love to get involved?\nWhy do niggas claim the streets and act just like the law?\n\nDrizzy could also be referring to people in his own team releasing information about his work. After accusations surfaced that he was using a ghost writer, Funk Flex leaked Drake reference tracks of other artists, particularly Quentin Miller, performing early iterations of his songs. Later when Drake released “Summer Sixteen,” Meek immediately followed up with “War Pain,” claiming he was prepared because ghostwriters tipped him off.\n\nThis may also be a reference to the one-two step dance where dancers literally move to the words one and two.", "annotation_id": "11532013", "url": "https://genius.com/11532013", "state": "accepted", "votes": 58, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jorja Interlude", "line": "I play my part too, like a sequel", "vault_lines": ["I play my part too, like a sequel"], "meaning": "“Play my part” is an idiom that means “to do what you should do.” It’s also an allusion to acting since actors literally play a part, which is why Drake plays on the homophones “too” and “two”—a sequel is “part two” in a series of movies.", "annotation_id": "11530880", "url": "https://genius.com/11530880", "state": "accepted", "votes": 62, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jorja Interlude", "status": "done", "targets": 6, "clicked": 6, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-jorja-interlude-lyrics", "genius_title": "Jorja Interlude"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Lust for Life", "line": "[Outro] Throw your ones up in the air Throw your ones up in the air for her, oh-oh Throw your ones up in the air Throw your ones up", "vault_lines": ["Throw your ones up in the air for her, oh-oh", "Throw your ones up"], "meaning": "This is the pre-chorus for the next song in So Far Gone, Houstatlantavegas. The phrase “throw your ones up in the air” refers to tossing one-dollar bills at the stripper as she dances.", "annotation_id": "36789680", "url": "https://genius.com/36789680", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Lust for Life", "line": "Everything is going as right as it can They tryna shoot down my flight before it lands, before it lands", "vault_lines": ["Everything is going as right as it can", "They tryna shoot down my flight before it lands, before it lands"], "meaning": "Drake believes that everything is going his way, but that there are people out there that are jealous of him", "annotation_id": "28593027", "url": "https://genius.com/28593027", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Lust for Life", "line": "I got plans I got a certain lust for life and as it stands", "vault_lines": ["I got a certain lust for life and as it stands"], "meaning": "Drake is saying that though he loves where he is, he is very busy, and that it will stay that way forever", "annotation_id": "28593011", "url": "https://genius.com/28593011", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Lust for Life", "line": "It’s funny when you comin’ in first, but you hope that you last You just hope that it last", "vault_lines": ["It's funny when you comin' in first, but you hope that you last", "You just hope that it last"], "meaning": "When you’re “first”, being extremely successful and having everything you want, you will always hope that it’ll last forever.", "annotation_id": "22072866", "url": "https://genius.com/22072866", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Lust for Life", "line": "And show up in a Margiela tux, I don’t really give a fuck", "vault_lines": ["And show up in a Margiela tux, I don't really give a fuck"], "meaning": "Maison Margiela is a French fashion company known for high-end products. Here Drake is saying that he could come to the club or your girl’s house with an expensive Margiela tux on and still be nonchalant.", "annotation_id": "20214505", "url": "https://genius.com/20214505", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Lust for Life", "line": "Fresher than a pillow with a mint on it", "vault_lines": ["Fresher than a pillow with a mint on it"], "meaning": "Drake is comparing his fresh style to a luxury hotel. Often, if you are in a good category hotel one of the little things they do to make you feel welcome is to leave a chocolate or mint on the bed pillow when they make up the room each day. In other words, they take care of you, or spoil you.", "annotation_id": "16491149", "url": "https://genius.com/16491149", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Lust for Life", "line": "The game got these old handprints on it But I’mma be the one to pour cement on it Uh, and start over", "vault_lines": ["The game got these old handprints on it", "But I'mma be the one to pour cement on it", "Uh, and start over"], "meaning": "When wet cement gets put laid, you can stick your hand in it and create a mold that lasts for years. But since Drake views himself as the leader of the new wave of rappers, he plans on paving over the metaphorical handprints to give everyone in the game a blank canvas to work with.", "annotation_id": "81546", "url": "https://genius.com/81546", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Lust for Life", "line": "Sayin’ she should be the one I see every time that I’m here But when am I really even here?", "vault_lines": ["Sayin' she should be the one I see every time that I'm here", "But when am I really even here?"], "meaning": "He’s always touring, in the studio in the States etc. that he doesn’t have time. Even if he’s in town he’ll be busy with bigger and better things.\n\nThis also speaks to the lies that Drake, and many other rappers/celebs, always tells women.  “Saying she should be the one I see every time that I’m here” is an example of Drake “spitting game” to try and get with her that night.  “But when am I really even here” seems to be Drake’s internal monologue; his way of acknowledging that he’s just lying to this chick.", "annotation_id": "81417", "url": "https://genius.com/81417", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Lust for Life", "line": "I’m tryna do it all tonight", "vault_lines": ["I'm tryna do it all tonight"], "meaning": "“Tonight” might be a Drake’s idea of him getting a mainstream attention. Same meaning found on the next album’s single “Over.”\n\nIdea of “faking ‘till making” is mentioned several times during Drake’s career, also on a single of a “Thank Me Later,” “Headlines” and on a track “Underground Kingz.”", "annotation_id": "81351", "url": "https://genius.com/81351", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
