{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Prioritizing", "line": "Spoon-feeding you my suggestions", "vault_lines": ["Spoon-feeding you my suggestions"], "meaning": "Means you’re constantly giving advice, support, and direction like a parent, but she’s not receiving or growing from it — just taking. Highlights the one-sided effort and exhaustion in the dynamic.", "annotation_id": "39959839", "url": "https://genius.com/39959839", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Prioritizing", "line": "What is the reality of moving away?", "vault_lines": ["What is the reality of moving away?"], "meaning": "Will the relief be real, or will I just carry the weight with me?\nWill I miss the chaos more than I admit?\nCan I actually stand on my own without her love defining me?\nIs the terror of the unknown worse than the terror of staying?", "annotation_id": "39959818", "url": "https://genius.com/39959818", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Prioritizing", "line": "Time for some prioritizing Time to open both those eyelids All these drinks are paralyzing Life right now is terrifying", "vault_lines": ["Time for some prioritizing", "Time to open both those eyelids", "All these drinks are paralyzing", "Life right now is terrifying"], "meaning": "you’re in that foggy 4 AM headspace—half buzzed, half spiraling, realizing the party’s over and reality’s knocking loud as hell.", "annotation_id": "39959801", "url": "https://genius.com/39959801", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Prioritizing", "line": "Time for some prioritizing Time to open both those eyelids All these drinks are paralyzing Life right now is terrifying", "vault_lines": ["Time for some prioritizing", "Time to open both those eyelids", "All these drinks are paralyzing", "Life right now is terrifying"], "meaning": "that terrifying feeling usually means your brain is screaming that something needs to change. The drinks are numbing it, but they’re also making the problems louder the next day.", "annotation_id": "39959791", "url": "https://genius.com/39959791", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Prioritizing", "line": "50K on one bag, you are having your way", "vault_lines": ["50K on one bag, you are having your way"], "meaning": "She is now making so much money, she can purchase a bag from Hermès or Chanel.", "annotation_id": "39959730", "url": "https://genius.com/39959730", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Prioritizing", "line": "So much we could question, so much they don’t explain", "vault_lines": ["So much we could question, so much they don't explain"], "meaning": "So much sinister things we can question that politicians have done, so much actions that they will never explain.", "annotation_id": "39959715", "url": "https://genius.com/39959715", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Prioritizing", "line": "Politicians, villains, they all one and the same", "vault_lines": ["Politicians, villains, they all one and the same"], "meaning": "Politicians sell lies and dreams to their voters, and once in power, they often sell their influence to the highest bidder… Which often doesn’t help those who voted the politician into office. Not much different from Villains we see on TV.", "annotation_id": "39959695", "url": "https://genius.com/39959695", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Prioritizing", "line": "A good job is like Waldo, don’t know where to find ’em", "vault_lines": ["A good job is like Waldo, don't know where to find 'em"], "meaning": "Drake uses a simile which references the animated children show “Where’s Waldo?” to liken the search for Waldo to a search for a good job.\n\nIn this line Drake either comments generally on the job market being devoid of quality jobs (either in pay, purpose, or both). Or alternatively Drake might be conveying a sarcastic dig at the person he’s addressing in the song, saying that they don’t know where to find a good job because they aren’t even making an attempt to find one for themselves, just like they aren’t searching for Waldo.", "annotation_id": "39779590", "url": "https://genius.com/39779590", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Prioritizing", "line": "Anxiety and high depression, seasonal if I was guessing", "vault_lines": ["Anxiety and high depression, seasonal if I was guessing"], "meaning": "Mental illnesses can be seasonal, especially bipolar disorder and PTSD (Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder). This means that these illnesses worsen around certain times of year or around the anniversary of a traumatic event. Interestingly, this phrasing could also be a loose reference to Drake’s mixtape, “Comeback Season.”", "annotation_id": "39857761", "url": "https://genius.com/39857761", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Prioritizing", "line": "Karma is about to come knocking", "vault_lines": ["Karma is about to come knocking"], "meaning": "In the context of the previous and following lines, the karma which Drake refers to, meaning the consequences for one’s actions, is karma to the entire modern humanity for its unchecked technological advancement and over dependence on media consumption and mass surveillance. Drake foresees the negative consequences for this arriving soon.", "annotation_id": "39832813", "url": "https://genius.com/39832813", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Prioritizing", "line": "Under her microscope, I be failin’ signs", "vault_lines": ["Under her microscope, I be failin' signs"], "meaning": "The lyric is “under her microscope, I be failin’ science”\n\nHe’s saying in her eyes, he’s falling short and not making the grade. Also the idea of putting someone under a microscope can mean to apply intense scrutiny or be overly critical.", "annotation_id": "39813611", "url": "https://genius.com/39813611", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Prioritizing", "line": "How many matchas can you consume in a day?", "vault_lines": ["How many matchas can you consume in a day?"], "meaning": "Matcha represents the modern obsession with wellness trends and ‘clean girl’ routines from japanese culture.\nDrake turns a trendy healthy drink into a dramatic existential question, which makes the line unexpectedly funny.\nThe line jokes about how modern self-care culture turns drinking green tea into a full-time personality trait.", "annotation_id": "39809191", "url": "https://genius.com/39809191", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Prioritizing", "line": "I’m so scared for what those times are gonna be like", "vault_lines": ["I'm so scared for what those times are gonna be like"], "meaning": "Drake is scared about what the future of this world looks like", "annotation_id": "39796094", "url": "https://genius.com/39796094", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Prioritizing", "line": "Ladies used to be free before 10 every night Now they got you all in a line standing outside", "vault_lines": ["Ladies used to be free before 10 every night", "Now they got you all in a line standing outside"], "meaning": "Drake is referring to the current generation lacking good women to take on dates. The reference to 10pm at night emphasizes the common age old saying that nothing good happens after dark. After 10, you have girls in the club, onlyfans girls, and escorts who work late at night while men end up tricking and waiting in line to get their turn at her.", "annotation_id": "39796065", "url": "https://genius.com/39796065", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Prioritizing", "line": "You don’t have a gag reflex, it’s blowing my mind", "vault_lines": ["You don't have a gag reflex, it's blowing my mind"], "meaning": "Drake is amazed at this girl not having a gag reflex, an involuntary muscle contraction preventing choking during oral sex. At the same time blowing someone’s mind is a synonyme for oral sex.", "annotation_id": "39792830", "url": "https://genius.com/39792830", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
