{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Summer Games", "line": "I kept it decent I kept you sane, I kept it peaceful, don’t lie", "vault_lines": ["I kept it decent", "I kept you sane, I kept it peaceful, don't lie"], "meaning": "Saying he was the one to hold her down and keep them together", "annotation_id": "31123651", "url": "https://genius.com/31123651", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Summer Games", "line": "You said “I love you” too fast So much for that, cause Summer just started, and we’re already done", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, you said \"I love you\" too fast", "So much for that, cause", "Summer just started, and we're already done", "You said \"I love you\" too fast", "So much for that, 'cause summer just started", "And we're already done"], "meaning": "", "annotation_id": "30251277", "url": "https://genius.com/30251277", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": false, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Summer Games", "line": "I used to love a good surprise And now, I’d rather know ahead of time", "vault_lines": ["I used to love a good surprise", "And now, I'd rather know ahead of time"], "meaning": "Here Drake is starting to acknowledge how tiring a relationship in this modern technological age we live in is. He wants to be in a relationship that doesn’t seem like he’s just waisting his time or just filling up time either.\n\nIn this day and age relationships don’t hold as much meaning, they’re all about status and how the other person makes you look, rather than how they make you feel.\n\nDrake has outgrown this and wants something real and simple, he wants to know where he stands with someone, whereas with this person he doesn’t know where he stands and their relationship seems to be complex and confusing to him.", "annotation_id": "29603528", "url": "https://genius.com/29603528", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Summer Games", "line": "How can you be angry on a night in July And be warm with me when it’s freezing outside You’re confusin’ me Don’t have me wastin’ my time", "vault_lines": ["How can you be angry on a night in July", "And be warm with me when it's freezing outside", "Don't have me wastin' my time", "You're confusin' me, don't have me wastin' my time"], "meaning": "Referring to the title of this song, “Summer Games”, July is known to be one of the hottest months during the summertime.\n\nIn these lines, Drake is having a conversation with a woman who’s been angry or upset at him and he’s questioning her motive(s).\n\nShe’s hot and cold with him all at the same time which is confusing him. He doesn’t want to waste his time if she’s going to continue to be this way.", "annotation_id": "29252422", "url": "https://genius.com/29252422", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Summer Games", "line": "Yeah, you say I led you on, but you followed me I follow one of your friends, you unfollow me Then you block them so they can’t see You liking someone just like me", "vault_lines": ["Then you block them so they can't see", "You liking someone just like me", "Yeah, you say I led you on, but you followed me", "I follow one of your friends, you unfollow me"], "meaning": "Drake is talking about a girl on some social media platform, most likely Instagram. Drake is known for talking, rapping, and singing about how technology and the internet only serve to alienate us from each other. On 0 to 100, Drake talks about the fear that a partner will get upset if she keeps scrolling through the pictures on his phone. With the release of Scorpion, Drake isn’t just tired of the internet, he’s having an existential crisis over it. He is entrenched in the internet because he has to be, but he doesn’t know what to do with it. It fuels him and tears him apart in equal measure. Whether on Emotionless where Drake says,\n\nI know a girl whose one goal was to visit Rome\nThen she finally got to Rome\nAnd all she did was post pictures for people at home\n’Cause all that mattered was impressin’ everybody she’s known\nI know another girl that’s cryin’ out for help\nBut her latest caption is “Leave me alone”\nI know a girl happily married ‘til she puts down her phone\nI know a girl that saves pictures from places she’s flown\nTo post later and make it look like she still on the go\n\nThis sentiment is also seen in Can’t Take a Joke where Drake confesses that nasty posts from anonymous strangers eat away at him.\n\nMy comment section killin’ me.\nI swear I get so passionate, y’all do not know the half of it.", "annotation_id": "14883650", "url": "https://genius.com/14883650", "state": "accepted", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Summer Games", "line": "Breakin’ my heart, tearin’ me apart Breakin’ me down when I’m already down Breakin’ my heart– breakin’ my heart– breakin’ my heart Breakin’ my heart– breakin’ my heart– Brea– brea– brea– brea– brea– brea– brea– brea Breakin’ my heart, tearin’ me apart Breakin’ me down when I’m already down Breakin’ my heart– breakin’ my heart– breakin’ my heart Breakin’ my heart– breakin’ my heart– Brea– brea– brea– brea– brea– brea– brea– brea– brea", "vault_lines": ["Breakin' my heart, tearin' me apart", "Breakin' me down when I'm already down", "Breakin' my heart– breakin' my heart– breakin' my heart", "Breakin' my heart– breakin' my heart–", "Brea– brea– brea– brea– brea– brea– brea– brea", "Brea– brea– brea– brea– brea– brea– brea– brea– brea"], "meaning": "From the perspective of a fan or someone outside his inner circle, Drake is considered to be a sensitive person. This is supported by Drake’s star sign being Scorpio; someone who is traditionally very passionate and values trust from those close to them more than other things in life. In fact, there are various memes across the internet to suggest that he is a very emotionally-invested human being.\n\n\n\nIt also shows in Drake music that he cares for women. While other prominent rappers such as 21 Savage and Kanye West brag about their “bitches” and “hoes”, Drake doesn’t often involve himself with those lyrical sentiments. Furthermore, the refrain on “Hold On, We’re Going Home” shows that he may very well have a lot of room in his heart for someone special:\n\nI got my eyes on you\nYou’re everything that I see\nI want your hot love and emotion endlessly\nI can’t get over you\nYou left your mark on me\nI want your hot love and emotion endlessly\n\nThis end to the verse indicates that another woman has “broken his heart”. However, when considering his emotionally-investive lyrics in the past, it wouldn’t be at all surprising that Drake has had his heart broken again.", "annotation_id": "14878078", "url": "https://genius.com/14878078", "state": "accepted", "votes": 45, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Summer Games", "status": "done", "targets": 8, "clicked": 8, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-summer-games-lyrics", "genius_title": "Summer Games"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Teenage Fever", "line": "You’re to blame for what we could have been ’cause look at what we are", "vault_lines": ["You're to blame for what we could have been 'cause look at what we are"], "meaning": "Drake feels that if the female would have put more effort into the relationship things may have worked out.", "annotation_id": "22140885", "url": "https://genius.com/22140885", "state": "pending", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Teenage Fever", "line": "This shit feels like teenage fever I’m not scared of it, she ain’t either Why second guess? I should have stayed ’Cause you know what’s on my mind, so", "vault_lines": ["Why second guess? I should have stayed", "This shit feels like teenage fever", "I'm not scared of it, she ain't either", "'Cause you know what's on my mind, so", "And you know what's on my mind, this time", "And you know what's on my mind, so"], "meaning": "A common symptom of “teenage fever” is simply indecisiveness, which leads to hesitation as a person is unsure whether romantic feelings are mutual, due to a lack of experience in the dating game.\n\nEven though Drake has an incredible amount of experience with romance; from dating pop star Rihanna to world tennis champion Serena Williams, and most recently Jennifer Lopez, and the fact he’s a worldwide superstar, the girl he’s just met is forcing him back into the position of the common teenager, suffering from the infamous “teenage fever.”", "annotation_id": "11579814", "url": "https://genius.com/11579814", "state": "accepted", "votes": 91, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Teenage Fever", "line": "I met someone new last night and we kicked it And I’m going back there tonight And you know what’s on my mind, this time Going back there tonight And you know what’s on my mind, so", "vault_lines": ["Last night we didn't say it", "'Cause you know what's on my mind, so", "I met someone new last night and we kicked it", "And I'm going back there tonight", "And you know what's on my mind, this time", "Going back there tonight", "And you know what's on my mind, so"], "meaning": "Since Drake’s love interest is unresponsive to his emotional signals, he’s spending time with another woman, likely to take his mind off of the troubles of unfulfilled romance.\n\nThis is not the first time Drake has chosen to substitute a woman with another just to avoid being lonely.", "annotation_id": "11564812", "url": "https://genius.com/11564812", "state": "accepted", "votes": 120, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Teenage Fever", "line": "Last night we didn’t say it But girl, we both thought it Why second guess? I should have stayed You say the word, I’m on the way", "vault_lines": ["Last night we didn't say it", "But girl, we both thought it", "Why second guess? I should have stayed", "You say the word, I'm on the way"], "meaning": "They didn’t say they wanted to have sex with each other, but the look in their eyes was enough that they both knew.\n\nUnfortunately for Drake, he hesitated and did not take that chance to make a move on her, so the night ended with him leaving. Anyone who’s had feelings for someone can relate to this, especially when it’s uncertain if the other person shares the same feelings as Drake probably thought.\n\nLooking back at that moment, he regrets second-guessing the situation. He tries to relieve his inner turmoil by telling her that, if she gives him that vibe again, he will be ready for that opportunity again.", "annotation_id": "11541750", "url": "https://genius.com/11541750", "state": "accepted", "votes": 78, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Teenage Fever", "line": "Your heart is hard to carry after dark", "vault_lines": ["Your heart is hard to carry after dark"], "meaning": "The expression, ‘carry your heart,’ was popularized by e. e. cummings' poem, “I carry your heart with me(i carry it in my heart)”. It refers to the kind of deep and profound love.\n\nDrake has trouble maintaining the integrity of this sensual love late at night when there is ample temptation, and before the end of the verse, he finds another love interest.\n\nHe’s likely having trouble with love because of the relationship problems he describes in the first verse; arguing, cheating, and selfishness.", "annotation_id": "11536011", "url": "https://genius.com/11536011", "state": "accepted", "votes": 135, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Teenage Fever", "line": "[Chorus: Jennifer Lopez] If you had my love And I gave you all my trust Would you comfort me? And if somehow you knew That your love would be untrue Would you lie to me? If you had my love And I gave you all my trust Would you comfort me? And if somehow you knew That your love would be untrue Would you lie to me?", "vault_lines": ["If you had my love", "And I gave you all my trust", "Would you comfort me?", "And if somehow you knew", "That your love would be untrue", "Would you lie to me?"], "meaning": "This chorus was sampled from American singer Jennifer Lopez’s 1999 hit “If You Had My Love.” from her album On The 6.\n\nDrake and Lopez were rumored to be dating after posting photos and videos together on their social media accounts a few months before the release of More Life. In an appearance on The Ellen Show, Lopez confirmed that the duo had collaborated, but she was unsure of where the track would end up.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/op_BiLgnAwY?t=4m10s\n\nSince this chorus is sampled, it’s likely that this isn’t the song Lopez referred to, and their impending collaboration is still yet to come.", "annotation_id": "11534812", "url": "https://genius.com/11534812", "state": "accepted", "votes": 290, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Teenage Fever", "line": "Your friends are scared to tell you you went too far Funny that it’s always been all about you from the start", "vault_lines": ["Your friends are scared to tell you you went too far", "Funny that it's always been all about you from the start"], "meaning": "Drake and his love interest are at a breaking point in their relationship. In the previous line he blames her for their current status, suggesting her behavior has created mistrust and hostility.\n\nWhen people argue they often do or say things to hurt one another, and “taking it too far” means the girl has gone beyond the bounds of arguing, causing irreparable damage to the relationship. Her friends are hesitant to tell her the truth about her actions, likely because they want to remain supportive.\n\nDrake recalls that since the start of the relationship she has been very self-centered, instead of reciprocating his love. This is likely why he seeks new companionship in the next line.", "annotation_id": "11534131", "url": "https://genius.com/11534131", "state": "accepted", "votes": 93, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Teenage Fever", "line": "Out of body That’s just how I feel when I’m around you, shawty", "vault_lines": ["That's just how I feel when I'm around you, shawty"], "meaning": "An out-of-body experience is an experience that typically involves a feeling of floating outside one’s body and, in some cases, the feeling of perceiving one’s physical body as if from a place outside one’s body.\n\nDrake is saying that when he is around this girl, it feels like his soul leaves his body as if he’s divine. This sounds like an extreme case of the butterflies.\n\nSurprisingly, this sounds similar to the feeling Drake described in 2010 when talking about Rihanna.", "annotation_id": "11534102", "url": "https://genius.com/11534102", "state": "accepted", "votes": 128, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Teenage Fever", "line": "[Outro: Dave] Yeah, slightly, huh, took a left turn there But very much 6 a.m.​ Slightly been awake for twenty-four hours So please forgive me More ideas and stuff comin’ Yeah, yeah, fam, I’m wafflin’ But man is tired, fam, Jesus Christ", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, slightly, huh, took a left turn there", "But very much 6 a.m.​", "Slightly been awake for twenty-four hours", "So please forgive me", "More ideas and stuff comin'", "Yeah, yeah, fam, I'm wafflin'", "But man is tired, fam, Jesus Christ"], "meaning": "Santan Dave, also known simply as Dave, is a British rapper hailing from South London. His lyrics touch upon conscious topics such as decision-making and inspiring fellow young people to become who they want to be.\n\nAlready an established artist in the UK by the time of the release of More Life, he gained attention overseas when Drake remixed his song “Wanna Know” and premiered it on OVO Sound Radio.\n\nDave explained to Ebro that he was unaware that the voice note would appear on the album, and it was a genuine conversation he’d been having:\n\nhttps://youtu.be/yEH6IU7pDOg?t=1778", "annotation_id": "11533288", "url": "https://genius.com/11533288", "state": "accepted", "votes": 243, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Teenage Fever", "status": "done", "targets": 9, "clicked": 9, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-teenage-fever-lyrics", "genius_title": "Teenage Fever"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Tim Westwood Freestyle 2012", "line": "This also for the hood stars that I created Whose booking rate went up right after we dated Girl you made it for real", "vault_lines": ["This also for the hood stars that I created", "Whose booking rate went up right after we dated", "Girl you made it for real"], "meaning": "Probably referring to Maliah Michel, an ordinary stripper who Drizzy had feelings for & dated. Her booking rates for performances greatly rose after the affair with Drake. So in a way she made it.", "annotation_id": "666338", "url": "https://genius.com/666338", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
