{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Brand New", "line": "And I hate hearing stories ’bout who you’ve been with That’s when I gotta hide what I’m feeling inside", "vault_lines": ["And I hate hearing stories 'bout who you've been with", "That's when I gotta hide what I'm feeling inside", "That's why I gotta ask"], "meaning": "Drake does not enjoy hearing stories about past partners of women he is around, since it makes him feel jealous, so he has to hide that negative feeling so that the woman thinks hes doesn’t care.", "annotation_id": "40763816", "url": "https://genius.com/40763816", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Brand New", "line": "Oh, girl (Ayy, ayy, ayy)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The “Ayy, ayy, ayy” are the same in “Forever”. But slowed.", "annotation_id": "30785693", "url": "https://genius.com/30785693", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Brand New", "line": "Did he take your clothes off just like this? Did he give you loving just like this? Did you spend the night in his bed on the very first date? Tell me baby, am I too late?", "vault_lines": ["Late, late, late, late", "Did he take your clothes off just like this?", "Did he give you loving just like this?", "Did you spend the night in his bed on the very first date?", "Tell me baby, am I too late?"], "meaning": "Perhaps while Drake and this lover have been apart–whether because they hadn’t met yet or were on a temporary break from their relationship–the girl slept with other men. Drake wonders whether he’s changed his ways too late. Or maybe he wonders if he simply met this girl too late in her life to ever have a chance with her.", "annotation_id": "25193403", "url": "https://genius.com/25193403", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Brand New", "line": "Or is everything I’m doing too late? Late, late, late, late", "vault_lines": ["Or is everything I'm doing too late?", "Late, late, late, late"], "meaning": "If we interpret this song as Drake speaking to a lover he is in an on-and-off relationship with, it would make sense for him to ask, “is everything I’ve done to change simply coming too late to fix what we had?”", "annotation_id": "25193394", "url": "https://genius.com/25193394", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Brand New", "line": "Racing against myself, but I’m a couple steps behind", "vault_lines": ["Racing against myself, but I'm a couple steps behind"], "meaning": "This line hammers home the three-sided interpretation of this song.\n\nHe’s racing against his own past, wondering whether everything he’s doing here is any different from the mistakes he’s pulled before (either with (1) this girl whom he’s in an on-and-off relationship with, or (2) previous girls from his past).\n\nHe’s also wondering whether, (3), to the girl, he is any better than her previous lovers, if we assume they’ve never met before.", "annotation_id": "25193375", "url": "https://genius.com/25193375", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Brand New", "line": "Is anything I’m doin’ brand new? Brand new (Brand new), brand new (Brand new), brand new", "vault_lines": ["Is anything I'm doin' brand new?", "Brand new (Brand new), brand new (Brand new), brand new", "Brand new (Brand new), brand new, brand new, brand new", "New, new, new, new, new"], "meaning": "The three meanings of this song play out again:\n\n\nDrake wonders whether the sex and romancing he’s giving his new lover seems fresh enough to her to keep him around – or if he’s just another notch on her belt, soon to be discarded.\nHe could also be asking himself, am I doing anything new here? Will I change from my old, dysfunctional ways from previous relationships? Or am I just replaying the same scenario that always plays out, where I worry what my girl is thinking of me, and whether I measure up, only to destroy it in the end?\nFinally he could be asking his former lover if anything this time around is different enough to actually keep it steady once and for all.", "annotation_id": "25193353", "url": "https://genius.com/25193353", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Brand New", "line": "Feel like I’m in crazy competition with the past That’s why I gotta ask", "vault_lines": ["Feel like I'm in crazy competition with the past", "That's why I gotta ask"], "meaning": "Three meanings:\n\n\nDrake could be referring to how he’s in competition with the sexual/romantic prowess of this woman’s past lovers, and is unsure whether he’ll measure up;\nDrake could also be referring to being in competition with the demons from his own past, and wondering whether his intimacy issues from past relationships will haunt him in this new one;\nDrake could be in an on-and-off relationship with this woman and is wondering whether it’s too late for both of them at this point.", "annotation_id": "25193326", "url": "https://genius.com/25193326", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Brand New", "status": "done", "targets": 7, "clicked": 7, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-brand-new-lyrics", "genius_title": "Brand New"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Flight’s Booked", "line": "Sometimes, we all feel hollow My heart, girl, you can borrow, mmm Please don’t make this song about you Please don’t make this song about you Please don’t make this song about you Please don’t make this song about you", "vault_lines": ["Sometimes, we all feel hollow", "My heart, girl, you can borrow, mmm", "Please don't make this song about you"], "meaning": "Here in the Outro (who sang it is not specified) the person is saying to his girl that sometimes we all feel hollow,most likely proposing the girl is going through something.\n\nHe then says this girl can borrow his heart, likely meaning hes willing to share the love from his heart to hers to try heal her from what shes going through\n\nHere Genius got the lyrics wrong. the actual lyrics are >“Please dont make this all about you”\n\nwhich goes back to the previous line where he says we all feel hollow, this girl is probably acting like shes the only person going through something and making it all about herself", "annotation_id": "40692259", "url": "https://genius.com/40692259", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Flight’s Booked", "line": "Lilah I know it’s getting late And I’m struggling to let go Although there’s distance between us There’s no place I’d rather be", "vault_lines": ["Although there's distance between us", "There's no place I'd rather be", "I know it's getting late", "And I'm struggling to let go"], "meaning": "Lilah Pi and Drake have had a rocky relationship, with the two rumored to be involved, but never officially dating. The two artists are separated physically, with Drake hailing from Toronto and Lilah based out of London. He elaborates on their struggles, emphasizing that despite them either being apart and growing apart, he still wants to be in the relationship. The name Lilah also means night in Arabic and Hebrew, as Drake uses her name to cleverly set-up his following lines.\n\nWhile this is the first mention of Lilah in his music, Drake would go on to namedrop Lilah, appearing on J Hus' June 2023 track, “\nWho Told You”, and saying:\n\nSo Lilah Pi, don’t make my eye cry\nLet me hold your controlla, I am not one of these controlling guys", "annotation_id": "26331780", "url": "https://genius.com/26331780", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Flight’s Booked", "line": "Getting late Why you gotta be Beside me Watching, needing, wanting me I’m afraid, don’t be I’m afraid, don’t be I’m afraid, don’t be I’m afraid, don’t be I’m afraid Don’t— , be—, don’t— Don’t— , be—, don’t— Don’t— , be—, don’t— Don’t— , be—, don’t— Don’t— , be—, don’t— Don’t— , be—, don’t— Don’t— , be—, don’t— Don’t— , be—, don’t—", "vault_lines": ["Why you gotta be", "Baby, don't be afraid", "Watching, needing, wanting me", "I'm afraid, don't be"], "meaning": "This is a slowed-down and chopped sample from the English R&B duo—conformed by Marsha Ambrosius and Natalie Stewart—Floetry’s 2003 single, “Getting Late.”\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=luuqF4bM_hw", "annotation_id": "26076820", "url": "https://genius.com/26076820", "state": "accepted", "votes": 73, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
