{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Legend", "line": "[Produced by PARTYNEXTDOOR]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The track samples Ginuwine’s “So Anxious.” The samples occur at 0:03, 1:03 and 3:43.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DT-75YEclqg", "annotation_id": "8641055", "url": "https://genius.com/8641055", "state": "accepted", "votes": 54, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Legend", "line": "Got a girl, she from the South Used to work, used to dance in Texas, now she clean the house", "vault_lines": ["got a girl, she from the South", "Used to work, used to dance in Texas, now she clean the house"], "meaning": "Drake also used this line to show that he can, in fact, “turn a hoe into a housewife”.", "annotation_id": "5212078", "url": "https://genius.com/5212078", "state": "verified", "votes": 54, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Legend", "line": "[Chorus]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This hook is ~absolutely~ about the death of Socrates. After being sentenced to death for crimes of corrupting the youth and the impiety of refusing the Athenian gods and introducing new deities, his death by hemlock was postponed until the end of the festival Delia. The interval inspired his friend Crito to offer escape and exile outside of Athens. Socrates knew that by accepting the offer, all of his principles regarding respecting the laws would immediately vanish, and his naysayers' desires to discredit him would finally gain credibility. Hence, the necessity for him to die to become a legend.", "annotation_id": "5063054", "url": "https://genius.com/5063054", "state": "verified", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Legend", "line": "And I, I just can’t pretend Seen too much, it’s so hard for me to let new people in", "vault_lines": ["And I, I just can't pretend", "Seen too much, it's so hard for me to let new people in"], "meaning": "As we all know Drake isn’t the type of guy to make new acquaintances.", "annotation_id": "5051286", "url": "https://genius.com/5051286", "state": "verified", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Legend", "line": "[Chorus]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake feels like due to his success as a rapper that when he dies, he will go down as one of the greatest of all time. A standard set for artists behind him", "annotation_id": "5046486", "url": "https://genius.com/5046486", "state": "verified", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Legend", "line": "Everyday, I was strugglin’ to learn what life’s about On my way, money taught me Spanish, make it ándale", "vault_lines": ["On my way, money taught me Spanish, make it ándale", "Everyday, I was strugglin' to learn what life's about"], "meaning": "Although it may sound like andale, it may be “on-delay” due to the fact that his new album wont be coming out for a while, and will probably generate a lot of profit.", "annotation_id": "5023358", "url": "https://genius.com/5023358", "state": "verified", "votes": -68, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Legend", "line": "When I pull up on a nigga tell that nigga back, back I’m too good with these words, watch a nigga backtrack", "vault_lines": ["When I pull up on a nigga tell that nigga back, back", "I'm too good with these words, watch a nigga backtrack", "I'm up first, I'm on tour,"], "meaning": "When he says “back track” he is also talking about when other rappers say things about him in songs, or in interviews they end up back tracking. Drake ends up having the better words and they have to make peace for the sake of their career.", "annotation_id": "4961866", "url": "https://genius.com/4961866", "state": "verified", "votes": 70, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Legend", "line": "I’m up first, I’m on tour,", "vault_lines": ["I'm up first, I'm on tour,"], "meaning": "On their 2014 collaborative tour Drake vs. Lil Wayne, he and his mentor let the audience choose who of the two would begin the section of the concert where they go head-to-head performing their biggest songs.\n\nhttps://vimeo.com/103026461", "annotation_id": "4890733", "url": "https://genius.com/4890733", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Legend", "line": "And I, I just can’t pretend Seen too much, it’s so hard for me to let new people in", "vault_lines": ["And I, I just can't pretend", "Seen too much, it's so hard for me to let new people in"], "meaning": "A Jewish mother in a comfortable Toronto suburb. A black father in Memphis. A successful career as a TV actor, and a world famous rapper. Drake’s seen a lot.\n\nHe repeats this sentiment on the outro for this project, saying he’s seen it all.\n\nHe’s actually been saying this for years:\n\nI’ve seen a lot, man. I’ve seen a lot of life, put it that way. I’ve been with the most blessed kids in the world. I’ve been with people whose life is right at the bottom of the barrel. I was on a TV show, I went to art school, I went to hood schools. I’ve lived. I’ve lived a full 24 years, man.", "annotation_id": "4890646", "url": "https://genius.com/4890646", "state": "accepted", "votes": 44, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Legend", "line": "They been off for a minute now You know they all sentimental now You know they all actin’ different now", "vault_lines": ["They been off for a minute now", "You know they all sentimental now", "You know they all actin' different now"], "meaning": "Nothing was the same when Drizzy blew up. There are many that used to hate, but now show love to the Papi.\n\n\n\nDrake hopped on Makonnen’s “Tuesday” and made Makonnen an overnight celebrity. Makonnen explains how it was the best Tuesday ever. His opinion of Drake is surely different now.\n\n\n\nFreddie Gibbs didn’t have great things to say about Drake in ‘09, but in 2014 he referred to Drake as “the best songwriter of our time.”", "annotation_id": "4889613", "url": "https://genius.com/4889613", "state": "accepted", "votes": 36, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Legend", "line": "It’s too late for my city, I’m the youngest nigga reppin’", "vault_lines": ["I'm the one, one", "It's too late for my city, I'm the youngest nigga reppin'"], "meaning": "Oh Lord, I’m the rookie and the vet\"\n\nAt the age of 28 Drake isn’t very young, but he’s the only rapper from Toronto, or even Canada, who is a major player in the rap game.", "annotation_id": "4889583", "url": "https://genius.com/4889583", "state": "accepted", "votes": 151, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Legend", "line": "6 G-O-D, I’m the holy one Yeah, you know wassup", "vault_lines": ["I'm the one, one", "6 G-O-D, I'm the holy one", "Yeah, you know wassup"], "meaning": "Towards the end of 2014, Drake revealed that he was the 6 God. This is him feeling his power and importance to Toronto, as the “6 side” refers to the city’s 416 /647 area codes.\n\nhttp://instagram.com/p/y3GCL0DQOU/?modal=true", "annotation_id": "4889570", "url": "https://genius.com/4889570", "state": "accepted", "votes": 77, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Legend", "line": "Oh my God, oh my God, if I die, I’m a legend Oh my God, oh my God, if I die, I’m a legend", "vault_lines": ["All I know, if I die, I'm a mothafuckin' legend", "If I die, all I know is I'm a mothafuckin' legend", "Oh my God, oh my God, if I die, I'm a legend"], "meaning": "Many people believe Drake has ten more years to go, but he feels like a legend in the present. Drizzy broke the Beatles record on Billboard Hot 100, and, in only five years, he was the artist with the most #1 songs on the Hip-Hop and R&B Billboard chart.\n\nAs JAY-Z said:\n\nMen lie, women lie, numbers don’t\n\nYoung Jeezy also used a similar line in his featuring verse on Drizzy’s 2009 single “I’m Goin In”:\n\nAnd I'ma be a legend even when my life end\nAnd I'ma be a legend even when this night ends", "annotation_id": "4889452", "url": "https://genius.com/4889452", "state": "accepted", "votes": 235, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Legend", "line": "Fuck ‘em all, they only pussy niggas shootin’ at the star", "vault_lines": ["Fuck 'em all, they only pussy niggas shootin' at the star"], "meaning": "Someone tells another to “shoot for the stars” to influence them to challenge themselves past their limits.\n\nDrake’s haters can’t hurt his celebrity status (stardom) in the same way it’s impossible to shoot a star from the earth.", "annotation_id": "4889133", "url": "https://genius.com/4889133", "state": "accepted", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Legend", "line": "I can’t change, this shit set in stone", "vault_lines": ["I can't change, this shit set in stone"], "meaning": "Drake can’t change who he is in life and the skills he brings to the game. What he and his crew put in motion can’t be stopped. He is immortal and others cannot outlive his fame.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/drake/status/563995236188581888", "annotation_id": "4888317", "url": "https://genius.com/4888317", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Legend", "line": "If I die, all I know is I’m a mothafuckin’ legend", "vault_lines": ["All I know, if I die, I'm a mothafuckin' legend", "If I die, all I know is I'm a mothafuckin' legend", "Oh my God, oh my God, if I die, I'm a legend"], "meaning": "Heroes get remembered, but legends never die\n\nIn 2011, Drake claimed he’s a descendant of either Bob Marley or Jimi Hendrix. He later said he wants to be his generation’s Marvin Gaye. Wherever he lands in the future, he’s already been immortalized.", "annotation_id": "4888175", "url": "https://genius.com/4888175", "state": "accepted", "votes": 78, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Legend", "line": "When I pull up on a nigga tell that nigga back, back I’m too good with these words, watch a nigga backtrack", "vault_lines": ["When I pull up on a nigga tell that nigga back, back", "I'm too good with these words, watch a nigga backtrack", "I'm up first, I'm on tour,"], "meaning": "To “pull up” is to challenge – Drake’s challenging his peers in a lyrical sense.\n\nHis lyrics are so profound, his foes have to rewind his music to fully understand it. But fear not, we got you covered!", "annotation_id": "4888078", "url": "https://genius.com/4888078", "state": "accepted", "votes": 188, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Legend", "line": "Right or wrong, I’ma write my wrongs", "vault_lines": ["Right or wrong, I'ma write my wrongs"], "meaning": "Drake used the “right/write wrongs” wordplay before, on Kendrick Lamar’s “Poetic Justice”:\n\nAnd they say communication save relations, I can tell. But I can never right my wrongs unless I write ‘em down for real, P.S.\n\nHowever, his usage of the homophone pair here on “Legend” alludes more to how Kanye used it on “Touch the Sky”:\n\nI’m trying to right my wrongs\nBut it’s funny, them same wrongs helped me write this song", "annotation_id": "4887986", "url": "https://genius.com/4887986", "state": "accepted", "votes": 45, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Legend", "line": "They can’t live this long You don’t know where you’re gonna go I got this shit mapped out strong", "vault_lines": ["They can't live this long", "You don't know where you're gonna go", "I got this shit mapped out strong"], "meaning": "While his competition is following trends, Drake has mapped out his career, making sure he never suffers from a setback. Drake is in it for the long run, not just the moment.", "annotation_id": "4887795", "url": "https://genius.com/4887795", "state": "accepted", "votes": 71, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Legend", "line": "I’m the one, one Why do I feel like the only one? Why do I feel like you owe me one?", "vault_lines": ["I'm the one, one", "Why do I feel like the only one?", "Why do I feel like you owe me one?"], "meaning": "Drake’s repeats his sentiments on Big Sean’s “Blessings”:\n\nI am convinced I’m the only one left\nThat’s still doing this shit, man\n\nHe’s also saying he’s the only one with this girl he’s talking to. He’s used this “only one/owe me one” rhyme on Take Care’s We’ll Be Fine.\"", "annotation_id": "4887597", "url": "https://genius.com/4887597", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Legend", "line": "Got a girl, she from the South Used to work, used to dance in Texas, now she clean the house", "vault_lines": ["got a girl, she from the South", "Used to work, used to dance in Texas, now she clean the house"], "meaning": "Drake’s an honorary citizen of Houston, frequenting the city and its strip clubs. Treasures was one of his favorites, as he mentioned on “From Time”:\n\nThinking ‘bout Texas, back when Porscha used to work at Treasures", "annotation_id": "4887554", "url": "https://genius.com/4887554", "state": "accepted", "votes": 44, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Legend", "line": "Way up north, packed in Honda cars They don’t know who we are", "vault_lines": ["Way up north, packed in Honda cars", "They don't know who we are"], "meaning": "He’s talking about his early days in Canada, where he got up to some shady side schemes while trying to make it big as a musician.\n\nAs seen in the promo, Jungle, Drake and his crew wanted to see if they would still need ID by the same time next year. At that time when they would hit up clubs in their hometown no one knew who they were so they needed ID.\n\nDrake uses the Honda to denote how far he has come since then. He now drives Rolls Royces and Bentleys.", "annotation_id": "4887539", "url": "https://genius.com/4887539", "state": "accepted", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Legend", "line": "Everyday, I was strugglin’ to learn what life’s about On my way, money taught me Spanish, make it ándale", "vault_lines": ["On my way, money taught me Spanish, make it ándale", "Everyday, I was strugglin' to learn what life's about"], "meaning": "As Drake began to travel across the globe, his paper-chasing introduced him to new places and languages. On Romeo Santos' “Odio” Drake proves this as he sings the bridge in Spanish.\n\nThe definition of the word “ándale” differs based on its context, but here it means quickly.", "annotation_id": "4887513", "url": "https://genius.com/4887513", "state": "accepted", "votes": 103, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
