{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sooner Than Later", "line": "I forgot to call you on your birthday You swear you’re the last thing on my mind, yeah There is nothing I can do to fix it All you ever asked me for was time, whoa", "vault_lines": ["I forgot to call you on your birthday", "You swear you're the last thing on my mind, yeah", "There is nothing I can do to fix it", "All you ever asked me for was time, whoa"], "meaning": "Drake expresses how he thinks his lover feels inferior to everything happening in his life and he feels powerless in the situation as he understands that his lover isn’t asking for alot , she’s asking for something he could easily provide", "annotation_id": "35039072", "url": "https://genius.com/35039072", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sooner Than Later", "line": "And what good is being famous if I’m never on your mind?", "vault_lines": ["And what good is being famous if I'm never on your mind?"], "meaning": "Drake meant by this line, what did he get out of being well known around the world but not enough to get his lover to think about him.", "annotation_id": "32693175", "url": "https://genius.com/32693175", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sooner Than Later", "line": "When the lights don’t glow the same way that they used to And I finally get a moment to myself I will realize you were everything I’m missing And you’ll tell me you’re in love with someone else", "vault_lines": ["When the lights don't glow the same way that they used to", "And I finally get a moment to myself", "I will realize you were everything I'm missing", "And you'll tell me you're in love with someone else"], "meaning": "When Drake’s fame subsides, he’ll realize that all he really needed was his lover. However, when he goes back to her, she will have already fallen in love with someone else.", "annotation_id": "31119497", "url": "https://genius.com/31119497", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sooner Than Later", "line": "So can you do me a favor? If I pull it together, make it sooner than later We won’t be here forever, and I realize I waited too long But please don’t move on", "vault_lines": ["If I pull it together, make it sooner than later", "We won't be here forever, and I realize I waited too long", "But please don't move on", "So can you do me a favor?"], "meaning": "The first part of the verse is from the perspective of the girl Drake is pursuing. She urges Drake to pull himself together as soon as possible, because they won’t always be together. In the second half, Drake admits his wrongdoing and realizes that he waited too long to get his act together. He begs the girl not to move on.", "annotation_id": "31119488", "url": "https://genius.com/31119488", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sooner Than Later", "line": "The girl or the world? You see, someone gotta lose I thought that I could have it all, do I really gotta choose?", "vault_lines": ["The girl or the world? You see, someone gotta lose", "I thought that I could have it all, do I really gotta choose?"], "meaning": "The status that Drizzy is now at in his career has him making tough decisions on what he needs and wants in his life. Decisions which he would prefer if he did not have to make, as it means sacrificing one for the other, essentially.\n\nWhen thinking about fame, we often think that it comes with getting and having whatever you want. Drake states that he had the same idea when he thought about making it big in the music industry. But he now realizes that it is not all that it seems to be, and he is reluctant to make the choice between his music career, industry and fans or the girl he is currently pursuing.", "annotation_id": "18050589", "url": "https://genius.com/18050589", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sooner Than Later", "line": "And I’m just trying to pay the price owing", "vault_lines": ["And I'm just trying to pay the price owing"], "meaning": "This a reference to the phrase “[you will] pay the price”.\n\nThroughout the song Drake discusses how fame is interrupting his love life with this girl and is consuming all of his time, and the choice he needs to make between the two.\n\nDue to music being his main priority, he had to sacrifice the girl, and due to this, he now has to pay the price for his actions, and that is what he is trying to do and explain in this song", "annotation_id": "18050585", "url": "https://genius.com/18050585", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sooner Than Later", "line": "What good is all the cash if it doesn’t buy time?", "vault_lines": ["What good is all the cash if it doesn't buy time?"], "meaning": "That’s a reference to a famous phrase “time is money”.", "annotation_id": "16514743", "url": "https://genius.com/16514743", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sooner Than Later", "status": "done", "targets": 7, "clicked": 7, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-sooner-than-later-lyrics", "genius_title": "Sooner Than Later"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Trophies", "line": "What’s the move? Can I tell the truth? If I was doing this for you then I’d have nothing left to prove Nah, this for me though I’m just tryna stay alive and take care of my people", "vault_lines": ["What's the move? Can I tell the truth?", "If I was doing this for you then I'd have nothing left to prove", "Nah, this for me though", "I'm just tryna stay alive and take care of my people"], "meaning": "Drake is doing nothing to impress those around him. Everything that he’s doing between music, acting, and whatever else is to take him and those closest to him to the top. He already alluded to that in “Tuscan Leather”, his longest introduction track on an album.\n\nDrizzy made 10.5 million this year along, being one of the Forbes 2013 Cash Kings, Aubrey is doing a pretty good job of taking care of his blood.\n\nNot to mention the reference to Take Care, his album that won a trophy, (Grammy), for hip hop album of the year", "annotation_id": "2611647", "url": "https://genius.com/2611647", "state": "accepted", "votes": 65, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Trophies", "line": "Bitch I go to Dreams with a suitcase", "vault_lines": ["Bitch I go to Dreams with a suitcase"], "meaning": "Club Dreams is a strip club located in Houston, Texas. According to this list, it is ranked #5 in all of Houston.\n\nIt’s no secret that Drake enjoys going to strip clubs, he enjoys making it rain as well. He brought a suitcase full of money just to do so.\n\n\n\nClub Dreams entendre aside, he’s also saying he’s living his dreams. You pack a suitcase to go somewhere you will be staying (indefinitely or permenantly), so he will remain living the dream. From a business perspective, the suitcase could also symbolize making a deal or coming to an agreement so he goes to dreams with a suitcase to make his dreams a reality (which he’s successfully accomplished).", "annotation_id": "2609672", "url": "https://genius.com/2609672", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Trophies", "line": "Bitch, check the numbers, I’m the one who really get it [Pre-Chorus 2] I told y’all muh’fuckas", "vault_lines": ["I told y'all muh'fuckas", "Bitch, check the numbers, I'm the one who really get it"], "meaning": "As he rapped in “5AM in Toronto”:\n\nYou underestimated greatly\nMost number ones ever, how long did it really take me?\n\nAnd guess who had the most Top 10s on the Hot 100 chart in 2013? Yes, Drizzy!", "annotation_id": "2608463", "url": "https://genius.com/2608463", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Trophies", "line": "I saw my parents split up right after the wedding", "vault_lines": ["I saw my parents split up right after the wedding"], "meaning": "Drake’s parents divorced when he was 5 years old, resulting in him being raised by his mother in Toronto. Meanwhile, his father lived in Memphis, where Drake decided to shoot the video for “Worst Behavior”", "annotation_id": "2608454", "url": "https://genius.com/2608454", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Trophies", "line": "She like, “I heard all your niggas stay where you stay” House so big I haven’t seen them boys in two days Bitch, I use a walkie-talkie just to get a beverage", "vault_lines": ["She like, \"I heard all your niggas stay where you stay\"", "House so big I haven't seen them boys in two days", "Bitch, I use a walkie-talkie just to get a beverage"], "meaning": "Most likely referring to the 12,500-square-foot, $7.7 million dollar, Hidden Hills, California mansion that he purchased in 2012.\n\nThis mansion has it all: waterfalls, a pool with a grotto, soaring ceilings with arched wood beams, a hot tub with an adjacent fireplace, a built-in library, game room, wine cellar, and a home theater.\n\n\n\nThis may be a response to Kat Stacks (a stripper whose hobbies include exposing rappers) when she went off on several YMCMB members, claiming they all live together.", "annotation_id": "2608441", "url": "https://genius.com/2608441", "state": "accepted", "votes": 51, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Trophies", "line": "This a “fuck-a-stripper-on-the-mink-rug” song", "vault_lines": ["This a \"fuck-a-stripper-on-the-mink-rug\" song"], "meaning": "Atypical of Drake, he usually makes songs about missing his ex’s, love, or sensitive style songs such as, “Doing It Wrong,” “Shot For Me” and “Find Your Love”.\n\nHe is stating how this song is quite the opposite. It’s about hittin' it and quitting it, with a stripper at that.", "annotation_id": "2366334", "url": "https://genius.com/2366334", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Trophies", "line": "Figured out this shit is simple", "vault_lines": ["Figured out this shit is simple"], "meaning": "In one of the trailers for Nothing Was the Same where Drake accepts his Grammy Award, he asks what the formula for his success has been? Is it his youth? Pure luck? Well, he seems to have found what it is. Happiness and Simplicity.\n\nhttp://vimeo.com/68930597#t=\n\nAlso continues the Wu Tang shouts from the NWTS recording process, playing off “Can It Be All So Simple” from “Enter The Wu-Tang (36 Chambers)”.", "annotation_id": "2366296", "url": "https://genius.com/2366296", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Trophies", "line": "Had hit records on my demo", "vault_lines": ["Had hit records on my demo"], "meaning": "Referring to his mixtape-era, songs with Trey Songz (like “Replacement Girl”) and other notable hits such as “Uptown” and “Successful” that were played on Toronto area radio before he even had a deal.\n\nAlternately, he had tracks produced by Hit-Boy on his demo.", "annotation_id": "2366197", "url": "https://genius.com/2366197", "state": "accepted", "votes": 68, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Trophies", "line": "Man, this shit is not a love song", "vault_lines": ["Man, this shit is not a love song"], "meaning": "A similar line was used by Chance The Rapper on Lil Wayne’s 2013 track “You Song”:\n\nThis is not a love song\nThis is a you song\nI just happen to love you\n\nDrake is defending himself, saying that he’s not all about love songs or being sad songs, he’s more than that, or even less.", "annotation_id": "2366112", "url": "https://genius.com/2366112", "state": "accepted", "votes": 67, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Trophies", "line": "I do not stay at the Intercontinental", "vault_lines": ["I do not stay at the Intercontinental"], "meaning": "“Intercontinental Hotels & Resorts” is a brand of luxury hotels. Drake doesn’t stay there because it all comes together at the condo\n\n\n\nThe Intercontinental is on the low end of luxury hotels.  When Drake stays at a hotel it’s only at the top hotels.", "annotation_id": "2364635", "url": "https://genius.com/2364635", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Trophies", "status": "done", "targets": 10, "clicked": 10, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-trophies-lyrics", "genius_title": "Trophies"}
