{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Exposed (Voyce Diss)", "line": "OK Voyce, we know you was a snitch But you don’t get your boys back like that", "vault_lines": ["OK Voyce, we know you was a snitch", "But you don't get your boys back like that"], "meaning": "According to the Merriam-Webster Dictionary, a snitch is “a person who tells someone in authority (such as the police or a teacher) about something wrong that someone has done”\n\nSnitching is frowned upon by just about everybody, including most authority, especially on your own. Even if your boys treat you wrong, there is NO reason to tell police, females, or social media incriminating evidence about them.\n\nCome on Voyce, just cause you mad don’t mean you gotta snitch on Drake.", "annotation_id": "2677434", "url": "https://genius.com/2677434", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Exposed (Voyce Diss)", "line": "I’m about loyalty man.", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake is chastising Voice from this point onwards because he he cherishes the quality of loyalty a lot like his YM counteparts\n\n\n\nBut Voice has been fake and selling out on and betraying almost all of his friends and even himself.", "annotation_id": "2609565", "url": "https://genius.com/2609565", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Exposed (Voyce Diss)", "line": "Damn V-O, sounds like you got a lot of niggas mad at you bruh Guess that’s what happens when uh, you a R&B Diva tryna live a rapper’s life You know what I’m saying", "vault_lines": ["Damn V-O, sounds like you got a lot of niggas mad at you bruh", "Guess that's what happens when uh, you a R&B Diva tryna live a rapper's life"], "meaning": "Drake is sympathizing with Voyce, as they were once friends. However, he does so in a playful, sarcastic manner.\n\nVoyce has gotten himself into some trouble. Trying to be a gangsta rapper, he was attempting to be hard by saying a lot of hurtful things about Drake and friends, most notable, Boi-1da. Instead of boosting his thug image, it set him back. The outcome was this song, lost of friends, and to be viewed as a disloyal, snake. To play with your friends is one thing, but to say harsh things in the presence of others who barely know them is harsh. Also, he threatened to harm Drake. Although Drake can take a threat, he cannot stand betrayal. This is also seen when The Weeknd signed to Universal instead of OVO. He is all about being loyal, as he is to Lil Wayne even after being offered many other record deals with legends such as Jay-Z and Dr. Dre.", "annotation_id": "2549211", "url": "https://genius.com/2549211", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Exposed (Voyce Diss)", "status": "done", "targets": 3, "clicked": 3, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-exposed-voyce-diss-lyrics", "genius_title": "Exposed (Voyce Diss)"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fortworth", "line": "The AC is broken, my hotel, it’s hot as hell", "vault_lines": ["The AC is broken, my hotel, it's hot as hell"], "meaning": "bars", "annotation_id": "39936464", "url": "https://genius.com/39936464", "state": "pending", "votes": 31, "second_sense": false, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fortworth", "line": "Don’t let your friends turn you against Me and convince you the time that we spent Wasn’t worth nothin’, didn’t mean what it meant ’Cause it did (It did) It meant the world to me It meant the world to me It meant the world to me Ayy", "vault_lines": ["Don't let your friends turn you against", "Me and convince you the time that we spent", "Wasn't worth nothin', didn't mean what it meant", "'Cause it did (It did)", "It meant the world to me"], "meaning": "Drake sounds vulnerable and emotionally exposed here, dropping the tough persona for a moment to express how deeply the relationship affected him. He’s hurt by the idea that outside opinions and influence from friends could make someone question or devalue the connection they shared. The same sentiment is directed towards his fans.\n\nThere’s a sense of frustration, sadness, and desperation in the way he keeps emphasizing how much it meant to him, almost like he’s trying to hold onto something that’s already slipping away.", "annotation_id": "39825046", "url": "https://genius.com/39825046", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fortworth", "line": "Experimental drugs that don’t help I’m pourin’ up a four by myself", "vault_lines": ["I'm pourin' up a four by myself", "Experimental drugs that don't help"], "meaning": "Drake uses the commonly used rap bar “pouring up a four”, which means adding four ounces of Codeine to prepare the experimental drug called lean.", "annotation_id": "39800596", "url": "https://genius.com/39800596", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fortworth", "line": "Bus rides, I’m counting LaQuintas out the window", "vault_lines": ["Bus rides, I'm counting LaQuintas out the window"], "meaning": "Referring to the chain of hotels, LaQuinta Inn and Suites, although he does pronounce it wrong. (It’s supposed to be la-keen-ta.)", "annotation_id": "39779722", "url": "https://genius.com/39779722", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fortworth", "line": "Tunechi got some drank and I might help myself", "vault_lines": ["Tunechi got some drank and I might help myself"], "meaning": "Lil' Wayne, often referred to as Tunechi, is Drake’s longtime collaborator and mentor. He is often associated with the drug mixture “drank” or “lean” (which he played a part in popularizing), made by combining prescription cough medication with soda beverages (connecting with the earlier line about walking to Circle K by himself)", "annotation_id": "39776443", "url": "https://genius.com/39776443", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fortworth", "line": "Runnin’ out of sodas, I might walk to Circle K by myself", "vault_lines": ["Runnin' out of sodas, I might walk to Circle K by myself"], "meaning": "Circle K is an international Canadian chain of convenience stores. By saying that he might walk to Circle K by himself, Drake puts himself in a vulnerable position physically, representing how mentally/emotionally vulnerable he feels.\n\nHe’s buying soda because he’s drinking lean, and references taking some from Wayne later in the verse.", "annotation_id": "39776406", "url": "https://genius.com/39776406", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fortworth", "line": "I’m getting booked in Little Rock, Arkansas New Haven, Connecticut, and places where they probably still fly the Confederate", "vault_lines": ["I'm getting booked in Little Rock, Arkansas", "New Haven, Connecticut, and places where they probably still fly the Confederate"], "meaning": "Drake possibly Could be referring to getting booked for shows/gigs in states that have had significant pasts in racism.\n\nDrake might also be expressing feeling constantly targeted or arrested across America, especially in places associated with racism and old Southern attitudes.", "annotation_id": "39776327", "url": "https://genius.com/39776327", "state": "pending", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
