{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumbotron Shit Poppin", "line": "[Chorus]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "On April 15, 2024, a reference track performed by Lil Yachty emerged:\n\nhttps://youtu.be/Gbj3My2_6UY?si=ASJ5HG5TgwzA53iX\n\nThe second and third-to-last lines of the sole verse are kept for the final release. This fact was not realized by most listeners before the leak.\n\nAccording to DJ Akademiks, Atlanta producer Metro Boomin leaked the reference track. Metro and Drake were notably engaged in a public feud at the time. The reference track was sent to multiple sources by an Atlanta phone number:\n\nhttps://x.com/notbobbalam/status/1779744657800409248?s=46\n\nWhile Yachty is credited as a writer on this song, the extent of his contributions seem to have been downplayed. Drake has been criticized for his use of writers since 2015, when a few reference tracks recorded by ghostwriter Quentin Miller for songs like “10 Bands” and his verse on Meek Mill’s “R.I.C.O.” were released by Funk Flex during an ongoing beef between Drake and Meek.", "annotation_id": "31884067", "url": "https://genius.com/31884067", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumbotron Shit Poppin", "line": "Ridin’ ’round with F&N, we like to hold hands", "vault_lines": ["Ridin' 'round with F&N, we like to hold hands"], "meaning": "We like to hold hands here refers to holding hands in the literal sense and holding handguns with reference to F&N rounds", "annotation_id": "30389542", "url": "https://genius.com/30389542", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumbotron Shit Poppin", "line": "Boat was too sipped out, he ain’t leave the bed", "vault_lines": ["Boat was too sipped out, he ain't leave the bed"], "meaning": "Probably referencing Lil Yachty, also known as ‘Lil Boat’, who’s a known Drake collaborator and friend. He also has songwriting credits on this song.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?app=desktop&v=UBTqCqQl2fY\n\nIn a reference/demo of the song that leaked on April 15th, 2024, Lil Yachty is heard saying “I sipped so much last night, it was hard to leave the bed”, making this line a direct reference to that demo.", "annotation_id": "30260129", "url": "https://genius.com/30260129", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumbotron Shit Poppin", "line": "We ain’t even out in Turks, she finna take sand", "vault_lines": ["We ain't even out in Turks, she finna take sand"], "meaning": "Bottling up sand from beaches that they visit it’s a known tourists habit.\nDrake tells that before they got to the exotic beaches of Turks and Caicos, the girl he’s with bottled up sand from a way less exotic beach, which surprised him.\n\nDrake visits and references Turks and Caicos a lot throughout his career:\n\n\nSend ‘em to Lagos or Turks and Caicos\nBarbados, Trinidad and Tobago\n- Omertà\n\nI see you back in Turks\nRemember who took you there first and don’t you forget it\n- Desires (feat. Future)\n\nI just got a mansion out in Turks and it’s a beachfront (Okay)\nIf she’s bringin' four friends, I know I’ll hit at least one (Okay, slatt, slatt, slatt, slatt)\n- Pain 1993 (feat. Playboi Carti)\n\nNaw, naw, piece of cake, naw, naw, Turks and Caic', yeah, yeah\nGo and get your friends, we can sneak away, yeah, yeah\n- Popstar (by DJ Khaled)\n\nVoodoo curse, it got him while I flew to Turks\nKnow the dogs had to hit them where we knew it hurts\n- Knife Talk (feat. 21 Savage & Project Pat)", "annotation_id": "29849279", "url": "https://genius.com/29849279", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumbotron Shit Poppin", "line": "I don’t fuck with drugs, poppin’ X for the first time That shit kicked in like a two-time world champ", "vault_lines": ["I don't fuck with drugs, poppin' X for the first time", "That shit kicked in like a two-time world champ"], "meaning": "X refers to the drug ecstasy, which is MDMA but in a tablet form. You build up a tolerance the more you take drugs, but as this is Drake’s first time, its effects are likely to kick in very profoundly, just as if a two time UFC champion, such as Conor McGregor, was to kick you in a fight.\n\nDrake could possibly be referring to McGregor as the two are good friends, with McGregor even bringing out Drake at the UFC 229 weigh-in before his classic fight against Khabib Nurmagomedov.", "annotation_id": "27092709", "url": "https://genius.com/27092709", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumbotron Shit Poppin", "line": "She vapin’ in my room, that shit lit up like a glow-lamp", "vault_lines": ["She vapin' in my room, that shit lit up like a glow-lamp"], "meaning": "Vaping is when you’re smoking a vape, also known as an electronic cigarette, which is an electronic device that stimulates tobacco smoking. In some types of vapes when you inhale they produce neon lighting, hence Drake saying it lit up like a glow lamp when she smoked it, which are lamps that also produce neon lighting.", "annotation_id": "27086002", "url": "https://genius.com/27086002", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumbotron Shit Poppin", "line": "Damn near dipped a pint of Tech in a Code Red", "vault_lines": ["Damn near dipped a pint of Tech in a Code Red"], "meaning": "TEC is an abbreviated term for Hi-Tech, which is a pharmaceutical brand of promethazine with codeine syrup, regularly drunk by rappers. Code Red is a Mountain Dew flavor and is often mixed with lean to mask the taste.\n\n\n\nPictured: Codeine phosphate syrup.\n\n\nHowever, Drake further employs a triple entendre as “TEC” can serve as a TEC-19. He implies that the bullet of the gun would go through his opponent’s body – leaving them constantly bleeding, thus, the code red.\n\nCode red is also a police code, which activates an emergency notification to all police officers in the area.", "annotation_id": "27053419", "url": "https://genius.com/27053419", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumbotron Shit Poppin", "line": "(Oogie Mane, he killed it)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This is the producer tag of Working on Dying member Oogie Mane, voiced by MATT OX. Oogie Mane produced Drake’s 2018 track “I’m Upset,” and is a frequent collaborator of Lil Uzi Vert, MATT OX, and Robb Bank$, among others.", "annotation_id": "27053416", "url": "https://genius.com/27053416", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumbotron Shit Poppin", "line": "Everybody got a stick, we don’t run fades", "vault_lines": ["Everybody got a stick, we don't run fades"], "meaning": "Drake mentions that his crew is carrying weaponry (sticks), so he doesn’t have to fight with fists (run a fade).\n\nHe cleverly uses a double entendre here, as a stick and fade are also different receiving routes in football. The stick route involves a player running forward about five yards before cutting back towards the quarterback, as opposed to a fade route, in which a receiver runs straight and towards the outside of the field, away from the passer.", "annotation_id": "27052724", "url": "https://genius.com/27052724", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumbotron Shit Poppin", "line": "(Wake up, F1LTHY)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Richard Ortiz, or better know professionally as F1LTHY, is a Philadelphia producer, which he is know for his agressive and colossal trap production alongside his most known tag. He has also worked with big artists such as Playboi Carti, Lil Yachty, and others.\n\nhttps://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcR06-_Tw-4SlwyZzJDbKSnKqxORZB9yLknSTw&usqp=CAU\n\nPhoto: F1LTHY\n\n\nThis song officially mark the producer’s first use of his tag in a Drake’s song, being that F1LTHY is also part of the collective group of producers known as Working on Dying, which collaborated with Drake in lastest records.", "annotation_id": "27052205", "url": "https://genius.com/27052205", "state": "accepted", "votes": 59, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumbotron Shit Poppin", "line": "Hmm-hmm, strapped up, fuck it, I’ma die lit", "vault_lines": ["Hmm-hmm, strapped up, fuck it, I'ma die lit"], "meaning": "Drake gives a clever nod to Atlanta rapper Playboi Carti for the second time on “Jumbotron Shit Poppin,” referencing his 2018 debut studio album Die Lit.\n\nWhile the title Die Lit is likely referring to a partying lifestyle due to its cover, Drake paraphrases it, claiming he’s willing to die for his cause and go out with a bang, or as he puts it, “die lit.”\n\nAlthough Drake and Playboi Carti only have one official collaboration—that of which being Drake’s May 2020 cut “Pain 1993”—Drake hopped on a remix of Carti’s leaked 2017 track “One Day” in September 2021.", "annotation_id": "27052177", "url": "https://genius.com/27052177", "state": "accepted", "votes": 118, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Jumbotron Shit Poppin", "line": "Up, 8 a.m., geekin’ hard, I’m a real vamp", "vault_lines": ["Up, 8 a.m., geekin' hard, I'm a real vamp"], "meaning": "“Geekin'” is a slang term to refer to one who’s happy and excited after consuming several drugs. Drake notes that he’s been awake all night until 8 AM on drugs — likening himself to a vampire as they are known to sleep in the day and stay awake at night.\n\nFurthermore, Drake could be referring to the popular Atlanta native, Playboi Carti who refers to himself as “King Vamp” — Carti’s sophomore album Whole Lotta Red even being a reference to it as vampires characteristically like blood. Despite the reference, this isn’t Drake’s first interaction with the Atlanta rapper as in May 2020, Carti appeared as a feature on Drake’s “Pain 1993.” F1LTHY, a producer on the song is also known heavily for working with Carti.", "annotation_id": "27052171", "url": "https://genius.com/27052171", "state": "accepted", "votes": 265, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
