{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Plastic Bag", "line": "If anybody know I know Yeah", "vault_lines": ["I know OG India and Suga there, aw yeah, aw yeah"], "meaning": "If there’s anyone who understands the inner-thoughts and motivations of strippers, it’s lady-whisperer-Drizzy. This is why he refers to them as “dancers” rather than “strippers,” out of respect. They’re likely only partaking in such activities to support themselves financially.", "annotation_id": "7844057", "url": "https://genius.com/7844057", "state": "accepted", "votes": 57, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Plastic Bag", "line": "Yeah, last time they seen this shit was BMF I know Big Meech and J-Bo, they was there I know OG India and Suga there, aw yeah, aw yeah", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, last time they seen this shit was BMF", "I know Big Meech and J-Bo, they was there", "I know OG India and Suga there, aw yeah, aw yeah"], "meaning": "In this line, “Big Meech” doesn’t refer to rapper Rick Ross, nor does “BMF” refer to Ross' track “B.M.F. (Blowing Money Fast)”. Instead, Future is talking about the Black Mafia Family organization led by Demetrius “Big Meech” Tenory and his second-in-command Chad “J-Bo” Brown.\n\n\n\nBig Meech (right) and J-Bo (left)\n\nThe BMF started in Detroit, but spread to the Atlanta area in the early 2000s, and used to throw parties in Atlanta’s famous strip clubs – OG India and Suga were famous dancers in these clubs. Future’s claiming that his city hasn’t seen anyone tear up the strip club like his crew ever since the leaders of BMF were locked up in 2005.", "annotation_id": "7838952", "url": "https://genius.com/7838952", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Plastic Bag", "line": "Hit the parking lot, it’s lookin’ like a video Bunch of pretty hoes, high saddity hoes", "vault_lines": ["Hit the parking lot, it's lookin' like a video", "Bunch of pretty hoes, high saddity hoes"], "meaning": "The scene in the parking lot outside the club is so lit that it looks like it could be a part of a music video. Incidentally, Future did actually shoot a video in the parking lot of Magic City for his track “Magic”:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vY7mHqFi_Kk\n\n“High saditty” is allegedly derived from “high society” and implies that the women in question are putting on airs or acting all bougie. Along with “pretty”, Future implies that he ain’t just just any regular women with him, it’s only attractive and classy-acting ladies.", "annotation_id": "7836091", "url": "https://genius.com/7836091", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Plastic Bag", "line": "Whole lot of Xans and we pass around candy", "vault_lines": ["Whole lot of Xans and we pass around candy"], "meaning": "Xans is short for Xanax, a prescription drug that helps treat anxiety and panic disorders. Xanax seems to be the “it” drug right now, as both Future and Drake have referenced them, albeit in pretty opposite ways.", "annotation_id": "7835008", "url": "https://genius.com/7835008", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Plastic Bag", "line": "Bust it out the wrapper, throw it in the air, aw yeah, aw yeah Throwed enough money on a Monday than you make in a year, aw yeah Ordered sixty thousand ones, told the owner ’bout to break a record", "vault_lines": ["Bust it out the wrapper, throw it in the air, aw yeah, aw yeah", "Throwed enough money on a Monday than you make in a year, aw yeah", "Ordered sixty thousand ones, told the owner 'bout to break a record", "Aw yeah, Magic City on a Monday"], "meaning": "Future presumably leans toward #TeamDrizzy in the Drake v. Meek beef, but this echoes a line from the latter’s verse on the Drake x Meek Mill collab “R.I.C.O.”: “I spend a day what you make a year”.\n\nThe average American has around a yearly income of $50,500 – Future is in a rare position where he can spend that and more only on a night out with strippers.\n\nPROPOSED SUGGESTION: Instead of “throwing more” , I hear, “throwed enough”", "annotation_id": "7834936", "url": "https://genius.com/7834936", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Plastic Bag", "line": "Mixin’ liquor cups with the sedatives", "vault_lines": ["Mixin' liquor cups with the sedatives"], "meaning": "Lean has become the go-to-party concoction for the rap scene since the early 1990s, popularized by DJ Screw. Drizzy isn’t necessarily the biggest advocate of the purple drank, but his partner-in-crime Future is obsessed with it, sprinkling references about it throughout his catalog, several times on this album alone.", "annotation_id": "7834921", "url": "https://genius.com/7834921", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Plastic Bag", "line": "Get a plastic bag Go ahead and pick up all the cash Go ahead and pick up all the cash You danced all night, girl, you deserve it Get a plastic bag Go ahead and pick up all the cash Go ahead and pick up all the cash You danced all night, girl, you deserve it", "vault_lines": ["Get a plastic bag", "Go ahead, pick up all the cash", "Go ahead, pick up all this cash", "Go ahead, get a plastic bag", "Go ahead and pick up all the cash", "You danced all night, girl, you deserve it"], "meaning": "When the club’s hours are over, the strippers take massive plastic bags and gather up all of the money from the floor. For an in-depth look into the inner-workings of a strip club, read Genius contributor Zach Schwartz’s Vice article “Twenty Hours in a New York Strip Club.”", "annotation_id": "7834880", "url": "https://genius.com/7834880", "state": "accepted", "votes": 127, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Plastic Bag", "line": "But for now, a nigga got the ones with me I be in the club with the bands like I got the keyboard and the drums with me", "vault_lines": ["I be in the club with the bands like I got the keyboard and the drums with me", "I roll up with the bands on me", "But for now, a nigga got the ones with me"], "meaning": "“Bands” is slang for large stacks of money held together by rubber bands. Drake hits the club with so many bands that it looks like he has a real band with him.\n\n\n\nDrake and his woes\n\nIt’s also possible “keyboards and drums” refers to keys (kilos) of cocaine, and the drums on the clip of a gun – both of which can be instrumental in making bands.", "annotation_id": "7834873", "url": "https://genius.com/7834873", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Plastic Bag", "line": "Niggas look at us like, “Maybe one day” Maybe one day, maybe one day", "vault_lines": ["Niggas look at us like, \"Maybe one day\"", "Maybe one day, maybe one day"], "meaning": "Drake and Future are the epitome of success, and act as a symbol for it, driving others to look up to them for inspiration. So when the artists Esco brings out for Magic City Mondays look at Future or Drake, they are motivated to “one day” rule the game.", "annotation_id": "7834870", "url": "https://genius.com/7834870", "state": "accepted", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Plastic Bag", "line": "Aw yeah, Magic City on a Monday Esco treat that shit like church on Sunday", "vault_lines": ["Magic City on a Monday, we worship this like a Sunday", "Aw yeah, Magic City on a Monday", "Esco treat that shit like church on Sunday"], "meaning": "Future’s DJ, DJ Esco, hosts Magic City Mondays, where he helps break some of Atlanta’s newest and hottest artists. The club and the Magic City Mondays phenomenon was profiled in a GQ documentary starring Future and Esco (NSFW).", "annotation_id": "7834851", "url": "https://genius.com/7834851", "state": "accepted", "votes": 60, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
