{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Motion", "line": "I’ve been moving state to state", "vault_lines": ["I don't have a fuck to give, I've been moving state to state"], "meaning": "Drake has started his “Would you like a Tour?” tour and is busy going from city to city, or “state to state”.", "annotation_id": "40570348", "url": "https://genius.com/40570348", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Motion", "line": "So I’m with her even when I’m here without her and she know it", "vault_lines": ["So I'm with her even when I'm here without her and she know it"], "meaning": "everything that he does or writes reminds him of his s/o at the time so he feels like she’s around , even when she’s away", "annotation_id": "34506487", "url": "https://genius.com/34506487", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Motion", "line": "[Outro: Drake, Sampha]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "In May 2011, Drake remixed SBTRKT’s “Wildfire.” SBTRKT is English producer, Aaron Jerome, who frequently collaborates with Sampha.\n\n\n\nTheir live show consists of Jerome utilizing electronic and acoustic drums alongside triggering samples and using a mixing desk, with Sampha playing keyboards, triggering vocal loops and singing.", "annotation_id": "1916645", "url": "https://genius.com/1916645", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Motion", "line": "And my dog Chubby Chub, that’s my nigga from the way", "vault_lines": ["And my dog Chubby Chub, that's my nigga from the way"], "meaning": "Chubbs is not only a member of Drake’s OVO crew, he is also Drake’s long time friend and bodyguard.\n\n\n\n“From the Way” is slang for Galloway, which is a popular neighborhood on the Eastside of Scarborough, which ties in with his next line.", "annotation_id": "1897120", "url": "https://genius.com/1897120", "state": "accepted", "votes": 67, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Motion", "line": "Everything that I write is either for her or about her", "vault_lines": ["Everything that I write is either for her or about her"], "meaning": "This could be about Drake’s fling, Nebby..\n\n\n\nThis line is also from Californication season 6 episode 12, which aired in 2013 and features character Hank Moody saying it to Atticus Fetch\n\nEverything I write is either for her or about her, so I’m always with her, even when I’m not.\n\nDrake name dropped the show before on Timbaland’s November 2009 track, “Say Something”:\n\nI sit and drink wine and watch Californication, to life", "annotation_id": "1896794", "url": "https://genius.com/1896794", "state": "accepted", "votes": 63, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Motion", "line": "’Cause we said “no strings attached” and I still got tied up in that", "vault_lines": ["'Cause we said \"no strings attached\" and I still got tied up in that"], "meaning": "Drake and his girl had agreed on unconditional sex, but Drake started catching feelings for her. He tweeted this line in May 2013:\n\nhttps://twitter.com/Drake/status/339238173202870272", "annotation_id": "1896751", "url": "https://genius.com/1896751", "state": "accepted", "votes": 102, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Motion", "line": "On the Eastside of the city, that’s where everybody stay", "vault_lines": ["On the Eastside of the city, that's where everybody stay"], "meaning": "Drake is giving a shoutout to Scarborough, a borough on the eastern fringe of Toronto proper. The area is stereotypically associated with violence due to its impoverished community. It frequently receives nicknames like Scareborough, Scarberia, Scarlem like Harlem, and Scomptown like Compton.", "annotation_id": "1896581", "url": "https://genius.com/1896581", "state": "accepted", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Motion", "line": "In my leather and my Timbs like it’s 1998", "vault_lines": ["In my leather and my Timbs like it's 1998"], "meaning": "“Timbs” is short for Timberlands, a footwear company founded in 1928. The company experienced a “golden age” of popularity amongst the hip-hop community during the 90s.", "annotation_id": "1896053", "url": "https://genius.com/1896053", "state": "accepted", "votes": 105, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
