{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Be In There (Ton Of Em)*", "line": "I should probably be in there with Thug and ’nem", "vault_lines": ["I should probably be in therе with Thug and 'nem"], "meaning": "On May 9th, 2022, members of Young Stoner Life were arrested and indicted on 56 counts of suspected gang-related crimes and alleged violation of Georgia’s RICO Act. Drake is close friends and collaborators with the label’s CEO, Young Thug, working with him on several collaborations, most recently on “Parade on Cleveland” and “Oh U Went” from Young Thug’s album BUSINESS IS BUSINESS which was worked on and released whilst Young Thug was incarcerated.\n\nDrake states that he thinks he should be in the same position as Young Thug in his RICO case due being associated with a high amount of people who all are presumably involved with many gang related crimes.", "annotation_id": "29441648", "url": "https://genius.com/29441648", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
