{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Greatness", "line": "My other niggas move keys, no off notes", "vault_lines": ["My other niggas move keys, no off notes"], "meaning": "“Keys” is a way of saying kilos (usually of drugs i.e. cocaine). “No off notes” refers to keys of a piano being pressed/moved.", "annotation_id": "40045660", "url": "https://genius.com/40045660", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Greatness", "line": "Got a cannon on my hip, but nigga, this is not Mariah", "vault_lines": ["Got a cannon on my hip, but nigga, this is not Mariah"], "meaning": "“Cannon on my hip” could likely be referring to Nick Cannon, who at the time was married to Mariah Carey.", "annotation_id": "40045624", "url": "https://genius.com/40045624", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
