{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Liability", "line": "Your mama the sweetest lady, that apple fell far from the tree", "vault_lines": ["Your mama the sweetest lady, that apple fell far from the tree"], "meaning": "“the apple doesn’t fall far from the tree” is an English saying that means a child usually has similar character or qualities to his or her parents.\n\nDrake twists this idiom to say that, in this case, the apple “fell far from the tree”, meaning, the girl he’s talking about didn’t acquire this sweet character and personality of her mother", "annotation_id": "34759285", "url": "https://genius.com/34759285", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Liability", "line": "At the beginning, it felt like you’re going harder than me Then you stepped back on this shit, girl, you hit the Harden on me", "vault_lines": ["At the beginning, it felt like you're going harder than me", "Then you stepped back on this shit, girl, you hit the Harden on me"], "meaning": "Drake references NBA player James Harden and his signature move, the step-back, in which the player pivots back to create space for a shot:\n\nhttps://youtu.be/X9GddRiKdXg?si=P9m_cU-8leXb5aSc\n\nDrake later again referenced Harden in his track “The Shoe Fits” from his November 2023 deluxe album For All The Dogs Scary Hours Edition:\n\n\nShe like, “Shh, quiet, everybody, the game started\nMy new boo hoopin' tonight and he said he play at the Garden\nHe said if I ain’t watching, then that nigga ain’t startin'”\nShe point to the guy that she talkin' ‘bout and it’s James Harden\n\nDamn, dog\nLost your, lost your girl to The Sniper, huh?\n13, good God\nI feel for you, bro\nLook", "annotation_id": "29526256", "url": "https://genius.com/29526256", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Liability", "line": "You put your words together like you getting points for that shit, like you playing Scrabble on me", "vault_lines": ["You put your words together like you getting points for that shit, like you playing Scrabble on me"], "meaning": "Scrabble is a word game where you score by building words from tiles where different letters have more or less value due to the complexity of the words they create.\n\nThe girl Drake is talking to is using words to spin the game on him, she’s being slick with her words and using them to play him. The girl knows she’s in the wrong maybe from her actions so now she’s manipulating him with words to make it so drake is in the wrong. “Getting points for that shit” means she’s trying so hard to make her words seem the truth and justified so much to the point where it’s almost like she thinks she’s getting scored on it.", "annotation_id": "26077270", "url": "https://genius.com/26077270", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Liability", "line": "Drinking your weight in champagne", "vault_lines": ["Drinking your weight in champagne"], "meaning": "Champagne is synonymous with Drake, most notably as his username on Instagram, champagnepapi. The drink is often used to mark successes and accomplishments during celebratory moments, which Drake has had many throughout his talented career.\n\nHere, it is used to mark an overly-hedonistic lifestyle. To drink one’s weight in champagne would be overconsumption, to say the least, but it fits in with singular focus on pleasure and irresponsibility in this verse.\nhttps://miro.medium.com/max/1400/0*AvU_2lCCXF9Tj4Uq", "annotation_id": "26077235", "url": "https://genius.com/26077235", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
