{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ratchet Happy Birthday", "line": "Cool your headtop", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake uses Toronto slang here. “Cool your head top”, means that someone needs to calm down or find a way to relax any anxiety or anger they may be feeling.", "annotation_id": "35064959", "url": "https://genius.com/35064959", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ratchet Happy Birthday", "line": "Yeah, who’s gonna love you on your worst day?", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, who's gonna love you on your worst day?"], "meaning": "Drake is alluding to a common trap that people, and in this case the woman falls into on her birthday, where she feels self conscious and potentially in herself on a day that is dedicated to her and celebrating the continuation of her life. Drake alludes to the fact that he is going to be the person to celebrate this unknown woman.", "annotation_id": "35064931", "url": "https://genius.com/35064931", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ratchet Happy Birthday", "line": "Seems like time’s out of our control", "vault_lines": ["Seems like time's out of our control"], "meaning": "Drake is saying that the time on clock is not important and not something that he and this unknown woman need to worry about at this time, and they should allow themselves to get lost in the moment and enjoy the celebration.", "annotation_id": "35064925", "url": "https://genius.com/35064925", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ratchet Happy Birthday", "line": "It’s your fuckin’ birthday (Oh, birthday, I need more liquor) It’s a fuckin’ celebration (Oh oh) Tonight we celebrate", "vault_lines": ["It's your fuckin' birthday (Oh, birthday, I need more liquor)", "It's a fuckin' celebration (Oh oh)", "Oh, it's your fuckin' birthday, oh, oh", "It's a celebration, oh oh", "It's your birthday, baby, it's your birthday"], "meaning": "Drake and Party seem to be serenading an unknown woman in these opening lyrics. Drake describing the occasion as a “fuckin' celebration” indicates that he intends to celebrate this woman’s birthday in an extravagant manner.", "annotation_id": "35064888", "url": "https://genius.com/35064888", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ratchet Happy Birthday", "line": "Seems like time’s out of our control (Oh oh)", "vault_lines": ["Seems like time's out of our control"], "meaning": "Drake notices this party they are celebrating at is late at night and cant have control of them selves let alone time.", "annotation_id": "29630689", "url": "https://genius.com/29630689", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ratchet Happy Birthday", "line": "It’s your brrrrrrr– It’s your fuckin’ birthday (Oh, birthday, I need more liquor)", "vault_lines": ["It's your fuckin' birthday (Oh, birthday, I need more liquor)", "It's a fuckin' celebration (Oh oh)", "Oh, it's your fuckin' birthday, oh, oh", "It's your birthday, baby, it's your birthday"], "meaning": "In this chorus, Drake refers to celebrating a birthday while being overally intoxicated, Drake lets us know that now he is obssesed and eager to consume more alcahol as he adds a unconsious rythem when he says “ its your brrrrrr-”", "annotation_id": "29630671", "url": "https://genius.com/29630671", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ratchet Happy Birthday", "line": "Anitta", "vault_lines": [", you hotter than Anitta"], "meaning": "Anitta is a Brazilian singer, songwriter, dancer and record producer. Anitta rose to fame in 2013 after releasing her single “Show das Poderosas,” which reached the top of Brazil’s Hot 100 Airplay chart.", "annotation_id": "19201193", "url": "https://genius.com/19201193", "state": "pending", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ratchet Happy Birthday", "line": "If it ain’t the real thing, you don’t want it GG, CC’s all on ya", "vault_lines": ["If it ain't the real thing, you don't want it", "GG, CC's all on ya"], "meaning": "“GG” and “CC” refer to Gucci and Chanel respectively; both companies are represented by logos with interlocking letters and produce high-end, luxurious garments.\n\nDrake’s lover expresses very strong materialistic values: she’ll only wear a certain piece of clothing if it’s both authentic and name-brand. This seemingly fits in with her spoiled nature and how she’s being gifted with Gucci, Chanel, and other pricey presents just only for her birthday.\n\nhttps://qph.fs.quoracdn.net/main-qimg-834a4042380d433cb1d186dfa45c5b84", "annotation_id": "14987383", "url": "https://genius.com/14987383", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ratchet Happy Birthday", "line": "Just say your piece and peace up like Ibiza", "vault_lines": ["Just say your piece and peace up like Ibiza"], "meaning": "“Peace up like Ibiza” refers to the island of Ibiza, located in the Mediterranean Sea, off the coast of Spain. It’s known for its quite peaceful nature, an abundance of clubs, and extreme drug availability.\n\n“Saying one’s piece” is equivalent to adding one’s opinion and serves as a bridge between this bar and the previous one involving the candy, Reese’s Pieces.", "annotation_id": "14897654", "url": "https://genius.com/14897654", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ratchet Happy Birthday", "line": "You talk so tough I know you’re soft like buttercups Reese’s, Reese’s, don’t be ridiculous", "vault_lines": ["Reese's, Reese's, don't be ridiculous", "You talk so tough", "I know you're soft like buttercups"], "meaning": "Reese’s Peanut Butter Cups are a chocolate candy produced by the Hershey Company. They are widely popular worldwide and known for a soft peanut butter flavoured filling.\n\nDrake isn’t particularly oblivious to his addressee’s cold facade. He senses a gentler side to an ostensibly emotionally detached girl, comparable to the doughy core of a Reese’s.\n\n\n\nThis could allude to Rihanna. Drake’s close enough to her to see through her “tough girl” image. He mentions buttercup in order to introduce a play on her nickname, flipping RiRi into “Reese’s, Reese’s.”", "annotation_id": "14895967", "url": "https://genius.com/14895967", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ratchet Happy Birthday", "status": "done", "targets": 10, "clicked": 10, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-ratchet-happy-birthday-lyrics", "genius_title": "Ratchet Happy Birthday"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Signs", "line": "Champagne with breakfast while I’m yawning You can’t drink all day if you don’t start in the morning", "vault_lines": ["Champagne with breakfast while I'm yawning", "You can't drink all day if you don't start in the morning"], "meaning": "Drake (Aubrey) is saying that he is in such a postition of self employment / financial freedom that he can drink alcohol at breakfast and his day will not be affected.\n\nHe (or his writers) also point out that it is impossible to drink for a whole day if you do not begin in the morning,", "annotation_id": "38311126", "url": "https://genius.com/38311126", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Signs", "line": "Signs of the times, I say all the time Taking my time, just gets harder to find it", "vault_lines": ["Signs of the times, I say all the time", "Taking my time, just gets harder to find it"], "meaning": "a denotation of something common or popular at that particular day in age – a “sign of the times.”\n\nDrake references the fact that (particularly in a romantic sense) the more he sits back and waits to find the relationship that is right for him, the harder it becomes to find.", "annotation_id": "30618203", "url": "https://genius.com/30618203", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Signs", "line": "[Outro: Young Thug]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The song has a very quiet outro after the last refrain, where you can hear the beginning of Young Thug’s verse from the leaked demo of “Signs” featuring him.", "annotation_id": "17263663", "url": "https://genius.com/17263663", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Signs", "line": "Oh, first night, holy night, five in the morning, yeah-yeah (Yeah) And it feels like you’re mine, signs of the times, oh, what a time", "vault_lines": ["Oh, first night, holy night, five in the morning, yeah-yeah (Yeah)", "And it feels like you're mine, signs of the times, oh, what a time", "Signs of the times, I say all the time"], "meaning": "Drake is admittedly a fan of late night/early morning intimacy with his lover. In “Come Thru” the 6 God expresses his love of the night:\n\nWe had the type of nights where morning comes too soon\n\nFurthermore, in “5AM in Toronto” Drizzy reveals the procedure behind stealing your girl at the crack of dawn, closing his verse with:\n\nIf I like her, I just fly her to the city I’m in", "annotation_id": "12411070", "url": "https://genius.com/12411070", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Signs", "line": "Railiza, you need a... money and visa", "vault_lines": ["Railiza, you need a... money and visa"], "meaning": "Railiza Cepeda is a model from the Dominican Republic who has been previously linked to Drizzy after she appeared in French Montana’s “No Shopping” visuals.", "annotation_id": "12278702", "url": "https://genius.com/12278702", "state": "accepted", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Signs", "line": "Yeah, vacation is done but I’m not finished, no", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, vacation is done but I'm not finished, no"], "meaning": "On March 2017’s More Life cut “Do Not Disturb,” Drake rapped:\n\nTakin' summer off, ‘cause they tell me I need recovery\nMaybe gettin’ back to my regular life will humble me\nI’ll be back in 2018 to give you the summary\n\nA month after More Life dropped, Drake did vacation in the Dominican Republic, but just two days into the summer, he dropped “Signs” and featured on PARTYNEXTDOOR’s “Freak In You (Remix)” and Metro Boomin’s “No Complaints.”", "annotation_id": "12215014", "url": "https://genius.com/12215014", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Signs", "line": "You wanna drink like Bajan and dance like Trini, yeah", "vault_lines": ["You wanna drink like Bajan and dance like Trini, yeah"], "meaning": "“Bajan” people are from Barbados, while “Trini” is short for “Trindadian,” people from the twin island Trinidad & Tobago. Both islands are a part of the West Indies, whose sounds and culture Drake is heavily influenced by.\n\nBajan people having a reputation for drinking a lot isn’t just a stereotype; reportedly, there is are multiple rum shops in every district in Barbados—fitting for the supposed birthplace of rum.\n\nThere are a lot of “fetes,” or parties, in Trinidad, and “wining,” or gyrating the hips. They also have a yearly Carnival Festival dubbed as the “greatest show on earth” where people parade in costumes and dance in the street for two days straight.\n\nIt may be a reach, but two artists closely associated with Drake, Rihanna and Nicki Minaj are, respectively, Bajan and Trinidadian.", "annotation_id": "12213956", "url": "https://genius.com/12213956", "state": "accepted", "votes": 80, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Signs", "line": "You want a supermodel pose like mi real friend Winnie (Like mi real friend)", "vault_lines": ["You want a supermodel pose like mi real friend Winnie (Like mi real friend)"], "meaning": "Drake is referencing his good friend and fellow Toronto native, supermodel Winnie Harlow. In an August 2015 interview with Complex, Winnie spoke about how she met Drake, and her relationship with his crew:\n\nI’m friends with his producer, 40, so I met everyone through him. I’m just like, the little sister. They call me the “6 Goddess.”\n\nThe same day that “Signs” was released, Winnie posted an Instagram picture, tagging Drake and quoting these lyrics:\n\n\n\nThe two were rumored to be dating in February of 2017, but Winnie was quick to dismiss those allegations in a tweet.", "annotation_id": "12204629", "url": "https://genius.com/12204629", "state": "accepted", "votes": 87, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Signs", "status": "done", "targets": 8, "clicked": 8, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-signs-lyrics", "genius_title": "Signs"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Work No Play", "line": "The game needs change and I’m the cashier", "vault_lines": ["The game needs change and I'm the cashier"], "meaning": "Arguably, Drake revolutionized rap in a way that no other rapper had done before. Not because of his catchy tunes or awards, but because of how he has redefined masculinity. As mentioned earlier in the song, Drake has been ridiculed for being “cheesy” or “too soft” for a rapper. While many rap songs in the early 2000s were about violence, having sex with women, and drugs, Drake broke expectations by singing about love and heartbreak. As opposed to degrading women through his lyrics, Drake applauds them for being strong, independent, educated, and accomplished.", "annotation_id": "24631469", "url": "https://genius.com/24631469", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Work No Play", "line": "Wheelchair Jimmy never saw this comin’ Only thing he’d say is to keep it one hunnid", "vault_lines": ["Wheelchair Jimmy never saw this comin'", "Only thing he'd say is to keep it one hunnid"], "meaning": "Drake started his career acting for a “Degrassi,” a Canadian teen drama franchise. He played the role of Jimmy Brooks, who spent the last several seasons in a wheelchair after being injured in a school shooting, hence the nickname “Wheelchair Jimmy.”", "annotation_id": "24631420", "url": "https://genius.com/24631420", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Work No Play", "line": "Post award depression taking a toll on me, I got four", "vault_lines": ["Post award depression taking a toll on me, I got four"], "meaning": "Drake has rapped about his mental health in previous songs. Examples include: “Anxiety is a drug that I use to get the job done” from ‘The Remorse’ and “You know I spend money because spending time is hopeless / And know I pop bottles because I bottle my emotions” from ‘Fear.’\n\n“I got four” refers to the fact that Drake has earned four Grammy awards.", "annotation_id": "24631376", "url": "https://genius.com/24631376", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Work No Play", "line": "This shit was ramen goin’ noodles at the garden Melo still fighting for that ring, I beg your pardon", "vault_lines": ["Melo still fighting for that ring, I beg your pardon", "This shit was ramen goin' noodles at the garden"], "meaning": "Here, “garden” refers to Madison Square Garden, the multi-purpose arena where the New York Knicks play their home games. “Melo” refers to Carmelo Anthony and the fact that he has still not won a NBA championship despite being named an NBA All-Star ten times and an All-NBA Team member six times.", "annotation_id": "24631349", "url": "https://genius.com/24631349", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Work No Play", "line": "Media think I’m losin’ but never check the score", "vault_lines": ["Media think I'm losin' but never check the score"], "meaning": "Recently, new trends on TikTok and Twitter poking fun at Drake have gone viral. These videos express the “cheesy side” of Drake.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ajXrR2dpPu4", "annotation_id": "24631336", "url": "https://genius.com/24631336", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Work No Play", "line": "Momma pour me a drink please I need a little more", "vault_lines": ["Momma pour me a drink please I need a little more"], "meaning": "Like a real multi-hyphenate, Drake owns his own whiskey company, called “Virginia Black.” His entrepreneurial spirit can also be seen in the music industry. Some of his pursuits include OVO Sounds, Young Money Entertainment, and 100 Thieves.", "annotation_id": "24631272", "url": "https://genius.com/24631272", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Work No Play", "line": "Dropped a single but I ain’t single no more", "vault_lines": ["Dropped a single but I ain't single no more"], "meaning": "Drake is renowned for his relationships with different women. His previous ex-relationships include Bella Harris, Imaan Hammam, Sophie Brussaux, and Rihanna. ‘Certified Lover Boy,’ his latest album, also points to this idea.", "annotation_id": "24631262", "url": "https://genius.com/24631262", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
