{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I Did (Grand Entrance)", "line": "I mean maybe I’m confused, ’cause I thought that we was enemies, yeah The big you is like a mini me", "vault_lines": ["I mean maybe I'm confused, 'cause I thought that we was enemies, yeah", "The big you is like a mini me"], "meaning": "Kendrick Lamar has a song titled “U,” Drake’s line could be seen as emphasizing that even when Kendrick is at his best, he is just a mere reflection or a smaller version of Drake.\n\nThese particular lines fits with Lamar’s sporadic release schedule and periods of silence, hence why Drake had it all wrong thinking they were rivals, highlighting the difference in their perceived levels of influence and success.", "annotation_id": "32930459", "url": "https://genius.com/32930459", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I Did (Grand Entrance)", "line": "It was meant to happen, the most trusted going triple platinum", "vault_lines": ["It was meant to happen, the most trusted going triple platinum"], "meaning": "All of Drake’s studio albums are certified x3 platinum or above by the RIAA, aside from his debut album, Thank Me Later, which is only platinum in the US (equating to 1 million copies sold).", "annotation_id": "22623386", "url": "https://genius.com/22623386", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I Did (Grand Entrance)", "line": "Like BIG U, man, I’m a legend in my city streets, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Like BIG U, man, I'm a legend in my city streets, yeah"], "meaning": "Like Big U, man, I’m a legend in my city streets, yeah\n—\nDrake is saying his impact in Toronto is equal to the impact Big U has had in LA helping break Kurupt & Nipsey Hussle to mainstream awareness", "annotation_id": "22330619", "url": "https://genius.com/22330619", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I Did (Grand Entrance)", "line": "Switch up the sentiment, rappin’ on instrumentals That’s how I paid the rent", "vault_lines": ["Switch up the sentiment, rappin' on instrumentals", "That's how I paid the rent"], "meaning": "This could be a stretch however this isn’t the first time Drake paid homage to Julez Santana or Dipset.\n\nFrom his album “Me to U”\n\nStreets to rap, yeah that’s the way I went\nNow it’s beats and rhymes, that’s the way I pay the rent", "annotation_id": "21800708", "url": "https://genius.com/21800708", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I Did (Grand Entrance)", "line": "I talked to God standin’ up straight, I don’t get on my knees That isn’t me, that’s not the person I was raised to be", "vault_lines": ["I talked to God standin' up straight, I don't get on my knees", "That isn't me, that's not the person I was raised to be"], "meaning": "A common position to be in when talking to God (praying) is kneeling. Drake is saying that instead of kneeling, he stands and that kneeling is not his thing to do.", "annotation_id": "21797344", "url": "https://genius.com/21797344", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I Did (Grand Entrance)", "line": "Presidential suites, we don’t get impeached", "vault_lines": ["Presidential suites, we don't get impeached"], "meaning": "Drake commonly mentions terms relating to presidency and the current president, Donald Trump. On this line, he particular jabs at Donald Trump, who was in fact impeached in January 2020.\n\nMentions presidential terminology in:\n\nDiplomatic Immunity\nChicago Freestyle\nWe’ll Be Fine\nUp All Night", "annotation_id": "21593353", "url": "https://genius.com/21593353", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I Did (Grand Entrance)", "line": "Ballin’ by the beach, like Miami Heat, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Ballin' by the beach, like Miami Heat, yeah"], "meaning": "The Miami Heat play at American Airlines Arena, which is only 4 miles away from Miami Beach.", "annotation_id": "21593294", "url": "https://genius.com/21593294", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
