{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Let’s Call It Off", "line": "Uh, when did you get like this? Least you coulda done is gone and give me a warning", "vault_lines": ["Uh, when did you get like this?", "Least you coulda done is gone and give me a warning"], "meaning": "Here Drake recalls the way she was when he first met her, but along the way something changed that is unbeknowst to him.", "annotation_id": "39407249", "url": "https://genius.com/39407249", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Let’s Call It Off", "line": "We just have had enough of us Let’s call the whole thing off We just have had enough of us", "vault_lines": ["Let's call the whole thing off", "We just have had enough of us"], "meaning": "This is kinda common sense but drake in this line is talking about how he is tired of his relationship with this girl and just wants to break up and go separate ways. Or end their little thing they have going on", "annotation_id": "33790004", "url": "https://genius.com/33790004", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Let’s Call It Off", "line": "[Verse 2: Drake]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This verse heavily interpolates the first verse off of the prominently sampled song Peter Bjorn & John’s “Let’s Call it Off”", "annotation_id": "32814519", "url": "https://genius.com/32814519", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Let’s Call It Off", "line": "The look on your face said you were expecting more But some things look better inside of the store", "vault_lines": ["The look on your face said you were expecting more", "But some things look better inside of the store"], "meaning": "his girl thought he changed and was a better man but turns out he was js faking it and she didnt rly know him like that", "annotation_id": "26974778", "url": "https://genius.com/26974778", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Let’s Call It Off", "line": "Uh, you look for reasons for us to argue I swear everytime I call, you just tell me how I don’t call you", "vault_lines": ["Uh, you look for reasons for us to argue", "I swear everytime I call, you just tell me how I don't call you"], "meaning": "Drake’s girl always finds a reason to argue with him, dating back to probably why he wants to restart and end the relationship with her: she creates too much toxicity", "annotation_id": "26901932", "url": "https://genius.com/26901932", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Let’s Call It Off", "line": "I just really wanna turn the wheels back Give you all your sweaters and your heels back Convince you that time will heal that", "vault_lines": ["I just really wanna turn the wheels back", "Give you all your sweaters and your heels back", "Convince you that time will heal that"], "meaning": "Drake wants to restart with this girl and end their relationship, now that he knows all she’s been through and what she’s really like. He believes that time will heal her", "annotation_id": "26901929", "url": "https://genius.com/26901929", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Let’s Call It Off", "line": "My girlfriend, my girlfriend, call herself my girlfriend", "vault_lines": ["My girlfriend, my girlfriend, call herself my girlfriend"], "meaning": "Drake has a girl but they don’t really have labels, she forces them on herself, calling her his girlfriend", "annotation_id": "26901921", "url": "https://genius.com/26901921", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Let’s Call It Off", "line": "Tell me that we ’posed to be together ’til the world end But I don’t really feel that", "vault_lines": ["Tell me that we 'posed to be together 'til the world end", "But I don't really feel that"], "meaning": "the dynamic of “forever & ever” comes up in drake and his girl’s relationship. He doesn’t really feel nor agree with this idea", "annotation_id": "26901917", "url": "https://genius.com/26901917", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
