{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "What If I Kissed You", "line": "If we were a secret, how long could you keep it Keep it to yourself, don’t tell nobody else? Nothin’ but mine, talkin’ bout mine Now you’re all mine, and you, you, you And you’d just be mine (Just be mine) And you’d just be mine, all mine", "vault_lines": ["Keep it to yourself, don't tell nobody else", "And you just be mine (Just be mine)", "And you just be mine, all mine", "And you'd just be mine (Just, just be mine)", "How would we explain it?", "If we were a secret, tell me, could you keep it?", "And you'd just be mine, all mine", "And you just be mine, oh, yeah", "And you just be mine, all mine, yeah", "If we were a secret, how long could you keep it?"], "meaning": ".", "annotation_id": "41372255", "url": "https://genius.com/41372255", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": false, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "What If I Kissed You", "line": "Take me, I’m yours, and I don’t really care who knows it Can we afford to be that open with all these emotions?", "vault_lines": ["I'll admit that I'm yours", "I don't really care who knows it", "But can we afford to be that open with all of these emotions", "Take me, I'm yours", "And I don't really care who knows it", "Can we afford to, that open with all these emotions"], "meaning": ".", "annotation_id": "41372254", "url": "https://genius.com/41372254", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": false, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "What If I Kissed You", "status": "done", "targets": 2, "clicked": 2, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-what-if-i-kissed-you-lyrics", "genius_title": "What If I Kissed You"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "With You", "line": "Busy as usual, but we should make some time", "vault_lines": ["Busy as usual, but we should make some time"], "meaning": "Drake and this woman are both focused on their careers and don’t have a lot of free time, unless they move some things in their schedules around to make time for each other.", "annotation_id": "26669735", "url": "https://genius.com/26669735", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "With You", "line": "Choosey lover for the moment Different story when I leave you Story up just to keep you I need you ’round, I need you, oh", "vault_lines": ["Choosey lover for the moment", "Different story when I leave you", "Story up just to keep you", "I need you 'round, I need you, oh"], "meaning": "While Drake confesses his feelings towards the girl he’s “linked up” with in the heat of the moment, he admits to “storying up” (making up a fake story) just to keep her around.\n\nA “choosey lover” is someone who is very selective in who they love/have sex with. While he acts as though she’s his main girl when he’s with her, the second he leaves, he’s out trying to find someone else to have a good time with.", "annotation_id": "9102347", "url": "https://genius.com/9102347", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "With You", "line": "It’s about us right now, girl, where you going? It’s about us right now, girl, where you going? I’m with you, oh woah You, woah", "vault_lines": ["It's about us right now, girl, where you going?", "I'm with you, woah", "It's about us right now, girl, where you going? Yeah", "I'm with you, oh woah", "It's all about us right now, girl, where you going?"], "meaning": "During their past collaborations, Drake and Party flaunt their money and success in hopes of winning over a woman. Even during one of their most confessional tracks “Come and See Me,” the two artists still expect the woman to make all the sacrifices.\n\nThe script is flipped here, PND (along with Drake) put emphasis on the duality of their relationship by using the word ‘us.’ In this scenario, the guys are putting in all the work, but their hopeful partners are preoccupied, either with other men or their careers.", "annotation_id": "9080236", "url": "https://genius.com/9080236", "state": "accepted", "votes": 74, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "With You", "line": "Oh, I know you feel what I feel Breaking you off, it’s so real I can’t fake that, babe", "vault_lines": ["Breaking you off, it's so real", "I can't fake that, babe", "I need you 'round, I need you, oh", "Oh, I know you feel what I feel"], "meaning": "“To break” a girl off is to sleep with them, ideally resulting in an orgasm (for her).\n\nPARTYNEXTDOOR has carved himself a reputation as being more than proficient in the bedroom, so there’s no need for this girl to fake her orgasm. During “Things & Such (Kehlani’s Freestyle),” rumoured to be confirmation of a relationship between the two, he sings:\n\nCrushing girl, I’m glad too\nFuck you ‘til you cum, girl I’m glad to\nYeah you know I had to\n\nClearly he’s experienced in the matter.", "annotation_id": "9076038", "url": "https://genius.com/9076038", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "With You", "line": "You do you, girl, the haters gon’ hate Cut them off like you a sensei, girl", "vault_lines": ["You do you, girl, the haters gon' hate", "Cut them off like you a sensei, girl"], "meaning": "PARTY just wants to enjoy the moment with this girl, but the haters are getting in the way. He recommends that she cut off communication with them in the same way a sensei might cut down an enemy.\n\nOn his track “Right Now,”  PARTY expressed similar disdain for haters:\n\nGirl cut them bitches off\nThey ain’t got shit to say", "annotation_id": "9074464", "url": "https://genius.com/9074464", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "With You", "line": "[Chorus: PARTYNEXTDOOR, Jeremih, PARTYNEXTDOOR & Jeremih]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The parts of the hook originally sung by Drake are now done by R&B singer Jeremih. The two have never properly collaborated on a track, only to be heard together on a remix the Chicago singer did to Drake’s “I Get Lonely Too” and “Amen”, the break-through single of current Drizzy rival, Meek Mill.\n\n\n\nSome fans have also speculated the voice heard is actually that of OVO signee Roy Woods, but according to the original booklet it’s definitely Jeremih.\n\nOn June 16th, Jeremih announced he would release a joint album with PARTYNEXTDOOR titled Late Night Party. Fans have since speculated that this song was originally made for that project before being given to Drake, who would end up replacing Jeremih’s verse.", "annotation_id": "9072913", "url": "https://genius.com/9072913", "state": "accepted", "votes": 62, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "With You", "line": "My love’s locked down and you cuffing it You’re the only one I trust with it You’re the only one that stuck with it (Uh)", "vault_lines": ["My love's locked down and you cuffing it", "You're the only one I trust with it", "You're the only one that stuck with it (Uh)"], "meaning": "This is a reference to Kanye West’s song “Love Lockdown.” PARTY keeps his girl “locked down” and “cuffed” because she’s the only girl he can truly trust.", "annotation_id": "9071646", "url": "https://genius.com/9071646", "state": "accepted", "votes": 37, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "With You", "line": "M.I.A. in the M.I.A", "vault_lines": ["M.I.A. in the M.I.A"], "meaning": "M.I.A. is an initialism for “Missing In Action.”  Although it has military roots, it has been generalized to civilian situations.\n\nMIA is also the three-letter code for Miami International Airport in Miami, Florida.  The acronym is often used to represent the whole city of Miami.\n\nDrake has voiced his love for Miami before, while PND also has spoken about hanging out in Miami.", "annotation_id": "9070878", "url": "https://genius.com/9070878", "state": "accepted", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "With You", "line": "Yeah, I can’t get enough of you, babe Bottles open up so you can try and open up for me, baby", "vault_lines": ["I can't fake that, babe", "Yeah, I can't get enough of you, babe", "Bottles open up so you can try and open up for me, baby"], "meaning": "PARTY compares the girl’s refusal to share her internal thoughts and feelings with him to a bottle, and coaxes her to come out of her shell. If a bottle can be opened up, then it’s possible for her to be open with him, too.\n\nAdditionally, people become much more relaxed and blunt when under the influence of alcohol. As the bottles “open up,” the likelihood of her letting PARTY sleep with her increases.", "annotation_id": "9070844", "url": "https://genius.com/9070844", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "With You", "line": "Mixing vodka and emotions, tapping into your emotions Dry cry ’cause I’m hopeless", "vault_lines": ["Mixing vodka and emotions, tapping into your emotions", "Dry cry 'cause I'm hopeless"], "meaning": "Mixing juice or soda with vodka is a common way to cut its strong taste. Instead, Drake drinks it straight to cope with his emotional turmoil.\n\nAlcohol has many emotional effects and Drake feels them starting to take over his train of thought. He harbors deep sadness for this woman, but struggles to actualize the emotion by producing tears.\n\n\n\nDrake borrows the “dry cry” lyric from Sizzla’s “Just One of Those Days,” a broken-hearted reggae anthem.\n\nFellow rapper Kanye West rapped a similar line in “Bittersweet Poetry”:\n\nAnd you mix them emotions with tequila\nAnd you mix that with a little bad advice", "annotation_id": "9070223", "url": "https://genius.com/9070223", "state": "accepted", "votes": 50, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "With You", "status": "done", "targets": 10, "clicked": 10, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-with-you-lyrics", "genius_title": "With You"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "A Night Off", "line": "Spending every moment in the studio I never said it’d be fair But when you’re all alone, I hope you truly know How bad I want to be there", "vault_lines": ["Spending every moment in the studio", "I never said it'd be fair", "But when you're all alone, I hope you truly know", "How bad I want to be there"], "meaning": "Here Drake is referencing his work ethic and talking about how he’s frequently in the studio making music. This is the lifestyle he wants but he has desires to see his girl when he’s done working.", "annotation_id": "20214651", "url": "https://genius.com/20214651", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "A Night Off", "line": "Can you work without a second for some fun? Now you finally got a moment to yourself, girl", "vault_lines": ["Can you work without a second for some fun?", "Now you finally got a moment to yourself, girl"], "meaning": "Speaking to MTV about this song Drake said that this was actually about a girl who asked him to “take a night off”, but he switched parts for the song, instead he’s telling a hard working woman to enjoy her free time with him.", "annotation_id": "4126462", "url": "https://genius.com/4126462", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "A Night Off", "line": "I want you on top, so let your hair down I took the night off for you Girl, I’m gonna turn the lights off, but keep your heels on They’re fittin’ for what we’re about to do", "vault_lines": ["I want you on top, so let your hair down", "I took the night off for you", "Girl, I'm gonna turn the lights off, but keep your heels on", "They're fittin' for what we're about to do", "I took a night off for you", "Took a night off for you", "But keep your heels on", "They're fittin' for what I'm about to do, oh"], "meaning": "This is a sly double entendre, sprinkled with some sexual innuendo:\n\n\nLloyd is taking the night off to spend some time with his babygirl\nLloyd is taking the night off of his babygirl, allowing her to be on top for once\n\n\n\nAlso, there is some small wordplay with “on TOP” and “hair DOWN.”", "annotation_id": "1630171", "url": "https://genius.com/1630171", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "A Night Off", "status": "done", "targets": 3, "clicked": 3, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-a-night-off-lyrics", "genius_title": "A Night Off"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Baby Come With Me", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-baby-come-with-me-lyrics", "genius_title": "Baby Come With Me"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Can I", "line": "Can I, baby? Can I, baby? Yeah, can I, baby? Can I, baby?", "vault_lines": ["Can I, baby? Can I, baby?", "Can I see you right now, I know the sun is up, baby?", "Can I ever make you feel like I'm down for you, baby?", "Can I finally take the time and open up to you, baby?", "Yeah, can I, baby? Can I, baby?", "Can I, baby? Can I? Before I turn the lights out", "Can I? Can I, baby?", "Can I bring you to the six where I really stay, baby?", "Can I tell you what I think my biggest flaw is, baby?", "Can I have an honest moment wit' you right now, baby?", "Can I get an honest answer from you right now, baby?"], "meaning": "Beyoncé monotonically chants the opening to all of Drake’s questions as he asks his girl permission to do various different things and closes with them with a pet name—her voice then eerily echoes and lingers in the background.", "annotation_id": "7911913", "url": "https://genius.com/7911913", "state": "accepted", "votes": 104, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Can I", "line": "[Verse: Drake & Beyoncé]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The whole verse structure (interpolation of Drake’s rap, into Beyoncé’s line) serve to give extra meaning to Drake’s line, in a similar manner to what Kanye achieved with Nina Simone’s sample in “Blood On The Leaves.”\n\nThe effect adds to the sense of venting in the song: there is a constant flow of interruption, as if the ‘Can I’ and ‘Baby’ are the girls attempts to enter into the conversation that Drake himself is asking for. Ironically (and tragically) his inability to allow her space stops that same conversation from happening and we understand—‘all we ever talk about is me’—as a kind of self-destructive, self-fulfilling prophecy.", "annotation_id": "6529203", "url": "https://genius.com/6529203", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Can I", "line": "Can I see you right now, I know the sun is up, baby? Sorry, I don’t really have a choice Can I ever make you feel like I’m down for you, baby? You do so much more than that for me Can I finally take the time and open up to you, baby? ’Cause that’s the side you never get to see", "vault_lines": ["Can I, baby? Can I, baby?", "Can I see you right now, I know the sun is up, baby?", "Sorry, I don't really have a choice", "Can I ever make you feel like I'm down for you, baby?", "You do so much more than that for me", "Can I finally take the time and open up to you, baby?", "Yeah, can I, baby? Can I, baby?", "'Cause that's the side you never get to see", "Can I? Can I, baby?", "Can I bring you to the six where I really stay, baby?", "Can I have an honest moment wit' you right now, baby?", "Can I get an honest answer from you right now, baby?"], "meaning": "This may allude to his unreleased track from If You Are Reading This It Is Too Late, “My Side”:\n\nYou don’t ever come to where I stay at\nIf anybody knows, girl you know, I know\n\nDrake has been feeling like his relationship with his girl hasn’t been working out. Drake blames himself for the failed relationship and wants to know how he can be completely devoted to her.", "annotation_id": "6525472", "url": "https://genius.com/6525472", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Can I", "line": "Can I call instead of text you on the hotline? Sometimes a nigga wanna hear your voice", "vault_lines": ["Can I, baby? Can I, baby?", "Can I call instead of text you on the hotline?", "Sometimes a nigga wanna hear your voice", "Can I? Can I, baby?"], "meaning": "It seems as if texting has replaced calling as the main form of communication, especially in this generation – Drake offers to call her on her hotline.\n\nDrake prefers hearing her voice over monotonous sound of a text message, or the humdrum vibrations that occur every other second.", "annotation_id": "6525457", "url": "https://genius.com/6525457", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Can I", "line": "Can I? Before I turn the lights out ’Fore I turn the lights out, tell me who the fuck you want to be", "vault_lines": ["Can I, baby? Can I, baby?", "Can I? Before I turn the lights out", "'Fore I turn the lights out, tell me who the fuck you want to be", "Can I? Before I turn the lights out one more time", "Can I, baby? Can I? Before I turn the lights out", "Tell me who the fuck you wanna be", "Can I? Can I, baby?", "Before I turn the lights out", "Tell me who the fuck you want to be"], "meaning": "Drake leaves this girl a very open question to determine what kind of person she is. Andre 3000 did something similar in the Outkast song “Da Art of Storytellin' (Part 1)”:\n\nTalking bout what we gonna be when we grow up\nI said what you wanna be, she said, “Alive”\nIt made me think for a minute, then looked in her eyes\n\nDrake may be looking for a deep thinker, like Sasha, to accompany him and hold him steady. Typically people want fame, fortune and parties to surround them, but with a man like Drake she has plenty of opportunities to build upon. Another simple choice, as Lennon put it, would be “happy” or “loved.”\n\nWhen I was 5 years old, my mother always told me that happiness was the key to life. When I went to school, they asked me what I wanted to be when I grew up. I wrote down ‘happy’. They told me I didn’t understand the assignment. I told them they didn’t understand life.\n- John Lennon\n\nWhatever her desires may be, Drake’s willing to give her the support to make it happen. However his interest in her is flickering and he doesn’t want another woman with no aspirations coming to him for fame and money. Drake needs a woman he can connect with deeply to ensure the light of their relationship remains bright. In the final line, he presses for an answer so he’ll know whether to keep the light of their connection burning or to shut it down.", "annotation_id": "6524883", "url": "https://genius.com/6524883", "state": "accepted", "votes": 61, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Can I", "line": "Can I have an honest moment wit’ you right now, baby? Tell me who the fuck you want to be Can I get an honest answer from you right now, baby? ’Cause all we ever talk about is me", "vault_lines": ["Can I, baby? Can I, baby?", "'Cause all we ever talk about is me", "'Fore I turn the lights out, tell me who the fuck you want to be", "Can I see you right now, I know the sun is up, baby?", "Yeah, can I, baby? Can I, baby?", "Tell me who the fuck you wanna be", "Can I? Can I, baby?", "Can I have an honest moment wit' you right now, baby?", "Tell me who the fuck you want to be", "Can I get an honest answer from you right now, baby?"], "meaning": "While the media and rap game are focused on Drake, he’s tired of the attention always being on him. Rather than every conversation feeling like an interview, he wants his girl to open up and let him know what she wants to do with the rest of her life.\n\nI needed to hear that shit, I hate when you’re submissive / Passive aggressive when we’re texting, I feel the distance\n\nIn order for him to truly open up to a girl like this, he needs her to let him in. Later in the verse he talks about his desire to hear her voice and wanting to open up to her, but first he needs to know what her aspirations are.", "annotation_id": "6524798", "url": "https://genius.com/6524798", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Can I", "line": "Can I tell you what I think my biggest flaw is, baby? I try to be consistent, but I can’t", "vault_lines": ["Can I, baby? Can I, baby?", "Yeah, can I, baby? Can I, baby?", "Can I? Can I, baby?", "Can I tell you what I think my biggest flaw is, baby?", "I try to be consistent, but I can't"], "meaning": "Drake’s flaw is that he can’t be consistent with women. No matter how many times he tries to do so, he ends up being inconsistent.", "annotation_id": "6494341", "url": "https://genius.com/6494341", "state": "accepted", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Can I", "line": "Can I bring you to the six where I really stay, baby? Show you why I am the way I am", "vault_lines": ["Can I, baby? Can I, baby?", "Yeah, can I, baby? Can I, baby?", "Can I? Can I, baby?", "Can I bring you to the six where I really stay, baby?", "Show you why I am the way I am"], "meaning": "Drake wants to bring this girl home. Toronto was given the nickname “The 6” because of its area codes 416 and 647.\n\nI was runnin' through the 6 with my woes\nYou know how that should go", "annotation_id": "6494255", "url": "https://genius.com/6494255", "state": "accepted", "votes": 52, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
