{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I Get Lonely", "line": "Waited on you for so long Too many days since January I’m still sitting here alone We should’ve did this already Said I got a email today Kind of thought that you forgot about me But I wanna hit you back to say Just like you, I get lonely", "vault_lines": ["Waited on you for so long", "When I get lonely", "Just like you, I get lonely too", "Too many days since January", "'Cause too many people wanna get me", "I get lonely too", "I'm still sitting here alone", "We should've did this already", "Said I got a email today", "Kind of thought that you forgot about me", "But I wanna hit you back to say", "Just like you, I get lonely"], "meaning": "These first verse expresses a strong sense of longing, loneliness, and frustration with how long he has been waiting for this person. He’s saying that a lot of time has passed since January, yet he is still alone and feels like their connection should have happened by now. When he receives an email from her, he initially wonders whether she has forgotten about him, which shows that he has been thinking about her and may feel uncertain about how much she cares. However, instead of ignoring her, he wants to respond and remind her that he understands what she is feeling because he gets lonely too", "annotation_id": "41554456", "url": "https://genius.com/41554456", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I Get Lonely", "line": "Don’t wanna come on strong ’Cause too many people wanna get me", "vault_lines": ["Don't wanna come on strong", "'Cause too many people wanna get me"], "meaning": "Drake is concerned that if he is overzealous with his affection too soon, he’ll get himself a woman who just wants him for his fame/money.", "annotation_id": "25152677", "url": "https://genius.com/25152677", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I Get Lonely", "line": "Just like you, I get lonely too Ooh, ooh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh Just like you, I get lonely too Ooh, ooh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh Just like you, I get lonely", "vault_lines": ["When I get lonely", "Just like you, I get lonely too", "Ooh, ooh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh", "I get lonely too", "Just like you, I get lonely"], "meaning": "Hook from TLC’s FAN MAIL sampled by Drake.\n\nIn the hook, he is pretty much stating that through her lone times while he is gone, he is also lonely. They aren’t steady right now, due to his career but it’s what he wants, and he wishes he could get to know someone and show him that he’s not the ‘'typical’‘ rapper. He wants to show her one-on-one that he’s different.\n\n‘'To a place just me and you ’", "annotation_id": "1849546", "url": "https://genius.com/1849546", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I Get Lonely", "status": "done", "targets": 3, "clicked": 3, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-i-get-lonely-lyrics", "genius_title": "I Get Lonely"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ice Melts", "line": "You need to fuckin’ stop watchin’ me", "vault_lines": ["You need to fuckin' stop watchin' me"], "meaning": "Ok, so, he wants YOU (YES YOU) to stop watching him, but you won’t. Stalking ass 🥷", "annotation_id": "33455208", "url": "https://genius.com/33455208", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ice Melts", "line": "I need you out in Jamaica, relaxin’", "vault_lines": ["I need you out in Jamaica, relaxin'"], "meaning": "In Drake’s More Life and Views, he is seen taking on a Jamaican accent and using patois (a Jamaican dialect). Drake embraces all different kinds of cultures in his music and this has contributed to his global success. For example, his song “One Dance”  is based of an African Music style called “Afrobeat” and has popularized Afrobeat artist “Wizkid”, and the song received over a billion plays on Spotify.\n\nhttps://genius.com/Drake-one-dance-lyrics\n\nDrake takes on the Jamaican accent and patois due to his time as a young adult in Toronto. 90% of Jamaicans living in Canada are in the Toronto area.", "annotation_id": "11793680", "url": "https://genius.com/11793680", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ice Melts", "line": "You’re a diamond out the rough or somethin’, somethin’ You need to give it up to someone You need to give luck to someone", "vault_lines": ["You need to give luck to someone", "You're a diamond out the rough or somethin', somethin'", "You need to give it up to someone"], "meaning": "A “diamond out the rough” refers to someone with tremendous potential, but who may appear damaged from bad experiences. In this case, Thugger sings of a special woman that makes him feel a way he doesn’t usually feel for women, despite the emotional baggage and guardedness she picked up from her past relationships.", "annotation_id": "11570710", "url": "https://genius.com/11570710", "state": "accepted", "votes": 36, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ice Melts", "line": "I still need some satisfaction A little less talk and a little more action", "vault_lines": ["I still need some satisfaction", "A little less talk and a little more action"], "meaning": "Drake alludes to “A Little Less Conversation” by Elvis Presley:\n\nA little less conversation, a little more action please\nAll this aggravation ain’t satisfactioning me\n\nThis girl’s iciness is interfering with Drizzy’s personal desires, and as Elvis would tell you, this can lead to some aggravation.", "annotation_id": "11559835", "url": "https://genius.com/11559835", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ice Melts", "line": "That must be why you move so icy (Ice)", "vault_lines": ["That must be why you move so icy (Ice)"], "meaning": "Similar to a theme explored on “Take Care”, Drake speculates that his love interest comes off as icy and cold because she’s previously been mistreated by men.\n\nThroughout the song, Drake, with the help of Young Thug, tries to convince this girl – who has become hardened on the outside – to let him inside and give him a chance. He wants the ice to melt.\n\nThe fact that the song’s title is “Ice Melts,‘’ along with the summer-y sound of the track, suggests that it indeed will.", "annotation_id": "11557390", "url": "https://genius.com/11557390", "state": "accepted", "votes": 37, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ice Melts", "line": "Feel a rump-rump Baby, I’m needin’ somethin’, somethin’", "vault_lines": ["Baby, I'm needin' somethin', somethin'"], "meaning": "Young Thug sings about feeling a woman’s rear-end and becoming aroused on this song’s chorus.\n\nThugger’s use of “rump-rump” here is also an instance of onomatopoeia, suggesting intimate activities with a significant other through his raspy and guttural vocals.\n\nThis wouldn’t be the first time Young Thug has manipulated his delivery. On the song “Harambe”, Thugger intentionally delivered raspy and guttural vocals to imitate the likeness of a gorilla.\n\n\n\nHear Young Thug confirm the lyrics here:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S3mh8mqK6_o&t=2970", "annotation_id": "11545699", "url": "https://genius.com/11545699", "state": "accepted", "votes": 63, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ice Melts", "line": "Slatt, slatt, slatt", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Slatt is a common slang word used by members of the Blood gang. In recent years, however, its usage has become watered down, and many now use it as an acronym for “Slime Love All The Time”. This ad-lib is found on many of Thug’s own songs, like in “Slime Shit”.\n\nYoung Thug claims to live the Slime Lifestyle and even released a whole mixtape series titled “Slime Season”.", "annotation_id": "11537589", "url": "https://genius.com/11537589", "state": "accepted", "votes": 52, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ice Melts", "line": "Jeffery (Mario) Jeffery, ayy", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Young Thug’s birth name is Jeffery Lamar Williams, and today he still uses Jeffery as one of his stage names. In fact, he named his popular 2016 mixtape JEFFERY.", "annotation_id": "11533672", "url": "https://genius.com/11533672", "state": "accepted", "votes": 53, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ice Melts", "line": "I want to see you do 911, fuck a Panamera (In a 911)", "vault_lines": ["I want to see you do 911, fuck a Panamera (In a 911)"], "meaning": "Drake is referring the Porsche Panamera versus the Porsche 911, which is 10 stacks more, essentially saying that he wants her to do bigger things.\n\n\n\nInterestingly, YG raps about how he prefers the Panamera on “Who Do You Love,” a 2014 track featuring Drake. It’s possible that’s the inspiration for this line.\n\nIn addition, this could be interpreted is a diss towards Meek Mill, who was featured on Omelly’s 2013 song Panamera.\n\nTheir summer 2015 beef resulted in one of the most famous diss tracks of all time and a Grammy Nomination. This entire album is filled with similar attacks on Meek.\n\nThis diss specifically could be referring to Nicki Minaj, who broke up in 2017 with Meek Mill. Drake and Minaj have a long flirtatious history, and he could be saying that her upgrade from Meek Mill to Drake would be of the same magnitude as of that from a Panamera to a Porsche 911.", "annotation_id": "11533094", "url": "https://genius.com/11533094", "state": "accepted", "votes": 69, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ice Melts", "line": "Icy like 1017", "vault_lines": ["Icy like there's nobody you'd ever need", "But you icy like 1017 (Icy)"], "meaning": "In this line, Drake uses Gucci Mane’s debut single, “Icy,” from his 2005 debut album, Trap House, to compare how emotionally closed-off the woman he’s singing about is to how much jewelry Gucci Mane wears, as “ice” is common slang term in hip-hop for jewelry, more specifically diamonds.\n\n1017 Brick Squad is Gucci Mane’s record label. Known affiliates of the label include Young Thug, Waka Flocka Flame, Chief Keef and of course Guwop himself.  Gucci, as well as other members of 1017 Brick Squad are known for rocking outlandish jewelry.", "annotation_id": "11531129", "url": "https://genius.com/11531129", "state": "accepted", "votes": 138, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ice Melts", "line": "Look, I want you to myself (Yeah) But I know you just left someone else, I know you did (I know) He did a number on you (Brrt)", "vault_lines": ["Look, I want you to myself (Yeah)", "But I know you just left someone else, I know you did (I know)", "He did a number on you (Brrt)"], "meaning": "In this section, Drake is referencing Nicki Minaj’s recent breakup with fellow rapper Meek Mill. Drake and Meek had a lengthy and widely publicized beef. He is subsequently taking shots at Meek while also trying to rekindle his relationship with Nicki.\n\nDrake’s verse on Minaj’s “Only,” off of her 2014 album The Pinkprint, cements Drizzy’s intentions with the female rap star rather bluntly.\n\nI never fucked Nicki, cause she got a man\nBut when that’s over, then I’m first in line\n\nNicki also seems to be featured on Drake’s official Instagram page several times roughly 1 week prior to the release of More Life, further reinforcing this theory.\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/BRjkO0nDhZb/?taken-by=champagnepapi", "annotation_id": "11531121", "url": "https://genius.com/11531121", "state": "accepted", "votes": 85, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ice Melts", "status": "done", "targets": 11, "clicked": 11, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-ice-melts-lyrics", "genius_title": "Ice Melts"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Princess", "line": "Shop until you drop in Bal Harbour", "vault_lines": ["Shop until you drop in Bal Harbour"], "meaning": "Bal Harbour Shops is a shopping mall that’s ranked across the highest-grossing retail centers in the world in Bal Harbour, Miami metropolitan area, Florida.\n\nAccording to a source as of April of 2026 it’s the most profitable mall in North America, ironically surpassing a shopping center from Drake’s home town Toronto.", "annotation_id": "39795854", "url": "https://genius.com/39795854", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Princess", "line": "And you work all week at the Equinox just to complain when I go", "vault_lines": ["And you work all week at the Equinox just to complain when I go"], "meaning": "Equinox is a high-end fitness gym.", "annotation_id": "39779392", "url": "https://genius.com/39779392", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
