{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Finesse", "line": "You and your sister Too hot to handle", "vault_lines": ["You and your sister", "Too hot to handle"], "meaning": "Drake could be talking about the two model sisters Gigi and Bella Hadid", "annotation_id": "16798972", "url": "https://genius.com/16798972", "state": "pending", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Finesse", "line": "Commitment Going the distance I’m new to all of this", "vault_lines": ["All the time, all the time, all the–", "All the time, all the time", "I'm new to all of this"], "meaning": "Drake commits that he would take time off his busy lifestyle to spend with his partner, something that he claims is particularly new to him. From his relationships with Jennifer Lopez to Rihanna, he avoids these situations due to his hectic schedule and his concerns that any potential lovers are looking for fame rather than a real relationship.\n\nHe previously mentioned this in his 2014 single, “Heat of the Moment” where he sings:\n\nYes Lord, yes Lord, yes Lord\nI’ve seen some things\nI wish we had met when I was in my teens\nYes Lord, yes Lord, yes Lord\nCause these days I only know conditional love\nI’m not used to settlin' down\nI’m too used to switchin' it up, oh", "annotation_id": "14942382", "url": "https://genius.com/14942382", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Finesse", "line": "Things would get cancelled I would make time for you", "vault_lines": ["Things would get cancelled", "I would make time for you"], "meaning": "Drake’s amazing streaming numbers, spectacular Billboard feats, many RIAA certifications and simply his good talent, have caused him to become a busy man. In Drake’s 2018 collaboration with Atlanta rapper Lil Baby titled, “Yes Indeed,” he raps;\n\nBooked for three years, man you can’t even book me", "annotation_id": "14882600", "url": "https://genius.com/14882600", "state": "accepted", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Finesse", "line": "Can’t be in a room with you and stand on different sides", "vault_lines": ["Can't be in a room with you and stand on different sides"], "meaning": "This line could be also directed at Rihanna. In October 2017, Drake and Rihanna both attended Chace Infinite’s—A$AP Rocky’s manager—and creative director, Capricorn Clark’s son birthday party in Los Angeles. However, neither Drake or Riri were pictured together at the event.", "annotation_id": "14880757", "url": "https://genius.com/14880757", "state": "accepted", "votes": 60, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Finesse", "line": "I want my baby to have your eyes I’m going against my own advice Should I do New York? I can’t decide Fashion week is more your thing than mine I can’t even lie, I’d rather stay inside I can’t do suit and tie", "vault_lines": ["I want my baby to have your eyes", "I'm going against my own advice", "Should I do New York? I can't decide", "Fashion week is more your thing than mine", "I can't even lie, I'd rather stay inside", "I can't do suit and tie"], "meaning": "Drake is likely alluding to model Bella Hadid. This is supported by what would be an allusion her model sister Gigi in his second verse:\n\nYou and your sister\nToo hot to handle\n\nIn 2017, it was rumored that Drake and Bella were dating, but broke up after Drake ghosted her. However, shortly after the release of Scorpion, in a June 2018 tweet, Bella cleared the air, saying she and Drake were only friends.\n\nIt’s also possible that Drake could also be talking about his old flame, Rihanna. Rihanna has since made a foray into the fashion world with her Fenty x PUMA line and her SAVAGE X FENTY lingerie. She also attended New York Fashion Week in 2017 to promote her FENTY Beauty cosmetics line.\n\nThe line “fashion week is more your thing than mine” was displayed on one of the promotional billboards for Scorpion in Times Square prior to its release.", "annotation_id": "14879602", "url": "https://genius.com/14879602", "state": "accepted", "votes": 104, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
