{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Q&A", "line": "Me and KD got way too much cheese like the— yeah, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Me and KD got way too much cheese like the— yeah, yeah"], "meaning": "Drake is saying he and KD have so much “cheese” (money) like the (cuts off). It’s possible that the punchline here is “macaroni”, which also rhymes with “goalie” from the previous line. Drake could be avoiding finishing the line because the pun is too cheesy. Macaroni and cheese is also referenced through Kevin Durant’s initials, KD, which could also stand for Kraft Dinner.", "annotation_id": "40003768", "url": "https://genius.com/40003768", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Q&A", "line": "Texting you, calling you, my phone bill did all the roaming", "vault_lines": ["Texting you, calling you, my phone bill did all the roaming"], "meaning": "In this line, Drake is saying he was constantly texting and calling someone, going all out to reach them. The “roaming” line plays on phone charges, suggesting he was so invested that it felt like he was even paying extra just to stay connected. It also hints that the distance made communication harder and more costly.", "annotation_id": "40003447", "url": "https://genius.com/40003447", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Q&A", "line": "Why are you kicking your feet up with niggas? Are you Michael Jordan?", "vault_lines": ["Why are you kicking your feet up with niggas? Are you Michael Jordan?"], "meaning": "The phrase “kicking your feet up” usually means to relax, take a break, or lounge. Drake asks the woman why she is spending time relaxing with other men, and compares this to iconic relaxed post-championship imagery of Michael Jordan, most notably following the Chicago Bulls' 1998 championship.\n\n\n\nKicking also likely refers to “kicks,” a slang word used for shoes. Michael Jordan’s Air Jordan shoe line launched in 1985 and has since become a legendary multi-billion-dollar global signature sneaker and sportswear franchise produced by Nike under the Jordan Brand.", "annotation_id": "39942731", "url": "https://genius.com/39942731", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Q&A", "line": "This ain’t my first rodeo with you, girl, come and ride my pony", "vault_lines": ["This ain't my first rodeo with you, girl, come and ride my pony"], "meaning": "Drake has a horse c**k", "annotation_id": "39894413", "url": "https://genius.com/39894413", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Q&A", "status": "done", "targets": 4, "clicked": 4, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-q-a-lyrics", "genius_title": "Q&A"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Screw The World (Interlude)", "line": "I’ma do it and I like to take my shit slow Uptempo is the beat I’m laid back and blowin’ on a Sweet Put your ass to sleep, do it", "vault_lines": ["I'ma do it and I like to take my shit slow", "Uptempo is the beat", "I'm laid back and blowin' on a Sweet", "Put your ass to sleep, do it"], "meaning": "This line breaks down the technical genius behind the “chopped and screwed” sound. Even when an instrumental is naturally fast-paced (“uptempo”), Screw manually pitches it down on his turntables to create a heavy, chopped, ultra-sluggish groove. Breathed down while smoking a “Sweet” (Swisher Sweets blunt),\n\n\n\nThe slowed-down tempo mimics the hypnotic, couch lock sensation of sipping lean, literally slowing down time for the listener (“put your ass to sleep”).", "annotation_id": "40986261", "url": "https://genius.com/40986261", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Screw The World (Interlude)", "line": "Screw the fuckin’ world on up", "vault_lines": ["Screw the fuckin' world on up"], "meaning": "This song samples Nas featuring Lauryn Hill’s song, “If I Ruled The World (Imagine That)”.\n\nDJ Screw is doing a wordplay on the title and adds his own influence into it, by replacing “rule” with “screw”.", "annotation_id": "29733963", "url": "https://genius.com/29733963", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Screw The World (Interlude)", "line": "Screwed Up Click", "vault_lines": ["Right before your eyes, Screwed Up Click"], "meaning": "Screwed Up Click (S.U.C) is a hip-hop collective group based in Houston, Texas led by DJ Screw. Some of the most notable rappers within it include H.A.W.K., Big Mello, Big Moe, Big Pokey, Botany Boys, ESG., Fat Pat, Big Floyd, Lil Flip, Lil Keke, Lil' O, and Z-Ro.", "annotation_id": "29730969", "url": "https://genius.com/29730969", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Screw The World (Interlude)", "line": "Uh, ’bout to screw the world", "vault_lines": ["Uh, 'bout to screw the world"], "meaning": "DJ Screw was known for being one of the greatest DJ’s in the genre of hip-hop. He was usually known to “screw” music, which was the ability to chop and screw his music.", "annotation_id": "29730635", "url": "https://genius.com/29730635", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Screw The World (Interlude)", "line": "Syrup in my cup", "vault_lines": ["Mr. Nine-Six, syrup in my cup"], "meaning": "‘syrup in my cup’ refers to lean, which is a recreational drug in the form of a liquid that traditionally contains prescription strength cough or cold syrup containing codeine and promethazine and a soft drink, usually sprite.", "annotation_id": "29728165", "url": "https://genius.com/29728165", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
