{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "True Bestie", "line": "Where my bestie at? Bring your best bitch out, she ain’t on shit ‘Cause my bitch bound to throw that ass, that’s my lil’ cute big booty bitch I call her Mia, she a diva, and she love to talk her shit Ho can’t address her, if she let her, my bitch bound to throw a fit ’Cause where my bestie at? Bring your best bitch out, she ain’t on shit ‘Cause my bitch bound to throw that ass, that’s my lil’ cute big booty bitch I call her Mia, she a diva, and she love to talk her shit Ho can’t address her, if she let her, my bitch bound to throw a fit", "vault_lines": ["Ho can't address her, if she let her, my bitch bound to throw a fit", "'Causе where my bestiе at?", "'Cause where my bestie at?", "Where my bestie at?", "Bring your best bitch out, she ain't on shit", "'Cause my bitch bound to throw that ass, that's my lil' cute big booty bitch", "I call her Mia, she a diva, and she love to talk her shit"], "meaning": "That entire chorus is taken from Iconic Savvy’s 2025 song “PSA” from her album 7con7c 7.", "annotation_id": "39795062", "url": "https://genius.com/39795062", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "True Bestie", "line": "Greaze", "vault_lines": ["Girl, pop your shit and talk greaze"], "meaning": "“Greaze” is a popular UK slang term originating from London. It is commonly used as a noun, an ad-lib, or a verb (often spelled “talking grease”) – Not to be confused with “Grease talk” like Rio Da Yung OG", "annotation_id": "39794543", "url": "https://genius.com/39794543", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
