{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "True Bestie", "line": "After this I wanna see you, I left all my cues in your clutch", "vault_lines": ["After this I wanna see you, I left all my cues in your clutch"], "meaning": "Drake is saying he wants to see the girl after the club, and that he has already left his “cues” in her clutch, a small handbag. In this setting, “cues” can mean hints that he is interested, but it may also suggest cash or something valuable placed in her purse", "annotation_id": "39791777", "url": "https://genius.com/39791777", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "True Bestie", "line": "You brown just like liquor, ’42 straight to the face", "vault_lines": ["You brown just like liquor, '42 straight to the face"], "meaning": "Drake is comparing his girl’s brown skin to Don Julio 1942 which is one of the most premium tequilas in the game, retailing around $160–$200 USD a bottle.\n\n“Straight to the face” means no mixer(a mixer is when a drink that is non alcaholic is mixed with an alcaholic drink,to add flavour), no chase (side drink), and usually directly sipping from the bottle. Drake says he wants her just like how you take a proper shot of 1942.", "annotation_id": "39782980", "url": "https://genius.com/39782980", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
