{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Go Out Tonight", "line": "Someone did me the same", "vault_lines": ["Someone did me the same"], "meaning": "drake got heartbroken 💔", "annotation_id": "40918342", "url": "https://genius.com/40918342", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Go Out Tonight", "line": "Call a couple friends you know you can have some fun with", "vault_lines": ["Call a couple friends you know you can have some fun with"], "meaning": "Drake reminds him that his ex is not the only person in his life. After a breakup, it is easy to become so focused on the person you lost that you forget about the friends and parts of your life that were there before them.\n\nCalling friends gives him something else to do and helps him feel like himself again. It also shows that moving on does not have to immediately mean finding another relationship. Sometimes it starts with simply being around people who make you happy.", "annotation_id": "40785388", "url": "https://genius.com/40785388", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Go Out Tonight", "line": "Order you a drink, don’t even overthink", "vault_lines": ["Order you a drink, don't even overthink"], "meaning": "Drake knows that sitting around thinking about the breakup is probably what has kept this person stuck in the first place.\n\nThe drink is almost beside the point. The real advice is to do something simple, get out of your own head, and stop replaying the same thoughts for one night.\n\nSometimes you do not need to solve everything immediately. You just need to give your brain a break from thinking about it.", "annotation_id": "40785376", "url": "https://genius.com/40785376", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Go Out Tonight", "line": "I think you should just get dressed and go out tonight", "vault_lines": ["I think you should just get dressed and go out tonight", "Go out tonight, yeah", "And go out tonight, go out tonight"], "meaning": "Sometimes healing begins before you feel healed. You do not necessarily wait until you want to go out. You get dressed first, then give yourself the chance to feel differently.", "annotation_id": "40785361", "url": "https://genius.com/40785361", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Go Out Tonight", "line": "I mean, I understand the pain", "vault_lines": ["I mean, I understand the pain"], "meaning": "Drake doesn’t suggest that healing happened through endlessly analysing the situation. He took some form of action, restored his sense of agency, and then let the situation become something in the past.\n\nThere is also an important distinction between processing pain and living inside it. You can acknowledge what happened without allowing the person who hurt you to continue occupying your mind indefinitely", "annotation_id": "40785352", "url": "https://genius.com/40785352", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Go Out Tonight", "line": "Oh, you don’t need that girl, she did it all wrong You was still you ’fore she ever came along", "vault_lines": ["Oh, you don't need that girl, she did it all wrong", "You was still you 'fore she ever came along"], "meaning": "Heartbreak can make a person feel as though losing someone means losing part of themselves, but this line challenges that idea: you existed before the relationship, and you are still yourself after it.", "annotation_id": "40785333", "url": "https://genius.com/40785333", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Go Out Tonight", "line": "Boy this house is way too clean (Way too clean) I don’t think there’s nothing more to do", "vault_lines": ["Boy this house is way too clean (Way too clean)", "I don't think there's nothing more to do", "Do, do, do, do, do, do"], "meaning": "There is literally nothing left to occupy the person: the chores are finished, the house is clean, and yet they continue to stay inside. The line suggests that sometimes the problem is not that we have nothing to do, but that we are using “nothing to do” as a reason not to move forward.", "annotation_id": "40785314", "url": "https://genius.com/40785314", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Go Out Tonight", "line": "You’ve been home for three whole days Actin’ like you got chores to do Ha-ha-ha, yeah", "vault_lines": ["You've been home for three whole days", "Actin' like you got chores to do", "Do, do, do, do, do, do"], "meaning": "Drake opens the song by immediately identifying the problem: heartbreak has turned staying home into a routine. The person is behaving as though there is always some task keeping them inside, but the implication is that the chores are merely an excuse. They are not really busy but instead they are avoiding the outside world.", "annotation_id": "40785300", "url": "https://genius.com/40785300", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Go Out Tonight", "status": "done", "targets": 8, "clicked": 8, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-go-out-tonight-lyrics", "genius_title": "Go Out Tonight"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Ones Go (Interlude)", "line": "[Verse 1: Drake]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "In this song (and especially this verse), Drizzy hit’s up a girl the summer before he released Take Care. He’s explaining to her the reasons why he had to make the moves he has in order to become the independent, well-off individual he is today. And that especially as Take Care builds hype/is released, he will become more independent and prosperous.\n\n\n\nAlthough he’s changed financially, he still wants to confirm that his personality hasn’t changed for the worse, and that this girl will still love him even after the time they have been and will be apart.", "annotation_id": "1721938", "url": "https://genius.com/1721938", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Ones Go (Interlude)", "line": "Summer’s mine", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake has a girl named summer. He references her in multiple songs. Nobody knows exactly who she is, but she has also been talked about by J. Cole.\n\nDrake’s quotes about Summer:\n\n\nWhen I got Summer a Michael Kors on my momma’s debit\n\nSummer is comin know you could feel it\n\n\nJ. Cole quotes about Summer:\n\n\nJust to say a few words to this bitch named Summer June will make four years since I gave you my number\n\nA year later Drake put his key in your ignition\n\n\nClearly this girl summer has been around, but nobody really knows who she is.", "annotation_id": "1439723", "url": "https://genius.com/1439723", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Ones Go (Interlude)", "line": "But the good ones go The good ones go if you wait too long But the good ones go The good ones go if you wait too long So you should go You should go, before you stay too long", "vault_lines": ["But the good ones go", "The good ones go if you wait too long", "So you should go", "You should go, before you stay too long"], "meaning": "He’s implying that a good partner who waits on a commitment in a relationship eventually leaves if the commitment takes to long to arrive.\n\nIn this case Drake is talking about the girl whom he wants to wait on him after his current life style comes to an end\n\nShe’ll be waiting for a very loooong time\n\nThe “you should go, before you stay too long” part is saying that she should focus on finding another man before she spends too much time trying to keep a relationship with drake. Eventually she’ll realize she’s wasted her time and all the “good ones” are taken.\n\nThe good ones go if you wait too long, meaning the good girls won’t stick around waiting for him to make a serious commitment.\n\nSo she should go before she stays too long and misses out on all the good men who would treat her better than Drake could.", "annotation_id": "576348", "url": "https://genius.com/576348", "state": "accepted", "votes": 148, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Ones Go (Interlude)", "line": "I swear I said it about a hundred times, I’ma need it back", "vault_lines": ["I swear I said it about a hundred times, I'ma need it back"], "meaning": "This line is a continuation of the last line spoken in Cameras (the previous song). During the outro Drake says,\n\nJust mail me my ring back, can’t keep that shit…\n\nDrake proposed to one of his lovers in the past, but somewhere along the way their plans fell through. He’s asked the girl for his ring back 100 times now, but she refuses to give it back to him.\n\nThere are a couple of other ways to interpret this line. Both ways interpret it as a continuation to the first line in this song:\n\n\nDrake took a vacation after Thank Me Later dropped and people thought he had fell off. Drake is telling the new rappers who have been trying to take his spot (on the radio stations & in the clubs) that he needs it back.\nHe’s looking to take a break from the girl he’s been dating. He wants his summer “back” so that he can do his own thing.", "annotation_id": "576301", "url": "https://genius.com/576301", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Ones Go (Interlude)", "line": "I shouldn’t be much longer But you shouldn’t have to wait Can’t lose you, can’t help it I’m so sorry, I’m so selfish", "vault_lines": ["I shouldn't be much longer", "But you shouldn't have to wait", "Can't lose you, can't help it", "I'm so sorry, I'm so selfish"], "meaning": "He’s alluded to diving into acting after this album and even signed with a top agency recently, so I guess she really won’t have to wait much longer for him to come around.\n\nHe’s telling her he’s almost done, and they get back to where they once was. He’s selfish because he can’t have her right now, but he doesn’t want anyone else to have her either\n\nDrake is saying that it shouldn’t take too much longer for him to get his self together and prepared to be in a committed relationship with her but she shouldn’t have to wait for him. Drake does not want to lose this woman, but he’s only thinking about himself and not how it affect her and that’s why he’s apologizing and saying he’s selfish", "annotation_id": "477523", "url": "https://genius.com/477523", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Ones Go (Interlude)", "line": "But don’t you go getting married Don’t you go get engaged I know you’re getting older Don’t have no time to waste", "vault_lines": ["But don't you go getting married", "Don't you go get engaged", "I know you're getting older", "Don't have no time to waste", "But you shouldn't have to wait"], "meaning": "Although he is working on himself right now, he doesn’t want the old fling to completely move on. She’s getting older, and when women get older they start to ponder and want marriage and what not. Drake doesn’t want her to move on.\n\nalthough Drake wants the best for her, and wants her to be happy, he also still has feelings for her and he’s not ready to give her up completely. The girl is getting older and she doesn’t want to waste her time waiting for something that may never happen\n\nThis also shows the selfish side of Drake. He wants to keep her for himself, while not being around.", "annotation_id": "477518", "url": "https://genius.com/477518", "state": "accepted", "votes": 56, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Ones Go (Interlude)", "line": "Uh, uh, I’ve been chillin’ in the city where the money’s thrown high and the girls get down In case you started to wonder why my new shit’s sounding so H-Town", "vault_lines": ["Uh, uh, I've been chillin' in the city where the money's thrown high and the girls get down", "In case you started to wonder why my new shit's sounding so H-Town"], "meaning": "Drake’s new style has been influenced greatly by Houston’s famed rap scene, especially the Screwed Up Click and UGK.\n\nHis shit will sound even more H-Town soon – he is releasing a special OG Ron C edition of the Take Care album – i.e., the album will be “chopped and screwed”.\n\nRon is a legendary H-Town mixtape DJ who co-founded Swishahouse Records and was one of the first people, along with DJ Screw, to do the now-famous “chopped and screwed” mixes of songs.  Here’s a link to “Headlines” chopped and screwed by Ron.\n\nHe’s also referring to his and 40’s love of R&B music. The group “H-Town” shares the same name as the nickname of Houston, his favorite city (outside of Toronto, of course). Double entendre swag.", "annotation_id": "440951", "url": "https://genius.com/440951", "state": "accepted", "votes": 56, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Ones Go (Interlude)", "status": "done", "targets": 7, "clicked": 7, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-good-ones-go-interlude-lyrics", "genius_title": "Good Ones Go (Interlude)"}
