{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Peak", "line": "That’s just a view from a cheap seat They don’t want problems with me", "vault_lines": ["That's just a view from a cheap seat", "They don't want problems with me"], "meaning": "This metaphor, ‘a view from a cheap seat,’ is used to describe someone’s point of view when they are not directly involved in a situation, but wish to politely comment on it anyway, in the sense that they don’t want to directly oppose Drake’s views, but make a sort of passing comment.", "annotation_id": "19326295", "url": "https://genius.com/19326295", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Peak", "line": "Where are all your good manners? Reply with pleasantries", "vault_lines": ["Where are all your good manners?"], "meaning": "A common stereotype is that English women act proper, and have good manners. As stated in the line before, Drake’s girl doesn’t have the “good manners” that she’s expected to have as an English woman.", "annotation_id": "14890738", "url": "https://genius.com/14890738", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Peak", "line": "People are only as tough as their phone allows them to be", "vault_lines": ["People are only as tough as their phone allows them to be"], "meaning": "On July 21st, 2015, Meek Mill accused Drake of having a ghostwriter, more specifically on his track “R.I.C.O.” which featured Drake and posted the following tweet:\n\n\n\nMore of Meek Mill’s tweets directed at Drake pertaining to him having a ghostwriter can be viewed here and a timeline of Drake and Meek Mill’s beef can be viewed here.\n\nDrake fired back at Meek Mill shortly after with his track “Charged Up” and followed this up by releasing a second diss titled “Back to Back”. It’s in this track Drake spits\n\nYeah, trigger fingers turn to Twitter fingers\nYeah, you gettin' bodied by a singin' nigga\nI’m not the type of nigga that’ll type to niggas\"\n\nAs Twitter is commonly accessed via a mobile device, Drake is saying people aren’t anywhere as tough in person as they are behind their phones, specifically on social media.", "annotation_id": "14889471", "url": "https://genius.com/14889471", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Peak", "line": "England breeds proper girls", "vault_lines": ["England breeds proper girls"], "meaning": "Drake may be talking about one of his two past lovers in this bar. The first is Jorja Smith, a British R&B singer that he once expressed romantic interest in 2017. She was even featured as part of the More Life playlist when she appeared on “Jorja Interlude”.\n\n\n\nDrake could also be referring to RAYE, the second of two English singers with whom Drizzy had something more than just an “one-off fling”.", "annotation_id": "14887588", "url": "https://genius.com/14887588", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Peak", "line": "Talk used to be cheap; nowadays, it’s free", "vault_lines": ["Talk used to be cheap; nowadays, it's free"], "meaning": "Drake allegedly was supposed to drop a song with Aaliyah that was called “Talk Is Cheap” and  he had even teased a video about it while on tour but fans never got that song.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Zz8lpQ3unbo", "annotation_id": "14882257", "url": "https://genius.com/14882257", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Peak", "line": "Piquing my interest She got peak like Montana", "vault_lines": ["She got peak like Montana"], "meaning": "“Piquing your interest” means to arouse, stimulate, or excite someone, subsequently gaining one’s attention. Drizzy compares a girl with a curvaceous body to a Montana Peak, a style of cowboy hat named after the mountainous State of Montana.\n\nFurthermore, ‘peak’ is also London slang to express a very serious, bad, or unfortunate situation. By saying that “she got peak,” Drake could be implying that his relationship with the girl changed for the worse.", "annotation_id": "14876739", "url": "https://genius.com/14876739", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Peak", "line": "Treat you like princess Rest in heaven, Diana", "vault_lines": ["Treat you like princess", "Rest in heaven, Diana"], "meaning": "Diana, The Princess of Wales, died on August 31st, 1997 due to injuries she sustained from a car crash while in Paris.\n\n\n\nShe was well known for using her fame to fight multiple causes such as AIDS/HIV-related causes, as well as bringing the royal family closer to the people of England.", "annotation_id": "14876522", "url": "https://genius.com/14876522", "state": "accepted", "votes": 69, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
