{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Supermax", "line": "It’s still “Heartbreak Drake,” but I glued it together", "vault_lines": ["It's still \"Heartbreak Drake,\" but I glued it together"], "meaning": "The Heartbreak Drake series consists of unofficial, bootleg mixtapes released by third-party DJs (most notably DJ Ill Will, DJ Rampage, and DJ Rockstar) around 2009. They were not official projects released by Drake.", "annotation_id": "40392984", "url": "https://genius.com/40392984", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Supermax", "line": "I’m big tired of fake love like tractor wheels", "vault_lines": ["I'm big tired of fake love like tractor wheels"], "meaning": "Drake’s always mentioned his frustration with people showing Fake Love to him but this lyric in particular is a clever double entendre. Big tired like tractor wheels because tractors are known for having huge tires.", "annotation_id": "39005878", "url": "https://genius.com/39005878", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Supermax", "line": "Do not come around the guys playin’ peacemaker They snaked me for now, but we’ll see later", "vault_lines": ["Do not come around the guys playin' peacemaker", "They snaked me for now, but we'll see later", "They snaked me for now, but we will see later"], "meaning": "These lines can be seen as a sneak diss to multiple rappers, including Future, Rick Ross, and J. Cole.\n\nFuture was one of the main characters in the beef, dropping two separate albums dissing Drake with Metro Boomin. After the dust has settled, Young Thug has posted on Twitter a call-out for peace between Future, Metro Boomin, and Drake, which Future reposted on his page.\n\nRick Ross was also dissing Drake on his diss song “Champange Moments” and claimed earlier this year that he’s open to squash the beef with Drake.\n\nAlthough J. Cole is naturaly fitting this category after dropping out from the beef with Kendrick Lamar and calling for peace in his song “Port Antonio”, this is less likely to be towards him since Drake liked his IG post on “Port Antonio” and is still following him on social media.", "annotation_id": "36200467", "url": "https://genius.com/36200467", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Supermax", "line": "Family only feels like a riddle to affiliates that thought that they were safe because they played the middle", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake is saying that people who are on the outskirts of his circle (affiliates) often don’t understand the depth or complexity of loyalty (“family”), especially when they try to remain neutral during conflict. They may think neutrality protects them, but in reality, not choosing a side can be seen as disloyal, and therefore they’re not as safe as they believe.", "annotation_id": "36154205", "url": "https://genius.com/36154205", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Supermax", "line": "Losin’ all these friends really got to me, I was talkin’ to Taylor over drinks, and it was gettin’ deep “Not everyone can handle this pressure and, in your city, you’re the national treasure,” that’s what she said to me", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The Boy is talking about a conversation he had with Taylor Rooks, an American sports journalist who is pretty close to him. She appeared in the music video of Jack Harlow’s “Churchill Downs”\nfeaturing Drake.\n\n\n\nDrake is referencing his longtime collaborators, who he considered like friends, that turned on him during his publicized feud with Kendrick Lamar.\n\nShe confirmed it via her Instagram story by sharing a screenshot of Drake’s livestream, ICEMAN EPISODE 1 with the caption “That’s what she said to me.”", "annotation_id": "36134810", "url": "https://genius.com/36134810", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Supermax", "status": "done", "targets": 5, "clicked": 5, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-supermax-lyrics", "genius_title": "Supermax"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "1Xtra Freestyle", "line": "I’m what Lebron was to Saint Vincent, Saint Marry", "vault_lines": ["I'm what Lebron was to Saint Vincent, Saint Marry"], "meaning": "Legendary basketball player LeBron James who is recognized as one of the greatest players in the NBA, used to study at the St. Vincent-St. Mary High School which is located in Ohio.\n\nIn 2017, LeBron donated a million dollars to his old school as a thank you to the school for his childhood.", "annotation_id": "22533250", "url": "https://genius.com/22533250", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "1Xtra Freestyle", "line": "I’m to fly, I keep it hip hop like Afu-Ra", "vault_lines": ["I'm to fly, I keep it hip hop like Afu-Ra"], "meaning": "Aaron Phillip, also known as Afu-Ra, is an American rapper from New York City.\n\nAfu-Ra made a song called “Hip Hop” and Drake is referring to that song.", "annotation_id": "22533005", "url": "https://genius.com/22533005", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "1Xtra Freestyle", "line": "Who else really trying to mess with Hollywood Cole I’m with Marley G though Treating Birmingham just like my Hollywood shows I’m trying to tell you something that you probably should know This that Slum Dog Millionaire Bollywood flow and uh My real friends never hearing from me Fake friends write the wrong answers on the mirror for me That’s why I pick and choose, I don’t get shit confused I got a small circle, I’m not with different crews We walk the same path, but got on different shoes Live in the same building, but we got different views I got a couple cars, I never get to lose Don’t like my women single, I like my chicks in twos And these days all the girls are down to roll We hit the strip club, and all them girls find a pole", "vault_lines": ["Who else really trying to mess with Hollywood Cole", "I'm with Marley G though", "Treating Birmingham just like my Hollywood shows", "I'm trying to tell you something that you probably should know", "And tell me today's weather"], "meaning": "This portion would later be recycled in his verse on Lil Wayne’s song, “Right Above It.” Check out the annotations here!", "annotation_id": "3407564", "url": "https://genius.com/3407564", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "1Xtra Freestyle", "line": "You know what it is, Drake and Tim Westwood", "vault_lines": ["You know what it is, Drake and Tim Westwood"], "meaning": "Tim Westwood is an English DJ and presenter of radio and television who has had a show for years on BBC Radio 1 and Radio 1 xtra.", "annotation_id": "3171965", "url": "https://genius.com/3171965", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
