{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "A Little Favour (GQ Freestyle)", "line": "Drizzy Drake, the only one that got the gift without the curse", "vault_lines": ["Drizzy Drake, the only one that got the gift without the curse"], "meaning": "Drake might be speaking on the infamous sophomore slump (jinx), wherein a musician’s second album fails to overcome their first in terms of strength. Drake had the opposite, you might say, as Take Care is near universally said to be superior to his debut Thank Me Later.\n\n\n\nHe’s also playing on the title of Jay-Z’s seventh album, The Blueprint 2. BP2 is a double album. The first album, The Gift tended to be more lively, while the second, The Curse was darker and more diss-laden.\n\nThus, Drake has the talent (gift), without any negative consequences (curse).", "annotation_id": "648444", "url": "https://genius.com/648444", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "A Little Favour (GQ Freestyle)", "line": "Ain’t ashamed to admit it, I be the same with it This shit is all about hits and misses", "vault_lines": ["Ain't ashamed to admit it, I be the same with it", "This shit is all about hits and misses"], "meaning": "Drake spends a lot of time talking about his challenges as well as his triumphs, whether it’s with women, his career, or his family. This is an extension of an idea he’s touched on before—\"I learned working with the negatives could make for better pictures\" from “HYFR”.", "annotation_id": "648440", "url": "https://genius.com/648440", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "A Little Favour (GQ Freestyle)", "line": "Young Frank,", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "He’s comparing himself to Frank Sinatra. He had a VMA promo and performance with MTV a while ago with this theme, http://youtu.be/DFlr_I6mkyo", "annotation_id": "648392", "url": "https://genius.com/648392", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "A Little Favour (GQ Freestyle)", "line": "Just got a couple Warhol’s for my hallways", "vault_lines": ["Just got a couple Warhol’s for my hallways"], "meaning": "Andy Warhol is a famous artist, credited for inventing Pop Art. With his paintings selling for tens of thousands of dollars, you have ‘ballin to get your hands on one!\n\n\n\nHis most expensive piece, Eight Elvises sold for $100,000,000", "annotation_id": "648387", "url": "https://genius.com/648387", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "A Little Favour (GQ Freestyle)", "line": "We all lust for the same women You know the ones we saw before we came in it", "vault_lines": ["We all lust for the same women", "You know the ones we saw before we came in it"], "meaning": "Drake is saying all rappers lust for the girls from back in their hood more than likely the ones they couldnt have back when they weren’t famous\n\nHe could still be talking about Rihanna here. Drake said in an interview that he was in a club in Toronto when she was there to shoot her first music video – “Pon De Replay”.", "annotation_id": "648218", "url": "https://genius.com/648218", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
