{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Circadian Rhythm", "line": "Writin’ they names on a list, baby", "vault_lines": ["Writin' they names on a list, baby"], "meaning": "This may allude to drake writing the names of the people who have turned on him and sided with Kendrick.", "annotation_id": "32883398", "url": "https://genius.com/32883398", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Circadian Rhythm", "line": "How many doors did they shut? How many feathers they pluck?", "vault_lines": ["How many doors did they shut? How many feathers they pluck?"], "meaning": "Here, Drake references his ability to capitalize on opportunity, and specifically references the weakness of people who don’t possess the ability.  By asking “How many doors they done shut?” Drake is referencing the fact that others do not have the ability to “walk through the door” or access these opportunities, which he possesses and uses as a way to show his superiority.  In a similar way, when he raps, “How many feathers they pluck?” he references a person’s inability to “fly” or capitalize on their opportunities, therefore suggesting they have less than him.  When a bird’s feathers are plucked, they’re unable to fly and therefore can’t run away and explore or grow.", "annotation_id": "32870320", "url": "https://genius.com/32870320", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Circadian Rhythm", "line": "Plug you in, now you lit, I pulled the plug, now you stuck", "vault_lines": ["Plug you in, now you lit, I pulled the plug, now you stuck"], "meaning": "“Plug you in, now you lit”: This suggests that Drake helped someone gain financial support, a luxury lifestyle or fame making them “lit,”. Pulling the plug indicates that Drake, after a breakup or fall-off took away that support.\n\nIts a line to affirm his god-line status with everyone around him depending on his power and affluence.", "annotation_id": "32866591", "url": "https://genius.com/32866591", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Circadian Rhythm", "line": "Shout to Machine, he a Wick, baby", "vault_lines": ["Shout to Machine, he a Wick, baby"], "meaning": "John Wick is an fictional movie character in the John Wick -movie series. In the movies, Wick serves as an agent with much experience in shooting.\n\nDrake shoutouts Machine, most likely referencing Toronto artist Pressa, who at one point went by the name Press Machine also adding that he’s as experienced a shooter as John Wick.", "annotation_id": "32793564", "url": "https://genius.com/32793564", "state": "pending", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Circadian Rhythm", "line": "Wanna turn you to a housewife and you never had to clean a dish, baby", "vault_lines": ["Wanna turn you to a housewife and you never had to clean a dish, baby"], "meaning": "In this line , Drake is promising his lady that if she were to marry him , she would be a housewife meaning she would not need to work .\n\nShe would stay at home and on top of that , she wouldn’t even need to do the house chores (which is common of housewives , but certainly not Drake’s housewife …)", "annotation_id": "32784650", "url": "https://genius.com/32784650", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Circadian Rhythm", "line": "Go invisible ink on them pics, baby", "vault_lines": ["Go invisible ink on them pics, baby"], "meaning": "When explicit images are sent through iMessage, senders often conceal them using the “invisible ink” effect, which covers the images with a layer of white dots and a blur until the recipient swipes to reveal the image.\n\nIn this line, Drake is asking the girl he calls “baby” in this verse to send explicit images of herself using the “invisible ink” effect, hence the phrase “Go[ing] invisible ink on them pics\".", "annotation_id": "32772390", "url": "https://genius.com/32772390", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Circadian Rhythm", "line": "Rap game like my sleepin’ pattern ’cause how the fuck I’m still up?", "vault_lines": ["How the fuck I'm still up?", "Rap game like my sleepin' pattern 'cause how the fuck I'm still up?"], "meaning": "Drake is referring to the 20v1 rap beef with Kendrick Lamar where they tried to “eliminate” him. He is asking how is he still successfully at the top of the rap game when they tried to eliminate him and label him things such as ‘a pedophile’.", "annotation_id": "32768523", "url": "https://genius.com/32768523", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Circadian Rhythm", "line": "Yeah, niggas don’t speak my language Niggas don’t speak my language Niggas don’t speak my language, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Niggas don't speak my language", "Niggas don't speak my language, yeah", "Yeah, niggas don't speak my language"], "meaning": "While this is not a direct shot at K-Dot, this could be taken as a subtle diss to the perceived difference in popularity between the two. Evidence of this can be found through K-Dot’s line in Euphoria where it reads, “I don’t wanna talk on no celly, huh, You know I got language barriers, huh It’s no accent you can sell me, huh.” To play off this, Drake is telling Kendrick that he’s right, they don’t speak the same language or are in the same conversations because Drake is on a way higher level doing way higher bigger and better things.", "annotation_id": "32758265", "url": "https://genius.com/32758265", "state": "pending", "votes": 36, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Circadian Rhythm", "line": "Rap game like my sleepin’ pattern ’cause how the fuck I’m still up?", "vault_lines": ["How the fuck I'm still up?", "Rap game like my sleepin' pattern 'cause how the fuck I'm still up?"], "meaning": "This is a play on words, Drake say rapping game like his sleeping pattern\n\nwhich are supposed to make him sleep but still up,  the up references to him being on the top for 15 years and over.\n\nSo basically is also saying that even if he is goes to sleep which means taking a break that you will still be on top of the game.", "annotation_id": "32755558", "url": "https://genius.com/32755558", "state": "pending", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Circadian Rhythm", "line": "How many funeral dates they plan for me and I dodged it like the truck? Yeah", "vault_lines": ["How many funeral dates they plan for me and I dodged it like the truck? Yeah"], "meaning": "This might be a reference to the beef , having Drake standing alone while facing numbers or rappers who were his friends before they switched sides.\n\nDrake has also say something similar in an unreleased song titled “piece of me \"where he said\n\"the plan a go away party for me every year but you know they gon still cancel it”", "annotation_id": "32755522", "url": "https://genius.com/32755522", "state": "pending", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
