{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Feel No Ways", "line": "I should be downtown, whipping on the way to you You got something that belongs to me", "vault_lines": ["I should be downtown, whipping on the way to you", "You got something that belongs to me"], "meaning": "Drake says he should be finding his way back to her because she got something that belongs to him… “His heart”", "annotation_id": "26969505", "url": "https://genius.com/26969505", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Feel No Ways", "line": "World’s, world’s, world’s famous World’s, world’s, world’s famous", "vault_lines": ["World's, world's, world's famous"], "meaning": "This sample is from the late Malcolm McLaren’s 1983 song, “Worlds Famous.”\nhttps://youtu.be/4aA0vDAwQls?t=160\n\nMcLaren was a major player in the UK punk scene as manager of the Sex Pistols.  He claimed to have orchestrated the aesthetic and commercial rise of the band,  which is disputed by its members. Sometime in 1980, Afrika Bambataa took him to a South Bronx block party and introduced him to hip-hop. He immediately saw a parallel between punk and hip-hop:  “I always thought hip-hop was the black punk rock. It had similar DIY aspects.” McClaren went on to release several hip-hop records and is credited as being one of the first proponents of the genre in the UK.", "annotation_id": "9088986", "url": "https://genius.com/9088986", "state": "accepted", "votes": 66, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Feel No Ways", "line": "World’s, world’s, world’s famous World’s, world’s, world’s famous", "vault_lines": ["World's, world's, world's famous"], "meaning": "This sample is from the late Malcolm McLaren’s 1983 song, “Worlds Famous.”\nhttps://youtu.be/4aA0vDAwQls?t=160\n\nMcLaren was a major player in the UK punk scene as manager of the Sex Pistols.  He claimed to have orchestrated both the entire aesthetic and the commercial rise of the band,  which is disputed by its members. Sometime in 1980, Afrika Bambaataa took him to a South Bronx block party and introduced him to hip-hop. He immediately saw a parallel between punk and hip-hop:  “I always thought hip-hop was the black punk rock. It had similar DIY aspects.” McClaren went on to release several hip-hop records and is credited as being one of the first proponents of the genre in the UK.", "annotation_id": "9088912", "url": "https://genius.com/9088912", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Feel No Ways", "line": "Your body language says it all Despite the things you said to me", "vault_lines": ["Your body language says it all", "Despite the things you said to me"], "meaning": "Body language encompasses any physical form of communication, from hand gestures to eye contact. Most of our communication stems from these nonverbal cues, thought to comprise up to 55% of our conversations.\n\nDrake is well experienced with his partners anatomy. Her true feelings are different than what she’s communicating to him in words.", "annotation_id": "9074579", "url": "https://genius.com/9074579", "state": "accepted", "votes": 51, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Feel No Ways", "line": "I tried with you There’s more to life than sleeping in and getting high with you I had to let go of us to show myself what I could do", "vault_lines": ["There's more to life than sleeping in and getting high with you", "I had to let go of us to show myself what I could do", "I tried with you"], "meaning": "While Drake put in a valiant effort for this relationship, he feels like they could never last. As an ambitious man, he wanted to get out and prove to himself what he accomplish.\n\n\n\nHowever, this girl just wanted to lay up in bed, smoke weed, and cuddle with Drake. He feels like she was holding him back and be needed change in his life to stay interested.\n\nDrake expressed a similar fear of complacency on “Too Much”:\n\nMost people in my position get complacent\nWanna come places with star girls, and they end up on them front pages", "annotation_id": "9072499", "url": "https://genius.com/9072499", "state": "accepted", "votes": 37, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Feel No Ways", "line": "[Produced By Jordan Ullman]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Jordan Ullman is one half of the Canadian R&B duo and OVO-signed production group Majid Jordan. Their first major hit was 2013’s “Hold On, We’re Going Home,” which they coproduced and contributed vocals to. Jordan handles the production side of the duo, while Majid contributes vocals.", "annotation_id": "9072048", "url": "https://genius.com/9072048", "state": "accepted", "votes": 88, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Feel No Ways", "line": "Feel a way, feel a way, young nigga feel a way I’ve stopped listenin’ to things you say ’Cause you don’t mean it anyway (Yeah) Feel a way, feel a way, young nigga feel a way", "vault_lines": ["Feel a way, feel a way, young nigga feel a way", "I've stopped listenin' to things you say", "'Cause you don't mean it anyway (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Drake had to let go of his girl to pursue his career, and now her words are making him feel guilty. She’s making him feel some type of way: guilty, sad, regretful.\n\n Drake’s invoking Rich Homie Quan’s “Type of Way.” Quan’s track exemplifies the many types of feelings this term can signify—love, jealousy, excitement. Making someone feel “a type of way” is a versatile term. Drake’s type of way describes his feelings about a love gone sour.\n\nBack in 2013, Drake almost lent to a verse to “Type of Way” but ended up hopping on “Versace” by Migos instead. He told MTV that he regrets not being on both:\n\nThat record is the song of the summer. I regret not getting on it…I wish I would’ve written that record. That’s Toronto talk—you feel a type of way, that’s our lingo, so I should’ve probably been involved in that.", "annotation_id": "9072003", "url": "https://genius.com/9072003", "state": "accepted", "votes": 89, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Feel No Ways", "line": "And that just didn’t sit right with you, yeah [Chorus] And now you’re tryna make me feel a way, on purpose Now you’re throwing it back in my face, on purpose Now you’re talking down on my name (Ah), on purpose, yeah And you don’t feel no way, you think I deserve it", "vault_lines": ["And that just didn't sit right with you, yeah", "And now you're tryna make me feel a way, on purpose", "Now you're throwing it back in my face, on purpose", "Now you're talking down on my name (Ah), on purpose, yeah", "And you don't feel no way, you think I deserve it", "Feel a way, feel a way, young nigga feel a way", "I tried with you"], "meaning": "Drake tried to make thing work, but couldn’t keep the relationship going. Now this girl is gassed and is slandering Drake all over town. A far cry from “Uptown,” in which the girl in question was in a rush to tell her friends about his impending success.\n\nBy making Drake feel guilty about choosing his career over his relationship, he claims she is missing the point. She’s trying to make him feel bad for chasing his dreams, when her guilt trip is the only truly negative reaction in the scenario.", "annotation_id": "9071077", "url": "https://genius.com/9071077", "state": "accepted", "votes": 108, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Feel No Ways", "line": "Who is it that’s got you all gassed up? (Yeah) Changin’ your opinion on me", "vault_lines": ["Who is it that's got you all gassed up? (Yeah)", "Changin' your opinion on me"], "meaning": "“Gassed up” means a person has been riled or manipulated to feel a certain way about a situation. “Gassed up” can mean someone’s hyped you up unrealistically, making you feel better than you actually are. Perhaps Drake’s girlfriend thinks she’s too good for Drake.\n\nDrake’s girl has been listening to her friends, and it seems where they were once excited by their relationship, they’re now unsure.\n\nIt’s possible his alleged DM'ing of porn star Mia Khalifa has something to do with this, and with his dating history plastered all over the internet, this girl might just be gassed up from rumor reports.", "annotation_id": "9071052", "url": "https://genius.com/9071052", "state": "accepted", "votes": 48, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Feel No Ways", "line": "I tried with you There’s more to life than sleeping in and getting high with you I had to let go of us to show myself what I could do", "vault_lines": ["There's more to life than sleeping in and getting high with you", "I had to let go of us to show myself what I could do", "I tried with you"], "meaning": "A throwback to the message on “Karaoke” off Drake’s first record, where he lamented the death of a relationship due to his desire to forge a rap career.\n\nThings have been so crazy and hectic\nI shoulda gotten back by now\nBut you know how much I wanted to make it\nIt’s probably better anyhow\nSo if you gotta go\nIf there’s anything I should know\nIf the spotlight makes you nervous\nIf you’re looking for a purpose\n\nOn this occasion it appears Drake tried significantly harder, but being stuck sleeping and getting high with her has diminished his work capacity. Although he hates sleeping alone, sleeping in is just less time to create music, to tour, to promote himself. To reach his full potential he requires no strings attached.", "annotation_id": "9070108", "url": "https://genius.com/9070108", "state": "accepted", "votes": 86, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Feel No Ways", "line": "I was only gone for the last few months But you don’t have the time to wait on me", "vault_lines": ["I was only gone for the last few months", "But you don't have the time to wait on me"], "meaning": "2015 was one of Drake’s busiest years, as he released two projects and toured heavily. He’s been seemingly on the go since “Karaoke,” in 2010, right up to “Hotline Bling” in 2015. So, the “last few months” could be read as the “last 6 years.”\n\nLuckily, he’s still found time for new love though.", "annotation_id": "9070082", "url": "https://genius.com/9070082", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
