{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Paris Morton Music", "line": "Who just had his linen suit dry-cleaned", "vault_lines": ["Who just had his linen suit dry-cleaned"], "meaning": "Can refer to his dad who is famous for his linen suits like on “You and the 6”.", "annotation_id": "40571755", "url": "https://genius.com/40571755", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Paris Morton Music", "line": "Hope you forgive me, never meant wrong Tried to be patient but waited too long But I would’ve came back, but I would’ve came back for you Would’ve came back, would’ve came back", "vault_lines": ["Would've came back for you, I just needed time", "Hope you forgive me, never meant wrong", "Tried to be patient but waited too long", "But I would've came back, but I would've came back for you"], "meaning": "Drake hopes the girl forgives him even though he is taking a while and he is insinuating that he would’ve came back as he might think it’s too late or she is tired of waiting", "annotation_id": "38970000", "url": "https://genius.com/38970000", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Paris Morton Music", "line": "And girls counting on me to be there like missing rubbers", "vault_lines": ["And girls counting on me to be there like missing rubbers"], "meaning": "Drake uses “missing rubbers” as a metaphor for situations where protection fails, suggesting that women count on him to step up and be reliable when things go wrong. The line emphasizes the pressure and responsibility placed on him in messy, unplanned situations.", "annotation_id": "38449888", "url": "https://genius.com/38449888", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Paris Morton Music", "line": "Or are you too scared to tell me that you met me And fear that I won’t remember?", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake reflects on how fame creates emotional distance, forcing him to “re-meet” people he already knows because they’re afraid he won’t remember them. He expresses insecurity and a desire to be accepted as his real self, not just as a celebrity.", "annotation_id": "38449860", "url": "https://genius.com/38449860", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Paris Morton Music", "line": "I’m urging all daughters to kiss their mothers With those lips that all that lipstick covers", "vault_lines": ["I'm urging all daughters to kiss their mothers"], "meaning": "Drake uses the lipstick as a symbol of adult identity and sexuality, reminding women that no matter how grown or glamorous they become, they’re still daughters. He’s saying maturity shouldn’t erase affection or closeness with your mother.", "annotation_id": "38449850", "url": "https://genius.com/38449850", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Paris Morton Music", "line": "But trust me, I still deliver like a midwife", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake uses some insane worplay in this verse. In the 17th century Europe, midwifes had the duty of delivering babies, and breastfeeding for Nobles, since they believed the practice of delivering babies and breastfeeding were below them.", "annotation_id": "33996765", "url": "https://genius.com/33996765", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Paris Morton Music", "line": "Reintroduced to people I’ve been introduced to Did you forget me?", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake is expressing that he feels overlooked / forgotten its a way of showing he feels undervalued", "annotation_id": "33455488", "url": "https://genius.com/33455488", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Paris Morton Music", "line": "I talk slicker than a pimp from Augusta", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake is probably cross referencing this add\n\nhttps://m.youtube.com/watch?v=s19GKC4s9d4", "annotation_id": "29645109", "url": "https://genius.com/29645109", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
