{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Slow It Down", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-slow-it-down-lyrics", "genius_title": "Slow It Down"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SNL: Bar Mitzvah in 1999", "line": "Daddy from Africa", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "His father, Dennis Graham, is of African descent. He has helped shaped Drake’s life. From phone calls and other recordings, Dennis has influenced Drake many of times. However, their relationship wasn’t always like this.", "annotation_id": "2693155", "url": "https://genius.com/2693155", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SNL: Bar Mitzvah in 1999", "line": "Best of worlds when you’re Jewish with black in ya", "vault_lines": ["Best of worlds when you're Jewish with black in ya"], "meaning": "In a sense, yes, this is a great combination of genes in life.\n\nAs a Jewish male, you will become a man at the early age of thirteen. As celebration, you will have a party called a Bar Mitzvah. You receive money among other gifts from your relatives and friends. This sets up for a great financial foundation. You may have heard of Drake’s a few times. He even re-did it and dedicated a music video to it. Also, many Jewish people have connections to people in high places, but this is not always the case.\n\nAs an African-American male, you are brought up in a sense of taking respectability, being independent, self-determination, and much more. You embrace culture and the history of your ancestors. Another thing is that they are widely known being talented individuals in the fields of sports and music.\n\n\n\nThe two races are more similar than most. The two both went through intense struggles of bondage and oppression. Hanukkah resembles Kwanzaa. Both strongly believe in family, loyalty, spiritual, and manhood. However, as a negative, both are highly hated in a historical context.", "annotation_id": "2693122", "url": "https://genius.com/2693122", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SNL: Bar Mitzvah in 1999", "line": "I read the Old Testament,", "vault_lines": ["I read the Old Testament,"], "meaning": "AKA the Torah – the central concept in Jewish tradition.", "annotation_id": "2692825", "url": "https://genius.com/2692825", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SNL: Bar Mitzvah in 1999", "line": "Like Baruch Yitadel Yisrael", "vault_lines": ["Like Baruch Yitadel Yisrael"], "meaning": "A play on words for the beginning of a Jewish prayer, often beginning with “Baruch” and including the word “Yisrael”.", "annotation_id": "2692816", "url": "https://genius.com/2692816", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SNL: Bar Mitzvah in 1999", "line": "At my show, you won’t simply put your hands in the air We can also raise a chair or recite a Jewish prayer", "vault_lines": ["We can also raise a chair or recite a Jewish prayer", "At my show, you won't simply put your hands in the air"], "meaning": "The Hora is a dance, where at bar and bat mitzvahs, the honoree is often raised up on a chair.\n\nIn a concert setting, it’s just another way to crowdsurf.\n\n\n\nDrake is Jewish and proud. He embraces Jewish culture by implying he may recite a traditional Jewish prayer at one of his shows (though that’s unlikely to actually happen).", "annotation_id": "2692813", "url": "https://genius.com/2692813", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SNL: Bar Mitzvah in 1999", "line": "Do not go to Feingold’s, though The pickles are rubber", "vault_lines": ["Do not go to Feingold's, though", "The pickles are rubber"], "meaning": "Looking through both New York and Toronto I can’t find a “Feingold’s Deli”. Although Feingold is a great stereotypical Jewish name, and a perfect name for a deli. Feingold’s sounds like a place that would have great pickles!\n\nA great Dill (or sour, or double sour) pickle has a great crunch and snap when you bite or break it. A rubbery pickle is a sign of an old or poorly made or maintained pickle.\n\n\n\nHate rubbery pickles.", "annotation_id": "2692548", "url": "https://genius.com/2692548", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SNL: Bar Mitzvah in 1999", "line": "I eat Hova with nova, knishes with my bitches A bagel and cream cheesy with my boy, his name is Weezy", "vault_lines": ["I eat Hova with nova, knishes with my bitches", "A bagel and cream cheesy with my boy, his name is Weezy"], "meaning": "I think he swapped the words here by accident. Clearly “Hova” is J-Hova, or Jay-z.  Nova is a cheap version of “Lox”, smoked salmon. Lox is what Jews put on bagels and cream cheese. Nova is lighter tasting than the traditional lox, and much easier to find (it’s almost impossible to find “real” Lox, what you’re eating is “Nova Lox”).\n\nThat Lox goes on top of a bagel with Cream Cheese. Clearly Weezy is Li'l Wayne.\n\n\n\nA knish is bread stuffed with, usually potatoes. There’s other kinds, but the “potato knish\"is the most famous.\n\n\n\nThe way the line is written is what was said, but I think it makes more sense had the words been swapped.See the line later where he clearly says “both of best worlds”.", "annotation_id": "2692504", "url": "https://genius.com/2692504", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SNL: Bar Mitzvah in 1999", "line": "Okra and matzahball, I’ll eat the rest of it", "vault_lines": ["okra and matzahball, I'll eat the rest of it"], "meaning": "Okra is a very common food amongst southern blacks, and matzahballs are very common food for jews.", "annotation_id": "2692297", "url": "https://genius.com/2692297", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SNL: Bar Mitzvah in 1999", "line": "Challah!", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Challah is the best bread out there.\n\nPronounced “Holla”, like “Can I holler at you for a minute”.", "annotation_id": "2692294", "url": "https://genius.com/2692294", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SNL: Bar Mitzvah in 1999", "line": "Chilling in Boca Raton with my mensch, Lenny Kravitz", "vault_lines": ["Chilling in Boca Raton with my mensch, Lenny Kravitz"], "meaning": "Boca Raton is a city in Florida where old Jews go to retire.\n\nhttps://maps.google.com/maps?client=safari&oe=UTF-8&q=boca+raton&ie=UTF-8&hq=&hnear=0x88d923c2ef36fb27:0xd23ea6eeca6095c9,Boca+Raton,+FL&gl=us&ei=z5DcUo6vIZLYoAS_0oLICw&ved=0CJ0BELYD\n\nMensch is the Yiddish word for “a great man”. (Yiddish basically being German-Jewish Ebonics, which came with Jews when they moved to the United States and became the basis of Jewish slang in the US.)\n\nLenny Kravitz is probably the most famous Celebrity who is half-black and half-Jewish. Of course, he had a child with another half-black and half-Jewish Celebrity, Lisa Bonet. That child is Zoe Kravitz, a model and actress, who was rumored to be Drake’s current girlfriend.\nhttp://hellobeautiful.com/2014/01/06/drake-calls-zoe-kravitz-his-everything/", "annotation_id": "2692224", "url": "https://genius.com/2692224", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SNL: Bar Mitzvah in 1999", "line": "I’m black and Jewish Don’t be so foolish I’m black and Jewish It’s a Mitzvah", "vault_lines": ["I'm black and Jewish", "Don't be so foolish", "Please don't forget I'm black, please don't forget I'm Jewish"], "meaning": "This is a great “Black & Jewish” song.\n\nBut don’t forget this one, one of the best!\nhttp://youtu.be/1TXNU1nh4E4\n\nPeople really like rhyming Hannukkah.", "annotation_id": "2692219", "url": "https://genius.com/2692219", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SNL: Bar Mitzvah in 1999", "line": "I play ball like Lebron and I know what a W-2 is", "vault_lines": ["I play ball like Lebron and I know what a W-2 is"], "meaning": "It is a stereotype that all black people are good at basketball, and that those who are white Hispanic or Asian are inferior to their skills.\nSomeone who Drake doesn’t mention is Amar'e Stoudemire a black NBA player who converted to Judaism.\n\n\n\nA W-2 is a type of tax form. This plays into the stereotype that Jews know a lot about money.", "annotation_id": "2691395", "url": "https://genius.com/2691395", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SNL: Bar Mitzvah in 1999", "line": "Birth right in Israel, mama from Canada", "vault_lines": ["Birth right in Israel, mama from Canada"], "meaning": "Birthright is the free trip to Israel Jews in their twenties get in order to experience life in the Holy Land. This helps Jews learn about why Israel is important and develop an affinity for the country. Before the Birthright trips were developed many American Jews, especially young ones who might otherwise not remember the horrors of the Holocaust or direct discrimination in America, were feeling disconnected from Israel. “Birthright” started as a way to combat that, by giving young Jews a guided trip through Israel with no requirement of repayment.", "annotation_id": "2691387", "url": "https://genius.com/2691387", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SNL: Bar Mitzvah in 1999", "line": "I celebrate Hanukkah, dated Rihannakah", "vault_lines": ["I celebrate Hanukkah, dated Rihannakah"], "meaning": "Hanukkah is a Jewish holiday that lasts for 8 days and is usually some time in December. Being Jewish, Drake would naturally celebrate it.\n\n\n\nDrake also dated Rihanna, although the details of their relationship haven’t been clarified all too much.", "annotation_id": "2691372", "url": "https://genius.com/2691372", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SNL: Bar Mitzvah in 1999", "line": "The only purple drink we sip is purple Manischewitz", "vault_lines": ["The only purple drink we sip is purple Manischewitz"], "meaning": "Manischewitz Wine is a winery in New York that specializes in certified Kosher wine, produced under the supervision of the Union of Orthodox Jewish Congregations of America. The wine is handled only by reliable  Mashgichim, who are Rabbis who supervise the process and witness all of the ingredients that go into the wine. Additionally, the wine is cooked immediately after the grapes have been crushed, which makes it remain kosher regardless of who opens or pours it.\n\n\n\nDrake prefers this purple drink over purple drank, a concoction typically made with codeine and sprite, and is widely popular in Texas.", "annotation_id": "2690744", "url": "https://genius.com/2690744", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SNL: Bar Mitzvah in 1999", "status": "done", "targets": 15, "clicked": 15, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-snl-bar-mitzvah-in-1999-lyrics", "genius_title": "SNL: Bar Mitzvah in 1999"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CAPO PLAZA", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-capo-plaza-lyrics", "genius_title": "CAPO PLAZA"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Doing It Wrong", "line": "And she’s the reason it happened, but she’s overreacting And it’s all because she don’t want things to change", "vault_lines": ["And she's the reason it happened, but she's overreacting", "And it's all because she don't want things to change"], "meaning": "Drake reflects on a breakup where his partner’s actions led to the split. However, he perceives her response as exaggerated, attributing it to her fear of change rather than the actual cause of the breakup. This highlights the complexity of relationships, where emotions can sometimes cloud the reasons behind their end.", "annotation_id": "35742358", "url": "https://genius.com/35742358", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Doing It Wrong", "line": "We live in a generation of not being in love and not being together", "vault_lines": ["We live in a generation of not being in love and not being together"], "meaning": "As opposed to older generations, the newer generations are getting into less relationships and having more flings", "annotation_id": "29732744", "url": "https://genius.com/29732744", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Doing It Wrong", "line": "’Cause you’ll say you love me, and I’ll end up lying And say, “I love you too”", "vault_lines": ["'Cause you'll say you love me, and I'll end up lying", "And say, \"I love you too\""], "meaning": "Drake cares about this girl so deeply that he holds himself back in order to prevent leading the girl on, and hurting her even more.\n\nCause you’ll say you love me…\n\nBy doing the things Drake states he can’t do in the previous lines, the girl may be lead on.\n\n…and I’ll end up lying\n\nHowever, Drake doesn’t feel the same way for some reason and will tell a lie which, in his opinion, is the lesser of two evils.\n\nAnd say I love you, too\n\nDrake knows that if it comes to this situation, he won’t be able to break her heart and tell her that he doesn’t feel the same way, ultimately hurting her even more in the long run.", "annotation_id": "441003", "url": "https://genius.com/441003", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Doing It Wrong", "line": "But I need someone different You know it, oh, you know it Oh, you know it, we both know it I need someone different You know it, oh, you know it Oh, you know it, we both know it", "vault_lines": ["But I need someone different", "You know it, oh, you know it", "Oh, you know it, we both know it", "I need someone different", "You know it, oh, she knows it", "Oh, I know it, we all know it"], "meaning": "The girl is indeed someone he cares for, but his assertion that he needs someone different is less about “variety” and more about being with the right person. This is further evidenced with the “something’s been missing” line.\n\nHe repeatedly expresses remorse over the breakup…but acknowledges that it was necessary for both parties.", "annotation_id": "12536870", "url": "https://genius.com/12536870", "state": "accepted", "votes": 62, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Doing It Wrong", "line": "I need someone different", "vault_lines": ["But I need someone different", "I need someone different"], "meaning": "Drake has moved on. He knows this isn’t the girl for him. He may think he should try and make it work with this girl, but he is aware of the fact that in the long run this isn’t the girl for him. He repeats this throughout the song, like he is convincing himself instead of convincing the girl.\n\nYour friendly neighborhood editor, iceberg, is an expert on this feeling. He gets over girls while they still love him more than ever for no reason other than his money, rapping skills, sweaters and disarming good looks.", "annotation_id": "609796", "url": "https://genius.com/609796", "state": "accepted", "votes": 61, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Doing It Wrong", "line": "But we sure make it feel like we’re together ’Cause we’re scared to see each other with somebody else", "vault_lines": ["But we sure make it feel like we're together", "'Cause we're scared to see each other with somebody else"], "meaning": "In conjunction with the previous line, he asserts that although couples aren’t actually in love or “together” maybe in the sense of values, goals, etc. They maintain artificial relationships that are fueled by surface level interaction and convenience.\n\nBeing scared to see someone you care about with someone else, usually arises from an individual questioning whether or not that person is “as good as it gets” and whether or not they can do better and/or find their “true love”.", "annotation_id": "517678", "url": "https://genius.com/517678", "state": "accepted", "votes": 177, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Doing It Wrong", "line": "When a good thing goes bad, it’s not the end of the world It’s just the end of a world that you had with one girl", "vault_lines": ["When a good thing goes bad, it's not the end of the world", "It's just the end of a world that you had with one girl"], "meaning": "Drake explains that when you break up with a girl, your entire life isn’t over, but instead, the moments you may be accustomed to spending with her are.\n\nWhen a good thing goes bad it’s not the end of the world\n\nA relationship doesn’t need to be romantic, it can be completely platonic but still have the same resulting feelings when it ends, often even worse. Just remember that there is still a world with seven-billion other people out there.\n\nIt’s just the end of a world that you had with one girl\n\nNotice how Drake uses ‘a’ here, as opposed to  ‘the’ when referring to the world. He may be trying to differentiate the actual physical world from the ‘bubble’ he had been living in with the girl he is talking about.\n\nNow that it’s over, Drake simply brushes it off as one girl in a world full of many.\n\nThe first two lines are lifted almost verbatim from the Don McLean song “When a Good Thing Goes Bad”. Lyrics from another McLean song, “The Wrong Thing to Do”, are later used in the chorus.", "annotation_id": "466540", "url": "https://genius.com/466540", "state": "accepted", "votes": 169, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Doing It Wrong", "line": "So cry if you need to, but I can’t stay to watch you That’s the wrong thing to do Touch if you need to, but I can’t stay to hold you That’s the wrong thing to do Talk if you need to, but I can’t stay to hear you That’s the wrong thing to do", "vault_lines": ["But I need someone different", "So cry if you need to, but I can't stay to watch you", "That's the wrong thing to do", "Touch if you need to, but I can't stay to hold you", "Talk if you need to, but I can't stay to hear you"], "meaning": "In this song, Drake explains some of the things that happen during a breakup.  Neither of them want to stay with each other but neither of them really want to leave\n\nIn these lines, Drake is talking about how he can stay and pretend with her but it’s not right because she’ll end up getting comfortable again\n\nThis is the part of the song most directly jacked from McLean’s tune.", "annotation_id": "443195", "url": "https://genius.com/443195", "state": "accepted", "votes": 171, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Doing It Wrong", "line": "[Outro: Stevie Wonder on Harmonica]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drizzy talked about Stevie’s contributions in an interview with The Village Voice right before Take Care’s release:\n\nWe had met and exchanged numbers a while ago so I called him when I was in LA, and he came to the studio I was working at, named Marvin’s Room. So he came and I had this song looped up named ‘Doing It Wrong,’ and it was just playing and Stevie said, ‘40 [Drake’s producing partner], turn the music up,’ and he was just vibing, being Stevie Wonder, sort of got quiet. And then he just went in the booth and brought life to this record, added all these musical pieces. He’s just, like, a dear friend of mine and a great person. I love working with him, and we’ll definitely work more in the future.\n\nThe harmonica part was used again in the track “Jorja Interlude,” on More Life.", "annotation_id": "438412", "url": "https://genius.com/438412", "state": "accepted", "votes": 270, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Doing It Wrong", "status": "done", "targets": 9, "clicked": 9, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-doing-it-wrong-lyrics", "genius_title": "Doing It Wrong"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Find Your Love", "line": "(Hey, hey, hey)", "vault_lines": ["I'm more than just an option (Hey, hey, hey)", "It's more than just a mission (Hey, hey, hey)", "You hear, but you don't listen (Hey, hey, hey)", "You better pay attention (Hey, hey, hey)", "Refuse to be forgotten (Hey, hey, hey)", "I took a chance with my heart (Hey, hey, hey)", "I'm more than just a number (Hey, hey, hey)", "I doubt you'll find another (Hey, hey, hey)", "So every single summer (Hey, hey, hey)"], "meaning": "These adlibs are done by Kanye West.", "annotation_id": "29631413", "url": "https://genius.com/29631413", "state": "pending", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Find Your Love", "status": "done", "targets": 1, "clicked": 1, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-find-your-love-lyrics", "genius_title": "Find Your Love"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Get It Together", "line": "You need me to get that shit together So we can get together You need me to get that shit together So we can get together", "vault_lines": ["You need me to", "We can be together, but", "You need me to get that shit together", "So we can get together"], "meaning": "Here Drake is referring to a recurring theme in his work: the necessity of taking personal responsibility, to improve shared relationships.\n\nAs he says in “Lose You,”\n\nI need to start sayin' shit when I notice it\nBe open with people I need some closure with\nBe honest with myself and take ownership\n\nThis is important because Drake is sometimes interpreted as putting the blame on his previous girlfriends. As we see in lines such as these, Drake is more likely to be concerned with his own self-improvement, for the benefit of others.", "annotation_id": "13022801", "url": "https://genius.com/13022801", "state": "accepted", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Get It Together", "line": "[Outro: Burna Boy & Drake] Hold one vibes Pree more life Cuh we ah pree more life Dun know already, cus’", "vault_lines": ["Cuh we ah pree more life", "Dun know already, cus'"], "meaning": "The outro was done by Nigerian Afrobeats artist Burna Boy.\n\n“Dun know” is slang for “of course” or “you already know” (or in this case, “you know already”). It’s of Jamaican patois origin and is used in Multicultural London English.", "annotation_id": "11556886", "url": "https://genius.com/11556886", "state": "accepted", "votes": 70, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Get It Together", "line": "[Verse 1: Jorja Smith]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Both of Jorja’s verses cover the verses in South African producer and DJ Black Coffee’s  2010 song “Superman.”\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ulN3QkamJUU\n\nThe only lyric that differs from the original song is Jorja’s initial “Hello.” In the original, Bucie sings “You know” instead.", "annotation_id": "11538150", "url": "https://genius.com/11538150", "state": "accepted", "votes": 57, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Get It Together", "status": "done", "targets": 3, "clicked": 3, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-get-it-together-lyrics", "genius_title": "Get It Together"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "King Leon (Street Cred)", "line": "Man, I am so far gone, bitch, I’m outta here", "vault_lines": ["Man, I am so far gone, bitch, I'm outta here"], "meaning": "Reference to his 2009 mixtape, So Far Gone.", "annotation_id": "39260847", "url": "https://genius.com/39260847", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "King Leon (Street Cred)", "line": "Дей, гиди, пушка-бойл—", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This song samples “Pilentse Pee” by The London Bulgarian Choir.\nThe original line from the intro is\n\nДей, гиди, пушка-бойлия?\n\nWhen translated, it reads as\n\nWhere is the long rifle?", "annotation_id": "31757242", "url": "https://genius.com/31757242", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
