{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Something", "line": "Fallin’ too fast, clearly rules don’t apply Can’t believe that I just met you", "vault_lines": ["Fallin' too fast, clearly rules don't apply", "Can't believe that I just met you"], "meaning": "“Fallin’ too fast” captures the tension between attraction and self-control. Drake recognizes that his emotions are developing faster than expected, but “rules don’t apply” suggests that the person feels like an exception to the boundaries he normally sets for himself. The line ultimately conveys how an unexpected connection can make someone disregard their usual caution.", "annotation_id": "41275003", "url": "https://genius.com/41275003", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Something", "line": "But I kept thinkin’ This could be somethin’ This could be somethin’ This could be somethin’ This could be, this could be This could be somethin’ This could be somethin’ This could be somethin’ Maybe it’s just nothin’ at all, oh But this could be somethin’ This could be somethin’ This could be, This could be This could be somethin’ This could be somethin’ This could be somethin’ Maybe it’s just nothin’ at all, at all, at all Maybe it’s just nothin’ at all, at all, at all", "vault_lines": ["But I kept thinkin'", "This could be somethin'", "This could be, this could be", "Maybe it's just nothin' at all, oh", "But this could be somethin'", "Maybe it's just nothin' at all, at all, at all"], "meaning": "Drake thinks that the girl he is seeing or talking to thinks that the relationship could be more deeper than what it is", "annotation_id": "36597980", "url": "https://genius.com/36597980", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
