{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Time", "line": "Heart’s still on javelin, baby", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "He’s still dealing with the piercing pain of heartbreak.", "annotation_id": "34741997", "url": "https://genius.com/34741997", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Time", "line": "I could be your man but maybe down the road", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "He wants to be in a relationship with this woman, but he just has absolutely no time for that now. That’s why he wishes all feelings of desire would disappear inside him, which is what it means when he says “rather see my heart turn to chrome, rather see my heart turn crystal.” He wants his heart to be stone-cold now so that he can deal with relationship stuff later.", "annotation_id": "34741939", "url": "https://genius.com/34741939", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Time", "line": "Right now I would rather see my heart turn to chrome", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake references the luxury clothing brand Chrome Hearts, popular for their jeans with leather crosses embroidered all over them.\n\nFrom denim to hoodies to custom Timberland boots to having the interior of his Rolls-Royce decorated by the brand, Drake has been seen rocking just about everything Chrome Hearts, and in May 2021 announced a collaboration with them, available for a limited time at the Chrome Hearts flagship store in Miami.", "annotation_id": "22917817", "url": "https://genius.com/22917817", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Time", "line": "You believe in angles more than angels", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake uses an anagram with “angles” and “angels” and reminds us of his 2018 hit single “Nice For What”:\n\nWith your phone out, gotta hit them angles\nWith your phone out, snappin' like you Fabo\n\nAs many girls put in a lot of effort to get their followers and likes up on social media, Drake thinks it’s more likely this girl believes in getting the perfect pic for the gram with her best angle and great lighting than the angels themselves.\n\nAt the end of the day, for all of humanity, humans have questioned, “Do Angels Exist? As that answer is still debated, IG models, however, have proved how to work their magic with the angles.", "annotation_id": "19846658", "url": "https://genius.com/19846658", "state": "pending", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Time", "line": "I just caught a shawty off a finsta", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "A “finsta” is a fake Instagram account or an account not publicly linked to a user’s primary one.\n\nFinstas are particularly useful for celebrities who wish to remain anonymous online while retaining an official page. Some celebrities have admitted to using them, like Justin Bieber and Bella Throne for example.\n\nDrake himself previously hinted at the existence of a finsta, writing in a now-deleted post on his real Instagram:\n\nme when I find a shordee that didn’t slash anyone famous yet… is this my finsta? shit it’s not.", "annotation_id": "19736400", "url": "https://genius.com/19736400", "state": "accepted", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Time", "line": "Yeah, I’m outside in an AMG Right outside, TT", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Mercedes-AMG is the luxury subsidiary of Daimler AG known for custom high-performance vehicles. All AMG engines come from the factory with twin turbos, hence the line “right outside, TT.” This is also a double entendre for the phrase “Too Turnt,” coined by Toronto rapper Robin Banks. Drake has previously used the abbreviation in his Instagram caption to nod his head to Banks:\n\n\n\nDrake later posted his Mercedes-AMG G63 on his Instagram story:", "annotation_id": "19718447", "url": "https://genius.com/19718447", "state": "accepted", "votes": 105, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Time", "line": "Just threw on a hoodie, it’s a Crenshaw", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake pays homage to the late rapper and community activist, Nipsey Hussle, who he collaborated with on the song “Killer”.  Nipsey’s clothing imprint, The Marathon Clothing, sold sweatsuits and other items that bore a Crenshaw logo.\n\n\n\nRap legend Snoop Dogg (left) posing with Nipsey Hussle in Marathon Clothing merch.\n\nNipsey came from the Crenshaw neighborhood of South Central Los Angeles.  He has said that versions of the Crenshaw logo were inspired by a similar logo worn by the character Tre in Boyz n the Hood, which was filmed in the same neighborhood.\n\nIn March 2019, Nipsey Hussle was killed outside of his Marathon Clothing store, located on Crenshaw and Slauson.", "annotation_id": "19717797", "url": "https://genius.com/19717797", "state": "accepted", "votes": 61, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Time", "status": "done", "targets": 7, "clicked": 7, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-time-flies-lyrics", "genius_title": "Time Flies"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Views From The 6", "line": "How is this shit goin’ how it is", "vault_lines": ["How is this shit goin' how it is"], "meaning": "Drake is in disbelief as to how things have been going so well for him recently.\n\nThis disbelief could be accredited to his successes in music as well as other endeavors, such as hosting the ESPYS and SNL.\n\nDrake has even managed to receive praises from Kanye for his musical achievements.", "annotation_id": "3954656", "url": "https://genius.com/3954656", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Views From The 6", "line": "I hope that they remember me, for everything I did", "vault_lines": ["I hope that they remember me, for everything I did"], "meaning": "Hoping people remember him when he’s gone, Drake is probably reflecting on the legacy of other artists that have passed and are still relevant such as Aaliyah and 2Pac. Every artist feels the need to etch out a place in time for themselves. It is thought that posthumous fame is the greatest of all.\n\nIn several interviews, Drizzy has always claimed to be about the “lasting power”. In an MTV interview, he explained he didn’t care about the sales of Nothing Was The Same, more so if the album would be as legendary as Take Care.", "annotation_id": "3954533", "url": "https://genius.com/3954533", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Views From The 6", "line": "I always seem to kill it and yet everybody lives", "vault_lines": ["I always seem to kill it and yet everybody lives"], "meaning": "Drizzy is always dropping some hot shit, whether singing a hook, doing a guest verse or even a remix. He kills it because he’s so good at what he does. At the same time, his parts of the song solely makes the record a hit. Thus, everybody is living off a Drake’s talents.\n\nDrake took a shot at a few other rappers in 5AM in Toronto claiming that they can’t kill anything.\n\nSo they never take shots, I got everybody on safety\nI could load every gun with bullets that fire backwards\nYou probably wouldn’t lose a single rapper\n\nThis may also be nod at his feud with Jay-Z. Drake has said he will try to kill a goat for the title of the best, but he also knows that dissing a rapper is silly and provides them with the attention of others including his fans, feeding that artist in the process. Continuing from that, Drake has been in various beefs with artists including Common and Pusha T and he hasn’t ended any careers.", "annotation_id": "3954518", "url": "https://genius.com/3954518", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Views From The 6", "line": "Back when I, was tryna’ make a, MI", "vault_lines": ["Back when I, was tryna' make a, MI"], "meaning": "Drizzy was a bit more introverted before the money was comin' in – i.e. before he made his first MI (Million)", "annotation_id": "3954471", "url": "https://genius.com/3954471", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Views From The 6", "line": "Plus you get more paper than I do, that shit attractive", "vault_lines": ["Plus you get more paper than I do, that shit attractive"], "meaning": "Although both Rihanna and Drake are worth millions, Rihanna currently makes more than Drake. Both stars made the Forbes 30 under 30: Music list in 2014. Rihanna was reported to have made 43 million this year, while Drake was reported to have made 30 million over the past 2 years.\n\nThe former Degrassi star has pulled in over $30 million in the past two years, boosted by live shows and endorsements with the likes of Sprite and Kodak.\n\nDrake is apparently attracted to the fact that Rihanna makes more money than himself. After all, mature women with more than him were the always the first to tempt him.", "annotation_id": "3954035", "url": "https://genius.com/3954035", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Views From The 6", "line": "What made us wanna act like we were married for two weeks? Now we back in California, we don’t even speak", "vault_lines": ["What made us wanna act like we were married for two weeks?", "Now we back in California, we don't even speak"], "meaning": "The honeymoon phase of a relationship is defined as the beginning of the relationship, where the couple gets to know each other and is blissfully unaware of their flaws – those will rear their ugly heads eventually.\n\nDrake reminisces on the short honeymoon phase he spent with Rihanna in Europe. He and Rihanna have gone from constantly conversing to not being able to stand the other speaking. At least they didn’t actually get married, like Ross and Rachel did on Friends.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8X-d3CTEEkM", "annotation_id": "3954011", "url": "https://genius.com/3954011", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Views From The 6", "line": "Ballin’ out, swear I use to be shy", "vault_lines": ["Ballin' out, swear I use to be shy"], "meaning": "Drake was raised with separated parents, this may have made ​​him a shy boy in childhood\n\n\n\nBut you know nothing was the same since he was introduced to the rap game.. Drizzy has grown as person, and musically. Staying at the top of the game, rolling with bad bitches made him confident, he is not shy anymore.", "annotation_id": "3953977", "url": "https://genius.com/3953977", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Views From The 6", "line": "It’s some views from the 6 Just some views from the 6", "vault_lines": ["It's some views from the 6", "Just some views from the 6"], "meaning": "Drizzy prominently projected the number 6, which most likely refers to his upcoming album – named for Toronto’s main area code 416. He also has a tattoo of this number on his rib to symbolize his Toronto birthplace.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/Drake/status/497148916240896000", "annotation_id": "3953976", "url": "https://genius.com/3953976", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Views From The 6", "line": "(Say Hi, M)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This audio sample is from a Viddy video from Rihanna. Having a conversation with her friend, Melissa Forde.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Lq-cuA3nhaY\n\nDrake also brought out Jen Rosales in Paris for HOWGH.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r3AJcsD5EIc", "annotation_id": "3953964", "url": "https://genius.com/3953964", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Views From The 6", "line": "Everyone said we look good on paper", "vault_lines": ["Everyone said we look good on paper"], "meaning": "Since Drake and Rihanna started their romance, magazines and gossip blogs have printed them as their cover page.\n\n\n\nLooks good on paper is an idiom that describes something that seems good/true, but may not actually be when applied to real life.\n\nDrake has a similar line on “Fireworks”:\n\nNow all of a sudden these gossip blogs want to cover me\nAnd you making it seem that it happened that way because of me", "annotation_id": "3953958", "url": "https://genius.com/3953958", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Views From The 6", "line": "You must remember wakin’ up in Paris with the blunt You must remember fuckin’ me like anytime you want", "vault_lines": ["You must remember wakin' up in Paris with the blunt", "You must remember fuckin' me like anytime you want"], "meaning": "This is a reference to Drake’s ex-girlfriend, Rihanna. He is reminiscing about the good times they had with each other. RiRi showed up to L’Avenue, one of Paris' most famous celebrity hotspots, on 23rd of February, to have dinner with her back then on-and-off boyfriend, Drake.\n\nDrake for this part spoke to Rolling Stone and revealed that she’s his ultimate fantasy:\n\nShe’s the ultimate fantasy. I mean, I think about it. Like, ‘Man, that would be good.’ We have fun together, she’s cool and shit. But we’re just friends, she’s my dog for life. I’m not after pussy like I was three years ago, when I was trying to make up for all the years when no girl would talk to me. But I haven’t met somebody that makes everybody else not matter.", "annotation_id": "3953906", "url": "https://genius.com/3953906", "state": "accepted", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Views From The 6", "line": "Things that make me miss you, where Jen and Melissa", "vault_lines": ["Things that make me miss you, where Jen and Melissa"], "meaning": "Jen Rosales (left) is Rihanna’s personal assistant, and Melissa Forde (right) is Rihanna’s bestfriend.\n\nWhen he sees Rih with these two he can’t help but miss her and wish he was there.", "annotation_id": "3953709", "url": "https://genius.com/3953709", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
