{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "London Tour Freestyle", "line": "[Verse 1]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This verse was later reused as the first verse on Drake’s November 2011 track, “Over My Dead Body”, which served as the opening track to Drake’s sophomore album Take Care.", "annotation_id": "2113683", "url": "https://genius.com/2113683", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "London Tour Freestyle", "status": "done", "targets": 1, "clicked": 1, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-london-tour-freestyle-lyrics", "genius_title": "London Tour Freestyle"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Madiba Riddim", "line": "I cannot tell who is my friend I need distance between me and them Gonna have to teach me how to love you again God knows I’m trying God knows I’m trying for you God knows I’m trying", "vault_lines": ["I cannot tell who is my friend", "I need distance between me and them", "Gonna have to teach me how to love you again", "God knows I'm trying", "God knows I'm trying for you"], "meaning": "Drake has developed paranoia over the course of his career, not knowing who he can trust. His relationship with a few people in the industry has soured over time. Such people include Meek Mill, who went from being a collaborator on “R.I.C.O.” to becoming embroiled in a highly public beef with the Toronto rapper after questioning the authenticity of Drake’s songwriting.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/MeekMill/status/623700698509758464\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDrake’s Cash Money Records boss Birdman has also fallen out with Drake’s mentor Lil Wayne, and that has surely changed the nature of the relationship between Drake and Birdman.\n\nSuch experiences have made Drake wary of the people around him and slow to trust and love, which he is trying to change for the girl he is singing to.", "annotation_id": "11795784", "url": "https://genius.com/11795784", "state": "accepted", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Madiba Riddim", "line": "Top story Wah?", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Popcaan says this.\nNotnice, one of Popcaans producers, just dropped the Top Story Riddim.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=08-8cjXK3rM\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PoURVxVDUZw", "annotation_id": "11616774", "url": "https://genius.com/11616774", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Madiba Riddim", "line": "People change, I’m not surprised Devil’s working overtime Voodoo spells put on my life It won’t work, they all have tried", "vault_lines": ["People change, I'm not surprised", "Voodoo spells put on my life", "It won't work, they all have tried"], "meaning": "Drake is used to people changing on him. The great majority of people that have beef with him are people that were once his friend. This theme is common in Drake’s music now, he also refers this issue in the outro of the album “Do Not Disturb.”\n\nVoodoo is a religious cult that uses magic to gain their desires with the help of an upper entity. Drake claims such evils will not work on him because he’s the 6 god. Of course, he doesn’t mean this literally, he’s just illustrating how far his enemies will go to stop him.", "annotation_id": "11538072", "url": "https://genius.com/11538072", "state": "accepted", "votes": 50, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Madiba Riddim", "line": "[Outro] You put food on the table for me, aye? Alright, fam, soft, I see you, aye? You pay my bills, right? It’s light You’re a wasteman", "vault_lines": ["You put food on the table for me, aye?", "Alright, fam, soft, I see you, aye?", "You pay my bills, right?"], "meaning": "The outro samples a clip from a YouTube video called “T-Dot Goon Scrap DVD!,” a video that parodies how the Toronto youth always get in fights in the oddest locations. The video was created by 4YallEntertainment, a fraternal duo of YouTubers hailing from Brampton, Ontario. Trey Richards, one of the brothers, quickly put out a post on Instagram, thanking Drake.\n\n\n\nA sequel to the video entitled “T-Dot Goon Scrap DVD 2”, featuring one of Drake’s frequent producers Boi 1-da and even Drake himself, was uploaded to YouTube by 4YallEntertainment on May 14, 2017.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gLTcllilxfk\n\nDrake previously acknowledged the YouTubers back in 2014 in a tweet with a link to one of their older videos, titled “ANY SONG @DRAKE TOUCHES IS HOT!”\n\nhttps://twitter.com/drake/status/539980765094612994?lang=en\n\nThese familiar faces were also present in OVO artist Roy Woods‘ music video for “Gwan Big Up Yourself.”\n\nThe two brothers also explained the sample being in the song in a vlog from them:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=b5dUMk6Tdrg", "annotation_id": "11534842", "url": "https://genius.com/11534842", "state": "accepted", "votes": 70, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Madiba Riddim", "line": "Anointed and protected, I was chosen", "vault_lines": ["Anointed and protected, I was chosen"], "meaning": "Continuing with religious imagery, Drake now establishes himself as divinely protected; he was anointed. Anointing the body or head with oil is common practice in Judaism and Christianity.\n\nDrake is Jewish and has referenced this on countless occasions such as in his skit on SNL and in the music video for his song “HYFR.” where they re-enact a Bar Mitzvah.\n\nIn the Bible, it states that:\n\nJesus Christ was anointed by God with the Holy Spirit to spread the Good News – Luke 4:18-19.\n\nIt is also believed that Jews are the chosen people.", "annotation_id": "11534570", "url": "https://genius.com/11534570", "state": "accepted", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
