{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Good*", "line": "You a slimed out baby, no good for me, no good Did a lot of things that I knew you would Let me in the city now I’m going through it Uh-huh You a slimed out baby, no good for me, no good Did a lot of dirt like I knew you would Let me on my own now I’m going through", "vault_lines": ["And you did me wrong", "'Cause I'm here for the night and I'm going through it", "You a slimed out baby, no good for me, no good", "Let me on my own now I'm...", "Did a lot of things that I knew you would", "Let me in the city now I'm going through it", "Did a lot of dirt like I knew you would", "Let me on my own now I'm going through"], "meaning": "The term “slimed out baby” denotes a double entendre. It can refer to Drake’s partner being ejaculated on (slimed) during sexual intercourse, or most likely, can refer to Drake using an ex-partner of his for his own personal benefit (most likely sexual) and then ends the relationship after fully exploiting her.\n\nDrake, who’s a highly sexually active individual, once experienced this after the accidental impregnation of French adult film actress Sophie Brussaux in January 2017, which led to the birth of their son Adonis Graham in that following October.\n\nDrake disregards his and his partner’s relationship as a whole and opts to be single, which is a topic further spoken on throughout September 2023’s “Slime You Out,” rapping:\n\nBitch, next time, I swear on my grandmother grave\nI’m slimin' you for them kid choices you made\nSlimin' you out, slimin' you out, slimin' you out\nAyy, this ain’t the littest I could get on you bitches\nSend wires on wires on wires like Idris\nYou lucky that I don’t take back what was given\n\nDepicted in “Slime You Out’s” alternative cover, American actress Halle Berry can literally be seen “slimed out,” after the 2012 Nickelodeon Kids' Choice Awards:\n\n\n\n Pictured: Halle Berry being slimed during the Kids' Choice Awards", "annotation_id": "29916981", "url": "https://genius.com/29916981", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Good*", "line": "I’m a turnt-up nigga from the 6ixside, breaking down a Backwood (Uh-huh)", "vault_lines": ["I'm a turnt-up nigga from the 6ixside, breaking down a Backwood (Uh-huh)"], "meaning": "Drake refers to his hometown of Toronto, Canada, which has been awarded the moniker “6,” which represents Toronto’s six boroughs: East York, Etobicoke, North York, Scarborough, Toronto, and York whilst also representing Toronto’s area codes “416” and “647.”\n\nDrake, who’s known for his illicit consumption of Marijuana, references American cigarette brand Backwoods Smokes, which was first introduced in 1973 by Universal Leaf Corporation.", "annotation_id": "29913639", "url": "https://genius.com/29913639", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
