{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Uuugly", "line": "CC, they want me to break it down CC, they need me to break it down Lemme go break it down", "vault_lines": ["CC, they want me to break it down", "CC, they need me to break it down", "Lemme go break it down"], "meaning": "“CC” refers to Camila Cabello, with Drake addressing her directly. “They want me to break it down” suggests that listeners someone expecting Drake to explain something.", "annotation_id": "32356849", "url": "https://genius.com/32356849", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Uuugly", "line": "This heart was broken a long time ago My blood, it pumps from my hungover liver, then straight to my bones", "vault_lines": ["My blood, it pumps from my hungover liver, then straight to my bones", "This heart was broken a long time ago"], "meaning": "Drake reflects on enduring emotional pain and its physical effects through the metaphor of the liver processing blood. The “hungover liver” signifies frequent drinking to cope with heartbreak.\n\nNormally, blood enters the liver through the hepatic artery and the portal vein, gets filtered and processed, then leaves through the hepatic veins to the heart before being pumped to the rest of the body. However, for Drake, the blood flows “straight to my bones,” skipping the heart because it’s broken.", "annotation_id": "32234314", "url": "https://genius.com/32234314", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Uuugly", "line": "Trying me Trying me (Trying me) Trying me, trying me", "vault_lines": ["Trying me, trying me"], "meaning": "This is another reference to the other Drake feature on the album in the song “HOT UPTOWN”\n\nTrying my patience\nTrying somethin' else might even work in your favor\nTrying to forget me doesn’t work when he’s basic\nTrying one more time ‘cause we look so good on paper\nTrying me\n\nThe many similarities between the songs might imply a connection between them. In this song, the main speaker is Drake while in “HOT UPTOWN” the main speaker is Camila. Both songs speak about a breakup which might imply that both songs refer to the same breakup from two different perspectives.", "annotation_id": "32220154", "url": "https://genius.com/32220154", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Uuugly", "line": "Two hands on your waist One hand on my face", "vault_lines": ["Two hands on your waist", "One hand on my face"], "meaning": "In “HOT UPTOWN” (Another Drake feature on this album) Camila is using this same line from her perspective\n\nTwo hands on my waist, one hand on your face", "annotation_id": "32220074", "url": "https://genius.com/32220074", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
