{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Thank You Letter", "line": "40", "vault_lines": ["This tape is for 40, Oliver", "This tape would not be possible without: Noel, Boi 1DA, Vinylz, 40"], "meaning": "Noah Shebib, also known als “40”, is also a fellow Torontonian. He’s one of Drake’s longtime producers from OVO Sound. They work together since 2005 and he produced four tracks on If You’re Reading This It’s Too Late: “Madonna,” “6 Man,” “You & the 6,” and “Jungle.”", "annotation_id": "9622476", "url": "https://genius.com/9622476", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Thank You Letter", "line": "Theo", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This references Theo Skudra, Drake’s personal photographer and the man behind many of Drake’s Instagram posts.\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/BIZRM3VDKDD/?taken-by=champagnepapi\n\nThe above images were taken by Skudra, who is tagged in the caption, and posted on Drake’s Instagram during his Summer Sixteen Tour with Future. Skudra also takes images of other members of the OVO label, with big names like PARTYNEXTDOOR often sharing Skudra’s work on their Instagram as well.\n\nCheck out Theo Skudra’s Instagram here.", "annotation_id": "9104634", "url": "https://genius.com/9104634", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
