{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Thank You Letter", "status": "done", "targets": 55, "clicked": 55, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-thank-you-letter-lyrics", "genius_title": "Thank You Letter"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "These Days", "line": "I’ve stopped the dreaming I don’t do too much scheming", "vault_lines": ["I've stopped the dreaming", "I don't do too much scheming", "I don't do too much talking these days"], "meaning": "having accomplished so much already in his career at the point of the writing of this song, Drake is left with nothing to prove.\n\nThis said, he is no longer ‘scheming’ up ways to make it to the top; he has already arrived.", "annotation_id": "30618256", "url": "https://genius.com/30618256", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "These Days", "line": "I sit inside a chauffeur car With windows down and count the stars", "vault_lines": ["I sit inside a chauffeur car", "With windows down and count the stars"], "meaning": "At this point in his career, having accomplished so much, Drake is expressing the fact that he has nothing left to prove.\n\nThis said, he spends his time in reflection of the wins with no worries on his mental, while being driven around in a car meant for a driver (likely a Rolls Royce, which has an upgrade option of (artificial) ‘stars’ in the ceiling).", "annotation_id": "29249819", "url": "https://genius.com/29249819", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "These Days", "line": "I’ve met some women I wish I had resisted these days", "vault_lines": ["I've met some women", "I wish I had resisted these days"], "meaning": "Likely a reference to his girlfriend in 2010-11, Erika Lee, whose voice appeared on his 2011 song ‘Marvin’s Room’.  She later sued Drake over a royalties' withholdings dispute with regards to the song.\n\nAlso, perhaps a reference to Rihanna – she and Drake dated off-and-on for years but did not end up together.\n\nWith a prolific dating history like Drake’s, stress and regret typically accompany, unfortunately.", "annotation_id": "29249432", "url": "https://genius.com/29249432", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "These Days", "line": "Yeah, I had a lover Don’t think I’d risk another These days These days And if I seem to be afraid Just listen to the life I’ve made in songs", "vault_lines": ["Don't think I'd risk another", "And if I seem to be afraid", "Just listen to the life I've made in songs", "These days I seem to think a lot", "I wish I had resisted these days", "These days I seem to think"], "meaning": "In the original version of “These Days,” Jackson Browne sings,\n\nNow if I seem to be afraid to live the life that I have made in song\nWell it’s just that I’ve been losing\nFor so long\n\nRather than admitting defeat, Drake modifies the lyrics to call attention to his earlier songs. He urges the listener to look at  his previous work in order to understand why he can’t commit to a relationship now. In songs like  “Marvin’s Room,” Drake expresses timidity in finding a partner. In “Find Your Love,” he worries about choosing the right partner.\n\nIn a 2010 interview, Drake said,\n\nI look for love in the wrong people. It just always seem like the women I find are poison for me. I love women that can just walk into a room and stop the whole area. And I think that those initial qualities always end up getting me hurt, which is a crazy thing for a guy to say.“", "annotation_id": "8903791", "url": "https://genius.com/8903791", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "These Days", "line": "These days These days I seem to think About how I have failed To change all of my ways", "vault_lines": ["These days I seem to think a lot", "These days I seem to think", "About how I have failed", "To change all of my ways"], "meaning": "Drake reflects on how much he has changed  over time. No doubt, Drake’s evolved over the years, even sparking a meme about it;\n\n\n\nAlthough he has grown up and changed a lot, Drake still feels as if he hasn’t changed enough—as if he’s stuck in his ways. He’s still singing, he’s still making songs about old flames; not much has changed.", "annotation_id": "8902317", "url": "https://genius.com/8902317", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "These Days", "line": "I’ve been out walking I don’t do too much talking these days These days These days I seem to think a lot About the things that I forgot to do", "vault_lines": ["I've been out walking", "I don't do too much scheming", "I don't do too much talking these days", "These days I seem to think a lot", "About the things that I forgot to do", "These days I seem to think"], "meaning": "While much of the song is a slightly-edited interpolation of Jackson Browne’s  “These Days,” the first verse is exactly the same as the original.\n\nBrowne wrote the first iteration of the song when he was 16. A few years later he was working as a songwriter, pitching his lyrics to various recording artists. German model and singer Nico was the first artist to record a version of the song. The song would later be recorded by Browne himself and Gregg Allman.\n\nDrake has never shied away from singing/rapping about his real feelings. Browne’s original lyrics fit within Drake’s canon—he often references feeling lonely, isolated, and nostalgic.", "annotation_id": "8899968", "url": "https://genius.com/8899968", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "These Days", "line": "These days", "vault_lines": ["I don't do too much talking these days", "These days I seem to think a lot", "I wish I had resisted these days", "These days I seem to think"], "meaning": "Drake uses this phrase to let the listener know that he is talking about how he currently feels.\n\nDrake contrasts life before fame with his current situation.  He uses this phrase in other songs, including “Jungle”.", "annotation_id": "8899153", "url": "https://genius.com/8899153", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "These Days", "status": "done", "targets": 7, "clicked": 7, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-these-days-lyrics", "genius_title": "These Days"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Yves Slatt Laurent", "line": "She let me fuck in Delilah (What?)", "vault_lines": ["She let me fuck in Delilah (What?)"], "meaning": "Delilah is an upscale nightclub in West Hollywood that he’s known to frequent.\n\n\n\nDrake pictured in Delilah\n\nThe venue later reappears in his high-profile Kendrick Lamar diss track “Family Matters,” where Drake frames it as a spot he can still freely access in LA, pushing back against any narrative that he’s been blacklisted from setting foot in LA:\n\nI get off the plane and nothing has changed, I head to Delilah with all of my ice\nHead to Delilah with all of my ice, head to Delilah with all of my ice", "annotation_id": "38585682", "url": "https://genius.com/38585682", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Yves Slatt Laurent", "line": "And I’m with the real king spider (What?)", "vault_lines": ["I'm with the O's and I'm with the cros", "And I'm with the real king spider (What?)"], "meaning": "Sp5der (spider) is a streetware brand founded by rapper Young Thug.", "annotation_id": "30812064", "url": "https://genius.com/30812064", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Yves Slatt Laurent", "line": "[Verse]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This song made waves after Drake posted a snippet on his IG of JOE KAY’s Boiler Room playing this song.", "annotation_id": "29904237", "url": "https://genius.com/29904237", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Yves Slatt Laurent", "line": "YSL baby I’m Yves slatt Laurent, ayy, woah", "vault_lines": ["YSL baby I'm Yves slatt Laurent, ayy, woah"], "meaning": "Addressing close friend and frequent collaborator Young Thug by his term “slatt,” he shouts him out in plead for response, who on May 9, 2022, alongside twenty-eight other associates from Thug’s independent record label Young Stoner Life (or “YSL” for short), were arrested and indicted for 56-counts of gang-related violence along with a violation of Georgia’s RICO Act.\n\nThese lyrics also serve as a double entendre, referring to French luxury fashion company Yves Saint Laurent (or “YSL” for short), who inspired the track’s title.\n\nDrake has also held a protest for Thug’s release in an August 2023 Instagram post:", "annotation_id": "29894329", "url": "https://genius.com/29894329", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Yves Slatt Laurent", "line": "Ain’t with the O, I don’t know you at all", "vault_lines": ["Ain't with the O, I don't know you at all"], "meaning": "October’s Very Own (officially known as OVO Sound), is Drake’s independent record label, co-founded by Drake himself, 40 and Oliver El-Khatib.\n\nAs of October 2023, fourteen people are signed to the label; consisting of nine artists and six producers.\n\nDrake claims if you aren’t associated with OVO (which is already a difficult record label to be signed to) you aren’t associated with Drake either.", "annotation_id": "29892878", "url": "https://genius.com/29892878", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Yves Slatt Laurent", "status": "done", "targets": 5, "clicked": 5, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-yves-slatt-laurent-lyrics", "genius_title": "Yves Slatt Laurent"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Body 2 Body (Lovesick)", "line": "Why are we in Chanel talkin’ ’bout life and shit? Got my emotions on open mic and shit", "vault_lines": ["Why are we in Chanel talkin' 'bout life and shit?", "Got my emotions on open mic and shit"], "meaning": "Here Drake seems to be questioning a woman’s interest in discussing each other’s life in a public location ( Chanel Store). Conversations which often lead him to opening up about personal matters and just like open mic are continually judged.", "annotation_id": "19129352", "url": "https://genius.com/19129352?", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
