{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Currents", "line": "We can move in slow motion if that’s what you want, babe", "vault_lines": ["We can move in slow motion if that's what you want, babe"], "meaning": "Right after this line, the squeaky bed sound effect, used throughout the verse as a sexual metaphor, slows down noticeably. It reflects Drake literally following through on the lyric, slowing down the tempo of the metaphorical (and physical) motion and adjusting to the other person.\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nI don’t want to come on too strong\nBut I’m moving to your rhythm", "annotation_id": "36279888", "url": "https://genius.com/36279888", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
