{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ring a Ding", "status": "done", "targets": 1, "clicked": 1, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-ring-a-ding-lyrics", "genius_title": "Ring a Ding"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Rusty Intro", "line": "D-D-DJ Frisco954, yo", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This is the producer tag for DJ Frisco954, a Fort Lauderdale DJ known for pioneering South Florida’s “fast music” scene, where rap and R&B tracks are sped up for clubs. The “954” is Broward County’s area code. Once told fast music was a waste of time, he earned Washington Post coverage in 2021 and has since sped up tracks for artists like Yung Miami. Landing a co-production credit on HABIBTI’s opening track marks his biggest placement yet.", "annotation_id": "41667501", "url": "https://genius.com/41667501?", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Rusty Intro", "line": "And God made me with the left hand, I cannot do everything right", "vault_lines": ["And God made me with the left hand, I cannot do everything right"], "meaning": "The phrase “God drew with his left hand” is a common expression which describes someone who is unconventional, awkward, clumsy, or uniquely made.", "annotation_id": "39869818", "url": "https://genius.com/39869818", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Rusty Intro", "line": "To all the sweethearts and the dates I’ve had", "vault_lines": ["To all the sweethearts and the dates I've had"], "meaning": "A melodic interpolation of a line from the second verse of “The Parting Glass”, a Scottish folk song famously covered by Ed Sheeran on his debut album.", "annotation_id": "39814288", "url": "https://genius.com/39814288", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Rusty Intro", "line": "I’m on a orange full moon right now, so I don’t want to nap", "vault_lines": ["I'm on a orange full moon right now, so I don't want to nap"], "meaning": "In some spiritual traditions, rare condition of orange full moon is believed to bring vibrant energy and creativity, which makes it the perfect time to stay awake, same reason why Drake doesn’t want to be asleep.\n\nThe orange moon also might be in reference to an Orange Moon Ibiza; a Mediterranean vodka, playing off the bartender line.\n\n\n\nOrange full moon can also refer to an Adderall pill, which is usually round and orange in 20 or 30 mg. The pill is known to make consumers lose sleep.", "annotation_id": "39799933", "url": "https://genius.com/39799933", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Rusty Intro", "status": "done", "targets": 4, "clicked": 4, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-rusty-intro-lyrics", "genius_title": "Rusty Intro"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Secrets", "line": "I can’t make you my girl till you’re riding", "vault_lines": ["I can't make you my girl till you’re riding"], "meaning": "Drake cannot start a relationship with this girl until he knows that she’s loyal to him and completely for him. Drake has sung/rapped many lyrics similar to this, like on Keep the Family Close:\n\n‘'And it’s all because you chose a side\nYou’re supposed to put your pride aside and ride for me’'\n\nor on Pipe Down:\n\n‘'I can’t believe you told me it was ride or die\n'Cause you’re not here, somehow you’re still alive’'\n\nBasically, Drake needs complete commitment from his girl.", "annotation_id": "37427766", "url": "https://genius.com/37427766", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
