{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Nothings Into Somethings", "line": "Nah, sha-nah-nah-nah-nah-nah Sha-nah-nah-nah-nah-nah", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake’s vocals play on the phrase “Should’ve known.” Even though he doesn’t agree with the woman in question’s choices, he knows he shouldn’t be surprised by them because of her past behavior.", "annotation_id": "11554514", "url": "https://genius.com/11554514", "state": "accepted", "votes": 72, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Nothings Into Somethings", "line": "[Intro: DJ Paul] You ever hear some slow tracks, you know what I’m sayin’? With, like, some pimpin’ to it, or somethin’ That you can relax, pop a top to, or somethin’?", "vault_lines": ["You ever hear some slow tracks, you know what I'm sayin'?", "With, like, some pimpin' to it, or somethin'", "That you can relax, pop a top to, or somethin'?"], "meaning": "DJ Paul is one of the two main producers of the American rap group Three 6 Mafia.\n\nIn an interview with Nardwuar, Drake stated that he is a huge Three 6 fan, as well as a huge fan of Paul and Juicy.\n\nDrake previously sampled DJ Paul’s “Ridin Spinners on ”Energy“ a track off his If You’re Reading This It’s Too Late mixtape.", "annotation_id": "11540730", "url": "https://genius.com/11540730", "state": "accepted", "votes": 55, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Nothings Into Somethings", "line": "I’m still posted up where you first found me", "vault_lines": ["I'm still posted up where you first found me"], "meaning": "Drake grew up and came of age in Toronto. Here, he is saying that, despite all the fame, success, and financial ability to fully relocate elsewhere, he still remains true to the 6, even going as far as constructing a mansion there.\n\nDrake references his hometown often in his discography, with songs such as “Know Yourself”, “You and the 6”, and “Star67”.\n\nThis concept of staying true to your home roots is a common one in the rap game, with examples from Kendrick Lamar, G-Eazy, and Future.", "annotation_id": "11535366", "url": "https://genius.com/11535366", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Nothings Into Somethings", "line": "Ask about that, you would say it was nothing But here’s another nothin’ that you made into somethin’ Can’t just leave it off that way", "vault_lines": ["Can't just leave it off that way", "Can't just leave it off that way, nah", "Ask about that, you would say it was nothing", "But here's another nothin' that you made into somethin'"], "meaning": "From Drake’s point of view, it wouldn’t have been a big deal for Serena to invite him to her wedding or at least inform him about it, but she made a “nothing” into “something” by not doing so.\n\nThe “nothing/something” motif could also be meant as a reference to “Kn0thing,” the Reddit username of Serena’s husband Alexis Ohanian (Co-Founder of Reddit). “Kn0thing” became Serena’s something.", "annotation_id": "11533707", "url": "https://genius.com/11533707", "state": "accepted", "votes": 75, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Nothings Into Somethings", "line": "Least, do I get an invitation or something?", "vault_lines": ["Least, do I get an invitation or something?"], "meaning": "Drake is at least hoping for an invitation to the wedding from the woman he wanted to be with, maybe to just wish her and her new husband a good life or to decide for himself if her new husband is worthy of being married to her and taking his place as her significant other.\n\nThis song probably references Drizzy’s on-again off-again flame, Serena Williams and her engagement to Reddit co-founder, Alexis Ohanian. With a combined net worth of around $160 million, that’s a wedding anyone would want an invite to.", "annotation_id": "11533280", "url": "https://genius.com/11533280", "state": "accepted", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Nothings Into Somethings", "line": "Did I just read that you just got engaged on me? I heard from your friend, you couldn’t even tell me Or better yet, wait on me", "vault_lines": ["Did I just read that you just got engaged on me?", "I heard from your friend, you couldn't even tell me", "Or better yet, wait on me"], "meaning": "This could be about his on and off relationship with Serena Williams, who recently got engaged to Reddit co-founder Alexis Ohanian.\n\nSerena’s friend that’s referenced here is likely Valerie Vogt, the current girlfriend of OVO crew member Angelo Ferraro, better known as OVOGelo.\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/BRMNS27DwlO", "annotation_id": "11532492", "url": "https://genius.com/11532492", "state": "accepted", "votes": 102, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Nothings Into Somethings", "line": "Big cup of Ac’, I’m drowsy", "vault_lines": ["Big cup of Ac', I'm drowsy"], "meaning": "Drake once again references being “on one” as he drinks the recreational drug beverage lean from a double cup. One of the main ingredients in the purple drank is the drowse-inducing promethazine/​codeine cough syrup made by the Actavis pharmaceutical company.", "annotation_id": "11531538", "url": "https://genius.com/11531538", "state": "accepted", "votes": 72, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
