{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Yebba’s Heartbreak", "line": "Can I show my love for you? (Can I show my love for you?)", "vault_lines": ["How much better can I show my love for you", "Show my love for you", "Can I show my love for you?"], "meaning": "fuck 😭", "annotation_id": "30650663", "url": "https://genius.com/30650663", "state": "pending", "votes": 62, "second_sense": false, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Yebba’s Heartbreak", "line": "”I do, I do, I do”? I do, I do, I do", "vault_lines": ["And all that you are, I do", "Reflection of the very moon, I do", "Than say \"I do, I do, I do\"?", "I do, I do, I do", "I do, I do, I do, I do, I do"], "meaning": "People say “I do” when getting married, this shows her true commitment to her lover.", "annotation_id": "30524546", "url": "https://genius.com/30524546", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Yebba’s Heartbreak", "line": "And all that you are, I do My single line of stars in noon Reflection of the very moon, I do", "vault_lines": ["And all that you are, I do", "My single line of stars in noon", "Reflection of the very moon, I do", "I do, I do, I do", "I do, I do, I do, I do, I do"], "meaning": "the person she is singing about consumes her whole life; they are reminded of them every time they see the stars and the moon. if this is linked back to yebba’s mother it is a reflection of how much she thinks about her; she sees her in every day beautiful things and can never escape the deep love she felt for her mother.", "annotation_id": "28018347", "url": "https://genius.com/28018347", "state": "pending", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Yebba’s Heartbreak", "line": "You may not know right where you’re going, but I do, I do, I do", "vault_lines": ["I do, I do, I do", "You may not know right where you're going, but", "I do, I do, I do, I do, I do"], "meaning": "this can be taken two ways:\n1) this is a reassurance that while you may not know the path you’re going down or whether your life has any purpose, that yebba knows they are important and loved.\n2) if this is about her mother, this tragically states that yebba knows what her mother ends up doing (su*cide) and acts as a final plea to her mother while she was alive that “i know where you’re going” but it doesn’t have to be that way.", "annotation_id": "28018345", "url": "https://genius.com/28018345", "state": "pending", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Yebba’s Heartbreak", "line": "[Verse: Yebba]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "‘Yebba’s Heartbreak’, presumed to be about a relationship, is actually an ode to her late mother Dawn, who sadly committed suicide in 2016. In this verse, Yebba seems to speak to her mother in a perspective prior to her passing.\n\nQuestioning what more she can do other than understand, Yebba attempts to convince her mother Dawn that there is a brighter future ahead, and says she’ll make everything up to her that made her mother feel less purpose. She swears that while her mothers suicidal feelings are overflowing, the opposing thoughts are the actual reality.\n\nFinally, Yebba expresses her love and how much her mother actually means, or unfortunately meant, to her.\n‘My single line of stars in noon.\n Reflection of the very moon’.\n\nBattling mental health is a real issue. Yebba often speaks on this subject, and her new album ‘Dawn’, named after her late mother details this.", "annotation_id": "26760923", "url": "https://genius.com/26760923", "state": "pending", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Yebba’s Heartbreak", "line": "How much better can I show my love for you", "vault_lines": ["How much better can I show my love for you", "Show my love for you", "Can I show my love for you?"], "meaning": "The song feels like a comforting lullaby or message to someone hurting or feeling overwhelmed with emotions. These emotions feel isolating leading the person to not feel or accept the love given to them. Yebba pleads & asks for better ways to show her love for them.", "annotation_id": "26463730", "url": "https://genius.com/26463730", "state": "pending", "votes": 36, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Yebba’s Heartbreak", "line": "And all the times you wasn’t chosen, well, I’ll make it up to you All of the feelings you’re not showing When your river’s overflowing", "vault_lines": ["And all the times you wasn't chosen, well, I'll make it up to you", "All of the feelings you're not showing", "When your river's overflowing"], "meaning": "Despite their attempt of hiding their true emotions, Yebba sees & empathizes the overwhelming river of feelings this person has. She comforts them & makes them feel seen by assuring them that in those times when they didn’t feel cared for or chosen, she’ll make it up to them by pouring more love in their cup.", "annotation_id": "26463717", "url": "https://genius.com/26463717", "state": "pending", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Yebba’s Heartbreak", "status": "done", "targets": 7, "clicked": 7, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-and-yebba-yebbas-heartbreak-lyrics", "genius_title": "Yebba’s Heartbreak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dead Presidents Freestyle", "line": "I’m picking and choosing an army and thinking of moving my talent is proven A show of hands who’s in?", "vault_lines": ["I'm picking and choosing an army and thinking of moving my talent is proven", "A show of hands who's in?"], "meaning": "At this early stage in Drake’s career, he was still making the transition from acting to rapping and continued to evolve by incorporating singing.\n\nDrake was also looking for like-minded people with talent to aid the evolution of his brand. This came to fruition through his OVO Sound Label which is home to an array of talent ranging from artists such as PARTYNEXTDOOR and Majid Jordan to producers like 40 and Boi-1da.", "annotation_id": "5021064", "url": "https://genius.com/5021064", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Dead Presidents Freestyle", "line": "Veterans like “How dare all of this arrogance” What you expect when all they do is draw comparisons between us and Americans", "vault_lines": ["Veterans like \"How dare all of this arrogance\"", "What you expect when all they do is draw comparisons between us and Americans"], "meaning": "People often catch feelings when Drake is compared to the OGs of Rap, but this paradigm isn’t self proclaimed – rap fans are the ones who have put him on the throne.\n\nIt bothers me when the God’s get to acting like the broads\n\n\n\nDrake probably didn’t expect that 10 years after recording this freestyle he would win a Rap Grammy over Nas who’s ironically sampled on the hook.", "annotation_id": "5021001", "url": "https://genius.com/5021001", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
