{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Yeah Yeah", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Bob-drake-yeah-lyrics", "genius_title": "Yeah"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Comments on Macklemore’s Post-Grammy Text", "line": "He made a brand of music that appealed to more people than me, Hov, Kanye and Kendrick.", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "However, Macklemore’s brand is smaller than any of these artists he mentions.\n\nIf you look at twitter followers as any indication:\n\nDrake: 14.2 million\nKanye: 10.3 million\nKendrick: 3.26 million\nHov: 2.97 million\n\nlastly,\nMacklemore: 2.7 million", "annotation_id": "2789839", "url": "https://genius.com/2789839", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Comments on Macklemore’s Post-Grammy Text", "line": "I was like, ’You won. Why are you posting your text message?", "vault_lines": ["I was like, 'You won. Why are you posting your text message?"], "meaning": "He shared the exchange on his Instagram\n\nhttp://imgur.com/SBogfgx\n\nDrake espouses the belief that an artist should take pride in their music. To admit inferiority is incomprehensible to Drake.", "annotation_id": "2789629", "url": "https://genius.com/2789629", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Comments on Macklemore’s Post-Grammy Text", "line": "That shit was wack as fuck", "vault_lines": ["That shit was wack as fuck"], "meaning": "http://instagram.com/p/jqXYYAwK_y/\n\nCheck out the RG breakdown of the photo here!\n\nI mean come on b, just take the trophies and shut up…", "annotation_id": "2789580", "url": "https://genius.com/2789580", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Comments on Macklemore’s Post-Grammy Text", "line": "No, in that case, you robbed everybody.", "vault_lines": ["No, in that case, you robbed everybody."], "meaning": "Drake’s stating that if Macklemore was going to text Kendrick saying that he should have won then he might as well send public condolences to all the other best rap album nominated artists: Jay-Z, Kanye, and Drake.\n\nThe psychologist’s view: This is the point in this monologue where Drake’s true intention shines through. He’s not really so aggrieved by Macklemore’s humility towards K.Dot as much as he’s aggrieved that Mack only swore his fealty to Kendrick. By doing so, Mack inadvertantly put Drake back in the context of his beef with Kendrick. Drake is (rightfully) not praised on an equivalent level, and so Drake’s pride is hurt. Instead of making a scene, and showing his feelings once again, by going directly after Kendrick on the topic of Grammy wins and losses, Drake uses Macklemore as a proxy.\n\nIt all seems so simple…", "annotation_id": "2789570", "url": "https://genius.com/2789570", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Comments on Macklemore’s Post-Grammy Text", "line": "Whether people wanna say it’s racial, or whether it’s just the fact that he tapped into something we can’t tap into.", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Macklemore has no shame admitting his White Privilege, and even made a song about it.\n\nWhat he tapped into was the play-it-safe parent market:\n\nI do think we have benefited from being white and the media grabbing on to something. A song like Thrift Shop was safe enough for the kids. It was like, “This is music that my mom likes and that I can like as a teenager,”… I’m a white guy, parents feel safe.\n\nMacklemore during his Rolling Stone interview on Race and Success", "annotation_id": "2789551", "url": "https://genius.com/2789551", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Comments on Macklemore’s Post-Grammy Text", "line": "And if you feel you didn’t deserve it, go get better — make better music.", "vault_lines": ["Just chill. Take your W, and if you feel you didn't deserve it, go get better — make better music."], "meaning": "This statement brings up another reason why a lot of people feel some type of way about The Heist winning the Grammy for Best Rap Album; it really wasn’t that good.\n\n\n\nWhile the album was insanely popular, it really wasn’t that loved by the critics, especially when you compare it to other nominees like Yeezus and good kid m.A.A.d city, which were both critically acclaimed.", "annotation_id": "2789498", "url": "https://genius.com/2789498", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Comments on Macklemore’s Post-Grammy Text", "line": "It felt cheap. It didn’t feel genuine. Why do that? Why feel guilt? You think those guys would pay homage to you if they won?", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake has a point here. Macklemore has a long history of dealing with his guilt throughout his music, but this is the Grammys. If you are too guilty to stand behind your work and just accept your award, then why should anyone else accept you? In this case it just seemed that Macklemore put out this picture to gain support from the Kendrick fans and separate himself from the controversy surrounding the situation in the hip-hop world.  Drake’s point is that a great wouldn’t degrade themselves, and in turn their music, to the point where they are sending text messages consoling the loser and immediately posting that picture to Instagram. Could you imagine Jay-Z doing that? Kendrick? Kanye (#mylaugh)?\n\n\n\n#OWNYOURSHIT", "annotation_id": "2789388", "url": "https://genius.com/2789388", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Comments on Macklemore’s Post-Grammy Text", "line": "To name just Kendrick? That shit made me feel funny.", "vault_lines": ["To name just Kendrick? That shit made me feel funny."], "meaning": "Probably because Macklemore didn’t only beat out Kendrick to win Best Rap Album, but also Jay Z, Kanye, and Drake himself.\n\n\n\nIn the Drake-Kendrick beef, this is a smart jab at Kendrick because here, Drake puts their respective albums at the same level. Mack apologized to Kendrick because he felt GKMC was the best album, not Nothing Was The Same.", "annotation_id": "2789261", "url": "https://genius.com/2789261", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Comments on Macklemore’s Post-Grammy Text", "status": "done", "targets": 8, "clicked": 8, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-comments-on-macklemores-post-grammy-text-lyrics", "genius_title": "Comments on Macklemore’s Post-Grammy Text"}
