{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Summers Over Interlude", "line": "Ooh, baby, yeah", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This song’s melody and vocals are reminiscent of Smokey Robinson’s 1965 single “Ooo Baby Baby,” in which Smokey laments the mistakes he made that ruined a past relationship.", "annotation_id": "9089435", "url": "https://genius.com/9089435", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Summers Over Interlude", "line": "Anywhere I go I can’t help but show I don’t feel the same Anywhere I go I can’t help but know I don’t feel the same Anywhere I go I can’t help but know", "vault_lines": ["Already told you, I don't feel the same", "I don't feel the same", "I can't help but show", "I can't help but know"], "meaning": "This could possibly refer to Drake’s love for his city, Toronto. The 6ix is one of the main themes of the album and he previously suggested that it would be called Views From The 6, but changed it to just Views.\n\nAubrey feels best when he’s in his own city. As a famous artist, he gets to travel a lot and visit the most wonderful places, but none of these places feel like home the way Toronto does.", "annotation_id": "9077572", "url": "https://genius.com/9077572", "state": "accepted", "votes": 48, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Summers Over Interlude", "line": "Days in the sun and nights in the rain", "vault_lines": ["Days in the sun and nights in the rain"], "meaning": "Even though Toronto’s known for its long, cold winters, the city also experiences warm summers. Due to its Nothern location, it usually rains a lot during this season.", "annotation_id": "9074606", "url": "https://genius.com/9074606", "state": "accepted", "votes": 56, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Summers Over Interlude", "line": "Found me some fun that’s good for the pain Already told you, I don’t feel the same I don’t feel the same", "vault_lines": ["Found me some fun that's good for the pain", "Already told you, I don't feel the same", "I don't feel the same"], "meaning": "This part is in reference to the ‘Summer’ part of the album, where Drake is regularly talking about a girl and the ups and downs of their time together. Here, at the end of the summer, the girl is hoping that their summer fling continues into the winter but Drake’s already lamenting its end–expressed through Majid’s sentimental vocals.\n\nThe fact that this interlude doesn’t feature Drake might represent the fact that Drake’s being purposefully indirect. The harshness of the way news is broken to this girl shows how harsh the winters in the 6 can be.", "annotation_id": "9071623", "url": "https://genius.com/9071623", "state": "accepted", "votes": 100, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Summers Over Interlude", "line": "Summer is over, simple and plain", "vault_lines": ["Summer is over, simple and plain"], "meaning": "Drake details the seasonal trajectory of Views on his Beats 1 interview.\n\nThe seasons of the 6 start with a harsh winter, which he expresses through solemn hip-hop. Winter’s followed by a hot summer, which represents with pop and R&B. Then, winter is upon us once again as summer ends, because in Toronto there are only two seasons.", "annotation_id": "9070825", "url": "https://genius.com/9070825", "state": "accepted", "votes": 56, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Summers Over Interlude", "status": "done", "targets": 5, "clicked": 5, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-summers-over-interlude-lyrics", "genius_title": "Summers Over Interlude"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2011 Juno Awards In Toronto", "line": "All these other girls they’re totally crazy, oh, oh, oh Only you can make me feel the way I feel Damn, I’m dying to make you feel like a woman, baby", "vault_lines": ["All these other girls they're totally crazy, oh, oh, oh", "Only you can make me feel the way I feel", "Damn, I'm dying to make you feel like a woman, baby"], "meaning": "A tribute to her song ‘Man! I Feel Like a Woman’\n\nOh, oh, oh, go totally crazy, forget I’m a lady\nMen’s shirts, short skirts\nOh, oh, oh, really go wild-yeah, doin' it in style\nOh, oh, oh, get in the actions feel the attraction\nColor my hair, do what I dare\nOh, oh, oh, I wanna be free, yeah, to feel the way I feel\nMan! I feel like a woman!", "annotation_id": "2219144", "url": "https://genius.com/2219144", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2011 Juno Awards In Toronto", "line": "You worked at McDonald’s and I eat McDonald’s", "vault_lines": ["You worked at McDonald's and I eat McDonald's"], "meaning": "True story – Shania worked at McDonald’s in Ontario.", "annotation_id": "2179854", "url": "https://genius.com/2179854", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2011 Juno Awards In Toronto", "line": "You’re from Timmins and I’m from Toronto", "vault_lines": ["You're from Timmins and I'm from Toronto"], "meaning": "Drake sang this song live to Shania Twain. She was born in Windsor, but her parents divorced at the age of two, and moved together with her mother to Timmins.\n\n\n\nAnd we all know that Drake is from Toronto, even though he sometimes feel like Atlanta adopted him", "annotation_id": "2179819", "url": "https://genius.com/2179819", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "weak"}
