{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Hold On", "line": "[Produced by Nineteen85, Majid Jordan & Noah “40” Shebib]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This song started as a beat by Nineteen85. Then Majid—half of the OVO-signed duo Majid Jordan—laid some vocals over it while Jordan sped it up to infuse the track with more energy. They handed it over to 40 and Drake, and the rest is history. As 40 told the FADER:\n\nMajid Jordan captures a moment that Drake and I have always been chasing.\n\nThis is a 100BPM song with a four-on-the-floor rhythm with a clap on every second beat for most of the track. The main arrangement is drums, synths, bass, vocals and backing vocals. It’s been described by SPIN as “synth-soaked R&B” meeting “slow-motion deep house”. The song uses a lot of reverb to give it a spacious feeling. During the final hook white noise cuts and hi-hats are added in to highlight the grand finalé.\n\nGrammy nominated producer Chilly Gonzales broke down the keys used in the beat:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1ysNZRt3hoE", "annotation_id": "2835527", "url": "https://genius.com/2835527", "state": "accepted", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Hold On", "line": "It’s hard to do these things alone", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake has vented about being/sleeping alone before.\n\nDrake’s had many relationships not work out and like he implies on “Find Your Love”, he’s sick of failed relationships and being alone. He’s also apparently looking to settle down in a way, as he refers to on “Girls Love Beyonce” in the second verse.\n\nDrizzy doesn’t like being like this:", "annotation_id": "2110549", "url": "https://genius.com/2110549", "state": "accepted", "votes": 61, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Hold On", "line": "I got my eyes on you You’re everything that I see I want your heart, love and emotion endlessly", "vault_lines": ["Gavе you everything I loved"], "meaning": "When one is truly in love, it’s often said they only have eyes for that one person. And with love comes infatuation, so much so that you just can’t get enough.", "annotation_id": "2089541", "url": "https://genius.com/2089541", "state": "accepted", "votes": 174, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Hold On", "line": "I can’t get over you You left your mark on me I want your hot love and emotion endlessly", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake is known for talking about women that leave an impression or “mark” on him in his songs. In the “Find Your Love” music video, Drake makes the whole theme of the video about a woman who left her “mark” on him.\n\nhttp://youtu.be/Xyv4Bjja8yc\n\nLater, he did the same with his first big radio single, “Best I Ever Had” from his EP/Mixtape So Far Gone\n\nAnd from “Take Care”\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-zzP29emgpg&feature=share&list=UUQznUf1SjfDqx65hX3zRDiA", "annotation_id": "2088672", "url": "https://genius.com/2088672", "state": "accepted", "votes": 84, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Hold On", "line": "’Cause you’re a good girl and you know it I know exactly who you could be", "vault_lines": ["'Cause you're a good boy and you know it", "Oh, you're a good boy and you know it"], "meaning": "Deep down, this girl is good and Drake can see who she really is. He wants to bring that out of her.\n\nIn what is assuredly not a coincidence, Drake has had past real-life dealings with a certain good girl gone bad.\n\nDrake’s interest helping his romantic interests—like helping his girl realize her full potential—comes up a lot in his work. Whether he’s worrying about a girl being lonely in a new city or feels bad for the 26-and-older girls who can’t maintain friendships—Drake stays concerned. He’s also known to use the romantic interests in his songs as a way to talk to himself—something he mentioned in his interview with Elliot Wilson.", "annotation_id": "2071883", "url": "https://genius.com/2071883", "state": "accepted", "votes": 79, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Hold On", "line": "Just hold on, we’re going home Just hold on, we’re going home", "vault_lines": ["So just hold on, we're going home, home"], "meaning": "Drake, in an interview/Q&A with Elliott Wilson, explained that he didn’t have time for romance at this point in his life. He’s talking to himself and his romantic interest when he says—\"just hold on,“ asking for her patience. He continued:\n\nI’m so dedicated to this (music), I’m so commited to this room, that I can’t really offer somebody the nurturing and the dedication and the loyalty and the consistency that it takes to maintain a relationship.\n\nExplaination ends at 13:32\nhttp://youtu.be/zv0S7zMzAJA?t=11m32s\n\nAnd Drake’s home is pretty ballin'. I mean 7 bedrooms, 9 bathrooms and 7500 square feet!? Check it out!\n\nDrake told MTV that this song was meant “to be played at weddings in ten years.  Or [to be something that] people that are away from their families in the Army could listen to.”", "annotation_id": "2071674", "url": "https://genius.com/2071674", "state": "accepted", "votes": 115, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Hold On", "line": "’Cause you’re a good girl and you know it You act so different around me", "vault_lines": ["'Cause you're a good boy and you know it", "Oh, you're a good boy and you know it"], "meaning": "Drake, in an interview/Q&A with Elliott Wilson, explained in detail what this line means to him.\n\nI’ve seen potential in women that they (my friends) have told me were no good….But maybe I see something in them, maybe OUR relationship is exciting.\n\nExplanation ends at 13:32\nhttp://youtu.be/zv0S7zMzAJA?t=12m55s\n\nAlternatively, this “good girl” might feel she has to act a certain way around Drake, but he still sees her for what she really is, good. No need to play “bad”, he likes her as she is.", "annotation_id": "2071670", "url": "https://genius.com/2071670", "state": "accepted", "votes": 118, "second_sense": true, "clicked": true, "click_status": "open", "strength": "accepted"}
