{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Deuces (Remix)", "status": "done", "targets": 21, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Chris-brown-deuces-remix-lyrics", "genius_title": "Deuces (Remix)", "genius_id": 1414, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Deuces (Remix)", "line": "You should have a travel agent, ’cause you a trip You should make your own toilet tissue since you the shit", "vault_lines": ["You should have a travel agent, 'cause you a trip", "You should make your own toilet tissue since you the shit"], "meaning": "In his lines Kanye makes a play on words with the expressions “you’re a trip” and “you’re the shit”.\n\nTo be a trip is essentially a wild or crazy person, and Kanye uses the word “trip” to compare to a travel agent on a plane trip.\n\nTo be the shit it’s when people think you’re cool or when people respect you, but Kanye is literally comparing this girl to a piece of shit (also a term for being a bad person), so she should make her own toilet tissue to clean herself up,", "annotation_id": "36665586", "url": "https://genius.com/36665586", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Deuces (Remix)", "line": "[Verse 6: Rick Ross]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Compared to the other verses, Ross’s seems to be one of the only ones that focuses entirely on himself after the breakup that the song is about.\n\nDrake is saddened by the breakup, Kanye is angry, and 3 Stacks is thinking about it in a introspective way, while Ross is only thinking about his lifestyle, which parallels when Kanye said:\n\nYou gon' be hot a little while, I'ma be rich forever", "annotation_id": "36422864", "url": "https://genius.com/36422864", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Deuces (Remix)", "line": "Your wrist and fingers glisten, ice cold like Michigan", "vault_lines": ["Your wrist and fingers glisten, ice cold like Michigan"], "meaning": "Michigan is a pretty cold place, the lowest temperature ever recorded in Michigan was 51°F/-46°", "annotation_id": "36422809", "url": "https://genius.com/36422809", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Deuces (Remix)", "line": "All that bullshit’s for the birds You ain’t nothin’ but a vulture-ure-ure-ure", "vault_lines": ["All that bullshit's for the birds", "You ain't nothin' but a vulture-ure-ure-ure"], "meaning": "The difference between a bird and vulture is that vultures are more suited for hunting and or killing, sometimes taking food.\n\nBirds are less hunting based and as aggressive as vultures.\n\nChris is calling a girl in particular a vulture and other people birds, as if she’s different from everyone else, but in a negative way.", "annotation_id": "36422771", "url": "https://genius.com/36422771", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Deuces (Remix)", "line": "Now I’m ghost, baby, four-door Rizzy Royce", "vault_lines": ["Now I'm ghost, baby, four-door Rizzy Royce"], "meaning": "There is a car known as a Rolls-Royce Ghost, which Rocky indirectly references earlier in the song. It is a full-sized luxury car manufactured by Rolls-Royce Motor Cars. The “Ghost” nameplate, named in honour of the Silver Ghost, a car first produced in 1906.", "annotation_id": "35545468", "url": "https://genius.com/35545468", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Deuces (Remix)", "line": "I’m stupid, but I won’t get my drama on What I’m dealin’ with is too real for me to comment on", "vault_lines": ["I'm stupid, but I won't get my drama on", "What I'm dealin' with is too real for me to comment on"], "meaning": "Kanye acknowledges his past mistakes of speaking without thinking (ie. the Taylor Swift VMA incident), but he knows when to draw the line. What you hear him rapping about is nowhere close to what he deals with on a daily basis. He doesn’t put all his shit on blast, unlike other rappers who tell all their secrets and leave nothing up to the imagination.", "annotation_id": "35128738", "url": "https://genius.com/35128738", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Deuces (Remix)", "line": "It’s hard to throw up the deuces ’Cause when you know it’s juicy", "vault_lines": ["It's hard to throw up the deuces", "'Cause when you know it's juicy"], "meaning": "3000 professes that when ‘it’s juicy’ (i.e the sex is good, girl’s pussy game is tight), it’s hard to end a relationship or say goodbye to a partner. Andre finds himself making seemingly deep conscientious excuses, which connects to the next line.\n\nThe conscientious excuses is reminiscent of the ancient Chinese philosopher and writer Confucius, made famous for his one-line reflections on society and his surroundings.\n\n3000 realises there excuses are just a cover for him not wanting to let go of an exciting and addictive sexual nymph.", "annotation_id": "35128640", "url": "https://genius.com/35128640", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Deuces (Remix)", "line": "Accordin’ to my old bish, I be on some new ish She was on some old ish, now I got a new bish Think I give two ish? You ain’t gonna do ish", "vault_lines": ["I'm on some new shit", "Accordin' to my old bish, I be on some new ish", "She was on some old ish, now I got a new bish", "Think I give two ish? You ain't gonna do ish"], "meaning": "Apparently, F-A-B-O-L-O-U-S somewhat censors himself to begin his verse. Although if given the choice, the uncensored version would look like this:\n\nAccordin' to my old bitch, I be on some new shit\nShe was on some old shit, now I got a new bitch\nThink I give two shits? You ain’t gonna do shit", "annotation_id": "31809169", "url": "https://genius.com/31809169", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Deuces (Remix)", "line": "What it entails is hard to say like sellin’ seashells By the seashore", "vault_lines": ["What it entails is hard to say like sellin' seashells"], "meaning": "No doubt that break ups are difficult and can leave one tongue-tied.\n\nIt’s also a reference to the tongue-twister: She sells seashells by the seashore", "annotation_id": "21859228", "url": "https://genius.com/21859228", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Deuces (Remix)", "line": "But I’ll fuck you right, I will, I fuck you right, I will I’ll fuck you like no one has ever, ever made you feel", "vault_lines": ["But I'll fuck you right, I will, I fuck you right, I will", "I'll fuck you like no one has ever, ever made you feel"], "meaning": "This is a nod to Usher’s bridge lyric on his 1997 slow jam “Nice & Slow”, except Drake goes full-time explicit with it.\n\n\n\nNow tell me, do you wanna get freaky?\n‘Cause I’ll freak you right, I will\nI’ll freak you right, I will\nI’ll freak you like no one has ever, ever made you feel\n\nThis wasn’t the first time Usher’s work was mentioned on “Deuces”, but it makes it the 2nd time noted on the remix version.", "annotation_id": "21859196", "url": "https://genius.com/21859196", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Deuces (Remix)", "line": "K-K-K-K-K-K-Mac", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The intro incorporates the producer tag for California writer and producer Kevin McCall, who is most famous for his collaborations with main artist Chris Brown. They’ve worked together many times before, on tracks like November 2011’s “Strip” and June 2012’s “2012.”\n\nMcCall actually appeared on the first version of the track and rapped the third verse, along with handling production duties. His vocals are still present throughout the song, as well.", "annotation_id": "18526649", "url": "https://genius.com/18526649", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Deuces (Remix)", "line": "Go on, got me hot, smokin’ like a chimney", "vault_lines": ["Go on, got me hot, smokin' like a chimney"], "meaning": "Double Entendre:\n\n\nSmoking like a chimney could mean because he is so mad(hot) that he is smoking.\nThis could also mean that he is trying to cope with this stress by smoking a lot of weed.", "annotation_id": "1718365", "url": "https://genius.com/1718365", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Deuces (Remix)", "line": "Got a bucket full of ice, and a watch to go with it (Ugh!)", "vault_lines": ["Got a bucket full of ice, and a watch to go with it (Ugh!)"], "meaning": "#Triple entendre\n\n\n\n“Ice” can mean “diamonds”. He has a lot of jewels, consequently it’s a duty to possess a diamond watch to go with that status\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBut “ice” can also mean “crystal meth”.\n\n\n\n\n\nA “bucket” of meth represents much money, so it goes with a luxury watch\n\n\n\nOr just a bucket full of ice cubes with that watch !", "annotation_id": "1632230", "url": "https://genius.com/1632230", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Deuces (Remix)", "line": "R-O-Z-A-Y on the wall in that Hall of Fame (Maybach Music, Ugh!)", "vault_lines": ["R-O-Z-A-Y on the wall in that Hall of Fame (Maybach Music, Ugh!)"], "meaning": "“Rozay” : that’s my nickname\nB.M.F.\n\nIt comes from the Rick’s favorite champagne, “François de Rozay”, made in Rozay-en-Brie", "annotation_id": "1631030", "url": "https://genius.com/1631030", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Deuces (Remix)", "line": "So when you talk ’bout, “You know who”", "vault_lines": ["So when you talk 'bout, “You know who”"], "meaning": "Once again he is talking about Amber Rose. When he hears something about her, he’s not going to comment on it, because he’s learned to keep his mouth shut about such things. (Can anyone say, “Taylor Swift?”)\n\nJay Z had a similar line on his song “Takeover” about Nas' then girlfriend and mother of his first child, Carmen:\n\nBecause you-know-who did you-know-what with you-know-who\nBut let’s keep that between me and you (for now)", "annotation_id": "56030", "url": "https://genius.com/56030", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Deuces (Remix)", "line": "You start to sound like Confucius when makin’ up excuses", "vault_lines": ["You start to sound like Confucius when makin' up excuses"], "meaning": "Confucius was an ancient Chinese philosopher known for his inspirational quotes regarding personal and government morality. Example:\n\nAn oppressive government is more to be feared than a tiger\n\n\n\nNo word as to whether or not he could rap like Three Stacks, though.", "annotation_id": "51685", "url": "https://genius.com/51685", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Deuces (Remix)", "line": "I gotta find me a new locomotive, stop makin’ sad songs", "vault_lines": ["I gotta find me a new locomotive, stop makin' sad songs"], "meaning": "Andre feels he needs to find himself a new girl (or “locomotive”, carrying on from the Caboose metaphor used in the previous line), so that he can once again be happy and no longer feel the need to make sad songs.\n\nThe “stop making sad songs” part may well be a reference to Eddie Murphy’s character in Dreamgirls, at the point in which he stops singing sad R'n'B songs and starts rapping (something which Andre could well have parallels with considering how little rapping was on The Love Below).", "annotation_id": "49660", "url": "https://genius.com/49660", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Deuces (Remix)", "line": "[Verse 4: Kanye West]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This verse refers to his issues with his ex, Amber Rose.\n\nWest also featured on (and co-produced) “Down”, a song on Brown’s previous album Exclusive.\n\nThey later collaborate for the third time on West’s song, “Waves”.", "annotation_id": "49657", "url": "https://genius.com/49657", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Deuces (Remix)", "line": "And the hardest part about the fuckin’ business is mindin’ your own", "vault_lines": ["And the hardest part about the fuckin' business is mindin' your own"], "meaning": "A play on the phrase “mind your own business” that illustrates the difficulty of Drake’s situation. Drake’s talking about the “fucking” business, literally. The hardest part about sex is making sure you get the most out of it, not your partner.\n\nThis line is also talking about the entertainment business, the hardest part about it is to learn to mind your own business and stay focused on the music. Also since he’s famous he’s in the spotlight and everyone is concerned about the things hes doing and the girl he is dating, when they need to be focused on their own selves.", "annotation_id": "49650", "url": "https://genius.com/49650", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Deuces (Remix)", "line": "Miss me a little when I’m gone", "vault_lines": ["Know you gon'miss me a little when I'm gone"], "meaning": "Sampled directly from the Drake (feat. Lil Wayne) track “Miss Me”. Since there was no official acapella made, it explains why it sounds weird. Since Drake appears on this song, one wonders why Fab just didn’t ask him to use the original masters.", "annotation_id": "41664", "url": "https://genius.com/41664", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Deuces (Remix)", "line": "Jay finally got it through my head not to run my mouth", "vault_lines": ["Jay finally got it through my head not to run my mouth"], "meaning": "Jay Z has made a career out of being subliminal and for the most part composed about issues, however Kanye is the very opposite. Though Jay has probably offered his fair share of advice for Ye, this is probably about when Kanye was on the tonight show and Jay Leno asked what Kanye’s mom would think about the stunt he pulled when he took the mic from Taylor swift. Kanye seemed very emotional about the question.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=A6bgSITBrVQ&feature=player_embedded", "annotation_id": "41662", "url": "https://genius.com/41662", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
