{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Grind", "line": "Trey Songz, the street’s Usher", "vault_lines": ["What up to Denik Rusha and Bei Major, Trey Songz, the street's Usher"], "meaning": "Both Trey Songz and Usher, like Drake, carry very similar themes in their music, mainly regarding their love and relationships with women. Drake has also previously stated his respect and admiration for both Trey and Usher.\n\nOn Drake’s 2013 release Nothing Was the Same, Drake also mentions Trey, but on a different context.\n\nThen she start telling me how I’ll never be as big as Trey Songz, boy was she wrong", "annotation_id": "1877156", "url": "https://genius.com/1877156", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "The Grind", "line": "I’m flyer than Aladdin on a carpet Saw A Whole New World when I made my profits", "vault_lines": ["I'm flyer than Aladdin on a carpet", "Saw A Whole New World when I made my profits"], "meaning": "A nice play on words. Saint Nick is comparing himself to a young boy coming up like Aladdin, except he’s flyer than a prince on his carpet. Also when the money came in he saw A Whole New World as in the popular song from the Orignal Aladdin Disney  Movie.\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=player_detailpage&v=-kl4hJ4j48s#t=86s", "annotation_id": "1544698", "url": "https://genius.com/1544698", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
