{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Ass so fat need a lap dance", "vault_lines": ["Ass so fat need a lap dance"], "meaning": "Referencing the hook from the 2011 Tyga song, “Lap Dance”.\n\nBenzo, batman, thick ho, lap dance\nAss so fat need a lap dance\nAss so fat I need a lap dance", "annotation_id": "17747764", "url": "https://genius.com/17747764", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I’m 5'5\" but I could 6-9", "vault_lines": ["I’m 5'5\" but I could 6-9"], "meaning": "Wayne makes a play on numbers. While he is only the average male height he is still tall enough to 69. 69 is a sexual position that involves the couple laying down into a 69 position where they are facing each other crouches performing oral sex on each other, this would obviously be easier if one was taller but Wayne can still do it well despite only being 5'5.\n\nWeezy has rapped about being successful despite not being tall is previous songs, such as Rick Ross’s 2008 song “Luxury Tax”:\n\nThey said I couldn’t play football, I was too small\nThey said I couldn’t play basketball, I wasn’t tall\nThey said I couldn’t play baseball at all\nAnd now every day of my life, I ball", "annotation_id": "14100496", "url": "https://genius.com/14100496", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Motherfucker I’m on my skateboard Watch me do a trick, ho", "vault_lines": ["Motherfucker I'm on my skateboard", "Watch me do a trick, ho"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is a avid lover of skateboarding. He even has his own private skate park in his house.\n\nIn an interview with ESPN he shows off his skating prowess and explains:\n\nThe moment I decided I wanted to skate I was watching Alex Miller a lot of T.V like I didn’t even know you could do this, I didn’t even know you could jump off stairs and I didn’t know you could skateboard at this age, where’s you parents?\n\nHe also explains:\n\nYou know in music we have restrictions, we have limits that you can’t do this because you want to be considered this or you can’t do this cause you’re gonna be considered that. In skateboarding you can just be free. What I can get from skateboarding that I can’t get from music is natural satisfaction.\n\nOn the cover of his Dedication 4 mixtape he is depicted holding a skateboard.", "annotation_id": "14100436", "url": "https://genius.com/14100436", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Shout out to Uncle Luke (Huh)", "vault_lines": ["Shout out to the infernos", "Shout out to Uncle Luke (Huh)"], "meaning": "“Pop That” samples the 1992 track “I Wanna Rock (Doo Doo Brown)” by rapper Uncle Luke. Ross shouts him out to credit the owner of the original sample.", "annotation_id": "14072571", "url": "https://genius.com/14072571", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Bitches know I’m that nigga, talkin’ four-door Bugatti", "vault_lines": ["Bitches know I'm that nigga, talkin' four-door Bugatti"], "meaning": "Bugatti is a high-end French car manufacturer popular among rappers. Ross is an avid car collector (you can view his collection here) he owns, several Maybachs, Lamborghinis, BMWs, and of course Bugattis.  His love for cars is so great he even named his Maybach Music Label after the Maybach brand.\n\n\n\nA few months prior to this song’s release in January, 2013  Ross also appeared on the popular Ace Hood song “Bugatti” which also featured Future.", "annotation_id": "14072232", "url": "https://genius.com/14072232", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Dropped Take Care, bought a mothafuckin’ crib", "vault_lines": ["Dropped Take Care, bought a mothafuckin' crib"], "meaning": "Drake is referencing his second studio album, Take Care which was released on the 15th of November, 2011 through Cash Money Records.\n\nThe sophomore album sold over 631,000 copies in its first week and in August of 2015 it was reported that the album had sold over 4,000,000 copies.\n\nThe album has gone 4X platinum in the U.S due to its very high sale numbers.", "annotation_id": "13232699", "url": "https://genius.com/13232699", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Bitch, I ball like two eyelids", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I ball like two eyelids"], "meaning": "Here, Wayne uses the homophone of “I” and “eye” to describe how much he balls. According to his net worth, he definitely has the ballin' aspect covered, much like an eyelid covers an eyeball. Wayne goes on to use other ocular metaphors later in his career.\n\nIf you don’t see what I’m sayin'\nI give your ass a fuckin' eye exam", "annotation_id": "11665026", "url": "https://genius.com/11665026", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "It’s Weezy F, fuck hoes", "vault_lines": ["It's Weezy F, fuck hoes"], "meaning": "One of Lil Wayne’s many nicknames is Weezy F Baby. In this case the F is for “fuck hoes.” It’s been used for “finisher”, “fuck you', and various others.", "annotation_id": "1894698", "url": "https://genius.com/1894698", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
