{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Got a Brinks truck in my pocket (Pocket)", "vault_lines": ["Got a Brinks truck in my pocket (Pocket)"], "meaning": "A Brinks truck is one that transports large amounts of money to/from places. Essentially, he has a lot of money in his possession.", "annotation_id": "1045116", "url": "https://genius.com/1045116", "state": "accepted", "votes": 45, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "And, nigga, you’s a square And I will twist you like in a Rubik’s", "vault_lines": ["And, nigga, you's a square", "And I will twist you like in a Rubik's"], "meaning": "A Rubik’s Cube is a square puzzle. The goal is to twist in order to match all the colors on every side. Wayne will fuck you up to look like this:\n\n\n\nHe has also used the twist/Rubik’s pun in Birdman’s song “Fire Flame.” .", "annotation_id": "1024491", "url": "https://genius.com/1024491", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Car’s tinted like Barack", "vault_lines": ["Car's tinted like Barack"], "meaning": "His windows are tinted super dark black just like the President’s windows so no one can see inside.\n\n\n\nThis line may also be referring to the colour of Barack Obama’s skin, meaning he is not fully black but has a ‘tinted’ skin colour, shaded white.", "annotation_id": "964136", "url": "https://genius.com/964136", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Sorry that’s a habit, smoke a spliff and then I vanish", "vault_lines": ["Sorry that's a habit, smoke a spliff and then I vanish"], "meaning": "Rozay hits it and quits it: smoke’s a bitch’s weed, and then displays his disappearing act.\n\n\n\nOne could even say that he kept a “magician theme” over the last few lines: rabbits, disappearing, smoke?", "annotation_id": "944305", "url": "https://genius.com/944305", "state": "pending", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Shout out my bitches too (Huh) We the 2 Live Crew Two for me, two for you (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["Shout out to the infernos", "Shout out my bitches too (Huh)", "We the 2 Live Crew", "Two for me, two for you (Woo)"], "meaning": "Ross puns on the name of his Miami rap forbears, 2 Live Crew.  The Crew’s head honcho was Luther Campbell, a.k.a. Uncle Luke, whose solo work is sampled in this very song", "annotation_id": "927296", "url": "https://genius.com/927296", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "What you twerkin’ with?", "vault_lines": ["Work, work, work, what you twerkin' with? (Bounce)", "Show me what you twerkin' with", "What you twerkin' with?"], "meaning": "Twerkin' is dancing that involves showing off your rear…ah hell, just go and watch some\n\nBesides being about twerking, it’s a play on words: “What you working with?” has commonly been used in rap songs to inquire about how well a woman can move her woman parts. French is asking her a question, knowing that the answer will come in the form of POPPING THAT.", "annotation_id": "927285", "url": "https://genius.com/927285", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Bitch! Stop talkin’ that shit And suck a nigga dick for some Trukfit", "vault_lines": ["Bitch! Stop talkin' that shit", "And suck a nigga dick for some Trukfit", "And, nigga, you's a square"], "meaning": "Wayne is referencing one of the most famous chants in all of bounce music; the New Orleans-created subgenre where Cash Money Records first made its name.  He has called back to this chant on previous occasions. This time, Wayne uses it to reference his own clothing line. (The original is “suck a nigga dick for an outfit.”)", "annotation_id": "926171", "url": "https://genius.com/926171", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I am rich like a bitch", "vault_lines": ["I am rich like a bitch"], "meaning": "This line makes no sense, partly because it was first said by Lil B. Weezy is infamously known for biting lyrics occasionally, so this shouldn’t be too shocking.\n\nLil B said this line in his song “Pretty Bitch” at the 2:48 mark.\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vAYrMJWvC44\n\nLil B and Lil Wayne worked together on Wayne’s “Grove Street Party” which is on Weezy’s Sorry 4 the Wait mixtape. Lil B spit a very…based verse, and it may have impressed Wayne to the point of using one of his lines.\n\nMost likey, this is actually a reference to “I’m RICHHHHH BITCH”, the classic saying from Chappelle Show.\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kMFJBd40Awo", "annotation_id": "852007", "url": "https://genius.com/852007", "state": "accepted", "votes": -3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I’m a beast, I’m off the leash", "vault_lines": ["I'm a beast, I'm off the leash"], "meaning": "Very reminiscent of Wayne’s verse on We Takin' Over:\n\nI am the beast, feed me rappers or feed me beats  I’m untamed, I need a leash", "annotation_id": "844634", "url": "https://genius.com/844634", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "It’s Truk the world It’s Truk yo girl", "vault_lines": ["It's Truk the world", "It's Truk yo girl"], "meaning": "Wayne likes to use the word “Truck” instead of “fuck” as the slogan for his clothing brand Trukfit.\n\nHe uses it the exact same way in “My Homies Still.”", "annotation_id": "844073", "url": "https://genius.com/844073", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "YMCM beat that pussy up, stop playin’", "vault_lines": ["Pop that pussy, pussy", "YMCM beat that pussy up, stop playin'"], "meaning": "Young Money Cash Money Billionaires (YMCMB) is Wayne’s label.\n\n\n\nHe plays off the last letter in “YMCMB”. Instead of stating the “B” he uses a word that starts with the letter “b”. .", "annotation_id": "843982", "url": "https://genius.com/843982", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
