{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I’m the life of the party, let’s get these hoes on the Molly", "vault_lines": ["I'm the life of the party, let's get these hoes on the Molly"], "meaning": "Molly is a Pure form of MDMA (ecstasy), usually a free powder or in capsules. Oftentimes MDMA is sold as molly. Should be white in color (when it’s pure) but is more often beige or yellow-brown, and sometimes brown or rarely gray.\n\nIronically, Ross would later get in serious trouble for rapping about giving a girl molly.", "annotation_id": "842998", "url": "https://genius.com/842998", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Don’t stop, pop that, don’t stop Pop that, pop that, pop that", "vault_lines": ["Don't stop, pop that, don't stop", "Pop that, pop that, pop that", "Pop that pussy, pussy", "Pop that, pop that"], "meaning": "Here is where the sample came from: Uncle Luke – “I Wanna Rock (Doo Doo Brown).” Classic.\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jzHeR-PTVtY&feature=results_video&playnext=1&list=PL21B2E18688750B93", "annotation_id": "842483", "url": "https://genius.com/842483", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Money ain’t a thing but a chicken wing", "vault_lines": ["Money ain't a thing but a chicken wing"], "meaning": "“Ain’t no thing but a chicken wing” is southern slang that has been around for a while. It even found it’s way into the Outkast song “Ain’t No Thang” where it can be heard in the chorus. .", "annotation_id": "842474", "url": "https://genius.com/842474", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "That’s gangsta: Al Capone", "vault_lines": ["That’s gangsta: Al Capone"], "meaning": "Al Capone is an old, Prohibition-era gangster who led a crime syndicate.\n\n\n\nFUN FACT: Al Capone’s physical and mental health deteriorated under the effects of neurosyphilis. Guess he really did “fuck a bitch and [be] gone.”", "annotation_id": "842311", "url": "https://genius.com/842311", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I make that pussy spit like Bone I’m talkin’ ’bout bone, bone, bone bone", "vault_lines": ["Pop that pussy, pussy", "I make that pussy spit like Bone", "I'm talkin' 'bout bone, bone, bone bone"], "meaning": "A shout out to the Bone Thugs-n-Harmony, saying he makes girls come like how Bone Thugs rap (VERY fast). “Spitting” is his way of saying “squirting.”\n\n\n\nHe also said “bone” 5 times: one for each member of the group.", "annotation_id": "842299", "url": "https://genius.com/842299", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Then beat that pussy like Klitschko", "vault_lines": ["Pop that pussy, pussy", "Then beat that pussy like Klitschko"], "meaning": "He beats it up like the boxing Klitschko brothers.\n\n\n\nAlso, Wayne is playing on the sentence, using ‘pussy’ and ‘KLIT(clit)schko’.\n\nFun Fact: Wladimir Klitschko’s partner Hayden Panettiere is much smaller than him, so with that size difference, you can imagine him beating it up.", "annotation_id": "842277", "url": "https://genius.com/842277", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I’m fuckin’ with French, excuse my French", "vault_lines": ["I'm fuckin' with French, excuse my French"], "meaning": "A play on the phrase “excuse my French” which basically just means “sorry for cursing” (since he just said “fuckin' with French). Excuse My French is also the name of French Montana’s debut album.", "annotation_id": "842265", "url": "https://genius.com/842265", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Film it, film it, this bitch want me to film it Ballin’, ballin’ like I play for New England", "vault_lines": ["Film it, film it, this bitch want me to film it", "Ballin', ballin' like I play for New England"], "meaning": "In their 2007 season, the New England Patriots started their season off with some controversy. In Week 2 head coach Bill Belichick and the Patriots were penalized by the NFL for their involvement in the videotaping of opponents' defensive signals from an unauthorized location in their Week 1 game against the New York Jets, referred to in the press as Spygate.\n\nThis line may also be referring to a horny female wanting Rick Ross to video record their sexual encounter.\n\nIronically, the New England Patriots NFL team has the best record in the league since 2001, and is the second most valuable team in the league according to Forbes and in those particular terms, Rozay does his fare share of winning.", "annotation_id": "842260", "url": "https://genius.com/842260", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Local club in my city, I fell in love with a stripper", "vault_lines": ["Local club in my city, I fell in love with a stripper"], "meaning": "In January, Ross threw his birthday party at Amnesia in South Beach.\n\nLike T-Pain, he’s in love with a stripperrr", "annotation_id": "842252", "url": "https://genius.com/842252", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I’m in that white ghost chasin’ Pac-Man Hundred out the lot,", "vault_lines": ["I'm in that white ghost chasin' Pac-Man", "Hundred out the lot,"], "meaning": "Rolls-Royce Phantoms, (in this case a $100.000 one,) have the nickname “Ghosts”, but they actually make a Ghost which is new to the RR lineup. French may be referring to either one.\n\n\n\nIn the arcade game Pac-Man, ghosts chase PacMan around the game. Although there is technically no white ghost, he is referring to the ghosts in general", "annotation_id": "842192", "url": "https://genius.com/842192", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I’m Young Papi, Champagne", "vault_lines": ["I'm Young Papi, Champagne"], "meaning": "One of Drake’s well known monikers (and Instagram name), especially around the ova circle is “Champagne Papi” which refers to his extensive love for wine and champagne.", "annotation_id": "840125", "url": "https://genius.com/840125", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Money comin’, money goin’, ain’t like you could take it with you (Alright)", "vault_lines": ["Money comin', money goin', ain't like you could take it with you (Alright)"], "meaning": "Drake and his crew are making money but spending it too because, like the line from the musical says, you can’t take it with you (when you die)\n\nDrake might be Jewish, but this is also a lesson from the New Testament, 1 Timothy 6:7\n\nFor we brought nothing into this world, and it is certain we can carry nothing out.\n\nPotentially a response to Pusha T, who said in Exodus 23:1 wealth don’t buy health, drake is telling him he would rather spend it he can’t take it with him", "annotation_id": "840094", "url": "https://genius.com/840094", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Greystone, twenty bottles that’s all me", "vault_lines": ["Greystone, twenty bottles that's all me"], "meaning": "Drake is referring to the extremely popular Greystone Manor nightclub in Hollywood. He is usually there on Sundays as it’s a hip-hop night. Proof: http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UXgQ4BFGNH4", "annotation_id": "839759", "url": "https://genius.com/839759", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "One of my closest dawgs got three kids and they all three But we always been that type of crew that been good without a plan B, so", "vault_lines": ["One of my closest dawgs got three kids and they all three", "But we always been that type of crew that been good without a plan B, so"], "meaning": "Drake’s crew has never been the type to need a backup plan, while also throwing in the Plan B line relating to his homie and his kids.\n\nNotice the slick homophone of “been good” and “be in good” – as in they get shit done without a back-up plan, the same way they be in “good” (pussy) without the morning-after pill.", "annotation_id": "839720", "url": "https://genius.com/839720", "state": "accepted", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Only thing you got is some years on me Man, fuck you and your time difference", "vault_lines": ["Only thing you got is some years on me", "Man, fuck you and your time difference"], "meaning": "Seems like lines directed at Pusha T, considering Pusha had some words for Drake recently. Also, Pusha is 35, while Drake is 25.\n\nDrake is also referencing Pusha T’s “I Don’t Like” verse, when Pusha says “Dope money, coke money/Hublot, my watch better.”\n\nBut besides Pusha, this is a possible shot at a few rappers older than him or have been/were rapping before him (i.e. DMX, Fabulous, Common, Ludacris). .\n\nNote: Pusha might’ve shot back at Drake with this line from “Blocka”. Both lines use “fuck you and your…”\n\nI ball hard and you bench ride, so fuck you and yo' bassline!", "annotation_id": "839716", "url": "https://genius.com/839716", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "Gettin cheddar packs like K.D., OKC that’s player shit", "vault_lines": ["Gettin cheddar packs like K.D., OKC that's player shit"], "meaning": "Drake tweeted this line not too long ago.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/Drake/status/209186783970340865\n\nDrizzy gets cheddar (money) like KD which stands for both Kraft Dinner, a brand of macaroni and cheese, and NBA player Kevin Durant. OKC is Durant’s team, Oklahoma City, and also means “Okay, see that’s player shit”.\n\nThe Oklahoma City reference does not come out of the blue.  Drake and his entourage shut down an Oklahoma City night club after massive amounts of marijuana smoke was seen coming out of the VIP section. Drake & Co escaped unscathed, however, the night club owner is suing for damages.\n\nKevin Durant is loving the exposure: https://twitter.com/KDTrey5/status/244635730364731392\n\nIt should also note that calling Kraft Mac and Cheese “KD” is a Canadian thing.\n\nAlso Kevin Durant and Drake had the same net worth at the time.", "annotation_id": "839696", "url": "https://genius.com/839696", "state": "accepted", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "We don’t dress alike, we don’t rap alike I shine different, I rhyme different", "vault_lines": ["We don't dress alike, we don't rap alike", "I shine different, I rhyme different"], "meaning": "Drake has often been accused of stealing the “Supa Dupa flow” style that he used early in his career.", "annotation_id": "839690", "url": "https://genius.com/839690", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I hope you pussy niggas hatin’ never make a nickel (Right)", "vault_lines": ["I hope you pussy niggas hatin' never make a nickel (Right)"], "meaning": "Drake is taking a subliminal shot at numerous rappers dissing him right now (Pusha-T, Fabolous, and all others )\n\nAlso many believe that some rappers will create beef with another rapper to promote an album. Drake believes that Common did this with “Sweet” (before they squashed their beef) as he stated on “Stay Schemin”\n\nThis is also a play on the expression ‘I hope you never make a dime’. By saying nickel instead of dime, Drake shows his true dislike of his haters.", "annotation_id": "839682", "url": "https://genius.com/839682", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "OVO, that’s major shit, Toronto with me, that’s mayor shit", "vault_lines": ["OVO, that's major shit, Toronto with me, that's mayor shit"], "meaning": "OVO (Drake’s music group October’s Very Own) is up and rising and becoming a major part of his career.\n\nToronto is his hometown and he will never forget that. Watch out, Rob Ford!", "annotation_id": "839679", "url": "https://genius.com/839679", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I’m about bein’ single, seein’ double, makin’ triple (Right)", "vault_lines": ["I'm about bein' single, seein' double, makin' triple (Right)"], "meaning": "Drake is all about no strings attached relationships (I mean, you only live once right?), getting drunk, and making three times as much money. Single, double, triple. Get it?", "annotation_id": "839673", "url": "https://genius.com/839673", "state": "accepted", "votes": 66, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Pop That", "line": "I go by the name Lil Tunechi", "vault_lines": ["I go by the name Lil Tunechi"], "meaning": "One of Lil Waynes many nicknames, ‘@LilTunechi’ is also his Twitter handle. It’s comprised of ‘Tune’ which was a nickname given to Wayne by his grandmother, and ‘chi’ which was added by Wayne to make it sound like ‘Gucci’, the clothing brand.", "annotation_id": "839651", "url": "https://genius.com/839651", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "status": "done", "targets": 28, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-gold-roses-lyrics", "genius_title": "Gold Roses", "genius_id": 4720076, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "“I gotta get the most of everything” is the axis on which it sit and twirls", "vault_lines": ["\"I gotta get the most of everything\" is the axis on which it sit and twirls"], "meaning": "The axis is the center that something spins around.\nHe’s saying his entire ambition is built around one core belief: “I have to get the most out of life.”\nThat means making the most money, having the biggest success, and not settling for less.", "annotation_id": "40874394", "url": "https://genius.com/40874394", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Lot of lives lost, but I never panicked Lot of lines crossed, I never did a Xanny", "vault_lines": ["Lot of lives lost, but I never panicked", "Lot of lines crossed, I never did a Xanny"], "meaning": "Ross remains calm during during a period of conflict, where death occurs regularly. This may allude to his childhood in Carol City, a poverty-stricken neighborhood in California.\n\nThe second bar is a double entendre with Ross comparing figurative “lines ” being crossed, as in someone escalating a situation , with “lines” of cocaine.\n\n This leads to his assertion of never doing a “Xanny”, a shortened term used to describe Xanax (alprazolam), a drug often used to relieve anxiety.", "annotation_id": "38336485", "url": "https://genius.com/38336485", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "‘Cause they’ll get to poppin’ out of place like they double jointed", "vault_lines": ["'Cause they'll get to poppin' out of place like they double jointed"], "meaning": "People that are double jointed experience bones popping out irregularly.", "annotation_id": "29608371", "url": "https://genius.com/29608371", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "And what I got for sale just sit on the scale Triple beam dream", "vault_lines": ["And what I got for sale just sit on the scale"], "meaning": "Ross has a song featuring Nas called Triple Beam Dreams, which is basically about growing up dreaming of being a rich drug dealer, when in reality Ross made those dreams come true but through a different method.", "annotation_id": "24054753", "url": "https://genius.com/24054753", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Paid the cost to be the boss wasn’t even my most expensive purchase", "vault_lines": ["Paid the cost to be the boss wasn't even my most expensive purchase"], "meaning": "A popular phrase.\n“Pay the cost to be the boss.” – Meaning that you have to sacrifice time, likeness and anything potential to be the leading figure in your own niche.\nDrake is claiming that although he is the boss, everything sacrificed for becoming his own boss doesn’t match whatever he’s spent in real life (or even the biggest sacrifice he made.)", "annotation_id": "20828400", "url": "https://genius.com/20828400", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "(Maybach Music)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Maybach Music Group (abbreviated as MMG) is an American record label founded in 2009 by Rick Ross. A number of solo albums and three compilation albums have been released under the label.", "annotation_id": "18512522", "url": "https://genius.com/18512522", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Before I’m gone outta this place, yeah Put some flowers in my vase, won’t you? Let me know that I did okay, yeah Don’t wait ’til some other day, no, no They love to wait ’til it’s too late, it’s too late", "vault_lines": ["You made me this way, yeah", "Before I'm gone outta this place, yeah", "Put some flowers in my vase, won't you?", "Let me know that I did okay, yeah", "Don't wait 'til some other day, no, no", "They love to wait 'til it's too late, it's too late", "They love to wait 'til it's too late, too late (Ayy)"], "meaning": "Speaking to Megan Ryte on Hot 97, Ross gave an explanation for the “Gold Roses” song title, saying:\n\nMe and him (Drake) were just conversating, and you know – Nipsey came up in our conversation, and we were just saying.. I wish he had an idea of the impact that he had and made on these streets, I pray he just had an idea.\n\nThis then led the conversation to a point where Drake stated:\n\nMan, I hope I can smell my flowers whilst I’m here.\n\nWhat Drake means by this is that whilst he’s still alive, he wants his fans and supporters to give him his dues and respects for the work he has put in before it’s too late.", "annotation_id": "17722069", "url": "https://genius.com/17722069", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Fly you out to Cannes, ménages with bitches", "vault_lines": ["Fly you out to Cannes, ménages with bitches"], "meaning": "Ross is known to take vacation in Cannes, France. He mentioned it before on his August 2012 track, “Diced Pineapples,” which is another collaboration with Drake:\n\nI'ma trip go to Cannes, France to catch a flick\n\nThe word “ménage” is short for the French word “Ménage à Trois,” which is three people having sex together.", "annotation_id": "17705247", "url": "https://genius.com/17705247", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Ten years in and y’all yet to hear my most impressive verses", "vault_lines": ["Ten years in and y'all yet to hear my most impressive verses"], "meaning": "While Drake released his first mixtape, Room for Improvement, well over a decade ago in 2006, it was 2009’s So Far Gone that put Drake on the Hip-Hop radar and well into mainstream success.\n\nDespite having 4 Grammy awards, having eight songs reach septuple platinum or better, and being the highest-certified digital singles artist ever in the US, Drizzy still believes his best is yet to come.", "annotation_id": "17703579", "url": "https://genius.com/17703579", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Still a part of shorty even if we’ve been livin’ apart", "vault_lines": ["Still a part of shorty even if we've been livin' apart"], "meaning": "The “shorty” in this line may be Drake’s son, Adonis Graham, who was born on October 11th, 2017, which is also the same month as Drake’s birthday. Adonis lives in France with his mom, Sophie Brussaux.", "annotation_id": "17690650", "url": "https://genius.com/17690650", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Tales about me are like corridos in Culiacán", "vault_lines": ["Tales about me are like corridos in Culiacán"], "meaning": "The Corrido is a Mexican musical genre developed in the 18th century, whose origins date back to the Spanish middle ages. One of its most popular subgenres is the Narcocorrido, songs that focus on drug smugglers, the lyrics refer to particular events and include real dates and places and also tend to speak approvingly of illegal activities, mainly drug trafficking. While Culiacán is the capital of the Mexican state, Sinaloa and is also one of the places where this genre is most heard and produced.\n\nDrake is likely comparing his legacy to notorious drug lords like, Joaquín Guzmán Loera, AKA El Chapo, Miguel Ángel Félix Gallardo or Rafael Caro Quintero, and the stories told of their legacies.", "annotation_id": "17690047", "url": "https://genius.com/17690047", "state": "accepted", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "A hundred room mansion but I felt abandoned", "vault_lines": ["A hundred room mansion but I felt abandoned"], "meaning": "In January 2014, Ross bought a 109 room mansion in Georgia from former heavyweight boxing champion, Evander Holyfield for $5.8 million.", "annotation_id": "17684539", "url": "https://genius.com/17684539", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Coming to America, really the set I’ll let your soul glow, I’m keepin’ you wet", "vault_lines": ["Coming to America, really the set", "I'll let your soul glow, I'm keepin' you wet"], "meaning": "Soul Glo is a fictional hair product from the 1988 movie, Coming to America. The product is applied to hair, particularly Jheri curl, in order to keep it shiny and moisturized.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o4AiHmhJGzw", "annotation_id": "17679787", "url": "https://genius.com/17679787", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "She got a thing for Chanel vintage that dropped before she could speak English", "vault_lines": ["She got a thing for Chanel vintage that dropped before she could speak English"], "meaning": "Chanel is a high fashion house founded by Coco Chanel in 1909 in Paris, France.\n\n\n\nDrake seems to imply that his romantic interest prefers Chanel accessories that were released before she was born.", "annotation_id": "17677669", "url": "https://genius.com/17677669", "state": "accepted", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Postcard from Grace Bay, sendin’ my distant regards", "vault_lines": ["Postcard from Grace Bay, sendin' my distant regards"], "meaning": "Grace Bay is a beach in Turks and Caicos. It has won countless awards for being the World’s best beach and accommodation destination.", "annotation_id": "17676551", "url": "https://genius.com/17676551", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "I’m all for spiritual liftin’, but I don’t fly Spirit", "vault_lines": ["I'm all for spiritual liftin', but I don't fly Spirit"], "meaning": "Spirit Airlines has consistently been ranked amongst the worst airline carriers in the world, primarily due to it charging for carry-on baggage, frequent cancellations and minimal leg room. In 2017, Spirit was named “the worst airline in America” by Consumeraffairs.com.\n\nIn May 2019, Drake was gifted a Boeing 767 plane from Canadian airline Cargojet, which is estimated to be worth around $200 million. That same month, Drake gave a tour of his plane.", "annotation_id": "17675696", "url": "https://genius.com/17675696", "state": "accepted", "votes": 55, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "I know they love to rock a check, but who gon’ do it really? Really?", "vault_lines": ["I know they love to rock a check, but who gon' do it really? Really?"], "meaning": "The Nike logo, called the “swoosh,” resembles a checkmark symbol, and one of their slogans is “Just Do It.”\n\nDrake has been signed to Nike’s Jordan Brand since December 2013, and has released six official collaboration sneakers.", "annotation_id": "17674753", "url": "https://genius.com/17674753", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "The one that’s rebuildin’ schools and feedin’ the homeless", "vault_lines": ["The one that's rebuildin' schools and feedin' the homeless"], "meaning": "In the January 2018 music video for “God’s Plan”, Drake uses the $1 million budget in Miami to pay people’s college tuition, or buy them clothes or groceries. Drake’s philanthropy also extends to his hometown of Toronto, where he partnered with the Raptors and donated $1 million to Welcome Toronto, a basketball, fashion and arts initiative.", "annotation_id": "17674392", "url": "https://genius.com/17674392", "state": "accepted", "votes": 37, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Roxx’ll do you filthy for me soon as I give him the nod Meanin’ he’ll blast for me like puttin’ the 6 with the God", "vault_lines": ["Roxx'll do you filthy for me soon as I give him the nod", "Meanin' he'll blast for me like puttin' the 6 with the God"], "meaning": "Johnny Roxx is a member of Drake’s crew and his personal trainer. Driz shouted him out before on September 2015’s “Change Locations”:\n\nRoxx got a case but they get off again\n\nAccording to Roxx, he and Drake have been friends for over 10 years.\n\n\n\nDrake pronounces ‘blast for me’ similar to blasphemy. He follows-up with his popular 6God nickname, which was birthed around the time he released his February 2015 album, If You’re Reading This It’s Too Late.", "annotation_id": "17674136", "url": "https://genius.com/17674136", "state": "accepted", "votes": 53, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Hop on a float to show the city the one they appointed", "vault_lines": ["Hop on a float to show the city the one they appointed", ", a buck on the shades"], "meaning": "Drake celebrated the Toronto Raptors' 2019 NBA championship by riding around the city on the team’s parade float. He also dropped two songs to commemorate the win, including ”Money in the Grave” featuring Rick Ross and Omertà.", "annotation_id": "17674119", "url": "https://genius.com/17674119", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Sashimi from Saito, you know that man two Michelin Star", "vault_lines": ["Sashimi from Saito, you know that man two Michelin Star"], "meaning": "Masaki Saito is the founder, owner and lead executive chef at Sushi Masaki Saito. He relocated his restaurant to Toronto from New York in February 2019. Sashimi is usually a thinly sliced, raw fish.\n\nDrake has a history of rapping about his taste for luxury food and restaurants. For example, on March 2013’s “5AM in Toronto” he says:\n\nEatin' like I’m seated at Swish, Sotto, and Joso’s\n\nMichelin Stars are a mark of quality awarded to a restaurant, or individual chefs, by anonymous reviewers. According to trip savvy, a two rating means:\n\nA restaurant worth a detour, indicating excellent cuisine and skillfully and carefully crafted dishes of outstanding quality\n\nInterestingly, there is a chef named Takashi Saito, who is the head chef at Sushi Saito in Tokyo, which is ranked number 26 of the 50 best restaurants in Asia, and holds a Michelin rating of 3.", "annotation_id": "17674002", "url": "https://genius.com/17674002", "state": "accepted", "votes": 45, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Mentally I’m already on next year, that’s some 20/20 clear vision", "vault_lines": ["Mentally I'm already on next year, that's some 20/20 clear vision"], "meaning": "“20/20 vision” or ‘normal vision,’ is a term used in ophthalmology, where a person can see clearly up to 20 feet away.\n\n\n\nAdditionally, since “Gold Roses” dropped in 2019, Drake’s making a slick play on next year being 2020. It highlights how Drizzy’s always plotting his next move and future success, a mindset that’s played a major role in keeping him at the top.", "annotation_id": "17673990", "url": "https://genius.com/17673990", "state": "accepted", "votes": 68, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Chanel in the mail, FedEx from Pharrell", "vault_lines": ["Chanel in the mail, FedEx from Pharrell"], "meaning": "In March 2019, Pharrell Williams collaborated with Chanel and released his iteration of Chanel glasses, sweatshirts, t-shirts, hoodies and tote bags. Some of the pieces can be seen in a GQ interview, and he also posted a snippet of the collection to his Instagram.\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/BvUXUIdBqxz/?utm_source=ig_embed", "annotation_id": "17673951", "url": "https://genius.com/17673951", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "I was nominated, never won a Grammy", "vault_lines": ["I was nominated, never won a Grammy"], "meaning": "As of this song’s release, Ross has been nominated for four Grammys:\n\n\nDJ Khaled’s “I’m On One” — Best Rap Collaboration (2012)\n\nGod Forgives, I Don’t — Best Rap Album (2013)\nChris Brown’s “New Flame” — Best R&B Song (2015)\n\n“Purple Lamborghini” — Best Song Written for Visual Media (2017)\n\n\n\nDrake, on the other hand, has been nominated a total of 42 times. The 6 God has won 4 awards, with his most recent being January 2018’s “God’s Plan.”\n\nOn November 20th, ‘Gold Roses’ itself was nominated for a Grammy.", "annotation_id": "17673946", "url": "https://genius.com/17673946", "state": "accepted", "votes": 63, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "All smiles, Kevin Durant trials Had to blow it on the court, I must have blew a milli’ I’m walkin’ on all charges, that’s my new Achilles", "vault_lines": ["Had to blow it on the court, I must have blew a milli'", "I'm walkin' on all charges, that's my new Achilles", ", a buck on the shades", "All smiles, Kevin Durant trials"], "meaning": "Drake uses wordplay to compare his legal court battles to Kevin Durant’s “trials” and tribulations on the basketball court. The former Golden State Warriors forward ruptured his right Achilles’ tendon during Game 5 of the 2019 NBA Finals. Drake attended the game courtside and was seen consoling KD as he walked off the court from the injury.\n\n\n\nDrake may also be playing on the Greek hero, Achilles, who was virtually invincible until an arrow struck his achilles heel.\n\nDrake has battled numerous court cases, from his July 2011 case where Ericka Lee claimed she was not compensated for helping write June 2011’s “Marvin’s Room,” to a 2017 case where Layla Lace falsely accused him of raping and impregnating her. Drake acknowledges the uphill challenge facing Durant, who is currently recovering from surgery and aiming to make a strong return back to the NBA.", "annotation_id": "17673930", "url": "https://genius.com/17673930", "state": "accepted", "votes": 88, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Tanenbaum know the logo on the jersey, it’s gettin’ purchased", "vault_lines": ["Tanenbaum know the logo on the jersey, it's gettin' purchased"], "meaning": "Drake intends to purchase the sponsorship rights to the NBA’s Toronto Raptors jerseys when the team’s current deal with Sun Life Financial is over. He also gives a shout out to Raptors co-owner Larry Tanenbaum.\n\nDrake and October’s Very Own won the logo spot on the Raptors training jerseys during the team’s 2019 championship season:", "annotation_id": "17673910", "url": "https://genius.com/17673910", "state": "accepted", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Vision wasn’t mine, told my niggas the vision was ours", "vault_lines": ["Vision wasn't mine, told my niggas the vision was ours"], "meaning": "Drake has chosen to work closely with his DJ, Future The Prince, and his childhood friend, manager, and producer, Oliver El-Khatib. Together, they run the October’s Very Own clothing line and label and have established lucrative deals with Nike’s Jordan Brand, the Toronto Raptors, Apple Music, and in July 2019, Sirius Radio.\n\nDrake mentions both Future and Oliver on June 2018’s ”Nonstop”:\n\nFuture took the business and ran it for me\nI let Ollie take the owl, told him brand it for me\n\n\n\nThis could also be a play on Canadian R&B duo dvsn (pronounced “division”), who signed to OVO in February 2016.", "annotation_id": "17673801", "url": "https://genius.com/17673801", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gold Roses", "line": "Point blank period, like a City Girl and then I bring it back to 50 world", "vault_lines": ["Point blank period, like a City Girl and then I bring it back to 50 world"], "meaning": "“Point blank period” is a popular phrase used to signify the end of an argument. Incidentally, the term “Periodt” developed into a meme when rap group, City Girls, whose vocals are featured on Drake’s June 2018 track, “In My Feelings,” dropped their debut mixtape Period in May 2018, which included a track of the same name. The first usage of “Periodt” on Twitter dates back to May 2009.\n\n50 is Drake’s friend “Fif,” whose real name is Anthony Soares—he was shot to death in September 2017. Drake plans to take his money to 50 in the afterlife, perhaps by being buried with it, as the title of his June 2019 track with Rick Ross, “Money In The Grave,” suggests.", "annotation_id": "17673769", "url": "https://genius.com/17673769", "state": "accepted", "votes": 53, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "status": "done", "targets": 31, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Migos-versace-remix-lyrics", "genius_title": "Versace (Remix)", "genius_id": 176872, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "My blunts is fat as Rasputia", "vault_lines": ["My blunts is fat as Rasputia"], "meaning": "Offset compares the weight of his blunt to Eddie Murphy’s plus sized character in Norbit", "annotation_id": "39677318", "url": "https://genius.com/39677318", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "Look at the watch, it blow hot like some Taki", "vault_lines": ["Look at the watch, it blow hot like some Taki"], "meaning": "Takeoff’s watch is fire, just like a bag of Taki’s, which are also hot. This line is very similar to the line Offset used later on Travis Scott’s posse cut,“Sloppy Toppy”\n\nShe a hottie like a bag of Takis", "annotation_id": "12573175", "url": "https://genius.com/12573175", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "You copped the Honda, I copped the Mazi You smoke the mid, I smoke exotic", "vault_lines": ["You copped the Honda, I copped the Mazi", "You smoke the mid, I smoke exotic"], "meaning": "Continuing the theme of the opening bar, Takeoff expresses how he is buying the big brands and luxury items at the top while others are stuck on the low-mid level.\n\nHonda is an affordable Japanese car manufacturer, which is usually considered as cost-effective middle-class cars, while Takeoff is driving much more expensive Italian Maserati (‘Mazi’) whips.\n\n\n\nSimilarly, while others are smoking bad-middle level weed, Takeoff is consuming high quality exotic sticky, which most likely comes from places like Kingston or Cali.", "annotation_id": "12274512", "url": "https://genius.com/12274512", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "You’d think I’m Egyptian, this gold on my body", "vault_lines": ["You'd think I'm Egyptian, this gold on my body"], "meaning": "https://players.brightcove.net/4863540648001/HklmClHkx_default/index.html?videoId=5236088418001", "annotation_id": "3277858", "url": "https://genius.com/3277858", "state": "verified", "votes": 142, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "[Chorus: Quavo]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The hook heard ‘round world. Notice how well the three syllables of Versace meld with the Migos triplet-centric flows, amd vice versa. After this, everyone from Drake (The Language) to Kanye (Sanctified) to Meek Mill (Ooh Kill 'Em) started jocking the “Migos” flow, although that’s not really their flow, per se…", "annotation_id": "3072060", "url": "https://genius.com/3072060", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "Versace, Versace Medusa head on me like I’m Illuminati (Versace!)", "vault_lines": ["Versace, Versace, Versace, Versace (Versace!)", "Versace, Versace Versace, Versace Versace", "Medusa head on me like I'm Illuminati (Versace!)"], "meaning": "Versace’s logo is the head of Medusa from Greek mythology (who had snakes for hair and whose gaze turned onlookers to stone). Since supposed symbols of the Illuminati often incorporate classical imagery and indicators of wealth, a Versace Medusa head would be very appropriate for Drake and Migos to wear if they were members of the Illuminati.\n\nFurthermore, several other famous rappers are accused as being associated with the Illuminati (especially Jay Z and Kanye West), so they are subtly holding themselves to their level of celebrity by making similar pretensions about themselves.", "annotation_id": "2638695", "url": "https://genius.com/2638695", "state": "accepted", "votes": 59, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "Versace my clothes while I’m sellin’ them bows", "vault_lines": ["Versace, Versace, Versace, Versace (Versace!)", "Versace, Versace Versace, Versace Versace", "Versace my clothes while I'm sellin' them bows"], "meaning": "Offset is saying he is wearing Versace shirt, shoes, and socks while he is on the street selling (bows) pounds of drugs. Most likely high grade marijuana, or possibly kilos of cocaine or crack.\nThis explanation was brought to you by versacemysocks from the comment section\n\nGotta pay for the shirts some type of way\n\n\n\nLong-sleeve BAROCCO CAMOUFLAGE SILK SHIRT", "annotation_id": "2609403", "url": "https://genius.com/2609403", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "Bricks by the boat, overload", "vault_lines": ["Bricks by the boat, overload"], "meaning": "Bricks most likely refers to cocaine here, since it was mentioned earlier in Quavo’s verse.\n\n\n\nOffset continues the “rich as hell” theme by saying he can afford copious amounts of narcotics to match his luxurious lifestyle.", "annotation_id": "1935937", "url": "https://genius.com/1935937", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "In a striped shirt like I’m Tony the Tiger", "vault_lines": ["In a striped shirt like I’m Tony the Tiger"], "meaning": "Tony the Tiger is the Frosted Flakes mascot, who appears on most of their commercials to promote their product. The animated tiger sports the same stripes from head-to-toe. Takeoff is saying that he rocks matching Versace shirts and shoes.", "annotation_id": "1913879", "url": "https://genius.com/1913879", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "I’m beatin’ the pot, call me Michael", "vault_lines": ["I'm beatin' the pot, call me Michael"], "meaning": "Takeoff knows he can whip crack, alluding to “Beat It” the mega-hit by Michael Jackson\n\n\n\n\nJust beat it, beat it, beat it, beat it\n\nYou wanna stay alive, better do what you can So beat it, just beat it\n\n\n\n\n\nThis line is similar to a line from Offset on “Trenchez.”\n\nI beat the pot up like I’m Cassius", "annotation_id": "1911286", "url": "https://genius.com/1911286", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "You can do Truey, I do it Versace", "vault_lines": ["Versace, Versace, Versace, Versace (Versace!)", "Versace, Versace Versace, Versace Versace", "You can do Truey, I do it Versace"], "meaning": "While others cop True Religion (‘Truey’) Takeoff outclasses them with his Versace and other luxury brands.", "annotation_id": "1904451", "url": "https://genius.com/1904451", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "I think I’m the don but no Rocco", "vault_lines": ["I think I'm the don but no Rocco"], "meaning": "A don is the leader of a mafia family, whose authority can only be challenged by the commission. Rocco was a high ranking member in the Falconne crime family in Mafia, a third person shooter game.\n\n\n\nEssentially, he’s saying he’s the boss of the rap game.\n\nOffset could also be referring to Rocko (the rapper), who named himself Rocko Da Don.", "annotation_id": "1903068", "url": "https://genius.com/1903068", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "Them blue and white diamonds, they look like the Pistons", "vault_lines": ["Them blue and white diamonds, they look like the Pistons"], "meaning": "The Detroit Pistons primary and secondary colors are blue and white.", "annotation_id": "1902669", "url": "https://genius.com/1902669", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "Versace, Versace I love it, Versace, the top of my Audi", "vault_lines": ["Versace, Versace, Versace, Versace (Versace!)", "Versace, Versace Versace, Versace Versace", "I love it, Versace, the top of my Audi"], "meaning": "Money, money, everywhere. Luxury style and a luxury car for a luxurious person living a luxurious lifestyle. What more could you ask for?", "annotation_id": "1901144", "url": "https://genius.com/1901144", "state": "accepted", "votes": 45, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "Just make sure that you got a back up plan ’Cause that shit might come in handy (go, go!)", "vault_lines": ["Just make sure that you got a back up plan", "'Cause that shit might come in handy (go, go!)"], "meaning": "Drake seems to be hyping up his upcoming album, Nothing Was the Same. Set to be released on September 17th and mentioned in the next line, Drake implies here that the album will completely blow away expectations and predictions (previous line “I got the world like ‘What the fuck is he planning?”).\n\nThe line could also allude to Drake’s plans to blow his competition out of the water with this album, forcing the need for back up plans or even a change in career for the competition. Albums set to be released in the third quarter along with Drake’s include big names such as Jay-Z, Chris Brown, Ace Hood, Big Sean, and Justin Timberlake.", "annotation_id": "1900648", "url": "https://genius.com/1900648", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "I been so quiet, I got the world like “What the fuck is he plannin’?” (What?)", "vault_lines": ["I been so quiet, I got the world like", "\"What the fuck is he plannin'?\" (What?)"], "meaning": "Drake hasn’t put forth a lot of information about his current project. He released “Started From the Bottom” and “5 AM in Toronto”, which sparked up talk about his new album. Before those releases, and ever since then, everyone has been talking about Nothing Was the Same, trying to figure out what Drake is going to do next.", "annotation_id": "1900474", "url": "https://genius.com/1900474", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "Try to take my sack Better run with it, nigga, don’t fumble", "vault_lines": ["Try to take my sack", "Better run with it, nigga, don't fumble"], "meaning": "Football wordplay.\n\n“Sack” is any defensive player tackling the QB behind the line of scrimmage.\n\n\n\n“Fumble” occurs when a player loses control of the football before being downed or scoring.\n\n\n\nIn this case, sack means a bag of weed. If you steal his stash, you better not drop it because he’s going to come after you.", "annotation_id": "1899828", "url": "https://genius.com/1899828", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "Versace, Versace, Versace, Versace Versace, Versace, Versace, Versace Versace, Versace Versace, Versace Versace Versace, Versace Versace, Versace Versace", "vault_lines": ["The pillows Versace, the sheets are Versace", "That's Migos and Drake at the Versace store", "Versace, Versace, Versace, Versace (Versace!)", "Versace, Versace Versace, Versace Versace", "Versace, my neck and my wrist is so sloppy", "Medusa head on me like I'm Illuminati (Versace!)", "I love it, Versace, the top of my Audi", "Shoes and shirt Versace", "I told that bitch \"Versace\"", "You can do Truey, I do it Versace", "Come in my room, my sheet Versace", "When I go to sleep I dream Versace", "Look at my closet, Versace, Versace", "King of Versace, Medusa my wifey", "My car is Versace, I got stripes on my Mazi", "Codeine sippin', Versace, I'm grippin'", "Versace my clothes while I'm sellin' them bows", "Versace take over, it took out my soul"], "meaning": "Versace is a famous clothing line founded by Gianni Versace in 1978, and first boutique founded in 2000, which many rappers wear and drop in lyrics in various songs.\n\n\n\nThe repetition implies the over saturation of the designer in the fashion world and a comment on the world’s obsession with having to constantly be considered in style.", "annotation_id": "1899433", "url": "https://genius.com/1899433", "state": "accepted", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "My plug, he John Gotti He give me the ducks, I know that they’re mighty", "vault_lines": ["My plug, he John Gotti", "He give me the ducks, I know that they're mighty"], "meaning": "Here, Quavo is calling his drug connect “John Gotti,” a notorious crime lord who throughout his active crime career sold a large amount of cocaine, heroin and other narcotics.\n\n\n\nHe gives him 12 bricks like John Gotti would and he knows that they’re great.\n\n\n\n“He give me the ducks, I know that they’re mighty” is also a reference to the Disney hockey movie, The Mighty Ducks.", "annotation_id": "1899420", "url": "https://genius.com/1899420", "state": "accepted", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "We stay at the mansion when we in Miami", "vault_lines": ["We stay at the mansion when we in Miami"], "meaning": "Drake frequents Miami, he even hangs with the Heat from time to time.\n\n\n\nHe doesn’t stay at any regular hotel when he’s in Miami, instead he stays at the Versace mansion on Ocean Drive right in the heart of South Beach, which is worth 125 million bucks.\n\n\n\nAdditionally, there is a nightclub that goes by the name “Mansion” that is located in Miami.\n\n\n\nRegardless of which one Drizzy is talking about, he only goes to the finest places.", "annotation_id": "1897411", "url": "https://genius.com/1897411", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "Word in New York is the Dyckman and Heights girls are callin’ me Papi (woo, woo)", "vault_lines": ["Word in New York is the Dyckman and Heights girls are callin' me Papi (woo, woo)"], "meaning": "Drake is talking about the girls that live in uptown Manhattan, the Washington Heights area which has a huge Dominican population.\n\nJust like he says in “The Motto”\n\nGo Uptown, New York City, bitch\nThem Spanish girls love me like I’m Aventura\n\n\n\n The famous Dominican music band.", "annotation_id": "1897144", "url": "https://genius.com/1897144", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "I’m tryna give Halle Berry a baby and no one can stop me (smash!)", "vault_lines": ["I'm tryna give Halle Berry a baby and no one can stop me (smash!)"], "meaning": "Halle is definitely worth giving a baby to.\n\nHowever, the French Canadian model Gabriel Aubry already gave her a baby. The two met at a Versace shoot in 2005, and Berry gave birth in 2008. The model’s surname is Aubry and he’s Canadian. Notice any similarities between him and Drake?\n\n\n\nWhat complicates matters even more is that she’s currently pregnant with child number two.", "annotation_id": "1897136", "url": "https://genius.com/1897136", "state": "accepted", "votes": 88, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "This for my niggas that call up Fernando to move a piano (brr, brr, brr!)", "vault_lines": ["This for my niggas that call up Fernando to move a piano (brr, brr, brr!)"], "meaning": "Shouting out people in the streets selling large amounts of cocaine. They call up their connect Fernando for the drugs.\n\n1 kilogram of cocaine is also known as a key.\n\nMost piano’s have 88 keys.\n\nThat is a huge amount of cocaine.\n\n\n\nLet me just take this further…\n\nThe average going price for a kilo of cocaine varies between $15,000 to $25,000 depending on where you are.\n\n15,000 * 88 = 1,320,000\n\nto\n\n25.000 * 88 = 2,200,000\n\nThat is a huge amount of money.\n\nOn “Da Rockwilder”, Redman says:\n\nYou ship off keys, and we ship Grand Pianos", "annotation_id": "1896916", "url": "https://genius.com/1896916", "state": "accepted", "votes": 53, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "This year I’m eatin’ your food And my table got so many plates on it (so many!) (damn!)", "vault_lines": ["This year I'm eatin' your food", "And my table got so many plates on it (so many!) (damn!)"], "meaning": "“Eating your food” is a metaphor for taking your money and preventing you from reaching success. By saying that he has a lot of plates on his table, he means he’s taking everybody’s money out here.\n\nHaving started the OVO Sound label, saying “my table has so many plates on it” may be suggesting that he has a lot of mouths to feed, so he’s coming for your food even harder.\n\nThe second part, (“my table got so many plates on it”), could also mean that he has the plates, (or the food), of so many other rappers on HIS table, which agrees with the first part where he implies that he is taking their money.", "annotation_id": "1896657", "url": "https://genius.com/1896657", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "I just won a Grammy (woo!)", "vault_lines": ["I just won a Grammy (woo!)"], "meaning": "Drake has one Grammy and has been nominated thirteen times. He won his first and only Grammy for Best Rap Album, Take Care.\n\n\n\nHe also drank shots out of Grammy Award with OVO crew in Promo of his album:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7c_iaA0xC9A", "annotation_id": "1896616", "url": "https://genius.com/1896616", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "Born in Toronto but sometimes I feel like Atlanta adopted us (go!)", "vault_lines": ["Born in Toronto but sometimes I feel like Atlanta adopted us (go!)"], "meaning": "Drake always says he’s felt like he’s from Atlanta. And Houston. And Vegas.\n\nHOUSTALANTAVEGAS\n\nHis apprentices, Migos, also hail from Atlanta.", "annotation_id": "1896354", "url": "https://genius.com/1896354", "state": "accepted", "votes": 44, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "I think I’m sellin’ a million first week Man, I guess I’m a optimist (milli!)", "vault_lines": ["I think I'm sellin' a million first week", "Man, I guess I'm a optimist (milli!)"], "meaning": "An optimist is someone who always looks on the bright side and feels positive about forthcoming events.\nDrake believes that his album will sell a million copies in its first week, but this is said tongue in cheek as he then suggests that maybe he’s being a bit too optimistic.\n\nThis dream would end up coming true for Drake as, in 2016, Views sold 1.2 million units in its first week.", "annotation_id": "1896350", "url": "https://genius.com/1896350", "state": "accepted", "votes": 67, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "Niggas be wantin’ a verse for a verse But man, that’s not a swap to me (nah!)", "vault_lines": ["Niggas be wantin' a verse for a verse", "But man, that's not a swap to me (nah!)"], "meaning": "Many rappers will swap verses with each other as a way to promote both artists and expand their fan bases, whilst also avoiding large feature costs. However, Drake believes his rhymes are so superior that swapping his bars for another artist’s lyrics is just not a good deal for him.", "annotation_id": "1896335", "url": "https://genius.com/1896335", "state": "accepted", "votes": 77, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "The album is comin’ September Just wait on it (just wait on it!)", "vault_lines": ["the album is comin' September", "Just wait on it (just wait on it!)"], "meaning": "Drake’s new album, Nothing Was The Same, was originally supposed to drop on September 17th, but was pushed back one week to September 24.\nhttps://twitter.com/Drake/statuses/370362629958537217\nhttp://vimeo.com/68930597\n\nThis is also a reference to the Migos song Just Wait On It. Takeoff’s adlib is especially reminiscent of this.", "annotation_id": "1896326", "url": "https://genius.com/1896326", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "Started a label,", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake started a label called “October’s Very Own” in 2012, and he has already signed various artists such as PARTYNEXTDOOR and ILoveMakonnen that are currently getting a lot of attention, thanks to Drake’s support.", "annotation_id": "1896324", "url": "https://genius.com/1896324", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Versace (Remix)", "line": "This is a gated community Please get the fuck off the property (gate!)", "vault_lines": ["This is a gated community", "Please get the fuck off the property (gate!)"], "meaning": "Drake recently purchased this $9 million mansion in LA, in the Hidden Hills gated community; a home to multiple celebrities.\n\n\n\nAs he said in Meek Mill’s “Amen:”\n\nI just bought me a crib so big it came with a moat\nFor niggas jumping the fence I hope you niggas can float", "annotation_id": "1896313", "url": "https://genius.com/1896313", "state": "accepted", "votes": 72, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "status": "done", "targets": 38, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/The-game-100-lyrics", "genius_title": "100", "genius_id": 2136824, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "[Verse 1: The Game]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "In the first verse, Game tells a story of being asked to run up on Drake and harm him (he doesn’t say who’s doing the asking). Of course, Game refuses to do that, and instead chooses to protect Drake and his whole October’s Very Own crew and give him some advice about the musical industry. This verse has a father-son vibe—Game gives Drake advice the same way Jay Z did to him on “Light Up”.", "annotation_id": "7633780", "url": "https://genius.com/7633780", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "Make a real nigga wanna give his life to God like, “Here it go”", "vault_lines": ["Make a real nigga wanna give his life to God like, \"Here it go\"", "Always be a real nigga"], "meaning": "The amount of The Game’s niggas that got killed hurts him. It makes him want to give his life to God; with no fuss. Just say “Here it go,” (‘it’ being his life) with no hesitation. I guess in his heart, he’ll know he will go to heaven if his life is given to God. This is similar to the lines from My Life.\n\nTake me away from the hood, like a state penitentiary\nTake me away from the hood, in a casket or a Bentley\nTake me away, like I overdosed on cocaine", "annotation_id": "7175990", "url": "https://genius.com/7175990", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "See, I know how it feel to be platinum-plus", "vault_lines": ["See, I know how it feel to be platinum-plus"], "meaning": "Game can empathise with Drake’s position as both rappers have multiple platinum albums (selling over a million copies) including their debuts The Documentary and Thank Me Later.\n\nThis also refers to their similar lyrical capabilities as “Platinum Plus” is a track by Hip Hop legend Big L. The track itself consists of multi-syllabic rhyming coated with an array of word play.", "annotation_id": "7175286", "url": "https://genius.com/7175286", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "You niggas don’t feel me though That was on Suge’s watch, I’ll take Suge’s watch", "vault_lines": ["You niggas don't feel me though", "That was on Suge's watch, I'll take Suge's watch"], "meaning": "Though 2Pac and The Notorious B.I.G. were the biggest names in hip-hop, Suge Knight’s attention didn’t do them any favors. Both were killed despite their “friendship” with Knight. Suge was with sitting in the car with Tupac when he was shot. Some said Suge told Tupac to take off his bulletproof vest not long before.\n\nGame has had his differences with Suge. He previously addressed Suge on his song My Bitch.", "annotation_id": "7172652", "url": "https://genius.com/7172652", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "Thank me later, thanks for nothin’, thanks for bluffin’ Thank you so, so much for wearin’ your true colors To every single fuckin’ function", "vault_lines": ["Thank me later, thanks for nothin', thanks for bluffin'", "Thank you so, so much for wearin' your true colors", "To every single fuckin' function"], "meaning": "While Drake feels like he’s always been straight with people, as you can tell by his sarcastic tone, it seems everyone else didn’t get the memo.\n\n\n\nThank Me Later is the name of Drake’s debut studio album; his third was Nothing was the Same. Drake suggests we should be thankful for that one too (we are!).", "annotation_id": "7169648", "url": "https://genius.com/7169648", "state": "accepted", "votes": 80, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "Niggas is jealous of you, so they try to wrap you up Tax you up, but it’s OVO/Blood Money", "vault_lines": ["Niggas is jealous of you, so they try to wrap you up", "Tax you up, but it's OVO/Blood Money"], "meaning": "OVO is the Canadian based collaboration group that includes rapper Drake. OVO stands for October’s Very Own as Drake was born October 24. Drake, Majid Jordan, PARTYNEXTDOOR, and Nineteen85 are all signed to OVOSound, but the crew spans more than just the signed artists.\n\nGame’s newly formed record label is “Blood Money\" and has also been on a tour named Blood Money.\n\nGame’s flow here is also reminiscent of Tupac’s famous lines in “Changes”:\n\n“Don’t let ‘em jack you up, back you up\nCrack you up and pimp-smack you up”", "annotation_id": "7169353", "url": "https://genius.com/7169353", "state": "accepted", "votes": 44, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "Just walkin’ ’round the crib like, ”Why a nigga can’t live? Get this money, fuck these bitches though?”", "vault_lines": ["Just walkin' 'round the crib like, \"Why a nigga can't live?", "Get this money, fuck these bitches though?\""], "meaning": "Game nods at two classics in quick succession. First he gets ins a reference to Hov’s iconic “Can I Live,” then gives us a riff on the Junior M.A.F.I.A. line from “Get Money”:\n\nFuck bitches, get money\nFuck niggas, get money", "annotation_id": "7169208", "url": "https://genius.com/7169208", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "My circle got so small that it’s a period, sayin’ to myself", "vault_lines": ["My circle got so small that it's a period, sayin' to myself"], "meaning": "Drake’s circle of friends has progressively gotten smaller as he succeeds. He has made his circle so small that it is the equivalent of a period (full stop), which is a pretty small circle to say the least.", "annotation_id": "7168367", "url": "https://genius.com/7168367", "state": "accepted", "votes": 69, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "Shit was so simple when Henchman was out He had a young nigga right there with Meech", "vault_lines": ["Shit was so simple when Henchman was out", "He had a young nigga right there with Meech"], "meaning": "This is a reference to the infamous James “Jimmy Henchman” Rosemond, who managed the record label Czar Entertainment, which Game was signed to for a while. Henchmen was Game’s manager during much of the beef with 50 Cent, and Game is reminiscent of a simpler time when he (Henchman) wasn’t in jail and friends and enemies were far more clear-cut.\n\n\n\nHenchman has been arrested numerous times on murder-for-hire and drug charges. In 2013 he was sentenced to life in prison for the murder of Lodi Mack, a friend of Tony Yayo, who is an associate and friend of 50 Cent. Yikes.", "annotation_id": "7168009", "url": "https://genius.com/7168009", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "Thinkin’ ’bout the beef like: “We can pass these mothafuckin’ straps like a physical”", "vault_lines": ["Thinkin' 'bout the beef like:", "\"We can pass these mothafuckin' straps like a physical\""], "meaning": "When you get a physical check-up at the doctor, one of the things they do is check your blood pressure. To do this they use a literal strap with a machine attached as seen below.\n\n\n\nGame and his homies will hand each other the strap (guns) during a beef like a doctor would handle the medical instrument.", "annotation_id": "7167876", "url": "https://genius.com/7167876", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "L.A. niggas be the craziest, these niggas do some shady shit", "vault_lines": ["L.A. niggas be the craziest, these niggas do some shady shit", "L.A. niggas be the craziest, yeah, one hunnid", "L.A., L.A. niggas be the craziest, one hunnid"], "meaning": "Game alludes to Treach from Naughty By Nature, who on their song “Craziest” rapped:\n\nLA Niggas be the craziest\n\nLos Angeles, California has some of the harshest hoods in America. There are cities such as Compton, Crenshaw, Watts, Inglewood, Long Beach and more.", "annotation_id": "7167708", "url": "https://genius.com/7167708", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "Do a nigga four favors, when you can’t do the fifth How soon they forget?", "vault_lines": ["Do a nigga four favors, when you can't do the fifth", "How soon they forget?"], "meaning": "These lyrics may be aimed at G-Unit. “Four favors” refers to the original members—50 Cent, Lloyd Banks, Young Buck, and Tony Yayo—Game was the “fifth.”\n\nGame is likely also making a play on the Fifth Amendment of the U.S. Constitution, which gives citizens the right to decline questions in an investigation or trial that might incriminate themselves.\n\nGame feels like he’s done a lot of favors for 50 and the Unit, but when he wanted to do his own thing or didn’t want to do something they asked, they forgot all he had already done.", "annotation_id": "7167601", "url": "https://genius.com/7167601", "state": "accepted", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "Heard about the shit with Diddy So I came through to vest you up", "vault_lines": ["Heard about the shit with Diddy", "So I came through to vest you up"], "meaning": "Game had heard about Drake’s fight with Diddy in Miami over the “0-100” beat, but instead of confronting Drake like he was instructed, he came through and offered to protect him. He would act as Drake’s bulletproof vest, rebounding any physical shots or mental hits from haters.", "annotation_id": "7167532", "url": "https://genius.com/7167532", "state": "accepted", "votes": 84, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "I got L.A. unified You better off committin’ suicide, teachers ain’t testin’ us", "vault_lines": ["I got L.A. unified", "You better off committin' suicide, teachers ain't testin' us"], "meaning": "LAUSD stands for L.A Unified School District – Game has L.A unified, like school districts. So instead of trying to off somebody, you might as well off yourself!\n\nSince L.A is unified under Game and Drake, no one wants to test them, not even the OG’s (teachers).", "annotation_id": "7167499", "url": "https://genius.com/7167499", "state": "accepted", "votes": 37, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "Niggas called me to set you up Want me to come and wet you up ’Cause you a out of town nigga like Biggie", "vault_lines": ["Niggas called me to set you up", "Want me to come and wet you up", "'Cause you a out of town nigga like Biggie"], "meaning": "Biggie was shot on March 9, 1997 in a drive-by shooting in Los Angeles. Just like The Notorious B.I.G., Drake’s an out of towner in L.A.\n\nIt seems Game got a call from one of his homeboys who wanted to put a hit on Drake. How true this is remains unclear.\n\nGame has a nice homage to Gangstarr with the “set you up / wet you up” couplet. On “Moment of Truth,” Guru said:\n\nThe same sheisty cats that you hang with, and do your thang with\nCould set you up and wet you up, nigga peep the language", "annotation_id": "7167396", "url": "https://genius.com/7167396", "state": "accepted", "votes": 75, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "Can’t think, so you roll up that indigo Stressin’ while drivin’ down Figuero’", "vault_lines": ["Can't think, so you roll up that indigo", "Stressin' while drivin' down Figuero'"], "meaning": "Indigo is a type of marijuana when held over a piece of black construction paper and slightly tapped, crystals fall from it, making the black construction paper sparkle.\n\nFigueroa Street is a street in Los Angeles County, California named for General José Figueroa.This street services some popular locations. As a matter of fact, ScHoolboy Q was raised around Figueroa.\n\nGame is driving down in California streets, and stressing, so he is smoking on high-potent marijuana strains, which could also help him to think.", "annotation_id": "7167356", "url": "https://genius.com/7167356", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "I would have all of your fans If I didn’t go pop and I stayed on some conscious shit", "vault_lines": ["If I didn't have money, respect and accomplishments", "I would have all of your fans", "If I didn't go pop and I stayed on some conscious shit"], "meaning": "I got love for you all but I’m tryna murder you niggas/Trying to make sure your core fans never heard of you niggas\n\nTwo years after “Control”, and perhaps the most socially conscious rap record in twenty years, is Drake still going at Kendrick Lamar?\n\nWhile Drizzy’s earlier mixtapes like Room For Improvement and Comeback Season would fit snugly into a conscious rapper’s body of work, he went mainstream after becoming popular with tracks like “Started From The Bottom”, “Take Care”, and “Best I Ever Had”. By moving towards a pop-orientated sound, Drake gained thousands of fans, but also allowed Kendrick to carve a niche of his own with little credible competition.", "annotation_id": "7167288", "url": "https://genius.com/7167288", "state": "accepted", "votes": 136, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "How are niggas s’posed to love you niggas? Heart beatin’ fast when I dap and when I hug you niggas Drake told me not to trust you niggas Your energy off, you’re finicky, I rush you niggas", "vault_lines": ["How are niggas s'posed to love you niggas?", "Heart beatin' fast when I dap and when I hug you niggas", "Drake told me not to trust you niggas", "Your energy off, you're finicky, I rush you niggas"], "meaning": "Game realizes the friends you never totally trust aren’t friends at all. He recalls advice from Dr. Dre to help guide Drake through his battle with Cash Money Records. This also serves as a warning to anyone who might put on a façades to deceive either of them.\n\nDrake said something similar on his song “Energy”:\n\nI got enemies, got a lot of enemies\nGot a lot of people tryna drain me of my energy\nThey tryna take the wave from a nigga", "annotation_id": "7167271", "url": "https://genius.com/7167271", "state": "accepted", "votes": 36, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "Might go to Jamaica, disappear again", "vault_lines": ["Might go to Jamaica, disappear again"], "meaning": "Drizzy reportedly recorded some tracks from his debut album “Thank Me Later” in Jamaica and performed numerous times on the Caribbean island. He recently took part in OVO affiliate and Jamaican dancehall star Popcaan’s “Unruly Prayer” music video.\n\nI swear that we made it, sell out that ting, I’m the king in Jamaica", "annotation_id": "7167264", "url": "https://genius.com/7167264", "state": "accepted", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "Got a nigga confused, but why a nigga gotta choose? Don’t even matter, dawg, cause I’ma always be a real nigga Always be a real nigga I never learned how to be nothin’ but a real nigga", "vault_lines": ["I got L.A. unified", "Got a nigga confused, but why a nigga gotta choose?", "Don't even matter, dawg, cause I'ma always be a real nigga", "Always be a real nigga", "I never learned how to be nothin' but a real nigga"], "meaning": "‘Being Real’ has played a quite significant role in every individual not only hip-hop, but in the outside world as well. Game is stating he’ll be real no matter the situation. He won’t choose between Birdman (Baby) or Lil Wayne because he finds it unnecessary. Regardless of a situation, he’ll always be a real nigga between his two companions.", "annotation_id": "7167242", "url": "https://genius.com/7167242", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "Blowin’ kush clouds until his ghost is in my Ghost, damn", "vault_lines": ["Blowin' kush clouds until his ghost is in my Ghost, damn"], "meaning": "Game is so high from smoking marijuana that he hallucinates and sees 4 Cent’s ghost in his car. This may be a nod to Method Man and Redman’s 2001 stoner classic How High—their characters use a dead friend’s ashes to fertilize their weed and then whenever they smoke it his ghost appears.\n\nHe’s also referring to the Rolls-Royce Ghost and alludes to its name.", "annotation_id": "7167209", "url": "https://genius.com/7167209", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "40, I’m fucked up", "vault_lines": ["40, I'm fucked up"], "meaning": "Since Drake is featured on the song it’s possible that Noah “40” Shebib, one of his main producers, was also present in the studio, when the song was recorded. After Game reminisced about some of his downs and the overall melancholy tone of the song, showing his mental instabliity. Of course he could also be  drunk and/or high.", "annotation_id": "7167204", "url": "https://genius.com/7167204", "state": "accepted", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "I’m in the club every time that they play the competition If they even play the competition and I seen the response they get Yeah, nobody’s even hearin’ it, on top of the pyramid", "vault_lines": ["I'm in the club every time that they play the competition", "If they even play the competition and I seen the response they get", "Yeah, nobody's even hearin' it, on top of the pyramid"], "meaning": "Drake doesn’t mind hearing music by another artist in the club because he sees how people react. When his shit plays, the club is lit – when someone else’s song comes on, not so much. This happened to Chris Brown earlier in 2015 when the DJ dropped Drake’s “Energy” at a party he was hosting.\n\nDuring an interview with The Fader in June 2015, Drake said he wasn’t competing with anyone at his level, but rather he’s “worried about the kid who’s sitting in his house, that wants to be better than me and everyone else. That’s who I’m competing with.”", "annotation_id": "7167186", "url": "https://genius.com/7167186", "state": "accepted", "votes": 63, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "Real nigga shit Other night at your crib, it was like me, Black, 40, OB We just sittin’ there talkin’ ’bout life Played some beats, but I forgot to tell you one thing", "vault_lines": ["Other night at your crib, it was like me, Black, 40, OB", "We just sittin' there talkin' 'bout life", "Played some beats, but I forgot to tell you one thing"], "meaning": "Game’s intro calls up memories of a casual studio session with Drake and his OVO Crew mates Noah ‘40’ Shebib and OB O'Brien. During this session, Game bestowed some knowledge on the younger rapper but apparently forgot to warn him about Cash Money Records not financially supporting their artists.", "annotation_id": "7167162", "url": "https://genius.com/7167162", "state": "accepted", "votes": 78, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "I would have so many friends If I didn’t have money, respect and accomplishments I would have so many friends If I held back the truth and I just gave out compliments", "vault_lines": ["I would have so many friends", "If I didn't have money, respect and accomplishments", "If I held back the truth and I just gave out compliments", "I would have so many more friends"], "meaning": "Unfortunately, the truth hurts more often than lies. Drake claims that his honesty, or “keeping it 8 more than 92” with people has led to very few friendships, as many are unable to handle the truth. Game expressed similar thoughts during his verse.\n\nThese lines are also an allusion to DJ Khaled’s song “No New Friends.”", "annotation_id": "7167159", "url": "https://genius.com/7167159", "state": "accepted", "votes": 60, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "I would have so many more friends If I lost my success and my confidence", "vault_lines": ["I would have so many friends", "I would have so many more friends", "If I lost my success and my confidence"], "meaning": "Drake has a notoriously small circle for one of two reasons: either his confidence and success intimidates people out of being his woe or, more likely, attracts fake friends which Drizzy has no time for.", "annotation_id": "7167123", "url": "https://genius.com/7167123", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "Miss 4 Cent, that was my real nigga Held a nigga down since he was a lil’ nigga If he was still alive, he would kill niggas He was Lil’ Snupe, I was Meek Mill Niggas know how it feel when you missin’ your nigga though", "vault_lines": ["Miss 4 Cent, that was my real nigga", "Held a nigga down since he was a lil' nigga", "If he was still alive, he would kill niggas", "He was Lil' Snupe, I was Meek Mill", "Niggas know how it feel when you missin' your nigga though", "You niggas don't feel me though", "Always be a real nigga"], "meaning": "4 Cent (also known as Billboard) was a close friend of Game and was killed due to gang violence, he and Game were involved in. Both would have done everything for the other, even kill someone. Game dedicated a song to him early in his career. He compares his relationship to the friendship Meek Mill and Lil' Snupe had, but similar to him this bond was violently broken after Snupe got shot at the age of 18.\n\nMeek reminisced about the death of his homie in multiple tracks including “Lil Nigga Snupe”.", "annotation_id": "7167020", "url": "https://genius.com/7167020", "state": "accepted", "votes": 88, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "Niggas’ll run up on your car, catch you off guard Like the Lil Wayne and Baby shit,", "vault_lines": ["Niggas'll run up on your car, catch you off guard", "Like the Lil Wayne and Baby shit,"], "meaning": "Game relies on his traditional namedrop here to add meaning to the simile.\n\n\n\nBaby and Lil Wayne have had a father and son relationship, since Wayne was signed by Birdman at the age of 9. Recently, they’ve been embroiled in monetary disputes, the likes of which were entirely unexpected, due to Wayne’s insistence on repping Cash Money.\n\nIt caught the industry off-guard, because despite some high profile splits, Cash Money and Lil Wayne were seen as rock solid.\n\nGame also could be referring to the time when rapper 40 Glocc actually did run up on Lil Wayne in Compton.\n\nAlso could be a reference to an incident in April—Wayne was caught off guard when his tour bus was shot up in Atlanta. Some people thought Baby was responsible.", "annotation_id": "7166934", "url": "https://genius.com/7166934", "state": "accepted", "votes": 87, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "So happy when Bleu Davinci got out We came up on these California streets", "vault_lines": ["So happy when Bleu Davinci got out", "We came up on these California streets"], "meaning": "Bleu Davinci was convicted, along with ten other Black Mafia Family members, who were sentenced over the week for their roles in the BMF cocaine distribution organization. Bleu DaVinci was recently released from prison after serving four years.", "annotation_id": "7166933", "url": "https://genius.com/7166933", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "Not even to H-Town So underground that I gotta be a trill nigga Strapped up from the waist down That’s word to Pimp C, J Prince is my real nigga", "vault_lines": ["Not even to H-Town", "So underground that I gotta be a trill nigga", "Strapped up from the waist down", "That's word to Pimp C, J Prince is my real nigga", "Always be a real nigga"], "meaning": "Game gives a shot out to deceased rapper Pimp C, one half of the rap duo Underground Kingz. UGK was widely responsible for the popularity of the word “trill”, a combination of “true” and “real”, which he claims to be. He’s strapped and ready for any enemy stepping up to him.\n\nJas Prince the son Rap-a-Lot Records CEO, J Prince discovered Drake in his early mixtape days, that’s why he is the big homie. Drake expressed his love multiple times in his tracks and considers Houston as his second home after Toronto.", "annotation_id": "7166924", "url": "https://genius.com/7166924", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "You dissin’ Drizzy, that’s cool, but don’t come to my city though", "vault_lines": ["You dissin' Drizzy, that's cool, but don't come to my city though"], "meaning": "Game is known for his love for artists in hip-hop. He implied his love and support for artists such as Rick Ross, Lil Wayne & Tyga.\n\nGame is stating that it’s fine if you throw shots at Drake, just don’t go to his city, Compton, California. He also brought Drake out to Compton for the shooting of this song, 100.", "annotation_id": "7166885", "url": "https://genius.com/7166885", "state": "accepted", "votes": 82, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "Screamin’ Frog name at the clouds, they don’t hear me though Guess they too busy with 2Pac and Biggie though", "vault_lines": ["Screamin' Frog name at the clouds, they don't hear me though", "Guess they too busy with 2Pac and Biggie though"], "meaning": "Frogg was a young rapper that was shot and killed at a liquor store in Compton and passed away at the scene. Frogg was well known in the L.A hip-hop scene and could always be seen hanging with Ken Malik, who is co-signed by Nipsey Hu$$le.\n\nGame understands that Frogg and Lil Snupe are in heaven with 2Pac, and The Notorious B.I.G., so they can’t be bothered to respond.\n\n\n\nGame released an emotional track called “Til We Meet Again (R.I.P. Frogg)” to honor the death of his close friend.\n\nGame talks about Frogg in here too.", "annotation_id": "7166880", "url": "https://genius.com/7166880", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "Y", "vault_lines": ["A vest for every nigga with an owl on his chest and what", "You better off committin' suicide, teachers ain't testin' us", "Niggas is jealous of you, so they try to wrap you up", "Tax you up, but it's OVO/Blood Money", "Do a nigga four favors, when you can't do the fifth", "Other night at your crib, it was like me, Black, 40, OB", "How soon they forget?", "Run up on you at your granny house, give you nine like Fif'", "How are niggas s'posed to love you niggas?", "Heart beatin' fast when I dap and when I hug you niggas", "Drake told me not to trust you niggas", "Your energy off, you're finicky, I rush you niggas", "Just walkin' 'round the crib like, \"Why a nigga can't live?", "Get this money, fuck these bitches though?\"", "\"We can pass these mothafuckin' straps like a physical\"", "This my city, nigga, everybody know it", "Ridin' 'round town, just me and my four-pound", "Tucked in my Tom Fords, hopin' I ain't gotta show it", "L.A. niggas be the craziest, these niggas do some shady shit", "Niggas'll run up on your car, catch you off guard", "Like the Lil Wayne and Baby shit,", "'all better not come to my studio with that fake shit", "Y'all better not come to my funeral with that fake shit", "Y'all better off realizin' there's nothin' that y'all could do wit' me", "Played some beats, but I forgot to tell you one thing", "L.A. niggas be the craziest, yeah, one hunnid", "Thank you so, so much for wearin' your true colors", "To every single fuckin' function", "Had niggas tell me to my face how we were family", "And how they love me while they were skimmin' off the budget", "Niggas called me to set you up", "Now, when I see 'em, they're the ones that's actin' funny", "I would have so many friends", "If I didn't have money, respect and accomplishments", "I would have all of your fans", "If I didn't go pop and I stayed on some conscious shit", "I would have so many more friends", "If I lost my success and my confidence", "Want me to come and wet you up", "I'm in the club every time that they play the competition", "If they even play the competition and I seen the response they get", "Yeah, nobody's even hearin' it, on top of the pyramid", "My circle got so small that it's a period, sayin' to myself", "Miss 4 Cent, that was my real nigga", "Niggas know how it feel when you missin' your nigga though", "'Cause you a out of town nigga like Biggie", "Can't think, so you roll up that indigo", "Blowin' kush clouds until his ghost is in my Ghost, damn", "Screamin' Frog name at the clouds, they don't hear me though", "Guess they too busy with 2Pac and Biggie though", "You niggas don't feel me though", "You dissin' Drizzy, that's cool, but don't come to my city though", "Heard about the shit with Diddy", "That's word to Pimp C, J Prince is my real nigga", "He had a young nigga right there with Meech", "So happy when Bleu Davinci got out", "Got a nigga confused, but why a nigga gotta choose?", "Don't even matter, dawg, cause I'ma always be a real nigga", "Always be a real nigga", "So I came through to vest you up"], "meaning": "Drake is no stranger to the phrase “keep it 100.” He made a pun out of it in his song “Too Much.” For those who do not know, keeping it 100 means to be true to yourself.\n\nDrizzy asks his haters to keep it 100, calling them out as fake. Ironically, many consider Drake to be fake – see “Started From The Bottom.”\n\n“L.A. niggas be the craziest” is an interpolation of “Craziest” by Naughty by Nature.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k1L2Fit9rjk", "annotation_id": "7166879", "url": "https://genius.com/7166879", "state": "accepted", "votes": 211, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "This my city, nigga, everybody know it Ridin’ ’round town, just me and my four-pound Tucked in my Tom Fords, hopin’ I ain’t gotta show it", "vault_lines": ["This my city, nigga, everybody know it", "Ridin' 'round town, just me and my four-pound", "Tucked in my Tom Fords, hopin' I ain't gotta show it"], "meaning": "Being from the streets, Game knows he could be a target at any time, and carried a “Four Pound” pistol around the city to protect himself.\n\nThe term “four pound” derives from the Desert Eagle 50 calibre handgun, which when fully loaded, weighs approximately four pounds.\n\n\n\nThere’s a juxtaposition between his Tom Ford designer clothes and his ongoing need to wear a gun—the hood still hasn’t left him but he tries to keep it hidden.", "annotation_id": "7166876", "url": "https://genius.com/7166876", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "[Chorus: Drake & The Game]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The majority of this verse and hook were freestyled at Coachella and during Drake’s Jungle tour. No word on whether this collaboration was already in the works and Drake gave us a sneak preview, or if Game required a verse and Drizzy turned it into a studio version.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=U4QhTxFOvuI", "annotation_id": "7166855", "url": "https://genius.com/7166855", "state": "accepted", "votes": 52, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "Had niggas tell me to my face how we were family And how they love me while they were skimmin’ off the budget Now, when I see ‘em, they’re the ones that’s actin’ funny People been reachin’ out to me And I’m on some straight unresponsive shit", "vault_lines": ["Had niggas tell me to my face how we were family", "And how they love me while they were skimmin' off the budget", "Now, when I see 'em, they're the ones that's actin' funny", "People been reachin' out to me", "And I'm on some straight unresponsive shit"], "meaning": "Its become clear who Drake’s addressing: Birdman and Cash Money Records. Drake talks ironically about the family and love from Cash Money, because Birdman excluded him from the cash.\n\n\n\nIt was all good just a week ago when they were singing “no new friends,” but since then, things changed with the YM vs CM feud. Drizzy’s become involved with Lil Wayne’s lawsuit, since Cash Money allegedly hasn’t paid Young Money for Drake solo recordings since early 2012.\n\nDrake’s been addressing this a lot lately – see  “Blessings” & “10 Bands.”", "annotation_id": "7166835", "url": "https://genius.com/7166835", "state": "accepted", "votes": 80, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "And I got a vest for 40, a vest for Hush A vest for every nigga with an owl on his chest and what", "vault_lines": ["And I got a vest for 40, a vest for Hush", "A vest for every nigga with an owl on his chest and what", "I got L.A. unified"], "meaning": "Noah Shebib, professionally known as 40, is a Canadian record producer from Toronto. Shebib has produced for Drake, Lil Wayne, Beyoncé, Alicia Keys, and Jamie Foxx, and is co-founder of Drake’s OVO movement (which features an OWL on its logo).\n\nHush is an affiliate of Drake and a supporter of his OVO Sound brand. A few months back, Hush took to Instagram to take shots at Tyga, and Chris Brown.", "annotation_id": "7166831", "url": "https://genius.com/7166831", "state": "accepted", "votes": 54, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "100", "line": "Run up on you at your granny house, give you nine like Fif’", "vault_lines": ["Run up on you at your granny house, give you nine like Fif'"], "meaning": "On April 24, 2000, 50 Cent was attacked and shot nine times, an experience he describes in “Many Men.” The shooting occurred outside of 50’s grandmother’s house (she had custody of him at the time). The Game threatens his opposition, but he’s also targeting Fif once more.\n\nThe tension between 50 Cent and The Game goes back to 2005. Even with G-Unit reuniting, the two haven’t shown the slightest interest in reconciliation.\n\n\n\nThe “9 like Fif'” may also refer to the four favors and the fifth from the previous line, since 4 and 5 add up to 9.", "annotation_id": "7166829", "url": "https://genius.com/7166829", "state": "accepted", "votes": 72, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "status": "done", "targets": 31, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/21-savage-issa-lyrics", "genius_title": "Issa", "genius_id": 2916012, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "Nigga, issa knife, came for a slice (Came for a what?)", "vault_lines": ["Nigga, issa knife, came for a slice (Came for a what?)", "Issa, issa, issa, issa, issa", "Issa, issa, issa... Issa", "Issa, issa, issa knife, lil' nigga"], "meaning": "Young Thug references 21 Savages’s iconic “issa knife” interview with DJ Vlad. Placed on the center of his forehead, 21’s tattoo of a dagger attracts a lot of attention, enough so that Savage has rapped about it before.\nhttps://youtu.be/2qoDi0Rul0Y?t=350\nThe story behind the tattoo is actually quite the tragedy. The FADER reported in Issue 107, “Savage World,” the true meaning behind the piece:\n\nIt’s a dagger, and an ode to his younger brother Quantivayus, who everyone called Tayman. The original inspiration was Tony Montana’s blade tattoo in Scarface. Savage and his brothers agreed to get the ink in the same place as Tony, between the thumb and the index finger. But Tayman jumped the gun, and went ahead and planted it right on his face, bold and bright. After Tayman was shot and killed, in a botched drug deal, Savage did the same.", "annotation_id": "18413792", "url": "https://genius.com/18413792", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "Bricks, this shit finna kill these niggas N-n-n-n-narcos Wheezy Beatz", "vault_lines": ["Bricks, this shit finna kill these niggas"], "meaning": "These are the producer tags for everyone who worked on the song:\n\n\nBricks Da Mane, who released the song and is said to be using it on his upcoming project\nTM88 of 808 Mafia previously used the Kill Bill siren as a sound effect in his beats, but he uses it more often as a producer tag now\nNarcos, the production duo made up of Chapo and French Connect, has the third tag\nWheezy, Young Thug’s go-to producer, has the last tag", "annotation_id": "13336606", "url": "https://genius.com/13336606", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "Issa Pyrex (Woo), I got crack (I got crinack)", "vault_lines": ["Issa Pyrex (Woo), I got crack (I got crinack)", "Issa, issa, issa, issa, issa", "Issa, issa, issa... Issa"], "meaning": "Pyrex is a brand that makes clear, low-thermal-expansion borosilicate glass used for laboratory glassware and kitchenware.\n\n\n\nPyrex is linked as the glassware to cook cocaine  in.", "annotation_id": "12246511", "url": "https://genius.com/12246511", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "Could’ve been had ’em, talk to Rika instead (yeah, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Could've been had 'em, talk to Rika instead (yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "Jerrika Karlae is Young Thug’s fiancée. In April 2015, he uploaded a picture of two diamond rings in a now-deleted Instagram post, indicating a proposal to his girlfriend which captioned “Will U? ? ?”\n\n\n\nIn an interview with DJ Vlad, Jerrika gave more insight about their relationship:\n\nHe completely swept me off my feet. That’s what people don’t know. He’s a charmer, especially with women. He will sweep you off your feet with his words.", "annotation_id": "12229677", "url": "https://genius.com/12229677", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "Let’s fight about it, hol’ up, she leave wit’ the winner, hol’ up", "vault_lines": ["Let's fight about it, hol' up, she leave wit' the winner, hol' up"], "meaning": "Following up on the last line, Thugger responds to Kylie’s boyfriend Tyga’s disses and subliminal shots towards 21 Savage, including but not limited to his snippet of 21’s No Heart.\n\n21 has shown he has a crush on Kylie Jenner and he would even fight Tyga for her. Thugger would know that so he states it for 21 in this line.\n\n\n\nThough Tyga and Kylie were presumably together when this was recorded, Kylie was dating Travis Scott when “Issa” was released.", "annotation_id": "11937707", "url": "https://genius.com/11937707", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "Issa nail polish (Issa nail polish), bitch, I’m petty (The most)", "vault_lines": ["Issa nail polish (Issa nail polish), bitch, I'm petty (The most)", "Issa, issa, issa, issa, issa", "Issa, issa, issa... Issa"], "meaning": "Drake touches on his feminine side mentioning the use of the “nail polish” emoji, used by mostly by females on social media to express their “pettiness” or simply rudeness, as well as using the most common insult thrown about by women being “bitch.”\n\nThis exploration of femininity is expected on a track with Young Thug, who is famous for controversially claiming there’s no such thing as gender.", "annotation_id": "11931792", "url": "https://genius.com/11931792", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "Got a coolin’ system, issa Tec (Thu thu thu thu thu)", "vault_lines": ["Got a coolin' system, issa Tec (Thu thu thu thu thu)", "Issa, issa, issa, issa, issa", "Issa, issa, issa... Issa"], "meaning": "21 is referring to the TEC-9, a popular firearm that has been banned in several states, such as California and New York. His TEC has a cooling system on it, which keeps it from overheating, letting him shoot it as much as they want.\n\n21 has referenced the firearm before on his song “No Target”, where he says\n\nThat Tec’ll bless ya, wow\n21, pew-pew-pew, blaow", "annotation_id": "11928505", "url": "https://genius.com/11928505", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "Issa bloody LaFerrari, issa fortune (Skrrt skrrrrrt)", "vault_lines": ["Issa bloody LaFerrari, issa fortune (Skrrt skrrrrrt)", "Issa, issa, issa, issa, issa", "Issa, issa, issa... Issa"], "meaning": "Made by the Italian sports car manufacturer Ferrari, the LaFerrari is the most expensive car ever sold at an auction with a price tag of $7 million. Even for Drake—the man who allegedly earned $150 million prior to taxes in 2017—$7 million is an expensive investment.", "annotation_id": "11928241", "url": "https://genius.com/11928241", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "Chopper singin’ (Singin’), Ginuwine (Brrrrr)", "vault_lines": ["Chopper singin' (Singin'), Ginuwine (Brrrrr)"], "meaning": "Ginuwine is an R&B singer best known for his 1996 single, “Pony”. 21’s  assault rifle, or “chopper,” often “sings\"—a euphemism for the act of shooting—much like Ginuwine.\n\n\n\nGinuwine’s popularity within rap music as a means of analogy has risen in the past year with the emergence of the Atlanta rap trio Migos—on 2016’s “Oh Me Oh My,” Quavo rapped:\n\nBirds singing just like Ginuwine", "annotation_id": "11928126", "url": "https://genius.com/11928126", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "Issa ton of these (Issa ton), Six God heavy (Six God heavy, ayy)", "vault_lines": ["Issa ton of these (Issa ton), Six God heavy (Six God heavy, ayy)", "Issa, issa, issa, issa, issa", "Issa, issa, issa... Issa"], "meaning": "Drizzy hails from Toronto, Canada, a location he often refers to the as “the 6” due to it’s area codes, 416 and 647, both including the number six. As the most popular artist to escape Toronto, Drake has labelled himself the “6 God,” solidifying his domination over the area.", "annotation_id": "11923581", "url": "https://genius.com/11923581", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "What’s in that Wraith, Savage? It’s some white, dawg It’s some nose-wipe (Wipe), that’s a slime (Slime)", "vault_lines": ["What's in that Wraith, Savage? It's some white, dawg", "It's some nose-wipe (Wipe), that's a slime (Slime)"], "meaning": "A Wraith is a brand of cars by the company Rolls Royce. These cars have become a frequently mentioned subject in rap due to their expensive nature. 21 previously mentioned Wraith in songs like “Lord Forgive Me” and “Organized Crime”.\n\n\n\nDespite the luxurious nature of his Wraith, 21 uses it to transport “nose white\"—a slang name for cocaine.", "annotation_id": "11922603", "url": "https://genius.com/11922603", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "If your watch ain’t cost a hundred, it ain’t shit (It ain’t shit, slime)", "vault_lines": ["If your watch ain't cost a hundred, it ain't shit (It ain't shit, slime)"], "meaning": "21 is a known watch enthusiast, and has an assortment of watches ranging from Audemars Piguets, to Patek Philippes, to Rolexes  — most notably his 2016 Rose gold Rolex Day-Date, fully covered in VVS stones,\n which cost him $100k.\n\nHe’s made mention of the watch before on his hit song “X”\n\nHold up, bitch my Rolex on fleek\nHold up, bitch my diamonds on fleek", "annotation_id": "11906948", "url": "https://genius.com/11906948", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "Issa, issa, issa Issa Issa, issa, issa Issa", "vault_lines": ["Issa Kylie, might be Jenner, hol' up", "I'm on Air One (Damn), issa nine (Nine)", "Issa paintin' (Bitch, that's art), half a ticket (Half a ticket)", "Issa jet (Phew), issa check (Check)", "Issa savage (Issa savage), now she wet (Now she wet)", "Issa Pyrex (Woo), I got crack (I got crinack)", "Got a coolin' system, issa Tec (Thu thu thu thu thu)", "If your bitch spend the night, issa sex (Slime)", "Issa X (Lil' nigga), it's respect", "If she don't check 'em (What she gon' do?), issa next (Next)", "Issa slice (Slice), yes or not (Yes or no?)", "Only one body (Only one body), issa squash (Hah)", "Issa babysitter (Ya dig?)", "I see whiskers (Cat), he scared, issa pig (Issa pig)", "Tremendous pool, issa livin' room", "Nigga, issa Patek, nigga, issa necklace (Patek)", "Nigga, issa knife, came for a slice (Came for a what?)", "Never tell the truth, issa lie (On God)", "Issa 21 (Young savage), issa Jeff (Issa Jeffery)", "Issa profit, dawg (Big racks), issa net (Got it on score)", "I watched you go sell four million, issa stretch (Issa, issa)", "You gave somethin' to the cops, issa sketch (Issa picture)", "Issa drawin' (It's Picasso),", "issa foreign (Foreign, skrrrrt)", "Girl, stop textin' me so much, issa 'nnoying (Bitch, stop texting me)", "Issa bloody LaFerrari, issa fortune (Skrrt skrrrrrt)", "Issa duffle bag (Duffle), issa Goyard (Goyard)", "Issa VVS (VVS), and it's swimmin' (Swimmin')", "Issa Thugger, issa lieutenant", "Boy with all the fuckery, issa menace", "Issa Rolls Royce (Skrrt, skrrt) and it's tinted (Skrrt, skrrt)", "Issa a Bentley (Skrrt, skrrt), it ain't rented (Hell nah)", "Issa diss song, now they missin' (Tried to tell 'em)", "Issa brown bag, issa blue cash", "Issa coup that's fast, issa green Xan", "Issa moshpit, issa bandana", "Issa Taliban, Alexander McQueen", "Issa 40 (Forty, shorty), issa 30 (Thirty, thirty)", "Issa Dessy (Issa Dessy), y'all not ready (Y'all ain't ready)", "Issa nail polish (Issa nail polish), bitch, I'm petty (The most)", "Issa ton of these (Issa ton), Six God heavy (Six God heavy, ayy)", "Issa knife, dawg (Issa knife) I got stripes, dawg", "Issa YSL (Slime), issa PDE (Slime)", "That's my old ting (That's my old ting), issa TBT (Hah)", "Issa tax bracket (Tax bracket),", "issa Stoney jacket (Stoney jacket)", "Issa 21, issa rat, issa pump, issa killer", "Issa pistol, iss' dismissal, issa kiss, if we catch her, yes, we kissed her", "Iss' dismissal, iss' dismiss you, issa pistol, issa spillin'", "Issa spillin', issa I'm bigger, issa (Woah)", "Issum killers, issum hitters, issa hit 'em with some missiles", "Issa (Shit), issa (Gotta hit 'em), issa fuck it, issa fuck 'em", "Issa fuck 'em, issa bust 'em, issa truck 'em, issa fuck 'em", "Issa buck 'em, issa just don't cuff 'em, 21", "Issa, issa, issa, issa, issa", "Issa, issa, issa... Issa", "Issa... slight problem, niggas poppin' like some popcorn, nigga", "Issa, issa, issa knife, lil' nigga"], "meaning": "“Issa” is a slang created and popularized by 21 Savage. He first used this catchphrase in his interview with DJ Vlad—“Issa Knife” quickly gained massive popularity and was the subject of many memes.", "annotation_id": "11905815", "url": "https://genius.com/11905815", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "Issa profit, dawg (Big racks), issa net (Got it on score)", "vault_lines": ["Issa profit, dawg (Big racks), issa net (Got it on score)", "Issa, issa, issa, issa, issa", "Issa, issa, issa... Issa"], "meaning": "In the 2017 edition of Hip Hop’s Wealthiest Artists, Drake landed at #5, at $90 million.\n\nDrake plays off “profit” and “net”; both meaning how much money he made. “Profit” and “net” refer to net income—how much you make after taxes and deductions.", "annotation_id": "11899768", "url": "https://genius.com/11899768", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "That’s my old ting (That’s my old ting), issa TBT (Hah)", "vault_lines": ["That's my old ting (That's my old ting), issa TBT (Hah)", "Issa, issa, issa, issa, issa", "Issa, issa, issa... Issa"], "meaning": "“Ting” is a term widely used in Jamaican culture to describe anything, especially women.\n“TBT” is short for Throwback Thursday — used when referring to an event or someone in the past. Drake is stating that this girl is just an ex from a long time ago.", "annotation_id": "11894968", "url": "https://genius.com/11894968", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "And I got Saint Laurent (I got Saint Laurent) on my garments (On my garments)", "vault_lines": ["And I got Saint Laurent (I got Saint Laurent) on my garments (On my garments)"], "meaning": "21 has been vocal in his love of Saint Laurent in recent times. He is almost always seen wearing the brand and has even changed his twitter name to “Saint Laurent Don”.\n\n\n\nSaint Laurent is a French luxury fashion house founded by Yves Saint Laurent in 1961. The brand has been a favorite of rappers such as Kanye West, Travis Scott and G-Eazy for many years.", "annotation_id": "11894844", "url": "https://genius.com/11894844", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "And I got a ’Rari (’Rari), and I got a Harley (And I got a Harley)", "vault_lines": ["And I got a 'Rari ('Rari), and I got a Harley (And I got a Harley)"], "meaning": "On October 22nd, 2016, 21 Savage turned 24. As a gift, Drake bought him a red Ferrari 488, which starts at $245,000.\n\n21 also talks about his Harley on his song “Partments”\n\nBitch I keep the choppa think I should a sell the Harley", "annotation_id": "11894827", "url": "https://genius.com/11894827", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "Tremendous pool, issa livin’ room", "vault_lines": ["Tremendous pool, issa livin' room", "Issa, issa, issa, issa, issa", "Issa, issa, issa... Issa"], "meaning": "In 2016, Thugger rented the Buckhead Mansion in Atlanta for $15K a month.\n\nThe house is 11,000 square feet in size, and as well an indoor swimming pool, the property boasts 6 bedrooms, 11 bathrooms, a solarium and a 4 car garage.", "annotation_id": "11894752", "url": "https://genius.com/11894752", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "Issa tax bracket (Tax bracket),", "vault_lines": ["Issa tax bracket (Tax bracket),", "Issa, issa, issa, issa, issa", "Issa, issa, issa... Issa"], "meaning": "Drake is flexing his net worth by telling everybody his tax bracket is above a lot of people. The official tax bracket in the U.S. is seen below\n\n\n\nThese numbers are only realized when you account for all that Drake has made. During his Summer Sixteen tour, Drake and Future grossed over $84.3 million over the three months they were on the road. On top of this, Drake’s album did major numbers, going 4x multi-platinum in 2016. Including various deals with Apple, Sprite and Nike, Drake, after taxes, earned only $38.5 million in the year of 2016. He makes so much that his taxes are beyond most of these other rappers.", "annotation_id": "11892214", "url": "https://genius.com/11892214", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "Issa Stoney jacket (Stoney jacket)", "vault_lines": ["issa Stoney jacket (Stoney jacket)", "Issa, issa, issa, issa, issa", "Issa, issa, issa... Issa"], "meaning": "Since prior to his 2017 “playlist” More Life, which was heavily influenced by British culture, Drake has associated himself with UK artists like Giggs, Skepta, and Dave.\n\nStone Island is an Italian brand but has become synonymous with British fashion in the 21st Century. Here Drake wears his Stone Island chain designed by celebrity jewellery, Ben Baller, who he is standing along side.", "annotation_id": "11892094", "url": "https://genius.com/11892094", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "You gave somethin’ to the cops, issa sketch (Issa picture) Issa drawin’ (It’s Picasso),", "vault_lines": ["You gave somethin' to the cops, issa sketch (Issa picture)", "Issa drawin' (It's Picasso),", "Issa, issa, issa, issa, issa", "Issa, issa, issa... Issa"], "meaning": "Once police are dedicated to solving a crime, they often request a ‘facial composite’, also known as a police sketch, is drawn with assistance from eye-witnesses in order aid the process of identifying a criminal. Essentially, Drake is calling you out for snitching to the police.", "annotation_id": "11892005", "url": "https://genius.com/11892005", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "I watched you go sell four million, issa stretch (Issa, issa)", "vault_lines": ["I watched you go sell four million, issa stretch (Issa, issa)", "Issa, issa, issa, issa, issa", "Issa, issa, issa... Issa"], "meaning": "In December 2016, Drake’s fourth studio album Views was certified quadruple platinum by the RIAA. In the music industry, platinum certification is achieved when a million units of a single/album has been sold.\n\nDrake’s stating that these other rappers achieving four million sales on an album is a “stretch” or very unlikely. He’s solidifying his position at the top of the rap game with his insane numbers.", "annotation_id": "11891924", "url": "https://genius.com/11891924", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "Issa knife, dawg (Issa knife) I got stripes, dawg", "vault_lines": ["Issa knife, dawg (Issa knife) I got stripes, dawg", "Issa, issa, issa, issa, issa", "Issa, issa, issa... Issa"], "meaning": "According to the Dictionary website, “Issa” is a slang term used by 21 Savage to combine the words “its” and “a.”\n\nIn this line, 21 Savage references his famous 2016 interview with DJ Vlad, where he claimed that the tattoo on his forehead was a “knife” as opposed to a cross.\n\nIn addition, 21 Savage boasts about his credibility and clout in the streets, which he later flexed about on his December 2018 track, “ASMR”:\n\nI got lots of stripes, all my niggas shyst\nYou can roll the dice, you might lose your life", "annotation_id": "11891828", "url": "https://genius.com/11891828", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "Nigga, we heartless (Heartless)", "vault_lines": ["Nigga, gon' harm you (Harm you), nigga, we heartless (Heartless)"], "meaning": "One of 21’s biggest songs to date, “No Heart,” details his life on the streets of Atlanta. It features some of his most raw lyrics, giving off the image that he actually doesn’t have a heart.\n\nWet your mama’s house, wet your grandma’s house\nKeep shootin' until somebody die\nSo many shots the neighbor looked at the calendar\nThought it was Fourth of July", "annotation_id": "11891810", "url": "https://genius.com/11891810", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "Issa VVS (VVS), and it’s swimmin’ (Swimmin’)", "vault_lines": ["Issa VVS (VVS), and it's swimmin' (Swimmin')", "Issa Rolls Royce (Skrrt, skrrt) and it's tinted (Skrrt, skrrt)", "Issa, issa, issa, issa, issa", "Issa, issa, issa... Issa"], "meaning": "VVS is a rating on the “clarity grading scale”. VVS diamonds have very few flaws within; these flaws are barely visible under 10 times magnification.\n\n“Swimming” refers to how much shine 21’s diamonds give off. They reflect light like water.\n\nOn Meek Mill’s “Offended”, 21 mentioned his VVS diamonds:\n\nVVSs on me, whoa\nVVSs on me, bling, badaboom, badabing", "annotation_id": "11891709", "url": "https://genius.com/11891709", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "Issa YSL (Slime), issa PDE (Slime)", "vault_lines": ["Issa YSL (Slime), issa PDE (Slime)", "Issa, issa, issa, issa, issa", "Issa, issa, issa... Issa"], "meaning": "YSL is an acronym for Young Stoner Life; Thugger’s apparel line, movement and label imprint under 300 Records. The YSL roster boasts artists like Gunna and Lil Duke. Also, in February 2017 Drake gifted Thugger a new YSL chain.\n\nPDE is short for Paradise East, a housing community in East Atlanta. The area birthed 21 Savage and various rappers associated with him and his Slaughter Gang, including Young Nudy, SahBabii and No Plug. 21 has mentioned PDE on songs such as “East Atlanta Day” or “I’m A Savage.”", "annotation_id": "11891048", "url": "https://genius.com/11891048", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "Girl, stop textin’ me so much, issa ’nnoying (Bitch, stop texting me)", "vault_lines": ["Girl, stop textin' me so much, issa 'nnoying (Bitch, stop texting me)", "Issa, issa, issa, issa, issa", "Issa, issa, issa... Issa"], "meaning": "Drake often expresses a dislike for texting girls he’s interested in and much prefers physical interactions. For example, in “Since Way Back” he sings:\n\nEverything these days is textual\nI just want to get a lil' sexual, with you", "annotation_id": "11890900", "url": "https://genius.com/11890900", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "Issa 21 (Young savage), issa Jeff (Issa Jeffery)", "vault_lines": ["Issa 21 (Young savage), issa Jeff (Issa Jeffery)", "Issa, issa, issa, issa, issa", "Issa, issa, issa... Issa"], "meaning": "Drake interpolates the song title and its features, by name-dropping 21 Savage and Jeffery, Young Thug’s government name which is Jeffery Lamar Williams.", "annotation_id": "11890895", "url": "https://genius.com/11890895", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "Issa 40 (Forty, shorty), issa 30 (Thirty, thirty) Issa Dessy (Issa Dessy), y’all not ready (Y’all ain’t ready)", "vault_lines": ["Issa 40 (Forty, shorty), issa 30 (Thirty, thirty)", "Issa Dessy (Issa Dessy), y'all not ready (Y'all ain't ready)", "Issa, issa, issa, issa, issa", "Issa, issa, issa... Issa"], "meaning": "“Issa 40” is a nod to Drizzy’s longtime friend and co-founder of his label, Noah “40” Shebib, whereas “issa 30” is a reference to Drake’s age of 30 years old, born 24 October 1986.\n\n\n\nDrake might also referring to Glock 30 and Glock 40 firearms, where next would be a “Dessy,” which is a 50. cal Desert Eagle.", "annotation_id": "11875747", "url": "https://genius.com/11875747", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "World is mine now (World is miiiine), it’s on Tony status (It’s on Tony status)", "vault_lines": ["World is mine now (World is miiiine), it's on Tony status (It's on Tony status)"], "meaning": "Drake is arguably one of the biggest stars on the world right now and broke several records with his most recent effort More Life, which became the most streamed album in one day with 61.3 million plays on Sunday, March 19 and had the most chart debuts on Billboard in one week with 21.\n\nTherefore he compares his mind-state to that of Tony Montana, the main character from the film Scarface, shortly after he killed his former boss Lopez and became the biggest drug kingpin in Miami. It’s also notable that Drake previously proclaimed himself being the “Tony of Toronto” on Future’s song “Tony Montana”:\n\nAnd shout out to Toronto, bitch, I’m Tony in my city", "annotation_id": "11872477", "url": "https://genius.com/11872477", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Issa", "line": "Issa Kylie, might be Jenner, hol’ up", "vault_lines": ["Issa Kylie, might be Jenner, hol' up", "Issa, issa, issa, issa, issa", "Issa, issa, issa... Issa"], "meaning": "Kylie Jenner is a the member of the Kardashian/Jenner family, and the youngest child of Kris Jenner. She is a social media mogul, and she owns her own makeup line.\n\nIn November 2016, 21 Savage tweeted a picture of Kylie Jenner with flirtatious heart-eyed emojis to show his fondness for the reality TV star.\n\nWhen asked about her in a TMZ interview, 21 said that he would “tear that ass up”:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=30L6BQYEZyc\n\nThese events incited a response from Kylie’s boyfriend at the time, Tyga, who had her post a preview of his diss response over 21 Savage’s “No Heart” instrumental. The two have since exchanged subliminal shots over social media. Eventually 21 called out Tyga by name at a late 2016 concert.", "annotation_id": "11273211", "url": "https://genius.com/11273211", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stuntin", "status": "done", "targets": 12, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-stuntin-lyrics", "genius_title": "Stuntin", "genius_id": 1651, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stuntin", "line": "MoneyOverBitches dot com, check the domain", "vault_lines": ["MoneyOverBitches dot com, check the domain"], "meaning": "He’s saying that the business comes first, and the women come after. MoneyOverBitches is also a nod to his own MOB.  “Check the domain” is a double entendre, which can be said either as it’s stated, or “Check the dough, mayne”.", "annotation_id": "37238662", "url": "https://genius.com/37238662", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stuntin", "line": "Drop a four in it and appreciate the greatness, Drizzy", "vault_lines": ["Drop a four in it and appreciate the greatness, Drizzy"], "meaning": "“Four” is a reference to the ratio of codeine/syrup to soda. Lil Wayne popularizes the ratio in his song “Me and My Drank” where he says “Drop a four in a 20 ounce and call it 24’s.”", "annotation_id": "30831338", "url": "https://genius.com/30831338", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stuntin", "line": "People ask me if I pray, I say, “Yeah, once in a blue moon” Oops, I mean a red moon, I did it again, Tune", "vault_lines": ["People ask me if I pray, I say, \"Yeah, once in a blue moon\"", "Oops, I mean a red moon, I did it again, Tune"], "meaning": "Drake is expressing he is not one to pray very often.  He uses a commonly used expression to even measure how rare it is. The moon is dubbed a “blue moon” if it is the second of two full moons within the same calendar month. This phenomena happens only once every few years. After Drake expresses his rarity, he realizes he made a mistake in speaking the color of the notorious gang the Crips. Wayne is affiliated with the Bloods, and the two aforementioned gangs are arch-rivals. The color of the Bloods is red, which makes Drake change the blue moon into a red moon. He then apologizes for making the mistake again like in their song Ransom. Drake said, “You ain’t heard of me then you should go and get a Blue’s Clue? Oops! I mean a red clue.\nWayne’s here, Soo-woo!”", "annotation_id": "13864299", "url": "https://genius.com/13864299", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stuntin", "line": "Stuntin’ is a habit, get it from my daddy", "vault_lines": ["Stuntin' is a habit, get it from my daddy"], "meaning": "Weezy is referencing one of his most iconic tracks “Stuntin' Like My Daddy” from his collaborative album with Birdman Like Father, Like Son. On the track, Wayne and Birdman detail their lavish lifestyles as pimps and rappers.", "annotation_id": "13571801", "url": "https://genius.com/13571801", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stuntin", "line": "The supplement I’ve taken got me feelin’ mighty", "vault_lines": ["The supplement I've taken got me feelin' mighty"], "meaning": "Double entendre: My Tee / Mighty\n\nMY Tee: “Promethazine codeine syrup weighs down your clothes, whatever you may be wearing and makes it feel heavy” -@Stasthagod\n\n\n\nMighty: also he could be referring to other drugs (Ex: MDMA, Weed) that has him feeling mighty(euphoria, endorphins).\n\n\n\na play on words…", "annotation_id": "3288219", "url": "https://genius.com/3288219", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stuntin", "line": "I’m just doin’", "vault_lines": ["I just listened back and now I'm sounding like a trumpet", "I just walk up on the scene, I'm about to take this", "I'm just havin' patience, 'cause I want it to make sense"], "meaning": "He’s just doing him, which means he is caring only about himself and doing what he wants. As he said in “Over”\n\nWhat am I doin'? Oh yeah, that’s right, I’m doin' me", "annotation_id": "3174620", "url": "https://genius.com/3174620", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stuntin", "line": "Just like Shaggy, I tote that boom-bastic", "vault_lines": ["Just like Shaggy, I tote that boom-bastic"], "meaning": "A reference to the song “Boombastic” by Jamaican musician Shaggy; Weezy gives his firearm another nickname.", "annotation_id": "3024551", "url": "https://genius.com/3024551", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stuntin", "line": "Frostbite Drizzy, nigga, nobody as cold as Drake", "vault_lines": ["Frostbite Drizzy, nigga, nobody as cold as Drake"], "meaning": "Taking a page out of his mentor Lil Wayne’s book by giving himself a nickname, here Drake proclaims he’s the nicest on the track. Anytime he’s invited to do a guest verse, he’s coldblooded, giving the invitee no room to shine.", "annotation_id": "3024548", "url": "https://genius.com/3024548", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stuntin", "line": "And homie’s scared, ’Cause his bitch like me", "vault_lines": ["And homie's scared, 'Cause his bitch like me"], "meaning": "The homie is scared ‘cause his girl is bout to leave him for weezy.\n\n\n\nWeezy is alluding to the original verse of Chris Brown on “Get Like Me\" by David Banner", "annotation_id": "1003599", "url": "https://genius.com/1003599", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stuntin", "line": "And 18 G’s is why the chicken crossed the street", "vault_lines": ["And 18 G's is why the chicken crossed the street"], "meaning": "A chicken is slang for a kilo of coke, which Wayne used to sell for 18G’s. So Weezy’s saying the chicken will only cross the street for 18000$.\n\nUsing a play on words with the expression “why did the chicken cross the road” and the chicken being “moved” or sold.", "annotation_id": "51656", "url": "https://genius.com/51656", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stuntin", "line": "I’m about to change the fucking game, pass the remote", "vault_lines": ["I'm about to change the fucking game, pass the remote"], "meaning": "When your team starts getting blown out you know you change to another game to avoid getting your heart stomped on anymore.\n\n\n\nYou change a channel with a remote, and Drake wants to change the rap game, therefore asking for a remote to make it more clever.", "annotation_id": "51653", "url": "https://genius.com/51653", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stuntin", "line": "All I hit is C-notes", "vault_lines": ["But I don't need my vocal cords, all I hit is C-notes"], "meaning": "“C-notes” refers to either hundred dollar bills or C-notes can be the first key on a piano, which is the lowest so  he could mean that he only sings in a low tone.", "annotation_id": "47191", "url": "https://genius.com/47191", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Grindin’", "status": "done", "targets": 20, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-grindin-lyrics", "genius_title": "Grindin’", "genius_id": 492278, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Grindin’", "line": "These niggas walk around with they chests out Like Janet Jackson and shit", "vault_lines": ["These niggas walk around with they chests out", "Like Janet Jackson and shit"], "meaning": "Weezy comically references the infamous moment where Janet Jackson ‘nip-slipped’ during a 2004 Superbowl half-time performance, likening it to men who walked around bare-chested as if to show bravado and dominance.", "annotation_id": "18208216", "url": "https://genius.com/18208216", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Grindin’", "line": "’Cause what’s the hottest shit on these corners?", "vault_lines": ["'Cause what’s the hottest shit on these corners?"], "meaning": "Continuing the previous line of why these hoes keep laying eyes on his crew, Lil Wayne asks a rhetorical question about who’s number one, or hottest, crew in the game. He’s obviously shouting out his group, YMCMB.\n\nThis is a reference to the track “Swagger Like Us,” which Wayne is featured on, that goes:\n\nNo one on the corner has swagger like us\nSwagger like us, swagger-swagger like us", "annotation_id": "3902121", "url": "https://genius.com/3902121", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Grindin’", "line": "Twap, twap! Twap, twap! In the new house, we got the twap", "vault_lines": ["In the new house, we got the twap"], "meaning": "Twap is Lil Wayne’s word for anything sexual or anything about the female figure.  It is created to define a girl who is a quick no strings attached fling.\n\nHe has mentioned it several times, and even freestyle-d about it on a live streaming:\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-wECbqccTkY", "annotation_id": "3895580", "url": "https://genius.com/3895580", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Grindin’", "line": "And I ain’t ever pay to be with no bitch (Woo!)", "vault_lines": ["Ain’t got time to bond with no bitch", "And I ain’t ever pay to be with no bitch (Woo!)"], "meaning": "Drizzy is so famous that women literally fall into his lap, no need to go out and pay any of them for sex in other words Prostitution. The benefits of fame.\n\nIt is a reference to the rumor started by the porn-star “Kakey XXX” saying he paid her to stay with him for a weekend or week.\n\nKakey claims that Drake is her ex, and stated more about situation:\n\nThis is Kakeyxxx i want to let y’all know me and Drake had sex plenty of times. The first time he did fly me to Toronto i gave him head real sloppy (he loves sloppy head!) i was suppose to leave the next day but he offered me $15,000 to stay longer. We had sex all night i even tried something he never did before he claimed he wanted me to suck his balls and lick his ass at the same time so i did! Shit for $15,000 why not.", "annotation_id": "3890140", "url": "https://genius.com/3890140", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Grindin’", "line": "Scoob, find another oo-wop", "vault_lines": ["Scoob, find another oo-wop"], "meaning": "DJ Scoob Doo is a producer for Wayne and works on Weezy Wednesdays. An oo-wop is two blunts rolled together and Wayne is known for blunt blowin'.", "annotation_id": "3890009", "url": "https://genius.com/3890009", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Grindin’", "line": "They flew out Invite ’em to my new house, my new house I’m fucking every night up in my new house ’Cause bitch I worked too hard for this new house, grindin’ I’m fucking every night up in my new house ’Cause bitch I worked too hard for this new house, I’m grindin’ I’m fucking every night up in my new house ’Cause bitch I worked too hard for this new house, I’m grindin’", "vault_lines": ["I’m grindin’, I’m grindin’, I’m grindin’ I promise", "Grindin’ for all my shit", "I’m grindin’ for all my shit", "I’m sweatin’ grindin’ this bitch, I need a shrine in this bitch", "Invite 'em to my new house, my new house", "I’m fucking every night up in my new house", "'Cause bitch I worked too hard for this new house, grindin’", "'Cause bitch I worked too hard for this new house, I'm grindin’"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne has been working hard lately, and occasionally bought a new mansion in LA. He invited his whole crew to his new house, and celebrated for his success. Lil Wayne unearths in this footage his new house in LA:\n\nhttp://youtu.be/oo7yX_WTaFg?t=1m33s\n\nThe way he says “grindin'” after referring to how hard he has worked to get his new house, is a way of showing that he isn’t done yet, and still grinding hard for more.\n\nWayne is also saying that he deserves to have sex every night in his new house because he worked so hard for his new house. That’s a lot of sex.", "annotation_id": "3889548", "url": "https://genius.com/3889548", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Grindin’", "line": "It ain’t rocket science just rockets", "vault_lines": ["It ain’t rocket science just rockets"], "meaning": "Continuing the previous line about getting money from drugs. Rockets could be referring to “Rocket caps” wich are Dome-shaped caps on crack vials or Marijuana cigarettes which are also called “rockets”.\n\n\n\nWayne of course has been arrested for drug possession on the past, on January 23, 2008, he was arrested alongside two others when his tour bus was stopped on Arizona after a show. He pleaded guilty but since he was already serving his other sentence he was able to serve 36 months of probation, which he was sentenced to on June 30, 2010.", "annotation_id": "3889446", "url": "https://genius.com/3889446", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Grindin’", "line": "My girl like it rough she said “find me a diamond” Her body be grindin’", "vault_lines": ["My girl like it rough she said “find me a diamond”", "Her body be grindin’"], "meaning": "A spin on the phrase “ diamond in the rough”, and it means a person who is generally of good character but lacks manners, education, or style.\n\nBy twisting this idiom Wayne’s saying that my how much he grinds he’s able to send perceptions of people from the hood mostly being “rough” amongst loads of rough, to people who can actually who can get as much diamonds as they want despite being “rough”. Rags to riches.", "annotation_id": "3889380", "url": "https://genius.com/3889380", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Grindin’", "line": "To take off her clothes like Leilani for niggas that’s grindin’", "vault_lines": ["to take off her clothes like Leilani for niggas that’s grindin’"], "meaning": "In the previous line Weezy mentions Naomi Campbell, a super model, while in this one he references Leilani Leeane. Who happens to be very famous in the porn industry.\n\nWayne wishes he was with a girl with the personality and beauty of Naomi, but the willingness to go crazy in bed like Leilani.", "annotation_id": "3889369", "url": "https://genius.com/3889369", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Grindin’", "line": "I need a bitch like Naomi", "vault_lines": ["I need a bitch like Naomi", "I’m sweatin’ grindin’ this bitch, I need a shrine in this bitch"], "meaning": "Naomi Campbell is assumed here, a major super-model who hangs out with Kate Moss.\n\nNaomi is known worldwide for her perfect body and face while modelling.\n\n\n\nWayne really wants a girl as good looking as her, and it appears he may have found one, as he’s been spotted out with Christina Milian many times, and there are even rumours of her pregnancy.", "annotation_id": "3889347", "url": "https://genius.com/3889347", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Grindin’", "line": "I got news for the monogamous niggas Yo’ bitch fucking anonymous niggas", "vault_lines": ["I got news for the monogamous niggas", "Yo' bitch fucking anonymous niggas"], "meaning": "Monogamy is when someone is in a relationship with the same person throughout the course of their life. Weezy has to tell any dude who is monogamous that their girl may not have the same beliefs on the dynamics of relationships.", "annotation_id": "3889301", "url": "https://genius.com/3889301", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Grindin’", "line": "I, I, I want that Brigitte Bardot hanging over my bed Fifty mill’ in one room (Huh?)", "vault_lines": ["I, I, I want that Brigitte Bardot hanging over my bed", "Fifty mill' in one room (Huh?)"], "meaning": "In his 2013 Interview with GQ, Drake claimed that he wanted to be as rich as Roman Abramovich – a multi-billionaire art patron. Seems like he wants more than to just have this kind of money, he wants to own the art as well – he wants Andy Warhol’s Brigitte Bardot hanging in his room.\n\n\n\nIn 2012, the painting sold for $56 million.\n\nIt seems that Drake is now wanting artwork in his room, after criticizing Jay-Z for having so much.", "annotation_id": "3889298", "url": "https://genius.com/3889298", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Grindin’", "line": "The feds be spying on all of us nigga These hoes be lying to all of us nigga", "vault_lines": ["The feds be spying on all of us nigga", "These hoes be lying to all of us nigga"], "meaning": "Feds is a slang for agents from the FBI. Feds are known for spying phone calls, and instant messaging networks. They tend to monitor everyone’s online activities, including email, to prevent future illegal activities.\n\nLil Wayne’s crew is known for doing  illegitimate activities, and that’s why feds keep spying them. He even has a whole song concerning feds watching.\n\nMost of these hoes have a common trait, which is lying. Some women lie concerning their relationship status, or other things to get what they want from Lil Wayne and his niggas.", "annotation_id": "3889293", "url": "https://genius.com/3889293", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Grindin’", "line": "Gone, goin’ to LA where I’m tryna get high and do a song every day", "vault_lines": ["Gone, goin' to LA where I’m tryna get high and do a song every day"], "meaning": "Drake owns an eight million dollar compound in LA. It features multiple housing structures, one of the largest residential pools in America, and of course a recording studio.", "annotation_id": "3889196", "url": "https://genius.com/3889196", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Grindin’", "line": "You, you could ask anyone out here who running the game? And they’ll tell you the truth, man, they tell you (And they tell you)", "vault_lines": ["You, you could ask anyone out here who running the game?", "And they’ll tell you the truth, man, they tell you (And they tell you)"], "meaning": "This line references Kanye West’s GQ interview where Kanye talked about no longer being the most popular person in rap:\n\nCurrently that spot is taken [by Drake]. Let’s be honest — he got last summer. And I’d never given it up till last summer. It’s a real question for me. Do I want to?", "annotation_id": "3889191", "url": "https://genius.com/3889191", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Grindin’", "line": "Whew, I ain’t crazy, I’m krazy and all of my niggas chaotic Dressed in all black like they gothic Music too loud to hear sirens, we pop, pop, pop up where you stay Knock, knock, knock, anyone home?", "vault_lines": ["Whew, I ain’t crazy, I’m krazy and all of my niggas chaotic", "Dressed in all black like they gothic", "Music too loud to hear sirens, we pop, pop, pop up where you stay", "Knock, knock, knock, anyone home?", "That’s me and all my niggas", "I know, I’m selling all of my cars", "I’m selling all of my watches"], "meaning": "Wayne is on a whole ‘nother level of 'craziness’. Instead of being crazy, he is “Krazy”. Weezy and his homies are crazy enough break into your house, or even drive by where you stay with no fear of the police.\n\nWeezy could also be changing the ‘c’ at the beginning of ‘crazy’ to a K due to his Blood Gang affiliation.\n\nGothics dress in all black, as his niggas are about to commit a serious crime. They listen to some loud, gangsta music to get their heart pumping and in the “mobbing” frame of mind.\n\nHe also references the single “Krazy” that he released for Tha Carter V earlier this year.", "annotation_id": "3889183", "url": "https://genius.com/3889183", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Grindin’", "line": "Yeah I got a new vision for all my shit (For all my) I don’t know what to call that shit (Don’t know what to call it) I know, I’m selling all of my cars I’m selling all of my watches I’m selling diamonds and all of that shit", "vault_lines": ["Nigga I’m grindin’ for all my shit", "Grindin’ for all my shit", "Yeah, I’m grindin’ for all my shit", "Man, I’m grindin’ for all my shit", "I’m grindin’ for all my shit", "Where I got it from? Nevermind that shit", "I got a new vision for all my shit (For all my)", "I don’t know what to call that shit (Don’t know what to call it)", "I know, I’m selling all of my cars", "I’m selling all of my watches", "I’m selling diamonds and all of that shit", "Realized I don’t need that shit (Don’t need it)"], "meaning": "Drake has had a new outlook on the things he owns, and he has been selling all the material things that amount to temporary wealth.\n\nThis may be the result of a new outlook on life that places value in his artistry and legacy—a stark contrast to his sentiments on one of his earliest hits, “Successful,” where he placed emphasis on having luxuries as a measure of success.\n\nI want the money, money and the cars\nCars and the clothes, the hoes, I suppose\nI just wanna be, I just wanna be successful\n\nHis “new vision” includes more focused business ventures, such as his work with the Toronto Raptors and Apple Music.", "annotation_id": "3889163", "url": "https://genius.com/3889163", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Grindin’", "line": "Heard Jay Z got a new Cognac, where to find that shit?", "vault_lines": ["Heard Jay Z got a new Cognac, where to find that shit?"], "meaning": "This is a reference to Jay Z’s cognac brand, D'usse. In fact, Wayne has a song dedicated to the drink: “D'usse”.\n\nHe’s also saying if you’re not rich, you would not know where to get it from. The rap cliche line: “Don’t ask where I got it from, you can’t afford it”.", "annotation_id": "3889122", "url": "https://genius.com/3889122", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Grindin’", "line": "I’m tryna turn M’s to B’s in this bitch (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I’m tryna turn M’s to B’s in this bitch (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Perhaps a reference to his Twitter exchange with Oklahoma oil billionaire T Boone Pickens, highlighting the difference between a billion and a mere million.\n\n\n\nA recent article explored why hip-hop has no billionaires. With his triple-threat capacity, Drake only needs a bit of a brand expansion to go from a milli (a milli, a milli, a milli…) to a billi.", "annotation_id": "3889090", "url": "https://genius.com/3889090", "state": "accepted", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Grindin’", "line": "Pick, Michael Jackson to Jordan to Tyson to Myers", "vault_lines": ["Pick, Michael Jackson to Jordan to Tyson to Myers"], "meaning": "Like Jay-Z in “Niggas in Paris”. Wayne is comparing different famous Michaels.\n\n\n\nMichael Jackson the King of Pop\n\nMichael Jordan, one of the greatet basketball players of all time, current owner of the Charlotte Hornets, famous for playing for the Chicago Bulls, making slamdunks from the free throw line, starring in the hit movie Space Jam and owning the popular sneaker line, the Air Jordans.\n\nMichael Tyson or commonly known as Mike Tyson or Iron Mike. He was the undisputed heavyweight champion of the world. He is also known for appearing in the movie “The Hangover” and biting a man’s ear off during a fight.\n\nMichael Myers is a famous fictional character from the Halloween series of slasher films.\n\n\n\n\n\nLil Wayne’s middle name is Michael. He’s comparing himself to these iconic figures to make a statement that he deserves a mention as a legend in hip hop.\n\nAlso a reference to one of The Notorious B.I.G.’s most famous lines from “Victory”:\n\nI perform like Mike\nAnyone — Tyson, Jordan, Jackson”", "annotation_id": "3889076", "url": "https://genius.com/3889076", "state": "accepted", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Having Our Way", "status": "done", "targets": 19, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Migos-having-our-way-lyrics", "genius_title": "Having Our Way", "genius_id": 6894107, "source": "api"}
