{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Girls Go Bad", "line": "Watching Boyz n The Hood Lets take a drive down memory lane", "vault_lines": ["Lets take a drive down memory lane"], "meaning": "Growing up, Game watched “Boyz N The Hood” a lot. The next song, “Ricky” is based off of the movie.", "annotation_id": "338548", "url": "https://genius.com/338548", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Girls Go Bad", "line": "Word on the news stand, Alicia got herself a man And thats my nigga Swizzy,", "vault_lines": ["Word on the news stand, Alicia got herself a man", "And thats my nigga Swizzy,"], "meaning": "Swizz Beatz is married to Alicia Keys.\n\n\n\nGame and Swizz previously collaborated on Game’s “Scream On ‘Em”", "annotation_id": "338546", "url": "https://genius.com/338546", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Girls Go Bad", "line": "All the girls that hold it down, getting beat on by they man", "vault_lines": ["All the girls that hold it down, getting beat on by they man"], "meaning": "Ironic that Game says this.. because three tracks earlier on the same album he suggests that he’d “snatch up Rihanna and throw her in front of a f—-n' train.” He may be homies with Chris Brown but that doesn’t at all justify this…..\n\n\n\nGuess Game doesn’t want to put all his eggs in one basket; part of him wants to keep the good girls from going bad, but a part of him wants to rap like the rapper that rap wants him to be. Similarly, on Martians Vs. Goblins, Game says he “spits like he had kids with Erykah Badu” (pointing out that Jay Electronica, Andre 3000, and The D.O.C. are all great rappers.) And noteworthy, while Common didn’t have kids with her, the two dated. Thus, the comparison can be made, and Common is known for having empowering lyrics for women (Andre 3000, who is actually the father of one of Erykah’s children, is actually quite empowering towards women too, especially with his intricate commentary on verses such as on The Real Her from Drake’s Take Care.) Yet maybe even Common can’t put all his eggs into one basket either. Check out the skit at the end of his song “The 6th Sense” ft. Bilal (definitely worth a listen, great satire towards rappers today and their façade with respect to… well, respecting women.)\n\n(skit starts around 4:15)\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LHv3-ESOOQE\n\nIt’s tough for artists to truly speak with respect towards women, because many would rather be consistent and relevant.\n\nWhile the R.E.D. Album is certainly a great purchase, songs like Martians Vs. Goblins with Tyler, the Creator and Taylor Made with Wiz Khalifa (not on the album) make it seem like Game is trying too hard to stay relevant. For him to hop on the Odd Future band wagon and the Taylor Gang bandwagon is a bit over the top… he’s coming off as a bit wishy-washy, because five years ago he probably would have talked shit about those camps. Good example of the inevitable decline of most rap careers. Lots of great rappers either lost it or they ain’t alive, sacrificing consistency for relevance.", "annotation_id": "334948", "url": "https://genius.com/334948", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Girls Go Bad", "line": "Do it girl, I’ll be the king to your Queen Latifah", "vault_lines": ["Do it girl, I'll be the king to your Queen Latifah"], "meaning": "Going off the previous line, he’s explaining his natural appreciation for women who have a lil' mo' cushin' fo' tha pushin'. (see below)\n\n\n\nQueen Latifah was also in the recording session of this song.", "annotation_id": "325813", "url": "https://genius.com/325813", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Girls Go Bad", "line": "This song remind me of Cat from Philly, a girl I used to love", "vault_lines": ["This song remind me of Cat from Philly, a girl I used to love"], "meaning": "A reference to Catya Washington, a model/video vixen from Philly.  She was in his video for Best I Ever Had and it is rumored that they dated.  She admits they dated.", "annotation_id": "324444", "url": "https://genius.com/324444", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Girls Go Bad", "line": "We don’t beat on Kat Stacks, we just bring it to an end", "vault_lines": ["We don't beat on Kat Stacks, we just bring it to an end"], "meaning": "Kat Stacks is a blogger famous for “exposing” rappers, as well as other musicians and even athletes by sleeping with them and then making a blog about it, trash talking them on everything from penis size to who peed the bed — then gives out their cell phone numbers.\n\n\n\nGame is saying that instead of beating her up, like in the video below, he would just ignore her. http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pawtO8xMh1E", "annotation_id": "324236", "url": "https://genius.com/324236", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Girls Go Bad", "line": "You want some money nigga? I ain’t get a deal with ya You ain’t saying nothing, you like a still picture You better thank God you still breathing air Cause you coulda went out like your boy Steve McNair", "vault_lines": ["You want some money nigga? I ain't get a deal with ya", "You ain't saying nothing, you like a still picture", "You better thank God you still breathing air", "Cause you coulda went out like your boy Steve McNair"], "meaning": "Game referring to his Father. His father wants, and needs money but Game is not dealing with him..\n\nMcNair was killed by his girlfriend/mistress, so his dad should thank God that his mom never took matters into her own hands.", "annotation_id": "324162", "url": "https://genius.com/324162", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Girls Go Bad", "line": "And we don’t wanna see Nicki fighting Lil Kim", "vault_lines": ["And we don't wanna see Nicki fighting Lil Kim"], "meaning": "The Game feels the same way Trina does about the beef between female rappers Nicki Minaj and Lil Kim.\n\nTrina had this to say on MTV NEWS:\n\nWe’re all ladies. Can’t we just make music and get our paper and keep it moving?! We all respect Kim. She opened the doors for us females. It’s all good – everybody’s eating, what’s the issue?\"", "annotation_id": "324127", "url": "https://genius.com/324127", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Girls Go Bad", "line": "And put roses on the grave of Kanye’s mama", "vault_lines": ["And put roses on the grave of Kanye's mama"], "meaning": "In a tribute to Kanye’s fallen mother, Game throws in a little play on Kanye’s song Roses, which is Kanye’s song about his grandmother’s hospital stay, which didn’t end in death", "annotation_id": "324120", "url": "https://genius.com/324120", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Girls Go Bad", "line": "I just had a daughter", "vault_lines": ["I just had a daughter"], "meaning": "Game had a daughter on August 21st 2010 named Cali Dream Taylor.", "annotation_id": "318755", "url": "https://genius.com/318755", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Good Girls Go Bad", "line": "My daddy used to beat up on my mama all day So I took my Chronic album and slept in the hallway", "vault_lines": ["My daddy used to beat up on my mama all day", "So I took my Chronic album and slept in the hallway"], "meaning": "He couldn’t stand watching his dad beat his mom, so he slept out in the hallway, listening to his favorite album to comfort him (The Chronic was like his teddy bear..)\n\n\n\nThe Chronic is one of his favorite albums. He has mentioned this in very many songs:\n-“The Documentary”\n-“Put You On The Game”\n-“California Vacation”\n\nGame often talks about his abusive father in songs..", "annotation_id": "318019", "url": "https://genius.com/318019", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
