{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 On / Thotful", "line": "(Mustard on the beat, ho)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Mustard’s producer tag in audible in the intro. The tag is sampled directly from YG’s at the end of his March 2011 track “I’m Good\":\n\nYeah, uh huh, that’s what I thought, motherfucker\nMustard on the beat, ho!\n\nIt has been frequently used in songs produced by Mustard, such as on Jeremih’s June 2014 track “Don’t Tell ’Em,” YG’s September 2013 hit “My Nigga,” and YG’s March 2014 track “Who Do You Love?”", "annotation_id": "17985352", "url": "https://genius.com/17985352", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 On / Thotful", "line": "Akinyele in the telly", "vault_lines": ["Akinyele in the telly"], "meaning": "Akinyele was a rapper prominent in the 1990s-2000s that “specialized” in sexually explicit rap music spawning albums like “Vagina Diner” and “Put It In Your Mouth”\n\n“Telly” is slang for hotel. So OB is saying that his girl is getting “sexually explicit” in the hotel.\n\nHe also made an Instagram post with this line. (click the image to read the caption on OB’s IG)\n\nhttp://instagram.com/p/rAuJD2nzdu/", "annotation_id": "3482638", "url": "https://genius.com/3482638", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 On / Thotful", "line": "For like the past five years All these niggas wanna shine, I got the flashlight here, man", "vault_lines": ["For like the past five years", "All these niggas wanna shine, I got the flashlight here, man"], "meaning": "It’s been 5 years since Drake’s legendary mixtape dropped. Drizzy has been the man in rap since then, and some could only dream to achieve what he has in that period of time.\n\n\n\nDrake is also saying that he is responsible for many artists 15 minutes of fame (e.g; The Weeknd, Migos, PARTYNEXTDOOR, and the list goes on), by saying they got their shine from the flashlight he’s holding.", "annotation_id": "3204894", "url": "https://genius.com/3204894", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 On / Thotful", "line": "You know I got another bar for ya I’ma chill baby, we don’t want the devil in this bitch, nah", "vault_lines": ["You know I got another bar for ya", "I'ma chill baby, we don't want the devil in this bitch, nah", "And you know, and you know, and you know"], "meaning": "Saying that he’s “got another bar” could be referencing a Xanax bar, given OB’s following line “I'mma chill baby”.\n\nHowever following the previous line, if OB dropped another bar referencing the number 6, he would have mentioned ‘six’ 3 times in a row – 666 – which people often associate with the devil.", "annotation_id": "3193723", "url": "https://genius.com/3193723", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 On / Thotful", "line": "Summer mine Yeah, the summer’s mine Yeah, the summer’s mine", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, the summer's mine"], "meaning": "This is very similar to the opening lines of Drake’s “Good Ones Go Interlude”\n\nSummer’s mine\nI swear I said about a hundred times, I'ma need it back", "annotation_id": "3191577", "url": "https://genius.com/3191577", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 On / Thotful", "line": "You can hear it in my voice, I’m goin’ way in", "vault_lines": ["You can hear it in my voice, I'm goin' way in"], "meaning": "#Wordplay!\n\nway in = Wayne\n\nWayne being fellow YMCMB rapper/founder, Lil Wayne, whom Drake collaborates with often.\n\n\n\nAlso a reference to I’m Goin In, one of the first tracks that Drake & Wayne collaborated on.", "annotation_id": "3190837", "url": "https://genius.com/3190837", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 On / Thotful", "line": "Woop, comin’ from the 6 side", "vault_lines": ["Woop, comin' from the 6 side"], "meaning": "Lately Drake has been referring to Toronto as “6” because of its area codes 416/647. He has a tattoo of it too.\n\n\n\nThis wasn’t the only time that Drake mentioned ‘6’.\n\nhttp://rapgenius.com/3271778", "annotation_id": "3190648", "url": "https://genius.com/3190648", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 On / Thotful", "line": "Flip modes on ya quick, got a few sides", "vault_lines": ["Flip modes on ya quick, got a few sides"], "meaning": "Drake is switching Modes from “softer” Singer/nice guy Drake to Cocky/Confident Dope Spitter Drake that people often seem to sleep on/forget about!\n\nDrake also continues his Busta Rhymes reference from the previous line, now mentioning the Flipmode Squad.", "annotation_id": "3190602", "url": "https://genius.com/3190602", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 On / Thotful", "line": "I got ’em all a check without the woo-hah", "vault_lines": ["I got 'em all a check without the woo-hah"], "meaning": "Playing off the homophones check and cheque and the well known line from Busta’s first single…\n\nWoo-Hah! I got you all in check\n\n…Drizzy’s helping all his OVO homies get paid (“I got ‘em all a cheque”).\n\n\n\nThough popularized by Busta, the phrase was originally used in “8th Wonder” by Sugar Hill Gang.", "annotation_id": "3190590", "url": "https://genius.com/3190590", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 On / Thotful", "line": "Your man’s gone and you don’t miss him Book you flights and confirmation Southwest Airlines you’ll still take it", "vault_lines": ["Me, you and your bitch", "Your man's gone and you don't miss him", "Book you flights and confirmation", "Southwest Airlines you'll still take it", "And you know, and you know, and you know"], "meaning": "Many believe that this refers to Karrueche Tran, Chris Brown’s former girlfriend. On a now deleted Instagram post, Brown said:\n\nI was locked up for damn near 4 months and only got 1 visit from you while u was hosting parties and taking secret trips to Toronto, going on dates with Drake\n\nWhat makes this worse is that Brown and Drake used to have beef, reportedly over another girl, Rihanna. Apparently, the best way to hurt someone you hate is to sleep with the person they love.\n\nIt doesn’t stop there–she’d be willing to fly with the lowly Southwest Airlines just to see him. It’s obvious that she really wanted to get away.", "annotation_id": "3190588", "url": "https://genius.com/3190588", "state": "pending", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 On / Thotful", "line": "You’re so thotful, you’re so thotful You’re so bad, girl, you’re so awful", "vault_lines": ["You're so thotful, you're so thotful", "You're so bad, girl, you're so awful", "You're so thotful, you're so, you're so"], "meaning": "A play on the term thoughtful, the woman in question is acting thotful, having left her partner to partake in casual sex with Drake.\n\nThe term thot originated as Chicago slang, meaning “that hoe over there.”\n\nNote the homophone for thoughtful and thotful.", "annotation_id": "3190554", "url": "https://genius.com/3190554", "state": "pending", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 On / Thotful", "line": "Crib in Calabasas, man, I call that shit the safe house Thirty minutes from L.A., the shit is way out", "vault_lines": ["Crib in Calabasas, man, I call that shit the safe house", "Thirty minutes from L.A., the shit is way out"], "meaning": "Calabasas is a city in California that is near LA, particularly 29.5 miles away. Calabasas has many notable wealthy residents including the Kardashian family, Will Smith, and Jennifer Lopez among others.\n\nDrake indicates that he has a house in Calabasas that he uses as a safe haven to get away from the media and troubles of the world. That’s a pretty expensive safe house, considering the median home value is just over a million dollars there.\n\nAlso note that Drake has a house in Hidden Hills, CA, which is only 9 minutes away from Calabasas.", "annotation_id": "3190397", "url": "https://genius.com/3190397", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 On / Thotful", "line": "Miracle, sit your ass right here, man", "vault_lines": ["Miracle, sit your ass right here, man"], "meaning": "He could be advising people to sit and admire his work and talent, but it’s most likely a simple reference to the beautiful model Miracle Watts, and we all know Drake has had history with vixens in the past..", "annotation_id": "3190389", "url": "https://genius.com/3190389", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
