{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Solid", "line": "Chrome Hearts", "vault_lines": ["Man, I love all of her Chrome Hearts"], "meaning": "Chrome Hearts is a luxury brand from Hollywood, founded in 1988 by Richard Stark, Leonard Kamhout and John Bowman. It is currently co-owned by Richard Stark and his wife Laurie Lynn Stark. Its logo contains a cross with the brand name around it on a circular ribbon. The brand produces silver, gold, and diamond accessories, alongside eyewear, leather, clothing and furniture", "annotation_id": "27360660", "url": "https://genius.com/27360660", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Solid", "line": "You had a buzz, but that shit was too little I promise you never was hot", "vault_lines": ["You had a buzz, but that shit was too little", "I promise you never was hot"], "meaning": "Based on current court preceding this is most likely a diss towards YFN Lucci, who is a fellow ATL rapper with a known ongoing feud with YSL members", "annotation_id": "26405044", "url": "https://genius.com/26405044", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Solid", "line": "I just put macaroni cheese in my pocket And it came with the sides", "vault_lines": ["I just put macaroni cheese in my pocket", "And it came with the sides"], "meaning": "Young Thug refers to Mac and Cheese, a common side dish and explains that he pockets it. This may be used as an equivalent to money, suggesting that Thug pockets the cash he collects.", "annotation_id": "25134880", "url": "https://genius.com/25134880", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Solid", "line": "Phantom whips I’m ridin’, all my friendships solid I get big deposits, all my whips exotic", "vault_lines": ["Phantom whips I'm ridin', all my friendships solid", "I get big deposits, all my whips exotic"], "meaning": "A Phantom is a luxury automobile made by Rolls Royce; Gunna keeps it 100 with his people, so they have his back, too; Gunna doesn’t see pennies in his bank account, he has big bucks from shows and business ventures; all of Gunna’s cars are, like the aforementioned Phantom, high-end, foreign, fancy, fly…and likely fast.", "annotation_id": "23714744", "url": "https://genius.com/23714744", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Solid", "line": "Phantom whips I’m ridin’, all my friendships solid", "vault_lines": ["Phantom whips I'm ridin', all my friendships solid"], "meaning": "A whip is an expensive, flashy sports car or sedan. Here Drake, is refering to the Rolls-Royce Phantom, an expensive, disproportionate deluxe car starting at 400 000 euros.\n\nSawetteee the ex-girlfriend of Quavo has bought one recently to take revenge on him from taking the car he bought him back because she left him… If you know where she took the money tell it here :) .", "annotation_id": "23399704", "url": "https://genius.com/23399704", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Solid", "line": "And I’m still hard body, I don’t fear nobody", "vault_lines": ["And I'm still hard body, I don't fear nobody"], "meaning": "Gunna makes a reference to his first mixtape, Hard Body, which he released in 2013 when he was still going by “Yung Gunna.” He’s saying that the fame hasn’t turned him soft.", "annotation_id": "22779701", "url": "https://genius.com/22779701", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Solid", "line": "Life’s Monopoly, goin’ broke not an option", "vault_lines": ["Life's Monopoly, goin' broke not an option"], "meaning": "This line is a nod to the popular board game “Monopoly,” a game where the objective is to buy as many of the in-game properties as possible to monopolize your worth. In order to do so you must be able to make smart financial decisions without going bankrupt which would mean you lost the game. Gunna views life as a board game, so going “broke” would mean he lost the game.", "annotation_id": "22761469", "url": "https://genius.com/22761469", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Solid", "line": "Stories you told me ’bout him, I can see that it’s night and day (He told me the truth)", "vault_lines": ["Stories you told me 'bout him, I can see that it's night and day (He told me the truth)"], "meaning": "This girl tells Drake lies in an attempt to make him switch on the people around him.\n\nWith “night and day,” Drake draws a contrast between the lies this girl originally told him and the actual truths, similar to the difference between clearness and darkness.\n\nDrake is no stranger to people switching up on him and telling him lies in attempt to cause problems. For that, he has surrounded himself with people he knows are loyal to him. He previously touched on this in his 2020’s song “War”:\n\nEveryone I know has codenames, anyone I’m beefin' with is a no-name", "annotation_id": "22755992", "url": "https://genius.com/22755992", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Solid", "line": "Since I been makin’ donations, see you like United Way (You know how I do)", "vault_lines": ["Since I been makin' donations, see you like United Way (You know how I do)"], "meaning": "United Way is widely considered to be one of the largest non-profit organizations in the world, providing fundraising campaigns for several aspects of the community.\n\nDrake compares this girl to United Way, as he continues to spend his money on her without any return, making it seem as he’s giving her “donations”. For that, he demands something in return, whether it being sexual or moral.", "annotation_id": "22755882", "url": "https://genius.com/22755882", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Solid", "line": "The touch is the Midas", "vault_lines": ["The touch is the Midas"], "meaning": "The legend of King Midas is a popular anecdote in Greek mythology. After Midas returned a long-lost satyr to Dionysus, the God promised him a wish. Midas wished that everything he touched would turn turn into gold, but this ultimately led to his death from starvation because his food became inedible.\n\n\n\nGunna compares his decadent, gold-filled lifestyle to possessing Midas' golden touch.", "annotation_id": "22755335", "url": "https://genius.com/22755335", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Solid", "line": "She said, “Fuck me and cum,” I just do it like Loverboy Nike", "vault_lines": ["She said, \"Fuck me and cum,\" I just do it like Loverboy Nike"], "meaning": "Gunna refers to the Certified Lover Boy x Nike merchandise drop in 2020. The collection features hoodies, t-shirts, socks, and hats with “CLB” in elegant script as well as heart icons and lipstick stains. Nike’s famous slogan is “Just Do It”, encouraging athletes to pursue their ambitions.\n\n\n\nCertified Lover Boy is the title of Drake’s upcoming studio album, which was expected to release in January 2021 but was eventually delayed.\nDrizzy first announced Certified Lover Boy in an Instagram caption in August 2020. The post accompanied the release of his late-summer hit, “Laugh Now Cry Later” featuring Lil Durk.", "annotation_id": "22755212", "url": "https://genius.com/22755212", "state": "accepted", "votes": 36, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Solid", "line": "Yeah, I just told ’em if he play Then we stoppin’ the growth of they dreads (Stoppin’ it)", "vault_lines": ["I want it painted, yeah", "Yeah, I just told 'em if he play", "Then we stoppin' the growth of they dreads (Stoppin' it)"], "meaning": "Thug threatens death on anyone who tries to come for him or his Young Stoner Life labelmates. Without the operation of vital organs, one’s hair, in this case dreadlocks, stops growing. Though hair may appear longer after death, this illusion is caused by skin retraction through the dehydration of the body.\n\nThugger made a similar comparison between hair and death on his 2015 track, “Don’t Know”:\n\nPush your top back ‘cause I feel like it a wig", "annotation_id": "22755136", "url": "https://genius.com/22755136", "state": "accepted", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Solid", "line": "Hop in a tank and move militant, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Hop in a tank and move militant, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah"], "meaning": "Drake is once again rapping about his insane car collection this time referring to his G650 Maybach Landaulet which is the only one of its kind in Canada.", "annotation_id": "22754496", "url": "https://genius.com/22754496", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Solid", "line": "Find me somewhere out in London, you know that’s the hideaway", "vault_lines": ["Find me somewhere out in London, you know that's the hideaway"], "meaning": "Drake has been known to party in London occasionally, such as in 2018 during his Scorpion rollout. He shouted the capital out on 2018’s “Nonstop”, rapping:\n\nBitch, I move through London with the Eurostep (Two)", "annotation_id": "22753285", "url": "https://genius.com/22753285", "state": "pending", "votes": 50, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Solid", "line": "Walkin’ from here to my bedroom, it feel like it’s miles away (There’s too many rooms)", "vault_lines": ["Walkin' from here to my bedroom, it feel like it's miles away (There's too many rooms)"], "meaning": "Drake flaunts the size of his massive $100 million dollar home, nicknamed The Embassy. The luxurious Toronto mansion has over 50,000 square feet, including an indoor pool and a NBA-size basketball court. Below is a photo of the 3,200 square foot master bedroom which Drake is referring to in the lyric:", "annotation_id": "22753101", "url": "https://genius.com/22753101", "state": "pending", "votes": 53, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Girl (Remix)", "status": "done", "targets": 9, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Jamie-foxx-digital-girl-remix-lyrics", "genius_title": "Digital Girl (Remix)", "genius_id": 786, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Girl (Remix)", "line": "I just hit Alt, Tab Switchin’ in between two convos", "vault_lines": ["I just hit Alt, Tab", "Switchin' in between two convos"], "meaning": "The Alt + Tab keyboard shortcut is a task switcher that lets you quickly jump between all your open applications or windows on a computer. Drake is fitting the theme of Digital with this clever computer reference, interchanging his conversations as he does his computer windows.", "annotation_id": "37987912", "url": "https://genius.com/37987912", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Girl (Remix)", "line": "We can work it out, no Nintendo", "vault_lines": ["We can work it out, no Nintendo"], "meaning": "I think he is talking about Wii Fit because Wii Fit is an exercising game", "annotation_id": "22592480", "url": "https://genius.com/22592480", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Girl (Remix)", "line": "Plus every good girl wanna go bad In Playboy mags like Stacey Dash Or Kim Kardash’, and be a lady aaaaat it", "vault_lines": ["Plus every good girl wanna go bad", "In Playboy mags like Stacey Dash", "Or Kim Kardash', and be a lady aaaaat it"], "meaning": "Kanye echoes his mentor and longtime collaborator Jay-Z’s sentiment from his 2001 single “Song Cry”:\n\nThey say you can’t turn a bad girl good\nBut once a good girl’s gone bad, she’s gone forever\n\nPlayboy is an iconic and notorious men’s lifestyle and entertainment magazine known for its pictures of nude and partially nude women. A woman featured in such a suggestive and risqué manner could be seen to be rebelling against typical female conformity.\n\nStacey Dash, the actress who appeared in the music video for Kanye’s 2004 song “All Falls Down,”, posed nude in a 2006 edition of Playboy.\n\nModel, designer, and reality star Kim Kardashian also posed nude for a 2007 issue of the magazine. Years after this song was released, Kim would go on to date Kanye West, and the two would eventually get married on May 24, 2014.\n\n\n\nIt is also worth noting that Rihanna, who has worked with Kanye and Drake, both of whom are featured on this song, named her 2007 hit album Good Girl Gone Bad.", "annotation_id": "18872255", "url": "https://genius.com/18872255", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Girl (Remix)", "line": "[Verse 4: Kanye West]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Kanye spit this verse back in 2008 on the Angie Martinez Show on Hot 97.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fLR8S1uTaw8", "annotation_id": "4637528", "url": "https://genius.com/4637528", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Girl (Remix)", "line": "They say I dress white, but my swag so urban", "vault_lines": ["They say I dress white, but my swag so urban"], "meaning": "Kanye is known for his simple yet refined clothing style (read: designer labels, all though he wore simpler yet refined clothing before the fame) even though other rappers say he dresses like a male model\n\n\n\n\n\nBut, like he said on Cold\n\n\nDon’t talk to me ‘bout style, nigga, I’ll mothafuckin’ embarrass you\n\nTalking ‘bout clothes, I’ll mothafuckin’ embarrass you.\n\n\n So it doesn’t matter what people see him wearing, it will always be better than what they have on.", "annotation_id": "1633884", "url": "https://genius.com/1633884", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Girl (Remix)", "line": "And I remember Amy, she used to AIM me", "vault_lines": ["And I remember Amy, she used to AIM me"], "meaning": "Wow, quite a Paronomasia there, Drake!\n\nDrake uses two “homonyms”, Amy and AIM me. AIM being:\n\nAOL\nInstant\nMessenger\n\n(which was an old way to mack online, before Facebook pokes..)", "annotation_id": "38263", "url": "https://genius.com/38263", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Girl (Remix)", "line": "Who’s that peekin in my window?", "vault_lines": ["Who's that peekin in my window?"], "meaning": "Allusion to Goodie Mobb’s 1995 hit “Cell Therapy”\n\nHe is referring to his computer screen as a window", "annotation_id": "38258", "url": "https://genius.com/38258", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Girl (Remix)", "line": "I like ’em brown, yellow, Puerto Rican, or Persian Dashiki, kimono, or turban", "vault_lines": ["I like 'em brown, yellow, Puerto Rican, or Persian", "Dashiki, kimono, or turban"], "meaning": "Kanye loves all the women all the women of the world: yellow, red and black and white\n\nThis is also an allusion to the A Tribe Called Quest song “Electric Relaxation”:\n\nI like em black, yellow, Puerto Rican or Haitian", "annotation_id": "35571", "url": "https://genius.com/35571", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Digital Girl (Remix)", "line": "Some girls’ll make you wait longer than A.C. Green Passion of the Christ, 33-Year Old Virgin", "vault_lines": ["Some girls'll make you wait longer than A.C. Green", "Passion of the Christ, 33-Year Old Virgin"], "meaning": "A.C. Green was a professional basketball player who was deeply religious and claims to have been a virgin throughout his entire NBA career!!\n\nJesus Christ was also notable for his purity and remained that way until his crucifixion (a “33-year old virgin”)\n\n\n\nLong story short Kanye is saying girls please “just give it up”", "annotation_id": "35569", "url": "https://genius.com/35569", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "More Than A Meme", "status": "done", "targets": 2, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Saturday-night-live-more-than-a-meme-lyrics", "genius_title": "More Than A Meme", "genius_id": 2473363, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "More Than A Meme", "line": "[Interlude: Drake + Drake as Rihanna]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake interpolates Rihanna’s smash single “Work”, which he is featured on.  He performs this part of the monologue as Rihanna, while wearing a wig.", "annotation_id": "9154362", "url": "https://genius.com/9154362", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "More Than A Meme", "line": "You can not move in with me if Trump wins I’m sorry, that’s no go", "vault_lines": ["You can not move in with me if Trump wins", "I'm sorry, that's no go"], "meaning": "In order to become the nominee for a political party in the Unites States, one must win primary elections by popular vote, which Trump has won by a landslide multiple times for the Republican party.\n\nBeing the Republican party nominees has moved Trump closer to potentially being president. Many Americans are so opposed to Donald Trump being elected president that they have stated they will move to Canada, Drake’s home country, if he is successful.\n\nThere is evidence that when Trump wins primaries,  searches for “how to move to Canada” spike over 350%, proving the fear of his potential presidency to be real.", "annotation_id": "9154351", "url": "https://genius.com/9154351", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "status": "done", "targets": 31, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Travis-scott-meltdown-lyrics", "genius_title": "MELTDOWN", "genius_id": 9368450, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "I’ll fuck a nigga bitch but she can’t have the baby (Have the baby)", "vault_lines": ["I'll fuck a nigga bitch but she can't have the baby (Have the baby)"], "meaning": "This can be a shot a Kylie Jenner, the mother of his 2 children. He had 2 babies by her. Around the time of the first one he didn’t want it to be out in public when everyone found out who the father was expecting", "annotation_id": "31294858", "url": "https://genius.com/31294858", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "Lil’ shawty a therapist (Yeah), poppin’ her shit", "vault_lines": ["Lil' shawty a therapist (Yeah), poppin' her shit"], "meaning": "A very well wordplay from La flame, this can be a triple entendres\n• the girl can be twerking(popping her ass)\n• she can be popping pills because Travis scott is known to be around a lot of drugs\n• She also can be talking shit (popping her shit) hence the term “popping her shit”.", "annotation_id": "31294827", "url": "https://genius.com/31294827", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "Yeah, is you fucking crazy? (Nah) Is you fucking crazy? (What?) Is you fucking crazy? (Nah, nah) Is you fucking crazy? Yeah Is you fucking crazy or what? Is you fuckin’, is you fuckin’ Is you fucking crazy?", "vault_lines": ["Is you fuckin' crazy? Is you fuckin' crazy? (Ah)", "Yeah, is you fucking crazy? (Nah)", "Is you fucking crazy? (What?)", "Is you fucking crazy? Yeah", "Is you fucking crazy or what?", "Is you fuckin', is you fuckin'", "Is you fucking crazy or what? Is you fucking crazy? (Fuckin' crazy)", "Is you fucking crazy? Uh"], "meaning": "Travis Scott and Drake throughout “MELTDOWN” go back and forth asking each other if they’re crazy.\n\nWhile it began in response to the end of Drake’s opening verse, it may also be a nod to the duo’s RIAA-diamond-certified hit, “SICKO MODE” from Scott’s 2018 record, ASTROWORLD — as the word “Sicko” is used to refer to a person mentally sick.\n\n“SICKO MODE” RIAA diamond certification.", "annotation_id": "29466410", "url": "https://genius.com/29466410", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "[Segue: Travis Scott]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Soon after the release of UTOPIA, fans noticed that the segue between Drake and Travis Scott uses a chord progression reminiscent of Kanye West’s 2013 song “New Slaves.”\n\nAdditionally, Travis had co-produced several songs on Yeezus, including the aforementioned “New Slaves.” It’s also important to note Travis' countless other Ye samples on UTOPIA. All of this led fans to believe the beats' similarities were intentional.\n\nAs fans had called out the production similarities, Travis didn’t sugarcoat Ye’s influence on his art. Instead, during his 2023 Circus Maximus concert in Rome, Italy, he credited Ye for his success, exclaiming:\n\nThere is no UTOPIA without Kanye West, [and] there is no Travis Scott without Kanye West", "annotation_id": "29457009", "url": "https://genius.com/29457009", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "Teatime like I got a cup of this shit", "vault_lines": ["Teatime like I got a cup of this shit"], "meaning": "The term: ‘tee-time,’ could be interpreted in two ways, in golf a Tee is a wooden stake that helps support a golf ball when you swing so teetime could be interpreted as ‘I’m getting my game,’ on or ‘I’m a player.’\n\n\n\nIt’s worth noting that in golf when you win a award it’s called a ‘cup.’\n\n\n\nAlso, [tee,] tea is commonly served in a teacup, so tea time is usually a gathering of people that is ready to ‘Spill the tea,’ or give out information.\n\nLess likely interpretation is that you can put a Mug or Cup on a t-shirt.\nLil Wayne who’s also known as ’T-Wayne,‘ is known for rocking a styrofoam cup, and Tyga who’s also known as T-raw sample 'drink in my cup,’ for his song: ‘Ready to Fuck.’", "annotation_id": "29351749", "url": "https://genius.com/29351749", "state": "pending", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "Blickey hanging on my side, it’s like it’s really hanging (Blickey, blickey, blaow)", "vault_lines": ["Blickey hanging on my side, it's like it's really hanging (Blickey, blickey, blaow)"], "meaning": "An image of Travis carrying a firearm or weapon (referred to as a “blickey”) on his side. The phrase “it’s like it’s really hanging” suggests that the firearm is visible and prominent as if it’s literally hanging from his side. The sound effects “blickey, blickey, blaow” could symbolize the action of drawing and firing the weapon.\n\nInterpreting these lines in the broader context of the song or Travis' style, he might be conveying an element of bravado, toughness, or street credibility. The use of such imagery could be intended to evoke a sense of power or danger associated with Travis.\n\nAdditionally, this kind of language is commonly found in hip-hop and rap lyrics, where artists often draw upon vivid imagery to communicate various aspects of their lives, experiences, or personas.", "annotation_id": "29340081", "url": "https://genius.com/29340081", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "Tee time like golf at a quarter to six", "vault_lines": ["Tee time like golf at a quarter to six"], "meaning": "A Tee Time is the time you want to play at a given golf course. It’s basically a golf course reservation.\nTee time’s purpose is to help organize players on the course and to maintain golfers’ flow around the course.", "annotation_id": "29220772", "url": "https://genius.com/29220772", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "Swanging in the pickup truck, baby, fuck Mercedes (Fuck Mercedes)", "vault_lines": ["Swanging in the pickup truck, baby, fuck Mercedes (Fuck Mercedes)"], "meaning": "Swangin is the act of switching lanes rapidly whilst driving. The term originated in Travis' hometown of Houston.", "annotation_id": "29192147", "url": "https://genius.com/29192147", "state": "pending", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "How many Texas boys done ran it up? A couple, maybe (Couple, maybe)", "vault_lines": ["How many Texas boys done ran it up? A couple, maybe (Couple, maybe)"], "meaning": "Travis Scott is from Houston, Texas which makes him a “Texas Boy”. Despite this, Travis has earned multiple RIAA awards and top chart hits. A example of this is his single “Sicko Mode” which peaked number one on the billboard charts.\n\n“Ran it up\" means you earned and worked hard for a large amount of money. It also means you are now earning more than you were before. Travis then says, “A couple maybe,\" meaning not many people from Texas get as much money as Travis. Travis could be mentioning Scarface Or Don Toliver  in the lyric \"A couple maybe” because both of these artists are from Texas. Don Toliver and Travis Scott have featured before in the songs “CAN’T SAY” and “Flocky Flocky”.", "annotation_id": "29189630", "url": "https://genius.com/29189630", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "My dick just got hard ’cause a wire just hit", "vault_lines": ["My dick just got hard 'cause a wire just hit"], "meaning": "Drake is implying that he has received a large amount of cash through a wire transfer—enough money to give him an erection.\n\nWire transfers are a digital method to move money quickly and securely between two electronic bank accounts.", "annotation_id": "29188730", "url": "https://genius.com/29188730", "state": "accepted", "votes": 60, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "T’d up right now", "vault_lines": ["T'd up right now"], "meaning": "“T’d up” is Toronto slang that traces its roots back to Driftwood/Wass Gang’s Robin Banks, who coined the term “TT,” meaning “Too Turnt.”\n\nThe term is most famously used by Drake in his May 2020, “Time Flies” in which he raps:\n\nYeah, I’m outside in an AMG\nRight outside, TT\nToo turnt, baby girl, you know me, yeah", "annotation_id": "29168112", "url": "https://genius.com/29168112", "state": "accepted", "votes": 61, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "Like TV producers we, grr, we airing this shit", "vault_lines": ["Like TV producers we, grr, we airing this shit"], "meaning": "Similar to TV producers, Drake airs things out, as TV shows are “aired” on channels. To air something out is to discuss an issue publicly, which he does throughout his verse, regarding Pusha T and Pharrell Williams.\n\nOld movie projectors make a “Grr”-like sound when turned on, similar to the sound of a firearm when shot. “Air out” is also a slang term for shooting a gun.", "annotation_id": "29156347", "url": "https://genius.com/29156347", "state": "accepted", "votes": 77, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "T time, T time T time, T time, T time", "vault_lines": ["T time, T time, T time", "Always on t-time, been ready (T, ah), yeah"], "meaning": "Drake suggests that it’s “teatime”, implying that he will spill the tea—a euphemism for sharing contentious information. This could be a direct introduction to how Drake alludes to Pusha T throughout his verse, possibly suggesting that it’s “[Pusha] T time”.\n\nHe also says, “Teatime” and “Tee time” on the first two lines of his verse, further leading to the reference of spilling the tea later in on the verse.\n\nHowever, this could also mean “Travis time”, as Travis Scott’s highly anticipated fourth studio album, UTOPIA, was approaching its release, after a five-year wait.\n\nLastly, this could also mean “Turn [up] time” as Drake’s verse is seen as “hype” and energized therefore when people listen to it, they, “turn up” as well as Drake himself saying in the previous line that he’s “T’d up right now”, meaning he is already turnt up.", "annotation_id": "29149261", "url": "https://genius.com/29149261", "state": "accepted", "votes": 165, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "My schedule is out, come spin us, for real", "vault_lines": ["My schedule is out, come spin us, for real"], "meaning": "Drake’s “schedule” being out refers to his It’s All a Blur Tour with Atlanta native, 21 Savage, following the duo’s collaborative full-length studio album, Her Loss.\n\nThe tour maps across the United States and Canada, starting from July 5, 2023, and ending on October 9, 2023. Drake states that if anyone has a problem with him, they can come to his show — as the dates were revealed through the pre-sale — and attempt to “spin [him],” a slang term to attack someone.\n\nFurthermore, “for real” sounds similar to “Pharrell” — a reference to Pharrell Williams who Drake alludes to following this lyric.\n\n\n\nPictured: Promotional cover for the It’s All a Blur tour", "annotation_id": "29149279", "url": "https://genius.com/29149279", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "Burn a athlete like it’s calories, find another flame hot as me, bitch", "vault_lines": ["Burn a athlete like it's calories, find another flame hot as me, bitch"], "meaning": "“LaFlame” is a popular moniker used to refer to Travis Scott as it means “The Flame” in Spanish, suggesting that like a fire, his music is hot — a slang term to refer to music as good.\n\nFor one to be the hottest, means that they are the best. This could possibly be a reference to the previous line by Travis directly telling his ex-girlfriend Kylie Jenner that it’s impossible to find someone as good as he is, being another dig towards Timothée Chalamet.\n\n\n\nPictured: Travis Scott (right) and Kylie Jenner (left) at the 2022 Billboard Music Awards at MGM Grand Garden Arena on May 15, 2022, in Las Vegas, Nevada", "annotation_id": "29149067", "url": "https://genius.com/29149067", "state": "accepted", "votes": 132, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "Man, the club ain’t been the same since we lost Mercedes (Straight up)", "vault_lines": ["Man, the club ain't been the same since we lost Mercedes (Straight up)", "Man, the clique ain't been the same since they lost the greatest (Nah, nah, nah)"], "meaning": "Mercedes Morr  (born Jenae Gagnier) was a popular Instagram and Onlyfans model from Houston who was killed in a 2021 murder-suicide by a supposed “crazed fan”. Drake dedicated his 2021 album Certified Lover Boy to Mercedes.", "annotation_id": "29147588", "url": "https://genius.com/29147588", "state": "accepted", "votes": 68, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "Niggas talkin’ Scarface, I’m that in real life (Ooh)", "vault_lines": ["Niggas talkin' Scarface, I'm that in real life (Ooh)"], "meaning": "Scarface is a 1983 American crime drama film that tells the story of Cuban refugee Tony Montana (aka Scarface), who arrives penniless in Miami during the Mariel boatlift and becomes a powerful and ruthless drug lord.", "annotation_id": "29147530", "url": "https://genius.com/29147530", "state": "accepted", "votes": 56, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "The boy going Lionel Messi, I go Tom Brady (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["The boy going Lionel Messi, I go Tom Brady (Woo)"], "meaning": "Travis Scott makes a reference to the Argentinian professional footballer (soccer player), Lionel Messi who is often regarded as the best player in his sport, and the American former football quarterback, Tom Brady who is known as one of the best quarterbacks in history.\n\n“The boy” refers to Drake as Travis states that he prefers Messi over Brady, possibly referring to how Drake bet $1 million on Argentina winning the FIFA World Cup 2022 against France.\n\nDrake previously referred to Messi on Future’s April 2022, “I’M ON ONE” in which he rapped:\n\nI’m just all about my goals like I’m Messi, what\n\nTravis referred to Brady on the third cut of UTOPIA, “THANK GOD”, in which he rapped:\n\nA quarterback calls, I don’t like 12, except Tom Brady", "annotation_id": "29147498", "url": "https://genius.com/29147498", "state": "accepted", "votes": 93, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "Me at the house, I got seven in heaven They think I’m satanic, I keep me a reverend", "vault_lines": ["Me at the house, I got seven in heaven", "They think I'm satanic, I keep me a reverend"], "meaning": "Following the Astroworld Festival crowd crush on November 5, 2021, many rap and hip-hop fans believed that the eight victims who died alongside the three hundred injured were part of a ritual and were sacrificed by Travis due to his alleged “Satanic tendencies,” thus being blamed for the incident alongside Satan, particularly on TikTok.\n\nTravis states that seven of the victims went to Heaven and notes that he keeps a reverend around him — a formal title for a Christian priest — to debunk the rumors. When asked in an interview about who he believes is responsible, Travis stated:\n\nSomething tragic happened here. What I’ve just been trying to get to the bottom of is what happened here and how it happened. I think the families are owed that. I think the community is owed that to know what happened here. I don’t want to speak too soon, I just want to figure out what happened", "annotation_id": "29147473", "url": "https://genius.com/29147473", "state": "accepted", "votes": 106, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "I told her I don’t got no cash and she said she could wait on a rack, on some Arabic shit", "vault_lines": ["I told her I don't got no cash and she said she could wait on a rack, on some Arabic shit"], "meaning": "Due to Drake’s Toronto accent, “a rack” sounds extremely similar to Iraq—an Arab country. Furthermore, “could wait” sounds like Kuwait, another Arab country.\n\nA “rack” is $1000, Drake says that the woman he’s with asks for money, however, he doesn’t carry cash with him due to his high level of fame.\n\nIn a podcast with Bobbi Althoff, Drake states that he doesn’t carry cash with him after she sarcastically asked for money. After Drake stated he doesn’t carry cash, Althof said that she could wait until after the podcast.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YrdQI3nqh7A&t=2070s", "annotation_id": "29147386", "url": "https://genius.com/29147386", "state": "accepted", "votes": 133, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "Man, fuck all that spinnin’ the narrative shit I melt down the chains that I bought from yo’ boss Give a fuck about all of that heritage shit Since V not around, the members done hung up the Louis, they not even wearing that shit Don’t come to the boy ’bout repairing some shit Don’t come to the boy about sparing some shit You lucky that Vogue was suing ’cause I would’ve been with the Wassas in Paris and shit", "vault_lines": ["Don't talk to the boy 'bout comparisons, shit", "Or come to the boy on some arrogant shit", "Man, fuck all that spinnin' the narrative shit", "I melt down the chains that I bought from yo' boss", "Give a fuck about all of that heritage shit", "Since V not around, the members done hung up the Louis, they not even wearing that shit", "Don't come to the boy 'bout repairing some shit", "Don't come to the boy about sparing some shit", "You lucky that Vogue was suing 'cause I would've been with the Wassas in Paris and shit", "And they scared of the seven (Seven)"], "meaning": "The promotion for Her Loss, the collaborative studio album between Drake and 21 Savage, was heavily reliant on faux Vogue magazines being produced and sold while each round of magazines further teased the release of the album.\n\nWeeks after the release of Her Loss, Drake and 21 Savage were forced to remove the faux magazines from production as they were hit by a lawsuit from Condé Nast, a media company. Despite Vogue’s American roots, the center of fashion is often considered Paris, hence the reference.\n\n“V” particularly refers to the late Virgil Abloh who was the artistic director of the Paris-based, Louis Vuitton. Drake is known to have had a close relationship with the late fashion designer as on Future’s January 2020, “Life Is Good,” Drake famously rapped:\n\nVirgil got the Patek on my wrist doin' front flips\n\nDrake sends shots toward Pharrell Williams who’s the newly appointed men’s creative director for Louis Vuitton, replacing Virgil, thus why Drake states that the fashion company isn’t as popular.\n\nFurthermore, Drake refers to the jewelry he flexed in the official music video for “Jumbotron Shit Poppin,” the thirteenth cut off of Her Loss which was noticed by fans to be designed by Williams, hence why Drake notes he merely melted it down.\n\n\n\nPictured: Drake boasting $3 million worth of jewelry previously owned by Pharrell Williams in the “Jumbotron Shit Poppin” music video\n\n\nPusha T is also (purposefully) caught in the crossfire, as he was spotted in Paris while attending Pharrell’s fashion show. Consequently, Drake raps that Pusha is lucky that Vogue sued him, otherwise he would have been with the Wass Gang — a street gang from Toronto — to harm the two.", "annotation_id": "29147192", "url": "https://genius.com/29147192", "state": "accepted", "votes": 300, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "Make a circus outside like it’s Barnum’s Bailey (It’s lit)", "vault_lines": ["Make a circus outside like it's Barnum's Bailey (It's lit)"], "meaning": "This creates a lively and attention-grabbing scene, referring to a circus organized by P.T. Barnum. It’s about making a lot of excitement and commotion to capture people’s attention and create an entertaining atmosphere. It can be used to describe a situation where there’s a lot of buzz and activity happening, drawing people’s interest and curiosity.\n\n\n\nFurthermore, this could also be a reference to Circus Maximus, Travis Scott’s new film, released alongside UTOPIA, on July 27, 2023.", "annotation_id": "29147004", "url": "https://genius.com/29147004", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "Don’t talk to the boy ’bout comparisons, shit Or come to the boy on some arrogant shit", "vault_lines": ["You talk to the cops on some therapist shit", "Don't talk to the boy 'bout comparisons, shit", "Or come to the boy on some arrogant shit", "Don't come to the boy 'bout repairing some shit", "Don't come to the boy about sparing some shit"], "meaning": "Drake makes it clear that he is not one to be compared with due to his mighty status in both the streets and the music industry.\n\nOn the 21 Savage-accompanied “Circo Loco,” Drake rapped about his close relationship with J Prince who was the target of a 1988 DEA investigation, confirming his ties to the streets:\n\nLinking with the opps, bitch, I did that shit for J Prince\nBitch, I did it for the mob ties\n\nHowever, it’s more widely known that Drake is incomparable in the music industry as he’s the highest streamed artist of all time therefore regardless of anyone else’s influence, he will always stand superior to them, thus why he suggests for them not to act arrogant while in his circumference.", "annotation_id": "29146937", "url": "https://genius.com/29146937", "state": "accepted", "votes": 70, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "And they scared of the seven (Seven) After one-three then we turn up eleven (Yeah) Keep this shit open like 7-Eleven (It’s lit)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, you scared of the 6", "And they scared of the seven (Seven)", "After one-three then we turn up eleven (Yeah)", "Keep this shit open like 7-Eleven (It's lit)"], "meaning": "Travis Scott makes a play on Drake’s lyric, “Yeah, you scared of the 6,” as he notes that his oppositions are scared of the “713” — an area code in Houston, Texas — Travis' hometown. Furthermore, Travis repeats “seven” three times, creating an angel number, contrasting Drake’s repetition of “6” which relates to Satan.\n\nFurthermore, Travis raps, “After one-three then we turn up eleven” on purpose as one plus three plus seven is equal to eleven. He uses a play on words as “MELTDOWN” is the seventh track on UTOPIA.\n\nAdditionally, Travis notes that he keeps his parties going as if they’re 7-Eleven — a convenience store chain in the United States which are known to be open twenty-four hours a day, seven days a week. This relates to E11EVEN, a popular nightclub in Miami, Florida, in which Travis has performed several times.\n\n\n\nPictured: Travis Scott performing at the E11EVEN nightclub in Miami, Florida, on December 7, 2018, in celebration of the Art Basel weekend\n\nIt’s also worth mentioning that Travis has stated that his favorite players in the National Basketball Association (NBA) are Kevin Durant who chose the number seven “because it stands for completion in the Bible and God rests on the seventh day after creating Heaven on Earth,” Kyrie Irving who chose the number eleven because “he was born at exactly 1:11 on March 23, 1992,” and James Harden who played with the number thirteen because “when [he] was a freshman, [he] had to choose [his] jersey number last, and it was between 13 and 52.”", "annotation_id": "29146928", "url": "https://genius.com/29146928", "state": "accepted", "votes": 107, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "(I-I—)", "vault_lines": ["I told her I don't got no cash and she said she could wait on a rack, on some Arabic shit", "I pull out a million and stare at the shit", "I melt down the chains that I bought from yo' boss", "You lucky that Vogue was suing 'cause I would've been with the Wassas in Paris and shit", "Me at the house, I got seven in heaven", "They think I'm satanic, I keep me a reverend", "I know what's at stake, I'm screamin', \"Free Jeffery\"", "Don't keep it sincere, I go Makaveli", "I got the juice, now it's heavy (Juice)", "Teatime like I got a cup of this shit", "The boy going Lionel Messi, I go Tom Brady (Woo)", "Now I let the chains hang, you gotta tuck yours maybe (Tuck it, tuck it)", "I love to fuck on a regular bitch"], "meaning": "This is part of the producer tag for the Philadelphia-based collective Working On Dying, with BNYX® being one of the most popular members of the collective producing on the track.\n\nI-I-I’m working on dying\n\nBNYX® has worked on several popular songs with both Travis Scott and Drake, In particular, he has produced the seventeenth cut of UTOPIA, “K-POP” by Travis, Bad Bunny and The Weeknd alongside Drake’s April 2023, “Search & Rescue” which peaked at #2 on the Hot 100.\n\n\n\nPictured: BNYX® on the cover of The Fader", "annotation_id": "29146911", "url": "https://genius.com/29146911", "state": "accepted", "votes": 98, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "Them boys rollin’ all brown like they whippin’ gravy", "vault_lines": ["Them boys rollin' all brown like they whippin' gravy"], "meaning": "Travis Scott is no stranger to the color brown. Many of his outfits and clothing he designs consists of some type of brown color.\n\n\n\nTravis Scott's brown Lamborghini Urus\n\n\nThis is one of many brown vehicles Travis Scott owns. The other brown cars are his Lamborghini Aventador & his Mercedes G-Wagon.", "annotation_id": "29146893", "url": "https://genius.com/29146893", "state": "accepted", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "You talk to the cops on some therapist shit You act like you love this American shit But, really, the truth is you scared of the 6 Yeah, you scared of the 6 Yeah, you scared of the 6 Your bodyguard put in some work on a fluke Now you wanna go and inherit that shit", "vault_lines": ["You talk to the cops on some therapist shit", "You act like you love this American shit", "But, really, the truth is you scared of the 6", "Yeah, you scared of the 6", "Your bodyguard put in some work on a fluke", "Now you wanna go and inherit that shit", "And they scared of the seven (Seven)", "Is you fucking crazy? Yeah", "Is you fuckin', is you fuckin'"], "meaning": "“6” refers to the six boroughs in Drake’s hometown of Toronto, Canada — East York, Etobicoke, North York, Scarborough, Toronto, and York.\n\nWhile representing his hometown — which is heavily gang affiliated — Drake insinuates and despises his oppositions as they have a habit of calling the police which is vastly looked down upon by gang-affiliated individuals.\n\nDespite not rapping about the aggressive side of the town he grew up in often, in Drake’s October 2014, “6 God,” he similarly rapped in a menacing cadence:\n\nI hear the talk on road is I’m the shit, boy\nPhone call back home, shit is hot up in the 6, boy (Hot up in the 6)\nShit hot up in the 6 right now\nShit hot up in the 6, boy (Hot up in the 6)\nShit is hot up in the 6 right now (Ga, ga, ga)\nCome see us and get it fixed, boy (Hey)\n\nFurthermore, this could be perceived as a dig towards Kanye West as in early 2023, while being harassed by paparazzi, Kanye was seen going to the Los Angeles Sheriff’s Office to stop the harassment. Furthermore, Kanye is known to suffer from several mental health disorders such as bipolar disorder which could be helped by seeing a therapist, however, Kanye has made it public that he refuses to see one. The lines could also reference Ye as Drake may be employing a metaphor, suggesting that Pusha-T is his bodyguard — who he mentions later in the track.\n\nDrake acknowledges that Pusha “put in some work,“ to find out that he has a son when he released his May 2018 Drake diss track, “The Story of Adidon.” Drake suggests that Ye wants to inherit the beef he has with Pusha.\n\nAdditionally, Drake repeats “6” three times in a sequence, likening himself to the Devil — suggesting that if he was in beef with another artist, he would simply destroy them, playing into the forthcoming lyrics where he notes that he can’t be compared to any other rapper.\n\nLikewise, this can also be a dig towards Childish Gambino who wrote, “This Is America,” a track which was originally a diss towards Drake.", "annotation_id": "29146884", "url": "https://genius.com/29146884", "state": "accepted", "votes": 176, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "Gave her the blues, not talkin’ ’bout belly Don’t keep it sincere, I go Makaveli I got the juice, now it’s heavy (Juice)", "vault_lines": ["Gave her the blues, not talkin' 'bout belly", "Don't keep it sincere, I go Makaveli", "I got the juice, now it's heavy (Juice)"], "meaning": "To give one “the blues” suggests that your actions make them feel as if they’re in a state of depression and are anxious — this is linked to the gut and brain connection which suggests that an anxious state can lead to stomach problems.\n\nThis is also a clear reference to the Mooringsport, Louisiana native, Lead Belly, a blues artist who’s known widely for his hit single, “Goodnight, Irene.”\n\n\n\nPictured: Lead Belly playing the guitar in New York, in approximately 1949, days before his passing\n\n\nMakaveli is a widely known pseudonym used by the late Hip-Hop legend, 2Pac. The moniker derives from Niccolò Machiavelli, an Italian diplomat who advocated using misconception and fear on one’s enemies, beliefs which Pac suggestively agrees with.\n\nTravis continues to state that he’s not one to be genuine and similarly to Makaveli, he’ll use misconception and deception to get what he pleases. When one is deceived, it can lead to stomach problems.\n\nFurthermore, Travis pays homage to Nas as he makes a reference to his character, in the 1998 crime drama, Belly, in which Nas played the character of Sincere. In the film, the character of Sincere tends to share several qualities of Machiavelli’s beliefs.\n\nContinuing the reference to films, Travis refers to the 1992 crime thriller, Juice, which starred 2Pac as he plays the fictional Roland Bishop. Employing a double entendre, Travis also states that he’s “got the juice,” suggesting that he has major power and influence in the music industry, having several chart-topping albums and singles.\n\nIt’s worth noting that the opening scene from Belly starts off with a blue tint effect and that hundred Dollar bills are often referred to as “Blues” due to the unique blue strip on the bills — Travis states that he gives women money, attracting them in the process.", "annotation_id": "29146858", "url": "https://genius.com/29146858", "state": "accepted", "votes": 77, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "Chocolate AP and chocolate the Vs (Vs), got the Willy Wonka factory (Vs)", "vault_lines": ["Chocolate AP and chocolate the Vs (Vs), got the Willy Wonka factory (Vs)"], "meaning": "Travis is saying that he has a liking for brown jewelry which is encrusted with diamonds as he notes that his Audemars Piguet is the color of chocolate and that the diamond quality is VS — very slightly included.\n\nWily Wonka is a fictional character from the 1971 musical, Willy Wonka & the Chocolate Factory. On December 15, 2023, Wonka, a remake of the original series will be released with American-French actor, Timothée Chalamet starring as Wonka.\n\n\n\nPictured: Timothée Chalamet starring as Willy Wonka, seen in the official trailer for the upcoming film\n\nDespite no direct diss, many fans perceived this as a diss towards Chalamet as he and Travis' ex-girlfriend Kylie Jenner are rumored to be dating since April 2023, hence the potential diss.", "annotation_id": "29146832", "url": "https://genius.com/29146832", "state": "accepted", "votes": 106, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "I’ll shoot your ass in Walmart like I’m DaBaby (In Walmart)", "vault_lines": ["I'll shoot your ass in Walmart like I'm DaBaby (In Walmart)"], "meaning": "On November 5, 2018, DaBaby was involved in a fatal shooting in which he killed someone in a Walmart. According to Baby, a gunman approached DaBaby and his family with a gun while they were shopping in the store and attempted to rob him, threatening the lives of Baby’s children in the process. In self-defence for himself and his family, Baby, carrying a firearm himself, shot and killed nineteen-year-old Jaylin Domonique Craig.\n\nThe only charges DaBaby received for the incident were for carrying a concealed weapon. They were eventually dropped in March 2019.", "annotation_id": "29146823", "url": "https://genius.com/29146823", "state": "accepted", "votes": 154, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MELTDOWN", "line": "She inching my way then she started confessing I know what’s at stake, I’m screamin’, “Free Jeffery” Connect collect calls right off of the celly", "vault_lines": ["She inching my way then she started confessing", "I know what's at stake, I'm screamin', \"Free Jeffery\"", "Connect collect calls right off of the celly"], "meaning": "Jeffery Lamar Williams, known professionally by his stage name, Young Thug was arrested on May 9, 2022, regarding a 56-count RICO indictment which stated he’s the leader of YSL — Thug’s record label which police claim is a street gang.\n\nTravis pleads for Thug’s freedom as he screams “Free Jeffery,” potentially due to the duo’s close relationship, having linked up several times to create some of each other’s most popular tracks such as “pick up the phone” and “Maria I’m Drunk.”\n\nFurthermore, Travis suggests that while in bed with a woman, she starts confessing her own secrets to convince him to do the same, however, Travis states that he knows not to share any secrets he may have in case of potentially incriminating any of his friends, such as Thug.\n\nA collect call is a call that allows a jail to connect to an approved cell number; Travis mentions this to insinuate he’s in connection with the aforementioned incarcerated rapper.\n\n\n\nPictured: Young Thug (left) and Travis Scott (right)", "annotation_id": "29146820", "url": "https://genius.com/29146820", "state": "accepted", "votes": 104, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bricks", "status": "done", "targets": 2, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Partynextdoor-bricks-lyrics", "genius_title": "Bricks", "genius_id": 9102897, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bricks", "line": "Yeah Said I was ready for you, but I lied I told you I need time to decide I’m here having the time of my life I own the things I said I’d never buy I only think of me, myself, and I They dropped off I’m still on the high Your friends are all still on my side They want us to work like a nine to five How are we supposed to find the time Pop champagne out the driver’s side Demonize girl I think that I’m vibes Gazza Gazza Too mix up in drama Save yourself, girl, don’t bother, yeah I didn’t deserve you and I still got ya", "vault_lines": ["And I see you in the city", "And I need ya, but you don't need me", "I don't see you, but my friends do", "I'm the one to blame", "I'll be here for you", "Said I was ready for you, but I lied", "I told you I need time to decide", "I'm here having the time of my life", "I own the things I said I'd never buy", "I only think of me, myself, and I", "They dropped off I'm still on the high", "Your friends are all still on my side", "They want us to work like a nine to five", "How are we supposed to find the time", "Pop champagne out the driver's side", "Demonize girl I think that I'm vibes", "Too mix up in drama", "Save yourself, girl, don't bother, yeah", "I didn't deserve you and I still got ya"], "meaning": "Peak.", "annotation_id": "35048719", "url": "https://genius.com/35048719", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": false, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bricks", "line": "[Interlude: Moodymann]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This is a sample from a live set by Detroit House producer and DJ Moodymann.\n\nThis interlude would later be used in Drake’s song, Passionfruit meaning this song was most likely scrapped in favour of Passionfruit.", "annotation_id": "34975717", "url": "https://genius.com/34975717", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
