{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Champion", "line": "’Cause I live this shit for real, niggas know me in the game They know!", "vault_lines": ["'Cause I live this shit for real, niggas know me in the game"], "meaning": "This line nods to Drake’s August 2011 track “Headlines,” on which he expresses his dedication to staying genuine as he gets more famous:\n\nThey know, they know, they know\nYeah, they know, yeah\nThat the real is on the rise", "annotation_id": "19554955", "url": "https://genius.com/19554955", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Champion", "line": "Yeah, okay, we made it to America I remember when I used to stay with Erykah", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, okay, we made it to America", "I remember when I used to stay with Erykah"], "meaning": "Drake hails from Toronto, Canada — he shows his pride for his city by mentioning it on songs like 2015’s “Energy” and “6 God.”\n\nErykah Badu is an American singer who Drake is friends with. On 2019’s “Days in the East,” he says:\n\nRemember one night I went to Erykah Badu house\nShe made tea for me\nWe talked about love and what life could really be for me\n\nHe also interpolated “You Got Me,” her collaboration with The Roots, on the outro of his 2015 track “6 Man.”", "annotation_id": "19554854", "url": "https://genius.com/19554854", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Champion", "line": "’Cause they killed my little cousin Nicholas But my memory’s only happy images", "vault_lines": ["'Cause they killed my little cousin Nicholas", "But my memory's only happy images"], "meaning": "Minaj’s cousin, Nicholas Telemaque, was shot and killed in July 2011, after leaving a nightclub in Brooklyn, New York. Minaj shared the news via Twitter the next day:\n\nMy precious cousin. My baby. Killed last nite.\n\nAccording to Daily Mail, Minaj’s other cousin spoke to Radar Online about the family’s reaction to his death:\n\nNicholas was a quiet person, but he could be the life and soul of the party, too. He did not run with gangs or anything like that. His friends have told us there wasn’t any trouble that night and we believe it could have been a case of mistaken identity.\n\n\n\nNicholas Telemaque before his death.", "annotation_id": "19554760", "url": "https://genius.com/19554760", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Champion", "line": "This one is for Tee-Tee, Tweety, Viola, Sharica Candace, Thembi, Lauren, Aisha", "vault_lines": ["This one is for Tee-Tee, Tweety, Viola, Sharica", "Candace, Thembi, Lauren, Aisha"], "meaning": "Nicki would later shout out her friends on A$AP Ferg’s 2017 release, “Plain Jane (Remix):”\n\nI’m with Candice, TT, Thembi, and Viola, mi amiga", "annotation_id": "15136084", "url": "https://genius.com/15136084", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Champion", "line": "What up, Nicki? It’s Nasty, yeah", "vault_lines": ["What up, Nicki? It's Nasty, yeah"], "meaning": "Nas has referred to himself as Nasty, or Nasty Nas, since even before his groundbreaking debut album, 1994’s Illmatic.  Perhaps most memorable is his sampling of his own voice on the outro of “N.Y. State of Mind,” taken from Main Source’s 1991 release, “Live at the Barbecue.”", "annotation_id": "15135985", "url": "https://genius.com/15135985", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Champion", "line": "This is meditation, higher education This the official, competitor elimination", "vault_lines": ["This is meditation, higher education", "This the official, competitor elimination"], "meaning": "When applying to college, admissions offices eliminate those who they think won’t be successful in college. Also, when applying for jobs, someone with a college degree is likely to get hired instead of someone with a high school education, hence competition getting “officially” eliminated just because of higher education.\n\nNicki has moved up  in society, despite the myriad obstacles that have stood in her way, hence the impossible act of “levitating” as a metaphor for her ascendance", "annotation_id": "682046", "url": "https://genius.com/682046", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Champion", "line": "Blasting Pac, little knot, I ain’t greedy I’m back to thugging, bitches", "vault_lines": ["Blasting Pac, little knot, I ain't greedy", "I'm back to thugging, bitches"], "meaning": "Despite repping the opposite coast as him, Nas has always acknowledged 2Pac as a talented artist.\n\n\n\nThe second line also gives a nod of approval to Pac’s thug life philosophy to come up from nothing to be something. The usage of ‘thuggin’ is a deliberate attempt that hints at that.", "annotation_id": "672351", "url": "https://genius.com/672351", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Champion", "line": "My 24th b-day, I’m sailing to Bermedy, you can see me on a yacht", "vault_lines": ["My 24th b-day, I'm sailing to Bermedy, you can see me on a yacht"], "meaning": "Bermuda or Somers Islands is a small island located off the east coast of the United States, its nearest landmass is Cape Hatteras, North Carolina.", "annotation_id": "668021", "url": "https://genius.com/668021", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Champion", "line": "Loud laughter, while writing my next chapter: Fast Cash Life Happily ever after Champions", "vault_lines": ["Loud laughter, while writing my next chapter: Fast Cash Life"], "meaning": "Nas has enough means to securely declare that the next phase of his life will continue to be about living “fast” and being wealthy/successful (happily ever after).\n\n\n\nThis lyric is also possibly an indication of his desire to expand into book writing. A veteran like Nas would surely have great advice, and his acclaimed discography more than qualifies his authoring skills already.", "annotation_id": "666612", "url": "https://genius.com/666612", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Champion", "line": "Straight balling in this bitch, Jeremy Lin; ’Melo", "vault_lines": ["Straight balling in this bitch, Jeremy Lin; 'Melo"], "meaning": "A couple of basketball references to New York Knicks' small forward Carmelo Anthony and point guard Jeremy Lin (formerly of the Knicks, currently with the Houston Rockets).\n\nCarmelo and Lin having an in-game conversation:", "annotation_id": "666551", "url": "https://genius.com/666551", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Champion", "line": "50 Cent Italian, icy flow", "vault_lines": ["50 Cent Italian, icy flow"], "meaning": "This is a double entendre.\n\nRapper 50 Cent is from the same neighborhood as Nicki in NYC so while Nicki is rapping about the hood she’s from she compares her flow to another famous rapper from her neighborhood.\n\nAlso Italian Ice is usually sold for 50 Cent on Ice Cream trucks, stands, etc.\n\nSo she compares her flow to 50 Cent & Italian Ice while referencing the hood she was raised in.", "annotation_id": "665847", "url": "https://genius.com/665847", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Champion", "line": "I saw my first two million dollars, I was 23", "vault_lines": ["I saw my first two million dollars, I was 23"], "meaning": "When Nas was 23 years old, he released his second studio album, It Was Written in 1996. After the low chart success of his debut album, Illmatic, Nas managed to go double platinum with this record, scoring his first $2 million.", "annotation_id": "665696", "url": "https://genius.com/665696", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Champion", "line": "Or Ferrari top down, screaming, “Money ain’t a thang!”", "vault_lines": ["Or Ferrari top down, screaming, \"Money ain't a thang!\""], "meaning": "This is a reference to Jay-Z and Jermaine Dupri’s single “Money Ain’t a Thang,”, the chorus of which was taken from Hov’s classic “Can’t Knock the Hustle (Remix).”", "annotation_id": "665663", "url": "https://genius.com/665663", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made Men", "status": "done", "targets": 12, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rick-ross-made-men-lyrics", "genius_title": "Made Men", "genius_id": 3091, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made Men", "line": "And I’m running straight up in the culo My wrist always on frío", "vault_lines": ["And I’m running straight up in the culo", "My wrist always on frío"], "meaning": "Some very entry level Spanish from Ross here, who has lived in Miami, Florida his entire life.\n\n“Culo” is basically a curse word that means ass/butt/behind\n“Frio” = cold", "annotation_id": "40932360", "url": "https://genius.com/40932360", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made Men", "line": "S65, I call it “Rihanna” It got a red top, but it’s white like Madonna", "vault_lines": ["It got a red top, but it's white like Madonna", "S65, I call it \"Rihanna\""], "meaning": "Ross compares the appearance of his Mercedes Benz S65 AMG Cabriolet to two female pop superstars, Rihanna and Madonna.\n\nHis car has a red convertible top – at the time of this songs release, Rihanna famously had her hair dyed red.\n\n\n\nHowever, Rihanna is from Barbados – the body of Ross’s car is white, like the Queen of Pop, Madonna, who is from Michigan and is very pale.", "annotation_id": "40932314", "url": "https://genius.com/40932314", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made Men", "line": "Made man, also known as “Papi Chulo” (Ugh)", "vault_lines": ["Made man, also known as \"Papi Chulo\" (Ugh)"], "meaning": "Papi chulo can mean a lot of things translated, main ones being pimp daddy or a real cool dude, Ross is reminding you that he is a boss in Spanish", "annotation_id": "31053713", "url": "https://genius.com/31053713", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made Men", "line": "Smoking bullriders,", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake is smoking “bullriders”. Bullriders are strong, This is a reference to the Bud he is smoking being strong", "annotation_id": "31053694", "url": "https://genius.com/31053694", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made Men", "line": "I say shout my driver, Lauren; that ’62 with curtains", "vault_lines": ["I say shout my driver, Lauren; that '62 with curtains"], "meaning": "Drake is in the back of a Maybach 62, a luxury automobile manufactured by Daimler ( Mercedes Benz ) from 2002 to 2012", "annotation_id": "31053669", "url": "https://genius.com/31053669", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made Men", "line": "Michael Jackson: Let it moonwalk", "vault_lines": ["Michael Jackson: Let it moonwalk"], "meaning": "MJ’s signature dance move was the moonwalk, referring back to the previous line about Ross' yayo “dancing”:", "annotation_id": "2870064", "url": "https://genius.com/2870064", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made Men", "line": "Got on my blue Dickie, shout out my nigga Roccett", "vault_lines": ["Got on my blue Dickie, shout out my nigga Roccett"], "meaning": "Roccett is a West Coast rapper and known member of the Crips. He was briefly signed to Jeezy’s CTE Word record label, but is now a Rick Ross/MMG affiliate. At the present time, Ross and Jeezy do not like each other.\n\nDickies is a clothing brand that is traditionally associated with gang attire on the West Coast.", "annotation_id": "89232", "url": "https://genius.com/89232", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made Men", "line": "Ashes to ashes, me, Rozay and Khaled", "vault_lines": ["Ashes to ashes, me, Rozay and Khaled"], "meaning": "Ashes to Ashes is the name of Rick Ross' mix tape that he released on Dec. 24, 2010.", "annotation_id": "88293", "url": "https://genius.com/88293", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made Men", "line": "Spending tomorrows money, I call it “Mañana”", "vault_lines": ["Spending tomorrows money, I call it \"Mañana\"", "S65, I call it \"Rihanna\""], "meaning": "Following on Rozay’s Spanglifications:\n\nDrake knows he’s going to make it big in the game, so he’s spending money he doesn’t have yet (did The Great Recession teach him nothing?!)\n\n(for the non-Spanish speakers, “mañana” means “tomorrow”)\n\nHe pronounces it as “moneyana” bc he said “tomorrow’s money” and tmrw is “mañana” in spanish.", "annotation_id": "88165", "url": "https://genius.com/88165", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made Men", "line": "I’m Damon Wayans, just know that homie don’t play that", "vault_lines": ["I’m Damon Wayans, just know that homie don’t play that"], "meaning": "“Homie don’t play that” was the catchphrase of Homie D. Clown in the Wayans Brothers sketch show In Living Color. He was played by Damon Wayans.", "annotation_id": "88158", "url": "https://genius.com/88158", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made Men", "line": "Got my revolver, too, I call it “Ving Rhames” You still a baby boy, we doing big things", "vault_lines": ["Got my revolver, too, I call it \"Ving Rhames\"", "You still a baby boy, we doing big things", "S65, I call it \"Rihanna\""], "meaning": "Ving Rhames starred in the film Baby Boy. His character snatches a gun away from someone trying to commit suicide.\n\nRevolver is also the aforementioned T-Pain’s fourth studio album.\n\n\n\nRoss is known to name his inanimate objects, such as having a Benz named after Bieber, and continues that trend by naming his gun after Rhames.\n\nRoss is also pointing out the fact that while you are essentially doing nothing, Ross keeps making mogul moves.", "annotation_id": "88046", "url": "https://genius.com/88046", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made Men", "line": "One of my baddest women ever, I call her “Rihanna” But that’s ’cause her name is Rihanna", "vault_lines": ["One of my baddest women ever, I call her \"Rihanna\"", "But that's 'cause her name is Rihanna", "S65, I call it \"Rihanna\""], "meaning": "Hah! Making fun of Rozay’s earlier metaphor!\n\n\n\nDrake was trying to trick us making us think “oh there’s another Rihanna?” (or as if he’s using the name “Rihanna” to represent an ideal, like Dante’s Beatrice)\n\n…but it was actually the singer Rihanna!\n\nUPDATE: Rihanna and Drake are now dating exclusively\n\nUPDATE 2 UPDATE: They broke up!", "annotation_id": "87813", "url": "https://genius.com/87813", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Every Girl", "status": "done", "targets": 3, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Jae-millz-every-girl-lyrics", "genius_title": "Every Girl", "genius_id": 1637421, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Every Girl", "line": "In about 3 years, holla at me Miley Cyrus", "vault_lines": ["In about three years, holla at me, Miley Cyrus"], "meaning": "Crazy ass bar\nMiley Cyrus was 17 at the time of the songs release, so in 3 years she would’ve been around 20", "annotation_id": "37474487", "url": "https://genius.com/37474487", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Every Girl", "line": "I exchange V cards with the retards", "vault_lines": ["I exchange V-cards with the retards"], "meaning": "I swear he only said this because it rhymed.\nIf “bald and wrinkly 40 year old dogs with rabies” rhymed any better he would’ve said that.", "annotation_id": "33299565", "url": "https://genius.com/33299565", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Every Girl", "line": "I don’t discriminate, no not at all Kit kat a midget if that ass soft I break her off", "vault_lines": ["I don't discriminate, no, not at all", "Kit-Kat a midget, if that ass soft, I break her off"], "meaning": "jay is saying that he dont give a fuck about race, if you short he gon divide yo booty cheeks like the red see", "annotation_id": "33133508", "url": "https://genius.com/33133508", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
