{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "4 My Town (Play Ball)", "line": "I ain’t never graduated, I ain’t got no cap and gown", "vault_lines": ["I ain't never graduated, I ain't got no cap and gown"], "meaning": "In America, when you graduate for degree-level or above (Associate, Bachelor’s, Master’s, and Doctoral degrees) you get a cap and gown (academic regalia)\n\n\n\nDrake is letting us know that he got successful even though he never graduated.", "annotation_id": "41581345", "url": "https://genius.com/41581345", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
