{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "4 My Town (Play Ball)", "line": "And how you stay grounded? Cash no go And how you stay mounded? Cash no flow And how you stay shining? Bentley off the floor And how you stay high? Purple pine dro", "vault_lines": ["And how you stay grounded? Cash no go", "And how you stay mounded? Cash no flow", "And how you stay shining? Bentley off the floor", "And how you stay high? Purple pine dro"], "meaning": "Even though Birdman is rich, he reminds himself that the cash could turn into a “no-go” any day. This keeps him modest hes rich (“mounded” is a synonym for “grounded”)\n\nMeanwhile, he tries to live every day to the fullest: his raised, luxury Bentley gleams after the car wash, and the purple, (hy)dro(ponically grown) marijuana keeps him high!", "annotation_id": "17635", "url": "https://genius.com/17635", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "4 My Town (Play Ball)", "line": "I rock stupid ice, Mr. Water Coolers", "vault_lines": ["I rock stupid ice, Mr. Water Coolers"], "meaning": "Much like the water cooler keeps water cold, Wayne keeps his neck cold with a lot of “ice” (diamonds)\n\n“Stupid” in this context is slang for “a lot of”\n\nAlso a reference to The Water Boy. “Stupid Ice” “Mr. Water coolers” = Adam Sandler as Bobby Bouche!", "annotation_id": "17631", "url": "https://genius.com/17631", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "4 My Town (Play Ball)", "line": "From the mud where they what you leave in your blood", "vault_lines": ["From the mud where they what you leave in your blood"], "meaning": "New Orleans, Louisana is dirty south for real, nicknamed the “Mud” by down in the dirty", "annotation_id": "16994", "url": "https://genius.com/16994", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "4 My Town (Play Ball)", "line": "Where the fuck is Stunna at?", "vault_lines": ["(Yeah), where the fuck is Stunna at?"], "meaning": "Birdman, also known as The Number One Stunna, is the CEO of Cash Money. Drizzy is handing it over to Birdman.", "annotation_id": "16987", "url": "https://genius.com/16987", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "4 My Town (Play Ball)", "line": "Have you feeling spiritual Pastor Kerney Thomas to these hoes - miwacles", "vault_lines": ["Pastor Kerney Thomas to these hoes - miwacles"], "meaning": "Pastor Kerney Thomas is a colorful televangelist (with a show on BET). The point being, when girls see Drake it’s a religious out-of-body experience\n\nHe is known for pronouncing the word “miracles” Bawbawa Walters-style\n\n\n\nKerney later made a direct contribution to hip-hop by recording a skit named Kerney Sermon (Skit) on J. Cole’s album Born Sinner.", "annotation_id": "16982", "url": "https://genius.com/16982", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "4 My Town (Play Ball)", "line": "Spades or the Opus, baby, what you got a feeling for?", "vault_lines": ["Spades or the Opus, baby, what you got a feeling for?"], "meaning": "“Which do you ladies prefer, Ace of Spades champagne or Opus One wine?”\n\n\n\nBoth of these pricey elixir brands were introduced to hip-hop on Jay-Z’s “Show Me What You Got”", "annotation_id": "16981", "url": "https://genius.com/16981", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "4 My Town (Play Ball)", "line": "Off a cup of C.J Gibson, man I’m faded off the brown", "vault_lines": ["Off a cup of C.J Gibson, man I'm faded off the brown"], "meaning": "“CJ Gibson” is a drink named after drake’s road manager – Remy Martin 1738, faded off the brown\n\nDrake explained it himself (the second video at the 3:26 mark)", "annotation_id": "16976", "url": "https://genius.com/16976", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "4 My Town (Play Ball)", "line": "Take yourself a picture when I’m standing at the mound", "vault_lines": ["Take yourself a picture when I'm standing at the mound"], "meaning": "Drake’s unmastered verse originally leaked as “Play Ball,” (but by the time the song was officially released) there weren’t any baseball metaphors (besides the baseball “mound”)\n\nHowever, if you do find yourself at a baseball game, don’t take pictures of the man standing at the mound", "annotation_id": "16974", "url": "https://genius.com/16974", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gonorrhea", "status": "done", "targets": 16, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-wayne-gonorrhea-lyrics", "genius_title": "Gonorrhea", "genius_id": 1339, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gonorrhea", "line": "And niggas don’t cross the line Niggas stay in line", "vault_lines": ["And niggas don't cross the line", "Niggas stay in line"], "meaning": "And niggas don’t cross the line\nNiggas stay in line—like welfare\n\nIn this bar, Wayne makes a tongue-in-cheek commentary on the  impoverishment experienced by some black Americans as a way of illustrating that people don’t “cross the line” and test him. Rather than test Wayne, other people “stay in line” as if they were black people waiting in a line for government-provided welfare.", "annotation_id": "41761593", "url": "https://genius.com/41761593", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Gonorrhea", "line": "Bitch, I’m in the building, you in the front yard", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I'm in the building, you in the front yard"], "meaning": "Similar lyrics can be found in “Presidente Carter”, with “Bitch I’m in the building you ain’t even in the lounge”.", "annotation_id": "38189959", "url": "https://genius.com/38189959", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
