{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Lie", "line": "Got your car note in my cup", "vault_lines": ["Got your car note in my cup"], "meaning": "Lean, a popular drug drink in Hip Hop Culture, is a mix of promethazine and codeine cough syrup   with jolly ranchers and sprite that give it sweetness and the trademark purple color. The drink is typically on ice, stirred never shaken and served in a double styrofoam cup. Back in the day, Actavis was a key lean ingredient. It has been discontinued due to Hip-Hop’s popularization of the drug and it’s misuse. 2 Chainz raps about how he still has some bottles of “Act” left in his cabinets in his hit Watch Out. Actavis makes lean super expensive. A typical pint of the cough syrup Actavis can cost between $250 to $400. In Houston, the birthplace of lean, a pint can sell for up to $1,000, and in Atlanta, pints have been reportedly sold for $1,200.\n\nA car note is your car payment. The average monthly car payment is about 500 dollars. 2 Chainz sips lean that costs twice that amount on the regular.\n\nLean:", "annotation_id": "14125503", "url": "https://genius.com/14125503", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Lie", "line": "Bread up and my top down (Down) On the block with a block out (Uh)", "vault_lines": ["Bread up and my top down (Down)", "On the block with a block out (Uh)"], "meaning": "2 Chainz has a large amount of “bread”, a slang term for money. He’s riding in his car with the top down.\n\nHe also plays on the double meaning of block:\n\n1 – the area bounded by four streets in a town or suburb\n\n2 – another word for “brick”, a packaged amount of drugs that weighs a pound or kilogram. “Brick” is usually used for cocaine.", "annotation_id": "13616557", "url": "https://genius.com/13616557", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Lie", "line": "(Cup) And your rent in my Swisher (True)", "vault_lines": ["And your rent in my Swisher (True)"], "meaning": "The marijuana that Chainz has rolled up in his Swisher Sweet blunt wrap is of such high quality that it costs more than your rent payment. He has exhibited his fondness of expensive, high quality marijuana strains such as Sour Diesel, Lemon Sour Diesel, Moonrock, and OG Kush throughout his catalogue of music. He later reuses this concept in his verse on “Ali Bomaye”.\n\nGot a bottle of cologne that cost more than your rent", "annotation_id": "11606955", "url": "https://genius.com/11606955", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Lie", "line": "Name a nigga that want some, I’ll out-rap his ass, out-trap his ass Put his ass in a plastic bag with his trashy ass, take him out Bring ’em in, them whole things", "vault_lines": ["Name a nigga that want some, I’ll out-rap his ass, out-trap his ass", "Put his ass in a plastic bag with his trashy ass, take him out", "Bring 'em in, them whole things"], "meaning": "This line basically talks about how I feel about a lot of MCs, about taking them out being a daily chore of mine.\n\nhttps://players.brightcove.net/4863540648001/HklmClHkx_default/index.html?videoId=5237798724001", "annotation_id": "943368", "url": "https://genius.com/943368", "state": "verified", "votes": 78, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Lie", "line": "(Movie) Bought my boo bigger tits and a bigger ass (Uh)", "vault_lines": ["Bought my boo bigger tits and a bigger ass (Uh)"], "meaning": "When people ask me what I meant about “bought my boo bigger tits and a bigger ass,” it’s kind of simple. I’m from Atlanta, home of the booty shots and breast implants. Well really Cali is the home of breast implants but I think we inherited a lot of that stuff. It just talks about me spending my money in another way. I buy something that she can have for the rest of her life: a new ass, new tits, bigger. By that time, it don’t matter what you look like when you got new tits and a new ass. You got that Barbie style, that Betty Boop swag. I’m from Atlanta and I spend my money wisely, I bought my boo some tits. TRU.\n\nhttps://players.brightcove.net/4863540648001/HklmClHkx_default/index.html?videoId=5237798401001", "annotation_id": "899787", "url": "https://genius.com/899787", "state": "verified", "votes": 148, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Lie", "line": "2 Chainz and Champagne, you want true? That’s true enough (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["2 Chainz and Champagne, you want true? That’s true enough (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Drake is referring to himself when he says Champagne. (His instagram name is “ChampagnePapi”, Champagne Papi is also his credit when producing.)\n\nAlso True/T.R.U, as in 2 Chainz' new album, his past mixtapes and stuff.", "annotation_id": "756823", "url": "https://genius.com/756823", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Lie", "line": "2Pac without a nose ring Thug Life,", "vault_lines": [", 2Pac without a nose ring"], "meaning": "2 Chainz said in an interview with Nardwuar that he just wanted to compare his work ethic to Tupac’s because of how much he grinded it out. .\n\nTupac also rocked a nose ring back in the day.", "annotation_id": "754149", "url": "https://genius.com/754149", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Lie", "line": "So I’m extra charged like a state tax", "vault_lines": ["Stay keepin' my cup full so I’m extra charged like a state tax"], "meaning": "A double entendre on the “estate tax” charged by the government upon death and the state tax on just about everything else.\n\nTraditionally, the more one makes, the more one loses at death without proper estate planning. Canadians like Drake potentially have to pay taxes to the U.S. and Canada upon death.\n\n“Extra charged” is a double entendre in the sense that Drake’s alcoholic beverage keeps him “extra charged” or energetic and fired up, and that state income tax can be considered an “extra charge” on top of federal income tax since it is collected at the discretion of each state, i.e. in some states it doesn’t apply.\n\nConsidering that he grew up in Canada and his father is from Tennessee, a state with no income tax, Drake wants us to know that he understands U.S. income tax laws because he gets paid in many different states.", "annotation_id": "754143", "url": "https://genius.com/754143", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Lie", "line": "Me and Chainz go way back", "vault_lines": ["Me and Chainz go way back"], "meaning": "Drake and 2 Chainz have known each other for quite some time now, dating back to 2009’s I Am Music Tour, and presumably further. .", "annotation_id": "754109", "url": "https://genius.com/754109", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Lie", "line": "Aww, that look like what’s her name (What’s her name?) Chances are it’s what’s her name (What’s her name?) Chances are if she was acting up, then I fucked her once and never fucked again (True)", "vault_lines": ["Aww, that look like what’s her name (What's her name?)", "Chances are it’s what's her name (What's her name?)", "Chances are if she was acting up, then I fucked her once and never fucked again (True)"], "meaning": "Chances are that the female is Rihanna. Rihanna has a song called “What’s My Name?” which featured Drake. These two dated for a very short time in 2009. .", "annotation_id": "754070", "url": "https://genius.com/754070", "state": "accepted", "votes": 61, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Lie", "line": "Forbes list like every year,", "vault_lines": ["Forbes list like every year,"], "meaning": "In 2011, Drake ranked 11th on Forbes' Hip-Hop Cash Kings list. Even though he didn’t make the top 10, he still raked in $10 million – nothing to be ashamed of.\n\nNow in 2012, Drake ranked 6th on the list. He made $20.5 million, definitely something to talk about!", "annotation_id": "754052", "url": "https://genius.com/754052", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Lie", "line": "I smoke strong; that Popeye", "vault_lines": ["Not I, I smoke strong; that Popeye"], "meaning": "Popeye is known for his outrageous strength and just like him, what 2 Chainz smokes is outrageously strong.\n\n\n\n Popeye gets his super strength from eating spinach.  2 chainz smokes super strong marijuana.", "annotation_id": "754016", "url": "https://genius.com/754016", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
