{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m On One", "line": "Yeah, too much money ain’t enough money", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, too much money ain't enough money"], "meaning": "Too much money aint enough money/Manny.‘ play on the scene in the Scarface movie when Tony was told he should be happy with what he got he responded to Manny “you be happy. me I want what’s coming to me, the world chico and everything in it.”\nthis one went over almost everyone’s head.", "annotation_id": "26726129", "url": "https://genius.com/26726129", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m On One", "line": "With my skin tan and my hair long and my fans who been so patient", "vault_lines": ["With my skin tan and my hair long and my fans who been so patient"], "meaning": "Here Drake is alluding to his upcoming music. Saying his fans have been patiently awaiting more from Drake. Drake establishes the fact that he will be entering a new era with a new look. Being a skin tan and longer hair that he got while being on his vacation mentioned in the next line. A new era separating his old look in 2010 Thank Me Later\n\n\n\n and his new look in 2011 Take Care.", "annotation_id": "21725865", "url": "https://genius.com/21725865", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m On One", "line": "And all my niggas got that heat, I feel like Pat Riley", "vault_lines": ["And all my niggas got that heat, I feel like Pat Riley"], "meaning": "Pat Riley became the Miami Heat’s team president in 1995. He acquired LeBron James and Chris Bosh to join Dwyane Wade in 2010, and the “Heatles” went on to win back-to-back championships in 2012 and 2013. Wayne sees himself as the team president of his Young Money team with star players such as Drake and Nicki Minaj, who bring the “heat” on wax with their hot songs, while Wayne has other associates who bring “heat” in the form of guns.", "annotation_id": "19031603", "url": "https://genius.com/19031603", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m On One", "line": "The ones beneath me recognize the red bottoms I wear (Check it)", "vault_lines": ["The ones beneath me recognize the red bottoms I wear (Check it)"], "meaning": "“Red Bottoms” are a brand of luxurious shoe that are designed by Christian Louboutin, a high end french designer. The bottom of the shoes are red, referring as to why if someone was beneath Ross both metaphorically and literally, they would be able to recognize the Christian Louboutin “Red Bottoms” he is wearing.", "annotation_id": "19030901", "url": "https://genius.com/19030901", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m On One", "line": "(Young Mula, baby)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Wayne gives a shoutout to his record label, Young Money, which he often refers to as “Yung Mula,” its nickname.\n\n“YMCMB” is an acronym that stands for Young Money Cash Money Billionaires.\nYoung Money is a subdivision of Cash Money Records, and the two of them combined make up for the larger Young Money Cash Money Billionaires whole.", "annotation_id": "17523614", "url": "https://genius.com/17523614", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m On One", "line": "[Produced by Noah “40” Shebib, T-Minus and Nikhil “Kromatik” Seetharam]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The sample for this beat comes from Treal Lee and Prince Rick’s “Throwed Off (Fuck Everybody)”.\n\nThe track pairs T-Minus with Drake’s go-to producer, Noah “40” Shebib. T-Minus' signature keys and ambient low end form the muscle here, but moody chords from 40 flesh out the mix.\n\nYou can hear the sample at 0:54 which is the same drum sound if you listen cafefully:\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QPU6nfsz3YM", "annotation_id": "2550689", "url": "https://genius.com/2550689", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m On One", "line": "All I care about is money and the city that I’m from", "vault_lines": ["All I care about is money and the city that I'm from"], "meaning": "Drake is from Toronto, Canada, and so is most of his OVO crew.", "annotation_id": "2098634", "url": "https://genius.com/2098634", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m On One", "line": "Bend shawty on the sink, do it for the thrill", "vault_lines": ["Bend shawty on the sink, do it for the thrill"], "meaning": "This line is very similar to a line from Fabolous' “In the Morning.”\n\n“You go from getting ready at the bathroom sink\nTo getting bent over it\nThen its over with”\n\nAlso, Ross surely could fuck his woman in any room of the house, but he does it over the sink for the rush of it. Sweaty feet on the linoleum, that’s a thrilling endeavor.", "annotation_id": "204881", "url": "https://genius.com/204881", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m On One", "line": "I ain’t went this hard since I was eighteen", "vault_lines": ["I ain't went this hard since I was eighteen"], "meaning": "Drake hasn’t gone this hard in his rap career since he was 18. Drake released his first mixtape, Room For Improvement in 2006, and he is now way older. He was around 19 years old when his first mixtape came out, so this is probably a reference to his early work.\n\nHe’s also implying that when you are young you party hard. Young people usually have fun and do things older people don’t do. So he’s partying like he did when he was younger.", "annotation_id": "204475", "url": "https://genius.com/204475", "state": "accepted", "votes": 44, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m On One", "line": "I’m killin’ these hoes, I swear I’m tryna stop the violence", "vault_lines": ["I'm killin' these hoes, I swear I'm tryna stop the violence"], "meaning": "Weezy is doing his part to keep malicious violence down, so instead of literally “killing” hoes, he “kills” them in a metaphorical sense (“seduces” them). He is also being sarcastic by saying he’s trying to stop the violence. He is killing the rap game lyrically and he says he’s trying to stop killing people “ lyrically.”\n\nThe Stop the Violence Movement was started by KRS-ONE in response to a death at a B.D.P concert and the killing of Scott La Rock. This spawned “Self Destruction”", "annotation_id": "204294", "url": "https://genius.com/204294", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m On One", "line": "It’s a slim chance I fall; Olive Oyl", "vault_lines": ["It's a slim chance I fall; Olive Oyl"], "meaning": "Weezy is comparing his chances of falling to the anorexic stature of Olive Oyl from Popeye.\n\nRZA dropped a similar line on 4th Chamber\n\n\n\nAlso, olive oil is far less dense than many other liquids, floating at the top of water, thus there is a slim chance for olive oil to “fall.”\n\nThis could also mean a reference to Cash Money’s CEO Ronald “Slim” Williams. He manages the promotion and distribution so that Weezy’s sales don’t fall.\n\nAlso notice that on this line he uses the “Supa Dupa” flow. Big Sean claimed to be the originator of this flow (although he isn’t) and other rappers using it (especially Drake in the song, “Forever”) has caused some buzz.\n\nThis could also possibly be a reference to this joke.", "annotation_id": "203847", "url": "https://genius.com/203847", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m On One", "line": "Call Marc Jacobs personally to make a pair", "vault_lines": ["Call Marc Jacobs personally to make a pair"], "meaning": "Marc Jacobs is the Creative Director of the French design house Louis Vuitton. He’s bragging to the chick that he can call him up and have him make her something expensive, a one of one.", "annotation_id": "201217", "url": "https://genius.com/201217", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m On One", "line": "Two white cups and I got that drink Could be purple or could be pink ‘Pendin’ on how you mix that shit", "vault_lines": ["Two white cups and I got that drink", "Could be purple or could be pink", "'Pendin' on how you mix that shit"], "meaning": "Famous concoction, popular in the South, is a mixture of prescription strength codeine-promethazine cough syrup and Sprite. It is referred to as purple drank, lean, barre, and syrup (or sizzurp.)\n\n\n\nThe variation between purple and pink comes from whether or not you “mix that shit.” The Sprite lightens the color of the purple syrup, making it pink, typically when there’s less syrup.\n\n(Note the 2 white cups Drake holds in the beginning of the video)", "annotation_id": "200310", "url": "https://genius.com/200310", "state": "accepted", "votes": 65, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m On One", "line": "Ooh, I’m about to go Andre the Giant", "vault_lines": ["Ooh, I'm about to go Andre the Giant"], "meaning": "Famous wrestling champ\n\n\n\nAndre the Giant was a huge man, as well as a very good wrestler. Wayne uses this metaphorically: He will continue to get bigger in the rap game, but before he dies he will also become much more skilled.", "annotation_id": "200308", "url": "https://genius.com/200308", "state": "accepted", "votes": 50, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m On One", "line": "I walk around the club, fuck everybody", "vault_lines": ["I walk around the club, fuck everybody"], "meaning": "He’s in his zone or element and not worried about anybody.\n\nAlso referring to the song “Throwed off” by Treal Lee, which Wayne freestyled over on his mixtape Sorry 4 the Wait.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tXBH_dPEgXk", "annotation_id": "200302", "url": "https://genius.com/200302", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m On One", "line": "Put an end to your world like the Mayans", "vault_lines": ["Put an end to your world like the Mayans"], "meaning": "People believed that the abrupt end to The Mayan calendar on December 21, 2012 was prophesying the end of the world.\n\nTechnically, it is incorrect to use the term “Mayans” when referring to the indigenous peoples of southeastern Mexico and parts of Central America, as it is an adjective.\n\nThe correct word is “Maya,” since it is a noun.", "annotation_id": "200023", "url": "https://genius.com/200023", "state": "accepted", "votes": 48, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m On One", "line": "I’m just feelin’ like the throne is for the takin’ (Watch me take it)", "vault_lines": ["I'm just feelin' like the throne is for the takin' (Watch me take it)"], "meaning": "More Wayne & Drake vs Kanye & Jay-Z? Possibly, especially because Jay-Z and Kanye collaboration album is called Watch the Throne.\n\nPeople assumed that this was a shot but Drake quickly put those rumors to rest as well as any speculation that he was beefing with Jay with this tweet..\n\nhttp://twitter.com/#!/Drake/status/71602847531282432\n\nJay-Z hears you…\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Re8S3xZbRNI&t=2m45s", "annotation_id": "199997", "url": "https://genius.com/199997", "state": "accepted", "votes": 81, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m On One", "line": "Me and 40 back to work, but we still smell like a vacation", "vault_lines": ["Me and 40 back to work, but we still smell like a vacation"], "meaning": "Drake is back to work with his producer, Noah “40” Sheib\n\nSmelling “like a vacation” could mean a few things:\n\n\nDrake and 40 are going hard, but making it look easy by bringing carefree vacation vibes to the studio.\nPerhaps the “smell” is of chill vacation vibes—palm trees, coconuts, sand, etc.\nOr maybe the weed they are smoking in the studio smells like the reefer they were blazing on vacation.", "annotation_id": "199950", "url": "https://genius.com/199950", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "I’m On One", "line": "[Intro: DJ Khaled & Drake] I get ’em up (I’m on one) I get ’em up (Fuck it, I’m on one) I get ’em up (I said, ”I’m on one”) DJ Khaled (Uh)", "vault_lines": ["I get 'em up (I'm on one)", "I'm on one, yeah", "Fuck it, I'm on one, yeah", "I said, \"I'm on one\"", "Fuck it, I'm on one", "'Cause I'm on one", "I said, \"Fuck it, I'm on one\"", "Yeah, I said, \"I'm on one\" (Uh-huh)"], "meaning": "In this context, “on one” means being under the effects of lean—promethazine and codeine mixed with Sprite. In the music video for the song, Drake can be seen holding a cup.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Z09lYqdxqzo\n\nThe line may have inspired from Eminem’s 2000 song “Drug Ballad”:\n\nBut in the long run, these drugs are probably going\nTo catch up sooner or later but fuck it, I’m on one", "annotation_id": "199938", "url": "https://genius.com/199938", "state": "accepted", "votes": 70, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
