{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mine", "line": "I’ve been watchin’ for the signs Took a trip to clear my mind, oh Now I’m even more lost", "vault_lines": ["I've been watchin' for the signs", "Took a trip to clear my mind, oh", "Now I'm even more lost"], "meaning": "Bey is watching for signs that sort out her thoughts. She’s stating in this verse she has many doubts “are we even gonna make it?”\n\nShe took a trip (probably a car ride) to clear her mind, but all it did was she got even more confused. Nothing seems te help get her thoughts straight and solve this puzzle: him en their relationship.", "annotation_id": "31529857", "url": "https://genius.com/31529857", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mine", "line": "From eight until late, I think ’bout you You own my nights, I don’t know what to do, do I can’t get no rest, can’t get no sleep, yeah", "vault_lines": ["From eight until late, I think 'bout you", "You own my nights, I don't know what to do, do", "I can't get no rest, can't get no sleep, yeah"], "meaning": "All he can think about is his girl. “You own my nights” is not in the literal way of course, but in the sense that he cannot sleep (hence the next line), because she’s on his mind 24/7.", "annotation_id": "31529848", "url": "https://genius.com/31529848", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mine", "line": "All I’m really askin’ for is you", "vault_lines": ["All I'm really askin' for is you"], "meaning": "She’s got everything she wants, but she can’t seem to really ‘get to’ him. He’s there, but not really there.", "annotation_id": "31529847", "url": "https://genius.com/31529847", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mine", "line": "All I’m really askin’ for is you", "vault_lines": ["All I'm really askin' for is you"], "meaning": "She’s got everything she wants, but she can’t seem to really ‘get to’ him. He’s there, but not really there.", "annotation_id": "31529844", "url": "https://genius.com/31529844", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mine", "line": "Got everything I’m asking for but you", "vault_lines": ["Got everything I'm asking for but you", "I got everything I'm askin' for but you"], "meaning": "She’s got everything she wants, but she can’t seem to really ‘get to’ him. He’s there, but not really there.", "annotation_id": "31529838", "url": "https://genius.com/31529838", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mine", "line": "Stop makin’ a big deal out of the little things ’Cause I got big deals and I got little things", "vault_lines": ["Stop makin' a big deal out of the little things", "'Cause I got big deals and I got little things"], "meaning": "Beyoncé’s life is a sequence of priorities, and Bey’s asking both the public and her lover to consider their priorities better. For one, she’s asking Jay not to sweat the small stuff, the little kinks or discrepancies that might exist between them. They’ve got much bigger things to worry about — children, marriage, finances, relationships, etc.\n\nShe’s perhaps also making a plea to the public and the press, here: stop worrying about all the nitty-gritty details of her life. Not every meal she eats, not every event she attends, not every step she takes needs to be documented and broadcasted. Not every little commentary is necessarily shady towards another person; there’s no reason to theorize and inflate something that simply isn’t there. There are bigger issues in the world and in Beyoncé’s body of work to shine the light on.\n\nThere could, perhaps, be a tad of self-reflection here as well. “Mine” is an incredibly introspective track, and this pre-hook might as well be Beyoncé reminding herself of what to prioritize and focus on.", "annotation_id": "11962813", "url": "https://genius.com/11962813", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mine", "line": "You the one they hate, this come with that (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["You the one they hate, this come with that (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Drake insinuates that his girl’s friends are not her real friends – they’re just jealous of her being prettier than them. Instead of dealing with them, she should just stick with Drizzy, who understands her and her situation and came comfort her like a real man would.\n\n\n\nThis line can also be heard as “You the one they hate, just come with that,” with “that” probably referring to the hate and problems that his girl is enduring.\n\n“You the one” could also be a reference to Rihanna’s song “You Da One”.", "annotation_id": "2581465", "url": "https://genius.com/2581465", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mine", "line": "We’re takin’ this a little too far We’re takin’ this a little too far We’re takin’ this a little too far", "vault_lines": ["Baby, if we are, we're takin' this a little too far", "We're takin' this a little too far", "'Cause if we are, we're takin' this a little too far", "If we are, we're takin' this a little too far"], "meaning": "Sampha provides echoing vocals here to build into Drake’s hook", "annotation_id": "2548405", "url": "https://genius.com/2548405", "state": "accepted", "votes": 50, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mine", "line": "Been havin’ conversations about breakups and separations", "vault_lines": ["Been havin' conversations about breakups and separations"], "meaning": "Since the marriage with the rap-mogul Jay Z in 2008, there have been many negative rumors about their relationship. The newest rumors were that Beyonce didn’t feel Jay Z was spending enough time with his family. But according to various sources, they’re trying to work it out by spending more time together.", "annotation_id": "2548379", "url": "https://genius.com/2548379", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mine", "line": "On my mind, up past my bedtime, no rest at the kingdom Alone in my place, my heart is away, all that I can think of is We should get married, we should get married Let’s stop holdin’ back on this and let’s get carried away", "vault_lines": ["On my mind, up past my bedtime, no rest at the kingdom", "Alone in my place, my heart is away, all that I can think of is", "We should get married, we should get married", "Let's stop holdin' back on this and let's get carried away", "Let's get carried away"], "meaning": "Bey and Hov wed on April 4, 2008. A couple years prior their relationship went through some struggles, as alluded to by Hov on “Lost One” from his 2006 album Kingdom Come.\n\nThis lyric seems to be from Bey’s perspective at the time, when she was away from Hov, and realised all she really wanted was to be with him after all – and now that their relationship is experiencing uncertainty once more, she is reminded of how much she struggled being without him – her “heart” – at the time.\n\nWhile in “Lost One” Jay attributes their relationship struggles to Bey’s devotion to her work, around the same time period she was quoted as saying,\n\nYou can’t rush a man into anything – whether it’s a relationship, marriage or having children. When he’s ready, he’ll let you know.\n\nThis suggests that the couple possibly experienced tensions about whether to make an official commitment through marriage, the uncertainties of which – even now that they are married – Beyoncé explores in this song. Perhaps that’s why when they finally tied the knot it was a low-key affair with only 30 guests.\n\n\n\nThe lyric “no rest at the kingdom” refers to Bey and Hov’s importance in each other’s lives – both are at the top of their respective fields, with Hov claiming King of New York and Beyoncé being, of course, the Queen. But both have talked about their difficulty forming relationships with the level of fame they’ve achieved, and the subsequent importance and sanctity of their relationship with one another. Even at the peak of their careers in 2006 – with Hov having just made his comeback from retirement and Beyoncé releasing her second album, Bey didn’t feel at peace without Hov present.", "annotation_id": "2548235", "url": "https://genius.com/2548235", "state": "accepted", "votes": 36, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mine", "line": "Don’t go ghost on me, I’ma go “Thriller” on you I’ma just (Pull up on you)", "vault_lines": ["(Pull up on you) I gotta pull up on you", "Don't go ghost on me, I'ma go \"Thriller\" on you", "I'ma just (Pull up on you)"], "meaning": "Michael Jackson released a song called “Ghosts” in July 1997 and his hit song “Thriller” in January 1982—where he comes back as a zombie chasing his love interest.\n\n\n\nNote that Drake also played Michael in a 2002 episode of Degrassi titled “Girls Just Wanna Have Fun” and he threatened to “go Thriller” again on March 2010’s “Thank Me Later.”.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hxujFadk2KU", "annotation_id": "2547996", "url": "https://genius.com/2547996", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mine", "line": "Are we gonna even make it? Oh ‘Cause if we are, we’re takin’ this a little too far If we are, we’re takin’ this a little too far Baby, if we are, we’re takin’ this a little too far", "vault_lines": ["Baby, if we are, we're takin' this a little too far", "We're takin' this a little too far", "Are we gonna even make it? Oh", "'Cause if we are, we're takin' this a little too far", "If we are, we're takin' this a little too far"], "meaning": "A reference to the “questioning” whether her and Jay are going to make it as a couple. She’s saying if they continue to question themselves then it’s already too late, they need to stop questioning and come to an answer.\n\n\n\nBey may also be referencing the song “Lift Off” from Jay and Kanye’s Watch the Throne. Beyonce is featured in that song, singing “How many people thought we could take it this far?”", "annotation_id": "2547985", "url": "https://genius.com/2547985", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mine", "line": "I’m not feelin’ like myself since the baby", "vault_lines": ["I'm not feelin' like myself since the baby"], "meaning": "In January of 2012, Bey gave birth to her and Jay Z’s daughter, Blue Ivy Carter. Postpartum depression, or PPD – which Bey may be nodding to here – is a disease that is estimated to affect 5 to 25 percent of women after they bear a child", "annotation_id": "2547939", "url": "https://genius.com/2547939", "state": "accepted", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
