{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CN TOWER", "line": "But the plane is on land tonight (Alright)", "vault_lines": ["But the plane is on land tonight (Alright)"], "meaning": "Building on the previous line, he emphasizes that though the “plane is on land”, Tokyo is down for him, making sure we know he’s talking about the woman, not the city.", "annotation_id": "35315679", "url": "https://genius.com/35315679", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CN TOWER", "line": "And what? And what? Buy another round And what do I know now? Surprise, surprise", "vault_lines": ["And what? And what? Buy another round", "And what do I know now? Surprise, surprise"], "meaning": "Drake is suggesting that whenever he wants to learn about the woman’s current situation, all he needs to do is “buy another round” – when he takes her friends out downtown, presumably paying their bills at upmarket bars or restaurants.", "annotation_id": "35315668", "url": "https://genius.com/35315668", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CN TOWER", "line": "You blocked me, I lost you, it’s a back and forth Think I even hit your email as a last resort", "vault_lines": ["You blocked me, I lost you, it's a back and forth", "Think I even hit your email as a last resort"], "meaning": "The Girl Blocked Drake and cut contact with him in all ways so he decided, as a last resort to Email her as there is no other option. Most people don’t Email each over casually nowadays so she must’ve not blocked his Email.", "annotation_id": "35236176", "url": "https://genius.com/35236176", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CN TOWER", "line": "Like a tiny house out back, I’m tryna shed some light", "vault_lines": ["Like a tiny house out back, I'm tryna shed some light"], "meaning": "Drake employs a double entendre, using shed to mean both a small backyard structure and providing some context or reasoning. He builds from the previous lines, claiming that he is trying to “shed light” on the situation and tell his side.\n\nIt’s worth noting that this could be a call-back to his beef with Kendrick Lamar. At the end of the music video for his May 2024 track “Family Matters”, the scene shifts to him talking in front of a shed in the backyard, with a solo shot of the shed being shown right after.\n\nEither intentionally or unintentionally, the lyric also mimics a line from Lamar’s September 2010 track “Cut You Off (To Grow Closer)”:\n\nAnd by the way, I'ma start finding more light to shed\nLike a small garage in your backyard", "annotation_id": "34652647", "url": "https://genius.com/34652647", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CN TOWER", "line": "What color’s the CN Tower? It’s blue now Like how I’m feelin’ ’bout you now I was too down, tell me what to do now, oh City is pretty when it’s dead just like a flower What color’s the CN Tower? It’s lit up green (It’s lit up green) Like the envy in people’s eyes, gettin’ in between (In between)", "vault_lines": ["City is prеtty when it's dead just like a flowеr", "What color's the CN Tower? It's blue now", "Like how I'm feelin' 'bout you now", "I was too down, tell me what to do now, oh", "City is pretty when it's dead just like a flower", "What color's the CN Tower? It's lit up green (It's lit up green)", "Like the envy in people's eyes, gettin' in between (In between)", "The city is pretty when it's dead just like a flower", "What color's the CN Tower? It's red tonight", "I came to the"], "meaning": "Drake references the CN Tower’s famous lights once more, comparing his emotions to the changing colors. Feeling blue about someone or something is commonly associated with sadness and feeling down, which he expresses in the first three lines.\n\nDrake also uses the color green to express envy, as the color is often intertwined with the emotion. He says he sees green and envy in other’s eyes, claiming they are jealous of what he and the woman have.", "annotation_id": "34648721", "url": "https://genius.com/34648721", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CN TOWER", "line": "Why did you cut this thing off like you had somethin’ more? ’Cause I just asked around, I just asked around Your friends can’t hold water, girl, they’d rather see you drown Know they tell me everything when I end up downtown", "vault_lines": ["Why did you cut this thing off like you had somethin' more?", "'Cause I just asked around, I just asked around", "Your friends can't hold water, girl, they'd rather see you drown", "Know they tell me everything when I end up downtown"], "meaning": "Drake suggests that the woman broke up with him because she wanted to hide something or someone else. He further proves his point by suggesting that he asked her friends, claiming they couldn’t back up her lies and ratted her out without hesitation.\n\nHe uses the expression “Can’t hold water,” a phrase that means a statement or argument doesn’t make sense or have truth to it. Drake claims her friends would rather see her fail or “drown,” meaning they didn’t back up her excuses.", "annotation_id": "34634333", "url": "https://genius.com/34634333", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CN TOWER", "line": "[Chorus: PARTYNEXTDOOR]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The music of this chorus and following verses is sampled from the track Lollipop by Lil Wayne from his 2008 album Tha Carter III.", "annotation_id": "34613863", "url": "https://genius.com/34613863", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CN TOWER", "line": "Touchpad, turn off the lights", "vault_lines": ["Touchpad, turn off the lights"], "meaning": "Drake evidently aims at Future again, sublimely dissing Future’s April 2012 breakout song, “Turn On the Lights” . He claims to stop playing the song, potentially referring to their deteriorating relationship.", "annotation_id": "34592200", "url": "https://genius.com/34592200", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CN TOWER", "line": "Cancel Japan tonight (Alright) Tokyo down for the boy (Alright)", "vault_lines": ["Cancel Japan tonight (Alright)", "Tokyo down for the boy (Alright)"], "meaning": "Reminiscent of his previous comments on his April 2024 track “Push Ups”, Drake takes another shot at Future and his alleged romantic interest, Just Tokyo.\n\nHe claims once again that him and Tokyo were involved, like his pervious lyrics on “Push Ups”, where he raps:\n\nYou pussies can’t get booked outside America for nan'\nI’m out in Tokyo because I’m big in Japan\nI’m the hitmaker y'all depend on\nBackstage in my city, it was friendzone", "annotation_id": "34578444", "url": "https://genius.com/34578444", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CN TOWER", "line": "Girl, I’m a fan in real life (Alright) You don’t even post on that site (Alright) The price, it definitely would’ve spiked (Alright)", "vault_lines": ["Girl, I'm a fan in real life (Alright)", "You don't even post on that site (Alright)", "The price, it definitely would've spiked (Alright)"], "meaning": "OnlyFans is a popular NSFW site where creators post illicit content, usually for a monthly subscription fee. Drake doesn’t just like this girl for the kind of posed content one would find on the website, but for what he sees from her in person, too.\n\nHe adds to the compliments, saying that, if she did make that kind of content, she could charge very high prices for it because she’s so beautiful.", "annotation_id": "34565347", "url": "https://genius.com/34565347", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CN TOWER", "line": "Thought you caught me slippin’, had me dead to rights", "vault_lines": ["Thought you caught me slippin', had me dead to rights"], "meaning": "This could be addressing Drake’s beef with the rap icon Kendrick Lamar and how everyone believed Kendrick won the beef by wrecking Drake lyrically. Drake may be trying to say that he is not down for the count and is not done.\n\nSomeone thought they had him in a vulnerable position, like he was being careless or off guard.\n\nThe phrase “dead to rights” can mean “caught in the act of doing something wrong”. The phrase is used to express having undeniable evidence against someone, like they’re guilty without a doubt.\n\nIt’s a flex, showing that Drake’s always a step ahead, even when people think they got him.", "annotation_id": "34564950", "url": "https://genius.com/34564950", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "CN TOWER", "line": "What color’s the CN Tower? It’s red tonight Just like the text I sent you from the bed tonight", "vault_lines": ["What color's the CN Tower? It's blue now", "What color's the CN Tower? It's lit up green (It's lit up green)", "What color's the CN Tower? It's red tonight", "Just like the text I sent you from the bed tonight"], "meaning": "The CN Tower is located in Toronto, Canada, and it is one of the tallest structures in the world. Opening in 1976, its primary purpose was to broadcast radio and television signals, ensuring clear communication. The structure held the title of World’s tallest freestanding structure from 1975 to 2007.\n\nThe CN Tower is famous for it’s lighting schedule, which glows red on Valentine’s Day, the same day as the album’s release. Drake likens the color of the tower to his previous message to his woman, claiming that he was left on read.", "annotation_id": "34561392", "url": "https://genius.com/34561392", "state": "accepted", "votes": 52, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
