{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Waiting Up", "line": "I know there’s other people that you talk to But I just hate gettin’ any proof shown to me, shown to me Uh, I know there’s other places that you could go but I’d just really love it if you made it home to me, home to me", "vault_lines": ["I know just how you feel", "I know just how you feel, how you feel", "I know there’s other people that you talk to", "But I just hate gettin' any proof shown to me, shown to me", "Uh, I know there’s other places that you could go but", "I'd just really love it if you made it home to me, home to me"], "meaning": "", "annotation_id": "35619010", "url": "https://genius.com/35619010", "state": "pending", "votes": -7, "second_sense": false, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Waiting Up", "line": "Yeah, I wonder if I should call you But then again you never call me And I’m just lookin’ at my phone girl And the last three messages are all me", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I wonder if I should call you", "But then again you never call me", "And I’m just lookin' at my phone girl", "And the last three messages are all me"], "meaning": "Drake usually has no problem getting girls to reply to his messages, there’s even been times where he wishes they wouldn’t. However, this particular woman doesn’t follow this trend, and even though he really likes her, he doesn’t want to be that guy who triple texts.\n\nDrake’s musical influence has slowly become synonymous with texting your ex or hopeful girlfriend. To the extent that a Drake Keyboard was developed that lets you send messages using the rapper’s lyrics!", "annotation_id": "8250677", "url": "https://genius.com/8250677", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Waiting Up", "line": "Yeah and it ain’t mornin’ but it’s late enough", "vault_lines": ["Yeah and it ain’t mornin' but it’s late enough"], "meaning": "Its not too early or too late. its just the right time for what he has planned.", "annotation_id": "715525", "url": "https://genius.com/715525", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Waiting Up", "line": "Gemini, I understand why ya uptight ’Cause once you give away the pussy, then you’re fucked, right?", "vault_lines": ["Gemini, I understand why ya uptight", "'Cause once you give away the pussy, then you’re fucked, right?"], "meaning": "Very clever wordplay that most women could relate to. Many males are notorious for “fucking then leaving.”\n\nAccording to Gemini women & Astrology, Gemini women tend to be anxious (uptight). Also, they quickly lose relationships and can’t find one of satisfaction, although they long for it. “Gemini” could also describe the the first line because they are very flirtatious.\n\n\n\nCould also mean that once a female gives away her pussy shes became emotionally attached but the guy could of just been using her, leaving her fucked physically and emotionally.\n\nThe second line is similar to a line by drake it Rihanna’s song “What’s My Name?”.\n\nThe square root of 69 is 8 something, right?", "annotation_id": "713987", "url": "https://genius.com/713987", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Waiting Up", "line": "Yeah, young girl, you love life Same birthday as Pac, thug life", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, young girl, you love life", "Same birthday as Pac, thug life"], "meaning": "Drake is talking about how his young love had the same birthday as 2Pac, June 16th.\n\n\n\nHe’s referring to canadian singer Keshia Chante.\n\n\n\nKeshia and Drake used to have a thing.\n\n\n\nHere is a video of Drake and Keshia on 106 & Park speaking a little bit on their past.", "annotation_id": "713962", "url": "https://genius.com/713962", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Life Is Good", "status": "done", "targets": 22, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Future-life-is-good-lyrics", "genius_title": "Life Is Good", "genius_id": 5111026, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Life Is Good", "line": "Bitch, this is fame, not clout", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, this is fame, not clout"], "meaning": "“Clout” is short-term relevance, whereas fame being well-known and influential. Drake is stating that he is not somebody to be associated with clout, as he has been famous for a very long time – topping multiple charts with hit after hit, and he has also worked with a diverse group of a variety of influential artists.", "annotation_id": "23121260", "url": "https://genius.com/23121260", "state": "pending", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Life Is Good", "line": "Baby got a ego twice the size of the crib I can never tell her shit, it is what it is (What?)", "vault_lines": ["Baby got a ego twice the size of the crib", "I can never tell her shit, it is what it is (What?)"], "meaning": "Drake, worth an estimated $150M won’t be running out of money any time soon.\n\nIn 2019 he aqcuired an OVO branded Boieng 767 named ‘Air Drake’ which was valued at $185M.\n\nIn 2020 he purchased a one off, exclusive $620,000 Roulette Wheel, 18K rose gold Jacob & Co watch. Just cause' he could.\n\nHis house is no different. In 2018 he started developing a (estimated) $7M, 50,000 square foot mansion which boasts a full sized basketball court. The mansion has built its own internet clout with several pictures and aerial shots of the houses building progress popping up online. The sheer size of the property is no secret.\n\nWith the size of the crib being general knowledge, Drake is saying that the ego of the woman he is dealing with is bigger than the aforementioned house. Drake is obviously figuratively speaking here, but the metaphor paints the picture well. He also laments that regardless of who he is, he can’t get through to her. Most people would respect someone who has achieved as much as Drake has, or accumulated the wealth he has, however, her ego prevents her from seeing Drake as anyone worth such respect.\n\n\n\nAlso, some clever wordplay has been worked into this segment. Note the words “baby” and “crib.” A double entendre for his lady friend/actual baby and his pad/actual baby crib.", "annotation_id": "19112121", "url": "https://genius.com/19112121", "state": "accepted", "votes": 44, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Life Is Good", "line": "Dropped three dollars on a ring, cost a Bentley truck, lil’ bitch, woo", "vault_lines": ["Dropped three dollars on a ring, cost a Bentley truck, lil' bitch, woo"], "meaning": "“Three dollars” is slang for $300,000. In fact, a 2020 Bentley Bentayga costs around $300,000.", "annotation_id": "18898329", "url": "https://genius.com/18898329", "state": "accepted", "votes": 50, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Life Is Good", "line": "Workin’ on a weekend like usual", "vault_lines": ["Workin' on a weekend like usual"], "meaning": "Drake has made similar claims in relation to his work ethic before, like on iLoveMakonnen’s April 2014 song, “Tuesday”:\n\nAnd when I’m puttin' work in on a weekend", "annotation_id": "18897527", "url": "https://genius.com/18897527", "state": "accepted", "votes": 96, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Life Is Good", "line": "Wine by the glass, your man a cheapskate, huh?", "vault_lines": ["Wine by the glass, your man a cheapskate, huh?"], "meaning": "A “cheapskate” is someone who refrains from spending a lot of money. In restaurants and bars, wine is usually sold four to five times higher than the bottle’s original price. The pricing depends on the restaurant, as well as the wine, though many premium wines are offered cheaply by glass.\n\nIn an October 2010 CBS interview, Drake claimed he’s a “wine fanatic” and that he has maintained relationships with different Canadian restaurants and their owners. In addition, Drake launched his own Champagne brand called Mod Sélection in 2019.", "annotation_id": "18815239", "url": "https://genius.com/18815239", "state": "accepted", "votes": 57, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Life Is Good", "line": "Got Promethazine in my blood and Percocet, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Got Promethazine in my blood and Percocet, yeah"], "meaning": "Promethazine is a prescription drug designed to treat symptoms of allergies and allergic reactions. It is also a key component of the popular recreational drug lean, or purple drank, along with codeine and soda.\n\nPercocet is a strong pain killer. Percocet and lean are not the same drug, but are often used recreationally.\n\n\n\nFuture has been known to glorify and prominently feature these drugs on his songs, most notably on his February 2017 mega-hit “Mask Off,”:\n\nPercocets (Ya), molly, Percocets (Percocets)\nPercocets (Ya), molly, Percocets (Percocets)\n\nOn his March 2015 song “56 Nights,” the trap star raps:\n\nPromethazine took my concentration\nTo another level then I elevated", "annotation_id": "18813042", "url": "https://genius.com/18813042", "state": "accepted", "votes": 70, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Life Is Good", "line": "I’m tryna tote that Draco in London and it’s extended, woo", "vault_lines": ["I'm tryna tote that Draco in London and it's extended, woo"], "meaning": "A Draco is a slang term used to describe a fully or semi-automatic firearm, such as an AK-47u/ a Mini AK-47.\n\n\n\nHowever, due to the Firearms (Danger Air Weapons) Rules 1969, it is illegal for a member of the public to have a fully automatic rifle such as a “Draco.” As such, Future would likely have to smuggle his Draco into London if he wishes to “tote” it in London with “an extended” magazine.", "annotation_id": "18810702", "url": "https://genius.com/18810702", "state": "accepted", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Life Is Good", "line": "Who gave you pills? Who gave you that dust? Pluto sent you on a lick, woo", "vault_lines": ["Who gave you pills? Who gave you that dust? Pluto sent you on a lick, woo"], "meaning": "Pluto is one of Future’s aliases and the name of his April 2012 debut album. In a Complex interview to promote the album, Future explained the meaning behind the alias:\n\n\nThat’s why I say “astronaut status” because that’s what I make, timeless music. Astronauts; it’s space. How long does it take to get to space? Timeless! It’s timeless. It’s music that is going to be around forever. That’s the kind of music I make—astronaut music. People don’t understand what I’m saying. It’s big. It’s bigger than life.\n\nIt takes so long to get to Pluto. It’s not even a planet no more. So when you listen to this music, you got to think outside the box because it’s not going to be a time period. You are going to be listening to this album a year from now and you’ll just be catching up.", "annotation_id": "18810645", "url": "https://genius.com/18810645", "state": "accepted", "votes": 64, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Life Is Good", "line": "I done flew one out to Spain to be in my domain and Audemars-ed the bitch, woo", "vault_lines": ["I done flew one out to Spain to be in my domain and Audemars-ed the bitch, woo"], "meaning": "Audemars Piguet (AP) is a Swiss brand of luxury watches and clocks founded in 1875. Future has name-dropped the brand many times on songs such as his October 2014 track, “Codeine Crazy”:\n\nRollie, AP, Hublot, triple time\n\nFurthermore, in 2019, Future appeared in an  infamous Instagram video with Young Thug where he claimed:\n\nYou identify my bitches with APs.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NvhKepTnZ-M", "annotation_id": "18809326", "url": "https://genius.com/18809326", "state": "accepted", "votes": 86, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Life Is Good", "line": "Niggas caught me slippin’ once, okay, so what?", "vault_lines": ["Niggas caught me slippin' once, okay, so what?"], "meaning": "Drake got caught “slipping” in May 2018 when Pusha T released the scathing diss track “The Story of Adidon,” on which he famously revealed that Drake fathered a child with French adult actress Sophie Brussaux. In a 2019 interview with Rap Radar, Drake admitted that he had lost the beef with Pusha largely based on the shocking nature of this information.", "annotation_id": "18809147", "url": "https://genius.com/18809147", "state": "accepted", "votes": 165, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Life Is Good", "line": "I’m tryna avoid nonsense, get Osama spray in this bitch, woo", "vault_lines": ["I'm tryna avoid nonsense, get Osama spray in this bitch, woo"], "meaning": "Osama bin Laden was the founder and leader of al-Qaeda, a terrorist group that’s responsible for many worldwide attacks. He’s well-known for masterminding the September 11, 2001 attacks on the World Trade Center and the Pentagon, which resulted in the deaths of nearly 3,000 people.\n\nThis prompted the “War on Terror” and resulted in a decade-long manhunt for bin Laden. He was shot and killed on May 2, 2011, by a team of US Navy SEALs in an operation ordered by then United States President Barack Obama.", "annotation_id": "18808602", "url": "https://genius.com/18808602", "state": "accepted", "votes": 65, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Life Is Good", "line": "Manor house in Rosewood, this shit too plush", "vault_lines": ["Manor house in Rosewood, this shit too plush"], "meaning": "The Manor House is a suite in London’s luxury five-star Rosewood Hotel.\n\n\n\nA section of the Manor House suite\n\nFollowing the release of his More Life playlist in 2017, Drake can be seen in a video exiting the hotel.", "annotation_id": "18808264", "url": "https://genius.com/18808264", "state": "accepted", "votes": 111, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Life Is Good", "line": "It’s cool, man, got red bottoms on Life is good, you know what I mean? Like", "vault_lines": ["It's cool, man, got red bottoms on", "Life is good, you know what I mean? Like"], "meaning": "This interlude comes from a January 2016 interview with French journalist and producer Mouloud Achour. The interview also seems to be the origin of this track’s title, “Life Is Good.”\n\n“Red bottoms” are the nickname of shoes made by Christian Louboutin—most of his shoes feature a red outsole.\n\n\n\nFuture has previously mentioned the brand of sneakers before, on his July 2018 track “31 DAYS”:\n\nGot red bottoms sittin' on my feet (Slatt)\n\nFuture’s ability to purchase and wear red bottoms shows his wealth which allows him to live comfortably, hence, “life is good”.", "annotation_id": "18807803", "url": "https://genius.com/18807803", "state": "accepted", "votes": 133, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Life Is Good", "line": "I’m on a PJ lightin’ it up, Backwood full of sticky, woo", "vault_lines": ["I'm on a PJ lightin' it up, Backwood full of sticky, woo"], "meaning": "“PJ” is slang for private jet, while Backwoods are a brand of cigars whose tobacco insides are commonly replaced with cannabis.\n\nLastly, “Sticky Icky OG Kush” is a strain of weed that gets it’s name from the syrupy resin that is on the nugs.", "annotation_id": "18807788", "url": "https://genius.com/18807788", "state": "accepted", "votes": 44, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Life Is Good", "line": "All fact though, we ordered the Fiji", "vault_lines": ["All fact though, carat the pinky", "All fact though, we ordered the Fiji"], "meaning": "Fiji Water is a brand of water from the Fiji islands, advertised as “Earth’s finest water.” According to their official site, the water comes from an artesian aquifer in Viti Levu, the largest island in Fiji.", "annotation_id": "18807749", "url": "https://genius.com/18807749", "state": "accepted", "votes": 48, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Life Is Good", "line": "Racks by the ton, I call up Serena", "vault_lines": ["Racks by the ton, I call up Serena"], "meaning": "Serena Williams is a tennis player and former world champion, who has won 23 major single titles. Rather than Williams' tennis rackets, Future has racks of cash by the ton, where one rack equals a thousand dollars.\n\n\n\nFuture also previously name-dropped Serena on “Big Rings” from his and Drake’s September 2015 collaborative mixtape, What a Time to Be Alive:\n\nI bought that bitch new Celine, I got rings, I got racks like Serena\n\nNotably, Drake—who’s also featured on this song—reportedly dated Serena in 2015.", "annotation_id": "18807735", "url": "https://genius.com/18807735", "state": "accepted", "votes": 67, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Life Is Good", "line": "I got pink toes that talk different languages, woo", "vault_lines": ["I got pink toes that talk different languages, woo"], "meaning": "“Pink toes” is slang for white women. Future often speaks about dating white women, like on his January 2019 track, “F&N”:\n\nI got so many white bitches, Ku Klux Klan", "annotation_id": "18807716", "url": "https://genius.com/18807716", "state": "accepted", "votes": 77, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Life Is Good", "line": "Know you see my texts, baby, please say some’", "vault_lines": ["Know you see my texts, baby, please say some'"], "meaning": "Drake raps from the perspective of a woman he is ignoring. He previously bragged about using this tactic on his 2015 track “Star67,” on which he raps:\n\nText from a centerfold, I ain’t reply\nLet her know I read it though, voice mail say she ready though\nNiggas know I’m credible, ain’t no pussy on a pedestal", "annotation_id": "18807677", "url": "https://genius.com/18807677", "state": "accepted", "votes": 77, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Life Is Good", "line": "Say my days are numbered, but I keep wakin’ up", "vault_lines": ["Say my days are numbered, but I keep wakin' up"], "meaning": "Drake could be saying he has received death threats. On the other hand, he has previously rapped about people claiming his career is at an end on September 2015’s “30 for 30 Freestyle”:\n\nWhen the higher-ups have all come together as a collective\nWith conspiracies to end my run and send me a message\n40, did you get the message?\n‘Cause I just checked my phone and I didn’t get it", "annotation_id": "18807621", "url": "https://genius.com/18807621", "state": "accepted", "votes": 101, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Life Is Good", "line": "Niggas gotta move off my release day, huh", "vault_lines": ["Niggas gotta move off my release day, huh"], "meaning": "This appears to be a shot at idol-turned-rival Kanye West. In a 2019 episode of Lebron James' show The Shop, Drake revealed that Kanye played a role in the delay of his June 2018 album, Scorpion. He recalled a trip to Wyoming to work on Kanye’s album, ye, where Kanye told him:\n\nYou need to be transparent with me and you gotta play me your music and tell me when you’re dropping and I know you don’t like to do things like that.\n\nSoon after Drake played him Scorpion and revealed its release date, Kanye announced his own rollout of G.O.O.D. Music releases. Those projects were set to drop week after week right around the time Drake was planning to put out his album.\n\nSo I wake up and all these dates are out, 1 by 1 by 1, all around June 15th.", "annotation_id": "18807502", "url": "https://genius.com/18807502", "state": "accepted", "votes": 92, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Life Is Good", "line": "Never turn my back on FBG, God forbid (What?)", "vault_lines": ["Never turn my back on FBG, God forbid (What?)"], "meaning": "“FBG” is an acronym for “Freeband Gang” or just Freebandz—Future’s crew and record label he founded after he signed a major-label deal with Epic Records in September 2011. In fact, Drake’s and Future’s friendship started the same month when they collaborated on “Tony Montana.” Since then, the two have remained friends and frequent collaborators, even dropping a mixtape in September 2015.\n\nOn February 21, 2017, Future did a Q&A session with his fans on Twitter to promote his then-appearance on The Tonight Show starring Jimmy Fallon. During the session, a fan asked Future to describe his relationship with Drake, to which he responded:\n\nI would describe my relationship with Drake as doing great business. We always know how to make great business, make good music, we get into the studio and we come up with different creative vibes. We go on tour, it’s always sold out. We give the fans something special. I feel like, the fans have made our relationship special. We take heed to that. It drives us, it’s like a driving force for our relationship.", "annotation_id": "18806350", "url": "https://genius.com/18806350", "state": "accepted", "votes": 155, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Life Is Good", "line": "Virgil got a Patek on my wrist goin’ nuts", "vault_lines": ["Virgil got the Patek on my wrist doin' front flips", "Virgil got a Patek on my wrist goin' nuts"], "meaning": "A well-known and revered figure within the fashion industry, Virgil Abloh was the founder and CEO of the popular luxury brand Off White, the creative director of Kanye West’s now-defunct Donda creative agency, and the artistic director of Louis Vuitton’s menswear collection from March 2018 until his untimely death in November 2021 following a battle with cancer.\n\nIn April 2019, Abloh commissioned  a one-of-one Patek Philippe Nautilus watch, courtesy of luxury watch customizers Mad Paris.\n\nWithin hours of the release of “Life Is Good,” both Drake and Abloh uploaded a picture of the customized Patek Philippe watch mentioned in this line. The emerald-encrusted design was later brought to life by celebrity jeweler Jacob Arabo in collaboration with Mad Paris.", "annotation_id": "18795590", "url": "https://genius.com/18795590", "state": "accepted", "votes": 236, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Truffle Butter", "status": "done", "targets": 20, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Nicki-minaj-truffle-butter-lyrics", "genius_title": "Truffle Butter", "genius_id": 622818, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Truffle Butter", "line": "You ain’t gotta tell your friend that I eat it in the mornin’ ‘Cause she gon’ say “I know”", "vault_lines": ["You ain't gotta tell your friend that I eat it in the mornin'", "'Cause she gon' say \"I know\""], "meaning": "This double entendre shows that the woman’s friend “knows,” without being told, that Wayne engages in cunnilingus in the morning because: (1) the friend can hear the woman’s morning-time moans; and (2) Wayne  previously slept with the friend, who is familiar with Wayne’s sexual proclivities.", "annotation_id": "38882193", "url": "https://genius.com/38882193", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Truffle Butter", "line": "I ain’t nothin’ like your last dude What’s his name? Not important", "vault_lines": ["I ain't nothin' like your last dude", "What's his name? Not important"], "meaning": "If Wayne is rapping about Christina Milian, some of her “last dudes” include Nick Cannon, whom she dated from 2003-2005, The-Dream, whom she married in September 2009 before separating 3 months later, and Jas Prince, whom she was with for 4 years before calling off their engagement and moving out.\n\n\n\nAs he’s done other times, Wayne uses nonchalance to signal confidence and power. He doesn’t care who her last man was—he’s not on Weezy’s level. He’s also confident in his own skills in the bedroom and not intimidated by her previous lovers. The way he delivers this line almost makes it sound like he’s flippantly making this joke during sex, before “goin' back in.”", "annotation_id": "7502379", "url": "https://genius.com/7502379", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Truffle Butter", "line": "Can I hit it in the bathroom? Put your hands on the toilet I’ll put one leg on the tub, girl This my new dance move, I just don’t know what to call it But, bitch, you dancin’ with the stars", "vault_lines": ["Can I hit it in the bathroom? Put your hands on the toilet", "I'll put one leg on the tub, girl", "This my new dance move, I just don't know what to call it", "But, bitch, you dancin' with the stars"], "meaning": "Wayne raps about his desire to have sex in a bathroom, detailing some of the positions he and his partner would try. At the time of this song’s release, Wayne was in a relationship with Christina Milian, a singer who had signed with Young Money (Wayne’s label) in 2012.\n\nAlso, from September to October 2013, Milian was a contestant on the 17th season of Dancing with the Stars, which Wayne subtly alludes to in these lines.", "annotation_id": "4630584", "url": "https://genius.com/4630584", "state": "accepted", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Truffle Butter", "line": "You know, yeah Touchin’, yeah Night of You know, yeah Touchin’, yeah Night of", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Nineteen85 slowed down Maya Jane Coles' “What They Say”, an electronic track (which in turn samples Triple X’s “Feel the Same”) for the backing of this beat.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WMYZI4lK9co#t=92", "annotation_id": "4543815", "url": "https://genius.com/4543815", "state": "accepted", "votes": 52, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Truffle Butter", "line": "[Verse 1: Drake]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake’s verse (as well as the beat) originated on Mally Mall’s “Whatcha Say.” It was likely one of the joints Nicki told Ryan Seacrest that Drake had sent her for The Pinkprint.", "annotation_id": "4543798", "url": "https://genius.com/4543798", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Truffle Butter", "line": "I could probably make some stepsisters fuck each other", "vault_lines": ["I could probably make some stepsisters fuck each other"], "meaning": "Girl-on-girl action is a popular male fantasy, and rappers are no different—see Young Thug’s “Danny Glover” for one example:\n\nI pass them a molly, now they kiss each other\nEvery time I fuck I gotta hit me least like two bitches\n\nDrake takes it a step further with step-sisters. Though they’re not actually related, one can still imagine some reluctance, but Drake’s confident he has the money and persuasive skill to get the sororal love going.", "annotation_id": "4536104", "url": "https://genius.com/4536104", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Truffle Butter", "line": "Pretty ladies, are you here? Truffle butter on your pussy", "vault_lines": ["Pretty ladies, are you here? Truffle butter on your pussy"], "meaning": "A lone Urban Dictionary definition led to the rumor that truffle butter was slang for a mixture of bodily fluids resulting from anal and vaginal sex. It seems unlikely, however, considering the artists on the song didn’t even know of this second meaning. Wayne, who makes the most sexual truffle butter reference of the 3, told GQ\n\nI thought truffle butter was something you put on steak or food or something like that, so I was saying like, I eat a lot of [pussy], and I’m gonna put that sauce on your “you know what.” I don’t know what no other truffle butter means!", "annotation_id": "4535510", "url": "https://genius.com/4535510", "state": "accepted", "votes": 105, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Truffle Butter", "line": "I’m so heartless, thoughtless, lawless, and flawless Smallest, regardless, largest in charge And born in New Orleans, get killed for Jordans", "vault_lines": ["I'm so heartless, thoughtless, lawless, and flawless", "Smallest, regardless, largest in charge", "And born in New Orleans, get killed for Jordans"], "meaning": "Lil Wayne may be shorter than most of his peers (5'6\"), but he stands tall metaphorically as the president of Young Money, and proves this by making eleven rhymes out of only twenty-one words.\n\nHe’s also tougher than his enemies thanks to his upbringing in a neighborhood in New Orleans – a city so rough that 27-year-old James Vaughn was killed for his Air Jordan 11 Retros in an East New Orleans mall on Christmas Day in 2014.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=s3jxbDDTjpo", "annotation_id": "4535481", "url": "https://genius.com/4535481", "state": "accepted", "votes": 79, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Truffle Butter", "line": "You see the fleet of all the new things Cop cars with the loose change All white like I move things Niggas see me rollin’ and they mood change Like a motherfucker", "vault_lines": ["You see the fleet of all the new things", "Cop cars with the loose change", "All white like I move things", "Niggas see me rollin' and they mood change"], "meaning": "Drake owns Chevy Malibus, Bugattis, Bentleys, and a BRABUS S-Coupe amongst many other cars, and shows them off to the women he takes home to prove his wealth. The most impressive part is that the expensive cars don’t make up the bulk of his purchases – he buys them with the extra money he has laying around.\n\n\n\nMost of these cars are white (e.g. his ride in the “Started from the Bottom” music video), which makes it look like he owns a bunch of white moving vans. Alternatively, the cars are so nice that it seems like he made money selling white cocaine.", "annotation_id": "4534746", "url": "https://genius.com/4534746", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Truffle Butter", "line": "I’m good with the ballpoint game, finger roll", "vault_lines": ["I'm good with the ballpoint game, finger roll"], "meaning": "Nicki uses her ball-point pen all the time, not just for writing verses, but also for autographs, endorsement deals, and contracts. A finger roll is used to describe a basketball layup that rolls off a player’s fingers. Nicki’s pen flows with the same ease.", "annotation_id": "4534611", "url": "https://genius.com/4534611", "state": "accepted", "votes": 50, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Truffle Butter", "line": "I’m still the highest sellin’ female rapper for the record Man, this the sixty-five millionth single sold I ain’t gotta compete with a single soul", "vault_lines": ["I'm still the highest sellin' female rapper for the record", "Man, this the sixty-five millionth single sold", "I ain't gotta compete with a single soul"], "meaning": "She’s not exaggerating about being the “highest sellin' female rapper” of all time (a title previously held by Missy Elliott). Nicki has sold over 65 million copies of her singles alone worldwide, since 2010. She’s also one of only a few artists to actually have 2 studio albums go platinum even after piracy got popular.", "annotation_id": "4534599", "url": "https://genius.com/4534599", "state": "accepted", "votes": 109, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Truffle Butter", "line": "Pretty women, what’s up? Is you here right now? You a stand-up or is you in your chair right now? Uh Do you hear me? I can’t let a wack nigga get near me", "vault_lines": ["Pretty women, what's up? Is you here right now?", "You a stand-up or is you in your chair right now? Uh", "Do you hear me? I can't let a wack nigga get near me", "Pretty women, are you here? Are you here right now, huh?"], "meaning": "A “stand up” person is one who is loyal and reliable. You can’t be a stand up if you’re sitting down, so she urges the women around her to get on their feet and support her.\n\n\n\n“Pretty women, wassup” is a female-centric version of Drake’s “real nigga, wassup?” on “The Motto;” reversing gender tropes is one of the biggest themes in Nicki’s lyrics.", "annotation_id": "4534438", "url": "https://genius.com/4534438", "state": "accepted", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Truffle Butter", "line": "I ain’t never need a man to take care of me Yo, I’m in that big boy, bitches can’t rent this I floss every day, but I ain’t a dentist", "vault_lines": ["I ain't never need a man to take care of me", "Yo, I'm in that big boy, bitches can't rent this", "I floss every day, but I ain't a dentist"], "meaning": "A “big boy” is 1990s slang for a 500 Series Mercedes-Benz, made popular by Ghostface Killah. Nicki can afford to buy this wildly expensive car without relying on a lover for cash, so she’s earned the right to floss and show it off when she wants. Doesn’t she know you don’t have to be a dentist to maintain proper oral hygiene? Of course, floss can also be slang for wearing a thong—so maybe she’s explaining her underwear preferences too.\n\n\n\nHer past manager, Debra Antley, got very specific about Nicki’s self-reliance in 2014.", "annotation_id": "4534359", "url": "https://genius.com/4534359", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Truffle Butter", "line": "Skateboard, I’m gnarly, Drake, Tunechi, and Barbie, you know", "vault_lines": ["Skateboard, I'm gnarly, Drake, Tunechi, and Barbie, you know"], "meaning": "Wayne pulls off a 720 here by rhyming gnarly with Barbie!\n\n\n\n“You know” also echoes the sample on this song, taken from Maya Jane Coles “What They Say”.", "annotation_id": "4534283", "url": "https://genius.com/4534283", "state": "accepted", "votes": 119, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Truffle Butter", "line": "I could be broke and keep a million dollar smile LOL to the bank, check in my account Bank teller flirtin’ after checkin’ my account", "vault_lines": ["I could be broke and keep a million dollar smile", "LOL to the bank, check in my account", "Bank teller flirtin' after checkin' my account"], "meaning": "Big money for the grill, so I’m never cheap talking\n\nEven if Weezy was to somehow lose all of his cash (which could happen if he keeps getting sued), the banks won’t be able to take his trademark diamond grill from him. This would frustrate the bankers, but turn on the girls that got a look at his net worth.\n\nThe diamonds in the grill are worth $150,000, and the other $850,000 comes from the words that pass through his grill and onto his hit records.\n\n\n\nAnd why can’t the bank take his million dollar smile?\n\nMost jewelry purchases are unsecured debts, and unsecured debts cannot be repossessed unless the jewelry company or creditors wins a lawsuit. So the only way Wayne could lose the grill is if he put the diamond up as collateral when he made the purchase, or if the credit company felt the return on diamonds that have been in someone’s mouth was worth the legal fees. Even if they won, they would likely offer him the chance to reaffirm his debt with them rather than seize the diamonds because of his potential for future earnings.", "annotation_id": "4534279", "url": "https://genius.com/4534279", "state": "accepted", "votes": 74, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Truffle Butter", "line": "I might kiss the baddest bitch if you dare me", "vault_lines": ["I might kiss the baddest bitch if you dare me"], "meaning": "Nicki has teased at getting intimate with some of the baddest women in the game – she shared a kiss with Madonna and got up close and personal with Cassie in “The Boys” music video. Don’t get it twisted, though – she told Rolling Stone in 2010 that while she “think[s] girls are sexy”, she’s not bisexual.\n\n\n\nSeeing as Nicki frequently refers to herself as the baddest bitch, maybe she’s going to pull an A-Rod?", "annotation_id": "4534211", "url": "https://genius.com/4534211", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Truffle Butter", "line": "Uh, thinkin’ out loud", "vault_lines": ["Yo, thinkin' out loud", "Uh, thinkin' out loud"], "meaning": "All three MCs start their verses with some variation of “I’m thinkin' out loud,” lending the song a breezy, friends-in-the-booth feeling. The recording was probably not a casual meeting, at all, but they’re good at sounding relaxed.", "annotation_id": "4534188", "url": "https://genius.com/4534188", "state": "accepted", "votes": 150, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Truffle Butter", "line": "New flow, I got a dozen of ’em", "vault_lines": ["New flow, I got a dozen of 'em"], "meaning": "Drizzy often brags about his variety of flows, but these flows usually get him in trouble. Ludacris has called Drake out for stealing his #hashtag flow, Big Sean has been credited with the Supa Dupa flow, and most recently Drizzy was accused of jacking Migos' flow.", "annotation_id": "4534062", "url": "https://genius.com/4534062", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Truffle Butter", "line": "Your whole style and approach I invented And I ain’t takin’ that back ’cause I meant it (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Your whole style and approach I invented", "And I ain't takin' that back 'cause I meant it (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Nicki single-handedly refreshed the stale state of female rappers before her, putting it in mint condition with her own unique style as an emcee. This paved the way for younger female rappers like Iggy Azalea and Azealia Banks to break into the mainstream after Nicki – something Iggy has acknowledged.", "annotation_id": "4534019", "url": "https://genius.com/4534019", "state": "accepted", "votes": 89, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Truffle Butter", "line": "I must have about a milli on me right now And I ain’t talkin’ about that Lil Wayne record", "vault_lines": ["I must have about a milli on me right now", "And I ain't talkin' about that Lil Wayne record", "I must have a quarter million on me right now"], "meaning": "To be clear, when Nicki states she has a milli, she’s strictly speaking on the $1,000,000 -not Weezy’s hit song “A Milli” (although Wayne does mention his millions in that track too).", "annotation_id": "4533991", "url": "https://genius.com/4533991", "state": "accepted", "votes": 55, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
