{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "3 On", "line": "I got’em all in check without the woo-hah Flip modes on ya quick, got a few sides", "vault_lines": ["I got'em all in check without the woo-hah"], "meaning": "“Woo-hah” Refers to Busta Rhymes‘ 1996 track titled “Woo Hah!! Got You All In Check”.  Busta Rhymes also founded the Flipmode Records) record label which was later renamed “Conglomerate”.", "annotation_id": "15724150", "url": "https://genius.com/15724150", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "3 On", "line": "It’s Young Money Records, get the record straight", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Young Money Records is the label that Drake is signed to. Some of his labelmates include  Nicki Minaj, Birdman, and Lil Wayne (who was also the founder). The label rose to fame with the song “BedRock”, which featured Wayne, Minaj, Drake, and a few others.", "annotation_id": "11738765", "url": "https://genius.com/11738765", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "3 On", "line": "Crib in Calabasas man I call that shit the safe house", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Calabasas is a wealthy city in California. Drake has one of many houses right next to the city, in the Hidden Hills. He owns an $8 million mansion there, with a huge pool. This is one house that he feels safe at, as it is a gated community. The community is very exclusive and very protected. Drake loves the town so much, he later made a song titled “4PM In Calabasas”.", "annotation_id": "10502533", "url": "https://genius.com/10502533", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "3 On", "line": "Yeah And now every time Drake out Cameras always flashing tryna put me on the takeout", "vault_lines": ["And now every time Drake out"], "meaning": "Drake has become such a big name that the paparazzi target him relentlessly. Any video or photo of Drake could end up on MediaTakeout (or any other gossip site), providing a big enough incentive for photographers to invade his privacy and try to document his every move.", "annotation_id": "9086371", "url": "https://genius.com/9086371", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "3 On", "line": "Yea, OB dat my brother like a Wayans", "vault_lines": ["Yea, OB dat my brother like a Wayans"], "meaning": "Drake shouts out OB O'Brien, a member of  the OVO crew. Drake compares the closeness of his friendship with OB to the blood relationship shared by brothers, specifically referencing his late-90s-sitcom compatriots, The Wayans Brothers.", "annotation_id": "8722046", "url": "https://genius.com/8722046", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "3 On", "line": "Comin’ from the 6 side", "vault_lines": ["Comin' from the 6 side"], "meaning": "Referencing the 416 area code of Toronto, Drake commonly refers to his hometown as “The Six,” a moniker he popularized.\n\nDrake explained his usage of the term on a 2016 appearance on The Tonight Show with Jimmy Fallon:\n\nYes, our area code is 416…\nWe were debating on ‘The Four,’ but I went tail-end on them and went 6.", "annotation_id": "8360599", "url": "https://genius.com/8360599", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "3 On", "line": "A nigga got a woosah", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "“Woosah,” a term popularized by Bad Boys II, means to calm down. Drake is bringing so much heat and getting so much attention, he needs to remind himself to take a second to breathe.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hibtZPMF9D0", "annotation_id": "8360593", "url": "https://genius.com/8360593", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
