{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cabaret", "line": "North pole boy from the T.O", "vault_lines": ["North pole boy from the T.O"], "meaning": "Drake is from Toronto (the T.O.) Canada which is very north and cold, hence Drake’s reference to the North Pole", "annotation_id": "16440699", "url": "https://genius.com/16440699", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cabaret", "line": "It’s a cabaret (Put on a show) Oh oh (Get on the floor)", "vault_lines": ["It's a cabaret (Put on a show)", "Oh oh (Get on the floor)", "Cabaret (Put on a show)"], "meaning": "Cabaret is a show of dancing, singing, or other light entertainment at a nightclub or restaurant. The show is usually intended for more adult audiences.", "annotation_id": "2240615", "url": "https://genius.com/2240615", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cabaret", "line": "Always strap up just for safety then go long Do my touchdown, dance in it, no clothes on", "vault_lines": ["Always strap up just for safety then go long", "Do my touchdown, dance in it, no clothes on"], "meaning": "Drake wraps it up in a latex for safety so he doesn’t get his girl pregnant.\n\nNotice the football to sex wordplay?\n\nDrake goes deep, all the way down field like a wide receiver would, and he always scores that touchdown. A touchdown always results in a dance, right?", "annotation_id": "2238914", "url": "https://genius.com/2238914", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cabaret", "line": ", girl, truth be told You set the pace then you ride it like cruise control", "vault_lines": [", girl, truth be told", "You set the pace then you ride it like cruise control"], "meaning": "Cruise control is a system that automatically controls the speed of a motor vehicle. The system takes over the throttle of the car to maintain a steady speed as set by the driver.\n\n\n\nHis girl controls what happens and how fast it happens, then she sets it to cruise control. Drake lays there as she rides him so he doesn’t have to do a thing.", "annotation_id": "2238855", "url": "https://genius.com/2238855", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cabaret", "line": "They ain’t really ready for me and that J.T., though", "vault_lines": ["They ain't really ready for me and that J.T., though"], "meaning": "Drake and Justin Timberlake are two of the hottest artists on the market right now. Therefor, the world may not be ready for a collaboration from the two. But, everyone better get ready because this is a song featuring the two artists.\n\nAlso, Drakes third album Nothing Was the Same will be released September 24th, 2013 and Justin Timberlake’s fourth album The 20/20 Experience Part 2/2 will be released less than a week later on September 27th, 2013. Those are two albums that will definitely be fighting for the number one spot on the charts!", "annotation_id": "2238825", "url": "https://genius.com/2238825", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cabaret", "line": "I been in the gym doing two-a-days for ya So I can lift ya up when I do the thang to ya D-do the thing to ya", "vault_lines": ["I been in the gym doing two-a-days for ya", "So I can lift ya up when I do the thang to ya", "D-do the thing to ya"], "meaning": "Lately, Drake has been hitting the gym not once, but twice a day; Presumably with his personal trainer, Jonny Roxx.\n\nNothing is more embarrassing than having your knees buckle when you’re trying to lift her up during sex.", "annotation_id": "2238823", "url": "https://genius.com/2238823", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cabaret", "line": "You’re Kryptonite, should probably have a cape to throw on", "vault_lines": ["You're Kryptonite, should probably have a cape to throw on"], "meaning": "Kryptonite is Superman’s weakness. The only thing that can hurt the man of steel.\n\nBut when a man or woman calls someone their kryptonite it means that, that is their weakness, they want it even though  he or she knows it’s bad for them.", "annotation_id": "2238817", "url": "https://genius.com/2238817", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cabaret", "line": "Presidential shit, girl, you up on the poles", "vault_lines": ["Presidential shit, girl, you up on the poles"], "meaning": "The girl is getting on the strip pole.\n\n\n\nIt’s like she’s on some presidential shit,\n\n1) getting up on the approval polls\n\n2) and getting up on the poles, like American flags.", "annotation_id": "2238801", "url": "https://genius.com/2238801", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cabaret", "line": "Okay, this just in, girl, the paper’s so long", "vault_lines": ["Okay, this just in, girl, the paper's so long"], "meaning": "No lie, Drake’s paper is definitely long. He was the sixth highest paid rapper of 2012, earning a total of about 20 million dollars. With Nothing Was The Same just coming out, this brings him even more funds to add to his already massive stack of dollars.\n\n\n\nDrake plays on Timberlakes first name as well, by saying this just in.", "annotation_id": "2238637", "url": "https://genius.com/2238637", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cabaret", "line": "Got a camera watchin’ every single move like casinos", "vault_lines": ["Got a camera watchin' every single move like casinos"], "meaning": "Casinos are known for having an extreme amount of cameras to watch everyone’s move. Just in case there is a dispute over something, because there is a lot of money involved.\n\n\n\nIn Drake’s case, he is an A list celebrity. The cameras from paparazzi are always focused on him. Paparazzi companies like TMZ find out the scoop on EVERY little celebrity thing.\n\nDrake could also be recording them and “making a movie” of them having sex.", "annotation_id": "2238623", "url": "https://genius.com/2238623", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cabaret", "line": "On my Eddie Murphy Boomerang for ya", "vault_lines": ["On my Eddie Murphy Boomerang for ya"], "meaning": "Eddie Murphy played Marcus Graham in Boomerang who is quite the ladies man. Like Marcus, Drake also seems to be quite the ladies man.  Further, Drake’s given name is Aubrey Graham, the same surname as Murphy’s character", "annotation_id": "2238498", "url": "https://genius.com/2238498", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cabaret", "line": "I’m tryna ease your mind", "vault_lines": ["I'm tryna ease your mind"], "meaning": "A nod to Lil Boosie’s song “Let Me Ease Ya Mind” – Drake is trying to relax this girls mind before they have sex so she feels comfortable.", "annotation_id": "2238322", "url": "https://genius.com/2238322", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
