{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sh!t (Remix)", "line": "Took niggas out the hood like I’m from there So you know it’s all good when I come there", "vault_lines": ["And niggas say it’s all good", "Took niggas out the hood like I'm from there", "So you know it's all good when I come there"], "meaning": "Drake, with his huge success over his career and helping of new artists coming through, believes he took niggas out the hood. Because of this, it’s all good and is welcomed very well whenever he arrives there.", "annotation_id": "35933244", "url": "https://genius.com/35933244", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sh!t (Remix)", "line": "And I brought my tour to your city, you my son there, nigga", "vault_lines": ["And I brought my tour to your city, you my son there, nigga"], "meaning": "Drake says here that while Kendrick thinks that he’s the leader or boss of his city (Compton), Drake still is bigger than him and more loved there. Drake would bring these sentiments up again during his beef with Kendrick Lamar in 2024, on the track ‘PushUps’\n\n‘'Get more love in the city that you from, nigga!’'", "annotation_id": "35933224", "url": "https://genius.com/35933224", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sh!t (Remix)", "line": "I’ll call Michael Jordan up and Mike will make it", "vault_lines": ["I'll call Michael Jordan up and Mike will make it"], "meaning": "Michael Jordan is notorious for not attending meetings and shutting down and  charging male celebrities exorbitant fees for a picture.\n https://www.si.com/nba/bulls/off-the-court/when-michael-jordan-ruthlessly-shut-down-chamillionaires-picture-request\n\nMichael Jordan did not even attend his Ring of Honor celebration with the Chicago Bulls.\n\nHowever if MJ respects you and what you do, he will make it, no fee.", "annotation_id": "31788247", "url": "https://genius.com/31788247", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sh!t (Remix)", "line": "And if a nigga say my name, he the hot shit But if I say the nigga name, he still the hot shit Fucked up, lucky I don’t feed into the gossip", "vault_lines": ["And if a nigga say my name, he the hot shit", "But if I say the nigga name, he still the hot shit", "Fucked up, lucky I don't feed into the gossip"], "meaning": "Drake refers to Kendrick’s verse in ‘Control – Big Sean’ (2013), where Kendrick sums up the following rappers:\n\n“But this is hip hop and them niggas should know what time it is\nAnd that goes for Jermaine Cole, Big KRIT, Wale\nPusha T, Meek Millz, A$AP Rocky, Drake\nBig Sean, Jay Electron', Tyler, Mac Miller\nI got love for you all but I’m tryna murder you niggas\nTryna make sure your core fans never heard of you niggas\nThey dont wanna hear not one more noun or verb from you niggas”", "annotation_id": "31651113", "url": "https://genius.com/31651113", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sh!t (Remix)", "line": "Ear Drummers", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "EarDrummers is one of the main producer tags from Mike WiLL Made-It, who was a main producer on this track. It is the main tag for his record label Ear Drummer Records as well.\n\nMike WiLL has collaborated with Juicy J, Future and Drake before individually, although this marks the first time that all four have appeared on the same track.", "annotation_id": "18103375", "url": "https://genius.com/18103375", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sh!t (Remix)", "line": "I’m the young rap nigga with the ’Melo deal", "vault_lines": ["I'm the young rap nigga with the 'Melo deal"], "meaning": "Carmelo Anthony has an extremely large contract, making $20+ million dollars a year from the Knicks alone. Plus then there’s the shoe sales, etc. Drake got the same deal Carmelo got with the Jordan Brand.\n\n\n\nMelo Deal also sounds like melody, referring to Drake’s well-known ability to sing and rap at the same damn time.", "annotation_id": "2566127", "url": "https://genius.com/2566127", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sh!t (Remix)", "line": "Peel off, then I’m ghost in my Phantom", "vault_lines": ["Peel off, then I'm ghost in my Phantom"], "meaning": "Double entendre\n\n“To go ghost” means to disappear, but at the same time he could be talking about his car a Roll Royce Phantom or a Roll Royce Ghost.\n\nSo Juicy is driving off in his Phantom/Ghost…\nAnd he calls it Casper", "annotation_id": "2565339", "url": "https://genius.com/2565339", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sh!t (Remix)", "line": "Just know a million ain’t shit once you get a mil’ And niggas say it’s all good That’s how you better feel, nigga, nah! Fuck that, this year I’m talking big stuff", "vault_lines": ["Just know a million ain't shit once you get a mil'", "And niggas say it’s all good", "That’s how you better feel, nigga, nah!", "Fuck that, this year I'm talking big stuff"], "meaning": "Drake is beyond the petty dreams of Money, Cars, Clothes & Hoes that he idolized in his younger days. He wants to make power moves and align himself with the rap moguls such as: Dr. Dre, Jay Z, and Diddy.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/Drake/status/207777078622420992\n\nThe “niggas say it’s all good” is a reference to Kendrick’s comments about Drizzy in a recent GQ feature.", "annotation_id": "2564542", "url": "https://genius.com/2564542", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sh!t (Remix)", "line": "I know y’all already know Mike Will Made It", "vault_lines": ["I know y'all already know Mike Will Made It"], "meaning": "Drizzy is giving Mike WiLL Made It a shoutout for producing the track. Drake has went in on other songs produced by Mike WiLL, such as Lil Wayne’s “Love Me” and 2 Chainz‘ “No Lie.”\n\nAlso could refer to Mike WiLL’s signature tag of saying his name through a synthesized voice at the beginning of the songs he produces. Due to Mike WiLL sounding off at the beginning of his songs, you know when a beat is made by him.", "annotation_id": "2564529", "url": "https://genius.com/2564529", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sh!t (Remix)", "line": "You need to come to OVO for a better deal", "vault_lines": ["You need to come to OVO for a better deal"], "meaning": "Drake feels that he can offer the best deal with his label OVO a.k.a. OVO Sound\n\n\n\nOVO (Octobers Very Own) is the self-started Label that spawned from Drakes original label/Movement ATF (All Things Fresh) The first OVO mixtape was Comeback Season. The rest, is History\n\nPossibly talking to those TDE members, telling them that OVO is the better label.", "annotation_id": "2564463", "url": "https://genius.com/2564463", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sh!t (Remix)", "line": "Fuck niggas gon’ be fuck niggas That’s why we never gave a fuck When a fuck nigga switched up, damn!", "vault_lines": ["That's why we never gave a fuck", "When a fuck nigga switched up, damn!"], "meaning": "IMPLYING THIS IS A SHOT AT KENDRICK: Drake was one of the first people outside Kendrick’s camp to hear Section 80 and contributed to him breaking into the mainstream scene:\n\n\nHe put Kendrick on his double Platinum selling album Take Care.\nAllowed him to open up for him on the Club Paradise tour which grossed $42 Million with 60 shows.\nOVO producer, T-Minus produced his hit record Swimming Pools.\nHe contributed a verse to his single, Poetic Justice.\n\n\n\nAfter all this, Kendrick switched up and called Drake out among other rappers on his long verse for Big Sean’s Control and later with seemingly subliminal shots on his BET cypher verse.\n\nDrake says Fuck niggas gon' be fuck niggas and keeps it moving. Also he stole the line from Kendrick Lamar on the song “ Blessed ”", "annotation_id": "2564451", "url": "https://genius.com/2564451", "state": "accepted", "votes": 106, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sh!t (Remix)", "line": "But I had to come through for the remix On my haven’t-done-a-verse-in-eight-weeks shit", "vault_lines": ["But I had to come through for the remix", "On my haven’t-done-a-verse-in-eight-weeks shit"], "meaning": "He came thru for the remix for Future who was also on tour with Drake for ‘Would You Like A Tour?’\n\n\n\nDrake finished the album and went straight to touring. He toured from October 18th, to December 18th. This remix dropped December 17th, which is exactly 2 months. This is one of his first verses since finishing the album.", "annotation_id": "2564429", "url": "https://genius.com/2564429", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sh!t (Remix)", "line": "I hear you talk about your city like you run that", "vault_lines": ["I hear you talk about your city like you run that"], "meaning": "This can be used for most rappers who think they are running their city, just wait until the OVO crew comes through.\n\nDirected at Kendrick Lamar for always talking about running the West Coast, more specifically LA and Compton and could be aimed towards his claimed king of New York line.", "annotation_id": "2564380", "url": "https://genius.com/2564380", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sh!t (Remix)", "line": "Just looking at the numbers, nigga, I feel amazing", "vault_lines": ["Just looking at the numbers, nigga, I feel amazing"], "meaning": "Drake’s success has garnered him attention from some amazing people, namely, His Airness Michael Jordan and the whole Jordan brand.\n\nDrake signed a lucrative shoe deal with the Jordan brand as part of Drake’s desire to dip his toes into the fashion world. Drake’s reaction to the news was positive\n\n“Today also happens to be one of the best days of my life, you know, growing up, I’m sure we all idolized this guy – he goes by the name of Michael Jordan. So today, I came to Portland, Oregon and I officially became inducted into the Team Jordan family.”\n\n\n\nPictured are Drizzy’s Sample Pack of his OVO Stingray 10’s\n\nThis also references Mike Will Made It’s hit 23 which uses Jordan as its source material and plays on the now famous producers name.", "annotation_id": "2564372", "url": "https://genius.com/2564372", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sh!t (Remix)", "line": "Yeah, I just think it’s funny how they dangling the bait But I’m the one that’s killing niggas on the hooks, though", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I just think it's funny how they dangling the bait", "But I'm the one that's killing niggas on the hooks, though"], "meaning": "Drizzy is most likely firing back at Pusha T, who dissed Drake in his song, King Push:\n\nI rap nigga ‘bout trap niggas\nI don’t sing hooks\n\nDrake is cleverly playing on the word hook in these lines, as it could also mean a fish hook used for catching fish. While everybody else is trying to catch fish (or in this case, beef) by dangling the bait, Drizzy is already killing them with his hooks, instead of responding and giving them exposure.\n\n#Shots Fired!", "annotation_id": "2554278", "url": "https://genius.com/2554278", "state": "accepted", "votes": 57, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Marvin’s Room", "status": "done", "targets": 24, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Drake-marvins-room-lyrics", "genius_title": "Marvins Room", "genius_id": 50895, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Marvin’s Room", "line": "After a while, girl, they all seem the same", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "After a while of luxurious and carefree lifestyle choices with these women, they all seem to come off the same to him. It is rumoured that Drake was listening to ‘All Girls Are The Same’ by fellow singer Juice WRLD when coming up with this line from his pen. Clever, Aubrey. Clever indeed.", "annotation_id": "40639752", "url": "https://genius.com/40639752", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Marvin’s Room", "line": "[Interlude: Drake] You not gon’ come? I guess I’m ’bout to just kick it here then", "vault_lines": ["Guess ima just kick it here then uhm"], "meaning": "To Aubrey’s dismay, it appears his lover does not show any intent on appearing at his location. He then decides to kick back on his own, spending this solemn and somber night by himself, with nothing but cups of the rosé and his own shadow.", "annotation_id": "40639733", "url": "https://genius.com/40639733", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
