{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Marvin’s Room", "line": "Too many drinks have been given to me I got some women that’s livin’ off me Paid for their flights and hotels, I’m ashamed", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The flow and cadence of these and the next 3 lines were interpolated by SZA while featuring on Travis Scott song “TELEKINESIS”:\n\nI still wanna be with you, trust me, I know that’s insane\nI’d rather fuck on you than fuck on lames\nI did some shit in Berlin, I’m OD\nWe both ain’t shit and it’s workin' for me\nWorkin' for me, yeah", "annotation_id": "30210385", "url": "https://genius.com/30210385", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Marvin’s Room", "line": "I’ve had sex four times this week, I’ll explain Havin’ a hard time adjustin’ to fame Sprite in there mixed up", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "As a coping mechanism for the stress of his new found fame, Drake is drinking Dirty Sprite a.k.a ‘Lean’ as well as having, what he believes, to be an excessive amount of sex", "annotation_id": "29436043", "url": "https://genius.com/29436043", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Marvin’s Room", "line": "And sittin’ talkin’ ’bout bitches that we almost had", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This song is about drake being in love with an ex girlfriend but then here he talks about being addicted to sitting and talking about women he almost had. The reason is because any woman that he gets can’t compare to the ex girlfriend that he is still in love with. He is trying to move past it, but all attempts fail and so he starts to romanticize girls that he almost had and wondering where those could’ve gone. In reality this is normal behavior for someone going through a tough break up as he tries to forget his ex.", "annotation_id": "28316730", "url": "https://genius.com/28316730", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Marvin’s Room", "line": "Lucky that you stayed on I need someone to put this weight on Fuck, I’m sorry", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "He could be “apologizing” for several things at this point.\n\n\nFor one, he could be apologizing to himself or some higher figure for becoming a mess and for all of the sins he’s recently committed (such as the heavy indulgence in lust/sex).\nHe could be apologizing to the girl’s (possible) new guy for the disrespect dished to him throughout this song (“Fuck that nigga…”).\nHe could be repenting to this girl for messing up and dialing her up with all these issues…\n\n\n\nIt could also be any combination of all three.\n\nThis closure is how Drake ultimately reacts to the “shame” he mentions he has earlier in the verse. Whether this is sincere or not…up for some debate (considering he is severely drunk at this point).", "annotation_id": "1530557", "url": "https://genius.com/1530557", "state": "accepted", "votes": 97, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Marvin’s Room", "line": "[Intro: Ericka Lee]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The woman whose phone calls are featured in this song, Ericka Lee, sued Drake over his use of her voice:\n\nAccording to Billboard, Lee filed a lawsuit in California federal court yesterday [February 2, 2012]. She claims that Drake texted her messages like, “U basically made that song” and “It’s shit without you.” While Drake has reportedly offered her a percentage of the publishing money, Lee seeks credit as a co-writer of the song and is seeking other damages.\n\nThe case was settled the following year out of court.\n\nDrake later went on to mention her on “Redemption” in 2016, saying:\n\nErika sued me and opened a business", "annotation_id": "570742", "url": "https://genius.com/570742", "state": "accepted", "votes": 417, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Marvin’s Room", "line": "Yeah, I hope no one heard that ‘Cause if they did, we gon’ be in some trouble, yeah If they did, we gon’ be in some trouble, trouble, oh", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "He hopes nobody heard this white girl say the word because there may be an altercation over its usage. The ending is supposed to illustrate that he feels more alone at this party of distanced, hostile people than he would if he were actually alone, and it’s made him even more depressed than he already was about missing his ex.", "annotation_id": "438896", "url": "https://genius.com/438896", "state": "accepted", "votes": 207, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Marvin’s Room", "line": "Her white friend said, “You niggas crazy,” I hope no one heard that", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The word “nigga” is considered a reclamation word, heavily rooted in black culture and speech, so it’s noteworthy for Drake to mention her being white because it is considered taboo for non-black people to use the word (especially white people), even if it is said in jest.", "annotation_id": "304571", "url": "https://genius.com/304571", "state": "accepted", "votes": 185, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Marvin’s Room", "line": "I’m just sayin’ you could do better Tell me, have you heard that lately? I’m just sayin’ you could do better And I’ll start hatin’ only if you make me", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "He actually implying that he himself is better, only because he is drunk, he is not saying her boyfriend is a bad boyfriend, as earlier stated in the lyrics, he is  implying that her current guy isn’t bad, just that he’s better.\n\nThe song continues with sections in which Drake tries to coerce his unwilling ex over the phone.  His efforts ultimately go unrewarded.", "annotation_id": "294817", "url": "https://genius.com/294817", "state": "accepted", "votes": 216, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Marvin’s Room", "line": "Are you drunk right now?", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Indeed he is, and she can tell because such blunt honesty rarely comes from someone sober.\n\nThis is a sample from a convo with Ericka Lee. Lee sued Drake for using her voice without her permission and excluding her from royalties, and they settled out of court.", "annotation_id": "235095", "url": "https://genius.com/235095", "state": "accepted", "votes": 243, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Marvin’s Room", "line": "Bet that you know them, I won’t say no names", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "He has been messing with girls within her circle, so instead of breaking up friendships, their names will remain anonymous.\n\nAlso, this is  a statement directed to the listener as if he doesn’t want to expose the girls who are living off of him to the rest of the world and embarrass them.", "annotation_id": "232966", "url": "https://genius.com/232966", "state": "accepted", "votes": 100, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Marvin’s Room", "line": "But I’ve been drinkin’ so much That I’ma call her anyway and say", "vault_lines": ["But I’ve been drinking so much", "But I've still been drinking so much", "So I'mma call you anyway and say"], "meaning": "Here we see an unusually aggressive side of Drake as he claims to be better than any new guy in his ex’s life.\n\nThis may be a reference to Rihanna and her on-again-off-again relationship with Chris Brown—which ended on a bad note after a violent dispute. Though Drake and Rih were never official, it was rumored for years that they were dating.", "annotation_id": "232956", "url": "https://genius.com/232956", "state": "accepted", "votes": 319, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Marvin’s Room", "line": "Flight’s in the morning What you doin’ that’s so important?", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Fun Fact: Drake tweeted this line a few weeks before dropping the song:\n\nhttp://twitter.com/#!/drakkardnoir/status/76950821367062529\n\nHe’s saying he feels hurt because he’s only here for tonight, he’s leaving in the morning, but the girl still isn’t interested in seeing him and she is acting like she is on the road all the time too.", "annotation_id": "229835", "url": "https://genius.com/229835", "state": "accepted", "votes": 167, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Marvin’s Room", "line": "Cups of the rosé", "vault_lines": ["Cups of the Rose"], "meaning": "Rosé is a wine (and can come in a champagne or sparkling variety). Rosé Imperial is made by Moet.\n\n\n\nSince champagne is usually for celebrating, this shows a turn of events that Drake wasn’t planning for – drunken emotions.", "annotation_id": "229816", "url": "https://genius.com/229816", "state": "accepted", "votes": 163, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Marvin’s Room", "line": "I don’t think I’m conscious of makin’ monsters Outta the women I sponsor ’til it all goes bad But, shit, it’s all good", "vault_lines": ["But now I'm all sober", "I think I'm addicted to all this shit"], "meaning": "The more Drizzy sponsors, or pays, for a woman’s wants, the more blinded the women become by the money.  They turn into fiends who are only out for Drake’s wallet, or he could be suggesting that he makes monsters out of the women he’s been with in his mind after the relationship goes bad to justify his actions or its failure.\n\nThese four lines really sum up Drake’s complicated relationship with women. Referring to women as bitches in one couplet and then realizing his own role in turning  them into “bitches” in the next.\n\nHe keeps making the same mistakes with the same type of girls he throws money at and he’s starting to realize it.\n\nThis could also relate to how he portrays his girls in his music: he can never seem to write songs about a healthy relationship, but he’s not aware of this until it’s too late and he’s out of the relationship. He makes a “monster” out of them when he writes a song, but he can never do that until it “all goes bad”.", "annotation_id": "229495", "url": "https://genius.com/229495", "state": "accepted", "votes": 146, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Marvin’s Room", "line": "I say fuck that nigga that you think you found And since you pick up, I know he’s not around, oh, oh", "vault_lines": ["And since you picked up I know he’s not around"], "meaning": "If she picked up a call from her ex, her current boyfriend must not be around. Otherwise, she’s gonna have some explaining to do!\n\nThere are few other notable things about these lines:\n\n\nDrake uses the term “think” as a way of making her doubt the dude is good for her.\n“Found” denotes she merely was looking for someone to replace the need for Drake.\nHer answering the phone gives him a reason to believe he still has a part of her.", "annotation_id": "229467", "url": "https://genius.com/229467", "state": "accepted", "votes": 368, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Marvin’s Room", "line": "Uh, cups of the XO", "vault_lines": ["Cups of the Rose"], "meaning": "XO Cafe Patron, though XO is a designation for “Extra Old” and could be a variety of liquors. It could be an allusion to Hennessy Cognac XO, too.\n\n\n\nIt’s notable that from the beginning of the 1st verse to now, Drizzy goes from sipping champagne (associated with celebration) to sipping XO, which is not only harder in alcohol content, but more associated with a different type of partying.\n\nAlso, XO references fellow Torontonian The Weeknd, the R&B singer whose label is called “XO” (he often sings about drinking lean from a styrofoam cup). Drake does frequently refer to lean in songs (cf. “I’m On One”).", "annotation_id": "229411", "url": "https://genius.com/229411", "state": "accepted", "votes": 256, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Know Bout Me", "status": "done", "targets": 9, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Timbaland-know-bout-me-lyrics", "genius_title": "Know Bout Me", "genius_id": 266799, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Know Bout Me", "line": "[Intro: Jay Z]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The “Jay Z feature” in this song is merely a two line intro. Jay might have been included in the intro as a show of approval for Drake’s borrowing of his flow from ‘Party People’, however, fans expecting “http://rapgenius.com/Drake-pound-cake-paris-morton-music-2-lyrics” style slams from Hov and Drake from Nothing Was The Same should look somewhere else.", "annotation_id": "2441535", "url": "https://genius.com/2441535", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Know Bout Me", "line": "[Verse 2: Drake]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "His whole verse is imitating Jay Z’s verse on another Timbaland track, “Party People” even including the stutter flow, Drizzy’s paying homage to Hov.\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P71crMPDd2U\n\nhttps://twitter.com/urwillOE/status/401477247464243200", "annotation_id": "2439518", "url": "https://genius.com/2439518", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Know Bout Me", "line": "On the sunset strip", "vault_lines": ["On the sunset strip"], "meaning": "The Sunset Strip is a stretch on Sunset Boulevard in Los Angeles.  It is well known for being place for many clubs and parties.", "annotation_id": "2437970", "url": "https://genius.com/2437970", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Know Bout Me", "line": "I just got back home, 40 days on vacation", "vault_lines": ["I just got back home, 40 days on vacation"], "meaning": "Being a multi-million dollar rapper, Spending 40 days on vacation in five-star hotels is not cheap. Drake can easily afford it though. It may also be a reference to his main producer 40.\n\nDrake may be comparing himself to Jesus, who, after his baptism, fasted for 40 days, forgoing temptation, known as the Temptation of Christ.  Drake is not fasting, rather, he’s feasting.", "annotation_id": "2437733", "url": "https://genius.com/2437733", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Know Bout Me", "line": "Ridin’ down Collins with my entourage following", "vault_lines": ["Ridin' down Collins with my entourage following"], "meaning": "Down Collins Avenue is right next to the beach, a luxury location with many luxury vehicles.\n\n\n\nThis also connects with  Meek Mill – Intro. Which is also all about dreams as well as making it as an artist.\n\nI’m riding down on Collins", "annotation_id": "2437299", "url": "https://genius.com/2437299", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Know Bout Me", "line": "In a whole ’nother realm If you want to make a movie let me know It’s a whole another film I suggest you get your dress for the Golden Globes", "vault_lines": ["What you know bout me, what you know bout me", "In a whole 'nother realm", "If you want to make a movie let me know", "It's a whole another film", "I suggest you get your dress for the Golden Globes"], "meaning": "Tim plays on realm/real from the previous bar, as well as reel/movie – you young kids might not know but reels were used in movie projectors in cinema. Tim has an ulterior motive though, he wants to make a porno with her.\n\nHe then goes onto mention the Golden Globes, the award show that honours both cinema & television. After he’s done with this bitch, she better get her shit together because she’s his date to the red carpet.", "annotation_id": "2437260", "url": "https://genius.com/2437260", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Know Bout Me", "line": "If this was 10 years ago nigga would’ve went diamond", "vault_lines": ["If this was 10 years ago nigga would've went diamond"], "meaning": "Drake is, in fact, America’s most pirated artist, according to data monitoring company Musicmetric.\n\n10 years ago albums used to sell nearly twice as much as they do today. This may have to do with how easy it is to simply pirate music for free thanks to the internet. A diamond record certifies 10 million copies sold.", "annotation_id": "2437237", "url": "https://genius.com/2437237", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Know Bout Me", "line": "Really do it the best, I’m DJ Khaled for real", "vault_lines": ["Really do it the best, I'm DJ Khaled for real"], "meaning": "DJ Khaled runs the We The Best music group, and although Drake isn’t part of that, he still raps the best, hence the comparison.\n\nThe two have worked together before, on “I’m On One” and “No New Friends.”", "annotation_id": "2437177", "url": "https://genius.com/2437177", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Know Bout Me", "line": "We gotta sell these bitches the dream, my nigga Niggas like Walt Disney around this bitch", "vault_lines": ["We gotta sell these bitches the dream, my nigga", "Niggas like Walt Disney around this bitch"], "meaning": "The Walt Disney Company is known for “making dreams come true”. Jay’s sentiment is insinuating that Disney is selling the “dream” through their market and corporation.", "annotation_id": "2437156", "url": "https://genius.com/2437156", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
