{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Recognize", "line": "You’re my nigga", "vault_lines": ["All these bitches know that you're my nigga"], "meaning": "🏳️‍🌈", "annotation_id": "41303833", "url": "https://genius.com/41303833", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": false, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Recognize", "line": "You got niggas and I got bitches You got niggas and I got bitches You got niggas", "vault_lines": ["Know, you got niggas and I got bitches", "You got niggas and I got bitches", "I want you, I want you"], "meaning": "may mga tao na di papayag na umalis ka. pero di naman gumagawa ng paraan para ikaw ay manatili", "annotation_id": "39266239", "url": "https://genius.com/39266239", "state": "pending", "votes": -2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Recognize", "line": "Then cut like kids cake", "vault_lines": ["Then cut like kids cake"], "meaning": "It’s *kiss cake\nA popular Caribbean bakery (PND has Jamaican roots)", "annotation_id": "36729305", "url": "https://genius.com/36729305", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Recognize", "line": "I gotta get you those snow tires for your Mercedes I’m glad you reminded me, baby", "vault_lines": ["Won't do for you, I do for you", "I gotta get you those snow tires for your Mercedes", "I'm glad you reminded me, baby", "I want you, I want you"], "meaning": "Snow tires are tires that are often used for driving cars on the snow and ice. Snow tires are slower than normal tires, but they are more cautious, reliable, and do not slip up.\n\nMercedes-Benz, aka Mercedes, is a luxury car brand that is known for its precise engineering and attention to detail.\n\nDrake may be explaining many different things here. Drake is most likely saying that he is more reliable and cautious than other men, referring to himself as snow tires and referring to the girl as a Mercedes (meaning that Drake considers the girl to be elite).\n\nDrake may also be stating the line very literally- he may be attempting to purchase snow tires for the girl’s Mercedes. Considering snow tires are relatively expensive and Mercedes-Benz cars are very expensive, Drake may just be referencing his ostentatious qualities. He may be demonstrating that money isn’t very important to him since he has so much, so he doesn’t mind spending money on snow tires for a girl.", "annotation_id": "31935708", "url": "https://genius.com/31935708", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Recognize", "line": "Girl, you must be doin’ magic Girl, you must be doin’ magic Turn fuckin’ you to a habit", "vault_lines": ["Girl, you must be doin' magic", "Turn fuckin' you to a habit"], "meaning": "PND feels like the girl he wants to fuck put him in a hypnosis to make him even like her more. He considers fucking her a habit, which can be due to the increase of liking her even more.", "annotation_id": "31215752", "url": "https://genius.com/31215752", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Recognize", "line": "Who do you fuck in the city when I’m not there? I owe you time", "vault_lines": ["Won't do for you, I do for you", "Who do you fuck in the city when I'm not there? I owe you time", "I want you, I want you"], "meaning": "WHO ARE YOU WITH WHEN IM NOT THERE?", "annotation_id": "31142266", "url": "https://genius.com/31142266", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": false, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Recognize", "line": "Know, you got niggas and I got bitches You got niggas and I got bitches You got niggas and I got bitches You got niggas", "vault_lines": ["Know, you got niggas and I got bitches", "You got niggas and I got bitches", "I want you, I want you"], "meaning": "Party is trying to persuade this woman to be in a relationship with him, but she denies because he has hella bitches. He argues that both of them have a roster, so this isn’t a valid excuse not to get with him.\n\nThis lyric can also be interpreted as Party saying they both have a roster, and that they’re both the shit. In that case, they might as well join forces and get together.", "annotation_id": "30860631", "url": "https://genius.com/30860631", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Recognize", "line": "The budget, I’m Party, so fuck it", "vault_lines": ["The budget, I'm Party, so fuck it"], "meaning": "Everybody knows Party gets money. He doesn’t need to set a budget for himself.", "annotation_id": "30860620", "url": "https://genius.com/30860620", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Recognize", "line": "I be tripping, but this money ain’t", "vault_lines": ["I be tripping, but this money ain't"], "meaning": "Party acknowledges that he fucks up sometimes, but he also acknowledges the fact that he has money. He uses this fact in an attempt to persuade somebody into a relationship with him.", "annotation_id": "30860610", "url": "https://genius.com/30860610", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Recognize", "line": "Girl, I see you", "vault_lines": ["Girl, I see you", "Stories of you and your girls is all I hear (Girl, let's—)", "I want you, I want you", "To turn up on me every night when I see you", "Better recognize when I see you"], "meaning": "Party is basically saying that he sees the girl that he wants her to “turn up on him” every night when she sees him (in other words partake in sexual activity)\nSo he recognizes her, but does she recognize him?", "annotation_id": "29508826", "url": "https://genius.com/29508826", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Recognize", "line": "The concierge told me my new baby looking like LeToya Luckett", "vault_lines": ["The concierge told me my new baby looking like LeToya Luckett"], "meaning": "The concierge is saying the girl he’s with looks great. LeToya Nicole Luckett-Walker is an American singer-songwriter and actress. She is known as a member of the R&B girl group Destiny’s Child, with which she won two Grammy Awards and released many successful commercial recordings. She has sold over 25 million records with Destiny’s Child.", "annotation_id": "18744132", "url": "https://genius.com/18744132", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Recognize", "line": "Lightskin got you new, new, do Even look like Lauren Lo too", "vault_lines": ["Lightskin got you new, new, do", "Even look like Lauren Lo too"], "meaning": "The girl he’s talking about is light skinned and has a new hairdo. He references “New New”, a light-skinned character played by Lauren London from the movie ATL.", "annotation_id": "12526232", "url": "https://genius.com/12526232", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Recognize", "line": "[Interlude: Top Cat & PARTYNEXTDOOR] Only special request fi the gyal dem From north, south, east and west For the body ah look good you know y’haffi God bless, bruk wild, bruk a man spine God bless, bruk wild, bruk a man spine (Gotta get real again)", "vault_lines": ["Gotta get real again, gotta get real again", "Only special request fi the gyal dem", "From north, south, east and west", "For the body ah look good you know y'haffi", "God bless, bruk wild, bruk a man spine", "Hit the club for you, you, you"], "meaning": "The song samples the classic reggae track titled “Request the Style” by Top Cat, primarily for the interlude, which uses the following words in a slightly faded out and cut up manner:\n\nSpecial request fi the gyal dem from north, south, east and west. For the body ah look good you know y'haffi God bless. Bruk wild, bruk a man spine\n\nhttp://youtu.be/oYliNalHXIs?t=5s", "annotation_id": "3871743", "url": "https://genius.com/3871743", "state": "accepted", "votes": 64, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Recognize", "line": "All of these things slip my mind, it’s been crazy", "vault_lines": ["All of these things slip my mind, it's been crazy"], "meaning": "Drizzy’s life is busy as hell, he can’t be expected to remember everything!\n\nHe stresses because he’s afraid his women might mistake his busy mind and even busier schedule for apathy.\n\nNote how “slip” refers back to the snow tires in the previous line: snow tires prevent slippage on roads in wintry weather.", "annotation_id": "3431037", "url": "https://genius.com/3431037", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Recognize", "line": "Gotta get real again, gotta get real again", "vault_lines": ["Gotta get real again, gotta get real again"], "meaning": "Party’s latest releases show that he isn’t wary about telling it how it is, whether he’s talking about the way he doesn’t want to mess around on a track like “Persian Rugs” or questioning whether he’s the only person feeling a type of way about life on “West District”.\n\nHe’s even open about being whipped by his girl on “Her Way”.\n\nDo you recognize the realness?\n\n\n\nThis could also be a reference to his song “Right Now,” where he says:\n\nI gotta keep it super real with ya, shawty\nI gotta keep it real real with ya\n\nHence PARTYNEXTDOOR saying, “gotta get real AGAIN.”", "annotation_id": "3430547", "url": "https://genius.com/3430547", "state": "accepted", "votes": 76, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Recognize", "line": "And she will not fuck with no broke niggas, no, nigga, only the richest", "vault_lines": ["And she will not fuck with no broke niggas, no, nigga, only the richest"], "meaning": "PARTY is messing with a woman that wants men with a lot of money. He seems to have a habit of messing with ladies that like to hang around guys of status, like in “Her Way”:\n\nShe wasn’t on a roll, now she roll another one up (rollin' marijuana)", "annotation_id": "3430306", "url": "https://genius.com/3430306", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Recognize", "line": "Let’s plan somethin’ out when I come back from Europe", "vault_lines": ["Let's plan somethin' out when I come back from Europe"], "meaning": "A portion of Drake’s “Would You Like A Tour” tour was held across Europe. Once he got back, he wanted to hook up with said girl.", "annotation_id": "3430254", "url": "https://genius.com/3430254", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Recognize", "line": "Sorry if my whip covered in dank ‘Cause I’ve been rollin’ with this skunk all day", "vault_lines": ["Sorry if my whip covered in dank", "'Cause I've been rollin' with this skunk all day"], "meaning": "PND apologizes for his car smelling like weed because he’s been rolling with this “skunk” all day, meaning some strain of weed with a very loud scent.\n\n\n\nIt should also be noted here that PND implements effective usage of double entendre.\n\nThe word “rollin” is utilized both as a reference to him rollin' around the 6, as well as rollin' up blunts/joints as he cruises through the city.", "annotation_id": "3430245", "url": "https://genius.com/3430245", "state": "accepted", "votes": 56, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Recognize", "line": "Let my money get older and older and older and older like Regis", "vault_lines": ["Let my money get older and older and older and older like Regis"], "meaning": "PND hopes his money keeps growing as he ages. He mentions ex-talk show host Regis Philbin, who was 83 years old as of the song’s release.\n\n\n\nPND also uses Migos' flow, which seems to be a trend, as Drake has done the same in “The Language” and “We Made It”.", "annotation_id": "3430212", "url": "https://genius.com/3430212", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Recognize", "line": "Yeah, shout the girls from the East who know what’s good with me, yeah (Girl, let’s—) Shout the ones from the West know what’s good with PND, oh-oh (G-girl, let’s—)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, shout the girls from the East who know what's good with me, yeah (Girl, let's—)", "Shout the ones from the West know what's good with PND, oh-oh (G-girl, let's—)"], "meaning": "All these “Girls, Girls, Girls”…\n\nBoth Drizzy and PND are popular with the Canadian ladies (and ladies everywhere). Drake gives a nod to the east side women, from the city of Toronto. “Days in the East”, anyone?\n\nPND hails from Mississauga, Ontario, which is just west of Toronto – he’s got the ladies there nailed down with his “West District” game.", "annotation_id": "3430185", "url": "https://genius.com/3430185", "state": "accepted", "votes": 83, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Recognize", "line": "Swear I’m withholdin’ my urges ’til you get this one-on-one shit like your name Katie Couric", "vault_lines": ["Swear I'm withholdin' my urges 'til you get this one-on-one shit like your name Katie Couric"], "meaning": "Katie Couric is a famous talk show host who once sat down with Drake for a one-on-one interview on a CBS online show:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MVX-M0AgUio\n\nThis one-on-one time is quite different, though, meaning sex. Instead of wanting to smash every girl in the world, he’s focused on that special somebody.", "annotation_id": "3430183", "url": "https://genius.com/3430183", "state": "accepted", "votes": 57, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Lose My Mind (Remix)", "status": "done", "targets": 3, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Jeezy-lose-my-mind-remix-lyrics", "genius_title": "Lose My Mind (Remix)", "genius_id": 3389, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Lose My Mind (Remix)", "line": "Half a million in a week, it’s only right I do", "vault_lines": ["Half a million in a week, it's only right I do"], "meaning": "Drake is referencing his debut studio album Thank Me Later selling 447k units its first week. The album dropped 12 days before the release of this song on June 15, 2010 debuting at #1.", "annotation_id": "33919993", "url": "https://genius.com/33919993", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
