{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Lose My Mind (Remix)", "line": "One-oh-three And both fingers to the haters tryna front on me, ahh!", "vault_lines": ["And both fingers to the haters tryna front on me, ahh!"], "meaning": "Drake is shouting out jeezy, thug motivation 103,", "annotation_id": "20227940", "url": "https://genius.com/20227940", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bring It Back", "status": "done", "targets": 6, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Trouble-and-mike-will-made-it-bring-it-back-lyrics", "genius_title": "Bring It Back", "genius_id": 2930981, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bring It Back", "line": "Extra million just to see the Maybach drop (Drop, drop)", "vault_lines": ["Extra million just to see the Maybach drop (Drop, drop)"], "meaning": "Drake is referring to the Maybach Landaulet which is a convertible version of the  luxury car. Another known celebrity with one is DJ Khaled.", "annotation_id": "25994726", "url": "https://genius.com/25994726", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bring It Back", "line": "As a git, I used to get the candy from Mr. Charlie (Mr. Charlie) Nowadays I ride a foreign by Mr. Charlie (Mr. Charlie) I got the candy now, sorry Mr. Charlie", "vault_lines": ["As a git, I used to get the candy from Mr. Charlie (Mr. Charlie)", "Nowadays I ride a foreign by Mr. Charlie (Mr. Charlie)", "I got the candy now, sorry Mr. Charlie"], "meaning": "This phrase has double meaning. Mr. Charlie is African-American slang for a dominating white man. Candy could mean drugs or money, showing how Trouble was formerly dependent on others, but is independent now.\n\nCharlie could be also playing on the name of the main character from Willie Wonka and the Chocolate Factory.", "annotation_id": "15845941", "url": "https://genius.com/15845941", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bring It Back", "line": "Crest white smile on my face", "vault_lines": ["Crest white smile on my face"], "meaning": "A salty fan tried to call out Drake for having dirty teeth:\n\nLmao all that money and ur teeth still look clean.\n\nThis prompted Drake to reveal the secret to his perfectly white teeth.\n\nI have a pink diamond in my tooth. I brush with activated charcoal before any club night where I will see baddies know dattttttttttt.", "annotation_id": "14161528", "url": "https://genius.com/14161528", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bring It Back", "line": "Do it for the six, because we started there (Started)", "vault_lines": ["Do it for the six, because we started there (Started)"], "meaning": "Drake is from the 6 = Toronto.\nTrouble is from the 6 = Zone 6, East Atlanta.\n\nIn Toronto, Canada, the term “the 6” actually has nothing to do with the area codes 416 and 647. In 1998, there was an amalgamation (uniting) of the six different boroughs — Etobicoke, North York, Scarborough, York, East York and Toronto — and they became one city: Toronto.\n\nMeanwhile, Atlanta is divided in six police patrol zones numbered 1 through 6. Zone 6 covers the eastside of Atlanta.", "annotation_id": "13881335", "url": "https://genius.com/13881335", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bring It Back", "line": "I got a girl that used to ride around with ‘Pac an’ them (’Pac)", "vault_lines": ["I got a girl that used to ride around with 'Pac an' them ('Pac)"], "meaning": "Drake has been linked to numerous women throughout his career, including Rashida Jones and Madonna.\n\nFrom Complex,\n\nDrake claims that he only admired Quincy Jones' daughter from afar. “I was, like, in love with Rashida. I love funny women and I love beautiful women and I love women that have great taste in music and Rashida is all those things,” he said. They met when she complimented his DJ set at a party, and coincidentally linked at a later date when they stayed at the same resort on vacation. Maybe they had that Black Jew connection, but Rashida is famously low key, and we know Drake would respect that.\n\nRashida’s sister Kidada was Pac’s fiancee up until the time of his death.\n\nDrake also named a song after Madonna from his 2015 If You’re Reading This It’s Too Late. The two kissed at Coachella sending the music world into a frenzy. Madonna and Pac allegedly dated for a brief period of time during the 90s. Pac even wrote Madonna a letter from prison about their failed relationship.", "annotation_id": "13214606", "url": "https://genius.com/13214606", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bring It Back", "line": "Yeah, Richard Mille, heavy on the watch (Bitch)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, Richard Mille, heavy on the watch (Bitch)"], "meaning": "Drake is referring to his luxury Swiss watch. Richard Mille is a ultra-high-end timepiece with a focus on flawless craftsmanship and cutting-edge design. Drake was once spotted wearing an exclusive Richard Mille RM011 Blue Ceramic watch while performing at Bliss nightclub in DC.\n\n\n\nThis watch costs around $160,000 US Dollars.", "annotation_id": "13214493", "url": "https://genius.com/13214493", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
