{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "WASTING TIME", "line": "Flushed the Magnums just so they not collectin’ my specimens, damn", "vault_lines": ["Flushed the Magnums just so they not collectin' my specimens, damn"], "meaning": "In this lyric, Drake explains that he flushes the condom he uses with his sexual partner down a toilet. He uses this to emphasize that he is so significant that people are willing to collect his sperm from his used Magnum condom.", "annotation_id": "30478533", "url": "https://genius.com/30478533", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "WASTING TIME", "line": "If you’re gonna waste your time Then waste your time with me", "vault_lines": ["Waste it with me", "If you're gonna waste your time (Yeah)", "Then waste your time with me"], "meaning": ".", "annotation_id": "30100471", "url": "https://genius.com/30100471", "state": "pending", "votes": -19, "second_sense": false, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "WASTING TIME", "line": "The boy is back, I never turned my back I just lapped ’em, so now all that they see is my back", "vault_lines": ["Girl, you all that I see (All that I see)", "The boy is back, I never turned my back", "I just lapped 'em, so now all that they see is my back"], "meaning": "Clever play on words by Drake. Much like the saying goes, Drake is simply alluding to the fact that he’ll never turn his back on whomever he’s referring to here.\n\nBut also, much like a track runner who distinctively runs “laps” around the track, Drake is implying he just “lapped” everyone who he considers competition. So since he’s ahead of all these people, they have no other option than to literally look at his back.\n\nhttps://gifer.com/en/AGYy", "annotation_id": "28847971", "url": "https://genius.com/28847971", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "WASTING TIME", "line": "But she got no furniture in the crib, I’ve been there", "vault_lines": ["But she got no furniture in the crib, I've been there"], "meaning": "This is a double entendre. Drake’s explaining that he can relate to being too broke to afford furniture in his condo before he made it. But he’s also telling her that he’s been to said ex-roommate’s condo.", "annotation_id": "28489894", "url": "https://genius.com/28489894", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "WASTING TIME", "line": "Checkmate, even though you hate that I even check her", "vault_lines": ["Checkmate, even though you hate that I even check her"], "meaning": "This line alludes back to the reference of Beth Harmon earlier in the verse, a fictional chess prodigy from novel-turned-Netflix hit show The Queen’s Gambit. Checkmate and check are standard chess terms and Drake uses the word “check” as if he were checking out – looking at – a woman.", "annotation_id": "26264912", "url": "https://genius.com/26264912", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "WASTING TIME", "line": "Plenty things count in life, but none of them is a thought of it", "vault_lines": ["Plenty things count in life, but none of them is a thought of it"], "meaning": "A common phrase of thought is “It’s the the thought that counts,” defined as “used to indicate that it is the kindness behind an act that matters, however imperfect or insignificant the act may be.”\n\nDrake disagrees and states that plenty of things count in life, however the thought doesn’t. He believes the thought should be expressed in some capacity, and there are plenty of ways to do that.\n\nThis feeds into the previous two lines where Drake has paid for an apartment for the girl in the Ten Thousand Building and has also bought her a G-Class Mercedes.", "annotation_id": "24664420", "url": "https://genius.com/24664420", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "WASTING TIME", "line": "You used to do skincare, but now you do swimwear", "vault_lines": ["You used to do skincare, but now you do swimwear"], "meaning": "Possibly an allusion to Drake’s on-off relationship to famous singer Rihanna. Rihanna owns and directs her own beauty company, Fenty Beauty. In past years, Fenty’s main products were skincare/makeup but in recent years have also introduced various swimwear lines.", "annotation_id": "23424365", "url": "https://genius.com/23424365", "state": "pending", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "WASTING TIME", "line": "I’ll still get an E for effort", "vault_lines": ["I'll still get an E for effort"], "meaning": "This line is a double-entendre as Drake is saying E for effort, but this can also be interpreted as “E4”. E4 being the most common first move in chess which goes with the theme earlier in the verse.", "annotation_id": "23422203", "url": "https://genius.com/23422203", "state": "pending", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "WASTING TIME", "line": "The Ten Thousand Building, get your ass an apartment", "vault_lines": ["The Ten Thousand Building, get your ass an apartment"], "meaning": "The Ten Thousand Building is a Luxury Apartment Building in Los Angeles, California. Apartments go for an estimated from $10k to $29k per month in this building. Drake provides his girl high end living arrangements….", "annotation_id": "23420395", "url": "https://genius.com/23420395", "state": "pending", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "WASTING TIME", "line": "Put you inside a G-Class, that’s just a starter kit", "vault_lines": ["Put you inside a G-Class, that's just a starter kit"], "meaning": "The Mercedes-Benz G Class (also known as a G-Wagen) is a luxury SUV. Two weeks before this song’s release, iSeeCars.com declared the 2021 model the fastest-selling vehicle in America, despite its average price tag of $174,887. However, that is likely due to limited supply compared with more widely-used cars.\n\n\n\nIn February 2019, Drake purchased a Mercedes-Benz Maybach G-650 Landaulet, which High Snobiety described as “a convertible version of the G-Wagen.” He has mentioned G-Wagens numerous times in his lyrics, including this line from his March 2021 hit “Lemon Pepper Freestyle”:\n\nG-Wagen for my bitch, that girl go live it up", "annotation_id": "23414330", "url": "https://genius.com/23414330", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "WASTING TIME", "line": "Swear I’m more “Purple Rain” Prince than Prince Charmin’ Disappointment, I stay expectin’ it, the pessimist gold medalist", "vault_lines": ["Swear I'm more \"Purple Rain\" Prince than Prince Charmin'", "Disappointment, I stay expectin' it, the pessimist gold medalist"], "meaning": "In the film Purple Rain, Prince’s autobiographical character is often possessive, manipulative, and even physically abusive to the women in his life. For example, after his love interest, Apollonia, takes a job singing in his rival’s band, Prince slaps her. He then performs a song about a promiscuous woman while staring directly at her, leaving her in tears.\n\n\n\nDrake wants to warn his prospective lover that, despite his nice-guy image, he can get jealous and suspicious too. Perhaps his fame has drawn more opportunistic women into his orbit, leading him to “expect disappointment” (i.e., cheating or extortion) from them.", "annotation_id": "23412028", "url": "https://genius.com/23412028", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "WASTING TIME", "line": "Say that then, Maybach Benz with me in the back When I was in Acura, still couldn’t clean up my act", "vault_lines": ["Say that then, Maybach Benz with me in the back", "When I was in Acura, still couldn't clean up my act"], "meaning": "Drake alludes to how he has come far from his Acura TSX to his Mercedes Benz Maybach, but how back then and now, he “still couldn’t clean up [his] act”.\n\nThis is not the first time that he has referenced his first car, as it made an appearance in “Under Ground Kings,” from his album Take Care, where Drake raps:\n\nThat was back in the days, Acura days\nI was a cold dude, I’m getting back to my ways.", "annotation_id": "23403970", "url": "https://genius.com/23403970", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "WASTING TIME", "line": "New piece around my neck, it’s chess games ’Cause shorty stay with calculated moves, like Beth Harmon", "vault_lines": ["New piece around my neck, it's chess games", "'Cause shorty stay with calculated moves, like Beth Harmon"], "meaning": "Drake compares his “shorty” to Beth Harmon, the fictional chess prodigy and the main character in The Queen’s Gambit, the 1983 thriller novel written by Walter Tevis.\n\nThe character is portrayed as a very intelligent and passionate person, who even learns Russian to eavesdrop on people.\n\n\n\n\nAnya Taylor-Joy as Beth Harmon in the Netflix mini-series adaptation of The Queen’s Gambit.", "annotation_id": "23398951", "url": "https://genius.com/23398951", "state": "accepted", "votes": 44, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "WASTING TIME", "line": "The way she with papi, man, you would think she’s a veteran on remembrance", "vault_lines": ["The way she with papi, man, you would think she's a veteran on remembrance"], "meaning": "Drake is referring to himself through the word “papi” due to his well-known nickname “Champagne Papi” deriving from his Instagram name. “Poppy” is a homophone of “papi” and is a type of red flower famously worn on Remembrance Day in Canada and the UK on November 11 to commemorate the lives lost in World War I. Veterans who survived wars when fighting for their nation often take part in such occasions to display solidarity between the Armed Forces–old and new. Like a Veteran always wears a poppy on Remembrance Day, Drake’s girl is always by his side.\n\n\n\nPictured: British Veterans wearing poppies in a Remembrance Day service", "annotation_id": "23398929", "url": "https://genius.com/23398929", "state": "pending", "votes": 53, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "WASTING TIME", "line": "Only time I play the back and forth is Aaliyah record", "vault_lines": ["Only time I play the back and forth is Aaliyah record"], "meaning": "Drake references his biggest influence, the late singer Aaliyah and her debut single, “Back & Forth,” released in 1994.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=a02dBbBGSPg\n\nThis is not the first time Drake references Aaliyah in his music. His latest effort being interpolating her 2001 single “More Than A Woman” on the Scorpion cut “Is There More” from 2018.", "annotation_id": "23398534", "url": "https://genius.com/23398534", "state": "accepted", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
