{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stay Schemin’", "line": "Maybach Music", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Rick Ross producer tag", "annotation_id": "31443377", "url": "https://genius.com/31443377", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stay Schemin’", "line": "Ordered her the filet, told ’em, “Butterfly it, she’ll love it.” She used to soda and nuggets, she really just out here thuggin’", "vault_lines": ["Ordered her the filet, told 'em, \"Butterfly it, she'll love it.\"", "She used to soda and nuggets, she really just out here thuggin'"], "meaning": "Butterflying a steak filet is when the chef delicately cuts slice from the middle of the filet downward until the steak resembles butterfly wings.\n\n\n\nIt is often only requested at high class restaurants, Drake is predicting her excitement to get to enjoy the higher class foods he notes by saying how shes used to eating less classy and expensive things like soda and nuggets.", "annotation_id": "18923383", "url": "https://genius.com/18923383", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stay Schemin’", "line": "Spaghetti bolognese in the Polo Lounge", "vault_lines": ["Spaghetti bolognese in the Polo Lounge"], "meaning": "The Polo Lounge is considered a hotspot for Hollywood eating. Obviously a lot of famous people like Drake eat there.\n\nHowever, spaghetti bolognese is not served at the Polo Lounge. Drake probably means Rigatoni Bolognese, served at lunch and dinner, which costs $56.\n\n\n\nRigatoni (pictured above) is an entirely different type of pasta than spaghetti (pictured below), so Drake either doesn’t know his pasta or he has enough clout to get an exclusive meal.", "annotation_id": "17616863", "url": "https://genius.com/17616863", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stay Schemin’", "line": "Watch the body tilt when you hit the head (Huh)", "vault_lines": ["Watch the body tilt when you hit the head (Huh)"], "meaning": "In his Decoded interview with Life + Times, French states that it means like when you take the leader of something out, everyone else falls. Hence the next line, “tryna beat the feds.” .\n\nIn a more literal sense, French can attest to being shot in the head because it happened to him. His attacker suffered the same fate, dying because of it. .", "annotation_id": "618973", "url": "https://genius.com/618973", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stay Schemin’", "line": "Million-dollar meetings in a Polo Lounge", "vault_lines": ["Million-dollar meetings in a Polo Lounge"], "meaning": "In repeating this line with the article “a” in lieu of “the,” Drizzy is emphasizing a second meaning. It’s possible that he is implying that not only is he going to million dollar meetings, but he’s doing it quite casually (as most big name rappers do) and he’s simultaneously sporting some Polo loungewear. The designer apparel would naturally be associated with and a direct product of Drake’s fame and fortune.\n\nIn saying this, he’s following up on the line “might look light,” for he’s saying that though his attire seems unfit for the occasion, he and his crew are important people (that happen to be able to get you gunned up quick.)\n\nAs Bear Bryant once candidly said: “When you get in the end zone, act like you’ve been there before.”", "annotation_id": "555586", "url": "https://genius.com/555586", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stay Schemin’", "line": "(Huh! Bitch, you wasn’t with me shootin’ in the gym)", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, you wasn't with me shootin' in the gym"], "meaning": "Bawse repeats the line for emphasis. Kobe’s wife wasn’t there when he was putting in the hard work to be famous, shooting thousands of jumpers in the gym. So now she doesn’t deserve ½ of what she didn’t work for.\n\n\n\nIn 2013, Vanessa Bryant responded to these lyrics in an Instagram comment and claimed Drake had apologized to her in a text.\n\n\nI love when immature kids quote a rapper that has never been friends with Kobe and knows nothing about our relationship. Just shows how gullible they are. I don’t need to be in the gym. I’m raising our daughters, signing checks and taking care of everything else that pertains to our home life. But thanks for your concern over an immature quote.\n\nI really wish people would stop THINK and then realize that they are being sucked into someone’s clear intention to monetize and gain attention off of our family’s heartache. This is real life. I hold down our home life so my husband can focus on his career. It’s a partnership.\n\nSince my husband isn’t friends with Drake, we received a text of an apology forwarded from his manager. It’s done and over with and it’s now time for people to THINK before speaking.", "annotation_id": "541830", "url": "https://genius.com/541830", "state": "accepted", "votes": 166, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stay Schemin’", "line": "Tell Lucian I said “fuck it,” I’m tearin’ holes in my budget", "vault_lines": ["Tell Lucian I said \"fuck it,\" I'm tearin' holes in my budget"], "meaning": "As in Lucian Grainge, the CEO of Universal Music Group, of which Young Money is a subsidiary.\n\nDrake is letting his boss know he doesn’t care if he’s exceeding his album budget, because a more quality product will ultimately garner him more profit.\n\nOn January 26, 2020, at the Universal Grammy afterparty, Lucian was asked about this line to which he replied:\n\nWhenever Drake calls up and says he needs more money for his project, I give it to him…because he’s the greatest.", "annotation_id": "538296", "url": "https://genius.com/538296", "state": "accepted", "votes": 63, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stay Schemin’", "line": "Stay schemin’ Niggas tryna get at me, dawg", "vault_lines": ["Niggas tryna get at me, dawg"], "meaning": "Borrowed from Nas' unreleased track “Day Dreamin (Stay Schemin)” Nas originally found the inspiration for his hook in Kurtis Blow’s 1982 song “Daydreamin”.", "annotation_id": "532400", "url": "https://genius.com/532400", "state": "accepted", "votes": 95, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stay Schemin’", "line": "Then gave my nigga Penthouse another 30 (Huh)", "vault_lines": ["Then gave my nigga Penthouse another 30 (Huh)"], "meaning": "This is not the first time Montana has shouted out his incarcerated friend.  Penthouse’s name comes up “What You Want From Me”\n\nOne writer tells us that “Penthouse” is also known as “Penthouse P” and that he was one of the biggest drug figures on Long Island", "annotation_id": "532392", "url": "https://genius.com/532392", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stay Schemin’", "line": "Niggas lost mills tryna beat the feds (Huh)", "vault_lines": ["Niggas lost mills tryna beat the feds (Huh)"], "meaning": "See here for more on rappers' grudging respect for federal crime-fighting forces in general (as opposed to local or state police).\n\nSpecifically, he is referring to the millions he spent personally to beat a murder charge.", "annotation_id": "532388", "url": "https://genius.com/532388", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stay Schemin’", "line": "From the hoopty coupe to that Ghost, dawg (Huh) Pigeons on the roof like Ghost Dog (Huh)", "vault_lines": ["From the hoopty coupe to that Ghost, dawg (Huh)", "Pigeons on the roof like Ghost Dog (Huh)"], "meaning": "Along with a bit of internal rhyming, French makes nice use of one of RG’s favorite literary devices, the homophone. The first “Ghost, dog” refers to the extremely expensive Rolls-Royce Ghost, which Montana now claims to be driving in place of his old, beat-up car.\n\n\n\nThe second iteration of the phrase refers to the movie called Ghost Dog: The Way of the Samurai, a 1999 film directed by Jim Jarmusch which starred Forest Whitaker as a hit man who only communicates by homing pigeon, and thus keeps a stable of birds.  Montana’s pigeons are of a different kind entirely – it’s slang for a kilo of coke\n\n\n\nPS, as Willy Staley for the NEW YORK MOTHERFUCKING TIMES has noted (in an article that mentions us!), he’s NOT saying “fanute” (this is a mondegreen). French even cleared it up with us!\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NFotPdXD_XY", "annotation_id": "532378", "url": "https://genius.com/532378", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stay Schemin’", "line": "I’m just hittin’ my pinnacle, you and pussy identical You like the fuckin’ finish line; we can’t wait to run into you", "vault_lines": ["I'm just hittin' my pinnacle, you and pussy identical", "You like the fuckin' finish line; we can't wait to run into you"], "meaning": "The young Drizzy taking age-related shots at Common, who at the time of this song was a few months from 40.\n\nDrake and Common did eventually run into each other at the 2012 Grammys. But according to Common, they squashed the beef once they meet face to face:\n\nWe had a talk, we had a conversation. It was a face-to-face, man-to-man, a positive thing. It was a good conversation. I’ve learned to respect him even more. I already thought he was a talented guy, but just from the conversation we had, I hold even more respect for him. We saw each other and the conversation was initiated. It was just a respectful conversation that needed to be had, so he knew that I’m not at him trying to destroy him as a human being. It was a Hip Hop battle to me. I had to put all of those things into Hip Hop… I gave him a pound, gave him a boom and it was all love.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ryO-eugtEBc\n\nDrake and Common were eventually spotted together at the 2012 NBA All-Star game after the beef ended:", "annotation_id": "532373", "url": "https://genius.com/532373", "state": "accepted", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stay Schemin’", "line": "Might look light, but we heavy though You think Drake will pull some shit like that? You never know", "vault_lines": ["Might look light, but we heavy though", "You think Drake will pull some shit like that? You never know"], "meaning": "While Drake and his cohorts may not appear to be tough, they may well surprise you with weapons and/or violence.  There’s also a pun here on Drizzy’s light-skinned appearance – the rapper is famously biracial.  Below with his mother, Sandi Graham:", "annotation_id": "532322", "url": "https://genius.com/532322", "state": "accepted", "votes": 63, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stay Schemin’", "line": "Double M, I got Gs out in California (Huh!)", "vault_lines": ["Double M, I got Gs out in California (Huh!)"], "meaning": "Ross puns on the name of his label, Maybach Music Group or MMG, suggesting that the Maybach Music folks make money (G’s) and/or know real “g’s” – gangsters – on the West Coast", "annotation_id": "532298", "url": "https://genius.com/532298", "state": "accepted", "votes": 51, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stay Schemin’", "line": "Dwight Howard on the post, dawg (Huh) My niggas got the powder through the post, dawg (Huh)", "vault_lines": ["Dwight Howard on the post, dawg (Huh)", "My niggas got the powder through the post, dawg (Huh)"], "meaning": "Montana stays “posted up” at his drug corner similar to how NBA big man Dwight Howard stays posted up in the basketball sense of the term\n\n\n\nContinuing with the homophones, as above, the second “post” here refers to sending drugs via the postal service", "annotation_id": "531510", "url": "https://genius.com/531510", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stay Schemin’", "line": "Gave my nigga Max 7-5 (Huh)", "vault_lines": ["Gave my nigga Max 7-5 (Huh)"], "meaning": "Referring to his pal, Dipset associate Charlie “Max B” Wingate, who is currently serving a 75 year sentence on armed robbery, kidnapping, and murder charges", "annotation_id": "531506", "url": "https://genius.com/531506", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stay Schemin’", "line": "Guess every team doesn’t come complete with niggas like ours", "vault_lines": ["Guess every team doesn't come complete with niggas like ours"], "meaning": "Drake is part of Young Money Cash Money Billionaires, a team run by Birdman, Lil Wayne, Nicki Minaj, Tyga, Busta Rhymes, et. al.\n\nHe could be taking swipes at G.O.O.D. Music, since Common is affiliated with that crew.\n\nAlso, Pusha T is signed to G.O.O.D. Music, and he has his own feud with Drake, as evident from “Sweet Freestyle” and “Don’t Fuck With Me.”", "annotation_id": "531503", "url": "https://genius.com/531503", "state": "accepted", "votes": 61, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stay Schemin’", "line": "Bag her like we in Publix, and take her ass out in public", "vault_lines": ["Bag her like we in Publix, and take her ass out in public"], "meaning": "Publix is a supermarket similar to Kroger or Whole Foods Market. The chain is Southern based and especially heavy in Florida, where it originated.  A long way from Toronto, Drake likely dropped the name for a little authenticity, because he often talks about being in Miami.\n\nDrake sounds a little bit like his labelmate:\n\n“And I got her nigga – grocery bag!”", "annotation_id": "531484", "url": "https://genius.com/531484", "state": "accepted", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stay Schemin’", "line": "Me and my man Oliver North, that’s how I roll around", "vault_lines": ["Me and my G from D.C., that's how I roll around", "Me and my man Oliver North, that's how I roll around"], "meaning": "Oliver is fellow Canadian OVO member Oliver El-Khatib, who Drake calls one of his closest friends and is Drizzy’s brand manager.  The “North” presumably comes from his Canadian heritage (he grew up in both London and Toronto), and is a pun on the controversial political figure Oliver North.  El-Khatib is pictured below:", "annotation_id": "531469", "url": "https://genius.com/531469", "state": "accepted", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stay Schemin’", "line": "That’s why I see no need to compete with niggas like y’all", "vault_lines": ["That's why I see no need to compete with niggas like y'all"], "meaning": "Drake’s producer and close friend Noah “40” Shebib responded to Common over Twitter:", "annotation_id": "531388", "url": "https://genius.com/531388", "state": "accepted", "votes": 55, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stay Schemin’", "line": "I just ask that when you see me you speak up, nigga, that’s all Don’t be duckin’ like you never wanted nothin’", "vault_lines": ["I just ask that when you see me you speak up, nigga, that's all", "Don't be duckin' like you never wanted nothin'"], "meaning": "Drake accused Common of avoiding him and addressed this at the Cali Christmas Concert after “Sweet” dropped.\n\nDrake and Common did eventually run into each other at the 2012 Grammys. But according to Common, they squashed the beef once they meet face to face:\n\nWe had a talk, we had a conversation. It was a face-to-face, man-to-man, a positive thing. It was a good conversation. I’ve learned to respect him even more. I already thought he was a talented guy, but just from the conversation we had, I hold even more respect for him. We saw each other and the conversation was initiated. It was just a respectful conversation that needed to be had, so he knew that I’m not at him trying to destroy him as a human being. It was a Hip Hop battle to me. I had to put all of those things into Hip Hop… I gave him a pound, gave him a boom and it was all love.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ryO-eugtEBc\n\nDrake and Common were eventually spotted together at the 2012 NBA All-Star game after the beef ended:", "annotation_id": "531372", "url": "https://genius.com/531372", "state": "accepted", "votes": 79, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stay Schemin’", "line": "Shawty wanna tell me secrets ’bout a rap nigga I tell that bitch it’s more attractive when you hold it down", "vault_lines": ["Shawty wanna tell me secrets 'bout a rap nigga", "I tell that bitch it's more attractive when you hold it down"], "meaning": "Here Drake alludes to the possible reason for Common’s beef:  They both have been romantically linked to tennis star Serena Williams.  See here for a rundown on the Drake-Serena relationship rumors\n\n\n\n\n\nIn an interview with VladTV after the beef, Common admitted it was a “war over a girl” saying:\n\nUnfortunately the war might have been over a girl, even though at the time I never said that. But it wasn’t totally that, it was more or less, ‘Do you respect me? Because I actually like you as an artist.’\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XlfqfLm27n8\n\nDrake could also be referring to radio host Charlamagne. With them too having had intercourse with the same girls, they now know certain things about each other when it comes to ‘the bedroom’ because of pillow talk.\n\nhttp://youtu.be/5X8JouGD_fo?t=3m34s", "annotation_id": "531314", "url": "https://genius.com/531314", "state": "accepted", "votes": 48, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stay Schemin’", "line": "Back when if a nigga reached it was for the weapon Nowadays niggas reach just to sell they record", "vault_lines": ["Back when if a nigga reached it was for the weapon", "Nowadays niggas reach just to sell they record"], "meaning": "Drake continues the Common-bashing here. Com’s single “Sweet” was released 1 ½ months before his ninth album, The Dreamer/The Believer, which sparked people’s interest as to who he was talking about. Here Drake suggests Common dissed him simply because he wanted to sell records by igniting a beef with Drake for no real reason.", "annotation_id": "531226", "url": "https://genius.com/531226", "state": "accepted", "votes": 74, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stay Schemin’", "line": "It bothers me when the gods get to actin’ like the broads", "vault_lines": ["It bothers me when the gods get to actin' like the broads"], "meaning": "Aimed at rapper Common. Common dissed Drake in the song “Sweet”–something he at first denied, and then grudgingly admitted.\n\nThis line establishes the verse as Drake’s counter-punch and indicates that Common is acting like a woman.  The “acting” word choice is a nod to Common’s burgeoning career as a thespian. The phrasing also gives Common respect for what he’s done in the rap game, just calling him a bitch for what he’s doing now\n\nWhile Drake has not directly confirmed that this section of the song is about Common, French Montana, who also appears on this track, has told interviewers to “read between the lines” to understand the tune.", "annotation_id": "531146", "url": "https://genius.com/531146", "state": "accepted", "votes": 160, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stay Schemin’", "line": "Kobe ’bout to lose a hundred fifty Ms", "vault_lines": ["Kobe 'bout to lose a hundred fifty Ms"], "meaning": "Kobe’s wife Vanessa filed for divorce in 2011 and seemed poised to make a killing off the split from the then-highest paid player in the NBA. Similar to Tiger and Elin' divorce, but Elin got 110 million! In the end, the couple didn’t go through with the divorce.", "annotation_id": "531133", "url": "https://genius.com/531133", "state": "accepted", "votes": 132, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "status": "done", "targets": 29, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/French-montana-no-shopping-lyrics", "genius_title": "No Shopping", "genius_id": 2554175, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "[Chorus: French Montana]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This hook could be a reference to Big Sean’s song “Mula”, from his Detroit mixtape, in which French Montana was featured.\n\nSeveral portions of “Mula” resemble the hook of “No Shopping”:\n\nBig Sean’s hook:\n\nAin’t nothing more important than the mula\nAin’t nothing more important than the mula\n\nSeveral parts of Montana’s verse:\n\nAin’t nothing more important than the mula\n\nAnd…\n\nWe ain’t shopping, buy the store\n\nAlthough Montana’s music career started in 2002, the year 2012 was when he picked up considerable hype as an artist. His single “Pop That” went certified platinum and his album Excuse My French was labeled as one of the most anticipated albums of the year by Complex.\n\n2012 was also the year “Mula” was released along with Big Sean’s Detroit mixtape.\n\nThis continuity in French Montana’s lyrics from his early years of commercial success to his current music may be his way of expressing that his goals haven’t changed throughout his career.\n\nFor French, money and success has remained of upmost importance.", "annotation_id": "10343408", "url": "https://genius.com/10343408", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "All about the mula, all about the mula (Woo) Word to the bird, I ain’t never take her fur shoppin’ (Ayy, woo)", "vault_lines": ["All about the mula, all about the mula (Woo)", "Word to the bird, I ain't never take her fur shoppin' (Ayy, woo)"], "meaning": "Every woman’s not a bird. I never take a bird shoppin’, I only take a lady shoppin’. A bird’ll have you and your father take her shopping. Have I ever bought a fur for a lady or a bird? Maybe for a lady before, yup. We’d get a custom somewhere downtown, it’s little spots right on 30th Street.", "annotation_id": "10138318", "url": "https://genius.com/10138318", "state": "verified", "votes": 73, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "[Verse 2: Drake & French Montana]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Me and Drake were supposed to do a song together for like two years now but he was working on his album and I was working on mine and we always had something going on. We finally got the time. Me and Drake got in the studio together to record this, we had a party the night before and the night after we recorded.\n\nHe already had “No Shopping,” he was like, “Yo let’s do this one.” I was like, “Let’s do it.” I put the hook and my verse on it, but he already had the verse on it. Once I finished my verse and hook he added four more bars.", "annotation_id": "10138281", "url": "https://genius.com/10138281", "state": "verified", "votes": 85, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "Haan, skrrt, skrrt", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "I feel like every once in a while, people come up with new things. The dab, the Skrrt ad-libs, there’s a lot of things, it’s probably just a phase that comes in and out.", "annotation_id": "10138272", "url": "https://genius.com/10138272", "state": "verified", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "Sippin’ on the drank, sippin’ on the drank (Yeah) Sippin’ on the drank, sippin’ on the drank (Yeah, woo)", "vault_lines": ["Sippin' on the drank, sippin' on the drank (Yeah)", "Yeah, sippin' on the drank, sippin' on the drank", "Yeah, sippin' on the drank, I ain't tryna think (Yeah)", "Sippin' on the drank, I ain't tryna think (Woo, ayy, ayy)"], "meaning": "I been drinkin’ Ciroc, Belaire, and some water. That brown be having so much sugar in it.", "annotation_id": "10138259", "url": "https://genius.com/10138259", "state": "verified", "votes": 87, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "I just told Drizzy, “Let me take Serena to the tropics”", "vault_lines": ["I just told Drizzy, \"Let me take Serena to the tropics\""], "meaning": "Yeah I asked him! We’re bros. That stays between us. You don’t get that one, you don’t get the bro conversation. [Laughs.] I’ve met Serena before, I’ve said hi. But me and bro always joke around like that so it’s not even that serious.", "annotation_id": "10138257", "url": "https://genius.com/10138257", "state": "verified", "votes": 53, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "I just bought Selena crib, I’m poppin’", "vault_lines": ["I just bought Selena crib, I'm poppin'"], "meaning": "I bought Selena Gomez’s most recent crib in Calabasas. I love living half hour, 45 minutes away from the city. Even over here in Jersey where I got my house, I like my space. If I wanna chill at the crib, I wanna feel like I’m outta town.\n\nI spoke with Selena, but I never met her. She was still living there when I bought it. Everybody wanna live there because you can be comfortable, it’s double gated, the air smells better. I wasn’t out there when that big fire happened but I had to call and make sure I had insurance on that house.", "annotation_id": "10138254", "url": "https://genius.com/10138254", "state": "verified", "votes": 61, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "Runnin’ through them keys way before Khaled (Another one)", "vault_lines": ["Runnin' through them keys way before Khaled (Another one)"], "meaning": "Me and Khaled got history. I met Khaled when I was signed to Akon in the mid-2000s but I wasn’t that poppin’ at the time so it took me a little minute. I’ve known him since back then. You gotta give Khaled his props, when he use you that mean you poppin’. Back when I was with Akon I wasn’t lit yet but when I got lit, he put me on the joint with him and Jay Z. I’m on his new album again. It’s a blessing to work with him, he’s a good dude.", "annotation_id": "10138240", "url": "https://genius.com/10138240", "state": "verified", "votes": 96, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "Last week, boy dem runnin’ in the room (Haan)", "vault_lines": ["Last week, boy dem runnin' in the room (Haan)"], "meaning": "“Boy Dem” is a term for the police used in Toronto-Jamaican slang. There is a deep influence of Jamaican culture in Toronto, and Drake has started incorporating more of the slang into his music.\n\n\n\n“Boy Dem”, sounds eerily similar to “Budden”; in which case Drake is referring to Joe Budden running his mouth about “Views” on his podcast.\n\nClick here for a slowed down version of this line.", "annotation_id": "10109213", "url": "https://genius.com/10109213", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "Took her out once she got attached to him Ring, ring, click, I’ll get back to ’em (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["Took her out once she got attached to him", "Ring, ring, click, I'll get back to 'em (Woo)"], "meaning": "Drake was spotted holidaying with Budden’s ex Tahiry, something he mentioned on “4PM In Calabasas.” Even though she was “attached” to Budden, Drake was able to swoop in.\n\nDuring that track Drake also rapped:\n\nAnd you even hit my line like where you been at\nIt’s always on some shit like when can I get a favor\nOr where my bitch at, like I’m about to tell you where she been at\nCosta Careyes, I got her kidnapped\n\nThe implication is that Budden was either calling Tahiry or Drake to find out what was happening with them. It seems like Drake never returned the call.", "annotation_id": "10108753", "url": "https://genius.com/10108753", "state": "accepted", "votes": 83, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "Yeah, and I know Taraji like I’m baby boy (Haan)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, and I know Taraji like I'm baby boy (Haan)", "And I fuck with Weezy and I'm Baby, boy (Haan)"], "meaning": "Actress Taraji P. Henson has starred in many big movies and TV shows over her career. Baby Boy was the film that got Taraji into the Hollywood spotlight and kick started her successful career in show biz.\n\n\n\nDrake was also rumored to be dating Taraji back when he first started catching a buzz in music.", "annotation_id": "10108628", "url": "https://genius.com/10108628", "state": "accepted", "votes": 69, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "Bitch, I just rapped and it went pop Next move better than my last move (Haan) Your next move can’t erase your past moves", "vault_lines": ["Bitch, I just rapped and it went pop", "Next move better than my last move (Haan)", "Your next move can't erase your past moves"], "meaning": "Drake gets grief for singing on songs, but even his straight rap tracks are commercially successful.\n\nDrake has been savvy in handling beef, notably out-maneuvering Meek Mill in 2015. Budden has also played beef intelligently, gathering huge media coverage for his songs dissing Drake.\n\nDrake claims that no move can erase Budden’s past business mistakes, likely referencing his falling out with Def Jam in the early 2000s.", "annotation_id": "10108607", "url": "https://genius.com/10108607", "state": "accepted", "votes": 97, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "How you out here celebratin’ like the winnin’ team? No, calm down, calm down Shit ain’t how you think it is, take a look around (Skrrt)", "vault_lines": ["How you out here celebratin' like the winnin' team?", "No, calm down, calm down", "Shit ain't how you think it is, take a look around (Skrrt)"], "meaning": "Drake likely references Budden’s Views critique, which gathered him a lot of press. “Take a look around” may be an invitation to see how commercially successful the album was, despite Budden’s criticism.\n\nAlthough this track was previewed before Budden released “Making A Murderer Pt. 1,” Drake utilises the same technique Budden employed—using previous song titles as diss material.\n\nBudden had a track titled “Calm Down” on his first record.", "annotation_id": "10108582", "url": "https://genius.com/10108582", "state": "accepted", "votes": 69, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "Word to Biggie, we’ll be Pac-in’ (We be Pac-in’, what?)", "vault_lines": ["Word to Biggie, we'll be Pac-in' (We be Pac-in', what?)"], "meaning": "French Montana mentions two of the biggest hip-hop artists and  influencers of all time: Biggie Smalls and Tupac Shakur. Biggie was the face of East Coast gangsta rap, while Tupac was the face of the West Coast.\n\nMontana flips Tupac’s name to mean “packing,” indicating he has a concealed firearm on him.", "annotation_id": "10108553", "url": "https://genius.com/10108553", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "Word to Diddy, we Cirocin’ (How we rockin’)", "vault_lines": ["Word to Diddy, we Cirocin' (How we rockin')"], "meaning": "Since 2007, marketing and promotion for CÎROC Ultra-Premium Vodka in the United States has been handled by Sean “Diddy” Combs. Diddy has widely endorsed Ciroc, and has brought other rappers on the endorsement team, like French and, most notably, DJ Khaled.", "annotation_id": "10108548", "url": "https://genius.com/10108548", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "Runnin’ with the pushas way before Malice (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["Runnin' with the pushas way before Malice (Woo)"], "meaning": "Referring to the rap duo Clipse, which consists of brothers Pusha T and Malice.\n\nPusha T’s lyrical content often revolves around drugs, and “pusha” is slang for drug dealer. Montana claims he was running with drug dealers and “coke boys” before the duo was ever formed, although Clipse was signed to a record label in 1996, when French was 12 years old.", "annotation_id": "10108545", "url": "https://genius.com/10108545", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "Caught her off the rebound, Ben Wallace, gave her four dollars (Haan)", "vault_lines": ["Caught her off the rebound, Ben Wallace, gave her four dollars (Haan)"], "meaning": "Ben Wallace was a professional basketball player who played center for the Detroit Pistons for a majority of his career. Wallace led the NBA in rebounding during the 2002 and 2003 seasons.\n\nhttps://m.youtube.com/watch?v=e7iF9McY_k4\n\nCatching a girl “off the rebound” means that you start a relationship with her just after she has left a relationship. There is a stereotype that someone on the rebound makes rash or illogical dating decisions because they’re in a weak emotional state.\n\nIn 2014, French’s ex-girlfriend Khloe Kardashian admitted on Keeping Up With The Kardashians that their relationship was a rebound:\n\nI jumped into something because I was just, like, lonely and destructive. But now I’m like, I just want to be alone.", "annotation_id": "10108539", "url": "https://genius.com/10108539", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "I’m steady droppin’ bombs on your head top (Haan) Been that way since I could make your bed rock (Haan) I’m on Bloor where you can’t shop (Skrrt)", "vault_lines": ["I'm steady droppin' bombs on your head top (Haan)", "Been that way since I could make your bed rock (Haan)", "I'm on Bloor where you can't shop (Skrrt)"], "meaning": "“Bed Rock” was an extremely popular song from 2009 which featured Drake. That song, along with “Best I Ever Had”, helped launch Drake to superstardom.\n\nBloor-Yorkville is an upscale shopping area in Toronto. Drake brags about using all the money he’s made to shop at these expensive stores.", "annotation_id": "10108520", "url": "https://genius.com/10108520", "state": "accepted", "votes": 88, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "And I’m sell off like the man that brought me in this thing (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["And I'm sell off like the man that brought me in this thing (Woo)"], "meaning": "“Sell off” is a Jamaican slang term which indicates the supreme aspect of something or someone.\n\nDrake may be referencing  Lil Wayne’s success and legendary status within the rap game. Wayne sold a million copies in a week with the Carter III, which Drake came close to when he sold a million copies of Views in just two weeks. Wayne also played quite an instrumental role in the early stages of Drake’s music career.", "annotation_id": "10108518", "url": "https://genius.com/10108518", "state": "accepted", "votes": 89, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "This week sold one-point-two (Haan) Yeah, it’s a Boucheron, baby boy", "vault_lines": ["This week sold one-point-two (Haan)", "Yeah, it's a Boucheron, baby boy"], "meaning": "Drake’s album Views sold 1.2 million copies in its first week. With such incredible sales numbers, Drake can easily afford expensive and rare Boucheron jewelry.", "annotation_id": "10108511", "url": "https://genius.com/10108511", "state": "accepted", "votes": 76, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "The birds want rings and tings, you know But we’ll never take the bird shoppin’, you know Still, you already dun know Big up, Six God", "vault_lines": ["The birds want rings and tings, you know", "But we'll never take the bird shoppin', you know", "Still, you already dun know", "Big up, Six God"], "meaning": "“Birds” is another term for women. French claims he won’t give women materialistic items like jewelry.\n\nFrench uses a Jamaican intonation here. He is from the Bronx, which has one of the largest Jamaican immigrant populations in the world.", "annotation_id": "10108510", "url": "https://genius.com/10108510", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "I’m supposed to be on a vacation right now But I’m home wildin’, word to DJ Khaled Back with another one", "vault_lines": ["I'm supposed to be on a vacation right now", "But I'm home wildin', word to DJ Khaled", "Back with another one"], "meaning": "Instead of enjoying his chart success from a beach in the tropics, Drake is back in the studio already, working on new music. In an interview with Zane Lowe on April 29, 2016, the same night he released Views, Drake said he was dropping more tracks in the summer.\n\n“Another one” is a meme phrase coined by DJ Khaled. The two worked on the Billboard Hot 100 hit “For Free” soon before this track was released.", "annotation_id": "10108504", "url": "https://genius.com/10108504", "state": "accepted", "votes": 79, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "And I fuck with Weezy and I’m Baby, boy (Haan)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, and I know Taraji like I'm baby boy (Haan)", "And I fuck with Weezy and I'm Baby, boy (Haan)"], "meaning": "Despite recent tension in the Cash Money camp, Drake re-affirms his allegiance to mentor Lil Wayne and label boss Birdman (Baby).", "annotation_id": "10108502", "url": "https://genius.com/10108502", "state": "accepted", "votes": 91, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "You don’t wanna hear Not Nice did thirteen And did another two for some other shit he didn’t do (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["You don't wanna hear Not Nice did thirteen", "And did another two for some other shit he didn't do (Woo)"], "meaning": "Baka, friend of Drake and member of OVO, goes by the name “Bakanotnice” on social media. In 2014, Baka spent 13 months in jail and was found guilty of human trafficking charges. By the time this song was released, Baka was back in jail for assaulting his ex-girlfriend.", "annotation_id": "10108492", "url": "https://genius.com/10108492", "state": "accepted", "votes": 89, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "You don’t really want the views You don’t want a snapshot of things goin’ on with the crew", "vault_lines": ["You don't really want the views", "You don't want a snapshot of things goin' on with the crew"], "meaning": "Budden felt as if Drake sounded “uninspired” on Views. Drake counters by saying Budden wouldn’t be happy if Drake unleashed the full force of his arsenal or his own viewpoint on Budden’s career.\n\nOVO, Drake’s crew, is also generating significant hype. PARTYNEXTDOOR, Majid Jordan, ​dvsn and Roy Woods have recently dropped successful and relevant projects.", "annotation_id": "10108489", "url": "https://genius.com/10108489", "state": "accepted", "votes": 75, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "Yeah, we the Army, better yet the Navy, boy (Haan)", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, we the Army, better yet the Navy, boy (Haan)"], "meaning": "Drake’s team is so big and determined to protect him that it’s like he has a personal army.\n\nThis is also a reference to B.G.’s line from “Cash Money Is an Army”:\n\nCash Money is a army nigga\nA Navy nigga\n\nSeveral other songs have interpolated B.G’s, including “Takeover” by Jay Z, Lil Wayne’s guest verse on Fabolous’s “Salute”, and even “G4L” by Drake’s rumored girlfriend Rihanna.", "annotation_id": "10108482", "url": "https://genius.com/10108482", "state": "accepted", "votes": 85, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "Sittin’ high, 6 God cover (Woo) Tell them hoes get low, 6 God comin’", "vault_lines": ["Sittin' high, 6 God cover (Woo)", "Tell them hoes get low, 6 God comin'"], "meaning": "French introduces us to the one who doesn’t need introducing: his guest Drake, the self-proclaimed 6 God.\n\n“Sittin' high” is a reference to the cover of Drake’s 2016 album VIEWS, which pictured him sitting on top of the CN Tower in Toronto. “Little Drake” quickly became a popular meme.", "annotation_id": "10108474", "url": "https://genius.com/10108474", "state": "accepted", "votes": 53, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "Pump, pump, pump it up (Skrrt) She got a good head on her, but I pump it up (Skrrt) I’m not a one hit wonder, they know all my stuff (Haan) You let me turn into the nigga that you almost was", "vault_lines": ["Pump, pump, pump it up (Skrrt)", "She got a good head on her, but I pump it up (Skrrt)", "I'm not a one hit wonder, they know all my stuff (Haan)", "You let me turn into the nigga that you almost was"], "meaning": "Drake interpolates Joe Budden’s 2003 hit “Pump It Up” to reference oral sex; he received a lot of attention after dissing him saying he should’ve let Joe perform this song at a Dallas concert.\n\nAfter hearing an early snippet of the line, Budden believed he was going to be dissed by Drake and preemptively recorded his dual diss tracks “Making a Murderer Pt. 1” and “Wake.”  Contrary to popular belief, the songs were responses to this track, not the other way around.\n\nBudden was the next “beast from the east” in the early 2000s, but his commercial career stagnated after “Pump It Up”. He wouldn’t make the US Billboard 100 again until 2012’s “She Don’t Put It Down,” which reached number 96. Conversely, Drake regularly features on the Billboard Charts. He’s comfortably eclipsed Joe’s potential.", "annotation_id": "10108467", "url": "https://genius.com/10108467", "state": "accepted", "votes": 209, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Shopping", "line": "I done seen a lot of shit and I done been in things (Haan) And I never started nothin’, I just finish things", "vault_lines": ["I done seen a lot of shit and I done been in things (Haan)", "And I never started nothin', I just finish things"], "meaning": "Drake claims he’s never started beef and isn’t a confrontational person. In an MTV interview about his dispute with Chris Brown, he said.\n\nI’m not confrontational, but if someone challenges, I’m not going to back down.\n\nFor the most part, Drake’s “beefs” have been initiated by other people, with the exception of Jay Z.  Common first dissed him on 2012’s “Sweet,” Kendrick used his name on “Control,” and Meek Mill launched an unprovoked attack via ghostwriting claims.\n\nThe only beef Drake’s really “finished” is that with Meek Mill, after his two diss tracks “Charged Up” and “Back to Back” won him the majority of fan support.", "annotation_id": "10108462", "url": "https://genius.com/10108462", "state": "accepted", "votes": 109, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Buffalo Freestyle", "status": "done", "targets": 12, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Benny-the-butcher-buffalo-freestyle-lyrics", "genius_title": "Buffalo Freestyle", "genius_id": 7131443, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Buffalo Freestyle", "line": "Psychic readin’s, corporate meetin’s, power lunches Private fundin’, hundred push-ups, hundred crunches Final touches, lemon squeezes, island breezes Press releases, movin’ speeches, multi-taskin’ Torches passin’, strong attractions, forceful actions What’s really crackin’? I guess I’m maintainin’, thanks for askin’", "vault_lines": ["Psychic readin's, corporate meetin's, power lunches", "Private fundin', hundred push-ups, hundred crunches", "Final touches, lemon squeezes, island breezes", "Press releases, movin' speeches, multi-taskin'", "Torches passin', strong attractions, forceful actions", "I guess I'm maintainin', thanks for askin'"], "meaning": "", "annotation_id": "34508606", "url": "https://genius.com/34508606", "state": "pending", "votes": -2, "second_sense": false, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Buffalo Freestyle", "line": "I keep my circle small so the blunt gets back quicker", "vault_lines": ["I keep my circle small so the blunt gets back quicker"], "meaning": "This has two meanings. First, if you keep your circle small while passing around the blunt while smoking Marijuana, you get your blunt back quicker than if you had more people passing it around. Second, with a small friend circle, people are more honest about telling Drake the blunt truth about him rather than giving him platitudes. So, he is surrounded by few dear friends instead of many yes men.", "annotation_id": "33550623", "url": "https://genius.com/33550623", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Buffalo Freestyle", "line": "Every day its like the new me, the business man, versus me as the criminal", "vault_lines": ["Every day its like the new me, the business man, versus me as the criminal"], "meaning": "As most hip-hop artists come from different backgrounds, especially gang lifestyle people and media usually bring up their past when they get successful.", "annotation_id": "32758597", "url": "https://genius.com/32758597", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Buffalo Freestyle", "line": "All that jealousy obvious, I got hipped to it Even your compliments startin’ to sound like bitterness All the pressure I’m livin’ with", "vault_lines": ["All that jealousy obvious, I got hipped to it", "Even your compliments startin' to sound like bitterness", "All the pressure I'm livin' with"], "meaning": "Success Breeds Resentment Benny the Butcher is lowkey underground but certainly he is heading to the top in he traverse through this rap game", "annotation_id": "32758587", "url": "https://genius.com/32758587", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Buffalo Freestyle", "line": "Every line delivered with hunger, my flow a sure thing like a death certificate", "vault_lines": ["Every line delivered with hunger, my flow a sure thing like a death certificate"], "meaning": "Johnny P’s Caddy by Benny the Butcher & J. Cole just to name a few Benny keeps delivering bars on bars 🔥🔥🔥like we on a jail cell", "annotation_id": "32758577", "url": "https://genius.com/32758577", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Buffalo Freestyle", "line": "True colors always come out like the Sun does ‘Specially when you assumin’ the role of that nigga", "vault_lines": ["True colors always comе out like the Sun does", "'Specially when you assumin' the role of that nigga"], "meaning": "Success Breeds Resentment Simply put, success often brings scrutiny and envy. Drake’s dominance in the music industry can lead to backlash from those who feel that his success overshadows other artists.", "annotation_id": "32758560", "url": "https://genius.com/32758560", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Buffalo Freestyle", "line": "You don’t have to see the score to know that I won some", "vault_lines": ["You don't have to see thе score to know that I won some"], "meaning": "He implies confidence and self-assurance.\n\nAs his achievements speak for themselves, and others can recognize your wins even without needing validation or proof.\n\nSuccess is evident through actions, presence, or reputation.", "annotation_id": "32758517", "url": "https://genius.com/32758517", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Buffalo Freestyle", "line": "I’m iller than the illness that these people wish me", "vault_lines": ["I'm iller than the illness that these people wish me"], "meaning": "Being the top rank musician Drake is today, in the most notorious beef in the 21st century any industry has seen for Kendrick Vs Drake; Despite the havoc drake stands in his analogy stating his ‘iller’ stronger, unstressed about who makes him ill as his iller than the illness people wish on him!", "annotation_id": "32756094", "url": "https://genius.com/32756094", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Buffalo Freestyle", "line": "Feel like Tune", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Lil Wayne is notoriously known to smoke during his recording sessions and while listening to his music a lighter flick can be heard before he starts rapping. Drake shouts out Wayne while you can hear him smoke during his intro.", "annotation_id": "32747225", "url": "https://genius.com/32747225", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Buffalo Freestyle", "line": "My resume is thicker than Nicki, I’m busy-busy", "vault_lines": ["My resume is thicker than Nicki, I'm busy-busy"], "meaning": "Drake is nodding to Nicki Minaj’s famous… um, “assets,” while doubling down on the idea that his accomplishments are massive.\n\n\nDrake is one of the most prolific artists of our time, recently releasing 100GB of unseen material on the 6th of August 2024.", "annotation_id": "32746540", "url": "https://genius.com/32746540", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Buffalo Freestyle", "line": "Wasn’t drivin’ Cadillac then, but shit still found a way to escalate quickly", "vault_lines": ["Wasn't drivin' Cadillac then, but shit still found a way to escalate quickly"], "meaning": "A simple play of words here. Drake says that although he hadn’t reached the level of fame and wealth he is at now, things still found its way to escalate (escalade).\nCadillac is a division of the American automobile manufacturer General Motors that designs and builds luxury vehicles. The Cadillac Escalade is a full-size luxury SUV are known for being one of the most reliable SUVs on the market.", "annotation_id": "32738783", "url": "https://genius.com/32738783", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Buffalo Freestyle", "line": "Drake be joshin’ around, but life wasn’t Nickelodeon or Disney, is you kiddin’ me?", "vault_lines": ["Drake be joshin' around, but life wasn't Nickelodeon or Disney, is you kiddin' me?"], "meaning": "“Joshing” is a term used to describe joking, or acting in a playful way. Drake uses this line to refer to his public persona and reputation for humor. We’ve seen examples of this multiple times, from the hyper self aware Editor’s Note from his album Scorpion, or the “Laugh Now, Cry Later” music video scene where he pokes fun at his own sensitive personality.\n\nIronically, during his years as a child actor, Drake appeared as a character named Jimmy Brooks for the Canadian teen television show Degrassi: The Next Generation.\n\n\n\nThe show originally premiered on CTV Television Network in Canada during 2001, but ended up airing on Nickelodeon’s sister channel TeenNick during the ninth season.\n\nDrake uses the wordplay of his name, “joshin'”, and Nickelodeon to reference the hit teen comedy Drake and Josh which also aired on Nickelodeon. The life portrayed by the characters in that show were very different from the rougher upbringing he experienced in his childhood.", "annotation_id": "24029284", "url": "https://genius.com/24029284", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
