{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Number 15", "line": "I get down like Curtis Snow Dare you to call my bluff", "vault_lines": ["I get down like Curtis Snow", "Dare you to call my bluff"], "meaning": "A joke here about the film Snow on tha Bluff.  The protagonist of the film, which blends real life and drama, is Curtis Snow", "annotation_id": "1439625", "url": "https://genius.com/1439625", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Number 15", "line": "Chain smoking in the city where they smoke you for chains", "vault_lines": ["Chain smoking in the city where they smoke you for chains"], "meaning": "This literary device is called epanodos – where words are repeated in reversed order.  See a great example from Run-DMC here", "annotation_id": "1439610", "url": "https://genius.com/1439610", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Number 15", "line": "Beefing with the BM Beefing with the boss, got fired by the GM", "vault_lines": ["beefing with the BM", "Beefing with the boss, got fired by the GM"], "meaning": "The “BM” and “GM” here stand for “baby momma” and “general manager” respectively.  This rhyme is reminiscent of Jaz' classic line on Jay-Z’s “Nigga What Nigga Who”:\n\n Fucking BM’s on the road\nWhen you had to be in bed at the PM", "annotation_id": "1439584", "url": "https://genius.com/1439584", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Number 15", "line": "From AM to PM,", "vault_lines": ["From AM to PM,"], "meaning": "Nickelus F is on a song called AM 2 PM off Drake’s debut mixtape Room For Improvement\n\nSome say Nickelus F is the Rhymefest to Drake’s Kanye.\n(Meaning on the come up Drake rapped with Nickelus F who has 3 features on drakes first mixtape) The same way Kanye used to work closely with Chicago artist Rhymefest.", "annotation_id": "1433024", "url": "https://genius.com/1433024", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Number 15", "line": "I wake up every mornin’ shower, gather my belongings", "vault_lines": ["I wake up every mornin' shower, gather my belongings"], "meaning": "Nickelus F quotes a line from his other song with Drake called AM 2 PM\n\nYo I wake up every morning, shower, gather my belongings", "annotation_id": "1433008", "url": "https://genius.com/1433008", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Number 15", "line": "Bradley Cooper, a future is limitless", "vault_lines": ["Bradley Cooper, a future is limitless"], "meaning": "Bradley Cooper stars in a film called Limitless where he takes a small pill and it opens up a whole new world for him where his opportunities and abilities are limitless\n\nSimilarly, Nickelus' future has no limits", "annotation_id": "1432938", "url": "https://genius.com/1432938", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Round of Applause", "status": "done", "targets": 7, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Waka-flocka-flame-round-of-applause-lyrics", "genius_title": "Round of Applause", "genius_id": 57289, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Round of Applause", "line": "[Verse 3: Waka Flocka Flame]", "vault_lines": ["Waka Flocka Flame, better known as Mr. Let It Go"], "meaning": "Lowkey sounds like Gucci Mane in this verse", "annotation_id": "40942139", "url": "https://genius.com/40942139", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Round of Applause", "line": "Make you rich, I feel like I should make commission on your ass", "vault_lines": ["Make you rich, I feel like I should make commission on your ass"], "meaning": "The individual who annotated the prior line clearly needs a lesson on United States history because they claim that the $50 bill does not have the face of a president on it. That face would be of Ulysses S Grant, however who served as the 18th president of the United States. Only the $100 bill does not feature a president, something that you would know if they passed United States history in high school.", "annotation_id": "35598385", "url": "https://genius.com/35598385", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Round of Applause", "line": "Throwin’ every president except for Nixon on your ass", "vault_lines": ["Throwin' every president except for Nixon on your ass"], "meaning": "Nixon, not being on any US currency suggests that Drake is spending all possible denominations of currency on the lady in question (keep in mind the both the $10 and $100 bills do not feature presidents)\n\nThis may be a stretch but in Thomas Pynchon’s 2009 book Inherent Vice, a plot point involves a large number of counterfeit bills with Nixon on them. With this added information it could also be implied that drake is throwing “real money”. It is unclear if Drake is a Pynchon fan or read the novel.  This would have to be a reference to the novel- not the later film adaptation, as this song was released 2 years prior to Inherent Vice’s theatrical release.", "annotation_id": "30490126", "url": "https://genius.com/30490126", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Round of Applause", "line": "Uh, bust it like you can’t afford a car", "vault_lines": ["Bust it, bust it, bust it, bust it, b-bust it, bust it", "Uh, bust it like you can't afford a car", "Bust it, bust it, bust it, bust it, bust it, bust it"], "meaning": "This is a homophone “Bust it” meaning shaking her ass, sounds like “bus it”, meaning to take a bus for transportation, which is what someone would do if they couldn’t afford a car.", "annotation_id": "21726168", "url": "https://genius.com/21726168", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Round of Applause", "line": "Bounce that ass, shake that ass like the Twerk Team (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["Bounce that ass, shake that ass like the Twerk Team (Woo)"], "meaning": "The Twerk Team are, according to their MySpace page, “[A] dance crew based out of Georgia and are basically on a grind to make twerking an official movement!!”\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hwNnVJ05apY", "annotation_id": "675488", "url": "https://genius.com/675488", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Round of Applause", "line": "I’m up in Stadium in D.C., still tippin’, man", "vault_lines": ["I'm up in Stadium in D.C., still tippin', man"], "meaning": "True indeed – Drake, Lil Wayne, Birdman, and Wale partied at DC’s Stadium (strip) Club in spring 2011.  See video here and here", "annotation_id": "675483", "url": "https://genius.com/675483", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Round of Applause", "line": "Pimpin’ like I’m Dolemite, hoes jump in my Caddy (Baow)", "vault_lines": ["Pimpin' like I'm Dolemite, hoes jump in my Caddy (Baow)"], "meaning": "Dolemite is a pimp from the classic blaxploitation movie of the same name.\n\n\n\nAnd what do pimps drive? Vintage Cadillacs.", "annotation_id": "405474", "url": "https://genius.com/405474", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
