{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Organization", "line": "If it’s a problem, I’m droppin’ location Or I send Kayla, she’s very persuasive", "vault_lines": ["If it's a problem, I'm droppin' location", "Or I send Kayla, she's very persuasive"], "meaning": "", "annotation_id": "41577991", "url": "https://genius.com/41577991", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": false, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Organization", "line": "GME, B.O.B., joint operations", "vault_lines": ["GME, B.O.B., joint operations"], "meaning": "Drake shouts out the record labels of Booggz (signed to Get Money Entertainment) and Smiley_61st (signed to Buy Or Bye Music Group).\n\nJoint operations are a strategy of warfare that uses multiple army’s combined arms under a unified command to accomplish a mission.", "annotation_id": "21719402", "url": "https://genius.com/21719402", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Organization", "line": "Walls are so tall, I don’t know who my neighbor is", "vault_lines": ["Walls are so tall, I don’t know who my neighbor is"], "meaning": "In September 2019, Drake was given permission by the city of Toronto to construct specialized walls around his $6.7 million mansion, as well as consent to grow 20 foot tall cedar trees to further preserve his privacy. The wall heights reach a maximum height of 4.4 meters, which is over twice the legal size of 2 meters.", "annotation_id": "18733231", "url": "https://genius.com/18733231", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Organization", "line": "Say she been fuckin’ with me since the Hazelton", "vault_lines": ["Say she been fuckin' with me since the Hazelton"], "meaning": "Drake references The Hazelton Hotel which is located at 118 Yorkville Ave. in Toronto, Canada. In 2017, Drake sold his Toronto luxury condo residence located at 1 St. Thomas St. for $3.75 million. Drake then took up residency at The Hazelton Hotel while his new Toronto home was being constructed. An inside look of the new home can be seen here.", "annotation_id": "18655065", "url": "https://genius.com/18655065", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Organization", "line": "Baka, my crodie, his songs are amazing But I knew that nigga when he wasn’t makin’ ’em", "vault_lines": ["Baka, my crodie, his songs are amazing", "But I knew that nigga when he wasn't makin' 'em"], "meaning": "Drake shouts out his close friend and OVO affiliate Baka Not Nice, who is also from Canada. He reached mainstream fame in March 2017 with the hit track, “Live Up to My Name.”\n\nDrizzy alludes to Baka’s origins as his personal bodyguard and also his 13-year stint in jail. While Baka’s now in the public scope and a successful rapper, he started out as Drake’s bodyguard and would defend him in any way necessary. Baka previously discussed his willingness to defend Drizzy on “Live Up To My Name”:\n\nGyah, gyah! Diss The Boy? Are you insane?\nI drink Henny when I shoot my pistol at the range\nThat way, when I’m tipsy, I still know I got my aim\nA.K.A. it’s Not Nice and it’s not a fuckin' game", "annotation_id": "18652602", "url": "https://genius.com/18652602", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made", "status": "done", "targets": 15, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Big-sean-made-lyrics", "genius_title": "Made", "genius_id": 1792, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made", "line": "You can play your heart out everyone don’t get a ring though", "vault_lines": ["You can play your heart out everyone don’t get a ring though"], "meaning": "Made an account just to emphasize the craziness of this bar. But simply. No matter how hard you try.. and try… and try. there’s always a chance your not reaching this goal you wish to achieve.", "annotation_id": "37717714", "url": "https://genius.com/37717714", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made", "line": "Used to ride escorts now I get escorted (do it)", "vault_lines": ["Used to ride escorts now I get escorted (do it)"], "meaning": "He went from riding in Ford Escorts (a modest car) to being chauffeured in luxury. It can also play on “escorts” meaning sex workers, flipping it to now having women accompany him.", "annotation_id": "36566661", "url": "https://genius.com/36566661", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made", "line": "I want the baddest chick to treat my stick like a thermometer", "vault_lines": ["I want the baddest chick to treat my stick like a thermometer"], "meaning": "Another metaphor for oral sex", "annotation_id": "24795749", "url": "https://genius.com/24795749", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made", "line": "I’m the head of my estate ain’t that ironic huh", "vault_lines": ["I’m the head of my estate ain't that ironic huh"], "meaning": "This is another play on the previous line where he continues with more political humor.  “Head of my estate” is another double play on words. Its “ironic” because “Head” is a term meaning oral sex, referencing Bill Clinton’s scandal while in office back in 1998", "annotation_id": "24795742", "url": "https://genius.com/24795742", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made", "line": "Call me Ron Burgundy y’all the other anchormen", "vault_lines": ["Call me Ron Burgundy y'all the other anchormen"], "meaning": "Ron Burgundy is the protagonist of the Anchorman movie series and is a fictional news anchor from San Diego, California. In the series, he was the top rated anchorman in his district and drew envy from his peers for his unprecedented success.\n\nDrake and Kanye both appeared in 2014’s Anchorman 2: The Legend Continues. Drake had a quick cameo at the beginning, while Kanye appeared in the star-studded fight scene at the end.", "annotation_id": "18189228", "url": "https://genius.com/18189228", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made", "line": "I sit tall, I swang low", "vault_lines": ["ho, I sit tall, I swang low"], "meaning": "Drake sits up with confidence.\n\nHere, Drake references the culture of “swangin'”, which is to ride slowly in a car, particularly Chevys and Cadillacs. It is mainly popular in the South and started out in Houston. It was made popular by Trae’s song Swang.\n\n\n\nDrake’s been swangin'.", "annotation_id": "2436883", "url": "https://genius.com/2436883", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made", "line": "I’m tryna move my momma from the ghettos to the meadows Well she can’t stay in that fucking hood forever, forever", "vault_lines": ["I’m tryna move my momma from the ghettos to the meadows", "Well she can’t stay in that fucking hood forever, forever"], "meaning": "Big Sean was tryna get enough money so his mother can finally move out the hood into a nicer, more comfortable place.\n\nLast part “forever, forever” is play on his mentor Kanye West’s hook from “Diamonds From Sierra Leone”.\nWhich again stains from André 3000’s verse on “Ms. Jackson”.", "annotation_id": "1076396", "url": "https://genius.com/1076396", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made", "line": "I be at the parties where you stuck outside and can’t come in", "vault_lines": ["I be at the parties where you stuck outside and can’t come in"], "meaning": "Drake gets in the party’s that you’re not “cool” enough to get into.\n\nBut apparently even Drake isn’t cool enough to get into the Miami Heat locker room:", "annotation_id": "1076386", "url": "https://genius.com/1076386", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made", "line": "Underground king", "vault_lines": ["I’m a underground king"], "meaning": "Underground often refers to the world of Underground unpublished music usually in the form of mixtapes.  Here, Drake says that he is the King of mixtapes, and a King of the Rap underground.\n\nHe’s also referring to UGK, who he has cited as an influence on his music. Even made a song about them. Also Drake started his career in Houston, which is where he met Lil Wayne and recorded most of So Far Gone. And also where he performed with Bun B at one his first live performances after releasing So Far Gone. It was huge.", "annotation_id": "166105", "url": "https://genius.com/166105", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made", "line": "Threw on my track team handed my baton to her Passed her blew her off, I chronic Veronica", "vault_lines": ["Threw on my track team handed my baton to her", "Passed her blew her off, I chronic Veronica"], "meaning": "In the relays, there are batons that you pass to your teammates. He handed his dick (baton) to Veronica then he passed and blew her off (probably to a 3rd-tier dude in his entourage).\n\nMaybe a stretch, but by mentioning “Vernonica,” Sean could be playing off of Drake’s Anchorman reference earlier in the song.\n\n\n\n“For the entire Channel 4 news team, I’m Veronica Corningstone.”\n“And I’m Ron Burgundy. Go fuck yourself, San Diego.”", "annotation_id": "53531", "url": "https://genius.com/53531", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made", "line": "Was made for that Mick Jagger shit", "vault_lines": ["Was made for that Mick Jagger shit"], "meaning": "Mike Jagger is the front man of the Rolling Stones. He’s trying to achieve a international rock star lifestyle.", "annotation_id": "52439", "url": "https://genius.com/52439", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made", "line": "Who got up on my nerves so I had to platonic her No that ain’t my girl but every leader needs a Monica", "vault_lines": ["Who got up on my nerves so I had to platonic her", "No that ain't my girl but every leader needs a Monica"], "meaning": "The girl was getting too annoying so he made her just friends.  But Chris Rock doesn’t believe this\n\nMonica Lewinsky is in so many rap songs because of what she did to the President.  That isn’t his girl but every leader needs a girl who he can smash and go back to his wife (Monica)", "annotation_id": "50671", "url": "https://genius.com/50671", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made", "line": "I’m just waiting on my cue dog no pledge", "vault_lines": ["I’m just waiting on my cue dog no pledge"], "meaning": "The Q Dogs (Omega Psi Phi) are a fraternity.  But Big Sean is not pledging, he is just waiting for his cue (turn)", "annotation_id": "50667", "url": "https://genius.com/50667", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made", "line": "Tell her bring some Ace of Spades no sparklers though", "vault_lines": ["Tell her bring some Ace of Spades no sparklers though"], "meaning": "Drake loves his Ace of Spades\n\n\n\nIn many night clubs it is standard procedure to have sparklers provided with VIP bottle service\n\nSince Drake has Ace of Spades all the time, he does not want to make it seem like this is a special occasion (or make a scene for the paparazzi)", "annotation_id": "50662", "url": "https://genius.com/50662", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Made", "line": "Low-key Peter Parker flow", "vault_lines": ["Low-key Peter Parker flow"], "meaning": "Peter Parker is low-key when he is in the streets but when crime starts, he becomes Spiderman\n\n\n\nDrake isn’t trying to pull any “super hero” moves here – just a subdued flow", "annotation_id": "50660", "url": "https://genius.com/50660", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
