{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Where Ya At", "status": "done", "targets": 24, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Future-where-ya-at-lyrics", "genius_title": "Where Ya At", "genius_id": 2213109, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "(Dog, Freeband—)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Future founded his record label Freebandz in December of 2012. His signed artists are collectively known as Freeband Gang.\n\n\n\nFreebandz logo", "annotation_id": "29587731", "url": "https://genius.com/29587731", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "Where your ass was at, dog, when I was serving pies?", "vault_lines": ["Where your ass was at, dog, when the bodies came sliding?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when I was serving pies?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when I was in the Pyrex?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when I was drinking Hi-Tech?", "Where your ass was at, dog? You came through the projects", "Where your ass was at when I was trapping in the store?", "Man, where your ass was at when we took the city over?", "Where your ass was at when all they'd ask was \"What's the hold up?\"", "Where your ass was at when niggas first got the news?", "Where your ass was at when we recorded in the bathroom?", "Where your ass was at? I take attendance like a classroom", "Where your ass was at, dog, when niggas wouldn't feed me?", "Man, where your ass was at, dog, when niggas wouldn't feed me?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when I was on my come-up? (At, come-up)", "Where your ass was at, dog, when bitches didn't need me?", "Where you ass was at when I was trapping in the store?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when niggas tried to run off?", "Where your ass was at, dog? You made me pull this gun out", "Where your ass was at, dog, you went and switched sides?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when niggas spread lies on him?"], "meaning": "A pie is a kilogram of cocaine. Future playfully conjures up an image of him selling pies at a diner, which could also indicate hard times, but he’s remembering his days dealing coke.", "annotation_id": "8030341", "url": "https://genius.com/8030341", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "Where your ass was at, dog, when I was in the Pyrex?", "vault_lines": ["Where your ass was at, dog, when the bodies came sliding?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when I was serving pies?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when I was in the Pyrex?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when I was drinking Hi-Tech?", "Where your ass was at, dog? You came through the projects", "Where your ass was at when I was trapping in the store?", "Man, where your ass was at when we took the city over?", "Where your ass was at when all they'd ask was \"What's the hold up?\"", "Where your ass was at when niggas first got the news?", "Where your ass was at when we recorded in the bathroom?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when niggas wouldn't feed me?", "Man, where your ass was at, dog, when niggas wouldn't feed me?", "Where your ass was at? Last winter was the coldest", "Where your ass was at, dog, when I was on my come-up? (At, come-up)", "Where your ass was at, dog, when bitches didn't need me?", "Where you ass was at when I was trapping in the store?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when niggas tried to run off?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when niggas spread lies on him?"], "meaning": "Future was in the Pyrex back when he had to cook up cocaine — the glassware is a trade favorite. Future’s come along way cooking crack on the stove.\n\nPyrex Vision was also a fashion brand for a short lived time from 2011-2013. Virgil Abloh has since been replaced the brand with Off-White – another label Future likes to rock.", "annotation_id": "8024486", "url": "https://genius.com/8024486", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "Had them bitches fall through fucking like a savage (Fall, savage)", "vault_lines": ["Had them bitches fall through fucking like a savage (Fall, savage)"], "meaning": "Future had some chicks come through for some rough sex. As in “Real Sisters,” Future’s always down for more than one girl at a time.", "annotation_id": "7398973", "url": "https://genius.com/7398973", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "Serve a lot of dog food, call you a mutt", "vault_lines": ["Serve a lot of dog food, call you a mutt"], "meaning": "“Dog” can be both a derogatory term, or one of endearment. “Dog food” is also slang for heroin. A “mutt” is a dog of mixed origin—if you don’t know what someone is is a whole lot harder to trust them. In this instance, you also can’t trust them because they’ll do any drug they can get their hands on, heroin or otherwise—a mutt’s a fiend.\n\nFuture has flipped the script on Drake’s earlier analogy.", "annotation_id": "7381321", "url": "https://genius.com/7381321", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "Heard that nigga came through squeezing on a ratchet (Slatt) Heard that nigga came through squeezing on a ratchet", "vault_lines": ["Heard that nigga came through squeezing on a ratchet (Slatt)"], "meaning": "Ratchet is a slightly outdated term for a gun, but the word has taken on new meanings—these days it usually means a pretty busted or kind of trashy girl.\n\nFuture isn’t dealing with your everyday kind of people, but he’s not afraid.", "annotation_id": "7381305", "url": "https://genius.com/7381305", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "12 tryin’ come in the spot to open up the dope Burglar bar doors got a young nigga confident Juugin’ out the stove and we still bangin’, honest Blowing on the O, yo, we call that ho an onion", "vault_lines": ["12 tryin' come in the spot to open up the dope", "Burglar bar doors got a young nigga confident", "Juugin' out the stove and we still bangin', honest", "Blowing on the O, yo, we call that ho an onion"], "meaning": "Future’s dope spot is open, populated by his “jumpers”, or squad members, who were also kind enough to lace him with strong marijuana. He and his squad are “juugin'” their wares, which means they’re still ruthless when they trap.\n\n\n\nDespite the illegality of his activities, Future was raised honest, juxtaposing just what “good” and “bad” means in the street, compared to suburban America.\n\n“O” and onion both describe an ounce of marijuana.", "annotation_id": "7381265", "url": "https://genius.com/7381265", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "Heard you tryna swim in the ocean no jacket (Swim, nigga, ha, ha)", "vault_lines": ["Heard you tryna swim in the ocean no jacket (Swim, nigga, ha, ha)"], "meaning": "Future is an adept Syrup drinker, a drug that has a multitude of side effects, all of which can be painful and confusing for the uninitiated.\n\nDon’t try and compete with this man when it comes to Promethazine. He’ll drink the ocean, you’ll drown in it.\n\nIt’s also a reference to unprotected sex.", "annotation_id": "7381192", "url": "https://genius.com/7381192", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "Where your ass at? We keep that fully loaded contracts", "vault_lines": ["Where your ass at? We keep that fully loaded contracts"], "meaning": "Contracts refer to two things in this case. Firstly, it is seen as weak in hip hop to lease, or rent vehicles rather than buying them outright. Future and his crew buy everything they own.\n\n\n\nSecondly, these fully loaded contracts are contract killers, or shooters. Future has real shooters on his team, so when these fake friends come around after he’s blown up looking for a hand out, he has individuals willing to take them out for him.", "annotation_id": "7381142", "url": "https://genius.com/7381142", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "60 for a walk through, bitch don’t panic (Woo, walk, Fu—)", "vault_lines": ["60 for a walk through, bitch don't panic (Woo, walk, Fu—)"], "meaning": "Future’s bragging that he gets $60,000 just to show up at a club & “walk through.” On The Breakfast Club Future mentioned he had no baby mama drama, thanks to his wealth, but he tried to play down just how much money he makes for an appearance. Back in 2013, Future was earning around $40k for a nightclub appearance. His post-Ciara fame and the success of Honest has allowed him to bump that fee up a bit.", "annotation_id": "7381115", "url": "https://genius.com/7381115", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "Man, where your ass was at, dog, when niggas wouldn’t feed me? Where your ass was at, dog, when bitches didn’t need me? Where your ass was at? Last winter was the coldest", "vault_lines": ["Where your ass was at, dog, when the bodies came sliding?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when I was serving pies?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when I was in the Pyrex?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when I was drinking Hi-Tech?", "Where your ass was at, dog? You came through the projects", "Where your ass was at when I was trapping in the store?", "Man, where your ass was at when we took the city over?", "Where your ass was at when niggas first got the news?", "Where your ass was at when we recorded in the bathroom?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when niggas wouldn't feed me?", "Man, where your ass was at, dog, when niggas wouldn't feed me?", "Where your ass was at? Last winter was the coldest", "Where your ass was at, dog, when bitches didn't need me?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when niggas tried to run off?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when niggas spread lies on him?"], "meaning": "Winter in Toronto is cold, and the winter of 2014 was Canada’s coldest ever. Drake imagines a dog stuck outside in the snow, uncared for and unloved, and questions the actions of those around him—he was a lonely mutt with no friends pre-fame, but these days he’s man’s best friend.", "annotation_id": "7381102", "url": "https://genius.com/7381102", "state": "accepted", "votes": 52, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "Lawyers and the commissary ain’t gon’ pay itself", "vault_lines": ["Lawyers and the commissary ain't gon' pay itself"], "meaning": "Drake takes care of his friends when they’re in trouble. Many of Drake’s friends have found themselves on the wrong side of the law, and when that happens, he’s the one paying for lawyers and the prison commissary.", "annotation_id": "7381071", "url": "https://genius.com/7381071", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "Where your ass was at when niggas first got the news?", "vault_lines": ["Where your ass was at, dog, when the bodies came sliding?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when I was serving pies?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when I was in the Pyrex?", "Where your ass was at when I was trapping in the store?", "Man, where your ass was at when we took the city over?", "Where your ass was at when all they'd ask was \"What's the hold up?\"", "Where your ass was at when niggas first got the news?", "Where your ass was at when we recorded in the bathroom?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when niggas wouldn't feed me?", "Man, where your ass was at, dog, when niggas wouldn't feed me?", "Where your ass was at? Last winter was the coldest", "Where your ass was at, dog, when niggas tried to run off?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when niggas spread lies on him?"], "meaning": "There were some who knew what was up as soon as Drake started dropping mixtapes like Room For Improvement and Comeback Season, but whoever Drake’s talking to wasn’t one of them. Maybe he learned when Lil Wayne joined the cause, but maybe not even then.", "annotation_id": "7378748", "url": "https://genius.com/7378748", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "Running through the pussy like a nigga going jogging", "vault_lines": ["Running through the pussy like a nigga going jogging"], "meaning": "Men burn an average of 100 calories during sex, but running was found to burn twice as many calories per minute. Either way, Future’s getting his exercise in.", "annotation_id": "7345845", "url": "https://genius.com/7345845", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "[Verse 3: Drake]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "On the Breakfast Club, Future explained that he wasn’t planning to have any features on DS2, but Drake asked if he could be on it the night before Future turned the album in. You don’t say no to Drake.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=INc5ks7bF9s", "annotation_id": "7344937", "url": "https://genius.com/7344937", "state": "accepted", "votes": 83, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "Where your ass was at? I take attendance like a classroom Man I ain’t got no choice ’Cause nowadays I swear this shit done changed up for the boy", "vault_lines": ["Where your ass was at, dog, when I was serving pies?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when I was in the Pyrex?", "Where your ass was at when I was trapping in the store?", "Where your ass was at when niggas first got the news?", "Where your ass was at? I take attendance like a classroom", "Man I ain't got no choice", "'Cause nowadays I swear this shit done changed up for the boy", "Where your ass was at? Last winter was the coldest"], "meaning": "Just as a teacher takes attendance to see who showed up to the class, Drake is taking notice to who was there and who wasn’t when he was working to the top. He’s probably not to happy to see all the new faces.\n\n\n\nDrake also had “no choice” on “Tony Montana,” an earlier collaboration with Future.", "annotation_id": "7344935", "url": "https://genius.com/7344935", "state": "accepted", "votes": 56, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "Where your ass was at when I was trapping in the store? Had to struggle to get where I’m at and sell dope", "vault_lines": ["Where your ass was at, dog, when the bodies came sliding?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when I was serving pies?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when I was in the Pyrex?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when I was drinking Hi-Tech?", "Where your ass was at when I was trapping in the store?", "Had to struggle to get where I'm at and sell dope", "Where your ass was at when niggas first got the news?", "Where your ass was at when we recorded in the bathroom?", "Where your ass was at? Last winter was the coldest", "Where you ass was at when I was trapping in the store?"], "meaning": "Future had to cook crack cocaine and sell dope to get to where he is. He’s not the only rapper to take this path, giving their career a kick-start with their drug money.\n\nIt continues a trend in modern music where an artist calls out “new” friends, who weren’t around when they were involved in the struggle, but all of a sudden come up with their hands out.", "annotation_id": "7344788", "url": "https://genius.com/7344788", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "Fuck where you was at, I had the 6 on my shoulders", "vault_lines": ["Fuck where you was at, I had the 6 on my shoulders"], "meaning": "Drake has discovered or given a crucial co-sign to many Toronto artists in the last few years. To name a notable few: The Weeknd, PARTYNEXTDOOR, and Majid Jordan.\n\nThe area code of Toronto is 416, the “6”. Drake told The Fader, “Toronto is the reason I do this.”\n\nHis tattoo of the 6 isn’t quite on his shoulder, but it’s close.", "annotation_id": "7344545", "url": "https://genius.com/7344545", "state": "accepted", "votes": 74, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "Put a pic with me on the ’gram, now you popping", "vault_lines": ["Put a pic with me on the 'gram, now you popping"], "meaning": "As Future’s songs rule the airwaves and his popularity rises, a simple picture with him on Instagram could boost your whole career. But such a favor isn’t intended for fake friends. This concept is even a skit on Future’s 56 Nights mixtape. A ‘fan’ wanting a picture with Future’s DJ, Esco, eventually gets punished by some mafia-like characters for flexing.\n\nDrake said something similar on the “Sh!t (Remix)”:\n\nAnd if a nigga say my name, he the hot shit\nBut if I say the nigga name, he still the hot shit", "annotation_id": "7344519", "url": "https://genius.com/7344519", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "Gas rolling up in the blunt, Amoco", "vault_lines": ["Gas rolling up in the blunt, Amoco"], "meaning": "The Amoco Corporation, originally Standard Oil, was a global chain of gas and petrol stations that merged with BP in 1998. But the gas Future refers to is weed, which we know Nayvadius likes to smoke.", "annotation_id": "7344485", "url": "https://genius.com/7344485", "state": "accepted", "votes": 29, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "Blowing on the O, yo, we call that ho an onion", "vault_lines": ["Blowing on the O, yo, we call that ho an onion"], "meaning": "Blowing smoke rings is pretty cool.\n\n\n\nHowever to blow weed by the “O” could also mean to smoke it by the ounce which can also be interpreted as a full onion.", "annotation_id": "7344425", "url": "https://genius.com/7344425", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "I’ll buy the neighbor’s house if they complain about the noise", "vault_lines": ["I'll buy the neighbor's house if they complain about the noise"], "meaning": "Drake is boasting that he is so rich and has so much power that if anyone has a problem with him he can easily take care of it.\n\nDrake can work from his home studio. He also has a gigantic pool perfect for hosting parties.\n\nAt Drake’s YOLO Estate in Hidden Hills, his neighbors include Kardashians. They’d be wise not to complain or he’ll buy their spot.\n\n\n\n\n\nIn September 2016 Drake actually bought his neighbor’s house in Beverly Hills and is now using it as a guest house.", "annotation_id": "7344338", "url": "https://genius.com/7344338", "state": "accepted", "votes": 112, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "Where your ass was at, dog, when niggas wouldn’t feed me? Where your ass was at, dog, when bitches didn’t need me? Where your ass was at, dog, when niggas tried to run off? Where your ass was at, dog? You made me pull this gun out", "vault_lines": ["Where your ass was at, dog, when the bodies came sliding?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when I was serving pies?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when I was in the Pyrex?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when I was drinking Hi-Tech?", "Where your ass was at, dog? You came through the projects", "Where your ass was at when niggas first got the news?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when niggas wouldn't feed me?", "Man, where your ass was at, dog, when niggas wouldn't feed me?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when bitches didn't need me?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when niggas tried to run off?", "Where your ass was at, dog? You made me pull this gun out", "Where your ass was at, dog, you went and switched sides?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when niggas spread lies on him?"], "meaning": "This song has the no new friends theme running through it. Future is addressing all of these new people around him, asking them where were they when he needed them the most, when he wasn’t as famous as he is now, when he didn’t have enough money to support himself and used to pick gang fights where bodies would come sliding. Instead of being there for him, his so called friends switched sides and ran off.\n\nFuture doesn’t need such fakes in his life—he’s down with his true friends.", "annotation_id": "7344335", "url": "https://genius.com/7344335", "state": "accepted", "votes": 127, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Where Ya At", "line": "Where your ass was at, dog, when I was drinking Hi-Tech?", "vault_lines": ["Where your ass was at, dog, when the bodies came sliding?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when I was serving pies?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when I was in the Pyrex?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when I was drinking Hi-Tech?", "Where your ass was at when I was trapping in the store?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when niggas wouldn't feed me?", "Man, where your ass was at, dog, when niggas wouldn't feed me?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when I was on my come-up? (At, come-up)", "Where your ass was at, dog, when bitches didn't need me?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when niggas tried to run off?", "Where your ass was at, dog, when niggas spread lies on him?"], "meaning": "Hi-Tech pharmaceuticals produces cough syrup with Promethazine and Codeine similar to Actavis. Like so many other “lean sippers” Future prefers Actavis over Hi-Tech. Actavis was pulled from stores for a bit, but Hi-Tech was still distributing the syrup. Hi-Tech’s also the cheaper brand—you’re only drinking it if you can’t afford or can’t access the good stuff—it’s tough times.", "annotation_id": "7344315", "url": "https://genius.com/7344315", "state": "accepted", "votes": 60, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "TWIST & TURN", "status": "done", "targets": 5, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Popcaan-twist-and-turn-lyrics", "genius_title": "TWIST & TURN", "genius_id": 5735255, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "TWIST & TURN", "line": "Before dat, we a chill with Noel and 40 at Jordan party", "vault_lines": ["Before dat, we a chill with Noel and 40 at Jordan party"], "meaning": "Noel Cadastre and Noah 40 Shebib are Drake’s exclusive engineers.\n\nNoel\n\n\n\nNoah", "annotation_id": "20547946", "url": "https://genius.com/20547946", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "TWIST & TURN", "line": "I know you know, seh you wan’ bruk it off, don’t?", "vault_lines": ["I know you know, seh you wan' bruk it off, don't?"], "meaning": "‘Bruk it’ is a Jamaican slang term for when a girl rides a man during sexual intercourse until he ejaculates insides her.\n\n‘Bruk’ is also a Jamaican slang term for ‘cumming’ or ejaculation.\n\n‘Bruk It’ has been popularized in Dancehall culture by songs such as Konshens' Bruk off yuh back https://youtu.be/QOpzGw4K9AA and Mr Vegas' Bruk it dung https://youtu.be/v5EBrftUKBY", "annotation_id": "20547855", "url": "https://genius.com/20547855", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "TWIST & TURN", "line": "Baby, ’cause mi eye too fry, I get burned, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Baby, 'cause mi eye too fry, I get burned, yeah"], "meaning": "This line could be interpreted one of two ways or even both but it all comes down to the meaning of ‘fry eye’ a Jamaican slang term for when a person is so high from smoking weed that their eyes have turned red or ‘fried’.\n\n\n\nDrake could be saying that whenever the girl ‘twists and turns’ she ‘fries his eyes’ or hypnotizes him or he could be saying that he especially loves when she ‘twists and turns’ whenever his ‘eyes are fried’ or whenever he is high.", "annotation_id": "20547815", "url": "https://genius.com/20547815", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "TWIST & TURN", "line": "Squid tell me gwan fix tings", "vault_lines": ["Squid tell me gwan fix tings"], "meaning": "Squid more popularly known as unruly squid is the nickname for Annalecia Sutherland who is the sister of Andre Sutherland better known as Popcaan.\n\n\n\nDrake sings that Squid told him to fix tings which is a Jamaican slang term which means to get one’s self together and to have the right mindset towards life.\n\nThe name of the project is also called Fixtape, which is a play on the word mixtape, but is intended to be seen as more than just a mixtape, more so a body of work one can draw inspiration from to ‘Fix Tings’ or operate the way one should.", "annotation_id": "20547804", "url": "https://genius.com/20547804", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "TWIST & TURN", "line": "Listen, you’ve been missing since 2016", "vault_lines": ["Listen, you've been missing since 2016"], "meaning": "Drake is referring to his complicated relationship with Rihanna in this verse. Rihanna’s last album, ANTI, was released in 2016.", "annotation_id": "20527240", "url": "https://genius.com/20527240", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
