{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "GLORIOUS", "line": "Oh, my God, look at that bumper", "vault_lines": ["Oh, my God, look at that bumper"], "meaning": "The line “…oh my God, look at that bumpa” is from “Keisha and Becky” is a line from Russ Millions and Tion Wayne’s 2019 song of the same name. https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTb0mHRQDaB1WrfSVZG74CA6IcKh8Y6LbE53iza7fPNfBY6-8MAeiVkyvar&s=10 Drake has been pushing UK hip hop for some time since the ever popular One Dance, and has since linked with the likes of Dave, Headie One, and Central Cee.", "annotation_id": "35114961", "url": "https://genius.com/35114961", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "GLORIOUS", "line": "Ayy, but if I bust her back, she gon’ need MB to adjust her back", "vault_lines": ["Ayy, but if I bust her back, she gon' need MB to adjust her back"], "meaning": "MB is referring to Drake’s personal Registered Massage Therapist whose name is Mbaye Kujabi.\n\nMbaye, is an African-Canadian who lives in Montreal Quebec, and Miami. His Instagram is @mbayepulse and you will be able to see he works with Drake, OVO, and numerous Actors’ Entertainers, and Professional Athletes across the globe.", "annotation_id": "34564205", "url": "https://genius.com/34564205", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "GLORIOUS", "line": "What’s hush always say? There’s so many ways to get paid", "vault_lines": ["What's hush always say? There's so many ways to get paid"], "meaning": "This is another reference to Bronx rapper Ice Spice and her 2023 track “In Ha Mood,” on which she raps:\n\nLike a million views in a day (Like)\nIt’s so many ways to get paid (Grrah)\n\nNotably, Drake says this is something his long-time friend and business associate OVO Hush regularly says, presumably referring to the many streams of income Drake has from music, touring and endorsements with companies such as Nike and Stake.\n\nFurther, this line could be interpreted as Drake alluding to inspiring Ice Spice’s lyric, as the two have a notable history despite never having collaborated on any music that has yet to be released. Alternatively, Hush may be a fan of Ice who regularly quotes her music.", "annotation_id": "34563255", "url": "https://genius.com/34563255", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "GLORIOUS", "line": "Like grrah, for sure, ten million views in a day", "vault_lines": ["Like grrah, for sure, ten million views in a day"], "meaning": "This is one of many references throughout the track to Bronx rapper Ice Spice. Specifically, this is a reference to her 2023 song “In Ha Mood,” in which she boasts about getting one million views in a day:\n\nLike a million views in a day (Like)\nIt’s so many ways to get paid (Grrah)\n\nIn this line, Drake even mimics Ice’s signature “grrah” ad-lib.\n\nNotably, Drake and Ice have interacted several times, with Ice appearing with Drake at his 2022 OVO Fest.", "annotation_id": "34563185", "url": "https://genius.com/34563185", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "GLORIOUS", "line": "He’s better off wavin’ a white flag, Baka seen bro, he was clutchin’ a side bag Yeah, straight up asked him, “What’s in the side bag?” Tapped his chest, there’s nothin’ inside that", "vault_lines": ["He's better off wavin' a white flag, Baka seen bro, he was clutchin' a side bag", "Yeah, straight up asked him, \"What's in the side bag?\" Tapped his chest, there's nothin' inside that"], "meaning": "Drake name-drops one of his day-one guys, Baka Not Nice, who is also an OVO artist and has been on Drake’s security team. Interestingly, this is the first time that Drake has mentioned Baka since Kendrick Lamar infamously mentioned him in “Not Like Us”.\n\nLink to Baka’s criminal history.\n\nThese lines describe Baka acting as bodyguard. In this scenario, Baka suspects a man is hiding a gun in his side bag and touches it to check if it’s empty. This moment aligns with Baka’s own lyrics on his breakout track “Live Up to My Name,” where he raps about concealing a weapon in a Louis Vuitton pouch:\n\nLouis pouch across my body, this is not for fashion\n\n\nPictured: Baka and Drake\n\nAfter this, in 2019, Drake rapped the following on “War,” which interestingly is known for being Drake’s first release wherein he hopped on a drill beat:\n\nThe LV pouch on chest is just for fashion, niggas just actin'", "annotation_id": "34561470", "url": "https://genius.com/34561470", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "GLORIOUS", "line": "It’s so fire, like, it’s for the streets, it’s for the baddies It’s for the ooters, it’s for everybody It just really gives me that vibe, like", "vault_lines": ["It's so fire, like, it's for the streets, it's for the baddies", "It's for the ooters, it's for everybody", "It just really gives me that vibe, like"], "meaning": "The song samples parts of Ice Spice’s July 2023 interview with Zane Lowe for Apple Music. Zane and Ice Spice touch on topics from unreleased music, how her stage name came to be, receiving free gifts, and her mentality when dealing with the industry. These clips are sampled throughout the song, as well as common adlibs that Ice Spice uses in her music.\n\nDrake and Ice Spice have a well-documented history, alibet very recent. It’s also worth noting that Drake  mimics the cadence and style of Ice Spice, as well as the beat gives a similar feel to her music.", "annotation_id": "34561158", "url": "https://genius.com/34561158", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Runaway (Free Larry Hoover Benefit Concert Version)", "status": "done", "targets": 2, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Kanye-west-and-drake-runaway-free-larry-hoover-benefit-concert-version-lyrics", "genius_title": "Runaway (Free Larry Hoover Benefit Concert Version)", "genius_id": 7616681, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Runaway (Free Larry Hoover Benefit Concert Version)", "line": "Someday I’m gon’ make you run away Someday, that’s what some would say Someway, he’s gon’ make you run away Someday he’s gon’ make you run away That’s what some will say", "vault_lines": ["Someday I'm gon' make you run away", "Someday, that's what some would say", "Someway, he's gon' make you run away", "Someday he's gon' make you run away", "That's what some will say", "Someday he gon' run away"], "meaning": "Kanye is suggesting that this is something people say about him – he’s going to make Kim run away, through proving himself to truly be a lover worth running away from – e.g. a bad one.", "annotation_id": "36339509", "url": "https://genius.com/36339509", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
