{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mr. Right Now", "status": "done", "targets": 13, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/21-savage-and-metro-boomin-mr-right-now-lyrics", "genius_title": "Mr. Right Now", "genius_id": 6017383, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mr. Right Now", "line": "We in quarantine (On God), but my M’s long (On God)", "vault_lines": ["We in quarantine (On God), but my M's long (On God)"], "meaning": "When this song was released, the world was in the midst of the coronavirus pandemic. This negatively affected the financial situations of millions of people around the world, particularly Americans. Initially, people were encouraged to quarantine themselves within their homes in an effort to hopefully protect them and others from contracting the virus.\n\nEntertainers, like Savage, were forced to postpone or cancel their concerts and tours due to regulations restricting or prohibiting large gatherings of people. However, Savage indicates that these restrictions did not limit or stop his inflow of wealth. As of this song’s release, Savage’s net worth is approximated at over $12 million and is still growing.\n\nMoreover, Savage is the sole owner of his masters, allowing him to control a variety of financial and business situations involving his music or likeness.", "annotation_id": "20978184", "url": "https://genius.com/20978184", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mr. Right Now", "line": "Put you in Chanel, I’ma teach you how to stunt (21)", "vault_lines": ["Put you in Chanel, I'ma teach you how to stunt (21)"], "meaning": "Chanel is a luxurious French brand that sells expensive clothes and fashion accessories. Savage mentions the brand in another SAVAGE MODE II track, “Rich Nigga Shit”:\n\nMy bitches be askin', “Where’s Chanel at?”\n\nSavage, himself, is often pictured wearing the brand:\n\n\n\nSavage wearing orange Chanel hip-tops", "annotation_id": "20967524", "url": "https://genius.com/20967524", "state": "accepted", "votes": 36, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mr. Right Now", "line": "I’ma slide anytime you want", "vault_lines": ["I'ma slide anytime you want"], "meaning": "“Slide,” in this context, means to meet with someone and have sex. Savage also used the term in a more literal way on his December 2018 song, “asmr”:\n\nSlide in and out (Out)\nSpend the night? I doubt (Doubt)", "annotation_id": "20967432", "url": "https://genius.com/20967432", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mr. Right Now", "line": "But she stay in apartments I got beef at (On God) Pussy so good, I had to sneak back (On God) Hit her with my Glizzy, boy, I keep that", "vault_lines": ["But she stay in apartments I got beef at (On God)", "Pussy so good, I had to sneak back (On God)", "Hit her with my Glizzy, boy, I keep that"], "meaning": "“Glizzy” is slang for a Glock. A Glock is an Austrian made semi-automatic pistol that’s popular among many law enforcement and government agencies.\n\nThough Savage is making a correlation between his gun and his male genitalia, it connects with the other two lines; since he’s in enemy territory, he keeps a Glock for protection.", "annotation_id": "20967168", "url": "https://genius.com/20967168", "state": "accepted", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mr. Right Now", "line": "Threw my heart out the window, feelings gone (21) Threw my heart out the window, but", "vault_lines": ["Threw my heart out the window, feelings gone (21)", "Threw my heart out the window, but"], "meaning": "Savage has rapped about not having a heart before on his July 2016 song, “No Heart”:\n\nI grew up in the streets without no heart\nI’m prayin' to my Glock and my carbon\n\nSavage being “heartless” likely comes from all of the violence and trauma he has endured over the years. His brother, Tayman, was killed in a botched drug deal, and on his 21st birthday, during an attempted robbery, his best friend, Johnny, was shot and killed. Savage was also shot six times.", "annotation_id": "20967015", "url": "https://genius.com/20967015", "state": "accepted", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mr. Right Now", "line": "She want me to fuck her to some Keith Sweat (21)", "vault_lines": ["She want me to fuck her to some Keith Sweat (21)", "She want me to fuck her to Beyoncé (Straight up)"], "meaning": "Keith Sweat is an R&B singer who rose to fame in the late ‘80s. He has several top ten Billboard hits, all which includes his June 1996 song, “Nobody” and his September 1996 song, “Twisted.” Savage furthers the song’s theme of his girl wanting to make love to R&B music.\n\nSavage and Keith are friends: they did a RapCaviar sit-down together in November 2017 and appeared in a skit together.", "annotation_id": "20961955", "url": "https://genius.com/20961955", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mr. Right Now", "line": "Ayy, turn your phone off, take your clothes off (21) I’m a savage, but I fuck her to a slow song (21) Turn the lights down (21), lay the pipe down (21) I ain’t Mr. Right, but I’m Mr. Right Now (Straight up)", "vault_lines": ["Turn your phone off, take your clothes off", "I'm a sav', but I fuck her to a slow song", "Ayy, turn your phone off, take your clothes off (21)", "I'm a savage, but I fuck her to a slow song (21)", "Turn the lights down (21), lay the pipe down (21)", "I ain't Mr. Right, but I'm Mr. Right Now (Straight up)"], "meaning": "“Mr. Right” is what many females call the perfect guy and the one they want to marry. However, Savage doesn’t want any extra ties to this girl; he just wants sex. He made this clear in the February 2019 video version of “a lot,” where he raps about not wanting to be married:\n\nBe a married man, right now I just can’t", "annotation_id": "20961757", "url": "https://genius.com/20961757", "state": "accepted", "votes": 91, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mr. Right Now", "line": "(Metro)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This is one of Metro Boomin’s many producer tags. This tag is voiced by Young Thug and comes from his November 2015 song, “Hercules.”\n\nThe tag, though rarely used, can be heard on songs like Gunna’s February 2018 song, “Car Sick,” and Nicki Minaj’s August 2018 song, “Chun Swae.”", "annotation_id": "20961233", "url": "https://genius.com/20961233", "state": "accepted", "votes": 56, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mr. Right Now", "line": "While I jump inside that box and have a field day I’m the slow stroke king, hit me anytime And my goal is to get you to the finish line", "vault_lines": ["While I jump inside that box and have a field day", "I'm the slow stroke king, hit me anytime", "And my goal is to get you to the finish line"], "meaning": "“Box” is slang for a woman’s vagina and “have a field day” is an idiom that means to get pleasure from doing something—in this instance, having sexual intercourse.\n\nA “stroke” is an action that’s done during intercourse where a male enters, then nearly exits his partner in slow, repetitive motions. Drake previously mentioned the sexual move on the February 2019 remix of Summer Walker song, “Girls Need Love”:\n\nArched back, deep stroke\n\nLastly, Drake getting his girl to the “finish line” likely means he’s gonna make her orgasm.", "annotation_id": "20961083", "url": "https://genius.com/20961083", "state": "accepted", "votes": 57, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mr. Right Now", "line": "Make that thing sing like Sade (21)", "vault_lines": ["Make that thing sing like Sade (21)"], "meaning": "Sade is a Grammy-winning British band that’s named after their lead singer, Sade Adu. She’s known for her soulful ballads about love and loss. Additionally, she’s one of the most successful British female artists of all time and has had a big influence on contemporary music. Savage plays on “sing,” as it also means to shoot a weapon.\n\nNotably, Drake is a big fan of Sade; he sampled one of her songs on his September 2011 single, “Free Spirit,” and got two portraits of her tatted on his body in 2017.", "annotation_id": "20960689", "url": "https://genius.com/20960689", "state": "accepted", "votes": 50, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mr. Right Now", "line": "1942, it ain’t no Chardonnay (21)", "vault_lines": ["1942, it ain't no Chardonnay (21)"], "meaning": "1942 or Don Julio 1942 is an expensive brand of tequila. It’s known for its refined taste because of its aging process.\n\nChardonnay, on the other hand, is a popular white wine that’s made from green-skinned grapes.", "annotation_id": "20960593", "url": "https://genius.com/20960593", "state": "accepted", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mr. Right Now", "line": "Yeah, said she wanna fuck to some SZA, wait ’Cause I used to date SZA back in ’08 If you cool with it, baby, she can still play", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, said she wanna fuck to some SZA, wait", "'Cause I used to date SZA back in '08", "If you cool with it, baby, she can still play"], "meaning": "SZA is an artist from St. Louis, Missouri, who is signed to Top Dawg Entertaiment. Her discography mainly consists of R&B music, which is why Drake’s girl chooses her music to make love to.\n\nSZA and Drake are friends; Drake liked a photo of her back in 2017. A month prior to this song’s release, he gave SZA a shoutout on his Instagram Stories with the caption, “Solana is the [chef’s] kiss,” which was in support of the music video for her September 2020 single, “Hit Different.”\n\nAlso, Drake rapped about knowing her “way back” on his January 2018 song, “Diplomatic Immunity”:\n\nI just pulled up on Solána show, the girl’s a natural\nI knew her way back when Hollywood was international\n\nTwo days after the song’s release, SZA confirmed that she and Drake actually did date, but it was in 2009, not 2008.\n\n\nSo It was actually 2009 lol 🙃.. in this case a year of poetic rap license mattered 🥴lol I think he jus innocently rhymed 08 w wait . Anybody who really knows me and was around during this time can confirm.. it’s all love all peace 🤝💎💫 .\n\nI just didn’t want anybody thinking anything underage or creepy was happening . Completely innocent . Lifetimes ago .\n\n\n\n\nSZA and Drake in Toronto during her 2017 CTRL Tour.", "annotation_id": "20959848", "url": "https://genius.com/20959848", "state": "accepted", "votes": 204, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mr. Right Now", "line": "Slip and slide like a waterfall You need some TLC, we can creep if you want (21)", "vault_lines": ["I'ma slide anytime you want", "Slip and slide like a waterfall", "You need some TLC, we can creep if you want (21)"], "meaning": "TLC is a female trio that consists of Tionne “T-Boz” Watkins, Lisa “Left Eye” Lopes and Rozonda “Chilli” Thomas. Following Lisa Lopes’ untimely death in 2002, the group continued as a duo. Savage plays on their group name as TLC also means “tender, loving, care.”\n\nSavage also name-drops their October 1994 song, “Creep,” and their November 1994 song, “Waterfalls.” Both songs were number one hits from the group’s sophomore studio album, CrazySexyCool.", "annotation_id": "20959780", "url": "https://genius.com/20959780", "state": "accepted", "votes": 79, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "U My Everything", "status": "done", "targets": 10, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Sexyy-red-and-drake-u-my-everything-lyrics", "genius_title": "U My Everything", "genius_id": 10419894, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "U My Everything", "line": "You the hood bitch of my dreams, Sexyy, girl, you just ask for me and I’m there", "vault_lines": ["You the hood bitch of my dreams, Sexyy, girl, you just ask for me and I'm there"], "meaning": "Staying true to his preferences on “As We Speak,” Drake still got a thing for ratchet girls:\n\nBack in America, fuckin' on hoes from the ratchet-est area, what?", "annotation_id": "39900303", "url": "https://genius.com/39900303", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "U My Everything", "line": "Verse 2: Drake", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "For this entire Verse, the music switches from the original to a lower pitch of Metro Boomin’s diss beat, “BBL Drizzy”, a beat mocking Drake’s butt causing it to become a meme.", "annotation_id": "35762518", "url": "https://genius.com/35762518", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "U My Everything", "line": "You send a pic in them shorts and I had to send you a caption like I was there", "vault_lines": ["You send a pic in them shorts and I had to send you a caption like I was there"], "meaning": "Drake responded to Red’s picture in her shorts by telling her what he would do to her sexually if he was there with her.", "annotation_id": "31862449", "url": "https://genius.com/31862449", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "U My Everything", "line": "You ain’t get your master’s, but I stay breakin’ your back in the master bedroom, I swear", "vault_lines": ["You ain't get your master's, but I stay breakin' your back in the master bedroom, I swear"], "meaning": "Drake employs another antanaclasis with the word ‘master’ to refer to a master’s degree and a master bedroom.\n\nAlso, notice the wordplay between “master” and “bachelor” from the previous bar.", "annotation_id": "31854555", "url": "https://genius.com/31854555", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "U My Everything", "line": "If you and your BD are calling it splits Then maybe we call it an accident You slip, you trip, you fall on my dick", "vault_lines": ["If you and your BD are calling it splits", "Then maybe we call it an accident", "You slip, you trip, you fall on my dick"], "meaning": "Drake uses a funny trope, where a girl tries to explain her infidelity as an accident by saying that she slipped and fell, landing on the guy’s dick.\n\nThis is probably a reference to a bar from Eminem and Dr. Dre’s track “Guilty Conscience”, where Dr. Dre (acting as Eminem’s conscience) tries to convince Eminem not to kill his girl and her partner after catching them cheating:\n\nWait, what if there’s an explanation for this shit?\n\nOnly for Eminem to respond:\n\nWhat, she tripped, fell, landed on his dick?\n\nAlso, notice the antanaclasis with the word “call” in “calling it splits” and “call it an accident”.", "annotation_id": "31854417", "url": "https://genius.com/31854417", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "U My Everything", "line": "I got a passion for you, I swear I got attraction for you, I swear Yeah, you think I’m a bachelor, girl, but I swear", "vault_lines": ["I got a passion for you, I swear", "I got attraction for you, I swear", "Yeah, you think I'm a bachelor, girl, but I swear"], "meaning": "Drake has been romantically linked to many women throughout his career, and he has never publicly had a stable long-term relationship. In 2022, he embraced his romantic history when he commissioned a 351-carat diamond necklace named “Previous Engagements” with 42 diamonds representing the times he considered proposing to various women but didn’t, a bold fashion statement that received criticism on social media.\n\nDespite his reputation as a bachelor, Drake is saying things with Sexyy Red are different.\n\nDrake wearing the “Previous Engagements” necklace", "annotation_id": "31850667", "url": "https://genius.com/31850667", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "U My Everything", "line": "But Red, don’t even worry about all of that shit Just keep it natural for ’em, I swear", "vault_lines": ["But Red, don't even worry about all of that shit", "Just keep it natural for 'em, I swear"], "meaning": "Sexyy Red has received attention on social media for her relatively slender body. This contrasts with the curvaceous hourglass figure that is the prevailing beauty standard for many female performers both in and out of hip hop, often achieved with a BBL surgery. Drake wants Red to keep her body natural and not give into social pressure. He says in the preceding bars that he’s paid for many other women to have BBLs, so him saying this to Red indicates that she’s special and exceptional in his eyes.", "annotation_id": "31850243", "url": "https://genius.com/31850243", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "U My Everything", "line": "I had some smoke in the city, I wanted to see you, but, baby, I couldn’t just dip", "vault_lines": ["I had some smoke in the city, I wanted to see you, but, baby, I couldn't just dip"], "meaning": "Drake seems to be referring to the shooting that took place at his Toronto mansion in May, 2024 that left one of his security guards injured. Drake cites the trouble in his city as the reason he couldn’t leave to see this special person.", "annotation_id": "31849287", "url": "https://genius.com/31849287", "state": "pending", "votes": 37, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "U My Everything", "line": "Maybe we go to Saint Lucia, I been there, so I’ll introduce you Or maybe you go to Saint Martin with me if these niggas take break and quit startin’ with me Maybe we go to Saint Kitts", "vault_lines": ["Maybe we go to Saint Lucia, I been there, so I'll introduce you", "Or maybe you go to Saint Martin with me if these niggas take break and quit startin' with me", "Maybe we go to Saint Kitts"], "meaning": "Playing off the name of St. Louis, Drizzy lists a few Caribbean islands he and Redd might take a vacation to. St. Lucia and St. Kitts and Nevis are both sovereign states, while St. Martin is divided in half between France and the Netherlands. All three islands are known for their lush coastlines, and the French half of St. Martin is famous for its nude beaches.\n\n\n\nDrizzy is a connoisseur of Caribbean destinations, having vactioned in Barbados, and the Turks and Caicos, among other locations.\n\nDrake is also referencing his (in)famous “20 v 1” beef with Kendrick Lamar and others with his line:\n\nif these niggas take break and quit startin' with me", "annotation_id": "31849114", "url": "https://genius.com/31849114", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "U My Everything", "line": "I changed a lot of girls’ lives for real They need a new body, they hittin’ me, ayy BBL Drizzy, they want a new body, they ask me for it The last one, Jung, he did it for free ’cause I sent over so many past ones for him", "vault_lines": ["I changed a lot of girls' lives for real", "They need a new body, they hittin' me, ayy", "BBL Drizzy, they want a new body, they ask me for it", "The last one, Jung, he did it for free 'cause I sent over so many past ones for him"], "meaning": "Drake put his spin on the “BBL Drizzy” meme which was started by Rick Ross in April 2024 and perpetuated by Metro Boomin in his instrumental track of the same name.\n\nWhile the meme started out accusing Drake of having undergone cosmetic surgery, including liposuction and abdomen implants, Drake asserts that his history with cosmetic surgeons actually stems from purchasing BBLs (Brazilian butt lifts) and other such procedures for the women he dates.\n\nDuring this part of the track, Drake raps over Metro’s “BBL Drizzy” beat Metro previously used to mock him, thereby serving as a clever effort by Drake to reclaim control over the narrative.\n\nDrake has a history of referencing BBLs in his music. Notably, he dedicated a track to the procedure titled “BBL Love (Interlude)” on his 2023 album For All The Dogs.\n\nRegarding his history with plastic surgeons, during a stop in Houston, Texas, for his “It’s All A Blur” tour in September 2023, Drake presented custom OVO scrubs to “renowned” plastic surgeon and “BBL specialist” Dr. Calvin Jung.", "annotation_id": "31848477", "url": "https://genius.com/31848477", "state": "accepted", "votes": 63, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
