{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Needle", "status": "done", "targets": 17, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Nicki-minaj-needle-lyrics", "genius_title": "Needle", "genius_id": 9816408, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Needle", "line": "If this Rollie on my wrist can’t weigh me down, eh-eh-mm What makes you think you could weigh me down? Stop it right now", "vault_lines": ["If this Rollie on my wrist can't weigh me down, eh-eh-mm", "If these diamonds in my ear can't weigh me down now", "What makes you think you could weigh me down? Stop it right now"], "meaning": "Drake is suggesting that if the weight of a very valuable watch doesn’t burden him, what could someone else possibly do to bring him down or affect him negatively?\n\nOr that he has achieved the wealth to own these things and is curious what the girl possibly has to offer him.\n\n“Stop it right now” : don’t even try to weigh down Drake, he’s got diamonds and Rollies and that doesn’t phase him.", "annotation_id": "33918985", "url": "https://genius.com/33918985", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Needle", "line": "Ghetto gyal have di wickedest slam, everybody know", "vault_lines": ["Ghetto gyal have di wickedest slam, everybody know"], "meaning": "Translation:\nEverybody knows ghetto girls have the best s*x.", "annotation_id": "33287277", "url": "https://genius.com/33287277", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Needle", "line": "Damn, Drizzy, another bitter ex, shout out my intellects", "vault_lines": ["Damn, Drizzy, another bitter ex, shout out my intellects"], "meaning": "The initial interpretation of this line insinuates Nicki is showing Drake [Drizzy] another bitter ex of Nicki. However, it could also be interpreted as Nicki calling Drake a bitter ex as, in the past, Drake has shown his affection for Nicki multiple times, whereas she declines and a string of bitterness was shown by Drake (humorously).", "annotation_id": "31044766", "url": "https://genius.com/31044766", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Needle", "line": "Gyal, haffi, gyal, haffi, haffi give me my ting Commission for the game that I be providing, ayy", "vault_lines": ["Gyal haffi, gyal haffi fi ah give me my ting", "Commission for the game that I be providing", "Gyal, haffi, gyal, haffi, haffi give me my ting", "Commission for the game that I be providing, ayy"], "meaning": "Nicki Minaj is a proud Trinidadian immigrant from Saint James, Port of Spain, Trinidad and Tobago. Although the official language of Trinidad is English, it’s more common for someone in Trinidad to speak Trinidadian Creole. As a result of her heritage, she speaks Creole and chooses to incorporate it into this part of the song. “Gyal” translates to “girl,” “Haffi” means “have to” and ting means “thing” So, she’s basically saying a girl had to give her something (most likely referring to money because of the lyric right after this one)\n\nThe lyric, “Commission for the game that I be providing,” suggests that Nicki is receiving payment or a commission for the music she makes, as rap music is sometimes referred to as the “Rap Game” or just the “Game.” It could also refer to any other payments she generates outside of rap, such as brand promotions and other social media revenue.\n\n\n\nNicki Minaj in Trinidad.", "annotation_id": "30530110", "url": "https://genius.com/30530110", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Needle", "line": "Man ah gwan from Toronto, Canada to OVO", "vault_lines": ["Man ah gwan from Toronto, Canada to OVO"], "meaning": "Drake started rapping in Toronto Canada and now has his own apparel brand and record label, both called OVO. Along with the previous line, this makes a cute couplet describing how far Drake and Nicki have come over the course of their careers.", "annotation_id": "30530090", "url": "https://genius.com/30530090", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Needle", "line": "[Intro: SZA]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The Intro is actually SZA’s voice memo, However, Nana Fofie is featured as additional vocals in timestamp 2:14.", "annotation_id": "30423427", "url": "https://genius.com/30423427", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Needle", "line": "I rap, but he wanna taste the icing", "vault_lines": ["I rap, but he wanna taste the icing"], "meaning": "Correct lyric is –\n\nI rap, but he want to taste the icing (i SING)\n\n\n\nNicki tweeted these lyrics 12.21.23", "annotation_id": "30405910", "url": "https://genius.com/30405910", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Needle", "line": "[Verse 1: Drake]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "“Needles” Was supposed to release on “For All The Dogs” By Drake and instead of Drake as the feature here it would have been Nicki as the feature on his album he decided the album wouldn’t fit the vibe of “For All the Dogs” and decided to give the song to Nicki\n\nAs Stated By Nicki Minaj while on stream with Kai Cenat.", "annotation_id": "30402604", "url": "https://genius.com/30402604", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Needle", "line": "Gyal haffi, gyal haffi fi ah give me my ting Commission for the game that I be providing", "vault_lines": ["Gyal haffi, gyal haffi fi ah give me my ting", "Commission for the game that I be providing", "Gyal, haffi, gyal, haffi, haffi give me my ting", "Commission for the game that I be providing, ayy"], "meaning": "Nicki Minaj is a proud Trinidadian immigrant from Saint James, Port of Spain, Trinidad and Tobago. Although the official language of Trinidad is English, it’s more common for someone in Trinidad to speak Trinidadian Creole. As a result of her heritage, she speaks Creole and chooses to incorporate it into this part of the song. “Gyal” translates to “girl,” “Haffi” means “have to” and ting means “thing” So, she’s basically saying a girl had to give her something (most likely referring to money because of the lyric right after this one)\n\nThe lyric, “Commission for the game that I be providing,” suggests that Nicki is receiving payment or a commission for the music she makes, as rap music is sometimes referred to as the “Rap Game” or just the “Game.” It could also refer to any other payments she generates outside of rap, such as brand promotions and other social media revenue.\n\n\n\nNicki Minaj in Trinidad", "annotation_id": "30402498", "url": "https://genius.com/30402498", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Needle", "line": "It gave nothin’, bitch", "vault_lines": ["It gave nothin', bitch"], "meaning": "This line is reference to Minaj’s beef with rapper Latto. Latto started a trend on Twitter of “It’s giving coke” as it relates to Minaj’s eccentric behavior. Minaj during her Queen Radio interviews advised that she has never done coke. She had admitted to Percocets which are referenced in her Pink Print album but not cocaine. Minaj is responding here saying that she does not do cocaine.", "annotation_id": "30376960", "url": "https://genius.com/30376960", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Needle", "line": "You’re like a needle, life’s a haystack", "vault_lines": ["You're like a needle, life's a haystack"], "meaning": "These lyrics suggest a feeling of searching for something specific or meaningful in the vastness of life, where the person or situation being referred to is likened to a needle in a haystack. It implies a sense of difficulty or challenge in finding that particular element.", "annotation_id": "30328846", "url": "https://genius.com/30328846", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Needle", "line": "Thank you for zero, next", "vault_lines": [", thank you for zero, next"], "meaning": "This line might be a reference to Ariana Grande’s “thank u, next” as her and Nicki are close friends and have released songs together.", "annotation_id": "30296498", "url": "https://genius.com/30296498", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Needle", "line": "[Bridge: Nicki Minaj, Nana Fofie, Nicki Minaj & Nana Fofie]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This is a voice memo by Nana Fofie that is set to the feeling of a voicemail or voice message.\n\nSee what she said about playing a role in the song on Twitter/X:\nhttps://x.com/nanafofiee/status/1733005126242013577?s=20", "annotation_id": "30296484", "url": "https://genius.com/30296484", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Needle", "line": "Gyal ah gwan from the likkle island gyal to CEO", "vault_lines": ["Gyal ah gwan from the likkle island gyal to CEO"], "meaning": "Nicki Minaj originally comes from Trinidad and Tobago , which is somehow considered an island. She is also the CEO of HEAVY ON IT RECORDS.", "annotation_id": "30293994", "url": "https://genius.com/30293994", "state": "pending", "votes": -10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Needle", "line": "Poppin’ out like a cork, ducking ’em like Björk", "vault_lines": ["Poppin' out like a cork, ducking 'em like Björk"], "meaning": "This line is referencing Björks iconic swan dress, worn at the 73rd Academy Awards in 2001. Swan is a type of duck.", "annotation_id": "30292990", "url": "https://genius.com/30292990", "state": "pending", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Needle", "line": "I was in Trinidad, let us consider that Immigrant to a boss, bitches bitter and mad", "vault_lines": ["I was in Trinidad, let us consider that", "Immigrant to a boss, bitches bitter and mad"], "meaning": "Nicki Minaj was born in Saint James, Port of Spain, Trinidad and Tobago and is now owner of Apple Music Show, “Queen Radio”", "annotation_id": "30287055", "url": "https://genius.com/30287055", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Needle", "line": "If these diamonds in my ear can’t weigh me down now What makes you think you could weigh me down? Stop it right now", "vault_lines": ["If these diamonds in my ear can't weigh me down now", "What makes you think you could weigh me down? Stop it right now"], "meaning": "By suggesting that even the literal weight of valuable diamonds doesn’t burden him is telling someone that they do not have the power to bring him down or affect him negatively.", "annotation_id": "30286145", "url": "https://genius.com/30286145", "state": "pending", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
