{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Tony Montana (Remix)", "status": "done", "targets": 8, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Future-tony-montana-remix-lyrics", "genius_title": "Tony Montana (Remix)", "genius_id": 51956, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Tony Montana (Remix)", "line": "I’m about to cop a tiger (Haha), and put it in the car seat (Ayy)", "vault_lines": ["I'm about to cop a tiger (Haha), and put it in the car seat (Ayy)", "I'm 'bout to cop the Porsche (Porsche)"], "meaning": "Tony Montana is seen in a 1963 Cadillac Series 62 Convertible with tiger print car seats in Scarface.", "annotation_id": "31132888", "url": "https://genius.com/31132888", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Tony Montana (Remix)", "line": "You want me to be the bad guy? Okay, it’s on then (Turn up)", "vault_lines": ["Want me to be the bad guy?", "You want me to be the bad guy? Okay, it's on then (Turn up)"], "meaning": "In an iconic scene in Scarface, Tony Montana stumbles out of a restaurant, yelling:\n\nYou need people like me so you can point your fingers and say ‘Hey there’s the bad guy!’ So that does that make you? Good guys? Don’t kid yourselves. You’re no better'n me. You just know how to hide – and how to lie. Me, I don’t have that problem. I always tell the truth – even when I lie. So say good night to the bad guy… You’re never gonna see a bad guy like me again.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dW37AGZ0Pj0", "annotation_id": "31132844", "url": "https://genius.com/31132844", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Tony Montana (Remix)", "line": "You fuckin’ with me, you’ll move to Alaska by the mornin’ (Aight)", "vault_lines": ["You fuckin' with me, you'll move to Alaska by the mornin' (Aight)"], "meaning": "After a police bust in the film Scarface, Tony Montana says to officers:\n\nSo you wanna waste everybody’s time? Here, I call my lawyer. Best lawyer in Miami. He’s so good, tomorrow morning you’re gonna be working in Alaska.", "annotation_id": "31132826", "url": "https://genius.com/31132826", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Tony Montana (Remix)", "line": "The world is mine", "vault_lines": ["The world is mine"], "meaning": "“The world is yours” was a tagline used several times throughout the Scarface film.", "annotation_id": "31132788", "url": "https://genius.com/31132788", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Tony Montana (Remix)", "line": "I come with the yayo", "vault_lines": ["I come straight from the east, where niggas split your cantaloupe", "Ain't nothin' about me ordinary, I come with the yayo"], "meaning": "From the Scarface IMDB page: “Tony Montana uses \"yeyo” as slang for cocaine. Al Pacino [actor playing Tony Montana] learned the word while learning the Cuban accent, and ad-libbed it during the chainsaw scene. Brian De Palma [director of Scarface] liked it enough to keep using it throughout the film.\"", "annotation_id": "31132765", "url": "https://genius.com/31132765", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Tony Montana (Remix)", "line": "Fuckin’ cockroaches", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The term: ‘Fuckin’ Cockroaches,‘ is a direct quote and reference from the movie Scarface; Tony Montana probably through the idea of calling his enemies 'cockroaches,’ from the famous Spanish song: “La Cucaracha.”", "annotation_id": "27578043", "url": "https://genius.com/27578043", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Tony Montana (Remix)", "line": "Tony Montana (Yeah), Tony Montana (Yeah), Tony Montana (Yeah), Tony Montana", "vault_lines": ["Tony Montana (Yeah), Tony Montana (Yeah), Tony Montana (Yeah), Tony Montana", "Tony Montana, Tony Montana (Who are you?), Tony Montana (Ayy)"], "meaning": "Tony Montana is the fictional role played by Al Pacino in the legendary film Scarface.\n\nMore importantly, this line has significance in hip hop culture. Future went on record claiming he was too high to word the lyrics properly. Upon hearing the distinct sound it added to the song, he decided to leave it. Many have claimed that it was this line that inspired the controversial subgenre “Mumble Rap”.", "annotation_id": "12759554", "url": "https://genius.com/12759554", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Tony Montana (Remix)", "line": "Motherfuckin’ Freebandz (Freebandz)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Future founded his record label Freebandz in December of 2012. His signed artists are collectively known as Freeband Gang.\n\n\n\nFreebandz logo\n\nOctobers Very Own is a record label Drake founded while XO is The Weeknd’s crew. The three artists collaborate quite often.", "annotation_id": "269973", "url": "https://genius.com/269973", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "królik w kapeluszu", "status": "done", "targets": 0, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Kkfwnosense-krolik-w-kapeluszu-lyrics", "genius_title": "królik w kapeluszu", "genius_id": 11043250, "source": "api"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Freak In You (Remix)", "status": "done", "targets": 7, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Partynextdoor-freak-in-you-remix-lyrics", "genius_title": "Freak In You (Remix)", "genius_id": 3131778, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Freak In You (Remix)", "line": "Yeah, the sex we have reminds me of the money and success a bit Yeah, ’cause even when I got it I just gotta keep getting it Even when I got it I just gotta keep getting it", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, the sex we have reminds me of the money and success a bit", "Yeah, 'cause even when I got it I just gotta keep getting it", "Even when I got it I just gotta keep getting it"], "meaning": "After going platinum in just one week with Views, dominating the charts for a record breaking eight uninterrupted years, setting the record for most Billboard Music Awards won in one year, and snagging the number four spot on Forbes' ‘Celebrity 100’ List for 2017 with $94 million, calling Drizzy “successful” would be an understatement.\n\nBut even with all his successes and fortune, Drake keeps coming back for more. We saw an example of that when he ended his March 2017 playlist More Life on “Do Not Disturb”:\n\nTakin' summer off, ‘cause they tell me I need recovery\nMaybe gettin’ back to my regular life will humble me\nI’ll be back in 2018 to give you the summary\n\nHe suggested the next time we’ll be hearing him on a new track would be in 2018, but Drizzy couldn’t resist getting back in the booth; just a couple days into summer 2017, he dropped “Signs,” and featured on Metro Boomin’s “No Complaints,” along with this track.", "annotation_id": "12223435", "url": "https://genius.com/12223435", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Freak In You (Remix)", "line": "Always going back to some shit that I already been in", "vault_lines": ["But I already know that", "Always going back to some shit that I already been in"], "meaning": "Drake is referring to his on-and-off relationship with popstar Rihanna. Drake and Rihanna met in 2005, and ever since their Take Care collaboration in 2011, they’ve been in and out of a relationship. They were last together in 2016.", "annotation_id": "12222061", "url": "https://genius.com/12222061", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Freak In You (Remix)", "line": "Yeah, I jump out of relationships before I get left in it", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, I jump out of relationships before I get left in it"], "meaning": "Prior to the song’s release, Drake has had a string of short relationships with multiple women, the most notable being with professional tennis player Serena Williams in 2015, his on-and-off flame Rihanna in 2016, and then Jennifer Lopez towards the end of the same year leading up to 2017.", "annotation_id": "12222056", "url": "https://genius.com/12222056", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Freak In You (Remix)", "line": "We can get wild like Olivia, we can get stoned like Sharon", "vault_lines": ["We can get wild like Olivia, we can get stoned like Sharon"], "meaning": "Drizzy plays on actresses Olivia Wilde and Sharon Stone’s last names, using them as adjectives. Getting “wild” means getting sexual, while getting “stoned” means smoking weed and getting high.\n\nWhile Stone has no public relationship with Drizzy, Wilde is a fan of his work; she tweeted about his 2011 album Take Care back in 2012 saying:\n\nNew Drake album is dope\n\nThey’ve been in attendance at the same NBA games on multiple occasions, but their relationship is nothing more than platonic.", "annotation_id": "12222049", "url": "https://genius.com/12222049", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Freak In You (Remix)", "line": "Quick, rush, rush, rush Baby, just like Kimora Lee, oh So pretty, girl, you belong in a gallery", "vault_lines": ["Freak in you (freak in you)", "Quick, rush, rush, rush", "Baby, just like Kimora Lee, oh", "So pretty, girl, you belong in a gallery"], "meaning": "PARTY references the co-founder of Def Jam, Russel Simmons, and his ex-wife Kimora Lee. Russel is currently involved with Rush Communications, while Kimora is modelling.", "annotation_id": "12217919", "url": "https://genius.com/12217919", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Freak In You (Remix)", "line": "Room full of beautiful women but I want one Room full of women and they notice me Now all they wanna listen to is Jodeci Freak in you (freak in you) Freak in you (freak in you) Is there a freak in you? (Freak in you)", "vault_lines": ["Room full of beautiful women but I want one", "Room full of women and they notice me", "Now all they wanna listen to is Jodeci", "Freak in you (freak in you)", "Is there a freak in you? (Freak in you)"], "meaning": "This chorus interpolates Jodeci’s “Freek'n You, which ties nicely into the Jodeci reference in the chorus, and the first verse’s reference to “Come and Talk to Me.”", "annotation_id": "12217879", "url": "https://genius.com/12217879", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Freak In You (Remix)", "line": "Wrote Take Care, but they push me to the point where I’m just not caring I’m just more ready than petty nowadays Young and in control, even when they stoop low I see anything is anything and everything’s a go But I already know that I’m just more ready than petty nowadays, juss know Young and in control, even when they stoop low I see anything is anything, I’m watching y’all close I’m just more ready than...", "vault_lines": ["Wrote Take Care, but they push me to the point where I'm just not caring", "I'm just more ready than petty nowadays", "Young and in control, even when they stoop low", "I see anything is anything and everything's a go", "But I already know that", "I'm just more ready than petty nowadays, juss know", "I see anything is anything, I'm watching y'all close", "I'm just more ready than...", "I see anything is anything, I'm watching y'all clone"], "meaning": "In 2013, The Weeknd spoke publicly about the writing he did for Drake’s 2011 album Take Care, claiming he gave Drake songs that were originally meant to appear on his own album, Kiss Land. Drake’s disclaiming the ghostwriting rumors.\n\nAfter Drake’s feud with Meek Mill in 2015, he shifted away from engaging in beefs. In 2017, he publicly squashed beefs with Ludacris and fellow Toronto native Tory Lanez. Despite being pitted against Kendrick Lamar due to the proximity of the releases dates for More Life and DAMN., Drake took to Instagram to congratulate Kendrick on the sales of his album.", "annotation_id": "12215557", "url": "https://genius.com/12215557", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mr. Wrong", "status": "done", "targets": 4, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Mary-j-blige-mr-wrong-lyrics", "genius_title": "Mr. Wrong", "genius_id": 58017, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mr. Wrong", "line": "Me and Mr. Wrong get along so good (So good) Even though he breaks my heart so bad (So bad) We got a special thing going on Me and Mr. Wrong (Mr. Wrong) Even if I try, no, I never could Give him up ’cause his love’s like that Ain’t no way that I’m moving on Oh, I love my Mr. Wrong", "vault_lines": ["Bad boys ain't no good", "Good boys ain't no fun", "Me and Mr. Wrong get along so good (So good)", "Even though he breaks my heart so bad (So bad)", "We got a special thing going on", "Me and Mr. Wrong (Mr. Wrong)", "Even if I try, no, I never could", "Give him up 'cause his love's like that", "Ain't no way that I’m moving on", "Oh, I love my Mr. Wrong", "I love my Mr. Wrong"], "meaning": "Inspired by and reflective of the classic Billy Paul song “Me and Mrs.Jones”.\nhttps://youtu.be/n2v98PGBZH4\n\nThat song tells the story of an extramarital affair between the singer and a married woman, using a male point of view. This song shares a similar story about an equally unhealthy relationship but mainly from the female point of view.\n\nNot only do the two songs share a similar message, but the lyrics of this song directly echo the ones in Billy Paul’s chorus.\n“Me and Mrs, Mrs. Jones\nMrs. Jones, Mrs. Jones, Mrs. Jones\nWe got a thing going on\nWe both know that it’s wrong\nBut it’s much too strong”", "annotation_id": "14793193", "url": "https://genius.com/14793193", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mr. Wrong", "line": "I’m wrong", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "With these two words, Drake pulls on the multiple meanings of “wrong” to take define his relationship with this girl at this moment.\n1- Wrong in his hopes that she will not hold a grudge, because she will be hurt and scarred by his behavior. He’s done this before and knows the outcome.\n2- Wrong in this behavior. He’s judging himself for not doing right by her or being the standup guy he knows she deserves (You did her wrong)\n3- Wrong as an identity. Drake IS Mr.Wrong", "annotation_id": "14792989", "url": "https://genius.com/14792989", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mr. Wrong", "line": "Don’t it seem like Like I’m always there when it matters But missing most of the other time", "vault_lines": ["Don’t it seem like", "Like I’m always there when it matters", "But missing most of the other time"], "meaning": "He is there when it is required the most, and that reflect the standard of a broken relationship; you’re not there on the regular, which indicates a lack of interest in the partner. Perhaps he is transmitting her the feeling of ignoration. It will probably make her even more paranoid if she still has feeling’s left for him.\n\nBut there have to be sacrifices given in a relationship. Especially in a relationship with someone that is aware of the fact that they can get whoever they want.  At least, he recognizes that he is doing something wrong. So instead of it being his fault, the blame can be put on her; considering that she doesn’t seem to pressure any change or bring forth limits.", "annotation_id": "13965828", "url": "https://genius.com/13965828", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Mr. Wrong", "line": "The rewards I see from working Made me an addict", "vault_lines": ["The rewards I see from working", "Made me an addict"], "meaning": "The benefits Drake receives from being a superstar include his ability to show up and get some whenever he wants, but now this has become a regular routine. He says it made him an addict to show that he knows it’s unhealthy.\n\nThe cars, the money the attention, all are coming from his grind, his work. He’s addicted to these benefits of his success, thus making him work harder", "annotation_id": "417718", "url": "https://genius.com/417718", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "My Way (Remix)", "status": "done", "targets": 11, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Fetty-wap-my-way-remix-lyrics", "genius_title": "My Way (Remix)", "genius_id": 1783757, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "My Way (Remix)", "line": "[Verse 2: Drake]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The lines “All I gotta do is put my mind to this shit” and “I like all my S’s with two lines through them shits” are reused from the chorus of Drake’s unfinished demo song “Concentrate”", "annotation_id": "28885692", "url": "https://genius.com/28885692", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "My Way (Remix)", "line": "And he mad as fuck, big ZooWap all she sing, ayy And he mad as fuck, big ZooWap in her dreams, ayy Well he mad as fuck, when they sex, she scream for me, ayy Big ZooWap what these niggas should be, ayy", "vault_lines": ["And he mad as fuck, big ZooWap all she sing, ayy", "And he mad as fuck, big ZooWap in her dreams, ayy", "Well he mad as fuck, when they sex, she scream for me, ayy", "Big ZooWap what these niggas should be, ayy", "They should call me James"], "meaning": "Fetty is the embodiment of the ultimate man. Since blowing up in late 2014 with “Trap Queen,” Fetty’s songs are spun every hour on the radio. It’s no wonder she yells his name when she’s having sex with her boyfriend. This explains why he’s mad!\n\n“ZooWap” is Fetty’s nickname.", "annotation_id": "6908241", "url": "https://genius.com/6908241", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "My Way (Remix)", "line": "If he disrespect, two shots and I won’t blink, ayy Never really cared what the fuck these niggas think, ayy I got deep pockets, I swear my shit’s on sink, ayy", "vault_lines": ["If he disrespect, two shots and I won't blink, ayy", "Never really cared what the fuck these niggas think, ayy", "I got deep pockets, I swear my shit's on sink, ayy"], "meaning": "Claiming not to care what others think is quite the contradictory statement, considering he’s willing to shoot someone for being disrespectful. It can’t go both ways Fetty!\n\nHis cash flow is so immense that the weight of the money brings down his pants, similar to a ship sinking. As of late 2015, his net worth is estimated at $2 million. One could say he’s the walking version of the Titanic.", "annotation_id": "6908228", "url": "https://genius.com/6908228", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "My Way (Remix)", "line": "Ba-Ba-Baby This is something you should know I don’t ever chase no hoes I spotted you, you had that glo Watch me pull out all this dough Take you where you want to go Flexin’ on your ex, I know He ain’t ever take you out Barely even left your house How dare that nigga run his mouth When his pockets in a drought The last single he put out Didn’t even make it out And he dumb as hell and I swear his ass don’t think, ayy", "vault_lines": ["This is something you should know", "I don't ever chase no hoes", "I spotted you, you had that glo", "Watch me pull out all this dough", "Take you where you want to go", "Flexin' on your ex, I know", "He ain't ever take you out", "Barely even left your house", "How dare that nigga run his mouth", "When his pockets in a drought", "The last single he put out", "Didn't even make it out", "And he dumb as hell and I swear his ass don't think, ayy", "Got something I want to say", "Take you where you wanna go"], "meaning": "Fetty wants to impress a girl who has recently became available. There’s something unique about her that stopped him in his tracks and caught his attention.\n\nIt seems her ex-boyfriend may have been in the music industry. While Fetty’s previous single “Trap Queen,” hit number two on Billboard’s Hottest 100 – this guy’s song is still unreleased, ouch!\n\nZoowap figures a good way of getting her attention is to flaunt his dollar bills. Every girl has places they’d like to go, and Fetty has the means to get her anywhere.", "annotation_id": "6908221", "url": "https://genius.com/6908221", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "My Way (Remix)", "line": "All I gotta do is put my mind to this shit (Goddamn)", "vault_lines": ["All I gotta do is put my mind to this shit (Goddamn)"], "meaning": "Drake believes he can conquer anything he sets his mind to. In February 2015, he tied the Beatles, with 14 Simultaneous Hot 100 Hits and later that year in September, he celebrated his 100th entry into the Hottest 100, becoming only the 4th artist in history to do so. He most definitely knows what he’s doing.\n\nWatch Drake discuss his musical process during Elliott Wilson’s CRWN series below.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/L7BCxCjxtgg?t=770", "annotation_id": "6362933", "url": "https://genius.com/6362933", "state": "accepted", "votes": 91, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "My Way (Remix)", "line": "First off, I’ma start by sayin’ this Goddamn, goddamn", "vault_lines": ["First off, I'ma start by sayin' this", "But first off I'ma start by saying this, ayy"], "meaning": "Ah, Drake getting meta by starting at the end! Meta in the initial Greek (μετά), translating in one way to “after”. He starts after he starts.\n\nThe cyclical effect is also in his saying of “goddamn” at the end of the verse: at the start of the verse you can hear Drizzy scream in the background “goddamn!”\n\nHe has a habit of getting meta. See “5am in Toronto”:\n\nThat’s why every song sound like Drake featuring Drake", "annotation_id": "6354531", "url": "https://genius.com/6354531", "state": "accepted", "votes": 104, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "My Way (Remix)", "line": "Drank a lot tonight, I know She can drive your car and you can roll Take you where you wanna go", "vault_lines": ["Take you where you want to go", "Drank a lot tonight, I know", "She can drive your car and you can roll", "Take you where you wanna go"], "meaning": "Ever the caring gentleman, Drake makes sure this girl (who’s had a little too much to drink) arrives home safely by asking her friend to drive. He’s known for these altruistic tendencies, as he rapped on PARTYNEXTDOOR’S “Recognize”:\n\nI gotta get you those snow tires for your Mercedes, I’m glad you reminded me baby", "annotation_id": "6350737", "url": "https://genius.com/6350737", "state": "accepted", "votes": 36, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "My Way (Remix)", "line": "Everybody tryna fuck you but I’m fine with that shit I never mind, girl, that’s just you", "vault_lines": ["Everybody tryna fuck you but I'm fine with that shit", "I never mind, girl, that's just you"], "meaning": "Every guy wants to sleep the girl he’s with, but he’s cool with it. In fact, he made an entire song about it – “Energy”:\n\nI got enemies, got a lot of enemies\nGot a lot of people tryna drain me of my energy\nThey tryna take the wave from a nigga\nFuckin’ with the kid and pray for your nigga\n\nFurthermore, in 2012, Drizzy was involved with Common in a beef over Serena Williams. Drake has also been linked to her in 2015.", "annotation_id": "6350666", "url": "https://genius.com/6350666", "state": "accepted", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "My Way (Remix)", "line": "Cancel out my ex, I put a line through that bitch", "vault_lines": ["Cancel out my ex, I put a line through that bitch"], "meaning": "Despite what the memes say, Drake’s cutting his former girl off. In math,  when cancelling “x” on both sides of an equation, you usually put a line through it to indicate it no longer exists.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dV6xgXXd51E\n\nThis alludes to Nino Brown in New Jack City, where he yells “cancel that bitch” after getting rid of his then-girlfriend.", "annotation_id": "6350331", "url": "https://genius.com/6350331", "state": "accepted", "votes": 147, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "My Way (Remix)", "line": "I like all my S’s with two lines through them shits", "vault_lines": ["I like all my S's with two lines through them shits"], "meaning": "An “S” with two lines through it is a dollar sign. Drake really likes dollars, considering he’s 28 sitting on 75 mill – check his net worth here!", "annotation_id": "6350304", "url": "https://genius.com/6350304", "state": "accepted", "votes": 123, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "My Way (Remix)", "line": "They should call me James Cause I’m goin’ hard in this bitch", "vault_lines": ["They should call me James", "Cause I'm goin' hard in this bitch"], "meaning": "James Harden (hard in) is the shooting guard for the Houston Rockets. Drake has made reference to Harden before and always reps Houston when he can.\n\nHarden has two gold medals under his belt, and is considered one of the most versatile and dangerous players in the NBA, scoring an average of 26 points per game during the 2014-15 season – that’s hard. Rumor has it his notorious beard is what gives him the strength to own the court.", "annotation_id": "6349957", "url": "https://genius.com/6349957", "state": "accepted", "votes": 226, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Look Alive", "status": "done", "targets": 23, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Blocboy-jb-look-alive-lyrics", "genius_title": "Look Alive", "genius_id": 3452330, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Look Alive", "line": "Niggas came up on this side, now they on the other side (Word, word, word)", "vault_lines": ["Niggas came up on this side, now they on the other side (Word, word, word)", "We up on the other side, niggas actin' like we tied"], "meaning": "Drake talks about how people switch teams and their allegiance. It is not the first time Drake has talked about people changing on him.\nOn “Keep the Family Close” Drake raps:\n\nAnd it’s all because you chose a side\nYou’re supposed to put your pride aside and ride for me, Guess it wasn’t time\nAnd of course you went and chose a side that wasn’t mine\n\nIn “Diplomatic Immunity” Drake seems to re-ignite his beef with Joe Budden, former co-host of Everyday Struggle, in a video about Drake on Everyday Struggle Joe seems to be rather harsh on Drake’s album. Drake clearly doesn’t like this due to the fact he “did not contribute to none of this.” While Budden fired shots at Drake’s career in the video, Drake fires shots at Budden’s career in these lines:\n\nShit is complex like short niggas ‘round tall ladies\nI gotta watch who I’m talkin’ to like it’s all-ages\nI’ve seen buddin' careers turn to sit around and talk about other careers, judgin' their peers\nKnowledge from niggas who did not contribute to none of this here\n\nIn an interview with Charlamagne Budden said he smoked Hookah with Drake prior to their beef and implies they were friends.\n\n“That [Drake’s lines on “No Shopping” about Budden’s “Pump it Up” that fired shots at Budden] felt like the ultimate diss to Budden… \"I’m hurt. I am hurt. I’m appalled that nigga who know my pen game…he know I don’t care about none of that fame, success, attention, none of that, he know what I do. And you want to use your celebrity to do that to me? We smoked hookah together. How could you do that?”\"", "annotation_id": "14006055", "url": "https://genius.com/14006055", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Look Alive", "line": "He not a plug, he middle man (Middle man)", "vault_lines": ["He not a plug, he middle man (Middle man)"], "meaning": "A plug is often someone who manufactures drugs, or at least is the primary distributor. In order to hide from authorities they will have other people selling them on the streets who are often called middle men- being between the producer and the buyer", "annotation_id": "13996039", "url": "https://genius.com/13996039", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Look Alive", "line": "Tay Keith, fuck these niggas up!", "vault_lines": ["Tay Keith, fuck these niggas up!"], "meaning": "This is Tay Keith’s producer tag and is said by Lil Juice, an artist from Clarksville, Tennessee.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/TayBeezy7/status/961963861455884289", "annotation_id": "13929026", "url": "https://genius.com/13929026", "state": "accepted", "votes": 88, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Look Alive", "line": "901 Shelby Drive, look alive, look alive (’Live)", "vault_lines": ["901 Shelby Drive, look alive, look alive ('Live)"], "meaning": "Shit is going to turn up. 901 Shelby Drive. We’re going to look alive for that one because Shelby Drive, it’s a street off Elvis Presley. Elvis Presley is one of the most famous streets in Memphis. That’s right off Shelby Drive. Shelby Drive, really, going toward the hood a way.\n\nThe whole city right now, they’re still shocked, like damn, he shouted the city like that. Yeah, he did. Everybody know Drake is from Memphis, from the Chris and everywhere. He’s all around. Everybody fuck with him.", "annotation_id": "13922246", "url": "https://genius.com/13922246", "state": "verified", "votes": 230, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Look Alive", "line": "Now a nigga on the floor talkin’ to the athletes (To the athletes) Now I’m so close to the game that I could steal the stat sheet (Stat sheet)", "vault_lines": ["Now a nigga on the floor talkin' to the athletes (To the athletes)", "Now I'm so close to the game that I could steal the stat sheet (Stat sheet)"], "meaning": "That shit crazy. Like believing that shit happen. Man, first nigga used to go to the court like last year nobody didn’t know me. I thought I’d be far back and fuck around, then get 30, you get that money and get enough money to just do anything. Shit, niggas just go to the court. When I go in the court, motherfuckers know me. The athletes know me. They’re looking at me. That’s your life.", "annotation_id": "13922228", "url": "https://genius.com/13922228", "state": "verified", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Look Alive", "line": "I got the rounds like Sugar Ray Robinson (Uh)", "vault_lines": ["I got the rounds like Sugar Ray Robinson (Uh)"], "meaning": "Rounds, when I’m making rounds I mean bullets. Sugar Ray Robinson is a legend. He got the most rounds, he got rounds.", "annotation_id": "13922208", "url": "https://genius.com/13922208", "state": "verified", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Look Alive", "line": "That—that nigga brown like cinnamon (Cinnamon)", "vault_lines": ["That—that nigga brown like cinnamon (Cinnamon)"], "meaning": "That nigga’s bad. He bad. Brown is an odd color. He odd. He stand out, but the wrong way.", "annotation_id": "13922201", "url": "https://genius.com/13922201", "state": "verified", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Look Alive", "line": "Drop a nigga like he litterin’ (Huh?)", "vault_lines": ["Drop a nigga like he litterin' (Huh?)"], "meaning": "In that city of mine, everybody dying. When niggas die we just say they drop. Then when you drop something you might get charged with littering. If the police around.", "annotation_id": "13922191", "url": "https://genius.com/13922191", "state": "verified", "votes": 38, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Look Alive", "line": "My—my—my weapon be a instrument I’ll blow you like a flute (Rrah)", "vault_lines": ["My—my—my weapon be a instrument", "I'll blow you like a flute (Rrah)"], "meaning": "In nine hood we’ve got a whole lot of weapons. It’s quick to get it blown away. I’ve got a gun. I’ll blow you away just like an instrument. If you blow it, any instrument that you blow in, you know what it is. Flute, you blow in a flute, you can blow into a trumpet. I just choose flute.", "annotation_id": "13922187", "url": "https://genius.com/13922187", "state": "verified", "votes": 48, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Look Alive", "line": "I’ma get the money (Word) Dr—Dr—Drizzy get the loot (The loot)", "vault_lines": ["I'ma get the money (Word)", "Dr—Dr—Drizzy get the loot (The loot)"], "meaning": "That’s my guy. He fucking with me the long ways, just like my brother. We like family.", "annotation_id": "13922170", "url": "https://genius.com/13922170", "state": "verified", "votes": 98, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Look Alive", "line": "I get racks to go outside and I split it with the guys (Outside)", "vault_lines": ["I get racks to go outside and I split it with the guys (Outside)"], "meaning": "Drake has grossed hundreds of millions of dollars in his career so far. He makes money for nearly anything he does. He splits it with his team (October’s Very Own), friends and family, and as seen in “God’s Plan” Music Video he also gives back to the community.", "annotation_id": "13906391", "url": "https://genius.com/13906391", "state": "accepted", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Look Alive", "line": "Shot to the chest have you gaspin’ for oxygen (Shots) I’ma spray ’em, just like Febreze (Huh, like Febreze)", "vault_lines": ["Shot to the chest have you gaspin' for oxygen (Shots)", "I'ma spray 'em, just like Febreze (Huh, like Febreze)"], "meaning": "Febreze is a brand that produces air fresheners and odor-eliminating products. Their most popular product, Febreze “Air” functions by pressing and holding the trigger which releases the odor-removing scents. BlocBoy JB is comparing this to the firing of a gun which he also describes as ‘spraying’ bullets.", "annotation_id": "13824331", "url": "https://genius.com/13824331", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Look Alive", "line": "This fuckin’ industry is cutthroat I’m not the same, man,", "vault_lines": ["Man, I'm not to blame, man, this fuckin' industry is cutthroat", "I'm not the same, man,"], "meaning": "Drake has a history of mistrust with the music industry. He’s made this clear earlier in his career, notably on 2015’s “You & The 6”:\n\nI pull the knife out my back and I cut the​ throat with it, momma\n\nThis line describes the vindictive nature of the rap industry and underlines how it affects the artists within it by forcing them to change and adapt to a very isolated world at the top.\n\nThe state of rap music and the music industry, in general, has a been common theme in Drake’s outlook on music and life in the later years. He “recently” dwelled upon the many attempts to discredit him during one of his rare interview appearances with DJ Semtex in 2017:\n\nhttps://youtu.be/vGTBc84iV7M?t=1795", "annotation_id": "13823324", "url": "https://genius.com/13823324", "state": "accepted", "votes": 24, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Look Alive", "line": "Pu—pull up broad day with a K, now he shiverin’ (He shiverin’)", "vault_lines": ["Pu—pull up broad day with a K, now he shiverin' (He shiverin')"], "meaning": "BlocBoy is referring to an AK-47, which is commonly shortened to AK or K in this case. He details how he’d very blatantly pull up in broad daylight with his gun and make someone “shiver” or shake out of fear.\n\n\n\nThis also ties in with the line several bars before when he mentions his Draco.", "annotation_id": "13823051", "url": "https://genius.com/13823051", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Look Alive", "line": "Came a long way from sittin’ in the nosebleeds (In the nosebleeds)", "vault_lines": ["Came a long way from sittin' in the nosebleeds (In the nosebleeds)"], "meaning": "The nosebleeds are used to classify the back row seats in a Stadium or concerts because of how high up they are in a Stadium\n\nThese seats are usually the cheapest and have the worst view out of all the seats in a venue.\n\nBlocBoy’s success in the rap game has given him the money to purchase court-side view seats, which he couldn’t afford in the past.", "annotation_id": "13822919", "url": "https://genius.com/13822919", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Look Alive", "line": "Pu—pu—pull up with that Draco (Huh?) Play with Drake and I’ma shoot (That’s on my mama)", "vault_lines": ["Pu—pu—pull up with that Draco (Huh?)", "Play with Drake and I'ma shoot (That's on my mama)"], "meaning": "A “Draco,” made popular in America by Soulja Boy, is the nickname for a Romanian variant of a Kalashnikov Model 1947. The \"Draco”, features a shorter barrel and gas tube than the AK-47, but also fires 7.62x39mm bullets.\n\nBoth 21 Savage and Kodak Black have name-dropped it in their lyrics, with Future naming a song after the gun:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OnhXkCPMeMc\n\nBlocBoy is also talking to the opposition, both in the “rap game” and real life: saying that he could fire back, with lyrics or bullets. This may also reference Blocboy’s “trademark dance” which is known as the shoot.", "annotation_id": "13812191", "url": "https://genius.com/13812191", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Look Alive", "line": "6 God, BlocBoy, 6 God, BlocBoy (Ooh) (Word) 6 God, BlocBoy, 6 God, BlocBoy (Ooh) (BlocBoy, 6 God)", "vault_lines": ["6 God, BlocBoy, 6 God, BlocBoy (Ooh) (Word)"], "meaning": "“The 6” is a nickname Drake gave his home city, Toronto, as 416 and 647 are area codes of Toronto, Ontario, Canada. He’s even got it tatted on him:\n\n\n\nDrake has referred to himself as the “6 God” many times in the past, even naming one of his songs from If You’re Reading This It’s Too Late after it.\n\nHe also shouts out BlocBoy JB, the main artist of this song.", "annotation_id": "13812119", "url": "https://genius.com/13812119", "state": "accepted", "votes": 79, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Look Alive", "line": "I’m only chasin’ after bags now I got a game plan and I’m out here with the woo!", "vault_lines": ["I'm only chasin' after bags now", "I got a game plan and I'm out here with the woo!"], "meaning": "Drake seemingly has a thought-out plan for 2018 and is doing nothing less than chasing the money.\n\nHe mentions this plan in the final lines of “Do Not Disturb” on his previously released album, More Life:\n\nTakin' summer off, ‘cause they tell me I need recovery\nMaybe gettin’ back to my regular life will humble me\nI’ll be back in 2018 to give you the summary", "annotation_id": "13809620", "url": "https://genius.com/13809620", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Look Alive", "line": "If I fucked up, I’ma be downtown, man Fourth floor bound, man, that’s if I get caught, man Pushed me to the edge, so it really ain’t my mothafuckin’ fault", "vault_lines": ["If I fucked up, I'ma be downtown, man", "Fourth floor bound, man, that's if I get caught, man", "Pushed me to the edge, so it really ain't my mothafuckin' fault", "I'ma get the money (Word)"], "meaning": "These lines are derived from Project Pat’s “Out There,” a song from his debut album, Ghetty Green:\n\nProject Pat, a nigga that’s down for his crown mane\nIf you​' ass step, I'ma be downtown mane\nFourth floor bound mane, that’s if I get caught mane\nPushed me to the edge, so it really ain’t my fault mane\n\nThe use of these lines was likely inspired by both Drake and BlocBoy JB’s ties to Memphis, the birthplace of Project Pat.\n\nThis isn’t the first time Drake has lifted a large portion of lyrics from another song. On YG’s 2014 single, “Who Do You Love,” Drake recited four lines from Rappin' 4-Tay’s “Playaz Club.”", "annotation_id": "13807449", "url": "https://genius.com/13807449", "state": "accepted", "votes": 102, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Look Alive", "line": "’Cause I told them that we put that shit behind us but I lied (Hah)", "vault_lines": ["'Cause I told them that we put that shit behind us but I lied (Hah)", "'Cause I told them that we put that shit behind us but I— (Hah)", "'Cause I told them to put that shit behind us but I lied (Hah)"], "meaning": "Drake holds grudges. Since the windfall of his highly public beef with Meek Mill has died down, Drake started to rap about settling his beefs for the good of all of the parties involved, but deep down he neither forgives nor forgets.\n\nHe rapped about a similar sentiment on “9” from his Views album:\n\nYou know 40 wants peace\nBut I’m down to cut ties for it", "annotation_id": "13806091", "url": "https://genius.com/13806091", "state": "accepted", "votes": 72, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Look Alive", "line": "They won’t be expectin’ shit when Capo go to slide (Hah)", "vault_lines": ["They won't be expectin' shit when Capo go to slide (Hah)"], "meaning": "Drake’s probably referring to Capo from Halal Gang in Toronto. Capo is friends with Halal Gang’s Smoke Dawg, Puffy L'z, and SAFE, who have been cosigned by Drake. MTV mentioned the gang in their 2016 piece “Toronto World: Drake, Halal Gang, and the Diaspora in the 6”:\n\nThe division that springs out of kids' departure from their parents' traditions is the space, place, and time that Halal Gang, made up of rappers Puffy L’z, Smoke Dawg, Mo-G, and SAFE, was formed. The use of the word halal, which means lawful in Arabic, is an homage to their Muslim roots. Halal Gang’s members are residents of Regent Park, a Downtown neighborhood where many East Africans and Caribbean people reside. SAFE is Eritrean; Smoke Dawg is Jamaican; both Puffy and Mo are Somali; all are practicing Muslims. Mo-G and SAFE are the group’s most prominent members, the ones who can rightfully claim that they’ve been cosigned by Drake.", "annotation_id": "13805598", "url": "https://genius.com/13805598", "state": "accepted", "votes": 58, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Look Alive", "line": "And I could let you check the tag now I’m rockin’ name brand,", "vault_lines": ["and I could let you check the tag now", "I'm rockin' name brand,", "You and you (You)"], "meaning": "Drake’s got nothing to hide when it comes to his wealth—he’ll even let you check the tag on his clothes to see he only wears name brands. For example, in the music video for this song, Drake is seen rocking a rare, vintage Ralph Lauren Polo Sport x NASA Anorak from 1992.\n\n\n\nDrake was also sponsored by Prada on the Boy Meets World tour.", "annotation_id": "13805369", "url": "https://genius.com/13805369", "state": "accepted", "votes": 50, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Look Alive", "line": "I’ve been gone since, like, July, niggas actin’ like I died", "vault_lines": ["I've been gone since, like, July, niggas actin' like I died"], "meaning": "With the release of Drake’s More Life album in March of 2017, Drake left everyone with some pretty detailed closure lyrics on the project’s 22nd and final track, “Do Not Disturb”:\n\nTakin' summer off, ‘cause they tell me I need recovery\nMaybe gettin’ back to my regular life will humble me\nI’ll be back in 2018 to give you the summary\n\nIn late June 2017, Drake released his single “Signs,” and also took part in Metro Boomin’s single released that same month entitled “No Complaints.” Both would be his last work under his name before disappearing from the music scene all the way up until January 2018 with the release of both “God’s Plan” and “Diplomatic Immunity” under the header Scary Hours.\n\nIt’s also worth noting several media outlets such as Billboard and HotNewHipHop were reporting that fact that Drake fell off the Billboard Hot 100 chart for the first time since 2009. This led to some fans to see this as the decline of Drake’s musical career and sparked rumors of his retirement.", "annotation_id": "13803819", "url": "https://genius.com/13803819", "state": "accepted", "votes": 140, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Parade on Cleveland", "status": "done", "targets": 17, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Young-thug-parade-on-cleveland-lyrics", "genius_title": "Parade on Cleveland", "genius_id": 9263017, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Parade on Cleveland", "line": "[Part II]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This part was actually recorded over a jail phone, due to Young Thug being locked up since May of 2022.\n\nWith the help of frequent collaborator, Metro Boomin, and Bainz, they made it sound like studio vocals.\n\nBainz was the one to announce and play the raw vocals live, as people were doubting that Young Thug’s vocals were actually recorded over a jail phone.", "annotation_id": "32997564", "url": "https://genius.com/32997564", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Parade on Cleveland", "line": "Sun’s up, I ain’t sleep, I been countin’ stacks", "vault_lines": ["Sun's up, I ain't sleep, I been countin' stacks"], "meaning": "This line is a metaphor for young thug’s career. The “sun” refers to young thug’s success, prosperity and labels. Sleep would mean to be lazy, which young thug wouldn’t do, as he has consistently put out singles, mixtapes, and albums throughout his career. Counting stacks refers to the above mentioned projects and the creation of them.\n\nBeing slept on is a common term for people not listening to your music, or not liking your music, so by saying that he didn’t sleep, he is saying that everyone loves him.\n\nAdditionally, drug dealers and gangsters have been known to weigh their money instead of simply counting it, so by saying that he is counting stacks, he is distancing himself from his charges of drugs, and gang related activity, saying that he made this money from legitimate means.", "annotation_id": "32695033", "url": "https://genius.com/32695033", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Parade on Cleveland", "line": "After we fuck, she told her friends, “Bitch, it’s crackin’” Made a jail call to your bitch, she say you down", "vault_lines": ["After we fuck, she told her friends, \"Bitch, it's crackin'\"", "Made a jail call to your bitch, she say you down"], "meaning": "“After we fuck, she told her friends, ‘Bitch, it’s crackin’”\n\nYoung Thug is describing a scenario where after he engages in sexual activity with a woman, she enthusiastically informs her friends about the encounter. The phrase “bitch, it’s crackin'” suggests that she’s excited and eager to share the news, indicating that the experience was enjoyable and noteworthy for her. This line underscores Young Thug’s sexual prowess and the positive impression he leaves on his partners.\n\n“Made a jail call to your bitch, she say you down”\n\nIn this line, Young Thug describes a situation where he contacts another man’s romantic partner while the man is incarcerated. The phrase “jail call” indicates that the man is in prison, and Young Thug is reaching out to his girlfriend or wife. The woman’s response, “she say you down,” implies that she’s willing to engage with Young Thug romantically or sexually while her partner is unavailable, suggesting infidelity or disloyalty on her part. This line highlights themes of betrayal, competition, and Young Thug’s ability to attract and seduce women, even when they’re already in relationships.", "annotation_id": "31039101", "url": "https://genius.com/31039101", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Parade on Cleveland", "line": "All the dawgs,", "vault_lines": ["All the pythons, all the vipers"], "meaning": "Drake might give a subtle hint at his upcoming album, For All The Dogs that hasn’t been given a release date. Or he (talking as young thug), might want to see his dawgs when he gets out of the RICO case, his YSL labelmates.", "annotation_id": "28960995", "url": "https://genius.com/28960995", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Parade on Cleveland", "line": "Michael Kors robe, mm-mm, nah, Michael Jackson", "vault_lines": ["Michael Kors robe, mm-mm, nah, Michael Jackson"], "meaning": "Michael Kors is a fashion company, and Young Thug states that is wearing a Michael Kors robe.", "annotation_id": "28944323", "url": "https://genius.com/28944323", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Parade on Cleveland", "line": "Spider back, I’m a big dawg, you a cat", "vault_lines": ["Spider back, I'm a big dawg, you a cat"], "meaning": "“Spider,” or “King Spider” is a popular moniker given to Young Thug by himself as he noted in his Big Boy Interview that the moniker represents how his oppositions don’t want to be caught in his metaphorical web.\n\nFurthermore, Thugger refers to himself as a “big dawg” suggesting he’s aggressive and has a low tolerance for nonsense while he simultaneously notes that oppositions are a cat — a statistically more submissive and less superior breed.\n\nThis could also pay homage to his appearance on Metro Boomin’s December 2022, “Metro Spider” in which he suggested that he’s superior to his opposition as he rapped:\n\nSpider, spider, spider, please dismiss these writers, yeah", "annotation_id": "28889930", "url": "https://genius.com/28889930", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Parade on Cleveland", "line": "Business is business, you owe me this time", "vault_lines": ["Business is business, business is business, business is business", "Business is business, business is business, yeah", "Business is business, business is business", "Business is business, you owe me this time"], "meaning": "“You owe me this time” was the lyric Drake chose to tease in the caption of his Instagram post of the BUSINESS IS BUSINESS cover artwork on June 22, 2023.\n\nThug responded in the post’s comments:\n\n\n\nThe pair are having a friendly back in forth, likely referring to their lengthy history of appearing on one another’s albums.", "annotation_id": "28888872", "url": "https://genius.com/28888872", "state": "accepted", "votes": 35, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Parade on Cleveland", "line": "Uh, I ain’t doin’ shit, man Just pushin’ more Peter, more sweeter, more completer Than any Peter pusher around See what I’m sayin’, twin? Ha (Ha-ha-ha)", "vault_lines": ["Uh, I ain't doin' shit, man", "Just pushin' more Peter, more sweeter, more completer", "Than any Peter pusher around", "See what I'm sayin', twin? Ha (Ha-ha-ha)"], "meaning": "Young Thug is referencing a line spoken by the character Shane Patton in the 2013 film Lone Survivor:\n\nI pushed more Peter, more sweeter, and more completer than any other Peter pusher around.\n\nThis is likely a subtle diss toward Thug’s frequent collaborator Gunna, who pleaded guilty during the RICO case they had both been involved in since May 9, 2022. Gunna was released from jail on December 14, 2022, while Thug remained imprisoned.\n\nThis could also be a subtle nod to Gunna, Thug, and Future’s January 2022 hit “pushin P,” with “Peter” substituting for “P.”", "annotation_id": "28881072", "url": "https://genius.com/28881072", "state": "pending", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Parade on Cleveland", "line": "I’m comin’ home I’m comin’ home", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Still in the perspective of Thugger, Drake states that Thug will come home and beat this case.\n\nThug has been incarcerated since May 9th of 2022 and his trial is still ongoing as of the release of this album.", "annotation_id": "28880140", "url": "https://genius.com/28880140", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Parade on Cleveland", "line": "Actually, I been trapped in, but I took a black bitch to Beverly Hills Now she white, Michael Jackson", "vault_lines": ["Actually, I been trapped in, but I took a black bitch to Beverly Hills", "Now she white, Michael Jackson"], "meaning": "Young Thug could be saying how Beverly Hills, a city located in Los Angeles County, California, can change a person’s culture and style.\n\nThe racial markup for the largest racial/ethnic group who currently reside in Beverly Hills are White, with an estimated percentage of 77.8%.\n\nWhen Thugger brought the black woman to Beverly Hills, and unfamiliar with the culture and community with mostly White people, eventually it grew to her and she ended up turning “White”. Hence, the reference to the iconic pop star, Michael Jackson, who had a skin transition he went through due to a skin disorder, Vitiligo.\n\n\n\nPictured: Michael Jackson’s skin tone transition", "annotation_id": "28876490", "url": "https://genius.com/28876490", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Parade on Cleveland", "line": "Business is business, business is business, business is business Business is business, business is business, yeah Business is business, business is business, business is business Business is business, business is business, yeah Business is business, business is business, business is business Business is business, business is business, yeah Business is business, business is business, business is business Business is business, business is business", "vault_lines": ["Business is business, business is business, business is business", "Business is business, business is business, yeah", "Business is business, business is business", "Business is business, you owe me this time"], "meaning": "In addition to promoting his album’s name, Young Thug’s repetition of “business is business” reinforces his profit-oriented thinking and effort to distinguish between personal and business matters.\n\nIn May of 2022, Thug was arrested and indicted on a slew of charges that name him as the leader of the Young Slime Life (YSL) criminal street gang. Twenty-six affiliates of Young Thug were also charged, most notably artists Gunna, Slimelife Shawty, and Lil Duke who are signed to Thug’s Young Stoner Life Records. Thug awaits trial while members of his music label have accepted plea agreements.\n\nOne week before the release of BUSINESS IS BUSINESS, Gunna released a Gift & a Curse under YSL records, his first album since accepting an Alford plea agreement in the trial. He and Lil Baby previously collaborated on the track “Business Is Business” on their 2018 joint project, Drip Harder, also released through YSL.", "annotation_id": "28876350", "url": "https://genius.com/28876350", "state": "accepted", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Parade on Cleveland", "line": "Metro", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This is one of American Record producer Metro Boomin’s many producer tags. It is voiced by Atlanta rapper Young Thug, with whom Metro Boomin has collaborated with numerous times throughout their careers, including on the tracks Metro Spider & Trance, both of which are on his second solo studio album, HEROES & VILLAINS. This tag debuted on Young Thug’s 2015 track, “Hercules.”", "annotation_id": "28876088", "url": "https://genius.com/28876088", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Parade on Cleveland", "line": "How the fuck you out here goin’ tit for tat? (Tit for tat)", "vault_lines": ["How the fuck you out here goin' tit for tat? (Tit for tat)"], "meaning": "“Tit for tat” is slang for hurting people intentionally after having previously injured them before, quite the same meaning as “retaliation.”\n\nDrake previously used this slang in his Link Up TV July 2018 freestyle “Behind Barz (Link Up TV Freestyle)”:\n\nAll that bark but we know he’s a cat\nI don’t really like goin' tit for tat", "annotation_id": "28875995", "url": "https://genius.com/28875995", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Parade on Cleveland", "line": "Hello, this is a prepaid call from Jeffery An inmate at the Cobb county adult detention facility", "vault_lines": ["Hello, this is a prepaid call from Jeffery", "An inmate at the Cobb county adult detention facility"], "meaning": "Young Thug, whose real name Jeffery Lamar Williams, was detained at the release of this song in 2023 at Cobb County Adult Detention Center. This recording is from the collect-call system in place.", "annotation_id": "28875940", "url": "https://genius.com/28875940", "state": "accepted", "votes": 48, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Parade on Cleveland", "line": "Ayy, soon as I’m fresh out the box like a Tic-Tac", "vault_lines": ["Ayy, soon as I'm fresh out the box like a Tic-Tac"], "meaning": "Here, Drake plays on the homonym “box.” “Box” is slang for a prison, therefore Drake is comparing Young Thug getting out of the box (prison) to how you take a Tic-Tac out of its box (container) in order to consume them.\n\n\n\nThugger has been in “the box” since May 9th 2022 after he and his YSL Crew were charged for a multitude of crimes. It has not yet been confirmed when Thug will be fresh out the box.\n\n\nDrake supporting Young Thug and YSL as he pleads “Free YSL” at a show of his.", "annotation_id": "28875939", "url": "https://genius.com/28875939", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Parade on Cleveland", "line": "Parade on Bleveland soon as I get home", "vault_lines": ["Parade on Blevеland soon as I get home", "Parade, parade on Bleveland soon as I get home"], "meaning": "Cleveland Ave. is where Young Thug and YSL spent time. Drake’s verse is written from the perspective of Jeffery, where he is saying that when he is free, he wishes to throw a parade in his community.\n\nIn order to refer to the “Bloods” version of a word, people will swap Cs for Bs. This results in Drake rapping Bleveland, instead of the proper street name, Cleveland Avenue.", "annotation_id": "28875921", "url": "https://genius.com/28875921", "state": "accepted", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Parade on Cleveland", "line": "Slime on your head, Nickelodeon time", "vault_lines": ["Slime on your head, Nickelodeon time"], "meaning": "Nickelodeon hosts its annual Kids' Choice Awards where the winners get green slime dumped on them.", "annotation_id": "28875881", "url": "https://genius.com/28875881", "state": "accepted", "votes": 43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
