{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wavin’ Flag", "line": "When I get older, when I get older I will be stronger, just like a waving flag", "vault_lines": ["When I get older", "When I get older, I will be stronger", "I will be stronger", "Just like a waving flag", "When I get older, when I get older", "I will be stronger, just like a waving flag"], "meaning": "These lyrics, although sung by a variety of different artists, are the same as the original, click here for an explanation!", "annotation_id": "2550243", "url": "https://genius.com/2550243", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wavin’ Flag", "line": "[Intro: All Artists] When I get older I will be stronger They’ll call me freedom Just like a waving flag [Verse 1: K’naan, Nelly Furtado, Sam Roberts & Arvil Lavigne] Born from a throne, older than Rome But violent prone, poor people zone But it’s my home, all I have known Where I got grown, but now it’s gone Out of the darkness, in came the carnage Threatening my very survival [Verse 2: Pierre Bouvier & Tyler Connolly] Fractured my streets and broke all my dreams Now feels like defeat to wretched retreat [Pre-Chorus: All Artists, Kardinal Offishall & Jully Black] So we struggling Fighting to eat And we wondering If we’ll be free We can not wait for some faithful day It’s too far away so right now I’ll say [Chorus: All Artists] When I get older, I will be stronger They’ll call me freedom, just like a waving flag And then it goes back, and then it goes back And then it goes back [Verse 2: Lights, Deryck Whibley, Serena Ryder & Jacob Hoggard] So many wars, settling scores All that we’ve been through and now there is more I hear them say love is the way Love is the answer that’s what they say [Verse 3: Emily Haines, Hawsley Workman, Drake & Chin Inteji] But were not just dreamers of broken down grievers A hand will reach us and will not forsake us This can’t control us, no it can’t hold us down We gon’ pick it up even though we still— [Pre-Chorus: Pierre Lapointe, All Artists, Fefe Dobson & Estherro] Struggling Au nom de la survie And we wondering Battant pour nos vie We patiently wait for some other day That’s too far away so right now I say [Chorus: All Artists & Drake] When I get older, I will be stronger They’ll call me freedom, just like a waving flag And then it goes back, and then it goes back And then it goes back When I get older, I will be stronger They’ll call me freedom, just like a waving flag And then it goes back, (Uh) and then it goes back (Well alright) And then it goes back", "vault_lines": ["When I get older", "Threatening my very survival", "Fractured my streets and broke all my dreams", "Now feels like defeat to wretched retreat", "If we'll be free", "We can not wait for some faithful day", "It's too far away so right now I'll say", "When I get older, I will be stronger", "I will be stronger", "They'll call me freedom, just like a waving flag", "And then it goes back, and then it goes back", "And then it goes back", "So many wars, settling scores", "All that we've been through and now there is more", "I hear them say love is the way", "Love is the answer that's what they say", "But were not just dreamers of broken down grievers", "A hand will reach us and will not forsake us", "This can't control us, no it can't hold us down", "They'll call me freedom", "We gon' pick it up even though we still—", "Au nom de la survie", "Battant pour nos vie", "We patiently wait for some other day", "That's too far away so right now I say", "We forget about the people still struggling", "Just like a waving flag", "You probably think that it's too far to even have to care", "And we can be the reason that they see their flag rise again", "Then it goes back", "When I get older, when I get older", "I will be stronger, just like a waving flag", "Born from a throne, older than Rome", "But violent prone, poor people zone", "But it's my home, all I have known", "Where I got grown, but now it's gone", "Out of the darkness, in came the carnage"], "meaning": "These lyrics, although sung by a variety of different artists are the same as the original, click here for an annotation!", "annotation_id": "2543011", "url": "https://genius.com/2543011", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wavin’ Flag", "line": "And assume that its really all love again, nah", "vault_lines": ["And assume that its really all love again, nah"], "meaning": "After Haiti’s earthquake there was a lot of media attention, everybody had there eye’s on the country’s situation. But, like all trends it was soon completely forgotten. Here Drake reminds us that just because you might no hear about Haiti’s situation as frequently as before it does not mean that everything is al right over there.", "annotation_id": "164235", "url": "https://genius.com/164235", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wavin’ Flag", "line": "[Chorus: Nikki Yanofsky & Drake, Matt Mays, Justin Nozuka] When I get older, I will be stronger They’ll call me freedom, just like a waving flag And then it goes back And then it goes back Then it goes back [Chorus: All Artists] When I get older, I will be stronger They’ll call me freedom, just like a waving flag And then it goes back, and then it goes back And then it goes back", "vault_lines": ["When I get older", "When I get older, I will be stronger", "I will be stronger", "They'll call me freedom, just like a waving flag", "And then it goes back, and then it goes back", "And then it goes back", "They'll call me freedom", "Just like a waving flag", "Then it goes back", "When I get older, when I get older", "I will be stronger, just like a waving flag"], "meaning": "The girl who sang for the Vancouver Winter Olympics official soundtrack.", "annotation_id": "124546", "url": "https://genius.com/124546", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
