{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "We In This Bitch 1.5", "line": "That girl don’t speak no Englo, but she know all my lingo", "vault_lines": ["That girl don't speak no Englo, but she know all my lingo"], "meaning": "The girl that Future is with is not fluent in English, but she still knows all the trap jargon.", "annotation_id": "1293550", "url": "https://genius.com/1293550", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "We In This Bitch 1.5", "line": "It should’ve been a designer party, all these designer round me Pick a name, anything, money can buy what?", "vault_lines": ["It should've been a designer party, all these designer round me", "Pick a name, anything, money can buy what?"], "meaning": "Double meaning:\n\n\n\n\nDesigner both refers to designer clothes brand such as Gucci, LV, Prada etc.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAnd it refers to designer drugs such as escasty, molly, MDMA, Salt bath, etc.\n\n\n\nSo when Future talks about designer parties – it can either be actually designers  products or drugs (or both?), and since we know he knows a lot about both things, both are quite possible.", "annotation_id": "1043829", "url": "https://genius.com/1043829", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "act ii: date @ 8 (remix)", "status": "done", "targets": 6, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/4batz-and-drake-act-ii-date-at-8-remix-lyrics", "genius_title": "act ii: date @ 8 (remix)", "genius_id": 10132312, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "act ii: date @ 8 (remix)", "line": "I’ll make them open up Chanel, ch-ch", "vault_lines": ["I'll make them open up Chanel, ch-ch"], "meaning": "Chanel is a luxury brand Drake is known for gifting to his ladies frequently. Drake reportedly had a Chanel bag claw machine at his birthday party back in 2023.\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/Cy9bzALPVes/?hl=en", "annotation_id": "36295992", "url": "https://genius.com/36295992", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "act ii: date @ 8 (remix)", "line": "Almost said I loved your ass right after we fucked Don’t know why, girl, it was on the tip of my tongue", "vault_lines": ["Almost said I loved your ass right after we fucked", "Don't know why, girl, it was on the tip of my tongue"], "meaning": "Drake is saying he nearly said (“on the tip of his tongue”) I love you after him and his partner had sex. This is common after hooking up, where some people have feelings so strong they want to say I love you. In this context it reaffirms Drake’s affection toward this woman. However, the first line juxtaposed with the second line adds a different meaning of Drake possibly saying the special three words directly to this girl’s butt since it was just on…the tip of his tongue.", "annotation_id": "36085857", "url": "https://genius.com/36085857", "state": "pending", "votes": -1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "act ii: date @ 8 (remix)", "line": "What did I do to deserve you? Don’t even know what I did Been prayin’ on it since a kid", "vault_lines": ["What did I do to deserve you?", "Don’t even know what I did", "Been prayin' on it since a kid"], "meaning": "NAH DRAKE", "annotation_id": "32560566", "url": "https://genius.com/32560566", "state": "pending", "votes": -17, "second_sense": false, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "act ii: date @ 8 (remix)", "line": "What kinda water they servin’ in Clayco? This is me talkin’, it’s not the añejo", "vault_lines": ["What kinda water they servin' in Clayco?", "This is me talkin', it's not the añejo"], "meaning": "This line is a shoutout to Clayton County, GA (ClayCo) known for artist Latto. Drake here is likely alluding to Latto’s sister Brooklyn Nikole\n\nIn 2024, it was rumored Drake and Brookyln were dating\n\nThis line is a reference to the phrase “There must be something in the water.” It’s often used to suggest that there’s something unusual happening within group of people. In this case the women in Clayco are naturally beautiful.\n\nAñejo is a specialty tequila typically brown. Drake here is expressing to Brooklyn that he really means what he says and it’s not the liquor talking.\n\nThe liquor in question here is most likely Don Julio 1942 Añejo Tequila as Drake often raps about the brand \nOne-nine-four-two hits my system, man get way too frosty, buzzy― Headie One & Drake – Only You Freestyle", "annotation_id": "31117226", "url": "https://genius.com/31117226", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "act ii: date @ 8 (remix)", "line": "I really gotta calm down ’Fore I end up in jeopardy just like the game show", "vault_lines": ["I really gotta calm down", "’Fore I end up in jeopardy just like the game show"], "meaning": "Being in “jeopardy” means to be in danger or at risk of death, while Jeopardy! is a classic television game show where contestants are given clues about a specific topic and they must identify what the clue describes. Drake refers to the actions that he’s done and that they may result in him being in danger or result in his death, which he once contemplated in 2011’s “We’ll Be Fine,” where he rapped:\n\nNever thoughts of suicide, I’m too alive\nBut I still treat it like it’s do or die\nEven though dying isn’t in the plans\nBut neither was making it, and here I am", "annotation_id": "31106774", "url": "https://genius.com/31106774", "state": "pending", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "act ii: date @ 8 (remix)", "line": "I’m a stand-up guy like Dave Chappelle", "vault_lines": ["I'm a stand-up guy like Dave Chappelle"], "meaning": "Drake employs a double entendre by referencing American stand-up comedian, Dave Chappelle, and then refers to himself as a “stand-up guy,” which is an informal term for one who is honest and straightforward.\n\nDrake and Dave Chappelle also once met in 2021, being seen in this picture together:", "annotation_id": "31092703", "url": "https://genius.com/31092703", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bigger Than You", "status": "done", "targets": 21, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/2-chainz-bigger-than-you-lyrics", "genius_title": "Bigger Than You", "genius_id": 3782528, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bigger Than You", "line": "You set it off like Cleo, I set it off like Boosie", "vault_lines": ["You set it off like Cleo, I set it off like Boosie"], "meaning": "2 Chainz here is making two references. One to the 1996 film Set It Off and another to Lil Boosie’s famous song titled  “ Set It Off”.  One of the characters in the film is named Cleo who is played by Queen Latifah.", "annotation_id": "17228892", "url": "https://genius.com/17228892", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bigger Than You", "line": "Barely came up out the mud like quicksand (barely)", "vault_lines": ["Barely came up out the mud like quicksand (barely)"], "meaning": "2 Chainz uses some clever wordplay in referring to quicksand, which is a pit of loose sand, silt, dirt, clay, etc. mixed with water which attributes the mixture with some of the properties of a liquid instead of being completely solid meaning you can sink and actually drown in quicksand if you struggle too much (although it is uncommon). “Mud” is also commonly used to describe a rough neighborhood where one was raised. Tity Boi used to be in the “mud” and “quicksand” and had to live through the “struggle”, but he made it out.", "annotation_id": "14819314", "url": "https://genius.com/14819314", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bigger Than You", "line": "Chain so big, should have came with a kick stand", "vault_lines": ["Chain so big, should have came with a kick stand"], "meaning": "2 Chainz is implying that his necklace is so big it resembles the chain of a bicycle that is normally placed beside the kickstand.", "annotation_id": "14812506", "url": "https://genius.com/14812506", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bigger Than You", "line": "I just bought a watch that’s plain like a Dickie suit (Plain)", "vault_lines": ["I just bought a watch that's plain like a Dickie suit (Plain)"], "meaning": "2 Chainz just bought a watch with no diamonds on it, commonly referred as “plain jane”.\n\nDickies is a company popular for workwear and has been very popular in hip-hop especially on the west coast scene since the late 80s.", "annotation_id": "14805180", "url": "https://genius.com/14805180", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bigger Than You", "line": "Quavo Sinatra, but we could never be the Rat Pack, nigga, naw", "vault_lines": ["Quavo Sinatra, but we could never be the Rat Pack, nigga, naw"], "meaning": "“Quavo Sinatra” is one of Quavo’s many nicknames, and was first used on Sean Paul’s track “Body”, featuring Migos:\n\nI wanna sing to her, Quavo Sinatra (brrr)\n\nDrake is referring to Frank Sinatra’s group, the Rat Pack, and implying that it would be impossible for Quavo, 2 Chainz, and himself to be as influential as that group.\n\nThis is not the first time Drake references Frank Sinatra, on his track “5 Am in Toronto” he rapped:\n\nSinatra lifestyle, I’m just bein’ frank with ya\n\n\n\nThis may be a reference to Logic–nicknamed Young Sinatra, he and his crew make up the RattPack, which stands for Real All The Time. Logic recently opened up about his love for Drake:\n\nDrake doesn’t realize, in many ways, he was like the big brother I never had. He set the example and paved the way for me to be myself. Now, whether I’m at the Grammys or whether I’m here or there, or whatever, he’ll show me love…People don’t realize what that’s like, what that means.", "annotation_id": "14804559", "url": "https://genius.com/14804559", "state": "accepted", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bigger Than You", "line": "Uh, yeah, I bought a ’Claren (Woo) I bought a ’Claren, didn’t wanna buy verts, uh", "vault_lines": ["Uh, yeah, I bought a 'Claren (Woo)", "I bought a 'Claren, didn't wanna buy verts, uh"], "meaning": "McLaren is a British car manufacturer best known for their luxurious sports cars.\n\nQuavo purchased a white McLaren 720s supercar, which costs around $360k, in late 2017. After his purchase, Quavo posted a picture of the car on his Instagram, where he stated to be the only rapper owning this type of vehicle.\n\n\n\nTo end the lines, Quavo says that he wouldn’t want to buy “verts”, which is a term used to describe a convertible car.", "annotation_id": "14804440", "url": "https://genius.com/14804440", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bigger Than You", "line": "Fuck with me, I got a retainer on a hit man (bop)", "vault_lines": ["Fuck with me, I got a retainer on a hit man (bop)"], "meaning": "‘Hitman’ is a term used to refer to a contract killer. In this line, 2 Chainz says if there is any trouble, he already has a down payment on a killer who will complete the job at a moments notice. A retainer is a fee paid  to someone in advance to secure their services when necessary.", "annotation_id": "14797461", "url": "https://genius.com/14797461", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bigger Than You", "line": "Half a million out in Vegas, it ain’t no blackjack, nigga, naw (Naw)", "vault_lines": ["Half a million out in Vegas, it ain't no blackjack, nigga, naw (Naw)"], "meaning": "Drake has been spotted in Vegas on multiple occasions most likely spending millions.\n\nBlackjack is a relatively easy game to play and is basically down to luck. Drake’s saying he isn’t playing blackjack because he feels he’s too good for it or its too easy. This could be a metaphor for him not playing with (rapping with) the basic (Blackjack) rappers in the game because he’s too good for them. He could also be saying that the rappers he doesn’t fuck with only got into the rap game through luck", "annotation_id": "14796547", "url": "https://genius.com/14796547", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bigger Than You", "line": "Touchscreen on my cars, vintage one to two", "vault_lines": ["Touchscreen on my cars, vintage one to two"], "meaning": "2 Chainz owns several cars, one of them being a 2017 Tesla S.\n\n\n\nHigh-end cars like the Tesla Model S and another of his cars, the Rhino GX have touchscreen control panels in the center console.\n\n\n\nChainz also mentions here his “vintage” cars, one of which is his Aston Martin Rapide.", "annotation_id": "14795633", "url": "https://genius.com/14795633", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bigger Than You", "line": "[Intro: Quavo & 2 Chainz]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "In late 2017, during a club appearance in Washington D.C., Quavo previewed a remix of Travis Scott’s “Butterfly Effect.”\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o3r9TTNSjmo\n\nAlthough the song was never released, Quavo has utilized some of the lyrics originally intended for the remix to fill out the intro, chorus, and outro of “Bigger Than You.”", "annotation_id": "14793173", "url": "https://genius.com/14793173", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bigger Than You", "line": "Uh, yeah, baller alert Lil biddy bitch I don’t call her alert (Brrrrp)", "vault_lines": ["Lil biddy bitch I don't call her alert (Brrrrp)"], "meaning": "BallerAlert, which was started in 2008, is a website that links gold diggers and TMZ.\n\nThe service started as a text message alert system that would notify users when and where celebs would be. Claiming that they stand “For Women Who Want the Ballerific Life.” However, many point to it as the hub for digital groupies.\n\n\n\nCredit for the original annotation goes to @dball1124.", "annotation_id": "14793156", "url": "https://genius.com/14793156", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bigger Than You", "line": "(Murda on the beat so it’s not nice)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This is one of Canadian producer Murda Beatz' production tags.\n\nThe voice tag first appeared on Baka’s song, “AKA,” which Murda produced in 2016.", "annotation_id": "14793086", "url": "https://genius.com/14793086", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bigger Than You", "line": "Watch on Young Dro now, man, boi-oing shit blingin’ off", "vault_lines": ["Watch on Young Dro now, man, boi-oing shit blingin' off"], "meaning": "Reference to Young Dro’s 2006 track, “Rubberband Banks”, where he raps:\n\nRubber band banks (boing yoing yoing yoing)\nTokyo Diamonds (joing yoing yoing yoing)", "annotation_id": "14791890", "url": "https://genius.com/14791890", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bigger Than You", "line": "Young champagne checkin’ in, man, Tity Boi shit ringin’ off", "vault_lines": ["Young champagne checkin' in, man, Tity Boi shit ringin' off"], "meaning": "“Young champagne” refers to Drake’s Instagram handle Champagnepapi and “Tity Boi” is what 2 Chainz was formally known before he changed his stage name.", "annotation_id": "14791545", "url": "https://genius.com/14791545", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bigger Than You", "line": "I sip some red wine, and chased it with the ’42", "vault_lines": ["I sip some red wine, and chased it with the '42"], "meaning": "‘Chasing’ refers to following the first drink with the second drink. In this case, 2 Chainz is sipping red wine first and chasing it with Don Julio 1942 Añejo Tequila.", "annotation_id": "14789445", "url": "https://genius.com/14789445", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bigger Than You", "line": "I show you how to get millions, nigga, that’s a mil plan, now", "vault_lines": ["I show you how to get millions, nigga, that's a mil plan, now"], "meaning": "‘Mil Plan’ is pronounced by 2 Chains as a homophone for ‘Meal Plan’ as a way to assimilate a fitness training regime for an athlete’s success to a million dollar training regime for success.", "annotation_id": "14789418", "url": "https://genius.com/14789418", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bigger Than You", "line": "When I was in juvie, I made ’em back out (Back that ass up) It was 400 degrees, you would have passed out (Ooh)", "vault_lines": ["When I was in juvie, I made 'em back out (Back that ass up)", "It was 400 degrees, you would have passed out (Ooh)"], "meaning": "This line pays direct homage to Cash Money legend, Juvenile, and his best selling album, 400 Degreez.\n\n2 Chainz talks about his time in a juvenile detention center after he was arrested at 15 for cocaine possesion, and how he made the people around him “back that ass up”. This line pays homage to 400 Degreez’s hit single, “Back that Azz Up”.\n\n400 Degreez was so hot, that those in its presence would pass out from the album’s prominence, just as one would pass out from heat exhaustion if exposed to temperatures as high as these.", "annotation_id": "14788801", "url": "https://genius.com/14788801", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bigger Than You", "line": "Uh, yeah, ring the alarm, Cartier bracelets on all of my arms", "vault_lines": ["Uh, yeah, ring the alarm, Cartier bracelets on all of my arms", "Uh, yeah, halo my son,"], "meaning": "Cartier is a high-end fashion brand which is known for its fancy and expensive merchandise. Even the cheapest of the brand’s bracelets cost over a thousand dollars, and the flashiest of the bracelets resemble golden panther heads laced in diamonds and other precious stones costing hundreds of thousands of dollars.\n\n\n\nWith bracelets of this stature, 2 Chainz is not simply wearing the brand, but flexing his wealth to everyone around him.", "annotation_id": "14788773", "url": "https://genius.com/14788773", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bigger Than You", "line": "‘Member I was on pre-paid, I would act like my shit was ringin’ off", "vault_lines": ["'Member I was on pre-paid, I would act like my shit was ringin' off"], "meaning": "Pre-paid is referring to a “pre-paid” phone. A person could go to a local store or gas station and purchase pre-paid cards that would give the cell phone a limited amount of minutes to make phone calls.\n\nDrake is referring to his humble beginnings, reminiscing how at one time his income was low enough to the point he had to buy pre-paid cards for calling minutes on his cell phone. Yet, he would act like his phone was “ringing off the hook”, a common phrase used to refer to someone getting a lot of phone calls, to seem like he was a big deal.\nThis line is related to Drake’s 2013 hit, Started From the Bottom.", "annotation_id": "14788733", "url": "https://genius.com/14788733", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bigger Than You", "line": "Uh, yeah, halo my son,", "vault_lines": ["Uh, yeah, ring the alarm, Cartier bracelets on all of my arms", "Uh, yeah, halo my son,"], "meaning": "2 Chainz’s son Halo Epps was born in October 2015.\n\nhttps://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcThHTmQtss0IABFKaNFOVN_NBsLOZfihxsPGrSJ3M6ZBLTY3hg\n\n2 Chainz raps from the perspective of his son Halo, shortly before his birth, in his song “Halo (Letter From My Unborn Son).\"", "annotation_id": "14788660", "url": "https://genius.com/14788660", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Bigger Than You", "line": "In the wheelchair, and I still perform (uh)", "vault_lines": ["in the wheelchair, and I still perform (uh)"], "meaning": "2 Chainz broke his leg just before embarking on the Pretty Girls Like Trap Music tour, promoting the album of the same name.\n\nRather than cancel his tour, Chainz incorporated his injury into his set and performed in a tricked-out pink wheelchair and had a professional dancer wheel him around the stage.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cJ0iq-qQJtg\n\n2 Chainz’s feature episode on the Netflix series Rapture details the injury and tour.", "annotation_id": "14788580", "url": "https://genius.com/14788580", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "GREECE", "status": "done", "targets": 9, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Dj-khaled-greece-lyrics", "genius_title": "GREECE", "genius_id": 5522492, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "GREECE", "line": "We The Best Music Another one DJ Khaled", "vault_lines": ["We The Best Music"], "meaning": "These are DJ Khaled’s trademark slogans that he often proclaims in the intro and outro of his songs. We The Best Music Group is a record label imprint of Epic Records that was founded by Khaled in 2008.\n\n“Another one” is Khaled’s signature way of announcing that he has another hit on his hands.", "annotation_id": "20359520", "url": "https://genius.com/20359520", "state": "accepted", "votes": 42, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "GREECE", "line": "Long time lookin’ for the bounce, yeah OZ had the bounce, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Long time lookin' for the bounce, yeah", "OZ had the bounce, yeah"], "meaning": "OZ is a notable producer from Zurich, Switzerland who has worked with Drake on many occasions.\n\nThe reasoning for his shoutout is that “Greece” was originally OZ’s track, who produced and recorded his own version with German lyrics. After he posted a few now-deleted snippets of it on Instagram, Drake commented under his post saying “drop Greece.”\n\nHowever, Drake later decided to record his own version of the song.", "annotation_id": "20251647", "url": "https://genius.com/20251647", "state": "accepted", "votes": 107, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "GREECE", "line": "She can’t help but get attached", "vault_lines": ["She can't help but get attached"], "meaning": "On his September 2013 song, “The Language,” Drake mentions how he isn’t a fan of girls getting too attached to him:\n\nAnd she way too attached to me\nHate when they get too attached to me\n\nHe similarly follows on his July 2018 “Behind Barz” freestyle:\n\nCan’t do love ‘cause they get too attached", "annotation_id": "20251503", "url": "https://genius.com/20251503", "state": "accepted", "votes": 48, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "GREECE", "line": "Gone out to Caicos, she can stay in my room She can stay in my room, and it ain’t my", "vault_lines": ["Gone out to Caicos, she can stay in my room", "She can stay in my room, and it ain't my"], "meaning": "“Caicos,” short for Turks and Caicos, is a group of islands in the Atlantic Ocean off the coast of the United States.\n\nDrake has been seen out in the islands many times. In December 2018 and May 2019, he posted pictures at a villa and on a patio at the destination, respectively. His private jet, known as Air Drake, was seen at a private airport on the island sometime after the Toronto Raptors—Drake’s hometown team—won the NBA championship in June 2019.\n\nHe previously mentioned the island on his May 2020 track “Pain 1993” where he boasted he has a beachfront mansion there:\n\nI just got a mansion out in Turks and it’s a beachfront", "annotation_id": "20251356", "url": "https://genius.com/20251356", "state": "accepted", "votes": 56, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "GREECE", "line": "Full speed, je suis ton génie", "vault_lines": ["Full speed, je suis ton génie"], "meaning": "“Je suis ton génie” is French for “I am your genie.” A genie is a spirit or imaginary creature that appears when you rub a magic lamp and grant wishes. Drake compares himself to a genie as he provides his woman with lavish trips and luxury clothing.", "annotation_id": "20251262", "url": "https://genius.com/20251262", "state": "accepted", "votes": 80, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "GREECE", "line": "Speedboats, baby, in Nikki Beach Waves in my ears, smokin’ weed (Oui, oui) Whippin’ through the sand in a Jeep (Oui, oui) All because of what I did on beats, baby", "vault_lines": ["All because of what I did on beats, baby", "Speedboats, baby, in Nikki Beach", "Waves in my ears, smokin' weed (Oui, oui)", "Whippin' through the sand in a Jeep (Oui, oui)"], "meaning": "Nikki Beach Worldwide is a luxury beach club brand that has locations worldwide, including in Greece. However, it’s possible that Drake’s talking about the Miami location as speedboats are a common sight in Miami.\n\nNotably, Nikki Beach is also a frequent spot for Sophie Brussaux—the mother of Drake’s child, Adonis—as in December 2019, she was seen at the Morocco location during a vacation with some friends.", "annotation_id": "20251060", "url": "https://genius.com/20251060", "state": "accepted", "votes": 60, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "GREECE", "line": "Come with me, leave all of your things, yeah We can stop at Gucci, stop at Louis V, yeah Come with me, fly you out to Greece Full speed, survoler Paris, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Come with me, leave all of your things, yeah", "We can stop at Gucci, stop at Louis V, yeah", "Come with me, fly you out to Greece", "Full speed, survoler Paris, yeah", "Full speed, survoler Paris"], "meaning": "Greece is a country located in southeastern Europe, known for its beaches, resorts, archeological sites, and whitewashed villages—making it a notable vacation spot for Drake and his woman.\n\n“Survoler Paris” is French for “fly over Paris.” With Drake being from Toronto, Canada, it’s possible he may fly over France—with Paris being its capital city—while on his way to Greece.\n\nGucci and Louis Vuitton are both expensive luxury clothing brands. Notably, both brands have stores located on the Greek island, Mykonos and in Athens, the capital city of Greece.", "annotation_id": "20250888", "url": "https://genius.com/20250888", "state": "accepted", "votes": 144, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "GREECE", "line": "Life’s sweet, baby, on a G-Wag", "vault_lines": ["Life's sweet, baby, iced out, baby", "Life's sweet, baby, on a G-Wag"], "meaning": "The G-Wagon is a G-Class SUV produced by the luxurious German automobile brand Mercedes-Benz. Their 2020 models are priced well over $100,000, making it one of the most expensive SUVs on the market.\n\nIn February 2019, Drake purchased a Mercedes-Maybach G650 Landaulet—a nicer rendition of the G-Wagon—for over $500,000. Notably, at the time of its purchase, it was reportedly the only one to exist in North America. After the purchase, Drake’s friend, Tony Bet went to Instagram to boast about the vehicle and its exclusivity.\n\n\n\nDrake’s Mercedes G650 Landaulet", "annotation_id": "20250687", "url": "https://genius.com/20250687", "state": "accepted", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "GREECE", "line": "Rolls Royce, baby, in Hidden Hills", "vault_lines": ["Rolls Royce, baby, in Hidden Hills"], "meaning": "Rolls-Royce is a popular British brand of luxury cars. In November 2019, Drake bought a custom-made, one of a kind Rolls-Royce Phantom for a reported $700,000.\n\nThe custom changes include a Bushukan yellow finish with a signature two-tone paint scheme, courtesy of Mansory—a luxury car modification company. Aside from that, the Rolls-Royce’s signature Spirit of Ecstasy bonnet ornament was replaced with a gold owl, which has two large diamonds that make up the owl’s eyes, that has Drake’s full name—Aubrey Drake Graham—engraved in it.\n\nThe brain-child behind the design none other than Drake’s friend and vehicle designer, Tony Bet, who unveiled the car on his Instagram:\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/B41aYtXpaEj/?utm_source=ig_embed\n\nThe Hidden Hills is an upscale, gated community located north of Los Angeles. It’s home to many celebrities including Drake himself, Kanye West, The Weeknd, French Montana, Angelina Jolie, Kylie Jenner—and the rest of the Kardashian/Jenner clan—and many others.", "annotation_id": "19826818", "url": "https://genius.com/19826818", "state": "accepted", "votes": 44, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Oh U Went", "status": "done", "targets": 12, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Young-thug-oh-u-went-lyrics", "genius_title": "Oh U Went", "genius_id": 9263022, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Oh U Went", "line": "I got her twerkin’ in Turks", "vault_lines": ["I got her twerkin' in Turks"], "meaning": "The mention of “Turks” is a clear reference to Turks and Caicos, an island destination emblematic of luxury and exclusivity, setting the tone for a lifestyle of indulgence. This imagery is subtly reinforced later with “cake off,” a phrase that not only denotes financial gain but also phonetically echoes “Caicos,” completing the reference in a clever, almost subliminal manner.", "annotation_id": "34479674", "url": "https://genius.com/34479674", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Oh U Went", "line": "They say that life’s about balance, baby, and the balance is in my account now", "vault_lines": ["They say that life's about balance, baby, and the balance is in my account now"], "meaning": "Drake makes a joke about life advice one might receive: “Life is about balance.” We could say that life is about different kinds of balance, like work-life balance, or the balance between risk and complacency.\n\nBut Drake makes a pun on the idea of balance, saying that life is about one’s “bank balance,” or the amount of money in one’s bank account.\n\nIf life is about balance, Drake says, he’s a master of this life with his large account balance.", "annotation_id": "29167041", "url": "https://genius.com/29167041", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Oh U Went", "line": "Okay, she got a Perc’ in her Birk’", "vault_lines": ["Okay, she got a Perc' in her Birk'"], "meaning": "She has a percocet in her Birkin bag. Drake’s girl lives lavishly with an expensive bag and access to drugs.", "annotation_id": "29167032", "url": "https://genius.com/29167032", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Oh U Went", "line": "I got more streams than y’all in February", "vault_lines": ["I got more streams than y'all in February"], "meaning": "February is always the shortest month in the year having 28 or 29 days.\n\nDrake is saying that he can get more streams than his opponents in less time than them.", "annotation_id": "28939269", "url": "https://genius.com/28939269", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Oh U Went", "line": "Get jammed first like the countdown", "vault_lines": ["If a nigga really try to jam me, get jammed first like the countdown"], "meaning": "It sounds as if Drake says “jammed first” to also sound like “Jan 1st” – the countdown to the New Year. Also sounds like Drake meant “jammed” like jamming chords on a guitar and countdown as a nod to the famous guitar solo in the song “The Final Countdown” by the band Europe. Jamming chords in the Final Countdown guitar solo.", "annotation_id": "28912790", "url": "https://genius.com/28912790", "state": "pending", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Oh U Went", "line": "She probably let both of us hit The way that she smirkin’ at Durk", "vault_lines": ["She probably let both of us hit", "The way that she smirkin' at Durk"], "meaning": "Drake shouts out Chicago rapper Lil Durk whom he collaborated with on the smash-hit “Laugh Now Cry Later” in 2020 and again on the Certified Lover Boy track “In The Bible” in 2021.\n\nDrake’s choice to use the word, “Smirk” when referring to this woman’s flirting is purposeful, as “Smurk” or “Smurkio” (a play on Durkio) are nicknames attributed to Lil Durk, having appeared as bars and ad-libs throughout his discography. A notable example is on 2020’s “All Love” when Durk raps:\n\n1942 with a small pill, she love the boat\nDurkio, Smurkio, yeah, she love the G.O.A.T.\n\nDurk reacted to this line in a November 2023 interview with Ari Melber, who asked him, “Is Drake correct, was she smirkin' at you?”\n\nhttps://youtu.be/cFjiqPHVeP4?si=2iriouRUo2uVG32l&t=1009\n\nDurk responded by saying, “Drake got his own world,” denying this supposed event’s legitimacy, however, laughing at the shoutout nonetheless.", "annotation_id": "28889122", "url": "https://genius.com/28889122", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Oh U Went", "line": "(Metro)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This is one of Metro Boomin’s most popular and classic producer tags to this date, debuting on Young Thug’s November 2015 track, “Hercules.”", "annotation_id": "28884046", "url": "https://genius.com/28884046", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Oh U Went", "line": "She gettin’ cake off the picture she take I say, “Girl, if it work then it work”", "vault_lines": ["She gettin' cake off the picture she take", "I say, \"Girl, if it work then it work\""], "meaning": "Drake is encouraging his girl to get herself paid off of the pictures she takes of herself and posting them.\n\nHe is not concerned about others looking at what he has, so if she is able to make herself some money, he is all for her doing it.", "annotation_id": "28879999", "url": "https://genius.com/28879999", "state": "pending", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Oh U Went", "line": "Fuck a wedding dress, I’m tryna merk it and skrrt", "vault_lines": ["Fuck a wedding dress, I'm tryna merk it and skrrt"], "meaning": "“Merk” means to dominate or excel in something, and in this context, it refers to sexual conquest. “Skrrt” is an onomatopoeic term representing the sound of tires screeching, signifying making a quick exit. Drake is dismissing the traditional notion of marriage and commitment represented by a wedding dress, opting instead for a casual sexual encounter.\n\nDrake also plays on the homophone “Merc,” referring to a Mercedes-Benz, alluding to driving off quickly in a luxury car immediately after the encounter. This highlights his preference for fleeting encounters and the lavish lifestyle associated with luxury cars.\n\nMoreover, Drake contrasts “wedding dress” with the homophone “skirt,” which is more casual attire compared to a wedding dress. This further implies Drake’s preference for quick, casual encounters over serious commitments.\n\nDrake in a Mercedes Maybach", "annotation_id": "28879718", "url": "https://genius.com/28879718", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Oh U Went", "line": "Yeah, look 6 God, he a visionary", "vault_lines": ["6 God, he a visionary"], "meaning": "Drake refers to his hometown of Toronto, Canada, which is often referred to as the “6” due to it consisting of six boroughs, East York, Etobicoke, North York, Scarborough, Toronto, and York.\n\nIn the lyric, Drake names himself a “visionary,” suggesting that he holds knowledge that others don’t — referring to his position in the rap industry, being the most streamed rapper in history.\n\nGiven that, this lyric is also a reference to Drake’s October 2014 smash hit, “6 God,” in which he raps:\n\nI’m the real 6 God, boy (Whoa)", "annotation_id": "28878812", "url": "https://genius.com/28878812", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Oh U Went", "line": "Oh, you went kingpin, oh, you went wings in", "vault_lines": ["Oh, you went kingpin, oh, you went wings in", "Oh, you had came in"], "meaning": "A kingpin is a leader of an organization, typically used to refer to the leader of a gang. Thug notes that he has the same level of authority in the music industry as a kingpin would have while simultaneously reinforcing his gangster-like image.\n\nRecorded prior to Thugger’s May 2022 arrest regarding a 56-count state RICO indictment, Thug could possibly be foreshadowing his untimely arrest like he has done several times, particularly on his appearance on Metro Boomin’s December 2022, “Metro Spider” in which he rapped:\n\nYeah, whole life still a gamble, mob life just like Sopranos", "annotation_id": "28876053", "url": "https://genius.com/28876053", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Oh U Went", "line": "I got more stones than a cemetery", "vault_lines": ["I got more soldiers than a military", "I got more stones than a cemetery"], "meaning": "Drake further sheds light on his extensive jewelry collection, comparing the diamonds or ‘stones’ in his jewelry, to the gravestones that ubiquitously cover cemeteries.\n\n5 months prior, Drake was seen in the Jumbotron Shit Poppin music video, flaunting his latest acquisitions from Pharell’s ‘JOOPITER’ auction– including a 14k three-tone N.E.R.D pendant that sold for $2,184,000.\n\n\n\n\n\nIn 2016, Drake asserted his dominance within the jewelry game, previously boasting the significant large sizes of his chains on Pop Style.", "annotation_id": "28875799", "url": "https://genius.com/28875799", "state": "pending", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
