{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SOMETHING ABOUT YOU", "line": "You’re babysittin’ that rosé (Come on, bitch)", "vault_lines": ["You're babysittin' that rosé (Come on, bitch)"], "meaning": "This could be a double entendre, meaning Rick Ross (aka Rozay (same pronunciation)) is a baby, and also calls him a b**** in the adlib.", "annotation_id": "35663165", "url": "https://genius.com/35663165", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SOMETHING ABOUT YOU", "line": "Slob me down, I know you want revenge", "vault_lines": ["Slob me down, I know you want revenge"], "meaning": "This could be a reference to when Future said “Slob on me nob” in King’s Dead since it also says “I know you want revenge” in the line, which could mean Drake wants revenge on Future, Kendrick, and all the others in the beef.", "annotation_id": "35663092", "url": "https://genius.com/35663092", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
