{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Come Up", "line": "And niggas still askin’ ’bout Detox I’ll tell you if you tell me who killed Pac", "vault_lines": ["And niggas still askin' 'bout Detox", "I'll tell you if you tell me who killed Pac"], "meaning": "Detox is an album that Dr.Dre has worked on for a very long time and hasn’t been released due to Dre being a perfectionist\n\nMany ask about when it will be released because of the instruments Dre puts out which gets a individual hooked onto it more than the lyrics\n\nAs far as the lyrics go Game is saying if you tell me what happened with 2pacs situation during his last days he will tell you about the detox album", "annotation_id": "23200432", "url": "https://genius.com/23200432", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Come Up", "line": "Yeah I got them Mike Vick fingas", "vault_lines": ["Hand on the Eagle, yeah I got them Mike Vick fingas"], "meaning": "He is referring to the time when Mike Vick joined the eagles and was playing unbelievably great", "annotation_id": "23200417", "url": "https://genius.com/23200417", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Come Up", "line": "Aight then, I’m at this Pacquiao fight then, with Tyson The way he’s stickin’, and movin’ the knife, Floyd might win", "vault_lines": ["Aight then, I'm at this Pacquiao fight then, with Tyson", "The way he's stickin', and movin' the knife, Floyd might win"], "meaning": "One of the many box references in Game’s flows,refering to Manny Pacquio, Mike Tyson and Floyd Mayweather .\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe three giants of box might be himself and the many forms this inner struggle takes during the process of creation . Might also be a reference to the giants of the rap game he is trying to overcome", "annotation_id": "1297484", "url": "https://genius.com/1297484", "state": "accepted", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Come Up", "line": "I’m in Toronto, DeMar got a condo", "vault_lines": ["I'm in Toronto, DeMar got a condo"], "meaning": "DeMar DeRozan is from Compton and now plays for the Toronto Raptors", "annotation_id": "684538", "url": "https://genius.com/684538", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "D4L", "status": "done", "targets": 14, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Future-drake-and-young-thug-d4l-lyrics", "genius_title": "D4L", "genius_id": 5520765, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "D4L", "line": "Now she want some LASIK Just to see the bag clearer, that way she can chase it", "vault_lines": ["Now she want a butt lift, now she want some LASIK", "Just to see the bag clearer, that way she can chase it"], "meaning": "LASIK is a very expensive surgery that improves people’s eyesight so that they don’t have to wear glasses anymore.\n\n“The bag” doesn’t refer to some actual bag but references the phrase “chase the bag,” which means to chase money. This is Drake’s creative way of calling this girl a gold digger. Even though they “just started fucking,” she’s already asking him for stuff.", "annotation_id": "38824088", "url": "https://genius.com/38824088", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "D4L", "line": "I ran a check up on my feet", "vault_lines": ["I ran a check up on my feet"], "meaning": "This means that he spent a lot of money on his shoes.", "annotation_id": "38823890", "url": "https://genius.com/38823890", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "D4L", "line": "Oh, my right wrist a Ferrari", "vault_lines": ["Oh, my right wrist a Ferrari"], "meaning": "This line might be “On my right wrist a Ferrari.” Either way, Future is saying the cost of the watch on his right hand is comparable to a Ferrari’s.", "annotation_id": "38823824", "url": "https://genius.com/38823824", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "D4L", "line": "All that brr, you gon’ think we from Saudi Arabia Money counter brr (Yeah), ayy", "vault_lines": ["All that brr, you gon' think we from Saudi Arabia", "Money counter brr (Yeah), ayy"], "meaning": "The “brr” sound is the noise of a money counter when counting stacks. They’re flexing heavy, comparing their cash flow to the oil wealth in Saudi Arabia.\nhttps://filepicker-images.genius.com/c06451bf866a9095bd04d2f7ecb08839a305392b6853bc1f2ca5ec27559d00f8%2Fthjmckxpq7", "annotation_id": "33867342", "url": "https://genius.com/33867342", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "D4L", "line": "I remember grade six, I was up in Payless tryna get some Asics Now I’m Nike’d down in a motherfuckin’ snake pit", "vault_lines": ["I remember grade six, I was up in Payless tryna get some Asics", "Now I'm Nike'd down in a motherfuckin' snake pit"], "meaning": "Payless ShoeSource is an international footwear chain that sells shoes at a discount price and Asics is an inexpensive Japanese shoe brand.\n\nNike is a popular brand that sells footwear, clothing, equipment, accessories, and more. Unlike Asics, most Nike products are expensive. Drake reflects on how he couldn’t afford expensive brands like Nike when he was younger and how he now can easily afford it.\n\n\n\nDrake wearing a Nike sweatsuit and Nike sneakers", "annotation_id": "19727409", "url": "https://genius.com/19727409", "state": "accepted", "votes": 41, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "D4L", "line": "Bowen Homes, you know, that shiesty shit (What’s hannenin’?)", "vault_lines": ["Bowen Homes, you know, that shiesty shit (What's hannenin'?)"], "meaning": "The Bowen Homes are a section of housing projects which were originally built in 1964 and were demolished in 2009. The homes were located in the Bankhead section of Atlanta, Georgia. Both Young Thug and Future are Atlanta natives.\n\nD4L are from the Bowen Homes and T.I. shot the music video for What Up, What’s Haapnin' at the Bowen Homes. The video can be viewed here.", "annotation_id": "19725363", "url": "https://genius.com/19725363", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "D4L", "line": "Richard Mille, all this year, nigga, what’s hannenin’? (What’s hannenin’?)", "vault_lines": ["Richard Mille, all year, what's hannenin'? (What's hannenin'?)", "Richard Mille, all this year, nigga, what's hannenin'? (What's hannenin'?)"], "meaning": "Richard Mille is a Swiss luxury watchmaker, famous for their unique casings and visible mechanics.\n\nThe RM 56-02 Tourbillon Sapphire is priced at insane $2,020,000 for its complex case design, pure sapphire, and pulleys air suspension movement.\n\n\n\nYoung Thug also name-dropped the Swiss watchmaker on his August 2018 track, “Tsunami”:\n\nI put your name on my wrist\nFat Richard Mille on my wrist", "annotation_id": "19718651", "url": "https://genius.com/19718651", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "D4L", "line": "Foreign breed, American, she call me papi (Yeah, yeah, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Foreign breed, American, she call me papi (Yeah, yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "Here, Future references Drake’s Instagram username, @champagnepapi. He also goes under the moniker “papi” when addressed by his foreign female counterpart, who presumably is of Spanish descent, since “papi” is Spanish for “daddy.”", "annotation_id": "19718303", "url": "https://genius.com/19718303", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "D4L", "line": "I eat calamari (Brr, yeah, yeah, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["I bought her a 'Rari (Swerve, skrrt), brr ('Rari, yeah)", "I eat calamari (Brr, yeah, yeah, yeah)"], "meaning": "Young Thug has previously displayed his affection for calamari. In the Jaden Smith-featured track, Sin.\n\nPlus she got red calamari skin", "annotation_id": "19717108", "url": "https://genius.com/19717108", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "D4L", "line": "On that Earl Manigault, shootin’ it out the spoon", "vault_lines": ["On that Earl Manigault, shootin' it out the spoon"], "meaning": "Earl Manigault was an American street basketball player, famous for his nickname as the Goat. Many believe that Earl is the origin of the GOAT acronym, meaning greatest of all time. GOAT is now a common term used in basketball debates as well as rap and other industries.", "annotation_id": "19717046", "url": "https://genius.com/19717046", "state": "pending", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "D4L", "line": "Woah, woah, Bankhead, started seein’ spaceships, woah", "vault_lines": ["Woah, woah, Bankhead, started seein' spaceships, woah"], "meaning": "Drake pays more homage to D4L as this is an allusion to the group’s November 2005 song, “Scotty”:\n\nI’m startin' to see spaceships on Bankhead", "annotation_id": "19716977", "url": "https://genius.com/19716977", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "D4L", "line": "(808 my crew) (Ayy, Southside, where you get all that drip?)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This is the producer tag of Atlanta-based producer Southside, who, alongside, fellow Atlanta producer Lex Luger, formed the iconic producer conglomerate 808 Mafia.\n\nThis is the fifth official collaboration between Drake and Southside, following:\n\n\n\n“Digital Dash” with Future (Sep. 2015)\n\n“Live from the Gutter” with Future\n\n“I’m the Plug” with Future (Sep. 2015)\n\n“Grammys” (Apr. 2016)\n\n\n\nSouthside has also produced on a number of tracks where Drake has been featured, most prominently seen on Gucci Mane’s January 2017 track “Both” and DJ ESCO’s June 2016 track “100it Racks.”", "annotation_id": "19716356", "url": "https://genius.com/19716356", "state": "accepted", "votes": 45, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "D4L", "line": "D4L, Stunna Man, say what’s hannenin’? (What’s hannenin’?)", "vault_lines": ["YSL bandana, man, what's hannenin'? (What's hannenin'?)", "D4L, Stunna Man, man, what's hannenin'? (What's hannenin'?)", "D4L, Stunna Man, say what's hannenin'? (What's hannenin'?)"], "meaning": "D4L is a 2000s rap group made up of Atlanta rappers Fabo, Mook-B, Stoney and Shawty Lo. The group is best known for their chart-topping November 2005 track “Laffy Taffy,” which hit #1 on the Billboard Hot 100 in January 2006. “Stunna Man” is a nod to Stoney, who was also known as Stuntman.\n\nThe phrase “What’s hannenin'?” was first popularized  by D4L on their 2005 track “I’m Da Man”\n\nThat’s what’s hannenin'\nAnd you know I keep work\nSeventeen five, same color t-shirt\nWhat’s hannenin', I’m the man, bitch I’m the man\n\nDrake would later use the phrase on his June 2010 single, “Miss Me”:\n\nI said, “Tell me what’s really goin' on”\nDrizzy back up in this thing, I’m ready, what’s hannenin'?", "annotation_id": "19716179", "url": "https://genius.com/19716179", "state": "accepted", "votes": 39, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "D4L", "line": "FBG, YSL, know just what’s brackin’, yeah (Yeah, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["FBG, YSL, know just what's brackin', yeah (Yeah, yeah)", "FBG, YSL, what's hannenin'? (What's hannenin'?)"], "meaning": "Drake, Future, and Young Thug each shout out their respective labels on the chorus of the track. Future (FREEBANDZ Gang, or FBG), Thugger (Young Stoner Life Records, or YSL) and Drake (October’s Very Own, or OVO) all founded and have at least partial ownership in their respective label.\n\nAll three of the featured artists have long collaboration histories with each other, and their labels have even teamed up to release two collaboration tapes:\n\n\nFBG & OVO for September 2015’s What a Time to Be Alive\n\nFBG & YSL for October 2017’s SUPER SLIMEY\n\n\n\n\nFuture and Thug have both confirmed that a sequel to SUPER SLIMEY is also coming soon, also incorporating YSL artist Gunna and Quality Control artist Lil Baby into the collaboration.", "annotation_id": "19715857", "url": "https://genius.com/19715857", "state": "accepted", "votes": 70, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Enough Said", "status": "done", "targets": 9, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Aaliyah-enough-said-lyrics", "genius_title": "Enough Said", "genius_id": 83754, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Enough Said", "line": "Don’t you ever wake up disgusted", "vault_lines": ["Don't you ever wake up disgusted"], "meaning": "Drake is aiming this at Chris Brown and his new song “Don’t Wake Me Up.” When Breezy does wake up, he will be sick at how little units Fortune has sold.\n\nChris Brown also must look at his past behavior each day, a reminder of his fights and assault cases, most predominantly his assault on singer and girlfriend Rihanna.", "annotation_id": "968442", "url": "https://genius.com/968442", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Enough Said", "line": "Running through the city with niggas I’d give a kidney", "vault_lines": ["Running through the city with niggas I'd give a kidney"], "meaning": "Drake is so close with his team that he would give a Kidney for them to improve their health. This could also be aimed to Noah 40 Shebib who has MS, MS has been known to cause Kidney stones, so Drake is saying how he would do anything to improve his friends health.", "annotation_id": "958930", "url": "https://genius.com/958930", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Enough Said", "line": "[Verse 3: Drake]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake putting together this posthumous record did not sit very well with Aaliyah’s producer when she was alive, Timbaland.  He told MTV:\n\n I know they trying to drop some Aaliyah records, but if he do it, it should be with me and Missy. The proper way for him to do that would be for me, him and Missy to be all on the record. The best decision, what the fans would want to see is all three of us. It can’t be something to make money off of ‘cause I think it’s wrong to make money off the dead.", "annotation_id": "958722", "url": "https://genius.com/958722", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Enough Said", "line": "Oh, so tell me what you would like me to do To help you, help me, help you", "vault_lines": ["So tell me what can I do to make", "Oh, so tell me what you would like me to do", "To help you, help me, help you", "Can't you talk to me?", "Tell me what you need", "Can you talk to me? (Can you talk to me?)"], "meaning": "Drake tweeted these lines in late July furthering his tradition of tweeting lyrics of songs before they drop\n\nhttps://twitter.com/Drake/status/228775433586483200\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nIt is probably influenced by one of Tom Cruise’s famous lines from “Jerry Maguire”:\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AGt5f70K02Q\n\n…HELP ME help you!", "annotation_id": "958696", "url": "https://genius.com/958696", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Enough Said", "line": "Went from my nigga serving it by the tele", "vault_lines": ["Went from my nigga serving it by the tele"], "meaning": "Tele is shorter version of telephone. Just like he said in Star67, back in the day, him and his boys used to be working on the phones selling scams.\n\nTelly is also short of Hotel. He can also be referencing his friends who used to work by hotels, selling drugs.", "annotation_id": "958598", "url": "https://genius.com/958598", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Enough Said", "line": "Girls that becoming ladies, and my friends are having babies", "vault_lines": ["Girls that becoming ladies, and my friends are having babies"], "meaning": "Drizzy is realizing that everyone is growing up around him\n\ncf. Terry Tate’s 1989 hit “Babies Having Babies”\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2s338u1Rrvg", "annotation_id": "958561", "url": "https://genius.com/958561", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Enough Said", "line": "Selling under 150 you niggas got to be kidding Is this even still a discussion?", "vault_lines": ["Selling under 150 you niggas got to be kidding", "Is this even still a discussion?"], "meaning": "Drake’s most recent album, Take Care sold 659,190 copies in its first week\n\nDrizzy is definitely throwing shade at Chris Brown’s first week sales of his latest album, Fortune: 134,000 in its first week… a significant drop from 270,000 of his previous album, F.A.M.E.", "annotation_id": "958510", "url": "https://genius.com/958510", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Enough Said", "line": "To venues in Manchester Just swerving with Balotelli", "vault_lines": ["to venues in Manchester", "Just swerving with Balotelli"], "meaning": "Mario Balotelli is a former starting striker for Manchester City. Currently playing as a striker for Ligue 1 club Nice as well as for national Italian team. The two starting hanging together in public in spring 2012", "annotation_id": "958506", "url": "https://genius.com/958506", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Enough Said", "line": "And babies are dropping dead in my city,", "vault_lines": ["And babies are dropping dead in my city,"], "meaning": "Referencing the 2012 Danzig shooting that happened in Scarborough, an east end district of Toronto. There were 23 people injured (including an infant) and 2 fatalities – a 17-year old girl and 23-year old man.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/Drake/status/225358554138284032", "annotation_id": "958476", "url": "https://genius.com/958476", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Over Here", "status": "done", "targets": 13, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Partynextdoor-over-here-lyrics", "genius_title": "Over Here", "genius_id": 176865, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Over Here", "line": "All I ever asked for was patience (That’s all I ever asked and you know it) Patience and pussy but mostly patience (Yeah, yeah, ‘cause you gon’ use it anyway)", "vault_lines": ["All I ever asked for was patience (That's all I ever asked and you know it)", "Patience and pussy but mostly patience (Yeah, yeah, 'cause you gon' use it anyway)"], "meaning": "😂😂", "annotation_id": "38205001", "url": "https://genius.com/38205001", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": false, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Over Here", "line": "I got hits, nigga, you just a batboy, for real", "vault_lines": ["I got hits, nigga, you just a batboy, for real"], "meaning": "Drake is most likely referencing the term “Batboy” from the hit 1999 comedy movie American Pie.\n\nIn the movie, Kevin Myers says, “You’re still just a batboy,” to Jim Levenstein when Jim jokes that he’s still on “third base” with his girlfriend. Implying that while Kevin is at least actively playing on the field, Jim isn’t even in the game, reduced to nothing more than a mere waterboy.\n\nIn the context of the movie, the term is used simply as a playful joke. Drake, however, uses this term figuratively to brag that he’s actively in the game getting major hits, while others are merely sitting on the sidelines.", "annotation_id": "35145515", "url": "https://genius.com/35145515", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Over Here", "line": "But I was there Nas don shit", "vault_lines": ["But I was there Nas don shit"], "meaning": "A reference to Nas “The Don”, a song from his tenth album, which received universal acclaim from critics. In the video for the song, Nas is the “Don” of his city, New York.\n\nIn relation to the previous lines, before making it in music Drake’s friends had to hustle and deal drugs, while he played the Don position.", "annotation_id": "4101889", "url": "https://genius.com/4101889", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Over Here", "line": "And sell the work right to Hush, y’all niggas must have forgot", "vault_lines": ["And sell the work right to Hush, y'all niggas must have forgot"], "meaning": "Refering to OVO crew member – Hush Moula\n\n\n\nHush all the way to the left", "annotation_id": "1898504", "url": "https://genius.com/1898504", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Over Here", "line": "Oliver North in the cut Dolce’d out, though", "vault_lines": ["Oliver North in the cut Dolce'd out, though"], "meaning": "Oliver North is a member of the OVO crew.\nhttps://twitter.com/OVORyan/status/236363090634096640\nhttp://instagram.com/p/Oa7QpNl4un/\n(See if you can spot Drizzy!)", "annotation_id": "1898490", "url": "https://genius.com/1898490", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Over Here", "line": "Backwoods get peeled, I smoke away all the tears", "vault_lines": ["Backwoods get peeled, I smoke away all the tears"], "meaning": "Drake is using these to roll up his blunt and smoke weed to take all of his pain and tears away.", "annotation_id": "1897725", "url": "https://genius.com/1897725", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Over Here", "line": "Go to Jungle, pick up my Ethiopian goddess", "vault_lines": ["Go to Jungle, pick up my Ethiopian goddess"], "meaning": "Drake has a thing for the beautiful women of East African/Ethiopian descent as referenced in songs like “Poetic Justice”:\n\nEthiopian girl, Ethiopian girl\nWith your long, curly hair and yo' big ass boo-tay\n\nand on “Where to Now”:\n\nYoung East African girl, you too busy fuckin' with your other man\n\nAlso, Jungle is slang used to refer to the neighborhood of Lawrence Heights of Toronto.", "annotation_id": "1897472", "url": "https://genius.com/1897472", "state": "accepted", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Over Here", "line": "Yeah, sure this ain’t Compton, but this ain’t a fairytale land neither", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, sure this ain't Compton, but this ain't a fairytale land neither"], "meaning": "Compton is one of the worst criminal cities in the United States. The height of their crime rate was in the early 90’s, when rap groups started taking over such as N.W.A. and Compton’s Most Wanted.\n\n\n\nTo sum it up, Drake is saying that life in Toronto isn’t close to the things you could experience in Compton, but it isn’t a fairytale either.\n\nHe’s also talking about the jokes people make about him not  starting from the bottom because he grew up in a nice neighborhood and never really struggled.", "annotation_id": "1896467", "url": "https://genius.com/1896467", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Over Here", "line": "Throwing money fast over here Blowing all this cash over here (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Throwing money fast over here", "Blowing all this cash over here (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Drake’s Club Paradise tour grossed over $42 million worldwide and he spent $50,000 in a strip club, so it’s safe to say that him and his OVO family are living well.", "annotation_id": "1896458", "url": "https://genius.com/1896458", "state": "accepted", "votes": 22, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Over Here", "line": "Nothing was the same, man, including y’all careers", "vault_lines": ["Nothing was the same, man, including y'all careers"], "meaning": "Nothing Was The Same is the name of Drake’s third studio album. Judging from the string of hits Drake has had in early 2013, “Started from the Bottom”, “5 AM In Toronto” and now these four new songs, it’s simple to see that Drake is going to have another successful year.\n\n“Nothing was the Same” also connotes a big transition, whether it be in Drake’s life, or the rap game.", "annotation_id": "1896440", "url": "https://genius.com/1896440", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Over Here", "line": "You supposed to be there when my head hurt", "vault_lines": ["You supposed to be there when my head hurt"], "meaning": "She needs to cater to every problem he has but instead she usually ducks out on him and he then acts like a stray puppy in that fashion. Also a continuation of the last line where he said him and his nigga’s are “bucking heads”.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/Drake/status/346551970032676864", "annotation_id": "1896435", "url": "https://genius.com/1896435", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Over Here", "line": "The new Cash Money, the new Roc-A-Fella Bunch of young rich niggas, turn around if you jealous, boy", "vault_lines": ["The new Cash Money, the new Roc-A-Fella", "Bunch of young rich niggas, turn around if you jealous, boy"], "meaning": "Drake wants his OVO label to be as successful as the two labels mentioned. And if people want to hate, he has no time for them.\n\nCash Money Records was founded by Birdman and Slim, and, much like Rocafella Records, was run from the ground up.\n\nBoth labels have been or are major mainstream labels in their prime, although Jay-Z has moved on to being the President of Def Jam and, now, his newest label RocNation.\n\nI guess you could say they’ve “started from the bottom", "annotation_id": "1896422", "url": "https://genius.com/1896422", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Over Here", "line": "I’m screaming OVO on the whole way out, though", "vault_lines": ["I'm screaming OVO on the whole way out, though"], "meaning": "October’s Very Own as Drizzy was born october 24. It’s also the name of an anual festival in Canada, aswell as the name of the record label Drizzy started – It’s his slogan, just like XO is The Weeknd’s.", "annotation_id": "1896158", "url": "https://genius.com/1896158", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Oprah’s Bank Account", "status": "done", "targets": 11, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Lil-yachty-and-dababy-oprahs-bank-account-lyrics", "genius_title": "Oprah’s Bank Account", "genius_id": 5166190, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Oprah’s Bank Account", "line": "(EarlOnTheBeat)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "EarlOnTheBeat is the producer tag of Isaac E. Bynum. The Atlanta-native has produced many tracks for Lil Boat like “Yacht Club” and “Get Dripped.”\n\nIn an interview with Billboard, the producer didn’t have high hopes for this beat. However, after listening to Yachty’s hook—along with DaBaby and Drake’s verse—the producer saw the potential of the track and the music video.\n\nIt’s different, but it’s hard.", "annotation_id": "19251017", "url": "https://genius.com/19251017", "state": "accepted", "votes": 33, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Oprah’s Bank Account", "line": "Back home, I’m the presi’, I’m Obama, ayy, I condone the drama, ayy", "vault_lines": ["Back home, I'm the presi', I'm Obama, ayy, I condone the drama, ayy"], "meaning": "Drake compares himself to the former 44th president of the United States, Barack Obama. The rapper and the politician are known friends; Drake once shared a letter from the Obama family on Instagram.\n\nAdditionally, both men are well-known for their large aircraft: during his presidency from 2008-2016, Obama was escorted in his private presidential Boeing 747 jet, the Air Force One; while Drake rides around in Air Drake, his personal Boeing 767 cargo jet with a custom decoration of the iconic OVO owl on the side.\n\n\n\nDrake has been no stranger to drama within the last few years. From his highly publicized beef with fellow rapper Pusha T that exposed his secret child to being called out as a culture vulture, Drizzy knows what it’s like to make headlines.\n\nAdditionally, the “I’m Obama” line became an internet meme for a while, leading to this magnificent creation.", "annotation_id": "19242307", "url": "https://genius.com/19242307", "state": "accepted", "votes": 40, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Oprah’s Bank Account", "line": "My bitch ’bout it ’bout it, she need her a tank", "vault_lines": ["My bitch 'bout it 'bout it, she need her a tank"], "meaning": "This line and the next are full of references to Master P, the legendary New Orleans rapper, producer and businessman and his label No Limit Records.\n\nThe phrase “bout it, bout it” is mostly associated with Master P. He had a song by the same name.\nAs is the adlib (uh) at the end of the line.\n\n\n\nThe emblem for No Limit Records was a tank.\n\n\n\nMaster P has mentioned in interviews that he called the label No Limit because he didn’t want there to be any limit to his riches and success and DaBaby echoes these sentiments while shouting out the label in the following line.", "annotation_id": "19241434", "url": "https://genius.com/19241434", "state": "pending", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Oprah’s Bank Account", "line": "Run me your body, I’ll put a Range on the road for you", "vault_lines": ["Run me your body, I'll put a Range on the road for you"], "meaning": "Drake shouts out the Range Rover, a luxury sports utility vehicle. He has been a fan of the vehicle from the start of his career, as seen by this 2011 Complex Cover story.\n\nTo run up on somebody is jargon for confronting a person with hostile motives (potentially robbing or killing them).", "annotation_id": "19241160", "url": "https://genius.com/19241160", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Oprah’s Bank Account", "line": "Money and me are the same, but I just don’t fold for you, yeah", "vault_lines": ["Money and me are the same, but I just don't fold for you, yeah"], "meaning": "While Drake equates himself to money (given his $150 million dollar net worth), the difference is he doesn’t “fold”. Cash literally folds when placed in a wallet, and the term fold also means to back down to someone or get played by them.", "annotation_id": "19241140", "url": "https://genius.com/19241140", "state": "pending", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Oprah’s Bank Account", "line": "Now his bitch goin’ Baby on Baby (Let’s go)", "vault_lines": ["Now his bitch goin' Baby on Baby (Let's go)"], "meaning": "Baby on Baby is the title of DaBaby’s 2019 debut album. The album’s third track “Goin Baby” has a similar line, where DaBaby raps:\n\nI’m goin' baby on baby (Uh-huh)", "annotation_id": "19241112", "url": "https://genius.com/19241112", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Oprah’s Bank Account", "line": "I’m blowin’ a bag in the Diamond District", "vault_lines": ["I'm blowin' a bag in the Diamond District"], "meaning": "The Diamond District is a block in Manhattan, New York where it is estimated that 80% of the diamonds which enter the United States are handled.\n\n\n\nTo “blow a bag” means to spend a lot of money in a short time; Drake has purchased jewelry in the Diamond District on many occasions, notably from jewelers like Mr. Flawless and Eliantte.\n\nThe Diamond District was also a filming location for Drake’s “When to Say When” music video, released one week prior to this track.", "annotation_id": "19241006", "url": "https://genius.com/19241006", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Oprah’s Bank Account", "line": "I tongued down Madonna, ayy, do you need pajamas? Yeah Stayin’ the night, girl, you promised it", "vault_lines": ["I tongued down Madonna, ayy, do you need pajamas? Yeah", "Stayin' the night, girl, you promised it", "Lockin' it down, lockin' it down, lockin' it down, I want you (I want you)"], "meaning": "Drake was infamously kissed by pop legend Madonna during his set at Coachella 2015. He appears to be laughing the incident off now, which is a stark contrast from his initial reaction:\n\n\n\nEarlier in 2015, Drake released his If You’re Reading This It’s Too Late mixtape which featured a song named after the popstar.\n\nIn the second part of the line, Drake asks this girl if he needs pajamas for the sleepover they’re about to have, that she apparently promised. Drake has rapped about having girls spend the night before, notably on “Wu-Tang Forever”:\n\nHow you feel about comin' home with a nigga for the night?", "annotation_id": "19240820", "url": "https://genius.com/19240820", "state": "accepted", "votes": 48, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Oprah’s Bank Account", "line": "Diamond in the rough, you look as good as Oprah’s bank account", "vault_lines": ["You look as good as Oprah's bank account", "Diamond in the rough, you look as good as Oprah's bank account"], "meaning": "A “diamond in the rough” is someone with potential or talent but lacking training or polish. Yachty previously described his girl as a “diamond in the rough” on his 2019 song “Forever World”.\n\nOprah Gail Winfrey is an American media executive, actress, and talk show host. As of the release of the song, Oprah’s net worth is estimated at $2.6B. Lil Yachty draws a parallel between Oprah’s bank account and his girl and insinuates that both are very attractive.\n\nThe music video for “Oprah’s Bank Account” pays homage to The Oprah Winfrey Show, Oprah’s hit talk show which ran for 25 years starting in 1986.\n\n\n\nLil Yachty dressed as Oprah; Oprah Winfrey", "annotation_id": "19240608", "url": "https://genius.com/19240608", "state": "accepted", "votes": 93, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Oprah’s Bank Account", "line": "City girl straight from the South", "vault_lines": ["City girl straight from the South"], "meaning": "Yachty subtly shouts out Quality Control label mates City Girls, comprised of JT and Yung Miami. The two act’s careers will forever be intertwined after Yachty wrote essentially all of the Girls' breakout November 2018 hit “Act Up.”\n\nYachty seemingly references a girl who – like the City Girls, who are from Miami, Florida – hails from the South.", "annotation_id": "19240512", "url": "https://genius.com/19240512", "state": "accepted", "votes": 45, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Oprah’s Bank Account", "line": "I hide in the cave like Osama did", "vault_lines": ["I hide in the cave like Osama did"], "meaning": "Drake compares his own tendency to remain at home to the hideout of Osama bin Laden, the founder of the militant Islamist organization al-Qaeda. The instrumental role of bin Laden in the September 11th terrorist attacks in New York led him to seek refuge in Afghanistan’s Tora Bora caves from U.S.-led military operations. On May 2nd of 2011, Osama was killed during a U.S. nighttime raid of a large compound he had constructed in Pakistan.\n\nIn 2018, Drake purchased and began renovating a multi-million dollar mansion in the upscale Toronto community of Bridle Path. Sporting a 10-car garage and a basketball court among other amenities, such a house gives little reason to leave.", "annotation_id": "19240505", "url": "https://genius.com/19240505", "state": "accepted", "votes": 44, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sho Me Love", "status": "done", "targets": 11, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Rich-gang-sho-me-love-lyrics", "genius_title": "Sho Me Love", "genius_id": 578430, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sho Me Love", "line": "Yeah, they tore down the Magnolia but this where my heart is at", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, they tore down the Magnolia but this where my heart is at"], "meaning": "The Magnolia Projects, officially C.J Peete Projects, was a housing projects in the Uptown section of New Orleans located in between the the 11th and 12th wards. Home to Juvenile,Turk, Soulja Slim, Magnolia Shorty, Jay Electronica and Curren$y. The projects was renamed Harmony Oaks after everything was removed following the damages of Hurricane Katrina. The area lives on in Juve’s heart and his “Nolia Clap\"video. https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cMXXemw2X_s", "annotation_id": "4636976", "url": "https://genius.com/4636976", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sho Me Love", "line": "Hurricanes, it took everything, but there’s money still to be got", "vault_lines": ["Hurricanes, it took everything, but there's money still to be got"], "meaning": "Hurricanes refers to Hurricane Katrina and the its aftermath in New Orleans. Although Katrina had its adverse effect on the city, there is faith in future prospects.", "annotation_id": "4502366", "url": "https://genius.com/4502366", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sho Me Love", "line": "Turk and Mannie I got love if we don’t ever make a track", "vault_lines": ["I show love, I show love", "Turk and Mannie I got love if we don't ever make a track", "I-I show love, I show love"], "meaning": "Juvie shouts out his former Cash Money label mates Turk and Mannie Fresh. Letting them both know that even if they don’t make a track due to Juvie being back on the camp,he still loves both of them. There’s no hard feelings.", "annotation_id": "4424623", "url": "https://genius.com/4424623", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sho Me Love", "line": "It still feel like yesterday when Magnolia Slim got shot I don’t know why they got ’em though Cause that ain’t the way that he rock", "vault_lines": ["It still feel like yesterday when Magnolia Slim got shot", "I don't know why they got 'em though", "Cause that ain't the way that he rock"], "meaning": "Magnolia Slim was the nickname of Soulja Slim, of No Limit fame, who wrote one of Juvenile’s biggest singles, Slow Motion.\n\nIt remains an unsolved murder, and Juve adds to the mystery by saying that wasn’t the way that he carried himself, implying he wasn’t about violence or gun culture.", "annotation_id": "4407783", "url": "https://genius.com/4407783", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sho Me Love", "line": "Screaming “Free BG” I wish he was here now to blow this sack", "vault_lines": ["Screaming \"Free BG\" I wish he was here now to blow this sack"], "meaning": "Juve wishes His fellow Hot Boy could be here to blow a fire ass bag.\n\nBut,\nFellow Hot Boys Member B.G. got sentenced 14 years in Prison after pleading guilty to two counts of being a felon in possession of a firearm   and one count of conspiracy to obstruct justice back in 2012.\n\nSo until B.Geezy is released Juve and Everybody will be Screaming “Free B.G.!!!!”\n\n#FREEB.G.", "annotation_id": "4407604", "url": "https://genius.com/4407604", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sho Me Love", "line": "I told Ms. Linda “I got you baby, my heart is yours til it stops” I do this cause I got real love, I don’t do this shit to get props", "vault_lines": ["I show love to my dogs, my dogs is all that I got", "I told Ms. Linda \"I got you baby, my heart is yours til it stops\"", "I do this cause I got real love, I don't do this shit to get props", "I show love, I show love", "I-I show love, I show love"], "meaning": "Juv told her she has his heart until he dies. This might be a subliminal shoutout to Drake; considering Drizzy’s statement to a girl on NWTS saying “It’s Yours”\nJuvenile doesn’t perform because he wants fame, he does it because he loves the fans and wants to put on for them.", "annotation_id": "4400653", "url": "https://genius.com/4400653", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sho Me Love", "line": "Rich Gang Rich girl", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Rich Gang is a loosely-defined group of artists put together by Birdman. It’s comprised mainly of Cash Money and Young Money artists, but it also includes anyone Birdman really likes. The “Rich Gang” and “rich girl” tags, sampled from “Tapout,” are present in a majority of the group’s releases.", "annotation_id": "4379453", "url": "https://genius.com/4379453", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sho Me Love", "line": "Slim and Baby that’s my uncles Man, I’m glad they brought me back", "vault_lines": ["Slim and Baby that's my uncles", "Man, I'm glad they brought me back"], "meaning": "Slim and Birdman are the two figures who started the legendary Cash Money Records. Juvenile first signed with them back in 1997, but he parted ways with the label in 2003.\n\n\n\nOn October 28th 2014, it was announced that he re-signed with Cash Money. Birdman said this about the re-signing:\n\nJuve went under the water without us, and I wanted to bring him back to the surface and leave him there because he’s talented as a motherfucker. You can’t take that away from him. He can rap his ass off. But like I was saying, it’s a mindset of people, and when you’re down you’re down; and when you’re, up you’re up. I just felt like he’s been underwater without us, and this [new track] with him and [Drake] could bring him above the rim.", "annotation_id": "4361150", "url": "https://genius.com/4361150", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sho Me Love", "line": "And I got Trukfit on my hat", "vault_lines": ["and I got Trukfit on my hat"], "meaning": "Juvenile shows support for Lil Wayne’s clothing brand, “TRUKFIT” by wearing a hat from the collection.", "annotation_id": "4359306", "url": "https://genius.com/4359306", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sho Me Love", "line": "GTV inside my cup", "vault_lines": ["GTV inside my cup"], "meaning": "GTV (Grand Touring Vodka) is the name of the alcoholic brand that produce their own vodka. Birdman partnered up with GTV in 2012 to help promote the drink and boost the sales of the vodka brand. GT Vodka can be seen in music videos from Drake, Lil Wayne, Tyga, and Nicki Minaj on a regular basis. You can also see the label’s tour bus showing Birdman and his drink:\n\n\n\nJuvenile is supporting Birdman’s partnership with GTV by drinking the product and promoting it in this song.", "annotation_id": "4359242", "url": "https://genius.com/4359242", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Sho Me Love", "line": "And Lil Weezy that’s my brother Fuck with him you gon’ get whacked", "vault_lines": ["And Lil Weezy that's my brother", "Fuck with him you gon' get whacked"], "meaning": "Lil' Wayne & Juvenile have known each other since 1996 when they were part of the Hot Boyz.", "annotation_id": "4359165", "url": "https://genius.com/4359165", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "WAIT FOR U", "status": "done", "targets": 5, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Future-wait-for-u-lyrics", "genius_title": "WAIT FOR U", "genius_id": 7945037, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "WAIT FOR U", "line": "Supposed to be your dog, but you done put me in a kennel", "vault_lines": ["Supposed to be your dog, but you done put me in a kennel"], "meaning": "Drake uses a play on the AAVE (African-American Vernacular English) slang, ‘dawg’, in a double entendre with its homophone and origin, ‘dog’. The variant, ‘dawg’, usually refers to a close friend or homie.\n\nThrough this similarity, Drake explains how he mistook her signs, outlining his disappointment after being ignored by his lover, comparing himself to a dog left alone in a kennel. With the truth revealed to him, Drake further laments his initial belief of a close relationship with her, somewhat like her ‘dawg’, realising his lack of importance to her:\n\nGuess I’m not the one that’s meant for you", "annotation_id": "26004932", "url": "https://genius.com/26004932", "state": "pending", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "WAIT FOR U", "line": "(ATL Jacob, ATL Jacob)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This is the producer tag of, ATL Jacob. The tag is voiced by fellow Atlanta native Young Scooter, and first appeared on Young Scooter’s February 2018 collaboration with Future, “Real Talk.” Previously the rapper used a different tag, as the old tag can be heard on the beginning of the same track.\n\nThe tag comes from the opening lines of the song, which was produced by ATL Jacob. The producer revealed more about the tag in a April 2019 DJ Smallz Eyes interview. In response to a question about whether he knew it would become his producer tag, Jacob said:\n\nAfter the song dropped, I kept listening to it. I (was) like, “ I might make this my tag.”", "annotation_id": "25950689", "url": "https://genius.com/25950689", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "WAIT FOR U", "line": "I won’t wait for you, for you", "vault_lines": ["I won't wait for you, for you", "When you drunk, you tell me exactly how you feel (I won't wait for you, for you)", "When I'm loaded, I keep it real (I won't wait for you, I won't wait for you)", "Need to tell a real one exactly what it is (I won't wait, won't wait, for you, for you)", "Early in the mornin', late at night (I won't wait for you)", "Don't say it 'cause you know that's what I wanna hear (I won't wait for you, I won't wait for you)", "I cannot convince you that I love you for a livin' (Won't wait for you, for you)", "Message say delivered, but I know that you don't get it (I won't wait for you)", "Why you introduce us if you knew that you was with him? (I won't wait for you, for you, for you)", "Made me shake his hand when y'all been fuckin' for a minute (I won't wait for you, for you)", "It don't even matter what time it is (I won't wait for you)", "Walk me off the plank because you know that I'm a swimmer (I won't wait for you)", "You pray for my demons, girl, I got you"], "meaning": "This is a sample from Tems‘ September 2020 R&B ballad, “Higher,” one of the more popular tracks off her debut EP, For Broken Ears.\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1kU5BzdfDfg&feature=emb_title\n\nFuture expressed his feelings on her voice and the sample’s use in a series of tweets on May 12, 2022.\n\nhttps://twitter.com/1future/status/1524813331730685958", "annotation_id": "25785220", "url": "https://genius.com/25785220", "state": "accepted", "votes": 92, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "WAIT FOR U", "line": "I been in the field like the children of the corn", "vault_lines": ["I been in the field likе the children of the corn"], "meaning": "Children of the Corn is a 1978 horror short story written by Stephen King. The children in the story are under the influence of an entity they call He Who Walks Behind the Rows, who has them kill all of the adults in the town.\n\nThe children often met and hid out in a cornfield, which Future directly compares to reference his “field” as his drug-dealing lifestyle.\n\n\n\nStill from the 1984 film adaptation of Children of the Corn", "annotation_id": "25704761", "url": "https://genius.com/25704761", "state": "accepted", "votes": 75, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "WAIT FOR U", "line": "You be textin’ back, you at Kiki on the river", "vault_lines": ["You be textin' back, you at Kiki on the river"], "meaning": "Kiki on the River is a high-end Greek restaurant located in Miami. The cuisine is known for its spacious Mediterranean island-inspired riverfront setting.\n\n\n\nInterior of Kiki on the River\n\nThis line is also a callback to Drake’s certified platinum 2018 track “In My Feelings”:\n\nKiki, do you love me? Are you riding?\nSay you’ll never ever leave from beside me", "annotation_id": "25704540", "url": "https://genius.com/25704540", "state": "accepted", "votes": 80, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
