{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 Mazza", "status": "done", "targets": 20, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Smiley-and-drake-2-mazza-lyrics", "genius_title": "2 Mazza", "genius_id": 11273485, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 Mazza", "line": "This kick iron stick like Jackie (Kick), I hate to argue with catties (Hate it)", "vault_lines": ["This kick iron stick like Jackie (Kick), I hate to argue with catties (Hate it)"], "meaning": "Jackie Chan is a martial artist, stuntman, and actor renowned for his acrobatic fighting style, innovative stunts, and comedic timing.\n\nA “stick” refers to a gun, and a firearm naturally has kickback when fired. Comparing it to Jackie Chan suggests the recoil hits quickly and forcefully, like the sharp punches he throws in his movies.\n\nA “catty” refers to a petty woman or one who is always looking for attention. Slimey is saying he doesn’t want to waste time arguing with them, especially when he is focused on more serious things in his life and career, a point he also makes in the track “In My Zone”:\n\nI’m collecting checks in the month\nI knew I was the one in the bunch\nBaby, I can’t even take you to brunch\nBaby, I’m going hard like a punch\nHow can I do it for you? I have to do it for me\nI’m stacking, I swear I was moving so cheap", "annotation_id": "37811685", "url": "https://genius.com/37811685", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 Mazza", "line": "My Houston lil’ bitch every week at Johnny’s, nigga (Johnny’s)", "vault_lines": ["My Houston lil' bitch every week at Johnny's, nigga (Johnny's)"], "meaning": "Double entendre. His girlfriend from Houston would frequently go to Johnny Dang’s jewelry store, which is based in Houston. She would also visit Johnny’s hamburger, a legendary burger joint in Scarborough, when she’s in the city of Toronto. The bar itself was 2 mazza.", "annotation_id": "35985547", "url": "https://genius.com/35985547", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 Mazza", "line": "Yeah, Mr. 2 Mazza, Mr. 2 Mazza, Mr. 2 Mazza (Maz’) And they callin’ me that ‘cause the chain and my grills is lookin’ too mazza (Diamond touch)", "vault_lines": ["And they callin' me that 'cause the watch too mazza (Maz')", "Yeah, yeah, and they callin' me that 'cause the spot's too mazza (Mod')", "Yeah, Mr. 2 Mazza, Mr. 2 Mazza, Mr. 2 Mazza (Maz')", "And they callin' me that 'cause the chain and my grills is lookin' too mazza (Diamond touch)"], "meaning": "Smiley starts the song by stating how  Mazza  things are for him, from the chain to the grills, while giving his signature shout out to the jeweller that created his items", "annotation_id": "35934890", "url": "https://genius.com/35934890", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 Mazza", "line": "Geo-Georgia Montizi is mazza (Yeah), the disclosure had sticks and a Masi’ (Patek)", "vault_lines": ["Geo-Georgia Montizi is mazza (Yeah), the disclosure had sticks and a Masi' (Patek)"], "meaning": "In Smiley’s disclosure after he was arrested, it stated  there were firearms found in his Mazda.", "annotation_id": "35934847", "url": "https://genius.com/35934847", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 Mazza", "line": "Lil’ garden girl straight from the hood, she got a lil’ condo at ’Sauga (Monroe)", "vault_lines": ["Lil' garden girl straight from the hood, she got a lil' condo at 'Sauga (Monroe)"], "meaning": "In this lyric Smiley is talking about a girl while also giving  reference to his neighborhood (Pelham Park Garden), and shouting out the Monroe Condos in Mississauga Ontario.", "annotation_id": "35934801", "url": "https://genius.com/35934801", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 Mazza", "line": "Astral could make one lap in here, come back with ten Em Ratas (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["Astral could make one lap in here, come back with ten Em Ratas (Woo)"], "meaning": "Astral, could be a shoutout to @photosbyastral. Who’s taken pictures of Drake and the OVO crew.\n\n“EmRata” is the nickname for runway model Emily Ratajkowski. Drake has previously mentioned EmRata in his song, Middle of the Ocean.\n\n…EmRata here fresh off divorce. And I’m trynna look in her eyes, maybe express my remorse…\"\n\nWhomever Astral is, Drake is implying he can do a whole lap around the club, or wherever they’re partying at and easily come back with women who are models like EmRata. Ten of them to be exact.", "annotation_id": "35913435", "url": "https://genius.com/35913435", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 Mazza", "line": "And they callin’ me that ’cause the watch too mazza (Maz’) Yeah, yeah, and they callin’ me that ’cause the spot’s too mazza (Mod’)", "vault_lines": ["And they callin' me that 'cause the watch too mazza (Maz')", "Yeah, yeah, and they callin' me that 'cause the spot's too mazza (Mod')", "Yeah, Mr. 2 Mazza, Mr. 2 Mazza, Mr. 2 Mazza (Maz')", "And they callin' me that 'cause the chain and my grills is lookin' too mazza (Diamond touch)"], "meaning": "In addition to his ability to make hits, Drake is known for his extensive watch collection, reportedly owning over one hundred timepieces from brands such as Rolex, Audemars Piguet and Richard Mille, as well as his impressive mega mansion, or “spot,” known as the Embassy.", "annotation_id": "35898074", "url": "https://genius.com/35898074", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 Mazza", "line": "Some nights I wanna cut ’cause the city’s been hot like lava (Fire)", "vault_lines": ["Some nights I wanna cut 'cause the city's been hot like lava (Fire)"], "meaning": "Despite his love for his hometown, there is a high level of crime and gang activity that makes it dangerous, or hot, for someone with Drake’s notoriety, fame and success. This is especially true given he was the subject of a shooting at his home in May 2024. That is why Drake needs to get out of town for a while to lie low and let the heat die down.\n\nSeparately, given that Drake is tapped in with meme culture, this may be a reference to the “Steve’s Lava Chicken” meme originating from the Minecraft movie.", "annotation_id": "35898058", "url": "https://genius.com/35898058", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 Mazza", "line": "Me, I’m the 6 God, Bob is a bulldog, both could have been at Gonzaga, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Me, I'm the 6 God, Bob is a bulldog, both could have been at Gonzaga, nigga"], "meaning": "The Gonzaga Bulldogs are a D1 intercollegiate men’s basketball team representing Gonzaga University, a private university in Spokane, Washington.\n\nDrake wearing a custom Gonzaga Bulldogs x Nocta jersey\n\nDrake, often called the “6 God” due to his influence in Toronto (commonly referred to as the 6 because of its 416 area code), refers to Smiley, also known as Mr. Bob or simply Bob, as a bulldog, alluding to his savage nature and reputation as a cold blooded killer in the Toronto underground.\n\nSeparately, and tying into the Bulldogs reference and the idea that he could have played for them, Drake is an avid basketball fan. He founded his own amateur league and built a full size basketball court at his Toronto mansion.", "annotation_id": "35898057", "url": "https://genius.com/35898057", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 Mazza", "line": "First floor room at the airport, Ramada, I’m tryna make the most out of nada (Nothing)", "vault_lines": ["First floor room at the airport, Ramada, I'm tryna make the most out of nada (Nothing)"], "meaning": "Ramada Plaza by Wyndham was a budget hotel located 5 kms from the Toronto International Airport and approximately 15 kms from downtown Toronto that has since closed down. Drizzy used to stay here in a room on the first floor while he was on the come up and had nothing to his name.", "annotation_id": "35898019", "url": "https://genius.com/35898019", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 Mazza", "line": "Yeah, lil’ Waterloo road trip, shorty see me", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, lil' Waterloo road trip, shorty see me", "Yeah, lil' Waterloo road trip, shorty see me and said, \"Oh shit, girl, that's Mr. 2 Mazza\" (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Drake is referencing the trips that he made to the City of Waterloo, a college town west of Toronto. He would frequent Waterloo for to see shorty (a girl) who was studying at the University of Waterloo where they would frequent parties at Laurier University together.", "annotation_id": "35897497", "url": "https://genius.com/35897497", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 Mazza", "line": "Me, I’m the 6 God, Bob is a bulldog, both could have been at Gonzaga, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Me, I'm the 6 God, Bob is a bulldog, both could have been at Gonzaga, nigga"], "meaning": "In parallel to the release of this song, Kendrick Lamar was performing his first of two shows of the GNX tour at Toronto.\n\nAs Kendrick shows in Drake’s hometown dissing him, Drake tries to remind him that he’s the 6 God.\n\nDrake makes a double-entendre by calling Bob a bulldog, as the full name of the basketball team of Gonzaga is “Gonzaga Bulldogs”.", "annotation_id": "35888744", "url": "https://genius.com/35888744", "state": "pending", "votes": -2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 Mazza", "line": "They sleeping on Smiggs like a Xanny (Sleep)", "vault_lines": ["They sleeping on Smiggs like a Xanny (Sleep)"], "meaning": "A Xanny, slang for Xanax, is a prescription drug known for its strong and sedative effects. Smiley is emphasising how deeply people are ignoring his music and not acknowledging him", "annotation_id": "35888681", "url": "https://genius.com/35888681", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 Mazza", "line": "I’m in Barrie, Muskoka, and Brampton, fuck Hollywood and the Hamptons (Fuck)", "vault_lines": ["I'm in Barrie, Muskoka, and Brampton, fuck Hollywood and the Hamptons (Fuck)"], "meaning": "Barrie, Muskoka, and Brampton are all situated in Ontario, Canada. Drake is emphasising his roots and pride in staying local. Rather than going to traditional celebrity hotspots like Hollywood or the Hamptons, he’s choosing to rep his home turf.", "annotation_id": "35888660", "url": "https://genius.com/35888660", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 Mazza", "line": "“Oh shit, girl, that’s Mr. 2 Mazza”", "vault_lines": ["and said, \"Oh shit, girl, that's Mr. 2 Mazza\"", "Yeah, Mr. 2 Mazza, Mr. 2 Mazza, Mr. 2 Mazza (Maz')", "Yeah, lil' Waterloo road trip, shorty see me and said, \"Oh shit, girl, that's Mr. 2 Mazza\" (Yeah)"], "meaning": "“Mazza” is UK slang for madness or something wild and intense. Drake calls himself “Mr. 2 Mazza” to reflect his over the top and crazy lifestyle", "annotation_id": "35888524", "url": "https://genius.com/35888524", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 Mazza", "line": "Yeah, Mr. 2 Mazza, my Hamilton girl look like Scarlett Johansson (Peace) Just with a way bigger bamski, and this is the anthem", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, Mr. 2 Mazza, my Hamilton girl look like Scarlett Johansson (Peace)", "Just with a way bigger bamski, and this is the anthem", "Yeah, Mr. 2 Mazza, Mr. 2 Mazza, Mr. 2 Mazza (Maz')"], "meaning": "Drake is referencing Hamilton, a city in Ontario, Canada, nodding to a girl from there. He compares her to Scarlett Johansson, who is widely regarded as very attractive, but adds that his girl has a “way bigger bamski\" (a slang term for a curvier figure/big behind).\n\nThis comparison recalls to a moment when both Drake and Scarlett Johansson appeared together on The Tonight Show, where Drake seemed to have a noticeable crush on her.", "annotation_id": "35888329", "url": "https://genius.com/35888329", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 Mazza", "line": "Grocery shoppin’ at Royal York Plaza Me and lil’ Sandra was broke on the Gaza", "vault_lines": ["Grocery shoppin' at Royal York Plaza", "Me and lil' Sandra was broke on the Gaza"], "meaning": "“Royal Plaza,” or Royal York Plaza, is a small strip mall in Etobicoke, Toronto. This isn’t a flex about expensive shopping but rather reminiscent of Drake’s memories of grocery shopping there with his mother, Sandra, who raised him as a single parent.\n\n\n\n“Gaza,” aka Gaza Strip, is a region known for its struggles and hardship. Drake links this to his own humble beginnings shopping at a modest strip mall with his mother (notice the wordplay; rather than saying the strip, he used the word “Gaza.”)\n\nThese bars are reminiscent of his bar from his 2020 collaboration with Headie One, “Only You Freestyle”:\n\nWith Pop Skull in Gaza, but not that Gaza, but still it’s a mazza", "annotation_id": "35888212", "url": "https://genius.com/35888212", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 Mazza", "line": "I remember pushin’ DT with the mandem, whipping two Mazdas (Double M)", "vault_lines": ["I remember pushin' DT with the mandem, whipping two Mazdas (Double M)"], "meaning": "Drake reminisces about his more humble days, driving around downtown Toronto (“DT”) with his friends in two Mazda cars, Highlighting how far he’s come since those simpler times. The reference to the “two Mazdas” also plays into the track’s title, “2 Mazza,” which is slang for “too wild or crazy.”", "annotation_id": "35888149", "url": "https://genius.com/35888149", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 Mazza", "line": "I’m in a Bridle path mansion (Path), Ferris Rafauli expansion (Yes)", "vault_lines": ["I'm in a Bridle path mansion (Path), Ferris Rafauli expansion (Yes)"], "meaning": "Drake is referring to his mansion in Canada, dubbed “The Embassy”, which is located in the richest neighborhood of Toronto, the Bridle Path neighborhood. The mansion is designed by architect and interior designer Ferris Rafauli.", "annotation_id": "35887442", "url": "https://genius.com/35887442", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "2 Mazza", "line": "I’m with Smiggalino, I’m with Smiggalachi, Mr. Don’t Mix The Gucci And Prada (I don’t)", "vault_lines": ["I'm with Smiggalino, I'm with Smiggalachi, Mr. Don't Mix The Gucci And Prada (I don't)"], "meaning": "Drake gives the bar an Italian feel by putting Italian twists on Smiley’s moniker, “Smiggy”, while mentioning two well-known Italian fashion brands\n\nDrake could also be referencing Smiley’s lyrics from their 2021 collaboration “Over The Top”:\n\nPrada and Gucci, it don’t go together\nLouis and Dior, I swear it go better", "annotation_id": "35885819", "url": "https://genius.com/35885819", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
