{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "One Day (Remix)", "line": "Me and Carnage, fifty hoes in our hotel, Ibiza shit", "vault_lines": ["Me and Carnage, fifty hoes in our hotel, Ibiza shit"], "meaning": "Drake mentions the time he spent in Ibiza, Spain with Guatemalan-American DJ and record producer Carnage, alluding to the duo having partaken in an orgy with upwards of fifty women.\n\nNotably, Carnage was the first to preview this song, playing it at a performance in Germany on September 2, 2021.", "annotation_id": "24051464", "url": "https://genius.com/24051464", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "One Day (Remix)", "line": "What’s that on your wrist? Man, it’s a Raphael", "vault_lines": ["What's that on your wrist? Man, it's a Raphael"], "meaning": "Drake references Swiss watch company Richard Mille’s range of watches in collaboration with Spanish tennis player Rafael Nadal.\n\nRichard Mille and Nadal launched their partnership in 2010, creating a series of lightweight watches for Nadal to wear whilst playing tennis.\n\nThese watches are highly sought after, with the RM 27-04 Tourbillon beginning at $1,050,000 with a total production run of just 50 units, and fetching upwards of $3.2 million on the aftermarket.\n\nDrake rapped about his Rafael Nadal Richard Mille watch on the track “You Only Live Twice” from his sixth studio album, Certified Lover Boy, rapping:\n\nYeah, two-point-two for the Rafael Nadal\nDon’t act like you’re happy for me now\n\n\n\nDrake wearing his limited edition Richard Mille x Rafael Nadal RM27-04", "annotation_id": "24051320", "url": "https://genius.com/24051320", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fo’ Real", "status": "done", "targets": 2, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Future-fo-real-lyrics", "genius_title": "Fo’ Real", "genius_id": 108718, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fo’ Real", "line": "We had a good year this year, we made a lot of fortunes (Bankroll) And we very fortunate (Woo, woo, woo)", "vault_lines": ["We had a good year this year, we made a lot of fortunes (Bankroll)", "And we very fortunate (Woo, woo, woo)"], "meaning": "He his first studio album “Pluto” in April of 2012. The album spawned four successful singles, including “Turn on the Lights”, which peaked at #2 on the US R&B/Hip-Hop Songs charts, #4 on the U.S. Rap Songs charts, and #1 on the Heatseekers Song charts. As of December 2, 2012 the album had sold over 217,000 copies in the United States\n\n\n\nHe also collaborated with artists like Rihanna, The Game and Lil Wayne for their albums.\n\nSo I’m sure he’s spot on with the statement that he made fortunes and for that he’s very fortunate", "annotation_id": "1401316", "url": "https://genius.com/1401316", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Fo’ Real", "line": "Even though I used to act, man, this shit is not a act, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Even though I used to act, man, this shit is not a act, nigga"], "meaning": "Before Drake became a rapper, he played a role as a character named “Jimmy” in the TV Show Degrassi: The Next Generation.\n\nDrake is saying that he is authentic and being himself. This is unlike when he acting as Jimmy on the T.V. show.", "annotation_id": "1401238", "url": "https://genius.com/1401238", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
