{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SPIDER-MAN SUPERMAN", "line": "The way we fucked is better than what we DM’d on Insta’ (Oh, yeah)", "vault_lines": ["The way we fucked is better than what we DM'd on Insta' (Oh, yeah)"], "meaning": "Drake and the woman have been exchanging sexually suggestive messages on Instagram. When they eventually met up in person to have sex, the chemistry and enjoyment exceeded that of their sexy messages.", "annotation_id": "36986490", "url": "https://genius.com/36986490", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SPIDER-MAN SUPERMAN", "line": "This girl wants, this girl wants me to save her, I— This girl wants me to save her, I can’t This girl wants me, this girl wants This girl wants me to save her, I can’t", "vault_lines": ["This girl wants, this girl wants me to save her, I—", "This girl wants me to save her, I can't", "This girl wants me, this girl wants", "This girl wants me"], "meaning": "“This girl wants me to save her” means that this girl wants Drake to finance her desired lifestyle (rent, clothes, cars, etc.)", "annotation_id": "36860111", "url": "https://genius.com/36860111", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SPIDER-MAN SUPERMAN", "line": "You kept askin’ if I’m extendin’ that spot or not Since you got what you wanted, we don’t talk a lot", "vault_lines": ["You kept askin' if I'm extendin' that spot or not", "Since you got what you wanted, we don't talk a lot"], "meaning": "“Extending that spot” implies that Drake has arranged for an apartment lease for a girl that he is talking to, and is paying her rent.\n\nThe following line implies that since Drake has paid her rent for this month, she has no reason to reach out to him anymore.", "annotation_id": "36860104", "url": "https://genius.com/36860104", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SPIDER-MAN SUPERMAN", "line": "How could you admire a man? They don’t even come nice to the dance", "vault_lines": ["They don't even come nice to the dance", "How could you admire a man?"], "meaning": "Earlier in Drake’s career, he developed a reputation for “cleaning up nice,” pulling up to red carpets in tailored suits and tuxedos. Here, Drake is saying “how could you be interested in someone who doesn’t clean up when you step out together?”", "annotation_id": "36860057", "url": "https://genius.com/36860057", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SPIDER-MAN SUPERMAN", "line": "Lucky for you, I don’t just love you for you I love you for who you tell me you’re gonna be one day too", "vault_lines": ["Lucky for you, I don't just love you for you", "I love you for who you tell me you're gonna be one day too"], "meaning": "Here, Drake expresses how he loves her for more than her physical appearance and who she is currently.\n\nHe also loves her aspirations and goals for her future that she’s shared with him.", "annotation_id": "35102329", "url": "https://genius.com/35102329", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SPIDER-MAN SUPERMAN", "line": "That girl took me for Spider-Man (It’s mad), Superman (Spider-Man)", "vault_lines": ["This girl took me for Spider-Man (Spider-Man), Supеrman (Superman, oh)", "Took me for Spider-Man", "Took me for Superman, ayy", "That girl took me for Spider-Man (It's mad), Superman (Spider-Man)"], "meaning": "Here, Drake expresses how the woman he is dealing with, expected him to be a “Super Hero” and “save” her from her current situation with money, experiences etc.\n\nThis is most likely a reference to Baby M who Drake has referenced in multiple songs from his Her Loss album. Specifically in the song Hours in silence Drake states: “ Baby M, you know I got a heart of gold, you pawned that sh** and hit the road”.\n\nDrake has had recent history with Baby M and conflict with NBA player Dillion Brooks who is her current boyfriend.", "annotation_id": "35102167", "url": "https://genius.com/35102167", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SPIDER-MAN SUPERMAN", "line": "(Houston girls love the way it goes, goes)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This is again sampled from the track “The Real Her” from Drake’s 2011 album Take Care:\n\nHouston girls love the way it goes down\nAtlanta girls love the way it goes down\nVegas girls love the way it goes down\n\nThis track is also reminiscent of Drake’s 2009 song “Houstatlantavegas” from the mixtape So Far Gone.", "annotation_id": "34593343", "url": "https://genius.com/34593343", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SPIDER-MAN SUPERMAN", "line": "[Outro: Drake]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "The outro extensively samples Drake’s November 2011 track with Lil Wayne and André 3000, “The Real Her”. It’s worth noting that through the song, Drake interpolates lyrics from the original track.", "annotation_id": "34562456", "url": "https://genius.com/34562456", "state": "accepted", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SPIDER-MAN SUPERMAN", "line": "Girl, I wish I could save you (Yeah), but I can’t (Okay, look)", "vault_lines": ["Now I'll admit that I wish I could save you (Savе you), but I can't", "Sorry-sorry, but I can't-can't, I'm sorry-sorry, but I can't-can't", "I'm sorry-sorry, but I can't, I'm sorry-sorry, but I can't", "Girl, I wish I could save you (Yeah), but I can't (Okay, look)"], "meaning": "Drake interpolates his 2011 collaboration with André 3000 and Lil Wayne, “The Real Her”:\n\nThey keep telling me don’t save you\nIf I ignore all that advice, then something isn’t right\n\n“The Real Her” can be heard as a sample in this track’s outro.", "annotation_id": "34560726", "url": "https://genius.com/34560726", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wildfire (OVO Remix)", "status": "done", "targets": 4, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Sbtrkt-wildfire-ovo-remix-lyrics", "genius_title": "Wildfire (OVO Remix)", "genius_id": 50199, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wildfire (OVO Remix)", "line": "If they kill me, bury me a legend, bitch better have my tomb right, ahh", "vault_lines": ["If they kill me, bury me a legend, bitch better have my tomb right, ahh"], "meaning": "Tombs of notable figures are known to be extravagantly designed or decorated.\n\nThis song is from 2011. Drake also expresses himself deserving the same posthumous title on the song “Legend” (2015).", "annotation_id": "31809585", "url": "https://genius.com/31809585", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wildfire (OVO Remix)", "line": "So-and-so just walked in, so what? I don’t really vibe with a lot of these niggas", "vault_lines": ["So-and-so just walked in, so what?", "I don't really vibe with a lot of these niggas"], "meaning": "A common theme in Drake’s music is not pretending to be friendly with industry peers that he doesn’t get along with.", "annotation_id": "31809553", "url": "https://genius.com/31809553", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wildfire (OVO Remix)", "line": "Your girlfriend at my next show, OVOXO, nigga", "vault_lines": ["Your girlfriend at my next show, OVOXO, nigga"], "meaning": "OVOXO is a combination of Drake’s label, October’s Very Own, and The Weeknd’s label, XO. The name represents their collaborative identity.", "annotation_id": "31809532", "url": "https://genius.com/31809532", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Wildfire (OVO Remix)", "line": "You ain’t living that boy, stop stealin’ that light", "vault_lines": ["You ain't living that boy, stop stealin' that light"], "meaning": "Drake is referring to rappers who rap about things they don’t experience. So he doesn’t want rappers to get attention, by talking about false things. Drake doesn’t think they deserve to get recognition and attention if they aren’t actually living what they are rapping about.\n\nEven though Drake isn’t referring to Rick Ross, because they are obviously good friends (since they’re working on a mixtape together). But Rick Ross is a great example of this, because he used to be a correctional officer\n\n\n\n#but\n raps about making, and selling drugs (he could sell drugs, but it’s unlikely).\n\nDrake is getting tired of these rappers that are being fake but getting a lot of fame from this, fame that he could be getting if these fake rappers weren’t getting it off of their lies.", "annotation_id": "1238738", "url": "https://genius.com/1238738", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MR RECOUP", "status": "done", "targets": 24, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/21-savage-and-drake-mr-recoup-lyrics", "genius_title": "MR RECOUP", "genius_id": 12822837, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MR RECOUP", "line": "My life ain’t a movie, bitch, it’s just us They can’t find the shooter, bitch, ’cause it’s us", "vault_lines": ["My life ain't a movie, bitch, it's just us", "They can't find the shooter, bitch, 'cause it's us"], "meaning": "This line is an interpolation of Fabolous’s verse on Joe Budden’s “She Don’t Put It Down (Remix)”, where he says, “If you looking for the best, tell ‘em it’s us.” Drake mirrors Fab’s signature mid-2000s cadence and “Brooklyn bounce” delivery.\n\nIn addition, Fabolous raps in his verse about not knowing who to trust, a theme Drake continues in his chorus.\n\nFabolous on She Don’t Put It Down (Remix)", "annotation_id": "38596523", "url": "https://genius.com/38596523", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MR RECOUP", "line": "Chubbs’ Tyler Perry, he make plays for the block", "vault_lines": ["Chubbs' Tyler Perry, he make plays for the block"], "meaning": "Similar to how the productions of Tyler Perry, American playwright/actor and creator of the Madea series, are aimed at his community; Drake’s Head of Security Chubbs makes plays to support Drake and those around him.", "annotation_id": "38004444", "url": "https://genius.com/38004444", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MR RECOUP", "line": "My opps be so broke that we’ve been shootin’ at the bus", "vault_lines": ["My opps be so broke that we've been shootin' at the bus"], "meaning": "A fun jab that highlights how poor his opps are—so poor in fact, that they have to take a bus to get around.  It’s funnier because of the use of the present participle “we [have been] shooting.”  This implies it’s an action that occurred at least once in the past and continues into the present.  This highlights the continued pressure 21 Savage places on his opps, as well as the enduring nature of their poverty.", "annotation_id": "37951692", "url": "https://genius.com/37951692", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MR RECOUP", "line": "Your initials just changed", "vault_lines": [", your initials just changed"], "meaning": "Drake’s real name is Aubrey Graham. In the context of the song, his initials shift from AG to AR, meaning Aubrey Recoup, which is also the initialism for ArmaLite rifles, so he is comparing himself to the weapon.", "annotation_id": "37935451", "url": "https://genius.com/37935451", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MR RECOUP", "line": "Pitch-black paint, but the seats, they vanilla (Go)", "vault_lines": ["Pitch-black paint, but the seats, they vanilla (Go)"], "meaning": "Savage’s car collection contains serveral luxury vehicles and is estimated to be worth more than $1.3 million dollars. Here, he describes a vehicle that has black exterior with white seats. This could refer to his Mercedes Maybach from his collection (pictured), or any of his other black vehicles with white seats.", "annotation_id": "37929425", "url": "https://genius.com/37929425", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MR RECOUP", "line": "Every single year, what I’m grossin’, it get bigger", "vault_lines": ["Every single year, what I'm grossin', it get bigger"], "meaning": "Savage boasts that as he has grown bigger in the rap game, over time the amount of money he grosses annually (total amount before taxes/expenses) increases. Savage owns his own masters which allows him to keep a greater share of streaming income, and brings in considerable revenue from touring too. Recent estimates put his net worth between $12-16 million.", "annotation_id": "37929407", "url": "https://genius.com/37929407", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MR RECOUP", "line": "Wasn’t even ’bout to rap on this, but it knocks", "vault_lines": ["Wasn't even 'bout to rap on this, but it knocks"], "meaning": "Drake recognizes that this instrumental is a bit goofy? It does knock though", "annotation_id": "37926935", "url": "https://genius.com/37926935", "state": "pending", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MR RECOUP", "line": "We was just on Yonge Street, they was eatin’ it up", "vault_lines": ["Us, us, it was us", "We was just on Yonge Street, they was eatin' it up"], "meaning": "Yonge Street is a prominent street in Toronto that runs through the downtown area. It has hundreds of restaurants and eateries.\n\nDrake here is using a double entendre: he’s being serviced in the car while driving (or being driven) through the street, surrounded by eateries.", "annotation_id": "37925976", "url": "https://genius.com/37925976", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MR RECOUP", "line": "Spade at the party", "vault_lines": ["Spade at the party, long wheelbase Range", "Spade at the party"], "meaning": "He said “Spade after party” in reference to DJ Spade who’s his tour DJ.", "annotation_id": "37925794", "url": "https://genius.com/37925794", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MR RECOUP", "line": "Long wheelbase Range", "vault_lines": ["Spade at the party, long wheelbase Range"], "meaning": "*Long wheelbase Range. This is referring to the Long wheelbase variant of the Range Rover. The longer body style allows for more luxurious and comfortable seating in the second row.", "annotation_id": "37924827", "url": "https://genius.com/37924827", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MR RECOUP", "line": "We the type of niggas, cut the tails off the rats (Bitch)", "vault_lines": ["We the type of niggas, cut the tails off the rats (Bitch)"], "meaning": "“Cut the tails off the rats” is a double entendre. Literally, it’s a brutal, permanent act against the rodent. But for 21, he’s cutting all ties and connections he has to rats, or otherwise known snitches.\n“Tail” is also a term to refer to an unwanted follower, who could also be a rat.", "annotation_id": "37919539", "url": "https://genius.com/37919539", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MR RECOUP", "line": "Go against the mob, you’ll be layin’ on your back (Frrt)", "vault_lines": ["Go against the mob, you'll be layin' on your back (Frrt)"], "meaning": "Going against the mob in a gun fight will most likely end in you dying and hence “layin' on your back” dead.", "annotation_id": "37919388", "url": "https://genius.com/37919388", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MR RECOUP", "line": "I got fifty-somethin’ old schools like my name Spitta (21)", "vault_lines": ["I got fifty-somethin' old schools like my name Spitta (21)"], "meaning": "Reference to New Orleans rapper Curren$y aka “Spitta” and his extensive collection of old school cars and lowriders", "annotation_id": "37918883", "url": "https://genius.com/37918883", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MR RECOUP", "line": "Drake is your daddy and he couldn’t find a sitter", "vault_lines": ["Drake is your daddy and he couldn't find a sitter"], "meaning": "Kendrick was topping charts hiphop when started to top on billboards less and less, some suggest that the this recent trough in the hiphop industry was because Drake wasn’t dropping. This suggests Drake thinks or believes his next album will revive the hiphop scene and prove his dominance in the scene.", "annotation_id": "37916407", "url": "https://genius.com/37916407", "state": "pending", "votes": -43, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MR RECOUP", "line": "Bro say, “Play it patient,” nah, dog, I’m in a rush, I’m tryna buck", "vault_lines": ["Bro say, \"Play it patient,\" nah, dog, I'm in a rush, I'm tryna buck"], "meaning": "21 Savage likes to get everything (in the hood) done quickly and doesnt wait for anything even if his friends tell him.", "annotation_id": "37915414", "url": "https://genius.com/37915414", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MR RECOUP", "line": "All these niggas cap, they exaggeratin’ hats (Pussy)", "vault_lines": ["All these niggas cap, they exaggeratin' hats (Pussy)"], "meaning": "21 Savage says how many rappers lie about their life for example, their street life and how they exaggerate everything based on their lifestyle", "annotation_id": "37915403", "url": "https://genius.com/37915403", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MR RECOUP", "line": "I converse with CEOs, you talk on the pillow (Go)", "vault_lines": ["I converse with CEOs, you talk on the pillow (Go)"], "meaning": "Savage contrasts his lifestyle with that of his opps. While Savage is conversing with powerful and rich executives and making business deals, his opps merely engage in pillow talk, the intimate conversations with a partner following sexual activity.", "annotation_id": "37913293", "url": "https://genius.com/37913293", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MR RECOUP", "line": "I’m tryna add him to the list like a deluxe, ayy", "vault_lines": ["I'm tryna add him to the list like a deluxe, ayy"], "meaning": "Adding someone to the list is a methaphorical slang of someone naming people in a list of who they want to take out (kill). The twist in the line is that 21 Savage compares it to “a deluxe”, better said an Album’s Deluxe version, which is when an extended version of ‘said album’ gets released again, this time including some new extra tracks. Thereby, an album’s tracklist extends, due to “songs being added on to the list”", "annotation_id": "37910899", "url": "https://genius.com/37910899", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MR RECOUP", "line": "No Face B, that’s my motherfuckin’ hitter", "vault_lines": ["No Face B, that's my motherfuckin' hitter"], "meaning": "“No Face B” most likely refers to Bash, a member from G-Way (Galloway), an area that Drake has close ties to, however it could refer to BFR Bundog, the older brother of Toronto rapper Pressa and is a senior member of the Driftwood Crips. Bundog is known for not showing his face, always wearing a mask and sunglasses.\n\nIn street/rap slang, a “hitter” is someone who handles threats or rivals, something Bundog has a reputation of doing. Bundog even allegedly shot Kodak Black during an altercation. Drake is boasting about having real steppers in his corner who are willing to handle beef in the streets for him.\n\n\n\nBundog", "annotation_id": "37910537", "url": "https://genius.com/37910537", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MR RECOUP", "line": "Mr. Recoup, that’s my other nickname", "vault_lines": ["Mr. Recoup, that's my other nickname"], "meaning": "“Recoup” literally means to get back what you lost.\nDrake calling himself “Mr. Recoup” suggests he sees himself as someone who always makes his money and status back — even after losses or setbacks. It’s flexing resilience and financial clout.\n\nThis can also be a reference to recouping his status and form after his feud with Kendrick.", "annotation_id": "37910511", "url": "https://genius.com/37910511", "state": "pending", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MR RECOUP", "line": "Niggas shot my brother, now I don’t know who to trust", "vault_lines": ["Niggas shot my brother, now I don't know who to trust"], "meaning": "21’s brother, Quantivayus “Tayman” Joseph, was shot and killed in a drug deal gone bad.\n\nAlso likely a double entendre alluding to various rappers who Drake felt turned on him during his feud with Kendrick Lamar.", "annotation_id": "37909173", "url": "https://genius.com/37909173", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MR RECOUP", "line": "Damn, Alex Moss, that’s a really big chain", "vault_lines": ["Damn, Alex Moss, that's a really big chain"], "meaning": "Alex Moss is celebrity jeweler known for creating extravagant custom pieces for stars like A$AP Rocky, Chief Keef, Tyler, the Creator, and Drake. He is known for his high-profile, intricate jewelry,  and has made a few pieces for Drake.", "annotation_id": "37908871", "url": "https://genius.com/37908871", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
