{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MOTH BALLS", "line": "Ooh, oh You’re doing that thing, you’re doing that thing You’re doing that thing, you’re doing that thing again", "vault_lines": ["You're doing that thing, you're doing that thing", "You're doing that thing, you're doing that thing again"], "meaning": "He’s focused on a specific action from the other person that he finds attractive or exciting, with repetition used to build rhythm and emphasis.", "annotation_id": "40237043", "url": "https://genius.com/40237043", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MOTH BALLS", "line": "On God, swimmin’ in the cat ’til I drown", "vault_lines": ["On God, swimmin' in the cat 'til I drown"], "meaning": "Cat is a euphemism for a woman’s vagina, due to it’s association with the word pussy. Drake is in the (wet) pussy for so long he may drown. Drake has several similar lyrics, most recently in BRIAN STEEL from the same album:\n\npussy so good, it could keep me inside", "annotation_id": "36977235", "url": "https://genius.com/36977235", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
