{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MOTH BALLS", "line": "Now shorties call me Drake, not Aubrey Graham, damn", "vault_lines": ["Now shorties call me Drake, not Aubrey Graham, damn"], "meaning": "‚Aubrey Drake Graham‘ is Drake‘s legal name. Now that he has become world famous under his stage name, people, including girls, refer to him as „Drake“. Before he became successful they would naturally refer to him by his legal name Aubrey Graham. His legal name has been the subject of discussion, notably in his famous interview with Bobbi Althoff:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-MlDq-BgY7s&pp=0gcJCfcAhR29_xXO", "annotation_id": "35028543", "url": "https://genius.com/35028543", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MOTH BALLS", "line": "Bitches wanna take a dip in my account", "vault_lines": ["Bitches wanna take a dip in my account"], "meaning": "Instead of wanting him for his personality or even looks, Drake says girls only want him for his money. They just want to have the nice things it can buy them. It plays on the idea of someone “swimming in money,” usually meaning that they’re individually very rich.\n\n\n\nThis line also ties in with the drowning bar right before it and the water bars in the chorus.", "annotation_id": "34673248", "url": "https://genius.com/34673248", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MOTH BALLS", "line": "This has to work so I get Neeks off that stove", "vault_lines": ["This has to work so I get Neeks off that stove"], "meaning": "Neeks is the nickname for Niko Carino, one of Drake’s closest friends and Co-Founder of OVO. Drake expresses urgency about his success, hoping to help Neeks to get away from working.\n\nOne of Drake’s oldest friends, Niko was introduced to Drake through the show Degrassi. Since then, the two have been inseparable, building a global empire with OVO and its subsidiaries.\n\nThis is far from the first time Drake has shown love to his right-hand man, mentioning him on his June 2010 track, “Miss Me”, where he raps:\n\nNeeks got the weed, Hush got a gun\nCJ got my credit cards and a lot of ones", "annotation_id": "34621371", "url": "https://genius.com/34621371", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MOTH BALLS", "line": "Treat her stomach to Michelin", "vault_lines": ["Treat her stomach to Michelin"], "meaning": "Michelin Stars are awarded to restaurants or individual chefs for excellence and superb quality levels. Over 3,600 restaurants in the world hold a Michelin Star, ranging from one star to around 150 with three stars.\n\nParty claims that he treats his woman to the best dining experience, on par with his lavish lifestyle. Recently, Drake and Party covered the checks for strangers dining at Tatiana on Valentine’s Day. While Tatiana isn’t a Michelin-starred restaurant, they do make an appearance in the Michelin Guide.", "annotation_id": "34589001", "url": "https://genius.com/34589001", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MOTH BALLS", "line": "Yorkville thrills, baby-blue pills, slop-top skills", "vault_lines": ["Yorkville thrills, baby-blue pills, slop-top skills"], "meaning": "Yorkville is an affluent neighborhood in Toronto known for its luxury shopping, high-end restaurants, and exclusive lifestyle. It’s one of Toronto’s most expensive and prestigious areas, often associated with celebrity culture and luxury living.\n\nThe line paints a picture of high-end lifestyle through multiple references:\n1. The reference to “Baby-blue pills” suggests themes of recreational drug use in wealthy circles;\n2. The mention of “skills” paired with “slop-top” uses wordplay to reference intimate activities.", "annotation_id": "34578807", "url": "https://genius.com/34578807", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MOTH BALLS", "line": "‘Sauga City kid, got you blushin’ on cam What?", "vault_lines": ["'Sauga City kid, got you blushin' on cam"], "meaning": "Mississauga is a city located just southwest of Toronto. It’s is one of Canada’s largest cities, best known as Ontario’s shopping capital.", "annotation_id": "34577936", "url": "https://genius.com/34577936", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MOTH BALLS", "line": "I remember baggin’ up at No Frills", "vault_lines": ["I remember baggin' up at No Frills"], "meaning": "No Frills is a Canadian supermarket chain. It’s best known for having discounted prices in comparison with it’s local competitors. It’s first store opened it’s doors in July 1978, in the East York district of Toronto. The company has since gone on to open over 300 locations across nine of the provinces in Canada.", "annotation_id": "34577871", "url": "https://genius.com/34577871", "state": "accepted", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MOTH BALLS", "line": "I been peakin’ off that Addy every day It’s been hard for me to put that shit away Drinkin’ four or five bottles of the wine Got a glass in my hand every time", "vault_lines": ["I been peakin' off that Addy every day", "It's been hard for me to put that shit away", "Drinkin' four or five bottles of the wine", "Got a glass in my hand every time"], "meaning": "Drake has mentioned using adderall before in the song “On BS”:\n\nPopped an Adderall, I feel like I can lift a tree up\n\nIt seems Drake may have developed an addiction to Adderall in the years between these tracks. This makes sense as he is also a heavy drinker which he denotes later on in the verse. Adderall can slow the effects of alcohol and could let him continue functioning despite the amount he drinks.", "annotation_id": "34574399", "url": "https://genius.com/34574399", "state": "accepted", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MOTH BALLS", "line": "Mothballs, I can’t get the smell out my clothes", "vault_lines": ["Mothballs, I can't get the smell out my clothes"], "meaning": "Drake is implying that on his clothes, there is a lingering smell similar to Mothballs that are used to freshen the scent in items like shoes. He could be implying that the perfume of the girl he was last with is still lingering on his clothes and cannot get off.", "annotation_id": "34572920", "url": "https://genius.com/34572920", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MOTH BALLS", "line": "I remember stressin’ over bills like a Buffalo fan, uh", "vault_lines": ["I remember stressin' over bills like a Buffalo fan, uh"], "meaning": "The Buffalo Bills are an American football team, who play in the AFC East division of the NFL. Based in Buffalo, New York, the team has never won a Super Bowl, famously losing four in a row from 1990 to 1993. In recent years, they have found success with six straight playoff appearances, but the title of Super Bowl champions still eludes them.\n\nDrake likens himself to a fan of the team, except he stresses over different bills. While the fans may be stressing over the team, Drake harkens back to when he was less famous, a time where he was more concerned about making money and making it big.\n\nWhile the Toronto native has never referenced the Bills directly in his music, he has a long history of showing love to the city of Buffalo, which is a short two and a half hour drive from his hometown. Drake has a close relationship with the city, even acknowledging his feelings about Buffalo and what the city means to him. Notably, on his March 2017 track “Can’t Have Everything”, Drizzy raps:\n\nWe evolved, used to think vacation meant Niagara Falls\nSwear to God, shout to Buffalo, never duckin' low", "annotation_id": "34572910", "url": "https://genius.com/34572910", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MOTH BALLS", "line": "YYZ, racing ’cause the gate ’bout to close", "vault_lines": ["YYZ, racing 'cause the gate 'bout to close"], "meaning": "YYZ is the IATA airport code for Toronto Pearson International Airport. The largest airport in Canada, it handled over 44 million passengers in 2023.\n\nDrake claims he is racing to the airport, as he is running late for his flight. The YYZ can also be heard as “Why’s Why’s he,” making it seem as if Drake is asking why someone is racing to the airport.", "annotation_id": "34564218", "url": "https://genius.com/34564218", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MOTH BALLS", "line": "I need a girl that’s on the cover of Vogue", "vault_lines": ["I need a girl that's on the cover of Vogue"], "meaning": "Vogue, also known as American Vogue, is a monthly fashion and lifestyle magazine all kinds of fashion and culture topics. Most of its covers feature celebrities, often women, who are either getting a lot of attention at the moment or have a lot to do with the world of style.\n\n\n\nDrake has alluded to wanting a cover model before on songs like “Jimmy Cooks”\n\n“Bitch, don’t tell me that you model if you ain’t been in Vogue”\n\nInstead of just showcasing his high standards, this bar might show that Drake is worried about being used for money or status. He wants to be with someone who’s at his level, someone famous enough to be on the cover of Vogue. This is supported by the lines directly before this, talking about helping his friends come up and needing security.", "annotation_id": "34561398", "url": "https://genius.com/34561398", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MOTH BALLS", "line": "She from Michigan, but she taste like water The cleanest water, ooh, yeah Clean as this cup", "vault_lines": ["She from Michigan, but she taste like water", "The cleanest water, ooh, yeah", "Clean as this cup"], "meaning": "The Flint water crisis took place in Flint, Michigan from 2014 to it’s resolution in 2021. The water was exposed to dangerous amounts of lead, leading to mass lead poisoning and detrimental long-term health effects. Plans to replace to pipes are expected to finish in August 2025.\n\nParty makes a sexual reference, saying that the woman he’s with tastes like pure water while he performs sexual acts. Party says that despite her being from Michigan, she tastes pure like clean water.", "annotation_id": "34560839", "url": "https://genius.com/34560839", "state": "accepted", "votes": 49, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
