{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Come Closer", "line": "Me, me number one inna me city Me steady repping, representing for me city, yo", "vault_lines": ["Me, me number one inna me city", "Me steady repping, representing for me city, yo", "Starboy, call me number one"], "meaning": "He states he is “number one in his city” meaning he is popular in his city of origin within Nigeria, this may mean he is well known for having “the sauce”. Repping means representing, he is representing his city during this song.", "annotation_id": "13041183", "url": "https://genius.com/13041183", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Come Closer", "line": "She give me tease and she pleasing my roja", "vault_lines": ["She give me tease and she pleasing my roja"], "meaning": "“Roger” is a slang word used to describe a man’s penis.\nWiz’s pronunciation of the word is based on the Nigerian (Pidgin-English) intonation to make it sound like “Roja”", "annotation_id": "11901625", "url": "https://genius.com/11901625", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Come Closer", "line": "Me come clean like me come inna me video", "vault_lines": ["Me come clean like me come inna me video"], "meaning": "Video shoots are made to put the artists in a beautiful light hence he metaphorically uses the term to say how fresh he his in person", "annotation_id": "11676558", "url": "https://genius.com/11676558", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Come Closer", "line": "One fuck cyaan hold me, we gotta go twice", "vault_lines": ["One fuck cyaan hold me, we gotta go twice"], "meaning": "“Cyaan” is a Jamaican slang word for “can’t”\n\nHere Drake is saying that a one-night-stand isn’t enough to hold him down to a relationship.\n\nIt could also mean that instead of having another one-night-stand he prefers having sex twice or more times in a night.", "annotation_id": "11295216", "url": "https://genius.com/11295216", "state": "accepted", "votes": 28, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Come Closer", "line": "What would I do without you, my chargie?", "vault_lines": ["What would I do without you, my chargie?"], "meaning": "“Chargie” is an urbanized Jamaican Patois term for friend. The term was made popular by Popcaan.\n\nIn this instance, Drake uses “chargie” as “lover”—he’d be lost without his girl.", "annotation_id": "11174506", "url": "https://genius.com/11174506", "state": "accepted", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Come Closer", "line": "Came into the game, no one replace me Me love my Hennessy straight with no chaser All of my guys know me all about me paper Me got me girls all around me, me no chaser, yah", "vault_lines": ["Came into the game, no one replace me", "Me love my Hennessy straight with no chaser", "All of my guys know me all about me paper", "Me got me girls all around me, me no chaser, yah"], "meaning": "Although Wizkid is now known worldwide for his efforts on Drake’s hit song “One Dance,” he had been experiencing commercial and critical success in Africa since the release of his 2010 single “Holla at Your Boy.” In 2013 he was ranked 5th on Forbes‘ list of the “Top 10 Richest/Bankable African Artists.”\n\nWizkid uses the word “chaser” here in two ways: firstly to describe a more palatable drink you consume after taking a shot of hard liquor; and secondly as someone who “chases” after girls for their attention. Wizkid prefers his Hennessy cognac straight with no chaser, just as he finds himself surrounded with beautiful woman without having to do any “chasing.”\n\nIn addition, the Hennessy name drop references one of the most recognizable lines from “One Dance.” Wizkid has history with the brand, having been tapped by them to produce a track, “Dance Go (Eau de Vie)” with 2Face Idibia, to promote the cognac in Nigeria.", "annotation_id": "11173604", "url": "https://genius.com/11173604", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Come Closer", "line": "We in Miami livin’ La Vida Loca, ayy", "vault_lines": ["We in Miami livin' La Vida Loca, ayy"], "meaning": "“La vida loca” literally means “the crazy life” in English. Wizkid takes his girl with him to Miami, FL to party like nothing matters at all—living the crazy life.\n\nPuerto Rican latin pop singer Ricky Martin once made a song about ‘la vida loca’, called “Livin' La Vida Loca”.\n\n\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=p47fEXGabaY", "annotation_id": "11172443", "url": "https://genius.com/11172443", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Come Closer", "line": "Yeah, Starboy dey here suh", "vault_lines": ["Starboy dey here suh"], "meaning": "“Starboy” is Jamaican slang for someone who is seen as cool or important, even if it’s just amongst their colleagues. “Deh suh” is patois for “over there.”\n\n“Starboy” also happens to be the name of Wizkid’s label, Starboy Entertainment, and The Weeknd’s 2016 album Starboy. Wizkid felt like The Weeknd stole his name, claiming to be “[the] Real Starboy” and calling the Canadian singer a fraud on his Twitter:\n\n\n\nThis is also likely a reference to The Weeknd’s “Starboy,” where Abel sings:\n\nGirls get loose when they hear this song", "annotation_id": "11172364", "url": "https://genius.com/11172364", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Come Closer", "line": "I just turn colder every time I try", "vault_lines": ["I just turn colder every time I try"], "meaning": "This is likely a reference to Meek Mill, who started beef with Drake in Summer 2015 when Meek mentioned Drake used ghostwriters on “R.I.C.O.”:\n\nhttps://twitter.com/MeekMill/status/623703382675460096?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw\n\nMeek and Drake were collaborators and friends, working together on “Amen” and the aforementioned “R.I.C.O.”. However, Meek turned on the friendship and betrayed Drake.\n\n\n\nThe mentality of making his clique safer has been a regular subject as-of-late, such as in “100”:\n\nMy circle got so small that it’s a period, sayin' to myself…\n\nAnd “Work”:\n\nSorry if I’m way less friendly\nI got niggas tryna end me, oh\n\n\n\nThese lines were teased in an Instagram post 3 months before the leak.\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/BLc3x4Ej7IL/\n\nToo mix up in drama to free my mind but I’m praying for you even in your darkest times. 💀", "annotation_id": "11172361", "url": "https://genius.com/11172361", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Only Me (Me & U Original)", "status": "done", "targets": 6, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Tems-only-me-me-and-u-original-lyrics", "genius_title": "Only Me (Me & U Original)", "genius_id": 9118054, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Only Me (Me & U Original)", "line": "She wants the daggering, she wants the agony", "vault_lines": ["She wants the pain and the agony I have in me", "She wants the daggering, she wants the agony"], "meaning": "She’s craving toxicity and the agony that comes with it", "annotation_id": "30502757", "url": "https://genius.com/30502757", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Only Me (Me & U Original)", "line": "We still need time to grow closer, like family We just need our space, so we avoid any tragedy", "vault_lines": ["We still need time to grow closer, like family", "We just need our space, so we avoid any tragedy"], "meaning": "Drake’s preaching patience for that family-like connection to blossom. And when he talks about needing space, it’s a call to avoid any unnecessary drama or complications. It’s that real talk about finding the right balance between closeness and personal freedom.", "annotation_id": "30502740", "url": "https://genius.com/30502740", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Only Me (Me & U Original)", "line": "Life is no fantasy, please do not daddy me", "vault_lines": ["Life is no fantasy, please do not daddy me"], "meaning": "Drake likes his independance. He’s all about keeping it real, not living in some girl’s fantasy where she thinks she can call the shots.", "annotation_id": "30502731", "url": "https://genius.com/30502731", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Only Me (Me & U Original)", "line": "While I stare in her eyes, she’s no casualty She wants the pain and the agony I have in me", "vault_lines": ["While I stare in her eyes, she's no casualty", "She wants the pain and the agony I have in me", "She wants the daggering, she wants the agony", "Only me, and, me, and"], "meaning": "As Drake locks eyes, he’s making it clear she holds more significance than a temporary connection. Her craving for his pain suggests a desire for a deep and authentic relationship, establishing a meaningful connection between them.", "annotation_id": "30502717", "url": "https://genius.com/30502717", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Only Me (Me & U Original)", "line": "She’s always mad at me, ’til I go deep in her soul", "vault_lines": ["She's always mad at me, 'til I go deep in her soul"], "meaning": "Drake is describing a relationship dynamic where his partner’s initial frustration transforms when he connects with her on a deeper level.", "annotation_id": "30502669", "url": "https://genius.com/30502669", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Only Me (Me & U Original)", "line": "Make me your matter, make me your matter, make me your matter", "vault_lines": ["Make me your matter, make me your matter, make me your matter", "Show me your substance, make me your person, make me your person"], "meaning": "It’s “make me your martyr” as in your sacrifice.", "annotation_id": "29705687", "url": "https://genius.com/29705687", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
