{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MEET YOUR PADRE", "status": "done", "targets": 10, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Partynextdoor-drake-and-chino-pacas-meet-your-padre-lyrics", "genius_title": "MEET YOUR PADRE", "genius_id": 11475999, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MEET YOUR PADRE", "line": "Mami, di qué tranza, yo hasta te pido a tu mamá, no hay temor", "vault_lines": ["Mami, di qué tranza, yo hasta te pido a tu mamá, no hay temor (Eso e', quilla", "Mami, di qué tranza, yo hasta te pido a tu mamá, no hay temor"], "meaning": "English translation:\n\nMami, what’s up, I’ll even ask your mom, there’s no fear\n\nWILD work from Chino Pacas", "annotation_id": "39909198", "url": "https://genius.com/39909198", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MEET YOUR PADRE", "line": "Take you to Santos, we can dance bachata (Mira, mira)", "vault_lines": ["Take you to Santos, we can dance bachata (Mira, mira)"], "meaning": "Santos is a city and municipality in the Brazilian state of São Paulo. While there, they will dance bachata, which is a sensual, romantic, and rhythmic latin dance and music genre that originated in the Dominican Republic.\n\n\n\nSantos is also a reference to the (“King of Bachata”) Romeo Santos who collaborated with Drake on the song Odio in 2014. This was Drake’s first song in Spanish.", "annotation_id": "36986935", "url": "https://genius.com/36986935", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MEET YOUR PADRE", "line": "I want your phone número, por favor", "vault_lines": ["I want your phone número, por favor"], "meaning": "Drake is asking for her phone number. He asks partially in spanish, as por favor means “please” and numero means “number”.", "annotation_id": "36986927", "url": "https://genius.com/36986927", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MEET YOUR PADRE", "line": "Text your friends, “¿Qué pasa?” Vamos, bring them to mi casa, por favor", "vault_lines": ["Text your friends, \"¿Qué pasa?\" Vamos, bring them to mi casa, por favor"], "meaning": "¿Qué pasa? is spanish for “what’s happening” and vamos means “let’s go”. After the woman checks what her friends are doing for the night, Drake wants her to bring them to his house (casa).", "annotation_id": "36986906", "url": "https://genius.com/36986906", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MEET YOUR PADRE", "line": "I’ll come and pick you up in Testarossa, ayy", "vault_lines": ["I'll come and pick you up in Testarossa, ayy"], "meaning": "Drake is going to pick the woman up in a Ferrari Testarossa. This is an iconic rear mid-engined Italian supercar, originally launched by Ferrari in 1984.", "annotation_id": "36986897", "url": "https://genius.com/36986897", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MEET YOUR PADRE", "line": "Take you to Kiki or the Boobie Trap-a", "vault_lines": ["Take you to Kiki or the Boobie Trap-a"], "meaning": "That phrase comes from the song “Meet Your Padre” by Drake, PARTYNEXTDOOR, and Chino Pacas. In the lyrics, Drake mentions taking someone to Kiki or the Boobie Trap-a, which likely refers to well-known nightlife spots. Kiki could be shorthand for a club or lounge, while Boobie Trap is a famous strip club in Miami. The line suggests a fun, carefree night out, possibly in a party atmosphere.", "annotation_id": "35534729", "url": "https://genius.com/35534729", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MEET YOUR PADRE", "line": "I can make you feel mucho mejor Meet me outside, por favor (Yeah, yeah) Without you, my heart’s in dolor", "vault_lines": ["I can make you feel mucho mejor", "Meet me outside, por favor (Yeah, yeah)", "Without you, my heart's in dolor"], "meaning": "“Mucho mejor,” “por favor,” and “dolor” are Spanish words that mean “much better,” “please,” and “pain,” respectively.\n\nThe lyrics translate as:\n\nI can make you feel much better\nMeet me outside, please\nWithout you, my heart is in pain", "annotation_id": "34621980", "url": "https://genius.com/34621980", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MEET YOUR PADRE", "line": "Quilla, vámono’ pa’ Sevilla", "vault_lines": ["Quilla, vámono' pa' Sevilla", "), baby (Vámono' pa' Sevilla)"], "meaning": "“Quilla” or “Quillo” is an abbreviation of “chiquilla” / “chiquillo,” an expression commonly used in Spain, particularly in Andalucia, to refer to a woman or a man in a friendly manner.", "annotation_id": "34562100", "url": "https://genius.com/34562100", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MEET YOUR PADRE", "line": "(Toma, Sevilla, Triana)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Triana is a neighborhood near to Guadalquivir in Seville, Spain, a city located in the Autonomous Community of Andalusia, from which Flamenco comes.", "annotation_id": "34562050", "url": "https://genius.com/34562050", "state": "accepted", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "MEET YOUR PADRE", "line": "[Chorus: Drake & Chino Pacas]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "English translation:\n\nI want to meet your mother, pay my respects to your father, my love\nBeautiful, you know it, and the way of looking at me in your eyes\nText your friends, “What’s up?” Come, bring them to my house, please\nMami, what’s up, I’ll even ask your mom, there’s no fear", "annotation_id": "34560903", "url": "https://genius.com/34560903", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "P power", "status": "done", "targets": 8, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Gunna-p-power-lyrics", "genius_title": "P power", "genius_id": 7231233, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "P power", "line": "How can I not be the topic discussion when niggas got rich off of droppin’ my govy?", "vault_lines": ["How can I not be the topic discussion when niggas got rich off of droppin' my govy?"], "meaning": "Govy is slang for government name. Drake is claiming that other rappers are achieving fame and getting attention by mentioning drake in their songs.", "annotation_id": "36524636", "url": "https://genius.com/36524636", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "P power", "line": "I’m comin’, my baby, fuck it, I’ll crocodile Birkin the baby (Fuck it)", "vault_lines": ["I'm comin', my baby, forget a crocodile Birkin, my baby", "I'm comin', my baby, fuck it, I'll crocodile Birkin the baby (Fuck it)"], "meaning": "Due to the irresistible sexual power that his lover possesses, Gunna is happy to purchase her a crocodile skin Hermès Birkin, a rare handbag that sells for upwards of $12,000 on the resale market.\n\nGunna previously mentioned the opulent bag on his 2018 track “Baby Birkin,” rapping a similar sentiment throughout the song:\n\nI have a daughter, I’m buying her baby Birkin", "annotation_id": "24982860", "url": "https://genius.com/24982860", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "P power", "line": "I hit Mercedes inside a Mercedes", "vault_lines": ["I hit Mercedes inside a Mercedes"], "meaning": "Gunna talks about how he had sex with a girl named Mercedes inside a Mercedes-Benz. This isn’t the first time Gunna has mentioned the car; he was featured on fellow ATL rapper Young Thug’s song ‘Diamonds Dancing’ where in the second verse of the song he states:\n\nSouthside, but not JD, pull up, AMG Mercedes (Mercedes)\n\nGunna is definitely fond of the German marque – he gifted his mother a Mercedes coupe for her birthday in January 2021.", "annotation_id": "24890063", "url": "https://genius.com/24890063", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "P power", "line": "I’m comin’, my baby, forget a crocodile Birkin, my baby", "vault_lines": ["I'm comin', my baby, forget a crocodile Birkin, my baby", "I'm comin', my baby, fuck it, I'll crocodile Birkin the baby (Fuck it)"], "meaning": "Referencing Gunna’s lyrics from earlier in the track, Drake claims that he can provide his lover with more than mere material items.\n\nDrake has a vast collection of Hermès Birkin handbags which he keeps for his future wife. The Birkin is one of the rarest and most expensive handbags in the world, with prices starting at $40,000 USD.\n\nNotably, Drake owns a Hermès Himalaya Birkin. Constructed from crocodile skin with 18k white gold and diamond hardware, the Himalaya Birkin is one of the rarest handbags in the world, selling at auction for $382,000 in 2017.\n\n\n\nA rare, matte gris cendré Himalaya Niloticus Crocodile Diamond Birkin 30 with 18k white gold & diamond hardware.", "annotation_id": "24899961", "url": "https://genius.com/24899961", "state": "pending", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "P power", "line": "How do you even be rockin’ with buddy The pictures I’ve seen, I’m like, “Damn, he got lucky” Take it from him and I leave him with nothin’", "vault_lines": ["How do you even be rockin' with buddy", "The pictures I've seen, I'm like, \"Damn, he got lucky\"", "Take it from him and I leave him with nothin'"], "meaning": "Drake flaunts his lothario lifestyle in keeping with the song’s braggadocious themes. He believes that the woman in question is too good for her current partner, questioning how the two are together.\n\nHe may be addressing (and confirming) the rumor that he slept with singer-songwriter Naomi Sharon whilst she was engaged. Sharon, who worked on Drake’s sixth studio album, Certified Lover Boy, broke up with her fiancé, Jamie Sun, shortly after the news broke.\n\n\n\nAlternatively, as “rockin’” and “Rocky” sound similar, this lyric could be aimed at at A$AP Rocky, given his relationship with Drake’s ex Rihanna and the announcement via Instagram (i.e., the “pictures” that Drake’s seen) that Rihanna was pregnant with Rocky’s child.", "annotation_id": "24899933", "url": "https://genius.com/24899933", "state": "pending", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "P power", "line": "The dash in the Benz is virtual, baby You seein’ 3D off a Perky, my baby", "vault_lines": ["The dash in the Benz is virtual, baby", "You seein' 3D off a Perky, my baby", "Seein' HD off the 2C, my baby"], "meaning": "A virtual dashboard, also known as a digital dash, is an electronic panel that provides drivers with a digital readout of data, such as miles per hour and rev counters, as opposed to a traditional analog dial.\n\n\n\nDrake has never shied away from showing off his opulent lifestyle. He could be referring to the Vision Mercedes-Maybach 6 Cabriolet concept which he previewed in the “Laugh Now Cry Later” music video.\n\n\n\nDrake compares the futuristic dashboard in his car to the effects felt whilst under the influence of a Percocet, a highly addictive opioid medication used to treat pain and a common drug of abuse.", "annotation_id": "24876840", "url": "https://genius.com/24876840", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "P power", "line": "Seein’ HD off the 2C, my baby", "vault_lines": ["Seein' HD off the 2C, my baby"], "meaning": "2C is a family of psychedelics but is considered a “designer drug” due to the effects being greater than hallucinations. The effects of 2Cs are not only seeing a distortion of reality but are similar to a stimulant, where the user feels more aware of their surroundings and more energized. As such, Drake states that he is able to see more clearly and in “high definition” on these drugs.", "annotation_id": "24876036", "url": "https://genius.com/24876036", "state": "accepted", "votes": 26, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "P power", "line": "Thirty-one gang, it get spooky, my baby", "vault_lines": ["Thirty-one gang, it get spooky, my baby"], "meaning": "Drake provides his lover with peace of mind, assuring her that, despite threats made against him, she is safe in his presence due to his gang affiliation.\n\nDrake invokes Halloween imagery, with “thirty-one gang” referencing his October’s Very Own collective, as Halloween falls on October 31, one week after his birthday. He has previously mentioned “Halloween Gang” regarding OVO, such as on his 2015 track “I’m The Plug, rapping:\n\nThis that OVO Halloween gang, you know how I’m rocking already\n\nHe alludes to “spooky,” gang-affiliated members of OVO, such as Baka Not Nice, who served jail time for charges relating to assault and illegal possession of firearms.", "annotation_id": "24860383", "url": "https://genius.com/24860383", "state": "pending", "votes": 34, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
