{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SOMEBODY LOVES ME PT. 2", "line": "[Chorus: PARTYNEXTDOOR]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This chorus is a reprise of the one from  the original “SOMEBODY LOVES ME.” off the collaborative record “$ome $exy $ongs 4 U” by Drake & PARTYNEXTDOOR.\n\n It brings back the same hook that went viral in the original, with verses that are completely new.", "annotation_id": "37757375", "url": "https://genius.com/37757375", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SOMEBODY LOVES ME PT. 2", "line": "Drizzy", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "nickname Drizzy. In 2007- 2008 a friend from Toronto named Foots was the first person to call him “Drizzy” he went on to create an email address with the name\"drizzydrake@rogers.com\"\n\nThis lead to a misunderstanding apon Drake’s first collaboration with Lil Wayne, in which Lil Wayne rapped Drakes name wrong. It went down well and to this day Drake sometimes refers to himself as Drizzy.", "annotation_id": "36861561", "url": "https://genius.com/36861561", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SOMEBODY LOVES ME PT. 2", "line": "I’m with C", "vault_lines": ["I'm doin' toasts with mimosas at the spa"], "meaning": "“C” here likely refers to Cash Cobain, the collaborator on the record and former ghostwriter for Drake.", "annotation_id": "36860020", "url": "https://genius.com/36860020", "state": "pending", "votes": -5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
