{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SOMEBODY LOVES ME PT. 2", "line": "Slizzy", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Cash Cobain popularized “Slizzy” as a term for a way of life focused on authenticity, freedom, and not judging others. It derived from the slang term “slime”.", "annotation_id": "36841360", "url": "https://genius.com/36841360", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SOMEBODY LOVES ME PT. 2", "line": "A thizz on a bridge, see the city lights", "vault_lines": ["A thizz on a bridge, see the city lights"], "meaning": "A “thizz” can refer to taking or being under the influence of MDMA/ecstasy, popularized by Mac Dre and other Bay Area rappers. This connects with the previous two lines both referring to the drug. ‘Thizz entertainment’ is also the name of Mac Dre’s record label.\n\nShe is taking the drug while on a bridge, likely the Bay Bridge or Golden Gate Bridge overlooking San Francisco. “Seeing the city lights” also refers to the visual sensations of being on ecstasy, which has mild hallucinogenic effects and can heighten and distort sensory perceptions.", "annotation_id": "36839522", "url": "https://genius.com/36839522", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SOMEBODY LOVES ME PT. 2", "line": "She said her bestie wanna get on and swap I said, “Well, this time, I might have to—” I said, “Well, this time, I might be a thot” I can’t tell y’all, “Stop”", "vault_lines": ["She said her bestie wanna get on and swap", "I said, \"Well, this time, I might have to—\"", "I said, \"Well, this time, I might be a thot\"", "I can't tell y'all, \"Stop\""], "meaning": "The woman lets Drake know that her best friend wants to get home and have sex with him, possibly the three of them together. In the original version of the song, when the woman shares this with Drake he responds “I’m shy, baby, and that’s doin' a lot”.\n\nThis time his response is different, and he has trouble resisting and telling them to stop. Instead, he thinks he might have to go along with their request and be a “thot”, slang for being a hoe.", "annotation_id": "36828588", "url": "https://genius.com/36828588", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SOMEBODY LOVES ME PT. 2", "line": "She just did a bean out in Boston, oh my", "vault_lines": ["She just did a bean out in Boston, oh my"], "meaning": "“Doing” a bean refers to taking a prescription drug such as ecstasy or molly. Boston’s nickname is “beantown” (derived from a colonial era popular bean dish), which completes the line of why the woman is doing a bean in Boston, specifically.", "annotation_id": "36824193", "url": "https://genius.com/36824193", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SOMEBODY LOVES ME PT. 2", "line": "My bitch said she need a Cash App, I’ma send that like Kai", "vault_lines": ["My bitch said she need a Cash App, I'ma send that like Kai"], "meaning": "Cash Cobain is making a wordplay reference by saying he will ‘send that like Kai.’ The line connects the idea of sending money (‘send that’) with Twitch star Kai Cenat’s last name, creating a clever play on words.", "annotation_id": "36824114", "url": "https://genius.com/36824114", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SOMEBODY LOVES ME PT. 2", "line": "A Tesla in Texas, self-drive", "vault_lines": ["A Tesla in Texas, self-drive"], "meaning": "Tesla is an are electric vehicles company famously created by Elon Musk. Some Teslas feature “self-driving” mode. The Gigafactory Texas is a large manufacturing hub for Tesla and the vehicles are very popular in Texas. Drake also now lives part-time in Texas, outside of Houston.\n\nThis likely also connects as a continuation with the previous line, and be a reference to a Tesla pill, a MDMA/ecstasy colorfully branded tablet taken as a party drug. She’s doing a bean in Boston, and a Tesla in Texas.", "annotation_id": "36818676", "url": "https://genius.com/36818676", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SOMEBODY LOVES ME PT. 2", "line": "I wear my Rollie upside down in the spot That way the sixes is always on top", "vault_lines": ["I wear my Rollie upside down in the spot", "That way the sixes is always on top"], "meaning": "A clever double entendre by Drake.\n\nThe number 6 is normally on the bottom of a watch face. However, Drake is wearing his Rolex watch (“Rollie”) upside down, suggesting that the number six is on top.\n\nThe number 6 heavily associated with Drake and the Toronto area code. Drake suggests that the 6 is “always on top,” which is why he wears his Rolex watch upside down. A sharp line suggesting he remains at the top of the rap game.", "annotation_id": "36818662", "url": "https://genius.com/36818662", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "SOMEBODY LOVES ME PT. 2", "line": "Beat that pussy, she scream out, “No más”", "vault_lines": ["Beat that pussy, she scream out, \"No más\""], "meaning": "No más is “no more” in spanish. Cash is saying he had sex with her (beat that pussy) until she told him “no more”.", "annotation_id": "36818652", "url": "https://genius.com/36818652", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "F**kin’ Problems (Clean Version)", "status": "done", "targets": 8, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/A-ap-rocky-fkin-problems-clean-version-lyrics", "genius_title": "F**kin’ Problems (Clean Version)", "genius_id": 4935604, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "F**kin’ Problems (Clean Version)", "line": "Make that thing thing like a or a", "vault_lines": ["Make that thing thing like a or a"], "meaning": "Semi and nine refer to guns (a “semi-automatic” and a gun that uses 9mm caliber bullets). Like the “popping” that comes from a gun when it’s shot, A$AP wants this girl to pop it for pimp.\n\nThe choice between “a semi or a nine” is a confusing one, because 9mm guns don’t come in revolver style—they are exclusively semi-automatic.\n\nSince a “nine” is a “semi” by definition, saying “make it pop like a semi or a nine” makes as much sense as saying “driving a BMW or a car.”", "annotation_id": "31845262", "url": "https://genius.com/31845262", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "F**kin’ Problems (Clean Version)", "line": "Verse 1: A$AP Rocky]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "It’s almost comical how profane this verse is. The censored version makes the verse sound very different, to the point where it’s pretty funny listening to it. Censored words:\n\n“bitches”\n“bitch”\n“pop”\n“semi”\n“nine”\n“raw”\n“motherfucker”\n“motherfuckers”\n“chrome”\n“nigga”\n“nigga”\n“nigga”\n“fuckin”\n“bitches”\n“rolling”\n“swishers”\n“bitches”\n“niggas”\n“lick it”\n“nigga”\n“niggerish”\n“nigga”\n“nigga”\n“fucking”\n“fucking”\n“dyke”\n“bitch”\nand last but not least, “fucking.”\nAbout 20% of the verse is changed (such as making “bitches” into “chickens”) or censored.", "annotation_id": "31845258", "url": "https://genius.com/31845258", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "F**kin’ Problems (Clean Version)", "line": "Bring your girls to the crib, maybe we can solve it, ayy", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "On the album version of the song, Drake performs both of these lines. However, in the music video, Drake performs the first line, and Rocky performs the second.", "annotation_id": "31845250", "url": "https://genius.com/31845250", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "F**kin’ Problems (Clean Version)", "line": "If findin’ somebody real is your p-p-problem (Yeah", "vault_lines": ["If findin' somebody real is your p-p-problem", "If findin' somebody real is your p-p-problem (Yeah"], "meaning": "On the album version of the song, Drake performs both of these lines. However, in the music video, Drake performs the first line, and Rocky performs the second.", "annotation_id": "31845246", "url": "https://genius.com/31845246", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "F**kin’ Problems (Clean Version)", "line": "And yeah, I like to, I got a p-p-problem", "vault_lines": ["And yeah, I like to, I got a p-p-problem"], "meaning": "The hook is centered around a pun—Chainz both has a “fuckin' problem,” and a problem with fucking—i.e. he enjoys it so much that it has become a problem.\n\nDrake detailed the hook’s genesis:\n\n“Fuckin’ Problems” came from a song me and 2 Chainz had done. He said in his verse—it was really slow too—“I love bad bitches too that’s a fuckin’ problem.” I stopped his verse while we were listening to it, and I said, “Yo, that needs to be a hook. I don’t know how we’re going to explain this to him that we chopped a piece of his verse to do the hook.”\n\n2 Chainz echoed Drake’s account and provided his perspective during a November 2020 interview.", "annotation_id": "31845241", "url": "https://genius.com/31845241", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "F**kin’ Problems (Clean Version)", "line": "And yeah, I like to, I got a p-p-problem I love bad bad, that’s my that’s my problem", "vault_lines": ["I love bad bad, that's my that's my problem", "And yeah, I like to, I got a p-p-problem"], "meaning": "The hook is centered around a pun—Chainz both has a “fuckin' problem,” and a problem with fucking—i.e. he enjoys it so much that it has become a problem.\n\nDrake detailed the hook’s genesis:\n\n“Fuckin’ Problems” came from a song me and 2 Chainz had done. He said in his verse—it was really slow too—“I love bad bitches too that’s a fuckin’ problem.” I stopped his verse while we were listening to it, and I said, “Yo, that needs to be a hook. I don’t know how we’re going to explain this to him that we chopped a piece of his verse to do the hook.”\n\n2 Chainz echoed Drake’s account and provided his perspective during a November 2020 interview.", "annotation_id": "31845238", "url": "https://genius.com/31845238", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "F**kin’ Problems (Clean Version)", "line": "And yeah, I like to, I got a p-p-problem I love bad bad, that’s my that’s my problem", "vault_lines": ["I love bad bad, that's my that's my problem", "And yeah, I like to, I got a p-p-problem"], "meaning": "The hook is centered around a pun—Chainz both has a “fuckin' problem,” and a problem with fucking—i.e. he enjoys it so much that it has become a problem.\n\nDrake detailed the hook’s genesis:\n\n“Fuckin’ Problems” came from a song me and 2 Chainz had done. He said in his verse—it was really slow too—“I love bad bitches too that’s a fuckin’ problem.” I stopped his verse while we were listening to it, and I said, “Yo, that needs to be a hook. I don’t know how we’re going to explain this to him that we chopped a piece of his verse to do the hook.”\n\n2 Chainz echoed Drake’s account and provided his perspective during a November 2020 interview.", "annotation_id": "31845235", "url": "https://genius.com/31845235", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "F**kin’ Problems (Clean Version)", "line": "I love bad bad, that’s my that’s my problem", "vault_lines": ["I love bad bad, that's my that's my problem"], "meaning": "The hook is centered around a pun—Chainz both has a “fuckin' problem,” and a problem with fucking—i.e. he enjoys it so much that it has become a problem.\n\nDrake detailed the hook’s genesis:\n\n“Fuckin’ Problems” came from a song me and 2 Chainz had done. He said in his verse—it was really slow too—“I love bad bitches too that’s a fuckin’ problem.” I stopped his verse while we were listening to it, and I said, “Yo, that needs to be a hook. I don’t know how we’re going to explain this to him that we chopped a piece of his verse to do the hook.”\n\n2 Chainz echoed Drake’s account and provided his perspective during a November 2020 interview.", "annotation_id": "31845232", "url": "https://genius.com/31845232", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
