{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "STAYING ALIVE", "status": "done", "targets": 13, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Dj-khaled-staying-alive-lyrics", "genius_title": "STAYING ALIVE", "genius_id": 8245178, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "STAYING ALIVE", "line": "Wanted me to lie, wanted me to cry, wanted me to die (Real life)", "vault_lines": ["Wanted me to lie, wanted me to cry, wanted me to die (Real life)"], "meaning": "This is a possible reference to DMX’s opening line on “Ruff Ryder’s Anthem” –\n“Niggas wanna try, niggas wanna lie/then niggas wonder why/niggas wanna die”. In “Ruff Ryders Anthem”, DMX also expresses displeasure, both at women and his haters.", "annotation_id": "29217967", "url": "https://genius.com/29217967", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "STAYING ALIVE", "line": "It’s not like I know what I want It’s not like I know what I need", "vault_lines": ["It's not like I know what I need", "It's not like I know what I want"], "meaning": "This is a reference to the song Wants and Needs on the Scary Hours 2 EP, which marked their fourth collaboration.", "annotation_id": "27534705", "url": "https://genius.com/27534705", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "STAYING ALIVE", "line": "Try me a hundred times", "vault_lines": ["Try me a hundred times"], "meaning": "Drake interpolates a similar phrase he used on Pipe Down, off the Certified Lover Boy album.\n\n\n Tried to run it back a hundred times, The world is yours, but the city's mine― Drake – Pipe Down", "annotation_id": "26678108", "url": "https://genius.com/26678108", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "STAYING ALIVE", "line": "Try me a hundred times", "vault_lines": ["Try me a hundred times"], "meaning": "Drake interpolates a similar phrase he used on Pipe Down, off the Certified Lover Boy album.\n\n\n Tried to run it back a hundred times, The world is yours, but the city's mine― Drake – Pipe Down", "annotation_id": "26475562", "url": "https://genius.com/26475562", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "STAYING ALIVE", "line": "They tryna seal the deal", "vault_lines": ["They tryna seal the deal"], "meaning": "Not only do the women in question wish to sleep with Drake, but they also seek to “seal the deal” by getting impregnated by him. Thus, Drake takes precautionary measures to avoid this situation, which has notably only happened once before.", "annotation_id": "26440093", "url": "https://genius.com/26440093", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "STAYING ALIVE", "line": "Baby gon’ hit it, then send her to me, yeah Or I’ma hit it and send her to Baby That’s how I get when this life get too crazy Woah, woah, for real, for real, woah", "vault_lines": ["Baby gon' hit it, then send her to me, yeah", "Or I'ma hit it and send her to Baby", "That's how I get when this life get too crazy", "Woah, woah, for real, for real, woah", "For real, for real", "Drizzy hit her, then he send her to me", "This life, it allowed me to take what I want"], "meaning": "Here, Drake details hip-hop’s groupie culture. Notably, earlier in his career, he voiced a contradictory statement, stating that he’s “selfish with [his] women” on Future’s July 2015 track “Where Ya At.” Thus, this bar seemingly indicates that the woman in question is a sexual deviant, so much so that Drake wants Baby to experience her prowess himself–a commendable show of generosity by Drizzy.", "annotation_id": "26440062", "url": "https://genius.com/26440062", "state": "pending", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "STAYING ALIVE", "line": "Woah, woah, woah-woah", "vault_lines": ["Woah, woah, for real, for real, woah"], "meaning": "Emphasizing his shock at the woman’s actions, as described in the previous lines, Drake references Lil Baby’s November 2019 single “Woah.”", "annotation_id": "26440047", "url": "https://genius.com/26440047", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "STAYING ALIVE", "line": "Hood nigga turned superstar, but I fuck her good like I’m still in the streets", "vault_lines": ["Hood nigga turned superstar, but I fuck her good like I'm still in the streets"], "meaning": "Baby harkens back to his humble beginnings as a “hood nigga.” Raised by his single mother in Atlanta’s Oakland City neighborhood, Baby committed crimes, such as drug dealing, to get by before pursuing a music career. Despite achieving success as a rapper, he has not forgotten his roots.", "annotation_id": "26440035", "url": "https://genius.com/26440035", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "STAYING ALIVE", "line": "‘Posed to be one of a kind, you puttin’ on miles, I thought you was down for the ride I’m tryna turn up her style, we go in Chanel, she get everything in her size She in some shit with another guy, I don’t even care, whenever I see you, you mine", "vault_lines": ["'Posed to be one of a kind, you puttin' on miles, I thought you was down for the ride", "I'm tryna turn up her style, we go in Chanel, she get everything in her size", "She in some shit with another guy, I don't even care, whenever I see you, you mine"], "meaning": "Baby alludes to an unfaithful partner. He initially believed her to be a desirable, “one of a kind” woman, hence why he took her on shopping sprees at luxury fashion brand Chanel. However, unbeknownst to him, she was “puttin' on miles” behind his back, presumably sleeping with other men whilst he was on the road. Ultimately, Baby is unfazed by her disloyalty, so long as she pleasures him when they are together.", "annotation_id": "26440008", "url": "https://genius.com/26440008", "state": "pending", "votes": 13, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "STAYING ALIVE", "line": "Another one, yeah", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "DJ Khaled’s signature producer tag, which is heard before most of his songs. It serves as a reminder for his listeners that he has yet another hit single in his hands.", "annotation_id": "26438174", "url": "https://genius.com/26438174", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "STAYING ALIVE", "line": "When I was broke, she was bein’ a tease Four pockets full, now she down on her knees", "vault_lines": ["When I was broke, she was bein' a tease", "Four pockets full, now she down on her knees"], "meaning": "Four Pockets Full, or 4PF, refers to the name of Lil Baby’s record label and also serves as an ode to Drake’s financial success. Drake juxtaposes an unspecified female’s utter and eager willingness to provide him with fellatio now that his financial situation has greatly improved from when he was broke.", "annotation_id": "26432043", "url": "https://genius.com/26432043", "state": "pending", "votes": 23, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "STAYING ALIVE", "line": "Drizzy hit her, then he send her to me I don’t talk, definition of P", "vault_lines": ["Baby gon' hit it, then send her to me, yeah", "Drizzy hit her, then he send her to me", "I don't talk, definition of P"], "meaning": "These lines could—possibly—be a triple entendre.\n\n“Definition of P” could allude to the word “player,” which refers to utilizing a female’s sexually. This could be the case here—as “Drizzy hit her” literally means he had sexual intercourse with her.\n\nLil Baby may be also be stating that he’s “Pushing P,” meaning to display one’s success. For the literal definition, it means “keeping it player” and “keeping it real,” coined by Baby’s friend and frequent collaborator Gunna on his January 2022 track “pushing P” which popularized the phrase.\n\nAlternatively, the line may allude to Gunna’s RICO situation. In May 2022, the rapper was arrested and accused of participation in street gang activity. In this case, “definition of P” may relate to be keeping quiet or not to “snitch,” perhaps to a boyfriend.", "annotation_id": "26431877", "url": "https://genius.com/26431877", "state": "accepted", "votes": 46, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "STAYING ALIVE", "line": "I-I-I-I’m stayin’ alive, we’re stayin’ alive, we’re stayin’ alive, we’re stayin’ alive", "vault_lines": ["I-I-I-I'm stayin' alive, I'm stayin' alive, we're stayin' alive, we're stayin' alive, for real (Oh, yeah)", "I put my feelings aside, you want me to die, but, baby, I'm stayin' alive", "I-I-I-I'm stayin' alive, we're stayin' alive, we're stayin' alive, we're stayin' alive", "I-I-I-I'm stayin' alive, we're stayin' alive, we're stayin' alive, we're stayin' alive, we", "I-I-I-I'm stayin' alive, I'm stayin' alive, I'm stayin' alive, I'm stayin' alive, for real (For real)", "I-I-I-I'm stayin' alive, we're stayin' alive, we're stayin' alive, we're stayin', we live"], "meaning": "On the song’s chorus, Drake interpolates the chorus of the Bee Gees' December 1977 disco single “Stayin' Alive:”\n\nWhether you’re a brother or whether you’re a mother\nYou’re stayin' alive, stayin' alive\nFeel the city breakin' and everybody shakin'\nAnd we’re stayin' alive, stayin' alive\nAh, ha, ha, ha, stayin' alive, stayin' alive\nAh, ha, ha, ha, stayin' alive", "annotation_id": "26431487", "url": "https://genius.com/26431487", "state": "accepted", "votes": 50, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
