{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Back on Road", "status": "done", "targets": 17, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Gucci-mane-and-drake-back-on-road-lyrics", "genius_title": "Back on Road", "genius_id": 2489747, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Back on Road", "line": "I left the trappin’ went to rap, thought you’d be happy for me (Huh?)", "vault_lines": ["I left the trappin' went to rap, thought you'd be happy for me (Huh?)"], "meaning": "Gucci says he left the drug scene behind & pursued a music career, he also playfully teases the subject by saying they’d be “happy for him” meaning they’d be relieved to see him gone.", "annotation_id": "37396444", "url": "https://genius.com/37396444", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Back on Road", "line": "And then your jealousy turned to hate, and you wrote a statement on me (Uh)", "vault_lines": ["And then your jealousy turned to hate, and you wrote a statement on me (Uh)"], "meaning": "Someone started off envious of Gucci Mane but eventually grew to actively dislike or resent them.\n\n“Wrote a statement on me” Likely refers to whoever Gucci is referencing snitching, informing, or testifying against him.", "annotation_id": "37396421", "url": "https://genius.com/37396421", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Back on Road", "line": "I’m just an East Atlanta nigga with a body on his belt", "vault_lines": ["I'm just an East Atlanta nigga with a body on his belt"], "meaning": "Gucci shows pride in his roots by labelling himself with East Atlanta.\n\nIn Hip-Hop, to have “a body” means they have killed someone.\n\n“On his belt” is a metaphor for a championship belt, marking Gucci as dangerous or respected through defeating his enemies.", "annotation_id": "37396394", "url": "https://genius.com/37396394", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Back on Road", "line": "Put that pistol on your partner, made him piss all on himself (Oh yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Put that pistol on your partner, made him piss all on himself (Oh yeah)"], "meaning": "The act of putting a pistol on someone is an explicit threat of lethal violence,  Gucci emphasizes the victim’s fear and humiliation to show he’s in control.", "annotation_id": "37396380", "url": "https://genius.com/37396380", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Back on Road", "line": "I went from trappin’ on the block to niggas trappin’ for me (Skrrt)", "vault_lines": ["I went from trappin' on the block to niggas trappin' for me (Skrrt)"], "meaning": "‘Trapping’ is selling drugs, often in small quantities, usually in a specific location called a “trap” (like a house, corner, or spot – or in this case, the block)\n\nConsignment is an arrangement where an owner (the consignor) gives goods to a third party (the consignee) to sell on their behalf\n\nGucci is saying he’s made his way up the ranks & is now a kingpin, and has men working for him.", "annotation_id": "37396288", "url": "https://genius.com/37396288", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Back on Road", "line": "‘Fore I send her back to you, she gon’ have Guwop on her breath (Guwop)", "vault_lines": ["'Fore I send her back to you, she gon' have Guwop on her breath (Guwop)"], "meaning": "“Guwop” is a nickname for Gucci Mane\n\nto have something ‘on your breath’ is a double-entendre, it can mean that someone is talking about someone/something a lot – as if your girl cant forget her time with Guwop – and can also mean a literal smell, likely from oral sex with Gucci.\n\nGucci is saying before he’s done with her, these things are happening.", "annotation_id": "37396270", "url": "https://genius.com/37396270", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Back on Road", "line": "[Chorus: Drake & Gucci Mane]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "This is not the first collaboration between Drake and Gucci on wax. They collaborated on “Believe It or Not,” which is also known as “In My Business” when including the added verse from Sean Garrett. They also had a unique collab on “Street Cred” which was originally Drake’s “King Leon” featuring Killer Mike and Gucci.", "annotation_id": "9288522", "url": "https://genius.com/9288522", "state": "accepted", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Back on Road", "line": "I got money that I saved then I’m back on road Get my jewelry out the safe ’cause I’m back on road (Yeah) I still do these hoes the same when I’m back on road If you wasn’t there for me when I was all alone Then, bitch, don’t expect no love when I’m back", "vault_lines": ["I got money that I saved then I'm back on road", "Get my jewelry out the safe 'cause I'm back on road (Yeah)", "I still do these hoes the same when I'm back on road", "If you wasn't there for me when I was all alone", "Then, bitch, don't expect no love when I'm back"], "meaning": "On May 26, 2016, Gucci Mane was released from prison after serving a three-year sentence for federal drug and gun charges. This is the third song he’s featured on within a week of being released from jail. He dropped “First Day Out Da Feds” on his first day out and featured on Kanye West’s posse cut “Champions” just days later.\n\nThis also is a warning to all the people who abandoned Guwop while he was away. You better get lost because Gucci’s home.", "annotation_id": "9282772", "url": "https://genius.com/9282772", "state": "accepted", "votes": 44, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Back on Road", "line": "I done had a million beefs but I ain’t never call for help I’ll take a nigga bricks and I done took a nigga re-up", "vault_lines": ["I done had a million beefs but I ain't never call for help", "I'll take a nigga bricks and I done took a nigga re-up"], "meaning": "Gucci Mane is independent and can handle his business himself; he even starting his own record label, 1017 Brick Squad. If it comes down to it he’ll  take someone’s bricks (kilos of drugs) or the re-up, which means a newly acquired stash.\n\nEven when handling beef with enemies or people trying to attack him, Gucci can handle it himself. As he said on “Bricks”:\n\nUsed to take my food out another nigga mouth\nWhen you showed me the guap then the trigger come out", "annotation_id": "9282682", "url": "https://genius.com/9282682", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Back on Road", "line": "Zone six", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Although Gucci was born in Birmingham, Alabama, he and his mother moved to Atlanta when he was very young. The Eastside of Atlanta is often referred to as Zone 6 due to the patrol zones that the Atlanta Police Department is divided.\n\n\n\nBoth Gucci and the Drake have adopted nicknames representing their hometowns by utilizing the number 6.", "annotation_id": "9282134", "url": "https://genius.com/9282134", "state": "accepted", "votes": 31, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Back on Road", "line": "See, I ain’t mad at you, homie, we ain’t got no beef (No) But I ain’t got no rat for you, I know you must love cheese", "vault_lines": ["See, I ain't mad at you, homie, we ain't got no beef (No)", "But I ain't got no rat for you, I know you must love cheese"], "meaning": "Beef is a feud between two or more individuals. Although Gucci’s “homies” snitched on him, he doesn’t hold a grudge or have any problems with them.\n\nRat out is a term for someone who snitches, while cheese is a slang term for money. Guwop does know things about them that can put them in jail as well, but he’s going to be the better man because he knows they need their money.\n\nNote the wordplay with “rat” and “cheese.”", "annotation_id": "9281624", "url": "https://genius.com/9281624", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Back on Road", "line": "I slap a nigga with a strap and then I throw him a hunnid (I know) He be like, “Fuck goin’ to trial, man, just throw me the money”", "vault_lines": ["I slap a nigga with a strap and then I throw him a hunnid (I know)", "He be like, \"Fuck goin' to trial, man, just throw me the money\""], "meaning": "Gucci’s squad don’t have to worry about the outcome of a trial or whether they might end up in jail—because Gucci has them covered with the bail money.\n\n\n\nGucci himself was arrested in late 2013 on weapons and drug charges. He was then sentenced on charges of weapon possession by a convicted felon, and was expected to be released in late 2016. Gucci, however, was released 3 months earlier than expected.", "annotation_id": "9281089", "url": "https://genius.com/9281089", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Back on Road", "line": "But when they let me out them gates, my bitch was waitin’ on me", "vault_lines": ["But when they let me out them gates, my bitch was waitin' on me"], "meaning": "Gucci’s girlfriend, model/entrepreneur Keyshia Ka'oir, was with him back when he was thrown in jail, and she actually stayed faithful to him and received him when he was released. According to Gucci on G.O.O.D. Music’s “Champions,” he gave her 2 million dollars as her reward:\n\nI gave my bitch two mil' cause she stuck around", "annotation_id": "9279688", "url": "https://genius.com/9279688", "state": "accepted", "votes": 20, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Back on Road", "line": "I’m the last real nigga left, I’m on an island by myself", "vault_lines": ["I'm the last real nigga left, I'm on an island by myself"], "meaning": "Gucci feels as if the only one that has kept it real after all these years. He doesn’t need fake people around him given that he can handle everything by himself pretty well.", "annotation_id": "9279411", "url": "https://genius.com/9279411", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Back on Road", "line": "These niggas fakin’ like they happy, but they mad I’m home (Home) I’m the 2K16 Al Capone", "vault_lines": ["These niggas fakin' like they happy, but they mad I'm home (Home)", "I'm the 2K16 Al Capone"], "meaning": "Gucci compares himself to ruthless gangster Al Capone who was a mafia boss in Chicago and had many criminal charges dismissed, like Gucci who killed someone getting off on self-defense.\n\nGucci thinks some people might not be so pleased upon his return from prison and they’re really just pretending they’re glad for him. They can’t stand him and actually hate him.", "annotation_id": "9279149", "url": "https://genius.com/9279149", "state": "accepted", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Back on Road", "line": "Can’t eat, can’t sleep, man, I miss these streets Muhammad Ali, and the streets miss me", "vault_lines": ["Can't eat, can't sleep, man, I miss these streets", "Muhammad Ali, and the streets miss me"], "meaning": "Gucci is likely describing the isolated feeling of being locked up. He couldn’t even eat or sleep due to the stress of being in a uncomfortable cell with a jail bed. He always had to keep one eye open watching his back. Gucci had to watch his back, but now he’s back on road.\n\nGucci has paved the way for trap artists and is one of the greatest in the streets, just like Muhammad Ali did in boxing. Ali passed away the day before this song was released.", "annotation_id": "9278959", "url": "https://genius.com/9278959", "state": "accepted", "votes": 57, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Back on Road", "line": "I’m my only competition, so I’m battlin’ with myself (It’s Gucci) Facin’ prison, drug addiction, it’s like I’m battlin’ with myself I done shook off all my demons, now I’m back to myself", "vault_lines": ["I'm my only competition, so I'm battlin' with myself (It's Gucci)", "Facin' prison, drug addiction, it's like I'm battlin' with myself", "I done shook off all my demons, now I'm back to myself"], "meaning": "Gucci Mane doesn’t have competition with anyone else, he just battles with his inner demons. In 2013, he admitted on Twitter to struggling with a lean addiction and going to rehab while in jail. He has been incarcerated multiple times and has had many run-ins with the law over the years. Check a full history of Gucci’s legal issues here.\n\nHowever, now he’s back home feeling like Gucci!\n\nhttps://twitter.com/gucci1017/status/381812243689918464", "annotation_id": "9278897", "url": "https://genius.com/9278897", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "LASERS", "status": "done", "targets": 6, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Partynextdoor-and-drake-lasers-lyrics", "genius_title": "LASERS", "genius_id": 11473554, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "LASERS", "line": "Can’t wait ’til you get that tattoo off the back of your neck", "vault_lines": ["Can't wait 'til you get that tattoo off the back of your neck"], "meaning": "Because the tattoo bears the name of the woman’s abusive ex man, Party is looking forward to the tattoo’s removal, which comes later in the song.", "annotation_id": "36986876", "url": "https://genius.com/36986876", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "LASERS", "line": "Never thought I’d see the day you cry ’Til you cried in my arms that night (Yeah) Said he hit you after that one fight Closed fist, he’s fried, I’m heated I don’t really want to speak about it", "vault_lines": ["Never thought I'd see the day you cry", "'Til you cried in my arms that night (Yeah)", "Said he hit you after that one fight", "Closed fist, he's fried, I'm heated", "I don't really want to speak about it"], "meaning": "The woman has always put on a brave face, and Drake therefore never thought he’d see her brought to tears. However, she cries to him when describing the abuse she suffered from her former partner, whose name she has tattooed on her.\nDrake is extremely upset and angry (heated) when he hears this news, to the point he doesn’t want to speak about it. Nevertheless, he vows to take revenge on this man who abused her, promising the man is “fried”.", "annotation_id": "36986813", "url": "https://genius.com/36986813", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "LASERS", "line": "Fact you still got it is insane This nigga done put you through too much pain", "vault_lines": ["Fact you still got it is insane", "This nigga done put you through too much pain"], "meaning": "Drake expresses surprise that the woman still has the tattoo containing the other man’s name, even after he has put her through so much, including physical abuse (previous lines). This leads into the later lines in the bridge that discuss the laser tattoo removal of the other man’s name.", "annotation_id": "36986797", "url": "https://genius.com/36986797", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "LASERS", "line": "Session number one, it’s gon’ hurt a little bit Session two, that hurt might make you learn a little bit Session three, I know that you’ll be used to that shit Least we’re starting fresh in my brain", "vault_lines": ["Session number one, it's gon' hurt a little bit", "Session two, that hurt might make you learn a little bit", "Session three, I know that you'll be used to that shit", "Least we're starting fresh in my brain"], "meaning": "Throughout the song, the two make references to a tattoo on the woman’s body. Here Drake details the process for her getting laser tattoo removal. The process of lasering your tattoo off, hence the name of the song, takes multiple sessions depending on color, shading, and other factors.\n\nThe line can also be taken as Drake trying to erase the memory of her last relationship out of his mind. Starting fresh means that Drake is trying to forget about the past and move forward.", "annotation_id": "34564398", "url": "https://genius.com/34564398", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "LASERS", "line": "Staring at your tattoo while I’m fucking you from the back", "vault_lines": ["Staring at your tattoo while I'm fucking you from the back", "While I'm fucking you passionately ('Ately)", "While I'm fucking you fast asleep"], "meaning": "PARTYNEXTDOOR possibly references the cover art from his most recent album, April 2024’s PARTYNEXTDOOR 4 (P4)\n\n\n\n\nPARTYNEXTDOOR 4 (P4) Cover Art", "annotation_id": "34561794", "url": "https://genius.com/34561794", "state": "accepted", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "LASERS", "line": "Baby, say my name like Beyoncé (Yeah)", "vault_lines": ["Baby, say my name, say my name", "Baby, say my name like Beyoncé (Yeah)"], "meaning": "Beyoncé got her first real success in music when she was in the R&B girl group, Destiny’s Child. One of their most successful songs was “Say My Name” from 1999, coming from the point of view a woman who realizes her partner is cheating on her.\n\nInstead of anyone cheating here, this is the opposite. The lyrics are meant to reassure a woman that the Drake and PARTYNEXTDOOR aren’t like her exes, or the guy in that song. They want this to last forever, emphasized by the focus on things like engagement or wedding rings and wanting her to get their name tattooed on her.\n\nBeyoncé also has a gorgeous voice. “Say my name like Beyoncé” could also reference how much Drake and PARTYNEXTDOOR like their girls’ voices. They love these women so much, she sounds like a famous singer to them, no matter what she’s saying.", "annotation_id": "34560841", "url": "https://genius.com/34560841", "state": "accepted", "votes": 25, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "On a Wave", "status": "done", "targets": 3, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Tinashe-and-drake-on-a-wave-lyrics", "genius_title": "On a Wave", "genius_id": 1891384, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "On a Wave", "line": "I’m on a wave, I’m on a ride I’m everywhere, I’m hard to find", "vault_lines": ["I'm everywhere, I'm hard to find", "I'm on a wave, wave", "I'm on a wave, I'm on a ride"], "meaning": "With the recent release of her debut album Aquarius and her appearances on hit singles, Tinashe is on a new wave of success. The tour dates and travel take her all over the world, but make it difficult to find her as she is constantly on the move.\nhttps://instagram.com/p/0iWigECRRD/?taken-by=tinashenow", "annotation_id": "6547409", "url": "https://genius.com/6547409", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "On a Wave", "line": "You finally start to care I show up so unprepared", "vault_lines": ["You finally start to care", "I show up so unprepared"], "meaning": "In “Take Care,” Drake says:\n\nWhen you’re ready, just say you’re ready\nWhen all the baggage just ain’t as heavy\nAnd the party’s over, just don’t forget me\nWe’ll change the pace and we’ll just go slow\n\nNow that a girl Drake wants him to be around more, he’s ironically too busy to be with her.", "annotation_id": "6547114", "url": "https://genius.com/6547114", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "On a Wave", "line": "I’m on a wave, I’m on a ride I’m everywhere, I’m hard to find", "vault_lines": ["I'm everywhere, I'm hard to find", "I'm on a wave, wave", "I'm on a wave, I'm on a ride"], "meaning": "Like Drake said in “Preach”:\n\nI’m on that wave tonight, I hope you not the crazy type, yeah\n\nBoth Drake and Tinashe have someone they care about in their lives, but they’re too busy working to spend time with them.", "annotation_id": "6547010", "url": "https://genius.com/6547010", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
