{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stars Align", "line": "Know about your sign ’cause it’s close to mine", "vault_lines": ["Know about your sign 'cause it's close to mine"], "meaning": "Majid’s birthday falls on the 22nd of October, making him a Libra, possibly a cusp between Libra and Scorpio!", "annotation_id": "39952889", "url": "https://genius.com/39952889", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stars Align", "line": "I’m gonna try and get it right this time I just really need a place and time", "vault_lines": ["I'm gonna try and get it right this time", "I just really need a place and time"], "meaning": "Drake comforts the ‘freaky girl’, stating that he will attempt to ‘get it right this time’. We can assume that by ‘it’, he means a relationship that he had with the girl, that may have been damaged and subsequently broken off.\n\nHe remarks that he “really needs a place and time”, which can be viewed as asking the lady to put faith in him and asking her to reach out to him, presumably to repair the relationship they may have previously had.", "annotation_id": "36353676", "url": "https://genius.com/36353676", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stars Align", "line": "I was just starin’ at your face online", "vault_lines": ["I was just starin' at your face online"], "meaning": "‘I was just starin’ at your face online' is mentioned by Drake as a reference to ‘Could it be your face I see on my computer screen’ from ‘Computer Love’ (1985) by Zapp.\n\nIn the 1980’s, computers we’re growing in popularity and Zapp correctly predicted the future of romance via computer.", "annotation_id": "25200411", "url": "https://genius.com/25200411", "state": "pending", "votes": 2, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stars Align", "line": "Freaky girl, Aries sign", "vault_lines": ["Freaky girl, Libra sign", "Freaky girl, Aries sign"], "meaning": "Drake mentions ‘Freaky girl, Aries sign’ in reference to ‘Zapp’ who sings ‘I no longer need astrology’ in ‘Computer Love’, a 1985 hit that samples ‘Temptations’ by ‘2Pac’.", "annotation_id": "25200330", "url": "https://genius.com/25200330", "state": "pending", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stars Align", "line": "I know you been searchin’ for someone To make you happy and get the job done You said you needed a man with money But I can’t be there, so will you still care? I know you been searchin’ for someone To make you happy and get the job done You said you needed a man with money But I can’t be there, so will you still care?", "vault_lines": ["I know you been searchin' for someone", "I know you need healin'", "To make you happy and get the job done", "You said you needed a man with money", "But I can't be there, so will you still care?"], "meaning": "Drake interpolates Easy Mo Bee’s chorus on 2Pac’s 1995 hit single, “Temptations”:\n\nI know you’ve been searching for someone\nTo make you happy and get the job done\nYou say you needed a man with money\nBut I can’t be there, and will you still care?\n\nEasy’s chorus is in turn an allusion to Zapp’s 1985 synth-pop track, “Computer Love,”—which both “Temptations” and “Stars Align” sample for their instrumentals, the lyrics on the first verse read:\n\nYou know I’ve been searching for someone\nWho can share that special love with me\nAnd your eyes have that glow\nCould it be your face I see on my computer screen", "annotation_id": "24965597", "url": "https://genius.com/24965597", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Stars Align", "line": "I’m tryna link on some ASAP vibes", "vault_lines": ["I'm tryna link on some ASAP vibes"], "meaning": "Perhaps more than meets the eye: Drake could refer directly to A$AP Rocky and his relationship with popstar and icon Rihanna, with whom Drake has a multiplex history with himself.\n\nMeaning there could still be some feelings left for Rihanna by Drake as he is trying to link with her in the same way A$AP does thus “on some ASAP vibes”. He confessed his love for her openly in 2016 at the VMAs.", "annotation_id": "24821333", "url": "https://genius.com/24821333", "state": "pending", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Never Satisfied", "status": "done", "targets": 6, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Future-never-satisfied-lyrics", "genius_title": "Never Satisfied", "genius_id": 395255, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Never Satisfied", "line": "​I found the one and say, “I’ll never cheat again” ​We don’t talk for like some months I ended up fucking with her friend", "vault_lines": ["​We don’t talk for like some months", "I ended up fucking with her friend", "​I found the one and say, \"I'll never cheat again\""], "meaning": "Only part in the song that sounds off to me. Openly lying about your character, and not really cheating, but labeling it as that because it sounds better than admitting whatever women he had feelings for didn’t want him back. IMO It sounds like things naturally faded out. Weird flex.\n\nP.S. Drake clearly didn’t get the memo that the song was about Women’s dissatisfaction, not his own. Make’s it sound like Future on the intro was calling him a btch, because he can’t understand why these btches are never satisfied..", "annotation_id": "39368214", "url": "https://genius.com/39368214", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Never Satisfied", "line": "Name a bag in the store that she ain’t got Name a designer store that we ain’t shop They ain’t never satisfied", "vault_lines": ["I ain't never satisfied, yeah, I ain't never satisfied, yeah, yeah", "Cause I ain't never satisfied", "I ain't never satisfied", "Name a bag in the store that she ain't got", "Name a designer store that we ain't shop", "They ain't never satisfied", "​Trying though, they ain't never satisfied", "I ain't never satisfied, yeah, I ain't never satisfied", "​But I ain't never satisfied", "Yeah, I ain't never satisfied, yeah"], "meaning": "Here, Future gives the examples of having every bag in a store and having been in every store and still not being satisfied. Excessive possesions and spending is a frequent theme in Future’s songs. Think of the song “Honest”’s chorus, which is from the same album.\n\n“Name another nigga hot, I’m just honest\nGold bottles on bottles, I’m just honest\n100,000 on watches, I’m just honest\nCoupes all on coupes, I’m just honest\nI keep a gang of bad bitches with me too\nAnd we ain’t never going back to what we used to do\nI was gon lie to you but I had to tell the truth\nI’m just bein' honest”", "annotation_id": "26668613", "url": "https://genius.com/26668613", "state": "pending", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Never Satisfied", "line": "(EarDrummers) (Mike WiLL Made-It)", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "EarDrummers is one of the main producer tags from Mike WiLL Made-It, who was a main producer on this track. It is the main tag for his record label Ear Drummer Records as well. The tag has been used multiple times in the past, perhaps most notably on March 2017’s “Perfect Pint.”\n\nMike WiLL has collaborated with both Future and Drake individually before, on tracks like January 2013’s track, “Love Me.”", "annotation_id": "18722211", "url": "https://genius.com/18722211", "state": "accepted", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Never Satisfied", "line": "My pain still runnin’ deeper than the ocean", "vault_lines": ["My pain still runnin' deeper than the ocean"], "meaning": "Even though future is well known and have money, he still have struggles. He now has to make good songs, to be able to survive.\n\nThis was a reference to a song Future made in the past, 2012\"’s Deeper Than The Ocean from the Astronaut Status mixtape.", "annotation_id": "3126748", "url": "https://genius.com/3126748", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Never Satisfied", "line": "I’m putting pressure on these niggas and I know", "vault_lines": ["I'm putting pressure on these niggas and I know"], "meaning": "A reference to OVO Fest where Drake brought out Ye. Kanye admitted Drizzy pressured him and Jay Z to make Watch the Throne\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=player_detailpage&v=Zakf6fwlP48#t=268", "annotation_id": "3089026", "url": "https://genius.com/3089026", "state": "accepted", "votes": 5, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Never Satisfied", "line": "​No matter what you do, it’s never enough ​I don’t understand these bitches, Drizzy ​Trying though, they ain’t never satisfied", "vault_lines": ["​No matter what you do, it's never enough", "I ain't never satisfied, yeah, I ain't never satisfied, yeah, yeah", "Cause I ain't never satisfied", "I ain't never satisfied", "​I don’t understand these bitches, Drizzy", "They ain't never satisfied", "​Trying though, they ain't never satisfied", "I ain't never satisfied, yeah, I ain't never satisfied", "​But I ain't never satisfied", "Yeah, I ain't never satisfied, yeah"], "meaning": "People put forth their most into their work, but the consumer will always want more, rather it’s bitches(Yes bitches expect more), fans, or family, everyone will always want more and expect more.\n\n\n\nThe irony is within this song, people got a snippet at first and thought it would be a really nice song. Sadly the song is barely 2 minutes and their is no Drake verse that everyone was expecting. Future pretty much paints the picture of how people feel when he gives, people will always want more. I doubt that’s the case but this song had a lot of potential to be more then what it is.", "annotation_id": "3086911", "url": "https://genius.com/3086911", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
