{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Both", "status": "done", "targets": 9, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Gucci-mane-both-lyrics", "genius_title": "Both", "genius_id": 2933001, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Both", "line": "But you ain’t gotta fuck with me, my nig, but you’re stuck with me But how you called the cops on me, my nig? You grew up with me", "vault_lines": ["But you ain't gotta fuck with me, my nig, but you're stuck with me", "But how you called the cops on me, my nig? You grew up with me"], "meaning": "In September 2013, one of Gucci’s friends called the police on him, complaining about his “erratic behavior.”\n\n The cops who arrived on the scene arrested him and found that he was in possession of a handgun and a small amount of marijuana. The arrest eventually led to a 183-day jail sentence.", "annotation_id": "11068280", "url": "https://genius.com/11068280", "state": "accepted", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Both", "line": "Yeah, you think I need you but I don’t Just left out Dubai with all my folk", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, you think I need you but I don't", "Just left out Dubai with all my folk"], "meaning": "Drake was indeed in Dubai a few weeks before this song’s release, as seen in several Instagram posts.\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/BNg9R-VDV-M/?taken-by=champagnepapi\n\nThis line could also be a reply to Rihanna’s ‘needed me’ song. Rihanna sang about how men she’s been rumored to be with (including Drake, A$AP Rocky etc) needed her for love, fame etc. But she’s a savage and only used them for sex. The release of this song happened just shortly after Drake’s breakup with Rihanna.", "annotation_id": "11030082", "url": "https://genius.com/11030082", "state": "accepted", "votes": 61, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Both", "line": "If Young Metro don’t trust you, I’m gon’ shoot you", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Metro Boomin informs us of his involvement in this song with one of his many production tags; past ones include “Metro Boomin wants some more, nigga” and “Young Metro, Young Metro, Young Metro.”\n\nThe line itself comes from the bridge of Uncle Murda’s “Right Now” and is delivered by Future, Metro Boomin’s longtime collaborator. It gained prominence after appearing on Drake and Future’s hit collaboration “Jumpman,” and even found itself in the political sphere, making its way into a Complex interview of former presidential candidate Ben Carson and protests of Donald Trump in Chicago.", "annotation_id": "11029534", "url": "https://genius.com/11029534", "state": "accepted", "votes": 74, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Both", "line": "This Patek Philippe gon’ make this crooked judge try throw the book at me I look like half a million worth of heroin when she look at me", "vault_lines": ["This Patek Philippe gon' make this crooked judge try throw the book at me", "I look like half a million worth of heroin when she look at me"], "meaning": "Patek Philippe is a Swiss luxury watch manufacturer known for their complicated timepieces. They are considered one of the most prestigious watch brands in the world, and come with a expensive price tag.\n\n\n\nA judge that abuses their authority is considered crooked, and “throwing the book” at someone means you’re seeking maximum punishment. Gucci’s expensive jewelry looks like something a drug dealer would wear, so the judge already thinks he’s guilty.", "annotation_id": "11027418", "url": "https://genius.com/11027418", "state": "accepted", "votes": 47, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Both", "line": "I got so many felonies, I might can’t never go to Canada But Drake said he gon’ pull some strings, so let me check my calendar", "vault_lines": ["I got so many felonies, I might can't never go to Canada", "But Drake said he gon' pull some strings, so let me check my calendar"], "meaning": "In the past, Gucci has been arrested for assault, probation violation, pushing a woman out of a moving vehicle, battery, reckless conduct, aggravated assault, carrying a concealed weapon, disorderly conduct (twice), and possession of marijuana.\n\nKnown for its strict laws on criminals entering the country, Canada would probably turn Gucci away. However, with Drake’s stardom, he’d be able to help Guwop enter seamlessly.\n\nThis isn’t the first time Drake has bragged about his ability to handle border issues. On “Dreams Money Can Buy”:\n\nLuckily, I’m the greatest my country’s ever seen\nSo chances are I get the border to issue me clearance\n\nAs well as “305 To My City:”\n\nYour girl got a DUI, I’ll make the calls to get y'all through customs\nTell your best friend, “Girl get your paperwork right”", "annotation_id": "11026525", "url": "https://genius.com/11026525", "state": "accepted", "votes": 109, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Both", "line": "I don’t usually do this ’less I’m drunk or I’m high But I’m both right now, got me talking about my life I don’t usually do this ’less I’m drunk or I’m high But I’m both right now I don’t usually do this ’less I’m drunk or I’m high But I’m both right now and I need ya in my life I don’t usually do this ’less I’m drunk or I’m high But I’m both right now", "vault_lines": ["I don't usually do this 'less I'm drunk or I'm high", "But I'm both right now, got me talking about my life", "But I'm both right now", "But I'm both right now and I need ya in my life"], "meaning": "Both alcohol and drugs change the brains chemistry by altering levels of neurotransmitters—the chemical that controls thought process, behaviour and emotion. This alters your perception and makes you do things you normally wouldn’t.\n\nDrake’s not afraid to mix weed and alcohol, as mentioned on “U With Me?”:\n\nAnd my house is the definition\nOf alcohol and weed addiction", "annotation_id": "11026353", "url": "https://genius.com/11026353", "state": "accepted", "votes": 165, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Both", "line": "I’m in an all-red drop tarantula, fuck a Challenger", "vault_lines": ["I'm in an all-red drop tarantula, fuck a Challenger"], "meaning": "Gucci is referring to the option to have the car as a “spider” or “spyder”—meaning a convertible or drop top. Guwop nicknames it a Tarantula, a type of spider.\n\n\n\nThe Dodge Challenger has taken on the role of the stereotypical choice when referring to the American muscle car, even adopting the slogan “classic American muscle car.” Since Challenger’s don’t come in a convertible option, Gucci doesn’t want to drive it. Perhaps he’d rather drive an import (like a Porsche or Ferrari.)\n\nAlso, “fuck a challenger” means that anyone who tries to challenge him is going to get messed up or killed.", "annotation_id": "11026255", "url": "https://genius.com/11026255", "state": "accepted", "votes": 51, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Both", "line": "This some shit I wrote about when I was broke See, the power of the mind is not a joke Man, I said that I would do it and I did Used to get left-overs out the fridge Nobody was famous where I lived ’Til I got it jumping at the crib Took a lot to be able to give, I mean", "vault_lines": ["This some shit I wrote about when I was broke", "See, the power of the mind is not a joke", "Man, I said that I would do it and I did", "Used to get left-overs out the fridge", "Nobody was famous where I lived", "'Til I got it jumping at the crib", "Took a lot to be able to give, I mean"], "meaning": "On 2009’s “Forever,” before Drake’s first album, he rapped:\n\nLast name Ever, first name Greatest\n\n7 years later, undeniable greatness and unparalleled influence in Toronto has led Drake to reminisce about the times where he wasn’t as well off as he is now.", "annotation_id": "11026141", "url": "https://genius.com/11026141", "state": "accepted", "votes": 95, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Both", "line": "Open water, my location is remote Shout-out Yachty but this ain’t a lil’ boat", "vault_lines": ["Open water, my location is remote", "Shout-out Yachty but this ain't a lil' boat"], "meaning": "Lil Boat is the nickname and alter ego of Atlanta rapper Lil Yachty.\n\nDrake plays on Lil Yachty’s nickname to emphasize the large size of the yacht he’s on.", "annotation_id": "11025543", "url": "https://genius.com/11025543", "state": "accepted", "votes": 199, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
