{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Stylist", "status": "done", "targets": 9, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/French-montana-no-stylist-lyrics", "genius_title": "No Stylist", "genius_id": 3916993, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Stylist", "line": "I got the game in a squeeze Who disagree? I wanna see one of y’all run up a B", "vault_lines": ["I got the game in a squeeze", "Who disagree? I wanna see one of y'all run up a B"], "meaning": "Drake claims that he’s currently at the top of rap game. “In a squeeze” could allude to the expression “in the palm of my hand” meaning he’s in control.\n\nOn July 7, 2018, Drake became the first ever artist to surpass 1 billion streams in one week. He challenges anyone who disagrees with him to achieve this feat before saying he’s not the hottest in the game.\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/p/Bk74N2rn4p0/?utm_source=ig_embed", "annotation_id": "15432877", "url": "https://genius.com/15432877", "state": "accepted", "votes": 72, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Stylist", "line": "And that’s Capo in the back, and that’s swole in the back", "vault_lines": ["And that's Capo in the back, and that's swole in the back"], "meaning": "Most likely referencing Capo from Halal Gang in Toronto. Drake has cosigned Smoke Dawg, Puffy L'z, and SAFE whom are all friends of Capo. MTV mentioned the gang in their 2016 piece “Toronto World: Drake, Halal Gang, and the Diaspora in the 6”\n\nSwole is slang for being muscular or buff, Drake used to be a skinny, ropy Wheelchair Jimmy (his character on “Degrassi: The Nest Generation”) to now nearly being a body builder. According to his personal trainer, Jonny Roxx, Drake has been putting in the time in order to obtain his new muscular physique. He is saying that he has gained muscle in his back.", "annotation_id": "15429292", "url": "https://genius.com/15429292", "state": "accepted", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Stylist", "line": "French Vanilla sippin’ on", "vault_lines": ["French Vanilla sippin' on"], "meaning": "French Montana is very close friends with the owner of Ciroc, Sean “Diddy” Combs. In this line, Montana is talking about the drink that P Diddy put out in honor of French Montana as this Ciroc line is called “French Vanilla”", "annotation_id": "15426303", "url": "https://genius.com/15426303", "state": "accepted", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Stylist", "line": "I’m in London, got my beat from London", "vault_lines": ["I'm in London, got my beat from London"], "meaning": "These lyrics are a direct sample from Kodak Black’s outro to his song “Roll in Peace,” featuring XXXTENTACION.\n\nThis is London on da Track’s tag who produced both “No Stylist” and “Roll in Peace.” London has used the producer tag, “We got London On Da Track” until this release.", "annotation_id": "15418653", "url": "https://genius.com/15418653", "state": "accepted", "votes": 72, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Stylist", "line": "Hoppin’ out the jet, Lears (Lear)", "vault_lines": ["Hoppin' out the jet, Lears (Lear)"], "meaning": "Learjet is a Canadian owned business jet manufacturer based in the United States. In 1990, Learjet Corporation filed for bankruptcy and was acquired by Bombardier Incorporated.\n\nBombardier Aerospace continue to manufacture models under the Learjet name.", "annotation_id": "15417990", "url": "https://genius.com/15417990", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Stylist", "line": "Iced out (Stylist), no stylist (Stylist) New Chanel, Saint Laurent, Gucci bag (Huh, haan) Lifestyle (Stylist), no stylist (Stylist) Louboutin, Jimmy Choo, that’s on you (Haan) Diamonds on my neck, frozen tears (Tears)", "vault_lines": ["Iced out (Stylist), no stylist (Stylist)", "New Chanel, Saint Laurent, Gucci bag (Huh, haan)", "Lifestyle (Stylist), no stylist (Stylist)", "Louboutin, Jimmy Choo, that’s on you (Haan)", "Diamonds on my neck, frozen tears (Tears)"], "meaning": "Chanel, Saint Laurent, Gucci, Louboutin, and Jimmy Choo are high-end, luxury clothing brands that have become an almost fundamental part of modern rap music.\n\n“Iced out” and “frozen” refers to diamond jewelry because of the resemblance between ice and diamonds when reflecting light.\n\nFrench makes it clear that he has a fine taste in clothing and jewelry, which means he doesn’t take advice from others. This is something that makes him stand out in the rap game, since other rappers often hire professional stylists.", "annotation_id": "15415907", "url": "https://genius.com/15415907", "state": "accepted", "votes": 89, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Stylist", "line": "No Chanel, Nike track, doin’ road with some waps", "vault_lines": ["No Chanel, Nike track, doin' road with some waps"], "meaning": "Drake recently signed a sneaker deal with Nike, after going back and forth with Adidas, which was scrapped once Pusha T released The Story of Adidon\n\n\n\nHere Drake is shouting out the American sportswear brand, claiming he doesn’t wear Chanel when doing road\n\n\n\nIn the UK, especially London, waps is a short way of saying ‘weapons’ and is seen as a gun rather than any other weapon. He is likely referring to this since it would keep with the theme of “doin' road” which again has South-London origin.\n\nAn example of this is seen with UK drill group 67 who have a song called ‘WAPS’. In which they repeatedly refer to their routine of killing, and also earning hard cash from the illegal and legal lifestyle they live.", "annotation_id": "15415205", "url": "https://genius.com/15415205", "state": "accepted", "votes": 69, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Stylist", "line": "In Delilah, word to Zack, I need action, that’s a fact", "vault_lines": ["In Delilah, word to Zack, I need action, that's a fact"], "meaning": "Delilah is a high-class gathering place in Los Angeles, California, where patrons can relax in a 1920s-esque vibe and order food and drinks.\n\nOn December 30th, 2017, Drake and Zack Bia met up with one another and went to Delilah through the back door to hangout.", "annotation_id": "15415190", "url": "https://genius.com/15415190", "state": "accepted", "votes": 53, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "No Stylist", "line": "Yeah, keepin’ it G, I told her, “Don’t wear no 350s ’round me”", "vault_lines": ["Yeah, keepin' it G, I told her, \"Don't wear no 350s 'round me\""], "meaning": "Drake forbid his girl from wearing Kanye West Yeezy 350 Boost sneakers in his presence, as the two rappers were at odds for much of 2018.\n\n\n\nDrake’s line continues a chain of subliminal disses fired between Drake and Kanye West for several months in 2018. The feud was ignited by some hostile Pusha T lines on the Kanye-produced “Infrared,” from Pusha’s 2018 release, DAYTONA. Drake’s “Duppy Freestyle” in May 2018 was in response to the Pusha T track and included some shots at Kanye as well. A few months later, Kanye tweeted an apology for allowing the Drake disses on “Infrared”:\n\n\n\nKanye would later mention this line during a Twitter rant about Drake:", "annotation_id": "15319804", "url": "https://genius.com/15319804", "state": "accepted", "votes": 177, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "FOR ALL THE BARBZ", "status": "done", "targets": 21, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Nicki-minaj-for-all-the-barbz-lyrics", "genius_title": "FOR ALL THE BARBZ", "genius_id": 9644467, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "FOR ALL THE BARBZ", "line": "Forty K a night to sleep at the Mark", "vault_lines": ["Forty K a night to sleep at the Mark"], "meaning": "The Mark Hotel is a high end hotel located in Manhattan, NYC. Supposedly Drake  stayed there for his Apollo Theater show in back in January 2023. It happened to be that he stayed at the $75,000-a-night penthouse there (reportedly the largest and most expensive hotel room in North America.)\n\nDrake happens to be a recurring guest there, he would notably stay at the hotel again in July 2023 where he was seen exiting the establishment wearing a dog mask, to promote the release of his much anticipated album at the time, For All My Dogs.\n\nhttps://filepicker-images.genius.com/b1e282eafe187b4c204a4357f0197f31dfa9eec879af36767ee840783410661b%2Fnna9slugvg", "annotation_id": "37621838", "url": "https://genius.com/37621838", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "FOR ALL THE BARBZ", "line": "Doctor’s office was the last time that you niggas even had your name on a chart", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Being a stable presence on the music charts, Drake dismisses his adversaries' relevance in the industry. The line jokingly hints that the only chart his competitors can claim to have their names on is a medical chart, not a music chart where artists measure commercial success. A medical chart is a form containing personal info like a patient’s name.", "annotation_id": "37621314", "url": "https://genius.com/37621314", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "FOR ALL THE BARBZ", "line": "Pushin’ your pen or you pushin’ your luck", "vault_lines": ["Ayo, pushin' your pen or you pushin' your luck"], "meaning": "In this line, Nicki is asking a rhetorical question if any of her opponents are “pushin” their luck with their recent success, or are they actually talented? Nick is insinuating that their musical success is actually due to many other factors, but none regarding their actual lyrical ability.", "annotation_id": "29894008", "url": "https://genius.com/29894008", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "FOR ALL THE BARBZ", "line": "She at all the parties, T’d up with 3Hunna She just did her body, she in love with Sosa", "vault_lines": ["She at all the parties, T'd up with 3Hunna", "She just did her body, she in love with Sosa"], "meaning": "3Hunna is the group that Chief Keef, Lil Reese, Lil Durk and other artists from Chicago are part of. The term refers to the 300 set located in the south side of Englewood, Chicago, as shown:\n\n\n\nTo be T’d up is slang for turnt up, like in a party for example.\n\n“She just did her body” means that the lady BigGucciSosa is talking about must have gotten some form of surgery done to alter her shape and/or physical appearance, most likely to please Chief sosa himself.\n\nOn a side note Chief Keef snapped on this chorus.", "annotation_id": "29877047", "url": "https://genius.com/29877047", "state": "pending", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "FOR ALL THE BARBZ", "line": "Walk-in closet, got more Chrome than a Stark", "vault_lines": ["Walk-in closet, got more Chrome than a Stark"], "meaning": "Drake alludes to renowned fictional character based off of Marvel’s Iron Man and Avengers franchises, Tony Stark, who was a multi-billionaire, founder of the Avengers, however most notably, the CEO of Stark Industries.\n\nIn one of the scenes featured in Iron Man 3, Tony can be literally seen walking into a closet filled with Iron Man suits, most notably being Iron Man Mark II:\n\n\n\n Pictured: Tony Stark walking into an Iron Man-filled wardrobe, with Iron Man Mark II being featured on the left \n\n\nThese lyrics can also be seen as a double entendre, referring to Richard Stark, who’s an American fashion designer and co-founder of American luxury fashion brand Chrome Hearts—a brand Drake has showed his admiration for throughout his rap lyrics and previously collaborated with to design a custom “Chrome Hearts Cullinan” back in April 2021.", "annotation_id": "29863759", "url": "https://genius.com/29863759", "state": "accepted", "votes": 16, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
