{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "FOR ALL THE BARBZ", "line": "H-h-here we go, he tryna make honey nut like Cheerios, uh (Ah, ah)", "vault_lines": ["H-h-here we go, he tryna make honey nut like Cheerios, uh (Ah, ah)"], "meaning": "In this line, Nicki uses a play on the cereal brand ‘Honey Nut Cheerios’ stating, He = Kenneth Petty, is trying to make honey=nicki, nut like cheerios", "annotation_id": "29853424", "url": "https://genius.com/29853424", "state": "pending", "votes": 12, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "FOR ALL THE BARBZ", "line": "I make the movies, I give you bitches cameos, uh (Ooh-ah)", "vault_lines": ["I make the movies, I give you bitches cameos, uh (Ooh-ah)"], "meaning": "Throughout her musical career, Nicki Minaj has also made a lane for herself on the big screen. She’s appeared in The Other Woman, Barbershop: The Next Cut & The Angry Birds Movie 2 to just name a few.\n\nWhile Nicki is starring in all of these big Hollywood films, she alludes to only giving her “opps” cameo roles.\n\nCameo roles are brief guest appearances in television and film.\n\nShe also ties this into how she has ran female rap for years by her lonesome and can be gracious enough to give other females cameos in the movie of female rap.\n\nhttps://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cameo_appearance", "annotation_id": "29853419", "url": "https://genius.com/29853419", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "FOR ALL THE BARBZ", "line": "I get these bitches scramblin’ when I throw the bait", "vault_lines": ["I get these bitches scramblin' when I throw the bait"], "meaning": "Nicki has been known to throw false information as a way to deter her “opps” (as she affectionately called her foes). Once Minaj drops these false “hints”, people have been seen to quickly “scramble” to either copy, or attempt to overshadow Nicki, when indeed it was her plan all along.", "annotation_id": "29853407", "url": "https://genius.com/29853407", "state": "pending", "votes": 15, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "FOR ALL THE BARBZ", "line": "These bitches don’t want beef, chef, hold the steak These bitches don’t want smoke, say “no” to vape", "vault_lines": ["These bitches don't want beef, chef, hold the steak", "These bitches don't want smoke, say \"no\" to vape"], "meaning": "“Smoke” and “beef” are both slang for conflict.\n\nThere are 2 plays on words here: Steak is a cut of beef, and vaping is an alternative to smoking cigarettes.", "annotation_id": "29853406", "url": "https://genius.com/29853406", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "FOR ALL THE BARBZ", "line": "Pink Friday 2, Heavy On It, overweight", "vault_lines": ["Pink Friday 2, Heavy On It, overweight"], "meaning": "A nod to her upcoming album, Pink Friday 2 and a play on her record label name, Heavy On It Records. The pun being an overweight person is heavy.", "annotation_id": "29853396", "url": "https://genius.com/29853396", "state": "pending", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "FOR ALL THE BARBZ", "line": "Bitches ain’t eatin’, worried about who overweight", "vault_lines": ["Bitches ain't eatin', worried about who overweight"], "meaning": "One of the biggest “criticisms” used towards Nicki is her weight. While she is in fact NOT overweight, it is something that is used to “drag” her across multiple social media platforms.\n\nIn recent years, “eating” and “ate” have been described as an action of someone doing something very well.\n\nShe iterates that the same people who are not doing well in their respective industries, are the exact people who are attacking Minaj over her physical appearance.", "annotation_id": "29853381", "url": "https://genius.com/29853381", "state": "pending", "votes": 19, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "FOR ALL THE BARBZ", "line": "Keep it a hundred, keep it in a trust If I lose ninety-nine, I still keep it a buck", "vault_lines": ["Keep it a hundred, keep it in a trust", "If I lose ninety-nine, I still keep it a buck"], "meaning": "“Keep it a hundred” and “keep it a buck” are both phrases for being honest and trustworthy.\nThe pun here is even if she loses everything she has she’ll still be a down to earth and honest person.", "annotation_id": "29853376", "url": "https://genius.com/29853376", "state": "pending", "votes": 14, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "FOR ALL THE BARBZ", "line": "Tummy on tuck and my titties reduct", "vault_lines": ["Tummy on tuck and my titties reduct"], "meaning": "Earlier this year, around the time of the filming of the Barbie World music video, Nicki Minaj made it to social media announcing her new breast reduction in a post stating “New boobs, who dis”", "annotation_id": "29853374", "url": "https://genius.com/29853374", "state": "pending", "votes": 17, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "FOR ALL THE BARBZ", "line": "One sub kill five bitches, OceanGate, mmm", "vault_lines": ["One sub kill five bitches, OceanGate, mmm"], "meaning": "OceanGate is a private American company that employs submersibles for tourism, research & exploration. In June of 2023, the submersible Titan, responsible for an expedition to the sunken ship Titanic imploded with 5 people onboard.\n\nA “sub” is also in reference to a “subliminal diss” which is a diss that isn’t apparent at first listen, but so integrated, that it needs to be uncovered and usually packs a big punch.\n\nNicki ties this OceanGate scandal to how her “sub(s)” can be used to “kill” (hit) 5 different people at the same time. This goes to show her insane ability to craft lyrics with multiple meanings and multiple targets.\n\nhttps://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/OceanGate", "annotation_id": "29853361", "url": "https://genius.com/29853361", "state": "pending", "votes": 30, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "FOR ALL THE BARBZ", "line": "VMA’s was a family reunion First time in a while I seen all of my sons", "vault_lines": ["VMA's was a family reunion", "First time in a while I seen all of my sons"], "meaning": "The MTV 2023 Video Music Awards (VMA) audience was FILLED with Barbz, Nicki’s fanbase. There were points where Nicki ran out of breath yet they crowds were talking for her.\n\nNicki is known as the Queen/ Mother of rap, her “sons” in this context being female rappers such as Cardi B, Megan Thee stallion and Ice Spice.", "annotation_id": "29853356", "url": "https://genius.com/29853356", "state": "pending", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
