{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Right Here", "status": "done", "targets": 4, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Justin-bieber-right-here-lyrics", "genius_title": "Right Here", "genius_id": 77620, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Right Here", "line": "’Cause I’m right here, ain’t nobody gotta hold ya ‘Cause I’m right here, ain’t nobody gon’ control ya ’Cause I’m right, right here, yeah, yeah I’m right here, I’m right here, I’m right here, I’m right here, yeah I’m right here, I’m right here, yeah I’m right here, I’m right here, yeah", "vault_lines": ["'Cause I'm right here, ain't nobody gotta hold ya", "'Cause I'm right here, ain't nobody gon' control ya", "'Cause I'm right, right here, yeah, yeah", "I'm right here, I'm right here, I'm right here, I'm right here, yeah", "I'm right here, I'm right here, yeah", "I'm right here, I'm right here, yeah yeah"], "meaning": "Bieber will be totally loyal to this girl. Nobody else has to control her or even needs to hold her because he will do all these things for her.\n\nIn 2012, Bieber earned 40 million dollars from the Believe tour, and earned almost 70 million more in 2013, so it’s safe to assume he can provide for this girl.\n\nAfter Believe’s release, Bieber got into a lot of legal trouble, making him a less-suitable candidate for a lover. However, he’s apologized for his ways, and even if he does drop the PG lyrics, he’s still a better person. In fact, Bieber says the biggest misconception about him is that he is a bad person–he’s not.", "annotation_id": "8608687", "url": "https://genius.com/8608687", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Right Here", "line": "No, ’cause I just wanna love you I will never ever put nobody up above you I just wanna kiss you, baby I just wanna hug you ’til the end, baby, ’til the end (’Til the end, girl)", "vault_lines": ["I just wanna hug you 'til the end, baby, 'til the end ('Til the end, girl)", "I will never ever put nobody else up above you", "No, 'cause I just wanna love you", "I will never ever put nobody up above you", "I just wanna kiss you, baby"], "meaning": "Bieber (or Drake) declares his everlasting love for this girl. He’s in love with her, and will continue to be so until, presumably, his death–“the end” of his life.\n\nNote the PG lyricism: he’ll “kiss” and “hug” her. Even Drake, who’s known for his “right there” lyrics about sex, keeps it totally appropriate for Bieber’s generally pre-teen fanbase. Of course, his style would later change with the release of his fifth album Purpose, but on Believe, JB’s still keeping it clean.", "annotation_id": "8608655", "url": "https://genius.com/8608655", "state": "accepted", "votes": 9, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Right Here", "line": "And I say, good girl’s got her mind right She been raised right, being patient I know you waiting Waiting on the good things when the time’s right You should let me get to know you, baby But I just wanna put it on you, if you want to Baby, tell me what you gon’ do, girl I can make you feel perfect, girl, you’re worth it I just need to see you work it, girl", "vault_lines": ["I just wanna hug you 'til the end, baby, 'til the end ('Til the end, girl)", "And I say, good girl's got her mind right", "She been raised right, being patient I know you waiting", "Waiting on the good things when the time's right", "You should let me get to know you, baby", "But I just wanna put it on you, if you want to", "Baby, tell me what you gon' do, girl", "I can make you feel perfect, girl, you're worth it", "I just need to see you work it, girl", "I just wanna kiss you, baby"], "meaning": "Drake and JB have found a good girl from a good home. This comes a huge contrast to previous Drake lines…\n\n “I like a bad bitch from a decent home”\n\nRegardless, they’ll wait for the good times when it’s right for them. Combine waiting until readiness with “I just wanna put it on you, if you want to” and “I just need to see you work it” means that they’re probably going to have sex. Of course, Bieber was barely 18 at this song’s release, so he’d want to make sure his lyrics involve clearly consensual sex, if any at all.", "annotation_id": "843228", "url": "https://genius.com/843228", "state": "accepted", "votes": 6, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Right Here", "line": "Say you’ll be mine, say we’ll be fine, say we’ll be together Selfish of me to ask, since I be the reason we don’t last forever Wished that you knew all that I do to make this thing go right Promise to be all that you need, I won’t leave you, baby", "vault_lines": ["Say you'll be mine, say we'll be fine, say we'll be together", "Selfish of me to ask, since I be the reason we don't last forever", "Wished that you knew all that I do to make this thing go right", "Promise to be all that you need, I won't leave you, baby"], "meaning": "Although JB pleaded for a girl to date him, Drizzy pleads with a girl to stay with him. Although he’s done a lot to keep the relationship together, he’s also apparently the reason it fell apart, which is an odd juxtaposition.\n\nRegardless of the possible breakup, Drake gives the same reasons to stay together as Bieber did: because he’ll love her, kiss her, won’t leave her, and hug her.\n\nNote that Drake has a solo song called “We’ll Be Fine” In that song, he also tries to let go of the past in a relationship.", "annotation_id": "842462", "url": "https://genius.com/842462", "state": "accepted", "votes": 21, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "S.O.Y.", "status": "done", "targets": 2, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Jori-vague-soy-lyrics", "genius_title": "S.O.Y.", "genius_id": 1906517, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "S.O.Y.", "line": "Did me wrong every time we were together, gether And that’s why", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Drake is gonna show this girl he’s doing just fine without her and in fact he’s gonna show her he’s doing great by stunting on her.", "annotation_id": "8552065", "url": "https://genius.com/8552065", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "S.O.Y.", "line": "Childish as it seems it will make it all better, better Selfish as it is this ain’t’ just about you noooooo", "vault_lines": ["Childish as it seems it will make it all better, better", "Selfish as it is this ain't' just about you noooooo"], "meaning": "Drake claims that this girl should not mistake this all for a cry for help and that he wants her back. It’s just for him and his ego to let her see how much he achieved.\n\n\n\nThis is probably what Drake hopes she be like when she sees him driving up and down.", "annotation_id": "6599620", "url": "https://genius.com/6599620", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
