{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ela É do Tipo (Remix)", "status": "done", "targets": 5, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Mc-kevin-o-chris-ela-e-do-tipo-remix-lyrics", "genius_title": "Ela É do Tipo (Remix)", "genius_id": 4961578, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ela É do Tipo (Remix)", "line": "[Verse 1: Drake]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Translation (Portuguese):\nPrimeira vez que eu te vi, eu não estava pensando em nós\nSó estava pensando em mim\nPrimeira vez que nós transamos foi na minha casa, uns dois anos depois\nMas foi o destino e eu acho que você gostou daquilo\nE agora nós estamos nesse lugar que nós dois odiamos\nE eu acho que precisamos sacrificar algo\nNão é justo, não é certo, é difícil\nVocê deixar aquele cara só pra vir ficar comigo", "annotation_id": "18395932", "url": "https://genius.com/18395932", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ela É do Tipo (Remix)", "line": "[Verse 2: Kevin o Chris]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Translation:\nShe’s the type of girl that talks a lot\nBut doesn’t just chitchat\nTake your clothes off, lay on my bed\nAnd while she’s talking, she takes my clothes off\nThis girl fucks really good\nAnd I can see she likes what she’s doing\nShawty is bad and nice\nShe let Kevin wanting for more", "annotation_id": "18395901", "url": "https://genius.com/18395901", "state": "accepted", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ela É do Tipo (Remix)", "line": "[Bridge | Ponte: Kevin o Chris]", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "Translation:\nHer mother tried to protect her too much\nAnd she turned to a control with no battery\nWhy’d you have to mistreat her?\nAnd now she’s overage and Kevin takers care", "annotation_id": "18395838", "url": "https://genius.com/18395838", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ela É do Tipo (Remix)", "line": "Vai, rebola pro pai, novinha, vai (Vai) Descendo (Vai), descendo Vai, rebola pro pai, vai, novinha, vai (Vai) Descendo (Vai), descendo Vai, rebola pro pai, novinha, vai (Vai) Descendo (Vai), descendo", "vault_lines": ["Vai, rebola pro pai, novinha, vai (Vai)", "Vai, rebola pro pai, vai, novinha, vai (Vai)"], "meaning": "Translation:\nGo, shake it for daddy, shawty, go (Go)\nGoing down (Go), going down\nGo, shake it for daddy, go, shawty, go (Go)\nGoing down (Go), going down\nGo, shake it for daddy, shawty, go (Go)\nGoing down (Go), going down", "annotation_id": "18395831", "url": "https://genius.com/18395831", "state": "accepted", "votes": 8, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Ela É do Tipo (Remix)", "line": "Vai, rebola pro pai, vai, novinha, vai (Vai) Descendo, (Vai) descendo", "vault_lines": ["Vai, rebola pro pai, novinha, vai (Vai)", "Vai, rebola pro pai, vai, novinha, vai (Vai)"], "meaning": "Translation: Go, wiggle for daddy, go, young one (Go) // Go down, (Go) down\n\n“Novinha” is a popular term in Brazilian funk music that refers to young girls. “Descendo” is a gerund for “go down”, and it means that the girl is wiggling and dancing down to the floor, another popular dance amongst the Brazilian funk culture.\n\nThe “daddy” is contrasting with the preceding lines in the Bridge, where it is aforementioned that the mother has raised her daughter in a strict, rigorous environment and that the daughter had become a “non battery control”.", "annotation_id": "18392195", "url": "https://genius.com/18392195", "state": "pending", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "LOYAL", "status": "done", "targets": 4, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Partynextdoor-loyal-lyrics", "genius_title": "LOYAL", "genius_id": 5043616, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "LOYAL", "line": "I got money on me and I’m loyal (Oh)", "vault_lines": ["I got money on me and I'm loyal"], "meaning": "Despite having money, and all the possibilities that come with it, PARTYNEXTDOOR claims he’s still loyal to his girl.", "annotation_id": "35150124", "url": "https://genius.com/35150124", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "LOYAL", "line": "Because, true, when we can party again You’ll see you, you’re my best friend", "vault_lines": ["Because, true, when we can party again", "You'll see you, you're my best friend", "You're my best friend", "We stay true, probably can party again, yeah, yeah", "Because, true, you're my best friend"], "meaning": "Drake and Party are reflecting on the fact, that despite them being apart from the woman they care about, they will always remain loyally, each other’s best friend.\n\nThe line further represents the pair’s loyalty to these women, and despite the even summer’s apart, they will remain faithful to them.", "annotation_id": "18773499", "url": "https://genius.com/18773499", "state": "pending", "votes": 10, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "LOYAL", "line": "But I don’t want war with you or my friends", "vault_lines": ["But I don't want war with you or my friends"], "meaning": "This line represents the tricky dichotomy of a relationship between spending time with your friends or your significant others. Drake and PARTY acknowledge that they want to accommodate both their girls and their friends.", "annotation_id": "18773493", "url": "https://genius.com/18773493", "state": "pending", "votes": 7, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "LOYAL", "line": "You, nuh need fi raise war with my friends", "vault_lines": ["You, nuh need fi raise war with my friends", "You nuh need fi raise war with my friends, no, no"], "meaning": "“Nuh need fi” is Jamaican Patois for “no need for.” PARTYNEXTDOOR—whose mother is also Jamaican—often uses patois in his music. For example, on Calvin Harris' February 2018 song “Nuh Ready Nuh Ready,” he uses patois on the chorus:\n\nMi and di mandem\nWe haffi run from half of di gyal dem", "annotation_id": "18512666", "url": "https://genius.com/18512666", "state": "accepted", "votes": 27, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
