{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "My Love", "status": "done", "targets": 5, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Majid-jordan-my-love-lyrics", "genius_title": "My Love", "genius_id": 2172771, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "My Love", "line": "I had an idea in my head I pictured this going differently", "vault_lines": ["I had an idea in my head", "I pictured this going differently"], "meaning": "Majid Al Maskati: There have definitely been moments where I’ve experienced something and I’ve felt really good about it.\n\nThen something happened and it’s gotten back to me and it’s been like, “Oh, that was surprising, I totally misread that situation.”", "annotation_id": "8598170", "url": "https://genius.com/8598170", "state": "verified", "votes": 51, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "My Love", "line": "Why you wanna be my love, is it just for show? Why you wanna be my love, my love, my love, love Why you wanna be my love, is it just for show? Why you wanna be my love, my love, my love, love Why you wanna be my love, my love, my love Why you wanna be my love, my love, my love Why you wanna be my love, my love, my love Why you wanna be my love, my love, my love Why you want to, why you want to Why you want to, why you want to", "vault_lines": ["Why you wanna be my love, my love, my love, love", "Why you wanna be my love, my love, my love", "Why you want to, why you want to", "Why do you wanna be my love?", "Why do you wanna be", "Why you wanna be my love, is it just for show?"], "meaning": "Majid Al Maskati: The hook is inspired by Drake. He was the person who came up with the idea of questioning if the love is genuine or if it’s just for show.\n\nI can relate to that as a person and as an artist; you’re coming up and your world is changing and you’re meeting lots of people. You’re unsure about whether relationships are real or not. It doesn’t even have to be about a lover, it can be with anyone you’re meeting.\n\nJordan Ullman: It’s the universal question that you’re trying to answer with the song. The two verses are just two different places while you’re questioning it.", "annotation_id": "8598132", "url": "https://genius.com/8598132", "state": "verified", "votes": 61, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "My Love", "line": "What makes you so ready right now After I waited on you for so long", "vault_lines": ["What makes you so ready right now", "After I waited on you for so long"], "meaning": "Drake is suspicious as to why this girl is so prepared to start a relationship with him now after all the time he was waiting on her cause she wasn’t sure. It seems that this is because the situation has now changed. With his new fame and fortune, he can be her “trophy” and she can “show [him] off”. But that’s not the kind of relationship Drake is interested in. He wants something real.", "annotation_id": "7263656", "url": "https://genius.com/7263656", "state": "accepted", "votes": 11, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "My Love", "line": "Even when you sleep in my bed I know you’re not mine officially", "vault_lines": ["Even when you sleep in my bed", "I know you're not mine officially"], "meaning": "Drake has had his experience in relationships with celebrities such as Rihanna and rumored to have had relationships with Karrueche Tran, Bernice Burgos, and many more. Drake is stating even if he had a sexual relationship in bed with a female, he knows she is not his officially.", "annotation_id": "7260204", "url": "https://genius.com/7260204", "state": "accepted", "votes": 18, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "My Love", "line": "You got your trophies I know how you like to show ’em off and shine ’em up, and line ’em up, oh I’m not your trophy, baby I won’t let you show me off or shine me, or line me up, no You got your trophies I know how you like to show ’em off and shine ’em up, and line ’em up, oh I’m not your trophy, baby I won’t let you show me off or shine me up, or line me up, no", "vault_lines": ["You got your trophies", "I know how you like to show 'em off and shine 'em up, and line 'em up, oh", "I'm not your trophy, baby", "I won't let you show me off or shine me, or line me up, no", "I won't let you show me off or shine me up, or line me up, no"], "meaning": "Drake is already aware of his girls various other love interests. He doesn’t want to be just another guy she sleeps with and brags about with her friends. His ever-rising fame only makes him more of a trophy, which he clearly doesn’t appreciate.\n\nShe is not the only one with “Trophies,” Drizzy has a few himself as well.\n\n\n\nAsked about the ‘trophy’ line by French interviewer Mouloud Achour, the group answered:\nhttps://youtu.be/8TRh7ml75ZI?t=459", "annotation_id": "7260055", "url": "https://genius.com/7260055", "state": "accepted", "votes": 32, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cannon Ball", "status": "done", "targets": 4, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Colin-munroe-cannon-ball-lyrics", "genius_title": "Cannon Ball", "genius_id": 32129, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cannon Ball", "line": "Pass my Moselys it’s all so bright", "vault_lines": ["Pass my Moselys it's all so bright"], "meaning": "Mosley Tribes are a brand of shades that Drake is known for wearing. Why would he need shades? Because his future is too bright.\n\n\n\nAs he said in “Juice”:\n\nI can’t see you through the Mosley Tribes\nSo I don’t even flinch if you throw me high-fives", "annotation_id": "2662781", "url": "https://genius.com/2662781", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cannon Ball", "line": "And I hope when dinner’s cold my niggas do not desert me", "vault_lines": [], "meaning": "If Drake’s dinner is cold, he isn’t eatin'. However, that’s impossible, as he constantly sells records and is one of the top artists in music. Looks like his homies are never going to desert, or leave, him.\n\n\n\nHe makes a play on the homophone, desert/dessert, as dessert is what comes after dinner.", "annotation_id": "2662765", "url": "https://genius.com/2662765", "state": "accepted", "votes": 3, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cannon Ball", "line": "Olympic pools of money I’m just glad I learned to swim Cannonball, bitch, I hope the divin’ board’s sturdy", "vault_lines": ["Cannonball, bitch, I hope the divin' board's sturdy"], "meaning": "Swimming pools used for the Olympics are just what you would imagine… BIG. These pools are 25x50 meters, and can hold over 600,000 gallons of water. To fill up one of these pools with money, you’d have to have a LOT.\n\n\n\nContinuing the reference, Drake takes a different approach to the title of this song, “Cannon Ball.” Instead of blowing up, Drake uses the swimming definition, insinuating that he’s diving into the money.\n\n\n\nNote: These two lines are a continuation of “goin' in,” as people typically say that they’re “going in” when going into the water at a pool or a beach.", "annotation_id": "2662711", "url": "https://genius.com/2662711", "state": "accepted", "votes": 4, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Cannon Ball", "line": "Look, like my big bro say I’m goin’ in", "vault_lines": ["Look, like my big bro say I'm goin' in"], "meaning": "On Drake’s song, “I’m Goin' In,” his “big bro” Lil Wayne sings the hook:\n\nI’m goin' in\nAnd I'mma go hard", "annotation_id": "2662694", "url": "https://genius.com/2662694", "state": "accepted", "votes": 1, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "accepted"}
{"type": "song", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Freshman", "status": "done", "targets": 5, "clicked": 0, "genius_url": "https://genius.com/Reiyang-freshman-lyrics", "genius_title": "Freshman", "genius_id": 7633017, "source": "api"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Freshman", "line": "What if my old life has left me far behind Someday I should go and write a song", "vault_lines": ["What if I’m hiding behind my song", "What if my old life has left me far behind", "Someday I should go and write a song"], "meaning": "Reiyang is feeling nostalgic for middle school. Becoming a freshman in high school is a scary experience, especially when he used to be the biggest & strongest boy in middle school.", "annotation_id": "24979772", "url": "https://genius.com/24979772", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Freshman", "line": "But not now, I don’t have the time", "vault_lines": ["But not now, I don’t have the time"], "meaning": "Unfortunately, Reiyang’s deferral from TCU and SMU forces him to write more college essays. Reiyang’s dream is to become an USC Trojan. He is very familiar with the Trojan’s already. (he uses XL, btw ladies)", "annotation_id": "24979323", "url": "https://genius.com/24979323", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Freshman", "line": "So one day I was walking home, my grades low as hell", "vault_lines": ["So one day I was walking home, my grades low as hell"], "meaning": "A 1480 SAT score is disappointing enough to be handed a flip phone and stripped of one’s Samsung.", "annotation_id": "24979312", "url": "https://genius.com/24979312", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Freshman", "line": "Alone with no one left to support me through", "vault_lines": ["Alone with no one left to support me through"], "meaning": "His parents must legally cut him off of health care by age 26. Thanks Affordable Care Act!", "annotation_id": "24979305", "url": "https://genius.com/24979305", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Drake", "song": "Freshman", "line": "This girl doesn’t want me in her life, oh well I’ll be", "vault_lines": ["This girl doesn’t want me in her life, oh well I’ll be"], "meaning": "Although she answered his phone call proposal with a resounding “NO!, he will not let her go. Hence, he follows her around while playing Fishtopia on Gimkit. The age old saying is true. Boys do chase girls.", "annotation_id": "24979295", "url": "https://genius.com/24979295", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
